      "comment": "Formats a language-related error message into the provided buffer\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate language manager is initialized by checking g_hLanguageInstance\n2. If not initialized, assert with \"sghLNGInstance\" and exit application with code -1\n3. Call FormatErrorMessage to format the error code into the buffer\n4. If formatting succeeds (EAX != 0), return true\n5. If formatting fails, copy fallback string \"Stupid Lng.cpp error.\" to buffer\n6. Return false on fallback path\n\nParameters:\n- dwErrorCode (uint): Error code to format into human-readable message\n- lpszBuffer (char *): Output buffer to receive formatted error string\n- dwBufferSize (uint): Size of output buffer in bytes\n\nReturns:\n- true (1): Error message successfully formatted via FormatErrorMessage\n- false (0): Formatting failed, fallback error string copied to buffer\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Asserts and terminates if called before language manager initialization\n- Fallback string is language-independent hardcoded English text\n- Buffer size passed to lstrcpynA ensures no overflow on fallback\n\nError Handling:\n- Missing language instance triggers FogAssert and ExitApplicationWithCode(-1)\n- FormatErrorMessage failure silently falls back to default string\n\nGlobal Data Access:\n- g_hLanguageInstance (0x6fbdc128): Language library HINSTANCE handle\n- g_pszDefaultLngError (0x6fba6258): Pointer to fallback error string\n\nDecompiler Notes:\n- bVar1 (fFormatResult): bool return from FormatErrorMessage\n- extraout_var: Phantom variable - upper 24 bits of EAX after FormatErrorMessage call\n- CONCAT31 check tests full 32-bit EAX, not just bool return\n\nCaller Context:\n- Registered as error handler by InitializeLanguageManager at 0x6fad12f5\n- Called via function pointer when language subsystem errors occur",
