      "comment": "Initialize memory management system with dynamic heap sizing based on available physical memory.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Retrieve system memory status structure via GlobalMemoryStatus\n2. Validate minimum physical memory requirement (27.7 MB minimum)\n3. Calculate available memory after subtracting reserved amount (11 MB)\n4. Compute and clamp primary heap size (10% of available, 3MB-5MB range)\n5. Initialize primary heap with calculated size\n6. Calculate remaining memory after primary heap allocation\n7. If fAllocateExtra flag set, subtract additional 10 MB and allocate extra heap\n8. Calculate secondary heap size (remaining - 2MB) / 3, clamped to 24MB-64MB\n9. Initialize secondary memory pool with calculated parameters\n10. Initialize base memory pool with fixed 2MB allocation\n\nParameters:\ndwHeapHandle - Heap handle for memory allocation operations\nnAllocateExtraFlag - Flag indicating whether to allocate additional 10MB heap\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Function does not return a value, terminates process on memory errors\n\nSpecial Cases:\nInsufficient Memory - Displays error message and exits if physical memory < 0x1a7d000 (27.7 MB)\nExtra Allocation - When nAllocateExtraFlag != 0, additional 10MB allocated via Ordinal_10089\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x1a7d000 (27,644,928) - Minimum required physical memory in bytes\n0xb00000 (11,534,336) - Reserved memory subtracted from total (11 MB)\n0x300000 (3,145,728) - Minimum primary heap size (3 MB)\n0x500000 (5,242,880) - Maximum primary heap size (5 MB)\n0xa00000 (10,485,760) - Extra allocation size when flag set (10 MB)\n0x200000 (2,097,152) - Base memory pool allocation (2 MB)\n0x1800000 (25,165,824) - Minimum secondary heap size (24 MB)\n0x4000000 (67,108,864) - Maximum secondary heap size (64 MB)\n0x7d000 (512,000) - Fixed parameter for secondary pool (512 KB)",
