      "comment": "Performs complete resource cleanup sequence by calling external ordinal functions and internal cleanup.\n\nAlgorithm:\n\n1. Call Ordinal_10090 with resource handle for initial cleanup phase\n2. Call Ordinal_10053 with same resource handle for secondary cleanup phase  \n3. Tail call to FUN_6fb90a00 for final internal cleanup\n\nParameters:\n\ndwResourceHandle (undefined4): 32-bit resource handle or identifier passed through ECX register using __fastcall convention. This handle is used by both external ordinal cleanup functions to identify the specific resource being cleaned up.\n\nReturns:\n\nvoid: Function does not return a value, uses tail call optimization for final cleanup call\n\nSpecial Cases:\n\nThis is a simple wrapper function that coordinates cleanup sequence. The tail call optimization (JMP instead of CALL+RET) to FUN_6fb90a00 means the final cleanup function returns directly to this function's caller.\n\nExternal Functions:\n\nOrdinal_10090: First phase cleanup function (external DLL ordinal)\nOrdinal_10053: Second phase cleanup function (external DLL ordinal)  \nFUN_6fb90a00: Final internal cleanup function (tail called)",
