      "comment": "Processes configuration level requirement and formats string output if conditions are met.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Retrieve configuration value from g_ConfigEntries array using provided index\n2. Query registry for \"Diablo II\\Aux Battle.net\" configuration data into buffer\n3. Map configuration value to required level using switch statement (2→2, 3→3, 4→4, 5|6→5, 7→7, default→1)\n4. Determine registry query result flag (0→0x22 failure, success→0x01)\n5. Compare registry result flag with required level - if result < required level, process string formatting\n6. Format buffer with string pattern if level requirement is met\n7. Update registry with formatted string output\n\nParameters:\n- nConfigIndex: Index into g_ConfigEntries array to retrieve configuration value\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No explicit return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Configuration values 5 and 6 both map to requirement level 5\n- Registry query failure (result 0) sets flag to 0x22\n- Switch statement default case maps unknown values to requirement level 1\n\nStructure Layout:\nConfigEntry (12 bytes):\nOffset | Size | Field Name    | Type  | Description\n0x00   | 4    | dwId         | uint  | Configuration identifier/index\n0x04   | 4    | pData        | void* | Pointer to configuration data\n0x08   | 4    | dwFlags      | uint  | Configuration flags/type data\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x22 - Registry query failure flag\n0x01 - Registry query success flag\n0x0c - Size of ConfigEntry structure (12 bytes)\n\nError Handling:\n- Registry query failure sets bRegistryResult to 0x22\n- Conditional string processing only occurs when registry result < required level",
