      "comment": "Play video by ID with CD switching and audio/video subsystem coordination.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate video ID against bounds (must be < DAT_6fbae2b0)\n2. Set video processing flag (DAT_6fbdc12f = 1)\n3. Call video preparation function (FUN_6fad14f0)\n4. Early return if video already playing (DAT_6fbdc12d != 0)\n5. Build video filename path from global table using video ID\n6. Handle special cases for video modes based on global flags\n7. Configure video and audio paths using format strings\n8. Initialize audio/video subsystems with timing measurements\n9. Handle special logic for video ID 7 (game DLL file validation)\n10. Switch to appropriate CD for video content\n11. Attempt video resource loading with error handling\n12. Play video with callback functions if resources loaded\n13. Handle post-video cleanup and CD restoration\n14. Reset processing flags and switch back to play CD\n\nParameters:\nnVideoId (int) - Video identifier index into global video table (0 to DAT_6fbae2b0-1)\n                 Special handling for video IDs 5, 6, and 7\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value, function manages video playback state globally\n\nSpecial Cases:\nVideo ID 7: Requires d2game.dll file existence check before playback\nVideo ID 6: Sets special video flag for intro sequence  \nVideo ID 5: Conditional behavior based on DAT_6fbdc130 flag\nInvalid ID: Logs error and terminates process with FUN_6fb9a10f(-1)\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0xC (12) - Video table entry stride for filename/flags lookup\n0x80 - File attribute flag for CreateFileA call\n0x12 - Audio subsystem parameter for FUN_6fb5d370 calls\n260 - Buffer size for video filename, path, and file path strings\n\nError Handling:\nBounds check failure: Logs error via Ordinal_10023, calls FUN_6fb9a10f(-1)\nFile not found for video 7: Calls FUN_6fadab30(0) twice and sets DAT_6fbdc12c\nResource loading failure: Falls back to default path construction\nVideo playback failure: Continues with cleanup sequence\n\nStructure Layout:\nVideo Table Entry (12 bytes):\nOffset  Size  Field Name     Type     Description\n+0x0    4     pVideoName     char*    Pointer to video filename\n+0x4    4     dwFlags1       uint     Video mode flags  \n+0x8    4     dwFlags2       uint     Audio path flags\n+0xC    -     (next entry)   -        Next 12-byte video entry",
      "tags": ["PROP_LARGE", "SRC_Video.cpp", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "STRUCT_Skill", "PARAM_1", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
