      "comment": "Disables video initialization system and resets video state flags.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Set global video initialization enabled flag to false (0x6fbdc12c = false)\n2. Call external video driver initialization function (Ordinal_10191)  \n3. Store inverse of driver result as success flag (0x6fbdc12e = driver_result == 0)\n4. Clear video state flags at 0x6fbdc130 and 0x6fbdc12f to 0\n\nParameters:\n  None\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Driver init failure (non-zero return) results in success flag being set to true\n  - Driver init success (zero return) results in success flag being set to false\n  - This suggests the flag indicates \"video driver needs reinitialization\"\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x6fbdc12c - g_fVideoInitEnabled: Global video initialization enabled flag\n  0x6fbdc12e - Global video driver reinitialization needed flag  \n  0x6fbdc12f - Video state flag (purpose TBD)\n  0x6fbdc130 - Video state flag (purpose TBD)",
