      "comment": "Pushes an application mode value onto the global application mode stack.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if stack is full (count > 4, max 5 elements)\n2. If stack full, trigger assertion error with debug info and terminate process\n3. Store the new application mode value at stack[count] position  \n4. Increment the stack count to reflect new element\n5. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\nnAppMode (int) - Application mode value to push onto stack\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\nStack Overflow: When count exceeds 4, calls assertion handler with error message\nMagic Numbers:\n0x4 (4) - Maximum stack index before overflow (stack size = 5)\n0xa6 (166) - Line number for assertion error message\n0xffffffff (-1) - Exit code passed to termination function\n\nGlobal Data Access:\nDAT_6fbdc264 - Application mode stack count (uint)\nDAT_6fbdc23c - Application mode stack array base (int[5])\nString references for error reporting (file path and assertion message)",
