      "comment": "Pops and returns the top application mode from the global application mode stack\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if stack is empty (g_dwStackCount == 0)\n2. If empty, log error message with mode information and terminate process\n3. Load top stack value from g_dwTopStackValue for return\n4. Shift all remaining stack elements down by one position\n5. Decrement stack counter\n6. Return popped application mode value\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\nuint - The application mode value that was popped from the stack top\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Empty Stack: Calls error logging (Ordinal_10023) with context strings and exits via FUN_6fb9a10f(-1)\n- Stack underflow protection via early termination prevents corruption\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x6fbdc264 - g_dwStackCount: Global stack counter/depth\n0x6fbdc23c - g_dwTopStackValue: Value at top of stack (to be returned)  \n0x6fbdc240 - g_adStackData: Start of 3-element application mode stack array\n0x6fbdc24c - Stack boundary (0x6fbdc240 + 12 bytes = 3 elements × 4 bytes)\n0xffffffff - Error code passed to termination function\n0xb0 - Error message buffer size parameter for logging\n\nError Handling:\n- Stack underflow: Logs error context and terminates process immediately\n- No graceful recovery - designed as fatal error condition\n- Error message includes source file paths and context information\n\nStructure Layout:\nGlobal Stack Structure (12 bytes at 0x6fbdc240):\nOffset | Size | Field Name    | Type | Description\n0x00   | 4    | element[0]    | uint | Bottom stack element  \n0x04   | 4    | element[1]    | uint | Middle stack element\n0x08   | 4    | element[2]    | uint | Top stack element",
