      "comment": "Developer-Only Command Line Help Display\n\nDisplays available command-line options in a MessageBox, but only for a specific\ndeveloper user (\"rseis\"). Uses a one-shot flag to prevent multiple displays.\n\nClassification: Internal Utility / Debug Function\nCallers: 0 (likely called from startup initialization via function pointer)\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if help already shown (g_fDevHelpShown != 0) - early exit if true\n2. Set one-shot flag to prevent future displays\n3. Get current Windows username via GetUserNameA\n4. Compare username to developer name \"rseis\" using SCompareN\n5. If comparison FAILS (not equal), show MessageBox with command-line options\n   Note: Logic is inverted - help shows when user is NOT the developer\n\nParameters: None\n\nReturns: void (implicit via stdcall with RET 0x8 cleaning 8 bytes - likely called as event handler)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Username buffer limited to 15 chars (buffer size 16 with null)\n- Only shown once per session via g_fDevHelpShown flag\n- Inverted logic: MessageBox shown when NOT matching \"rseis\"\n\nGlobals Accessed:\n- g_fDevHelpShown (0x6fbdc260): One-shot flag, 0=not shown, 1=shown\n- szDevUserName (0x6fbae6d4): Developer username \"rseis\"\n- PTR_s_Available_command_line_options (0x6fba62f0): Help text pointer\n- PTR_g_szDiabloII (0x6fba6260): Window title \"Diablo II\"\n\nAPI Calls:\n- GetUserNameA: Retrieves current Windows username\n- SCompareN: Storm string comparison (case-sensitive, max length)\n- MessageBoxA: Displays modal dialog box",
