      "comment": "Pre-commits a 96MB memory pool by touching every page.\n\nAllocates a large memory block (0x6000000 = 96MB) and writes zero to the first byte of every 4KB page, forcing the OS to commit physical memory for each page. The allocation is then released back to the pool for later use.\n\nThis technique ensures physical memory is pre-faulted and available, reducing page fault latency during gameplay.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate 96MB via FogMemAlloc from WINMAIN.CPP line 285\n2. Calculate end pointer (base + 0x6000000)\n3. Loop: Write 0 to first byte of each 4KB page (stride 0x1000)\n4. Release allocation back to memory pool\n5. Return 1 (success)\n\nParameters:\n  None (void function)\n\nReturns:\n  int - Always returns 1 (TRUE/success)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x6000000 - 96MB allocation size (96 * 1024 * 1024)\n  0x1000 - 4KB page size (standard x86 page)\n  0x11d (285) - Source line number in WINMAIN.CPP\n\nSSA Variables (register-based, not renameable):\n  puVar2 (pbCurrentPage): byte* - Current page pointer, iterates in 4KB increments\n  puVar1 (pbEndAddress): byte* - End address sentinel (base + 96MB)\n\nNote: RET 0x8 suggests function may have had hidden stack parameters at some point. No callers found - likely called via function pointer during initialization.",
