      "comment": "Match Command Line Option With Developer Help Display\n\nSearches through a table of command-line option strings to find a match against\nthe provided context. If no match is found, displays developer command-line help\n(for non-developer users only).\n\nClassification: Initialization / Command-Line Parser\nCallers: 0 xrefs (likely called via function pointer from startup)\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize option index counter to 0\n2. Set pointer to start of command-line option string table (g_apszCmdLineOptions)\n3. Loop through option table entries:\n   a. If current option string pointer is not NULL:\n      - Call LocaleMapStringWithConversion to compare option with context string\n      - If match found (returns 0): store index in g_nMatchedCmdLineOptionIndex, return\n   b. Advance to next table entry, increment index\n   c. Continue until reaching table end (PTR_g_pdwBasePropertyString_6fbae4c8)\n4. No match found - check if developer help already shown (g_fDevHelpShown)\n5. If not shown:\n   a. Set one-shot flag g_fDevHelpShown = 1\n   b. Get current Windows username via GetUserNameA (max 15 chars)\n   c. Compare username to developer name \"rseis\" via SCompareN\n   d. If NOT matching developer: show MessageBox with command-line help\n\nParameters:\npCmdLineContext (dword): Pointer to command-line context structure\n  - Offset +0x18: Pointer to string to match against option table\n\nReturns: void (implicit success via stored index or help display)\n\nGlobals Accessed:\n- g_apszCmdLineOptions (0x6fbae49c): Array of command-line option string pointers\n- g_nMatchedCmdLineOptionIndex (0x6fbae468): Stores matched option index on success\n- g_fDevHelpShown (0x6fbdc260): One-shot flag preventing repeated help display\n- szDevUserName (0x6fbae6d4): Developer username \"rseis\"\n- g_pszCmdLineHelp (0x6fba62f0): Command-line help text pointer\n- g_pszDiabloII (0x6fba6260): \"Diablo II\" window title\n\nAPI Calls:\n- LocaleMapStringWithConversion: Case-insensitive locale-aware string comparison\n- GetUserNameA: Retrieve current Windows username\n- SCompareN: Storm library string comparison\n- MessageBoxA: Display modal dialog\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Option table contains 11 entries (0x6fbae49c to 0x6fbae4c8, stride 4)\n- Some table entries may be NULL (skipped during iteration)\n- Help only shown once per session (one-shot pattern)\n- Inverted logic: help shown when NOT matching developer username",
