      "comment": "Validates and retrieves a string from global video interface structure.\n\nAlgorithm:\n\n1. Check if global video interface pointer (g_dwVideoPlaybackState) is non-NULL\n2. If NULL, return NULL immediately (no interface available)\n3. Calculate string pointer by adding offset 0x1a to interface base address\n4. Initialize string length counter to -1 for REPNE SCASB instruction\n5. Perform string length calculation using optimized REPNE SCASB assembly\n6. Check if calculated string length is greater than 1 character\n7. Return string pointer if valid length, otherwise return NULL\n\nParameters:\n\nNone - function takes no parameters\n\nReturns:\n\nchar * - Pointer to validated string at interface offset 0x1a, or NULL if:\n  - Global video interface pointer is NULL\n  - String at offset 0x1a is empty or only contains null terminator\n\nSpecial Cases:\n\nString length validation uses REPNE SCASB with ECX=-1 initialization. After REPNE completes, ECX contains -(length+2), so the check for iVar2 != -2 ensures the string has at least 1 character plus null terminator.\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n\n0x1a (26 decimal) - Offset within video interface structure to string field\n-1 - Initial value for string length counter (ECX register for REPNE SCASB)\n-2 - Threshold value indicating empty string (only null terminator found)\n\nError Handling:\n\nReturns NULL for any validation failure condition without throwing exceptions.\nCaller must check return value before dereferencing string pointer.",
