      "comment": "Retrieves the filename string from active video playback state if valid.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if global video playback state pointer is non-null\n2. Calculate string pointer at offset 0x32 within state structure\n3. Scan string using REPNE SCASB to determine length efficiently\n4. Validate string has content (length > 1 character)\n5. Return pointer to string if valid, NULL otherwise\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\nchar * - Pointer to filename string at state+0x32 if video active and filename valid\nNULL - If no active video state or filename is empty/null\n\nSpecial Cases:\nString length validation uses efficient x86 REPNE SCASB instruction for scanning.\nEmpty string (length <= 1) returns NULL to prevent invalid filename usage.\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset | Size | Field Name    | Type  | Description\n0x00   | 50   | (unknown)     | byte  | Video state data\n0x32   | ?    | szFilename    | char* | Null-terminated filename string\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x32 (50) - Offset to filename string within video playback state structure\n-2 - String length check value (iVar2 starts at -1, decrements during scan)",
