      "comment": "Checks if video playback flag bit 2 is set in the global video state structure.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load the global video playback state pointer from g_dwVideoPlaybackState\n2. Access the flag byte at offset 0x1ea within the video state structure\n3. Perform bitwise AND with 0x04 to isolate bit 2\n4. Return the masked result (nonzero if bit 2 set, zero if clear)\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\nbyte - Nonzero if video flag bit 2 is set, zero if clear\n\nSpecial Cases:\nThe function accesses offset 0x1ea (490 decimal) which indicates this is a large video state structure. Bit 2 (0x04) likely represents a specific video playback mode or capability flag.\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x1ea (490) - Offset to flags field in video playback state structure\n0x04 - Bit mask for flag bit 2",
