      "comment": "Sets video playback flag bit 3 (0x8) in the global video state structure.\n\nAlgorithm:\n\n1. Load global video playback state pointer from g_dwVideoPlaybackState\n2. Set bit 3 (0x8) in byte at offset 0x1ea within the video state structure\n3. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\n\nNone\n\nReturns:\n\nNothing (void)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n- 0x1ea: Offset within video playback state structure for flag byte\n- 0x8: Flag bit 3, indicates video flag 4 is set\n\nFlag Bits:\n\nVideo State Flags at offset 0x1ea:\nBit | Hex  | Description\n----|------|------------\n0   | 0x01 | Video flag 1\n1   | 0x02 | Video flag 2  \n2   | 0x04 | Video flag 3\n3   | 0x08 | Video flag 4 (set by this function)\n4   | 0x10 | Video flag 5\n5   | 0x20 | Video flag 6\n6   | 0x40 | Video flag 7\n7   | 0x80 | Video flag 8",
