      "instructions": ["0x21D0|MOV|EAX, [0x6fbdc260]", "0x21D5|SUB|ESP, 0x14", "0x21D8|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0x21DA|JNZ|0x6fad222d", "0x21DC|LEA|EAX, [ESP]", "0x21E0|LEA|ECX, [ESP + 0x4]", "0x21E4|PUSH|EAX", "0x21E5|PUSH|ECX", "0x21E6|MOV|dword ptr [0x6fbdc260], 0x1", "0x21F0|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x8], 0xf", "0x21F8|CALL|dword ptr [0x6fba5008]", "0x21FE|PUSH|0x7fffffff", "0x2203|LEA|EDX, [ESP + 0x8]", "0x2207|PUSH|0x6fbae6d4", "0x220C|PUSH|EDX"],
      "comment": "ShowDevHelpIfNotDeveloper - Callback to display developer command-line help\n\nShows a message box with command-line help if the current Windows user is not\na recognized developer. This is a one-shot callback invoked during command\nline parsing in InitializeGameApplication.\n\nClassification: Callback/Handler - invoked by ParseCommandLineArgs\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check g_fDevHelpShown flag - if already shown, exit immediately\n2. Set g_fDevHelpShown = 1 to prevent repeat displays\n3. Get current Windows username (max 15 chars) via GetUserNameA\n4. Compare username against szDevUserName (\"rseis\") using SCompareN\n5. If username does NOT match developer name, show MessageBoxA with help text\n6. Return (void function)\n\nParameters: None (void)\n\nReturns: void\n\nGlobals Accessed:\n  g_fDevHelpShown (0x6fbdc260) - Flag to prevent multiple help displays (R/W)\n  szDevUserName (0x6fbae6d4) - Developer username string \"rseis\" (R)\n  g_pszCmdLineHelp (0x6fba62f0) - Pointer to command-line help text (R)\n  g_pszDiabloII (0x6fba6260) - Pointer to \"Diablo II\" window title (R)\n\nCalled By: ParseCommandLineArgs (via function pointer at 0x6fad1fee)\n\nCallees:\n  GetUserNameA - Windows API to get current username\n  SCompareN - String comparison (Storm library)\n  MessageBoxA - Windows API to display message box\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If username matches \"rseis\", no message box is shown (developer mode)\n  - Maximum username length is 15 characters (buffer is 16 with null)\n  - Only displays once per application run due to g_fDevHelpShown guard",
      "tags": ["PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_0"]
    },
