      "comment": "Show Developer Help on Initialization\n\nDisplays command-line help MessageBox during game initialization, but only for\nnon-developer users. Uses one-shot flag to prevent multiple displays per session.\n\nClassification: Initialization / Debug Helper\nCaller: InitializeGameApplication (via function pointer at 0x6fad1fe9)\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if help already shown via g_fDevHelpShown flag - early exit if set\n2. Set one-shot flag to 1 to prevent re-display\n3. Get current Windows username via GetUserNameA (max 15 chars)\n4. Compare username to developer name \"rseis\" using SCompareN\n5. If usernames differ (not developer), display help MessageBox\n   Note: Inverted logic - help shown when NOT matching developer\n\nParameters: None\n\nReturns: void (RET 0x4 cleans 4 bytes - likely called via __stdcall pointer)\n\nGlobals Accessed:\n- g_fDevHelpShown (0x6fbdc260): One-shot flag, 0=not shown, 1=shown\n- szDevUserName (0x6fbae6d4): Developer username \"rseis\"\n- g_pszCmdLineHelp (0x6fba62f0): Pointer to command-line help text\n- g_pszDiabloII (0x6fba6260): Pointer to window title \"Diablo II\"\n\nAPI Calls:\n- GetUserNameA: Get current Windows username\n- SCompareN: Storm library string comparison\n- MessageBoxA: Display modal dialog with help text",
      "tags": ["PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_0"]
