      "api_calls": ["GetGameState", "InitializeApplicationDisplay"],
      "instructions": ["0x22B0|PUSH|ESI", "0x22B1|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0x22B3|CALL|0x6fb9921a", "0x22B8|CMP|ESI, EAX", "0x22BA|JZ|0x6fad2354", "0x22C0|MOV|EAX, ESI", "0x22C2|SUB|EAX, 0x0", "0x22C5|JZ|0x6fad22ec", "0x22C7|SUB|EAX, 0x2", "0x22CA|JNZ|0x6fad230c", "0x22CC|MOV|EAX, 0x320", "0x22D1|MOV|dword ptr [0x6fbae0e8], 0x258", "0x22DB|MOV|[0x6fbae0e4], EAX", "0x22E0|MOV|dword ptr [0x6fbdc018], 0x1", "0x22EA|JMP|0x6fad2311"],
      "comment": "Configures graphics mode and screen resolution parameters for Diablo II rendering system.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get current graphics mode setting from system\n2. Compare with requested graphics mode parameter\n3. If modes match, exit early (no reconfiguration needed)\n4. Switch on graphics mode parameter value:\n   - Mode 0: Set 640x480 resolution with low quality flag\n   - Mode 2: Set 1024x768 resolution with high quality flag\n   - Other modes: Use existing screen dimensions\n5. Calculate viewport height as screen height minus 40 pixels (UI space)\n6. Set back buffer dimensions to match screen dimensions\n7. Apply new graphics mode setting to system\n8. Initialize screen rendering subsystem with new parameters\n9. Initialize graphics hardware buffers\n10. Enable fullscreen mode with parameter 1\n11. Configure graphics pipeline settings\n12. Initialize screen drawing surface\n\nParameters:\n  nGraphicsMode (int): Graphics mode index to configure\n    0 = 640x480 low quality mode\n    2 = 1024x768 high quality mode\n    Other values = Keep current resolution settings\n\nReturns:\n  void: Function performs configuration and returns\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  Early exit if requested mode matches current system mode\n  UI viewport reserves 40 pixels vertical space (0x28) for interface\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x1e0 (480): Screen height for low resolution mode\n  0x280 (640): Screen width for low resolution mode  \n  600: Screen height for high resolution mode\n  800: Screen width for high resolution mode\n  0x28 (40): UI interface height reserved space\n  0: Low quality graphics flag\n  1: High quality graphics flag\n\nStructure Layout:\nGlobal Configuration Variables:\n  g_dwScreenWidth: Current screen width in pixels\n  g_dwScreenHeight: Current screen height in pixels\n  g_dwBackBufferWidth: Back buffer width (matches screen width)\n  g_dwBackBufferHeight: Back buffer height (matches screen height)\n  g_dwViewportHeight: Viewport height (screen height - 40)\n  g_dwGraphicsQualityFlag: Quality setting (0=low, 1=high)",
      "tags": ["PARAM_1"]
    },
