      "comment": "Main window procedure callback for the game window.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize output parameters (dwHandled=0, dwReturnValue=0)\n2. Log the incoming Windows message for debugging via LogWindowMessage\n3. Get global flag state via GetGlobalFlag\n4. If global flag is 0 (disabled) OR message is WM_CLOSE (0x10):\n   a. Call DispatchWindowMessage with output parameters\n   b. If dispatch succeeded (non-zero) AND message was handled (dwHandled != 0):\n      Return dwReturnValue from dispatch handler\n5. If message not handled or flag is set: Call DefWindowProcA for default processing\n\nParameters:\nhWnd - Handle to the window receiving the message\nuMsg - Windows message identifier (WM_KEYDOWN, WM_CLOSE, etc.)\nwParam - First message parameter (virtual key, control ID, etc.)\nlParam - Second message parameter (key state, control handle, etc.)\n\nReturns:\nuint - Message processing result (from custom handler or DefWindowProcA)\n\nSpecial Cases:\nWM_CLOSE (0x10) always goes to dispatch regardless of global flag state\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x10 - WM_CLOSE message ID (forces dispatch even when flag set)",
