      "comment": "Processes an array of message entries by dispatching them to appropriate handlers based on message type.\n\nAlgorithm:\n\n1. Validate nWindow parameter is not NULL (exit with fatal error if NULL)\n2. Initialize loop counter dwIndex to 0\n3. For each message entry in the array:\n   a. Extract message type (switch value), message value, and parameter from structure\n   b. Switch on message type (0-3):\n      - Type 0: Validate message value is not WM_COMMAND (0x111), call Ordinal_417\n      - Type 1: Call Ordinal_414 with window handle and message data\n      - Type 2: Call Ordinal_416 with window handle and message data  \n      - Type 3: Call Ordinal_415 with window handle and message data\n   c. Increment counter and advance to next message entry\n4. Return when all entries processed\n\nParameters:\n\nnWindow - Window handle for message processing (validated non-NULL)\npMessageArray - Pointer to array of MessageEntry structures  \ndwMessageCount - Number of entries in the message array\n\nReturns:\n\nvoid - Function does not return a value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- NULL nWindow parameter triggers fatal error via Ordinal_10023 and FUN_6fb9a10f(-1)\n- WM_COMMAND (0x111) message value in Type 0 triggers fatal error\n- Message types > 3 are silently ignored (no handler called)\n\nStructure Layout:\nMessageEntry (12 bytes):\nOffset  Size  Field Name      Type    Description\n0x00    4     dwMessageType   uint    Message type selector (0-3)\n0x04    4     dwMessageValue  uint    Message identifier (e.g., WM_COMMAND)\n0x08    4     dwParameter     uint    Additional message parameter",
      "tags": ["MOD_CORE", "PARAM_3", "SRC_WNDPROC.CPP"]
