      "comment": "Initializes the performance tracking system and zeroes performance counter structure.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Set g_fPerformanceInitialized to false (0)\n2. Check if g_fPerformanceTrackingEnabled is currently false (0)\n3. If so, set g_fPerformanceTrackingEnabled to true (1) \n4. Call Ordinal_10021 (D2COMMON allocation function) to allocate PerformanceCounters structure\n5. If allocation successful, zero-initialize all performance counter fields:\n   - Zero counters at offsets 0x4, 0x8, 0x10, 0x14 (primary counters)\n   - Zero timer group fields at offsets 0x24, 0x28, 0x2c (timer group 1)\n   - Zero timer group fields at offsets 0x30, 0x34, 0x38 (timer group 2)  \n   - Zero counter set 2 fields at offsets 0x48, 0x4c, 0x50 (counter set 2)\n   - Zero counter set 3 fields at offsets 0x60, 0x64, 0x68 (counter set 3)\n6. Call Ordinal_10093 (D2COMMON performance subsystem initialization)\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If g_fPerformanceTrackingEnabled is already true, function exits early\n- If memory allocation fails, function continues and calls Ordinal_10093 anyway\n- Function assumes PerformanceCounters structure is at least 0x6C bytes\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset | Size | Field Name           | Type | Description\n-------|------|---------------------|------|-------------\n0x00   | 4    | dwReserved          | uint | Reserved field, not initialized\n0x04   | 4    | dwCounter1          | uint | Primary counter 1\n0x08   | 4    | dwCounter2          | uint | Primary counter 2\n0x0C   | 4    | dwReserved2         | uint | Reserved field 2\n0x10   | 4    | dwCounter3          | uint | Primary counter 3\n0x14   | 4    | dwCounter4          | uint | Primary counter 4\n0x24   | 4    | dwTimerGroup1       | uint | Timer group 1 counter\n0x28   | 4    | dwTimerGroup2       | uint | Timer group 2 counter\n0x2C   | 4    | dwTimerGroup3       | uint | Timer group 3 counter\n0x30   | 4    | dwTimerGroup4       | uint | Timer group 4 counter\n0x34   | 4    | dwTimerGroup5       | uint | Timer group 5 counter\n0x38   | 4    | dwTimerGroup6       | uint | Timer group 6 counter\n0x48   | 4    | dwCounterSet2Start  | uint | Counter set 2 start\n0x4C   | 4    | dwCounterSet2_1     | uint | Counter set 2 counter 1\n0x50   | 4    | dwCounterSet2_2     | uint | Counter set 2 counter 2\n0x60   | 4    | dwCounterSet3Start  | uint | Counter set 3 start  \n0x64   | 4    | dwCounterSet3_1     | uint | Counter set 3 counter 1\n0x68   | 4    | dwCounterSet3_2     | uint | Counter set 3 counter 2\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x24 (36 decimal) - Offset to timer group start\n0x30 (48 decimal) - Offset to timer group 4 start  \n0x48 (72 decimal) - Offset to counter set 2 start\n0x60 (96 decimal) - Offset to counter set 3 start\n0x64 (100 decimal) - Offset to counter set 3 counter 1\n0x68 (104 decimal) - Offset to counter set 3 counter 2\n\nError Handling:\n- No explicit error handling for allocation failure\n- Continues execution even if allocation fails\n- Assumes D2COMMON ordinal functions are available",
