      "comment": "Initializes the D2CMP.DLL compression engine and resets context state.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if compression engine is already initialized (DAT_6fbdc290 != 0) or needs initialization (DAT_6fbdc288 == 0)\n2. Set initialization state: DAT_6fbdc288 = 1 if it was 0, otherwise keep current value\n3. Reset deinitialization flag: DAT_6fbdc290 = 0 to mark engine as active\n4. If initialization is required (DAT_6fbdc288 != 0):\n   a. Call Ordinal_10021() from D2CMP.DLL to allocate compression context structure\n   b. If context allocated successfully, zero-initialize all fields:\n      - Clear control fields: offsets 0x4, 0x8, 0x10, 0x14\n      - Clear buffer management: offsets 0x24, 0x28, 0x2c  \n      - Clear state tracking: offsets 0x30, 0x34, 0x38\n      - Clear statistics: offsets 0x48, 0x4c, 0x50\n      - Clear extended data: offsets 0x60, 0x64, 0x68\n   c. Call Ordinal_10093() from D2CMP.DLL to complete engine initialization\n5. Set engine active flag: DAT_6fbdc290 = 1 to mark initialization complete\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\nNone\n\nSpecial Cases:\nEngine state is tracked by global flags DAT_6fbdc288 (initialization needed) and DAT_6fbdc290 (engine active)\nIf Ordinal_10021() fails to allocate context, initialization continues without context structure\nFunction uses __stdcall convention with no parameters\n\nStructure Layout:\nCompressionContext (108 bytes):\nOffset  Size  Field Name              Type   Description\n0x00    4     dwReserved0             uint   Reserved field (not initialized)\n0x04    4     dwField4                uint   Control field (zeroed)\n0x08    4     dwField8                uint   Control field (zeroed)  \n0x0C    4     dwFieldC                uint   Reserved (not accessed)\n0x10    4     dwField10               uint   Control field (zeroed)\n0x14    4     dwField14               uint   Control field (zeroed)\n0x18-0x20     Reserved block                 Not accessed in initialization\n0x24    4     dwField24     