      "instructions": ["0x2D70|SUB|ESP, 0x4c0", "0x2D76|PUSH|EBX", "0x2D77|MOV|EBX, ECX", "0x2D79|MOV|ECX, dword ptr [ESP + 0x4c8]", "0x2D80|PUSH|EBP", "0x2D81|PUSH|ESI", "0x2D82|PUSH|EDI", "0x2D83|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [ECX + 0x14]", "0x2D86|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x18], EBX", "0x2D8A|TEST|EAX, 0x408", "0x2D8F|JNZ|0x6fad3174", "0x2D95|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [EBX + 0x24]", "0x2D98|ADD|EAX, 0x14", "0x2D9B|JNZ|0x6fad2db8", "0x2D9D|PUSH|0x77"],
      "comment": "Renders a grid pattern overlay on screen with adaptive rendering modes.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate renderer flags - Skip if flags 0x408 (skip render/disabled) are set\n2. Get viewport bounds from renderer and validate boundaries exist\n3. Check screen coordinates are within viewport bounds (x/y min/max tests)\n4. Get viewport state and verify state level value is available\n5. Branch on state level: < 4 uses simple mode, >= 4 uses complex mode\n6. Simple mode (state < 4): Initialize 8x8 pixel grid (768 bytes)\n   - If flag bit 0 clear: Call FUN_6fad3e20 to generate pixel data\n   - If flag bit 0 set: Fill buffer with 0xff (white) in 12-byte stride pattern\n7. Complex mode (state >= 4): Initialize 6x6 vertex grid (432 bytes)\n   - Check renderer mode: mode 0 = direct render, mode != 0 = transformed\n   - Apply screen alignment offset based on alignment field (1=left, 2=right)\n   - For each grid cell (6x6), check if border cell (row/col 0 or 5)\n   - Generate vertex coordinates with 16-pixel X stride and 8-pixel Y stride\n   - Apply screen offset transformation for alignment modes\n8. Submit render data via Ordinal_10079 with vertex buffer\n9. Handle debug overlays if flag bit 1 set in viewport\n   - Show bounds overlay if enabled and time limit not exceeded\n   - Show grid overlay if enabled and time < 100ms\n10. Set render complete flag 0x20000 in renderer flags\n11. Update tracking bounds if enabled (min/max X/Y coordinates)\n\nParameters:\nthis - Renderer instance containing viewport, mode, and timing configuration\npRenderer - Additional renderer structure with alignment and viewport data\npViewport - Viewport bounds structure with flags and boundary pointers  \ndwTexture - Texture ID or screen X coordinate for positioning\nnScreenX - Screen X coordinate for grid positioning\nnScreenY - Screen Y coordinate for grid positioning  \nnGridX - Grid X offset for pattern alignment\nnGridY - Grid Y offset for pattern alignment\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value, renders directly to screen buffer\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Early return if renderer flags 0x408 set (disabled/skip render)\n- Fatal error if viewport bounds pointer is NULL (calls FUN_6fb9a10f)\n- Coordinates outside viewport bounds skip rendering silently\n- State level determines rendering complexity (simple vs vertex-based)\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x408 - Renderer disable flags (skip render + disabled)\n0x20000 - Render complete status flag\n0xff - Alpha/color value for white pixels\n0x10 - X coordinate stride (16 pixels)\n0x8 - Y coordinate stride (8 pixels) \n0xc - Vertex structure stride (12 bytes)\n0x10000 - Fixed-point coordinate multiplier for transforms\n100 - Time threshold for grid overlay display",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "SRC_dFloor.cpp", "STRUCT_ItemData", "GFX_DRAW", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData", "PROP_LARGE", "PARAM_8", "STRUCT_Path", "STRUCT_Skill", "STRUCT_Other", "PROP_LOOPHEAVY", "MOD_DRAW"]
