      "comment": "Converts screen coordinates to map coordinates and processes map tile drawing.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Store original screen coordinates in temporary variables\n2. Add offset of 5 pixels to Y coordinate for map alignment  \n3. Call coordinate conversion function (Ordinal_10111) to transform to map space\n4. Add viewport offset constant 0x28 to Y coordinate for rendering adjustment\n5. Validate game context exists (DAT_6fbe9284), abort if invalid\n6. Apply viewport camera offsets from structure (offset 0x3c for X, 0x40 for Y)\n7. Retrieve current game context handle via Ordinal_10033\n8. If valid game context, call FUN_6fad2d70 to process map tile drawing\n\nParameters:\n- this: ViewportContext * - Viewport structure containing camera offsets and bounds (auto-parameter in ECX register, shows as void* due to __thiscall convention limitation)\n- nScreenX: int - Screen X coordinate to convert\n- nScreenY: int - Screen Y coordinate to convert\nIMPLICIT: Global game context DAT_6fbe9284 must be initialized\n\nReturns:\n- void: Function performs coordinate conversion and triggers map drawing\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If DAT_6fbe9284 is null, function calls error handler and terminates process\n- If Ordinal_10033 returns null context, no map tile processing occurs\n\nNote: Function uses 2 non-renameable auto-generated variables optimized by compiler:\n- this (ECX register): Auto-parameter for __thiscall, type shows as void* but actually ViewportContext*\n- unaff_EDI (EDI register): Unaffected register used for temporary coordinate storage\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n- 0x05: Y-axis alignment offset for map coordinate system\n- 0x28: Rendering offset constant added to transformed Y coordinate  \n- 0x3c: Byte offset to camera X offset in ViewportContext structure\n- 0x40: Byte offset to camera Y offset in ViewportContext structure\n- 0x01: Drawing mode flag passed to map tile processor\n\nError Handling:\n- Validates global game context DAT_6fbe9284 exists before proceeding\n- If context null, calls Ordinal_10023 error handler with source file info\n- Terminates process with FUN_6fb9a10f(-1) on critical failure\n\nStructure Layout:\nViewportContext (64 bytes total):\nOffset | Size | Field Name      | Type | Description\n0x00   | 4    | dwTimestamp     | uint | Frame timestamp\n0x04   | 4    | dwFlags         | uint | Viewport state flags\n0x08   | 4    | dwUpdateFlag1   | uint | Update trigger flags\n0x0C   | 4    | dwUpdateFlag2   | uint | Secondary update flags  \n0x10   | 4    | nFrameCounter   | int  | Frame counter\n0x18   | 4    | nUnknown18      | int  | Unknown field\n0x1C   | 4    | nUnknown1C      | int  | Unknown field\n0x20   | 4    | nViewportMode   | int  | Viewport rendering mode\n0x24   | 4    | pGameData       | void*| Pointer to game data\n0x28   | 4    | nGameLevel      | int  | Current game level\n0x2C   | 4    | nLeftBound      | int  | Left viewport boundary\n0x30   | 4    | nRightBound     | int  | Right viewport boundary\n0x34   | 4    | nTopBound       | int  | Top viewport boundary\n0x38   | 4    | nBottomBound    | int  | Bottom viewport boundary\n0x3C   | 4    | nCameraOffsetX  | int  | Camera X offset (used here)\n0x40   | 4    | nCameraOffsetY  | int  | Camera Y offset (used here)",
