      "comment": "Initialize viewport context and render grid patterns for level visualization.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize viewport context with screen dimensions from D2 engine APIs\n2. Set up viewport bounds and camera offset calculations\n3. Get level data and validate level existence\n4. Process level data arrays to iterate through level objects\n5. For each level object, render grid patterns at multiple zoom levels (1-3)\n6. If grid rendering enabled, calculate optimal grid coordinates with 5-unit alignment\n7. Render grid boundaries for left, right, top, and bottom viewport edges\n8. Convert screen coordinates to map coordinates for proper positioning\n\nParameters:\n- pViewportContext: Pointer to viewport context structure for rendering state\n- nLevelId: Level identifier for loading specific level data\n\nReturns:\nvoid (no return value)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Exits with fatal error if level data or act handle is null\n- Skips grid rendering if grid display disabled in viewport settings\n- Uses 5-unit grid alignment for consistent visual appearance\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n- 0x50 (80): Base viewport width offset for centering\n- -0x50 (-80): Base viewport height offset for centering  \n- 0x80000000: Minimum viewport bound marker (signed int minimum)\n- 0x7fffffff: Maximum viewport bound marker (signed int maximum)\n- 0x2b8 (696): Offset to level data flags in level structure\n- 0x28 (40): Additional coordinate offset for grid alignment\n- 0x1e (30): Grid spacing calculation constant\n- 0x19 (25): Alternative grid spacing for different zoom levels\n\nStructure Layout:\nViewportContext offsets accessed:\n- +0x00: dwRenderMode - Primary rendering mode flags\n- +0x04: dwRenderFlags - Secondary rendering options\n- +0x08: dwUpdateFlag1 - First update state indicator  \n- +0x0c: dwUpdateFlag2 - Second update state indicator\n- +0x10: nCameraScale - Camera zoom scale factor\n- +0x14: dwLastUpdateTime1 - First timing tracker\n- +0x18: dwLastUpdateTime2 - Second timing tracker\n- +0x1c: pRenderBuffer - Pointer to rendering buffer\n- +0x20: nCameraId - Camera identifier\n- +0x24: pLevelContext - Pointer to level context structure\n- +0x28: dwGridEnabled - Grid display enable flag\n- +0x2c: nLeftBound - Left viewport boundary\n- +0x30: nRightBound - Right viewport boundary  \n- +0x34: nTopBound - Top viewport boundary\n- +0x38: nBottomBound - Bottom viewport boundary\n- +0x3c: nXOffset - X coordinate offset for screen positioning\n- +0x40: nYOffset - Y coordinate offset for screen positioning",
