      "comment": "Processes sprite alpha animation and renders visible sprites in viewport layers.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get current tick count for animation timing\n2. Get current state level and expansion status flags\n3. Calculate viewport bounds and grid size parameters\n4. Iterate through all sprite layers (1-4)\n5. For each layer, iterate through grid slots in squared grid pattern\n6. Process linked list of sprite nodes in each active grid slot\n7. Check if sprite flags match current layer mask (bit 14 shift pattern)\n8. Handle alpha animation state transitions based on flags and timing\n9. Calculate screen coordinates relative to viewport center offsets\n10. Perform viewport bounds checking for visibility culling\n11. Convert grid coordinates to tile coordinates (8-pixel units)\n12. Choose rendering quality based on state level (low vs high quality)\n13. Call appropriate rendering function with sprite data and alpha values\n14. Mark sprite as processed with visibility flag (0x20000)\n15. Advance to next sprite in linked list chain\n\nParameters:\npViewportState - Pointer to viewport state structure containing grid data, bounds, and offsets\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- State level < 4: Uses low quality rendering path (768-byte buffer)\n- State level >= 4: Uses high quality rendering path (432-byte buffer) \n- Alpha animation: Interpolates between min/max alpha over 500ms duration\n- Expansion check: Uses different rendering function when expansion installed\n- Viewport bounds: Early exit if sprite position outside visible area\n- Error handling: Assert and terminate on null viewport bounds pointer\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x14 - Viewport bounds structure offset\n0x24, 0x28 - Viewport offset coordinates  \n0xeaa8 - Grid data pointer offset\n0xeab0 - Grid size value offset\n0x50, 0xffffffb0 (-80) - Viewport center offsets\n0xe - Layer mask bit shift (creates 0x4000, 0x8000, 0x10000, 0x20000 masks)\n0x408 - Skip rendering flag mask (bit 10 + bit 3)\n0x2 - Alpha animation active flag\n0x400 - Zero alpha visibility flag\n0x20000 - Sprite processed flag\n0x1f4 (500) - Animation duration in milliseconds\n0x77 (119) - Assert error code for null viewport bounds\n\nStructure Layout:\nViewportState offsets:\n0x14 - pViewBounds (pointer to bounds rectangle)\n0x24 - nOffsetX (viewport X offset)  \n0x28 - nOffsetY (viewport Y offset)\n0xeaa8 - pGridData (pointer to sprite grid)\n0xeab0 - nGridSize (grid dimensions)\n\nSpriteObject offsets:\n0x0 - nPosX (sprite X position)\n0x4 - nPosY (sprite Y position) \n0x14 - dwFlags (visibility and layer flags)\n0x18 - pImageData (pointer to sprite image data)\n0x24 - dwAnimFlags (animation state flags)\n0x28 - byCurrentAlpha (current transparency value)\n0x29 - byMinAlpha (minimum alpha value)\n0x2a - byMaxAlpha (maximum alpha value) \n0x2c - dwAnimStartTick (animation start timestamp)\n\nSpriteListNode offsets:\n0x4 - nGridPosX (grid X coordinate in 8-pixel units)\n0x8 - nGridPosY (grid Y coordinate in 8-pixel units)\n0xc - pSpriteObject (pointer to sprite data)\n0x10 - pNext (next node in linked list)",
