      "comment": "Fill an 8x8 grid of PixelVertex structures with color or coordinate data.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check fill mode parameter to determine operation type\n2. If fill mode is non-zero (palette fill mode):\n   a. Get base color from D2Common color palette (Ordinal_10926)\n   b. Extract RGB color components via D2Common (Ordinal_10927)\n   c. Fill 8x8 grid with fixed color values:\n      - Offset +0: Base color byte\n      - Offset +1: Green component \n      - Offset +2: Blue component\n      - Offset +3: Red component\n   d. Advance buffer pointer by 0xc (12 bytes) per vertex\n3. If fill mode is zero (coordinate calculation mode):\n   a. Initialize grid traversal starting at bottom-left\n   b. Calculate X coordinate: (column * 8) - 8\n   c. Calculate Y coordinate: (row * 8) - 8  \n   d. Call coordinate processing function (FUN_6fad5c70)\n   e. Process each vertex with adjacent coordinate references\n   f. Advance buffer pointer by 0xc per vertex\n\nParameters:\n- pVertexGrid: Pointer to output buffer for 64 PixelVertex structures\n- nGridWidth: Grid width dimension (typically 8)\n- nGridHeight: Grid height dimension (typically 8)\n- nFillMode: Operation mode (0=coordinates, non-zero=palette colors)\n\nReturns:\n- void (fills buffer directly)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Grid hardcoded to 8x8 regardless of width/height parameters\n- Coordinate mode uses (index * 8) - 8 formula for positioning\n- Palette mode fills all vertices with same color values\n\nStructure Layout:\nPixelVertex (12 bytes):\nOffset | Size | Field | Type | Description\n-------|------|-------|------|-------------\n0x00   | 1    | color | byte | Base color index\n0x01   | 1    | green | byte | Green component  \n0x02   | 1    | blue  | byte | Blue component\n0x03   | 1    | red   | byte | Red component\n0x04   | 8    | ?     | ?    | Unknown fields\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n- 0x8 (8): Fixed grid dimension and coordinate stride\n- 0xC (12): PixelVertex structure size\n- 0x6fbe9284: Global color palette context pointer",
