      "comment": "Renders a 6x6 grid pattern of elements with color and position data.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize local copy of base X coordinate\n2. Get default color value from graphics context (Ordinal_10926)\n3. Adjust X coordinate based on horizontal alignment mode:\n   - Mode 1: Apply negative screen width quarter offset (left align)\n   - Mode 2: Apply positive screen width quarter offset (right align)\n   - Other modes: No adjustment\n4. Retrieve color components (R, G, B) from graphics context (Ordinal_10927)\n5. Initialize outer loop for 6 rows (row index 0-5)\n6. Initialize inner loop for 6 columns (column index 0-5)\n7. For each grid element:\n   - Skip if border mode enabled and not on border (edges only)\n   - Calculate X position: (column - row) * 16 + adjusted base X\n   - Calculate Y position: base Y + (column + row) * 8\n   - If render border disabled: call FUN_6fad5c70 with calculated positions\n   - If render border enabled: store color components directly in grid data\n8. Advance to next element (12-byte stride)\n9. Continue until all 36 elements processed\n\nParameters:\npGridData: Pointer to grid data buffer (36 elements, 12 bytes each)\nnBaseX: Base X coordinate for positioning\nnBaseY: Base Y coordinate for positioning  \nnOffsetX: X offset for tile positioning calculations\nnTileSize: Size multiplier for tile spacing (8-pixel base)\nnRenderBorder: Border rendering mode (0=call renderer, 1=store colors only)\nnHorizontalAlign: Horizontal alignment (1=left, 2=right, other=center)\nnBorderMode: Border display mode (0=all elements, 1=edges only)\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Screen width division uses bit manipulation for efficiency: (width + (width >> 31 & 3)) >> 2\n- Grid element stride is 12 bytes (3 color bytes + padding + 2 int positions)\n- Border mode renders only edge elements (index 0 or 5 in either dimension)\n- Position calculation creates diamond/isometric pattern: X = (col-row)*16, Y = (col+row)*8\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset  Size  Field Name    Type    Description\n0x00    1     bColor1       byte    First color component\n0x01    1     bColor2       byte    Second color component  \n0x02    1     bColor3       byte    Third color component\n0x03    1     bPadding      byte    Padding/alignment\n0x04    4     nXPosition    int     Calculated X coordinate\n0x08    4     nYPosition    int     Calculated Y coordinate\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x10 (16): X coordinate multiplier for diamond pattern spacing\n0x08 (8): Y coordinate multiplier and tile spacing base unit\n0x0c (12): Grid element structure size in bytes\n0x05 (5): Maximum grid index for border detection\n0x01 (1): Left alignment mode identifier\n0x02 (2): Right alignment mode identifier",
      "tags": ["PARAM_8", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "STRUCT_Skill", "STRUCT_ItemData", "PROP_LOOPHEAVY", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
