      "comment": "Processes grid pattern elements for screen rendering with coordinate transformation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Store starting X coordinate for current processing loop\n2. Get alpha value from render context via Ordinal_10926(g_hRenderContext) \n3. Initialize screen offset based on nOffsetMode parameter value\n4. Calculate horizontal screen offset for alignment adjustment:\n   - Mode 1: Set negative offset = -(screen_width + alignment_correction) >> 2\n   - Mode 2: Set positive offset = (screen_width + alignment_correction) >> 2  \n   - Default: No horizontal offset applied\n5. Get RGB color values from render context via Ordinal_10927(g_hRenderContext)\n6. Process 6x6 grid of elements in nested loops (row/column iteration)\n7. For each grid element, check border mask conditions:\n   - Skip if nBorderMask enabled AND current position not on border (row/col 0 or 5)\n8. Transform local grid coordinates to world coordinates (* 0x10000 for 16.16 fixed point)\n9. If nMode != 0: Call Ordinal_10066 for coordinate projection with nMode parameter\n10. If nMode == 0: Call Ordinal_10066 for projection then FUN_6fad5c70 for additional processing\n11. Apply horizontal screen offset to transformed X coordinate\n12. Write final values to GridPatternElement structure:\n    - Offset +0: Alpha value from render context\n    - Offset +1: Red color component  \n    - Offset +2: Green color component\n    - Offset +3: Blue color component\n    - Offset +4: Final X coordinate (transformed + screen offset)\n    - Offset +8: Final Y coordinate (transformed)\n13. Advance to next element (+12 bytes) and continue until all 36 elements processed\n\nParameters:\npbGridElements (ECX): Pointer to array of 36 GridPatternElement structures (6x6 grid)\nnStartX (EDX): Starting X coordinate for grid positioning\nnStartY (stack +0x4): Starting Y coordinate for grid positioning  \nnMode (stack +0x8): Processing mode (0=full processing, non-zero=basic projection)\nnOffsetMode (stack +0xc): Screen offset calculation mode (1=left, 2=right, 0=center)\nnBorderMask (stack +0x10): Border-only processing flag (0=all elements, 1=border only)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Results written directly to GridPatternElement array\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Border-only rendering: When nBorderMask=1, only processes elements at grid edges (indices 0,5)\n- Fixed-point coordinates: All coordinates scaled by 0x10000 for sub-pixel precision\n- Screen alignment: Offset calculation uses (width + (width>>31 & 3))>>2 for proper division\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x10000 (65536) - Fixed-point scaling factor for coordinate precision\n0xc (12) - Size of GridPatternElement structure in bytes  \n0x6 (6) - Grid dimensions (6x6 = 36 total elements)\n0x1f (31) - Bit mask for sign extension in screen width division\n0x3 (3) - Alignment mask for proper division rounding\n0x2 (2) - Right shift amount for division by 4\n\nStructure Layout:\nGridPatternElement (12 bytes):\nOffset | Size | Field Name | Type | Description\n-------|------|------------|------|-------------\n+0x0   | 1    | byAlpha    | byte | Alpha transparency value\n+0x1   | 1    | byColorR   | byte | Red color component  \n+0x2   | 1    | byColorG   | byte | Green color component\n+0x3   | 1    | byColorB   | byte | Blue color component\n+0x4   | 4    | nPosX      | int  | Final X coordinate (world space)\n+0x8   | 4    | nPosY      | int  | Final Y coordinate (world space)",
      "tags": ["PARAM_6", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "STRUCT_Skill", "STRUCT_ItemData", "PROP_LOOPHEAVY", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
