      "comment": "Creates and initializes a new audio context structure for audio processing\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate buffer count parameter (must be > 0, max 18 allowed)\n2. Increment global audio context counter (DAT_6fbe8f08)\n3. Allocate memory for audio context structure (158 bytes via Ordinal_10042)\n4. Copy base values from source data structure to context\n5. Set flag based on source data flags (0x200000 bit test)\n6. Calculate and store audio buffer sizes using Ordinal_10327/10330\n7. Store mode, buffer count, and byte parameters\n8. Initialize buffer size fields (bufferCount * 8)\n9. Link context into global audio context chain\n10. Conditionally allocate additional data for mode 2 (0xb5 bytes)\n11. Update global context head pointer and return new context\n\nParameters:\npSourceData - Pointer to audio source data structure containing base values and flags\nnMode - Audio processing mode (2 triggers additional allocation)  \nnBufferCount - Number of audio buffers to allocate (clamped to 1-18 range)\nbParam1 - First byte parameter stored at offset 0x24\nbParam2 - Second byte parameter stored at offset 0x25  \nbParam3 - Third byte parameter stored at offset 0x26\nbParam4 - Fourth byte parameter stored at offset 0x27\n\nReturns:\nPointer to newly allocated and initialized audio context structure\nNULL if nBufferCount <= 0\n\nSpecial Cases:\nBuffer count clamped to maximum 18 (0x12) if exceeded\nMode 2 triggers additional memory allocation via Ordinal_10042(0xb5,0)\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x9e (158) - Base allocation size for audio context structure\n0x12 (18) - Maximum allowed buffer count \n0x200000 - Flag bit mask in source data structure at offset 0xe8\n0xb5 (181) - Additional allocation size for mode 2 processing\n0xd (13) - Right shift amount for size calculations from Ordinal functions\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset  Size  Field Name        Type     Description\n0x00    4     dwBaseValue       uint     Copy of pSourceData[0]\n0x04    4     dwSecondValue     uint     Copy of pSourceData[2] \n0x08    1     bFlag             byte     Flag based on 0x200000 bit test\n0x0C    4     nMode             int      Processing mode parameter\n0x10    4     dwFirstSize       uint     (Ordinal_10327 result >> 13) + 4\n0x14    4     dwSecondSize      uint     (Ordinal_10330 result >> 13) + 4  \n0x18    4     dwBufferSize1     uint     nBufferCount * 8\n0x1C    4     dwBufferSize2     uint     nBufferCount * 8 (duplicate)\n0x20    4     dwCounter         uint     Always zero\n0x24    1     bParam1           byte     First byte parameter\n0x25    1     bParam2           byte     Second byte parameter  \n0x26    1     bParam3           byte     Third byte parameter\n0x27    1     bParam4           byte     Fourth byte parameter\n0x28    4     pNext             ptr      Previous global context head (DAT_6fbe8f04)\n0x2C    4     dwReserved        uint     Always zero\n0x30    4     pAdditionalData   ptr      Optional allocation for mode 2",
