      "comment": "Sets the radius for a light source with validation and clamping.\n\nAlgorithm:\n\n1. Validate radius is positive (> 0)\n   - If nRadius < 1, abort with error message \"Tried to set a light's radius to ...\"\n   - Call FUN_6fb9a10f(-1) to terminate execution\n\n2. Clamp radius to maximum allowed value\n   - If nRadius > 17 (0x11), clamp to 18 (0x12)\n   - Light radius range is 1-18 units\n\n3. Validate light data pointer is not NULL\n   - If pLightData == NULL, abort with error message \"ptLight\"\n   - Call FUN_6fb9a10f(-1) to terminate execution\n\n4. Set radius in light structure\n   - Store (nRadius * 8) in pLightData->dwRadiusUnits (offset 0x1c)\n   - Radius is stored as 8-unit increments for internal calculations\n\nParameters:\n\npLightData - Pointer to LightData structure containing light properties\nnRadius - Desired radius value in logical units (valid range 1-18)\n\nReturns:\n\nvoid - Function does not return a value\n      Aborts process execution if validation fails\n\nSpecial Cases:\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x1c (28) - Offset to dwRadiusUnits field in LightData structure\n0x12 (18) - Maximum allowed radius value\n0x8 (8) - Scaling factor for radius storage (logical to internal units)\n0xffffffff (-1) - Error code passed to termination function\n\nStructure Layout:\n\nOffset  Size  Field Name      Type      Description\n------  ----  --------------  --------  ---------------------------\n0x00    4     dwType          uint      Light type identifier\n0x04    4     pOwner          void*     Pointer to owning object\n0x08    2     wFlags          ushort    Light behavior flags\n0x0a    2     wState          ushort    Current light state\n0x0c    4     nPosX           int       X coordinate position\n0x10    4     nPosY           int       Y coordinate position\n0x14    4     nPrevPosX       int       Previous X position\n0x18    4     nPrevPosY       int       Previous Y position\n0x1c    4     dwRadiusUnits   uint      Radius in 8-unit increments\n\nError Handling:\n\nRadius validation failure - Logs error to debug output, terminates process\nNULL pointer validation failure - Logs error to debug output, terminates process\nBoth error conditions are fatal and cannot be recovered from",
