      "comment": "Sets the radius for a light source with validation and special handling for static lights.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate radius is not negative - terminate program with error if below zero\n2. Clamp radius to maximum value of 18 (0x12) to prevent overflow\n3. Validate light pointer is not NULL - terminate program with error if null\n4. Apply radius clamping again as safety check\n5. Calculate and store radius squared value (radius * 8) in light structure fields\n6. Handle special case for static lights (type 2) by clearing cache fields\n\nParameters:\nparam_1 - Pointer to light structure containing radius and type information\nparam_2 - Light radius value to set (clamped to range 0-18)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Function terminates program on validation failure, otherwise returns normally\n\nSpecial Cases:\nFor static lights (type 2 at offset 0xc), clears cached static map pointer and related flags\nMaximum radius is clamped to 18 (0x12) to prevent buffer overflow in light calculations\nNegative radius triggers immediate program termination via FUN_6fb9a10f(-1)\nNULL light pointer triggers immediate program termination via assertion\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0xd6 (214) - Line number for radius validation error in dLightMap.cpp\n0xda (218) - Line number for NULL pointer validation error in dLightMap.cpp  \n0x12 (18) - Maximum allowed light radius value\n0xe3 (227) - Error code for static light cache invalidation warning\n2 - Static light type identifier at structure offset 0xc\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset | Size | Field Name    | Type | Description\n0x0c   | 4    | nType        | uint | Light type (2 = static light)\n0x18   | 4    | nRadius      | uint | Light radius * 8 (squared for distance calcs)\n0x1c   | 4    | nRadiusSq    | uint | Light radius * 8 (backup/alternate field)\n0x2c   | 4    | dwCacheFlags | uint | Static light cache validity flags  \n0x30   | 4    | pStaticMap   | ptr  | Pointer to precomputed static light map",
