      "comment": "Retrieves the number of processed audio samples from an AudioContext.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate AudioContext pointer is not NULL\n2. If NULL, log fatal error and terminate process\n3. Read sample count value from AudioContext at offset 0x18 (24 decimal)\n4. Divide sample count by 8 using right shift to get processed samples\n5. Return processed sample count as integer\n\nParameters:\npAudioContext - Pointer to AudioContext structure containing audio processing state\n\nReturns:\nint - Number of processed audio samples (raw sample count / 8)\n      Returns 0 if AudioContext is NULL (after logging fatal error)\n\nSpecial Cases:\nIf AudioContext pointer is NULL, function calls logging function with fatal error message\nand terminates the process via exit function (does not return)\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x18 (24) - Offset to sample count field in AudioContext structure\n0x3 - Right shift count to divide by 8 (2^3 = 8)\n\nStructure Layout:\nAudioContext structure (52 bytes total):\nOffset  Size  Field Name           Type    Description\n0x00    ?     [unknown fields]     ?       Audio context header/state\n0x18    4     dwSampleCount        uint    Raw sample count buffer\n0x1C    ?     [remaining fields]   ?       Additional audio processing data",
