      "comment": "Sets RGB color values for a light structure\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate light pointer is not NULL\n2. If NULL, log error message with ptLight context and terminate process\n3. Store red color value at offset 0x25 in light structure\n4. Store green color value at offset 0x26 in light structure  \n5. Store blue color value at offset 0x27 in light structure\n\nParameters:\npLight (LightStruct *): Pointer to light structure to modify, validated for NULL\nbRedValue (byte): Red component value (0-255) stored at structure offset +0x25\nbGreenValue (byte): Green component value (0-255) stored at structure offset +0x26  \nbBlueValue (byte): Blue component value (0-255) stored at structure offset +0x27\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Function does not return value on success\nIMPLICIT: Process termination if pLight parameter is NULL\n\nSpecial Cases:\nNULL Pointer Validation: If pLight is NULL, calls Ordinal_10023 error logging with \"ptLight\" message, then FUN_6fb9a10f(-1) which terminates the process\nRGB Storage: Color components are stored as individual bytes at consecutive offsets 0x25, 0x26, 0x27 within the LightStruct\n\nStructure Layout:\nLightStruct color field locations:\nOffset | Size | Field     | Type | Description\n-------|------|-----------|------|------------------\n0x25   | 1    | bColorRed | byte | Red color component\n0x26   | 1    | bColorGreen| byte | Green color component  \n0x27   | 1    | bColorBlue | byte | Blue color component\n\nError Handling:\nNULL pLight: Logs error via Ordinal_10023 then terminates via FUN_6fb9a10f(-1)\nNo validation of RGB range - accepts any byte values 0x00-0xFF",
