      "comment": "Remove an AudioContext node from the global linked list.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate input parameter is not NULL\n2. Initialize traversal variables: pCurrent (iVar1) = list head, pPrevious (iVar3) = NULL\n3. Traverse linked list to find matching AudioContext node:\n   a. Compare current node address with target pContext\n   b. If match found, proceed to removal\n   c. If no match, advance: pPrevious = pCurrent, pCurrent = pCurrent->next (offset +0x28)\n   d. Continue until end of list reached\n4. Remove matching node from linked list:\n   a. If node is list head (pPrevious == NULL): Update list head to point to node->next\n   b. If node is in middle/end: Link previous node to current node's next pointer\n5. Check if node has associated resources at offset +0x30\n6. Call cleanup functions: Ordinal_10043(0x11a,0) if resources exist, Ordinal_10043(0x11c,0) always\n7. Increment global removal counter at 0x6fbe8f0c\n8. Return successfully\n9. Error path: If node not found in list, call assertion failure (Ordinal_10023) and exit program\n\nParameters:\npContext (AudioContext *): Pointer to AudioContext node to remove from linked list\n\nReturns:\nvoid: No return value, function exits program if node not found\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- NULL input parameter: Function returns immediately without action\n- Node not found in list: Triggers assertion failure and program termination\n- Empty list: Triggers assertion failure and program termination\n- Single node removal: List head becomes NULL\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x28 (40): Offset to next pointer in AudioContext structure\n0x30 (48): Offset to resource flag/data field in AudioContext structure  \n0x11a (282): Cleanup function code for resource deallocation\n0x11c (284): Cleanup function code for context deallocation\n0x113 (275): Error code for assertion failure in list removal\n\nGlobal Variables:\nDAT_6fbe8f04: AudioContext list head pointer\n_DAT_6fbe8f0c: Global counter of removed AudioContext nodes\n\nStructure Layout:\nAudioContext (52 bytes total):\nOffset | Size | Field Name | Type | Description\n+0x28  | 4    | next       | AudioContext * | Pointer to next node in linked list\n+0x30  | 4    | resources  | int/flags | Resource allocation flag or data pointer\n\nError Handling:\n- Input validation: NULL parameter check returns early\n- List integrity: Node not found triggers assertion failure with source location\n- Program termination: Uses FUN_6fb9a10f(-1) for fatal error exit",
