      "api_count": 9,
      "api_calls": ["UNITS_GetRoom", "ExtractRoomTileList", "GetUnitColorComponents", "GetRoomStatBytes", "GetDataField", "GetUnitColorComponents", "GetRoomStatBytes", "GetDataField", "CopyOrInitCoords"],
      "instructions": ["0x4640|SUB|ESP, 0x4c", "0x4643|PUSH|EBX", "0x4644|PUSH|EBP", "0x4645|PUSH|ESI", "0x4646|PUSH|EDI", "0x4647|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0x4649|CALL|0x6fb62880", "0x464E|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0x4650|JZ|0x6fad497c", "0x4656|PUSH|EAX", "0x4657|CALL|0x6fb98164", "0x465C|MOV|EDI, EAX", "0x465E|TEST|EDI, EDI", "0x4660|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x28], EDI", "0x4664|JZ|0x6fad497c"],
      "comment": "Initializes the global color palette buffer with device-specific color values.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate device context availability via FUN_6fb62880() and Ordinal_10342()\n2. If validation fails or device context is null, clear entire palette to zero\n3. For valid device context, enumerate attached display devices\n4. Get color system information via Ordinal_10035() to retrieve device array and count\n5. Extract color components from primary device using FUN_6fae8d30()\n6. If color extraction fails, use Ordinal_10054() for alternate color retrieval\n7. As fallback, query render context colors via Ordinal_10927() and Ordinal_10926()\n8. Combine RGB components into 32-bit color value (B-G-R-A byte order)\n9. Fill entire 48x49 palette grid with primary device color\n10. For each additional device in array:\n    a. Skip if device handle matches primary device\n    b. Extract device-specific color components \n    c. Get device position via Ordinal_10034() and calculate screen coordinates\n    d. Validate coordinates are within 0-48 range for both X and Y axes\n    e. Fill rectangular region in palette grid with device color\n\nParameters:\nhDeviceContext (int): Handle to device context for color extraction, 0 to clear palette\n\nReturns:\nvoid: No return value, modifies global g_aColorPalette buffer directly\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Invalid device context: Clears entire palette to black (0x00000000)\n- Color extraction failure: Uses progressive fallback methods for color values\n- Out of bounds coordinates: Skips device color assignment to prevent buffer overflow\n- Device array bounds: Processes up to nDeviceCount entries safely\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x30 (48): Palette grid width in entries\n0x31 (49): Palette grid height in entries  \n0x60 (96): Row stride in bytes (48 entries × 2 DWORDs per entry)\n0x6fbe4700: Base address of global color palette buffer\n0x6fbe8d80: End address of palette buffer (calculated boundary)\n0x6fbe02e8: Global X coordinate offset base\n0x6fbe02ec: Global Y coordinate offset base\n\nStructure Layout:\nColorPaletteEntry (8 bytes per entry):\nOffset  Size  Field Name    Type  Description\n0x00    4     dwReserved    uint  Reserved field, always set to 0\n0x04    1     byRed         byte  Red color component (0-255)\n0x05    1     byGreen       byte  Green color component (0-255) \n0x06    1     byBlue        byte  Blue color component (0-255)\n0x07    1     byAlpha       byte  Alpha component (0-255)",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "STRUCT_Room2", "STRUCT_ItemData", "PARAM_1", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData", "STRUCT_StatList", "PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Path", "STRUCT_Skill", "PROP_LOOPHEAVY"]
