      "instructions": ["0x49C0|MOV|EAX, [0x6fbe9284]", "0x49C5|PUSH|ESI", "0x49C6|PUSH|0x6fad5b50", "0x49CB|PUSH|EAX", "0x49CC|CALL|0x6fb9816a", "0x49D1|MOV|dword ptr [0x6fbe42fc], 0x0", "0x49DB|MOV|ESI, 0x1", "0x49E0|MOV|ECX, 0x6fbe4300", "0x49E5|MOV|EAX, 0x10000", "0x49EA|ADD|ECX, 0x4", "0x49ED|CDQ|", "0x49EE|IDIV|ESI", "0x49F0|INC|ESI", "0x49F1|CMP|ECX, 0x6fbe46fc", "0x49F7|MOV|dword ptr [ECX + -0x4], EAX"],
      "comment": "Initialize reciprocal lookup table for fast division operations\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize graphics rendering context via D2CMP.DLL ordinal function\n2. Clear initialization flag at global address 0x6fbe42fc to 0\n3. Set starting index to 1 for reciprocal calculations  \n4. Initialize pointer to lookup table base address 0x6fbe4300\n5. For each index from 1 to 1023 (array boundary 0x6fbe46fc):\n   a. Calculate next table entry pointer (current + 4 bytes)\n   b. Convert index to 64-bit for precise division\n   c. Compute reciprocal: 0x10000 / index (65536 / index)\n   d. Store result as 32-bit integer at current table position\n   e. Advance to next table entry\n   f. Increment index counter\n6. Continue until pointer reaches table boundary\n\nParameters:\nNone (void function)\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Division by zero prevented by starting index at 1 not 0\n- 64-bit intermediate calculation prevents integer overflow during division\n- Table size: 1023 entries * 4 bytes = 4092 bytes total\n- Reciprocal values range from 65536 (index=1) down to 64 (index=1023)\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x10000 (65536) - Fixed-point reciprocal multiplier for division optimization\n0x6fbe42fc - Global initialization flag (0 = table ready, non-zero = uninitialized)  \n0x6fbe4300 - Reciprocal lookup table base address\n0x6fbe46fc - Table boundary address (0x6fbe4300 + 1023*4 bytes)\n\nError Handling:\nNo explicit error checking - assumes valid memory ranges and D2CMP.DLL availability\n\nAlgorithm Verification:\nStep 3 maps to: nIndex = 1 (0x6fad49db)\nStep 4 maps to: pdwTableEntry = &DAT_6fbe4300 (0x6fad49e0)  \nStep 5a maps to: pdwNextEntry = pdwTableEntry + 1 (0x6fad49ea)\nStep 5b maps to: llDividend = (longlong)nIndex (cast for precision)\nStep 5c maps to: 0x10000 / llDividend (0x6fad49ee IDIV)\nStep 5d maps to: *pdwTableEntry = result (0x6fad49f7)\nStep 5f maps to: nIndex++ (0x6fad49f0 INC)",
