      "comment": "Processes audio contexts with display coordinate integration for spatial audio effects.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize display boundaries by getting screen dimensions and calculating viewport margins (-24 to +24 pixels)\n2. Clear audio processing state and reset global audio context counter\n3. Get display handle and validate for pixel testing capability\n4. Process color palette visibility: scan 48x60 grid (0x30 x 0x3C) using pixel testing to mark visible palette entries\n5. Initialize audio context processing loop traversing linked list starting from DAT_6fbe8f04\n6. For each audio context: increment global counter and get next pointer\n7. Load sound resources if context counter is zero and base value is not 6 (invalid state)\n8. Calculate sound buffer sizes by bit-shifting resource dimensions and adding padding\n9. Handle buffer size transitions with 8-unit steps toward target size\n10. Clamp maximum buffer size to 248 units (0xF8) to prevent overflow\n11. Process audio based on context mode: Mode 0 calls direct processing, Mode 2 handles buffered processing with allocation\n12. For other modes: perform spatial audio calculation using distance-based volume with boundary checking\n13. Calculate 3D audio positioning using 8-unit grid alignment and distance formulas\n14. Apply volume scaling based on distance attenuation and context parameters\n15. Remove expired contexts when counter reaches zero and buffer size becomes negative\n\nParameters:\nNone (void function)\n\nReturns:\nNone (void function)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Contexts with base value 6 are skipped (invalid/disabled state)\n- Buffer sizes clamped to maximum 248 to prevent audio buffer overflow\n- Spatial audio only processed for modes other than 0 and 2\n- Expired contexts automatically removed from linked list when counter expires\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x18 (24) - Display viewport margin in pixels\n0x30 (48) - Color palette width scan dimension  \n0x3C (60) - Color palette height scan dimension\n0x900 (2304) - Total palette entries (48 * 48)\n0x22 (34) - Pixel test mode parameter\n0xF8 (248) - Maximum audio buffer size limit\n0xD (13) - Bit shift for sound resource size calculation\n0x430 - Memory deallocation size parameter\n0x449 - Memory allocation size parameter for Mode 2 buffering\n\nAudioContext Structure Layout:\nOffset  Size  Field Name        Type     Description\n+0x00   4     pNext            void*    Pointer to next context in linked list\n+0x04   4     dwCounter        uint     Processing counter, context removed when zero\n+0x08   4     dwBaseValue      uint     Audio type identifier (6 = invalid)\n+0x0C   4     dwSecondValue    uint     Secondary audio parameter\n+0x10   1     bFlag            byte     Processing flag for resource selection\n+0x11   3     padding          byte[3]  Structure alignment padding\n+0x14   4     dwFirstSize      uint     Primary audio buffer size\n+0x18   4     dwSecondSize     uint     Secondary audio buffer size  \n+0x1C   4     dwBufferSize1    uint     Current buffer size\n+0x20   4     dwBufferSize2    uint     Target buffer size\n+0x24   4     nMode            int      Processing mode (0=direct, 2=buffered, other=spatial)\n+0x28   4     dwReserved       uint     Reserved field for Mode 2 state\n+0x2C   4     pAdditionalData  void*    Allocated buffer pointer for Mode 2\n+0x30   1     bParam1          byte     Spatial audio parameter 1\n+0x31   1     bParam2          byte     Spatial audio parameter 2\n+0x32   1     bParam3          byte     Spatial audio parameter 3\n+0x33   1     bParam4          byte     Spatial audio parameter 4\n\nError Handling:\n- Invalid display handles cause pixel testing to be skipped\n- NULL sound resources result in size calculation being bypassed\n- Memory allocation failures in Mode 2 leave pAdditionalData as NULL\n- Boundary checks prevent spatial audio processing outside viewport limits",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "STRUCT_ItemData", "PARAM_0", "GFX_DRAW", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData", "STRUCT_MonsterData", "PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Skill", "SRC_dLightMap.cpp", "PROP_LOOPHEAVY", "MOD_DRAW"]
