      "instructions": ["0x4D10|MOV|EAX, EDX", "0x4D12|PUSH|EBX", "0x4D13|MOV|EDX, dword ptr [0x6fbe02e8]", "0x4D19|PUSH|ESI", "0x4D1A|SAR|ECX, 0x3", "0x4D1D|SUB|ECX, EDX", "0x4D1F|PUSH|EDI", "0x4D20|JS|0x6fad4e32", "0x4D26|CMP|ECX, 0x30", "0x4D29|JGE|0x6fad4e32", "0x4D2F|MOV|EDX, dword ptr [0x6fbe02ec]", "0x4D35|SAR|EAX, 0x3", "0x4D38|SUB|EAX, EDX", "0x4D3A|JS|0x6fad4e32", "0x4D40|CMP|EAX, 0x30"],
      "comment": "Applies color mixing and lighting effects to a color palette entry at specified coordinates.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Convert world coordinates to palette grid coordinates (divide by 8, subtract base offset)\n2. Validate coordinates are within 48x48 palette grid bounds (0x30)\n3. Calculate linear palette index using formula: y * 48 + x\n4. Extract current red value from palette entry and add light intensity\n5. Clamp adjusted red value to 255 maximum\n6. If global lighting enabled (DAT_6fbaec04 != 0):\n   a. Load light multiplier from lookup table using adjusted red as index\n   b. Calculate new green = (current_green * red_value + input_green * intensity) * multiplier >> 16\n   c. Calculate new blue = (current_blue * red_value + input_blue * intensity) * multiplier >> 16  \n   d. Calculate new alpha = (current_alpha * red_value + input_red * intensity) * multiplier >> 16\n   e. Clamp all color components to 255 maximum\n   f. Store all four color components back to palette entry\n7. Otherwise set red to adjusted value, clear green/blue/alpha to 0\n\nParameters:\n- nXCoordinate: World X coordinate to be converted to palette grid position\n- nYCoordinate: World Y coordinate to be converted to palette grid position\n- nLightIntensity: Light intensity factor for brightness calculation\n- dwRedComponent: Red color component for mixing (byte value in low 8 bits)\n- dwGreenComponent: Green color component for mixing (byte value in low 8 bits) \n- dwBlueComponent: Blue color component for mixing (byte value in low 8 bits)\n\nReturns:\n- void: Function modifies global color palette array directly\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Coordinates outside 48x48 grid bounds are ignored (early return)\n- Light intensity values > 254 are clamped to 255\n- Color component results > 255 are clamped to 255\n- When lighting disabled, only red channel updated, others zeroed\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n- 0x3: Bit shift amount for coordinate conversion (divide by 8)\n- 0x30: Palette grid dimension (48x48 entries)\n- 0xff: Maximum color component value (255)\n- 0xfe: Light intensity clamp threshold (254)\n- 0x10: Bit shift for fixed-point arithmetic (divide by 65536)\n\nStructure Layout:\nColorPaletteEntry (8 bytes):\n| Offset | Size | Field   | Type | Description           |\n|--------|------|---------|------|-----------------------|\n| +0x4   | 1    | byRed   | byte | Red color component   |\n| +0x5   | 1    | byGreen | byte | Green color component |\n| +0x6   | 1    | byBlue  | byte | Blue color component  |\n| +0x7   | 1    | byAlpha | byte | Alpha transparency    |",
      "tags": ["PARAM_6", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PROP_LEAF", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
    },
