      "instructions": ["0x4E40|SUB|ESP, 0x3c", "0x4E43|PUSH|EBX", "0x4E44|PUSH|EBP", "0x4E45|PUSH|ESI", "0x4E46|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0x4E48|PUSH|EDI", "0x4E49|MOV|ECX, dword ptr [ESI + 0x18]", "0x4E4C|TEST|ECX, ECX", "0x4E4E|JLE|0x6fad5322", "0x4E54|CMP|ECX, 0x100", "0x4E5A|JGE|0x6fad5322", "0x4E60|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [ESI + 0x10]", "0x4E63|LEA|EBX, [ECX + ECX*0x1]", "0x4E66|MOV|EDX, EAX", "0x4E68|AND|EDX, 0x7"],
      "comment": "Computes dynamic lighting effects for audio-visual context display\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate light radius (must be > 0 and < 256 pixels)\n2. Calculate adjusted coordinates by subtracting light radius from X/Y positions\n3. Align coordinates to 8-pixel boundaries using bitwise operations\n4. Check if light area fits within world bounds using global limit values\n5. Clear light intensity buffer (1024 entries) to prepare for new computation\n6. Compute light intensity grid by sampling color palette based on world coordinates\n7. Fill intensity buffer with scaled color values (shifted left by 4 bits)\n8. Generate light ray pattern using nested coordinate loops for visual effect\n9. Call lighting functions (FUN_6fad5330, FUN_6fad53e0) with computed coordinates\n10. Apply final lighting computation using distance-based intensity calculations\n11. Call pixel lighting function (FUN_6fad4d10) with RGBA color components\n\nParameters:\npAudioContext - AudioContext pointer containing light position, radius, and color data\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Function modifies global lighting buffers and calls rendering functions\n\nSpecial Cases:\nLight radius <= 0 or >= 256 pixels results in early return with no lighting applied\nCoordinates outside world bounds result in early return with no lighting applied\nLight intensity < 16 applies distance-based lighting calculation\nLight intensity >= 16 skips pixel processing\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x100 (256) - Maximum allowed light radius in pixels\n0x400 (1024) - Size of light intensity buffer in entries\n0x10 (16) - Light intensity threshold for pixel processing",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_StatList", "STRUCT_MonsterData", "PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Path", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "STRUCT_Skill", "PARAM_1", "PROP_LOOPHEAVY", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
