      "comment": "Applies dynamic lighting blending at specified coordinates based on global lighting mode.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check global lighting mode from DAT_6fbe8f00 (0-4 valid range)\n2. Mode 1: Simple light copy - copy source light value to destination if available\n3. Mode 2: Vertical blend - blend current position with vertically offset position using global blend factor\n4. Mode 3: Horizontal blend - blend current position with horizontally offset position using global blend factor  \n5. Mode 4: Single position blend - apply light value from vertically offset position\n6. Calculate array indices using Y * 0x40 + X pattern for 64-wide lighting grid\n7. Read from source light array (DAT_6fbdc2e4) or fallback to destination array (DAT_6fbe02fc)\n8. Perform alpha blending using formula: ((0x100 - blendFactor) * src + blendFactor * dst) >> 8\n9. Store final blended light value to destination array at coordinate position\n\nParameters:\nnLightX - X coordinate in lighting grid (0-63 range)\nnLightY - Y coordinate in lighting grid (0-63 range)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Modifies global destination light array DAT_6fbe02fc in-place\n\nSpecial Cases:\nSwitch default/invalid mode: Function returns without processing\nZero light value: Uses fallback value from destination array instead of source\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x40 (64) - Width of lighting grid for Y coordinate stride calculation\n0x100 (256) - Maximum blend factor value for 8-bit alpha blending\n0x8 (8) - Right shift amount for fixed-point division by 256\n\nGlobal Data Dependencies:\nDAT_6fbe8f00 - Current lighting blend mode (1=copy, 2=vertical, 3=horizontal, 4=single)\nDAT_6fbe02f8 - Horizontal offset for source light sampling\nDAT_6fbdc2e0 - Vertical offset for source light sampling  \nDAT_6fbdc2e4 - Source light intensity array (0=use fallback)\nDAT_6fbe02fc - Destination light array (modified by this function)\nDAT_6fbe46fc - Global blend factor (0-256 range, higher = more destination influence)",
