      "instructions": ["0x5540|SUB|ESP, 0x34", "0x5543|PUSH|EBX", "0x5544|PUSH|EBP", "0x5545|PUSH|ESI", "0x5546|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0x5548|XOR|EBX, EBX", "0x554A|PUSH|EDI", "0x554B|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [ESI + 0x18]", "0x554E|CMP|EAX, EBX", "0x5550|JLE|0x6fad58da", "0x5556|CMP|EAX, 0x100", "0x555B|JGE|0x6fad58da", "0x5561|ADD|EAX, EAX", "0x5563|MOV|ECX, 0x400", "0x5568|SAR|EAX, 0x3"],
      "comment": "Generates static light map data by sampling light values in a grid pattern for rendering optimization.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate light radius between 1 and 255 pixels\n2. Calculate sample grid dimensions (radius * 2 / 8)\n3. Initialize temporary light buffer DAT_6fbe02fc (1024 DWORD array)\n4. Skip processing if light type is 6 (special case)\n5. Load room data using compression flag (FUN_6fb60e80 vs FUN_6fb60e10)\n6. Obtain room light handle via Ordinal_10342, abort if invalid\n7. Get room base coordinates using Ordinal_10326/10329 (subtract 32 pixel offset)\n8. Sample light in 64x64 grid using Ordinal_10118 with 0x22 flag\n9. Fill collision map DAT_6fbdc2e4 (0x10 = blocked, 0x00 = passable)\n10. Calculate complex lighting patterns in nested coordinate loops\n11. Call CalculateLightRayDirection and BlendLightingAtCoordinates for each sample\n12. Validate output buffer is uninitialized (fStaticValid must be 0)\n13. Verify static map buffer pointer is valid (pnStaticMap not NULL)\n14. Copy processed light data from temp buffer to output map\n15. Mark static map as valid (fStaticValid = 1)\n\nParameters:\npLightContext    LightContext pointer containing light configuration\n  dwType         Light type (6 = special case, skip processing)\n  pData          Room data pointer for light calculations  \n  bUseCompression Flag: 0 = FUN_6fb60e10, 1 = FUN_6fb60e80\n  dwXCoordinate  Light X position in world coordinates\n  dwYCoordinate  Light Y position in world coordinates\n  dwLightRadius  Light radius in pixels (must be 1-255)\n  fStaticValid   Validation flag (must be 0 on entry)\n  pnStaticMap    Output buffer for static light map data\n\nReturns:\nvoid             No return value, modifies pnStaticMap buffer\n\nSpecial Cases:\nIf dwLightRadius <= 0 or >= 256, function returns early without processing\nIf dwType == 6, function returns early (special light type)\nIf room data load fails, function returns early\nIf room light handle is invalid (0), triggers assertion failure\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x6           Special light type that bypasses all processing\n0x100         Maximum allowed light radius (256 pixels)\n0x22          Light sample flag for Ordinal_10118 function\n0x20          Coordinate offset subtracted from room base position\n0x40          Grid sample size (64x64 sampling pattern)\n0x1000        Total samples in collision map (64 * 64)\n0x10          Collision map value for blocked/lit areas\n0x00          Collision map value for passable/unlit areas\n0x400         Size of temporary light buffer (1024 DWORDs)\n0x37c         Assertion line number for invalid room handle\n0x3bc         Assertion line number for already-initialized static map\n0x3bd         Assertion line number for NULL static map buffer\n\nError Handling:\nInvalid room handle triggers Ordinal_10023 assertion with line 0x37c\nAlready-initialized static map triggers assertion with line 0x3bc  \nNULL output buffer triggers assertion with line 0x3bd\nAll assertion failures call FUN_6fb9a10f with -1 (fatal exit)",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Light", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "STRUCT_ItemData", "PARAM_1", "GFX_DRAW", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData", "STRUCT_StatList", "PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Path", "STRUCT_Skill", "SRC_dLightMap.cpp", "PROP_LOOPHEAVY", "MOD_DRAW"]
