      "instructions": ["0x58F0|SUB|ESP, 0x1c", "0x58F3|PUSH|EBX", "0x58F4|PUSH|EBP", "0x58F5|PUSH|ESI", "0x58F6|PUSH|EDI", "0x58F7|MOV|EDI, ECX", "0x58F9|MOV|ESI, dword ptr [EDI + 0x18]", "0x58FC|TEST|ESI, ESI", "0x58FE|JLE|0x6fad5ae6", "0x5904|CMP|ESI, 0x100", "0x590A|JGE|0x6fad5ae6", "0x5910|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [EDI + 0x10]", "0x5913|MOV|ECX, EAX", "0x5915|AND|ECX, 0x7", "0x5918|SUB|EAX, ECX"],
      "comment": "Applies lighting effects with distance-based attenuation to the static map\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate light radius is within bounds (0 < radius < 0x100)\n2. Calculate 8-byte aligned adjusted coordinates by masking low 3 bits and subtracting radius\n3. Compute half radius in tiles (radius * 2 >> 3) for boundary calculations\n4. Check adjusted coordinates plus half radius are within static map boundaries using global DAT_ variables\n5. Validate light data pointer (pnStaticMap) and valid flag (fStaticValid) are non-null\n6. Extract light intensity from byte offset 0x24 and prepare intensity scaling factor\n7. Process 2D grid from adjusted coordinates, iterating through (halfRadius+1) x (halfRadius+1) tiles\n8. For each tile position, check if light data value is below intensity threshold (0x10)\n9. Calculate Manhattan distance using absolute values of X and Y coordinate differences\n10. Apply distance attenuation using magic constants (0x3d7, 0x197) based on dominant axis\n11. Compute final intensity using radius minus distance, scaled by light intensity factor\n12. Calculate blended intensity using light data shift and tile coverage (8 - (lightData >> 1))\n13. Call ApplyColorMixingToPalette with computed intensity and RGB color bytes from offsets 0x25-0x27\n\nParameters:\npLightSource (LightStruct *): Pointer to light source structure containing:\n  - Offset 0x10: X coordinate (uint)\n  - Offset 0x14: Y coordinate (uint) \n  - Offset 0x18: Light radius (uint, must be 0 < radius < 0x100)\n  - Offset 0x24: Light intensity (byte)\n  - Offset 0x25: Red color component (byte)\n  - Offset 0x26: Green color component (byte)\n  - Offset 0x27: Blue color component (byte)\n  - Offset 0x2c: Valid flag (uint, must be non-zero)\n  - Offset 0x30: Pointer to light data array (int *)\nIMPLICIT unaff_EDI (uint): Image X coordinate for rendering\nIMPLICIT unaff_ESI (uint): Image Y coordinate for rendering\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value, modifies color palette directly via ApplyColorMixingToPalette\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If radius <= 0 or >= 0x100, function returns early without processing\n- If adjusted coordinates plus half radius exceed static map boundaries, returns early\n- If light data pointer is null, triggers assertion and terminates (0x3e6)\n- If valid flag is zero, triggers assertion and terminates (0x3e7)\n- Light intensity attenuation uses threshold of 0x10 to skip processing dim lights\n- Distance calculation uses optimized absolute value with bit manipulation\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x100 (256): Maximum allowed light radius in pixels\n0x3e6 (998): Assertion line number for null light data pointer\n0x3e7 (999): Assertion line number for invalid light valid flag  \n0x10 (16): Light intensity threshold for processing eligibility\n0x3d7 (983): Primary distance attenuation factor for dominant axis\n0x197 (407): Secondary distance attenuation factor for non-dominant axis\n0x1f (31): Bit mask for sign extension in absolute value calculation\n\nGlobal Dependencies:\nDAT_6fbe02f0: Static map maximum X boundary\nDAT_6fbe02e8: Static map minimum X boundary  \nDAT_6fbe02f4: Static map maximum Y boundary\nDAT_6fbe02ec: Static map minimum Y boundary\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset | Size | Field Name | Type | Description\n-------|------|------------|------|-------------\n0x10   | 4    | nX         | uint | Light source X coordinate\n0x14   | 4    | nY         | uint | Light source Y coordinate  \n0x18   | 4    | nRadius    | uint | Light radius (0 < radius < 0x100)\n0x24   | 1    | byIntensity| byte | Base light intensity value\n0x25   | 1    | byRed      | byte | Red color component\n0x26   | 1    | byGreen    | byte | Green color component\n0x27   | 1    | byBlue     | byte | Blue color component\n0x2c   | 4    | fValid     | uint | Validation flag (must be non-zero)\n0x30   | 4    | pnLightData| int* | Pointer to light data array",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Light", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PARAM_1", "GFX_DRAW", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData", "STRUCT_MonsterData", "PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Skill", "SRC_dLightMap.cpp", "MOD_DRAW"]
