      "comment": "Cleanup all audio contexts by iterating through linked list and releasing resources\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if global audio context list head is null, exit if empty\n2. Iterate through each AudioContext node in the linked list\n3. For each context, check if display context pointer exists at offset +0x30\n4. If display context exists, call cleanup function with parameter 0x48a\n5. Always call cleanup function with parameter 0x48c for each context\n6. Advance to next context using pointer at offset +0x28\n7. Continue until reaching null pointer (end of list)\n8. Set global list head to null when complete\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\nIf global list head is already null, immediately sets it to 0 and returns early\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x48a (1162 decimal) - Cleanup parameter for contexts with display\n0x48c (1164 decimal) - Standard cleanup parameter for all contexts\n0x28 (40 decimal) - Offset to pNextContext pointer in AudioContext structure  \n0x30 (48 decimal) - Offset to pDisplayContext pointer in AudioContext structure\n\nStructure Layout:\nAudioContext (52 bytes total):\nOffset  Size  Field Name        Type            Description\n0x00    40    [various fields]  mixed           Context data fields\n0x28    4     pNextContext      AudioContext *  Pointer to next context in list\n0x30    4     pDisplayContext   void *          Pointer to display context (nullable)",
