      "comment": "Maps pixel coordinates to color palette RGBA values for rendering\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Convert pixel coordinates to grid coordinates by dividing by 8 (right shift 3)\n2. Subtract grid base offset from global offset variables (DAT_6fbe02e8, DAT_6fbe02ec)  \n3. Clamp grid X coordinate to valid range [0, 0x2F] (48 grid units maximum)\n4. Clamp grid Y coordinate to valid range [0, 0x2F] (48 grid units maximum)\n5. Calculate palette index using grid formula: Y * 0x30 + X (48x48 grid layout)\n6. Retrieve Red component from g_aColorPalette[index].byRed and store to output\n7. If color mode enabled (DAT_6fbaec04 != 0), retrieve Green, Blue, Alpha components\n8. Store RGB components to respective output pointers\n\nParameters:\nnPixelX      - Pixel X coordinate in world space\nnPixelY      - Pixel Y coordinate in world space  \npbRed        - Output pointer for Red component (0-255)\npbGreen      - Output pointer for Green component (0-255)\npbBlue       - Output pointer for Blue component (0-255) \npbAlpha      - Output pointer for Alpha component (0-255)\n\nReturns:\nvoid         - Color components returned via output pointers\n\nSpecial Cases:\nGrid coordinates clamped to [0, 0x2F] range to prevent palette array bounds overflow\nColor components only written if DAT_6fbaec04 color mode flag is non-zero\nRed component always written regardless of color mode flag\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x03         - Right shift count for divide-by-8 pixel-to-grid conversion\n0x2F         - Maximum grid coordinate (47 decimal, 48x48 grid)\n0x30         - Grid stride multiplier (48 decimal, grid width)\n\nStructure Layout:\nColorPaletteEntry (8 bytes):\nOffset  Size  Field       Type    Description\n+0x00   4     (unknown)   dword   Reserved/padding bytes\n+0x04   1     byRed       byte    Red component (0-255)\n+0x05   1     byGreen     byte    Green component (0-255) \n+0x06   1     byBlue      byte    Blue component (0-255)\n+0x07   1     byAlpha     byte    Alpha component (0-255)",
      "tags": ["PARAM_6", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PROP_LEAF"]
