      "comment": "Apply palette data using audio context coordinates.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract coordinate values from audio context at offsets 0x10 and 0x14\n2. Call external palette application function with lighting buffer, color palette, and coordinates\n3. Return immediately after operation completes\n\nParameters:\nNone - Function operates on global state\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Function is called conditionally when DAT_6fbf21e0 != 0 in parent context\n- Relies on g_pAudioContextListHead being properly initialized\n- Audio context offsets 0x10 and 0x14 contain coordinate data\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x10 - X coordinate offset in AudioContext structure\n0x14 - Y coordinate offset in AudioContext structure\n\nError Handling:\nNo error handling - assumes valid global state",
