      "comment": "Calculate weighted distance between two audio values\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Convert input values to absolute values using bit manipulation\n2. Compare the absolute values to determine primary and secondary components\n3. Apply weighted formula: larger_value * 983 + smaller_value * 407\n4. Normalize result by dividing by 1024 (right shift 10 bits)\n5. Return the calculated distance as unsigned integer\n\nParameters:\nnValue1 (int): First audio value (can be negative)\nnValue2 (int): Second audio value (can be negative)\n\nReturns:\nuint: Weighted distance between the two values, normalized to prevent overflow\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Negative input values are converted to absolute values before calculation\n- The larger absolute value gets weight 0x3d7 (983 decimal)\n- The smaller absolute value gets weight 0x197 (407 decimal)\n- Result is scaled down by 1024 to keep values in reasonable range\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x3d7 (983): Primary weight for the larger absolute value\n0x197 (407): Secondary weight for the smaller absolute value  \n0xa (10): Right shift amount for divide by 1024 normalization",
