      "comment": "Processes screen fade overlay effect with timer-based alpha blending and position alignment\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if fade effect is active (g_dwFadeEndTime != 0)\n2. Get current system tick count for timing calculations\n3. Compare fade end time to current time to determine if effect should expire\n4. If fade has expired, clear the timer and exit early\n5. Calculate time remaining until fade completion\n6. Calculate bottom position for overlay (screen height minus 47 pixels)\n7. Get alignment mode from FUN_6fae4fd0() (1=left-aligned, 2=right-aligned, other=centered)\n8. Adjust horizontal positioning based on alignment mode\n9. Calculate fade alpha value using linear interpolation (0-255 over 500ms duration)\n10. Call graphics function to render the fade overlay\n\nParameters:\nNone (void function)\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Early exit when g_dwFadeEndTime is 0 (no active fade)\n- Early exit when current time >= fade end time (expired fade)\n- Left alignment (mode 1): overlay width reduced by half screen width\n- Right alignment (mode 2): horizontal offset set to half screen width\n- Center alignment (other modes): no position adjustments\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x2f (47): Bottom margin offset from screen height\n0xff (255): Maximum alpha value for full opacity\n500: Fade duration in milliseconds\n1: Left alignment mode constant\n2: Right alignment mode constant",
