      "comment": "Loads and updates global RGBA color values for the render context.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize global color values using Ordinal_10927 with g_hRenderContext\n2. Set global color alpha value using Ordinal_10926 \n3. Get current render handle using FUN_6fb62880\n4. If render handle exists, get color interface with Ordinal_10342\n5. If color interface valid, read RGBA values into local buffer with Ordinal_10054\n6. Check if any color component is non-zero (R, G, B, A)\n7. If any component active, update global color values:\n   - DAT_6fbe8f1b (Alpha) = A component\n   - DAT_6fbe8f1a (Red) = R component  \n   - DAT_6fbe8f18 (Blue) = B component\n   - DAT_6fbe8f19 (Green) = G component\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x6fbe8f1a - Global Red color component storage\n0x6fbe8f18 - Global Blue color component storage  \n0x6fbe8f19 - Global Green color component storage\n0x6fbe8f1b - Global Alpha color component storage\n0x6fbe9284 - Global render context handle storage (g_hRenderContext)\n\nError Handling:\n- If FUN_6fb62880 returns NULL, function exits without updating colors\n- If Ordinal_10342 returns NULL, function exits without updating colors\n- Invalid color values (all zero) are ignored, keeping existing global values\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Color values are read as packed RGBA uint (dwRgbaColors) then split into byte components\n- Byte offsets: +0 = Red, +1 = Green, +2 = Blue, +3 = Alpha\n- Only updates global colors if at least one component is non-zero",
