      "instructions": ["0x5F70|SUB|ESP, 0x48", "0x5F73|PUSH|EBX", "0x5F74|PUSH|EBP", "0x5F75|PUSH|ESI", "0x5F76|PUSH|EDI", "0x5F77|MOV|EBX, EDX", "0x5F79|MOV|EDI, ECX", "0x5F7B|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x24], EBX", "0x5F7F|CALL|0x6fae4fd0", "0x5F84|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x1c], EAX", "0x5F88|CALL|0x6fb99256", "0x5F8D|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x30], EAX", "0x5F91|CALL|0x6fad27b0", "0x5F96|MOV|ESI, EAX", "0x5F98|CALL|dword ptr [0x6fba6098]"],
      "comment": "Processes tile rendering with alpha blending and animation effects for Diablo II graphics engine.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate shadow layer parameter (0 or 1 only, abort otherwise with debug error)\n2. Initialize rendering context, bank value, and state level from game subsystems\n3. Retrieve current tick count for time-based alpha animations\n4. Traverse linked list of tile nodes starting from pTileList->field_0x14\n5. For each tile node, get tile data pointer from offset 0xc\n6. Validate tile type is not 0xf (invalid/end marker), abort if invalid\n7. Process alpha animation flags (bit 0x2):\n   - If alpha disabled or animation expired: Set target alpha directly\n   - If animation active: Calculate interpolated alpha based on time progression\n   - Update tile alpha value and visibility flags (0x400 for invisible tiles)\n8. Process fade-out flags (bit 0x4):\n   - Clear fade flag and set removal flag (0x8) when time expires\n9. Apply shadow layer filtering based on tile flags (0x1c000 mask)\n10. Skip hidden tiles (flags 0x408) or mismatched shadow layer\n11. Get tile sprite coordinates from lookup tables (0x6fba6300 base)\n12. Select coordinate table based on tile flags bit 0x1:\n    - Clear: Use table at 0x6fbaed00 (48-byte stride)\n    - Set: Use table at 0x6fbaeee0 (48-byte stride) \n13. Convert pixel coordinates to color palette using MapPixelToColorPalette\n14. Build color buffer with RGB components and alpha blending\n15. Calculate final screen coordinates:\n    - Bank mode 0: Apply view offset transformation  \n    - Bank mode 1: Use absolute tile node coordinates\n16. Render tile sprite using appropriate ordinal function:\n    - Alpha 0xff: Use Ordinal_10080 (no alpha)\n    - Other: Use Ordinal_10081 (with alpha blending)\n17. Set success flag (0x20000) if rendering succeeded\n18. Move to next tile node via offset 0x10\n19. Continue until no more nodes in linked list\n\nParameters:\npTileList - Pointer to first tile node in rendering list  \ndwShadowLayer - Shadow layer filter (0=normal, 1=shadow, other=abort)\npViewData - View transformation data for coordinate calculations\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value, modifies tile states and renders to screen\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Invalid shadow layer (not 0 or 1) triggers debug abort via Ordinal_10023\n- Tile type 0xf indicates end of valid tiles, triggers error abort  \n- Alpha value 0xff uses optimized non-alpha rendering path\n- Time-based alpha animations use 500ms interpolation periods\n- Invisible tiles (alpha 0) get visibility flag 0x400 set\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0xf - Invalid/terminal tile type marker\n0x2 - Alpha animation active flag\n0x4 - Fade-out timer active flag  \n0x8 - Tile removal/deletion flag\n0x400 - Tile hidden/invisible flag\n0x408 - Combined hidden state mask\n0x1c000 - Shadow layer identification mask\n0x20000 - Rendering success flag\n0x6fba6300 - Base address of sprite coordinate lookup table\n0x6fbaed00 - Primary tile coordinate table base\n0x6fbaeee0 - Secondary tile coordinate table base  \n500 (0x1f4) - Alpha animation period in milliseconds\n0x10624dd3 - Magic multiplier for fast division by 500\n\nStructure Layout:\n\nTileNode (20 bytes):\nOffset | Size | Field       | Type      | Description  \n0x00   | 4    | dwPosX      | int       | Node X position\n0x04   | 4    | dwPosY      | int       | Node Y position  \n0x08   | 4    | field_8     | dword     | Reserved field\n0x0c   | 4    | pTileData   | TileData* | Pointer to tile data\n0x10   | 4    | pNext       | TileNode* | Next node in list\n\nTileData (48+ bytes):\nOffset | Size | Field       | Type   | Description\n0x00   | 4    | dwPosX      | int    | Tile X coordinate\n0x04   | 4    | dwPosY      | int    | Tile Y coordinate  \n0x14   | 4    | dwFlags     | dword  | Visibility and state flags\n0x18   | 4    | pTileInfo   | void*  | Sprite/texture data pointer\n0x1c   | 4    | dwTileType  | dword  | Tile type identifier\n0x24   | 4    | dwAnimFlags | dword  | Animation control flags\n0x28   | 1    | byAlpha     | byte   | Current alpha value\n0x29   | 1    | byStartAlpha| byte   | Animation start alpha\n0x2a   | 1    | byEndAlpha  | byte   | Animation target alpha  \n0x2c   | 4    | dwTimestamp | dword  | Animation start time",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "STRUCT_Room2", "GFX_DRAW", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "SRC_dWall.cpp", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData", "STRUCT_StatList", "PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Path", "PARAM_3", "STRUCT_Skill", "STRUCT_Other", "MOD_DRAW"]
