      "api_calls": ["GetExpansionModeIfInitialized", "GfxCallVtableMethod0xA4", "GfxCallVtableMethod0xA4"],
      "instructions": ["0x6400|SUB|ESP, 0x10", "0x6403|PUSH|EBX", "0x6404|PUSH|EBP", "0x6405|PUSH|ESI", "0x6406|PUSH|EDI", "0x6407|MOV|EDI, ECX", "0x6409|MOV|ESI, dword ptr [EDI + 0xeab0]", "0x640F|MOV|EBP, dword ptr [EDI + 0xeaa8]", "0x6415|IMUL|ESI, ESI", "0x6418|CALL|0x6fae4fd0", "0x641D|MOV|EBX, EAX", "0x641F|MOV|EAX, ESI", "0x6421|DEC|ESI", "0x6422|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0x6424|JZ|0x6fad6524"],
      "comment": "Processes and renders a 2D grid of tiles with multiple rendering modes\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract grid size (nGridSize) and tile list pointer from ViewData structure\n2. Initialize render context flags from FUN_6fae4fd0()\n3. Iterate through nGridSize × nGridSize tile grid\n4. For each grid row, traverse linked list of tile nodes\n5. Check tile flags to determine rendering mode:\n   - If flags & 0x03 == 0: Map pixel colors and render with color palette\n   - If flags & 0x01 != 0: Render with coordinate transformation using Ordinal_10082\n   - If flags & 0x02 != 0: Process special rendering using FUN_6fb90e70\n6. Apply coordinate transformation relative to camera position for positioned tiles\n7. After each row, check if alpha rendering is needed (dwPosX != 0)\n8. If alpha rendering required, call ProcessTileRenderingWithAlpha\n9. Advance to next tile row using pointer arithmetic\n\nParameters:\npViewData: ViewData structure containing camera position, offsets, and tile grid data\n   - dwOffsetX/dwOffsetY: Screen rendering offsets\n   - dwCameraBaseX/dwCameraBaseY: Camera world position\n   - Tile grid data at offset 0xeaa8 (TileNode list pointer)\n   - Grid dimensions at offset 0xeab0 (grid size value)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value, performs rendering operations through function calls\n\nSpecial Cases:\nGrid is processed row by row with nGridSize × nGridSize total iterations\nTile flags determine rendering path: 0x01 = coordinate transform, 0x02 = special mode, 0x03 = color palette\nAlpha rendering is conditional based on dwPosX field in TileNode structure\nCamera coordinate transformation: worldX = (viewOffsetX - cameraBaseX) + tileX\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x03 (3): Tile flag mask for mode detection\n0x01 (1): Tile flag for coordinate transformation mode  \n0x02 (2): Tile flag for special rendering mode\n0x555 (1365): Array index for ViewData structure fields (offset 0xeab0 / 4)\n0xeaa8 (60072): ViewData offset to tile list pointer\n0xeab0 (60080): ViewData offset to grid size value\n0x18 (24): Offset to tile data field in tile structure\n4: Fixed parameter passed to Ordinal_10082 (render mode/flags)\n\nStructure Layout:\nTileNode structure (20 bytes):\nOffset  Size  Field Name  Type           Description\n0x00    4     flags       uint           Tile rendering mode flags\n0x04    4     posX        uint           Tile X coordinate  \n0x08    4     posY        uint           Tile Y coordinate\n0x0C    4     pData       void*          Pointer to tile-specific data\n0x10    4     pNext       TileNode*      Next node in linked list\n0x14    4     dwPosX      uint           Alpha rendering flag\n\nViewData key fields accessed:\nOffset  Size  Field Name       Type        Description  \n0x04    4     dwOffsetX        uint        Screen X rendering offset\n0x08    4     dwOffsetY        uint        Screen Y rendering offset\n0x24    4     dwCameraBaseX    uint        Camera world X position\n0x28    4     dwCameraBaseY    uint        Camera world Y position\n0xEAA8  4     pTileGrid        TileNode*   Pointer to tile grid list\n0xEAB0  4     nGridSize        uint        Tile grid dimensions",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "STRUCT_Skill", "PARAM_1", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
