      "instructions": ["0x6530|MOV|EAX, [0x6fbaf14c]", "0x6535|AND|EAX, 0xff", "0x653A|SHR|EAX, 0x1", "0x653C|AND|EAX, 0x1", "0x653F|RET|"],
      "comment": "Checks if enhanced sorting mode is enabled by reading global processing flags.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Read 32-bit global processing flags from g_dwProcessingFlags (0x6fbaf14c)\n2. Mask lower byte to isolate relevant flag bits (flags & 0xFF)\n3. Right-shift by 1 bit to position sorting mode flag to bit 0\n4. Mask result with 0x1 to extract only the sorting mode bit\n5. Return 1 if sorting mode enabled, 0 if disabled\n\nParameters:\nNone - function takes no parameters\n\nReturns:\nuint - 1 if enhanced sorting mode is enabled, 0 if standard mode\n\nSpecial Cases:\nOnly examines bit 1 of the global flags (0x02 when set)\nOther flag bits are ignored by this function\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0xFF (255) - Byte mask to isolate lower 8 bits of flags\n0x1 (1) - Right shift count to position bit 1 to bit 0  \n0x1 (1) - Final mask to extract single bit result\n\nFlag Bits:\nBit 0: Unknown/unused by this function\nBit 1 (0x02): Enhanced sorting mode enable flag\nBits 2-7: Other processing flags (not examined)",
      "tags": ["PARAM_0", "PROP_LEAF", "PROP_SMALL"]
    },
