      "comment": "Controls bit 0 of the global processing flags register.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Test input flag parameter for zero/non-zero condition\n2. If fDisable is non-zero, clear bit 0 of g_dwProcessingFlags (disable processing)\n3. If fDisable is zero, set bit 0 of g_dwProcessingFlags (enable processing)\n4. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\n- fDisable (int): Boolean flag controlling bit 0 state\n  - Non-zero: Clear bit 0 (disable processing feature)\n  - Zero: Set bit 0 (enable processing feature)\n\nReturns:\n- void: No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Function uses inverted logic: non-zero input disables the flag\n- Bit manipulation uses bitwise AND with 0xFFFFFFFE to clear bit 0\n- Bit manipulation uses bitwise OR with 0x1 to set bit 0\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n- 0xFFFFFFFE: Bitmask to clear bit 0 (preserve all other bits)\n- 0x1: Bitmask to set bit 0",
