      "comment": "Checks if processing mode flag bit 8 is enabled in global flags register.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load global processing flags from g_dwProcessingFlags (0x6fbaf14c)\n2. Right shift flags by 8 positions to move bit 8 to bit 0 position  \n3. Mask with 0x1 to isolate the bit value\n4. Return the isolated bit value (0 or 1)\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\nuint: 1 if processing mode flag bit 8 is set, 0 if clear\n\nSpecial Cases:\nProcessing mode flag bit 8 (0x100) controls specific processing behavior.\nFunction called by video playback and processing routines to check mode state.\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x8 (8): Bit position to extract from flags register\n0x1: Mask to isolate single bit value after shift\n0x100: Actual bit value in flags register (bit 8)\n0x6fbaf14c: Memory address of g_dwProcessingFlags global variable\n\nFlag Bits:\nBit 8 (0x100): Processing mode enable flag",
