      "comment": "Initialize game state and configure global variables based on state parameter.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate game state parameter is in valid range (0-3)\n2. Check state-specific prerequisites in global flags\n3. Store validated state in global storage\n4. Verify initialization subsystem is available\n5. Process state-specific configuration:\n   - State 0: Reset frame counter to zero\n   - State 1: Initialize subsystem and set frame limit with 0x20 offset\n   - State 2: Get version, apply locale conversion, configure display parameters based on version\n   - State 3: Clear game process flag\n\nParameters:\n  nGameState (int): Game state identifier (0=reset, 1=initialize, 2=configure, 3=shutdown)\n\nReturns:\n  void: No return value, function performs state configuration\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Invalid state (< 0 or >= 4): Triggers assertion failure and program termination\n  - Null subsystem: Triggers assertion failure and program termination  \n  - State 1 with DAT_6fbe9020 flag set: No operation performed\n  - State 2 with DAT_6fbe901c flag set: No operation performed unless state is 2\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x20 (32): Frame buffer offset added to base frame count\n  0x2a (42): Display parameter value for standard versions\n  0xaa (170): Display parameter value for extended configurations\n  0x1c (28): Display parameter value for compact configurations\n  0x38 (56): Display parameter value for intermediate configurations\n  0x100 (256): Frame limit for high-performance versions (0x78, 0x79)\n  0x6d-0x70 (109-112): Version range for standard configuration\n  0x75 (117): Version requiring intermediate configuration\n  0x78-0x79 (120-121): High-performance versions\n  0x137 (311): Error code for subsystem initialization failure\n  0x12a (298): Error code for invalid state parameter",
