      "comment": "Configure network latency timing parameters based on environment type\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get network connection status and verify environment available\n2. Retrieve environment ID and check environment type \n3. If environment type is not 0x04, reset timing flags and configure default values\n4. Get random timing base values using Ordinal_10918()\n5. Set latency timing globals: DAT_6fbe8f54, DAT_6fbe8f38, DAT_6fbe8f3c, DAT_6fbe8f30\n6. Use environment ID switch statement to determine timing configuration:\n   - Cases 0x6d-0x70: Set 25ms minimum timing (0x19)\n   - Cases 0x78-0x79: Enable initialization flag  \n   - Case 0x75: Set initialization mode\n7. Check if random timing value meets minimum threshold\n8. If below threshold and not forced, reset timing flags and exit\n9. Apply initialization flag and call InitializeGameState if needed\n10. Validate timing state and handle cleanup\n\nParameters:\nnForceReset (int) - Force reset flag: 0=normal operation, non-zero=force timing reset\n\nReturns:\nAlways returns 0 (success)\n\nSpecial Cases:\nIf network unavailable, uses hardcoded fallback values:\n- DAT_6fbe8f54 = 0x138 (312ms)\n- DAT_6fbe8f38 = 0x4e2 (1250ms) \n- DAT_6fbe8f30 = 0x7f (127ms)\n- DAT_6fbe8f3c = 0x7f (127ms)\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x04 - Environment type threshold\n0x7d - Base latency offset (125ms)\n500 - Base timing interval (500ms)\n0x5c - Secondary latency offset (92ms)\n0x19 - Minimum timing threshold (25ms)\n0x138 - Fallback latency (312ms)\n0x4e2 - Fallback interval (1250ms)\n0x7f - Fallback secondary latency (127ms)\n\nError Handling:\nCalls Ordinal_10023 and FUN_6fb9a10f for critical timing violations\nResets global timing flags on errors or threshold failures\nHandles particle data cleanup on timing state changes",
      "tags": ["PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "SRC_Env.cpp", "PARAM_1", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "MOD_GAME"]
