      "comment": "Initialize weather effect system with rain and bubble overlay parameters.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call FUN_6fad6870(1) to initialize weather subsystem\n2. Check if weather system is already initialized (DAT_6fbe9028 flag)\n3. If not initialized, call FUN_6fb62880() to test latency capability\n4. If latency test fails, set default hardcoded timing values\n5. If latency test passes, call Ordinal_10918() three times to generate random timing offsets\n6. Set initialized flag (DAT_6fbe9028 = 1) and base timing value\n7. Initialize base weather effect parameters (timing and intensity values)\n8. Check game difficulty level using Ordinal_10001() for values 0x02 and 0x04\n9. If difficulty is 0x02 or 0x04, multiply base timing by 3 for increased effect\n10. Initialize secondary timing parameters and array indices\n11. Generate color palette arrays for weather effects in loop (12 iterations):\n    - Calculate color values for rain effects using division and character arithmetic\n    - Generate different color intensities for 4 rain overlay arrays\n    - Generate color values for bubble effects using similar calculations\n12. Load rain overlay graphics files (Rain1-Rain4) using wsprintfA and ConcatenateFormatAndProcess\n13. Process loaded rain graphics through Ordinal_10046() for format conversion\n14. Load bubble overlay graphics files (bubble1-bubble4) using same process\n15. Process loaded bubble graphics through Ordinal_10046() for format conversion\n16. Clear initialization counter and return\n\nParameters:\nnGameDifficulty (int) - Game difficulty level passed in ECX register, checked for values 0x02 and 0x04\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value, initializes global weather effect data structures\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If DAT_6fbe9028 is already 1, skips initialization and only sets runtime parameters\n- If FUN_6fb62880() returns 0, uses hardcoded fallback values instead of random generation\n- Difficulty levels 0x02 and 0x04 cause 3x timing multiplier for enhanced effects\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x1d4c (7500) - Base timing interval for weather effects\n0xfa (250) - Secondary timing parameter  \n3000 - Base duration for weather effects\n0x7d (125) - Timing offset base value\n0x138 (312) - Hardcoded timing fallback value\n0x4e2 (1250) - Hardcoded secondary timing fallback\n0x7f (127) - Hardcoded offset fallback value\n0x5c (92) - Random offset addition base\n500 - Random timing addition base\n0x32 (50) - Additional timing parameter\n0xc (12) - Loop iteration count for color generation\n0x28 (40) - Timing offset increment per iteration\n0x18 (24) - Iteration offset increment  \n0x50 (80) - Loop counter increment\n0x1e0 (480) - Loop termination condition\n260 - File path buffer size for wsprintfA",
      "tags": ["PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "SRC_Env.cpp", "STRUCT_Skill", "STRUCT_ItemData", "PARAM_1", "PROP_LOOPHEAVY", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "MOD_GAME", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
