      "comment": "Initialize the flag system state if not already initialized.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if tertiary flag system is already initialized (g_dwTertiaryFlags == 0)\n2. If uninitialized, reset secondary flags to zero state\n3. Set tertiary flags to active state (0x1) to mark system as initialized\n4. Set primary flags to active state (0x1) to enable flag operations\n5. Store initialization context ID for future reference\n\nParameters:\ndwContextId (int): Initialization context identifier passed in ECX register\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value, performs in-place flag system initialization\n\nSpecial Cases:\nIf g_dwTertiaryFlags is already non-zero, function performs early return with no operations\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x1 - Active flag state indicating system is initialized and operational\n0x0 - Reset state for secondary flags during initialization\n\nGlobal Variables Modified:\ng_dwSecondaryFlags (0x6fbe8fa4) - Reset to 0 during initialization\ng_dwTertiaryFlags (0x6fbe9008) - Set to 1 to mark system initialized  \ng_dwPrimaryFlags (0x6fbe8f80) - Set to 1 to enable flag operations\ng_dwInitializationContext (0x6fbaf158) - Stores context ID for reference",
