      "comment": "Configures a rain splash effect element for rendering with position and visual parameters.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate compression system state using FUN_6fb62880()\n2. If validation fails, trigger fatal error with assertion (0x2d0) and terminate process\n3. Obtain rain element index from Ordinal_10064() \n4. If element index is valid (-1 check), calculate element structure pointer:\n   - Base: g_dwCompressionObject2 + 0x11c (rain element array)\n   - Offset: (element_index >> 16) * 0x18 (24-byte stride per element)\n5. Determine rendering mode using Ordinal_10010()\n6. Configure position based on rendering mode:\n   - Mode 0 (Relative): Calculate offset from reference position (Ordinal_10918())\n     * Get reference position and subtract 0x28\n     * Use absolute value if negative\n     * Calculate adjustment: (abs_diff * -2) + 0x50\n     * If adjustment is zero, use 0 for secondary position\n     * Set X: (reference - adjustment) + nBaseOffsetX\n     * Set Y: reference + nBaseOffsetY\n   - Mode != 0 (Absolute): Use scaled absolute coordinates\n     * Get X scaling factor from Ordinal_10918()\n     * Set X: (scale_x * 0x10000) + nAbsoluteX\n     * Get Y scaling factor from Ordinal_10918()\n     * Set Y: (scale_y * 0x10000) + nAbsoluteY\n7. Generate element type flags using Ordinal_10917()\n8. Calculate final type: (flags & 1) + 2 (range: 2-3)\n9. Validate type range (must be ≤ 3), trigger fatal error (0x2e8) if invalid\n10. Initialize remaining fields: +0x10 = 0, +0x14 = 2\n\nParameters:\nnBaseOffsetX - Base X coordinate offset for relative positioning mode\nnBaseOffsetY - Base Y coordinate offset for relative positioning mode  \nnAbsoluteX - Absolute X coordinate for absolute positioning mode\nnAbsoluteY - Absolute Y coordinate for absolute positioning mode\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value, function operates through side effects on rain element structure\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Invalid compression state: Triggers fatal assertion at 0x2d0 and process termination\n- Invalid element index (-1): Function returns early without configuring element\n- Type flags out of range (>3): Triggers fatal assertion at 0x2e8 and process termination\n- Zero adjustment calculation: Uses 0 instead of recalculating reference position\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x11c - Offset to rain element array within compression object\n0x18 (24) - Size of each rain element structure in bytes\n0x28 (40) - Reference position adjustment constant for relative mode\n0x10000 (65536) - Scaling factor for absolute positioning coordinates\n0x2d0 (720) - Error code for compression system validation failure\n0x2e8 (744) - Error code for invalid rain element type range\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset | Size | Field Name | Type | Description\n+0x4   | 4    | nPosX      | int  | Rain element X position (screen coordinates)\n+0x8   | 4    | nPosY      | int  | Rain element Y position (screen coordinates)  \n+0xc   | 4    | dwType     | uint | Element type/flags (2-3 range, controls visual appearance)\n+0x10  | 4    | dwField16  | uint | Unknown field, initialized to 0\n+0x14  | 4    | dwField20  | uint | Unknown field, initialized to 2",
