      "api_calls": ["FogAssert", "AllocDataArrayEntry", "GetExpansionModeIfInitialized", "GetRandomBoundedValue", "GetRandomBoundedValue", "GetRandomBoundedValue", "GetRandomBoundedValue"],
      "instructions": ["0x71A0|SUB|ESP, 0x8", "0x71A3|PUSH|EBX", "0x71A4|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x8], EDX", "0x71A8|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x4], ECX", "0x71AC|CALL|0x6fb62880", "0x71B1|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0x71B3|JNZ|0x6fad71d3", "0x71B5|PUSH|0x2fa", "0x71BA|PUSH|0x6fbaf1c4", "0x71BF|PUSH|0x6fbaf228", "0x71C4|CALL|0x6fb99a7a", "0x71C9|ADD|ESP, 0xc", "0x71CC|PUSH|-0x1", "0x71CE|CALL|0x6fb9a10f", "0x71D3|MOV|ECX, dword ptr [0x6fbe9000]"],
      "comment": "Setup and position a grid element for rendering operations.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate grid system availability by calling system initialization check\n2. If validation fails, log fatal error and terminate process with exit code -1\n3. Get current screen coordinates using coordinate transformation system\n4. If coordinate valid (not -1), calculate grid element pointer from base array\n5. Check rendering mode via display state query\n6. For mode 0 (random positioning):\n   a. Get random coordinate value and subtract center offset (0x28)\n   b. Calculate absolute distance from center for jitter calculation\n   c. Apply jitter formula: (distance * -2 + 0x50) for shake effect\n   d. Set X position: (random - jitter) + input X offset\n   e. Set Y position: input Y offset + random coordinate - 0x1e adjustment\n7. For non-zero mode (screen positioning):\n   a. Get screen-relative random values and subtract 2 for border padding\n   b. Scale by 0x10000 (65536) for high-precision coordinates\n   c. Set X position: (scaled random - 2) + screen X parameter\n   d. Set Y position: (scaled random - 2) + screen Y parameter\n8. Initialize element state fields: flags=0, type=2, state=2\n\nParameters:\nnXOffset (ECX) - X coordinate offset for element positioning\nnYOffset (EDX) - Y coordinate offset for element positioning  \nnScreenX (stack) - Screen X coordinate for high-precision mode\nnScreenY (stack) - Screen Y coordinate for high-precision mode\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Function modifies grid element structure in global grid array\n\nSpecial Cases:\nGrid system failure triggers fatal error with code 0x2fa and process termination\nInvalid coordinates (-1) result in early return with no grid element modification\nRandom positioning applies center bias with jitter effect using 0x28 center and 0x50 max offset\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x28 (40) - Center coordinate offset for random positioning calculations\n0x50 (80) - Maximum jitter range for shake effect in random mode\n0x1e (30) - Y coordinate adjustment offset for vertical alignment\n0x10000 (65536) - Coordinate scaling factor for high-precision screen mode\n0x2fa (762) - Fatal error code for grid system initialization failure\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset | Size | Field | Type | Description\n0x00   | 4    | dwField0 | uint | Reserved/unused field\n0x04   | 4    | dwXPos | uint | Calculated X position coordinate\n0x08   | 4    | dwYPos | uint | Calculated Y position coordinate  \n0x0C   | 4    | dwType | uint | Element type identifier (set to 2)\n0x10   | 4    | dwFlags | uint | Element flags (set to 0)\n0x14   | 4    | dwState | uint | Element state (set to 2)",
