      "comment": "Validates graphics device initialization and capabilities.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get graphics device handle from internal system\n2. If no graphics handle available, return validation failure\n3. Create graphics device context using the handle\n4. Initialize device context for rendering\n5. Configure device for graphics operations\n6. Test device capabilities and return success status\n\nParameters:\nNone - function operates on global graphics state\n\nReturns:\nbool - true if graphics device validation successful, false otherwise\n      - true: Device initialized and ready for graphics operations\n      - false: Device unavailable, initialization failed, or capabilities insufficient\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Early return false when no graphics handle available\n- Device validation involves multiple API calls that must all succeed",
