      "comment": "Main game frame processing function that handles compression object updates, entity processing, and timed spell effects.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get current game state and initialize pause/spell flags\n2. If game state active, query compression handle data to determine pause and spell flags\n3. Check compression objects and clean up inactive ones if pause flag set\n4. Update global pause and spell state flags\n5. Get frame counter and validate game state still active\n6. If frame counter advanced, update global frame counter and process entities:\n   - If not paused, process first compression object entities with position updates\n   - Process second compression object entities with timer decrements\n   - Handle game state transitions and frame timing calculations\n   - Update position interpolation values\n7. If spell flag active, process timed spell effects\n8. If game state invalid, trigger error handler and exit\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value, function processes game state in-place\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If game state is invalid (nGameState == 0), calls error handler and exits with code -1\n- Compression objects are only processed if their count field (+0x114 offset) is non-zero\n- Entity arrays use 0x24-byte stride for first object, 0x18-byte stride for second object\n- Frame timing uses complex interpolation between states 1 and 3\n- Game state cycles: 0 → 1 → 2 → 3 → 0 (wrapping at 4)\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x114 - Compression object entity count field offset\n0x11c - Compression object entity array pointer offset\n0x110 - Compression object maximum entity index offset\n0x24 - First compression object entity stride (36 bytes)\n0x18 - Second compression object entity stride (24 bytes)\n0x1ff - Animation frame mask (511 frames)\n0x19 - Animation timing divisor (25)\n0x545 - Error code line number for invalid game state",
      "tags": ["PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "SRC_Env.cpp", "STRUCT_Skill", "STRUCT_ItemData", "PARAM_0", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "MOD_GAME", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
