      "comment": "Updates snow particle system and manages timing counters.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if snow particle count is below threshold (g_dwCompressionObject1[0x114] < g_dwBufferFlags)\n2. If below threshold, initialize snow particles in loop until threshold met\n3. Calculate movement delta based on flag state (2 if DAT_6fbe9014 is 0, else 1)\n4. Adjust DAT_6fbe8f3c position value based on DAT_6fbe8f30 target and delta\n5. Decrement timer DAT_6fbe8f54 by 1\n6. If timer reaches 0, reset with random values:\n   - If DAT_6fbe9014 is 0: timer = random() + 125, target = random() + 92\n   - If DAT_6fbe9014 is 1: timer = random() + 250, target varies based on g_dwQuaternaryBufferSize\n7. If g_dwTertiaryFlags is set, decrement DAT_6fbe8f38 and set g_dwPrimaryFlags when it reaches 0\n\nParameters:\nNone (operates on global state variables)\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- DAT_6fbe9014 flag controls timer values and movement behavior\n- g_dwQuaternaryBufferSize affects random target calculation when flag is set\n- Multiple global timers and flags coordinate snow system state\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x114 - Offset to particle count in compression object\n0x7d - Base timer value (125 decimal) for normal mode\n0x5c - Base target value (92 decimal) for normal mode  \n0xfa - Base timer value (250 decimal) for enhanced mode\n0x177 - Random parameter (375 decimal) for normal timer\n0x47 - Random parameter (71 decimal) for normal target\n0x36b - Random parameter (875 decimal) for enhanced timer",
