      "comment": "Renders sprites and overlay elements to the screen during game execution.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Retrieve game context and validate availability\n2. Check for active graphics context and set context flag\n3. Validate game context is available, exit with error if not\n4. Update primary timing flags and decrement frame counter\n5. Handle frame counter expiration and timing state transitions\n6. Set secondary timing flags based on counter state\n7. Initialize progress bar rendering if in initialization phase\n8. Render timer progress bar with calculated coordinates\n9. Check for sprite count threshold (>10) for overlay rendering\n10. Calculate screen coordinates based on display mode adjustment\n11. Render progress overlay bar using calculated dimensions\n12. Process sprite rendering if context and compression data available\n13. Calculate screen clipping bounds based on display mode\n14. Iterate through sprite object array from compression context\n15. Skip inactive sprites (type == 0)\n16. Handle animated sprites with timing calculations\n17. Calculate sprite dimensions using animation frame data\n18. Check sprite bounds against screen clipping rectangle\n19. Render sprite using calculated coordinates and color parameters\n20. Handle static sprites with direct coordinate mapping\n21. Use offset tables for sprite positioning adjustments\n22. Advance to next sprite in array and repeat until complete\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Function performs rendering operations with no return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Exits immediately if no game context available (calls FUN_6fb9a10f with -1)\n- Skips sprite rendering if sprite count <= 10\n- Uses different coordinate calculations based on display mode (1 or 2)\n- Handles both animated and static sprite types with different rendering paths\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x571 - Error line number for missing game context\n0x2f - Screen margin offset (47 pixels)\n0xff - Maximum color alpha value\n0x5 - Overlay rendering type/mode\n0x114 - Offset to sprite array active flag in compression object\n0x11c - Offset to sprite object array pointer\n0x110 - Offset to sprite count in compression object\n0x25 - Offset to blend mode byte in sprite object\n0x24 - Offset to color index byte in sprite object\n0x10 - Size multiplier for offset table entries (16 bytes)\n0x28 - Sprite object structure size (40 bytes)\n0xca - Progress bar identifier constant (202)\n0x19 - Progress bar Y offset (25 pixels)\n500 - Timer base offset value\n200 - Animation coordinate offset value\n\nError Handling:\n- Missing game context triggers assertion with file/line info\n- Invalid sprite indices are bounds-checked before array access\n- Screen coordinate validation prevents off-screen rendering\n- Animation frame bounds are validated before calculation\n\nStructure Layout:\nSprite Object (40 bytes):\n| Offset | Size | Field Name    | Type  | Description                    |\n|--------|------|---------------|-------|--------------------------------|\n| 0x00   | 2    | wType         | ushort| Sprite type/active flag        |\n| 0x02   | 4    | nX            | int   | X coordinate                   |\n| 0x04   | 4    | nY            | int   | Y coordinate                   |\n| 0x06   | 4    | nWidth        | int   | Sprite width                   |\n| 0x08   | 4    | nHeight       | int   | Sprite height                  |\n| 0x0c   | 4    | nAnimFrame    | int   | Animation frame index          |\n| 0x10   | 4    | dwFlags       | uint  | Rendering flags                |\n| 0x1c   | 4    | dwStaticFlag  | uint  | Static sprite indicator        |\n| 0x24   | 1    | byColorIndex  | byte  | Color palette index            |\n| 0x25   | 1    | byBlendMode   | byte  | Alpha blending mode            |",
      "tags": ["PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "SRC_Env.cpp", "STRUCT_Skill", "STRUCT_ItemData", "PARAM_0", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "MOD_GAME", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
