      "instructions": ["0x7EF0|SUB|ESP, 0x64", "0x7EF3|PUSH|EBX", "0x7EF4|PUSH|EBP", "0x7EF5|PUSH|ESI", "0x7EF6|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0x7EF8|PUSH|EDI", "0x7EF9|MOV|EBP, EDX", "0x7EFB|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x1c], ESI", "0x7EFF|CALL|0x6fb99256", "0x7F04|MOV|EDI, dword ptr [0x6fbae0e4]", "0x7F0A|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x24], EAX", "0x7F0E|MOV|EAX, [0x6fbae0e8]", "0x7F13|XOR|EBX, EBX", "0x7F15|ADD|EAX, -0x2f", "0x7F18|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x10], EBX"],
      "comment": "Renders all visible entities within screen boundaries after applying camera offset transformations.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Store entity container pointer and initialize camera/rendering state\n2. Get current rendering mode from graphics subsystem via Ordinal_10010\n3. Copy screen dimensions and calculate maximum Y coordinate (screen height - 47)\n4. Determine camera transformation mode by calling FUN_6fae4fd0 camera subsystem\n5. Apply camera offset transformations based on transformation mode:\n   - Mode 1: Calculate negative X offset and reduce effective screen width\n   - Mode 2: Calculate positive X offset for right side rendering\n6. Get entity array pointer from container at offset 0x11C\n7. Initialize 72-byte rendering buffer (18 DWORDs) with zeros using REP STOSD\n8. Iterate through all entities in container up to count at offset 0x110:\n   - Skip inactive entities (first short == 0)\n   - For Mode 0 (normal): Apply direct coordinate transformation and clip test\n   - For other modes: Use coordinate projection via Ordinal_10065/10066\n   - Load entity color from color array using entity's color index\n   - Call Ordinal_10072 graphics primitive renderer with transformed coordinates\n9. Advance to next entity using 24-byte stride (0xC * 2)\n\nParameters:\npEntityContainer (EntityContainer*): Pointer to entity container structure with:\n  - Offset 0x110: Entity count (int)\n  - Offset 0x11C: Pointer to entity array (RenderEntity*)\npdwColorArray (uint*): Array of DWORD color values indexed by entity color index\n\nReturns:\nvoid: No return value, renders entities directly to active graphics surface\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Camera Mode 1: Applies negative X offset, reduces effective screen width by 2*offset\n- Camera Mode 2: Applies positive X offset for right-side view\n- Screen Clipping: Only renders entities within bounds [nLeftOffset, nMaxScreenY]\n- Color Indexing: Entity color index at offset +6 scales by 4 for DWORD array access\n- Graphics Buffer: 72-byte buffer layout matches Ordinal_10072 parameter structure\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x110 (272): Offset to entity count in container structure\n0x11C (284): Offset to entity array pointer in container structure\n0x2F (47): Screen boundary margin subtracted from screen height\n0x12 (18): Number of DWORDs in graphics rendering buffer (72 bytes total)\n0xC (12): Half-stride for entity pointer advancement (24-byte total stride)\n0xFFFFFFFF: Color mask parameter passed to graphics renderer\n\nStructure Layout:\nRenderEntity (24 bytes):\nOffset | Size | Field Name   | Type   | Description\n0x00   | 2    | wActive      | ushort | Active flag (0=inactive, non-zero=active)\n0x02   | 4    | nXCoord      | int    | World X coordinate\n0x04   | 4    | nYCoord      | int    | World Y coordinate\n0x06   | 4    | nColorIndex  | int    | Index into color array\n0x08   | 4    | dwRenderData | uint   | Additional rendering parameters",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PARAM_2", "STRUCT_Skill", "STRUCT_ItemData", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
    },
