      "instructions": ["0x8540|PUSH|EBX", "0x8541|PUSH|EBP", "0x8542|XOR|EBP, EBP", "0x8544|PUSH|ESI", "0x8545|MOV|dword ptr [0x6fbaf7ac], 0x4", "0x854F|MOV|dword ptr [0x6fbe92b0], EBP", "0x8555|CALL|0x6fae5560", "0x855A|CMP|dword ptr [0x6fbe926c], EBP", "0x8560|JZ|0x6fad8675", "0x8566|CALL|0x6fae4fd0", "0x856B|CMP|EAX, 0x3", "0x856E|JZ|0x6fad8675", "0x8574|MOV|EBX, dword ptr [ESP + 0x10]", "0x8578|PUSH|EDI", "0x8579|XOR|ESI, ESI"],
      "comment": "ProcessMouseClickInScrollWindow - Handles left mouse click events within scroll window regions.\n\nProcesses mouse clicks by determining if the click falls within left or right scroll \nwindow boundaries based on the current scroll mode. If click is outside both scroll \nregions, it issues a UI interaction command to handle the click normally.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Set g_dwCurrentProcessingState = 4 (mouse click processing mode)\n2. Clear g_dwEventCompletionFlag and call ClearUnitSelectionError()\n3. Early exit if g_dwPostGameRenderMode == 0 (post-game screen)\n4. Get current scroll window mode; early exit if mode == 3 (disabled)\n5. Extract mouse X coordinate from pMouseEvent+0x0C (low word)\n6. Extract mouse Y coordinate from pMouseEvent+0x0C (high word via >> 16)\n7. Check LEFT scroll region (mode == 2):\n   - X must be > 0 AND X < (screenWidth / 2)\n   - Y must be > 0 AND Y < (screenHeight - 0x2F)\n   - If all true, set fLeftRegionClick = true\n8. Check RIGHT scroll region (mode == 1):\n   - X must be > (screenWidth / 2) AND X < screenWidth\n   - Y must be > 0 AND Y < viewportHeight\n   - If all true, set fRightRegionClick = true\n9. If click in either scroll region: set pMouseEvent+0x18 = 0, pMouseEvent+0x1C = 0\n   and call InsertCacheNodeWithCookie(pMouseEvent), then return\n10. Otherwise (normal click area):\n    - Set g_dwMouseClickProcessingResult = 1\n    - Call GetGameContext() to get game state\n    - Build dwFlags from global state flags (0x8 if run mode, 0x4 if state flag set)\n    - If game context valid (*pContext == 0), call ProcessUIInteractionCommand(3, mouseX, mouseY, flags)\n    - Set pMouseEvent+0x18 = 1, pMouseEvent+0x1C = 0\n    - Call InsertCacheNodeWithCookie(pMouseEvent)\n\nParameters:\npMouseEvent (dword) - Pointer to mouse event data structure:\n  +0x0C: Packed coordinates (low word = X, high word = Y)\n  +0x18: Processing result flag (1 = processed normally, 0 = scroll region)\n  +0x1C: Secondary result flag (always set to 0)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value. Side effects via global state and pMouseEvent fields.\n\nGlobals Accessed:\ng_dwCurrentProcessingState @ 0x6FBAF7AC - Processing state (set to 4)\ng_dwEventCompletionFlag @ 0x6FBE92B0 - Event completion (cleared to 0)\ng_dwPostGameRenderMode @ 0x6FBE926C - Post-game screen mode\ng_dwScreenWidth @ 0x6FBAE0E4 - Screen width for boundary checks\ng_dwScreenHeight @ 0x6FBAE0E8 - Screen height for boundary checks  \ng_dwViewportHeight @ 0x6FBDC010 - Viewport height for right region check\ng_dwMouseClickProcessingResult @ 0x6FBE92AC - Result of click processing\ng_dwGlobalState @ 0x6FBE92B4 - Global state for run mode flag\ng_dwAlwaysRunSetting @ 0x6FBE92B8 - Always run setting\ng_nGlobalStateFlag @ 0x6FBE92BC - Additional state flag\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x04 - Mouse click processing state\n0x2F (47) - Bottom margin offset for left scroll region\n0x03 - UI interaction command type for normal click\n0x08 - Run mode flag in dwFlags\n0x04 - State flag in dwFlags\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Early exit if post-game render mode is 0\n- Early exit if scroll window mode is 3 (disabled)\n- Scroll region clicks bypass normal UI command processing\n- ProcessUIInteractionCommand only called if game context first dword is 0",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_1", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
    },
