      "comment": "Process clear selection UI message (message type 0x10).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Set g_dwCurrentProcessingState to 0x10 (clear selection mode)\n2. Clear g_dwUICommandResult to 0\n3. Set g_dwUICommandPending to 1 (command in progress)\n4. Clear g_dwEventCompletionFlag\n5. Call ClearUnitSelectionError to reset selection error state\n6. Check g_dwPostGameRenderMode - exit early if 0 (not in game)\n7. Get game context via GetGameContext\n8. If pGameContext->placeholder == 0:\n   - Extract screen coordinates from pMessage->wScreenX and wScreenY\n   - Call ProcessUIInteractionCommand with action type 5 (clear selection)\n   - Store result in g_dwUICommandResult\n9. Call AssertInventoryStatsExist to validate inventory stats\n10. If stats valid, call QuerySystemInfoAndIncrementCounters\n11. Mark message as processed: pMessage->dwProcessed = 1\n12. Clear result field: pMessage->dwResult = 0\n13. Insert message into cache via InsertCacheNodeWithCookie\n\nParameters:\npMessage (UIInputMessage *) - Pointer to UI input message structure\n  +0x00: dwUnknown00 - Reserved\n  +0x04: dwUnknown04 - Reserved\n  +0x08: wFlags - Input flags passed to ProcessUIInteractionCommand\n  +0x0C: wScreenX - Screen X coordinate\n  +0x0E: wScreenY - Screen Y coordinate\n  +0x18: dwProcessed - Set to 1 when message handled\n  +0x1C: dwResult - Result code (set to 0)\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Early exit if g_dwPostGameRenderMode is 0 (not in active game)\n- ProcessUIInteractionCommand only called if pGameContext->placeholder == 0\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x10 - Processing state for clear selection message\n5 - Action type for clear selection in ProcessUIInteractionCommand",
