      "instructions": ["0x8720|MOV|EAX, [0x6fbe926c]", "0x8725|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0x8727|JZ|0x6fad878c", "0x8729|PUSH|ESI", "0x872A|PUSH|EDI", "0x872B|MOV|EDI, dword ptr [ESP + 0xc]", "0x872F|MOV|ESI, dword ptr [0x6fbe92cc]", "0x8735|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [EDI + 0x8]", "0x8738|SHR|EAX, 0x10", "0x873B|MOVSX|ECX, AX", "0x873E|ADD|ESI, ECX", "0x8740|MOV|EAX, ESI", "0x8742|MOV|dword ptr [0x6fbe92cc], ESI", "0x8748|CDQ|", "0x8749|XOR|EAX, EDX"],
      "comment": "Process mouse wheel input event and dispatch accumulated scroll to handlers.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if post-game render mode is active (g_dwPostGameRenderMode != 0)\n2. If inactive, return early without processing\n3. Extract signed wheel delta from high word of message lParam (dwMessageParam + 8)\n4. Accumulate delta into global wheel accumulator (g_nMouseWheelAccumulator)\n5. Calculate absolute value of accumulated delta for threshold comparison\n6. If absolute accumulated value exceeds threshold (0x77 = 119 ticks):\n   a. Compute wheel notches by dividing accumulator by 0x78 (120 ticks per notch)\n   b. Call DispatchMouseWheelEvent with computed notch count\n   c. Reset accumulator to zero\n7. Mark message as processed by setting flags at offsets +0x18 and +0x1c\n8. Insert processed event into cache via InsertCacheNodeWithCookie\n\nParameters:\ndwMessageParam (uint) - Pointer to Windows message structure containing wheel data.\n  Offset +0x08: High word contains signed wheel delta (HIWORD of wParam)\n  Offset +0x18: Processed flag (set to 1)\n  Offset +0x1c: Error/status flag (set to 0)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If g_dwPostGameRenderMode is 0, function exits without processing (not in game)\n- Wheel delta accumulates until threshold reached, allowing smooth scrolling\n- Division by 0x78 converts raw delta ticks to logical wheel notches\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x10 (16) - Bit shift to extract high word from dword\n0x77 (119) - Threshold for accumulated wheel delta (one less than notch size)\n0x78 (120) - Wheel ticks per logical notch (WHEEL_DELTA standard value)\n0x1f (31) - Bit shift for sign extension in absolute value calculation\n0x88888889 - Magic number for signed division by 120 optimization",
