      "comment": "ProcessExtendedMouseButtonUp - Handles Mouse4/Mouse5 button release events\n\nCallback/Handler function that processes extended mouse button (Mouse4/Mouse5) \nrelease events when post-game rendering is active.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if g_dwPostGameRenderMode is non-zero (post-game rendering active)\n2. If zero, exit early without processing\n3. Extract button type from high word of pUiMessage[2] (offset +0x8)\n4. If button type == 1: invoke Mouse4 lift callback\n5. Else if button type == 2: invoke Mouse5 lift callback\n6. Set pUiMessage[6] (offset +0x18) = 1 (mark as processed)\n7. Set pUiMessage[7] (offset +0x1c) = 0 (clear cookie/state)\n8. Call InsertCacheNodeWithCookie to requeue message for cache processing\n\nParameters:\n  pUiMessage - Pointer to UI message structure containing:\n               [2] (+0x8): Button type in high word (1=Mouse4, 2=Mouse5)\n               [6] (+0x18): Processed flag (set to 1 on completion)\n               [7] (+0x1c): Cookie/state value (cleared to 0)\n\nReturns: void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Early exit if g_dwPostGameRenderMode == 0 (not in post-game mode)\n- Only processes button types 1 (Mouse4) and 2 (Mouse5)\n- Other button types still get cached but no callback is invoked\n\nRelated Functions:\n- ProcessExtendedMouseButtonDown (0x6fad87f0) - handles button press\n- InvokeMouse4LiftCallback (0x6fafd930) - Mouse4 release handler\n- InvokeMouse5LiftCallback (0x6fafd9b0) - Mouse5 release handler\n- InsertCacheNodeWithCookie - message queue management\n\nGlobal State:\n- g_dwPostGameRenderMode (0x6fbe926c): Controls post-game rendering state",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Inventory", "PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_1", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
