      "instructions": ["0x8890|PUSH|ESI", "0x8891|MOV|ESI, dword ptr [ESP + 0x8]", "0x8895|MOV|AX, word ptr [ESI + 0x8]", "0x8899|AND|EAX, 0xfff0", "0x889E|CMP|AX, 0xf130", "0x88A2|JZ|0x6fad88b9", "0x88A4|CMP|AX, 0xf100", "0x88A8|JZ|0x6fad88b9", "0x88AA|CMP|AX, 0xf010", "0x88AE|JNZ|0x6fad88cd", "0x88B0|CALL|0x6fb99298", "0x88B5|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0x88B7|JZ|0x6fad88cd", "0x88B9|PUSH|ESI", "0x88BA|MOV|dword ptr [ESI + 0x18], 0x1"],
      "comment": "Registers a UI element for cache insertion if it matches valid cacheable types.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract element type code from offset +0x08 (mask upper 12 bits with 0xFFF0)\n2. Check if type is 0xF130 (scrollable panel) or 0xF100 (static panel) - register directly\n3. If type is 0xF010 (conditional panel), call Ordinal_10028 to validate registration eligibility\n4. If Ordinal_10028 returns zero, element is not cacheable - abort\n5. Set cache state at offset +0x18 to 1 (mark as registered)\n6. Set cache cookie at offset +0x1c to 0 (initial cookie value)\n7. Call InsertCacheNodeWithCookie to add element to UI cache\n\nParameters:\n  pUIElement (void*) - Pointer to UI element structure with type code at +0x08\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value; element is inserted into cache if valid\n\nUI Element Type Codes (masked with 0xFFF0):\n  0xF130 - Scrollable panel (directly cacheable)\n  0xF100 - Static panel (directly cacheable)\n  0xF010 - Conditional panel (requires Ordinal_10028 validation)\n  Other  - Not cacheable, function returns early\n\nStructure Layout (UI Element):\n  Offset  Size  Field           Description\n  +0x08   2     wTypeCode       UI element type identifier\n  +0x18   4     dwCacheState    1=registered in cache, 0=not registered\n  +0x1c   4     dwCacheCookie   Cache node cookie value (set to 0 on registration)\n\nCallers:\n  Called from 90+ locations including mouse input handlers, dialog processing,\n  automap rendering, quest UI, and viewport validation functions.",
