      "comment": "Processes keyboard state and manages global flags for game state control.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if context state flag is set at offset +8\n2. If state flag set, perform cleanup sequence and reset global state flag\n3. Check for keyboard configuration key (0x22) availability using FUN_6fafe710\n4. If key available, get virtual key code with FUN_6fafe370 and test async key state\n5. Clear global state if key not currently pressed (no high bit 0x8000)\n6. Handle first global state condition block when value != 0x10\n7. Set various global flags and call processing functions\n8. Build flag combination based on global state conditions (flags 0x8 and 0x4)\n9. Call graphics/display functions with calculated flag parameter\n10. Handle second global state condition block when different value != 0x10\n11. Initialize different global settings and call ordinal handler if needed\n12. Set context completion status to 0 before function exit\n\nParameters:\npContext - Pointer to KeyboardStateContext structure containing state information\n  Field at +0x8: State flag indicator (triggers cleanup sequence if non-zero)\n  Field at +0x18: Completion status field (set to 0 on normal exit)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Function does not return a value, operates through side effects on global state\n\nSpecial Cases:\nEarly return occurs if state flag at pContext+8 is non-zero, bypassing normal processing\nMultiple global state variables are managed based on configuration and key state\nFunction coordinates between keyboard input and display/graphics subsystems\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x22 (34) - Virtual key configuration identifier passed to lookup functions\n0x10 (16) - Global state threshold value for condition checks\n0x8000 - Async key state high bit mask indicating key currently pressed\n0x8 (8) - Global state flag value for state accumulation\n0x4 (4) - Additional state flag OR mask for extended conditions\n0xd (13) - Error/cleanup function parameter for state reset\n0x