      "comment": "Initializes post-game UI by processing UI states and calculating window borders.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if post-game render mode is active (g_dwPostGameRenderMode != 0)\n2. If not active, exit early\n3. Call ProcessUIStatesByResourceBuffer(0, 1) to query UI resource state\n4. If UI state query returns non-zero (busy/error), exit early\n5. Call CalculateWindowBorders(0) to reset window border calculations\n6. Call ProcessUIStatesByResourceBuffer(1, 0) to apply UI state changes\n7. Return via tail-call to ProcessUIStatesByResourceBuffer\n\nClassification: Initialization function - sets up post-game UI state\n\nParameters: None (void)\n\nReturns: void (no return value)\n\nPhantom Variables:\n- dVar1 (dwUIStateResult): SSA temporary for EAX return from ProcessUIStatesByResourceBuffer\n\nControl Flow:\n- Entry at 0x6fad8a40: Load g_dwPostGameRenderMode\n- Early exit at 0x6fad8a6c if render mode is 0\n- Early exit at 0x6fad8a6c if first UI state call returns non-zero\n- Tail-call exit at 0x6fad8a67 via JMP to ProcessUIStatesByResourceBuffer\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Uses tail-call optimization: final call to ProcessUIStatesByResourceBuffer is via JMP not CALL\n- Function has no callers - likely called via function pointer table or registered callback\n\nCallees:\n- ProcessUIStatesByResourceBuffer(nForceProcess, dwUIId) at 0x6fb5d910\n- CalculateWindowBorders(nEnable) at 0x6faf5730\n\nGlobals Accessed:\n- g_dwPostGameRenderMode (0x6fbe926c) - READ - Controls post-game rendering mode",
