      "api_calls": ["GfxUpdateWindowVisibility", "GetUnitLevel", "GetUnitX", "GetRoomStatBytes", "GfxInterface_CallMethod0x78", "GetEntityField", "GetLevelDataEntry", "FogAssert", "RenderScene", "ProcessPaletteCleanup", "...+4 more"],
      "instructions": ["0x8E60|SUB|ESP, 0x24", "0x8E63|PUSH|EDI", "0x8E64|MOV|EDI, ECX", "0x8E66|CALL|0x6fb5e890", "0x8E6B|CALL|0x6fb992c2", "0x8E70|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0x8E72|JNZ|0x6fad9060", "0x8E78|PUSH|ESI", "0x8E79|CALL|0x6fb62880", "0x8E7E|MOV|ESI, EAX", "0x8E80|LEA|EAX, [ESP + 0x28]", "0x8E84|LEA|ECX, [ESP + 0x24]", "0x8E88|PUSH|EAX", "0x8E89|LEA|EDX, [ESP + 0x24]", "0x8E8D|PUSH|ECX"],
      "comment": "Main game frame rendering loop - processes complete frame update and scene rendering.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize game engine state and check if game update pending (Ordinal_10026)\n2. If no pending update, early exit\n3. Get game context (player unit) and extract viewport coordinate rectangle\n4. Get unit level (Y coord) and unit X position\n5. Calculate camera position centered on unit: camera = unitPos - (rectSize / 2)\n6. Apply screen shake offset to camera coordinates\n7. If previous camera position was valid (!= -1), calculate camera delta for scrolling\n8. Store current camera as previous for next frame\n9. Update configuration values with new camera position\n10. Update scroll view state (no animation)\n11. Process game frame update (game logic tick)\n12. Get room stat bytes for RGB palette adjustment\n13. Call Ordinal_10050 (unknown palette operation)\n14. Get unit stat from game context for level data lookup\n15. If unit exists, get entity field and lookup level data entry\n16. Assert level data exists or fatal exit with code -1\n17. Get render data pointer from level data offset +700\n18. Render scene with level render data\n19. If rendering succeeded (extraout_EAX_00 != 0):\n    a. Process palette cleanup\n    b. Update viewport position\n    c. If scroll mode != 3, process main rendering pipeline\n    d. Process game state and render frame\n    e. Render composite unit frames\n    f. NoOperation (placeholder/timing)\n    g. If not skipping screen resources, draw them\n    h. Log performance statistics\n    i. Handle graphics overwrite counter with error logging\n    j. Initialize graphics interface for next frame\n\nParameters:\n  nSkipScreenResources (ECX) - If non-zero, skips ProcessScreenResourceDrawing call\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Previous camera position of -1 indicates first frame (no delta calculation)\n  - Scroll mode 3 bypasses main rendering pipeline\n  - Graphics overwrite counter going negative triggers error message and reset\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x5ea (1514) - Source line number for level data assertion\n  700 (0x2BC) - Offset to render data pointer in level data structure\n  0xffffffff (-1) - Invalid/uninitialized camera position marker\n  3 - Scroll window mode that skips main rendering pipeline\n\nGlobals Modified:\n  g_nPreviousCameraX (0x6fbaf87c) - Previous frame camera X position\n  g_nPreviousCameraY (0x6fbaf880) - Previous frame camera Y position\n  g_nCameraDeltaX (0x6fbe92d8) - Camera X movement since last frame\n  g_nCameraDeltaY (0x6fbe92dc) - Camera Y movement since last frame\n  g_nGfxOverwriteCounter (0x6fbaf7b0) - Graphics overwrite error counter",
      "tags": ["SRC_Game.cpp", "PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_1", "STRUCT_Other", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "MOD_GAME", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
