      "instructions": ["0x9230|PUSH|ESI", "0x9231|CALL|dword ptr [0x6fba6098]", "0x9237|MOV|ESI, EAX", "0x9239|MOV|EAX, [0x6fbe906c]", "0x923E|CMP|EAX, ESI", "0x9240|JNC|0x6fad9275", "0x9242|CALL|0x6fadcc70", "0x9247|MOV|EAX, [0x6fbdc250]", "0x924C|MOV|dword ptr [0x6fbe9070], ESI", "0x9252|TEST|byte ptr [EAX + 0x1ea], 0x4", "0x9259|JZ|0x6fad9269", "0x925B|ADD|ESI, 0x1388", "0x9261|MOV|dword ptr [0x6fbe906c], ESI", "0x9267|POP|ESI", "0x9268|RET|"],
      "comment": "Updates loading screen timer and triggers background updates when timeout expires.\n\nAlgorithm:\n\n1. Get current system tick count from GetTickCount API\n2. Compare current tick against stored timer threshold (DAT_6fbe906c)\n3. If threshold not reached, return early without action\n4. Call FUN_6fadcc70() to perform background update operation\n5. Update last tick timestamp (_DAT_6fbe9070) to current tick\n6. Check video playback state flags in global structure at offset 0x1ea\n7. Test bit 4 (0x04) to determine if video is currently playing\n8. If video playing: Set next timeout to current tick + 5000ms (5 seconds)\n9. If no video: Set next timeout to current tick + 15000ms (15 seconds)\n\nParameters:\n\nNone (void function)\n\nReturns:\n\nNone (void function)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n\n- Function uses different timeout intervals based on video playback state\n- Timer comparison uses unsigned arithmetic to handle tick rollover\n- Background update always called when timer expires regardless of video state\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n\n0x1ea (490) - Offset to video state flags in global video structure\n0x04 - Bit mask for video playback active flag  \n5000 - Short timeout interval in milliseconds (5 seconds) for video playback\n15000 - Long timeout interval in milliseconds (15 seconds) for normal operation\n\nError Handling:\n\nNo explicit error handling - relies on API and callee error handling",
