      "comment": "Updates performance metrics from timing data structure and calculates running average.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Copy 8 DWORDs (32 bytes) from pTimingData+4 to global metrics array (g_adTimingMetrics)\n2. Store current tick count in g_dwLastTickCount (offset 0x10 within metrics array)\n3. Calculate elapsed time since last reference tick (GetTickCount - DAT_6fbe9070)\n4. Store elapsed time in g_dwMovementRange for movement calculations\n5. If sample count less than 10, update running average:\n   - Compute weighted sum: previous_average * sample_count\n   - Add current elapsed time to weighted sum\n   - Increment sample count\n   - Divide by new sample count to get updated average\n   - Store in g_dwMetricsCounter\n\nParameters:\npTimingData (ECX) - Pointer to timing data structure; data copied from offset +4\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Running average only updated for first 10 samples (stabilization period)\n- After 10 samples, g_dwMetricsCounter maintains final average value\n- g_dwMovementRange always updated regardless of sample count\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x6fbe90a4 - Start of global timing metrics array (g_adTimingMetrics)\n0x6fbe90c4 - End of metrics array (32 bytes / 8 DWORDs)\n0x6fbe90b4 - Offset 0x10 within array for last tick timestamp\n10 (0x0a) - Maximum sample count for running average calculation\nDAT_6fbe9070 - Reference tick count (set by UpdateLoadingScreenTimer)",
