      "comment": "Main game frame processing tick - core game loop function.\n\nHandles a single frame tick of the game, including UI interaction,\nnetwork packet processing, game entity updates, and performance monitoring.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get game context and check server port mode (0=singleplayer, 1=TCP/IP)\n2. For local modes, check if processing should skip (Ordinal_10026)\n3. If UI resource buffers active with valid context, update frame and return early\n4. Process message log records\n5. Handle left-click targeting if enabled (ProcessUIInteractionCommand mode 1)\n6. Handle right-click UI commands if pending (ProcessUIInteractionCommand mode 4)\n7. Check Shift key state (VK_SHIFT=0x10) for global state flag\n8. Send periodic metrics packet every 15s (or 5s in video mode)\n9. Update global status timestamp\n10. Calculate performance metrics every 3000ms (frame rate averaging)\n11. Check if frame interval elapsed, process skill target actions if ready\n12. Process network I/O:\n    - Ordinal_10003/10004/10005: Network state management\n    - Ordinal_10008 loop: Read game commands until -1\n    - Ordinal_10007 loop: Read game packets until -1\n13. Process Battle.net channel join\n14. For non-local modes: Handle timeout disconnection (30s, 180s thresholds)\n15. If game rendering active:\n    - Iterate all rooms in act (linked via +0x7C offset)\n    - For unprocessed rooms (flag +0x48 bit 0 clear):\n      ProcessUnitSpawnSlots, AllocateUnitCopiesFromTemplate, ProcessRoomValidation\n    - DeactivateAllUnits, GetUnitSlotStates, ProcessGraphicsFrameUpdate\n    - InitializeEntitySlots, UpdateRoomAnimationState\n    - ProcessAllMissilesAndItems if room updated\n    - ProcessUnitStateTimeout, UpdateClientNodeFromCursor\n    - Increment frame counter, every 13th frame call GetUnitOrderTarget\n16. Adjust frame timing based on elapsed time vs interval\n17. Process audio if valid (Ordinal_10029/10031, SetSoundVolume)\n18. Render frame via g_pActivePointer callback\n19. If game system enabled: ComparePaletteBuffers, ProcessUIStatesByResourceBuffer\n20. For port 6/8: Signal thread sync via critical section\n\nClassification: Main Loop/Worker Function\nCaller: Called from main game thread (1 xref at 6fadacea)\n\nParameters: None (uses globals for game state)\n\nReturns: void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Early return if Ordinal_10026 returns non-zero (processing blocked)\n- Early return if UI buffers active with valid game context\n- Frame skipping logic when performance degrades (g_dwFrameSkipCounter)\n- Timeout handling for network modes (7,9=Battle.net disconnect after 30s idle)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x10: VK_SHIFT virtual key code\n- 0xd (13): Frame counter modulus for periodic unit order checks\n- 0xbb8 (3000): Performance sample interval in milliseconds\n- 0x3a98 (15000): Normal metrics send interval\n- 0x1388 (5000): Video mode metrics interval\n- 0x7530 (30000): Battle.net idle timeout\n- 0x2bf20 (180000): Palette check timeout\n- 0x258 (600): Loading screen countdown frames\n- 0x2710 (10000): Thread wait timeout\n\nError Handling:\n- Returns silently on blocked processing or early context checks\n- Network packet loops terminate on -1 return value\n- Thread sync uses 10 second timeout",
      "tags": ["PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_0", "PROP_LOOPHEAVY", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
