      "comment": "Main server monitoring thread that handles connection state and video playback transitions.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize server status and playback state variables to 0\n2. Enter infinite monitoring loop\n3. Acquire critical section lock on server state data (0x6fbe90d0)\n4. Read shutdown signal (DAT_6fbe92a4) and active connection flag (DAT_6fbe92a0)\n5. Release critical section lock\n6. If active connection flag set, execute shutdown sequence:\n   - Call Ordinal_10006() for cleanup\n   - Call Ordinal_10005(0,1) to signal shutdown completion\n   - Delete critical section\n   - Output \"Open server thread shut down\" debug message\n   - Return 1 (success)\n7. If no shutdown signal, enter server polling loop:\n   - Call Ordinal_10003() for server maintenance\n   - Get server status using Ordinal_10004(0)\n   - If server status non-zero, call Ordinal_10005(0,0) and break\n   - Sleep 10ms and continue polling\n8. If server status still zero, sleep 10ms and retry server polling\n9. Sleep 30ms (0x1e) before game interface check\n10. Get game interface pointer via GetGameInterface()\n11. If game interface valid, get current playback state via Ordinal_10016(1)\n12. If playback state changed, handle state transition:\n    - If current state < threshold (DAT_6fbaf8bc) and new state >= threshold:\n      Call interface method at offset +0x9c (likely stop/pause playback)\n    - If current state >= threshold and new state < threshold:\n      Call interface method at offset +0x34 with video data pointer (g_dwVideoPlaybackState + 0x255)\n13. Update current playback state and continue monitoring loop\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\n1 - Success (shutdown sequence completed)\nNever returns during normal operation (infinite loop)\n\nSpecial Cases:\nSleep intervals: 10ms for server polling, 30ms for game interface checks\nCritical section protects concurrent access to server state variables\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x6fbe90d0 - Critical section for server state synchronization\n0x6fbe92a4 - Shutdown signal flag (DAT_6fbe92a4)\n0x6fbe92a0 - Active connection flag (DAT_6fbe92a0)\n0x1e (30) - Game interface polling interval in milliseconds\n0xa (10) - Server status polling interval in milliseconds\nDAT_6fbaf8bc - Video playback state threshold for transitions\n+0x9c - Game interface method offset (stop/pause playback)\n+0x34 - Game interface method offset (start/resume playback)\n0x255 - Video data offset from g_dwVideoPlaybackState base\n\nError Handling:\nFunction handles server shutdown gracefully via critical section protection\nNo explicit error returns during normal monitoring operation\n\nStructure Layout:\nGameInterface vtable structure (160 bytes total):\nOffset | Size | Field Name    | Type  | Description\n0x00   | 4    | vtable        | void* | Virtual function table pointer\n0x04   | 48   | reserved1     | byte  | Reserved/unknown data\n0x34   | 4    | pfnMethod34   | void* | Start/resume playback method\n0x38   | 100  | reserved2     | byte  | Reserved/unknown data  \n0x9C   | 4    | pfnMethod9C   | void* | Stop/pause playback method",
      "tags": ["PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_0", "PROP_LOOPHEAVY"]
