      "comment": "Increments the global screen index counter and inserts a cache node into the cache system.\n\nClassification: Initialization/Wrapper function\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Read current screen index from g_byCurrentScreenIndex\n2. Increment screen index by 1\n3. Write updated index back to g_byCurrentScreenIndex\n4. Set cache node active flag at offset +0x18 to 1 (initialized)\n5. Clear cache node cookie/link field at offset +0x1c to 0\n6. Call InsertCacheNodeWithCookie to insert node into cache linked list\n\nParameters:\n  pCacheNode (void *) - Pointer to cache node structure to initialize and insert\n    Structure layout (partial):\n      Offset  Size  Field          Description\n      +0x18   4     dwActiveFlag   Set to 1 to mark node as active/initialized\n      +0x1c   4     dwCookie       Cleared to 0 before insertion\n\nReturns: void\n\nGlobal Variables:\n  g_byCurrentScreenIndex (byte at 0x6fbe9294) - Current screen/slide index counter\n    Used by slideshow/beta screen system to track which screen is being displayed\n    Incremented each time a new cache node is inserted\n\nCalled Functions:\n  InsertCacheNodeWithCookie - Thunk to external cache insertion routine (via IAT jump at 0x6fba6194)\n\nRelated Functions:\n  InitAndInsertCacheNode (0x6fad88e0) - Similar but does NOT increment screen index\n  FUN_6fad9d20 - Main slideshow handler that reads g_byCurrentScreenIndex",
