      "comment": "Conditionally increments the global screen index and inserts a cache node into the cache system.\n\nClassification: Initialization/Wrapper function (variant of IncrementScreenIndexAndInsertCacheNode)\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load pCacheNode pointer from stack parameter\n2. Test flag field at offset +0xc for bit 0x40000000 (CACHE_FLAG_SKIP_INDEX)\n3. If flag NOT set (bit clear), increment g_byCurrentScreenIndex by 1\n4. Set cache node active flag at offset +0x18 to 1 (initialized)\n5. Clear cache node cookie/link field at offset +0x1c to 0\n6. Call InsertCacheNodeWithCookie to insert node into cache linked list\n\nParameters:\n  pCacheNode (void *) - Pointer to cache node structure to initialize and insert\n    Structure layout (partial):\n      Offset  Size  Field              Description\n      +0x0c   4     dwFlags            Flag field, bit 30 (0x40000000) = skip screen index increment\n      +0x18   4     dwActiveFlag       Set to 1 to mark node as active/initialized\n      +0x1c   4     dwCookie           Cleared to 0 before insertion\n\nReturns: void\n\nFlag Bits:\n  0x40000000 (bit 30) at +0xc - CACHE_FLAG_SKIP_INDEX\n    When SET: Do not increment g_byCurrentScreenIndex (node is being reinserted/recycled)\n    When CLEAR: Increment screen index (new node being added)\n\nGlobal Variables:\n  g_byCurrentScreenIndex (byte at 0x6fbe9294) - Current screen/slide index counter\n    Conditionally incremented based on cache node flag state\n\nRelated Functions:\n  IncrementScreenIndexAndInsertCacheNode (0x6fad9cb0) - Always increments screen index\n  FUN_6fad9d20 - Main slideshow handler that reads g_byCurrentScreenIndex",
      "tags": ["PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_1", "STRUCT_Control", "PROP_SMALL", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
