      "api_count": 11,
      "api_calls": ["GfxUpdateWindowVisibility", "RenderScene", "ComparePaletteBuffers", "GfxInterfaceCall84", "GfxInterfaceCall84", "GfxInterfaceCall84", "GfxInterfaceCall84", "GfxInterfaceCall84", "GfxInterfaceCall84", "GfxInitializeInterface", "...+1 more"],
      "instructions": ["0x9D20|SUB|ESP, 0x14c", "0x9D26|PUSH|EBX", "0x9D27|PUSH|EBP", "0x9D28|PUSH|ESI", "0x9D29|PUSH|EDI", "0x9D2A|CALL|0x6fb992c2", "0x9D2F|MOV|EBP, dword ptr [0x6fba6098]", "0x9D35|XOR|EBX, EBX", "0x9D37|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0x9D39|JNZ|0x6fad9ebf", "0x9D3F|PUSH|EBX", "0x9D40|PUSH|EBX", "0x9D41|PUSH|EBX", "0x9D42|PUSH|0x1", "0x9D44|CALL|0x6fb992b6"],
      "comment": "Processes and displays beta screen slideshow images in a tiled 3x2 grid pattern.\n\nClassification: Callback/Handler - Called by ProcessMessagePumpWithCallback during slideshow mode.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call Ordinal_10026 to check game state; if non-zero, skip rendering\n2. Call RenderScene with g_InvalidTooltipMarker; if render fails, return early\n3. Get current screen index from g_dwCurrentScreenIndex (masked to byte)\n4. If index < g_nBetaScreenCount, check if texture already loaded\n5. If texture not loaded, build path \"%s\\ui\\betascreens\\%s\" and load via ConcatenatePathAndWriteFile\n6. Store texture handle in g_anScreenTextureHandles[index * 4]\n7. Store timestamp from GetTickCount in g_adwScreenTimestamps[index * 4]\n8. Call ComparePaletteBuffers to sync palette\n9. Initialize 18-DWORD render params array to zero\n10. Set params[1] = texture handle, params[2] = tile index, params[3] = 0\n11. Render 6 tiles in 3x2 grid pattern via GfxInterfaceCall84:\n    - Tiles 0-2: Y=0x100, X=0x000/0x100/0x200 (top row)\n    - Tiles 3-5: Y=0x1E0, X=0x000/0x100/0x200 (bottom row)\n12. Call GfxInitializeInterface to finalize\n13. Check timeout: if index >= count OR timestamp + 10000ms < current tick, advance\n14. Increment screen index; if all screens shown, cleanup loop:\n    - For each screen with texture, call ReportValidationError to free\n    - Clear texture handle and timestamp\n15. Log \"slide show end\" and call SetGlobalState(0) to exit slideshow\n\nParameters: None (void)\n\nReturns: void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- 10000ms (10 second) display duration per screen\n- Screen array uses 16-byte stride (4 DWORDs per entry)\n- Grid rendering uses 256-pixel (0x100) tile width\n- Top row at Y=0x100 (256), bottom row at Y=0x1E0 (480)\n\nGlobal Data:\n- g_dwCurrentScreenIndex (0x6FBE9294): Current slideshow position (byte)\n- g_nBetaScreenCount (0x6FBAF7A0): Total screens to display (10)\n- g_anScreenTextureHandles (0x6FBAF704): Array of loaded texture handles\n- g_adwScreenTimestamps (0x6FBAF700): Array of display start times\n- g_apszScreenFilenames (0x6FBAF70C): Array of screen filename pointers\n\nOrdinal Calls:\n- Ordinal_10026: D2Gfx.GetGameState - Check rendering state",
      "tags": ["PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Path", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_0"]
    },
