      "comment": "Validates if current resource position is within center screen region and inserts cache node.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate screen bounds: bottom = screenHeight - 0x50, centerX = screenWidth / 2\n2. Get current resource X position via GetCurrentResourceID()\n3. Get current resource Y position via GetResourceFlags()\n4. Check if resource X is within centerX +/- 0x30 (96 pixel horizontal tolerance)\n5. Check if resource Y is within (screenHeight - 0x70) to (screenHeight - 0x50)\n6. If within center region: set g_fResourceInCenterRegion = 1\n7. Clear targeting state: g_fTargetingEnabled, g_dwUICommandResult, g_fTargetingActive, g_dwUICommandPending all set to 0\n8. Set cache node fields: pCacheNode[6] = 1 (offset 0x18), pCacheNode[7] = 0 (offset 0x1C)\n9. Call InsertCacheNodeWithCookie to add node to cache\n\nParameters:\npCacheNode - Pointer to cache node structure (uint *). Fields at offset 0x18 and 0x1C are modified.\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If resource is outside center region, targeting state is still cleared and cache insert occurs\n- Only difference is g_fResourceInCenterRegion flag is not set when outside region\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x30 (48) - Horizontal tolerance from center (total 96 pixel width)\n0x50 (80) - Bottom margin from screen height\n0x70 (112) - Top margin for Y validation region\n0x18 (24) - Offset to cache node validation flag\n0x1C (28) - Offset to cache node status field",
