      "instructions": ["0xA030|MOV|EAX, [0x6fbae0e8]", "0xA035|PUSH|EBX", "0xA036|PUSH|EBP", "0xA037|PUSH|ESI", "0xA038|LEA|EBX, [EAX + -0x50]", "0xA03B|MOV|EAX, [0x6fbae0e4]", "0xA040|CDQ|", "0xA041|SUB|EAX, EDX", "0xA043|XOR|EBP, EBP", "0xA045|MOV|ESI, EAX", "0xA047|PUSH|EDI", "0xA048|SAR|ESI, 0x1", "0xA04A|MOV|dword ptr [0x6fbe92e4], EBP", "0xA050|SUB|ESI, 0x30", "0xA053|CALL|0x6fb8f680"],
      "comment": "Validates if current resource position is within the screen center region and updates cache node.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get screen height and calculate bottom bound (screenHeight - 0x50 = 80 pixels from bottom)\n2. Calculate horizontal center (screenWidth / 2)\n3. Clear g_fResourceInCenterRegion flag to 0\n4. Get current resource X position via GetCurrentResourceID()\n5. Get current resource Y position via GetResourceFlags()\n6. Check if X is within center region: (centerX - 0x30) <= X <= (centerX + 0x30) (96 pixel range)\n7. Check if Y is within bottom region: (screenHeight - 0x70) <= Y <= (screenHeight - 0x50)\n8. If resource is within bounds:\n   a. Set g_fResourcePositionValid = 1\n   b. Set pCacheNode+0x18 = 1 (processed flag)\n   c. Set pCacheNode+0x1c = 0 (result code)\n   d. Insert cache node via InsertCacheNodeWithCookie\n9. If resource is outside bounds:\n   a. Clear targeting globals: g_fTargetingEnabled, g_dwUICommandResult\n   b. Clear active targeting: g_fTargetingActive, g_dwUICommandPending\n   c. Set pCacheNode+0x18 = 1 and pCacheNode+0x1c = 0\n   d. Insert cache node\n\nParameters:\n  pCacheNode - Pointer to cache node structure with fields at +0x18 (processed) and +0x1c (result)\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value. Updates globals and cache node state.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  Function has no direct callers - likely invoked via function pointer table\n  Screen center region is 96x32 pixels near bottom center of screen\n  Clearing targeting state when outside bounds prevents stale targeting\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x30 = 48 pixels - half-width of center region\n  0x50 = 80 pixels - upper Y bound offset from screen bottom\n  0x60 = 96 pixels - full width of center region\n  0x70 = 112 pixels - lower Y bound offset from screen bottom\n  0x18 = cache node processed flag offset\n  0x1c = cache node result code offset",
