      "instructions": ["0xA0D0|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [ESP + 0x4]", "0xA0D4|MOV|ECX, 0x1", "0xA0D9|TEST|dword ptr [EAX + 0xc], 0x40000000", "0xA0E0|JNZ|0x6fada0e8", "0xA0E2|MOV|dword ptr [0x6fbe9258], ECX", "0xA0E8|PUSH|EAX", "0xA0E9|MOV|dword ptr [EAX + 0x18], ECX", "0xA0EC|MOV|dword ptr [EAX + 0x1c], 0x0", "0xA0F3|CALL|0x6fb99c36", "0xA0F8|RET|0x4"],
      "comment": "Marks a cache node as active and inserts it into the cache system.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load cache node pointer from stack parameter\n2. Check if cache node flags (offset +0x0C) has bit 0x40000000 clear\n3. If bit clear, set g_fResourcePositionValid flag to 1 (resource position is valid)\n4. Set cache node active flag (offset +0x18) to 1\n5. Clear cache node pending field (offset +0x1C) to 0\n6. Call InsertCacheNodeWithCookie to add node to cache\n7. Return to caller (stdcall cleans 4 bytes from stack)\n\nParameters:\npCacheNode (CacheNode*) - Pointer to cache node structure to mark and insert\n  Offset +0x0C: dwFlags - Node flags (bit 0x40000000 = external position management)\n  Offset +0x18: fActive - Active status flag (set to 1)\n  Offset +0x1C: dwPending - Pending operation counter (cleared to 0)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\nFlag Bit 0x40000000 - When set in dwFlags, indicates resource position is managed\n  externally so g_fResourcePositionValid is not updated. When clear, this function\n  takes ownership of position validation by setting the global flag to 1.",
