      "api_count": 48,
      "api_calls": ["GfxUpdateWindowVisibility", "RenderScene", "InitActPalette", "ProcessPaletteCleanup", "GfxInterfaceCall84", "GfxInterfaceCall84", "GfxInterfaceCall84", "GfxInterfaceCall84", "GfxInterfaceCall84", "GfxInterfaceCall84", "...+38 more"],
      "instructions": ["0xA130|SUB|ESP, 0x528", "0xA136|PUSH|EBX", "0xA137|PUSH|EBP", "0xA138|CALL|0x6fb992c2", "0xA13D|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0xA13F|JNZ|0x6fada973", "0xA145|XOR|EBX, EBX", "0xA147|MOV|EBP, 0x1", "0xA14C|PUSH|EBX", "0xA14D|PUSH|EBX", "0xA14E|PUSH|EBX", "0xA14F|PUSH|EBP", "0xA150|CALL|0x6fb992b6", "0xA155|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0xA157|JZ|0x6fada9be"],
      "comment": "Renders the endgame victory/completion screen with character title and credits.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if video playback is active via Ordinal_10026; if so, skip to cleanup\n2. Call RenderScene to initialize the scene; if fails, return early\n3. If background not loaded (g_pEndgameBackground == 0):\n   a. Select background filename based on g_bCurrentFrameIndex (endgame vs endgame2)\n   b. Copy filename to local buffer using strcpy pattern\n   c. Format UI menu path and load via ConcatenatePathAndWriteFile\n   d. Store loaded asset handle in g_pEndgameBackground\n   e. Load palette files (.dat and .pl2) via InitActPalette\n4. If OK button not loaded (g_pEndgameOkButton == 0):\n   a. Format endgameok UI path and load\n   b. Store handle in g_pEndgameOkButton\n5. Initialize 18-element render context array to zeros\n6. Set render context: [1]=background handle, [2]=frame index, [3]=0\n7. Call ProcessPaletteCleanup\n8. Render background tiles based on resolution:\n   - 640x480 mode (g_bCurrentFrameIndex==0): 8 tiles in 2x4 grid\n   - 800x600 mode: 12 tiles in 4x3 grid\n9. Set font to style 3 (credits font)\n10. Render string 0x13EA centered at Y=62 (640) or Y=100 (800)\n11. For 640x480 mode only: Render string 0x13EB at Y=107\n12. Render string 0x13EC at Y=232 (640) or Y=272 (800)\n13. Get video playback state and extract character name from offset 0xB8\n14. Convert character name to Unicode and render centered at Y=187\n15. Get difficulty flags from video state offset 0x1EA:\n    - Bit 0x04: Hardcore flag\n    - Bit 0x20: Expansion flag\n16. Calculate title tier based on g_byVideoFrameCount (0=Normal, 1=Nightmare, 2=Hell)\n17. Call CalculateCharacterTitleTier with difficulty params\n18. If title string returned, concatenate with character name and render at Y=277/357\n19. Set font to style 1 (button font)\n20. Render OK button at bottom center (Y = screenHeight - 80)\n21. Render string 0x13EE on OK button, adjust position if g_fResourceInCenterRegion\n22. Call ProcessScreenResourceDrawing and GfxInitializeInterface\n23. Cleanup phase (if g_fResourcePositionValid != 0):\n    a. Free g_pEndgameBackground via ReportValidationError\n    b. Free g_pEndgameOkButton via ReportValidationError\n    c. Call SetGlobalState(0) to reset state\n\nParameters: None (void function)\n\nReturns: void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Different tile layouts for 640x480 vs 800x600 resolutions\n- Title tier calculation differs by difficulty (Normal/NM/Hell)\n- Hardcore and Expansion flags affect title string\n- g_byVideoFrameCount determines difficulty: 0=Normal, 1=Nightmare, 2=Hell\n\nString IDs:\n- 0x13EA (5098): Main title text\n- 0x13EB (5099): Secondary title (640x480 only)\n- 0x13EC (5100): Third title text\n- 0x13EE (5102): OK button text\n\nGlobals Modified:\n- g_pEndgameBackground: Loaded background asset handle\n- g_pEndgameOkButton: Loaded OK button asset handle",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PROP_NOCALLER", "STRUCT_ItemData", "PARAM_0", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData", "PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Path", "STRUCT_Skill", "PROP_LOOPHEAVY", "UI_MENU"]
