      "comment": "Determines if remote session features should be enabled based on system state.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Query system metrics for remote session status using GetSystemMetrics(SM_REMOTESESSION)\n2. Validate remote session is active (non-zero return value)\n3. Check if remote session support is globally enabled (DAT_6fbe9298 != 0)\n4. Evaluate configuration mode from DAT_6fbe91c0:\n   - Mode 1: Return status based on DAT_6fbe91b8 boolean flag\n   - Mode 2: Return true if DAT_6fbe91b4 equals 4 or 5 (specific remote session types)\n   - Other modes: Return false\n5. Return false if any validation fails\n\nParameters:\n  None\n\nReturns:\n  bool: true if remote session features should be enabled\n        false if remote session not active, not supported, or invalid configuration\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x4b (75): SM_REMOTESESSION - GetSystemMetrics parameter for remote session detection\n  1: Primary remote session mode - uses DAT_6fbe91b8 flag\n  2: Secondary remote session mode - validates specific session types  \n  4: Valid remote session type identifier\n  5: Valid remote session type identifier\n\nGlobal Variables:\n  DAT_6fbe9298: Global remote session support enable flag\n  DAT_6fbe91c0: Remote session configuration mode selector\n  DAT_6fbe91b8: Primary mode boolean status flag\n  DAT_6fbe91b4: Secondary mode session type identifier",
