      "comment": "Determines if a remote session is currently active based on global session state variables.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if remote session functionality is enabled (g_dwRemoteSessionEnabled != 0)\n2. If session state is 1 (active), return true immediately \n3. If session state is 2 (conditional), check session type:\n   - Type 4 (0x4): Return true (active session)\n   - Type 5 (0x5): Return true (active session)\n   - Any other type: Return false\n4. If remote session disabled or other states, return false\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\nbool: true if remote session is active, false if inactive or disabled\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Magic Number 0x1: Session state indicating active remote session\n- Magic Number 0x2: Session state indicating conditional activation\n- Magic Number 0x4: Session type for standard remote session  \n- Magic Number 0x5: Session type for enhanced remote session\n- When g_dwRemoteSessionEnabled is 0, function always returns false regardless of other state\n\nGlobal Variables:\n- g_dwRemoteSessionEnabled (0x6fbe9298): Master enable flag for remote session functionality\n- g_dwSessionState (0x6fbe91c0): Current session state (1=active, 2=conditional, other=inactive)\n- g_dwSessionType (0x6fbe91b4): Session type identifier when state is conditional",
