      "comment": "Checks if current session is a valid remote desktop connection.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if remote session flag is enabled (g_dwRemoteSessionFlag != 0)\n2. Verify remote session state is not 1 (disconnected/invalid state)\n3. Confirm remote session state equals 2 (connected/active state)\n4. Validate session type is not 4 (invalid session type)\n5. Ensure session type equals 5 (valid remote desktop session type)\n6. Return 1 if all conditions met, 0 otherwise\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\n1 - Session is a valid remote desktop connection\n0 - Session is invalid, local, or wrong type\n\nSpecial Cases:\nRemote session validation requires all conditions to pass for positive result.\nAny single condition failure results in rejection.\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x1 (1 decimal) - Invalid/disconnected remote session state\n0x2 (2 decimal) - Valid/connected remote session state  \n0x4 (4 decimal) - Invalid session type identifier\n0x5 (5 decimal) - Valid remote desktop session type",
