      "comment": "Main game loop execution and shutdown sequence handler.\n\nOrchestrates the complete game session lifecycle: initialization, main loop execution,\nmessage pumping, and orderly shutdown with resource cleanup.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Save initial tick count for timing statistics\n2. Check global init flag (0x6fbe929c); if zero, call SetGlobalState(1)\n3. Store initial tick count via GetTickCount()\n4. Call GetVersionExA to populate OS version info at 0x6fbe91b0\n5. Set remote desktop flag (0x6fbe9298) based on OS version check\n6. Initialize exception handler and resource tracking systems\n7. Process compression objects with flag=0\n8. Get log level (0xa) and call InitializeExceptionHandler with log path\n9. Call GetGameState() to retrieve current state\n10. Branch on game state: if state is 3, 7, or 9 goto video playback mode\n11. For states 6 or 8: initialize critical section, create worker thread\n12. For states 3/7/9: call PlayVideoById with video ID from globals\n13. Process message arrays and initialize graphics/gouraud tables\n14. Check IsRemoteSessionActive and IsRemoteSessionHandlingReady\n15. Enter message pump loop: while (IsRemoteSessionHandlingReady()) { PeekMessageA loop }\n16. Process remote session cleanup if needed\n17. Submit telemetry log records with timing data\n18. Check game mode flags and queue appropriate log messages\n19. If main loop flag (0x6fbe9250) set, process main game loop\n20. If exit flag (0x6fbe9254) set, call SetGlobalState(5) then cleanup\n21. If reconnect flag (0x6fbe9278) set, call SetGlobalState(7), set reconnect pending\n22. If shutdown flag (0x6fbe927c) set, process shutdown with video mode checks\n23. Call GetSystemMetrics(0x4B) to check SM_REMOTESESSION for Remote Desktop\n24. Process video mode transitions based on OSVERSIONINFO fields\n25. Queue log messages based on game mode and video configuration\n26. Call cleanup functions: CleanupAllUnitTables, FreeUnitData, DestroyGameState\n27. Release pool allocations and destroy memory pools\n28. Free async data lists and audio context\n29. Clear unit tables and flush validation errors\n30. Log final timing statistics (total elapsed time)\n31. Return exit code 6\n\nParameters:\n  None - Function takes no parameters\n\nReturns:\n  int - Always returns 6 (normal shutdown exit code)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Remote Desktop session: Special handling via SM_REMOTESESSION check\n  - Video playback mode: Separate path for cinematic sequences\n  - Reconnect mode: Sets flags but doesn't immediately exit\n  - Error states: Logs errors before cleanup\n\nOrdinal Calls:\n  Ordinal_10006 (Storm.dll) - GetGlobalState - retrieves current global state value\n  Ordinal_10029 (Storm.dll) - SleepEx/Timer - delays execution for specified interval (180ms)\n\nPhantom Variables (decompiler artifacts, cannot be renamed):\n  extraout_var, extraout_var_00..03 - undefined3 implicit return bytes from bool functions\n  These represent high bytes of EAX after bool return calls via CONCAT31() pattern\n\nGlobal State Accessed:\n  0x6fbe929c - g_nLoadingScreenCountdown (init flag)\n  0x6fbe9298 - g_dwRemoteSessionEnabled (Remote Desktop flag)\n  0x6fbe9260 - g_dwServerPort (game state)\n  0x6fbe9250 - g_dwMainLoopActiveFlag (DAT_6fbe9250)\n  0x6fbe9254 - g_dwVideoFrameUpdateFlag (exit requested flag)\n  0x6fbe9278 - g_nCurrentVideoId (reconnect requested flag)\n  0x6fbe927c - g_fGameDifficultyResetDisabled (shutdown in progress flag)\n  0x6fbe91b0 - g_stOsVersionInfo (OSVERSIONINFO struct, 148 bytes)\n  0x6fbe91c0 - g_dwSessionState (OS platform ID)\n  0x6fbe91b4 - g_dwSessionType (OS minor version)\n  0x6fbe91b8 - g_dwRemoteSessionEnabled check field (OS major version)\n  0x6fbdc250 - g_dwVideoPlaybackState (video/graphics mode structure pointer)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x4B (75) - SM_REMOTESESSION - GetSystemMetrics parameter for Remote Desktop check\n  0x94 (148) - sizeof(OSVERSIONINFOA)\n  0xB4 (180) - Timer interval constant for Ordinal_10029\n  0x5a6 (1446) - Resource cleanup ID\n  6 - Return code for normal shutdown",
      "tags": ["SRC_Game.cpp", "NET_CLIENT", "PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_0", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "MOD_GAME", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
