      "comment": "Shutdown and cleanup all game subsystems during application termination.\n\nClassification: Cleanup/Destructor - Called during game shutdown to release resources.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call CleanupGouraudTables to deallocate Gouraud shading table memory\n2. Call ProcessAndReportValidationErrors to process and report pending validation errors\n3. Call ProcessGameContextList to notify and release game context linked list\n4. Call CleanupPlayerActionQueues to release player action queue structures\n5. Call CleanupLinkedListNodes to cleanup global linked list nodes\n6. Call GetInitFlag to deactivate window and set visibility\n7. Return 1 in EAX (success indicator, not captured by caller)\n\nParameters:\nNone - Function operates on global subsystem state.\n\nReturns:\nvoid (declared) - However, MOV EAX,0x1 before RET sets success indicator.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Called from data reference at 0x6fbae490, likely a function pointer table for shutdown handlers\n- Each cleanup function handles its own NULL checks for empty data structures\n- Order of cleanup is significant: rendering tables first, then validation, game contexts, player queues, linked lists, and finally window state\n\nError Handling:\nIndividual cleanup functions handle their own error conditions and assertions.\nCleanupGouraudTables may terminate via ExitApplicationWithCode for missing required tables.",
