      "comment": "Checks context cleanup flag and invokes D2Common cleanup callback if set.\n\nClassification: Thunk/Wrapper - Conditionally invokes external cleanup function.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Read byte flag at pCallbackContext+0x214\n2. If flag is non-zero, call Ordinal_10036 with ECX=0\n3. Return immediately\n\nParameters:\n  pCallbackContext - void * [ECX, __fastcall] - Pointer to context structure\n    +0x214: byte - Cleanup required flag (non-zero triggers callback)\n\nReturns: void\n\nCallees:\n  Ordinal_10036 (D2Common) - External cleanup/reset function, called with ECX=0\n\nCross-References:\n  Referenced from function pointer table at 0x6fbafa0c (DATA xref)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Early exit if cleanup flag is zero (no callback invoked)\n  - Tail-call optimization: JMP to Ordinal_10036 instead of CALL+RET",
