      "comment": "Validates and sets the game act environment based on GameParams.\n\nClassification: Worker function - validates act state and delegates to D2Win\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Read nAct field from pGameParams at offset 0x1FA (506 bytes)\n2. If nAct is 0, return early (no act change needed)\n3. Assert nAct <= 5 (NUM_ACTS), exit with error code -1 if violated\n4. Assert nAct >= 1, exit with error code -1 if violated  \n5. Decrement nAct to convert from 1-based to 0-based index\n6. Call Ordinal_10009(nAct - 1) to set act environment\n\nParameters:\n  pGameParams (ECX) - Pointer to GameParams structure\n    - Offset 0x1FA (506): nAct field (int) - Act number 1-5\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - nAct == 0: Silent early return, no environment change\n  - nAct > 5: FogAssert failure at line 0xd27 (3367), app exits -1\n  - nAct < 1: FogAssert failure at line 0xd28 (3368), app exits -1\n\nCalled From:\n  Function pointer table at 0x6fbafa00 (game initialization dispatch)\n\nNotes:\n  - Acts are 1-indexed in GameParams (1-5) but 0-indexed for D2Win (0-4)\n  - Ordinal_10009 = D2Win.SetActEnvironment (sets visual/audio act theme)\n  - Source file: C:\\Projects\\Diablo2\\Source\\D2Client\\...",
