      "comment": "Process registration table configuration entry and copy network settings to global variables.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load reference registration string \"REGISTRATION_TABLE\" from 0x6fbae7f4  \n2. Calculate pointer to registration key at configuration entry offset +0x32\n3. Begin character-by-character string comparison in optimized 2-byte chunks\n4. Compare each character using lexicographic ordering with SBB result calculation\n5. If registration keys don't match (nCompareResult != 0), copy IP from +0x32 to global\n6. Copy server IP address from offset +0x1a to global buffer at 0x6fbe9198\n7. Copy server port DWORD from offset +0x14 to global variable at 0x6fbe9260  \n8. Copy server type WORD from offset +0x18 to global variable at 0x6fbe9048\n9. Copy server ID DWORD from offset +0x221 to global variable at 0x6fbe9190\n10. Return with all network configuration globals updated\n\nParameters:\n- pConfigEntry (NetworkConfigEntry *): Pointer to network configuration structure containing registration key at +0x32, server IP at +0x1a, port at +0x14, type at +0x18, and server ID at +0x221\n\nReturns:\n- void: No return value, function updates global network configuration variables directly through side effects\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- String comparison uses optimized 2-byte chunk processing for performance\n- If registration key exactly matches \"REGISTRATION_TABLE\", IP copy step is bypassed \n- All server configuration fields are copied unconditionally regardless of key match\n- Uses lstrcpyA for safe string copying with null termination\n\nStructure Layout:\n| Offset | Size | Field Name | Type | Description |\n|--------|------|------------|------|-------------|\n| +0x14  | 4    | dwServerPort | DWORD | Server port number for network connection |\n| +0x18  | 2    | wServerType | WORD | Server type identifier or protocol flag |  \n| +0x1a  | 16   | szServerIP | char[16] | Null-terminated server IP address string |\n| +0x32  | 32   | szRegistrationKey | char[32] | Registration table identifier string |\n| +0x221 | 4    | dwServerID | DWORD | Unique server identifier for session tracking |",
