      "comment": "Validates network configuration state and updates global IP address if needed.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load pointer to state flag field at offset 0x4a from network config structure\n2. Load pointer to comparison string \"0\" at global address 0x6fbae7f4\n3. Compare state flag string character-by-character with \"0\" using strcmp-style loop\n4. Process comparison in pairs of characters for optimization\n5. If strings differ, calculate non-zero comparison result using SBB instructions\n6. If comparison result is non-zero, copy hostname from offset 0x32 to global IP buffer\n7. Use lstrcpyA to copy hostname string to destination buffer at 0x6fbaf4f8\n\nParameters:\npNetworkConfig (NetworkConfigEntry*): Pointer to network configuration structure\n  - Contains hostname string at offset 0x32 (50 bytes)\n  - Contains state flag character at offset 0x4a (74 bytes)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Function modifies global state only\n\nSpecial Cases:\nState flag \"0\" means inactive/disabled - no action taken\nAny other character in state flag triggers hostname copy to global buffer\nString comparison uses optimized 2-byte-at-a-time algorithm for performance\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset | Size | Field Name  | Type    | Description\n-------|------|-------------|---------|----------------------------------\n0x00   | 50   | unknown     | byte[50]| Unknown configuration data\n0x32   | 24   | hostname    | char[24]| Network hostname or IP address\n0x4a   | 1    | state_flag  | char    | Configuration state ('0' = inactive)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x32 (50): Offset to hostname string field in NetworkConfigEntry\n0x4a (74): Offset to state flag character in NetworkConfigEntry\n0x6fbae7f4: Global address of comparison string \"0\"\n0x6fbaf4f8: Global IP address buffer \"207.82.87.139\"",
