      "comment": "Validates and processes server address field from configuration data.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract string pointer from configuration data at offset +0x62 (server address field)\n2. Initialize reference pointer to global zero string constant \"0\" \n3. Compare input string with \"0\" character by character in loop:\n   a. Load character from both strings\n   b. Compare characters for equality\n   c. If unequal, calculate comparison result (-1, 0, or 1) and break\n   d. If current character is null terminator, strings are equal (break with 0)\n   e. Advance to next character pair and continue loop\n4. If comparison result is non-zero (strings differ), copy input string to default server IP buffer\n5. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\n- pConfigData (ConfigData*): Pointer to configuration data structure containing server address at offset +0x62\n\nReturns:\n- void: No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If server address field equals \"0\", no action taken (keeps existing default IP)\n- If server address field contains any other value, overwrites default IP with new address\n- String comparison handles null terminators correctly to avoid buffer overruns\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n- 0x62 (98): Offset to server address string field within configuration structure  \n- \"0\": Reference string indicating \"use default server address\"\n- \"207.82.87.133\": Default server IP address string buffer destination\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset | Size | Field Name       | Type     | Description\n-------|------|------------------|----------|----------------------------------\n0x00   | 98   | reserved         | byte[98] | Unknown configuration fields  \n0x62   | 32   | szServerAddress  | char[32] | Server address string field",
