      "comment": "Initializes remote session message processing and wheel mouse support based on session state.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if running in remote session using GetSystemMetrics(SM_REMOTESESSION)\n2. If not remote session, skip to wheel mouse registration\n3. If remote session enabled and session state is 1 (WTS_SESSION_STATE_ACTIVE):\n   - Process primary message entry array (DAT_6fbaf830) with 1 entry\n4. If remote session enabled and session state is 2 (WTS_SESSION_STATE_DISCONNECTED):\n   - Check session type for RDP (4) or RemoteApp (5)\n   - Process secondary message entry arrays (DAT_6fbaf840, DAT_6fbaf858) with 2 entries each\n5. For active sessions only, register Microsoft wheel mouse support:\n   - Register \"MSH_WHEELSUPPORT_MSG\" custom window message\n   - Find MouseZ Magellan wheel support window\n   - Send test message to verify wheel support\n   - If successful, store message ID and process wheel message array (DAT_6fbaf870)\n6. Return session type for disconnected sessions or window handle for others\n\nParameters:\nNone - function takes no parameters\n\nReturns:\nHWND - Window handle from API calls, session type cast to HWND for disconnected sessions, or 0 on failure\n\nSpecial Cases:\nSession state values: 1=WTS_SESSION_STATE_ACTIVE, 2=WTS_SESSION_STATE_DISCONNECTED  \nSession type values: 4=RDP, 5=RemoteApp\nMagic number 0x4b=SM_REMOTESESSION system metric\n\nStructure Layout:\nMessageEntry arrays contain window message processing instructions for remote session management",
