      "comment": "Destructor for GameDataCollection - systematically cleans up linked lists and deallocates memory.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Set up SEH exception frame with handler at 0x6fba4251\n2. Set vtable pointer to DestroyGameDataObject vtable (0x6fba63dc)\n3. Clear status flag at offset 0x10 to indicate destruction in progress\n4. Process main linked list: while element count > 0, remove elements from end using FUN_6fadc720/FUN_6fadc380\n5. Process secondary structure arrays: iterate through each element in param[6] array\n6. For each 12-byte structure, traverse doubly-linked lists and unlink nodes\n7. Update previous/next pointers to maintain list integrity during unlinking\n8. Handle negative offset values using bitwise NOT operation\n9. Clean up 12-byte structures using FUN_6fadc3c0 deallocator\n10. Deallocate main structure array using Ordinal_403 with magic number -2\n11. Final cleanup: process remaining main list elements using FUN_6fadc6f0\n12. Unlink final list head node and clear element count\n13. Restore exception list and return\n\nParameters:\npGameDataCollection (GameDataCollectionObj *): Pointer to collection structure containing:\n  - vtablePtr: Virtual function table pointer (set to destructor vtable)\n  - pDataArray: Pointer to main data array\n  - nElementCount: Number of elements in main array\n  - dwFlags: Status/control flags (cleared during destruction)  \n  - nStructCount: Count of secondary 12-byte structures\n  - pStructArray: Pointer to array of linked list structures\n  IMPLICIT: ECX register contains pGameDataCollection (__fastcall convention)\n\nReturns:\nvoid: No return value. Modifies collection structure in-place, deallocates memory.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Handles empty lists gracefully with count checks to prevent access violations\n- Processes negative offset values using bitwise NOT operation (addresses 0x42-0x46)\n- Uses 12-byte stride (0xC) for secondary structure array iteration\n- Magic number 0xFFFFFFFE (-2) passed to Ordinal_403 memory deallocator\n- Exception handler ensures cleanup on errors during destruction process\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset | Size | Field Name      | Type      | Description\n-------|------|-----------------|-----------|---------------------------\n0x00   |  4   | vtablePtr      | void*     | Virtual function table pointer\n0x04   |  4   | pDataArray     | void*     | Pointer to main data array  \n0x08   |  4   | field_8        | uint      | Unknown field\n0x0C   |  4   | nElementCount  | uint      | Number of elements in main array\n0x10   |  4   | dwFlags        | uint      | Status/control flags\n0x14   |  4   | field_14       | uint      | Unknown field\n0x18   |  4   | nStructCount   | uint      | Count of 12-byte structures\n0x1C   |  4   | pStructArray   | void*     | Pointer to structure array",
