      "comment": "Cleanup and deallocate all elements in a game data list structure.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Setup structured exception handling frame for safe cleanup operations\n2. Validate element count is non-zero (pGameDataList->nElementCount != 0)  \n3. Iterate through each element in pGameDataList->pElements array:\n   a. Calculate current element pointer (base + index * 0xc stride)\n   b. Set exception state to 0x0 (normal operation)\n   c. While element data count > 0 (piElement->nCount > 0):\n      - Call FUN_6fadc900(piElement->nCount, piElement->dwFlags) to get data item\n      - Call FUN_6fadc380(piDataItem) to deallocate the data item  \n   d. Reset exception state to 0xffffffff (cleanup complete)\n   e. Call FUN_6fadc380(&piElement->pData) to deallocate element data pointer\n   f. Increment element index and advance pointer by 0xc bytes\n4. After processing all elements, check if main data pointer exists\n5. If pGameDataList->pElements != NULL:\n   - Call Ordinal_403 to deallocate the elements array using string s___AV__TSExplicitList_USGAMEDATA__6fbafe38\n6. Restore exception handling state and return\n\nParameters:\npGameDataList (GameDataList*) - Pointer to game data list structure to cleanup\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If element count is 0, skips element processing but still checks for array deallocation\n- Uses structured exception handling to ensure cleanup completes even if errors occur\n- Exception state values: 0xffffffff (default), 0x0 (processing element data)\n\nStructure Layout:\nGameDataList (12 bytes):\nOffset  Size  Field Name       Type               Description\n0x0     4     dwUnknown        uint              Unknown field (not accessed)\n0x4     4     nElementCount    uint              Number of elements in array  \n0x8     4     pElements        GameDataElement*  Pointer to elements array\n\nGameDataElement (12 bytes):\nOffset  Size  Field Name       Type              Description\n0x0     4     dwFlags     