      "comment": "Allocates and inserts a new game data node into a managed list structure.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate memory for new GameDataNode using Ordinal_401 with calculated offset (nBaseOffset + 0x6ce4)\n2. If allocation succeeds, initialize node fields at offsets +4, +8, +C, +10 to zero\n3. If insertion mode is non-zero (nInsertionMode != 0):\n   a. Determine insertion point: use list base+4 if no allocated node, otherwise use list base + allocated node\n   b. If existing node found at insertion point, perform list removal:\n      - Extract current node pointer and index values\n      - Calculate target position using index (negative indices use bitwise complement)\n      - Update forward and backward link pointers\n      - Clear current position pointers\n   c. Choose insertion strategy based on mode:\n      - Mode 1: Insert at head of list, update list head pointer at offset +8\n      - Mode != 1: Insert after current position, maintain list order\n   d. Update all relevant pointers to maintain list integrity\n\nParameters:\nthis - Pointer to GameDataList structure containing list management data\nnInsertionMode - Controls insertion behavior (0=no insert, 1=insert at head, other=insert in sequence)  \nnBaseOffset - Base memory offset added to 0x6ce4 for allocation calculation\ndwFlags - Allocation flags ORed with 0x8, passed to memory allocator\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Function modifies list structure in-place through pointer manipulation\n\nSpecial Cases:\nIf allocation fails (Ordinal_401 returns 0), function continues with null node pointer\nIf nInsertionMode is 0, only allocation and initialization occur without list insertion\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x6ce4 - Base offset constant added to nBaseOffset for memory allocation\n0x8 - Flag mask ORed with dwFlags parameter before allocation\n0xfffffffe (-2) - Fixed parameter passed to Ordinal_401 allocator\n\nStructure Layout:\nGameDataNode (20 bytes):\nOffset | Size | Field Name    | Type | Description\n+0x0