      "comment": "Destroys and deallocates a game data collection structure and all contained elements.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if collection has active linked list pointer at offset +0x10\n2. If linked list exists, unlink it using position calculation from offset +0x14\n3. Store list pointer and clear both list pointer (+0x10) and position (+0x14)\n4. Process all elements in collection array if count (+0x4) is non-zero\n5. For each element, unlink its ListNode at offset +0xc from element\n6. If element has nested collection at offset +0x4, recursively unlink it\n7. Use CalculateGameDataCollectionPosition to get proper unlinking position\n8. Clear nested collection pointer and position fields\n9. Advance to next element using stride of 0x6ce4 bytes (27876 bytes)\n10. Continue until all elements processed based on count\n11. If array buffer exists at offset +0x8, deallocate using Ordinal_403\n\nParameters:\npGameDataCollection (int *): Pointer to GameDataCollection structure to destroy\n\nReturns:\nvoid: No return value\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset | Size | Field Name           | Type    | Description\n+0x4   | 4    | dwElementCount      | uint    | Number of elements in array\n+0x8   | 4    | pElementArray       | void *  | Pointer to element array buffer\n+0x10  | 4    | pLinkedListNode     | void *  | Active linked list node pointer\n+0x14  | 4    | dwListPosition      | uint    | Position/index in linked list\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x6ce4 (27876): Element stride size in bytes for array iteration\n0x10: Offset to linked list node pointer\n0x14: Offset to linked list position field\n0xc: Offset to ListNode within each array element\n0x4: Offset to nested collection pointer within element\n0x8: Offset to nested collection position within element\n0xffffffff (-1): Invalid collection index passed to position calculation\n\nError Handling:\n- Null pointer checks for linked list node (+0x10) before unlinking\n- Null pointer checks for element count (+0x4) before array processing\n- Null pointer checks for nested collections (+0x4) before recursive unlinking\n- Null pointer checks for array buffer (+0x8) before deallocation\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Negative position values (bit 31 set) use bitwise NOT for position calculation\n- Empty collections (count = 0) skip array processing entirely\n- Elements without nested collections skip recursive unlinking\n- Collections without array buffers skip final deallocation",
