      "comment": "Sends a video playback parameters packet to the network.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Set packet type identifier to 100 (0x64)\n2. Copy source data using Ordinal_501 with max length 0x7FFFFFFF\n3. Determine server type based on g_dwServerPort value:\n   - Port 0: Server type 3\n   - Port 6: Server type 1  \n   - Port 8: Server type 2\n   - Other: Server type 0\n4. Check processing mode flag and get config value\n5. Get return value from Ordinal_10007\n6. Initialize video flags if not set (set to 0x100004)\n7. Extract video playback parameters from g_dwVideoPlaybackState structure\n8. Copy destination buffer using Ordinal_501 from global data\n9. Send packet using Ordinal_10005 with 0x2E (46) byte payload\n10. Update global counters: DAT_6fc04128 += 0x2E, DAT_6fc04130 += 1\n\nParameters:\ndwPlaybackId: undefined4 - Playback session identifier or handle\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If video flags at offset 0x204 are zero, initializes to 0x100004\n- Server type mapping uses switch-style logic with specific port values\n- Uses 0x7FFFFFFF as maximum string copy length (safety limit)\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x64 (100): Packet type identifier for video playback\n0x7FFFFFFF: Maximum string copy length safety limit\n0x100004: Default video flags value (bit 2 + bit 20 set)  \n0x2E (46): Fixed packet payload size in bytes\n0x202-0x20B: VideoPlaybackParams structure field offsets\n\nStructure Layout:\nVideoPlaybackParams (at g_dwVideoPlaybackState + offset):\nOffset Size Field Name    Type    Description\n0x202  2    wVideoParam0  ushort  Video parameter 0\n0x204  4    dwVideoFlags  uint    Video control flags  \n0x208  1    byVideoParam1 byte    Video parameter 1\n0x209  1    byVideoParam2 byte    Video parameter 2\n0x20A  1    byVideoParam3 byte    Video parameter 3\n0x20B  1    byVideoParam5 byte    Video parameter 5",
