      "comment": "Sends a single-byte heartbeat/keep-alive packet (0x68 'h') to the server.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate 1 byte on stack for packet data\n2. Set packet type byte to 0x68 (ASCII 'h' - heartbeat identifier)\n3. Call Ordinal_10005 with packet data (1 byte payload, channel 0)\n4. Increment g_dwTotalBytesCompressed by 1 (packet size)\n5. Increment g_dwCompressionCount by 1 (packet count)\n6. Clean up stack and return\n\nParameters:\nNone - Takes no parameters\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Minimal packet size: only 1 byte of payload data\n- Called via thunk at 0x6fae1dd0\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x68 (104, 'h') - Heartbeat packet type identifier\n0x1 - Payload size in bytes\n0x0 - Channel parameter for Ordinal_10005\n\nRelated Functions:\nOrdinal_10005 - D2Net packet transmission function\nthunk_SendHeartbeatPacket @ 0x6fae1dd0 - Thunk wrapper\n\nGlobal State Modified:\ng_dwTotalBytesCompressed @ 0x6fc04128 - Incremented by 1\ng_dwCompressionCount @ 0x6fc04130 - Incremented by 1",
