      "instructions": ["0xCC70|SUB|ESP, 0xc", "0xCC73|PUSH|ESI", "0xCC74|MOV|ESI, dword ptr [0x6fba6098]", "0xCC7A|CALL|ESI", "0xCC7C|MOV|EDX, dword ptr [0x6fbe92f0]", "0xCC82|MOV|ECX, EAX", "0xCC84|SUB|ECX, EDX", "0xCC86|CMP|ECX, 0x1388", "0xCC8C|JC|0x6fadccd1", "0xCC8E|MOV|[0x6fbe92f0], EAX", "0xCC93|MOV|byte ptr [ESP + 0x4], 0x6a", "0xCC98|CALL|ESI", "0xCC9A|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x5], EAX", "0xCC9E|CALL|0x6fad92f0", "0xCCA3|LEA|EDX, [ESP + 0x4]"],
      "comment": "Periodically sends metrics data packet every 5 seconds to monitoring system\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get current system tick count via GetTickCount()\n2. Calculate elapsed time since last metrics transmission (stored in g_dwLastMetricsTick)\n3. Check if 5000ms (0x1388) have elapsed since last transmission\n4. If insufficient time has passed, exit without action\n5. Update last transmission timestamp to current tick count\n6. Initialize 9-byte packet with header byte 0x6A\n7. Get current system tick for packet timestamp\n8. Retrieve metrics counter via GetMetricsCounter()\n9. Calculate metrics value by right-shifting counter by 1 bit (divide by 2)\n10. Send 9-byte packet via Ordinal_10005 with channel 0\n11. Increment global packet counter (g_dwTotalPacketSize) by 9 bytes\n12. Increment global transmission counter (g_dwTransmissionCount) by 1\n\nParameters:\nNone - Function takes no parameters\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Function returns no value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Timer threshold: 0x1388 (5000ms) controls transmission frequency\n- Packet header: 0x6A indicates metrics packet type\n- Metrics scaling: Counter value divided by 2 before transmission\n- Global state: Updates g_dwLastMetricsTick, g_dwTotalPacketSize, g_dwTransmissionCount\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x1388 (5000) - Timer threshold in milliseconds for periodic transmission\n0x6A (106) - Packet header byte identifying metrics data type\n0x9 (9) - Fixed packet size in bytes\n0x1 (1) - Right shift amount for metrics value scaling\n0x0 (0) - Channel identifier for Ordinal_10005 transmission",
