      "instructions": ["0xCCE0|PUSH|ECX", "0xCCE1|LEA|EAX, [ESP + 0x3]", "0xCCE5|PUSH|0x1", "0xCCE7|PUSH|EAX", "0xCCE8|PUSH|0x0", "0xCCEA|MOV|byte ptr [ESP + 0xf], 0x66", "0xCCEF|CALL|0x6fb99852", "0xCCF4|MOV|EAX, [0x6fc04128]", "0xCCF9|MOV|EDX, dword ptr [0x6fc04130]", "0xCCFF|INC|EAX", "0xCD00|INC|EDX", "0xCD01|MOV|[0x6fc04128], EAX", "0xCD06|MOV|EAX, [0x6fbe9260]", "0xCD0B|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0xCD0D|MOV|dword ptr [0x6fc04130], EDX"],
      "comment": "Process server port configuration and trigger game interface callbacks during system initialization.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Create 32-bit parameter by concatenating 0x66 prefix with 3-byte global state result\n2. Call system logging function Ordinal_10005 to record configuration event  \n3. Increment global counters DAT_6fc04128 and DAT_6fc04130 to track initialization calls\n4. Check server port configuration against known values (0, 1, 6, 7, 8, 9)\n5. If port is 0 or 1, skip to interface callback section  \n6. If port is 6, jump directly to interface callback handling\n7. If port is 7, 8, or 9, skip game system setup and proceed to interface callback\n8. For all other port values, enable game system and reset state variables\n9. Set g_dwGameSystemEnabled to 1 (enabled state)\n10. Clear DAT_6fbe926c and DAT_6fbe9268 state variables to 0\n11. If server port is 6 or 7, retrieve game interface and invoke callback function\n12. Get game interface pointer via GetGameInterface() function\n13. If interface is valid, call function at offset 0x9c with processed parameter\n\nParameters:\nbyGlobalStateResult (undefined3): 3-byte result from SetGlobalState function passed in ECX register\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Function performs configuration actions without return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x66 - Prefix byte for creating game interface parameter (0x66 combined with 3-byte input)\n0x9c - Offset to callback function in game interface vtable (156 decimal)\n0x0, 0x1 - Special server port values that bypass game system initialization  \n0x6 - Server port value that skips to interface callback immediately\n0x7, 0x8, 0x9 - Server port values that skip game system setup but allow interface callbacks\n0x1 - Enabled state value for g_dwGameSystemEnabled flag\n0x0 - Reset state value for DAT_6fbe926c and DAT_6fbe9268 variables\n\nError Handling:\nFunction checks GetGameInterface() return value for NULL before calling interface callback\nNo explicit error codes returned - errors handled by skipping interface callback invocation",
      "tags": ["PARAM_1"]
    },
