      "comment": "Submits a telemetry log record with event type and data parameters.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize 32-byte telemetry record structure on stack\n2. Set record type byte to 0x65 (telemetry record identifier)\n3. Copy input parameters to record structure (dwEventData, wEventType)\n4. Get current instance pointer using GetCurrentInstance\n5. Call function pointer at offset 0x5c from instance to get result\n6. Call Ordinal_10007 to get additional flag byte\n7. Check if processing mode flag is set via IsProcessingModeFlagSet\n8. If processing mode enabled, get config value via GetConfigValue, else use default from DAT_6fbe9194\n9. Initialize buffer using Ordinal_501 with global data reference DAT_6fbe910c\n10. Submit complete record via Ordinal_10005 with 29-byte (0x1d) payload\n11. Update global counters: increment DAT_6fc04128 by 0x1d bytes, increment DAT_6fc04130 count\n\nParameters:\nwEventType (CX): Event type identifier (16-bit)\ndwEventData (EDX): Event-specific data value (32-bit)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x65 - Telemetry record type identifier\n0x1d (29) - Record payload size in bytes\n0x5c - Offset to function pointer in instance structure\n0x7fffffff - Maximum size parameter for Ordinal_501\nDAT_6fbe9194 - Default processing mode flag value\nDAT_6fbe910c - Global data reference for buffer initialization\nDAT_6fc04128 - Global byte counter (incremented by payload size)\nDAT_6fc04130 - Global record counter (incremented by 1)\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset | Size | Field Name           | Type | Description\n-------|------|---------------------|------|----------------------------------\n0x00   | 1    | bRecordType         | byte | Record type (0x65)\n0x01   | 4    | dwParam2Copy        | uint | Copy of dwEventData parameter\n0x05   | 2    | wParam1Copy         | word | Copy of wEventType parameter  \n0x07   | 1    | (padding)           | byte | Stack alignment\n0x08   | 4    | dwInstanceResult  