      "comment": "Calculates a scaled ratio with 8-bit precision and stores result globally.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if denominator is zero to prevent division by zero\n2. If zero, set global result to zero and return early  \n3. Scale numerator by 256 (left shift 8 bits) for fixed-point precision\n4. Perform signed integer division: (numerator * 256) / denominator\n5. Store calculated ratio in global variable DAT_6fbe92f4\n\nParameters:\n  nNumerator - Input numerator value for ratio calculation\n  nDenominator - Input denominator value for ratio calculation\n\nReturns:\n  void - Result stored in global DAT_6fbe92f4\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  Division by zero: When nDenominator is 0, sets global result to 0\n  Precision: Uses 8-bit scaling where 256 represents 1.0 (100%)\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x8 (8) - Left shift count for 8-bit scaling factor\n  256 - Scaling factor representing 1.0 in fixed-point arithmetic",
      "tags": ["PARAM_2", "PROP_LEAF", "PROP_SMALL"]
