      "instructions": ["0xCE20|SUB|ESP, 0x714", "0xCE26|MOV|AL, [0x6fbe910c]", "0xCE2B|PUSH|EBX", "0xCE2C|PUSH|EBP", "0xCE2D|PUSH|ESI", "0xCE2E|TEST|AL, AL", "0xCE30|PUSH|EDI", "0xCE31|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x20], ECX", "0xCE35|JNZ|0x6fadce55", "0xCE37|PUSH|0x18c", "0xCE3C|PUSH|0x6fbafe98", "0xCE41|PUSH|0x6fbafe80", "0xCE46|CALL|0x6fb99a7a", "0xCE4B|ADD|ESP, 0xc", "0xCE4E|PUSH|-0x1"],
      "comment": "Processes and transmits Diablo 2 character save data (.d2s file) over network connection\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check global initialization flag DAT_6fbe910c, terminate program if not initialized\n2. Clear game state and format file path using player name from global data\n3. Open character save file (.d2s) for binary reading\n4. Seek to end of file to determine file size, then reset to beginning\n5. Allocate buffer (0x1a0 bytes) and read entire file into memory\n6. Close file handle and validate buffer allocation succeeded\n7. If progress display enabled, perform initial progress setup with 8 delay cycles\n8. Calculate number of full 255-byte chunks to transmit (fileSize / 255)\n9. For each full chunk:\n   a. Set packet header: type=0x69, size=0xff (255 bytes), file_size=original\n   b. Copy 255 bytes from file buffer to transmission buffer\n   c. Transmit packet using network protocol (Ordinal_10005)\n   d. Update global transmission statistics (bytes sent, packet count)\n   e. If progress display enabled, update progress bar and sleep 250ms per cycle\n10. Process remaining partial chunk (fileSize % 255 bytes):\n    a. Set packet header: type=0x69, size=remainder, file_size=original\n    b. Copy remaining bytes to transmission buffer\n    c. Transmit final packet with adjusted size (remainder + 7 header bytes)\n11. Send completion signal (Ordinal_10043) with parameters 0x203, 0\n12. Update final progress indicator based on total chunks processed\n\nParameters:\nfShowProgress (int) - Boolean flag controlling progress bar display and timing delays\n                     Non-zero enables progress updates with Sleep(250ms) cycles\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Function does not return value\n      Terminates program on critical errors (uninitialized state, file access failure)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Program termination via FUN_6fb9a10f(-1) on initialization or file access errors\n- Progress calculation prevents division by zero when nChunksRemaining = 0\n- File size = 0 results in nChunksRemaining = 0, skips chunk processing loop\n- Buffer allocation failure (pbFileData == NULL) triggers error termination\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x69 - Packet type identifier for character data transmission\n0xff - Maximum chunk size (255 bytes) for data packet payload\n0x1a0 - File buffer allocation size (416 bytes)\n0x18c - Error code for uninitialized state termination  \n0x1d3 - Error code for file access failure termination\n0xfa - Sleep duration in milliseconds (250ms) for progress display\n0x106 - Total packet size (255 data bytes + 7 header bytes)\n0x203 - Completion signal parameter for successful transmission\n0x800 - Progress counter increment (2048) for display calculation\n0x7 - Header overhead bytes added to final partial packet size\n\nError Handling:\n- Global flag check prevents execution in uninitialized game state\n- File open failure triggers immediate program termination with error code 0x1d3\n- File seek operations validate successful positioning before proceeding  \n- Memory allocation failure check ensures valid buffer before file operations\n- All error paths call FUN_6fb9a10f(-1) for controlled program termination\n\nState Machine:\nState 1: Initialization - Check global flag, format file path, open file\nState 2: File Reading - Determine size, allocate buffer, read entire file\nState 3: Chunk Processing - Transmit data in 255-byte packets with headers\nState 4: Completion - Send final partial chunk and completion signal\nState 5: Cleanup - Update progress and return (or terminate on errors)",
      "tags": ["PROP_LARGE", "SRC_Msg.cpp", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "STRUCT_Skill", "PARAM_1", "PROP_LOOPHEAVY", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "MOD_GAME", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
