      "comment": "Queries system information via external API and increments success counters.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate 512-byte buffer on stack (0x200 bytes)\n2. Call external API Ordinal_10005 with parameters (1, buffer_address, 1)\n3. Test API return value for success (non-zero)\n4. If successful, increment global counter at 0x6fc04128\n5. If successful, increment global counter at 0x6fc04130\n6. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\nAPI call failure - counters remain unchanged if Ordinal_10005 returns 0\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x200 (512) - Buffer size allocated on stack\n0x1 - First parameter to API call (likely operation mode)\n0x1 - Third parameter to API call (likely flags or count)\n0x6fc04128 - Global counter #1 incremented on success\n0x6fc04130 - Global counter #2 incremented on success\n\nError Handling:\nFunction performs silent failure - no error reporting if API call fails\nCounters are only incremented on API success (non-zero return)",
