      "comment": "Records event data to system log by creating a 3-byte buffer and calling external logging service.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate local 3-byte buffer on stack\n2. Copy event type byte and event data word to buffer\n3. Extract high byte of event data word  \n4. Call external logging function with parameters (1, buffer_address, 3)\n5. If logging successful, increment global byte counter by 3\n6. If logging successful, increment global event counter by 1\n7. Return void\n\nParameters:\nbEventType (byte): Event classification type stored in CL register\nwEventData (ushort): Event-specific data payload stored in DX register\n\nReturns:\nvoid: Function performs logging operation without return value\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x1: Log priority level passed to external function\n0x3: Buffer size in bytes (event type + event data)\n0x6fc04128: Global byte counter address\n0x6fc04130: Global event counter address\n\nError Handling:\nIf external logging function returns 0, counters are not incremented\nNo explicit error propagation - failed logging is silently ignored",
