      "comment": "Sends a 5-byte protocol message and updates transmission statistics.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract low and high bytes from wParam2 using byte casting and bit shifting\n2. Pack all parameters into a 5-byte buffer: bOpcode, wParam1 (2 bytes), wParam2 low byte\n3. Store wParam2 high byte separately in stack variable  \n4. Call external protocol transmission function with buffer pointer and length 5\n5. If transmission succeeds (non-zero return), increment global statistics counters\n\nParameters:\nbOpcode - Single byte operation code or message type identifier\nwParam1 - First 16-bit parameter value for protocol message\nwParam2 - Second 16-bit parameter value, split into high and low bytes\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Function does not return a value to caller\n\nSpecial Cases:\nProtocol function call with parameters (1, buffer_ptr, 5) suggests message type 1\nOn successful transmission: increments byte counter by 5, message counter by 1\nUses CONCAT operations to reconstruct packed data from individual parameters\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x1 (1) - Protocol message type identifier passed to transmission function\n0x5 (5) - Fixed message length for this protocol message type\n0x6fc04128 - Global byte transmission counter address\n0x6fc04130 - Global message transmission counter address",
