      "comment": "Send packet data to compression/hashing system and update statistics.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Construct 9-byte data structure by packing parameters\n2. Pack bPacketType into first byte of buffer\n3. Split dwData1 into 4 bytes: 3 lower bytes + 1 upper byte\n4. Split dwData2 into 4 bytes: 3 lower bytes + 1 upper byte  \n5. Arrange bytes as: [bPacketType][dwData1 low 3][dwData1 high 1][dwData2 low 3][dwData2 high 1]\n6. Call compression function Ordinal_10005 with mode=1, buffer pointer, length=9\n7. If compression succeeds (returns non-zero):\n   - Increment g_dwTotalBytesCompressed by 9 bytes\n   - Increment g_dwCompressionCount by 1 operation\n\nParameters:\nbPacketType - Byte identifying packet type/category for compression\ndwData1 - First 32-bit data value to include in compressed packet\ndwData2 - Second 32-bit data value to include in compressed packet\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Function always returns, success determined by global counter updates\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If Ordinal_10005 returns 0 (compression failed), counters remain unchanged\n- Function uses __fastcall convention: bPacketType in CL, dwData1 in EDX, dwData2 on stack\n- All 32-bit values stored in little-endian format in 9-byte buffer\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x01 - Compression mode parameter passed to Ordinal_10005\n0x09 - Fixed buffer size for all packet data (9 bytes)\n0x18 - Right shift amount (24 bits) to extract high byte from 32-bit value\n\nError Handling:\n- No explicit error handling - relies on Ordinal_10005 to validate input\n- Failed compression indicated by zero return value from Ordinal_10005\n- Statistics counters only updated on successful compression\n\nData Structure Layout:\nByte    Size  Field              Type     Description\n0       1     bPacketType        byte     Packet type identifier\n1-3     3     dwData1[0:23]     uint     Lower 24 bits of first data value\n4       1     dwData1[24:31]    byte     Upper 8 bits of first data value\n5-7     3     dwData2[0:23