      "comment": "Packs five data values into 17-byte buffer and compresses them using D2CMP compression\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Pack parameters into 17-byte buffer using CONCAT operations\n2. Place bPacketType in first byte of buffer\n3. Pack dwData1-4 as 4-byte values, extracting high bytes for cross-alignment\n4. Create packed structure with byte interleaving pattern\n5. Call D2CMP compression function (Ordinal_10005) with mode=1, size=0x11\n6. If compression succeeds, update global compression statistics\n7. Increment total compressed bytes counter (DAT_6fc04128) by 0x11\n8. Increment compression operation counter (DAT_6fc04130) by 1\n\nParameters:\n- bPacketType: Packet type identifier for first byte of buffer\n- dwData1: First 32-bit data value to pack\n- dwData2: Second 32-bit data value to pack  \n- dwData3: Third 32-bit data value to pack\n- dwData4: Fourth 32-bit data value to pack\n\nReturns:\n- void (no return value)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If D2CMP compression fails (returns 0), statistics are not updated\n- Buffer packing uses byte-level CONCAT operations for cross-DWORD alignment\n- Total packed size is always 17 bytes (0x11) regardless of data content\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n- 0x11 (17): Fixed buffer size for 1 byte + 4 DWORDs = 17 bytes total\n- 0x1: Compression mode parameter for D2CMP function\n- DAT_6fc04128: Global counter for total compressed bytes\n- DAT_6fc04130: Global counter for compression operations\n\nError Handling:\n- Function continues normally if compression fails\n- No error propagation or validation of input parameters\n- Compression failure detected by zero return from Ordinal_10005",
