      "comment": "Builds and sends a packet with command ID 0x5d\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract byte components from dwData parameter (low, mid, high bytes)\n2. Construct 7-byte packet structure on stack:\n   - Byte 0: Command ID (0x5d constant)\n   - Byte 1: Subcommand (bSubcommand parameter)\n   - Byte 2: Flags byte (0x1 if nEnableFlags != 0, else 0x0)\n   - Bytes 3-6: dwData parameter (little-endian)\n   - Byte 6: High byte from dwData >> 24\n3. Call Ordinal_10005 to send packet (mode=1, length=7)\n4. If send successful, increment global packet counters\n\nParameters:\nbSubcommand (byte): Subcommand identifier for packet type\ndwData (uint): 32-bit data payload for packet\nnEnableFlags (int): Flag to enable packet flags byte (non-zero = enabled)\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If nEnableFlags is 0, flags byte is set to 0x0\n- If nEnableFlags is non-zero, flags byte is set to 0x1\n- Packet counters only incremented on successful send\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x5d (93 decimal): Primary command identifier\n0x1: Enabled flags value when nEnableFlags != 0\n7: Fixed packet length in bytes\n1: Send mode parameter for Ordinal_10005\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset | Size | Field Name | Type | Description\n0      | 1    | bCommandId | byte | Command identifier (0x5d)\n1      | 1    | bSubcommand| byte | Subcommand parameter\n2      | 1    | bFlags     | byte | Flags (0x1 if enabled, 0x0 if disabled)\n3      | 4    | dwData     | uint | Data payload (little-endian)\n\nError Handling:\n- Ordinal_10005 return value checked for success/failure\n- Global counters DAT_6fc04128 (bytes sent) and DAT_6fc04130 (packets sent) only updated on success",
