      "comment": "Log a 6-byte packet to compression system and increment telemetry counters\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract low 16 bits of packet data into wLowData\n2. Extract high 16 bits of packet data into wHighData  \n3. Build 6-byte packet structure: [byPacketType][0x5E][wLowData][wHighData]\n4. Call Ordinal_10005 compression function with packet buffer\n5. If compression succeeds, increment global byte and packet counters\n\nParameters:\nbyPacketType: Packet type identifier or command code\ndwPacketData: 32-bit packet payload or flags data\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If Ordinal_10005 fails (returns 0), counters are not incremented\n- Packet always includes 0x5E marker byte at offset 1\n- Total packet size is fixed at 6 bytes\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x5E (94): Packet type marker/delimiter byte\n0x10 (16): Right shift for extracting high 16 bits \n6: Fixed packet size in bytes\n1: First parameter to Ordinal_10005 (compression mode/flags)\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset | Size | Field Name | Type | Description\n0      | 1    | Type       | byte | Packet type from byPacketType parameter\n1      | 1    | Marker     | byte | Fixed marker byte (0x5E)\n2      | 2    | LowData    | word | Low 16 bits of dwPacketData\n4      | 2    | HighData   | word | High 16 bits of dwPacketData",
