      "comment": "Packs byte data into two 32-bit values and calls compression function with statistics tracking.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract low and high 16-bit portions of the packed value parameter\n2. Construct first packed data: [low16bits][firstByte][0x55]\n3. Construct second packed data: [secondByte][thirdByte][high16bits]\n4. Call compression function (Ordinal_10005) with packed data buffer\n5. If compression succeeds, increment global byte counter by 8 bytes\n6. If compression succeeds, increment global operation counter by 1\n\nParameters:\nchFirstByte - First byte of data to be packed\nnPackedValue - 32-bit value to be split into high/low 16-bit components  \nchSecondByte - Second byte of data to be packed\nchThirdByte - Third byte of data to be packed\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\nMagic number 0x55 is always inserted as the lowest byte of first packed value\nCompression function receives exactly 8 bytes (2 x 32-bit values)\nGlobal counters are only updated on successful compression (non-zero return)\n\nGlobal Variables:\nDAT_6fc04128 - Total bytes processed counter (incremented by 8)\nDAT_6fc04130 - Total operations counter (incremented by 1)",
