      "comment": "Compress 12-byte data buffer and update compression statistics.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract low/high 16-bit portions from input 32-bit values\n2. Construct first buffer word: combine marker byte (0x56) with bMarker parameter\n3. Construct second buffer word: combine high/low portions of dwData1\n4. Construct third buffer word: combine bFlag1/bFlag2 with high portion of dwData2\n5. Call compression function with buffer address and 12-byte length\n6. If compression successful, increment global compression statistics\n\nParameters:\nbMarker - Byte marker value for first buffer position\ndwData1 - Primary 32-bit data value (split into high/low words)\ndwData2 - Secondary 32-bit data value (split into high/low words)\nbFlag1 - First flag byte for buffer construction\nbFlag2 - Second flag byte for buffer construction\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\nCompression statistics only updated on successful compression (non-zero return)\nFixed marker value 0x56 prepended to all compressed buffers\nBuffer constructed in little-endian format with specific byte ordering\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x56 (86) - Fixed buffer marker byte prepended to all data\n0xc (12) - Buffer size in bytes passed to compression function\n0x10 (16) - Right shift amount for extracting high 16 bits from 32-bit values",
