      "comment": "Sends a network message with command ID 0x57 and optional string data.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Build message header with command byte 0x57 and sequence byte from Ordinal_10007()\n2. Copy input string to message buffer offset +2 (maximum 256 bytes via strncpy)\n3. Set null terminator at end of string data\n4. Calculate total message length using REPNE SCASB string scan\n5. Verify total message size does not exceed D2NET_MAX_MESSAGE_SIZE (0x1FF = 511 bytes)\n6. If size exceeded, trigger assertion with file/line info and terminate process\n7. Copy message data to local buffer using optimized DWORD and byte copy loops\n8. Call compression function Ordinal_10005() with mode 1, buffer, and size\n9. If compression successful, increment global compression statistics\n\nParameters:\n  lpszMessage: char * - Input string to include in message payload (max 256 bytes)\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value, function either succeeds or terminates process\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If input string + header exceeds 511 bytes, calls FUN_6fb9a10f(-1) to terminate\n  - Empty or null string input is handled (creates header-only message)\n  - Uses REPNE SCASB for efficient string length calculation\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x57: Message command/type identifier\n  0x100: Maximum string copy length (256 bytes)\n  0x1FF: D2NET_MAX_MESSAGE_SIZE limit (511 bytes)\n  0x200: Local buffer size (512 bytes)\n\nError Handling:\n  - Size validation prevents buffer overflow attacks\n  - Assertion mechanism logs error location before process termination\n  - strncpy() prevents buffer overrun during string copy\n\nStructure Layout:\nNetworkMessage (259 bytes total):\n  Offset  Size  Field Name     Type     Description\n  0x00    1     bCommand       byte     Message type (always 0x57)\n  0x01    1     bSequence      byte     Sequence/flags from Ordinal_10007()\n  0x02    256   szData         char[]   String payload data\n  0x102   1     bTerminator    byte     Null terminator (0x00)",
