      "comment": "Sends a D2NET message with opcode 0x5C containing a parameter byte, data value, and string payload.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize 6-byte message header with opcode 0x5C\n2. Set header[1] to parameter byte value (byParam)\n3. Set header[2-5] to 4-byte data value (dwDataValue)\n4. Copy input string to local buffer with strncpy (max 16 chars)\n5. Calculate total message length (6-byte header + string length)\n6. Validate message length against D2NET_MAX_MESSAGE_SIZE (511 bytes)\n7. If oversized, trigger assertion and fatal error\n8. Copy header and string data to output buffer using optimized dword/byte copying\n9. Compress and send message via Ordinal_10005\n10. Update global compression statistics if successful\n\nParameters:\n- byParam: Single byte parameter value stored at header offset 1\n- lpszMessage: Null-terminated string message payload (max 16 characters)\n- dwDataValue: 4-byte data value stored at header offsets 2-5\n\nReturns:\n- void (no return value, function exits via compression call)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Message length > 511 bytes: Triggers fatal assertion and process termination\n- Empty/null string: Still sends 6-byte header with null terminator\n- Compression failure: Function returns without updating statistics\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n- 0x5C: Message opcode identifier for this message type\n- 0x10: Maximum string length for strncpy buffer (16 bytes)\n- 0x1FF: Maximum message size check (511 bytes = D2NET_MAX_MESSAGE_SIZE)\n- 6: Fixed header size (opcode + param + dword value)\n\nMessage Header Structure:\n| Offset | Size | Field        | Type | Description               |\n|--------|------|--------------|------|---------------------------|\n| 0      | 1    | byOpcode     | byte | Message type (0x5C)       |\n| 1      | 1    | byParam      | byte | Parameter value           |\n| 2      | 4    | dwDataValue  | uint | 4-byte data payload       |\n\nError Handling:\n- String too long: Truncated by strncpy to 16 characters\n- Message oversized: Fatal error via Ordinal_10023 and FUN_6fb9a10f\n- Compression failure: Silent failure, no statistics update\n\nNote: Function uses 2 phantom stack variables (local_216, local_217) optimized away by decompiler.",
