      "comment": "Compresses network message data using ZLIB compression for transmission efficiency.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Copy first 3 bytes of input message to header buffer (dwMessageHeader)\n2. Copy remaining message data (offset +3) to temporary buffer using memcpy (max 0x100 bytes)\n3. Check if extended data exists at offset +0x103 and append if present (max 0x10 bytes)\n4. Validate total message length does not exceed 0x200 bytes (D2NET_MAX_MESSAGE_SIZE)\n5. Copy assembled message from temp buffer to output buffer using optimized word/byte copy\n6. Compress output buffer using ZLIB compression (mode=1, buffer, length)\n7. Update global compression statistics if compression succeeded\n\nParameters:\npbMessageBuffer - Pointer to input network message buffer containing header and data\n\nReturns:\nvoid (no return value, compression result tracked via global statistics)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If total message length exceeds 0x200 bytes, triggers assertion failure and exits process\n- Extended data at offset +0x103 is optional and conditionally copied\n- Global variables g_dwTotalBytesCompressed and g_dwCompressionCount track statistics\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x100 (256) - Maximum size for primary message data copy\n0x103 (259) - Offset to check for extended message data  \n0x10 (16) - Maximum size for extended data copy\n0x200 (512) - D2NET_MAX_MESSAGE_SIZE limit for total message\n0x1ff (511) - Size check threshold (MAX_SIZE - 1)\n\nError Handling:\n- Length validation prevents buffer overflow in compression buffer\n- Assertion macro triggers fatal error with source file and line information\n- Process termination via FUN_6fb9a10f(-1) on validation failure",
