      "instructions": ["0xD9B0|MOV|EAX, [0x6fbe9260]", "0xD9B5|SUB|ESP, 0x200", "0xD9BB|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0xD9BD|JZ|0x6fadd9c4", "0xD9BF|CMP|EAX, 0x1", "0xD9C2|JNZ|0x6fadd9cd", "0xD9C4|CALL|0x6fb992c2", "0xD9C9|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0xD9CB|JNZ|0x6fadda23", "0xD9CD|CALL|dword ptr [0x6fba6098]", "0xD9D3|SUB|EAX, dword ptr [0x6fbe92fc]", "0xD9D9|CMP|EAX, 0x2710", "0xD9DE|JBE|0x6fadda0c", "0xD9E0|MOV|ECX, 0x6", "0xD9E5|CALL|0x6fad9070"],
      "comment": "Processes game connection timeout and handles incoming network packets.\n\nCalled as a callback from ProcessMessagePumpWithCallback during game initialization.\nMonitors elapsed time since connection start and triggers timeout after 10 seconds.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if server port mode is 0 (local) or 1 (single player)\n2. If local/single player mode, call Ordinal_10026 (D2Net.CheckPacketAvailable)\n3. If packet available (non-zero return), jump to packet processing\n4. Get current tick count and calculate elapsed time since g_dwConnectionStartTime\n5. If elapsed time > 10000ms (10 seconds), trigger connection timeout:\n   a. Call SetGameDifficulty(6) to set difficulty\n   b. Set g_dwGameSystemInitialized = 1\n   c. Set g_dwPostGameStateFlags = 0\n   d. Return true (connection complete/timed out)\n6. Call Ordinal_10017 (D2Net.PollNetworkEvents) to check for network events\n7. If no network event (return 0), return true (continue waiting)\n8. Process incoming packet:\n   a. Call Ordinal_10008 (D2Net.ReceivePacket) into local_200 buffer\n   b. Call ProcessGameCommand with packet buffer and length\n   c. Return whether g_dwPostGameStateFlags is non-zero\n\nParameters:\n  None (uses global state)\n\nReturns:\n  bool - true if connection established or timed out, false to continue polling\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - 10 second timeout triggers game initialization with difficulty 6\n  - Server port mode 0/1 uses different packet check path\n  - Packet buffer is 512 bytes on stack\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x2710 (10000) - Connection timeout in milliseconds (10 seconds)\n  0x6 - Game difficulty value set on timeout\n  0x200 (512) - Packet buffer size\n\nOrdinal References:\n  Ordinal_10026 - D2Net.CheckPacketAvailable\n  Ordinal_10017 - D2Net.PollNetworkEvents\n  Ordinal_10008 - D2Net.ReceivePacket",
      "tags": ["PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_0"]
