      "comment": "Shuts down the compression service by clearing initialization flag and calling cleanup routine.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if compression service is initialized via g_fCompressionServiceInitialized flag\n2. If not initialized (flag is 0), return 0 immediately - no cleanup needed\n3. Clear the initialization flag to prevent multiple shutdown attempts\n4. Call D2CMP.DLL Ordinal_10050 to perform actual compression service cleanup\n5. Return the result from the cleanup routine\n\nParameters:\n(none)\n\nReturns:\nSuccess (0) if compression service was not initialized or cleanup completed successfully\nError code from D2CMP.DLL cleanup routine if cleanup fails\n\nSpecial Cases:\nMultiple calls to this function are safe - subsequent calls after first shutdown return 0\nFunction acts as one-time shutdown guard using initialization flag\n\nError Handling:\nNo validation - assumes D2CMP.DLL is loaded and ordinal is valid\nPasses through any error codes from compression service cleanup routine",
