      "comment": "Processes network tick and checks for connection timeout.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call D2Net.Ordinal_10026 to process network tick\n2. Check server port mode (0=single-player, 1=TCP/IP):\n   - If single-player or TCP/IP, call D2Net.Ordinal_10003 (tick handler)\n3. Call D2Net.Ordinal_10008 to receive incoming packet data\n4. Pass received packet buffer to ProcessGameCommand for processing\n5. Get current tick count and compare against last network timestamp\n6. If more than 10000ms (10 seconds) elapsed, return true (timeout)\n7. Otherwise return true if g_dwPostGameStateFlags == 0\n\nParameters:\n- None\n\nReturns:\n- bool: true if network timeout exceeded (10+ seconds) OR if post-game state flags cleared\n        false if within timeout and post-game state flags are set\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 10000 (0x2710): Network timeout threshold in milliseconds (10 seconds)\n- 0, 1: Server port values for single-player and TCP/IP modes\n\nGlobals Referenced:\n- g_dwServerPort (0x6fbe9260): Current server connection port/mode\n- g_dwLastNetworkTimestamp (0x6fbe9300): Last network activity timestamp\n- g_dwPostGameStateFlags (0x6fbe9268): Post-game state flags\n\nOrdinal Functions:\n- D2Net.Ordinal_10026: Network tick processing\n- D2Net.Ordinal_10003: Single-player/TCP tick handler\n- D2Net.Ordinal_10008: Receive packet data into buffer",
