      "comment": "Initialize monster data tables and load monster data files.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Clear monster transform array (575 entries x 8 bytes = 4600 bytes at 6fbe9308)\n2. Initialize each array entry with DWORD pairs, filling 1150 DWORDs total\n3. Loop through all monster indices (0 to array end at 6fbea500)\n4. For each monster index, call Ordinal_10582 to get monster data pointer\n5. If monster data exists, read bytes at offsets 0x16d and 0x16e\n6. Combine bytes: high_byte * 256 + low_byte to form transform value\n7. Store transform value in current array position, advance by 8 bytes\n8. Set terminator at 6fbea500 to 0\n9. Load RandTransforms.dat file using FUN_6fb99358\n10. If file loads successfully, read 7680 bytes into buffer at 6fbea508\n11. Close RandTransforms.dat file and set loaded flag at 6fbec308\n12. Load GreenBlood.dat file using FUN_6fb99358\n13. If file loads successfully, allocate 256-byte buffer using Ordinal_10042\n14. If allocation fails, trigger fatal error with file/line info\n15. Clear allocated buffer (64 DWORDs = 256 bytes)\n16. Read 256 bytes from GreenBlood.dat into allocated buffer\n17. Close GreenBlood.dat file and store buffer pointer at 6fbec30c\n\nParameters:\n  None\n\nReturns:\n  void - Function performs initialization, no return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If monster data pointer is NULL, stores 0 for transform value\n  - If RandTransforms.dat fails to load, transform array remains initialized but data buffer stays unloaded\n  - If GreenBlood.dat fails to load, green blood data stays NULL\n  - Memory allocation failure for green blood triggers fatal error and program termination\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x47e (1150) - Number of DWORDs to initialize in transform array\n  0x16d (365) - Offset to low byte of monster transform value in monster structure\n  0x16e (366) - Offset to high byte of monster transform value in monster structure  \n  0x1e00 (7680) - Size in bytes of RandTransforms.dat data to read\n  0x50 (80) - Size in DWORDs for green blood buffer allocation (80*4=320 bytes)\n  0x100 (256) - Size in bytes of GreenBlood.dat data to read\n  0x40 (64) - Number of DWORDs to clear in green blood buffer (64*4=256 bytes)\n\nError Handling:\n  - Ordinal_10582 returns NULL: Store 0 transform value, continue processing\n  - File open failure: Skip file processing, leave data uninitialized\n  - Memory allocation failure: Call error handler Ordinal_10023, terminate with FUN_6fb9a10f(-1)\n\nStructure Layout:\nMonster data structure (accessed at offsets from Ordinal_10582 result):\nOffset  Size  Field Name        Type    Description\n0x16d   1     transformLowByte  byte    Low byte of monster transform value\n0x16e   1     transformHighByte byte    High byte of monster transform value",
