      "comment": "Comprehensive resource cleanup and shutdown routine for linked list management and memory buffers.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if linked list head pointer (DAT_6fbea500) is non-null\n2. If list exists, traverse each node using next pointer at offset +0x1004\n3. For each node, call Ordinal_10043(0x85, 0) - likely resource cleanup API\n4. Continue until reaching end of list (next pointer is null)\n5. Clear the list head pointer to null (DAT_6fbea500 = 0)\n6. Initialize memory clearing loop from 0x6fbe930c to 0x6fbea504\n7. Clear each dword (4 bytes) in the memory region with stride of 8 bytes\n8. Continue until reaching end address 0x6fbea504\n9. Check if cleanup flag (DAT_6fbec30c) is set\n10. If flag set, call Ordinal_10043(0x91, 0) - final cleanup API call\n11. Clear the cleanup flag to zero (DAT_6fbec30c = 0)\n12. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If list head is null, skips list traversal (steps 2-4)\n- If cleanup flag is zero, skips final API call (steps 10-11)\n- Memory clearing always occurs regardless of list/flag states\n- Function handles empty list gracefully without errors\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n- 0x85: First cleanup command for Ordinal_10043 API\n- 0x91: Second cleanup command for Ordinal_10043 API  \n- 0x1004: Offset to next pointer in linked list nodes (4100 bytes)\n- 0x6fbe930c: Start address of memory region to clear\n- 0x6fbea500: Global linked list head pointer address\n- 0x6fbea504: End address of memory clearing region\n- 0x6fbec30c: Global cleanup completion flag address\n\nError Handling:\n- No explicit error checking - assumes all operations succeed\n- Ordinal_10043 API calls may handle internal errors silently\n- Function designed as unconditional cleanup routine",
