      "comment": "Loads monster-specific palette shift data for character visualization\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Retrieve unit pointer using unit ID parameter via Ordinal_10582()\n2. Extract character ID from unit structure (bytes at +0x16d/+0x16e)\n3. Check existing palette cache list (DAT_6fbea500) for character ID match\n4. Return early if palette data already loaded for this character ID\n5. Construct file path by concatenating \"Data\\Global\\Monsters\\\" + character name + \"\\Cof\\palshift.dat\"\n6. Open palette file using FUN_6fb99358() and verify successful load\n7. Allocate palette data structure (0x402 integers = 0x1008 bytes) via Ordinal_10042()\n8. Initialize allocated memory to zero (0x402 * 4 bytes)\n9. Load palette data from file using FUN_6fb99435() and close file\n10. Apply special palette transformation for character type 0x02 (8 iterations, 0xff entries each)\n11. Store character ID in first dword of palette structure\n12. Link new palette entry to global cache list (DAT_6fbea500)\n13. Update palette lookup table starting at DAT_6fbe930c for quick access\n\nParameters:\ndwUnitId - Unit identifier used to locate unit structure and extract character information\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value, operates by side effect on global palette cache\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Early return if character ID already has palette data loaded\n- Fatal error via FUN_6fb9a10f(0xffffffff) if palette memory allocation fails\n- Special palette processing for character type 0x02 with 8x256 color transformation\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x16d/0x16e - Character ID bytes in unit structure (little-endian word)\n0x344 - Character type field in unit structure  \n0x401 - Next pointer offset in palette cache entry (0x1004 bytes)\n0x402 - Size of palette data array (1026 integers)\n0x801 - Palette data section offset for color transformation\n0x800 - Base offset for palette lookup during transformation\n0x40 - Stride for color transformation loops (64 bytes)\n0x02 - Character type requiring special palette processing\n0xe9 - Error code passed to Ordinal_10042() for memory allocation\n0xea - Line number for fatal error reporting\n0x200 - Size of color transformation array\n0x201 - Destination offset for transformed palette data\n\nStructure Layout:\nPalette Cache Entry:\nOffset  Size  Field Name    Type    Description\n0x00    4     dwCharId      dword   Character identifier from unit +0x16d/+0x16e\n0x04    1024  aPaletteData  int[256] Primary palette color mapping\n0x404   1024  aTransformed  int[256] Transformed palette for character type 0x02  \n0x804   4     pNext         ptr     Pointer to next cache entry (offset 0x401 words)\n\nError Handling:\n- File load failure: Silent return without palette creation\n- Memory allocation failure: Fatal termination via FUN_6fb9a10f(0xffffffff)\n- Invalid unit ID: Handled by Ordinal_10582() returning null pointer\n- Character type validation: Only type 0x02 receives palette transformation",
