      "comment": "Cleanup and reset all monster data management systems during shutdown.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Traverse the linked list of active monster data nodes from g_pMonsterDataHead\n2. For each node, call Ordinal_10043(0x110, 0) to release resources\n3. Follow the next pointer at offset 0x1004 to continue traversal\n4. Continue until reaching the end of the linked list (next pointer is NULL)\n5. Reset the global head pointer g_pMonsterDataHead to NULL\n6. Zero out the entire monster data array g_adMonsterDataArray (4600 bytes)\n7. Iterate through array in 8-byte chunks, setting each uint pair to 0\n8. Call FUN_6fadde20() to cleanup specific monster resource types:\n   - 0x16b: Unknown monster resource type 363\n   - 0x16c: Unknown monster resource type 364\n   - 0x1a4: Unknown monster resource type 420\n   - 0x1a5: Unknown monster resource type 421\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value, function performs cleanup operations\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If g_pMonsterDataHead is NULL, skips linked list cleanup\n- Array clearing always occurs regardless of linked list state\n- Resource cleanup calls always occur after array clearing\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x1004 (4100) - Offset to next pointer in MonsterDataNode structure\n0x110 (272) - Resource type parameter passed to Ordinal_10043 for cleanup\n0x16b (363) - Monster resource type identifier for cleanup\n0x16c (364) - Monster resource type identifier for cleanup\n0x1a4 (420) - Monster resource type identifier for cleanup\n0x1a5 (421) - Monster resource type identifier for cleanup\n\nStructure Layout:\nMonsterDataNode (4104 bytes total):\nOffset  Size  Field Name  Type                Description\n0x0000  4100  data        byte[4100]         Monster data payload\n0x1004     4  pNext       MonsterDataNode*   Pointer to next node in linked list\n\nError Handling:\nNo explicit error handling - assumes all operations succeed during shutdown.",
