      "comment": "Retrieves pointer to transform data based on transform type and index\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate input transform info - must have type 1 (active transform)\n2. Look up base offset from transform table at index param[1] * 2\n3. Return NULL if no valid offset found in table\n4. Get transform type using helper function FUN_6fb62950\n5. For transform types 0-1: validate index range 363-364 (0x16B-0x16C)\n6. For color mode enabled: return base + type*256 + 0x804 offset\n7. For transform types 2-7: check color mode and return appropriate offset\n8. For transform types 8+: validate global flag DAT_6fbec308\n9. Adjust type index (subtract 8) and validate range 0-29 (0x1E)\n10. Return pointer to 256-byte transform blocks in DAT_6fbea508 array\n11. Default case: return base + type*256 + 4 offset\n\nParameters:\npTransformInfo - Pointer to transform info structure with type and index fields\n                 Field 0: Transform type (must be 1 for validation)\n                 Field 1: Transform index for table lookup\n\nReturns:\nNon-NULL - Pointer to transform data block (256-byte aligned)\nNULL     - Invalid transform type, index out of range, or no data available\n\nSpecial Cases:\nTransform types 0-1 require index in range 363-364 (0x16B-0x16C)\nTransform types 8+ require global flag DAT_6fbec308 to be non-zero\nIndex range 0-29 for adjusted transform types (original - 8)\nColor mode affects offset calculation: +0x804 when enabled, +4 when disabled\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x16B (363) - Minimum valid index for transform types 0-1\n0x16C (364) - Maximum valid index for transform types 0-1  \n0x100 (256) - Transform data block size and stride multiplier\n0x804 (2052) - Color mode enabled offset addition\n0x04 (4) - Color mode disabled offset addition\n0x1E (30) - Maximum adjusted transform type index\n0x08 (8) - Transform type adjustment offset\n\nError Handling:\nReturns NULL for invalid transform type (not 1)\nReturns NULL for zero offset in transform table lookup\nReturns NULL for index out of valid range (types 0-1)\nCalls error handler Ordinal_10023 and terminates for invalid adjusted type range\n\nNote: Function uses 2 phantom variables (extraout_var, extraout_var_00) from CONCAT31 \noperations that were optimized away by decompiler but represent high bytes of EAX \nregister from IsColorModeEnabled() function calls",
