      "comment": "Calculate animation frame value with offset adjustment for unit processing.\nThis function retrieves the base frame count from animation context and adds a fixed offset.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize animation state by calling Ordinal_10913\n2. Retrieve base frame count from animation context via Ordinal_10918  \n3. Add fixed offset of 9 to the base frame result\n4. Return the adjusted frame value for animation processing\n\nParameters:\npUnit - Pointer to UnitAny structure containing animation and path context\nnFrameOffset - IMPLICIT in EDX: 16-bit frame offset value used in calculations\n\nReturns:\nSuccess: Calculated frame value (base frame count + 9 offset)\nNo error conditions detected - function always returns valid frame value\n\nSpecial Cases:\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x9 (9) - Fixed frame adjustment offset added to base calculation\n0x4 - UnitAny structure field offset for dwClassId or similar identifier\n0x2C (44) - UnitAny structure field offset for pPath or animation context\n\nStructure Layout:\nUnitAny structure access pattern observed:\nOffset | Size | Field Name | Type | Description\n0x04   | 4    | dwClassId  | uint | Class identifier for unit type\n0x2C   | 4    | pPath      | void*| Path or animation context pointer\n\nAlgorithm Verification:\nStep 1: Initialize animation state -> CALL Ordinal_10913 at 0x6fade1c2\nStep 2: Get base frame count -> CALL Ordinal_10918 at 0x6fade1ce\nStep 3: Add frame offset -> ADD EAX,0x9 at 0x6fade1d3 \nStep 4: Return adjusted value -> RET instruction at 0x6fade1d7",
