      "globals": ["0x11E278|g_dwExceptionHandlerInitialized|0x0", "0xE354|switchdataD_6fade354|0x0", "0xE348|switchdataD_6fade348|6fade2bf", "0xDFFE0|g_pCurrentLogBuffer|6fbec328", "0x11E268|g_nRecordsToRead|0x0", "0xFFFFFFFF90530000||", "0x11E270|g_pGameContextListHead|00000000", "0xFFFFFFFF90530004||", "0xE448|switchdataD_6fade448|6fade2d2", "0xFFFFFFFF90530018||"],
      "api_count": 2,
      "api_calls": ["FogMemAlloc", "FogMemAlloc"],
      "instructions": ["0xE1F0|MOV|EAX, [0x6fbee278]", "0xE1F5|PUSH|EBX", "0xE1F6|PUSH|ESI", "0xE1F7|XOR|ESI, ESI", "0xE1F9|PUSH|EDI", "0xE1FA|CMP|EAX, ESI", "0xE1FC|MOV|EBX, EDX", "0xE1FE|MOV|EDI, ECX", "0xE200|JZ|0x6fade340", "0xE206|CMP|EDI, 0x111", "0xE20C|JA|0x6fade2a9", "0xE212|JZ|0x6fade2bf", "0xE218|LEA|EAX, [EDI + -0x10]", "0xE21B|CMP|EAX, 0xf2", "0xE220|JA|0x6fade340"],
      "comment": "Logs Windows messages to circular buffer for debugging purposes\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if message logging is enabled (g_fMessageLoggingEnabled)\n2. Filter messages by ID to log only specific Windows messages\n3. Handle WM_COMMAND (0x111): Log mouse clicks, keyboard input, and controls\n4. Handle WM_KEYDOWN (0x100): Log keystroke events\n5. Handle mouse messages (0x200-0x205): Log mouse movement and clicks\n6. Handle window messages (0x10, 0x101, 0x102): Log window focus/paint events\n7. Check if current log buffer has space (500 entries max)\n8. If buffer full, allocate new 8000-byte buffer using Ordinal_10042\n9. Chain new buffer to previous buffer via linked list\n10. Calculate entry address using current index * 16 bytes per entry\n11. Get timestamp from GetGlobalFrameCounter()\n12. Store log entry: timestamp, message ID, wParam, lParam\n13. Increment buffer index for next entry\n\nParameters:\ndwMessageId - Windows message identifier (WM_KEYDOWN, WM_COMMAND, etc.)\ndwWParam - First message parameter (virtual key codes, control IDs)\ndwLParam - Second message parameter (key state, control handles)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\nBuffer allocation when exceeding 500 entries (0x1f4)\nLinked list management for multiple log buffers\nMessage filtering for performance (only logs specific message types)\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x100 - WM_KEYDOWN message ID\n0x111 - WM_COMMAND message ID  \n0x200-0x205 - Mouse message range (WM_MOUSEMOVE to WM_RBUTTONDBLCLK)\n0x10 - WM_CLOSE message ID\n0x101 - WM_KEYUP message ID\n0x102 - WM_CHAR message ID\n0x1f4 - Maximum entries per buffer (500 decimal)\n0x35 - Allocation type for Ordinal_10042\n8000 - Offset to current index in buffer structure (0x1f40)\n0x1f44 - Offset to reserved field in buffer structure\n0x1f48 - Offset to next buffer pointer in buffer structure\n\nStructure Layout:\nMessageLogBuffer (at g_pCurrentLogBuffer):\nOffset  Size  Field Name        Type    Description\n8000    4     dwCurrentIndex    uint    Current log entry index (0-499)\n8004    4     dwReserved1       uint    Reserved field (always 0)\n8008    4     pNextBuffer       void*   Pointer to next buffer in chain\n\nMessageLogEntry (16 bytes per entry):\nOffset  Size  Field Name        Type    Description\n0       4     dwTimestamp       uint    Frame counter timestamp\n4       4     dwMessageId       uint    Windows message identifier\n8       4     dwParam2          uint    wParam from Windows message\n12      4     dwParam3          uint    lParam from Windows message",
      "tags": ["SRC_Record.cpp", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PARAM_3", "MOD_GAME"]
    },
