      "instructions": ["0xE460|SUB|ESP, 0x1c", "0xE463|PUSH|EBX", "0xE464|PUSH|ESI", "0xE465|PUSH|EDI", "0xE466|PUSH|0x0", "0xE468|PUSH|0x80", "0xE46D|PUSH|0x2", "0xE46F|PUSH|0x0", "0xE471|PUSH|0x0", "0xE473|PUSH|0x40000000", "0xE478|PUSH|0x6fbb0018", "0xE47D|CALL|dword ptr [0x6fba6084]", "0xE483|MOV|EDX, dword ptr [0x6fbee270]", "0xE489|MOV|EDI, EAX", "0xE48B|MOV|EAX, 0x1"],
      "comment": "Creates a data record file and writes linked data structures to disk\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Open record file \"Record_dr1\" with write access using CreateFileA\n2. Initialize node counter to 1 and set header record counts\n3. Traverse linked list starting from g_pFirstDataNode (0x6fbee270)\n   - Count total nodes by following pNext pointers (+0x1f48 offset)\n   - Increment counter for each valid node\n4. Calculate final record size: base size + node_count * 500 - 500\n5. Get current frame counter from game engine\n6. Get render context information via Ordinal_10089\n7. Write record header (20 bytes) containing size and count information\n8. Write extended header (20 bytes) with frame and render data\n9. Iterate through all data nodes starting from g_pFirstDataNode\n   - Write each node's data buffer (size << 4 bytes from +0x1f40 offset)\n   - Follow pNext pointer to next node (+0x1f48 offset)\n   - Continue until pNext is NULL\n10. Close file handle and return\n\nParameters:\nNone (void function using global data)\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x40000000 - GENERIC_WRITE file access\n0x02 - CREATE_ALWAYS disposition \n0x80 - FILE_ATTRIBUTE_NORMAL\n0x1f40 (8000) - Offset to data size field in DataRecordNode\n0x1f48 (8008) - Offset to pNext pointer in DataRecordNode\n0x14 (20) - Size of record headers\n500 - Size multiplier for final calculation\n\nStructure Layout:\nDataRecordNode (8012 bytes total):\nOffset   Size    Field Name     Type                Description\n+0x0000  8000    dataBuffer     byte[8000]         Raw data storage\n+0x1f40  4       nDataSize      uint               Size of valid data\n+0x1f44  4       dwReserved     uint               Reserved/padding\n+0x1f48  4       pNext          DataRecordNode*    Next node pointer\n\nError Handling:\n- No explicit error checking on file operations\n- Assumes valid linked list structure\n- Does not validate file write success",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Inventory", "PARAM_0", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
