      "comment": "Process all game contexts in the global linked list by notifying subsystems.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load head pointer from global game context list (g_pGameContextListHead)\n2. Check if list is not empty (head pointer non-null)\n3. For each context in linked list:\n   a. Store current context pointer for iteration\n   b. Load next context pointer from offset 0x1f48 before processing\n   c. Call Ordinal_10043 with parameters (0x120, 0) to notify subsystem\n   d. Continue to next context until end of list (null pointer)\n4. Return when all contexts processed\n\nParameters:\nNone - operates on global game context linked list\n\nReturns:\nvoid - no return value, processing function only\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x1f48 (8008) - Offset within GameContext structure for next pointer in linked list\n0x120 (288) - First parameter to Ordinal_10043, likely message ID or notification type  \n0 - Second parameter to Ordinal_10043, likely flags or additional data (none)\n\nStructure Layout:\nGameContext structure (60164 bytes total):\nOffset   Size  Field Name       Type            Description\n0x1f48   4     pNext           GameContext *   Next context pointer for linked list traversal\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Empty list (g_pGameContextListHead == NULL) causes immediate return\n- Single context with NULL next pointer processes once then exits  \n- Function safely handles circular references by advancing pointer before call",
      "tags": ["SRC_Record.cpp", "PARAM_0", "MOD_GAME", "PROP_SMALL"]
