      "instructions": ["0xE590|MOV|EAX, [0x6fbee274]", "0xE595|SUB|ESP, 0x8", "0xE598|PUSH|EBX", "0xE599|PUSH|EBP", "0xE59A|PUSH|ESI", "0xE59B|PUSH|EDI", "0xE59C|XOR|EDI, EDI", "0xE59E|CMP|EAX, EDI", "0xE5A0|JZ|0x6fade5b0", "0xE5A2|MOV|dword ptr [0x6fbee274], EDI", "0xE5A8|POP|EDI", "0xE5A9|POP|ESI", "0xE5AA|POP|EBP", "0xE5AB|POP|EBX", "0xE5AC|ADD|ESP, 0x8"],
      "comment": "Reads demo recording file (Record.dr1) and loads message log buffers.\n\nClassification: Worker function - performs file I/O and buffer chain initialization\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check g_dwStateInitPending; if set, clear it and return early (deferred init)\n2. Set g_dwStateActive = 1 to indicate active reading state\n3. Open \"Record.dr1\" file with GENERIC_READ access\n4. Read 4-byte file version into dwFileVersion (discarded)\n5. Read 0x14 (20) bytes file header into g_sgtReadFileHeader structure\n6. If header version (g_sgtReadFileHeader) != 1, disable recording and exit\n7. Loop through g_nFileHeaderHolders buffer holders:\n   a. For index > 0: Allocate 0x1F4C (8012) byte buffer via FogMemAlloc\n   b. Initialize buffer fields at offsets +0x1F40, +0x1F44, +0x1F48 to 0\n   c. Link new buffer to chain via g_pCurrentLogBuffer->pNext\n   d. Update g_pCurrentLogBuffer to new buffer\n8. Determine records to read: min(g_nFileHeaderRecords, 500)\n9. Assert if partial buffer (records < 500) is not the last holder\n10. Read (g_nRecordsToRead * 16) bytes into current buffer\n11. Reset g_pCurrentLogBuffer to &g_aLogBufferStart after loading\n12. Close file handle\n13. Call Ordinal_10010 (Fog.dll) to finalize state\n\nParameters: None (uses global state)\n\nReturns: void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Early exit if g_dwStateInitPending is set (deferred initialization)\n- File version 1 required; other versions disable recording (g_dwStateActive=0, g_dwGlobalFlag=0)\n- Partial buffer assertion: last holder must contain remaining records\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x1F4C (8012): Size of MessageLogBuffer allocation\n- 0x1F40 (8000): Offset to nRecordCount field in buffer\n- 0x1F44 (8004): Offset to nRecordWritePos field in buffer\n- 0x1F48 (8008): Offset to pNext pointer in buffer\n- 0x1F4 (500): Maximum records per buffer\n- 0x14 (20): File header structure size\n- 0x10 (16): Size of each record entry\n\nStructure Layout (MessageLogBuffer at 0x1F4C bytes):\nOffset   Size   Field           Type       Description\n0x0000   8000   aRecords        byte[8000] Record data (500 x 16-byte entries)\n0x1F40   4      nRecordCount    uint       Number of records in buffer\n0x1F44   4      nRecordWritePos uint       Current write position\n0x1F48   4      pNext           void*      Pointer to next buffer in chain\n\nGlobals Used:\n- g_dwStateInitPending (0x6FBEE274): Deferred init flag\n- g_dwStateActive (0x6FBEE27C): Recording active flag\n- g_pCurrentLogBuffer (0x6FBAFFE0): Current buffer pointer\n- g_pLogBufferChain (0x6FBAFFE4): Buffer chain anchor\n- g_sgtReadFileHeader (0x6FBEC310): File header structure\n- g_nFileHeaderHolders (0x6FBEC314): Number of buffer holders\n- g_nFileHeaderRecords (0x6FBEC318): Records in last holder\n- g_nRecordsToRead (0x6FBEE268): Records to read this iteration\n- g_aLogBufferStart (0x6FBEC328): Static buffer start address\n- g_dwGlobalFlag (0x6FBEE280): Global recording flag",
      "tags": ["SRC_Record.cpp", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PARAM_0", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "MOD_GAME", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
