      "comment": "Exception handler callback invoked during structured exception handling\n\nClassification: Callback/Handler - registered by InitializeExceptionHandler\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call WriteDataRecordToFile to persist game state before handling exception\n2. Check if previous exception handler exists (g_dwPreviousExceptionHandler != 0)\n3. If previous handler exists, chain to it with same parameters\n4. Return (exception may continue propagating via previous handler)\n\nParameters:\ndwExceptionCode (uint) - Exception code identifying the exception type\ndwExceptionFlags (uint) - Exception flags (continuable, noncontinuable, etc.)\npContextRecord (CONTEXT *) - Pointer to CONTEXT structure with CPU state\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Control transfers to previous handler or returns\n\nCaller Analysis:\nSingle reference from InitializeExceptionHandler at 0x6fade730\nRegistered via ExchangeExceptionHandler as the active exception handler\nStored at g_dwPreviousExceptionHandler for handler chaining\n\nHandler Chain:\nThis handler always runs WriteDataRecordToFile first to save state\nThen chains to any previously installed handler\nEnsures data persistence even during crash scenarios\n\nReferenced Globals:\ng_dwPreviousExceptionHandler (0x6fbec324) - Previous handler function pointer",
      "tags": ["PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_3", "PROP_SMALL"]
