      "comment": "Toggles the global state active flag between active and pending initialization.\n\nClassification: Internal utility / State toggle\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Read g_dwStateActive flag from memory\n2. If state is currently active (non-zero):\n   a. Clear g_dwStateActive to 0 (deactivate)\n   b. Return\n3. If state is not active (zero):\n   a. Set g_dwStateInitPending to 1 (request initialization)\n   b. Return\n\nParameters: None (void)\n\nReturns: void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Function never sets g_dwStateActive to 1 directly; it only clears it\n- Activation is requested via g_dwStateInitPending flag\n- Another function (likely initialization routine) monitors g_dwStateInitPending\n  and sets g_dwStateActive when initialization completes\n\nRelated Globals:\n- g_dwStateActive (0x6fbee27c): Current active state flag\n- g_dwStateInitPending (0x6fbee274): Initialization request flag\n\nCross-References:\n- Called by: ResetGlobalStateWrapper (0x6fad1d60)\n- g_dwStateActive also accessed by: GetGlobalState, ReadDemoRecordFileInternal\n- g_dwStateInitPending also accessed by: GetGlobalState, ReadDemoRecordFileInternal",
