      "instructions": ["0xE7A0|MOV|EAX, [0x6fbee280]", "0xE7A5|SUB|ESP, 0x8", "0xE7A8|PUSH|EBX", "0xE7A9|XOR|EBX, EBX", "0xE7AB|PUSH|ESI", "0xE7AC|CMP|EAX, EBX", "0xE7AE|PUSH|EDI", "0xE7AF|JZ|0x6fade7cf", "0xE7B1|CMP|dword ptr [0x6fbaffe0], EBX", "0xE7B7|JZ|0x6fade7cf", "0xE7B9|CALL|0x6fadb860", "0xE7BE|MOV|EDI, EAX", "0xE7C0|MOV|EAX, [0x6fbec31c]", "0xE7C5|CMP|EDI, EAX", "0xE7C7|JL|0x6fade7d6"],
      "comment": "Process pending message log records from the global log buffer chain.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate global logging state (g_dwGlobalFlag and g_pCurrentLogBuffer)\n2. Get current game frame counter and compare against log threshold (0x6fbec31c)\n3. Check if current buffer has unprocessed records (0x1f44 vs 0x1f40)\n4. For each unprocessed record in 16-byte MessageLogEntry format:\n   a. Validate record frame matches current frame (corruption detection)\n   b. Extract record parameters from offsets +4, +8, +12\n   c. Call Ordinal_10027 to prepare record for processing\n   d. Call Ordinal_412 to execute the actual record processing\n   e. Increment processed record count (0x1f44)\n   f. Check if buffer is exhausted or chain continues (0x1f48)\n5. Handle buffer chain traversal when current buffer reaches 500 record limit\n6. Terminate processing when frame threshold exceeded or null buffer reached\n\nParameters:\nNo input parameters - operates on global log buffer state\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Processing continues until buffer exhausted or frame limit reached\n\nSpecial Cases:\nFrame limit exceeded (dwCurrentFrame >= 0x6fbec31c): Sets g_dwGlobalFlag = 0 to disable logging\nBuffer corruption detected: Calls error handler with code 0x12a then terminates (0xffffffff)\nRecord overflow (>499 records): Calls error handler with code 0x189 then terminates (0xffffffff)\nBuffer chain exhaustion: Returns normally when g_pCurrentLogBuffer becomes null\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x1f44 (8004): Offset to current record read index in log buffer\n0x1f48 (8008): Offset to next buffer pointer in chain structure  \n0x1f40 (8000): Offset to total record count in current buffer\n0x10 (16): Size of each MessageLogEntry record structure\n0x1f4 (500): Maximum records per buffer before chain advancement\n0x189 (393): Error code for record count overflow\n0x12a (298): Error code for frame validation failure\n0x6fbec31c: Global frame threshold for log processing cutoff\n0x6fbee280: Address of g_dwGlobalFlag control variable\n0x6fbaffe0: Address of g_pCurrentLogBuffer pointer\n\nStructure Layout:\nMessageLogEntry (16 bytes):\nOffset | Size | Field Name | Type | Description\n0x00   | 4    | dwFrame    | uint | Game frame when record was created\n0x04   | 4    | dwParam1   | uint | First processing parameter  \n0x08   | 4    | dwParam2   | uint | Second processing parameter\n0x0C   | 4    | dwParam3   | uint | Third processing parameter\n\nMessageLogBuffer Structure (partial):\nOffset | Size | Field Name      | Type | Description\n0x1F40 | 4    | nTotalRecords   | int  | Total records in this buffer\n0x1F44 | 4    | nReadIndex      | int  | Current read position (0-499)\n0x1F48 | 4    | pNextBuffer     | ptr  | Pointer to next buffer in chain",
      "tags": ["SRC_Record.cpp", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PARAM_0", "STRUCT_Other", "PROP_LOOPHEAVY", "MOD_GAME"]
