      "comment": "Add player action to the action queue, managing node allocation and queue processing\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate player ID (-1 triggers fatal error with debug info)\n2. Search active queue (DAT_6fbee284) for existing node with matching player ID\n3. If found with matching player name, update existing node fields\n4. If not found, search free queue (DAT_6fbee288) for available node\n5. Allocate new node (0xd5 = 213 bytes) if no free nodes available\n6. Initialize node with zero fill (0x21 * 4 = 132 bytes cleared)\n7. Set node timestamp via FUN_6fb82290 (system time function)\n8. Copy player name to node start with optimized string copy (MOVSD/MOVSB)\n9. Set node fields: player ID (+0x10), action param (+0x1c), action type (+0x20), priority (+0x22), data (+0x30), flags (+0x44)\n10. Copy event name to node (+0x46) with optimized string copy\n11. Copy target name to node (+0x4a) with optimized string copy\n12. Set description field (+0x66): player name if event name empty, otherwise formatted string\n13. Link node to front of active queue (DAT_6fbee284)\n14. Get current player via FUN_6fb62880, extract ID from offset +8\n15. Find current player in queue and extract priority (+0x22)\n16. Process entire queue with FUN_6fadf420/FUN_6fadf4c0 cleanup operations\n17. Execute queue management functions: FUN_6fadf5f0, FUN_6fadf580, FUN_6fadf780, FUN_6fadf480\n18. Handle special case for priority -1 with FUN_6fadf7d0\n19. Final cleanup with FUN_6fb30200\n\nParameters:\nnPlayerId - Player identifier (int, -1 triggers fatal error)\ndwActionParam - Action-specific parameter value (uint)\npbPlayerName - Player name string (byte*, copied to node start)\nwActionType - Type of action being queued (ushort, stored at +0x20)\nwPriority - Action priority level (ushort, stored at +0x22)\ndwData - Additional action data (uint, stored at +0x30)\ndwTimestamp - Timestamp parameter (uint, stored at +0x14 but overwritten with FUN_6fb82290)\nwFlags - Action flags (ushort, stored at +0x44)\nlpszEventName - Event name string (char*, copied to +0x46)\nlpszTargetName - Target name string (char*, copied to +0x4a)\nIMPLICIT: ECX = nPlayerId, EDX = dwActionParam\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\nPlayer ID -1 triggers fatal error with debug output and program termination\nEmpty event name causes player name to be copied to description field\nNon-empty event name triggers formatted string creation at +0x66\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x6fbee284 - Global pointer to active queue head\n0x6fbee288 - Global pointer to free queue head  \n0x6fbee28c - Global pointer to processing queue\n0xd5 (213) - Node allocation size in bytes\n0x21 (33) - DWORDs to clear during initialization (132 bytes)\n0x10 - Player ID field offset\n0x1c - Action parameter field offset\n0x20 - Action type field offset  \n0x22 - Priority field offset\n0x30 - Data field offset\n0x34 - Timestamp field offset\n0x44 - Flags field offset\n0x46 - Event name field offset\n0x4a - Target name field offset\n0x66 - Description field offset\n0x80 - Next pointer field offset\n-1 (0xffff) - Default priority when current player not found\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset  Size  Field Name       Type                Description\n0x00    16    playerName      byte[16]            Player name string\n0x10    4     playerId        int                 Player identifier\n0x1c    4     actionParam     uint                Action parameter\n0x20    2     actionType      ushort              Action type code\n0x22    2     priority        ushort              Priority level\n0x30    4     data            uint                Additional data\n0x34    4     timestamp       uint                System timestamp\n0x44    2     flags           ushort              Action flags\n0x46    4     eventName       byte[4]             Event name string  \n0x4a    28    targetName      byte[28]            Target name string\n0x66    26    description     byte[26]            Description string\n0x80    4     pNext           PlayerActionNode*   Next node pointer",
