      "comment": "Searches a linked list for a specific integer value.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract linked list head pointer from UnitAny's list head field at offset +0x38\n2. Begin traversal starting from head node\n3. Check if current node is NULL (end of list reached)\n4. If NULL, return 0 (value not found)\n5. Compare current node's data value with search target\n6. If values match, return 1 (value found)\n7. Advance to next node using next pointer at offset +0x4\n8. Repeat from step 3 until match found or list exhausted\n\nParameters:\npUnit (UnitAny*): Pointer to UnitAny object containing linked list head at offset +0x38\nnSearchValue (int): Integer value to search for in linked list nodes\n\nReturns:\n1 if search value found in any list node\n0 if search value not found or list is empty\n\nStructure Layout:\nListNode (8 bytes):\nOffset  Size  Field     Type    Description\n+0x0    4     data      int     Node data value\n+0x4    4     next      ptr     Pointer to next ListNode\n\nUnitAny with List Head (partial):\nOffset  Size  Field     Type         Description  \n+0x38   4     listHead  ListNode*    Head pointer of linked list",
