      "comment": "Cleanup and release all player action queue structures and associated memory.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Traverse primary action queue (DAT_6fbee284) linked list by following +0x80 next pointers\n2. For each queue node: call FUN_6fb822d0 to cleanup data pointer at +0x34 offset\n3. Traverse secondary action list at +0x38 offset, following +0x4 next pointers\n4. For each action in secondary list: call Ordinal_10043(0x10d, 0) to free memory blocks\n5. Clear queue node's action list pointer (+0x38) and call Ordinal_10043(0x14a, 0) to free node\n6. Move to next queue node via +0x80 pointer until end of chain\n7. Clear global primary queue head pointer (DAT_6fbee284) \n8. Repeat steps 1-6 for secondary action queue (DAT_6fbee288) using same structure layout\n9. Clear global secondary queue head pointer (DAT_6fbee288)\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\nEmpty queues (NULL globals) are handled gracefully by initial NULL checks\nBroken chain links are handled by NULL pointer checks in while loops\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x34 (52) - Offset to data pointer field in queue node structure\n0x38 (56) - Offset to action list head pointer in queue node structure  \n0x80 (128) - Offset to next queue node pointer in structure\n0x4 - Offset to next action pointer in action list node\n0x10d (269) - Ordinal for memory deallocation function (likely GlobalFree)\n0x14a (330) - Ordinal for queue node deallocation function\n0x156 (342) - Ordinal for secondary queue node deallocation function\n\nStructure Layout:\nQueue Node Structure (minimum 132 bytes):\nOffset  Size  Field Name           Type    Description\n+0x34   4     pData               void*    Pointer to associated data requiring cleanup\n+0x38   4     pActionList         void*    Head of linked action list\n+0x80   4     pNextQueueNode      void*    Next queue node in chain\n\nAction List Node Structure (minimum 8 bytes):\nOffset  Size  Field Name           Type    Description  \