      "comment": "Inserts a string node into a lexicographically ordered binary search tree.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate input node pointer - return early if NULL\n2. Initialize traversal state: previous node as NULL, current node as input\n3. Calculate pointer to next field at offset 0x80 from current node\n4. Retrieve next node from current->pNext field\n5. If no previous node exists, jump to insertion point setup\n6. Begin comparison loop with current node's key string\n7. Compare characters byte-by-byte using lexicographical ordering\n8. For equal characters, advance both string pointers by 2 bytes\n9. Continue comparison until null terminator or difference found\n10. Calculate comparison result: -1 (less), 0 (equal), 1 (greater)\n11. If current key < previous key, traverse to next node in tree\n12. Update traversal pointers: parent, iterator, continue search\n13. If traversal reaches end (next node is NULL), prepare insertion\n14. At insertion point: either root insertion or parent link update\n15. For root insertion: set tree root to previous node, link input as next\n16. For parent insertion: update parent->pNext to previous->pNext, link nodes\n17. Set current node to next node, continue processing if not NULL\n18. Return to step 3 for next iteration\n\nParameters:\npNode (StringTreeNode *): Node to insert containing key string and next pointer\n\nReturns:\nvoid: Function performs in-place tree modification\n\nSpecial Cases:\nNULL input: Function returns immediately without modification\nRoot insertion: When previous node is NULL, node becomes new tree root\nLexicographical ordering: Comparison uses byte-by-byte string comparison\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset | Size | Field Name | Type              | Description\n0x00   | 128  | szKey      | char[128]         | Null-terminated key string\n0x80   | 4    | pNext      | StringTreeNode *  | Pointer to next node in tree\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x80 (128): Offset to pNext field in StringTreeNode structure\n0x2: String comparison advancement (2 bytes per iteration)\n0x0: NULL pointer constant for tree traversal termination",
