      "comment": "Inserts a node into a sorted linked list maintaining priority order.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize head pointer to NULL for accumulating processed nodes\n2. Process all nodes in the incoming linked list chain\n3. For each node, get pointer to its next field (offset 0x80)\n4. Store next node reference for continued iteration\n5. If no head yet established, set current node as new head\n6. Otherwise, traverse existing sorted list to find insertion point\n7. Compare node priorities (offset 0x18) to maintain ascending order\n8. Insert node after last node with higher or equal priority\n9. Update list linkage: set current node's next to insertion point's next\n10. Set insertion point's next to current node\n11. Continue until all nodes processed\n\nParameters:\npNodeToInsert - Pointer to SortedListNode to insert (may be chain of nodes)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Function modifies linked list structure in place\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset | Size | Field Name  | Type              | Description\n-------|------|-------------|-------------------|---------------------------\n0x00   | 24   | data        | byte[24]         | Node data payload\n0x18   | 4    | dwPriority  | uint             | Sort priority (ascending)\n0x1C   | 100  | padding1    | byte[100]        | Reserved/padding space\n0x80   | 4    | pNext       | SortedListNode * | Pointer to next node\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- NULL input pointer: Function returns immediately with no operation\n- Single node: Inserted as new head if list was empty\n- Chain insertion: Entire chain processed node by node maintaining individual priorities\n- Equal priorities: New nodes inserted after existing nodes with same priority",
