      "comment": "Search for a node containing a specific short value in a linked list.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize current node pointer to global list head (DAT_6fbee28c)\n2. Check if list head is non-null, return null if empty list\n3. Begin traversal loop through linked list nodes\n4. Compare current node's value (offset 0) with search target\n5. If values match, return pointer to current node\n6. Load next node pointer from current node (offset 8)\n7. Continue loop until next pointer is null\n8. Return null if value not found in any node\n\nParameters:\n- nSearchValue: short value to search for in the linked list\n\nReturns:\n- void *: Pointer to the node containing the target value, or null if not found\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Empty list (head is null): Returns null immediately\n- Value not in list: Returns null after full traversal\n- First node match: Returns immediately without traversal\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset | Size | Field Name | Type    | Description\n-------|------|------------|---------|----------------------------------\n0x00   | 2    | value      | short   | Data value for comparison\n0x02   | 2    | padding    | short   | Alignment padding\n0x04   | 4    | unused     | uint    | Unused field\n0x08   | 4    | next       | void *  | Pointer to next node in list",
