      "comment": "Searches for a short value in the global short list and creates new node if not found.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if global short list head (g_pShortListHead) is null\n2. If not null, traverse linked list comparing each node's value to target\n3. If matching node found, return immediately (no action needed)\n4. If end of list reached without match, proceed to allocation\n5. Allocate new 12-byte ShortListNode using Ordinal_10042 (0x1f9 bytes, flag 0)\n6. Initialize all 6 short fields to zero (clearing 12-byte structure)\n7. Set node's value field to target short value\n8. Link new node as new head: node->pNext = old_head, head = node\n9. Return (void function)\n\nParameters:\n- nValue (short): Target value to search for in linked list\n\nReturns:\n- void: No return value, modifies global list state\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Empty list (g_pShortListHead == NULL): Skips search, proceeds to allocation\n- Value already exists: Early return without allocation (prevents duplicates)\n- Memory allocation failure: Function assumes Ordinal_10042 succeeds\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n- 0x1f9 (505): Memory allocation size parameter for Ordinal_10042\n- 0x0: Flags parameter for Ordinal_10042 (no special allocation flags)\n- 0x8: Offset to next pointer field in ShortListNode structure\n- 12 bytes: Total ShortListNode structure size (6 shorts)\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset | Size | Field Name | Type    | Description\n-------|------|------------|---------|------------------\n0x0    | 2    | nValue     | short   | Stored value\n0x2    | 2    | wPadding   | ushort  | Alignment padding\n0x4    | 4    | reserved1  | uint    | Unused field\n0x8    | 4    | pNext      | void*   | Next node pointer\n\nError Handling:\n- No explicit error checking for allocation failure\n- Assumes Ordinal_10042 always returns valid pointer\n- Function design prevents duplicate values through early return",
