      "comment": "Deallocates all remaining list nodes in the global linked list and calls cleanup routine for each node.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load global list head pointer from g_pListHead (0x6fbee28c)\n2. Check if list is empty (head pointer is NULL)\n3. If empty, explicitly set head pointer to NULL and return\n4. Traverse linked list using next pointer at offset +8\n5. For each node, call Ordinal_10043 cleanup routine with parameters 0x22c and 0\n6. Continue until reaching end of list (next pointer is NULL)\n7. Set global list head pointer to NULL to mark list as empty\n\nParameters:\n  None\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If list is already empty, function safely returns after setting head to NULL\n  - Function assumes all nodes have valid next pointers at offset +8\n  - Cleanup routine Ordinal_10043 is called for each node before deallocation\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x22c (556 decimal) - Cleanup operation code parameter for Ordinal_10043\n  0x0 - Secondary parameter for Ordinal_10043 cleanup routine\n  0x8 - Offset to next pointer in ListNode structure\n\nStructure Layout:\n  ListNode (8 bytes):\n    Offset  Size  Field Name   Type        Description\n    +0x0    4     data         void*       Node data pointer\n    +0x4    4     reserved     uint        Reserved field or additional data\n    +0x8    4     pNext        ListNode*   Pointer to next node in list",
