      "instructions": ["0xF4C0|MOV|EAX, [0x6fbee284]", "0xF4C5|PUSH|ESI", "0xF4C6|XOR|ESI, ESI", "0xF4C8|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0xF4CA|JZ|0x6fadf512", "0xF4CC|PUSH|EBX", "0xF4CD|PUSH|EDI", "0xF4CE|MOV|DX, word ptr [EAX + 0x22]", "0xF4D2|CMP|DX, word ptr [ECX]", "0xF4D5|JNZ|0x6fadf504", "0xF4D7|LEA|EDX, [EAX + 0x80]", "0xF4DD|MOV|EDI, EAX", "0xF4DF|TEST|ESI, ESI", "0xF4E1|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [EDX]", "0xF4E3|JZ|0x6fadf4f5"],
      "comment": "Removes a player node from the global player linked list based on matching player ID.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize previous node tracker to null (pPreviousNode = 0)\n2. Load head of global player list (g_pPlayerListHead) into current node pointer\n3. Check if list is empty - if so, return immediately\n4. Begin traversal loop through linked list nodes\n5. Compare player ID at offset +0x22 with target ID from request\n6. If IDs match (found target node):\n   a. Get pointer to next field (offset +0x80)\n   b. Load next node address from current node\n   c. If no previous node (removing head):\n      - Update global head pointer to next node\n      - Set removed node's next to request's storage pointer\n      - Store removed node address in request's storage pointer\n   d. If has previous node (removing middle/tail):\n      - Update previous node's next pointer to skip current node\n      - Set removed node's next to request's storage pointer  \n      - Store removed node address in request's storage pointer\n7. If IDs don't match:\n   a. Load next node address from current node's next field\n   b. Update previous node tracker to current node\n8. Advance to next node and repeat until end of list\n9. Return (void function)\n\nParameters:\npRequest - PlayerRemovalRequest structure containing:\n  +0x0: wPlayerIdToFind (ushort) - Player ID to search for and remove\n  +0x4: ppRemovedNode (void**) - Pointer to store removed node address\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value, operates by side effect on global list and request structure\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Empty list: Function returns immediately without modification\n- Player not found: List remains unchanged, request storage unmodified\n- Removing head node: Global g_pPlayerListHead updated to new head\n- Single node removal: List becomes empty, g_pPlayerListHead set to null\n\nStructure Layout:\nPlayer node structure (inferred from access patterns):\nOffset | Size | Field Name    | Type    | Description\n+0x22  | 2    | wPlayerId     | ushort  | Unique player identifier\n+0x80  | 4    | pNext         | void*   | Pointer to next player node\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x22 (34 decimal) - Offset to player ID field in player node structure\n0x80 (128 decimal) - Offset to next pointer field in player node structure\n\nGlobal Variables:\ng_pPlayerListHead (0x6fbee284) - Head pointer of global player linked list\n\nAlgorithm Verification:\nThe function implements standard singly-linked list node removal with the following operations:\n- Linear search by key comparison\n- Pointer chain relinking to maintain list integrity  \n- Head pointer update when removing first node\n- Previous node tracking for mid-list removal\n- Result storage in caller-provided structure field",
