      "comment": "Sorts the global linked list of ShortListNode items in ascending order by their ushort values.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if global list head (g_pShortListHead) is NULL, if so, return immediately\n2. Initialize sorted list head pointer to NULL (local accumulator)\n3. While global list is not empty:\n   a. Remove first node from global list and store as nodeToInsert  \n   b. Update global head to next node in chain\n   c. If sorted list is empty, insert nodeToInsert as first element\n   d. Otherwise, traverse sorted list to find correct insertion position:\n      - Compare nodeToInsert value with current node values\n      - Find position where nodeToInsert.value < current.value \n      - Insert nodeToInsert before that position\n   e. Add nodeToInsert to sorted list at correct position\n4. When global list is exhausted, replace global head with sorted list head\n\nParameters:\n- void - Function takes no parameters, operates on global state\n\nReturns:\n- void - Function modifies global state (g_pShortListHead) but returns no value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Empty list (g_pShortListHead == NULL): Function returns immediately, no sorting needed\n- Single node: Node remains in place, no movement required  \n- Equal values: Preserves original order (stable sort)\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset | Size | Field Name | Type            | Description\n-------|------|------------|-----------------|-----------------------------------\n0x0    | 2    | value      | ushort         | Sorting key value\n0x8    | 4    | pNext      | ShortListNode* | Pointer to next node in list\n\nAlgorithm Implementation:\n- Uses classic insertion sort algorithm for linked lists\n- Maintains sorted invariant: each insertion preserves ascending order\n- Time complexity: O(n²) worst case, O(n) best case for nearly sorted\n- Space complexity: O(1) - sorts in-place using existing node structures",
