      "comment": "Sorts linked lists of nodes by their sort values using insertion sort algorithm.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Iterate through global list chain starting from g_pListHead (DAT_6fbee28c)\n2. Check if sorting mode is enabled via IsSortingModeEnabled()\n3. For each list, perform insertion sort on nodes by sortValue field\n4. Sort nodes in ascending order by comparing sortValue at offset +0x18\n5. Update next pointers at offset +0x80 to maintain sorted order\n6. Perform string comparison on byte data for secondary sort criteria\n7. Move to next list via nextList pointer and repeat process\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value\n\nStructure Layout:\nSortableList (8 bytes):\n  Offset  Size  Field      Type              Description\n  +0x00   4     firstNode  SortableNode *    Pointer to first node in list\n  +0x04   4     nextList   SortableList *    Pointer to next list\n\nSortableNode (12 bytes):\n  Offset  Size  Field      Type    Description\n  +0x00   4     sortValue  int     Primary sort value at offset +0x18\n  +0x04   4     data       void *  Node data pointer\n  +0x08   4     nextNode   void *  Next node pointer at offset +0x80\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Function handles empty lists (null firstNode)\n- Supports mixed data types: ushort and byte arrays\n- String comparison used for byte data secondary sorting\n- Preserves original order for equal sort values\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x18 (24) - Offset to sortValue field in node structure\n0x80 (128) - Offset to nextNode pointer in node structure",
