      "comment": "Merge source player list nodes into the main player list, maintaining proper list structure\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize tail pointer to null and get head of source list\n2. While source list has nodes:\n   a. If destination list is empty, set head to first source node\n   b. If destination list exists, append source node to tail\n   c. Clear source node's next pointer to prevent dangling references\n   d. Traverse to end of destination list to update tail pointer\n   e. Move to next node in source list\n3. Continue until all source nodes are merged\n\nParameters:\nNone - operates on global list pointers\n\nReturns:\nvoid - modifies global lists in place\n\nStructure Layout:\nPlayerNode structure (18 bytes):\nOffset  Size  Field Name    Type           Description\n0x00    4     unknown       undefined4     Unknown field\n0x04    4     pNext         PlayerNode *   Pointer to next node in list\n0x08    4     unknown2      undefined4     Unknown field  \n0x0C    4     unknown3      undefined4     Unknown field\n0x12    2     unknown4      undefined2     Unknown field\n\nGlobal Variables:\ng_pSourcePlayerList (0x6fbee28c) - Head of source list to merge from\ng_pPlayerListHead (0x6fbee284) - Head of destination list to merge into\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Empty source list: Function returns immediately without changes\n- Empty destination list: First source node becomes new head\n- Single node lists: Proper tail tracking maintained\n- Large lists: Efficient O(n) traversal to find tail once per source node",
