      "comment": "Moves a player node to the head of the linked list for quick access.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize pPreviousNode to 0 for tracking previous node\n2. Load pCurrentNode from g_pPlayerListHead\n3. Return early if list is empty (g_pPlayerListHead == 0)\n4. Loop through linked list:\n   a. Set pFoundNode = pCurrentNode for current iteration\n   b. Check if current node's player ID (offset +0x10) matches nPlayerId\n   c. If match found AND pPreviousNode != 0 (not first node):\n      - Update previous node's next pointer (+0x80) to found node's next\n      - Set found node's next pointer to current list head\n      - Update g_pPlayerListHead to point to found node\n   d. Advance: pCurrentNode = current node's next pointer (+0x80)\n   e. Update: pPreviousNode = pFoundNode\n   f. Continue while pCurrentNode != 0\n\nParameters:\n- nPlayerId (int): Player ID to search for and move to list head\n\nReturns:\n- void: No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If nPlayerId matches first node (pPreviousNode == 0), no move needed\n- If nPlayerId not found, list remains unchanged\n- Empty list (g_pPlayerListHead == 0) returns immediately\n\nStructure Layout:\nPlayer Node Structure (inferred):\nOffset  Size  Field Name   Type     Description\n+0x10   4     nPlayerId    int      Unique player identifier\n+0x80   4     pNext        uint*    Pointer to next player node\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n- 0x10 (16): Offset to player ID field in player node\n- 0x80 (128): Offset to next pointer field in player node",
