      "comment": "Search for a player node by player ID in the global player list and associated action lists.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate input: Return NULL if player ID is -1 (invalid ID marker)\n2. Get head of global player list from g_pPlayerListHead\n3. Return NULL if player list is empty (head pointer is NULL)\n4. Iterate through main player node linked list:\n   a. Compare player ID at offset 0x10 with target ID\n   b. Return current player node pointer if match found\n   c. If no match, iterate through action sub-list at offset 0x38:\n      - Check each action node's player ID at offset 0x0\n      - Return parent player node if action matches target ID\n      - Follow next pointer at offset 0x4 to continue action list\n   d. Move to next player node using pointer at offset 0x80\n5. Return NULL if player ID not found in any node or action list\n\nParameters:\nnPlayerId (int): Target player ID to search for, -1 indicates invalid/unset ID\n\nReturns:\nPlayerNode*: Pointer to player node containing the target ID, or NULL if not found\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Player ID -1 is treated as invalid and causes immediate NULL return\n- Function checks both main player records and associated action sub-lists\n- Returns parent PlayerNode even when match found in action sub-list\n\nStructure Layout:\nPlayerNode structure accessed at these offsets:\nOffset  Size  Field Name       Type    Description\n0x10    4     nPlayerId        int     Main player identifier\n0x38    4     pPlayerActions   ptr     Head of player action linked list\n0x80    4     pNextPlayer      ptr     Next player node in main list\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x10 (16): Offset to player ID field in PlayerNode\n0x38 (56): Offset to player action list head in PlayerNode  \n0x80 (128): Offset to next player node pointer\n0x04 (4): Offset to next pointer in player action list nodes\n-1: Invalid player ID sentinel value",
