      "comment": "Checks if the given player node has a duplicate player ID in the global player list and returns the ID if duplicates exist.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize duplicate counter to 0\n2. Validate input player node pointer is not NULL  \n3. Validate global player list head is not NULL\n4. Iterate through global player list starting from g_pPlayerListHead\n5. For each player node, compare player ID at offset 0x22 with input node's ID\n6. Increment duplicate counter for each matching ID found\n7. Follow linked list pointer at offset 0x80 to next node\n8. Continue until end of list (NULL pointer)\n9. Check if more than 1 duplicate found (original + duplicates)\n10. Return player ID if duplicates exist, otherwise return -1\n\nParameters:\npPlayerNode - Pointer to PlayerSlotData structure containing player information and linked list navigation\n\nReturns:\nPlayer ID (short) - If duplicate player IDs found (count > 1)  \n-1 (short) - If no duplicates found or invalid parameters\n\nSpecial Cases:\nNULL input parameter returns -1 immediately\nEmpty global player list returns -1  \nSingle occurrence returns -1 as no duplicates exist\n\nStructure Layout:\nPlayerSlotData structure accessed:\nOffset | Size | Field Name | Type  | Description\n0x22   | 2    | playerId   | ushort| Unique player identifier  \n0x80   | 4    | pNext      | void* | Pointer to next node in linked list\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x22 (34) - Offset to player ID field in PlayerSlotData structure\n0x80 (128) - Offset to next pointer in PlayerSlotData linked list  \n-1 - Error return value indicating no duplicates or invalid input\n1 - Threshold for duplicate detection (count > 1 means duplicates exist)",
