      "comment": "Searches the global player list to find a player by unit ID and returns their index.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate input unit pointer is not null and extract unit ID from offset +8\n2. Check if unit ID is valid (not -1) and player list head exists\n3. Traverse player list starting from g_pPlayerListHead\n4. For each player node, compare stored ID at offset +0x10 with target ID\n5. If no match found, traverse linked list at offset +0x38 for sub-nodes\n6. For each sub-node, compare ID at offset +0x0 with target ID\n7. If match found, verify node exists and return player index from offset +0x22\n8. Move to next player node via offset +0x80 and repeat until end of list\n9. Return 0xFFFF if no matching player found\n\nParameters:\npUnit (UnitAny *) - Pointer to unit structure containing ID at offset +8\n\nReturns:\nPlayer index (ushort) - Index of matching player from offset +0x22\n0xFFFF - No matching player found or invalid input\n\nSpecial Cases:\nMagic number 0xFFFF represents \"not found\" condition\nUnit ID of -1 (0xFFFFFFFF) treated as invalid/uninitialized\n\nStructure Layout:\nUnitAny structure (input):\nOffset | Size | Field | Type | Description\n+0x08  | 4    | dwId  | uint | Unit identifier for matching\n\nPlayerNode structure (traversed):\nOffset | Size | Field      | Type           | Description\n+0x10  | 4    | dwUnitId   | uint           | Unit ID for matching\n+0x22  | 2    | wIndex     | ushort         | Player index (return value)\n+0x38  | 4    | pSubNodes  | PlayerNode *   | Linked list of sub-nodes\n+0x80  | 4    | pNext      | PlayerNode *   | Next player in main list\n\nSub-node structure (linked list at +0x38):\nOffset | Size | Field  | Type        | Description\n+0x00  | 4    | dwId   | uint        | Unit ID for comparison\n+0x04  | 4    | pNext  | SubNode *   | Next node in linked list",
