      "comment": "Process player state transitions and manage player list reorganization\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate input player state object is non-null\n2. Process state transition via switch statement on state field (offset 0x30):\n   - State 0 -> 4: Set packet type 0x06 (player join)\n   - State 1: Log critical error and terminate with exit code -1\n   - State 2 -> 1: Set packet type 0x08 (player leave)  \n   - State 3 -> 1: Set packet type 0x09 (player disconnect)\n   - State 4 -> 0: Set packet type 0x07 (player rejoin)\n3. Log six-byte packet with packet type and player ID (offset 0x10)\n4. Retrieve current player ID from game session context\n5. Search global player list for matching player ID or child list entries\n6. Store target player's short value if found, otherwise use -1\n7. Process all players in global list - create short nodes and remove from main list\n8. Rebuild player list based on sorting mode (tree or list insertion)\n9. Sort all short nodes in ascending order\n10. If target player found, move their node to head of short list\n11. Reconstruct main player list from short nodes in sorted order\n12. Clean up temporary short node list\n13. If no target found, move matching player to head of main list\n14. Finalize player list state via cleanup function\n\nParameters:\npPlayerState (PlayerSlotData *): Player state object containing transition info\n  - Offset 0x10: Player ID (uint)\n  - Offset 0x30: Current state value (uint) - see State Machine below\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value, operates on global player list state\n\nSpecial Cases:\nState value 1 triggers critical error termination\nInvalid or null input parameter skips all processing\nPlayer ID -1 indicates session context failure\nEmpty player list skips list processing operations\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x06 - Packet type for player join\n0x07 - Packet type for player rejoin  \n0x08 - Packet type for player leave\n0x09 - Packet type for player disconnect\n0x10 - Offset to player ID field\n0x22 - Offset to short value field\n0x30 - Offset to state field\n0x38 - Offset to child list pointer\n0x80 - Offset to next player node\n0x1F9 - Allocation ID for short nodes\n0x22C - Deallocation ID for cleanup\n0x4BD - Error code for state 1 termination\n-1 - Invalid/not found indicator\n\nState Machine:\nState 0: Initial/Join -> State 4 (Active)\nState 1: Error -> Terminate (Fatal)\nState 2: Leave -> State 1 (Disconnected)\nState 3: Disconnect -> State 1 (Disconnected)  \nState 4: Active -> State 0 (Rejoining)\n\nError Handling:\nState 1 logs error to debug output and calls exit(-1)\nNull player state pointer bypasses all processing\nInvalid player IDs default to -1 (not found)\nMemory allocation failures not explicitly handled",
