      "comment": "Processes player disconnection by cleaning up player lists and reorganizing data structures.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get current player ID from global context (FUN_6fb62880 + 0x8)\n2. Search main player list (g_pPlayerListHead) for matching player ID (offset +0x10)\n3. Check nested connection list (offset +0x38) for player ID matches\n4. Mark player as disconnected (set flag at +0x30, invalidate value at +0x22 to 0xFFFF)\n5. If player not found, log error and terminate with FUN_6fb9a10f\n6. Process all players through short list structure for reorganization\n7. Remove player nodes from lists using RemovePlayerNodeFromList\n8. Sort remaining nodes based on mode: string tree or sorted list\n9. Move target player to list head if sVar10 != -1\n10. Rebuild player list from short list nodes (link via offset +0x80)\n11. Deallocate remaining nodes and update global player list head\n12. Log disconnection event with 6-byte packet (type 9, player ID)\n\nParameters:\nNone (uses global player context)\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Player ID -1 indicates no current player, triggers error path\n- Missing player in main list causes application termination\n- Target value -1 skips player reordering step\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x10: Player ID offset in player node structure\n0x22: Player value/index field (set to 0xFFFF on disconnect)\n0x30: Player status/flags field (set to 1 on disconnect)\n0x38: Nested connection list pointer\n0x80: Next player node pointer (linked list traversal)\n0x4e3: Error code passed to Ordinal_10023 logging function\n9: Packet type for disconnection logging\n\nStructure Layout:\nPlayer Node Structure (size unknown):\nOffset  Size  Field Name        Type    Description\n+0x10   4     nPlayerId        int     Unique player identifier\n+0x22   2     sPlayerValue     short   Player index/value (-1 when disconnected)\n+0x30   4     dwPlayerFlags    uint    Player status flags (1 = disconnected)\n+0x38   4     pConnectionList  int*    Pointer to