      "instructions": ["0x101B0|PUSH|EBX", "0x101B1|PUSH|ESI", "0x101B2|PUSH|EDI", "0x101B3|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0x101B5|CALL|0x6fb62880", "0x101BA|MOV|EBX, dword ptr [EAX + 0x8]", "0x101BD|TEST|ESI, ESI", "0x101BF|JZ|0x6fae041c", "0x101C5|MOV|EDX, dword ptr [ESI + 0x10]", "0x101C8|PUSH|0x8", "0x101CA|MOV|ECX, EBX", "0x101CC|CALL|0x6fb823e0", "0x101D1|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0x101D3|JNZ|0x6fae01e0", "0x101D5|CMP|word ptr [ESI + 0x20], 0x9"],
      "comment": "Processes player removal request and manages roster state transitions\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate request pointer is non-NULL, return early if invalid\n2. Get game context and check player eligibility for removal based on ID and level threshold\n3. If player not eligible (level < 9 and not in active roster), return early\n4. Update roster tracking structures and send command 0x5D packet notification\n5. Validate action type is not -1 (invalid), return if invalid action\n6. Search global player list (g_pPlayerListHead) for target player by mode ID\n7. Verify action type matches between request and found player entry\n8. Mark player as removed by setting action type to -1 and status to 1\n9. Rebuild player roster by processing all active players through short list\n10. Sort and reorganize roster data structures using appropriate sorting method\n11. Clear player list head and rebuild from sorted short list nodes\n12. Deallocate temporary data structures and finalize roster state\n13. If action type was unspecified, move player to list head for cleanup\n\nParameters:\npRequest (PlayerRemovalRequest *): Pointer to player removal request structure containing:\n  +0x10: Player ID (DWORD) - unique identifier for target player\n  +0x20: Player level (USHORT) - minimum level 9 required for removal eligibility  \n  +0x22: Action type (SHORT) - specific removal action (-1 = invalid, others valid)\n\nReturns:\nvoid: No return value, operates through side effects on global roster state\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Level threshold: Players below level 9 cannot be removed unless already in active roster\n- Action type -1: Invalid action, triggers early return without roster changes\n- Null player request: Function returns immediately without processing\n- Player not found: Triggers fatal error via Ordinal_10023 and FUN_6fb9a10f(-1)\n- Action type mismatch: Returns without changes if request action != player action\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x10: Offset to player ID field in request structure\n0x20: Offset to player level field in request structure  \n0x22: Offset to action type field in request structure\n0x80: Offset to next pointer in linked list node structures\n0x72: Error code for player roster lookup failure\n0x4e3: Error code for player validation failure (decimal 1251)\n4: Command type for SendPacketWithCommand5d notification\n8: Flag parameter for roster state operations\n9: Minimum player level threshold for removal eligibility\n-1 (0xFFFF): Invalid/unspecified action type marker\n0xFFFFFFFF: Invalid mode ID sentinel value",
      "tags": ["PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Inventory", "STRUCT_Skill", "PARAM_1", "STRUCT_Other", "PROP_LOOPHEAVY", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "MOD_GAME", "SRC_Roster.cpp"]
