      "comment": "Retrieves a DWORD value from offset 0x10 in a Unit structure\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate input parameter pUnit is not NULL\n2. If pUnit is NULL, return error value 0xffffffff  \n3. If pUnit is valid, dereference pointer to access Unit structure\n4. Read DWORD value from field at offset 0x10 in the structure\n5. Return the retrieved DWORD value to caller\n\nParameters:\n  pUnit (Unit *): Pointer to Unit structure containing data fields\n\nReturns:\n  Success: DWORD value from Unit.field_0x10 (32-bit value at offset 0x10)\n  Error: 0xffffffff if pUnit is NULL pointer\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - NULL pointer protection prevents access violations\n  - Magic number 0xffffffff indicates invalid Unit reference\n  - Offset 0x10 represents field at byte position 16 in Unit structure\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset | Size | Field Name    | Type  | Description\n0x00   | 4    | field_0x00   | dword | First field (unknown purpose)\n0x04   | 4    | field_0x04   | dword | Second field (unknown purpose) \n0x08   | 4    | field_0x08   | dword | Third field (unknown purpose)\n0x0C   | 4    | field_0x0C   | dword | Fourth field (unknown purpose)\n0x10   | 4    | field_0x10   | dword | Target field returned by this function\n0x14   | 4    | field_0x14   | dword | Sixth field (unknown purpose)",
