      "instructions": ["0x104D0|PUSH|EBX", "0x104D1|PUSH|ESI", "0x104D2|MOV|ESI, dword ptr [0x6fbee284]", "0x104D8|CMP|ECX, -0x1", "0x104DB|JZ|0x6fae06d1", "0x104E1|TEST|ESI, ESI", "0x104E3|JZ|0x6fae06d1", "0x104E9|CMP|dword ptr [ESI + 0x10], ECX", "0x104EC|JZ|0x6fae0510", "0x104EE|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [ESI + 0x38]", "0x104F1|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0x104F3|JZ|0x6fae0500", "0x104F5|CMP|dword ptr [EAX], ECX", "0x104F7|JZ|0x6fae0510", "0x104F9|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [EAX + 0x4]"],
      "comment": "Updates player data and reorganizes player/short value lists.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate nPlayerId is not -1, return early if invalid\n2. Search player list (g_pPlayerListHead) for matching player ID\n3. Check main player nodes and their sublists for player ID match\n4. If player found, update player data fields:\n   - Store dwPlayerData at offset +0x14\n   - Store dwFlags masked with 0xFFFF at offset +0x24\n5. Get current player ID from global state via FUN_6fb62880\n6. Search for current player's short value in player list\n7. Process all player nodes into short list:\n   - Extract short value from each player node (+0x22 offset)\n   - Find or create ShortListNode for each value\n   - Remove player nodes from main list using RemovePlayerNodeFromList\n8. Clear main player list (g_pPlayerListHead = 0)\n9. Process short list nodes:\n   - Check sorting mode with IsSortingModeEnabled\n   - Insert into sorted tree or sorted list based on mode\n   - Update unused field with insertion result\n10. Sort short list nodes in ascending order\n11. If current player has valid short value (not -1):\n    - Find matching short list node\n    - Move it to head of list for priority processing\n12. Rebuild player list from short list:\n    - Link all player nodes in sequence\n    - Set g_pPlayerListHead to first player\n    - Chain remaining nodes via +0x80 offset\n13. Deallocate remaining list nodes\n14. If no current player, move target player to head\n15. Call FUN_6fb30200 for final cleanup\n\nParameters:\nnPlayerId    - Player ID to update (-1 indicates invalid)\ndwPlayerData - Data value to store at player offset +0x14  \ndwFlags      - Flag value (masked to 16-bit) stored at offset +0x24\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Early return if nPlayerId is -1 (invalid player)\n- Early return if g_pPlayerListHead is NULL (no players)\n- Handles current player priority by moving to list head\n- Processes both main player nodes and their sublists\n\nStructure Layout:\nPlayer Node Structure (PlayerSlotNode - 128 bytes):\nOffset Size Field Name    Type        Description\n+0x10  4    nPlayerId     int         Player identifier\n+0x14  4    dwPlayerData  uint        Updated by dwPlayerData parameter  \n+0x22  2    nShortValue   short       Short value for list sorting\n+0x24  4    dwFlags       uint        Updated by dwFlags parameter (16-bit)\n+0x38  4    pSubNodes     int*        Pointer to subnode list\n+0x80  4    pNext         PlayerNode* Next player node in list\n\nShortListNode Structure (12 bytes):\nOffset Size Field Name Type           Description\n+0x00  2    value      short          Short value for sorting\n+0x02  2    padding    short          Alignment padding  \n+0x04  4    unused     uint           Player node pointer during processing\n+0x08  4    next       ShortListNode* Next node in short list",
