      "comment": "Searches for player slot data by player ID in linked player list structure.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate input parameter is not -1 (invalid player ID)\n2. Check global player list head pointer is not null\n3. Iterate through primary player slot linked list (PlayerSlotNode chain)\n4. For each primary node, check if player ID at offset +0x10 matches target\n5. If no match in primary node, iterate through secondary linked list at offset +0x38\n6. For each secondary node, check if player ID at offset +0x0 matches target\n7. If match found in either list, return data value from offset +0x14\n8. If no match in secondary list, advance to next primary node via offset +0x80\n9. Continue until all primary nodes exhausted\n10. Return 0 if player ID not found in any list\n\nParameters:\nnPlayerId - Player ID to search for (int via ECX register)\n\nReturns:\nPlayer slot data value from offset +0x14 if found, 0 if not found\n\nSpecial Cases:\nPlayer ID -1 (0xFFFFFFFF) treated as invalid, returns 0 immediately\nEmpty player list (g_pPlayerListHead null) returns 0\nNull PlayerSlotNode encountered during traversal treated as list end\n\nStructure Layout:\nPlayerSlotNode (128 bytes):\nOffset  Size  Field Name        Type    Description\n+0x10   4     dwPlayerId        int     Player identification number\n+0x14   4     dwSlotData        int     Player slot data to return\n+0x38   4     pSecondaryList    int*    Pointer to secondary player list\n+0x80   4     pNextPrimary      int*    Pointer to next primary PlayerSlotNode\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0xFFFFFFFF (-1) - Invalid player ID constant\n0x10 (16) - Offset to player ID field in PlayerSlotNode\n0x14 (20) - Offset to slot data field in PlayerSlotNode  \n0x38 (56) - Offset to secondary list pointer in PlayerSlotNode\n0x80 (128) - Offset to next primary node pointer in PlayerSlotNode",
