      "comment": "Validates player exists in player list and removes player if found.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate input player ID - return true immediately if nPlayerId is -1 (invalid ID)\n2. Check if global player list head exists - return true if g_pPlayerListHead is null\n3. Traverse main player node linked list starting from g_pPlayerListHead\n4. For each player node, compare direct player ID at offset 0x10 with target nPlayerId\n5. If direct match found, jump to removal logic at LAB_6fae07a3\n6. If no direct match, iterate through sub-node list at offset 0x38 (pListTail)\n7. For each sub-node, compare ID at offset 0x0 with target nPlayerId\n8. If sub-node match found, jump to removal logic at LAB_6fae07a3\n9. Move to next main player node via offset 0x80 (next pointer)\n10. Repeat until end of main list reached\n11. At removal logic: call FUN_6fb62880() to get context object\n12. Extract field at offset 0x8 from context and call FUN_6fb823e0() for removal\n13. Return true if removal operation succeeds (returns 0), false otherwise\n14. Return true if player not found in any list\n\nParameters:\nnPlayerId - Player ID to search for and remove from player lists\n\nReturns:\ntrue - Player not found in lists OR removal operation succeeded\nfalse - Player found but removal operation failed\n\nSpecial Cases:\nInvalid Player ID (-1): Returns true immediately without searching\nEmpty Player List: Returns true if g_pPlayerListHead is null\nPlayer Found: Attempts removal via FUN_6fb823e0() with parameter 4\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x10 (16 decimal): Offset to nPlayerId field in PlayerSlotNode structure\n0x38 (56 decimal): Offset to pListTail (sub-node list pointer) in PlayerSlotNode structure\n0x80 (128 decimal): Offset to next player node pointer in PlayerSlotNode structure\n0x8 (8 decimal): Offset to context field in object returned by FUN_6fb62880()\n4: Constant parameter passed to FUN_6fb823e0() removal function\n\nStructure Layout:\nPlayerSlotNode (128 bytes total)