      "comment": "Searches player slot list for a player with specified ID and returns pointer to player data offset.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate input parameters (player ID must not be -1 and global player list must exist)\n2. Iterate through main player slot linked list starting from g_pPlayerListHead\n3. For each main player slot, check if stored player ID at offset +0x10 matches target ID\n4. If main slot match found, jump to return logic\n5. If no direct match, iterate through nested sub-list at offset +0x38\n6. For each sub-slot entry, check player ID at offset +0x00 for target match\n7. If sub-slot match found, jump to return logic using main slot pointer\n8. Continue to next main slot via next pointer at offset +0x80\n9. Return player slot pointer + 0x66 if found, NULL if not found\n\nParameters:\nnPlayerId (int): Target player ID to search for in the player slot list\n\nReturns:\nvoid*: Pointer to player data at offset +0x66 from player slot base if found\nNULL: If player ID not found, invalid ID (-1), or empty player list\n\nSpecial Cases:\nPlayer ID -1 is treated as invalid and causes immediate NULL return\nEmpty player list (g_pPlayerListHead == NULL) causes immediate NULL return\nMagic offset 0x66 indicates specific player data structure location within slot\n\nStructure Layout:\nMain Player Slot (PlayerSlotData):\nOffset  Size  Field Name       Type                Description\n+0x00   4     (unknown)        -                   -\n+0x10   4     nPlayerId        int                 Player ID for direct lookup\n+0x38   4     pSubSlotList     PlayerSlotData*     Pointer to nested sub-slot list\n+0x66   ?     playerData       -                   Target return data location\n+0x80   4     pNext            PlayerSlotData*     Next main slot in linked list\n\nSub-Slot Entry:\nOffset  Size  Field Name       Type                Description\n+0x00   4     nPlayerId        int                 Player ID for sub-slot lookup\n+0x04   4     pNext            SubSlotEntr