      "comment": "Retrieves player target data pointer by searching player list with player info\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate pPlayerInfo is not NULL (assert with error 0x5d1)\n2. Validate first field of player info is 0 (assert with error 0x5d2)  \n3. Extract player ID from pPlayerInfo[2] (offset +0x8)\n4. Return early if player ID is -1 (invalid)\n5. Search main player list starting from g_pPlayerListHead\n6. For each node, check if node->nPlayerId (offset +0x10) matches target\n7. If main node matches, return pointer to target data (node + 0x66)\n8. Search sub-node linked list at node->pSubNodeList (offset +0x38)\n9. For each sub-node, check if sub-node->nPlayerId matches target\n10. If sub-node matches, return pointer to target data (main_node + 0x66)\n11. Move to next main node via node->pNext (offset +0x80)\n12. Repeat until all nodes searched\n13. Fallback to Ordinal_10424(pPlayerInfo) if not found in list\n14. Assert with error 0x5db if fallback also fails\n\nParameters:\npPlayerInfo - Pointer to player information structure containing player ID at offset +8\n\nReturns:\nPointer to 26-byte target data block at offset +0x66 from matching player node\nResult from Ordinal_10424() fallback function if player not found in main list\nFunction never returns NULL (asserts on failure)\n\nSpecial Cases:\nPlayer ID -1 triggers early search termination\nValidation failures trigger fatal assertions with diagnostic messages\nFunction uses two-level search: main nodes with sub-node linked lists\n\nStructure Layout:\nPlayerInfo structure:\n  Offset  Size  Field Name           Type    Description\n  +0x0    4     dwValidationField    uint    Must be 0 for validation\n  +0x4    4     dwUnknown1          uint    Reserved/padding\n  +0x8    4     nPlayerId           int     Player ID for search\n\nPlayerListNode structure:\n  Offset  Size  Field Name           Type    Description  \n  +0x10   4     nPlayerId           int     Node's player ID\n  +0x38   4     pSubNodeList        