      "comment": "Updates data fields for a specific player in the global player list structure.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate input player ID (reject -1)\n2. Check if global player list head exists  \n3. Iterate through main player list nodes\n4. For each node, check if player ID matches at offset 0x10\n5. If no match, iterate through sub-list at offset 0x38\n6. Check each sub-list node for matching player ID\n7. If match found, update data fields at offsets 0x3c and 0x40\n8. Continue to next main list node via offset 0x80 if no match\n\nParameters:\n  nPlayerId (ECX): Player identifier to search for\n  nDataValue1 (EDX): First data value to store at offset 0x3c  \n  nDataValue2 (Stack[0x4]): Second data value to store at offset 0x40\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value, function operates by side effect\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Player ID of -1 is invalid and causes immediate return\n  - NULL player list head causes immediate return\n  - NULL player node during search causes safe exit\n  - Function handles two-level list structure (main list + sub-lists)\n\nStructure Layout (PlayerListNode - 154 bytes):\n  Offset | Size | Field Name    | Type  | Description\n  0x10   | 4    | dwPlayerId    | int   | Player identifier\n  0x38   | 4    | pSubList      | int*  | Pointer to sub-list head\n  0x3c   | 4    | dwDataField1  | int   | First data field (updated by nDataValue1)  \n  0x40   | 4    | dwDataField2  | int   | Second data field (updated by nDataValue2)\n  0x80   | 4    | pNextNode     | int*  | Pointer to next main list node\n\nError Handling:\n  - Gracefully handles NULL pointers in list traversal\n  - Validates player ID before search operation\n  - No error codes returned, operates silently on failure",
