      "comment": "Searches the player list for a player by ID and returns pointer to player data.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load head of player list from g_pPlayerListHead global\n2. If list is empty (NULL), return 0 (not found)\n3. Traverse linked list using next pointer at offset +0x80\n4. For each node, check two player ID fields at offsets +0x3c and +0x40\n5. If either ID matches nPlayerId parameter, return pointer to data at offset +0x66\n6. Continue until end of list or match found\n7. Return 0 if player not found\n\nParameters:\nnPlayerId (int) - Player ID to search for in the list\n\nReturns:\nPlayerListNode * - Pointer to player data structure at offset +0x66 from node base\nNULL (0) - Player ID not found in list\n\nStructure Layout:\nPlayerListNode (154 bytes total):\nOffset  Size  Field Name          Type    Description\n+0x3c   4     dwPlayerId1         uint    Primary player identifier\n+0x40   4     dwPlayerId2         uint    Secondary player identifier  \n+0x66   ?     playerData          ?       Player data structure (return offset)\n+0x80   4     pNext               ptr     Next node in linked list\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Function checks TWO player ID fields per node (+0x3c and +0x40)\n- Returns pointer offset +0x66 bytes from node base, not node base itself\n- Uses __fastcall convention with nPlayerId passed in ECX register",
