      "comment": "Checks for conflicting player connections in the player list\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract player ID from input parameter using offset 0x8\n2. Call GetPlayerId function to retrieve player ID value  \n3. Return 0 (no conflict) if player ID is -1 (invalid)\n4. Return 0 (no conflict) if player list head is null\n5. Traverse player linked list starting from g_pPlayerListHead\n6. For each node, check if player ID matches extracted ID\n7. If IDs match but player field at offset 0x10 differs, return 1 (conflict found)\n8. Continue to next node using pointer at offset 0x80\n9. Return 0 (no conflict) if end of list reached without finding conflict\n\nParameters:\n- pPlayerData: Pointer to player data structure containing player information\n\nReturns:\n- 1 if conflicting player found (same ID but different field value)\n- 0 if no conflict found or invalid input\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Player ID -1 indicates invalid/disconnected player (no conflict)\n- Empty player list (g_pPlayerListHead == null) results in no conflict\n- Function stops at first conflict found, does not count total conflicts\n\nStructure Layout:\nPlayer List Node Structure (estimated from access patterns):\nOffset  Size  Field Name    Type    Description\n+0x10   4     dwPlayerField dword   Player-specific field (session/connection data)\n+0x22   2     wPlayerId     word    Unique player identifier  \n+0x80   4     pNext         ptr     Pointer to next node in linked list",
