      "instructions": ["0x10A00|PUSH|EBX", "0x10A01|PUSH|ESI", "0x10A02|MOV|ESI, dword ptr [0x6fbee284]", "0x10A08|CMP|ECX, -0x1", "0x10A0B|JZ|0x6fae0bf6", "0x10A11|TEST|ESI, ESI", "0x10A13|JZ|0x6fae0bf6", "0x10A19|CMP|dword ptr [ESI + 0x10], ECX", "0x10A1C|JZ|0x6fae0a40", "0x10A1E|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [ESI + 0x38]", "0x10A21|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0x10A23|JZ|0x6fae0a30", "0x10A25|CMP|dword ptr [EAX], ECX", "0x10A27|JZ|0x6fae0a40", "0x10A29|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [EAX + 0x4]"],
      "comment": "Sets a player's priority value and completely reorganizes the player list with special positioning.\n\nAlgorithm:\n\n1. Validate input player ID is not -1, return early if invalid\n2. Search player list (g_pPlayerListHead) for player matching nPlayerId\n3. Search sub-nodes at offset 0x38 if main player ID doesn't match\n4. Return early if player not found in list or sub-nodes\n5. Store sPriorityValue at offset 0x22 in found player structure\n6. Call FUN_6fb62880() to get priority player ID from system state\n7. Search for priority player in list and save their current priority value (sVar9)\n8. Process all players in list to create short list nodes for reorganization\n9. For each player, find or create ShortListNode with their priority value\n10. Remove all players from main list using RemovePlayerNodeFromList()\n11. Re-sort and re-insert all players based on current sorting mode\n12. Call SortShortListNodesAscending() to order by priority values\n13. If priority player exists (sVar9 != -1), move them to list head\n14. Reconstruct main player list from sorted short list in priority order\n15. Handle special positioning for priority player found in step 6-7\n16. Clean up temporary short list nodes with DeallocateRemainingListNodes()\n17. If no priority player found, move system priority player to head\n18. Call FUN_6fb30200() for final list state update\n\nParameters:\n\nnPlayerId (int): Target player ID to update priority for (-1 = invalid)\nsPriorityValue (short): New priority value to store at offset 0x22\n\nReturns:\n\nvoid - Function modifies global player list state\n\nSpecial Cases:\n\nPlayer ID -1 triggers early return without processing\nMissing player in list/sub-nodes triggers early return\nPriority player value -1 indicates no special positioning needed\nEmpty player list (g_pPlayerListHead == 0) triggers early return\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n\n0x10 - Player ID field offset in PlayerListNode structure\n0x22 - Priority value field offset (16-bit short value)\n0x38 - Sub-nodes pointer offset for player search\n0x80 - Next player pointer offset in linked list\n0x1f9 - Allocation ID for short list node creation\n-1 (0xFFFF) - Invalid/unset priority value indicator\n\nStructure Layout:\n\nPlayerListNode structure (size 154 bytes):\nOffset | Size | Field Name       | Type          | Description\n0x10   | 4    | nPlayerId       | int           | Unique player identifier\n0x22   | 2    | sPriorityValue  | short         | Player priority for sorting\n0x38   | 4    | pSubNodes       | void *        | Pointer to sub-node list\n0x80   | 4    | pNext           | PlayerListNode* | Next player in linked list\n\nShortListNode structure (size 12 bytes):\nOffset | Size | Field Name | Type | Description  \n0x00   | 2    | value      | short| Priority value for sorting\n0x04   | 4    | unused     | uint | Player node pointer during reconstruction\n0x08   | 4    | next       | void*| Next node in temporary sort list\n\nNote: Function uses SSA temporary variables (iVar2, iVar3, sVar9, uVar5, etc.) that cannot be renamed due to compiler optimization.",
