      "comment": "Search player list by ID and set padding field value.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate input: Return early if player ID is -1 or player list head is null\n2. Traverse main player list starting from g_pPlayerListHead\n3. For each player node, check if nPlayerId matches target ID\n4. If match found in main list, jump to field update logic\n5. If no match, traverse sub-node list for current player\n6. Check each sub-node for matching player ID\n7. If match found in sub-list, jump to field update logic\n8. Move to next player node via abTargetData[4] offset (+0x80)\n9. Continue until end of list reached\n10. When match found: Validate player node is not null\n11. Mask padding value to 8-bit range (& 0xFF)\n12. Store masked value in dwPadding8 field (+0x30 offset)\n13. Call FUN_6fb30200() for post-update processing\n\nParameters:\nnPlayerId (int): Target player ID to search for (-1 indicates invalid)\ndwPaddingValue (uint): Value to store in padding field (masked to byte)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value, operates by side effect\n\nSpecial Cases:\nPlayer ID -1 treated as invalid input and causes early return\nNull player list head causes early return without processing\nNull player node after match found causes early return without update\nPadding value automatically masked to 0xFF range before storage\n\nStructure Layout:\nPlayerListNode offsets accessed:\n+0x10: nPlayerId (int) - Player identifier for matching\n+0x30: dwPadding8 (uint) - Target field for value storage  \n+0x38: pSubNodeList (int *) - Pointer to sub-node linked list\n+0x80: Next node via abTargetData[4] - Link to next player node\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x10 (16): Offset to nPlayerId field in PlayerListNode\n0x30 (48): Offset to dwPadding8 field in PlayerListNode  \n0x38 (56): Offset to pSubNodeList field in PlayerListNode\n0x80 (128): Offset to next node pointer via abTargetData[4]\n0xFF (255): Mask for converting uint to byte range\n-1: Invalid player ID sentinel value",
