      "instructions": ["0x10C50|PUSH|ESI", "0x10C51|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0x10C53|MOV|ECX, dword ptr [0x6fbee284]", "0x10C59|PUSH|EDI", "0x10C5A|CMP|ESI, -0x1", "0x10C5D|MOV|EDI, EDX", "0x10C5F|JZ|0x6fae0cbe", "0x10C61|TEST|ECX, ECX", "0x10C63|JZ|0x6fae0cbe", "0x10C65|CMP|dword ptr [ECX + 0x10], ESI", "0x10C68|JZ|0x6fae0c88", "0x10C6A|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [ECX + 0x38]", "0x10C6D|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0x10C6F|JZ|0x6fae0c7c", "0x10C71|CMP|dword ptr [EAX], ESI"],
      "comment": "Process network action for a specific player by searching the player list hierarchy.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate input player ID (must not be -1) and global player list exists\n2. Search main player list nodes for matching player ID\n3. If player not found in main node, search sub-node list iteratively  \n4. If player found in sub-nodes, jump to processing section\n5. Continue to next main player node via next pointer (+0x80 offset)\n6. Repeat search until player found or list exhausted\n7. When player found, validate player node is not null\n8. Call FUN_6fb82310 with player ID and action type for initialization\n9. Call FUN_6fb82420 with player ID, action type, and masked action data (0xFFFF)\n10. Call FUN_6fb30200 for global state synchronization\n11. Call FUN_6fb62880 to get game state handle\n12. Validate action type matches game state handle offset +0x8\n13. If validation passes, call FUN_6fae1880 with player ID for finalization\n\nParameters:\n  nPlayerId (int): Unique player identifier to search for (-1 = invalid)\n  nActionType (int): Type of network action to process  \n  dwActionData (uint): Action-specific data payload (only lower 16 bits used)\n\nReturns:\n  void: Function performs side effects, no return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Returns early if nPlayerId is -1 (invalid player)\n  - Returns early if global player list head is null\n  - Returns early if player node becomes null during processing  \n  - Returns early if action type validation fails against game state",
