      "comment": "Checks if two players exist in the player list and have the same target area ID.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate first player ID is not -1 and player list exists\n2. Search player list for first player ID in main nodes and subnodes\n3. Set pPlayer1Node to found node or NULL if not found\n4. Validate second player ID is not -1 and player list exists\n5. Search player list for second player ID in main nodes and subnodes  \n6. Set pPlayer2Node to found node or NULL if not found\n7. If both players found, compare target area IDs at offset +0x22\n8. Return 1 if both players exist and have matching non-negative target areas\n9. Return 0 if either player not found or target areas don't match\n\nParameters:\nnPlayer1Id - First player identifier to search for\nnPlayer2Id - Second player identifier to search for\n\nReturns:\n1 - Both players found and have matching target area IDs\n0 - Either player not found or target areas don't match or invalid\n\nSpecial Cases:\nPlayer ID -1 (0xFFFFFFFF) is treated as invalid and skips search\nTarget area ID -1 (0xFFFF) is treated as invalid even if both players have it\nSearch includes both main player nodes and their associated subnodes\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0xFFFFFFFF (-1) - Invalid player ID marker\n0xFFFF (-1) - Invalid target area ID marker\n0x10 - PlayerListNode.nPlayerId offset\n0x38 - PlayerListNode.pSubNodeList offset  \n0x80 - Next PlayerListNode offset (abTargetData + 4)\n0x22 - Target area ID offset in PlayerListNode (dwPadding4 + 2)\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset  Size  Field Name        Type                Description\n0x10    4     nPlayerId         int                 Main player identifier\n0x22    2     wTargetAreaId     short              Target area/level ID\n0x38    4     pSubNodeList      int*               Pointer to subnode list  \n0x80    4     pNextNode         PlayerListNode*    Next node in main list\n\nError Handling:\nReturns 0 for any validation failure or search miss\nNo error reporting -