      "comment": "Sets a flag value for a player by searching through the player list hierarchy.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate player ID is not -1 (invalid)\n2. Validate global player list head exists\n3. Iterate through main player list nodes\n4. For each node, check if nPlayerId matches target\n5. If no match, iterate through sub-node list at node->pSubNodeList\n6. Check each sub-node ID against target player ID\n7. If match found (main or sub), set dwPadding1 field to masked flag value\n8. Mask flag value with 0xff to ensure single byte storage\n9. Exit immediately after setting flag\n\nParameters:\nnPlayerId (int): Target player ID to search for (-1 is invalid)\nnFlagValue (int): Flag value to set, will be masked to single byte (0xff)\n\nReturns:\nvoid: No return value, silently fails if player not found\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Player ID -1 is treated as invalid and causes immediate return\n- NULL global player list head causes immediate return\n- Player not found results in no action (silent failure)\n- Flag value automatically masked to 0xff for byte storage\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0xff (255): Byte mask to ensure flag value fits in single byte\n-1: Invalid player ID constant\n0x10: PlayerListNode nPlayerId field offset\n0x14: PlayerListNode dwPadding1 field offset\n0x38: PlayerListNode pSubNodeList field offset\n0x80: PlayerListNode next pointer field offset (abTargetData + 4)",
