      "comment": "Search player list for specified player ID and return padding value from matching node.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate input player ID is not -1 (invalid)\n2. Check global player list head is not null\n3. Iterate through main player list nodes\n4. For each node, compare nPlayerId field against target ID\n5. If no match in main node, iterate through sub-node list\n6. For each sub-node, compare ID against target\n7. If match found in sub-nodes, mark found and exit loops\n8. If no match in current node, advance to next via abTargetData+4 pointer\n9. Call FUN_6fb62880 to get current player ID context\n10. Compare target ID against current player context\n11. If target is current player or no node found, return 0\n12. If valid node found and target is not current player, return dwPadding1\n\nParameters:\nnPlayerId - Target player ID to search for in the player list\n\nReturns:\nPlayer node padding value (dwPadding1) if found and not current player\n0 if player ID is invalid, not found, or matches current player context\n\nSpecial Cases:\nPlayer ID -1 is treated as invalid and causes immediate return of 0\nIf target player matches current player context from FUN_6fb62880, return 0\n\nStructure Layout:\nPlayerListNode:\nOffset  Size  Field Name      Type                Description\n0x10    4     nPlayerId       int                 Player identifier\n0x14    4     dwPadding1      undefined4          Padding/status value returned\n0x38    4     pSubNodeList    int *               Pointer to sub-node chain\n0x80    4     next            PlayerListNode *    Next node in main list chain\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x10 - Offset to nPlayerId in PlayerListNode\n0x14 - Offset to dwPadding1 return value\n0x38 - Offset to pSubNodeList pointer  \n0x80 - Offset to next node pointer in abTargetData\n0x08 - Offset to current player ID in FUN_6fb62880 result structure",
