      "comment": "Cleanup and release all nodes in the global linked list\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if global node list head pointer is NULL\n2. If NULL, set head pointer to NULL (safety redundancy) and return early\n3. Iterate through linked list starting from head node\n4. For each node, save next pointer from offset 0x30 before processing\n5. Call Ordinal_10043 with parameters (0x2f, 0) to release/cleanup current node\n6. Advance to next node using saved pointer\n7. Continue until reaching NULL terminator\n8. Set global head pointer to NULL to indicate empty list\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\nEmpty list (NULL head pointer) - Function returns immediately after redundant NULL assignment\nSingle node - Processes one node then terminates normally\nCircular reference protection - None implemented; assumes well-formed NULL-terminated list\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x2f (47 decimal) - First parameter to Ordinal_10043, likely cleanup/release operation type\n0x30 (48 decimal) - Offset to next pointer field in node structure\n0x0 - Second parameter to Ordinal_10043, likely flags or context parameter\n\nStructure Layout:\nBased on memory access pattern at offset 0x30:\nOffset | Size | Field Name | Type    | Description\n+0x30  | 4    | pNext      | void *  | Pointer to next node in linked list\n\nError Handling:\nNo explicit error handling - assumes valid node structure format\nNo validation of node pointers before dereferencing\nRelies on NULL termination for loop exit condition",
