      "comment": "Adds a new pet roster node or updates an existing one in the global pet registry linked list.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. If nNodeType == 7 (cleanup mode), scan list for nodes with type 7 and different GUID\n2. Remove first matching stale node (type 7 with different GUID) via ReleasePoolAllocation\n3. Search for existing node matching dwPetGUID\n4. If found, update node fields: nNodeType at +0x04, dwOwnerUnitGUID at +0x0C, dwPetClassId at +0x00, reset padding21-24 to 0\n5. If not found, allocate new 0x34 (52) byte node via FogMemAlloc\n6. Zero-initialize new node with REP STOSD (13 dwords)\n7. Populate fields: dwPetGUID at +0x08, dwOwnerUnitGUID at +0x0C, nNodeType at +0x04, dwPetClassId at +0x00\n8. Set padding17-20 to 100 (0x64) at offset +0x1C\n9. Link new node at head of list (pNext = old head, update g_pPetRosterHead)\n\nParameters:\n  dwPetGUID (ECX) - Unique identifier for the pet unit, used as search key\n  dwOwnerUnitGUID (EDX) - GUID of the pet's owner unit, stored at offset +0x0C\n  nNodeType (Stack+0x04) - Node type flag; 7 triggers stale node cleanup before add/update\n  dwPetClassId (Stack+0x08) - Pet class identifier, stored at offset +0x00\n\nReturns: void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Type 7 mode removes one stale node before processing (prevents list bloat)\n  - New nodes get priority 100 at offset +0x1C (padding17-20)\n  - Updated nodes reset padding21-24 to 0\n\nStructure Layout (LinkedListNode, 52 bytes):\n  Offset  Size  Field         Description\n  0x00    4     dwPetClassId  Pet class identifier\n  0x04    4     nNodeType     Node type flag (7 = active pet)\n  0x08    4     dwPetGUID     Pet unit GUID (search key)\n  0x0C    4     dwOwnerGUID   Owner unit GUID\n  0x1C    4     dwPriority    Priority value (set to 100 on create)\n  0x20    4     dwFlags       Status flags (reset on update)\n  0x30    4     pNext         Next node pointer",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Path", "STRUCT_Inventory", "STRUCT_Skill", "PARAM_4", "PROP_LOOPHEAVY", "STRUCT_Control", "MOD_GAME", "STRUCT_PlayerData", "SRC_RosterPets.cpp"]
