      "comment": "Updates or creates pet node registry entry with specified data and handles pet-specific operations.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Remove any duplicate pet type 7 nodes with different IDs (cleanup phase)\n2. Search for existing node with matching pet ID\n3. If pet type is 7 and no matching node found, allocate new node (52 bytes)\n4. Zero-initialize new node and populate basic fields (ID, owner, type, param4)\n5. Set initial health to 100 and link into global pet registry list\n6. Search for target node again to verify allocation\n7. If node not found, trigger fatal assertion error\n8. Update node with current data (ID, owner, type, pet data array)\n9. For pet type 7 (special pets), perform additional pet-specific operations\n10. Call pet management functions for positioning, validation, and visibility\n\nParameters:\ndwPetId - Unique pet identifier for registry lookup\nnOwnerPlayerId - Player ID who owns this pet\nnPetType - Type of pet (7 = special pet with enhanced processing)\nnParam4 - Additional parameter stored in node\npPetData - Pointer to 3-element data array [data1, data2, data3]\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value (function always completes or exits via assertion)\n\nSpecial Cases:\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x7 (7) - Special pet type requiring enhanced processing and cleanup\n0x64 (100) - Initial pet health value for new registrations\n0x59 (89) - Memory pool ID for node deallocation\n0x7a (122) - Memory pool ID for new node allocation\n0x34 (52) - Size of PetNode structure in bytes\n0xd (13) - Number of DWORDs to clear during initialization\n0x95 (149) - Error code for pet registry assertion failure\n\nError Handling:\n- Missing pet registry triggers fatal assertion with error code 149\n- Calls exit(-1) if critical pet lookup fails\n- Automatic cleanup removes conflicting pet type 7 entries\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset | Size | Field Name      | Type     | Description\n-------|------|-----------------|----------|------------------------------------------\n0x00   | 4    | dwParam4        | uint     | Additional parameter value\n0x04   | 4    | nType          | int      | Pet type (7 = special processing)\n0x08   | 4    | dwId           | uint     | Unique pet identifier\n0x0c   | 4    | nParam2        | int      | Owner player ID\n0x10   | 4    | dwReserved10   | uint     | Reserved field\n0x14   | 4    | dwReserved14   | uint     | Reserved field  \n0x18   | 4    | dwReserved18   | uint     | Reserved field\n0x1c   | 4    | dwInitialValue | uint     | Initial health (100)\n0x20   | 4    | dwFlags        | uint     | Status flags (0 = reset)\n0x24   | 4    | dwData1        | uint     | First pet data value\n0x28   | 4    | dwData2        | uint     | Second pet data value\n0x2c   | 4    | dwData3        | uint     | Third pet data value  \n0x30   | 4    | pNext          | PetNode* | Next node in linked list",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PROP_NOCALLER", "STRUCT_ItemData", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "MOD_GAME", "STRUCT_PlayerData", "STRUCT_Path", "STRUCT_Skill", "PARAM_5", "PROP_LOOPHEAVY", "STRUCT_Pet", "SRC_RosterPets.cpp"]
