      "instructions": ["0x11400|PUSH|ESI", "0x11401|MOV|ESI, dword ptr [0x6fbee290]", "0x11407|PUSH|EDI", "0x11408|XOR|EDI, EDI", "0x1140A|TEST|ESI, ESI", "0x1140C|JZ|0x6fae1465", "0x1140E|CMP|dword ptr [ESI + 0x8], ECX", "0x11411|JZ|0x6fae141f", "0x11413|MOV|EDI, ESI", "0x11415|MOV|ESI, dword ptr [ESI + 0x30]", "0x11418|TEST|ESI, ESI", "0x1141A|JNZ|0x6fae140e", "0x1141C|POP|EDI", "0x1141D|POP|ESI", "0x1141E|RET|"],
      "comment": "Removes or marks a pet node from the global linked list by search key\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load global linked list head pointer g_pLinkedListHead\n2. Initialize previous node pointer to NULL\n3. Return early if list is empty\n4. Traverse list comparing each node's dwSearchKey (offset +0x8) with parameter\n5. Track previous node for list unlinking\n6. If current node's pNext is NULL and key not found, return (not found)\n7. When matching node found, check node type field at offset +0x4\n8. If type == 7 (PET_TYPE_ACTIVE), get game context and compare node's game ID\n9. If node's game ID (offset +0xc) matches current game context ID (offset +0x8):\n   - Mark node as pending removal by setting flag at offset +0x20 to 1\n   - Return without removing from list (deferred cleanup)\n10. Otherwise, unlink node from list:\n    - If previous is NULL, update list head to current->pNext\n    - Else set previous->pNext = current->pNext\n11. Call ReleasePoolAllocation to free the node memory (208 bytes at 0x6fbb0184)\n\nParameters:\n  dwSearchKey (ECX) - uint: Key to search for in linked list nodes (matches dwSearchKey at offset +0x8)\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Empty list: Returns immediately without action\n- Key not found: Returns without modifying list\n- Type 7 node with matching game ID: Marks for deferred removal instead of immediate removal\n- Type 7 node with non-matching game ID: Removes immediately\n- Non-type-7 node: Always removes immediately\n\nStructure Layout (LinkedListNode at offset):\nOffset  Size  Field          Type    Description\n0x00    4     unknown        uint    Reserved/padding\n0x04    4     dwNodeType     uint    Node type (7 = PET_TYPE_ACTIVE)\n0x08    4     dwSearchKey    uint    Search key for lookup\n0x0C    4     dwGameId       uint    Game context ID\n0x20    4     dwPendingFlag  uint    Pending removal flag (1 = marked)\n0x30    4     pNext          void*   Next node pointer\n\nRelated Functions:\n- GetGameContext: Gets current game context pointer\n- ReleasePoolAllocation: Frees node memory to pool",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Inventory", "STRUCT_Skill", "PARAM_1", "MOD_GAME", "SRC_RosterPets.cpp"]
