      "comment": "Validates player connection status and permissions for a given player ID.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if global player list head (g_pNodeListHead) exists\n2. Traverse PlayerListNode linked list via next pointers at offset +0x30\n3. Compare player ID at offset +0x8 with target nPlayerId\n4. If match found, validate player is not null pointer\n5. Check player status at offset +0x4 is in valid range (0x11-0x12, decimal 17-18)\n6. Get current player context via FUN_6fb62880()\n7. Compare current player ID at offset +0x8 with found player ID at offset +0xc\n8. If same player, return 1 (same player validation)\n9. Get PlayerSlotData for current player via FindPlayerNodeById()\n10. Check for duplicate player ID using CheckPlayerIdDuplicate()\n11. Get PlayerSlotData for target player via FindPlayerNodeById()\n12. Check for duplicate player ID using CheckPlayerIdDuplicate()\n13. Compare duplicate check results for both players\n\nParameters:\nnPlayerId - Target player ID to validate connection for\n\nReturns:\n0 - Player not found, invalid, or duplicate check failed\n1 - Same player as current context\n2 - Valid different player, duplicate checks passed\n3 - Player found with valid status range (17-18)\n\nSpecial Cases:\nStatus range 0x11-0x12 (17-18) indicates connected/active players\nCheckPlayerIdDuplicate returns -1 for invalid/duplicate players\nFunction validates both connection status and anti-duplication measures\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x8 - Player ID field offset in PlayerListNode\n0x4 - Player status field offset in PlayerListNode  \n0xc - Secondary player ID field offset in PlayerListNode\n0x30 - Next node pointer offset in PlayerListNode (linked list traversal)\n0x11 (17) - Minimum valid player status\n0x12 (18) - Maximum valid player status\n\nStructure Layout:\nPlayerListNode offsets:\nOffset  Size  Field Name    Type    Description\n+0x4    4     dwStatus      uint    Player connection status\n+0x8    4     nPlayerId     int     Primary player identifier\n+0xc    4     nSecondaryId  int     Secondary player identifier  \n+0x30   4     pNext         ptr     Next node in linked list\n\nNote: Function uses register-optimized local variables for list traversal and validation.",
      "tags": ["PARAM_1", "PROP_LOOPHEAVY"]
    },
