      "comment": "Searches linked list for node with matching search key and returns pointer to data area\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load global linked list head pointer (g_pLinkedListHead)\n2. Check if list is empty, return NULL if so\n3. Iterate through linked list using next pointers at offset +0x30\n4. Compare search key at offset +0x8 with target key parameter\n5. If match found, validate node pointer is non-NULL\n6. Return pointer to data area at offset +0x24 from node base\n7. If no match found after traversing entire list, return NULL\n\nParameters:\ndwSearchKey (int) - Search key value to locate in linked list nodes\n\nReturns:\n- Non-NULL pointer to data area (offset +0x24 from node) if key found\n- NULL (0) if key not found or list is empty\n- NULL (0) if matching node pointer is corrupted\n\nStructure Layout:\nLinkedListNode structure (52 bytes):\nOffset  Size  Field Name      Type                Description\n+0x00   8     (unknown)       byte[8]            Unknown header fields\n+0x08   4     dwSearchKey     int                Search/lookup key\n+0x0C   24    (padding)       byte[24]           Reserved/padding area  \n+0x24   12    dataArea        byte[12]           Data payload area (function returns pointer here)\n+0x30   4     pNext           LinkedListNode*    Pointer to next node in list",
