      "comment": "Calculates the usage limit for a specific skill by counting matching entities and consulting skill database.\nThis function validates skill usage restrictions by examining a global entity list and computing limits.\nThe function first counts entities matching the skill criteria, then consults external validation functions.\nIt enforces usage limits by returning the minimum of entity count and computed database limit.\nInvalid skills bypass limit computation and return raw entity counts for basic tracking.\nThe algorithm handles both entity-based counting and external limit verification seamlessly.\nThis is part of the skill system's usage restriction and validation framework.\nThe function integrates with Ordinal_10949 and Ordinal_10968 for external limit computation.\nIt uses a switch-based validation system to determine which skills require limit checks.\nThe implementation ensures fair usage limits while maintaining performance through efficient list traversal.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize entity counter to zero for tracking matching entities\n2. Traverse global linked list of entities starting from g_pLinkedListHead  \n3. For each node, compare skill ID (offset +0x4) with requested skill parameter\n4. If skill matches, compare entity value (offset +0xc) with pEntity+8 field\n5. Increment counter for each entity that matches both criteria\n6. Validate skill ID through switch statement for allowed skills only\n7. For valid skills (4,5,6,10,11,12,15), call Ordinal_10949 to get handle\n8. Call Ordinal_10968 with entity pointer, handle, and quantity to get computed limit\n9. Return minimum of entity count and computed limit to enforce restrictions\n10. For invalid skills, bypass limit computation and return raw entity count\n\nParameters:\npEntity: Pointer to UnitAny structure containing comparison criteria at +8 offset\nnSkillId: Skill or spell identifier to check usage limits for (integer)\n\nReturns:\nInteger count representing usage limit for the specified skill:\n- For valid skills: minimum of entity count and computed database limit\n- For invalid skills: raw entity count from linked list traversal  \n- Zero if no matching entities found in the global list",
      "tags": ["PARAM_2"]
    },
