      "comment": "Searches linked list for node matching specified criteria.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate search context pointer is not null\n2. Get head of global node list from g_pLinkedListHead\n3. Traverse linked list until end reached\n4. For each node, check if node type matches dwNodeType parameter\n5. If type matches, check if search key matches value from search context\n6. If both match, apply optional flag condition check\n7. If dwOptionalFlag is 0, verify node flags field is 0\n8. If dwOptionalFlag is non-zero, skip flags check\n9. Return node value if all conditions met\n10. Continue to next node in linked list if no match\n11. Return 0xFFFFFFFF if no matching node found\n\nParameters:\n- pSearchContext: SearchContext* - Pointer to search context structure containing search key at offset +8\n- dwNodeType: uint - Node type value to match against node field\n- dwOptionalFlag: uint - Optional flag (0=strict match with flags check, non-zero=relaxed match)\n\nReturns:\n- Success: uint value from matching node's value field\n- Failure: 0xFFFFFFFF when no matching node found or invalid parameters\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Returns 0xFFFFFFFF immediately if pSearchContext is null\n- Returns 0xFFFFFFFF if g_pLinkedListHead is null (empty list)\n- When dwOptionalFlag=0, matching node must have flags field set to 0\n\nStructure Layout:\nLinkedListNode Structure (accessed via g_pLinkedListHead):\nContains node type, search key, flags, and next pointer for traversal\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0xFFFFFFFF (4294967295): Error return value indicating no match found",
