      "comment": "Process PvP player interactions for entities in the game world\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize by getting the global linked list head and current player data\n2. Iterate through all entities in the global linked list\n3. Check if current entity type equals 4 (player entity type)\n4. Get target player data using entity search key\n5. Search for target player in linked list to find their node\n6. Validate PvP interaction conditions:\n   - Check if current player exists\n   - If target player node not found, verify both players are type 1\n   - Call distance/interaction validation (Ordinal_10563)\n   - If target player node exists, check player IDs don't match\n   - Call CanPlayersInteractPvP to validate interaction rules\n7. Set interaction result based on validation outcome\n8. Update target player state with interaction result via two function calls\n9. Continue to next entity in linked list\n\nParameters:\nNone (void function)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value, operates on global game state\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Entity type 4: Player entities that can participate in PvP\n- Player type 1: Standard player entities for interaction validation\n- Magic number 0x4: Player entity type constant for filtering\n- Magic number 0x1: Standard player type for validation checks\n\nStructure Layout:\nLinkedListNode structure (52 bytes):\nOffset | Size | Field         | Type | Description\n0x00   | 4    | dwSearchKey   | uint | Entity search/lookup key\n0x04   | 4    | unknown5-8    | uint | Entity type (assembled from 4 bytes)\n0x08   | 4    | dwSearchKey   | uint | Secondary search key  \n0x0C   | 4    | padding1-4    | uint | Player ID (assembled from 4 bytes)\n0x30   | 4    | pNext         | ptr  | Pointer to next node in list",
