      "comment": "Updates data fields in a linked list node and applies effects if appropriate.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Retrieve head of global linked list (g_pLinkedListHead)\n2. Traverse linked list searching for node with matching dwSearchKey\n3. Return early if no matching node found\n4. Update node data fields from parameters:\n   - Store nDataValue as 4 bytes in padding17-20 (little-endian)\n   - Store lower 16 bits of wFlags in padding5-8 (little-endian)\n5. Read effect type from node's unknown5-8 bytes into nEffectType\n6. If nEffectType equals 7 (special effect type):\n   - Call FUN_6fb60e10 to get effect data pointer\n   - Call Ordinal_10564 to get current effect value\n   - Calculate percentage: (current_value * nDataValue) / 100\n   - Call Ordinal_10517 to apply calculated effect value with type 6\n\nParameters:\n  dwSearchKey - Search key to locate target node in linked list\n  nDataValue - Integer value to store in node and use for effect calculations\n  wFlags - Flags value (only lower 16 bits used) to store in node\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Returns early if global linked list is NULL (g_pLinkedListHead == NULL)\n  - Returns early if no node with matching dwSearchKey is found\n  - Effect calculation only occurs if node's effect type equals 7\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x7 (7) - Effect type that triggers special percentage-based calculation\n  0x6 (6) - Effect type parameter passed to Ordinal_10517\n  0xffff (65535) - Mask applied to wFlags to extract lower 16 bits\n\nStructure Layout:\nLinkedListNode structure accessed at these offsets:\nOffset  Size  Field Name    Type    Description\n0x08    4     dwSearchKey   dword   Search key for node identification  \n0x10    4     padding5-8    byte[4] Storage for wFlags data (little-endian)\n0x1C    4     padding17-20  byte[4] Storage for nDataValue data (little-endian)\n0x04    4     unknown5-8    byte[4] Effect type identifier bytes\n0x30    4     pNext         ptr     Pointer to next node in linked list\n\nError Handling:\n- No explicit error handling for NULL pointers beyond early return\n- Assumes valid LinkedListNode structure and proper linked list integrity\n- External function calls (Ordinals) may have their own error handling",
