      "comment": "Searches linked list for node with matching key and returns packed 4-byte value from padding fields.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize current node pointer to global linked list head (g_pLinkedListHead)\n2. Check if linked list is empty (head is null)\n3. If not empty, traverse linked list:\n   a. Compare current node's dwSearchKey field with search parameter\n   b. If match found, pack 4 bytes from padding17-20 fields into return value\n   c. If no match, advance to next node via pNext pointer\n   d. Continue until end of list (pNext is null)\n4. Return packed 4-byte value if match found, otherwise return 0\n\nParameters:\ndwSearchKey (int): Search key to match against node dwSearchKey field (offset +0x8)\nIMPLICIT: None\n\nReturns:\nint: Packed 4-byte value constructed from padding17-20 fields if match found, 0 if not found\n- Success: Non-zero packed value from bytes at offsets padding17-20 in matching node  \n- Failure: 0 when no node with matching dwSearchKey found or list is empty\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Empty list (g_pLinkedListHead is null): Returns 0 immediately\n- No matching node found: Returns 0 after full traversal\n- Multiple nodes with same key: Returns value from first matching node encountered\n\nStructure Layout:\nLinkedListNode structure accessed:\nOffset | Size | Field Name   | Type | Description\n+0x08  | 4    | dwSearchKey  | int  | Search key for node identification\n+0x1C  | 1    | padding17    | byte | First byte of packed return value\n+0x1D  | 1    | padding18    | byte | Second byte of packed return value  \n+0x1E  | 1    | padding19    | byte | Third byte of packed return value\n+0x1F  | 1    | padding20    | byte | Fourth byte of packed return value\n+0x30  | 4    | pNext        | ptr  | Pointer to next node in linked list",
