      "comment": "Search linked list for node by search key and return its value\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load global linked list head pointer from g_pLinkedListHead\n2. Check if list head is NULL, return 0 if empty list\n3. Begin linear search through linked list nodes\n4. Compare current node's dwSearchKey field (offset +0x8) with target search key\n5. If keys match, extract 4-byte value from node start (offset +0x0)\n6. If keys don't match, advance to next node via pNext pointer (offset +0x30)\n7. Continue until match found or end of list reached\n8. Return node value if found, 0 if not found\n\nParameters:\nnSearchKey (int): Target search key to locate in linked list nodes\n\nReturns:\nSuccess: 4-byte uint value from matching node (offset +0x0 in LinkedListNode)\nFailure: 0 if search key not found or list is empty\n\nStructure Layout:\nLinkedListNode at offset +0x0:\nOffset  Size  Field Name      Type    Description\n+0x0    4     dwValue         uint    Value returned by this function\n+0x8    4     dwSearchKey     uint    Search key for node identification  \n+0x30   4     pNext          ptr     Pointer to next node in linked list\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Empty list (g_pLinkedListHead == NULL) returns 0 immediately\n- Node found but somehow NULL pointer check returns 0 (defensive programming)\n- Search key 0 is valid and will be searched normally",
