      "comment": "Search linked list for node matching specified key and return packed data value.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load global linked list head pointer from g_pLinkedListHead (0x6fbee290)\n2. Check if list is empty (head pointer is NULL)\n3. If empty, jump to return 0 (no match found)\n4. Begin traversal loop starting from head node\n5. Compare current node's dwSearchKey field (offset +0x8) with nSearchKey parameter\n6. If key matches, proceed to extract data value\n7. If key doesn't match, advance to next node via pNext pointer (offset +0x30)\n8. If next pointer is NULL, exit loop and return 0\n9. If key matches, validate node pointer is not NULL\n10. If node is NULL, return 0 (safety check)\n11. Pack four byte fields (unknown5-8) into 32-bit return value using bit fields\n12. Return packed data value to caller\n\nParameters:\nnSearchKey (int): Search key value to match against node dwSearchKey field\n\nReturns:\nundefined4: Packed 32-bit value containing four bytes from matching node's data fields\n            Returns 0 if no matching node found or if node pointer is NULL\n\nSpecial Cases:\nEmpty list (g_pLinkedListHead == NULL) immediately returns 0\nNode pointer validation prevents dereferencing NULL after match\n\nStructure Layout:\nLinkedListNode structure (52 bytes total):\nOffset | Size | Field        | Type         | Description\n+0x4   | 4    | dwReturnData | undefined4   | Primary return value field\n+0x8   | 4    | dwSearchKey  | uint         | Key field for node identification  \n+0x30  | 4    | pNext        | LinkedListNode* | Pointer to next node in list\n+unknown offsets | 1 | unknown5 | byte | First byte of packed return value\n+unknown offsets | 1 | unknown6 | byte | Second byte of packed return value  \n+unknown offsets | 1 | unknown7 | byte | Third byte of packed return value\n+unknown offsets | 1 | unknown8 | byte | Fourth byte of packed return value",
