      "comment": "Searches linked list for node with matching search key and transmits extracted data.\nThis function iterates through the global linked list to find a node with a specific\nsearch key, extracts 4 bytes of data from the node, validates the session, and\ntransmits the data via a communication channel. Used for network data synchronization.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate global linked list head pointer is not NULL\n2. Iterate through linked list nodes comparing dwSearchKey fields  \n3. When match found, extract 4 bytes from node's padding fields into data value\n4. If no match found, set data value to -1 (invalid marker)\n5. Call FUN_6fb62880() to get current session information\n6. Validate session is active (session ID not -1)\n7. If session invalid, log error and terminate with FUN_6fb9a10f()\n8. If data value valid (!= -1), call FUN_6fb823e0() to transmit 8 bytes\n9. Return transmission result or 1 if no matching node found\n\nParameters:\npSearchableNode (SearchableListNode*): Pointer to searchable node structure containing search key at offset +8\n\nReturns:\nuint: Transmission result from FUN_6fb823e0() on success, 1 if no matching node found\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Returns 1 when no matching node found in linked list\n- Terminates process if session validation fails  \n- Uses padding1-4 fields to construct 4-byte data value for transmission\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x8 - Size parameter for FUN_6fb823e0() transmission call\n-1 - Invalid marker for both data value and session ID",
