      "comment": "Process skill cooldown timers for a specific player's active skills\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Traverse global linked list starting from g_pLinkedListHead\n2. For each node, reconstruct player ID from padding bytes (dwSearchKey comparison field)\n3. Skip nodes that don't match the target player ID (dwPlayerId parameter)\n4. Reconstruct skill type from unknown bytes and validate range (362 < skillType < 365)\n5. Skip nodes outside valid skill type range (cooldown-eligible skills only)\n6. Locate item pointer using node's dwSearchKey via FUN_6fb60e10 lookup\n7. Get current item state/status via FUN_6fb62950\n8. Search linked list again to find target player node matching item's player reference\n9. Extract target player ID from found node's padding bytes\n10. Validate current player context via FUN_6fb62880 (abort if invalid player ID)\n11. Compare target player with current player context via FUN_6fb823e0\n12. Set success flag based on comparison result (1 if match, 0 if mismatch)\n13. Compare current item state with item function result via FUN_6fb628f0\n14. If states match, call FUN_6fb62920 to update item with success flag\n15. Always call FUN_6fb628c0 to finalize item processing with success flag\n16. Continue to next node until list exhausted\n\nParameters:\ndwPlayerId - Target player identifier to process cooldowns for\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value (side effects update game state)\n\nSpecial Cases:\nInvalid player context triggers assertion failure and program termination\nSkills outside range 362-364 are ignored (non-cooldown skills)\nMissing item pointers are silently skipped\nTarget player mismatch results in failure flag (dwSuccessFlag = 0)\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x16a (362) - Minimum cooldown skill type (exclusive bound)\n0x16c (364) - Maximum cooldown skill type (exclusive bound)  \n0x16d (365) - Upper validation bound\n-1 (0xFFFFFFFF) - Invalid player/target ID sentinel\n1 - Success flag for matching operations\n0 - Failure flag for mismatched operations\n8 - Comparison parameter for player validation\n\nStructure Layout:\nLinkedListNode (52 bytes):\nOffset  Size  Field Name    Type    Description\n0x00    4     unknown1-4    byte    Player ID reconstruction bytes\n0x04    4     unknown5-8    byte    Skill type reconstruction bytes  \n0x08    4     dwSearchKey   uint    Item lookup key\n0x0C    4     padding1-4    byte    Player ID storage bytes\n0x30    4     pNext         ptr     Next node in linked list\n\nError Handling:\nInvalid player context (-1) triggers Ordinal_10023 assertion\nProgram terminates via FUN_6fb9a10f on assertion failure\nMissing nodes or items are silently ignored (continue processing)",
