      "instructions": ["0x11980|SUB|ESP, 0x5f4", "0x11986|CMP|EDX, -0x1", "0x11989|PUSH|EBX", "0x1198A|PUSH|ESI", "0x1198B|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0x1198D|JZ|0x6fae1cf4", "0x11993|XOR|EAX, EAX", "0x11995|MOV|AL, byte ptr [ESI]", "0x11997|ADD|EAX, 0xffffff59", "0x1199C|CMP|EAX, 0x5", "0x1199F|JA|0x6fae1cf4", "0x119A5|JMP|dword ptr [EAX*0x4 + 0x6fae1d00]", "0x119AC|POP|ESI", "0x119AD|MOV|dword ptr [0x6fbe9268], 0x1", "0x119B7|POP|EBX"],
      "comment": "Processes game command packets from the network or save file system.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate packet length - return early if length is -1 (invalid packet)\n2. Switch on command type byte (first byte of packet):\n   - 0xA7: Set global flag DAT_6fbe9268 to 1 (enable some system)\n   - 0xA8: Set global flag DAT_6fbe9268 to 0 (disable some system)\n   - 0xAB: Process file data chunk for progressive file transfer\n   - 0xAC: Set game difficulty level based on numeric parameter\n3. Command 0xAB file data processing:\n   - Check if file buffer DAT_6fbee294 is allocated, allocate if needed\n   - If packet[2] != 0, clear buffer and reallocate (reset transfer)\n   - Copy data from packet[7...] to file buffer at current offset\n   - Update buffer position DAT_6fbee298 by length in packet[1]\n   - If total bytes received equals expected size packet[3-6], finalize file\n   - Generate file path using format string and write buffer to file\n4. Command 0xAC difficulty processing:\n   - Extract 4-byte difficulty value from packet[1-4]\n   - Map values 1-24 to difficulty levels 0-26 via lookup table\n   - Default to difficulty 9 for unmapped values\n\nParameters:\n- pCommandPacket (byte *): Pointer to command packet buffer\n- nPacketLength (int): Length of packet in bytes, -1 indicates invalid packet\n\nReturns:\n- void: Function processes commands and returns without value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Length -1: Early return without processing (invalid packet marker)\n- Command 0xAB with packet[2] != 0: Resets file transfer and clears buffer\n- File buffer size > 0x81 bytes: Enables video processing and file writing\n- DAT_6fbe910c == 0: Triggers error path with debug info and program termination\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n- 0xA7 (167): Enable system flag command\n- 0xA8 (168): Disable system flag command  \n- 0xAB (171): File data transfer command\n- 0xAC (172): Set difficulty command\n- 0x46 (70): Buffer allocation type parameter\n- 0x3F (63): Buffer deallocation type parameter\n- 0x55 (85): File processing completion type parameter\n- 0x81 (129): Minimum buffer size threshold for file operations\n\nError Handling:\n- Invalid packet length: Silent return without processing\n- File buffer allocation failure: Uses existing global buffer or reallocates\n- File creation failure: Continues processing without writing data\n- Missing debug flag: Triggers assertion with source file path and line number",
