      "comment": "Initializes post-game state after game session ends.\n\nClassification: Initialization function - sets up rendering mode and clears palette for post-game UI.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Set g_dwPostGameRenderMode to 1 (enable post-game rendering)\n2. Clear g_pCurrentPalette to NULL (reset palette pointer)\n3. Retrieve game context unit stat via GetGameContextUnitStat\n4. If game context is NULL, trigger fatal error and exit\n5. Get entity field from game context\n6. Get character tier index from experience value\n7. Initialize game units with monster definitions\n8. Get game context as UnitAny pointer\n9. Clear unit inventory slots for the unit\n\nParameters: None (void)\n\nReturns: void (does not return on error - calls ExitApplicationWithCode)\n\nError Handling:\n- If GetGameContextUnitStat returns NULL, logs fatal error \"Could not get act\"\n  at D2Client.cpp line 0x65a (1626 decimal) and exits with code -1\n\nGlobal State Modified:\n- g_dwPostGameRenderMode: Set to 1 (DWORD at 0x6fbe926c)\n- g_pCurrentPalette: Set to NULL (pointer at 0x6fbe9274)\n\nCallees:\n- GetGameContextUnitStat: Retrieves game context unit stat\n- GetEntityField: Gets entity field from game context\n- GetCharacterTierIndex: Gets character tier from experience\n- InitializeGameUnitsWithMonsterDefinitions: Initializes monster unit data\n- GetGameContext: Returns current game context pointer\n- ClearUnitInventorySlots: Clears inventory slots for unit\n\nCross-References: No direct callers found - likely called via function pointer or jump table",
