      "comment": "Initialize game difficulty based on current server port configuration\n\nClassification: Initialization function - sets up game difficulty state based on server type\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if server port is dedicated server type (7) or LAN server type (9)\n2. If dedicated/LAN server AND global status is zero, set difficulty level 8\n3. Check if server port is client type (2) or singleplayer type (3)\n4. If client/singleplayer AND post-game render mode is active, set difficulty level 7\n5. Enable game system flag (set g_dwGameSystemEnabled = 1)\n\nParameters:\nNone - reads global state directly\n\nReturns:\nvoid - no return value, operates by side effect on global difficulty state\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Dedicated Server (port 7): Sets difficulty 8 only if global status uninitialized\n- LAN Server (port 9): Same behavior as dedicated server\n- Client Connection (port 2): Sets difficulty 7 if post-game rendering active\n- Singleplayer (port 3): Same behavior as client connection\n- Other port values: Only enables game system without changing difficulty\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x7: Dedicated server port identifier\n0x9: LAN server port identifier  \n0x2: Client connection port identifier\n0x3: Singleplayer mode port identifier\n0x8: Difficulty level for server modes (dedicated/LAN)\n0x7: Difficulty level for client modes (client/singleplayer)\n0x1: Game system enabled flag value\n\nCross-References:\n- g_dwServerPort (0x6fbe9260): Current server connection type\n- g_dwPostGameRenderMode (0x6fbe926c): Post-game rendering state flag\n- g_dwGameSystemEnabled (0x6fbe9270): Master game system enable flag\n\nCallees:\n- GetGlobalStatus(): Returns current global initialization status\n- SetGameDifficulty(): Applies difficulty level with bounds checking",
