      "comment": "Initialize game context from packet data by looking up unit and setting state.\n\nClassification: Thunk/Wrapper - Translates packet data into game context initialization.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract unit ID from packet offset +2 (DWORD)\n2. Extract slot type from packet offset +1 (BYTE)\n3. Call FindUnitInHashTable(nUnitId, nSlotType) to locate unit in hash table\n4. Call InitializeGameContextAndState(pGameContext) with returned context\n5. Tail-call NoOperation() (stub function)\n\nParameters:\npbPacketData (byte *) - Pointer to packet data structure\n  +0x01: Slot type (BYTE) - Unit slot type for hash table lookup\n  +0x02: Unit ID (DWORD) - Unit identifier for hash table lookup\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value, modifies global game context state\n\nPacket Structure Layout:\nOffset  Size  Field       Description\n0x00    1     header      Packet header/type (not used here)\n0x01    1     nSlotType   Unit slot type for hash lookup\n0x02    4     nUnitId     Unit identifier\n\nCallees:\n- FindUnitInHashTable: Locates unit by ID and slot type\n- InitializeGameContextAndState: Sets up game context globals\n- NoOperation: Stub (tail call)\n\nNotes:\n- No callers found - likely called via function pointer table or packet handler\n- Wrapper pattern: unpacks packet fields and delegates to core functions",
