      "comment": "Handle incoming unit state message and dispatch to state action handler.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate 7-element parameter array on stack (28 bytes)\n2. Zero-initialize all 7 elements using REP STOSD\n3. Extract first parameter byte from pbMessage[7] into adParams[0]\n4. Extract second parameter byte from pbMessage[8] into adParams[1]\n5. Extract operation type byte from pbMessage[6]\n6. Call DispatchUnitStateAction(operationType, pUnit, adParams, 1)\n7. Return\n\nParameters:\n- pUnit (UnitAny*, ECX): Target unit for state operation\n- pbMessage (byte*, EDX): Pointer to network message packet\n  - pbMessage[6]: Operation type byte (0-4, see DispatchUnitStateAction)\n  - pbMessage[7]: First parameter byte (stored in adParams[0])\n  - pbMessage[8]: Second parameter byte (stored in adParams[1])\n\nReturns:\n- void: No return value. State changes are applied via DispatchUnitStateAction.\n\nMessage Format:\n  Offset 6: Operation type (byte) - determines which handler executes\n  Offset 7: Param 1 (byte) - meaning depends on operation type\n  Offset 8: Param 2 (byte) - meaning depends on operation type\n\nReferenced from message handler table at 0x6fbb02a8.\nCallback invoked by message dispatch system for unit state updates.",
