      "comment": "Process unit movement packet and dispatch state action.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract parameter values from packet:\n   - Offset +0x7 (word): Parameter 1 for state action\n   - Offset +0x9 (word): Parameter 2 for state action  \n   - Offset +0xB (byte): Parameter 3 for state action\n2. Extract coordinates from packet:\n   - Offset +0xC (word): X coordinate\n   - Offset +0xE (word): Y coordinate\n3. Call ValidateAndProcessUnitMovement with unit, coordinates, and zero movement params\n4. Extract action type from packet offset +0x6 (byte)\n5. Call DispatchUnitStateAction with action type, unit, parameter array, and flags=1\n\nParameters:\npUnit (IMPLICIT ECX): Pointer to UnitAny structure being moved\npbPacket (IMPLICIT EDX): Pointer to packet data containing movement and state info\n  Packet Layout:\n  +0x6: byte - Action type for state dispatch\n  +0x7: word - State parameter 1\n  +0x9: word - State parameter 2\n  +0xB: byte - State parameter 3\n  +0xC: word - X coordinate\n  +0xE: word - Y coordinate\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Passes zeros for movement type, target X, and target Y to ValidateAndProcessUnitMovement\n- State action parameters passed as uint array on stack (dwParam1, dwParam2, dwParam3)",
