      "comment": "Handle unit state action packet by unpacking fields and dispatching.\n\nClassification: Callback/Handler - invoked by network packet processing system.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract unit type from packet offset +5 (byte)\n2. Extract parameter 0 (wParam0) from packet offset +6 (ushort, zero-extended)\n3. Extract parameter 1 (wParam1) from packet offset +8 (ushort, zero-extended)\n4. Extract parameter 2 from packet offset +10 (byte, zero-extended)\n5. Extract parameter 3 from packet offset +12 (byte, zero-extended)\n6. Extract parameter 4 from packet offset +13 (signed char, sign-extended)\n7. Extract parameter 5 from packet offset +14 (byte, zero-extended)\n8. Extract parameter 6 from packet offset +11 (byte, zero-extended)\n9. Build parameter array on stack [dwParam0..dwParam6]\n10. Call DispatchUnitStateAction(nUnitType, pUnit, pParams, 1)\n\nParameters:\n- pUnit (UnitAny*, ECX): Target unit for state action\n- pPacketData (byte*, EDX): Network packet data buffer\n\nReturns: void\n\nPacket Structure (offsets from pPacketData):\nOffset  Size  Field        Description\n+0x05   1     nUnitType    Unit type identifier for dispatch\n+0x06   2     wParam0      First word parameter (ushort)\n+0x08   2     wParam1      Second word parameter (ushort)\n+0x0A   1     byParam2     Byte parameter 2\n+0x0B   1     byParam6     Byte parameter 6 (out of order in struct)\n+0x0C   1     byParam3     Byte parameter 3\n+0x0D   1     chParam4     Signed char parameter 4\n+0x0E   1     byParam5     Byte parameter 5\n\nNotes:\n- No callers found - likely registered as packet handler callback\n- Passes constant flags value of 1 to dispatch\n- Parameter array passed by pointer to DispatchUnitStateAction",
