      "comment": "Parse packet data and dispatch unit state action.\n\nExtracts state parameters from packet buffer and builds a parameter block\nfor DispatchUnitStateAction. Used to process incoming network messages\nthat modify unit state.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate 24-byte stack frame for parameter block\n2. Extract unit type from pbPacketData[5] for dispatch selection\n3. Extract dwStateParam1 from pbPacketData[6] (byte, zero-extended)\n4. Extract dwStateParam2 from pbPacketData[7..10] (dword)\n5. Extract dwStateParam3 from pbPacketData[11] (byte, zero-extended)\n6. Initialize dwActionType = 2, dwReserved = 0, dwParamCount = 4\n7. Call DispatchUnitStateAction(nUnitType, pUnit, &paramBlock, 1)\n8. Clean up stack and return\n\nParameters:\n- pUnit (UnitAny*, ECX): Target unit to apply state action\n- pbPacketData (byte*, EDX): Packet buffer containing state parameters\n\nPacket Format:\nOffset  Size  Field\n+0x05   1     nUnitType - Unit type for dispatch selection\n+0x06   1     dwStateParam1 - First state parameter\n+0x07   4     dwStateParam2 - Second state parameter (dword)\n+0x0B   1     dwStateParam3 - Third state parameter\n\nParameter Block Layout (24 bytes):\nOffset  Field           Value\n+0x00   dwStateParam1   From packet[6]\n+0x04   dwStateParam2   From packet[7..10]\n+0x08   dwStateParam3   From packet[11]\n+0x0C   dwActionType    Constant 2\n+0x10   dwReserved      Constant 0\n+0x14   dwParamCount    Constant 4\n\nReturns: void\n\nCalled By: Possibly via function pointer table (no direct xrefs found)",
