      "comment": "Process unit movement message and dispatch state action.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate pUnit and pbMoveData are non-null; return if either is null\n2. Extract X coordinate from pbMoveData[5:7] (ushort at offset +5)\n3. Extract Y coordinate from pbMoveData[7:9] (ushort at offset +7)\n4. Extract direction/flags byte from pbMoveData[9] (byte at offset +9)\n5. Initialize movement parameters on stack (dwMoveType=2, dwMoveFlags=0, dwTargetType=4, dwTargetFlags=0)\n6. Call ValidateAndProcessUnitMovement(pUnit, dwXCoord, dwYCoord, 0, 0, 0) to process movement\n7. Call DispatchUnitStateAction(7, pUnit, &dwXCoord, 1) to dispatch state action type 7\n\nParameters:\npUnit (IMPLICIT ECX): Pointer to UnitAny structure to move\npbMoveData (IMPLICIT EDX): Pointer to movement data packet with format:\n  +0x05: ushort - X coordinate\n  +0x07: ushort - Y coordinate\n  +0x09: byte - Direction/flags\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nStructure Layout (Movement Data Packet):\nOffset  Size  Field       Type    Description\n0x05    2     wXCoord     ushort  Target X coordinate\n0x07    2     wYCoord     ushort  Target Y coordinate\n0x09    1     byDirection byte    Movement direction or flags\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Early return if pUnit is NULL\n- Early return if pbMoveData is NULL\n- Action type 7 is dispatched with coordinates as parameters",
