      "comment": "Processes a server command to change unit state.\n\nClassification: Worker function - handles incoming unit state change commands from server\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract unit type byte from command data at offset +1\n2. Extract unit ID dword from command data at offset +2\n3. Copy 20 bytes (5 dwords) of state data from offset +6 to local buffer\n4. Look up the unit in hash table using FindUnitInHashTable(unitId, unitType)\n5. If unit not found, log warning message and return\n6. If unit found, call ProcessUnitStateChanges(pUnit, stateData) to apply changes\n\nParameters:\n  pCommandData (byte *, ECX) - Pointer to packed command buffer with structure:\n    +0x00: byte  - Command ID (not used in this function)\n    +0x01: byte  - Unit type\n    +0x02: dword - Unit ID\n    +0x06: byte[20] - State change data (5 dwords)\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nCommand Data Layout:\n  Offset  Size   Field          Description\n  0x00    1      byCommandId    Command identifier (skipped)\n  0x01    1      byUnitType     Unit type for hash table lookup\n  0x02    4      dwUnitId       Unit GUID for lookup\n  0x06    20     adStateData    State change parameters (5 dwords)\n\nError Handling:\n  If unit not found in hash table, logs warning with unit type and ID\n\nCross-References:\n  Callers: None identified (may be called via function pointer table)\n  Callees: FindUnitInHashTable, QueueLogMessage, ProcessUnitStateChanges",
