      "comment": "Process unit state change command packet from client.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract unit ID from packet offset +2 (4 bytes)\n2. Extract command type from packet offset +1 (1 byte) \n3. Extract new state value from packet offset +6 (4 bytes)\n4. Call FUN_6fb60e10 to lookup unit by ID and command type\n5. If unit not found, log warning message and return early\n6. If unit found, call FUN_6fb852d0 to apply state change\n7. Return after processing\n\nParameters:\npPacket - Pointer to PacketHeader containing unit state change command data\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value, function processes command and updates unit state\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If unit lookup fails, logs \"WARNING: sSCmd_UnitChangeStateVal, Attempt to change state on a\" message\n- Warning includes command type and unit ID for debugging\n\nStructure Layout:\nPacketHeader at pPacket:\nOffset  Size  Field Name    Type    Description\n------  ----  ----------    ----    -----------\n+0x1    1     bCmdType      byte    Command type identifier  \n+0x2    4     dwUnitId      uint    Target unit identifier\n+0x6    4     nNewState     int     New state value to apply\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x1 - Command type byte offset in packet\n0x2 - Unit ID dword offset in packet  \n0x6 - New state value offset in packet",
