      "comment": "Handles server command 0xA8 (SCMD_UnitChangeStateValVal) to apply state changes to a unit.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract unit type (byte at offset +1), unit ID (dword at offset +2), state index (dword at offset +6)\n2. Extract state flags (dword at offset +10) and state data (dword at offset +14)\n3. Call FindUnitInHashTable to locate the unit by ID and type\n4. If unit not found, log warning message and return\n5. If unit found, call ApplyEntityStateChange with state index, flags, and data\n\nParameters:\n  pbPacket (ECX): Pointer to server packet buffer with structure:\n    +0x00: byte  - Packet opcode (0xA8)\n    +0x01: byte  - Unit type\n    +0x02: dword - Unit ID\n    +0x06: dword - State index\n    +0x0A: dword - State flags\n    +0x0E: dword - State data value\n\nReturns: void\n\nPacket Structure (18 bytes total):\n  Offset  Size  Field        Description\n  0x00    1     byOpcode     Packet identifier (0xA8)\n  0x01    1     byUnitType   Unit type for hash lookup\n  0x02    4     dwUnitId     Unit ID for hash lookup\n  0x06    4     nStateIndex  Index of state to modify\n  0x0A    4     dwFlags      State modification flags\n  0x0E    4     dwStateData  State value to apply\n\nCallees:\n  FindUnitInHashTable - Locates unit in client unit table\n  QueueLogMessage - Logs warning on missing unit\n  ApplyEntityStateChange - Applies state change to unit",
