      "instructions": ["0x12670|PUSH|EBX", "0x12671|PUSH|EBP", "0x12672|PUSH|ESI", "0x12673|PUSH|EDI", "0x12674|MOV|EDI, ECX", "0x12676|XOR|EDX, EDX", "0x12678|MOV|ECX, dword ptr [EDI + 0x2]", "0x1267B|MOV|DL, byte ptr [EDI + 0x1]", "0x1267E|MOV|BP, word ptr [EDI + 0x6]", "0x12682|MOV|BX, word ptr [EDI + 0x8]", "0x12686|CALL|0x6fb60e10", "0x1268B|MOV|ESI, EAX", "0x1268D|TEST|ESI, ESI", "0x1268F|JZ|0x6fae2735", "0x12695|XOR|EAX, EAX"],
      "comment": "Process a unit warp packet by setting up coordinates and validating packet constraints.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract coordinates (X, Y) from warp packet at offsets +6 and +8\n2. Extract additional packet fields (unit ID at +2, byte at +1, level at +10)  \n3. Call FUN_6fb60e10 to look up the unit being warped using unit ID and byte param\n4. If unit found, call FUN_6fb61180 to set unit coordinates and level parameter\n5. Get the act for this unit using Ordinal_10342\n6. If act retrieval fails, display error \"Could not get act\" and terminate\n7. Get level ID from act using Ordinal_10057 and convert to byte with Ordinal_10001\n8. Store level byte in unit structure at offset +5 (0x14 in assembly)\n9. Set render context handle in unit structure at offset +6 (0x18 in assembly)\n10. Check if unit needs initialization: if unit[0] == 0 AND unit[0xe] != 0\n11. If initialization needed, call Ordinal_10214 and Ordinal_10184 with 0x1c09\n12. Get current unit using FUN_6fb62880 and compare with warp target unit\n13. If warping current unit, validate packet with Ordinal_10083\n14. If validation fails, display \"Illegal packet in sSCmd_UnitWarp\" error and terminate\n15. If validation succeeds, update timeout deadline to 3000ms\n\nParameters:\npWarpPacket - Pointer to PacketData structure containing warp coordinates and unit info\n  +1: byte unitType - Type/category of unit being warped\n  +2: uint unitId - Unique identifier for the unit to warp\n  +6: ushort coordX - Target X coordinate for warp destination  \n  +8: ushort coordY - Target Y coordinate for warp destination\n  +10: byte levelParam - Level-related parameter for warp operation\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value, function terminates process on critical errors\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Terminates process if unit lookup fails (act retrieval returns 0)\n- Terminates process if illegal packet detected when warping current unit\n- Only performs validation checks when warping the current unit (not other units)\n- Updates timeout deadline only for current unit warp operations\n- Unit initialization only occurs when unit[0] == 0 AND unit[0xe] != 0\n\nStructure Layout:\nPacketData structure:\nOffset | Size | Field Name | Type   | Description\n+0x01  | 1    | unitType   | byte   | Type/category of unit  \n+0x02  | 4    | unitId     | uint   | Unique unit identifier\n+0x06  | 2    | coordX     | ushort | Target X coordinate\n+0x08  | 2    | coordY     | ushort | Target Y coordinate  \n+0x0A  | 1    | levelParam | byte   | Level-related parameter\n\nUnit structure access:\nOffset | Size | Field Name     | Type | Description\n+0x00  | 4    | flags          | uint | Unit status flags\n+0x14  | 1    | levelId        | byte | Current level identifier\n+0x18  | 4    | hRenderContext | uint | Render context handle\n+0x38  | 4    | pExtendedData  | uint | Pointer to extended unit data\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x1c09 - Extended data initialization parameter for Ordinal_10184\n0x66b - Error code line number for \"Could not get act\" error\n0x974 - Error code line number for \"Illegal packet in sSCmd_UnitWarp\" error  \n3000 - Timeout deadline value in milliseconds for warp operations\n0xffffffff - Process termination code (-1)",
