      "comment": "Dispatches skill visual effect rendering based on network packet type.\n\nClassification: Dispatcher function - routes incoming skill effect packets to specialized rendering handlers.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract packet fields: effect type (offset +2), target mode (offset +4), coordinates (offsets +0x10, +0x14), target unit ID (offset +0xc)\n2. Look up source unit in hash table using unit ID at packet offset +7 and type byte at offset +6\n3. Look up target unit in hash table using dwTargetUnitId and type byte at offset +0xb\n4. Switch on wEffectType to select handler index (0-8) from effect type mapping\n5. If effect type recognized, call handler function via g_apfnEffectHandlers[nHandlerIndex]\n6. Pass handler: wTargetMode, dwCoordX, dwCoordY, and render mode byte at packet offset +1\n\nParameters:\n  pbPacket - Pointer to skill effect network packet (byte *, ECX via __fastcall)\n\nPacket Structure Layout:\n  Offset  Size  Field             Description\n  0x00    1     byPacketId        Packet identifier\n  0x01    1     byRenderMode      Rendering mode passed to handler\n  0x02    2     wEffectType       Skill effect type (switch selector)\n  0x04    2     wTargetMode       Target mode passed to handler\n  0x06    1     bySourceUnitType  Unit type for source lookup\n  0x07    4     dwSourceUnitId    Source unit ID for hash lookup\n  0x0B    1     byTargetUnitType  Unit type for target lookup\n  0x0C    4     dwTargetUnitId    Target unit ID for hash lookup\n  0x10    4     dwCoordX          X coordinate for effect\n  0x14    4     dwCoordY          Y coordinate for effect\n\nEffect Type to Handler Mapping:\n  0x0103 (259) -> Index 0: RenderAreaEffectByMode\n  0x010D (269) -> Index 1: CreateGameObjectByMode\n  0x0112 (274) -> Index 2: GenerateMissileSpawnPoints\n  0x00FE (254) -> Index 3: PlaySoundAndOverlayByType\n  0x0109 (265) -> Index 4: DispatchOverlayEffectByType\n  0x0118 (280) -> Index 5: ExecuteSkillMode\n  0x00F9 (249) -> Index 6: AccessResourceType249\n  0x00F4 (244) -> Index 7: PlaySequentialAudioSounds\n  0x0133 (307) -> Index 8: InitializeAudioPlaybackParams\n\nReturns: void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Unrecognized effect types (default case) exit without calling any handler\n- Both source and target units are looked up but results not used directly in this function\n- Handler table at 0x6fbb01e8 contains 9 function pointers\n\nRelated Data:\n- g_apfnEffectHandlers at 0x6fbb01e8 (function pointer table)\n- Switch lookup table at 0x6fae2a90",
