      "comment": "Initialize monster region statistics from a unit structure\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract region/level ID from unit structure at offset +1 (ushort)\n2. Bounds check: verify region ID is less than 0x23F (575 max regions)\n3. If valid, tail-call InitializeMonsterRegionStats with region ID and 0\n4. If invalid (>= 575), return immediately without action\n\nParameters:\n  pUnit (ECX) - Pointer to unit structure containing region ID at offset +1\n    Offset +1: ushort wRegionId - Level/region identifier\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value, delegates to InitializeMonsterRegionStats\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Region ID >= 0x23F (575): Silently returns without initialization\n  - Uses tail-call optimization (JMP instead of CALL/RET)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x23F (575) - Maximum valid region ID (D2 level count limit)\n  0x01 - Offset of region ID field in unit structure\n\nRelated Functions:\n  InitializeMonsterRegionStats() - Target function that performs actual initialization",
