      "instructions": ["0x12BB0|SUB|ESP, 0x10", "0x12BB3|PUSH|EBX", "0x12BB4|PUSH|EBP", "0x12BB5|PUSH|ESI", "0x12BB6|PUSH|EDI", "0x12BB7|MOV|EDI, ECX", "0x12BB9|XOR|ESI, ESI", "0x12BBB|OR|EBX, 0xffffffff", "0x12BBE|MOV|AL, byte ptr [EDI]", "0x12BC0|MOV|byte ptr [ESP + 0x10], AL", "0x12BC4|CALL|0x6fb62880", "0x12BC9|MOV|EBP, EAX", "0x12BCB|TEST|EBP, EBP", "0x12BCD|JNZ|0x6fae2bed", "0x12BCF|PUSH|0xae1"],
      "comment": "Process unit stat update packets from server.\n\nHandles server-to-client packets 0x19-0x1F that update player unit statistics.\nEach packet type has different encoding for stat ID and value:\n  0x19: Add byte delta to stat 0x0E (Life)\n  0x1A: Add byte delta to stat 0x0D (Mana)\n  0x1B: Add word delta to stat 0x0D (Mana)\n  0x1C: Set stat 0x0D (Mana) to dword absolute value\n  0x1D: Set stat ID (byte) to value (byte)\n  0x1E: Set stat ID (byte) to value (word)\n  0x1F: Set stat ID (byte) to value (dword)\n\nAfter updating the stat, performs special processing for stats 0-12\nvia secondary jump table for visual/UI updates.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize nValue=0, nStatId=0xFFFFFFFF\n2. Read packet opcode from pbPacketData[0]\n3. Get player unit via GetGameContext(), assert non-null\n4. Switch on packet opcode (0x19-0x1F):\n   - 0x19/0x1A: Get current stat value, add byte delta from [1]\n   - 0x1B: Get current mana, add word delta from [1]\n   - 0x1C: Set mana to dword value from [1]\n   - 0x1D: Stat ID from [1], value byte from [2]\n   - 0x1E: Stat ID from [1], value word from [2]\n   - 0x1F: Stat ID from [1], value dword from [2]\n5. Call SetUnitStat(pUnit, nStatId, nValue)\n6. If stat ID > 0x0C, return early\n7. Otherwise, execute stat-specific handler via secondary jump table\n\nParameters:\n  pbPacketData (ECX): Pointer to packet data buffer\n    [0] = Packet opcode (0x19-0x1F)\n    [1] = Stat ID or delta value (depends on opcode)\n    [2] = Value (for opcodes 0x1D-0x1F)\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - NULL unit context triggers assertion and application exit\n  - Stats 0x0D (Mana) and 0x0E (Life) have dedicated opcodes\n  - Stats 0-12 trigger post-update handlers for UI refresh\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x19-0x1F: Server stat update packet opcodes\n  0x0D (13): Mana stat ID\n  0x0E (14): Life stat ID\n  0x0C (12): Max stat ID for secondary processing\n  0xAE1 (2785): Source line number for assertion\n\nSecondary Jump Table (stat IDs 0-12):\n  DAT_6fae2d40[nStatId] indexes into PTR_LAB_6fae2d30 for handlers",
      "tags": ["SRC_SCmd.cpp", "PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_1", "MOD_GAME"]
    },
