      "comment": "Processes a unit stat update message received from the server.\n\nParses a network message containing unit GUID, stat ID, and value.\nLooks up the unit in the hash table and applies the stat change,\nthen triggers appropriate side effects based on which stat was modified.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract nValue from message offset +6 (4 bytes)\n2. Look up unit by GUID from message offset +1\n3. Extract stat ID from message offset +5\n4. If unit not found, exit early\n5. Call SetUnitStat to apply the stat value\n6. Switch on stat ID for special handling:\n   - Case 0, 2: If unit is player, refresh item effects\n   - Case 6: If value non-zero and unit mode is 0x11, clear state and update flags\n   - Case 0xC: Build nested message and process items, then refresh if player\n\nParameters:\n  pbMessage (ECX) - Pointer to stat update message packet\n    +0x01: DWORD - Unit GUID for hash table lookup\n    +0x05: BYTE  - Stat ID (determines special handling path)\n    +0x06: DWORD - Stat value to apply\n\nReturns: void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Stat 0/2: Triggers item effect refresh for player unit only\n  - Stat 6: Clears unit state and updates flags if mode is 0x11 (NPC mode)\n  - Stat 0xC: Constructs internal message (type 0x47) to process unit items\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x11 - Unit mode indicating NPC/object state requiring transition\n  0x47 - Internal message type for ProcessUnitItemsFromNodeData\n  5    - Transition state parameter for ClearUnitStateAndProcessTransition",
