      "instructions": ["0x12E30|SUB|ESP, 0x24", "0x12E33|PUSH|ESI", "0x12E34|PUSH|0xf", "0x12E36|LEA|EAX, [ESP + 0x8]", "0x12E3A|PUSH|ECX", "0x12E3B|PUSH|EAX", "0x12E3C|CALL|0x6fb99b0a", "0x12E41|LEA|ECX, [ESP + 0x4]", "0x12E45|PUSH|0x8", "0x12E47|PUSH|ECX", "0x12E48|CALL|0x6fb99b04", "0x12E4D|LEA|EDX, [ESP + 0x4]", "0x12E51|PUSH|0xf", "0x12E53|PUSH|EDX", "0x12E54|CALL|0x6fb99b04"],
      "comment": "Parses a bit-packed network packet containing player unit stats and position updates.\n\nClassification: Worker function (network packet handler)\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize bit buffer with 15-byte packet data\n2. Skip 8-bit packet header\n3. Read 15-bit hitpoints value\n4. Read 15-bit mana value\n5. Read 15-bit stamina value\n6. Read 7-bit stamina percentage\n7. Read 7-bit experience modifier\n8. Read 16-bit X position\n9. Read 16-bit Y position (stored as low/high bytes)\n10. Read 8-bit X delta (signed offset)\n11. Read 8-bit Y delta (signed offset)\n12. Get player unit from game context\n13. If player unit exists:\n    a. Set stat 6 (HP) = hitpoints << 8\n    b. Set stat 8 (Mana) = mana << 8\n    c. Set stat 10 (Stamina) = stamina << 8\n    d. Set stat 0x4A (74) = stamina pct byte\n    e. Set stat 0x1A (26) = experience modifier\n14. Convert delta bytes to signed (subtract 0x100 if > 0x80)\n15. Call ValidateAndProcessUnitMovement with position data\n16. If hitpoints != 0 and unit field_c == 0x11 (state):\n    Clear unit state and process transition\n\nParameters:\n  pbPacketData (ECX) - Pointer to 15-byte bit-packed network packet\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Returns immediately if GetGameContext returns NULL\n  - State transition only occurs if hitpoints != 0 and unit state == 0x11\n\nStat ID Reference:\n  6 = Hitpoints (scaled by 256)\n  8 = Mana (scaled by 256)\n  10 = Stamina (scaled by 256)\n  0x1A (26) = Experience modifier\n  0x4A (74) = Stamina percentage\n\nPacket Layout (15 bytes, bit-packed):\n  Bits 0-7: Packet header (skipped)\n  Bits 8-22: Hitpoints (15 bits)\n  Bits 23-37: Mana (15 bits)\n  Bits 38-52: Stamina (15 bits)\n  Bits 53-59: Stamina percentage (7 bits)\n  Bits 60-66: Experience modifier (7 bits)\n  Bits 67-82: X position (16 bits)\n  Bits 83-98: Y position (16 bits)\n  Bits 99-106: X delta (8 bits, signed)\n  Bits 107-114: Y delta (8 bits, signed)",
      "tags": ["PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_1"]
    },
