      "comment": "Configure unit graphics rendering and display parameters\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract mode value from unit structure at offset +0x7 (2-byte word)\n2. Call FUN_6fb60e10 to retrieve graphics data structure using unit's class ID (+0x3 offset)\n3. Call D2COMMON.DLL ordinal 10953 to configure primary graphics settings\n   - Pass graphics data pointer, mode value, and unit parameters from offsets +0x9 and +0x2\n4. Call D2COMMON.DLL ordinal 11030 to configure secondary graphics settings\n   - Pass graphics data pointer, mode value, and unit parameter from offset +0xa\n5. Call FUN_6fb4ea70 to finalize graphics configuration (tail call optimization)\n\nParameters:\npUnit (int *): Pointer to unit data structure containing graphics configuration\n  IMPLICIT ECX: Unit pointer passed via fastcall register\n\nReturns:\nvoid: Function performs configuration and returns nothing\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Function uses offsets +0x2, +0x3, +0x7, +0x9, +0xa from unit structure\n- Tail call optimization used for final graphics finalization step\n- D2COMMON.DLL ordinals suggest Diablo II game engine integration\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset  Size  Field Name       Type    Description\n+0x2    1     byParameter1     byte    First parameter for graphics config\n+0x3    4     dwClassId        uint    Unit class identifier for graphics lookup\n+0x7    2     wMode            ushort  Graphics display mode\n+0x9    1     byParameter2     byte    Second parameter for graphics config  \n+0xa    1     byParameter3     byte    Third parameter for graphics config",
