      "comment": "Parse skill update network packet and apply skill delta to matching unit.\n\nClassification: Packet Handler - processes incoming server message for skill modifications.\n\nAlgorithm:\n\n1. Extract signed skill delta from packet byte[5] with sign extension (-128 to 127)\n2. Extract unit type filter from packet byte[6]\n3. Extract skill state filter from packet byte[7]\n4. Look up target unit by GUID from packet bytes[1-4] via FindUnitInHashTable\n5. If unit found, apply skill delta via ProcessUnitActiveSkills with filters\n\nParameters:\n\npbPacketData - Pointer to raw packet data buffer (passed in ECX via __fastcall)\n\nPacket Structure (8 bytes minimum):\n\nOffset | Size | Field              | Description\n-------|------|--------------------|----------------------------------\n+0x00  |  1   | byOpcode           | Packet opcode (not parsed here)\n+0x01  |  4   | dwUnitGUID         | Unit GUID to look up in hash table\n+0x05  |  1   | nSignedDelta       | Signed skill delta (-128 to +127)\n+0x06  |  1   | byUnitTypeFilter   | Unit type filter (0 = all types)\n+0x07  |  1   | bySkillStateFilter | Skill state filter (4 = all states)\n\nReturns:\n\nvoid - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n\n- If unit GUID lookup fails, function silently returns without processing\n- Delta byte is treated as signed: values > 0x80 are sign-extended to negative\n- Sign extension: nDelta = byte - 0x100 when byte > 0x80 (e.g., 0xFF becomes -1)\n\nCallees:\n\n- FindUnitInHashTable: Locates UnitAny by GUID (param_2=0 for type filter)\n- ProcessUnitActiveSkills: Applies delta to skills matching filter criteria",
      "tags": ["PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_1"]
    },
