      "comment": "Processes a network packet containing a list of skills to set on a unit.\n\nClassification: Packet Handler - processes server-to-client skill list update\n\nPacket Structure (variable length):\n  Offset  Size  Field         Description\n  +0x00   1     byOpcode      Packet opcode (not accessed here)\n  +0x01   1     bySkillCount  Number of skill entries in packet\n  +0x02   4     dwUnitGUID    Unit GUID to look up\n  +0x06   3*N   SkillEntries  Array of skill entries (N = bySkillCount)\n\nSkill Entry Structure (3 bytes each):\n  Offset  Size  Field         Description\n  +0x00   2     wSkillId      Skill ID\n  +0x02   1     bySkillLevel  Skill level to set\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Extract skill count from packet offset +1\n  2. Get pointer to skill entries at packet offset +6\n  3. Look up unit by GUID from packet offset +2 using FindUnitInHashTable\n  4. If unit found and skill count > 0:\n     5. Loop through each skill entry:\n        a. Read skill ID (2 bytes) and level (1 byte)\n        b. Call SetUnitSkillLevel(pUnit, wSkillId, byLevel, 0)\n        c. Advance pointer by 3 bytes to next entry\n        d. Decrement counter and repeat until zero\n\nParameters:\n  pbPacketData (ECX): Pointer to raw packet data\n\nReturns: void\n\nLoop Details:\n  Counter: uVar2 (unsigned), initialized from bySkillCount\n  Bounds: [bySkillCount, 0), decrements to zero\n  Stride: 3 bytes per skill entry\n  Exit: uVar2 == 0\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If unit not found in hash table, returns immediately without error\n  - If skill count is 0, loop body never executes\n  - Fourth parameter to SetUnitSkillLevel is always 0 (unknown flag)",
      "tags": ["PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_1"]
    },
