      "comment": "Processes skill operation for a game unit entity.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check unit processing flag at offset +0xb for completion status\n2. If flag is clear (0x00), proceed with skill processing\n3. Retrieve target unit using unit ID from offset +0x3 via FUN_6fb60e10\n4. Validate unit pointer, abort with error 0xc06 if null\n5. Acquire skill handle using Ordinal_10949 with -1 parameter\n6. Validate skill handle, abort with error 0xc09 if zero\n7. Execute skill operation via Ordinal_11012 with handle and skill data\n\nParameters:\npUnitData - Pointer to UnitAny structure containing unit and skill information\n  +0x03: uint - Unit ID for target lookup\n  +0x07: ushort - Additional unit data (word value)  \n  +0x09: byte - Skill operation parameter\n  +0x0b: byte - Processing completion flag (0=process, non-zero=skip)\n\nReturns:\nNone (void function)\n\nSpecial Cases:\nIf processing flag at +0xb is non-zero, function returns immediately\nError 0xc06: Unit lookup failed (null pointer from FUN_6fb60e10)\nError 0xc09: Skill handle acquisition failed (zero return from Ordinal_10949)\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0xc06 (3078) - Unit lookup failure error code\n0xc09 (3081) - Skill handle acquisition failure error code\n0xffffffff (-1) - Invalid/default parameter for skill operations",
