      "comment": "Processes a compression/decompression request by dispatching to appropriate handlers.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract flags (ushort) from request structure at offset +7\n2. Extract size parameter (uint) from request structure at offset +9  \n3. Call FUN_6fb60e10 to allocate/get buffer using resourceId from offset +2\n4. Check decompression flag (byte) at offset +6\n5. If flag is set (compression): Call Ordinal_10961 with buffer, flags, and size\n6. If flag is clear (decompression): Call Ordinal_10962 with buffer, flags, and size\n\nParameters:\npRequest (CompressionRequest): Structure containing compression request data with fields:\n  - offset +2: dwResourceId (uint) - Resource identifier for buffer allocation\n  - offset +6: bIsCompression (byte) - Flag indicating compression (1) vs decompression (0)  \n  - offset +7: wFlags (ushort) - Compression algorithm flags\n  - offset +9: dwSize (uint) - Size parameter for operation\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Function does not return a value, operations are performed through called functions\n\nSpecial Cases:\nThis function acts as a dispatcher, routing compression vs decompression requests to \ndifferent ordinal functions based on the flag byte. The ordinals handle the actual\ncompression/decompression work.\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset | Size | Field Name      | Type   | Description\n+0     | 2    | dwType         | uint   | Request type identifier  \n+2     | 4    | dwResourceId   | uint   | Resource ID for buffer allocation\n+6     | 1    | bIsCompression | byte   | 0=decompress, 1=compress\n+7     | 2    | wFlags         | ushort | Algorithm-specific flags\n+9     | 4    | dwSize         | uint   | Size parameter for operation",
