      "comment": "Wrapper that copies an ItemRequest structure from ECX to a local stack buffer and\nprocesses it via ProcessGroundItemPlacement.\n\nClassification: Thunk/Wrapper - wraps ProcessGroundItemPlacement with stack copy.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate 0x44 (68) bytes on stack for local ItemRequest buffer\n2. Copy 0x11 (17) dwords from pItemRequest (ECX) to stack buffer via REP MOVSD\n3. Pass stack buffer pointer to ProcessGroundItemPlacement\n4. Clean up stack and return\n\nParameters:\npItemRequest (ECX): Pointer to source ItemRequest structure (17 dwords = 68 bytes)\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nMemory Model:\n- Stack allocation: 0x44 bytes for local ItemRequest copy\n- Input ownership: Does not take ownership of pItemRequest, copies data\n- The copy prevents the called function from modifying the caller's data\n\nAssembly Notes:\n- REP MOVSD copies 17 dwords (ECX=0x11) from ESI to EDI\n- ESI = pItemRequest (ECX parameter), EDI = ESP+0x8 (stack buffer)\n- __fastcall: first param in ECX, passed to ProcessGroundItemPlacement in ECX",
