      "comment": "Parses a variable-length network message packet and dispatches it to ProcessNetworkMessage.\n\nCopies packet header fields (10 bytes fixed) and two variable-length strings from\nthe input buffer into a local stack structure, then passes it to ProcessNetworkMessage.\n\nClassification: Worker function - performs packet parsing before dispatch\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Copy fixed header bytes: MsgType (offset 0), SubType (1), Flags (2), Reserved (3)\n2. Copy sequence number (offset 4-7, 4 bytes)\n3. Copy option bytes: Option1 (offset 8), Option2 (offset 9)\n4. Copy first string from offset 10 (max 16 chars) to local buffer\n5. Calculate length of first string using SStrLen\n6. Copy second string from (offset 10 + strlen + 1) with max 256 chars\n7. Call ProcessNetworkMessage with pointer to local structure\n\nParameters:\n  pbPacketData (ECX) - Pointer to raw network packet buffer containing:\n    - Fixed 10-byte header\n    - Two null-terminated strings (variable length)\n\nReturns: void\n\nStack Structure Layout (local_11c at ESP):\n  Offset  Size  Field        Type    Description\n  0x00    1     byMsgType    byte    Message type identifier\n  0x01    1     bySubType    byte    Message subtype\n  0x02    1     byFlags      byte    Message flags\n  0x03    1     byReserved   byte    Reserved/padding\n  0x04    4     dwSequence   uint    Sequence number or timestamp\n  0x08    1     byOption1    byte    Additional option byte 1\n  0x09    1     byOption2    byte    Additional option byte 2\n  0x0A    16    szSource     char[]  First string (max 16 chars)\n  0x1A    258   szPayload    char[]  Second string (max 256 chars)\n\nInput Packet Format:\n  Bytes 0-9: Fixed header (copied directly)\n  Bytes 10+: First null-terminated string (player/source name)\n  After first string null: Second null-terminated string (message/payload)",
