      "comment": "Wrapper function that copies page data to a protected stack buffer before processing.\n\nClassification: Thunk/Wrapper - copies data to protected stack then delegates.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate 48-byte stack buffer (SUB ESP, 0x30)\n2. Save ESI and EDI registers (PUSH ESI, PUSH EDI)\n3. Load source pointer from ECX into ESI (MOV ESI, ECX)\n4. Set loop counter to 11 DWORDs (MOV ECX, 0xB)\n5. Set destination to stack buffer (LEA EDI, [ESP+8])\n6. Copy 44 bytes via REP MOVSD (11 iterations x 4 bytes)\n7. Copy final byte via MOVSB (byte 45 of 45)\n8. Load stack buffer address to ECX for fastcall (LEA ECX, [ESP+8])\n9. Call ProcessInventoryPageOperation(ECX) to process copied data\n10. Restore registers and return (POP EDI, POP ESI, ADD ESP 0x30, RET)\n\nParameters:\npPageData - byte* in ECX (__fastcall), pointer to 45-byte page data structure:\n  +0x00: Page operation type char ('9' = delete, else insert/replace)\n  +0x03: Page index byte (0-7 valid, 0xFF = invalid)\n  +0x0B: Target unit ID (dword)\n  +0x0F: Item subtype (ushort)\n  +0x11: X position (ushort)\n  +0x13: Y position (ushort)\n  +0x21: Inventory mode flag (dword)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - All operations performed through ProcessInventoryPageOperation.\n\nPurpose:\nCopies volatile page data to protected stack memory before processing,\npreventing modification during inventory operations. This ensures atomic\nprocessing of inventory page commands by isolating the data from external changes.\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x30 (48) - Stack buffer size in bytes (45 used + 3 alignment)\n0xB  (11) - Number of DWORDs to copy (11 x 4 = 44 bytes)",
