      "comment": "Wrapper to copy unit record to local stack and call SetUnitAttribute.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Copy dword (unit ID) from pUnitRecord[0] to local dwUnitId\n2. Copy word (slot index) from pUnitRecord[1] to local wSlotIndex  \n3. Copy byte (attr value) from pUnitRecord+6 to local byAttrValue\n4. Call SetUnitAttribute with pointer to local record copy\n5. Return\n\nParameters:\npUnitRecord (ECX): Pointer to 7-byte unit record structure:\n  Offset 0x0: dword - Unit ID for hash table lookup\n  Offset 0x4: word - Slot index parameter\n  Offset 0x6: byte - Attribute value to set\n\nReturns:\nvoid (modifies unit attribute via SetUnitAttribute)\n\nClassification:\nThunk/Wrapper - Copies input record to stack then delegates to SetUnitAttribute.\nAppears to be called from contexts requiring stack-based parameter passing.\n\nStructure Layout (7 bytes):\nOffset  Size  Field       Type    Description\n0x0     4     dwUnitId    uint    Unit ID for hash lookup\n0x4     2     wSlotIndex  ushort  Slot index passed to hash lookup\n0x6     1     byAttrValue byte    Attribute value to write\n\nNote: No direct callers found - may be referenced via function pointer or\nfrom external module.",
