      "comment": "Process inventory update packet to modify unit item color attributes.\n\nClassification: Network Packet Handler - processes incoming inventory update messages\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract packet fields: item code (offset 6), color low (offset 8), color high (offset 10), flag (offset 12)\n2. Validate packet type byte at offset 5 equals 0x01\n3. Look up unit from hash table using unit ID at packet offset 1\n4. If unit found, get linked unit at offset 0x70 (inventory owner)\n5. Get unit structure base via GetUnitFieldAt0xCC\n6. Write item code to next item pointer field (base + 4)\n7. Write color attributes to structure fields (base + 12): low byte, high byte, and high color value\n8. If flag indicator non-zero, set unit flag bit 0x04 (inventory dirty)\n9. Always set unit flag bit 0x01 (needs update)\n10. Invoke unit initialization callbacks to propagate state changes\n\nParameters:\npPacketData (byte *) - Pointer to raw packet buffer with following layout:\n  +0x01: Unit ID (dword) - ID used for hash table lookup\n  +0x05: Packet type (byte) - Must be 0x01 to process\n  +0x06: Item code (ushort) - Value written to item field\n  +0x08: Color low (ushort) - Low byte extracted for color[0], high byte for color[1]\n  +0x0A: Color high (ushort) - Low byte extracted for color[2]\n  +0x0C: Flag indicator (short) - Non-zero triggers flag bit 0x04\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value; modifies unit state in-place\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Early exit if packet type != 0x01 (silent ignore)\n- Early exit if unit not found in hash table (no error)\n- Flag bit 0x04 only set when flag indicator is non-zero\n- Flag bit 0x01 always set on successful processing\n\nFlag Bits:\n0x01 - Unit needs update (always set)\n0x04 - Inventory dirty flag (conditional on packet flag field)",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_1", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
