      "comment": "Extract unit creation parameters from packed descriptor and allocate unit.\n\nClassification: Thunk - forwards extracted fields to AllocateAndInitializeUnit\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract dwUnitType from descriptor offset +1 (dword)\n2. Extract dwUnitClass from descriptor offset +5 (byte)\n3. Extract dwRoomX from descriptor offset +0x16 (ushort)\n4. Extract dwRoomY from descriptor offset +0x18 (ushort)\n5. Pass pointer to offset +6 as nUnitMode parameter\n6. Tail-call AllocateAndInitializeUnit with extracted parameters\n\nParameters:\npDescriptor (ECX) - Pointer to packed unit creation descriptor structure\n  +0x01: dword dwUnitType - Unit type (player=0, monster=1, object=2, missile=3)\n  +0x05: byte dwUnitClass - Unit class identifier\n  +0x06: int nUnitMode - Unit mode/action state (passed by pointer)\n  +0x16: ushort wRoomX - Initial room X coordinate\n  +0x18: ushort wRoomY - Initial room Y coordinate\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Unit allocation result handled by callee\n\nSpecial Cases:\nNo callers found - may be dead code or called via function pointer table\nDescriptor layout suggests network packet or serialized game state structure\nOffset +0 byte appears unused (descriptor starts at +1)",
