      "comment": "Submits a player action event to the action queue for processing\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract event name string pointer from pActionEventData structure at offset 0x22\n2. Calculate string length using string scan with REPNE SCASB instruction \n3. Compute event name terminator address by adding length to base pointer\n4. Extract all event parameters from structure offsets:\n   - Player ID from offset 0x3 (int)\n   - Action parameter from offset 0x7 (byte)\n   - Player name buffer from offset 0x8 (byte array)\n   - Action type from offset 0x18 (ushort)\n   - Priority from offset 0x1a (ushort) \n   - Data value combined from offsets 0x1c and calculated length\n   - Timestamp from offset 0x1e (ushort)\n   - Flags from offset 0x20 (ushort)\n5. Call AddPlayerActionToQueue with extracted parameters and calculated string pointers\n\nParameters:\npActionEventData - Pointer to PlayerActionEvent structure containing action data\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset Size Field Name    Type      Description\n0x00   3    padding       byte[3]   Structure alignment padding\n0x03   4    nPlayerId     int       Target player identifier\n0x07   1    bActionParam  byte      Action-specific parameter value\n0x08   16   szPlayerName  byte[16]  Player name buffer (null-terminated)\n0x18   2    wActionType   ushort    Type of action to perform  \n0x1a   2    wPriority     ushort    Processing priority level\n0x1c   2    wDataLow      ushort    Lower 16 bits of action data\n0x1e   2    wTimestamp    ushort    Event timestamp value\n0x20   2    wFlags        ushort    Action processing flags\n0x22   32   szEventName   char[32]  Event name string buffer\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x22 (34 decimal) - Offset to event name string in structure\n0xffffffff (4294967295) - Initial string length counter for REPNE scan",
