      "comment": "Handle server command to transfer unit class attributes.\n\nClassification: Thunk/Wrapper - copies command data to stack then delegates to TransferUnitClassAttributes.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Copy 7-byte command structure from input buffer to stack locals\n   - Bytes 0-3: Unit ID and flags (dwUnitIdAndFlags)\n   - Bytes 4-5: Attribute data (wAttributeData)\n   - Byte 6: Extra flag (bExtraFlag)\n2. Get current game context via GetGameContext()\n3. If game context is NULL, assert error \"UnitGetControlUnit()\" and exit with code -1\n4. Pass pointer to stack copy to TransferUnitClassAttributes for processing\n\nParameters:\npbCmdData (byte *): Pointer to 7-byte server command data structure in ECX (__fastcall)\n  [+0x0]: dword - Contains unit ID and flag bits\n  [+0x4]: word - Attribute data\n  [+0x6]: byte - Extra flag byte\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- NULL game context triggers fatal assertion (line 0xfc3 = 4035)\n- Assertion string \"UnitGetControlUnit()\" indicates control unit validation context\n- Stack copy ensures command data is preserved during processing\n\nSource File: D2Client\\SCmd.cpp (from assertion path)",
