      "comment": "ProcessCorpseMessage - Wrapper for corpse/dead body message processing\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate 12 bytes on stack for local message copy\n2. Copy 10-byte CorpseMessage structure from input to stack:\n   - Copy dword at offset 0 (message type + has corpse flag + padding)\n   - Copy dword at offset 4 (unit GUID)\n   - Copy word at offset 8 (corpse GUID low bytes)\n3. Call FUN_6fb81f60 with pointer to stack copy for actual processing\n4. Clean up stack and return\n\nParameters:\n  pCorpseMsg (ECX): CorpseMessage * - Pointer to 10-byte corpse message structure\n    +0x00 bMessageType: byte - Message type identifier\n    +0x01 bHasCorpse: byte - Flag indicating corpse presence (checked by callee)\n    +0x02 dwUnitGuid: uint - GUID of the unit associated with corpse\n    +0x06 dwCorpseGuid: uint - GUID of the dead body/corpse unit\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value\n\nClassification: Thunk/Wrapper\n  Copies message to stack and delegates to FUN_6fb81f60 which performs actual\n  corpse processing including inventory item removal and unit hash table updates.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - No callers found in static analysis - likely called via function pointer table\n  - Message copied to stack ensures callee can modify without affecting original",
