      "comment": "Dispatches pet roster update messages to add/update or remove handlers.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check action flag at message offset +1\n2. If flag is non-zero (add/update action):\n   a. Extract pet GUID from offset +9\n   b. Extract owner unit GUID from offset +5\n   c. Extract node type from offset +2\n   d. Extract pet class ID from offset +3\n   e. Call AddOrUpdatePetRosterNode with extracted parameters\n3. If flag is zero (remove action):\n   a. Extract pet GUID from offset +9\n   b. Call RemoveOrMarkPetNode to remove/mark the pet\n\nParameters:\n  pbPetMessage (ECX) - Pointer to packed pet message structure:\n    +0x00: byte  - Unknown/reserved\n    +0x01: byte  - Action flag (0=remove, non-zero=add/update)\n    +0x02: byte  - Pet node type\n    +0x03: ushort - Pet class ID\n    +0x05: uint  - Owner unit GUID\n    +0x09: uint  - Pet GUID\n\nReturns: void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Zero action flag triggers pet removal regardless of other fields\n  - Non-zero action flag triggers add/update with full parameter extraction",
