      "comment": "Dispatches list update commands to appropriate handler based on command type flag.\n\nRoutes to UpdatePlayerDataAndReorganizeLists if byUsePlayerData is non-zero,\notherwise routes to UpdateLinkedListNodeData.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract byUsePlayerData flag from pCommand+0x1\n2. Extract wDataValue from pCommand+0x2 (passed as second parameter)\n3. Extract dwSearchKey from pCommand+0x4 (passed as first parameter via ECX)\n4. Extract wFlags from pCommand+0x8 (passed as third parameter via stack)\n5. If byUsePlayerData != 0: call UpdatePlayerDataAndReorganizeLists\n6. Else: call UpdateLinkedListNodeData\n\nParameters:\n  pCommand (ECX) - ListUpdateCommand * - Pointer to command structure\n    +0x0: byPadding - Unused padding byte\n    +0x1: byUsePlayerData - Flag: non-zero routes to player data handler\n    +0x2: wDataValue - ushort data value passed to handler\n    +0x4: dwSearchKey - dword search key passed to handler\n    +0x8: wFlags - ushort flags passed to handler\n\nReturns: void\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset  Size  Field           Type    Description\n0x00    1     byPadding       byte    Unused padding\n0x01    1     byUsePlayerData byte    Handler selection flag\n0x02    2     wDataValue      ushort  Data value for handler\n0x04    4     dwSearchKey     dword   Search key for handler\n0x08    2     wFlags          ushort  Flags for handler\n\nClassification: Dispatcher/Router - routes commands to specialized handlers\nCallers: None detected (likely called via function pointer or jump table)\nCallees: UpdatePlayerDataAndReorganizeLists, UpdateLinkedListNodeData\n\nDecompiler Artifacts:\n  unaff_ESI - Not actually used; ESI is push/pop preserved, decompiler shows\n              phantom CONCAT22 for 16-to-32 bit extension of wFlags\n  wFlags local - Decompiler artifact; actual wFlags is pCommand->wFlags (ushort)",
