      "comment": "Processes player data update record by validating and applying data values to game objects.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract player ID from data record offset +0x1\n2. Extract primary data value from record offset +0x15  \n3. Extract secondary data value from record offset +0x19\n4. Look up game object using primary data value (type 2)\n5. If object found, apply data from record offset +0x5 to object\n6. Check if secondary data value is valid (!= 0xffffffff)\n7. If valid, look up second game object using secondary data value (type 2)\n8. If second object found, apply same data from record offset +0x5\n9. Update player data fields with all three values\n\nParameters:\npbDataRecord (byte *) - Pointer to structured data record containing player update information\n  +0x1: Player ID (int)\n  +0x5: Data payload to apply to objects  \n  +0x15: Primary data value/object ID (uint)\n  +0x19: Secondary data value/object ID (uint, 0xffffffff = invalid)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value, performs updates in-place\n\nSpecial Cases:\n0xffffffff in secondary data value indicates no second object to process\nNULL object lookup results are safely ignored (no processing performed)\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x1 (1) - Offset to player ID field in data record\n0x5 (5) - Offset to data payload in record  \n0x15 (21) - Offset to primary data value in record\n0x19 (25) - Offset to secondary data value in record\n0x2 (2) - Object lookup type parameter for FUN_6fb60e10\n0xffffffff - Invalid/null secondary data value marker\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset | Size | Field Name      | Type | Description\n+0x1   | 4    | nPlayerId       | int  | Player identifier\n+0x5   | ?    | DataPayload     | ?    | Data to apply to objects\n+0x15  | 4    | dwDataValue1    | uint | Primary object/data identifier  \n+0x19  | 4    | dwDataValue2    | uint | Secondary object/data identifier",
