      "comment": "Handles incoming guild post packet (type 0x86).\n\nClassification: Packet Handler / Thunk\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if packet type byte equals 0x86 (guild post packet)\n2. If not matching, return immediately without processing\n3. Extract packet fields from buffer offsets:\n   - Offset 0x1: ushort (message/chunk identifier)\n   - Offset 0x3: ushort (combined with high word of ptr as uint)\n   - Offset 0x5: ushort (chunk length)\n   - Offset 0x7: byte* (pointer to chunk data)\n4. Call FUN_6fb8ede0 to append guild post chunk to legacy engine\n\nParameters:\npPacket (ECX, byte *): Pointer to network packet buffer\n  - Offset 0x0: Packet type identifier (0x86 for guild post)\n  - Offset 0x1: Message/chunk ID (ushort)\n  - Offset 0x3: Chunk index/sequence (ushort)\n  - Offset 0x5: Data length (ushort)\n  - Offset 0x7: Chunk payload data (variable length)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value\n\nPacket Structure (Guild Post - Type 0x86):\nOffset  Size  Field        Description\n0x00    1     bType        Packet type (0x86)\n0x01    2     wMsgId       Message identifier\n0x03    2     wChunkIndex  Chunk sequence number\n0x05    2     wDataLen     Length of payload data\n0x07    N     abData       Payload data bytes\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Non-0x86 packets: Silently ignored, early return\n- Delegates to AppendGuildPostChunk via FUN_6fb8ede0\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x86 - Guild post packet type identifier (-0x7a signed)",
