      "comment": "Thunk: Parses a player network action packet and forwards to ProcessPlayerNetworkAction.\n\nClassification: Thunk/Wrapper - extracts fields from packet and delegates processing.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load wActionData from packet offset +9 into AX (2 bytes)\n2. Load nActionType from packet offset +5 into EDX (4 bytes)\n3. Load nPlayerId from packet offset +1 into ECX (4 bytes)\n4. Push wActionData onto stack (3rd parameter)\n5. Call ProcessPlayerNetworkAction(nPlayerId, nActionType, wActionData)\n6. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\n  pbPacketData (ECX, byte *): Pointer to raw network packet buffer\n    +0x01: nPlayerId (int, 4 bytes) - Target player identifier\n    +0x05: nActionType (int, 4 bytes) - Action type code\n    +0x09: wActionData (ushort, 2 bytes) - Action-specific data payload\n\nReturns: void - No return value\n\nPacket Layout:\n  Offset  Size  Field         Type    Description\n  0x00    1     header        byte    Packet type byte (not parsed here)\n  0x01    4     nPlayerId     int     Target player ID\n  0x05    4     nActionType   int     Action type code\n  0x09    2     wActionData   ushort  Action-specific payload data\n\nCalled Functions:\n  ProcessPlayerNetworkAction @ 0x6fae0c50 - Processes parsed player action\n\nDecompiler Discrepancies:\n  in_EAX appears in decompiler as undefined4 but only AX (16-bit) is actually\n  used. The CONCAT22 in decompiled output is artifact of partial register usage.",
