      "comment": "Dispatches item unit commands to appropriate handler functions based on command type byte.\n\nClassification: Dispatcher/Router function\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate 252-byte local buffer on stack\n2. Copy 252 bytes (0x3F dwords) from input command buffer to local buffer using REP MOVSD\n3. Extract command type byte from offset +1 of local buffer (masked to 0xFF)\n4. Validate command type <= 0x17, else fall through to default exit\n5. Use jump table at 0x6fae4760 to dispatch to handler based on command type:\n   - 0x00: InitializeItemVariation - Initialize item variation data\n   - 0x01: CreateUnitWithItemAndSkillData - Create unit with item and skill info\n   - 0x02: CreateItemInPlayerInventory - Create item directly in player inventory\n   - 0x03: PlaceUnitItemOnGround - Place unit's item on ground\n   - 0x04: ProcessItemIntoPlayerInventory - Process item transfer to inventory\n   - 0x05-0x09, 0x11, 0x13-0x17: LogPoolWarning - Invalid/deprecated commands\n   - 0x0A: ProcessUnitInventory - Process unit inventory operations\n   - 0x0B-0x0C: ProcessItemInGameWorld - Process item in game world\n   - 0x0D: ProcessInventoryItemLookup - Lookup item in inventory\n   - 0x0E: EquipItemOnUnit - Equip item on unit\n   - 0x0F: PlaceItemInInventorySlot - Place item in specific inventory slot\n   - 0x10: ProcessPlayerItemAction - Process player item action\n   - 0x12: CreateUnitWithItemData - Create unit with item data\n6. Handler functions receive pointer to local buffer copy via ECX (__fastcall)\n\nParameters:\n  pbCommandBuffer (ECX): Pointer to 252-byte command buffer containing item unit command\n                         Offset +0: Unknown header byte\n                         Offset +1: Command type byte (0x00-0x17)\n                         Offset +2-251: Command-specific payload data\n\nReturns: void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Commands 0x05-0x09, 0x11, 0x13-0x17 log warning \"These should be scmd_itemunitex messages!\"\n  indicating they should use extended item unit command protocol instead\n- Command values > 0x17 silently ignored (no handler, returns immediately)\n\nJump Table: Located at 0x6fae4760 with 24 entries (0x00-0x17)\n\nStructure Layout (Command Buffer):\nOffset  Size  Field           Type    Description\n0x00    1     byHeader        byte    Unknown header/padding byte\n0x01    1     byCommandType   byte    Command type selector (0x00-0x17)\n0x02    250   abPayload       byte[]  Command-specific payload data",
