      "instructions": ["0x14930|SUB|ESP, 0x48", "0x14933|PUSH|EBX", "0x14934|PUSH|EBP", "0x14935|PUSH|ESI", "0x14936|PUSH|EDI", "0x14937|MOV|EDI, EDX", "0x14939|CMP|EDI, -0x1", "0x1493C|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x14], EDI", "0x14940|JZ|0x6fae4c37", "0x14946|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x1c], EDI", "0x1494A|MOV|EBP, ECX", "0x1494C|CALL|dword ptr [0x6fba6098]", "0x14952|CMP|EDI, 0x1f4", "0x14958|JLE|0x6fae4960", "0x1495A|INC|dword ptr [0x6fc04134]"],
      "comment": "Process incoming game command packets from network buffer\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate buffer size is not -1, early return if invalid\n2. Call GetTickCount for performance timing\n3. Increment large packet counter if buffer size exceeds 500 bytes (0x1f4)\n4. Loop through buffer processing individual packets:\n   a. Read command ID from current packet position\n   b. Validate packet size using Ordinal_10030, return if invalid\n   c. Check command ID bounds (must be <= 0xa6), abort with error if exceeded\n   d. Calculate command table index (commandId * 3) for lookup tables\n   e. Retrieve expected packet size from DAT_6fbb0214[index]\n   f. Get handler function pointer from PTR_LAB_6fbb0210[index]\n   g. If expected size != 0xffffffff, validate actual size matches expected\n   h. If command requires data buffering (DAT_6fbb0218[index] != 0):\n      - Determine parameter count based on command ID range (0x67-0x6d uses 1, others use param[1])\n      - Allocate packet data node via FUN_6fb60e10\n      - Get existing or create new PacketData buffer via FUN_6fb635c0/FUN_6fae4d40\n      - Validate buffer won't exceed maximum size (DAT_6fbee29c)\n      - Copy packet data to buffer using DWORD-aligned copy with byte remainder\n      - Increment buffer usage counter\n   i. Handle special command parsing:\n      - Command 0xd: If second byte is 1, call FUN_6fb60e10 with uint at offset 2\n      - Command 0x18: Parse 15-byte packet into bit buffer using Ordinal_10126/10130 sequence\n      - Command 0x95: Parse 13-byte packet into bit buffer using Ordinal_10126/10130 sequence  \n      - Command 0x96: Parse 9-byte packet into bit buffer using Ordinal_10126/10130 sequence\n   j. Execute command handler function if pointer is not null\n   k. Update global statistics and advance to next packet in buffer\n5. Increment total packets processed counter and return\n\nParameters:\npbPacketBuffer: Pointer to network buffer containing one or more game packets\nnBufferSize: Total size of buffer in bytes, or -1 to skip processing\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\nCommand ID bounds checking with immediate abort on overflow (>0xa6)\nSize validation aborts with error messages on mismatch\nBuffer overflow protection using DAT_6fbee29c maximum size\nSpecial parsing for commands 0xd, 0x18, 0x95, 0x96 with different bit field extraction\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0xa6 (166): Maximum valid command ID, bounds check threshold\n0x1f4 (500): Large packet size threshold for performance counter\n0x67-0x6d (103-109): Command ID range using single parameter count\n0xd (13): Command requiring special single-parameter processing\n0x18 (24): Command requiring 15-byte bit field parsing\n0x95 (149): Command requiring 13-byte bit field parsing  \n0x96 (150): Command requiring 9-byte bit field parsing\n0xffffffff: Invalid/variable packet size marker\n\nError Handling:\nSize mismatch: Ordinal_10023 error with message then FUN_6fb9a10f(-1) abort\nCommand overflow: Ordinal_10023 error with bounds message then abort\nBuffer overflow: Ordinal_10023 error with size limit message then abort\n\nStructure Layout:\nCommand dispatch uses triple-indexed arrays:\n- DAT_6fbb0214[cmdId*3]: Expected packet size (0xffffffff = variable)\n- PTR_LAB_6fbb0210[cmdId*3]: Function pointer to command handler\n- DAT_6fbb0218[cmdId*3]: Data buffering required flag (0=no, 1=yes)",
