      "comment": "Expands buffer capacity by allocating larger buffer and copying existing data.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize global buffer size constant if not set by scanning configuration table\n2. Find maximum size entry across all buffer configurations and add 5 for header overhead\n3. Retrieve or create buffer header structure for the specified context\n4. If header not found, allocate new 16-byte header and initialize all fields to zero\n5. Calculate new expanded buffer size (current size + 5) multiplied by global size constant\n6. Allocate new buffer memory with calculated size using memory allocator\n7. Zero-initialize entire new buffer using optimized DWORD and byte filling loops\n8. If existing buffer data exists, copy old buffer content to new buffer using memory copy\n9. Free old buffer memory if it existed\n10. Update buffer header with new size and pointer to expanded buffer\n11. Return pointer to updated buffer header structure\n\nParameters:\nnBufferContext (int): Buffer context identifier used to lookup buffer configuration\n\nReturns:\nBufferHeader *: Pointer to buffer header structure containing updated size and buffer pointer\nReturns existing header if found, newly allocated header if not found\nNever returns NULL - allocates new header if lookup fails\n\nSpecial Cases:\nBuffer size constant DAT_6fbee29c initialized on first call by scanning global table 0x6fbb0214-0x6fbb09e8\nEach table entry is 12 bytes with structure: [size, flags, reserved]\nGlobal size constant becomes (max_size_found + 5) for expansion overhead\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x141f (5151) - Memory allocation type for buffer header (16 bytes)\n0x1424 (5156) - Memory allocation type for buffer data \n0x1428 (5160) - Memory deallocation type for old buffer\n0x6fbb0214 - Start of buffer configuration table\n0x6fbb09e8 - End of buffer configuration table (exclusive)\n0x5 - Buffer expansion overhead added to current size\n0xc (12) - Size of each configuration table entry\n\nStructure Layout:\nBufferHeader (16 bytes):\nOffset | Size | Field Name    | Type  | Description\n0x00   | 4    | nCurrentSize  | int   | Current buffer size in elements\n0x04   | 4    | nFlags        | int   | Buffer state flags\n0x08   | 4    | nReserved     | int   | Reserved field (always 0)\n0x0C   | 4    | pBufferData   | void* | Pointer to allocated buffer data",
