      "instructions": ["0x14E90|SUB|ESP, 0x8", "0x14E93|PUSH|EBX", "0x14E94|PUSH|EBP", "0x14E95|PUSH|ESI", "0x14E96|PUSH|EDI", "0x14E97|MOV|EBP, ECX", "0x14E99|CALL|0x6fb635c0", "0x14E9E|MOV|EBX, EAX", "0x14EA0|TEST|EBX, EBX", "0x14EA2|JZ|0x6fae4f69", "0x14EA8|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [EBX + 0x4]", "0x14EAB|MOV|ECX, dword ptr [EBX]", "0x14EAD|CMP|EAX, ECX", "0x14EAF|JLE|0x6fae4ecf", "0x14EB1|PUSH|0x16be"],
      "comment": "Processes all commands in a network packet by dispatching each to its handler function.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate packet pointer is not null (get packet structure from nPacketId)\n2. Validate packet bounds (used count must not exceed total count)\n3. Initialize command processing loop index to 0\n4. For each command in packet (loop while index < total count):\n   a. Calculate command data offset (index * command stride + data buffer base)\n   b. Read command size using Ordinal_10030() validation function\n   c. Return early if command size validation fails\n   d. Extract command ID byte from command data buffer\n   e. Validate command ID is within range (must be <= 0xA6, NUM_SCMDS)\n   f. Lookup command dispatch entry in table (CommandDispatchEntry array)\n   g. Validate expected command size matches actual size (if not -1)\n   h. Validate command handler function pointer is not null\n   i. Call command handler function with command data\n   j. Increment command index and continue loop\n5. Zero out processed packet data buffer (clear all command data)\n6. Reset packet command count to 0 (mark packet as empty)\n\nParameters:\nnPacketId (int): Packet identifier used to retrieve PacketData structure\n\nReturns:\nvoid: No return value, processing errors cause program termination\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Command ID > 0xA6: Triggers fatal error \"bCmd < NUM_SCMDS\" (line 0x16CA)\n- Size mismatch: Triggers fatal error \"ptMsgStruct->nCmdSize == ...\" (line 0x16CD)  \n- Null handler: Triggers fatal error \"ptMsgStruct->pfProcessUnit\" (line 0x16CF)\n- Validation failure: Returns early without processing remaining commands\n- All errors call FUN_6fb9a10f(0xFFFFFFFF) for program termination\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0xA6 (166): Maximum valid command ID (NUM_SCMDS boundary check)\n0x16BE: Error code for packet bounds validation failure\n0x16CA: Error code for invalid command ID (exceeds NUM_SCMDS)\n0x16CD: Error code for command size validation mismatch  \n0x16CF: Error code for null command handler function pointer\n0xFFFFFFFF: Fatal error code passed to termination function\n\nStructure Layout:\nPacketData (20 bytes):\nOffset  Size  Field Name    Type    Description\n0x00    4     nUsedCount    int     Number of commands currently in packet\n0x04    4     nTotalCount   int     Maximum number of commands packet can hold\n0x08    4     (reserved)    int     Unused field or padding\n0x0C    4     pDataBuffer   byte*   Pointer to command data buffer\n\nCommandDispatchEntry (12 bytes) - Array at 0x6FBB0214:\nOffset  Size  Field Name       Type     Description  \n0x00    4     dwMinSize        uint     Minimum valid command size (-1 = any size)\n0x04    4     dwExpectedSize   uint     Expected command size for validation\n0x08    4     pfnHandler       void*    Function pointer to command handler\n\nError Handling:\n- Packet bounds exceeded → Ordinal_10023() error reporting → FUN_6fb9a10f() termination\n- Invalid command ID → Ordinal_10023() error reporting → FUN_6fb9a10f() termination  \n- Command size mismatch → Ordinal_10023() error reporting → FUN_6fb9a10f() termination\n- Null handler pointer → Ordinal_10023() error reporting → FUN_6fb9a10f() termination\n- Command validation failure → Silent early return without processing remaining commands",
      "tags": ["SRC_SCmd.cpp", "STRUCT_Packet", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PARAM_1", "NET_PACKET", "STRUCT_Other", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "MOD_GAME", "NET_SCMD", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
