      "api_count": 2,
      "api_calls": ["SetRenderMode", "FogFatalError"],
      "instructions": ["0x14FE0|PUSH|ESI", "0x14FE1|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0x14FE3|CMP|ESI, 0x3", "0x14FE6|JA|0x6fae50a8", "0x14FEC|JMP|dword ptr [ESI*0x4 + 0x6fae50c4]", "0x14FF3|MOV|EAX, [0x6fbae0e4]", "0x14FF8|CDQ|", "0x14FF9|AND|EDX, 0x3", "0x14FFC|ADD|EAX, EDX", "0x14FFE|SAR|EAX, 0x2", "0x15001|NEG|EAX", "0x15003|JMP|0x6fae5017", "0x15005|MOV|EAX, [0x6fbae0e4]", "0x1500A|CDQ|", "0x1500B|AND|EDX, 0x3"],
      "comment": "Configures the scroll window display mode and offset calculations for screen rendering.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate scroll mode parameter is within valid range (0-3)\n2. If mode > 3, trigger assertion with \"Setting scroll window mode\" error message then exit\n3. Calculate horizontal scroll offset based on mode using screen width division by 4\n4. Mode 0: Set offset to 0 (no scrolling)\n5. Mode 1: Set offset to -(screen_width / 4) (left scroll)\n6. Mode 2: Set offset to +(screen_width / 4) (right scroll) \n7. Mode 3: Set offset to 0 (center/default)\n8. Store the scroll mode value in global state variable\n9. Call graphics system refresh function to apply changes\n10. Jump to mode-specific handler function via dispatch table\n\nParameters:\ndwScrollMode (uint): Scroll window mode selector\n  - 0x00: No horizontal offset (centered)\n  - 0x01: Left offset by quarter screen width\n  - 0x02: Right offset by quarter screen width  \n  - 0x03: Default/center position\n  - >3: Invalid, triggers assertion failure\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Function does not return for invalid modes (calls exit)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Invalid mode (>3): Displays error \"Setting scroll window mode\" at line 93 and terminates process\n- Screen width division uses arithmetic right shift for performance (divide by 4)\n- Offset calculation includes sign adjustment for proper two's complement handling\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n- 0x03: Maximum valid scroll mode index\n- 0x1f: Mask for sign extension during division (0x1F = 31 decimal)\n- 0x02: Right shift count for divide by 4 operation  \n- 0x5d: Line number (93 decimal) for assertion error message\n- 0xffffffff: Exit code (-1) passed to termination function\n\nError Handling:\n- Mode validation: Bounds check against maximum value 3\n- Assertion failure: Calls Ordinal_10024 with source file info and line number\n- Process termination: Calls FUN_6fb9a10f with exit code -1 (does not return)",
      "tags": ["SRC_scroll.cpp", "PARAM_1", "MOD_GAME"]
    },
