      "comment": "Calculates the relative viewport X position adjusted for scroll offset.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Read current absolute viewport X coordinate from global state\n2. Read current scroll offset X value from global state  \n3. Subtract scroll offset from viewport coordinate to get relative position\n4. Return the calculated relative viewport X coordinate\n\nParameters:\nNone - Function takes no parameters\n\nReturns:\nint - Relative viewport X coordinate after scroll offset adjustment\n  - Positive values: Viewport positioned right of scroll reference point\n  - Negative values: Viewport positioned left of scroll reference point\n  - Zero: Viewport aligned with scroll reference point\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- When scroll offset is zero, returns absolute viewport position\n- Used extensively (18 xrefs) throughout rendering and UI positioning code\n- Critical for coordinate transformation between screen space and world space\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n- 0x6fbee2a8: Address of g_nViewportX (absolute viewport X coordinate)\n- 0x6fbee2b4: Address of g_nScrollOffsetX (horizontal scroll adjustment)\n\nError Handling:\nNo error handling required - simple arithmetic operation on global state",
