      "comment": "Updates the viewport position based on scroll mode and player coordinates.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Set initial horizontal offset to -160 pixels (_DAT_6fbee2ac = -0xa0)\n2. Check g_nScrollMode for viewport centering behavior:\n   - Mode 2: Center horizontally (offset = screen_width/2 - 160)  \n   - Mode 3: No horizontal offset (offset = 0)\n   - Other: Keep default offset (-160)\n3. Get current player handle via FUN_6fb62880()\n4. Retrieve player X coordinate using Ordinal_10333(handle)\n5. Retrieve player Y coordinate using Ordinal_10334(handle)\n6. Calculate viewport X position: player_x - screen_width/2\n7. Calculate global Y value: player_y - screen_height/2 + 16\n8. Get additional coordinate offsets via FUN_6fae7230(&nOffsetX, &nOffsetY)\n9. If offsets retrieved successfully, apply them to viewport position\n\nParameters:\nNone - operates on global state\n\nReturns:\nvoid - updates global viewport variables\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0xa0 (160): Default horizontal viewport offset in pixels\n0x10 (16): Vertical adjustment offset for Y coordinate calculation\n0x02 (2): Scroll mode for horizontal centering\n0x03 (3): Scroll mode for no horizontal offset\n\nGlobal Variables Modified:\n_DAT_6fbee2ac: Horizontal offset value based on scroll mode\ng_nViewportX: Final viewport X coordinate (player-centered)\ng_dwGlobalValue: Final viewport Y coordinate with offset",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Inventory", "PARAM_0", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control"]
