      "comment": "Validates a unit for selection and updates global selection state flags.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if unit pointer is NULL\n2. If NULL, set error flag (g_bUnitSelectionError = 1) and clear selection flag  \n3. If valid unit, perform hit test validation via FUN_6fb62b10\n4. Clear error flag (g_bUnitSelectionError = 0) initially\n5. If hit test fails (returns 0), clear selection flag and return\n6. If hit test passes, call FUN_6fae5360 to process the selection\n7. Set error flag (g_bUnitSelectionError = 1) after processing\n8. Clear selection state flag (g_bUnitSelected = 0) before returning\n\nParameters:\npUnit: Pointer to unit structure to validate for selection (UnitAny*)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Function sets global flags instead of returning values\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- NULL unit pointer immediately sets error state and clears selection\n- Failed hit test clears selection flag but does not set error flag\n- Successful hit test triggers selection processing and sets error flag\n\nGlobal State Modified:\ng_bUnitSelectionError (0x6fbee2d4): Selection error/completion flag\ng_bUnitSelected (0x6fbee2d0): Current unit selection state flag",
      "tags": ["PARAM_1"]
    },
