      "comment": "Processes and validates unit selection state for game entities.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Early exit if unit selection error flag is set\n2. Check if unit validation function indicates current unit is already selected\n3. If current unit matches selected unit, call finalization and exit\n4. Initialize selection state and validate unit pointer is non-null\n5. Test unit validity using validation function (logs assertion if invalid)\n6. Check if unit already matches currently selected unit (type and ID)\n7. If match found, set current unit flag and skip to finalization\n8. Handle unit type 5 (items) by getting unit data and calling ordinal handlers\n9. Update global selection state with new unit type and ID\n10. Branch processing based on unit type:\n    - Type 1 (Player): Validate player data structure and update global player statistics\n    - Type 2 (Monster): Check validity and throttle debug messages to 500ms intervals\n    - Type 5 (Item): Get unit data and call ordinal selection handlers\n\nParameters:\npUnit - Pointer to unit structure containing type, ID, and type-specific data\n        IMPLICIT: Uses __fastcall convention with pUnit passed in ECX register\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Function modifies global unit selection state and may update player statistics\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Early return if g_bUnitSelectionError is set (prevents selection during error state)\n- Null unit pointer clears selection state\n- Player type (1) requires additional validation of player structure at offsets 0x2ab, 0x2ad, 0x35c\n- Monster type (2) includes debug logging with timestamp throttling (500ms minimum interval)\n- Item type (5) processes selection both before and after state update\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x01 - Player unit type\n0x02 - Monster unit type \n0x05 - Item unit type\n0x04 - Monster subtype exclusion check (param_1[3] != 4)\n0x3D - Packet type for LogFiveBytePacket (monster selection)\n0x1F4 - Throttle interval in milliseconds (500 decimal)\n0x2AB - Player structure validation offset (must be non-zero)\n0x2AD - Player structure validation offset (must be zero)\n0x35C - Player structure validation offset (must be zero for stats update)\n0x3E - Monster structure timestamp offset (param_1[0x3e])\n\nStructure Layout:\nUnit Structure (accessed as int array):\nOffset | Size | Field Name | Type | Description  \n0x00   | 4    | dwType     | uint | Unit type (1=Player, 2=Monster, 5=Item)\n0x04   | 4    | pData      | ptr  | Pointer to type-specific data structure\n0x08   | 4    | dwId       | uint | Unique identifier for this unit instance\n0x0C   | 4    | dwSubType  | uint | Sub-classification (monsters use for validation)\n0xF8   | 4    | dwLastMsg  | uint | Timestamp of last debug message (monsters only)\n\nError Handling:\n- Invalid units trigger assertion via Ordinal_10025 with debug strings\n- Null pointer handling for safe unit clearing\n- Timestamp validation prevents debug spam for monster selections\n- Player data structure validation before statistics update\n- Graceful handling of missing unit data pointers",
      "tags": ["SRC_Select.cpp", "PARAM_1", "MOD_GAME"]
