      "comment": "Processes unit targeting and selection based on mouse cursor position and game state.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate targeting prerequisites - check unit selection error state\n2. Get scroll window mode and handle special mode 3 (clear selection)\n3. Get mouse cursor coordinates from screen position functions\n4. Perform boundary checks - validate cursor within game area minus UI margins\n5. Check exclusion zone - skip targeting if cursor in UI exclusion rectangle\n6. Handle split screen mode - validate cursor position for left/right screen halves\n7. Apply viewport perspective correction if 3D mode is enabled\n8. Calculate world coordinates by adding viewport offsets to cursor position\n9. Handle existing unit selection - validate selected unit and check if cursor over it\n10. Get player unit and validate it exists with valid room data\n11. Initialize level iteration - get room data structure for current level\n12. Process all units in each room across all levels with safety counter\n13. For each unit, check targeting eligibility and distance requirements\n14. Apply special targeting timeout logic for targetable units (type 5)\n15. Calculate unit selection priority based on type using priority table at 0x6fbb0df0\n16. Handle special cases - player units get priority boost, pets get penalty\n17. For objects (type 2), check quest state and apply angle-based priority logic\n18. Compare priorities and distances to determine best target candidate\n19. Select unit with highest priority or closest distance for tie-breaking\n20. Call ProcessUnitSelection with final target candidate\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Mode 3: Immediately clears selection via ProcessUnitSelection(NULL)\n- Cursor below screen height - 49 pixels: Early exit with clear selection\n- UI exclusion zones: Areas where targeting is disabled\n- Split screen modes: Left half only (mode 1) or right half only (mode 2)\n- 3D perspective correction: Complex trigonometry for isometric projection\n- Unit iteration safety: Maximum 30,000 units prevents infinite loops\n- Targeting timeout: 500ms delay for eligible targets prevents spam clicking\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n- 0x31 (49): UI margin from bottom of screen for targeting boundary\n- 0x66666667: Magic number for fast division by 10 in perspective math\n- 0x28 (40): Perspective correction constant for isometric projection\n- 0x1f (31): Bit mask for sign extension in perspective calculation\n- 0x4 (4): Right shift by 2 for quarter division in perspective\n- 0x3 (3): Unit type for items/objects (non-targetable for selection)\n- 0x5 (5): Unit type for monsters/NPCs (targetable entities)\n- 0x1 (1): Unit type for players (special priority handling)\n- 0x2 (2): Unit type for objects/items (quest-dependent targeting)\n- 0x14c (332): Offset to quest state flag in object structure\n- 0x2c (44): Offset to unit list head in room structure  \n- 0x10c (268): Offset to next unit pointer in UnitAny structure\n- 500: Targeting timeout duration in milliseconds\n- 30000: Maximum unit iteration limit for safety\n\nError Handling:\n- g_bUnitSelectionError: Global flag prevents targeting when set\n- Null unit validation: Checks for valid player unit and room data\n- Array bounds checking: Validates level indices and unit counts\n- Infinite loop protection: Unit count limit with error logging\n\nStructure Layout:\nUnitAny structure key fields:\n- +0x00: dwUnitType (0=player, 1=npc, 2=object, 3=item, 4=tile, 5=monster)\n- +0x04: dwUnitId (unique identifier within type)\n- +0x0C: dwFlags (various unit state flags)\n- +0x10C: pNext (pointer to next unit in room list)\n\nRoom structure fields:\n- +0x2C: pUnitList (head of linked list for units in this room)\n\nPriority table at 0x6fbb0df0:\nUnit type priority values for selection preference",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "STRUCT_Room2", "STRUCT_Room1", "STRUCT_ItemData", "PARAM_0", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "MOD_GAME", "STRUCT_PlayerData", "STRUCT_StatList", "SRC_Select.cpp", "PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Path", "STRUCT_Skill", "PROP_LOOPHEAVY"]
    },
