      "comment": "Updates a value in a linked list node identified by key from source node.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate nUnused parameter is not NULL (unused context parameter)\n2. Validate nSourceNodePtr parameter is not NULL  \n3. Extract search key from nSourceNodePtr structure at offset +8\n4. Call FindLinkedListNodeByKey with extracted key to locate target node\n5. Store nNewValue at offset +8 of the target node (replacing existing value)\n6. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\nnUnused (int): Unused context parameter, validated but not used in processing\nnSourceNodePtr (int): Pointer to source structure containing search key at offset +8\nnNewValue (int): New value to store in the target linked list node\n\nReturns:\nvoid: No return value, performs in-place update of target node\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If nUnused is NULL (0): Function returns immediately without processing\n- If nSourceNodePtr is NULL (0): Function returns immediately without processing  \n- Target node lookup relies on FindLinkedListNodeByKey success\n\nStructure Layout:\nNode Structure (accessed at offsets):\nOffset | Size | Field Name | Type | Description\n+0x8   | 4    | nKey/nData | int  | Search key (source) or data value (target)\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x8: Offset for both search key extraction and data value storage",
