      "comment": "Copies configuration data to global variables and sets initialization flag\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate input pointer is not NULL\n2. If valid, copy first 4 dwords from ConfigData structure to global memory\n3. Set global initialization flag to 1 (initialized state)  \n4. If NULL, set global initialization flag to 0 (uninitialized state)\n5. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\npConfigData - Pointer to ConfigData structure containing configuration values\n\nReturns:\nvoid (no return value)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- NULL pointer handling: Sets flag to 0 without copying data\n- Global variables at 0x6fbee2c0-0x6fbee2cc store the 4 configuration dwords\n- Global flag at 0x6fbee2d8 tracks initialization state (0=uninitialized, 1=initialized)\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset | Size | Field Name | Type | Description\n-------|------|------------|------|------------\n0x0    | 4    | dw1        | uint | First configuration value\n0x4    | 4    | dw2        | uint | Second configuration value  \n0x8    | 4    | dw3        | uint | Third configuration value\n0xc    | 4    | dw4        | uint | Fourth configuration value",
