      "instructions": ["0x15C20|SUB|ESP, 0x78", "0x15C23|PUSH|EBX", "0x15C24|PUSH|EBP", "0x15C25|PUSH|ESI", "0x15C26|PUSH|EDI", "0x15C27|MOV|ESI, EDX", "0x15C29|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x14], ECX", "0x15C2D|CALL|0x6fb9833e", "0x15C32|MOV|EDI, EAX", "0x15C34|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x1c], EDI", "0x15C38|CALL|0x6fb62880", "0x15C3D|TEST|ESI, ESI", "0x15C3F|MOV|EBX, EAX", "0x15C41|JZ|0x6fae5c93", "0x15C43|CMP|dword ptr [ESI], 0x0"],
      "comment": "Finds and selects the optimal target unit based on specified criteria and game state.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize game state context and current player position\n2. Validate target unit if provided - return early if valid and meets criteria\n3. Check game mode flags to determine search strategy:\n   - Mode 0x78: Perform proximity-based unit search with distance calculations\n   - Mode 0x74: Execute directional search using coordinate offsets\n   - Mode 0x80: Use precise coordinate targeting with pathfinding validation\n4. For proximity search (mode 0x78):\n   - Check command type - if 0x5A and target is type 4, validate with Ordinal_10802\n   - Initialize search parameters structure with type 0x2002 or 0x3002\n   - Set callback function for special case 0x5A (address 0x6fae5fb0)\n   - Execute area search using Ordinal_10401 and process results\n   - Iterate through result list finding unit with minimum distance\n5. For directional search (mode 0x74):\n   - Calculate search offsets using bit operations on unit flags\n   - Apply coordinate transformations from offset tables at 0x6fba641c and 0x6fba643c\n   - Perform line-of-sight checks and unit validation\n   - Return first valid unit meeting visibility and interaction criteria\n6. For coordinate targeting (mode 0x80):\n   - Use provided coordinates or extract from target unit\n   - Validate pathfinding accessibility with terrain checks\n   - Return null if destination unreachable, otherwise update coordinates\n\nParameters:\nnCommand: Command identifier determining search behavior (0x5A triggers special handling)\npTargetUnit: Current target unit pointer (null for coordinate-based searches)\npnXCoord: Pointer to X coordinate for result or input targeting\npnYCoord: Pointer to Y coordinate for result or input targeting  \nnMode: Operation flags controlling search strategy activation\n\nReturns:\nPointer to best matching unit meeting search criteria\nNULL if no valid target found or search failed\nOriginal target unit if it remains valid after validation\n\nSpecial Cases:\nCommand 0x5A with unit type 4 requires special validation via Ordinal_10802\nSearch types 0x2002 and 0x3002 indicate different proximity algorithms\nMode flags 0x78, 0x74, 0x80 are mutually exclusive operation modes\nCallback function 0x6fae5fb0 used for specialized command 0x5A processing\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x5A (90): Special command requiring type 4 validation\n0x2002: Standard proximity search type\n0x3002: Enhanced proximity search type  \n0x20: Alternative search type for command 0x5A\n0x78: Game state offset for proximity search flag\n0x7C: Game state offset for enhanced search flag\n0x80: Game state offset for coordinate targeting flag\n0x74: Game state offset for directional search flag\n0x70: Game state offset for visibility validation flag\n0x3A: Unit structure offset for interaction flags\n0x6fba645c: Start of coordinate offset table\n0x6fba641c: X offset lookup table base address\n0x6fba643c: Y offset lookup table base address\n\nError Handling:\nReturns original unit if validation confirms it remains optimal\nReturns NULL for failed pathfinding or inaccessible coordinates\nGracefully handles null target unit by using coordinate mode\nValidates game state consistency before executing searches",
