      "instructions": ["0x15FF0|MOV|EAX, [0x6fbf21b0]", "0x15FF5|SUB|ESP, 0xc", "0x15FF8|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0x15FFA|JZ|0x6fae601a", "0x15FFC|PUSH|0xca", "0x16001|PUSH|0x6fbb0ef4", "0x16006|PUSH|0x6fbb0ee4", "0x1600B|CALL|0x6fb99a7a", "0x16010|ADD|ESP, 0xc", "0x16013|PUSH|-0x1", "0x16015|CALL|0x6fb9a10f", "0x1601A|MOV|EAX, [0x6fbf21b4]", "0x1601F|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0x16021|JZ|0x6fae6041", "0x16023|PUSH|0xcb"],
      "comment": "Initialize all Gouraud shading lookup tables for graphics rendering.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate that tables are not already allocated (exit with error if they are)\n2. Call DirectDraw initialization (Ordinal_10178)\n3. Allocate sgpGouraudTblX (0x9000 bytes) - X-coordinate lookup table  \n4. Fill sgpGouraudTblX with 512x512 32-bit pointer entries to color palette offsets\n5. Allocate sgpGouraudTblY (0x4003 bytes) - Y-coordinate lookup table\n6. Fill sgpGouraudTblY with 512x512 byte entries for Y-coordinate gradients\n7. Allocate sgpGouraudTblXVal (0x8003 bytes) - X-value lookup table\n8. Fill sgpGouraudTblXVal with 512x512 byte entries for X-value gradients  \n9. Allocate gpSubtileGouraudTbl (0x20000 bytes) - Subtile lookup table\n10. Fill gpSubtileGouraudTbl with 512x512 32-bit entries for subtile addressing\n11. Allocate gpTileGouraudTbl (0xa003 bytes) - Tile lookup table\n12. Fill gpTileGouraudTbl with 512x512 byte entries using 40-step gradients\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Function does not return on error (calls FUN_6fb9a10f with -1)\n\nSpecial Cases:\nTerminates program if any Gouraud table is already allocated\nUses complex bit manipulation for gradient calculations with sign extension\nDifferent loop counts per table: 8, 16, 32, 32, 40 elements per row\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x9000 - Size of X-coordinate table (36864 bytes)\n0x4003 - Size of Y-coordinate table (16387 bytes) \n0x8003 - Size of X-value table (32771 bytes)\n0x20000 - Size of subtile table (131072 bytes)\n0xa003 - Size of tile table (40963 bytes)\n0x10000 - Loop increment (65536) for 512x512 grid calculation\n0x200000 - Loop limit (2097152) for outer loops\n0x1fffff - Mask value (2097151) for loop boundary check\n0x6fbeeb28 - Base address of color palette for pointer calculations\n0xca, 0xcb, 0xcc, 0xcd, 0xce - Error codes for table allocation failures\n0x66666667 - Magic constant for division by 40 optimization\n\nError Handling:\nEach table allocation is validated - calls Ordinal_10023 with specific error code if already allocated\nCalls FUN_6fb9a10f(-1) to terminate program on any allocation error",
      "tags": ["PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "STRUCT_Skill", "SRC_View.cpp", "PARAM_0", "PROP_LOOPHEAVY", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "MOD_GAME", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
