      "comment": "Deallocates Gouraud shading table memory and validates proper cleanup.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if main Gouraud table (DAT_6fbf21b0) is allocated\n2. Validate required Y table (DAT_6fbf21b4) exists, report error 0xfb if missing\n3. Validate required XVal table (DAT_6fbf21b8) exists, report error 0xfc if missing  \n4. Validate required SubtileGouraud table (DAT_6fbf21c0) exists, report error 0xfd if missing\n5. Validate required TileGouraud table (DAT_6fbf21c4) exists, report error 0xfe if missing\n6. Free main Gouraud table using FUN_6fb997fb\n7. Free Y table if allocated\n8. Free XVal table if allocated\n9. Free SubtileGouraud table if allocated\n10. Free TileGouraud table if allocated\n11. Clear all global table pointers to NULL\n12. Reset Gouraud initialization flag (DAT_6fbeeaf8) to 0\n13. Report and clear validation error handles if present\n\nParameters:\nNone - Function operates on global Gouraud table state\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\nEarly return if main Gouraud table (DAT_6fbf21b0) is NULL\nFatal termination via FUN_6fb9a10f(0xffffffff) for missing required tables\nValidation error cleanup handled separately from memory deallocation\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0xfb (251) - Error code for missing sgpGouraudTblY table\n0xfc (252) - Error code for missing sgpGouraudTblXVal table  \n0xfd (253) - Error code for missing gpSubtileGouraudTbl table\n0xfe (254) - Error code for missing gpTileGouraudTbl table\n0xffffffff - Fatal error termination code\n\nError Handling:\nMissing required tables trigger Ordinal_10023 error reporting\nFatal process termination via FUN_6fb9a10f for critical validation failures\nValidation error handles cleared via ReportValidationError",
