      "comment": "Initialize viewport rectangle structures with bounds and clipping regions.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate viewport pointer is not NULL, exit with error if invalid\n2. Set bounds rectangle from provided left, top, right, bottom coordinates\n3. Determine windowed mode status via API call\n4. Set clipping rectangle with screen dimensions plus padding (-80 to screen+80 horizontally, -80 to screen-47 vertically)\n5. If windowed mode enabled, adjust clipping rectangle margins (-45 left, -30 top, +30 bottom)\n6. Set viewport active flag (bit 0) to mark structure as initialized\n\nParameters:\npViewport - Pointer to ViewportRect structure containing flags and two RECT structures\nnLeft - Left coordinate for bounds rectangle  \nnTop - Top coordinate for bounds rectangle\nnRight - Right coordinate for bounds rectangle\nnBottom - Bottom coordinate for bounds rectangle\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value, exits process on NULL pointer\n\nSpecial Cases:\nNULL viewport pointer triggers assertion and process termination\nWindowed mode applies additional margin adjustments to clipping rectangle\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x15e (350) - Error code for NULL viewport assertion\n0xffffffff (-1) - Exit code for process termination  \n0x50 (80) - Screen padding for clipping rectangle\n0x2f (47) - Bottom margin adjustment for clipping rectangle\n0x1e (30) - Windowed mode margin adjustment for top/bottom\n0x2d (45) - Windowed mode margin adjustment for left side\n0x1 - Active flag bit in viewport flags\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset | Size | Field Name | Type     | Description\n-------|------|------------|----------|---------------------------\n0x0    | 4    | dwFlags    | uint     | Status flags, bit 0 = active\n0x4    | 16   | rcBounds   | tagRECT  | Object bounds rectangle  \n0x14   | 16   | rcClip     | tagRECT  | Screen clipping rectangle",
