      "comment": "Extract coordinate rectangle fields from a data structure.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract left coordinate from structure offset +4 and store through output pointer\n2. Extract top coordinate from structure offset +8 and store through output pointer  \n3. Extract right coordinate from structure offset +12 and store through output pointer\n4. Extract bottom coordinate from structure offset +16 and store through output pointer\n\nParameters:\n  pSource (CoordinateRect *) - Input structure containing coordinate data\n  pnLeft (int *) - Output pointer to receive left coordinate value\n  pnTop (int *) - Output pointer to receive top coordinate value  \n  pnRight (int *) - Output pointer to receive right coordinate value\n  pnBottom (int *) - Output pointer to receive bottom coordinate value\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value, results stored through output pointers\n\nStructure Layout:\n  Offset | Size | Field Name | Type | Description\n  ------ | ---- | ---------- | ---- | -----------\n  0x00   | 4    | dwHeader   | uint | Header/type identifier\n  0x04   | 4    | nLeft      | int  | Left coordinate\n  0x08   | 4    | nTop       | int  | Top coordinate  \n  0x0C   | 4    | nRight     | int  | Right coordinate\n  0x10   | 4    | nBottom    | int  | Bottom coordinate\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - All output pointers must be valid (not NULL)\n  - No validation performed on input parameters\n  - Coordinates extracted as-is without range checking",
