      "comment": "Updates configuration values and sets dirty flag when changes detected.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Compare current configuration value at offset 0x24 with dwNewValue1\n2. If values differ, jump to update sequence\n3. Compare current configuration value at offset 0x28 with dwNewValue2  \n4. If values match, exit without changes\n5. Store dwNewValue2 at configuration offset 0x28\n6. Load current flags from configuration base address\n7. Set bit 0 (dirty flag) using OR operation with 0x1\n8. Store dwNewValue1 at configuration offset 0x24\n9. Write modified flags back to configuration base address\n\nParameters:\n- pConfigData (dword *): Pointer to configuration data structure\n- dwNewValue1 (dword): New value to store at offset 0x24 (index 9)\n- dwNewValue2 (dword): New value to store at offset 0x28 (index 10)\n\nReturns:\n- void: No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If both values match current configuration, function returns early with no modifications\n- Configuration structure accessed at offsets: 0x00 (flags), 0x24 (value1), 0x28 (value2)\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n- 0x1: Dirty flag bit mask for configuration change detection\n- 0x24: Byte offset for configuration value 1 (36 decimal, index 9)\n- 0x28: Byte offset for configuration value 2 (40 decimal, index 10)\n\nError Handling:\n- No error checking performed - assumes valid pConfigData pointer\n- No bounds checking on configuration structure access",
