      "comment": "Applies time-based screen shake offset calculations to X/Y coordinates.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get current system time using GetTickCount()\n2. Calculate elapsed time since shake start time (DAT_6fbf1c28)\n3. Check if total shake duration (fade + sustain + decay) has exceeded elapsed time\n4. If duration exceeded, reset shake state and exit early\n5. Determine shake phase based on elapsed time vs fade duration (DAT_6fbeeaf0)\n6. If in fade-in phase: calculate proportional intensity based on elapsed/fade ratio\n7. If in sustain phase: use full shake intensity (DAT_6fbf21a8)  \n8. If in decay phase: calculate decaying intensity based on remaining time\n9. Generate random X offset using intensity * 2 as range, subtract intensity for centering\n10. Generate random Y offset using same method\n11. Store calculated offsets in global shake state variables\n12. Apply offsets to input coordinate pointers\n13. Update shake state with final intensity value\n\nParameters:\npnXOffset (int*): Pointer to X coordinate to modify with shake offset\npnYOffset (int*): Pointer to Y coordinate to modify with shake offset\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\nMagic number 0x2c added to random seed base for distribution variance\nZero intensity check prevents unnecessary random generation calls\nDivision by zero protection for fade and decay duration globals\n\nGlobal Variables:\nDAT_6fbf1c28 - Shake start time (ticks)\nDAT_6fbeeae8 - Shake decay duration (ticks) \nDAT_6fbf1d70 - Shake sustain duration (ticks)\nDAT_6fbeeaf0 - Shake fade-in duration (ticks)\nDAT_6fbf21a8 - Base shake intensity value\nDAT_6fbf21ac - Current X shake offset\nDAT_6fbeeaf4 - Current Y shake offset\n\nNote: Function uses 1 stack-allocated temporary variable optimized away by decompiler",
