      "comment": "Sets the alpha transparency level for the Gouraud shading table system.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Convert input percentage (0-20) to alpha value (0-255) using formula: (nIntensityPercent * 255) / 20\n2. Clamp calculated alpha to valid range (0-255)\n3. Check if global Gouraud table handle exists, create if needed\n4. Get current alpha value from table\n5. If target equals current, exit early\n6. Calculate smooth transition value with ±6 unit deadband\n7. Apply new alpha value to table or cleanup if zero\n\nParameters:\n- nIntensityPercent: Input intensity percentage (0-20 scale)\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Values below 0 are clamped to 0\n- Values above 255 are clamped to 255\n- Zero alpha destroys the table and clears global handle\n- Smooth transitions prevent flickering with ±6 unit deadband\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n- 0x14 (20): Scale factor for percentage conversion\n- 0xff (255): Maximum alpha value\n- 0x1c4 (452): Table creation parameter\n- 6: Smoothing deadband for alpha transitions",
