      "comment": "Scales a width value by dividing by 5 and stores the result in the global boundary.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Multiply dwWidth by magic constant 0xCCCCCCCD (loaded in EAX)\n2. Shift right by 2 bits to complete integer division by 5\n3. Store scaled result to g_dwScaledWidthBoundary global\n4. Call Ordinal_10329 (D2Common.GetUnitX) to get unit X coordinate\n\nParameters:\ndwWidth (uint): Width value to scale (passed in ECX via __fastcall)\nIMPLICIT in_EAX: Magic constant 0xCCCCCCCD for division by 5\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Result stored in g_dwScaledWidthBoundary global\n\nSpecial Cases:\nFunction has no callers detected - may be called via function pointer\nUsed by ValidateCoordinatesInBounds to check X coordinate boundaries\nThe division by 5 scales map coordinates to screen space\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0xCCCCCCCD: Magic multiplier for unsigned division by 5\n0x2: Shift amount to complete division (total shift of 34 bits from 64-bit multiply)",
