      "comment": "Scales height boundary and sets up room element iteration for coordinate validation.\n\nNOTE: This function is ORPHANED CODE - it is the continuation of ScaleAndStoreWidthBoundary\nat 0x6fae7520. Ghidra incorrectly split the function at this address. The instruction at\n0x6fae7533 (MOV EAX, 0xCCCCCCCD) falls through directly to this code (MUL EDX at 0x6fae7538).\nThese should be merged into a single function.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Scale dwHeight by dividing by 5 using magic multiplication (in_EAX * dwHeight >> 34)\n2. Store scaled result to g_dwScaledHeightBoundary (0x6fbf21ec)\n3. Call Ordinal_10329 (D2Common.GetUnitX) to get unit X coordinate as flags\n4. Call Ordinal_10326 (D2Common.GetUnitY) to get unit Y coordinate as source ID\n5. Get room pointer from unit via UNITS_GetRoom using unaff_ESI\n6. Retrieve region map data element using room, source ID, and flags\n7. Store region map element to g_dwRegionMapElement (0x6fbf21e8)\n8. Iterate over all room elements using callback at LAB_6fae7580\n\nParameters:\npUnit (int *): Pointer to unit structure (passed via ECX, but uses unaff_ESI internally)\ndwHeight (dword): Height value to scale and store as boundary (passed via EDX)\nIMPLICIT in_EAX (uint): Magic constant 0xCCCCCCCD for division by 5 (set by caller)\nIMPLICIT unaff_ESI (int *): Unit pointer used for UNITS_GetRoom call (pUnit)\nIMPLICIT in_stack_00000034 (Room *): Room pointer passed to ForEachRoomElement\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Results stored in global variables g_dwScaledHeightBoundary and g_dwRegionMapElement\n\nPhantom Variables (Decompiler-generated, cannot be renamed):\nextraout_EAX (uint): Return value from Ordinal_10329, stored as dwFlags\nextraout_EAX_00 (uint): Return value from Ordinal_10326, stored as dwSourceId  \nextraout_EAX_01 (undefined4): Return value from GetRegionMapDataElement, stored to global\nppBuffer (void **): Room pointer returned by UNITS_GetRoom\ndwFlags (uint): X coordinate from Ordinal_10329, passed to GetRegionMapDataElement\ndwSourceId (uint): Y coordinate from Ordinal_10326, passed to GetRegionMapDataElement\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- No direct callers detected - this is fall-through code from ScaleAndStoreWidthBoundary\n- The callback LAB_6fae7580 is passed to ForEachRoomElement for per-element processing\n- Used by ValidateCoordinatesInBounds to check Y coordinate boundaries\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0xCCCCCCCD: Magic multiplier for unsigned division by 5 (set by caller in EAX)\n0x22 (34): Total shift amount for 64-bit multiply result to complete /5 division\n\nGlobals Modified:\ng_dwScaledHeightBoundary (0x6fbf21ec): Stores height/5 for boundary checks\ng_dwRegionMapElement (0x6fbf21e8): Stores region map data element result\n\nOrdinal References:\nOrdinal_10329 = D2Common.GetUnitX - Returns unit X coordinate in EAX\nOrdinal_10326 = D2Common.GetUnitY - Returns unit Y coordinate in EAX\n\nRelated Functions:\nScaleAndStoreWidthBoundary (0x6fae7520): Preceding function that falls through to this code\nValidateCoordinatesInBounds: Uses the global boundaries set by this function",
