      "comment": "Validates whether entity coordinates are within valid map boundaries.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check global flag DAT_6fbb0fbc to determine validation method\n2. If flag is 0 (coordinate mode), convert entity ID to screen coordinates using Ordinal_10034\n3. Scale unit position coordinates by factor of 5 and add to converted coordinates\n4. Check if scaled X coordinate is within valid range (DAT_6fbf21f0 * 5 ± 20)\n5. If X is valid, verify entity type allows horizontal movement (cases 1,4,5,7,8,10,12)\n6. Check if scaled Y coordinate is within valid range (DAT_6fbf21ec * 5 ± 20) \n7. If Y is valid, verify entity type allows vertical movement (cases 2,3,6,7,9,11,12)\n8. If flag is non-zero (entity mode), validate using entity data pointer at offset +0x10\n9. Verify entity data exists and field at offset +0x28 matches DAT_6fbf21e8\n10. Compare entity coordinates against global boundaries DAT_6fbf21f0 and DAT_6fbf21ec\n11. Return true if coordinates are valid, false otherwise\n\nParameters:\ndwEntityId (uint): Entity identifier passed to coordinate conversion function\npUnit (UnitAny *): Pointer to unit structure containing position and type data\n\nReturns:\nbool: true if coordinates are within valid boundaries, false if out of bounds\n\nSpecial Cases:\nEntity types 7 and 12 allow both horizontal and vertical movement\nCoordinate validation includes 20-unit buffer zone (0x14) around boundaries\nGlobal validation flag DAT_6fbb0fbc switches between coordinate and entity modes\n\nStructure Layout:\nUnitAny at pUnit:\nOffset | Size | Field | Type | Description\n+0x08  | 4    | nX    | int  | Entity X coordinate\n+0x0C  | 4    | nY    | int  | Entity Y coordinate  \n+0x10  | 4    | pData | int* | Pointer to entity data structure\n+0x1C  | 4    | dwType| uint | Entity type/category (1-12)\n\nEntity Data Structure at pUnit->pData:\nOffset | Size | Field     | Type | Description\n+0x00  | 4    | nCoordX   | int  | Primary X coordinate\n+0x04  | 4    | nCoordY   | int  | Primary Y coordinate\n+0x28  | 4    | dwValidation | uint | Validation field compared with DAT_6fbf21e8\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x14 (20): Boundary buffer zone in coordinate units\n0x5 (5): Coordinate scaling factor for map calculations\nDAT_6fbf21f0: Global X boundary limit\nDAT_6fbf21ec: Global Y boundary limit  \nDAT_6fbf21e8: Entity validation constant\nDAT_6fbb0fbc: Validation mode flag (0=coordinate mode, 1=entity mode)",
