      "comment": "Adds a new render queue entry with transformed coordinates to the rendering queue.\n\nAlgorithm:\n\n1. Read current queue index from render context (offset 0xea64)\n2. Increment queue index counter for next entry allocation  \n3. Check if queue is not full (limit is 3000 entries)\n4. Calculate queue entry pointer: base + (index * 5) + 1 (5 uint elements per entry)\n5. Initialize queue entry with type 1 (active), entity reference, and null next pointer\n6. Call coordinate transform function (Ordinal_10034) with entity ID and output buffer\n7. Calculate transformed X coordinate: (transform_x + entity_x_base * 5) * 8\n8. Calculate transformed Y coordinate: (transform_y + entity_y_base * 5) * 8\n9. Set bit flag in render context using global bit mask at offset 0xc\n10. Find end of linked list starting from list node head pointer\n11. Append new queue entry to end of linked list\n\nParameters:\n\npRenderContext (uint*): Main rendering context containing queue array and counter\npListNode (RenderListNode*): Linked list node containing head pointer at offset 0x10\npEntity (uint*): Entity structure with coordinate bases at offsets 8 and 0xc\ndwEntityId (uint): Entity identifier passed to coordinate transform function\n\nReturns:\n\nvoid - Function performs operation without return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n\n- If queue is full (>= 3000 entries), function returns early without adding entry\n- If linked list is empty (head pointer is null), new entry becomes head\n- Coordinate calculation uses fixed multiplier of 5 and scale factor of 8",
