      "instructions": ["0x18000|PUSH|EBP", "0x18001|PUSH|ESI", "0x18002|PUSH|EDI", "0x18003|MOV|EDI, ECX", "0x18005|MOV|EBP, EDX", "0x18007|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [EDI + 0xea64]", "0x1800D|CMP|EAX, 0xbb8", "0x18012|LEA|ECX, [EAX + 0x1]", "0x18015|MOV|dword ptr [EDI + 0xea64], ECX", "0x1801B|JNC|0x6fae8080", "0x1801D|LEA|EDX, [EAX + EAX*0x4]", "0x18020|PUSH|EBX", "0x18021|MOV|EBX, dword ptr [ESP + 0x14]", "0x18025|LEA|ESI, [EDI + EDX*0x4 + 0x4]", "0x18029|PUSH|EBX"],
      "comment": "Adds a new data entry to the managed data pool with coordinate calculation and linked list insertion.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Read current pool index from pDataPool[0x3a99] and increment counter \n2. Check if pool has capacity (index < 3000), exit early if full\n3. Calculate entry address: pDataPool + (index * 5) + 1 (20-byte entries)\n4. Initialize entry fields: flags=0, param=dwParam, next=NULL  \n5. Call Ordinal_10326(dwParam) to get X coordinate, shift left by 3, store in entry[1]\n6. Call Ordinal_10329(dwParam) to get Y coordinate, shift left by 3, store in entry[2] \n7. Set global bitmask flag: pDataPool[0] |= gdwBitMasks_exref[3]\n8. Insert entry into linked list at pManager[4] (offset 0x10)\n9. If list empty, set as head; otherwise traverse to tail and append\n\nParameters:\npDataPool - Pointer to data pool structure containing counter at offset 0x3a99 and entry array starting at offset +1\npManager - Manager structure with linked list head pointer at offset 0x10  \ndwParam - Parameter passed to coordinate calculation functions (Ordinal_10326, Ordinal_10329)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value, function always succeeds within capacity limit\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Pool capacity limit: 3000 entries maximum, function exits silently if exceeded\n- Empty linked list: New entry becomes head node when pManager[4] == NULL\n- Non-empty list: Traverses to tail node (next == NULL) before appending\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x3a99 (15001) - Pool counter/index offset in pDataPool structure  \n0x10 (16) - Linked list head pointer offset in manager structure\n3000 (0xbb8) - Maximum pool capacity limit\n5 - Entry size multiplier (20 bytes = 5 × 4-byte fields)\n3 - Bit shift amount for coordinate values (multiply by 8)\n0xc (12) - Offset in gdwBitMasks_exref for global state flag\n\nStructure Layout:\nDataEntryNode (20 bytes):\nOffset | Size | Field Name | Type     | Description  \n0x00   | 4    | dwFlags    | uint     | Entry status flags (initialized to 0)\n0x04   | 4    | dwX        | uint     | X coordinate (from Ordinal_10326 << 3)  \n0x08   | 4    | dwY        | uint     | Y coordinate (from Ordinal_10329 << 3)\n0x0c   | 4    | dwParam    | uint     | Original parameter value\n0x10   | 4    | pNext      | void*    | Pointer to next entry in linked list",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_3", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
