      "instructions": ["0x18380|PUSH|EBX", "0x18381|PUSH|EDI", "0x18382|CALL|0x6fb62880", "0x18387|MOV|EBX, EAX", "0x18389|TEST|EBX, EBX", "0x1838B|JZ|0x6fae8453", "0x18391|PUSH|EBX", "0x18392|CALL|0x6fb98164", "0x18397|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0x18399|JZ|0x6fae8453", "0x1839F|PUSH|0x98", "0x183A4|PUSH|0x2", "0x183A6|PUSH|EAX", "0x183A7|CALL|0x6fb98374", "0x183AC|MOV|EDI, EAX"],
      "comment": "Initialize waypoint visual effect including portal animation and glow overlays.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get current game context (player unit)\n2. Return early if game context is NULL\n3. Get room data from player unit via UNITS_GetRoom\n4. Return early if room is NULL\n5. Find waypoint tile in room at coordinates (2, 0x98)\n6. Return early if waypoint tile not found\n7. Configure inventory fade effect (type 0x1251, duration 0x2d5, flag 1)\n8. Get waypoint X coordinate via Ordinal_10326\n9. Get waypoint Y coordinate via Ordinal_10329\n10. Create drawable object at waypoint position (type 0x152)\n11. If drawable created successfully:\n    a. Set drawable coordinates with offset 0x28\n    b. Set graphics property value 0x200 (glow intensity)\n    c. Apply color effect 0x46 (portal glow color)\n    d. Set graphics info field bit 1 (enable rendering)\n12. Initialize overlay data on tile (type 0xB5=portal, mode 2)\n13. Initialize monster region stats (type 0xD3, region 1)\n\nParameters:\n  None - uses implicit game context\n\nReturns:\n  void - always returns after initialization\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Early exit if game context unavailable\n  - Early exit if player not in valid room\n  - Early exit if waypoint tile not found at expected coordinates\n  - Drawable creation can fail silently (overlay still created)\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x1251 (4689) - Inventory fade effect type for waypoint\n  0x2d5 (725) - Fade effect duration in frames\n  0x98 (152) - Waypoint tile Y coordinate\n  0x152 (338) - Drawable object type ID for waypoint portal\n  0x28 (40) - Coordinate offset for drawable positioning\n  0x200 (512) - Graphics property value for glow intensity\n  0x46 (70) - Color effect index for portal glow\n  0xB5 (181) - Overlay type for waypoint portal effect\n  0xD3 (211) - Monster region stat type for waypoint area\n\nOrdinal Functions:\n  Ordinal_10326 - D2Common.UNITS_GetTileX - Get X coordinate of tile\n  Ordinal_10329 - D2Common.UNITS_GetTileY - Get Y coordinate of tile\n\nClassification: Initialization function - sets up waypoint visual state",
      "tags": ["PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_0"]
    },
