      "comment": "Initialize special visual effects when entering Act 4 Town (Pandemonium Fortress).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Set global town portal active flag (g_dwTownPortalActiveFlag = 1)\n2. Get game context/player unit pointer via GetGameContext()\n3. If no valid player unit, exit early\n4. Get player's current room via UNITS_GetRoom()\n5. If no valid room, exit early\n6. Get room's level ID via GetEntityField() (returns area/act ID)\n7. Compare level ID against 0x6c (108 = Pandemonium Fortress/Act 4 Town)\n8. If not in Act 4 Town, exit early\n9. Get player X coordinate via Ordinal_10326 (D2Common.UNITS_GetXCoord)\n10. Get player Y coordinate via Ordinal_10329 (D2Common.UNITS_GetYCoord)\n11. Initialize visual effect structure at player location with type 0x174\n12. Initialize monster region stats with type 0xf3 for region 1\n\nParameters:\n  None (void)\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Function only activates in Act 4 Town (level ID 0x6c/108)\n  - All other areas cause early exit without effect initialization\n  - Invalid player unit or room causes silent early return\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x6c (108) - Level ID for Pandemonium Fortress (Act 4 Town)\n  0x174 (372) - Visual effect type ID for portal/town effect\n  0xf3 (243) - Monster region stat initialization type\n  0x1 - Region ID for initialization, also portal active flag value\n\nRelated Functions:\n  GetGameContext() - Returns player unit pointer\n  UNITS_GetRoom() - Gets room/area from unit (D2Common)\n  GetEntityField() - Gets level ID from room\n  Ordinal_10326 - D2Common.UNITS_GetXCoord\n  Ordinal_10329 - D2Common.UNITS_GetYCoord\n  InitializeStructureAndCallHandler() - Creates visual effect at coordinates\n  InitializeMonsterRegionStats() - Initializes monster data for region",
      "tags": ["PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_0"]
