      "comment": "Initializes a complex visual effect sequence with layered display and positioning.\n\nAlgorithm:\n\n1. Obtain game resource handle via resource management system\n2. Validate resource handle availability before proceeding\n3. Create initial effect object container using resource handle\n4. Validate effect object creation success before setup\n5. Allocate effect object memory buffer (size 0x178 bytes)\n6. Validate memory allocation success before configuration\n7. Initialize primary visual effect layer (type 0x1250, display layer 0x15e)\n8. Configure effect animation parameters (type 0x23, object reference, zero motion)\n9. Extract X coordinate from effect object positioning data\n10. Extract Y coordinate from effect object positioning data  \n11. Create positioned effect instance (resource, position 0x175, coordinates, enabled)\n12. Validate effect instance creation before final setup\n13. Configure effect properties using object data at offset +0x8\n14. Finalize effect state and enable for rendering\n\nParameters:\nNone - uses internal game state and resource management\n\nReturns:\nvoid - success indicated by completing initialization sequence\nFailure modes silently abort at validation checkpoints\n\nSpecial Cases:\nResource unavailable - silent early return at step 2\nEffect creation failure - silent early return at step 4  \nMemory allocation failure - silent early return at step 6\nPosition creation failure - silent early return at step 11\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x178 (376 decimal) - Effect object memory buffer size in bytes\n0x1250 (4688 decimal) - Primary visual effect type identifier\n0x15e (350 decimal) - Display layer/rendering order for visual effect\n0x23 (35 decimal) - Animation/effect parameter configuration type\n0x175 (373 decimal) - Positioned effect instance type identifier\n0x8 (8 decimal) - Byte offset to object properties in effect structure",
      "tags": ["PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_0"]
