      "comment": "Creates a missile effect at a portal tile location in the current game.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get the current game context (player unit)\n2. If no valid player unit, exit early\n3. Get the room containing the player unit\n4. If no valid room, exit early\n5. Find room tile with type 2 (portal) at Y coordinate 0x1CC (460)\n6. If no matching tile found, exit early\n7. Get X coordinate from tile via Ordinal_10329 (D2Common.GetTileX)\n8. Get Y coordinate from tile via Ordinal_10326 (D2Common.GetTileY)\n9. Create missile type 0x210 (528) at tile coordinates with flags=1\n10. If missile created successfully, set target unit to 0x19 (25)\n\nParameters:\nNone - Uses global game context\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Exits early if game context is NULL (no active game)\n- Exits early if player has no valid room\n- Exits early if no portal tile (type 2) found at coordinate 0x1CC\n- Missile creation may fail, in which case target is not set\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x2 - Tile type (portal/waypoint tile)\n0x1CC (460) - Fixed Y coordinate for portal tile search\n0x210 (528) - Missile type ID for portal effect\n0x1 - Missile creation flags\n0x19 (25) - Target unit type/ID for missile\n\nOrdinal Function Reference:\nOrdinal_10329 - D2Common.GetTileX - Gets X coordinate from tile\nOrdinal_10326 - D2Common.GetTileY - Gets Y coordinate from tile\n\nFunction Classification:\nWorker function - Creates visual missile effect at portal locations\nNo callers found - Likely callback or event handler for portal activation",
      "tags": ["PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_0"]
    },
