      "instructions": ["0x18670|PUSH|EBP", "0x18671|PUSH|ESI", "0x18672|CALL|0x6fb62880", "0x18677|MOV|EBP, EAX", "0x18679|TEST|EBP, EBP", "0x1867B|JZ|0x6fae86df", "0x1867D|PUSH|EBP", "0x1867E|CALL|0x6fb98164", "0x18683|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0x18685|JZ|0x6fae86df", "0x18687|PUSH|0x20e", "0x1868C|PUSH|0x1", "0x1868E|PUSH|EAX", "0x1868F|CALL|0x6fb98374", "0x18694|MOV|ESI, EAX"],
      "comment": "Activates waypoint visual effects by spawning missiles at the waypoint tile location.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get current game context (player unit) via GetGameContext\n2. Validate game unit is not NULL, exit early if invalid\n3. Get the room containing the player unit via UNITS_GetRoom\n4. Validate room is not NULL, exit early if invalid\n5. Find waypoint tile in room using FindRoomTileByCoord(room, 1, 0x20E)\n   - Type 1 indicates waypoint tile search\n   - 0x20E (526) is waypoint tile identifier\n6. Validate waypoint tile found, exit early if not found\n7. Get tile X coordinate via Ordinal_10326 (D2Common.GetTileX)\n8. Get tile Y coordinate via Ordinal_10329 (D2Common.GetTileY)\n9. Spawn first visual effect (type 0x25E/606) at tile coordinates\n10. Spawn second visual effect (type 0x25B/603) at tile coordinates\n11. Set flag 0x40000 on tile at offset 0xEC to mark waypoint as activated\n\nParameters: None (uses global game context)\n\nReturns: void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Early exit if game context is NULL\n- Early exit if player room is NULL\n- Early exit if waypoint tile not found in room\n- Flag 0x40000 at tile[0x3B] (offset 0xEC) marks activation state\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x20E (526) - Waypoint tile type identifier\n0x25E (606) - First waypoint activation effect/missile type\n0x25B (603) - Second waypoint activation effect/missile type\n0x40000 - Waypoint activated flag bit\n0xEC (236) - Tile structure offset for flags field (tile[0x3B])\n\nOrdinal References:\nOrdinal_10326 - D2Common.GetTileX - Returns tile X world coordinate\nOrdinal_10329 - D2Common.GetTileY - Returns tile Y world coordinate",
      "tags": ["PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_0"]
    },
