      "instructions": ["0x18700|SUB|ESP, 0x58", "0x18703|PUSH|EBX", "0x18704|MOV|EBX, ECX", "0x18706|TEST|EBX, EBX", "0x18708|PUSH|ESI", "0x18709|JZ|0x6fae87a5", "0x1870F|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [EBX + 0x4]", "0x18712|SUB|EAX, 0x21c", "0x18717|JZ|0x6fae8731", "0x18719|DEC|EAX", "0x1871A|JZ|0x6fae872a", "0x1871C|DEC|EAX", "0x1871D|JNZ|0x6fae87a5", "0x18723|MOV|EAX, 0x1da", "0x18728|JMP|0x6fae8736"],
      "comment": "Processes game event notifications and creates corresponding message structures for inter-system communication.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate the input game object pointer is not NULL\n2. Read the event type from game object offset +4 (dwEventType field)\n3. Map event type to resource ID based on predefined mapping table\n4. If event type is unrecognized (not 0x21c/0x21d/0x21e), return immediately\n5. Call Ordinal_10342 to extract object data from game object\n6. Call Ordinal_11087 with extracted data, resource type 2, and mapped resource ID\n7. If resource lookup fails, return without creating message\n8. Initialize 88-byte message buffer by zero-filling 22 dwords\n9. Populate GameMessage structure fields in specific order\n10. Call FUN_6fb77720 to process and validate message buffer structure\n11. If message processing succeeds, call Ordinal_11140 with result and resource data\n12. Complete notification processing and return to caller\n\nParameters:\npGameObject - Pointer to GameObject structure containing event information\n              dwEventType field at offset +4 determines message type and processing path\n              Must not be NULL or function returns immediately without processing\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Function performs notification processing without return value\n       Success indicated by completion of message processing chain\n       Failure cases result in early return without error codes\n\nSpecial Cases:\nUnrecognized event types cause immediate return without processing\nNULL game object pointer bypasses all processing logic\nResource lookup failure prevents message structure creation  \nMessage buffer processing failure skips final notification call\nAll error conditions handled by early return without error reporting\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x21c (540) - Game event type A requiring resource ID 0x1db (475)\n0x21d (541) - Game event type B requiring resource ID 0x1dc (476)  \n0x21e (542) - Game event type C requiring resource ID 0x1da (474)\n0x420 (1056) - Standard message type identifier for game events\n0x16 (22) - Message buffer size in dwords (88 total bytes)\n2 - Resource type parameter for Ordinal_11087 lookup function\n1 - Standard flags value for processed game event messages\n\nStructure Layout:\nGameObject (pGameObject parameter):\nOffset | Size | Field Name | Type | Description\n0x00   | 4    | dwObjectId | uint | Unique object identifier\n0x04   | 4    | dwEventType| uint | Event type (0x21c/0x21d/0x21e)\n0x08   | 4    | pData      | void*| Object-specific data pointer\n0x0C   | 4    | dwFlags    | uint | Object state and property flags\n\nGameMessage (dwMessageBuffer stack structure):\nOffset | Size | Field Name        | Type   | Description\n0x00   | 4    | dwMessageType     | uint   | Message type (0x420)\n0x04   | 4    | pSender          | void*  | Source game object pointer\n0x08   | 4    | pTarget          | void*  | Target game object pointer  \n0x0C   | 4    | dwReserved1      | uint   | Reserved for future use\n0x10   | 4    | dwMessageSubType | uint   | Message subtype (0x21d)\n0x14   | 4    | dwReserved2      | uint   | Reserved for future use\n0x18   | 4    | dwData1          | uint   | Resource data field 1\n0x1C   | 4    | dwData2          | uint   | Resource data field 2\n0x20   | 4    | reserved3        | uint   | Reserved for alignment\n0x24   | 4    | reserved4        | uint   | Reserved for alignment\n0x28   | 4    | reserved5        | uint   | Reserved for alignment\n0x2C   | 4    | dwFlags          | uint   | Message processing flags",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PARAM_1", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
