      "instructions": ["0x18820|SUB|ESP, 0x58", "0x18823|PUSH|ESI", "0x18824|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0x18826|PUSH|EDI", "0x18827|MOV|ECX, 0x16", "0x1882C|XOR|EAX, EAX", "0x1882E|LEA|EDI, [ESP + 0x8]", "0x18832|STOSD.REP|ES:EDI", "0x18834|LEA|ECX, [ESP + 0x8]", "0x18838|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x18], 0x11c", "0x18840|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0xc], ESI", "0x18844|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x10], ESI", "0x18848|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x34], 0x1", "0x18850|CALL|0x6fb77720", "0x18855|TEST|EAX, EAX"],
      "comment": "Processes multiple resource requests in sequence, with optional cleanup call for first request.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize request buffer by zeroing uint array of 22 elements (0x16 * 4 bytes)\n2. Set resource ID to 0x11c and request count to 1\n3. Call lookup function FUN_6fb77720 with buffer to retrieve resource\n4. If resource found (non-null result), call cleanup function Ordinal_11140 with parameter 0x32\n5. Re-initialize buffer by zeroing array again\n6. Set resource ID to 0x128 and request count to 1, call lookup function\n7. Set resource ID to 0x125 (keeping same buffer state), call lookup function again\n8. Return without cleanup for second and third requests\n\nParameters:\nIMPLICIT ECX (pThis): Object instance pointer for member function context\n\nReturns:\nvoid: No return value, function performs resource operations with side effects\n\nSpecial Cases:\nOnly the first resource request (0x11c) triggers cleanup if successful\nSubsequent requests (0x128, 0x125) are processed without conditional cleanup\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x11c (284): First resource identifier requiring cleanup on success\n0x128 (296): Second resource identifier, no cleanup\n0x125 (293): Third resource identifier, no cleanup\n0x32 (50): Cleanup operation parameter for Ordinal_11140\n0x16 (22): Buffer size in uint elements (88 bytes total)\n1: Standard request count for all operations",
