      "instructions": ["0x188B0|SUB|ESP, 0x58", "0x188B3|PUSH|EBX", "0x188B4|PUSH|EBP", "0x188B5|PUSH|ESI", "0x188B6|PUSH|EDI", "0x188B7|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0x188B9|PUSH|0x173", "0x188BE|PUSH|0x2", "0x188C0|PUSH|ESI", "0x188C1|CALL|0x6fb98164", "0x188C6|PUSH|EAX", "0x188C7|CALL|0x6fb98374", "0x188CC|MOV|EDI, EAX", "0x188CE|TEST|EDI, EDI", "0x188D0|JZ|0x6fae88e4"],
      "comment": "Initializes a window structure and handles window coordinate processing for UI rendering\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize API parameters (dwAPIParam1=2, dwAPIParam2=0x173)\n2. Call Ordinal_10342 to get window handle from input handle  \n3. Validate window handle using Ordinal_11087 with parameters\n4. If validation fails (result==0), get adjusted coordinates from original handle\n5. If validation succeeds, get coordinates directly from validated handle  \n6. Initialize 22-element window structure array with zeros\n7. Set structure fields with magic numbers and coordinates\n8. Call FUN_6fb77720 to process window structure\n9. Create window/object using FUN_6fb77d70 with coordinates and flags\n10. If creation succeeds, finalize with Ordinal_11142\n\nParameters:\nnWindowHandle - Input window or object handle for coordinate processing\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value, operates by side effect\n\nSpecial Cases:\nHandle validation failure triggers coordinate adjustment (-15 offset)\nStructure initialized as 88-byte array (22 DWORDs)\nWindow creation failure is silently ignored (no error handling)\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x173 (371) - API parameter for window validation\n0x2 (2) - API parameter type specifier  \n0x420 (1056) - Primary window type identifier\n0x123 (291) - Secondary window type identifier\n0xf (15) - Coordinate adjustment offset for failed validation\n0x14c (332) - Window creation parameter\n0x16 (22) - Structure array element count (22 DWORDs = 88 bytes)",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Path", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PARAM_1", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
