      "comment": "Initializes game feature with version validation and global state management\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Set configuration constants (type=3, value=0x271)\n2. Get object handle from game context via Ordinal_10342\n3. Initialize configuration using Ordinal_11087 with handle and constants\n4. If initialization succeeds:\n   a. Call feature setup functions (FUN_6fb979a0, FUN_6fb97b10, FUN_6fb97b40, FUN_6fb97be0, FUN_6fb98000)\n   b. Enable feature via Ordinal_11142\n   c. Get version info via FUN_6fb634e0\n   d. If version available, check if in valid range (0x83-0x84)\n   e. If version out of range, clear initialized flag\n   f. If version valid and feature not initialized but enabled:\n      - Get context object via FUN_6fb62880\n      - If context valid, trigger feature activation (FUN_6fae9840 with 0x27f, 1)\n      - Set initialized flag to 1\n\nParameters:\nnGameContext - Game context identifier for initialization\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\nVersion range check ensures compatibility (0x83 = 131, 0x84 = 132)\nGlobal flags prevent double initialization and track state\nMagic number 0x27f (639) used in feature activation call\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x3 (3) - Configuration type constant\n0x271 (625) - Configuration value constant  \n0x12c (300) - Timeout value for FUN_6fb97b10\n0x83 (131) - Minimum supported version\n0x84 (132) - Maximum supported version\n0x27f (639) - Feature activation parameter",
