      "instructions": ["0x18D30|PUSH|ESI", "0x18D31|MOV|ESI, EDX", "0x18D33|PUSH|ECX", "0x18D34|CALL|0x6fb98140", "0x18D39|CMP|EAX, 0x8", "0x18D3C|JZ|0x6fae8da4", "0x18D3E|CMP|EAX, 0x6a", "0x18D41|JLE|0x6fae8d7c", "0x18D43|CMP|EAX, 0x6c", "0x18D46|JG|0x6fae8d7c", "0x18D48|MOV|EAX, [0x6fbf2274]", "0x18D4D|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0x18D4F|JZ|0x6fae8e0b", "0x18D55|CMP|dword ptr [0x6fbb10f0], -0x1", "0x18D5C|JNZ|0x6fae8e0b"],
      "comment": "Retrieves RGB color components based on specified color mode for palette configuration\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate color mode using Ordinal_10057(nColorMode)\n2. If mode is 8 (special mode):\n   - Check global flag DAT_6fbf2270 for special handling\n   - If flag is 0, call Ordinal_10002(0,1) for validation\n   - If validation passes, set RGB components to (0xFF, 0x40, 0x30)\n   - If DAT_6fbb10ec is -1, return 0x50\n   - Otherwise, perform brightness calculation: (DAT_6fbb10ec * 0x80) / 0x1e\n   - Convert float result to integer using __ftol() and return value\n3. If mode is in range 107-108 (0x6b-0x6c):\n   - Check DAT_6fbf2274 flag and DAT_6fbb10f0 condition\n   - If both conditions met, set RGB to (0xFF, 0x40, 0x30) and return 0xa0\n   - Otherwise fall through to default case\n4. For all other modes:\n   - Extract RGB components from ConfigurationData_6fbf2240 structure\n   - Set pbRedComponent = byte at offset +8, pbGreenComponent = byte at offset +9, pbBlueComponent = byte at offset +10\n   - Return ConfigurationData_6fbf2240.dwReserved1 as status code\n5. Return 0 if no conditions met (error case)\n\nParameters:\n  nColorMode (int): Color mode identifier (8=special mode, 107-108=range mode, others=default)\n  pbRedComponent (byte *): Output pointer for red color component (0-255)\n  pbGreenComponent (byte *): Output pointer for green color component (0-255)\n  pbBlueComponent (byte *): Output pointer for blue color component (0-255)\n\nReturns:\n  int: Status code or computed brightness value\n    0x50 - Special mode with uninitialized brightness\n    0xa0 - Range mode with special conditions\n    ConfigurationData_6fbf2240.dwReserved1 - Default mode return value\n    Computed value - Brightness calculation result for special mode\n    0 - Error condition or no matching case\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  Mode 8 requires global flags DAT_6fbf2270=0 and successful Ordinal_10002 validation\n  Modes 107-108 require DAT_6fbf2274≠0 and DAT_6fbb10f0=-1 for special handling\n  Default RGB values from ConfigurationData_6fbf2240 at bytes +8,+9,+10\n  Brightness formula: (value * 128) / 30 with float conversion\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x08 (8) - Special color mode for brightness calculation\n  0x6b (107) - Lower bound of range mode\n  0x6c (108) - Upper bound of range mode  \n  0xFF (255) - Maximum red component for special modes\n  0x40 (64) - Green component for special modes\n  0x30 (48) - Blue component for special modes\n  0x50 (80) - Return value for uninitialized brightness\n  0xa0 (160) - Return value for range mode with special conditions\n  0x80 (128) - Brightness multiplier in calculation\n  0x1e (30) - Brightness divisor in calculation\n\nStructure Layout:\nConfigurationData_6fbf2240 (44 bytes):\nOffset | Size | Field Name    | Type | Description\n+0     | 4    | dwReserved1   | uint | Default return status code\n+8     | 1    | bRedDefault   | byte | Default red color component\n+9     | 1    | bGreenDefault | byte | Default green color component  \n+10    | 1    | bBlueDefault  | byte | Default blue color component",
