      "comment": "Validates room handle and processes room state transition if conditions are met.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate room handle parameter for null pointer\n2. If invalid (null), trigger assertion error with debug information  \n3. Exit program with error code -1 (fatal error path)\n4. Query room state using Ordinal_10057(nRoomHandle)\n5. Check if room state equals 8 (specific processing state)\n6. Verify global processing flag DAT_6fbf2270 is enabled\n7. If both conditions met, call FUN_6fae8e70 for room processing\n8. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\nnRoomHandle (int) - Handle or identifier for the room to validate and process\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value, function either processes room or exits on error\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- NULL room handle triggers program termination with assertion\n- Room state 8 appears to be a trigger condition for special processing\n- Global flag at 0x6fbf2270 acts as master enable for processing\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x343 (835 decimal) - Line number in source file for assertion\n0x8 - Room state constant indicating processing-ready status\n-1 (0xffffffff) - Fatal error exit code\n\nError Handling:\n- Invalid room handle: Assertion with debug info, program termination\n- Debug assertion includes source file path and line number\n- Non-recoverable error path using FUN_6fb9a10f exit function",
