      "comment": "Performs pathfinding with randomized retry logic for Diablo II target positioning.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize pathfind handle via FUN_6fb62880() and validate non-zero\n2. Clear PathfindInfo structure buffer (22 dwords = 88 bytes)\n3. Configure pathfind parameters (type=0x2003, enabled=1, flags=0x11f)\n4. Get base coordinates for target via Ordinal_10034(dwTargetId, &nBaseX)\n5. Begin retry loop (max 25 attempts, max 3 successful attempts)\n6. Calculate randomized target coordinates:\n   - X = nBaseX + random_offset (if nRandomRangeX != 0)\n   - Y = nBaseY + random_offset (if nRandomRangeY != 0)\n7. Store target coordinates in PathfindInfo structure\n8. Attempt pathfind via Ordinal_10118(dwTargetId, X, Y, 5)\n9. On pathfind failure (result == 0): execute pathfind command via FUN_6fb77720()\n10. On pathfind success (result != 0): decrement success counter\n11. Increment attempt counters and continue until 3 successes or 25 attempts\n\nParameters:\ndwTargetId (uint) - Target entity/object identifier for pathfinding\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value (fire-and-forget pathfind operation)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Early exit if FUN_6fb62880() returns NULL (pathfind system unavailable)\n- Early exit if retry count exceeds 24 (0x18)\n- Random coordinate calculation skipped if range values are zero\n- Loop terminates on 3 successful pathfind attempts or 25 total attempts\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x2003 (8195) - PathfindInfo type/mode identifier\n0x11f (287) - Pathfind flags/configuration value\n0x18 (24) - Maximum retry attempts\n0x3 (3) - Maximum successful pathfind attempts\n0x5 (5) - Pathfind operation type parameter\n\nStructure Layout:\nPathfindInfo (88 bytes):\nOffset  Size  Field Name      Type    Description\n+0x00   4     dwType         uint    Pathfind operation type (0x2003)\n+0x04   4     hTarget        uint    Target handle from pathfind system\n+0x08   4     field_0x8      uint    Reserved/padding\n+0x0C   4     field_0xC      uint    Reserved/padding\n+0x10   4     field_0x10     uint    Pathfind flags (0x11f)\n+0x14   4     field_0x14     uint    Target X coordinate\n+0x18   4     field_0x18     uint    Target Y coordinate\n+0x1C   4     field_0x1C     uint    Reserved/padding\n+0x20   4     field_0x20     uint    Reserved/padding\n+0x24   4     field_0x24     uint    Reserved/padding\n+0x28   4     field_0x28     uint    Reserved/padding\n+0x2C   4     field_0x2C     uint    Enable flag (1=enabled)\n...     ...   ...           ...     Additional reserved fields",
