      "comment": "Initializes special feature for unit if unit type is valid and conditions are met.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate unit ID is non-zero (early exit if NULL)\n2. Get unit type using Ordinal_10057 API call\n3. Check if unit type is in valid range (0x83 to 0x84 inclusive)\n4. If type invalid, clear special feature initialized flag and exit\n5. If type valid and feature not already initialized and feature is enabled:\n   a. Get target unit pointer from FUN_6fb62880\n   b. If valid pointer obtained, call FUN_6fae9840 to initialize feature\n   c. Set special feature initialized flag to true\n\nParameters:\nnUnitId (int): Unit identifier to initialize special feature for\n               Zero/NULL values are handled gracefully with early return\n\nReturns:\nvoid: No return value, function operates via side effects on global state\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Unit type outside 0x83-0x84 range clears initialization flag\n- Feature already initialized: no operation performed\n- Feature disabled globally: no operation performed\n- Failed to get target unit pointer: no operation performed\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x83 (131): Minimum valid unit type for special feature\n0x84 (132): Maximum valid unit type for special feature\n0x27f (639): Feature initialization parameter passed to FUN_6fae9840\n\nGlobal State:\ng_fSpecialFeatureInitialized (0x6fbf2280): Tracks if special feature is active\ng_fSpecialFeatureEnabled (0x6fbf227c): Controls if feature can be initialized",
