      "comment": "Display countdown message for remaining items or time limit.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get current counter value via Ordinal_10055()\n2. Validate that global limit (DAT_6fbf2278) is set and current value is below limit\n3. Retrieve data structure via FUN_6fb60e10() using global stored field value\n4. Verify data structure is valid (not null) and check structure field at offset +0xc\n5. Check if within valid range (current value >= limit - 0x46)\n6. Initialize Unicode string buffer (256 wide characters) using constructor\n7. Calculate remaining count (limit - current) and get resource string via Ordinal_10004()\n8. Format message into Unicode buffer using sprintf\n9. Display message through UI system using ordinal functions:\n   - Ordinal_10127() for UI preparation\n   - Ordinal_10121() for UI update  \n   - Ordinal_10117() with parameters (0x177, 9) for display\n   - Ordinal_10127() for UI cleanup\n\nParameters:\nNone (void function)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Early return if DAT_6fbf2278 is zero (limit not set)\n- Early return if current index >= limit (no remaining items)\n- Early return if data structure invalid or field at +0xc equals 0xc\n- Early return if current index < (limit - 0x46) (too far from limit)\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0xc - Structure field offset for validation check\n0x46 (70) - Minimum proximity threshold to display countdown\n0x100 (256) - Unicode buffer size in wide characters  \n0x177 (375) - UI display parameter for Ordinal_10117\n0x9 (9) - UI display parameter for Ordinal_10117",
