      "comment": "Validates that a skill ID falls within the item skill range.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if nSkillId >= SKILL_ITEM_START (0xd9 / 217)\n2. If below minimum, assert \"nSkillId >= SKILL_ITEM_START\" and exit\n3. Check if (nSkillId - SKILL_ITEM_START) < NUM_ITEM_SKILLS (4)\n4. If above maximum, assert \"nSkillId - SKILL_ITEM_START < NUM_ITEM_SKILLS\" and exit\n5. Return successfully if skill ID is valid\n\nParameters:\n  nUnused (ECX) - Unused parameter, always ignored\n  nSkillId (EDX) - Skill ID to validate, must be in range [217, 220]\n\nReturns:\n  void - Function returns normally only if assertion passes\n         Calls ExitApplicationWithCode(-1) on assertion failure\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Valid item skill IDs: 217 (0xd9) through 220 (0xdc) inclusive\n  - SKILL_ITEM_START = 217 (0xd9)\n  - NUM_ITEM_SKILLS = 4\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0xd9 (217) - SKILL_ITEM_START constant\n  0x04 - NUM_ITEM_SKILLS constant\n  0x20 (32) - Line number for lower bound assertion\n  0x21 (33) - Line number for upper bound assertion\n  0xffffffff (-1) - Exit code for assertion failure\n\nSource File: C:\\Projects\\Diablo2\\Source\\D2Client\\SKILLS\\SkillItem.cpp",
