      "instructions": ["0x19450|SUB|ESP, 0x8", "0x19453|PUSH|EBP", "0x19454|PUSH|ESI", "0x19455|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0x19457|PUSH|EDI", "0x19458|TEST|ESI, ESI", "0x1945A|MOV|EDI, EDX", "0x1945C|JZ|0x6fae95ce", "0x19462|PUSH|EDI", "0x19463|CALL|0x6fb98398", "0x19468|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0x1946A|JNZ|0x6fae948a", "0x1946C|PUSH|0xac", "0x19471|PUSH|0x6fbb120c", "0x19476|PUSH|0x6fbb128c"],
      "comment": "Processes skill effects by looking up and executing handlers from the skill effect table.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate pCaster is not null, return if invalid\n2. Retrieve skill data pointer using Ordinal_10594 with nSkillId\n3. Validate skill data exists, abort with assertion if null\n4. Validate skill effect data exists at offset 0x6c, abort with assertion if null\n5. Search skill effect table (DAT_6fba6480) for matching nSkillId\n6. Iterate through 28-byte table entries using pointer arithmetic (piVar2 += 7)\n7. Return if skill not found in table (reached end address 0x6fba69bf)\n8. Calculate table offset as nTableIndex * 0x1c (28 bytes per entry)\n9. Store backup source unit value using FUN_6fb63760\n10. Save original skill parameters using Ordinal_10175 and Ordinal_10176\n11. Apply skill parameters: if nSourceUnit == 0 use Ordinal_10170, else Ordinal_10344\n12. Execute condition check function pointer if present, skip effects if returns 0\n13. Execute action handler function pointer if present\n14. Process sound effect 1 using FUN_6fb8d210 if ID != 0\n15. Process sound effect 2 using FUN_6fb8d210 if ID != 0\n16. Process missile effect using FUN_6fb931f0 if ID != -1 (0xFFFFFFFF)\n17. Process skill effect using FUN_6fae9840 if ID != 0xFFFF\n18. Restore original skill parameters: if backup == 0 use Ordinal_10170, else Ordinal_10344\n\nParameters:\npCaster - UnitAny pointer to the unit casting the skill\nnSkillId - Integer skill identifier to look up in effect table\ndwSkillLevel - Skill level or additional parameter passed to effect handlers\nnSourceUnit - Source unit identifier, 0 uses parameter restoration\ndwParam1 - First skill parameter for effect processing\ndwParam2 - Second skill parameter for effect processing\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value, function performs side effects through skill system\n\nSpecial Cases:\nSkill data validation failures trigger assertions with error codes 0xAC and 0xAD\nFunction aborts execution via FUN_6fb9a10f(0xffffffff) on validation failure\nTable search boundary check prevents buffer overflow at 0x6fba69bf\nCondition function can skip all effect processing by returning 0\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x6c - Offset to skill effect data pointer in skill data structure\n0x1c (28) - Size of each SkillEffectEntry in the effect table\n0x6fba6480 - Base address of skill effect lookup table\n0x6fba69bf - End boundary address for table iteration safety\n0xAC - Error code for missing skill data assertion\n0xAD - Error code for missing skill effect data assertion\n0xFFFFFFFF - Invalid/disabled missile effect indicator\n0xFFFF - Invalid/disabled skill effect indicator\n\nStructure Layout:\nSkillEffectEntry (28 bytes):\nOffset | Size | Field Name        | Type  | Description\n0x00   | 4    | dwSkillId         | uint  | Skill identifier for lookup\n0x04   | 4    | pfnSoundEffect1   | void* | Sound effect 1 function pointer  \n0x08   | 4    | pfnSoundEffect2   | void* | Sound effect 2 function pointer\n0x0C   | 4    | nMissileId        | int   | Missile effect ID (-1 = disabled)\n0x10   | 4    | pfnConditionCheck | void* | Condition validation function\n0x14   | 2    | wSkillEffectId    | ushort| Skill effect ID (0xFFFF = disabled)\n0x16   | 2    | wPadding          | ushort| Structure alignment padding\n0x18   | 4    | pfnActionHandler  | void* | Main action function pointer",
      "tags": ["MOD_SKILLS", "PARAM_6", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "UI_SKILLS", "SRC_SkillItem.cpp", "STRUCT_Other", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
