      "api_count": 7,
      "api_calls": ["UNITS_GetOwnerGuid", "UNITS_GetUnitY", "GetPathPosX", "GetPathPosY", "UNITS_GetUnitDirection", "UNITS_GetOwnerGuid", "UNITS_GetUnitY"],
      "instructions": ["0x196A0|SUB|ESP, 0x40", "0x196A3|PUSH|EBX", "0x196A4|PUSH|EBP", "0x196A5|PUSH|ESI", "0x196A6|PUSH|EDI", "0x196A7|MOV|EBX, EDX", "0x196A9|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0x196AB|CALL|0x6fb63760", "0x196B0|MOV|EDI, EAX", "0x196B2|XOR|EBP, EBP", "0x196B4|CMP|EDI, EBP", "0x196B6|JZ|0x6fae96ce", "0x196B8|PUSH|EDI", "0x196B9|CALL|0x6fb98122", "0x196BE|MOV|dword ptr [EBX], EAX"],
      "comment": "Calculates the absolute X and Y coordinates for a game unit\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call FUN_6fb63760(pUnit) to check if unit has associated path/movement data\n2. If path data exists (return value != 0):\n   - Call Ordinal_10326(pathData) to get X coordinate from path\n   - Call Ordinal_10329(pathData) to get Y coordinate from path  \n   - Store results in output parameters pX and pY\n3. If path data is null (return value == 0):\n   - Read unit data from pUnit->field_0x38\n   - Call Ordinal_10175(unitData) to get X coordinate from unit\n   - Call Ordinal_10176(unitData) to get Y coordinate from unit\n   - Store results in output parameters pX and pY\n4. If both coordinates are non-zero, return 1 (success)\n5. If either coordinate is zero, perform fallback calculation:\n   - Call Ordinal_10457(pUnit) to get unit direction/facing value\n   - Extract direction index by masking with 0xFF and shifting right by 3\n   - Initialize direction offset lookup table with predefined coordinate deltas\n   - Call Ordinal_10326(pUnit) to get base X coordinate\n   - Call Ordinal_10329(pUnit) to get base Y coordinate\n   - Add directional X offset from table[directionIndex] to base X\n   - Add directional Y offset from table[directionIndex + 8] to base Y\n   - Store final coordinates in output parameters\n6. Return 1 (success)\n\nParameters:\npUnit - Pointer to UnitAny structure containing unit position data\npX - Output pointer to store calculated X coordinate\npY - Output pointer to store calculated Y coordinate\n\nReturns:\nAlways returns 1 (success/true) indicating coordinates were calculated\n\nSpecial Cases:\nIf primary coordinate lookup fails (coordinates are zero), function falls back to\ndirectional calculation using unit facing and predefined offset table\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x38 - Offset to unit data field in UnitAny structure\n0xFF - Mask for direction value extraction  \n0x3 - Right shift count to extract direction index (divides by 8)\n8 - Y offset table starts at index 8 in direction lookup table\n\nDirection Offset Table Layout:\nIndex 0-7: X coordinate offsets for 8 directions\nIndex 8-15: Y coordinate offsets for 8 directions\nValues: 0, -1, -2, -1, 0, 1, 2, 1 (X offsets)\n        0, -1, 0, 1, 2, 1, 0, 1 (Y offsets)",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Path", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PARAM_3", "STRUCT_Skill", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
