      "comment": "Scales a 2D vector to ensure minimum magnitude by applying progressive scaling factors.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate initial magnitude squared: X² + Y²\n2. If magnitude squared < 4, scale both components by 4x and recalculate magnitude squared  \n3. If magnitude squared < 16, scale both components by 2x\n4. Return modified values through pointer parameters\n\nParameters:\npnX (int *): Pointer to X coordinate component, modified in-place\npnY (int *): Pointer to Y coordinate component, modified in-place\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Results returned through modified pointer parameters\n\nSpecial Cases:\nVector (0,0) becomes (0,0) - no scaling applied for zero vector\nVector (1,0) becomes (8,0) after 4x then 2x scaling\nVector (1,1) becomes (4,4) after 4x scaling only (magnitude² = 2→32≥16)\nVector (2,2) becomes (4,4) after 2x scaling only (magnitude² = 8→32≥16)\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x4 (4): Minimum threshold for first scaling pass\n0x10 (16): Minimum threshold for second scaling pass  \n4: Scaling factor for initial magnitude boost\n2: Scaling factor for final magnitude adjustment",
      "tags": ["PARAM_2", "PROP_LEAF"]
    },
