      "comment": "Scales a 2D vector by repeatedly halving until magnitude squared is within threshold.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load Y coordinate value from second parameter\n2. Load and negate X coordinate value from first parameter \n3. Calculate initial magnitude squared: nXValue² + nYValue²\n4. While magnitude squared exceeds threshold (3):\n   a. Divide Y value by 2 using arithmetic shift\n   b. Divide X value by 2 using arithmetic shift\n   c. Recalculate magnitude squared with new values\n5. Store final X value back to first parameter location\n6. Store final Y value back to second parameter location\n\nParameters:\npnXCoordinate - Pointer to X coordinate value (modified in place)\npnYCoordinate - Pointer to Y coordinate value (modified in place)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Coordinates are modified in place through pointer parameters\n\nSpecial Cases:\nInitial coordinates are scaled down by powers of 2 until the sum of their\nsquares is 3 or less. X coordinate is negated before scaling calculations.\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x3 (3) - Magnitude squared threshold for scaling termination",
