      "comment": "Calculate target coordinates for missile creation with fallback direction offset table\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if missile has a memory pool handle via FUN_6fb63760\n2. If memory pool exists, get coordinates from pool via Ordinal_10326/10329\n3. If no memory pool, use missile pMemPool field and call Ordinal_10175/10176\n4. If either coordinate is zero, calculate fallback coordinates using direction table\n5. Get direction index from missile via Ordinal_10457, mask to 0xFF and shift right 3 bits\n6. Use direction index to look up X/Y offsets from static coordinate offset table\n7. Add offsets to base coordinates from Ordinal_10326/10329\n8. If coordinates are still zero after fallback, log error message via Ordinal_10018/10025\n9. If both coordinates remain zero, return NULL\n10. Otherwise, create missile via FUN_6fb77dd0 and return result\n\nParameters:\npMissile - Pointer to UnitAny structure representing the missile or source unit\ndwTargetX - Target X coordinate for error logging (missile ID or coordinate)\ndwTargetY - Target Y coordinate for error logging (missile ID or coordinate)\n\nReturns:\nPointer to created missile structure on success\nNULL (0x0) if target coordinates could not be calculated",
