      "comment": "Fires a missile with target coordinate validation and fallback calculation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if entity has active missile target using FUN_6fb63760\n2. If no active target, get coordinates from entity structure at offset 0x38\n   - Use Ordinal_10175/10176 to extract X/Y coordinates from entity data\n3. If active target exists, get coordinates directly using Ordinal_10326/10329\n4. If coordinates are zero/invalid, calculate fallback position using lookup table:\n   - Get entity direction flags using Ordinal_10457, mask to 0xFF and shift right 3 bits\n   - Use hardcoded 16-element lookup table with direction offset values\n   - Add lookup values to entity's current coordinates (Ordinal_10326/10329)\n5. If coordinates still invalid after fallback, log error and continue\n6. If both X and Y coordinates are zero, return failure (0)\n7. Validate distance to target using Ordinal_10398, must be <= 100 units\n8. If distance valid, call missile firing function FUN_6fb77d70 with all parameters\n9. Return missile firing result or 0 for failure\n\nParameters:\nnEntityId (int): Entity/unit identifier for missile source\ndwMissileId (uint): Missile type identifier for projectile to fire  \ndwFlags (uint): Additional missile behavior flags or parameters\n\nReturns:\nuint: Missile firing result (non-zero for success, 0 for failure)\n- 0: Invalid coordinates, excessive distance, or missile firing failed\n- Non-zero: Successful missile launch with target validation passed\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Zero coordinates trigger fallback calculation using direction-based lookup table\n- Distance validation prevents missiles from firing beyond 100 unit range\n- Error logged to debug output when coordinates remain invalid after fallback\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x38: Offset to coordinate data structure in entity\n0xFF: Mask for direction flags extraction  \n0x03: Bit shift count for direction calculation (divide by 8)\n100: Maximum allowed distance in game units for missile range\n0x7A: Error line number in source file for debug logging\n\nLookup Table Layout (16 elements):\nIndex  X_Offset  Y_Offset  Purpose\n0-7    Primary direction offsets for entity facing\n8-15   Secondary Y direction offsets  \nValues: 0, -1, -2, 1, 2 represent coordinate adjustments\n\nNote: Function uses 17 phantom variables optimized away by decompiler for stack-based lookup table storage.",
