      "comment": "Validates game entity state and checks availability in equipment slots.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if entity is active by testing *pEntity != 0, return 1 if inactive\n2. Retrieve entity handle using Ordinal_10434(pEntity, 0)\n3. Return 1 if entity handle is null (validation failed)\n4. Check entity validation state using Ordinal_10781(entityHandle)\n5. If entity requires validation, clear validation flag and get entity ID\n6. If validation fails and entity has flag 0x9d set, return 1 (blocked)\n7. Access entity property at offset 0x84 (132 decimal) for slot information\n8. Check slot 4 availability using Ordinal_10257(slotData, 4)\n9. If slot 4 available and passes validation checks, verify slot compatibility\n10. Test slot using Ordinal_10767, Ordinal_10759, or flag 0x7d check\n11. If slot 4 validation succeeds, return Ordinal_10834 result\n12. Check slot 5 availability using Ordinal_10257(slotData, 5)\n13. If slot 5 unavailable or validation fails, return 0\n14. Perform same compatibility checks for slot 5\n15. Return Ordinal_10834 result for slot 5 or 0 if all validations fail\n\nParameters:\npEntity (GameInterface*): Pointer to game interface structure with slot data at offset 0x84\n\nReturns:\ndword: Entity validation result\n  - 0: Validation failed, entity not usable\n  - 1: Basic validation passed, entity blocked by flags\n  - Other: Entity ID from successful slot validation (Ordinal_10834 result)\n\nSpecial Cases:\nEntity structure must have valid slot data at offset 0x84 (132 bytes from base)\nValidation flag 0x9d indicates entity is temporarily blocked\nSlot compatibility flag 0x7d used for final slot verification checks\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x84 (132): Offset to slot data structure within entity\n0x9d (157): Entity blocking flag for temporary restrictions  \n0x7d (125): Slot compatibility verification flag\n4: Equipment slot 4 identifier\n5: Equipment slot 5 identifier",
