      "comment": "Initializes lighting effects for audio sources based on effect configuration data.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Retrieve effect configuration data using Ordinal_10589 with effect type\n2. Check lighting enable flag at offset +0x10 in configuration\n3. If lighting enabled:\n   a. Create audio context with lighting parameters from config (+0x12, +0x13, +0x14)\n   b. Set light radius from configuration byte at +0x10\n   c. Add context to global list using Ordinal_10958\n   d. Clean up previous context if it existed\n\nParameters:\npAudioSource - Pointer to audio source data structure for effect attachment\nnEffectType - Effect type identifier passed to configuration lookup\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value, operates through side effects\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If lighting flag (offset +0x10) is 0, function returns early without creating effects\n- If context addition fails (Ordinal_10958 returns NULL), no cleanup performed\n- Configuration data structure accessed at fixed offsets +0x10 to +0x14\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x10 - Offset to lighting enable flag (byte)\n0x12 - Offset to lighting parameter 1 (byte) \n0x13 - Offset to lighting parameter 2 (byte)\n0x14 - Offset to lighting parameter 3 (byte)\n0xff - Alpha/opacity value passed to CreateAudioContext\n0x1 - Fixed parameters passed to CreateAudioContext (possibly flags)",
