      "api_calls": ["ValidateUnitEntity", "GetRangedAttackMissileType", "UNITS_GetOwnerGuid", "UNITS_GetUnitY", "GetPathPosX", "GetPathPosY", "UNITS_GetUnitDirection", "UNITS_GetOwnerGuid", "UNITS_GetUnitY", "FormatStringVarArgs", "...+1 more"],
      "instructions": ["0x19C80|SUB|ESP, 0x78", "0x19C83|PUSH|EBX", "0x19C84|MOV|EBX, ECX", "0x19C86|PUSH|EBP", "0x19C87|PUSH|ESI", "0x19C88|MOV|ESI, dword ptr [EBX + 0xe8]", "0x19C8E|PUSH|EDI", "0x19C8F|OR|ESI, 0x40", "0x19C92|PUSH|EBX", "0x19C93|MOV|dword ptr [EBX + 0xe8], ESI", "0x19C99|CALL|0x6fb983e6", "0x19C9E|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0x19CA0|MOV|ECX, EBX", "0x19CA2|JZ|0x6fae9dd5", "0x19CA8|CALL|0x6fae9ac0"],
      "comment": "Fires a ranged attack missile from the specified unit toward a target position.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Set unit state flag 0x40 at offset 0xE8 (ranged attack in progress)\n2. Validate unit entity - if invalid, get mercenary position and exit via NoOperation\n3. Validate entity state - exit if state validation fails\n4. Get ranged attack missile type - exit if type is 0xFFFF (no missile)\n5. Attempt to get target from mercenary position (GetMercenaryPosition)\n6. If no mercenary target, get target from unit's path (GetPathPosX/Y at offset 0x38)\n7. If target coordinates are zero, calculate fallback using direction lookup:\n   - Get unit direction via Ordinal_10457, extract direction index (bits 3-7)\n   - Use direction offset table: X offsets [0,-1,-2,-1,0,1,2,1], Y offsets [2,1,0,-1,-2,-1,0,1]\n   - Add direction offset to unit's current position (Ordinal_10326/10329)\n8. If target still zero, log warning \"Missile %d fired with zero target\"\n9. If valid target, call CreateProjectileFromUnit with missile type and coordinates\n\nParameters:\n  pGameInterface (ECX) - GameInterface* pointer containing unit data and state\n\nReturns:\n  void - Creates projectile as side effect\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Invalid unit: Calls GetMercenaryPosition then NoOperation (cleanup path)\n- No missile type (0xFFFF): Early exit without firing\n- Zero target: Logs warning but still attempts to fire if direction fallback produces valid coords\n\nDirection Offset Table (8 directions, indexed by direction >> 3):\n  Index  X-Offset  Y-Offset  Direction\n  0      0         2         South\n  1      -1        1         Southeast\n  2      -2        0         East\n  3      -1        -1        Northeast\n  4      0         -2        North\n  5      1         -1        Northwest\n  6      2         0         West\n  7      1         1         Southwest\n\nOrdinal Functions:\n- Ordinal_10326: D2Common.GetUnitX - Get unit X coordinate\n- Ordinal_10329: D2Common.GetUnitY - Get unit Y coordinate\n- Ordinal_10457: D2Common.GetUnitDirection - Get unit facing direction (0-255)",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PROP_NOCALLER", "STRUCT_Room2", "STRUCT_ItemData", "PARAM_1", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "TBL_skills", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData", "STRUCT_StatList", "STRUCT_Path", "UI_SKILLS", "STRUCT_Skill", "SRC_Skills.cpp"]
    },
