      "comment": "Processes skill effect execution through dispatch tables and handles audio context cleanup.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Retrieve context handle for the skill from the skill context using Ordinal_10323\n2. If context handle is null, exit early (no skill to process)\n3. Get skill effect ID from context handle using Ordinal_10963\n4. Retrieve skill data parameters using Ordinal_10968 with context, handle, and flag=1\n5. If skill effect ID < 6 (low-priority effects):\n   a. Check if handler exists in PTR_LAB_6fba69c4 dispatch table at [ID*2]\n   b. If no handler, set flag 0x40 at context+0xe8 (mark as unhandled)\n   c. If handler exists, call the handler function\n   d. Retrieve audio context using Ordinal_10958 with context and flag=0\n   e. If audio context exists, remove it from the audio context list and return\n6. If skill effect ID >= 6 (high-priority effects requiring range lookup):\n   a. Initialize table index to 0 and pointer to DAT_6fba69f0 range table\n   b. Loop through range table entries until finding ID within range [base, base+count]\n   c. Each entry is 8 bytes: [base_value, count_value]\n   d. If ID exceeds current range, advance to next entry (pointer += 8, index++)\n   e. If pointer exceeds 0x6fba6a3f (table end), exit function\n   f. Retrieve function pointer from 0x6fbb129c table at [index*8]\n   g. If function pointer is null, call error handler and terminate\n   h. Call the skill handler function with skill data parameter\n\nParameters:\nnSkillContext (int): Skill context structure containing effect parameters and state\n\nReturns:\nvoid: No return value - function performs side effects on skill and audio systems\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Early exit if no valid context handle retrieved from skill context\n- Low-priority effects (ID < 6) use direct dispatch table PTR_LAB_6fba69c4\n- High-priority effects (ID >= 6) require range table lookup in DAT_6fba69f0\n- Audio context cleanup only occurs for low-priority effects with valid audio contexts\n- Error handling for null function pointers calls debugging functions and terminates\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x6: Threshold separating low-priority from high-priority skill effects\n0xe8: Offset in skill context for unhandled effect flags  \n0x40: Flag bit marking unhandled skill effects\n0x6fba69c4: Base address of low-priority effect handler dispatch table\n0x6fba69f0: Base address of high-priority effect range lookup table  \n0x6fba6a3f: End boundary of range lookup table\n0x6fbb129c: Base address of high-priority effect handler dispatch table\n0x21c: Error code for null function pointer assertion",
