      "comment": "Validates and processes skill activation with target validation\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call validation function (Ordinal_10462) on unit\n2. Check if validation passed and unit state is not 1 (inactive)\n3. If valid, call skill preparation function (FUN_6faea800)\n4. Retrieve target unit using skill parameters at offsets +8 and +12\n5. If target found, execute skill sequence:\n   - Set unit state via Ordinal_10344\n   - Reset unit flags via FUN_6fb632e0  \n   - Execute skill with all parameters via FUN_6faea200\n6. If no target found, handle error:\n   - Log error code 7 via FUN_6fb863a0\n   - Output error message via Ordinal_11100\n\nParameters:\npUnit - Pointer to unit/player structure performing the skill\npSkillParams - Pointer to SkillParams structure containing skill data\n  IMPLICIT ECX: pUnit (fastcall convention)\n  IMPLICIT EDX: pSkillParams (fastcall convention)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value, function handles success/failure internally\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Unit state 1 (inactive) skips skill preparation\n- Missing target triggers error logging and diagnostic output\n- Error code 7 indicates invalid skill target\n\nStructure Layout:\nSkillParams (20 bytes):\nOffset Size Field Name    Type Description\n+0x00  4    dwSkillId     uint Primary skill identifier\n+0x04  4    dwParam1      uint First skill parameter  \n+0x08  4    dwParam2      uint Target resolution parameter 1\n+0x0C  4    dwParam3      uint Target resolution parameter 2\n+0x10  4    dwTargetParam uint Target-specific parameter\n\nError Handling:\n- FUN_6fb863a0(7, pUnit, NULL, 0) logs error condition\n- Ordinal_11100 outputs diagnostic info with file/line reference\n- Error message: \"StartsStartSkillID - Invalid Target\"",
