      "comment": "Executes a player skill action with target coordinates and animation handling.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate skill data exists via Ordinal_10594(nSkillId), abort on null\n2. Check if skill has animation data at offset 0x68 in skill structure\n3. If animation exists, determine player position from inventory or coordinates\n4. Calculate movement deltas using direction table for skill positioning\n5. Switch on skill animation type (1=0x04, 2=0x1C09, 3=0x180, 4=0x804, 5=0x805)\n6. Execute skill animation via Ordinal_11026() with calculated position\n7. Validate player inventory context and skill compatibility checks\n8. Handle skill level management - create new skill or validate existing\n9. Process skill coordinates via Ordinal_10955() for targeting validation\n10. Apply skill effects based on player state (current vs other players)\n11. Check skill interrupt conditions via player data validation\n12. Determine final player state based on skill requirements and player class\n13. Route to appropriate skill handler function via dispatch table lookup\n14. Update player state via FUN_6fb86790() with calculated state value\n\nParameters:\npPlayer    - Pointer to player unit structure containing state and inventory\nnSkillId   - Skill identifier for lookup in skill data tables\nnTargetX   - Target X coordinate for skill execution positioning  \nnTargetY   - Target Y coordinate for skill execution positioning\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Function performs side effects on player state and game world\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Skill ID 0xB5 requires player state == 1 for execution\n- Skills 0x29, 0xE6, 0x10A bypass normal state validation \n- Skill levels > 20 split into base (20) + bonus components\n- Player class affects state calculation (Necromancer=8, other=7)\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x04   - Basic skill animation flag\n0x1C09 - Complex skill animation with extended timing  \n0x180  - Medium duration skill animation\n0x804  - Combat skill animation type 4\n0x805  - Combat skill animation type 5\n0x14   - Maximum base skill level (20 decimal)\n0x68   - Skill data animation flag offset\n0x74   - Skill data validation flag offset\n0x85   - Skill data interrupt flag offset\n0xE9   - Skill data state change flag offset\n0x198  - Player class identifier offset\n0x21   - Player coordinate field offset (0x84 bytes)\n\nStructure Layout:\nSkill Data Structure (via Ordinal_10594):\nOffset | Size | Field Name        | Type  | Description\n0x68   | 1    | animationType     | byte  | Skill animation mode (1-5)\n0x74   | 4    | validationFlags   | int   | Skill validation requirements  \n0x85   | 1    | interruptFlag     | byte  | Can skill be interrupted\n0xE9   | 1    | stateChangeFlag   | byte  | Does skill change player state\n\nPlayer Unit Structure:\nOffset | Size | Field Name     | Type    | Description\n0x00   | 4    | playerState    | uint    | Current player state value\n0x38   | 4    | coordinates    | uint    | Player position data\n0x84   | 4    | targetCoords   | uint    | Target coordinate storage\n\nDirection Delta Table (anDirectionDeltas):\nIndex | X Delta | Y Delta | Purpose\n0-7   | -1,0,+1 | -1,0,+1 | 8-direction movement for skill positioning  \n8-15  | -1,0,+1 | -1,0,+1 | Secondary offset table for animation timing",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "STRUCT_Room2", "STRUCT_Room1", "STRUCT_ItemData", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "TBL_skills", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData", "PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Path", "UI_SKILLS", "PARAM_4", "STRUCT_Other", "SRC_Skills.cpp"]
