      "comment": "Process skill effect at specified coordinates with unit validation and multiple rendering passes.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract left coordinate (pCoordinateRect[2]) and top coordinate (pCoordinateRect[3]) from coordinate rect\n2. Validate unit state using Ordinal_10462 to check if unit can process effects\n3. If validation succeeds, call FUN_6faea800 for preliminary effect setup\n4. Execute primary effect rendering using Ordinal_10170 with unit offset 0x38 and coordinates\n5. Apply secondary effect processing using Ordinal_10413 with unit and coordinates\n6. Reset unit effect state using Ordinal_10344 with zero flag\n7. Perform final effect rendering using FUN_6faea200 with complete coordinate rect data\n\nParameters:\nnUnitHandle (int): Handle to unit object (game entity receiving effect)\npCoordinateRect (int *): Pointer to 5-element coordinate rectangle structure\n  [0] - Base X coordinate\n  [1] - Base Y coordinate  \n  [2] - Left boundary (extracted as nRectLeft)\n  [3] - Top boundary (extracted as nRectTop)\n  [4] - Additional coordinate parameter passed to final render\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value (effect processing is fire-and-forget)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If Ordinal_10462 validation returns 0, skips preliminary effect setup (FUN_6faea800)\n- Unit offset 0x38 contains effect context handle passed to primary renderer\n- Final renderer receives complete coordinate set including base coords and boundaries\n\nStructure Layout:\nCoordinateRect (20 bytes):\nOffset | Size | Field Name    | Type | Description\n   0   |  4   | nBaseX        | int  | Base X coordinate\n   4   |  4   | nBaseY        | int  | Base Y coordinate  \n   8   |  4   | nLeftBound    | int  | Left boundary coordinate\n  12   |  4   | nTopBound     | int  | Top boundary coordinate\n  16   |  4   | nExtraParam   | int  | Additional parameter for final render",
