      "comment": "Initializes a game object configuration structure with object metadata and optional data copying.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize object configuration array (adwObjectConfig) with 22 dwords set to zero\n2. Set first element (offset 0) to 3 (base configuration type)\n3. Retrieve and store ordinal data result #1 from object reference (Ordinal_10326)\n4. Retrieve and store ordinal data result #2 from object reference (Ordinal_10329)\n5. Store object ID in configuration array at offset 1\n6. Store additional data parameter in configuration\n7. Store class type parameter in configuration\n8. If control flags parameter (dwControlFlags) is non-zero: set flag bit 0x4 in configuration and store flags value in local storage\n9. Check mode selector parameter (dwModeSelector): if equals 0xffff, skip array copy; otherwise proceed to copy\n10. If not 0xffff: copy all 22 dwords from adwObjectConfig to adwConfigCopy, then store mode value in copied array\n11. Call FUN_6faea9e0 with initialized object configuration and optional copied array (NULL if mode was 0xffff)\n12. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\n- dwObjectId (ECX): Object identifier or reference value\n- dwDataRef (EDX): Reference to object data source for ordinal lookups\n- dwClassType (Stack+4): Game object class or type identifier\n- dwModeSelector (Stack+8): Configuration variant selector; 0xffff = skip array copy, else copy configuration\n- dwAdditionalData (Stack+C): Additional parameter data to store in configuration\n- dwControlFlags (Stack+10): Control/flag parameter; non-zero triggers flag bit 0x4 in config\n\nReturns:\n- void (no return value)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Magic Number 0x16 (22): Size of configuration arrays in dwords; loop counter for initialization and copy\n- Magic Number 0x3: Base configuration type value\n- Magic Number 0x4: Flag bit set in configuration when control flags non-zero\n- Magic Number 0xffff: Mode selector value that bypasses array copying\n- When dwModeSelector = 0xffff: Function passes NULL pointer to FUN_6faea9e0 instead of array copy\n- When dwModeSelector != 0xffff: Function passes pointer to copied array for further processing",
