      "comment": "Initializes two target structures with precomputed sine/cosine wave data.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate local stack array (adSineWaveTable[128]) with 512 bytes\n2. Initialize array with precomputed sine/cosine wave values (indices 0-127)\n3. Test if pTarget2 is NULL (EDI == 0)\n4. If pTarget2 is NULL:\n   a. Loop nIndex from 0 to 0x100 by 4 (64 iterations)\n   b. Load sine from adSineWaveTable[nIndex]\n   c. Load cosine from adSineWaveTable[nIndex + 0x100]\n   d. Store to pTarget1[7] and pTarget1[8]\n   e. Check pTarget1[4] == 0xb0\n   f. If match, XOR pTarget1[0] with 0x4000\n   g. Call FUN_6fb77720(pTarget1)\n5. If pTarget2 is not NULL:\n   a. Loop nIndex from 0 to 0x100 by 4 (64 iterations)\n   b. Call Ordinal_10918() for target selection\n   c. Distribute sine/cosine to pTarget1 or pTarget2 based on result\n   d. Call FUN_6fb77720(pCurrentTarget)\n\nParameters:\npTarget1 - Primary target structure (ECX); contains fields at [0]=flags, [4]=type, [7]=sine, [8]=cosine\npTarget2 - Optional secondary target (EDX); if NULL, only pTarget1 is processed\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Modifies pTarget1 and/or pTarget2 in place through FUN_6fb77720 calls\n\nSpecial Cases:\nType indicator 0xb0 at [4] triggers XOR of pTarget1[0] with 0x4000 bit\nCosine values use offset +0x100 relative to sine (second half of table)\nLoop processes 128 uint values (0x100 bytes) across sine/cosine pairs\nNULL pTarget2 forces single-target processing path\nNote: Function uses assembly-only temporary variables optimized away during decompilation\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset | Size | Field Name | Type | Description\n0      | 4    | flags      | uint | Bit flags; 0x4000 toggled if [4]==0xb0\n4      | 4    | type       | uint | Type indicator; 0xb0 triggers flag XOR\n7      | 4    | sineValue  | uint | Precomputed sine wave value\n8      | 4    | cosineValue| uint | Precomputed cosine wave value",
