      "instructions": ["0x1AF60|PUSH|EBX", "0x1AF61|PUSH|EBP", "0x1AF62|PUSH|ESI", "0x1AF63|MOV|ESI, EDX", "0x1AF65|LEA|EBP, [ECX + -0x1]", "0x1AF68|MOV|EAX, 0x66666667", "0x1AF6D|IMUL|EBP", "0x1AF6F|SAR|EDX, 0x1", "0x1AF71|MOV|EAX, EDX", "0x1AF73|PUSH|EDI", "0x1AF74|SHR|EAX, 0x1f", "0x1AF77|ADD|EDX, EAX", "0x1AF79|CMP|EDX, 0x7", "0x1AF7C|JLE|0x6faeaf9c", "0x1AF7E|PUSH|0x3d4"],
      "comment": "Applies DCT (Discrete Cosine Transform) rotation matrices to coefficient array.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate coefficient count by dividing (param - 1) by 5; if quotient > 7, error/abort\n2. Initialize output array indices [7] and [8] with base values DAT_6fba6ab4 and DAT_6fba6ad4\n3. Call FUN_6fb77720 to process initial configuration\n4. Outer loop: iterate through rotation index (0 to 0x1b step 4, max 8 rotations)\n   5. Inner loop: for each rotation, apply cosine transform with column stride\n      - Loop through column index (0 to 0x10 step 4, max 4 columns)\n      - Decrement coefficient counter by 2 each iteration\n      - If coefficient counter < 1, break inner loop\n      - Multiply rotation matrix values by column vector (standard DCT step 1)\n      - Apply rotation: pdwCoefficientArray[7] = DAT_6fba6a60[index] * DAT_6fba6a40[col]\n      - Apply rotation: pdwCoefficientArray[8] = DAT_6fba6a7c[index] * DAT_6fba6a50[col]\n      - Call FUN_6fb77720 to output transformed values\n      - Apply inverse rotation (orthogonal complement)\n      - pdwCoefficientArray[7] = DAT_6fba6a7c[index] * DAT_6fba6a40[col]\n      - pdwCoefficientArray[8] = DAT_6fba6a60[index] * DAT_6fba6a50[col]\n      - Call FUN_6fb77720 to output inverse transform\n   6. Post-rotation: apply diagonal scaling (diagonal elements only)\n      - pdwCoefficientArray[7] = DAT_6fba6a98[rotation_index]\n      - pdwCoefficientArray[8] = DAT_6fba6ab8[rotation_index]\n      - Call FUN_6fb77720 to finalize scaling\n   7. Move to next rotation matrix (index += 4)\n   8. Decrement coefficient counter\n   9. If rotation index >= 0x1b (28 bytes, 7 rotations completed), exit and return\n10. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\nnCoefficientCount: Coefficient count for validation (count-1 must satisfy (count-1)/5 <= 7)\npdwCoefficientArray: Array pointer; indices [7] and [8] used for output coefficients\n\nReturns:\nvoid (no return value)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If (nCoefficientCount - 1) / 5 > 7: Call error handler (Ordinal_10023) then abort (FUN_6fb9a10f)\n- If nCoefficientDecrement == 0 at outer loop start, return immediately\n- If nCoefficientDecrement < 1 during inner loop, break and proceed to post-rotation step\n- Maximum 8 rotation matrices applied (rotation_index limit 0x1b = 27 bytes / 4-byte stride)\n- Maximum 4 column transformations per rotation (column_index limit 0x10 = 16 bytes / 4-byte stride)\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x01: Coefficient count validation magic multiplier (actually uses 0x66666667 for division by 5)\n0x07: Maximum quotient threshold for (count-1)/5\n0x04: Stride for rotation index and column index iteration\n0x10: Column loop limit (16 bytes for 4 values at 4-byte stride)\n0x1c: Rotation index loop limit (28 bytes = 0x1c, = 7 rotations of 4 bytes each)\n\nData Table References:\nDAT_6fba6a40: Column cosine values (16 bytes = 4 values @ 4-byte stride)\nDAT_6fba6a50: Column sine values (16 bytes = 4 values @ 4-byte stride)\nDAT_6fba6a60: Rotation matrix row 1 cosine (28 bytes = 7 values @ 4-byte stride)\nDAT_6fba6a7c: Rotation matrix row 1 sine (28 bytes = 7 values @ 4-byte stride)\nDAT_6fba6a98: Diagonal scaling row 1 (28 bytes = 7 values @ 4-byte stride)\nDAT_6fba6ab4: Initial output[7] seed value\nDAT_6fba6ad4: Initial output[8] seed value\nDAT_6fba6ab8: Diagonal scaling row 2 (28 bytes = 7 values @ 4-byte stride)",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Inventory", "PARAM_2", "UI_SKILLS", "SRC_Skills.cpp", "TBL_skills"]
