      "comment": "Initializes configuration structure from entity parameters and processes it to populate output data structure.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize configuration array (5 dwords): [3, nEntityId, 0, 0, 0]\n2. Call Ordinal_10326() to get first ordinal value, store in dwOrdinal1\n3. Call Ordinal_10329() to get second ordinal value, store in dwOrdinal2\n4. Store nDataType parameter in dwDataType\n5. Validate stack pointer against 0x4c; if mismatch, log error and terminate with exit code -1\n6. Call InitializeDataStructureFromInput(adwConfig, adwOutput) to process configuration\n7. Call Ordinal_10402() for post-processing\n8. Return dwResult (status value from output array)\n\nParameters:\nnEntityId (dword, ECX): Entity or item ID to initialize; used as config[1]\nnDataType (dword, EDX): Data type identifier; typically hardcoded to 4 when called\n\nReturns:\ndwResult (dword, EAX): Status/result value retrieved from adwOutput array; used for error propagation\n\nSpecial Cases:\nStack validation failure (stack pointer != 0x4c): Logs s_ptTarget_6fbb13ec with g_szSourceFileName then terminates via FUN_6fb9a10f(-1)\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset  Size  Field Name        Type      Description\n----    ----  ----------        ----      -----------\n0x00    0x4   [3]               dword     Configuration type identifier (always 3)\n0x04    0x4   [1]               dword     Entity ID parameter\n0x08    0x4   [2]               dword     Reserved/padding\n0x0C    0x4   [3]               dword     Reserved/padding\n0x10    0x4   [4]               dword     Reserved/padding\n\nOutput Array Layout:\nOffset  Size  Field Name        Type      Description\n----    ----  ----------        ----      -----------\n0x00    0x4   [0]               dword     Processing flags\n0x04    0x4   [1]               dword     Entity reference\n0x08    0x4   [2]               dword     Data identifier\n0x0C    0x4   [3]               dword     Configuration data\n0x10    0x4   [4]               dword     Resource count or status\n0x14    0x4   [5]               dword     Return value (dwResult)",
