      "instructions": ["0x1B580|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [ECX + 0x50]", "0x1B583|PUSH|ESI", "0x1B584|MOV|ESI, 0x64", "0x1B589|SUB|ESI, EDX", "0x1B58B|SAR|EAX, 0x8", "0x1B58E|IMUL|ESI, EAX", "0x1B591|MOV|EAX, 0x51eb851f", "0x1B596|IMUL|ESI", "0x1B598|SAR|EDX, 0x5", "0x1B59B|MOV|EAX, EDX", "0x1B59D|POP|ESI", "0x1B59E|SHR|EAX, 0x1f", "0x1B5A1|ADD|EDX, EAX", "0x1B5A3|SHL|EDX, 0x8", "0x1B5A6|MOV|dword ptr [ECX + 0x50], EDX"],
      "comment": "Applies percentage-based damage/armor reduction to a unit.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load current value from pUnit->dwDamageClass at offset 0x50\n2. Extract effective value by right-shifting 8 bits (logical shift right)\n3. Calculate reduction: (100 - dwReductionPercent) * effectiveValue\n4. Divide by 100 using fast integer division via magic multiplier 0x51eb851f\n5. Apply sign extension correction via right shift 0x1f and addition (rounding adjustment)\n6. Restore to fixed-point format by shifting left 8 bits\n7. Write result back to pUnit->dwDamageClass\n\nThe fixed-point format stores actual damage/armor value in high byte (bits 8-31), \nenabling efficient scaling and percentage calculations while maintaining precision.\n\nParameters:\n- pUnit: Pointer to unit structure containing damage/armor class value at offset +0x50\n- dwReductionPercent: Percentage reduction (0-100, where 100 = no damage, 0 = full damage)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Modifies pUnit->dwDamageClass in place\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If dwReductionPercent = 0: Full damage (multiply by 1.0)\n- If dwReductionPercent = 100: No damage (multiply by 0.0)\n- Fixed-point format ensures value fits in dword after calculations\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x50: Offset to damage/armor class field within UnitAny structure\n- 0x100 (256): Fixed-point scaling factor (value in bits 8-31)\n- 0x51eb851f: Fast division constant (multiplied by 100, magnitude-normalized)\n- 0x8: Right shift in fixed-point multiplication (reciprocal scale)\n- 0x5: Additional shift for rounding correction\n- 0x1f: Sign extension mask for signed arithmetic",
