      "instructions": ["0x1B5B0|SUB|ESP, 0x4c", "0x1B5B3|PUSH|EBX", "0x1B5B4|PUSH|EBP", "0x1B5B5|PUSH|ESI", "0x1B5B6|PUSH|EDI", "0x1B5B7|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x18], EDX", "0x1B5BB|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0x1B5BD|CALL|0x6fb63760", "0x1B5C2|MOV|EDI, EAX", "0x1B5C4|XOR|EBX, EBX", "0x1B5C6|CMP|EDI, EBX", "0x1B5C8|JZ|0x6faeb5da", "0x1B5CA|PUSH|EDI", "0x1B5CB|CALL|0x6fb98122", "0x1B5D0|MOV|EBP, EAX"],
      "comment": "Calculate positional offsets for skill area effects based on entity orientation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Determine if entity is in town or wilderness by calling FUN_6fb63760 (returns 0 if town)\n2. If in town, fetch X/Y offsets using entity field +0xe with Ordinal_10175 and Ordinal_10176\n3. If in wilderness, fetch X/Y offsets with Ordinal_10326 and Ordinal_10329\n4. If fetched offsets are zero, calculate default offsets using lookup table:\n   a. Extract character class bits (0-2) from entity type using (Ordinal_10457 & 0xff) >> 3\n   b. Initialize anOffsetTable[16] with predefined offset values\n   c. Add table values to offsets: nXOffset += anOffsetTable[index], nYBase += anOffsetTable[index+8]\n5. Call Ordinal_10913 to initialize skill effect processing\n6. Iterate nIterations times calculating and validating positions:\n   a. Generate random offset: if nStride*2==0 use 0, else call Ordinal_10918\n   b. Calculate X position: (randomOffset - nStride) + nXOffset\n   c. Calculate Y position: (randomOffset - nStride) + nYBase\n   d. Validate position with Ordinal_10398; if result < 2, decrement counter, else apply effect\n   e. Apply skill effect at validated position using FUN_6fb77e50\n\nParameters:\n  pEntity: Pointer to entity structure containing position data and offsets at field +0xe\n  dwEffectType: Effect type constant (e.g., 0x184 for skill damage effects)\n  nIterations: Number of positions to calculate and process (skill area size)\n  nStride: Half-width offset for position randomization (calculated as nIterations/3)\n  nParam5: Parameter passed to effect function (skill level or damage amount)\n\nReturns:\n  void - Function applies skill effects to valid positions as side effect\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  Lookup table values 0xffffffff (-1) and 0xfffffffe (-2) handle edge positioning\n  If nStride*2==0, position uses base offset without randomization\n  Positions failing validation are counted but not processed with effect function\n  Uses Diablo II ordinal calling convention for entity and skill operations",
