      "comment": "Process unit ability assignment and error handling for a game entity.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load unit slot configuration: dwSlotType from pUnit[0], dwSlotFlags from pUnit[8]\n2. Call RegisterAbility (Ordinal_10470) with parameters: priority=0, type=6, duration=0x32 (50 ticks), slot_type=dwSlotType, flags=dwSlotFlags\n3. Test return value nAbilityHandle for success (non-zero)\n4. If error: Call NotifyAbilityError (Ordinal_10477) with nAbilityHandle and error callback FUN_6faeb760\n5. If error: Call AbilityApplyEffect (Ordinal_10475) with pUnit and nAbilityHandle for error processing\n6. Return void\n\nParameters:\npUnit (UnitAny *): Pointer to unit structure containing ability configuration at offsets 0 and 8\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Function performs side effects (error callbacks) but returns no status\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Success path (nAbilityHandle == 0): No error callbacks executed, function returns silently\n- Error path (nAbilityHandle != 0): Both error notification and effect application occur in sequence\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x32: Duration value (50 ticks) passed to ability registration\n0x6: Type parameter for ability registration (likely spell type discriminator)\n0: Priority parameter (lowest priority, may defer ability execution)\n\nStructure Layout (UnitAny):\nOffset | Size | Field Name | Type | Description\n0x0    | 4    | dwSlotType | uint | Ability slot type/category identifier\n0x8    | 4    | dwSlotFlags| uint | Ability configuration flags\n\nNote: Function uses __fastcall calling convention with unit pointer in ECX register.",
