      "comment": "Error callback handler that dispatches ability-specific error processing based on type code.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Retrieve ability handle from ability data using Ordinal_10323 (GetAbilityHandle)\n2. Validate ability handle is non-null before proceeding\n3. Check if ability has error flag 0x12 using Ordinal_10487 (CheckAbilityError)\n4. Early return if error flag 0x12 is set (error already handled)\n5. Retrieve ability flags from handle using Ordinal_10985 (GetAbilityFlags)\n6. Test if bit 1 (0x02) is set in flags, early return if set (processing disabled)\n7. Retrieve ability type code from handle using Ordinal_10963 (GetAbilityTypeCode)\n8. Normalize type code by subtracting 0x6b base value\n9. Range check normalized type: if > 0x2c (44 decimal), early return (invalid type)\n10. Use jump table at 0x6faeb7d0 to map type code to handler index\n11. Indirect jump through table at 0x6faeb7c0 using handler index\n12. Dispatch to ability-specific error handler based on type\n\nParameters:\npAbilityData (uint *): Pointer to ability data structure passed from ProcessUnitAbility error path\n\nIMPLICIT:\nECX: Contains pAbilityData on entry per __fastcall convention\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Function performs side effects through error handler dispatch, no return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Null handle (nAbilityHandle == 0): Early return without error processing\n- Error flag 0x12 set: Early return, error already processed by another handler\n- Flag bit 1 set (0x02): Early return, ability error processing disabled\n- Invalid type code (out of range): Early return without handler dispatch\n- Type code not in jump table: Falls through to return without action\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x12 (decimal 18): Error flag identifier for duplicate error check\n0x02 (bit 1): Ability flag controlling error processing enable/disable state\n0x6b (decimal 107): Base value subtracted from type code for table normalization\n0x2c (decimal 44): Maximum normalized type code index for jump table bounds check\n0x84 (decimal 132): Type code for FUN_6faee610 error handler (shared with 0x8f)\n0x8f (decimal 143): Type code for FUN_6faee610 error handler (shared with 0x84)\n0x97 (decimal 151): Type code for FUN_6faeef40 error handler\n0x6faeb7d0: Address of type-to-index mapping table (byte array)\n0x6faeb7c0: Address of indirect jump table (function pointer array)\n\nError Handling:\n- Invalid handle: Silent early return\n- Duplicate error (flag 0x12): Silent early return to prevent double processing\n- Processing disabled (bit 1): Silent early return per configuration\n- Out of bounds type: Silent early return, unrecognized ability type\n\nDispatched Error Handlers:\n- Type 0x6b: FUN_6faf4340(pAbilityData) - Specific ability type error handler\n- Type 0x84: FUN_6faee610(pAbilityData) - Shared error handler for types 0x84/0x8f\n- Type 0x8f: FUN_6faee610(pAbilityData) - Shared error handler for types 0x84/0x8f\n- Type 0x97: FUN_6faeef40(pAbilityData) - Specific ability type error handler\n\nJump Table Implementation:\nThe function uses a two-level dispatch mechanism for efficient type routing:\n1. Primary table at 0x6faeb7d0: Maps normalized type code (0-0x2c) to handler index (0-3)\n2. Secondary table at 0x6faeb7c0: Maps handler index to function pointer\nThis approach reduces code size compared to direct function pointer table with 44 entries\n\nAssembly Pattern:\nMOV CL, byte ptr [EAX + 0x6faeb7d0]  ; Load handler index from type table\nJMP dword ptr [ECX*0x4 + 0x6faeb7c0] ; Indirect jump through pointer table",
      "tags": ["PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_1"]
