      "comment": "Process active skills attached to a unit and apply delta operations based on filters.\n\nAlgorithm:\n\n1. Validate input parameters (pUnit != NULL, nDelta != NULL)\n2. Validate unit has skill list at offset +0xcc (pUnit->hSkillInfo != NULL)\n3. Get first skill from unit's skill list using Ordinal_10948\n4. Iterate through all skills in linked list:\n   a. Get next skill pointer for iteration\n   b. Get skill ID from current skill node\n   c. Get skill level for this unit\n   d. Get skill info structure from skill ID\n   e. If skill info is NULL, trigger assertion failure at line 0x5b2\n   f. Apply filter conditions:\n      - Check skill level > 0\n      - Check skill is usable (Ordinal_11040)\n      - Check unit type filter matches (dwUnitTypeFilter == 0 OR matches byte at +0x140)\n      - Check skill state filter (bySkillStateFilter == 4 OR matches byte at +0xd4 + 1)\n      - Check skill timer/cooldown == -1 (not on cooldown)\n   g. If all conditions pass:\n      - Apply delta operation with Ordinal_11031(pUnit, dwSkillId, nDelta)\n      - Get skill state with Ordinal_10949(-1)\n      - If skill state exists and skill level is now 0, remove skill with Ordinal_10951\n5. Refresh unit skills with Ordinal_10941 after iteration completes\n\nParameters:\n\npUnit - Pointer to UnitAny structure whose skills should be processed\nnDelta - Delta value to apply to matching skills (increment/decrement)\ndwUnitTypeFilter - Unit type filter (0 = all types, else must match +0x140 field)\nbySkillStateFilter - Skill state filter (4 = all states, else must match +0xd4 + 1)\n\nReturns:\n\nvoid - No return value, terminates via FUN_6fb9a10f if assertions fail\n\nSpecial Cases:\n\nAssertion failures trigger program termination via FUN_6fb9a10f(-1):\n- Line 0x5a7: pUnit is NULL (\"hUnit\" assertion)\n- Line 0x5a8: nDelta is NULL (\"nDelta != 0\" assertion)\n- Line 0x5aa: Unit skill list is NULL (\"hSkillInfo\" assertion)\n- Line 0x5b2: Skill info structure is NULL (\"ptSkill\" assertion)\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n\n0xcc (204 decimal) - Offset to skill list handle in UnitAny structure\n0xd4 (212 decimal) - Offset to skill state byte in skill info structure\n0x140 (320 decimal) - Offset to unit type byte in skill info structure\n0x4 - Special bySkillStateFilter value meaning \"match all skill states\"\n-1 (0xffffffff) - Timer value indicating skill is not on cooldown\n0x5a7 (1447 decimal) - Source line for \"hUnit\" assertion\n0x5a8 (1448 decimal) - Source line for \"nDelta != 0\" assertion\n0x5aa (1450 decimal) - Source line for \"hSkillInfo\" assertion\n0x5b2 (1458 decimal) - Source line for \"ptSkill\" assertion\n\nError Handling:\n\nAll validation failures use Ordinal_10023 to log assertion with source file name and line number, then terminate via FUN_6fb9a10f(-1). No graceful error recovery - function expects valid inputs.\n\nStructure Layout - UnitAny (partial):\n\nOffset | Size | Field Name  | Type | Description\n-------|------|-------------|------|----------------------------------\n+0xcc  |  4   | hSkillInfo  | int  | Handle/pointer to skill list\n\nStructure Layout - Skill Info (partial):\n\nOffset | Size | Field Name      | Type | Description\n-------|------|-----------------|------|--------------------------------\n+0xd4  |  1   | bySkillState    | byte | Skill state/type (filtered +1)\n+0x140 |  1   | byUnitType      | byte | Unit type filter value",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "UI_SKILLS", "STRUCT_Skill", "PARAM_4", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "SRC_Skills.cpp", "TBL_skills", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
