      "instructions": ["0x1B970|SUB|ESP, 0x48", "0x1B973|PUSH|EBP", "0x1B974|PUSH|ESI", "0x1B975|PUSH|EDI", "0x1B976|MOV|EDI, ECX", "0x1B978|PUSH|EDX", "0x1B979|CALL|0x6fb9836e", "0x1B97E|MOV|ESI, EAX", "0x1B980|PUSH|EDI", "0x1B981|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x10], ESI", "0x1B985|CALL|0x6fb98164", "0x1B98A|XOR|EBP, EBP", "0x1B98C|CMP|ESI, EBP", "0x1B98E|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x10], EAX", "0x1B992|JNZ|0x6faeb9b2"],
      "comment": "Validates whether a skill can be cast at the target position with line-of-sight check.\n\nAlgorithm:\n\n1. Retrieve skill parameters from skill ID (Ordinal_10589)\n2. Retrieve unit stats pointer (Ordinal_10342)\n3. If skill parameters are null, trigger fatal error (0x5e8)\n4. If unit stats are null, return false (invalid unit)\n5. Attempt to get path/waypoint data (FUN_6fb63760)\n6. Determine target coordinates:\n   a. If path data exists, extract X/Y from path (Ordinal_10326/10329)\n   b. If no path data, extract from unit's pMemPool field (offset 0x38)\n7. If target coordinates are (0,0), calculate position from unit facing:\n   a. Get unit direction (Ordinal_10457), mask to 0-31 range, divide by 8\n   b. Initialize 8-direction offset lookup table (X offsets in [0-7], Y offsets in [8-15])\n   c. Get unit's current position (Ordinal_10326/10329)\n   d. Add directional offset: X += table[direction], Y += table[direction+8]\n8. If both coordinates are non-zero, perform line-of-sight check:\n   a. Call Ordinal_10120 with unit stats, target X, Y, skill param byte at offset 0x6d (appears twice), and constant 5\n   b. Return inverted result: true if LOS clear (sLosResult == 0), false if blocked\n9. Return false if any validation fails\n\nParameters:\n\npUnit - Pointer to UnitAny structure representing the casting unit\nwSkillId - Skill identifier to validate for casting (word type, 16-bit)\n\nIMPLICIT:\nwSkillIdHigh - High word of skill ID register (EDX upper bits), concatenated with wSkillId\n\nReturns:\n\ntrue - Skill can be cast at target position (line-of-sight is clear)\nfalse - Skill cannot be cast (invalid unit, no stats, coordinates invalid, or LOS blocked)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n\nIf skill parameters are null (Ordinal_10589 returns 0), function triggers fatal error at line 0x5e8 in g_szSourceFileName and terminates process with exit code 0xFFFFFFFF (-1).\n\nDirection Offset Table (8 directions):\nDirection 0 (N):  X=0,  Y=-2    Direction 1: X=-1, Y=-1\nDirection 2 (W):  X=-2, Y=0     Direction 3: X=-1, Y=1\nDirection 4 (S):  X=0,  Y=2     Direction 5: X=1,  Y=1\nDirection 6 (E):  X=2,  Y=0     Direction 7: X=1,  Y=-1\n\nDirection is calculated as: (unit_direction & 0xFF) >> 3, yielding values 0-31 mapped to 8 cardinal/ordinal directions.\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n\n0x38 (56 decimal) - Offset to pMemPool field in UnitAny structure\n0x6d (109 decimal) - Offset to skill parameter byte (possibly range or collision flags)\n0xff (255 decimal) - Mask for extracting direction byte from full direction value\n0x5e8 (1512 decimal) - Error line number for skill parameter validation failure\n5 - Constant parameter to line-of-sight check (possibly check type or max range)\n\nError Handling:\n\nNull skill parameters trigger fatal error via Ordinal_10023 (assertion) followed by FUN_6fb9a10f (process termination).\nNull unit stats cause early return false without error.\nInvalid coordinates (0,0 after fallback calculation) return false.\nFailed line-of-sight check returns false.",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "STRUCT_Room2", "STRUCT_ItemData", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "TBL_skills", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData", "STRUCT_StatList", "STRUCT_Path", "PARAM_2", "UI_SKILLS", "STRUCT_Skill", "STRUCT_Other", "SRC_Skills.cpp"]
