      "instructions": ["0x1BAB0|PUSH|ESI", "0x1BAB1|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0x1BAB3|PUSH|ESI", "0x1BAB4|CALL|0x6fb983c2", "0x1BAB9|PUSH|0x0", "0x1BABB|PUSH|EAX", "0x1BABC|CALL|0x6fb984d0", "0x1BAC1|CMP|dword ptr [ESI], 0x0", "0x1BAC4|JNZ|0x6faebad8", "0x1BAC6|PUSH|0x0", "0x1BAC8|PUSH|0x0", "0x1BACA|PUSH|0x1", "0x1BACC|MOV|EDX, ESI", "0x1BACE|MOV|ECX, 0x8cb", "0x1BAD3|CALL|0x6fb8d210"],
      "comment": "Plays a sound effect when a unit or entity is created.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call Ordinal_10323 to obtain a sound handle for the unit type\n2. Call Ordinal_10980 with the sound handle and 0 to prepare audio playback\n3. Check if the unit type pointer dereferences to 0 (NULL unit type check)\n4. If unit type is 0, call FUN_6fb8d210 to play sound ID 0x8cb (2251 decimal) at unit location\n5. Return 1 (success)\n\nParameters:\npUnitType - Pointer to integer representing unit type identifier\n            Used to determine which sound effect to play\n            When dereferenced value is 0, triggers default creation sound\n\nReturns:\n1 - Always returns 1 indicating successful sound playback initialization\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x8cb (2251) - Sound effect ID for unit creation event\n               Played when unit type is 0 (default/base unit type)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If *pUnitType == 0, plays default creation sound 0x8cb\n- If *pUnitType != 0, skips sound playback (handled elsewhere)\n- Ordinal_10323 and Ordinal_10980 are external audio system functions\n- FUN_6fb8d210 appears to be PlaySoundAtLocation with coordinates and flags",
      "tags": ["PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_1", "PROP_SMALL"]
