      "comment": "Process game interface difficulty level and apply to game state.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate the game interface object state\n2. If validation fails, return false immediately\n3. Retrieve current difficulty value from game ordinal (Ordinal_10365)\n4. Process difficulty value through adjustment function (FUN_6fb868b0)\n5. Subtract 3 from processed difficulty and clamp to non-negative range\n6. Apply clamped difficulty value to game state via FUN_6fb8d210 with constant 0x8b8\n7. Return true to indicate successful processing\n\nParameters:\n  pGameInterface (GameInterface *) - Pointer to the game interface object to process\n\nReturns:\n  bool - true (1) if difficulty was successfully processed and applied\n         false (0) if game interface validation failed\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Difficulty clamping: (value - 3) & ((int)(value - 3) < 0) - 1\n    This expression ensures result is non-negative by masking with -1 when negative\n  - Magic constant 0x8b8 (2232 decimal) appears to be a game state identifier or event code\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x8b8 (2232) - Game state constant passed to FUN_6fb8d210\n  0x3 (3) - Difficulty adjustment offset\n  0.0 - Default float parameter for FUN_6fb8d210\n  0 - Default int parameter for FUN_6fb8d210",
      "tags": ["PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_1"]
    },
