      "comment": "Initialize dual sound effects for unit hit feedback\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Create initial sound effect with sound ID 0x8c7 for the unit\n2. Initialize local variables: nParam5 = 0, flParam4 = 0.0, flParam3 = 0x8 (1.12104e-44)\n3. Query hit class sound ID table with hit class value 6\n4. Create second sound effect using the hit class sound ID returned from step 3\n5. Return success status (1)\n\nParameters:\n  nUnit - Unit pointer for which to create sound effects\n\nReturns:\n  1 - Success, sound effects created\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x8c7 (2247) - Primary sound effect ID for initial effect\n  6 - Hit class index for table lookup\n  0x8 - Interpreted as float bits (1.12104e-44), param3 value for second sound call\n  0x0 - Zero values for param4 and param5 in both sound calls\n  1 - Success return value",
      "tags": ["PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_1"]
