      "globals": ["0xFFFFFFFF9052FFA0||", "0xFFFFFFFF9052FF94||", "0xFFFFFFFF9052FFA4||", "0xFFFFFFFF90530000||", "0xFFFFFFFF9052FF90||", "0xFFFFFFFF9052FF9C||", "0xFFFFFFFF9052FF98||", "0xFFFFFFFF9052FFA8||", "0xFFFFFFFF9053001C||", "0xFFFFFFFF9052FFAC||", "0xFFFFFFFF9052FFBC||", "0xFFFFFFFF9052FFB8||", "0xFFFFFFFF9052FFC0||", "0xFFFFFFFF9052FFD4||", "0xFFFFFFFF9052FFC4||", "0xFFFFFFFF9052FFC8||"],
      "api_count": 19,
      "api_calls": ["UNITS_GetSummonOwnerUnitId", "GetSkillsTxtId", "GetSkillOwnerType", "GetSkillTargetX", "GetSkillTargetY", "GetMonsterResurrectMode", "SetUnitScrollPos", "GetUnitWeaponClass", "UNITS_GetOwnerGuid", "UNITS_GetUnitY", "...+9 more"],
      "instructions": ["0x1BE40|SUB|ESP, 0x70", "0x1BE43|PUSH|EBP", "0x1BE44|PUSH|ESI", "0x1BE45|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0x1BE47|PUSH|EDI", "0x1BE48|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x1c], EDX", "0x1BE4C|PUSH|ESI", "0x1BE4D|CALL|0x6fb983c2", "0x1BE52|MOV|EBP, EAX", "0x1BE54|TEST|EBP, EBP", "0x1BE56|JZ|0x6faebfc2", "0x1BE5C|PUSH|EBP", "0x1BE5D|CALL|0x6fb98338", "0x1BE62|MOV|EDI, EAX", "0x1BE64|PUSH|EBP"],
      "comment": "Executes one repetition of a multi-shot skill (e.g., Strafe, Multiple Shot) and queues the next.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Store skill mode parameter in local variable\n2. Call Ordinal_10323 to get the active skill from unit (returned in EAX as pSkill)\n3. If no skill active, return early\n4. Get skill ID from skills.txt via GetSkillsTxtId\n5. Get remaining shot count via GetSkillOwnerType\n6. If no shots remaining (count == 0), return early\n7. Get target X/Y coordinates from skill\n8. Look up target unit in hash table using target coordinates\n9. If target unit not found in hash table:\n   a. Get monster resurrect mode for fallback targeting\n   b. Call BuildAndExecuteItemQuery with -1 (0xffffffff) as target to find new target\n   c. If query returns null, skip scroll position update\n10. If target exists, call SetUnitScrollPos to align unit facing\n11. Initialize unit coordinates (X/Y) to 0\n12. Call CalculateUnitCoordinates to get firing position\n13. Get weapon class via GetUnitWeaponClass\n14. Zero-initialize projectile data structure (22 dwords = 88 bytes)\n15. Set projectile type to 0x21 (missile type constant)\n16. Store owner unit pointer in projectile data\n17. Call Ordinal_10326 and Ordinal_10329 for auxiliary projectile setup\n18. Copy unit coordinates to projectile launch position\n19. Calculate animation type: 0xD5 for weapon class 1, 0xD6 otherwise\n20. Call InitializeAndAllocateProjectile to create the missile\n21. Decrement remaining shot count and update via SetSkillOwnerType\n22. If more shots remain (count > 0):\n    a. Query for next target (reuse current or find new)\n    b. If new target found, update unit direction and skill target coords\n    c. Get damage reduction data and apply via ApplyDamageReduction\n\nParameters:\npUnit (ECX): Pointer to attacking unit (player/monster)\ndwSkillMode (EDX): Skill execution mode flags\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Early exit if no active skill (pSkill == NULL)\n- Early exit if shot count exhausted (dwShotsRemaining == 0)\n- Target acquisition fallback if hash lookup fails\n- Weapon class determines animation: 0xD5 (bow) or 0xD6 (crossbow)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x21 - Projectile type identifier for multi-shot missiles\n0xD5 - Animation type for weapon class 1 (bow)\n0xD6 - Animation type for other weapon classes (crossbow)\n0xFFFFFFFF - Invalid unit ID used when no specific target\n0x16 - Loop counter for zeroing 22 dwords (88 bytes)\n\nOrdinal Functions:\nOrdinal_10323 - D2Common.GetUnitSkill - Get active skill from unit\nOrdinal_10326 - D2Common.GetUnitX - Get unit X coordinate\nOrdinal_10329 - D2Common.GetUnitY - Get unit Y coordinate",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_MonsterData", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PARAM_2", "PROP_NOCALLER", "STRUCT_Skill", "STRUCT_ItemData", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
    },
