      "instructions": ["0x1C170|PUSH|EBX", "0x1C171|PUSH|ESI", "0x1C172|PUSH|EDI", "0x1C173|MOV|EDI, ECX", "0x1C175|PUSH|EDI", "0x1C176|CALL|0x6fb983c2", "0x1C17B|MOV|ECX, EDI", "0x1C17D|MOV|EBX, EAX", "0x1C17F|CALL|0x6fb63760", "0x1C184|TEST|EBX, EBX", "0x1C186|MOV|ESI, EAX", "0x1C188|JNZ|0x6faec190", "0x1C18A|POP|EDI", "0x1C18B|POP|ESI", "0x1C18C|XOR|EAX, EAX"],
      "comment": "Validates entity and initializes it with item query results.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call Ordinal_10323(nEntity) to validate entity and get validation handle\n2. Call FUN_6fb63760(nEntity) to get existing item data pointer\n3. If validation failed (handle == 0), return false immediately\n4. Call FUN_6fb8d210 with magic number 0x8cb, entity, and parameters (3, 0, 0)\n5. If item data pointer is null, execute item query:\n   a. Call BuildAndExecuteItemQuery with entity, -1 (all items), type 4, mode 4\n   b. Store query result in pdwItemData\n   c. If query result is also null, call Ordinal_10980(handle, 0) and return true\n6. Initialize dwOrdinal10326 to 0 for parameter passing\n7. Call Ordinal_10329(pdwItemData) to get secondary data value\n8. Call Ordinal_10326(pdwItemData) to get primary ordinal value\n9. Call Ordinal_10216 with entity field at offset 0x38, primary ordinal, secondary data, and zero\n10. Call InitializeEntityDataStructure(nEntity, 4) to initialize entity with type 4 data\n11. Call Ordinal_10980(validation handle, initialization result) to store result\n12. Call Ordinal_10981(validation handle, first dword from item data)\n13. Call Ordinal_10982(validation handle, third dword from item data at offset 0x8)\n14. Return true for successful completion\n\nParameters:\nnEntity (int): Entity structure pointer; accessed at offset 0x38 for nested structure reference\n\nReturns:\nbool: false if entity validation fails (Ordinal_10323 returns 0); true otherwise\n\nSpecial Cases:\nMagic number 0x8cb passed to FUN_6fb8d210 (decimal 2251) - likely entity type or operation code\nQuery parameters 0xffffffff (all items), 4 (item type), 4 (query mode) when no existing data\nItem data structure has dwords at offsets 0x0 and 0x8 extracted and stored via ordinal functions\nEarly return with true when validation succeeds but query returns no results\n\nItem Data Structure Layout:\nOffset  Size  Field Name              Type   Description\n0x00    0x4   dwItemField0            uint   First item parameter stored via Ordinal_10981\n0x04    0x4   dwItemField1            uint   Second field (not directly accessed)\n0x08    0x4   dwItemField2            uint   Third item parameter stored via Ordinal_10982",
      "tags": ["PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_1"]
