      "instructions": ["0x1C220|PUSH|EBX", "0x1C221|PUSH|ESI", "0x1C222|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0x1C224|PUSH|EDI", "0x1C225|PUSH|ESI", "0x1C226|CALL|0x6fb983c2", "0x1C22B|MOV|EDI, EAX", "0x1C22D|PUSH|EDI", "0x1C22E|CALL|0x6fb98458", "0x1C233|MOV|EBX, EAX", "0x1C235|PUSH|EDI", "0x1C236|CALL|0x6fb98512", "0x1C23B|MOV|ECX, EAX", "0x1C23D|MOV|EDX, EBX", "0x1C23F|CALL|0x6fb60e10"],
      "comment": "Consume one charge from an item with charges and apply associated effects.\n\nAlgorithm:\n\n1. Retrieve charge state object from unit\n2. Get current charge index and item type from charge state\n3. Search for existing charge item using type and index\n4. If no charge item found, execute item query to find it\n5. If still no item found after query, return early (no charges available)\n6. Get current charge count from charge state\n7. Decrement charge count by 1 and update charge state\n8. If remaining charges > 0, execute item query for next charge item\n9. If next charge item found:\n   - Get item X and Y coordinates\n   - Perform operation on unit's memory pool with coordinates and zero flag\n   - Update charge state with item's first and third dword values\n   - Retrieve updated charge state object\n   - Get damage value from charge state\n   - Apply damage reduction to unit with damage value\n   - Get skill/effect type\n   - Execute skill effect with unit and zero parameters\n10. Return\n\nParameters:\n\npUnit - Pointer to UnitAny structure representing the unit consuming charges\n\nReturns:\n\nvoid - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n\n- If no charge item exists initially, attempts to find via item query before failing\n- If charge count becomes 0 or negative after decrement, skips effect application\n- If item query for next charge fails, skips effect application phase\n- Uses zero-initialized float and int parameters for final skill execution\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n\n0x4 (4 decimal) - Item query criteria flag\n0x4 (4 decimal) - Item query flags parameter\n0x0 (0 decimal) - Zero flag parameter for coordinate operation\n0x38 (56 decimal) - Offset to pMemPool field in UnitAny structure",
      "tags": ["PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_1"]
    },
