      "globals": ["0xFFFFFFFF90530000||", "0xFFFFFFFF9053001C||", "0xFFFFFFFF90530004||", "0xD6B24|g_AmazonSkillDescriptorTable|0x1b", "0xD6B28|DAT_6fba6b28|0x0"],
      "api_count": 3,
      "api_calls": ["UNITS_GetSummonOwnerUnitId", "SetOverlayCallback", "FogAssert"],
      "instructions": ["0x1C400|PUSH|ESI", "0x1C401|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0x1C403|PUSH|EDI", "0x1C404|MOV|EDI, EDX", "0x1C406|PUSH|ESI", "0x1C407|CALL|0x6fb983c2", "0x1C40C|SUB|EDI, 0x6", "0x1C40F|JS|0x6faec482", "0x1C411|CMP|EDI, 0x1e", "0x1C414|JGE|0x6faec482", "0x1C416|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0x1C418|JZ|0x6faec47d", "0x1C41A|LEA|EDI, [EDI + EDI*0x4]", "0x1C41D|PUSH|EBX", "0x1C41E|MOV|EBX, dword ptr [ESP + 0x10]"],
      "comment": "Execute Amazon character class skill with validation and missile targeting.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate skill has execution permission via Ordinal_10323(pUnit)\n2. Calculate skill table index: nSkillIndex = nSkillId - 6\n3. Validate nSkillIndex in range [0, 30) - covers Amazon skill IDs 6-35\n4. If out of range, trigger assertion with error message and terminate\n5. If no permission (fHasPermission == 0), return early without execution\n6. Look up skill descriptor in g_AmazonSkillDescriptorTable at [nSkillIndex * 20]\n7. If descriptor.dwTargetType != 0xFFFF, call CalculateMissileTargetCoordinates\n8. Set unit flag pUnit->dwFlags |= 0x40 after missile targeting\n9. If descriptor.pfnSkillHandler == NULL, set flag 0x40 and skip handler\n10. Otherwise, call descriptor.pfnSkillHandler() with unit and flags\n11. Retrieve audio context via Ordinal_10958(pUnit, 0)\n12. If audio context exists, remove it with RemoveAudioContextFromList\n\nParameters:\n  pUnit (ECX) - Pointer to UnitAny executing the skill\n  nSkillId (EDX) - Skill identifier (expected range: 6-35 for Amazon skills)\n  dwFlags (Stack[0x4]) - Execution flags passed to skill handler\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value\n  Terminates process if skill ID validation fails\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - SKILL_ID_BASE = 6 (Amazon skill IDs start at 6)\n  - NUM_AMAZON_SKILLS = 30 (0x1E) skill slots in descriptor table\n  - Flag 0x40 at offset 0xE8 indicates skill execution state\n  - Assertion uses format: \"nSkillId >= 0 && nSkillId < NUM_AMAZON_SKILLS\"\n  - FUN_6fb9a10f(0xFFFFFFFF) is process termination after assertion\n\nStructure Layout - Amazon Skill Descriptor (20 bytes, stride 0x14):\n\nOffset | Size | Field Name      | Type        | Description\n-------|------|-----------------|-------------|----------------------------------\n0x00   | 4    | dwTargetType    | uint        | Missile target type (0xFFFF = none)\n0x04   | 4    | pfnSkillHandler | code *      | Skill execution callback function\n0x08   | 12   | (unknown)       | byte[12]    | Additional skill parameters\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x6 - SKILL_ID_BASE - Minimum valid Amazon skill ID\n  0x1E (30) - NUM_AMAZON_SKILLS - Maximum skill count\n  0x14 (20) - Skill descriptor structure size/stride\n  0xFFFF - NO_TARGET - Indicates skill has no missile targeting\n  0x40 - SKILL_EXECUTION_FLAG - Unit flag set during skill execution\n  0xE8 (232) - Offset to dwFlags field in UnitAny structure\n  0x293 (659) - Assertion line number in source file\n  0xFFFFFFFF - Process termination error code\n\nError Handling:\n  - Out-of-range skill ID triggers Ordinal_10023 assertion\n  - Assertion displays: file path, line 0x293, condition string\n  - Process terminates via FUN_6fb9a10f(0xFFFFFFFF) after assertion\n  - No permission check returns early without error\n  - NULL skill handler treated as valid (sets flag but skips execution)",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Inventory", "PROP_NOCALLER", "UI_SKILLS", "SRC_SkillsAma.cpp", "PARAM_3", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control"]
