      "comment": "Execute Fire Blast skill effect callback for Assassin.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Set skill execution flag (0x40) on unit's GfxFrame field at offset 0xE8\n2. Calculate unit's current world coordinates via CalculateUnitCoordinates()\n3. Create Fire Blast missile (ID 0x181) at unit's position with target skill parameter\n4. If missile creation succeeds, set missile target unit to NULL (self-targeting projectile)\n5. Initialize game object properties with effect ID 0x103 for visual/audio effects\n\nParameters:\n  pUnit - UnitAny pointer for unit executing skill, IMPLICIT ECX\n  dwMissileTargetSkill - Missile target skill ID from skill params table, IMPLICIT EDX\n\nReturns:\n  void - Missile and effects applied in place\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Missile creation may fail if projectile limit reached; effect still applied\n  - Target unit set to 0 indicates self-targeting (no homing behavior)\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x40 - Skill effect executed flag bit (set in unit flags)\n  0xE8 - Offset to dwGfxFrame in UnitAny[4] (232 bytes from base)\n  0x181 (385) - Fire Blast missile type ID\n  0x103 (259) - Fire Blast visual effect ID for InitializeGameObjectProperties\n\nStructure Layout:\n  UnitAny[4].dwGfxFrame at offset 0xE8:\n    Bit 6 (0x40) - Skill effect execution flag\n\nCross-Reference:\n  Called from ExecuteSkillEffectCallback via function pointer table at 0x6FBA6D80\n  Table index 0 corresponds to skill ID 0xFB (251) - Fire Blast",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Inventory", "PARAM_2", "PROP_NOCALLER", "STRUCT_Control"]
