      "comment": "Initializes skill handle for skill ID 0x10a and creates context for unit.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Save ESI/EDI registers, preserve pUnit in ESI\n2. Call GetUnitSkillById(pUnit, 0x10a, -1) to get skill handle for skill ID 266\n3. If skill handle is NULL:\n   a. Assert with \"hSkill\" error message (line 0x3f)\n   b. Exit application with code -1 (fatal error)\n4. Call SetSkillOwnerType(pSkill, 0) to set skill owner to primary/player\n5. Call InitializeContextHandleOrCreateNew(pUnit) to initialize context\n6. Restore registers and return\n\nParameters:\n  pUnit (ECX) - Pointer to UnitAny structure for the unit requiring skill init\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Fatal assertion if skill ID 0x10a not found on unit\n  - Function does not return if skill lookup fails\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x10a (266) - Specific skill ID being initialized\n  -1 - Skill mode parameter (any mode)\n  0 - Owner type for SetSkillOwnerType (primary/player)\n  0x3f (63) - Source line number for assertion\n\nError Handling:\n  Uses FogAssert with \"hSkill\" string if GetUnitSkillById returns NULL\n  Calls ExitApplicationWithCode(-1) after assertion - no recovery\n\nClassification: Worker function - Skill/context initialization",
