      "instructions": ["0x1C6E0|SUB|ESP, 0x60", "0x1C6E3|PUSH|EBX", "0x1C6E4|PUSH|EBP", "0x1C6E5|PUSH|ESI", "0x1C6E6|MOV|EBX, EDX", "0x1C6E8|PUSH|EDI", "0x1C6E9|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0x1C6EB|PUSH|-0x1", "0x1C6ED|MOV|EDX, 0x10a", "0x1C6F2|CALL|0x6fb98230", "0x1C6F7|MOV|EDI, dword ptr [ESI + 0xe8]", "0x1C6FD|MOV|EBP, EAX", "0x1C6FF|LEA|EAX, [ESP + 0x14]", "0x1C703|AND|EDI, 0xffffffbf", "0x1C706|PUSH|EAX"],
      "comment": "Executes a skill (ID 0x10a) and creates an associated projectile for the unit.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Retrieve skill 0x10a (266) from unit using GetUnitSkillById\n2. Clear bit 0x40 in unit's field at offset 0xe8 (animation/state flags)\n3. Calculate unit's current coordinates via CalculateUnitCoordinates\n4. If coordinate calculation fails, exit early\n5. Get skill owner type; if owner type is 0 (no owner):\n   a. Zero out 0x16 (22) dwords in projectile data structure\n   b. Set projectile type to 0x20 (32)\n   c. Set projectile skill ID to 0x1fc (508)\n   d. Copy unit coordinates to projectile\n   e. Set owner and target to the source unit\n   f. Call InitializeAndAllocateProjectile to create projectile\n   g. If projectile created, set coordinates with flags 0xf\n   h. Get monster data field 0xFC for skill 0x10a\n6. Set skill owner type to (monster data value - 1)\n7. Check if unit has state flag 0xc set\n8. If flag set, update animation data upper bits to 0xb and set 0x800 at offset 0x54\n\nParameters:\n  pUnit (ECX) - UnitAny* - Source unit executing the skill\n  dwSkillParam (EDX) - dword - Parameter passed to projectile data structure\n\nReturns: void\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x10a (266) - Skill ID being executed\n  0x1fc (508) - Projectile skill ID\n  0x20 (32) - Projectile type identifier\n  0x40 - Bit mask cleared in unit field 0xe8\n  0xc - State flag checked for animation update\n  0xb - Animation data upper bits value\n  0x800 - Value written to offset 0x54 when state active\n  0xf - Drawable coordinate flags\n  0x16 (22) - Number of dwords zeroed in projectile structure\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If CalculateUnitCoordinates returns 0, function exits without action\n  - If skill owner type is non-zero, projectile creation is skipped\n  - Projectile is only positioned if allocation succeeds",
