      "comment": "Validates entity state consistency between two related game objects.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Retrieve related entity pointer using helper function FUN_6fb63760\n2. If related entity is NULL, validation fails immediately\n3. Call Ordinal_10342 on primary entity handle to get state identifier\n4. Call Ordinal_10082 to check state validity (returns 0 for valid)\n5. If primary entity state is invalid, validation fails\n6. Repeat state check (steps 3-4) for related entity pointer\n7. If related entity state is invalid, validation fails\n8. Check first field of related entity: must be 0 or 1\n9. If all checks pass, return 1 (success), otherwise return 0 (failure)\n\nParameters:\n  nEntityHandle (int) - Handle or identifier for primary game entity to validate\n\nReturns:\n  1 (0x1) - Both entities have valid state and related entity type field is 0 or 1\n  0 (0x0) - Validation failed: NULL related entity, invalid state, or type field not 0/1\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Related entity NULL check prevents dereferencing invalid pointers\n  - State validation uses external ordinal functions (DLL imports)\n  - Related entity first field (*pnRelatedEntity) constrained to binary values\n  - Function has no callers in analyzed code (may be invoked via function pointer table)\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x0 (decimal 0) - NULL pointer check and valid state return from Ordinal_10082\n  0x1 (decimal 1) - Valid type value for related entity first field and success return\n  0x38 (decimal 56) - Offset used in helper function FUN_6fb63760 for entity field access",
