      "comment": "Validates object state and triggers action if conditions are met.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Retrieve first object pointer from context by calling FUN_6fb63760\n2. Retrieve second object pointer from same context\n3. Exit if second object pointer is null\n4. Get value from context using Ordinal_10342 and validate with Ordinal_10082\n5. Exit if validation fails (non-zero return)\n6. Get value from second object using Ordinal_10342 and validate with Ordinal_10082\n7. Exit if validation fails (non-zero return)\n8. Read flag dword from second object at offset 0x0\n9. Check if flag value is 0 or 1, exit if not\n10. Check if first object pointer is valid, exit if null\n11. Call FUN_6fb931f0 with first object and parameters (0xbe, 2, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0)\n12. Call FUN_6fb8d210 with parameters (0x950, first object, 0.0, 0.0, 0)\n\nParameters:\n  nContext (int) - Context or parent structure pointer passed in ECX, used to retrieve object pointers\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Function exits early if second object pointer is null\n  - Function exits if either Ordinal_10082 validation returns non-zero\n  - Flag at offset 0x0 of second object must be exactly 0 or 1 to proceed\n  - First object pointer must be valid to trigger actions\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0xbe (190 decimal) - Parameter passed to FUN_6fb931f0, likely action or message type\n  0x950 (2384 decimal) - Parameter passed to FUN_6fb8d210, likely event or command code\n  0x2 (2 decimal) - Third parameter to FUN_6fb931f0\n  0x0 or 0x1 - Valid flag values at offset 0x0 of second object",
