      "comment": "Initialize compression context with D2COMMON compression library.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Create compression handle via Ordinal_10470 with parameters: type=0, mode=4, flags=0, first param, third param\n2. If handle creation fails (returns 0), skip initialization and return success\n3. Associate compression parameters with handle via Ordinal_10475\n4. Retrieve error code via Ordinal_10993 with value 0x10e (270 decimal)\n5. Configure handle with error code via Ordinal_10465 using property ID 0x44 (68 decimal)\n6. Finalize compression context via Ordinal_10376\n7. Always return true indicating function completed\n\nParameters:\n  pCompressionParams - Pointer to compression parameter structure containing:\n                       [0x0] First configuration value (passed to handle creation)\n                       [0x4] Second configuration value (not used in this function)\n                       [0x8] Third configuration value (passed to handle creation)\n\nReturns:\n  true - Function always returns success (1)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If Ordinal_10470 returns 0 (NULL handle), initialization steps are skipped\n  - Function returns true even if handle creation fails\n  - No error propagation to caller\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x0 (Type parameter) - Compression type identifier\n  0x4 (Mode parameter) - Compression mode (decimal: 4)\n  0x0 (Flags parameter) - No special flags\n  0x10e (Error code request) - Error code identifier (decimal: 270)\n  0x44 (Property ID) - Handle property identifier (decimal: 68)",
