      "comment": "Fires missile at mercenary position and sets unit state flag.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get mercenary position coordinates from unit via GetMercenaryPosition\n2. If mercenary position is valid (non-NULL):\n   a. Fire missile ID 0x215 (533) with target validation using dwFlags\n   b. Set flag bit 0x40 in unit state field at offset 0xe8 (dwGfxFrame)\n3. Return (void function)\n\nParameters:\npUnit (UnitAny *): Pointer to unit structure, passed in ECX\ndwFlags (uint): Missile behavior flags, passed in EDX\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If mercenary position is NULL (no valid mercenary), function exits early without firing\n- Flag 0x40 at offset 0xe8 indicates mercenary missile has been fired\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x215 (533): Missile type identifier for mercenary attack\n0x40: Flag bit set in dwGfxFrame to mark missile fired state\n0xe8 (232): Offset to dwGfxFrame field in UnitAny (index 4, field dwGfxFrame)\n\nRelated Functions:\n- GetMercenaryPosition: Returns mercenary coordinates or NULL\n- FireMissileWithTargetValidation: Fires missile with distance/coordinate validation",
