      "comment": "Set priority level based on threshold value with validation check\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call FUN_6fb63760 to validate object and store result\n2. Call Ordinal_10323 to retrieve handle identifier from object\n3. Check validation result\n4. If validation failed (result == 0), set priority level 0 and return success\n5. If validation succeeded, determine priority level by threshold\n6. If nThresholdValue <= 5, use priority level 1\n7. If nThresholdValue in range 6-11, use priority level 2\n8. If nThresholdValue >= 12, use priority level 3\n9. Call Ordinal_10980 to apply computed priority level to handle\n10. Return success (1)\n\nParameters:\n  nObjectHandle - Handle or identifier to object for validation and configuration\n  nThresholdValue - Threshold value for priority level calculation (compared against 5 and 11)\n\nReturns:\n  Always returns 1 (success)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Validation failure results in priority level 0\n  - Threshold boundaries: 5 (level 1/2 boundary), 11 (level 2/3 boundary)\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x00 (0) - Priority level for validation failure\n  0x01 (1) - Base priority level for low thresholds (<=5)\n  0x02 (2) - Mid-range priority level (6-11)\n  0x03 (3) - High priority level (>=12)\n  0x05 (5) - Lower threshold boundary for priority level decision\n  0x0B (11) - Upper threshold boundary for priority level decision\n  0x06 (6) - Start of mid-range priority (implicit)\n  0x0C (12) - Start of high priority (implicit)",
      "tags": ["PARAM_2", "PROP_NOCALLER"]
