      "comment": "Validates mercenary position state by checking if state value is 0 or 1.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call GetMercenaryPosition to retrieve position state pointer for unit\n2. If position pointer is NULL, return false (no position data)\n3. Dereference position pointer to get state value\n4. Check if state value equals 1 - if so, return true (valid)\n5. Check if state value equals 0 - if so, return true (valid)\n6. Otherwise return false (invalid state)\n\nParameters:\npUnit (UnitAny *): Pointer to unit structure (mercenary) passed in ECX\n\nReturns:\nbool: true if position state is valid (0 or 1), false otherwise\n\nClassification: Validation helper function (leaf-like, single callee)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Returns false if GetMercenaryPosition returns NULL\n- Only states 0 and 1 are considered valid\n- Any other state value (2+) returns false\n\nRelated Functions:\n- GetMercenaryPosition: Retrieves position coordinate pointer from unit animation data",
      "tags": ["PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_1", "PROP_SMALL"]
