      "comment": "Renders area-of-effect visual effects based on skill mode and coordinates.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Retrieve primary skill data using GetSkillData1(0x103) where 0x103 (259) is skill ID\n2. Retrieve secondary skill data using GetSkillData2(0x103) for same skill\n3. Validate render mode is 2 (single effect) or 3 (dual effect)\n4. If coordinates are packed (nCoordPacked != 0), extract X and Y using coordinate helpers\n5. Render first area effect (ID 0x22c/556) at specified center coordinates\n6. If mode is 3, render second area effect (ID 0x22d/557) with alternate skill data\n\nParameters:\n  pContext - Rendering context structure pointer (RenderContext*) for effect system\n  nCoordPacked - Packed coordinate value (0 if using explicit coordinates)\n  dwFlags - Flags passed to area effect rendering function\n  nCenterX - Center X coordinate for area effect (overwritten if nCoordPacked != 0)\n  nCenterY - Center Y coordinate for area effect (overwritten if nCoordPacked != 0)\n  nRenderMode - Render mode selector: 2 = single effect, 3 = dual effect\n  IMPLICIT dwImplicitEDI - Additional parameter passed via EDI register to area effect function\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If nRenderMode is not 2 or 3, function returns immediately without rendering\n  - When nCoordPacked is non-zero, nCenterX and nCenterY parameters are ignored\n  - Mode 3 uses different skill data (nSkillData2) for second effect layer\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x103 (259) - Skill ID passed to skill data retrieval functions\n  0x22c (556) - Primary area effect ID for first visual layer\n  0x22d (557) - Secondary area effect ID for second visual layer (mode 3 only)\n  2 - Single effect render mode\n  3 - Dual effect render mode\n\nExternal Dependencies:\n  Ordinal_10990 - Retrieves primary skill-related data for skill ID\n  Ordinal_10991 - Retrieves secondary skill-related data for skill ID\n  Ordinal_10326 - Extracts X coordinate from packed coordinate value\n  Ordinal_10329 - Extracts Y coordinate from packed coordinate value\n  GenerateRandomPointsInRadius - Generates circular area effect at specified coordinates",
