      "comment": "Generate random points within a circular radius and process valid locations.\n\nAlgorithm:\n\n1. Store radius value in temporary variable for later use\n2. Get context handle from pGameContext object via Ordinal_10342\n3. Seed or initialize random number generator via Ordinal_10913\n4. Calculate radius squared (nRadius * nRadius) for distance comparisons\n5. Initialize local stack structure (88 bytes, 0x16 dwords) to zero\n6. Set up structure fields:\n   - dwStructFlag = 1 (initialization flag)\n   - dwFlagsCopy = dwFlags (copy flags parameter)\n   - dwEffectIdCopy = dwEffectId (copy effect ID)\n   - pContextCopy = pContext (copy context pointer)\n7. Loop nRadiusSquared times to generate random points:\n   a. Generate random X offset: nOffsetX = nRadius - Ordinal_10918()\n   b. Generate random Y offset: nOffsetY = nRadius - Ordinal_10918()\n   c. Check if point is within circular radius using distance formula:\n      if (nOffsetX² + nOffsetY² <= nRadiusSquared)\n   d. Calculate absolute target coordinates:\n      nTargetX = nOffsetX + nCenterX\n      nTargetY = nOffsetY + nCenterY\n   e. Validate location via Ordinal_10042(dwContextHandle, nTargetX, nTargetY)\n   f. If location is valid (return != 0), process it via FUN_6fb77720(&local_58)\n8. Return after processing all iterations\n\nParameters:\n\nIMPLICIT pGameContext - Primary game context pointer passed via ECX register (__thiscall convention)\n  NOTE: Auto-parameter 'this' cannot be renamed due to Ghidra __thiscall implementation\n  Type: GameContext* (60164 bytes - contains game state, rendering, and resource management)\npContext - Secondary game context or data pointer\n  Type: GameContext* (likely same structure or related context object)\ndwEffectId - Effect or spell identifier (0x22c, 0x22d, 0x230, 0x231 observed)\nnCenterX - Center X coordinate for radius calculation\nnCenterY - Center Y coordinate for radius calculation  \nnRadius - Radius value for circular area generation\ndwFlags - Flags parameter passed to processing function\n\nReturns:\n\nvoid (no return value)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n\nIf nRadius is 0 or negative, loop body never executes (0 < nRadiusSquared fails)\nRandom number generation uses rejection sampling - generates points in square bounding box,\n  only processes those within circular radius using Pythagorean distance check\nNumber of actual processed points depends on collision detection and circle hit rate\n  (approximately π/4 ≈ 78.5% of generated points fall within circle)\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n\n0x16 (22 decimal) - Stack structure size in dwords (88 bytes total)\n1 - Initialization flag value for dwStructFlag\n\nStructure Layout (88 bytes on stack):\n\nOffset  Size  Field Name        Type      Description\n------  ----  ----------------  --------  ------------------------------------\n+0x00   4     dwStructFlag      uint      Initialization flag (set to 1)\n+0x04   84    [remaining data]  byte[84]  Additional structure fields (not directly accessed)\n        \nThe structure is passed to FUN_6fb77720 for processing valid locations.\nThe full structure layout and field meanings would be defined in FUN_6fb77720 analysis.\n\nImplementation Notes:\n\nThis function demonstrates __thiscall calling convention with auto-parameter in ECX.\nCompleteness limited by auto-parameter 'this' which cannot be renamed (Ghidra limitation).",
