      "comment": "Dispatches game object creation based on mode selector parameter.\\n\\nAlgorithm:\\n\\n1. Validate prerequisites: mode selector must be 2 or 3, and data reference must be non-zero\\n2. If mode selector equals 2: Call Ordinal_10590 to retrieve control flags for magic number 0x22f\\n3. For mode 2: Create game object via InitializeGameObject with class type 0x22f, mode 0xffff (skip array copy), additional data, and control flags\\n4. If mode selector equals 3: Retrieve ordinal data results from data reference using Ordinal_10326 and Ordinal_10329\\n5. For mode 3: Create game object with sine wave data via InitializeTrigonometricTable using class type 0x22e, ordinal results, additional data, and stride value 4\\n6. Return if validation fails or after successful object creation\\n\\nParameters:\\n\\npGameContext (ECX): Pointer to game context or object container where new object will be created\\nnDataRef (EDX): Data reference or object source identifier used for ordinal lookups (must be non-zero)\\ndwAdditionalData (Stack+4): Additional parameter data passed to object initialization functions\\ndwUnused1 (Stack+8): Unused parameter (reserved)\\ndwUnused2 (Stack+C): Unused parameter (reserved)\\nnModeSelector (Stack+10): Mode selector determining object creation path: 2 = standard initialization, 3 = sine wave initialization\\n\\nIMPLICIT: EBX register preserved across mode 3 path, passed to InitializeTrigonometricTable\\n\\nReturns:\\n\\nvoid (no return value)\\n\\nSpecial Cases:\\n\\nMagic Number 0x22f (559): Class type for mode 2 standard object initialization\\nMagic Number 0x22e (558): Class type for mode 3 sine wave object initialization\\nMagic Number 0xffff (65535): Mode parameter passed to InitializeGameObject to skip array copy operation\\nMagic Number 0x4 (4): Stride value for sine wave data processing in mode 3 path\\nIf nModeSelector is not 2 or 3: Function returns immediately without creating object\\nIf nDataRef is zero: Function returns immediately without creating object (validation failure)\\nMode 2 path casts pGameContext from GameContext* to dword before passing to InitializeGameObject\\nMode 3 path passes pGameContext as GameContext* directly to InitializeTrigonometricTable\\n\\nError Handling:\\n\\nNo explicit error codes returned; validation failures result in silent return\\nCaller must verify object creation success through separate means\\n\\nNote: Function uses unaff_EBX phantom variable (preserved register) passed to InitializeTrigonometricTable in mode 3 path",
