      "comment": "Initialize trigonometric lookup table with 128 sine/cosine values\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Populate 128-entry sine/cosine lookup table (0-127) with hardcoded values\n2. Initialize trailing structure fields (22 uint entries) to zero\n3. Save context pointer and copy input parameters to local variables\n4. Set error label pointer based on table type (0x238 vs others)\n5. Loop through table with configurable stride (nStride * 4 bytes)\n6. For each iteration: extract upper/lower values from table entries\n7. Call Ordinal_10918() with current values to perform operation\n8. Call FUN_6fb77720() to retrieve object pointer from structure\n9. If object exists and table type is 0x238, allocate memory and call Ordinal_11140()\n10. Advance offset by stride and repeat until 256 bytes processed\n\nParameters:\n  this - Object context pointer (passed in ECX per __thiscall convention)\n  nTableType - Table type identifier (0x238, 0x22e, or other)\n  dwParam1 - First operation parameter\n  dwParam2 - Second operation parameter  \n  dwParam3 - Third operation parameter\n  nStride - Loop stride multiplier (controls iteration step size)\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x238 (568) - Special table type requiring memory allocation path\n  0x22e (558) - Alternate table type using error label LAB_6faed240\n  0x118 (280) - Size parameter for memory allocation in Ordinal_10991\n  0x100 (256) - Total bytes to process in main loop\n  0x80 (128) - Offset to structure fields / table entry count\n  0x16 (22) - Count of trailing structure fields to zero-initialize\n  0x40-0x7f (64-127) - Upper half of lookup table indices\n  0x00-0x3f (0-63) - Lower half of lookup table indices\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  If nTableType != 0x238, pbErrorLabel points to LAB_6faed240\n  If piObject is NULL, skip memory allocation/Ordinal_11140 call\n  Stride determines iteration spacing: offset += (nStride * 4)",
