      "comment": "Generates missile spawn points based on entity position and spawn mode\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Retrieve two spawn type values (0x112) from ordinal functions\n2. Check if spawn mode is 2 or 3, exit if neither\n3. If entity reference is non-zero, extract coordinates from entity\n4. Generate first set of random points (type 0x230) around center\n5. If spawn mode is 3, generate second set (type 0x231) using alternate spawn type\n\nParameters:\n  pGameContext (GameContext *) - Game context object passed as 'this' to GenerateRandomPointsInRadius\n  nEntityRef (int) - Entity reference for coordinate extraction (0 uses provided coords)\n  dwRadius (uint) - Radius for random point generation\n  nCenterX (int) - Center X coordinate (or extracted from entity if nEntityRef != 0)\n  nCenterY (int) - Center Y coordinate (or extracted from entity if nEntityRef != 0)\n  nSpawnMode (int) - Spawn mode: 2 = single spawn type, 3 = dual spawn type\n\nReturns:\n  void - Spawn points generated via GenerateRandomPointsInRadius side effects\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If nSpawnMode is not 2 or 3, function returns immediately without generating points\n  - If nEntityRef is 0, uses provided nCenterX/nCenterY directly\n  - If nEntityRef is non-zero, extracts coordinates using Ordinal_10326/10329\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x112 (274) - Spawn type parameter passed to ordinal functions\n  0x230 (560) - Primary missile spawn point type\n  0x231 (561) - Secondary missile spawn point type (dual mode only)\n  0x2 - Single spawn type mode\n  0x3 - Dual spawn type mode\n\nOrdinal Functions:\n  Ordinal_10990(0x112) - Retrieves first spawn type value\n  Ordinal_10991(0x112) - Retrieves second spawn type value\n  Ordinal_10326(nEntityRef) - Extracts X coordinate from entity\n  Ordinal_10329(nEntityRef) - Extracts Y coordinate from entity",
