      "comment": "Plays a sound effect and creates a visual overlay based on effect type.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate pOverlayTarget is not NULL\n2. Switch based on nEffectType parameter\n3. Case 1: Create overlay 0x11f with mode 2, play sound 0x8f9\n4. Case 2: Create overlay 0x120 with mode 2, play sound 0x8fa\n5. Case 3: Create overlay 0x121 with mode 2, play sound 0x8fb\n6. Invalid type: Return without action\n\nParameters:\n  nSoundId - Sound source identifier passed to sound system\n  pOverlayTarget - Target unit/entity for overlay attachment (must not be NULL)\n  nEffectType - Effect type selector (1, 2, or 3)\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If pOverlayTarget is NULL, function returns immediately without action\n  - If nEffectType is not 1, 2, or 3, no overlay or sound is played\n  - All overlays use mode=2 in FUN_6fb931f0 call\n  - All sounds play at coordinates (0.0, 0.0) with param_5=0\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x11f (287) - Overlay ID for effect type 1\n  0x120 (288) - Overlay ID for effect type 2\n  0x121 (289) - Overlay ID for effect type 3\n  0x8f9 (2297) - Sound ID for effect type 1\n  0x8fa (2298) - Sound ID for effect type 2\n  0x8fb (2299) - Sound ID for effect type 3\n  2 - Overlay mode parameter (constant across all cases)\n\nFunction Pointer Context:\n  This function is part of a dispatch table at 0x6fbb01e8\n  Called indirectly via: CALL [EDI*4 + 0x6fbb01e8]\n  EDI index determines which handler function executes",
