      "comment": "Dispatches overlay visual effects and sound effects based on overlay type\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate fEnabled parameter is non-zero, return early if zero\n2. Check nOverlayType value using switch-like logic (DEC instructions)\n3. For nOverlayType == 1: Create overlay 0x122 and play sound 0x8ea\n4. For nOverlayType == 2: Create overlay 0x123 and play sound 0x8eb\n5. For nOverlayType == 3: Create overlay 0x124 and play sound 0x8ec\n6. For all other values: Return without action\n7. Call FUN_6fb931f0 to create overlay with mode 2 (no position params)\n8. Call FUN_6fb8d210 to play sound effect at entity location\n\nParameters:\n  pEntity - Pointer to entity structure (passed in ECX)\n  fEnabled - Boolean flag to enable effect dispatch (passed in EDX, low byte DL)\n  nOverlayType - Overlay type selector 1-3 (passed on stack at [ESP+0x14])\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If fEnabled is 0, function returns immediately without processing\n  - If nOverlayType is not 1, 2, or 3, no overlay or sound is created\n  - Each overlay type maps to specific overlay ID and sound ID pair\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x122 (290) - Overlay ID for type 1\n  0x123 (291) - Overlay ID for type 2  \n  0x124 (292) - Overlay ID for type 3\n  0x8ea (2282) - Sound effect ID for type 1\n  0x8eb (2283) - Sound effect ID for type 2\n  0x8ec (2284) - Sound effect ID for type 3\n  2 - Mode parameter for overlay creation (fixed position mode)\n\nNote: Function uses phantom register variable in_register_00000009 (undefined3) optimized away by decompiler during EDX bool parameter handling",
