      "api_calls": ["UNITS_GetOwnerGuid", "UNITS_GetUnitY", "GetMonsterResurrectMode", "InitRngSeed", "GetRandomBoundedValue", "GetRandomBoundedValue", "GetItemRandSeed", "MissileSetTargetUnit", "SetMissileTargetUnitId"],
      "instructions": ["0x1D4A0|SUB|ESP, 0x5c", "0x1D4A3|PUSH|EBX", "0x1D4A4|PUSH|EBP", "0x1D4A5|PUSH|ESI", "0x1D4A6|MOV|ESI, EDX", "0x1D4A8|PUSH|EDI", "0x1D4A9|MOV|EDI, dword ptr [ESP + 0x74]", "0x1D4AD|TEST|ESI, ESI", "0x1D4AF|MOV|EBX, ECX", "0x1D4B1|JZ|0x6faed4c5", "0x1D4B3|PUSH|ESI", "0x1D4B4|CALL|0x6fb98122", "0x1D4B9|PUSH|ESI", "0x1D4BA|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x14], EAX", "0x1D4BE|CALL|0x6fb9811c"],
      "comment": "Execute skill with different firing modes based on mode parameter.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Determine skill level: If nSkillId is 0, use dwTargetY as skill level, \n   otherwise call Ordinal_10326 to get skill level and Ordinal_10329 to get \n   target ID\n2. Branch based on nMode parameter to execute different skill behaviors\n3. Mode 1 (Single Missile): Fire single missile (ID 0x234) at target, set \n   light radius to 4 if missile has light, call FUN_6fb8d210 with code 0x985\n4. Mode 2 (Trigonometric Table): Call InitializeTrigonometricTable with \n   missile ID 0x238, skill level, target coordinates, and count 0x10\n5. Mode 3 (Multiple Projectiles): Get projectile count (0x118), seed RNG, \n   initialize missile structure with mode=3, loop to spawn projectiles at \n   random offsets\n\nParameters:\n  pCaster - Pointer to caster unit entity\n  nSkillId - Skill identifier (0 means use dwTargetY as skill level directly)\n  dwTargetX - Target X coordinate or target entity ID\n  dwTargetY - Target Y coordinate or skill level (if nSkillId is 0)\n  dwTargetId - Target entity ID or target Y coordinate\n  nMode - Execution mode: 1=single missile with light, 2=trigonometric pattern, \n          3=random projectile spread\n  IMPLICIT unaff_EDI - Unknown implicit EDI parameter passed to \n                       InitializeTrigonometricTable\n\nReturns:\n  None (void)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If nSkillId is 0, function treats dwTargetY as skill level instead of \n    coordinate\n  - Mode 3: If both random offsets are 0, sets X offset to 0x14 (20) to avoid \n    spawning at exact center\n  - Mode 3 initializes 0x16 (22) DWORDs on stack for missile structure\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x234 (564) - Missile ID for Mode 1 (single missile with light effect)\n  0x238 (568) - Missile ID for Mode 2 (trigonometric pattern)\n  0x239 (569) - Missile ID for Mode 3 (random spread projectiles)\n  0x985 (2437) - Effect code passed to FUN_6fb8d210\n  0x88 (136) - Offset to LightStruct pointer in missile structure\n  4 - Light radius value for Mode 1 missile\n  0x118 (280) - Parameter to Ordinal_10994 to get projectile count\n  0x10 (16) - Count parameter for trigonometric table\n  0x16 (22) - Number of DWORDs to zero-initialize for missile structure\n  3 - Missile mode value for Mode 3\n  0x14 (20) - Default X offset when both random offsets are zero\n  0x10000 (65536) - Multiplier for Y coordinate in packed coordinate value\n\nCoordinate Packing:\n  Final coordinate for Mode 3 is packed as: nOffsetY * 0x10000 + (dwOffsetX & 0xFFFF)\n  High word contains Y offset, low word contains X offset",
      "tags": ["PARAM_6", "STRUCT_Inventory", "STRUCT_Skill", "STRUCT_Room2", "STRUCT_Room1", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
