      "instructions": ["0x1D720|PUSH|ESI", "0x1D721|PUSH|EDI", "0x1D722|SUB|EDX, 0xfb", "0x1D728|MOV|EDI, ECX", "0x1D72A|JS|0x6faed7ff", "0x1D730|CMP|EDX, 0x1e", "0x1D733|JGE|0x6faed7ff", "0x1D739|LEA|ESI, [EDX + EDX*0x4]", "0x1D73C|SHL|ESI, 0x2", "0x1D73F|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [ESI + 0x6fba6d78]", "0x1D745|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0x1D747|JZ|0x6faed7b0", "0x1D749|PUSH|EAX", "0x1D74A|CALL|dword ptr [0x6fba60d0]", "0x1D750|TEST|EAX, EAX"],
      "comment": "Executes visual and audio effects for Assassin skills based on skill chart lookup.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Convert skill ID to table index by subtracting 0xFB (251, base Assassin skill ID)\n2. Validate index is in range [0, 29] (NUM_ASSASSIN_SKILLS = 30)\n3. Assert and exit if index out of bounds\n4. Calculate table offset: index * 0x14 (20 bytes per entry)\n5. Check if skill has callback function pointer at +0x08\n6. If callback exists, validate it with IsBadCodePtr\n7. Assert and exit if callback pointer is invalid\n8. Call the skill callback function\n9. If callback returns 0 (success), call Ordinal_10324 and handle state transitions\n10. If callback returns non-zero or no callback, apply default effects:\n    a. Apply state handler from +0x00 if non-zero\n    b. Apply overlay from +0x04 if not -1\n    c. Apply sound/light effect from +0x0C if not 0xFFFF\n\nParameters:\n  pAudioSource (ECX): AudioSourceData pointer - target for visual/audio effects\n  nSkillId (EDX): Skill ID in range [0xFB, 0x118] (251-280 Assassin skills)\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nStructure Layout (sgpctSkillChartAssassin, stride 0x14):\n  Offset  Size  Field              Description\n  +0x00   4     dwStateHandlerId   State handler ID for InitializeGameObjectProperties\n  +0x04   4     nOverlayId         Overlay ID (-1 = none) for InitializeOverlayData\n  +0x08   4     pfnDoSkill         Callback function pointer (NULL = use defaults)\n  +0x0C   4     nSoundId           Sound/light effect ID (0xFFFF = none)\n  +0x10   4     (unknown)          Reserved/padding\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Skill ID out of bounds: Triggers FogAssert and ExitApplicationWithCode(-1)\n  - Bad callback pointer: Triggers FogAssert and ExitApplicationWithCode(-1)\n  - Callback returns 0: Process state transitions on pAudioSource->dwValue1\n  - dwStateHandlerId == 0: Skip state handler initialization\n  - nOverlayId == -1: Skip overlay initialization\n  - nSoundId == 0xFFFF: Skip audio/lighting effect\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0xFB (251): First Assassin skill ID\n  0x1E (30): NUM_ASSASSIN_SKILLS count\n  0x14 (20): Skill chart entry stride\n  0x35A (858): Assert line number for bounds check\n  0x35F (863): Assert line number for callback validation\n\nSource: C:\\Projects\\Diablo2\\Source\\D2Client\\SKILLS\\SkillsAss.cpp",
      "tags": ["MOD_SKILLS", "PARAM_2", "PROP_NOCALLER", "UI_SKILLS", "CLASS_ASSASSIN", "SRC_SkillsAss.cpp"]
    },
