      "comment": "Initializes game object configuration with calculated stride-based offset.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Retrieve stride value from ordinal table entry 0x82 (130 decimal) via Ordinal_10990\n2. Retrieve base offset from ordinal table entry 0x94 (148 decimal) via Ordinal_10590\n3. Set configuration flag bit 0x40 in object flags field at offset +0xe8\n4. Calculate final offset: stride * (index - 1) + base offset\n5. Call InitializeGameObject with object pointer, class type 0x94, mode 0xffff, index value, and calculated offset\n\nParameters:\n- pObjectBase (ECX): Pointer to game object base structure with flags at offset +0xe8\n- nIndexValue (EDX): Index value for stride calculation (1-based index)\n\nReturns:\n- void (no return value)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Magic Number 0x82 (130): Ordinal table entry for stride lookup\n- Magic Number 0x94 (148): Ordinal table entry for base offset lookup; also used as class type parameter\n- Magic Number 0x40 (64): Flag bit set in object configuration flags (bit 6)\n- Magic Number 0xffff (65535): Mode selector indicating no array copy in InitializeGameObject\n- Offset 0xe8 (232): Location of object configuration flags field in structure\n- Stride Calculation: stride * (index - 1) + base_offset produces element offset for array-like structure access",
      "tags": ["PARAM_2", "PROP_NOCALLER"]
    },
