      "comment": "Initialize game object and play activation sound effect.\n\nAlgorithm:\n\n1. Set bit 0x40 in flags field at offset 0xe8 of input object\n2. Retrieve related object reference by calling FUN_6fb63760 with pObject\n3. If related object pointer is not NULL:\n   a. Call FUN_6fb7afc0 with pRelatedObject and zero parameter (positioning/movement function)\n   b. Play sound effect 0x9c3 using FUN_6fb8d210 with pRelatedObject as position source\n   c. Pass zero coordinates (0.0, 0.0) and zero extra parameter to sound function\n\nParameters:\n\npObject - Pointer to game object structure being initialized (GameObjectWithFlags *)\n          IMPLICIT: ECX register (fastcall convention)\n          Structure Requirements: Must contain dwFlags field at offset +0xe8\n\nReturns:\n\nvoid - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n\nIf FUN_6fb63760 returns NULL, sound playback and positioning calls are skipped.\nOnly the flag bit 0x40 is set on the input object in this case.\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n\n0xe8 (232 decimal) - Offset to dwFlags field in GameObjectWithFlags structure\n0x40 (64 decimal, bit 6) - Flag bit being set to mark object as initialized/active\n0x9c3 (2499 decimal) - Sound effect ID for activation sound\n0.0 (float) - Default X and Y coordinates passed to sound function (uses object position)\n\nStructure Layout:\n\nOffset | Size | Field Name | Type    | Description\n-------|------|------------|---------|----------------------------------\n0x00   | 232  | padding    | byte[]  | Unknown preceding fields\n0xe8   | 4    | dwFlags    | uint    | Object state flags (bit 6 = initialized)",
