      "comment": "Initializes a game object by setting ordinal-based flags and calling core initialization with calculated data offsets.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Retrieve ordinal data structure #1 for class type 0x95 (skill data tables)\n2. Set bit 0x40 in game object flags at offset 0xe8 (enable ordinal-based processing)\n3. Retrieve ordinal data structure #2 for class type 0x95\n4. Calculate data offset using stride from ordinal data #1 at offset 0x78\n5. Call InitializeGameObject with object pointer, class type, mode, index, and calculated offset\n\nParameters:\n- pGameObject (ECX): Pointer to GameObject structure to initialize\n- nOrdinalIndex (EDX): One-based ordinal index for data lookup (1-N range)\n\nReturns:\n- void (no return value)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Magic Number 0x95 (149): Class type identifier passed to ordinal lookup functions\n- Magic Number 0x40 (64): Flag bit set at offset 0xe8 to enable ordinal processing mode\n- Magic Number 0xffff (65535): Mode selector passed to InitializeGameObject (skip array copy mode)\n- Offset 0xe8: GameObject flags field modified via bitwise OR\n- Offset 0x78: Stride value in ordinal data structure #1 used for array indexing\n\nAlgorithm Verification:\n- Step 1 maps to 0x6faed8fc: CALL Ordinal_10589 with 0x95 parameter\n- Step 2 maps to 0x6faed903-0x6faed910: MOV/OR/MOV sequence modifying [pGameObject+0xe8]\n- Step 3 maps to 0x6faed916: CALL Ordinal_10590 with 0x95 parameter\n- Step 4 maps to 0x6faed91b-0x6faed924: Load stride, multiply by (index-1), add to base\n- Step 5 maps to 0x6faed936: CALL InitializeGameObject with 6 parameters\n\nIndex Calculation:\n- Formula: pOrdinalData2 + (stride * (nOrdinalIndex - 1))\n- stride = *(int *)(pOrdinalData1 + 0x78)\n- Converts 1-based index to zero-based offset\n- Multiplies by stride to get byte offset into data array\n- Adds base address from pOrdinalData2 to get final pointer\n",
