      "comment": "Plays resistance-based sound effect for hit class damage calculation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n\n1. Call Ordinal_10365() to get current hit class type (physical, fire, cold, etc.)\n2. Call FUN_6fb868b0(pUnit, hit class) to calculate resistance-adjusted damage value\n3. Decrement resistance value by 1 and apply signed saturation mask\n4. Call FUN_6fb8d210() to play sound effect 0x9c9 with calculated volume:\n   - Sound ID: 0x9c9 (2505 decimal)\n   - Source unit: pUnit\n   - Volume: Based on resistance-adjusted damage (float cast of (value - 1))\n   - Pan: 0.0 (centered)\n   - Flags: 0 (default playback)\n5. Return 1 (success)\n\nParameters:\n\n  pUnit (UnitAny*) - Pointer to unit structure being hit\n\nReturns:\n\n  int - Always returns 1 (success)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n\n  - Resistance value clamping: Uses signed saturation via SETS/DEC/AND pattern\n  - If calculated value is 0 or negative, result becomes 0xFFFFFFFF after saturation\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n\n  0x9c9 (2505) - Sound effect ID for resistance-based hit feedback",
