      "comment": "Process audio effect for entity based on state flags.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract entity flags from offset 0x44 and mask upper 24 bits\n2. Check if masked flags value is less than 0x600\n3. If condition fails, return early without processing audio\n4. Initialize audio parameters: zero value, zero float, small float constant (0x4 = 5.60519e-45)\n5. Call Ordinal_10365() to generate or retrieve sound identifier\n6. Call FUN_6fb86850() with entity and sound ID to get audio context\n7. Call FUN_6fb8d210() to process audio with context, entity, and float parameters\n8. Call FUN_6faed9e0() to find target entity for audio effect\n9. If target entity found (non-null):\n   a. Retrieve parameter 1 from target entity via Ordinal_10329()\n   b. Retrieve parameter 2 from target entity via Ordinal_10326()\n   c. Call Ordinal_10216() with entity offset 0x38 value, both parameters, and zero\n\nParameters:\n  pEntity - Pointer to game entity structure (int *)\n    Offset 0x44 (index 0x11): Entity state flags (upper 24 bits checked)\n    Offset 0x38 (index 0x0e): Handle or identifier used in final audio call\n\nReturns:\n  None (void function)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If (flags & 0xffffff00) >= 0x600, function returns immediately without processing\n  - If FUN_6faed9e0() returns NULL, skips Ordinal_10216 call\n  - Magic number 0x600 (1536 decimal) appears to be audio processing threshold\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x600 (1536 decimal) - Audio processing threshold for entity flags\n  0xffffff00 - Bit mask to isolate upper 24 bits of flags\n  0x4 (5.60519e-45 as float) - Small float constant for audio processing\n  0x11 (17 decimal) - Array index for flags field (offset 0x44 bytes)\n  0x0e (14 decimal) - Array index for handle/ID field (offset 0x38 bytes)\n\nStructure Layout:\n  Entity Structure (accessed as int array):\n  Offset  Size  Field Name       Type    Description\n  0x38    4     entityHandle     int     Handle/ID used in audio processing call\n  0x44    4     stateFlags       uint    Entity state flags (upper 24 bits checked)",
