      "comment": "Find nearest item to player unit by priority distance value\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize tracking variables: get default item from FUN_6fb63760\n2. Set min priority to 0xFFFFFFFF (max uint), max priority to 0\n3. Get player unit coordinates via Ordinal_10326 (X) and Ordinal_10329 (Y)\n4. Build query structure: zero 14 DWORDs at local_38, set field[0]=0x583, field[1]=5, field[2]=pUnit, field[3]=X, field[4]=Y\n5. Create context handle via Ordinal_11094 and initialize with Ordinal_11096(handle, X, Y)\n6. Execute item query via Ordinal_10401 with query parameters (handle, buffer, coords, mode=3)\n7. Open query results with Ordinal_10403(buffer) to populate item array\n8. Iterate through all items in result array (count in local_4c, array at local_60):\n   - For each item pointer, validate accessibility via FUN_6fb63e80(pUnit, pItem)\n   - Validate item state via Ordinal_10361(pUnit, pItem, 0)\n   - If both validations pass, read priority value from pItem[2] (offset +0x8)\n   - Track minimum priority item in local_74 (selected result)\n   - Track maximum priority item in local_6c (fallback option)\n   - Track last valid item in local_70 (iteration tracking)\n9. Apply selection logic: if last valid item equals min priority item, use max priority item instead\n10. Fallback: if no item selected, call FUN_6fb63760 to get default item\n11. Cleanup: close query with Ordinal_10402(buffer) and release context with Ordinal_11095(handle)\n12. Return selected item pointer\n\nParameters:\npUnit - Pointer to player unit entity requesting nearest item search\n\nReturns:\nPointer to selected item entity based on priority criteria, or default item if no valid items found\n\nSpecial Cases:\nWhen last valid item matches minimum priority item (line 68), function selects maximum priority item instead\nThis prevents selecting the same item repeatedly when multiple items have identical minimum priority\nIf no items pass validation checks, function returns default item from FUN_6fb63760\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x583 (1411 decimal) - Query structure identifier/type code at offset +0x0\n0x5 (5 decimal) - Query mode constant at offset +0x4  \n0x3 (3 decimal) - Search radius parameter for Ordinal_10401 (3-tile range)\n0xFFFFFFFF - Maximum uint32 value used as initial minimum priority sentinel\n0x8 - Byte offset to priority field in item structure (pItem[2])\n0xe (14 decimal) - Number of DWORDs to zero-initialize in query structure\n\nStructure Layout:\nQuery Structure (56 bytes starting at local_38):\nOffset | Size | Field Name       | Type  | Description\n-------|------|------------------|-------|----------------------------------\n+0x0   | 4    | dwTypeCode       | uint  | Query type identifier (0x583)\n+0x4   | 4    | dwMode           | uint  | Query mode constant (5)\n+0x8   | 4    | pPlayerUnit      | int*  | Pointer to requesting player unit\n+0xC   | 4    | dwUnitX          | uint  | Player X coordinate\n+0x10  | 4    | dwUnitY          | uint  | Player Y coordinate\n+0x14  | 40   | Reserved         | byte  | Additional query parameters (zeroed)",
