      "instructions": ["0x1DC20|PUSH|ESI", "0x1DC21|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0x1DC23|CALL|0x6fb63760", "0x1DC28|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0x1DC2A|JZ|0x6faedc4f", "0x1DC2C|PUSH|EAX", "0x1DC2D|CALL|0x6fb98578", "0x1DC32|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0x1DC34|JZ|0x6faedc4f", "0x1DC36|PUSH|0x0", "0x1DC38|PUSH|0x0", "0x1DC3A|PUSH|0x0", "0x1DC3C|MOV|EDX, ESI", "0x1DC3E|MOV|ECX, 0x9c0", "0x1DC43|CALL|0x6fb8d210"],
      "comment": "Validates client context and plays a specific sound effect if validation succeeds.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate client context path by calling FUN_6fb63760(nClientContext)\n2. If validation fails (returns 0), jump to return_failure\n3. Validate sound system availability by calling Ordinal_11019(nValidationResult)\n4. If sound system unavailable (returns 0), jump to return_failure\n5. Play sound effect 0x9c0 (2496 decimal) via FUN_6fb8d210 with:\n   - Sound ID: 0x9c0\n   - Client context: nClientContext\n   - Position X: 0.0\n   - Position Y: 0.0\n   - Flags: 0\n6. Return 1 (success)\n7. return_failure: Return 0 (failure)\n\nParameters:\n- nClientContext (int in ECX): Client context handle or pointer, passed through to sound system\n\nReturns:\n- 1 (true): Sound validation and playback succeeded\n- 0 (false): Validation failed or sound system unavailable\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n- 0x9c0 (2496): Sound effect ID for client-specific event\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Function short-circuits on first validation failure\n- Both client path and sound system must be available for sound playback\n- Sound plays at origin (0.0, 0.0) with no special flags",
      "tags": ["PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_1"]
    },
