      "instructions": ["0x1DC60|PUSH|ESI", "0x1DC61|PUSH|EDI", "0x1DC62|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0x1DC64|CALL|0x6fb63760", "0x1DC69|MOV|ECX, dword ptr [ESI + 0xe8]", "0x1DC6F|MOV|EDI, EAX", "0x1DC71|OR|ECX, 0x40", "0x1DC74|TEST|EDI, EDI", "0x1DC76|MOV|dword ptr [ESI + 0xe8], ECX", "0x1DC7C|JZ|0x6faedca3", "0x1DC7E|PUSH|EDI", "0x1DC7F|CALL|0x6fb9857e", "0x1DC84|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0x1DC86|JZ|0x6faedca3", "0x1DC88|XOR|EDX, EDX"],
      "comment": "Release associated object from game entity and send notification event.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Retrieve associated object pointer from game object via FUN_6fb63760\n2. Set flag bit 0x40 (64 decimal) at offset 0xe8 (232 decimal) in game object flags field\n3. Validate retrieved object pointer is non-NULL\n4. Call D2COMMON.Ordinal_10359 to validate object state\n5. If validation succeeds (non-zero return), proceed with cleanup\n6. Call FUN_6fb7afc0 with object pointer and 0 to release/cleanup object\n7. Send game event notification 0x9c3 (2499 decimal) with game object as parameter\n\nParameters:\n  pGameObject - Pointer to GameObjectWithFlags structure (236 bytes) containing entity data\n                Parameter passed via ECX register (__fastcall convention)\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If associated object pointer is NULL, function returns early without cleanup\n  - If D2COMMON.Ordinal_10359 validation fails (returns 0), cleanup is skipped\n  - Flag 0x40 is set regardless of whether associated object exists or validation succeeds\n  - Event 0x9c3 is only triggered if both object exists and validation passes\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x40 (hex) = 64 (decimal) - Flag bit set at offset 0xe8 to mark state change\n  0xe8 (hex) = 232 (decimal) - Offset to flags field in GameObjectWithFlags structure\n  0x9c3 (hex) = 2499 (decimal) - Game event notification ID for object release\n",
      "tags": ["PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_1"]
    },
