      "comment": "Initializes game object properties for a unit using hit class data.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Retrieve hit class value from unit via GetUnitInvWidth\n2. Get object ID from hit class base table via GetHitClassBaseValue  \n3. Initialize game object properties with object ID and unit at origin (0,0) with no flags\n4. Return TRUE (1) indicating success\n\nParameters:\n  nUnitPtr (int): IMPLICIT ECX - Pointer to UnitAny structure cast as int\n\nReturns:\n  dword - Always returns 1 (TRUE) on completion\n\nCallees:\n  - GetUnitInvWidth: Retrieves hit class/inventory width byte from unit\n  - GetHitClassBaseValue: Looks up object ID from hit class table (validates input, asserts on invalid range)\n  - InitializeGameObjectProperties: Applies object properties to unit at given position\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Position is always (0.0, 0.0) - unit positioned at origin\n  - Flags parameter is always 0 - no special initialization flags\n  - GetHitClassBaseValue may assert if hit class > 13 or unit is null\n  - extraout_var is decompiler artifact from byte-to-dword register promotion\n\nClassification: Initialization function - sets up unit object properties",
