      "comment": "Automatically picks up the nearest item if player state allows it.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if player flags at offset 0x44 (masked with 0xffffff00) are less than 0x600\n2. If check passes, initialize search parameters with 4.0 pixel radius\n3. Call Ordinal_10365() to get pickup radius configuration\n4. Call FUN_6fb86850 to get target entity for player\n5. Call FUN_6fb8d210 to perform entity search/validation with radius parameters\n6. Call FindNearestItemByPriority to locate the nearest prioritized item\n7. If item found, get item coordinates via Ordinal_10329 (X) and Ordinal_10326 (Y)\n8. Call Ordinal_10216 with player's entity handle at offset 0x38 and item coordinates to execute pickup\n\nParameters:\n  pPlayerUnit - Pointer to player unit structure (int *)\n    Offset 0x38 (56 bytes): Entity handle for pickup command\n    Offset 0x44 (68 bytes): Player state flags checked against 0x600 threshold\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If player flags >= 0x600, function returns immediately without attempting pickup\n  - If FindNearestItemByPriority returns NULL, no pickup is attempted\n  - Search radius initialized to 4.0 pixels (0x00000004 as float = 5.60519e-45)\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x44 (68 decimal) - Offset to player state flags in unit structure\n  0xffffff00 - Mask for extracting high 24 bits of flags\n  0x600 (1536 decimal) - Threshold value for pickup eligibility check\n  0x38 (56 decimal) - Offset to entity handle in unit structure\n  0x11 (17 decimal) - Array index equivalent to offset 0x44 (17 * 4 = 68 bytes)\n  0x0e (14 decimal) - Array index equivalent to offset 0x38 (14 * 4 = 56 bytes)\n  5.60519e-45 - Float representation of integer 4 (search radius in pixels)",
      "tags": ["PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_1"]
    },
