      "instructions": ["0x1E130|SUB|ESP, 0x8", "0x1E133|PUSH|EBX", "0x1E134|PUSH|EBP", "0x1E135|PUSH|ESI", "0x1E136|PUSH|EDI", "0x1E137|MOV|EBX, EDX", "0x1E139|MOV|EDI, ECX", "0x1E13B|PUSH|EBX", "0x1E13C|MOV|ESI, dword ptr [EDI + 0x38]", "0x1E13F|CALL|0x6fb9845e", "0x1E144|MOV|EBP, EAX", "0x1E146|PUSH|EBX", "0x1E147|CALL|0x6fb98458", "0x1E14C|MOV|EDX, dword ptr [EDI]", "0x1E14E|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x10], EAX"],
      "comment": "Initialize graphics rendering context for a unit entity.\n\nAlgorithm:\n\n1. Retrieve graphics data handle from unit structure (offset 0x38)\n2. Query graphics context dimensions (width and height)\n3. Store unit type from unit structure base field\n4. Configure graphics context with command 0x1101\n5. Initialize graphics data with zero coordinates (twice)\n6. Set graphics viewport with queried dimensions\n7. Set graphics mode parameter to 9\n8. Determine alpha/transparency based on unit type:\n   - Type 1 (Player): Read alpha from unit data at offset 0x1a0 (uint)\n   - Other types: Read alpha from unit data at offset 0x41 (byte)\n9. Apply alpha value (shifted left 8 bits) to graphics data\n10. Bind graphics data to unit pointer with zero flags\n\nParameters:\n\n  pUnit - Pointer to UnitAny structure containing entity data\n  dwGraphicsContext - Graphics rendering context handle from Ordinal_10949/10950\n\nReturns:\n\n  void - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n\n  - Unit type 1 treated specially with different data structure and alpha offset\n  - Alpha value from byte sources expanded to match uint format via left shift\n  - Graphics data handle stored at UnitAny offset 0x38 (field index 14)\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n\n  0x1101 - Graphics context configuration command\n  0 - Initial coordinate values for graphics data\n  9 - Graphics rendering mode parameter\n  0x38 (offset 0xe * 4) - Graphics data handle field in UnitAny\n  0x1a0 - Alpha field offset in player unit data structure\n  0x41 - Alpha field offset in non-player unit data structure\n  8 (shift) - Bit shift to align byte alpha to uint format\n\nStructure Field Access:\n\n  UnitAny:\n    +0x00 (offset 0) - dwUnitType (type discriminator: 1=Player, other=NPC/Object)\n    +0x04 (offset 1) - pUnitData (pointer to type-specific data structure)\n    +0x38 (offset 14) - pGraphicsData (graphics rendering data handle)",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Inventory", "PARAM_2", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
    },
