      "comment": "Calculate and apply path velocity for unit movement based on distance and velocity table\n\nAlgorithm:\n\n1. Retrieve unit field data at offset 0x38 from unit structure\n2. Extract X and Y coordinates from dwUnknownId parameter using Ordinal_10976 and Ordinal_10977\n3. Get velocity-related value from unit field using Ordinal_10147\n4. Validate velocity value bits 8-15 is non-zero, abort with assertion if zero\n5. Calculate path length using Ordinal_10398 with unit pointer and coordinates\n6. Enforce minimum path length of 1 if calculated value is less than 1\n7. Calculate velocity scale factor using formula path length << 16 divided by velocity value << 12\n8. Clamp velocity scale factor to maximum by decrementing if greater than 1\n9. Search g_aVelocityTable to find matching entry where nPathLength >= nThreshold\n10. Calculate final velocity using entry multiplier times nPathLength plus entry base value\n11. Enforce minimum velocity of 500 if calculated value is less\n12. Call FUN_6fb979a0 to prepare unit for movement\n13. Call FUN_6fb97b90 to set unit velocity with negated calculated velocity as Y-component\n14. Call FUN_6fb97f00 to apply velocity scale factor to unit\n\nParameters:\n\n  pUnit (UnitAny *) - Pointer to UnitAny structure receiving velocity calculation\n  dwUnknownId (uint) - Encoded coordinate or identifier used to extract X and Y position\n\nReturns:\n\n  void - Function modifies unit state directly through called functions",
