      "instructions": ["0x1E2C0|SUB|ESP, 0x14", "0x1E2C3|PUSH|EBX", "0x1E2C4|PUSH|EBP", "0x1E2C5|PUSH|ESI", "0x1E2C6|MOV|EBX, EDX", "0x1E2C8|PUSH|EDI", "0x1E2C9|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0x1E2CB|PUSH|EBX", "0x1E2CC|CALL|0x6fb9845e", "0x1E2D1|MOV|EDI, EAX", "0x1E2D3|PUSH|EBX", "0x1E2D4|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x20], EDI", "0x1E2D8|CALL|0x6fb98458", "0x1E2DD|MOV|EBP, EAX", "0x1E2DF|PUSH|ESI"],
      "comment": "Validate skill target coordinates and initialize skill execution context.\n\nAlgorithm:\n\n1. Extract target X and Y coordinates from graphics context\n2. Retrieve current unit position coordinates for comparison\n3. Determine skill ID based on unit type (monster uses 0x23f, player uses actual skill ID)\n4. Check if unit is already at target position\n5. If not at target and unit can move, handle error based on unit type\n6. If at target position, set skill preparation state and update coordinates\n7. Handle post-validation setup based on unit type and skill\n8. For Phoenix Strike, calculate projectile trajectory\n9. Validate line of sight and collision detection\n10. If valid target, setup graphics effect and return success\n\nParameters:\n\npUnit - Pointer to UnitAny structure being controlled\ndwGraphicsContext - Graphics context handle containing target information\nnSkillParam - Skill execution parameter (non-zero triggers animation)\n\nReturns:\n\n1 - Skill targeting validated successfully and initialized\n0 - Skill targeting failed validation (not at target position)",
      "tags": ["PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PARAM_3", "STRUCT_Skill", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
