      "instructions": ["0x1E610|PUSH|ESI", "0x1E611|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0x1E613|PUSH|EDI", "0x1E614|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [ESI + 0x38]", "0x1E617|PUSH|EAX", "0x1E618|CALL|0x6fb985f6", "0x1E61D|MOV|EDI, dword ptr [ESI]", "0x1E61F|DEC|EDI", "0x1E620|NEG|EDI", "0x1E622|SBB|EDI, EDI", "0x1E624|AND|EDI, 0xffffff80", "0x1E627|ADD|EDI, 0x100", "0x1E62D|CMP|EAX, EDI", "0x1E62F|JZ|0x6faee68d", "0x1E631|PUSH|EBX"],
      "comment": "Validates and corrects skill animation speed based on character type.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Retrieve current animation speed from skill data at offset 0x38 (dwAnimationSpeed field)\n2. Calculate expected animation speed based on character type:\n   - If *pSkillData == 1: expectedSpeed = 0x100 (256 decimal)\n   - Otherwise: expectedSpeed = 0x80 (128 decimal)\n3. If current speed matches expected speed, return immediately (no correction needed)\n4. Query skill target information to get X coordinate bounds (min/max)\n5. If no target found, set bounds to zero\n6. Otherwise, extract min/max X coordinates from target data\n7. Retrieve skill flags and unit GUID for correction context\n8. Apply animation speed correction using Ordinal_10126 with all context data\n9. Update skill data structure with corrected speed and bounds via FUN_6fb61180\n10. Initialize compression state for skill animation data\n11. Send skill update notification (opcode 0x36) to synchronize state\n\nParameters:\n- pSkillData: Pointer to skill data structure (minimum 60 bytes)\n  - Offset 0x00 (uint): Character type flag (1 = specific type, other = default)\n  - Offset 0x38 (uint): Current animation speed value (dwAnimationSpeed)\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If current animation speed already matches expected value, function returns early without corrections\n- Character type 1 uses doubled animation speed (256) compared to default (128)\n- If skill has no target (Ordinal_10323 returns 0), bounds are zeroed before correction\n- Animation speed mismatch typically occurs after skill state changes or network desync\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n- 0x0E (14 decimal): Offset to dwAnimationSpeed field in skill structure\n- 0x100 (256 decimal): Animation speed for character type 1\n- 0x80 (128 decimal): Default animation speed for other character types\n- 0xFFFFFF80 (-128 as signed): Bitmask for default speed calculation\n- 0x36 (54 decimal): Skill update notification opcode\n- 0 (parameter 3): Reserved/unused parameter in speed correction call",
      "tags": ["PARAM_1"]
