      "comment": "Process unit graphics context based on current state flags\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Acquire graphics context handle with task ID 0xFFFFFFFF (current task)\n2. Retrieve context state flags from graphics context\n3. Read unit type from first field of UnitAny structure\n4. If graphics context is valid (non-zero):\n   a. Check if flag 0x100 (SKILL_VALIDATION_REQUIRED) is set\n   b. If set, validate skill target and initialize graphics\n   c. If validation returns 0 (failure), exit early\n   d. Check if flag 0x80 (INITIALIZE_GRAPHICS) is set\n   e. If set, initialize unit graphics context and calculate path velocity, then return\n   f. If unit type is not 1 (not a player), release graphics context with flag 0x1000\n\nParameters:\n  pUnit - Pointer to UnitAny structure containing unit data and type\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Early return if graphics context is NULL (0)\n  - Early return if skill validation fails when flag 0x100 is set\n  - Player units (type 1) skip graphics context release in final branch\n  - Flag 0x80 and 0x100 are mutually exclusive execution paths\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0xFFFFFFFF - Current task ID for graphics context acquisition\n  0x100 (256) - SKILL_VALIDATION_REQUIRED flag - triggers skill target validation\n  0x80 (128) - INITIALIZE_GRAPHICS flag - triggers graphics initialization\n  0x1000 (4096) - Context release flag for non-player units\n  0x1 (1) - Player unit type constant\n  0x84 (132) - Graphics context type parameter for Ordinal_10949",
      "tags": ["PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_1"]
