      "api_calls": ["FindInfoNodeById", "GetUnitFlags", "GetSkillTargetY", "GetSkillFlags", "SetUnitScrollPos", "GetUnitInvWidth", "SetSkillClientFunc"],
      "instructions": ["0x1E820|PUSH|EBX", "0x1E821|PUSH|EBP", "0x1E822|PUSH|ESI", "0x1E823|PUSH|EDI", "0x1E824|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0x1E826|MOV|EDX, 0x8f", "0x1E82B|CALL|0x6fb98602", "0x1E830|MOV|EDI, EAX", "0x1E832|PUSH|EDI", "0x1E833|CALL|0x6fb9849a", "0x1E838|TEST|EDI, EDI", "0x1E83A|MOV|EBX, EAX", "0x1E83C|JZ|0x6faee8e3", "0x1E842|TEST|BH, 0x1", "0x1E845|JZ|0x6faee8bd"],
      "comment": "Process unit AI behavior based on graphics context flags.\n\nAlgorithm:\n\n1. Retrieve graphics context handle for current frame\n2. Query context flags to determine required AI behavior mode\n3. Early return if no valid graphics context exists\n4. Check flag 0x100 (skill/item interaction mode):\n   a. Validate skill target and initialize skill execution\n   b. Return early if validation fails\n   c. Retrieve item type and context parameters\n   d. Search for valid target item (prioritize type 6 = gold/special items)\n   e. If no item found via type search, use nearest item by priority\n   f. If still no valid target, set unit action state to 0x400 (idle/ready)\n   g. If valid target found:\n      - Set unit target pointer to target item\n      - Clear path state\n      - Retrieve skill context parameters\n      - Calculate path to target with zero coordinates (auto-calculate)\n      - Initialize movement/path system for approach\n5. Check flag 0x80 (graphics initialization mode):\n   a. If NOT set, apply state flag 0x1000 to graphics context (standby)\n   b. If set:\n      - Initialize unit graphics context with current frame data\n      - Calculate and set path velocity for unit movement\n      - Return\n\nParameters:\n\n  pUnit - Pointer to UnitAny structure representing the game entity\n\nReturns:\n\n  void - No return value (state changes applied directly to unit structure)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n\n  - Flag 0x100 and 0x80 can both be set; 0x100 is processed first\n  - Item type 6 is special-cased for direct search failure fallback\n  - Zero coordinates (0.0, 0.0) in path calculation trigger auto-targeting\n  - State 0x400 represents idle/ready action when no valid interaction target\n  - State 0x1000 represents standby/waiting mode in graphics context\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n\n  0x100 (256 decimal) - Skill/item interaction mode flag in context flags\n  0x80 (128 decimal) - Graphics initialization mode flag in context flags\n  0x400 (1024 decimal) - Unit action state: idle/ready for interaction\n  0x1000 (4096 decimal) - Graphics context state: standby/waiting mode\n  6 - Item type for gold or special pickup items\n  0x15 (21 decimal) - Offset in UnitAny structure for action state field (pPath field at offset 0x54 bytes)",
      "tags": ["PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_1"]
    },
