      "comment": "Creates skill-based projectiles at target coordinates.\n\nThis function handles projectile creation for specific skill types (0xF9, 0xFC, 0xFF)\nby finding a valid collision tile at the target location and spawning projectiles.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call Ordinal_10323 to get skill from unit (returns in pSkill via calling convention)\n2. Set unit flag at offset 0xE8 by OR-ing with 0x40 (mark projectile creation active)\n3. If no skill, exit early\n4. Get skill target Y coordinate (represents skill type ID)\n5. Check if skill type matches 0xF9 (249), 0xFC (252), or 0xFF (255)\n6. If not matching type, exit early\n7. Get skill owner type as target X coordinate\n8. Get skill target X coordinate as target Y\n9. Get room from unit and find region at target coordinates\n10. Find valid collision tile at target location (flags=0x1000, count=1)\n11. Zero-initialize projectile parameters structure (22 dwords = 88 bytes)\n12. Set projectile flags to 0x2001\n13. Store owner unit pointer in params\n14. Store skill param in params\n15. Get skill target type and store in params\n16. Copy validated tile coordinates to params\n17. Call InitializeAndAllocateProjectile first time (skill target type)\n18. Set params skill type to 0x73 (115) for second projectile\n19. Call InitializeAndAllocateProjectile second time\n20. If second projectile created successfully, call InitializeGameObjectProperties\n    with mode 0x9C6 (2502)\n\nParameters:\n  pUnit - UnitAny pointer to unit creating projectile (ECX)\n  dwSkillParam - Skill parameter value (EDX)\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Returns early if pSkill is NULL\n  - Returns early if skill type not 0xF9, 0xFC, or 0xFF\n  - Only calls InitializeGameObjectProperties if second projectile created\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x40 - Unit flag bit for projectile creation active\n  0xE8 - Unit offset to flags field (pUnit[4].dwGfxFrame in UnitAny[4])\n  0xF9 (249), 0xFC (252), 0xFF (255) - Valid skill type IDs for projectile creation\n  0x2001 - Projectile flags (enables specific projectile behaviors)\n  0x1000 - Collision tile search flags\n  0x73 (115) - Secondary projectile skill type\n  0x9C6 (2502) - Game object property mode for projectile initialization\n  0x16 (22) - Number of dwords to zero-initialize in projectile params",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_MonsterData", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PARAM_2", "PROP_NOCALLER", "STRUCT_Skill", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
