      "comment": "Renders a UI control with modified transparency/alpha blending.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Retrieve current alpha/light value from control structure at offset 0x38\n2. Calculate modified alpha based on transparency mode:\n   - Mode 0: Add 0x2A (42 decimal) for higher transparency\n   - Mode 1: Add 0x15 (21 decimal) for lower transparency\n3. Mask result with 0x3F (63 decimal, 6-bit mask) and apply temporarily\n4. Check viewport state with Ordinal_10010\n5. Calculate screen coordinates:\n   - If in viewport mode (return != 0): Convert world coordinates to screen\n   - If not in viewport: Get direct screen coordinates\n6. Call rendering function FUN_6fb91fe0 with calculated coordinates\n7. Restore original alpha/light value\n\nParameters:\n  pControl - Pointer to UI control structure (offset 0x38 contains alpha/light value)\n  dwColor - Color value or rendering flags\n  nTransparencyMode - Transparency mode selector:\n                      0 = Higher transparency (add 42)\n                      1 = Lower transparency (add 21)\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Alpha mask 0x3F limits blending to 6-bit range (0-63)\n  - Different transparency deltas suggest two visibility states\n  - Viewport check determines coordinate system (world vs screen)\n  - First DWORD of pControl checked for zero (control state flag)\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x38 (56) - Offset to alpha/light value in control structure\n  0x2A (42) - Transparency delta for mode 0 (higher transparency)\n  0x15 (21) - Transparency delta for mode 1 (lower transparency)\n  0x3F (63) - Alpha channel mask (6-bit, limits to 0-63 range)\n  0x60 (96) - Flags parameter for coordinate conversion function\n  0x0E (14) - Array index for alpha value (56/4 = 14th uint element)",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Inventory", "PARAM_3", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
