      "instructions": ["0x1EE50|SUB|ESP, 0xc", "0x1EE53|PUSH|EBX", "0x1EE54|PUSH|EBP", "0x1EE55|PUSH|ESI", "0x1EE56|PUSH|EDI", "0x1EE57|MOV|EDI, ECX", "0x1EE59|MOV|EDX, 0x97", "0x1EE5E|CALL|0x6fb98602", "0x1EE63|MOV|EDX, dword ptr [EDI]", "0x1EE65|XOR|ECX, ECX", "0x1EE67|TEST|EDX, EDX", "0x1EE69|SETZ|CL", "0x1EE6C|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0x1EE6E|MOV|EBP, EAX", "0x1EE70|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [EDI + 0x38]"],
      "comment": "Finalizes a skill effect and performs cleanup operations on the unit.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Look up skill info node with ID 0x97 from the unit\n2. Check if unit type (field_0) is zero to determine tile flag mode\n3. Get linked unit pointer from offset 0x38\n4. Calculate tile flags: 0x100 if unit type non-zero, 0x180 if zero\n5. If skill info not found, exit early\n6. Get skill owner type (target X coordinate) and target Y from skill info\n7. Get skill flags from skill info\n8. If (flags & 0x3) == 0x3 (both bits set - full completion):\n   a. Clear unit state flag 0x36 (skill active flag)\n   b. Get unit collision width attribute\n   c. Get room from unit\n   d. Clear map cell flags in radius around target position\n   e. Update tile attributes on linked unit\n   f. Set item data field 0x50 (0x3C01 or 0x1C09 based on unit type)\n   g. Clear skill client function (set to NULL)\n   h. Find stat 0x9E3 in unit stat list and initialize inventory state\n   i. Return\n9. Else if (flags & 0x1) != 0 (only bit 0 set - partial):\n   a. Set animation data upper bits to 3\n   b. Set offset 0x54 to 0x500\n10. Return\n\nParameters:\n  pUnit (ECX) - Pointer to unit to finalize skill effect on\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Early exit if skill info node 0x97 not found\n  - Different cleanup paths based on skill flags:\n    Flags 0x3: Full cleanup with map/tile/inventory updates\n    Flags 0x1: Partial update with animation state change only\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x97 - Skill info node ID for this skill type\n  0x36 - Unit state flag for skill active\n  0x100/0x180 - Tile flag values (based on unit type)\n  0x3C01/0x1C09 - Item data field values (based on unit type)\n  0x9E3 - Stat ID for inventory-related stat\n  0x500 - Animation/state value for partial completion\n  0x3 - Completion flag check mask (both bits must be set)",
      "tags": ["PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_1", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
