      "comment": "Logs ability errors while managing critical section synchronization state.\n\nAlgorithm:\n\n1. Retrieve global critical section handle via Ordinal_10950\n2. If critical section exists, check lock state flags via Ordinal_10985\n3. If bit 0 (lock held flag) is set, set bit 1 (nested operation flag) via Ordinal_10984\n4. Look up error handler by code 0x9e3 via FUN_6fb86ce0\n5. Process error handler via FUN_6fb8d060\n6. Send event notification (type 0x36) to unit via Ordinal_10486\n\nParameters:\n\n  pUnit (UnitAny *) - Pointer to game entity experiencing ability error\n\nReturns:\n\n  void - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n\n  - If critical section handle is NULL, function returns early without logging\n  - Bit 0 in lock flags indicates critical section is currently locked\n  - Bit 1 is set to indicate nested error logging during locked state\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n\n  0x97 (151) - Critical section identifier for ability error logging\n  0x9e3 (2531) - Error handler lookup code for ability errors\n  0x36 (54) - Event notification type for ability error events\n  0x1 - Lock held flag (bit 0)\n  0x2 - Nested operation flag (bit 1)\n\nError Handling:\n\n  - Null critical section causes silent early return\n  - Error logging occurs even if critical section is locked\n  - Setting bit 1 prevents recursive error logging",
      "tags": ["PARAM_1"]
    },
