      "comment": "Creates multiple projectile missiles in a spread pattern from a shooter unit.\n\nAlgorithm:\n\n1. Set shooter unit flag 0x40 at offset 0x3a (marks unit as missile source)\n2. If fCreateTargeted is set, create initial targeted missile:\n   a. Decrement nMissileCount by 1\n   b. Calculate target coordinates using CalculateMissileTargetCoordinates\n   c. If missile created successfully and fCollisionFlag set, enable collision at offset 0xe\n   d. Apply dwTargetY parameter to missile\n3. Zero-initialize 88-byte missile creation structure (0x16 DWORDs = 88 bytes)\n4. Populate missile creation structure:\n   a. dwMissileFlags = 0x21 (base flags)\n   b. pMissileOwner = pShooterUnit\n   c. dwSourceX = Ordinal_10326(pShooterUnit) - get unit X coordinate\n   d. dwSourceY = Ordinal_10329(pShooterUnit) - get unit Y coordinate\n   e. dwDestinationX = dwTargetX\n   f. pfnCallback = FUN_6faef270 (missile update callback)\n   g. If fCollisionFlag set, OR dwMissileFlags with 0x2000\n   h. dwMissileType = dwMissileId\n5. Calculate current unit coordinates into nCoordX and nCoordY arrays\n6. Validate coordinates are non-zero, abort with error 0x5f if validation fails\n7. Create remaining missiles in loop (nMissileCount iterations):\n   a. Store current shot index in nShotIndex\n   b. Create missile using FUN_6fb77720 with structure pointer\n   c. If missile created and fCollisionFlag set, enable collision at offset 0xe\n   d. Apply dwTargetY parameter to missile\n   e. Increment loop counter\n\nParameters:\n\npShooterUnit - Pointer to UnitAny shooter entity creating missiles\ndwMissileId - Missile type identifier for creation\nnMissileCount - Total number of missiles to create in spread pattern\ndwTargetX - X coordinate of target destination\nfCollisionFlag - Flag to enable missile collision detection (non-zero enables)\ndwTargetY - Y coordinate of target destination (applied via Ordinal_10377)\nfCreateTargeted - Flag to create initial targeted missile before spread (non-zero enables)\n\nIMPLICIT:\nNone\n\nReturns:\n\nvoid - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n\nIf fCreateTargeted is non-zero, creates one targeted missile before creating spread missiles and decrements nMissileCount\nIf coordinates are zero after validation, aborts with error message at 6fbb1614\nIf fCollisionFlag is set, enables collision at missile offset 0xe (piVar1[0xe]) for each created missile\nIf nMissileCount <= 0 after initial decrement, no spread missiles are created\n\nNote: Function uses 3 SSA temporary variables optimized by decompiler (iVar2 for loop counter, piVar1 for created missile pointers, puVar3 for zero-init pointer). Stack padding bytes (in_stack_0000000d, in_stack_00000015) are artifacts from bool parameter alignment.\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n\n0x40 (64 decimal) - Shooter unit active missile flag at offset 0x3a\n0x21 (33 decimal) - Base missile flags for creation structure\n0x2000 (8192 decimal) - Collision enabled flag for missile creation\n0x16 (22 decimal) - DWORD count for structure zero-initialization (88 bytes total)\n0x3a (58 decimal) - Offset in UnitAny for missile shooter flag\n0x0e (14 decimal) - Offset in missile structure for collision flag\n0x5f (95 decimal) - Error code for coordinate validation failure\n0xffffffff (-1) - Fatal error code passed to FUN_6fb9a10f\n\nStructure Layout:\n\nMissile Creation Structure (88 bytes at local_58):\nOffset  Size  Field Name         Type        Description\n------  ----  -----------------  ----------  -----------\n+0x00   4     dwMissileFlags     uint        Missile behavior flags (0x21 base, 0x2000 collision)\n+0x04   4     pMissileOwner      UnitAny *   Pointer to shooter unit\n+0x08   4     dwMissileType      uint        Missile type identifier\n+0x0c   4     dwSourceX          uint        Starting X coordinate from shooter\n+0x10   4     dwSourceY          uint        Starting Y coordinate from shooter\n+0x14   4     dwDestinationX     uint        Target X coordinate\n+0x18   4     