      "comment": "Fires missile type 461 (0x1CD) and sets skill active flag on unit.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call FireMissileWithTargetValidation with unit, missile ID 461, and flags\n2. Set bit 0x40 at unit offset +0xE8 (dwUnitFlags or skill active state)\n3. Return (void)\n\nParameters:\npUnit (UnitAny *): Pointer to the unit firing the missile (ECX, __fastcall)\ndwFlags (uint): Missile behavior flags passed to firing function (EDX, __fastcall)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- No callers found - likely invoked via function pointer or callback table\n- Missile ID 461 (0x1CD) is hardcoded - specific skill/ability missile\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x1CD (461): Missile type identifier\n0xE8: Offset to unit flags/state field in UnitAny structure\n0x40: Bit flag for skill/missile active state\n\nStructure Access:\nOffset  Size  Field              Description\n+0xE8   4     dwUnitFlags        Unit state flags, bit 0x40 set after missile fire",
