      "comment": "Creates a single projectile missile of type 478 (0x1DE) at target coordinates.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Push hardcoded parameters for CreateMultipleShotMissiles call\n2. Call CreateMultipleShotMissiles with:\n   - pShooterUnit as missile owner\n   - Missile ID 0x1DE (478)\n   - Count = 1 (single missile)\n   - dwTargetX as destination X\n   - fCollisionFlag = false (no collision)\n   - dwTargetY = 0x200 (512 fixed)\n   - fCreateTargeted = false\n3. Return\n\nParameters:\npShooterUnit (UnitAny *): Pointer to unit firing the missile (ECX, __fastcall)\ndwTargetX (uint): Target X coordinate for missile destination (EDX, __fastcall)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- No callers found - likely invoked via function pointer table or skill callback\n- Single missile creation (count=1) unlike spread-pattern variants\n- Fixed Y target of 0x200 (512) regardless of input\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x1DE (478) - Missile type identifier (specific projectile type)\n0x200 (512) - Fixed target Y coordinate\n0x1 (1)     - Missile count (single shot)\n0x0 (0)     - Collision and targeted flags disabled\n\nClassification: Thunk/Wrapper - Wraps CreateMultipleShotMissiles with hardcoded missile parameters",
      "tags": ["PARAM_2", "PROP_NOCALLER", "PROP_SMALL"]
