      "api_count": 1,
      "api_calls": ["MissileSetTargetUnit"],
      "instructions": ["0x1F510|SUB|ESP, 0x58", "0x1F513|MOV|EDX, ECX", "0x1F515|PUSH|EDI", "0x1F516|MOV|ECX, 0x16", "0x1F51B|XOR|EAX, EAX", "0x1F51D|LEA|EDI, [ESP + 0x4]", "0x1F521|STOSD.REP|ES:EDI", "0x1F523|MOV|ECX, dword ptr [ESP + 0x68]", "0x1F527|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [ESP + 0x64]", "0x1F52B|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x8], EDX", "0x1F52F|MOV|EDX, dword ptr [ESP + 0x60]", "0x1F533|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x1c], ECX", "0x1F537|LEA|ECX, [ESP + 0x4]", "0x1F53B|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x4], 0x1", "0x1F543|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x18], EAX"],
      "comment": "Play two sequential audio sounds using the D2Client audio engine.\n\nThis function initializes an audio parameter structure, creates audio sources for two consecutive sound IDs (0x1e0 and 0x1df), and plays the second sound using the D2Common audio playback system.\n\nAlgorithm:\n\n1. Allocate 0x58-byte stack structure for audio parameters\n2. Zero-initialize entire parameter structure (0x16 dwords = 88 bytes)\n3. Populate audio parameter structure with provided values:\n   - Set flags field to 1 (enable audio)\n   - Store dwParam1, dwParam2, dwParam3 into structure offsets\n   - Set initial sound ID to 0x1e0\n4. Create first audio source by calling FUN_6fb77720 with sound ID 0x1e0\n5. Update sound ID to 0x1df in parameter structure\n6. Create second audio source by calling FUN_6fb77720 with sound ID 0x1df\n7. If second audio source created successfully (non-NULL):\n   - Call Ordinal_11140 to play/start the audio source with dwParam4\n8. Return (audio playback continues asynchronously)\n\nParameters:\n\n  dwParam1 - First data value stored at parameter structure offset 0x30\n  dwParam2 - Second data value stored at parameter structure offset 0x18\n  dwParam3 - Third data value stored at parameter structure offset 0x08\n  dwParam4 - Parameter passed to Ordinal_11140 for audio playback control\n\nReturns:\n\n  void - Function does not return a value\n  Audio playback initiated if successful\n\nSpecial Cases:\n\n  - If FUN_6fb77720 returns NULL for sound 0x1df, playback is skipped\n  - First sound (0x1e0) is created but not explicitly played\n  - Only the second sound (0x1df) is played via Ordinal_11140\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n\n  0x1e0 (480 decimal) - First audio sound ID\n  0x1df (479 decimal) - Second audio sound ID  \n  0x16 (22 decimal) - Structure size in dwords (88 bytes total)\n  0x58 (88 decimal) - Stack frame size in bytes\n\nAudio Parameter Structure Layout:\n\nOffset | Size | Field Name      | Type | Description\n-------|------|-----------------|------|----------------------------------\n 0x00  |  4   | dwFlags         | uint | Audio flags (set to 1)\n 0x08  |  4   | dwValue3        | uint | Third parameter value\n 0x14  |  4   | dwSoundId       | uint | Sound ID (0x1e0 then 0x1df)\n 0x18  |  4   | dwValue2        | uint | Second parameter value\n 0x30  |  4   | dwValue1        | uint | First parameter value\n ...   | ...  | (other fields)  | ...  | Remainder zero-initialized",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Path", "PARAM_4", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
    },
