      "comment": "Processes and triggers sound effect for a game unit.\n\nAlgorithm:\n\n1. Get map ID (Ordinal_10949 with 0xffffffff)\n2. Get compression handle for unit (Ordinal_10342)\n3. Get file handle for sound (Ordinal_10968 with map ID, enable flag 1)\n4. Validate all resources exist (pUnit, map ID, file handle)\n5. Check if sound already active for unit (FUN_6fb86ce0 with sound ID 0x91f)\n6. If compression handle valid, check if compressed (Ordinal_10082)\n7. If not compressed and no active sound, create new sound (FUN_6fb8d210 with ID 0x91f)\n8. Play sound effect three times (FUN_6faef620 called 3x)\n9. If sound already active, modify existing sound (FUN_6fb8cf80 with modify flag)\n\nParameters:\n\n  pUnit (UnitAny*) - Pointer to game unit structure\n\nReturns:\n\n  void - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n\n  - Early return if pUnit is null\n  - Early return if map ID cannot be retrieved\n  - Early return if file handle is null\n  - Skips sound creation if already active for unit\n  - Only modifies existing sound if one is already playing\n\nMagic Numbers:\n\n  0xffffffff - Invalid/default map ID parameter\n  0x91f (2335) - Sound effect ID for unit action\n  0x1 - Enable flag for file handle retrieval\n  0x3 - Number of sound effect repetitions",
