      "instructions": ["0x1F620|SUB|ESP, 0xa8", "0x1F626|PUSH|EBX", "0x1F627|PUSH|EBP", "0x1F628|PUSH|ESI", "0x1F629|PUSH|EDI", "0x1F62A|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x18], EDX", "0x1F62E|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0x1F630|MOV|EDI, 0xfffffff9", "0x1F635|MOV|ECX, 0x5", "0x1F63A|XOR|EDX, EDX", "0x1F63C|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x30], EDI", "0x1F640|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x58], EDI", "0x1F644|LEA|EDI, [ESI + 0x2c]", "0x1F647|MOV|EBX, 0x7", "0x1F64C|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x24], ECX"],
      "comment": "Spawns a randomized sound effect with positional variations\n\nCreates a sound spawn configuration with coordinate offsets selected from a randomized\nlookup table, then spawns the sound through the audio system. Typically called in\nsuccession (3x) to create layered or repeated sound effects.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize anOffsetTable[20] with X/Y coordinate offset pairs\n   - Indices 0-15 contain offset values (7, 5, 0, -5, -7)\n   - Pattern: X offsets at even indices, Y offsets at +8 indices\n2. Generate random seed via Ordinal_10918() and save for later use\n3. Get random offset index (0-15) via Ordinal_10918()\n4. Retrieve unit position via Ordinal_10326/10329 (X/Y getters)\n5. Look up X/Y offsets from anOffsetTable using random index\n6. Determine sound ID based on third random value:\n   - Value 1 → 0x247\n   - Value 2 → 0x249  \n   - Default → 0x245\n7. Zero-initialize spawn configuration structure (88 bytes at anOffsetTable[16])\n8. Populate spawn structure fields:\n   - dwFlags = 3 (spawn mode flags)\n   - pUnit = pSourceUnit (source unit pointer)\n   - dwSoundId = selected sound ID\n   - nTargetX = unit X + random X offset\n   - nTargetY = unit Y + random Y offset\n   - nExtentY = Y offset magnitude (calculated from lookup)\n   - nExtentX = -(X offset magnitude)\n   - nContext = passed-through context value\n9. Call FUN_6fb77720 to spawn sound with configuration\n10. If spawn successful, configure sound source:\n    - Set random seed via FUN_6fb97b10\n    - Update X position via Ordinal_11140\n    - Update Y position via Ordinal_11142\n\nParameters:\n  pSourceUnit - UnitAny * - Unit originating the sound effect\n  nContext - int - Context value passed through to spawn structure (purpose unknown)\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If FUN_6fb77720 returns NULL, sound spawn failed silently\n  - Parent function calls this 3 times in succession for layered effects\n  - Random offsets create spatial variation in sound positioning\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x245 (581 dec) - Default sound ID for effect\n  0x247 (583 dec) - Alternate sound ID (random variant 1)\n  0x249 (585 dec) - Alternate sound ID (random variant 2)\n  0x16 (22 dec) - Structure clear loop count (88 bytes / 4 = 22 dwords)\n  3 - Spawn configuration flags (meaning unknown)\n  7 - Maximum positive coordinate offset\n  -7 (0xFFFFFFF9) - Maximum negative coordinate offset  \n  5 - Medium positive coordinate offset\n  -5 (0xFFFFFFFB) - Medium negative coordinate offset\n\nOffset Lookup Table Structure:\n  Index    Value    Description\n  0        7        X offset variant 1\n  1        5        Y offset variant 1\n  2        0        X offset variant 2 (no offset)\n  3        -5       X offset variant 3\n  4        -7       X offset variant 4\n  5        -5       Y offset variant 2\n  6        0        Y offset variant 3 (no offset)\n  7        5        Y offset variant 4\n  8        0        X offset variant 5\n  9        5        Y offset variant 5\n  10       7        X offset variant 6\n  11       5        Y offset variant 6\n  12       0        Y offset variant 7\n  13       -5       Y offset variant 7\n  14       -7       X offset variant 8\n  15       -5       Y offset variant 8\n  \n  Note: X offsets at indices 0-15, corresponding Y offsets at indices +8\n  Pattern provides 8 distinct offset pair combinations for sound positioning",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "STRUCT_Room2", "STRUCT_Room1", "STRUCT_ItemData", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData", "STRUCT_StatList", "STRUCT_MonsterData", "STRUCT_Path", "PARAM_2", "STRUCT_Skill"]
