      "comment": "Access resource type 249 and perform operation with parameter.\n\nAlgorithm:\n\n1. Call Ordinal_10949 with -1 (0xFFFFFFFF) to obtain resource handle for type 0xF9 (249 decimal)\n2. Check if returned handle is non-zero (valid)\n3. If handle valid, call Ordinal_10980 with handle and dwParameter to perform operation\n4. Return regardless of outcome (no error propagation)\n\nParameters:\n\ndwResourceType (uint): Resource type identifier - NOTE: Currently unused, hardcoded to 0xF9 in EDX register before Ordinal_10949 call\ndwParameter (uint): Operation parameter passed to Ordinal_10980 for processing\n\nIMPLICIT: EDX = 0xF9 (249 decimal) - Resource type constant loaded before Ordinal_10949 call\n\nReturns:\n\nvoid - No return value, no error indication\n\nSpecial Cases:\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0xFFFFFFFF (-1): Passed to Ordinal_10949, likely indicates \"current process/thread\" or \"default context\"\n- 0xF9 (249): Resource type identifier loaded into EDX, overrides dwResourceType parameter\n- 0x10 (16): Stack cleanup value in RET instruction (2 parameters × 4 bytes)",
