      "instructions": ["0x1F9E0|PUSH|EBX", "0x1F9E1|PUSH|ESI", "0x1F9E2|PUSH|EDI", "0x1F9E3|MOV|EDI, ECX", "0x1F9E5|MOV|ESI, EDX", "0x1F9E7|PUSH|EDI", "0x1F9E8|CALL|0x6fb983c2", "0x1F9ED|SUB|ESI, 0xdd", "0x1F9F3|JS|0x6faefa9e", "0x1F9F9|CMP|ESI, 0x1e", "0x1F9FC|JGE|0x6faefa9e", "0x1FA02|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0x1FA04|JZ|0x6faefa98", "0x1FA0A|LEA|ESI, [ESI + ESI*0x4]", "0x1FA0D|MOV|EBX, dword ptr [ESP + 0x10]"],
      "comment": "Process Druid skill activation and execute skill-specific callback function\n\nAlgorithm:\n\n1. Validate unit pointer using Ordinal_10323\n2. Calculate skill table index: nTableOffset = (nSkillId - 0xDD)\n3. Validate skill ID is in Druid range (0xDD to 0xFB, decimal 221 to 251)\n   - If out of range: Log error \"nSkillId >= 0 && nSkillId < NUM_SKILLS\" and terminate\n4. If validation passed and nTableOffset in valid range (0 to 30):\n   a. Calculate byte offset into SkillParams table: nTableOffset = nTableOffset * 0x14\n   b. Check if dwTargetId at table[nTableOffset+0] is not 0xFFFF (valid target)\n      - If valid: Call CalculateMissileTargetCoordinates with target ID\n      - Set unit flag: pUnit[0x3A] |= 0x40 (skill processed flag)\n   c. Check function pointer at table[nTableOffset+4]\n      - If NULL: Set unit flag pUnit[0x3A] |= 0x40\n      - If non-NULL: \n        * Validate pointer with IsBadCodePtr\n        * If invalid: Log error with file/line and terminate\n        * If valid: Call skill-specific callback via function pointer\n   d. Retrieve audio context for unit with Ordinal_10958(pUnit, 0)\n   e. If audio context exists: Remove it with RemoveAudioContextFromList\n5. Return\n\nParameters:\n\npUnit - Pointer to UnitAny structure representing player/monster entity\nnSkillId - Skill ID to activate (Druid skill range 0xDD-0xFB)\ndwTargetFlags - Target flags for skill activation (passed to CalculateMissileTargetCoordinates)\n\nReturns:\n\nvoid - No return value, terminates process on validation failures\n\nSpecial Cases:\n\nSkill ID out of Druid range (< 0xDD or >= 0xFC): Logs assertion failure and terminates\nInvalid function pointer in skill table: Logs assertion with source file \"sgpctSkillChartDruid_nSkillId\" and terminates\nTarget ID 0xFFFF (invalid target): Skips missile calculation but continues processing\nNULL function pointer: Sets unit flag but skips callback execution\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n\n0xDD (221) - Minimum Druid skill ID (base offset for table lookup)\n0x1E (30) - Number of Druid skills in table\n0x14 (20) - Size of SkillParams structure in bytes\n0xFFFF (65535) - Invalid target ID marker\n0x40 (64) - Skill processed flag bit in unit flags at offset 0x3A\n0x252 (594) - Error line number for skill ID range assertion\n0x25D (605) - Error line number for function pointer validation\n\nError Handling:\n\nSkill ID validation: nSkillId must be in range 0xDD-0xFB (30 Druid skills)\nFunction pointer validation: IsBadCodePtr check prevents crashes from corrupted skill table\nAssertion failures call Ordinal_10023 (log) then FUN_6fb9a10f (terminate)\n\nStructure Layout:\n\nSkillParams (20 bytes stride):\nOffset  Size  Field Name         Type        Description\n0x00    4     dwTargetId         uint        Missile target ID (0xFFFF = no target)\n0x04    4     pfnCallback        void(*)()   Skill effect callback function pointer\n0x08    12    (reserved)         byte[12]    Additional skill parameters\n\nFlag Bits:\n\npUnit[0x3A] bit flags (offset 0xE8 from unit base):\n0x40 (bit 6) - Skill effect processed flag",
      "tags": ["MOD_SKILLS", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PROP_NOCALLER", "UI_SKILLS", "PARAM_3", "SRC_SkillsDruid.cpp", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "CLASS_DRUID"]
