      "comment": "Executes Druid skill visual and audio effects based on skill chart lookup.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate skill ID is in Druid range (0xDD-0xFA, indices 0-29)\n2. Assert if skill ID out of bounds and terminate\n3. Calculate table offset: (nSkillId - 0xDD) * 0x14 (20-byte entries)\n4. If start skill function pointer exists:\n   a. Validate pointer with IsBadCodePtr\n   b. Assert if invalid pointer and terminate\n   c. Call start skill function\n   d. If function returns 0 (success):\n      - Call Ordinal_10324 (D2Common function)\n      - Process state transitions via ClearUnitStateAndProcessTransition\n      - Return early\n5. If effect ID at offset +0 is non-zero:\n   - Call InitializeGameObjectProperties with effect ID\n6. If overlay ID at offset +4 is not -1:\n   - Call InitializeOverlayData with overlay ID and type 2\n7. If sound ID at offset +12 is not 0xFFFF:\n   - Call InitializeAudioLightingEffect with sound ID\n\nParameters:\n  pAudioSource (ECX): Pointer to AudioSourceData for skill effect context\n  nSkillId (EDX): Skill identifier (must be 0xDD-0xFA for Druid skills)\n\nReturns:\n  void - Effects applied directly to game state\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Invalid skill ID causes assertion failure and application exit\n  - Invalid function pointer causes assertion failure and application exit\n  - Skill IDs 0xDD = 221 (SKILL_DRUID_START), 0xFA = 250 (max Druid skill)\n  - Table has 30 entries (NUM_DRUID_SKILLS = 0x1E)\n\nStructure Layout (sgpctSkillChartDruid entry, 20 bytes):\n  Offset  Size  Field           Type      Description\n  0x00    4     dwEffectId      uint      Game object effect identifier\n  0x04    4     nOverlayId      int       Overlay animation ID (-1 = none)\n  0x08    4     pfnStartSkill   FARPROC   Skill start callback function\n  0x0C    4     wSoundId        ushort    Sound effect ID (0xFFFF = none)\n  0x10    4     dwReserved      uint      Padding/reserved\n\nGlobals Referenced:\n  g_aSkillChartDruid (0x6fba7240): Base of Druid skill chart table",
      "tags": ["MOD_SKILLS", "PARAM_2", "PROP_NOCALLER", "UI_SKILLS", "SRC_SkillsDruid.cpp", "CLASS_DRUID"]
