      "comment": "Creates a projectile from a mercenary unit toward the player unit.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get mercenary position via GetMercenaryPosition(pUnit)\n2. If no mercenary position found, return early (no projectile created)\n3. Initialize 22-dword (0x58 byte) projectile configuration struct to zero\n4. Set configuration flags to 0x2 (adjust target mode)\n5. Set projectile type to 0x205\n6. Set source unit pointer to pUnit in both slots [1] and [2]\n7. Store dwTargetData parameter in slot [12] (0x2c offset)\n8. Calculate X delta: Ordinal_10326(mercenary) - Ordinal_10326(pUnit)\n9. Calculate Y delta: Ordinal_10329(mercenary) - Ordinal_10329(pUnit)\n10. Call InitializeAndAllocateProjectile with configuration\n11. If projectile created successfully:\n    a. Set target Y offset to negated Y delta via MissileSetTargetUnit\n    b. Set target X offset via SetMissileTargetUnitId\n\nParameters:\npUnit (UnitAny *, ECX): Source unit (player) for projectile targeting\ndwTargetData (dword, EDX): Target configuration data stored in projectile config\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value; projectile creation is fire-and-forget\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Returns early without action if GetMercenaryPosition returns NULL\n- Projectile direction is from mercenary toward player (mercenary pos - player pos)\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x2: Projectile flags - adjust target coordinate mode\n0x205: Projectile type ID (mercenary-specific projectile)\n0x16 (22): Number of dwords in projectile configuration struct\n0x58 (88): Total size of projectile config struct in bytes\n\nOrdinal References:\nOrdinal_10326: D2Common.GetUnitX - retrieves unit X coordinate\nOrdinal_10329: D2Common.GetUnitY - retrieves unit Y coordinate\n\nStructure Layout (ProjectileConfig at local_58):\nOffset  Size  Field           Type        Description\n0x00    4     dwFlags         dword       Projectile behavior flags (0x2)\n0x04    4     pSourceUnit1    UnitAny *   Source unit pointer slot 1\n0x08    4     pSourceUnit2    UnitAny *   Source unit pointer slot 2 \n0x10    4     dwProjectileType dword      Projectile type ID (0x205)\n0x24    4     dwDeltaX        uint        X coordinate delta\n0x28    4     nDeltaY         int         Y coordinate delta  \n0x2c    4     dwTargetParam   dword       Target parameter from input",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_MonsterData", "STRUCT_Path", "PARAM_2", "PROP_NOCALLER", "STRUCT_Room2", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
