      "api_count": 19,
      "api_calls": ["FogAssert", "UNITS_GetUnitY", "UNITS_GetOwnerGuid", "SetPositionCoords", "GetPathPosY", "GetPathPosX", "SetPathDirectionToTarget", "GetMissileTemplateRecord", "GetRandomBoundedValue", "UNITS_GetOwnerGuid", "...+9 more"],
      "instructions": ["0x1FC70|SUB|ESP, 0x6c", "0x1FC73|PUSH|EBX", "0x1FC74|PUSH|EBP", "0x1FC75|PUSH|ESI", "0x1FC76|MOV|EBX, ECX", "0x1FC78|PUSH|EDI", "0x1FC79|MOV|ECX, 0x16", "0x1FC7E|XOR|EAX, EAX", "0x1FC80|LEA|EDI, [ESP + 0x24]", "0x1FC84|STOSD.REP|ES:EDI", "0x1FC86|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x10], EDX", "0x1FC8A|MOV|ECX, EBX", "0x1FC8C|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x24], 0x25", "0x1FC94|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x28], EBX", "0x1FC98|CALL|0x6fb63760"],
      "comment": "Spawns mercenary projectiles for a unit attack.\n\nClassification: Worker function - Creates and configures multiple projectile entities\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Zero-initialize 0x16 DWORDs of local missile spawn context on stack\n2. Set missile type to 0x25 (mercenary projectile type)\n3. Store owner unit pointer in spawn context\n4. Get mercenary position from GetMercenaryPosition\n5. If mercenary position valid:\n   a. Assert path pointer exists at unit offset 0x38\n   b. Get path Y coordinate via Ordinal_10329\n   c. Get path X coordinate via Ordinal_10326\n   d. Update position with SetPositionCoords\n   e. Validate unit and process global data\n6. Get unit path Y position and X position\n7. Set path direction to target via SetPathDirectionToTarget\n8. Get missile template record for ID 0x18e\n9. Get graphics info field value for rendering\n10. Calculate target count: template[0x7c] + projectileCount - 1\n11. Extract missile speed offset from template[0x58]\n12. Loop 2 times (spawn 2 projectiles):\n    a. Set missile ID to 0x18e, randomize to 399 (0x18f) if random(2) != 0\n    b. Get X/Y coordinates via ordinals\n    c. Calculate random speed from g_anSpeedModifiers lookup table\n    d. Get current path X/Y positions\n    e. Allocate and initialize projectile via InitializeAndAllocateProjectile\n    f. If allocation succeeds:\n       - Assert projectile path exists\n       - Set cell direction count\n       - Calculate and set missile target X: (offset << 8) / targetCount\n       - Set missile target unit, field 2C, drawable coordinates\n       - Update graphics info offsets\n       - Set GFX property values with negative velocity: (-2 * (gfxInfo+8)) / targetCount\n\nParameters:\npUnit (ECX) - UnitAny*, owner unit (mercenary) initiating projectile spawn\nnProjectileCount (EDX) - int, base count affecting target calculation\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Asserts on null path pointer at offsets 0xbd and 0xde\n- Calls ExitApplicationWithCode(-1) on assertion failure\n- Always spawns exactly 2 projectiles regardless of nProjectileCount\n- nProjectileCount affects dwTargetCount calculation, not actual count\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x25: Missile type identifier for mercenary projectiles\n- 0x18e (398): Primary missile template ID\n- 0x18f (399): Alternative missile template ID (random selection)\n- 0x7c: Offset to target count field in missile template\n- 0x58: Offset to speed modifier byte in missile template\n- 0x38: Offset to path pointer in UnitAny structure\n- 0xbd, 0xde: Assert line numbers in source file\n\nGlobal References:\n- g_anSpeedModifiers (0x6fba74d8): int[5] lookup table for random speed values\n- szAssertVarPath (0x6fbb1708): \"hPath\" assert variable name\n- szAssertSourceFile (0x6fbb1710): Source file path for asserts",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PROP_NOCALLER", "STRUCT_Room1", "STRUCT_ItemData", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData", "MOD_SKILLS", "STRUCT_StatList", "STRUCT_MonsterData", "STRUCT_Path", "PARAM_2", "UI_SKILLS", "STRUCT_Skill", "SRC_SkillsEMon.cpp"]
