      "comment": "Initialize viewport object with centered velocity calculation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Create or retrieve viewport object for object type 0x194 (404 decimal)\n2. Get dimension value from viewport object (value is shifted by 11 bits = 2048 scale)\n3. Add 0x28 (40 decimal) padding to dimension\n4. Query external function Ordinal_11122 to get velocity divisor\n5. If divisor is zero, use half dimension as velocity (dimension / 2)\n6. Otherwise, calculate velocity as dimension divided by divisor\n7. Set viewport position to origin (x=0, y=0) with scaled dimension\n8. Set viewport velocity to (x=0, y=0, -velocity) with fixed-point shift flag\n9. Apply viewport updates to finalize changes\n\nParameters:\n  pViewportObject (int *) - Pointer to viewport or game object requiring viewport initialization\n  dwObjectType (uint) - Object type identifier passed to viewport creation (0x194 = 404)\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If Ordinal_11122 returns 0, velocity defaults to dimension / 2\n  - Negative velocity (-nVelocityDivisor) suggests downward or backward scrolling\n  - Magic number 0x194 (404) identifies specific viewport/object type\n  - Magic number 0x28 (40) adds padding to dimension calculation\n  - Shift value 0xb (11 bits) represents fixed-point scale factor of 2048\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x194 (404 decimal) - Viewport object type identifier\n  0x28 (40 decimal) - Dimension padding offset\n  0xb (11 decimal) - Fixed-point shift for 2048 scale factor",
      "tags": ["PARAM_2", "PROP_NOCALLER"]
