      "comment": "Initializes game object properties and fires missile type 0x222 at target.\n\nClassification: Wrapper function - combines initialization and missile firing operations.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize game object properties with fixed parameters:\n   - Object type: 0x1217\n   - Asset index: 0\n   - Position: (0.0, 0.0)\n   - Flags: 0\n2. Fire missile type 0x222 using entity and flags from parameters\n3. Return 1 (always succeeds regardless of missile firing result)\n\nParameters:\n  nEntityId (int, ECX): Entity/unit identifier for missile source\n  dwFlags (uint, EDX): Additional missile behavior flags passed to FireMissileWithTargetValidation\n\nReturns:\n  int: Always returns 1 (success indicator)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Return value is hardcoded to 1 and does not reflect actual missile firing success\n  - FireMissileWithTargetValidation result is ignored\n  - Object type 0x1217 is a fixed constant for this specific missile setup\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x1217: Game object type identifier for initialization\n  0x222: Missile type identifier\n  0x0: Zero values for asset index, position, and flags\n\nCallers: None found (may be called via function pointer or unresolved reference)",
