      "comment": "Creates scatter missiles based on monster stat for a source unit.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get scatter count from monster stat 0x11D (285) scaled by monster level\n2. Get source unit X and Y coordinates via Ordinal_10326/10329\n3. Initialize 14-element search parameter array to zero\n4. Set unit filter to 0x3002 (missile units) and store source unit\n5. Get room from source unit for spatial search\n6. Initialize unit find data structure with room and coordinates\n7. Collect all units matching filter in the area\n8. For each collected unit (up to nMissileCount):\n   a. Get unit coordinates via ordinals\n   b. Create missile type 0x24B (587) at unit position with mode=1\n   c. If missile created successfully:\n      - Get base target X coordinate from missile\n      - Generate random offset in range [0,20) then subtract 10 for [-10,+10)\n      - Set randomized target position on missile\n      - Set missile data field 0x2C to same position\n9. Free the unit find data allocation\n\nParameters:\n  pSourceUnit (ECX): Source unit to spawn missiles around\n  nMonsterLevel (EDX): Monster level for stat scaling\n\nReturns:\n  void (EAX set to 1 on exit but return type is void)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If no units found (nMissileCount <= 0), loop skipped\n  - Null missile from InitializeStructureAndCallHandler skips target setup\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x11D (285): Monster stat ID for scatter count\n  0x3002: Unit filter flags for missiles\n  0x24B (587): Missile type ID\n  0x14 (20): Random range for scatter offset\n  0x0E (14): Search parameter array size\n  0x2C (44): Offset to missile data field for target position",
