      "comment": "Launches a catapult missile of type 0x197 (407) with trajectory.\n\nThunk/Wrapper function that calls LaunchCatapultMissileWithTrajectory\nwith a hardcoded missile type ID.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Push target parameter onto stack\n2. Load missile type 0x197 into EDX\n3. Call LaunchCatapultMissileWithTrajectory(pUnit, 0x197, nTargetParam)\n4. Return 1 (success)\n\nParameters:\n  pUnit (ECX) - Pointer to UnitAny structure (source unit launching missile)\n  nTargetParam (EDX/stack) - Target parameter passed to trajectory calculation\n\nReturns:\n  int - Always returns 1 (success indicator)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  None - simple wrapper with no validation\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x197 (407) - Hardcoded missile type ID for this catapult variant\n\nDecompiler Discrepancy:\n  Decompiler shows void return, but assembly shows MOV EAX,0x1 before RET,\n  indicating function returns success value of 1.\n\nNote: No callers found - may be called via function pointer table or orphaned.",
