      "comment": "Applies skill effect at unit's current position if coordinates are valid.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call CalculateUnitCoordinates to retrieve unit's X and Y map coordinates\n2. If coordinate calculation succeeds (returns non-zero), proceed with effect application\n3. Call FUN_6fb77e50 to apply skill effect with effect type 0x226, coordinates, and effect parameters\n4. If coordinate calculation fails, return without applying effect\n\nParameters:\n  pUnit: Pointer to UnitAny structure representing game entity (player, monster, NPC)\n  dwEffectType: Effect type identifier passed to skill effect function (stored in EDX)\n  IMPLICIT ESI: Preserved across calls, contains original pUnit pointer\n  IMPLICIT EDI: Preserved across calls, contains original dwEffectType value\n\nReturns:\n  void - Function applies skill effect as side effect if coordinates valid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  If CalculateUnitCoordinates returns 0 (coordinate calculation failed), function returns early without applying effect\n  Effect type 0x226 corresponds to offset in BnetData structure (_9 field at +0x226)\n  \nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x226 (550 decimal): Offset to byte field in BnetData structure, used as effect type parameter",
