      "instructions": ["0x201F0|PUSH|ESI", "0x201F1|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0x201F3|CMP|dword ptr [ESI], 0x1", "0x201F6|JNZ|0x6faf0242", "0x201F8|PUSH|ESI", "0x201F9|CALL|0x6fb985e4", "0x201FE|CMP|EAX, 0x1ec", "0x20203|JNZ|0x6faf0242", "0x20205|PUSH|0x0", "0x20207|PUSH|0x0", "0x20209|PUSH|0x0", "0x2020B|MOV|EDX, ESI", "0x2020D|MOV|ECX, 0x989", "0x20212|CALL|0x6fb8d210", "0x20217|PUSH|0x1"],
      "comment": "Apply special skill effects based on player type and class.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if player unit type is Player (dwType == 1)\n2. Query player skill level using Ordinal_11056\n3. If skill level equals 0x1ec (492), apply special skill initialization:\n   a. Apply skill effect 0x989 (2441) via FUN_6fb8d210\n   b. Get player X coordinate via Ordinal_10329\n   c. Get player Y coordinate via Ordinal_10326\n   d. Create skill 0x1c3 (451) at player location via FUN_6fb77d70\n   e. If skill creation succeeds, apply additional effect 0xc0 (192) via Ordinal_10377\n4. Check if player class ID is Assassin (dwClassId == 0x220 / 544)\n5. If Assassin, create skill 0x266 (614) at player location\n6. Return success (1)\n\nParameters:\n  pPlayer - Pointer to UnitAny structure representing the player\n    IMPLICIT: ECX register (passed via __fastcall convention)\n\nReturns:\n  1 - Always returns success\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Function applies skills only for specific conditions (type 1, skill level 0x1ec, class 0x220)\n  - Skills are created at player's current coordinates\n  - No error checking on coordinate retrieval\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x1 (1) - Player unit type identifier\n  0x1ec (492) - Required skill level threshold\n  0x989 (2441) - Skill effect ID for initial application\n  0x1c3 (451) - Primary skill ID to create\n  0xc0 (192) - Secondary effect parameter\n  0x220 (544) - Assassin class identifier\n  0x266 (614) - Assassin-specific skill ID\n\nStructure Layout:\n  UnitAny structure (48 bytes):\n  Offset  Size  Field Name   Type   Description\n  +0x00   4     dwType       uint   Unit type (0=Player, 1=Monster, etc.)\n  +0x04   4     dwClassId    uint   Class/monster type identifier",
      "tags": ["PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_1"]
