      "comment": "Applies a colored overlay visual effect to a game unit.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Retrieve renderer ID using configuration index 0x12d (301)\n2. Retrieve red color component value using configuration index 0x12d\n3. Retrieve green color component value using configuration index 0x12d\n4. Retrieve blue color component value using configuration index 0x12d\n5. Scale each RGB component from 0-25 range to 0-1000 range by multiplying by 1000 and dividing by 0x19 (25)\n6. Store rendering state with scaled RGB values using SetRenderingState\n7. Apply overlay effect code 0xc5 (197) to the unit with mode 2 (persistent overlay)\n\nParameters:\npUnit - Pointer to UnitAny structure representing the game entity to apply overlay effect\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value, function only applies visual overlay effect\n\nSpecial Cases:\nConfiguration Index: 0x12d (301 decimal) is used for all four retrieval operations to fetch renderer and RGB component values from game configuration.\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x12d (301) - Configuration index for overlay color settings\n0x19 (25) - Maximum value in source color scale (0-25 range)\n1000 - Target scale maximum for normalized color values (0-1000 range)\n0xc5 (197) - Overlay effect identifier code\n2 - Overlay mode (persistent overlay that remains visible)\n",
      "tags": ["PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_1"]
    },
