      "comment": "Creates visual effect objects for a skill execution.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call Ordinal_10323 (D2Common.GetUnitSkill) to get the skill from nUnitId\n2. If skill is null, exit early\n3. Get skill owner type (X coordinate) from skill via GetSkillOwnerType\n4. Get skill target X (Y coordinate) from skill via GetSkillTargetX\n5. Create first effect object with type 0x73 (115) via InitializeStructureAndCallHandler\n6. If first object created successfully, configure it with InitializeGameObjectProperties\n   using object ID 0x99a (2458) with zero position offsets\n7. Create second effect object with type 0x207 (519) via InitializeStructureAndCallHandler\n\nParameters:\n  nUnitId (ECX) - Unit ID to retrieve skill from\n  dwFlags (EBP) - Flags passed to effect object creation\n\nReturns: void\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x73 (115)  - First effect object type ID\n  0x207 (519) - Second effect object type ID  \n  0x99a (2458) - Game object properties ID for first effect\n\nCallees:\n  Ordinal_10323 - D2Common.GetUnitSkill - retrieves Skill* for unit\n  GetSkillOwnerType - Gets owner type/X coordinate from skill\n  GetSkillTargetX - Gets target X/Y coordinate from skill\n  InitializeStructureAndCallHandler - Creates effect structure objects\n  InitializeGameObjectProperties - Configures game object display properties",
