      "comment": "Creates a visual effect missile and clears the unit's graphics state flag bit 6.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call CreateMissileWithScaledRange with skill ID 0x137 (311) and coordinates 0x20B/0x20C\n2. If missile creation succeeds (non-NULL return):\n   a. Allocate and initialize graphics info field for the missile\n   b. Set drawable object coordinates with Z offset -37 (0x25)\n   c. Set graphics info field bit 1 to mark as initialized\n3. Clear bit 6 (0x40) of the unit's dwGfxFrame field at offset 0xE8\n4. Return (void function)\n\nParameters:\n  pUnit - Pointer to the source UnitAny structure (ECX, __fastcall)\n  nTargetY - Target Y coordinate passed to missile creation (EDX, __fastcall)\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  If missile creation fails (returns NULL), graphics initialization is skipped\n  The flag clear at offset 0xE8 always executes regardless of missile success\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x137 (311) - Skill ID for the visual effect missile type\n  0x20B (523) - Target X coordinate constant\n  0x20C (524) - Target Y coordinate constant (passed as range param)\n  -0x25 (-37) - Z offset for drawable object positioning\n  0xBF - AND mask to clear bit 6 (0x40) of dwGfxFrame\n  0xE8 - Offset to dwGfxFrame field in UnitAny structure (array index 4)\n\nFlag Bits:\n  Bit 6 (0x40) at offset 0xE8 - Graphics state flag cleared by this function\n\nClassification: Worker function - Creates visual effect and updates unit graphics state",
