      "comment": "Initializes a handle object with field values from a source object.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Obtain a handle from the context using Ordinal_10323\n2. Retrieve the source object pointer from the context using FUN_6fb63760\n3. Validate source object is not NULL\n4. Validate source object passes integrity check (Ordinal_11018)\n5. Copy first field from source to handle using Ordinal_10980 (Ordinal_10326)\n6. Copy second field from source to handle using Ordinal_10981 (Ordinal_10329)\n7. Copy third field from source offset +0x4 to handle using Ordinal_10982\n8. Return success status\n\nParameters:\n  pContext - Context pointer containing source object reference\n\nReturns:\n  1 (0x1) - Successfully initialized handle with all fields copied\n  0 (0x0) - Failed validation: source object NULL or integrity check failed\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If FUN_6fb63760 returns NULL, initialization fails immediately\n  - If Ordinal_11018 validation fails, no fields are copied\n\nStructure Layout:\nSource object has at least one direct field:\n  Offset  Size  Field Name  Type  Description\n  +0x0    4     field1      uint  First field accessed via Ordinal_10326\n  +0x4    4     field3      uint  Third field accessed directly\n  (field2 accessed via Ordinal_10329, offset unknown)\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x1 (decimal 1) - Success return value indicating all fields copied\n  0x0 (decimal 0) - Failure return value for validation errors\n  0x4 (decimal 4) - Byte offset to third field in source object structure",
