      "comment": "Executes a monster skill that fires a missile and initializes game object properties.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Retrieve the active skill from the unit via Ordinal_10323\n2. Assert that skill pointer is valid (fatal error if null)\n3. Get skill owner type (used as X coordinate for position)\n4. Get skill target X coordinate (used as Y coordinate for position)\n5. Set position coordinates on unit's path structure at offset +0x38\n6. Fire missile type 0x73 with target validation and flags\n7. Initialize game object properties with type 0x99a\n\nParameters:\n  pUnit (UnitAny *): Pointer to the unit executing the skill (ECX)\n  dwFlags (dword): Missile behavior flags passed to FireMissileWithTargetValidation (EDX)\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If skill retrieval returns NULL, triggers FogAssert and exits with code -1\n  - The skill owner type and target X are cast to ushort for SetPositionCoords\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x38: Offset to pPath (path structure pointer) in UnitAny\n  0x73: Missile type identifier for skill projectile\n  0x99a: Game object property type identifier (2458 decimal)\n  0x2c5: Assert line number in source file (709 decimal)\n\nSource File: C:\\Projects\\Diablo2\\Source\\D2Client\\SKILLS\\SkillsEMon.cpp",
