      "comment": "Thunk wrapper that initializes a context handle with ID 0x13d (317).\n\nClassification: Thunk/Wrapper\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Save EDX register (caller-saved for __fastcall)\n2. Load context type ID 0x13d into EDX as second parameter\n3. Call InitializeContextHandleOrCreateNew(pContext, 0x13d)\n4. Return result from called function\n\nParameters:\n  pContext - Pointer to context structure to initialize (passed in ECX)\n  IMPLICIT EDX = 0x13d - Context handle type identifier\n\nReturns:\n  dword - Result from InitializeContextHandleOrCreateNew (success/handle value)\n\nCalled Function:\n  InitializeContextHandleOrCreateNew at 0x6faf4b20 - Creates or initializes context handle\n\nNotes:\n  This is a simple thunk that forwards to InitializeContextHandleOrCreateNew\n  with a fixed context type ID of 0x13d. The value 0x13d (317 decimal) likely\n  identifies a specific context type or resource category.",
