      "comment": "Creates a missile and sets its velocity vector based on unit position delta.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Create missile at target coordinates via CalculateMissileTargetCoordinates with missile type 0x24d\n2. If missile creation failed (NULL), exit early\n3. Calculate unit's current coordinates via CalculateUnitCoordinates\n4. If coordinate calculation failed, exit early\n5. Get missile's current X coordinate via Ordinal_10326 (D2Common.GetUnitX)\n6. Get missile's current Y coordinate via Ordinal_10329 (D2Common.GetUnitY)\n7. Calculate velocity Y = -(nUnitY - missileY) and set via MissileSetTargetUnit\n8. Calculate velocity X = (nUnitX - missileX) and set via SetMissileTargetUnitId\n\nParameters:\npUnit - Source unit for coordinate calculation and missile origin\ndwMissileId - Missile type identifier passed to CalculateMissileTargetCoordinates\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x24d (589) - Missile type constant passed to CalculateMissileTargetCoordinates\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Returns early if missile creation fails\n- Returns early if unit coordinate calculation fails\n- Velocity Y component is negated (-(nUnitY - missileY))\n\nCalled Functions:\n- CalculateMissileTargetCoordinates: Creates missile at calculated target position\n- CalculateUnitCoordinates: Gets unit X/Y coordinates\n- Ordinal_10326: D2Common.GetUnitX - Gets missile X coordinate\n- Ordinal_10329: D2Common.GetUnitY - Gets missile Y coordinate\n- MissileSetTargetUnit: Sets missile velocity Y component\n- SetMissileTargetUnitId: Sets missile velocity X component",
