      "comment": "Monster AI handler for skill 0x126 execution with distance-based targeting.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate unit is a monster (type 1), assert and exit if not\n2. Get skill 0x126 from monster's skill list\n3. If skill not found, set skill level to 1 and retry getting skill\n4. Assert if skill still not found after creation\n5. Get and increment skill owner type counter\n6. Get current skill target coordinates (X, Y)\n7. Calculate distance from monster to target coordinates\n8. Set execution flag if distance > 5 OR owner count > 0x22 (34)\n9. Branch based on field at offset 0xC:\n   - If field_0xC == 1 (mode 1):\n     a. If execution flag set, search for unit at coordinates using filter callback\n     b. If unit found, initialize its equipment slots\n     c. Set skill ID to 0x1D4 (468)\n   - If field_0xC == 2 (mode 2):\n     a. Get random value 0-1 using unit state as seed\n     b. Set skill ID to 0x1D2 + random (466 or 467)\n   - Otherwise return without executing\n10. If execution flag set:\n    a. Reset skill owner type to 0\n    b. Update skill target coordinates from monster position\n    c. Execute monster skill with determined skill ID and flags 0x100\n\nParameters:\n  pMonster - UnitAny * [ECX] - Monster unit to execute skill for, must be type UNIT_MONSTER\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Early exit if unit type is not monster (asserts and terminates)\n  - Early exit if skill cannot be created (asserts and terminates)\n  - Early exit if field_0xC is not 1 or 2\n  - Skill 0x126 is auto-created at level 1 if not present\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x126 (294) - Skill ID being managed\n  0x1D4 (468) - Skill ID executed in mode 1\n  0x1D2 (466) - Base skill ID for mode 2 random selection\n  0x22 (34)   - Owner count threshold for execution\n  5           - Distance threshold for execution\n  0x100 (256) - Skill execution flags",
      "tags": ["MOD_SKILLS", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PROP_NOCALLER", "UI_SKILLS", "SRC_SkillsEMon.cpp", "STRUCT_ItemData", "UNIT_MONSTER", "PARAM_1", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control"]
