      "comment": "Initializes audio playback parameter structure and triggers sound playback.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate 88-byte (0x58) parameter structure on stack (22 dwords)\n2. Zero-initialize entire parameter structure using REP STOSD\n3. Set playback flags field at offset 0x10 to 0x1f2 (498 decimal)\n4. Set dwFlags parameter at offset 0x2c\n5. Set dwSoundId parameter at offsets 0x4 and 0x8 (duplicated)\n6. Pass structure pointer to FUN_6fb77720 for audio playback execution\n\nParameters:\n  dwUnusedECX - Unused parameter in ECX register (fastcall convention)\n  dwSoundId - Sound identifier copied to offsets 0x4 and 0x8 in parameter structure\n  dwFlags - Flags value stored at offset 0x2c in parameter structure\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - This is a thin wrapper that exists solely to initialize a parameter structure\n  - The sound ID is duplicated at two locations in the structure (offsets 0x4 and 0x8)\n  - First parameter (ECX) is not used in this function despite fastcall convention\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x1f2 (498) - Default playback flags stored at offset 0x10\n  0x58 (88) - Size of AudioPlaybackParams structure in bytes\n  0x16 (22) - Number of dwords to zero-initialize (22 * 4 = 88 bytes)\n\nStructure Layout:\n  Offset  Size  Field Name           Type   Description\n  ------  ----  ------------------   -----  -----------\n  0x00    4     dwBaseField          uint   Base field (zero-initialized)\n  0x04    4     dwSoundId1           uint   Sound identifier (first copy)\n  0x08    4     dwSoundId2           uint   Sound identifier (second copy)\n  0x0C    4     dwReserved1          uint   Reserved (zero-initialized)\n  0x10    4     dwPlaybackFlags      uint   Playback flags (set to 0x1f2)\n  ...     ...   ...                  ...    (Additional fields zero-initialized)\n  0x2C    4     dwFlags              uint   Caller-provided flags parameter\n  ...     ...   ...                  ...    (Remaining fields zero-init