      "instructions": ["0x21070|SUB|ESP, 0x8", "0x21073|PUSH|ESI", "0x21074|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0x21076|PUSH|ESI", "0x21077|CALL|0x6fb9864a", "0x2107C|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [ESI + 0xe8]", "0x21082|OR|AL, 0xe", "0x21084|PUSH|ESI", "0x21085|MOV|dword ptr [ESI + 0xe8], EAX", "0x2108B|CALL|0x6fb98164", "0x21090|PUSH|EAX", "0x21091|CALL|0x6fb98140", "0x21096|PUSH|EAX", "0x21097|CALL|0x6fb9817c", "0x2109C|CMP|AL, 0x1"],
      "comment": "Spawns a projectile from the given unit and repositions the unit.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize unit animation via InitializeUnitAnimation\n2. Set unit flags at offset 0xe8 (OR with 0x0e)\n3. Get unit's current room via UNITS_GetRoom\n4. Get entity field and determine character tier via GetCharacterTierIndex\n5. Based on tier (0x01 = elite):\n   - Elite tier: projectile type 0x4c\n   - Normal tier: projectile type 0x142\n6. Get target coordinates via Ordinal_10329 (GetUnitY) and Ordinal_10326 (GetUnitX)\n7. Create projectile via CreateProjectileFromUnit with attack type 1\n8. Get unit path pointer from offset 0x38\n9. Get current unit position for collision search\n10. Call GetUnitCollisionSize to determine collision radius\n11. Search for valid collision tile via FindValidCollisionTileSimple\n    - Attribute mask: 0x1c09 (walkable terrain flags)\n    - Mode: 1 (simple search)\n12. If no valid tile found, log warning \"hRoom\" at line 0x3d\n13. Set unit position via SetUnitPositionAndClearFlags\n14. If position set fails, log warning \"fRet\" at line 0x40\n15. Apply tile attribute pattern with flags 0x1000, size type 1\n\nParameters:\n  pUnit (ECX) - UnitAny* - Pointer to unit spawning the projectile\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value (EAX set to 1 at end but not returned)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Elite units (tier 0x01) use projectile type 0x4c\n  - Normal units use projectile type 0x142\n  - Logs warning if no valid room tile found for positioning\n  - Logs warning if unit position update fails\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x0e - Flag bits to set on unit field 0xe8\n  0x4c - Elite projectile type ID\n  0x142 - Normal projectile type ID\n  0x1c09 - Collision tile attribute mask\n  0x1000 - Tile attribute pattern flags\n  0x38 - Offset to unit path pointer\n  0xe8 - Offset to unit flags field\n\nOrdinal References:\n  Ordinal_10329 - D2Common.GetUnitY\n  Ordinal_10326 - D2Common.GetUnitX",
      "tags": ["SRC_SkillsMon.cpp", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PROP_NOCALLER", "UI_SKILLS", "PARAM_1", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
