      "comment": "Synchronizes entity coordinate data between client context and D2COMMON.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate the client context and retrieve associated entity pointer\n2. If validation fails (NULL entity), return success without synchronization\n3. Retrieve context handle from client context (Ordinal_10323)\n4. Retrieve first coordinate value from validated entity (Ordinal_10326)\n5. Store first coordinate to context handle (Ordinal_10980)\n6. Retrieve second coordinate value from validated entity (Ordinal_10329)\n7. Store second coordinate to context handle (Ordinal_10981)\n8. Return success status\n\nParameters:\npContext - Pointer to ClientSyncContext structure (contains entity reference at offset +0x38)\n\nReturns:\nAlways returns 1 (success) regardless of validation outcome\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If entity validation fails, function returns success without performing synchronization\n- No error propagation occurs when entity is NULL\n- Coordinate synchronization is skipped silently on validation failure\n\nExternal Dependencies:\n- FUN_6fb63760: Validates context and retrieves entity pointer from offset +0x38\n- Ordinal_10323 (D2COMMON.DLL): Retrieves context handle from client context\n- Ordinal_10326 (D2COMMON.DLL): Retrieves first coordinate value from entity\n- Ordinal_10329 (D2COMMON.DLL): Retrieves second coordinate value from entity\n- Ordinal_10980 (D2COMMON.DLL): Stores first coordinate to context handle\n- Ordinal_10981 (D2COMMON.DLL): Stores second coordinate to context handle\n\nNote:\nThis function has no known callers and may be unused or called indirectly through\nfunction pointer table. The coordinate values synchronized are likely X and Y position\ndata based on the paired get/set pattern.",
      "tags": ["PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_1"]
