      "instructions": ["0x21200|PUSH|ESI", "0x21201|PUSH|EDI", "0x21202|MOV|EDI, ECX", "0x21204|CALL|0x6fb63760", "0x21209|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0x2120B|JNZ|0x6faf1210", "0x2120D|POP|EDI", "0x2120E|POP|ESI", "0x2120F|RET|", "0x21210|MOV|ESI, dword ptr [EDI + 0x38]", "0x21213|PUSH|0x5", "0x21215|PUSH|ESI", "0x21216|CALL|0x6fb98554", "0x2121B|PUSH|0x2", "0x2121D|PUSH|ESI"],
      "comment": "Initialize pathfinding system with automatic retry logic\n\nAlgorithm:\n\n1. Validate PathfindInfo structure by calling FUN_6fb63760\n   - Returns early with false if validation fails\n   \n2. Extract path handle from PathfindInfo.field_0x38\n\n3. First initialization attempt with high-priority settings:\n   - Call Ordinal_10188 with mode 5 (set pathfinding mode)\n   - Call Ordinal_10185 with priority 2 (set priority level)\n   - Call Ordinal_10142 with PathfindInfo and flags 0 (configure pathfinding)\n   - Call Ordinal_10154 to validate path setup\n\n4. If first attempt fails, retry with reduced priority:\n   - Call Ordinal_10185 with priority 1 (lower priority)\n   - Call Ordinal_10142 with PathfindInfo and flags 0 (reconfigure)\n   - Call Ordinal_10154 to validate path setup\n   - Return false if second attempt also fails\n\n5. On successful validation:\n   - Call Ordinal_10323 to get path result from PathfindInfo\n   - Call Ordinal_10984 with result and flag 1 (finalize pathfinding)\n   - Return true to indicate success\n\nParameters:\n\npPathfindInfo - Pointer to PathfindInfo structure containing pathfinding state\n                Field at offset 0x38 contains the path handle used for D2COMMON operations\n\nReturns:\n\ntrue (1) - Pathfinding initialization succeeded (either first or second attempt)\nfalse (0) - Pathfinding initialization failed after validation or both retry attempts\n\nSpecial Cases:\n\nThe function implements a two-tier retry mechanism:\n- First attempt uses priority 2 (higher priority pathfinding)\n- Second attempt uses priority 1 (lower priority fallback)\nThis ensures pathfinding can succeed even under resource constraints\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n\n0x38 (56 decimal) - Offset to path handle field in PathfindInfo structure\n5 - Pathfinding mode parameter for Ordinal_10188\n2 - High priority level for first initialization attempt  \n1 - Low priority level for retry attempt\n0 - Flags parameter for Ordinal_10142 configuration",
      "tags": ["PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_1"]
    },
