      "instructions": ["0x21270|PUSH|ESI", "0x21271|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0x21273|CALL|0x6fb63760", "0x21278|MOV|ECX, EAX", "0x2127A|TEST|ECX, ECX", "0x2127C|JZ|0x6faf12b9", "0x2127E|MOV|ESI, dword ptr [ESI + 0x4]", "0x21281|CMP|ESI, 0x1e", "0x21284|JZ|0x6faf12a3", "0x21286|CMP|ESI, 0x20", "0x21289|JZ|0x6faf12a3", "0x2128B|PUSH|0x0", "0x2128D|PUSH|0x0", "0x2128F|PUSH|0x0", "0x21291|PUSH|0x0"],
      "comment": "Apply class-specific visual overlay effect to a unit based on its class ID.\n\nAlgorithm:\n\n1. Retrieve overlay target from unit context via FUN_6fb63760\n2. If target is NULL, exit early (no overlay applied)\n3. Read unit's class ID from pUnit->dwClassId (offset +0x4)\n4. Check if class ID is 0x1e (Necromancer) or 0x20 (Druid)\n5. If class matches (0x1e or 0x20):\n   - Apply overlay type 0x24 (class-specific transformation overlay)\n6. If class does NOT match:\n   - Apply overlay type 0x23 (generic buff/skill overlay)\n7. Call FUN_6fb931f0 to create and attach overlay to target\n\nParameters:\n\npUnit (ECX) - Pointer to UnitAny structure representing the unit receiving overlay\n              ACTUAL TYPE: UnitAny * (displayed as int * due to type validation issue)\n\nReturns:\n\nvoid - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n\n0x1e (30 decimal) - Necromancer class ID\n0x20 (32 decimal) - Druid class ID\n0x23 (35 decimal) - Generic buff/skill visual overlay type\n0x24 (36 decimal) - Class-specific transformation overlay type (shapeshifting)\n\nStructure Layout:\n\nUnitAny Structure (48 bytes):\nOffset | Size | Field Name    | Type  | Description\n-------|------|---------------|-------|----------------------------------\n  +0x0 |   4  | dwUnitType    | uint  | Unit type (0=Player, 1=NPC, etc)\n  +0x4 |   4  | dwClassId     | uint  | Character class identifier\n  +0x8 |   4  | pMemPool      | void* | Memory pool pointer\n  +0xc |   4  | dwUnitId      | uint  | Unique unit identifier\n +0x10 |   4  | dwMode        | uint  | Current unit mode/state\n +0x14 |   4  | pUnitData     | void* | Unit-specific data pointer\n +0x18 |   4  | dwActId       | uint  | Act identifier\n +0x1c |   4  | pAct          | void* | Act structure pointer\n +0x20 |   4  | pSeed         | void* | Random seed pointer\n +0x24 |   4  | pPath         | void* | Pathfinding data pointer\n +0x28 |   4  | dwGfxFrame    | uint  | Current graphics frame\n +0x2c |   4  | dwFrameRemain | uint  | Frames remaining\n\nError Handling:\n\nEarly exit if FUN_6fb63760 returns NULL (no overlay target available).\nNo error reporting - silent failure if target unavailable.\n\nImplementation Notes:\n\nThis function specifically handles Necromancer (0x1e) and Druid (0x20) shapeshifting\noverlays differently from other class abilities. Shapeshifting forms (Werebear, Werewolf)\nrequire overlay type 0x24 for proper visual transformation, while standard buffs and\nauras use overlay type 0x23. The function is called from a function pointer table at\n0x6fba79c8, suggesting it's part of a larger overlay dispatch system.",
      "tags": ["PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_1"]
    },
