      "comment": "Clears unit targeting state by resetting target coordinates and targeting flag.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call GetUnitTargetXY to retrieve unit's current target X/Y coordinates\n2. If target X coordinate is <= 0 (invalid), clear pUnit->field_0x48 (target X storage)\n3. Always clear pUnit->field_0x5c (targeting active flag byte)\n\nParameters:\n  pUnit (ECX) - Pointer to UnitAny structure to clear targeting state\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nStructure Offsets:\n  Offset  Size  Field               Description\n  0x48    4     dwTargetX           Target X coordinate (cleared if invalid)\n  0x5c    1     bTargetingActive    Targeting flag (always cleared)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - No callers found - may be dead code or called via function pointer table\n  - Always clears targeting flag regardless of coordinate validity\n\nClassification: Leaf worker function",
