      "instructions": ["0x212F0|SUB|ESP, 0x68", "0x212F3|PUSH|EBX", "0x212F4|PUSH|EBP", "0x212F5|PUSH|ESI", "0x212F6|PUSH|EDI", "0x212F7|MOV|EDI, ECX", "0x212F9|PUSH|EDI", "0x212FA|CALL|0x6fb983c2", "0x212FF|MOV|ESI, EAX", "0x21301|PUSH|ESI", "0x21302|CALL|0x6fb9845e", "0x21307|MOV|EBP, EAX", "0x21309|PUSH|ESI", "0x2130A|CALL|0x6fb98458", "0x2130F|MOV|DL, 0x16"],
      "comment": "Spawns a directional projectile from a unit toward its skill target.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get the unit's current skill and retrieve skill owner type and target X coord\n2. Build direction offset lookup table (80 bytes) on stack for projectile positioning\n3. Calculate direction from unit to target using UNITS_GetDirectionToCoord\n4. Convert precise direction to cardinal direction (0-7)\n5. Get unit's current X/Y position via Ordinal_10326/Ordinal_10329\n6. Look up offset values based on cardinal direction using GetDirectionOffsets\n7. Calculate base projectile spawn position (unit position + direction offset)\n8. Get unit's target coordinates via GetUnitTargetXY\n9. Apply secondary offset from lookup table based on target+direction index\n10. Skip secondary offset if lookup returns 'c' (0x63 = invalid/skip marker)\n11. Call CreateProjectileFromUnit with missile type 0x20 and calculated position\n\nParameters:\npUnit (ECX) - Pointer to the source unit spawning the projectile\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Projectile created as side effect\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x20 - Missile type ID passed to CreateProjectileFromUnit\n0x63 ('c') - Invalid/skip marker in direction lookup table\n0x68 - Stack frame size (104 bytes for lookup tables)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If direction lookup returns 'c' (0x63), secondary offset is skipped\n- Direction lookup table uses cardinal direction * 9 + offset indexing",
