      "comment": "Handle graphics context error codes based on context state flags.\n\nAlgorithm:\n\n1. Retrieve graphics context handle from unit structure\n2. Query context state flags to determine error handling mode\n3. Test if flag 0x02 (CONTEXT_CONSUMED) is set in context flags\n4. If flag 0x02 is set (context was consumed):\n   a. Mark graphics context as released/consumed with flag 0\n   b. Set error code 0x13 (SKILL_INTERRUPTED) on unit\n   c. Return\n5. If flag 0x02 is not set (context still active):\n   a. Set error code 0x0b (INVALID_TARGET) on unit\n   b. Return\n\nParameters:\n\npUnit - Pointer to UnitAny structure representing the game entity\n\nReturns:\n\nvoid - No return value (error state applied directly to unit structure)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n\n- Flag 0x02 determines which error path executes (mutually exclusive)\n- Error code 0x13 indicates skill was interrupted after context consumption\n- Error code 0x0b indicates invalid target or action before context consumption\n- Graphics context marked with flag 0 indicates complete release/consumption\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n\n0x02 (2 decimal) - CONTEXT_CONSUMED flag - indicates graphics context was consumed/processed\n0x13 (19 decimal) - SKILL_INTERRUPTED error code - skill execution was interrupted\n0x0b (11 decimal) - INVALID_TARGET error code - target validation or action failed\n0x0 (0 decimal) - Context release flag - marks graphics context as fully consumed",
      "tags": ["PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_1"]
