      "instructions": ["0x215B0|SUB|ESP, 0x60", "0x215B3|LEA|EAX, [ESP + 0x4]", "0x215B7|PUSH|EBX", "0x215B8|PUSH|ESI", "0x215B9|MOV|ESI, EDX", "0x215BB|MOV|EBX, ECX", "0x215BD|PUSH|EAX", "0x215BE|LEA|EDX, [ESP + 0xc]", "0x215C2|CALL|0x6fae96a0", "0x215C7|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0x215C9|JZ|0x6faf16aa", "0x215CF|PUSH|EBX", "0x215D0|CALL|0x6fb98164", "0x215D5|MOV|ECX, dword ptr [ESP + 0xc]", "0x215D9|MOV|EDX, dword ptr [ESP + 0x8]"],
      "comment": "Spawns three nova-style projectiles radiating from a unit's position.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate source unit X/Y coordinates via CalculateUnitCoordinates\n2. Return immediately if coordinate calculation fails\n3. Get unit's room and find region by coordinates\n4. Validate entity DRLG subtype - return if non-zero (outdoor/invalid)\n5. Zero-initialize 22-dword projectile data structure on stack\n6. Set base projectile type to 0x21 (33) with flags 0x82\n7. Store source unit pointer and spawn area ID in structure\n8. Get spawn area X coordinate via Ordinal_10326 (D2Common.GetAreaX)\n9. Calculate delta X = area_x - source_x\n10. Get spawn area Y coordinate via Ordinal_10329 (D2Common.GetAreaY)\n11. Calculate delta Y = area_y - source_y\n12. Spawn first projectile at (source_x - delta_y, source_y + delta_x)\n13. Spawn second projectile at (source_x + delta_y, source_y - delta_x)\n14. Set third projectile type based on unit class:\n    - Class 0x2d (45): type = 0x14b (331)\n    - Other classes: type = 0x113 (275)\n15. Spawn third projectile at origin offsets (0, 0)\n\nParameters:\npSourceUnit - Source unit that projectiles emanate from\nnSpawnAreaId - Area ID used to calculate spawn direction via Ordinal_10326/10329\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value, spawns projectiles as side effect\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Returns early if CalculateUnitCoordinates fails (returns 0)\n- Returns early if ValidateEntityDrlgSubType returns non-zero\n- Class 0x2d (45) uses different central projectile type (0x14b vs 0x113)\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x21 (33) = Nova projectile type for side projectiles\n0x82 (130) = Projectile flags (preset coords + adjust mode)\n0x2d (45) = Unit class ID that uses alternate projectile type\n0x14b (331) = Central projectile type for class 0x2d units\n0x113 (275) = Central projectile type for other units (0x14b - 0x38)\n0x16 (22) = Number of dwords zeroed in projectile structure\n\nOrdinal Functions:\nOrdinal_10326 = D2Common.GetAreaX - Gets X coordinate for spawn area\nOrdinal_10329 = D2Common.GetAreaY - Gets Y coordinate for spawn area",
