      "api_calls": ["UNITS_GetOwnerGuid", "UNITS_GetUnitY", "UNITS_GetOwnerGuid", "UNITS_GetUnitY", "UNITS_GetDirectionToCoord", "SetUnitDirection"],
      "instructions": ["0x216F0|SUB|ESP, 0x68", "0x216F3|PUSH|EBX", "0x216F4|PUSH|ESI", "0x216F5|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x14], EDX", "0x216F9|MOV|EBX, ECX", "0x216FB|CALL|0x6fb63760", "0x21700|MOV|ESI, EAX", "0x21702|TEST|ESI, ESI", "0x21704|JZ|0x6faf1834", "0x2170A|PUSH|EBP", "0x2170B|PUSH|EDI", "0x2170C|PUSH|ESI", "0x2170D|CALL|0x6fb98122", "0x21712|MOV|EDI, EAX", "0x21714|PUSH|ESI"],
      "comment": "Spawns a tracking projectile for mercenary units with position interpolation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get mercenary position data via GetMercenaryPosition, exit if NULL\n2. Retrieve source unit X/Y coordinates via Ordinal_10326/10329 (D2Common.GetUnitX/GetUnitY)\n3. Retrieve target position X/Y coordinates for mercenary\n4. Calculate absolute delta X = |sourceX - mercX| and delta Y = |sourceY - mercY|\n5. Determine interpolation axis based on which delta is larger\n6. If deltaX < deltaY: interpolate along X axis 4 steps toward source\n7. Else: interpolate along Y axis 4 steps toward source\n8. Zero-initialize 0x58-byte projectile data structure (22 dwords)\n9. Calculate target offsets: deltaX = targetX - mercX, deltaY = targetY - mercY\n10. Set control flags = 3 (enable adjustments + offset mode)\n11. Calculate spawn position: targetX = deltaX/6 - 1 + mercX\n12. Set projectile type = 0x18 (24) for tracking missile type\n13. Calculate spawn Y: targetY = deltaY/6 - 1 + mercY\n14. Store source unit and missile ID in projectile data\n15. Calculate direction from unit to target via UNITS_GetDirectionToCoord\n16. Map direction byte through quadrant table then index table for final angle\n17. Set unit direction via SetUnitDirection for visual orientation\n18. Initialize and allocate projectile via InitializeAndAllocateProjectile\n\nParameters:\npUnit (UnitAny *): Source unit pointer (mercenary caster)\ndwMissileId (dword): Missile type identifier passed to projectile initialization\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Projectile allocated internally, no return value\n\nSSA Variables (decompiler temporaries):\npdVar1: Position pointer from GetMercenaryPosition, then projectile data array iterator\niVar2: Holds nDeltaX (absolute X distance), then nSourceY, then interpolated Y coord\niVar3: Loop counter (4 iterations), then nDeltaY (absolute Y distance)\nextraout_EAX: Return from Ordinal_10326 (source X coordinate)\nextraout_EAX_00: Return from Ordinal_10329 (source Y coordinate)\nextraout_EAX_01: Return from Ordinal_10326 (merc X coordinate)\nextraout_EAX_02: Return from Ordinal_10329 (merc Y coordinate)\nextraout_AL: Direction byte from UNITS_GetDirectionToCoord\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- NULL mercenary position: function returns early without spawning\n- Interpolation ensures projectile spawns partway to target (4 steps from source)\n- Direction mapping uses two lookup tables for smooth angle quantization\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x3 (3): Control flags - enable coordinate adjustments and offset mode\n0x4 (4): Interpolation step count for position adjustment\n0x6 (6): Divisor for spawn offset calculation (1/6 of total distance minus 1)\n0x16 (22): Number of dwords in projectile data structure (0x58 bytes)\n0x18 (24): Projectile type ID for tracking missile\n0x6fbb1894: Direction quadrant lookup table (64 bytes, maps direction to quadrant 0-3)\n0x6fbb18d4: Direction index lookup table (maps quadrant to final direction byte)\n\nOrdinal Functions:\nOrdinal_10326 = D2Common.GetUnitX - Get unit X coordinate\nOrdinal_10329 = D2Common.GetUnitY - Get unit Y coordinate",
