      "instructions": ["0x21840|SUB|ESP, 0x6c", "0x21843|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x10], EDX", "0x21847|LEA|EAX, [ESP + 0x4]", "0x2184B|PUSH|EBP", "0x2184C|MOV|EBP, ECX", "0x2184E|PUSH|EAX", "0x2184F|LEA|EDX, [ESP + 0x8]", "0x21853|CALL|0x6fae96a0", "0x21858|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0x2185A|JZ|0x6faf1944", "0x21860|PUSH|EBX", "0x21861|PUSH|ESI", "0x21862|PUSH|EDI", "0x21863|PUSH|EBP", "0x21864|CALL|0x6fb98122"],
      "comment": "Spawns a burst of 3 directional projectiles from the source unit in a spread pattern.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get unit world coordinates via CalculateUnitCoordinates\n2. Return early if coordinate calculation fails (return 0)\n3. Get unit path coordinates via Ordinal_10326 (GetPathPosX) and Ordinal_10329 (GetPathPosY)\n4. Calculate delta between unit position and path position (nDeltaX, nDeltaY)\n5. Determine direction quadrant based on sign of deltas:\n   - Both negative: zero out X delta\n   - X zero: set X delta to negative of Y delta\n   - X positive, Y negative: zero out Y delta\n   - X positive, Y zero: set Y delta equal to X delta\n   - X positive, Y positive: zero out X delta\n   - X negative, Y positive: zero out Y delta\n   - X negative, Y zero: set Y delta equal to X delta\n6. Zero-initialize 22 dwords of projectile configuration buffer (0x58 bytes)\n7. Set projectile flags to 0x3 (preset coords mode + offset adjustment)\n8. Loop 3 times through g_anDirectionalProjectileDeltas array [0, 1, 2]:\n   a. Add current delta offset to accumulated delta\n   b. Calculate spawn offset as (accumulated_delta + sign_adjust) >> 3\n   c. Set spawn area ID to 0x11b\n   d. Calculate spawn coordinates by adding offset to path coordinates\n   e. Store missile type ID and source unit reference in config\n   f. Call InitializeAndAllocateProjectile to spawn projectile\n9. Return after spawning all 3 projectiles\n\nParameters:\npSourceUnit - UnitAny pointer to the unit spawning projectiles (in ECX)\ndwMissileTypeId - Missile type ID for the projectiles being spawned (in EDX)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\nIf CalculateUnitCoordinates returns 0, function returns immediately without spawning\nProjectiles spawn at incrementally offset positions creating a spread pattern\nDirection quadrant logic ensures consistent spread regardless of unit facing\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x3 - Projectile flags: bit 0 (preset coords) + bit 1 (offset adjustment)\n0x11b (283) - Spawn area ID constant\n0x16 (22) - Number of dwords to zero-initialize (88 bytes / 4)\n0x7 - Sign adjustment mask for divide-by-8 rounding\n0x3 - Right shift count for divide-by-8 operation\ng_anDirectionalProjectileDeltas at 0x6fbb18d8 - Array [0, 1, 2] for spread offsets\n\nOrdinal References:\nOrdinal_10326 = D2Common.GetPathPosX - Gets X coordinate from unit path\nOrdinal_10329 = D2Common.GetPathPosY - Gets Y coordinate from unit path",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_StatList", "STRUCT_Path", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PARAM_2", "PROP_NOCALLER", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
