      "api_count": 11,
      "api_calls": ["GetUnitPathCoordMismatchFlag", "GetUnitSkillById", "GetSkillLevel", "UNITS_GetRoom", "UNITS_GetOwnerGuid", "UNITS_GetUnitY", "PATH_GetDirection", "GetCardinalDirection", "GetDirectionOffsets", "FindRegionByCoordinates", "...+1 more"],
      "instructions": ["0x21A50|SUB|ESP, 0x70", "0x21A53|PUSH|EBX", "0x21A54|PUSH|EBP", "0x21A55|PUSH|ESI", "0x21A56|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0x21A58|PUSH|EDI", "0x21A59|XOR|EBX, EBX", "0x21A5B|MOV|EDI, dword ptr [ESI + 0x38]", "0x21A5E|TEST|EDI, EDI", "0x21A60|JZ|0x6faf1b9f", "0x21A66|PUSH|EDI", "0x21A67|CALL|0x6fb98674", "0x21A6C|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0x21A6E|JZ|0x6faf1b9f", "0x21A74|PUSH|0x1"],
      "comment": "Creates a missile with directional offset positioning based on unit facing.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate unit has valid path pointer at offset +0x38\n2. Call Ordinal_10234 to verify path is initialized\n3. Retrieve game state and level information from unit\n4. Get unit's current X and Y coordinates (Ordinal_10326/10329)\n5. Build direction lookup table with offset bytes for 8 directions\n6. Get unit's facing direction from path (Ordinal_10159)\n7. Convert direction to index 0-7 using modulo operation (Ordinal_11053)\n8. Select direction offset byte from lookup table using calculated index\n9. Decode direction byte into X/Y offsets using Ordinal_11055\n10. Add offsets to unit position to calculate missile spawn point\n11. Check collision at calculated position (Ordinal_10042/10082)\n12. If no collision, initialize missile structure (0x58 bytes)\n13. Set missile spawn position (adjusted coordinates)\n14. Set missile target position (double offset from spawn)\n15. Call FUN_6fb77720 to create missile object\n16. Call FUN_6fb8d210 to spawn missile ID 0x726 (1830)\n17. Return pointer to created missile or NULL on failure\n\nParameters:\n  pUnit - Pointer to UnitAny structure containing path and position data\n  IMPLICIT EDX - May contain additional game state flags\n\nReturns:\n  Non-NULL - Pointer to created missile structure\n  NULL - Path invalid, path not initialized, or collision detected at spawn point\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Returns NULL if unit->pPath (offset +0x38) is NULL\n  - Returns NULL if Ordinal_10234 validation fails\n  - Returns NULL if collision detected at calculated spawn position\n  - Missile spawns at unit position plus directional offset\n  - Target position is double the offset from spawn point\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x38 - Offset to pPath in UnitAny structure\n  0x1416080a - Packed direction lookup base (contains offsets for 4 cardinal directions)\n  0x12, 0x10, 0x0e, 0x0c - Direction offset bytes for diagonal directions\n  0x25 (37) - Missile type identifier in structure\n  0x8f (143) - Missile behavior flags\n  0x3 - Missile state (active/spawning)\n  0x16 (22) - Loop counter for zeroing 0x58 bytes (22 * 4 = 88 bytes)\n  0x726 (1830) - Missile skill/spell ID to spawn\n  0xff (255) - Mask for direction index modulo operation\n\nDirection Lookup Table:\n  Index 0-7 maps to 8 compass directions (N, NE, E, SE, S, SW, W, NW)\n  Bytes at offsets 0-7: 0x0a, 0x08, 0x16, 0x14, 0x12, 0x10, 0x0e, 0x0c\n  Each byte encodes packed X/Y offset pair decoded by Ordinal_11055\n\nMissile Structure Layout (0x58 bytes):\n  Offset  Size  Field Name        Type        Description\n  +0x00   4     dwMissileType     uint        Type identifier (0x25)\n  +0x04   4     pOwner            UnitAny*    Pointer to owning unit\n  +0x10   4     dwMissileFlags    uint        Behavior flags (0x8f)\n  +0x14   4     nSourceX          int         Spawn X coordinate\n  +0x18   4     nSourceY          int         Spawn Y coordinate\n  +0x1C   4     nTargetX          int         Target X coordinate\n  +0x20   4     nTargetY          int         Target Y coordinate\n  +0x28   4     dwMissileState    uint        State (0x3 = active)\n  +0x2C   4     dwMissileLevel    uint        Skill level",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_StatList", "STRUCT_MonsterData", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "STRUCT_ItemData", "PARAM_1", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
