      "instructions": ["0x21BB0|SUB|ESP, 0x8", "0x21BB3|LEA|EAX, [ESP]", "0x21BB7|PUSH|ESI", "0x21BB8|MOV|ESI, EDX", "0x21BBA|PUSH|EDI", "0x21BBB|MOV|EDI, ECX", "0x21BBD|PUSH|EAX", "0x21BBE|LEA|EDX, [ESP + 0x10]", "0x21BC2|CALL|0x6fae96a0", "0x21BC7|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0x21BC9|JZ|0x6faf1be8", "0x21BCB|MOV|ECX, dword ptr [ESP + 0x8]", "0x21BCF|MOV|EDX, dword ptr [ESP + 0xc]", "0x21BD3|SAR|ESI, 0x1", "0x21BD5|PUSH|0x3"],
      "comment": "Process walkable tiles in a circle around a unit with scaled radius.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get unit tile coordinates using CalculateUnitCoordinates\n2. If coordinate lookup fails, return early without processing\n3. Calculate effective radius as (nBaseRadius >> 1) + 3 (half base radius plus 3)\n4. Call ProcessCircleWithinDistance with unit, coordinates, radius, flags 0x8E, and random check 3\n\nParameters:\npUnit (UnitAny *) - Pointer to unit structure, passed in ECX (__fastcall)\nnBaseRadius (int) - Base radius value, passed in EDX; actual radius = (nBaseRadius / 2) + 3\n\nReturns: void\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x8E (142) - Flags/item code for ProcessCircleWithinDistance tile processing\n3 - Random check parameter for tile validation probability\n(nBaseRadius >> 1) + 3 - Radius scaling: halves base radius and adds fixed offset of 3\n\nRelated Functions:\nCalculateUnitCoordinates - Gets absolute X/Y tile coordinates for unit\nProcessCircleWithinDistance - Processes tiles within circular area",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Inventory", "PARAM_2", "PROP_NOCALLER"]
