      "instructions": ["0x21C80|SUB|ESP, 0x58", "0x21C83|PUSH|EBX", "0x21C84|PUSH|EBP", "0x21C85|PUSH|ESI", "0x21C86|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0x21C88|PUSH|EDI", "0x21C89|MOV|ECX, 0x16", "0x21C8E|XOR|EAX, EAX", "0x21C90|LEA|EDI, [ESP + 0x10]", "0x21C94|MOV|EBX, EDX", "0x21C96|LEA|EBP, [ESI + 0x2c]", "0x21C99|STOSD.REP|ES:EDI", "0x21C9B|MOV|EDX, 0x4", "0x21CA0|MOV|ECX, EBP", "0x21CA2|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x10], 0x25"],
      "comment": "Configure audio playback parameters for 3D positional audio\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Zero-initialize 88-byte configuration structure (22 dwords)\n2. Set configuration type flag to 0x25 (base audio configuration)\n3. Check audio processing mode and set 0x4000 flag if active\n4. Copy audio context and parameters into configuration structure\n5. Retrieve original coordinates (X/Y) from audio context\n6. Obtain audio data pointer and calculate adjusted playback index\n7. Check for alternate audio context and retrieve target coordinates\n   - If no alternate context: Get target coordinates directly\n   - If alternate context exists: Transform coordinates and update target\n8. Create audio object from configuration structure\n9. If audio object created successfully:\n   a. Retrieve object information structure\n   b. Get data pointer from audio object\n   c. Calculate playback value from data offset 0x7c + table offset - 1\n   d. Apply +3 adjustment if object type is 0x167 (special audio type)\n   e. Set playback parameters at object offset 0xe\n   f. Calculate and set volume/pitch ratio using byte at offset 0x58\n   g. Configure start and end playback positions\n\nParameters:\npAudioContext   - Pointer to audio context structure containing spatial info\n                 Offset 0x38 contains reference to coordinate data\ndwAudioParams   - Audio parameter flags controlling playback behavior\npPlaybackTable  - Pointer to table of playback indices indexed by mode\nnTableOffset    - Offset into playback data for this audio instance\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If audio processing mode is active, configuration type gets 0x4000 flag\n- If FUN_6fb63760 returns non-zero, coordinates are transformed via alternate context\n- If object type at offset 0x1 is 0x167, playback value increased by 3\n- If FUN_6fb77720 returns NULL, no audio object configuration occurs\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x25 (37)     - Base audio configuration type flag\n0x4000 (16384) - Audio processing active flag mask\n0x16 (22)     - Configuration structure size in dwords (88 bytes)\n0x38 (56)     - Offset to coordinate reference in audio context\n0x167 (359)   - Special audio object type requiring +3 adjustment\n0x7c (124)    - Offset to base playback value in data structure\n0x58 (88)     - Offset to volume/pitch parameter byte\n0xe (14)      - Offset to playback parameter in audio object (14 dwords = 56 bytes)",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Inventory", "STRUCT_Skill", "PARAM_4", "STRUCT_Room2", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
