      "comment": "Clears the owner type for a unit's current skill.\n\nThis is a simple wrapper function that retrieves the unit's current skill\nand resets its owner type to 0 (cleared/no owner state).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call Ordinal_10323(pUnit) to get the unit's current Skill pointer from ECX\n2. Call SetSkillOwnerType(pSkill, 0) to reset the skill's owner type to zero\n3. Return 1 (TRUE) indicating successful completion\n\nParameters:\n  pUnit (ECX, UnitAny*): Pointer to the unit whose skill owner type will be cleared\n    IMPLICIT: Passed via ECX register in __fastcall convention\n\nReturns:\n  int: Always returns 1 (TRUE) indicating successful completion\n    - No failure conditions exist in this function\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Ordinal_10323 is D2Common.GetUnitSkill - retrieves the current skill from the unit\n  - Owner type value 0 typically means \"no owner\" or \"cleared\" state\n  - This function appears to be a callback used during skill cleanup or reset operations\n  - The function has no callers detected, suggesting it may be invoked via function pointer\n\nClassification: Wrapper/Thunk function - calls two D2Common functions and returns constant",
