      "comment": "Cycle skill owner type counter and play audio on wrap-around\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get current skill from unit via Ordinal_10323 (SKILLS_GetCurrentSkill)\n2. Get skill's owner type counter via GetSkillOwnerType\n3. Increment owner type counter\n4. If counter overflows (becomes negative after increment):\n   - Set new owner type value (incremented value) and return early\n5. If counter wraps to non-negative:\n   - Reset owner type to 0\n   - Initialize audio parameter array with values [-1, -3, -2, -1, 0]\n   - Call ConfigureAudioPlayback with unit, 0xAC params, audio table, and offset\n\nParameters:\npUnit       - UnitAny* in ECX, unit whose skill owner type to cycle\nnTableOffset - int in EDX, offset into audio playback table\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Early return when owner type counter overflows (stays negative)\n- Audio playback only triggered when counter wraps from max to 0\n- No callers found - may be called via function pointer table\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0xAC (172)      - Audio parameter flags for ConfigureAudioPlayback\n0xFFFFFFFF (-1) - Audio param indices at positions 0 and 3\n0xFFFFFFFD (-3) - Audio param index at position 1\n0xFFFFFFFE (-2) - Audio param index at position 2\n0x00000000 (0)  - Audio param index at position 4 (terminator)",
