      "comment": "Sets a mercenary unit to neutral/idle mode (mode 0x1b).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call GetMercenaryPosition to retrieve mercenary entity from unit\n2. If no mercenary entity found (NULL), return 0 (implicit)\n3. Call ProcessEntityModeParameters with mode 0x1b and count 0\n4. Return 1 indicating successful mode change\n\nParameters:\npUnit (UnitAny *): Pointer to unit structure (player or entity with mercenary)\n\nReturns:\nint: 1 on success (mercenary mode updated)\n     0 on failure (no mercenary entity found) - implicit from no EAX set\n\nDecompiler Discrepancies:\n- Assembly shows MOV EAX, 0x1 before RET but decompiler shows void return\n- Actual return type is int, not void\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x1b (27): Neutral/idle mode parameter for ProcessEntityModeParameters\n0x0: Count parameter (no count-based processing)\n0x1: Success return value\n\nRelated Functions:\n- GetMercenaryPosition: Retrieves mercenary entity pointer from unit\n- ProcessEntityModeParameters: Applies mode settings to entity",
