      "comment": "Sets update-related flag bits on a unit structure\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load current flags DWORD from unit structure at offset 0xE8\n2. OR flags with 0x0E to set bits 1, 2, and 3\n3. Store modified flags back to unit structure\n4. Return success (1)\n\nParameters:\n  pUnit (int): Pointer to unit structure (passed in ECX via __fastcall)\n\nReturns:\n  int: Always returns 1 (success)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Operation is idempotent if bits already set\n  - No null pointer validation performed\n  - No callers found in current binary (possibly orphaned or called via pointer)\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0xE8 (232): Offset to unit flags DWORD within unit structure\n  0x0E (14, binary 00001110): Flag mask setting bits 1, 2, and 3\n\nFlag Bits (0x0E):\n  Bit 1 (0x02): Update flag 1\n  Bit 2 (0x04): Update flag 2\n  Bit 3 (0x08): Update flag 3\n\nDecompiler Discrepancy:\n  Decompiler shows void return, but assembly clearly returns 1 in EAX",
