      "comment": "Plays an audio source by creating and initializing an audio context, then optionally triggers a special sound effect.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate audio source by checking if first field (dwValue1) is non-zero, return 0 if invalid\n2. Retrieve audio context pointer from audio source using helper function\n3. Return 0 if audio context retrieval failed\n4. Initialize the audio context with the retrieved pointer\n5. Query the sound type from the audio source\n6. If sound type equals 0x3a (58 decimal), trigger special sound effect 0x3aa with audio source\n7. Return 1 indicating success\n\nParameters:\n  pAudioSource - Pointer to AudioSourceData structure containing audio data\n                 Must have valid dwValue1 field (non-zero) to proceed\n\nReturns:\n  0 - Audio source invalid (dwValue1 is zero) or audio context creation failed\n  1 - Audio context successfully created and initialized\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x3a (58) - Sound type value that triggers special effect\n  0x3aa (938) - Special sound effect ID to play when type is 0x3a\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If dwValue1 field of audio source is zero, function returns immediately without processing\n  - Audio context creation may fail even if audio source is valid, returns 0\n  - Sound effect 0x3aa only triggered for specific sound type 0x3a, otherwise skipped",
