      "comment": "Creates multiple projectiles (missiles) for a unit with type-based selection.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Set unit gfx flag 0x40 at offset 0xe8 (projectile active flag)\n2. Default projectile type to 0x38\n3. If unit type is monster (1) and armor type is 0x1ec, use alternate type 0x1c2\n4. Zero-initialize 0x58-byte projectile data structure (22 dwords)\n5. Set projectile flags to 0x21, store source unit pointer\n6. Call Ordinal_10326/10329 to get unit coordinates\n7. Store callback function and projectile type in structure\n8. Call CalculateUnitCoordinates to get spawn position (nDX, nDY)\n9. Assert coordinates are non-zero (fatal error if both zero)\n10. Loop (nExtraProjectiles + 2) times calling InitializeAndAllocateProjectile\n\nParameters:\n  pUnit (ECX) - Source unit creating the projectiles\n  nExtraProjectiles (EDX) - Additional projectiles beyond base 2\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Monster with armor type 0x1ec gets projectile type 0x1c2 instead of 0x38\n- Zero coordinates trigger assertion failure and application exit\n- Total projectiles created = nExtraProjectiles + 2\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x38 - Default projectile type index\n  0x1c2 - Alternate projectile type for armor 0x1ec monsters\n  0x1ec - Special monster armor type check value\n  0x21 - Projectile control flags (preset coords mode)\n  0x40 - Unit gfx flag for projectile state\n  0xe8 - Offset to dwGfxFrame in UnitAny structure\n  0x16 - Loop count for zeroing structure (22 dwords)\n  0x3ae - Source line number for assertion",
