      "comment": "Initializes a game object by setting flags and delegating to core initialization routine.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Set bit 0x40 in flags field at offset 0xe8 of the game object\n2. Read class/type field from offset 0x4 of the game object\n3. Calculate dwClassType: if field value equals 0xf3, result is 0xb0; otherwise apply mask 0xFFFFFFC7 and add 0xb0\n4. Call Ordinal_10590 with calculated class type to obtain control flags\n5. Invoke InitializeGameObject with game object pointer, class type, mode 0xffff, additional data, and control flags\n6. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\n- pGameObject (ECX): Pointer to GameObjectWithFlags structure to initialize\n- dwAdditionalData (EDX): Additional configuration data passed to initialization routine\n\nReturns:\n- void (no return value)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Magic Number 0x40: Flag bit set in object flags field at offset 0xe8\n- Magic Number 0xf3: Comparison value for class/type field determining class type calculation\n- Magic Number 0xb0: Base value added to calculate final class type (decimal 176)\n- Magic Number 0xFFFFFFC7: Mask applied when type field != 0xf3 (clears bits 3-5)\n- Magic Number 0xffff: Mode selector passed to InitializeGameObject to skip array copy\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset | Size | Field Name      | Type | Description\n-------|------|-----------------|------|------------\n0x4    | 4    | dwClassType     | uint | Object class or type identifier\n0xe8   | 4    | dwFlags         | uint | Object control flags bitfield",
      "tags": ["PARAM_2", "PROP_NOCALLER"]
