      "comment": "Applies a screen shake visual effect to a unit by randomizing position offsets.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Set unit flag 0x40 at offset 0xe8 (dwGfxFrame) to mark shake state\n2. Call CalculateMissileTargetCoordinates with mode 0xab for initial visual\n3. Get path pointer from unit offset 0x38 (pMemPool field)\n4. Get scroll position: use mercenary position if available, otherwise use path position\n5. Clear scroll position by calling SetPlayerScrollPos with NULL\n6. Loop 3 times applying random shake offsets:\n   a. Get random value 0-1; if non-zero, negate X offset (toggle between +5/-5)\n   b. Get random value 0-1; if non-zero, negate Y offset (toggle between +5/-5)\n   c. Set new position at (baseX + offsetX, baseY + offsetY)\n   d. Update visual with CalculateMissileTargetCoordinates\n7. Restore original scroll position\n\nParameters:\npUnit (UnitAny *): [ECX] Pointer to unit receiving shake effect\ndwParam (uint): [EDX] Parameter passed to CalculateMissileTargetCoordinates\n\nReturns: void\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x40: Shake effect flag applied to dwGfxFrame\n0xab (171): Mode parameter for CalculateMissileTargetCoordinates (shake visual type)\n0x38: Offset to pMemPool/path pointer in UnitAny\n0xe8: Offset to dwGfxFrame in UnitAny (via pUnit[4].dwGfxFrame)\n5: Base shake offset magnitude in pixels\n3: Number of shake iterations\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If GetMercenaryPosition returns NULL, uses GetPathPosX/Y for base coordinates\n- Random offset direction creates oscillating shake pattern",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Inventory", "PARAM_2", "PROP_NOCALLER", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
