      "comment": "Initializes missile path with randomized targeting behavior.\n\nCalled as callback during projectile initialization. Seeds RNG based on path position\nand randomly decides whether to calculate path to target (80% chance).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Return early if pMissile is NULL\n2. Get missile target X coordinate via GetMissileTargetX\n3. If target X >= 78 (0x4E), cap at 77 (0x4D) and update missile data\n4. Get path pointer from pMissile offset +0x38\n5. Get path X position via GetPathPosX\n6. Seed RNG state at pMissile->nState using (pathPosX + nRngOffset)\n7. Generate random value 0-99 via GetRandomBoundedValue\n8. If random >= 20 (80% probability):\n   a. Set path type to 10 (seeking behavior)\n   b. Set cell direction count to capped target X value\n   c. Calculate unit path to target\n\nParameters:\n  pMissile [ECX] - UnitAny pointer to missile unit, contains path at +0x38 and RNG state\n  nRngOffset [EDX] - Offset added to path position for RNG seeding\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- NULL missile pointer causes immediate return\n- Target X capped at 77 to prevent overflow\n- 20% chance to skip path calculation entirely (random < 20)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x4D (77): Maximum target X value\n- 0x4E (78): Threshold for capping target X\n- 0x38: Offset to path pointer in UnitAny\n- 10: Path type for seeking behavior\n- 100: Random value bound\n- 20: Threshold for path calculation (0x14)",
