      "comment": "Clears the client function callback for a unit's current skill.\n\nThis wrapper function retrieves the unit's current skill and resets its\nclient function pointer to 0 (NULL), effectively disabling any client-side\nskill callback processing.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call D2Common.Ordinal_10323(pUnit) to get the unit's current Skill*\n2. Call SetSkillClientFunc(pSkill, 0) to clear the client function pointer\n3. Return 1 (TRUE) indicating successful completion\n\nParameters:\n  pUnit (ECX, UnitAny*): Pointer to the unit whose skill client function will be cleared\n    IMPLICIT: Passed via ECX register in __fastcall convention\n\nReturns:\n  int: Always returns 1 (TRUE) indicating successful completion\n    - No failure conditions exist in this function\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Ordinal_10323 is D2Common.GetUnitSkill - retrieves current skill from unit\n  - Client function value 0 means no callback/disabled state\n  - Likely used during skill cleanup, reset, or deactivation operations\n  - No callers detected - may be invoked via function pointer table\n\nClassification: Wrapper/Thunk - calls two D2Common functions and returns constant",
