      "comment": "Copy or clear window contents using device context operations\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Retrieve device context handle from window handle (Ordinal_10323)\n2. Query current width dimension (Ordinal_10977)\n3. Query current height dimension (Ordinal_10978)\n4. If either dimension is non-zero:\n   a. Reset width to 0 (Ordinal_10981)\n   b. Reset height to 0 (Ordinal_10982)\n   c. Get device context from original window handle (Ordinal_10342)\n   d. Create or select compatible object with dimensions (Ordinal_10042)\n   e. If object creation succeeds:\n      - Get device context again (Ordinal_10342)\n      - Create or select compatible object again (Ordinal_10042)\n      - Perform BitBlt or similar graphics operation (Ordinal_10126) with 0x100 flag and dimension 1\n\nParameters:\n  dwHwnd (uint) - Window handle to operate on\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If both width and height are 0, function returns immediately without operations\n  - If first object creation fails (Ordinal_10042 returns 0), skips BitBlt operation\n  - Magic number 0x100 passed to Ordinal_10126 (likely SRCCOPY raster operation code)\n  - Magic number 1 passed as fourth parameter to Ordinal_10126 (possibly transparency or mode flag)\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x100 (256 decimal) - Graphics operation flag, likely SRCCOPY raster-op code for BitBlt\n  1 (decimal) - Mode or transparency flag for graphics operation\n  0 (decimal) - Reset value for width/height dimensions\n\nSSA Temporaries (Non-renameable):\n  iVar1 - Queried width dimension from Ordinal_10977\n  iVar3 - Height value used in object creation operations\n  uVar2 - Temporary device context handle from Ordinal_10342\n\nNotes:\n  - Function uses D2COMMON.DLL ordinal imports (10323, 10977, 10978, 10981, 10982, 10342, 10042, 10126)\n  - Ordinals suggest graphics device context manipulation and BitBlt-style operations\n  - Appears to perform window content copying or clearing operations\n  - Double devi