      "comment": "Initializes skill targeting for a mercenary unit with randomized skill count.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get mercenary position coordinates from unit animation state\n2. Early return if no valid mercenary position found\n3. Call Ordinal_10323 for skill setup (exact purpose unknown)\n4. Retrieve monster initialization stats pointer for unit's class ID\n5. Initialize timer/RNG state structure on stack\n6. Seed RNG with 'SEIS' signature (0x53454953)\n7. Store mercenary X position in RNG state high dword\n8. Calculate skill count range from monster stats (offset 0x1E5 - 0x1E4)\n9. If range non-zero, get random value within range\n10. Add base skill count (offset 0x1E4) to random value\n11. Clamp final skill count to minimum of 1\n12. Set skill owner type with calculated skill count\n13. Set skill target X coordinate from mercenary position[2]\n14. Set skill target Y coordinate from mercenary position[0]\n\nParameters:\npUnit (UnitAny *, ECX): Pointer to mercenary unit structure\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value but modifies global skill state via SetSkill* functions\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Returns immediately if GetMercenaryPosition returns NULL\n- Skill count clamped to minimum 1 even if monster stats indicate 0\n- pSkill variable appears uninitialized in decompiler - likely retrieved via Ordinal_10323\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x53454953 ('SEIS'): RNG seed signature for skill initialization\n0x1E4 (484): Monster stats offset for minimum skill count byte\n0x1E5 (485): Monster stats offset for maximum skill count byte\n0x4: UnitAny.dwClassId offset\n\nRelated Functions:\n- GetMercenaryPosition: Retrieves position array from unit animation state\n- GetMonsterInitStatsPtr: Returns pointer to monster initialization stats table\n- InitTimerState: Initializes 8-byte timer/RNG structure\n- InitRngSeed: Seeds RNG state with 32-bit value\n- GetRandomBoundedValue: Returns random value in range [0, bound)\n- SetSkillOwnerType: Sets skill instance owner type/count\n- SetSkillTargetX/Y: Sets skill targeting coordinates",
