      "comment": "Creates and launches a missile projectile from a unit (typically mercenary/pet).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Set unit gfx flag 0x40 at offset 0xe8 (missile animation flag)\n2. Get mercenary position via GetMercenaryPosition\n3. Calculate unit coordinates via CalculateUnitCoordinates\n4. If coordinate calculation fails, exit early\n5. Zero-initialize 0x58-byte missile setup structure (22 dwords)\n6. Set base missile flags to 0x20\n7. Copy unit coordinates to missile start position\n8. Set missile ID to 0x149 (329 decimal)\n9. If no mercenary position, set flags to 0x420 (coordinate-targeting mode)\n10. Store source unit, target position, and missile parameters\n11. Call InitializeAndAllocateProjectile to create missile\n12. If missile creation fails, exit\n13. If mercenary exists: MissileSetTargetUnit(missile, 1) - unit target mode\n14. If no mercenary: MissileSetTargetUnit(missile, 2) - coordinate target mode\n15. For coordinate targeting: call Ordinal_10326/10329 to get deltas\n16. Calculate packed target coordinate (deltaY << 16 | deltaX)\n17. Set missile target position via SetMissileTargetUnitId\n\nParameters:\n  pUnit (ECX) - UnitAny* - Source unit launching the missile\n  nMissileFlags (EDX) - int - Additional missile configuration flags\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Returns early if CalculateUnitCoordinates fails\n  - Returns early if InitializeAndAllocateProjectile fails\n  - Different targeting modes based on mercenary presence\n\nMissile Setup Structure (0x58 bytes at ESP+0x18):\n  Offset  Size  Field            Description\n  0x00    4     dwFlags          Base flags (0x20 or 0x420)\n  0x04    4     pSourceUnit      Pointer to source unit\n  0x08    4     pSourceUnit2     Duplicate source unit ptr\n  0x0C    4     pdwMercPos       Mercenary position pointer\n  0x10    4     nMissileId       Missile type ID (0x149)\n  ...\n  0x1C    4     nStartX          Starting X coordinate\n  0x20    4     nStartY          Starting Y coordinate\n  0x2C    4     nMissileParam    Missile flags parameter",
