      "comment": "Spawns a Bone Spirit missile (ID 0xBF) at the unit's calculated coordinates.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate unit coordinates via CalculateUnitCoordinates, exit if fails\n2. Get monster data field F0 for monster type 0xD4 (212)\n3. Get monster base ID for type 0xD4\n4. Zero out 0x16 (22) DWORDs of the missile parameter structure\n5. Set structure field 0x00 to 1 (flags/marker)\n6. Copy source unit pointer, coordinates, and missile ID (0xBF) to structure\n7. Call InitializeAndAllocateProjectile to create the missile\n8. If successful, set missile field 0x18 to 0x8E (142)\n9. Calculate target X = (dwMonsterDataF0 * (nParam2 - 1)) / 2 + dwMonsterBaseId\n10. Set missile target X coordinate\n\nParameters:\n  pUnit (ECX) - Source unit that spawns the missile\n  nParam2 (EDX) - Parameter used to calculate missile target position\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0xD4 (212) - Monster type ID used for coordinate calculation\n  0xBF (191) - Bone Spirit missile ID\n  0x8E (142) - Value set to missile field 0x18\n  0x16 (22) - Number of DWORDs to clear in missile params structure",
