      "comment": "Initializes a missile group with associated graphical objects for visual effects.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Fire two missiles with IDs 0x150 and 0x151 using FireMissileWithTargetValidation\n2. Get entity coordinates via Ordinal_10329 (GetUnitY) and Ordinal_10326 (GetUnitX)\n3. Create four graphical objects at entity coordinates:\n   - ID 0x14F: First graphics layer (stored in EBX)\n   - ID 0x151: Second graphics layer (stored in local)\n   - ID 0x14E: Unit-based object (pUnit)\n   - ID 0x14D: Unit-based object (pUnit_00)\n4. If first graphics layer (0x14F) created, set property values (flags=0xF, value=1)\n5. If second graphics layer (0x151) created, set property values (flags=0xF, value=1)\n6. If first missile (0x150) created:\n   - Set drawable coordinates to (0, 0, 0x15F9)\n   - Set property values (flags=-0x19/0xFFFFFFE7, value=1)\n7. If second missile (0x151) created:\n   - Set drawable coordinates to (0, 0, 0x15F9)\n   - Set property values (flags=-0x19/0xFFFFFFE7, value=1)\n8. If unit-based object (0x14E) created:\n   - Set missile target flag 0x80 on both unit objects\n\nParameters:\nnEntityId (int, ECX): Entity/unit ID to attach missiles and graphics to\ndwFlags (dword, EDX): Behavior flags passed to missile and graphics creation\n\nReturns:\nint: Always returns 1 (success)\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x150: First missile type ID\n0x151: Second missile type/graphics ID (dual use)\n0x14F: First graphics layer ID\n0x14E: Third graphics layer ID (unit-based)\n0x14D: Fourth graphics layer ID (unit-based)\n0xF: Graphics property flags for visual layers\n-0x19 (0xFFFFFFE7): Graphics property flags for missiles\n0x15F9: Z-coordinate/layer depth value\n0x80: Missile target flag\n\nFunction Classification: Worker function - creates missile/graphics group\nCallers: No direct callers found (may be called via function pointer)",
