      "instructions": ["0x22D10|PUSH|EBX", "0x22D11|PUSH|ESI", "0x22D12|PUSH|EDI", "0x22D13|MOV|EDI, ECX", "0x22D15|PUSH|-0x1", "0x22D17|MOV|EDX, 0xd8", "0x22D1C|CALL|0x6fb98230", "0x22D21|MOV|ESI, dword ptr [EDI + 0x50]", "0x22D24|MOV|EBX, EAX", "0x22D26|PUSH|EBX", "0x22D27|SAR|ESI, 0x8", "0x22D2A|CALL|0x6fb9845e", "0x22D2F|CMP|ESI, 0x6", "0x22D32|JZ|0x6faf2d78", "0x22D34|CMP|ESI, 0x16"],
      "comment": "Process entity state transition based on current state code\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Acquire global handle by calling Ordinal_10949 with handle value 0xffffffff\n2. Extract state code from entity data at offset 0x50 by shifting right 8 bits\n3. Query current counter value from system using handle (Ordinal_10976)\n4. Branch based on extracted state code:\n   a. If state code is 6: Call Ordinal_10372 to set entity state to 7, write result code 0x3200 to offset 0x54\n   b. If state code is 0x16 (22 decimal):\n      - If counter value >= 4: Call Ordinal_10372 to set entity state to 0x28, write result code 0x1100 to offset 0x54\n      - If counter value < 4: Increment counter and update system state (Ordinal_10980)\n   c. If state code is 0x1e (30 decimal): Call FUN_6fb86790 with parameter 0xc, then call FUN_6fb63670 to finalize processing\n5. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\npEntityData - Pointer to entity data structure containing state information at offset 0x50 and result field at offset 0x54\nIMPLICIT: ECX contains pEntityData pointer (fastcall convention)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value, modifies entity data structure in place\n\nSpecial Cases:\nState codes not matching 6, 0x16, or 0x1e cause function to return immediately with no action\nCounter threshold of 4 determines whether state 0x16 transitions immediately or increments\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0xffffffff - Invalid/default handle value passed to Ordinal_10949\n0x50 - Byte offset to state code field in entity structure (dword at offset 0x14 in uint array)\n0x54 - Byte offset to result code field in entity structure (dword at offset 0x15 in uint array)\n0x08 - Right shift amount to extract high byte of state code\n0x06 - State code for type 6 entity transition\n0x16 - State code for type 22 entity transition with counter check\n0x1e - State code for type 30 entity finalization\n0x07 - Target state value for state code 6 transition\n0x28 - Target state value (40 decimal) for state code 0x16 when counter >= 4\n0x0c - Parameter value (12 decimal) passed to FUN_6fb86790 for state 0x1e\n0x3200 - Result code written for state 6 completion\n0x1100 - Result code written for state 0x16 with high counter\n0x04 - Counter threshold for state 0x16 branching logic\n\nState Machine:\nState 1 (code 6): Entity requires state update to 7, write success code 0x3200\nState 2 (code 0x16): Entity requires counter-dependent transition\n  - If counter < 4: Increment counter, continue in current state\n  - If counter >= 4: Transition to state 0x28, write code 0x1100\nState 3 (code 0x1e): Entity requires finalization via FUN_6fb86790 and FUN_6fb63670\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset  Size  Field Name    Type   Description\n------  ----  ----------    ----   -----------\n0x50    4     StateCode     uint   State identifier with high byte at bits 8-15\n0x54    4     ResultCode    uint   Operation result code written by state handlers",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Inventory", "PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_1"]
    },
