      "api_calls": ["UNITS_GetSummonOwnerUnitId", "SetOverlayCallback", "FogAssert"],
      "instructions": ["0x22D90|PUSH|ESI", "0x22D91|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0x22D93|PUSH|EDI", "0x22D94|MOV|EDI, EDX", "0x22D96|PUSH|ESI", "0x22D97|CALL|0x6fb983c2", "0x22D9C|SUB|EDI, 0x9c", "0x22DA2|JS|0x6faf2e15", "0x22DA4|CMP|EDI, 0x3d", "0x22DA7|JGE|0x6faf2e15", "0x22DA9|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0x22DAB|JZ|0x6faf2e10", "0x22DAD|LEA|EDI, [EDI + EDI*0x4]", "0x22DB0|PUSH|EBX", "0x22DB1|MOV|EBX, dword ptr [ESP + 0x10]"],
      "comment": "Execute skill-specific effects and behaviors for Diablo II skills\n\nAlgorithm:\n\n1. Validate unit context by calling Ordinal_10323 to check unit validity\n2. Calculate skill table index by subtracting 0x9C (156 decimal) from skill ID to normalize to 0-based index\n3. Validate skill index is within valid range (0 to 0x3C inclusive, 61 skills total)\n4. If validation fails, call assertion handler with error message and terminate\n5. If unit validation passed, process skill effects:\n   a. Check if skill has missile targeting data (value != 0xFFFF at offset 0x0 in skill entry)\n   b. If missile targeting exists, call CalculateMissileTargetCoordinates and set unit flag 0x40 at offset +0xE8\n   c. Check if skill has callback function pointer at offset 0x4 in skill entry\n   d. If callback exists, invoke it with unit and extra parameter; otherwise set unit flag 0x40\n6. Remove audio context associated with the unit by calling Ordinal_10958 then RemoveAudioContextFromList\n\nParameters:\n\n  pUnit (UnitAny *) - Pointer to game entity executing the skill\n  nSkillId (int) - Raw skill ID from game (156-217 range expected, gets normalized to 0-61 index)\n  dwExtraParam (dword) - Extra parameter passed to skill callback functions\n\nReturns:\n\n  void - No return value\n  Terminates process if skill ID out of valid range\n\nSpecial Cases:\n\n  - Skill IDs below 156 (0x9C) or above 217 (0xD9) trigger assertion failure\n  - Skills with 0xFFFF missile target value skip missile calculation\n  - Skills with NULL callback pointer set flag 0x40 instead of executing callback\n  - Unit flag 0x40 at offset +0xE8 indicates skill effect completion or pending state\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n\n  0x9C (156 decimal) - Base skill ID offset, subtracted to normalize to table index\n  0x3D (61 decimal) - Maximum skill index (exclusive upper bound, 0-60 valid range)\n  0x14 (20 bytes) - Stride of skill effect table entries\n  0xFFFF - Sentinel value indicating no missile targeting for this skill\n  0x40 - Unit flag bit set when skill completes or has no custom callback\n  0xE8 (232 decimal) - Offset to unit flags field in UnitAny structure\n  0x683 (1667 decimal) - Assertion error code for invalid skill ID\n\nStructure Layout:\n\nSkill Effect Table Entry (20 bytes at 0x6FBA79C4):\nOffset | Size | Field Name           | Type    | Description\n-------|------|----------------------|---------|------------------------------------------\n0x00   | 4    | dwMissileTarget      | dword   | Missile targeting parameter (0xFFFF = none)\n0x04   | 4    | pfnSkillCallback     | code *  | Function pointer to skill-specific handler\n0x08   | 12   | (unknown fields)     | byte[12]| Additional skill parameters (not accessed)\n\nError Handling:\n\n  - Invalid skill index triggers Ordinal_10023 assertion with file/line info\n  - Assertion message: \"nSkillId >= 0 && nSkillId < NUM_SKILLS\"\n  - Terminates via FUN_6fb9a10f(0xFFFFFFFF) after assertion (process exit)",
      "tags": ["SRC_SkillsMon.cpp", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PROP_NOCALLER", "UI_SKILLS", "PARAM_3", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control"]
