      "api_count": 7,
      "api_calls": ["UNITS_GetOwnerGuid", "UNITS_GetUnitY", "GetApproxDistanceToCoords", "UNITS_GetOwnerGuid", "UNITS_GetUnitY", "UNITS_GetDirectionToCoord", "SetUnitDirection"],
      "instructions": ["0x22F30|SUB|ESP, 0x6c", "0x22F33|PUSH|ESI", "0x22F34|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0xc], EDX", "0x22F38|LEA|EAX, [ESP + 0x8]", "0x22F3C|PUSH|EDI", "0x22F3D|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0x22F3F|PUSH|EAX", "0x22F40|LEA|EDX, [ESP + 0xc]", "0x22F44|CALL|0x6fae96a0", "0x22F49|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0x22F4B|JZ|0x6faf3020", "0x22F51|PUSH|EBX", "0x22F52|PUSH|EBP", "0x22F53|PUSH|ESI", "0x22F54|CALL|0x6fb98122"],
      "comment": "Launches a projectile from a source unit toward a calculated target position.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get target coordinates from source unit via CalculateUnitCoordinates\n2. If coordinate calculation fails, exit early\n3. Get current X position of source unit via Ordinal_10326 (D2Common.GetUnitX)\n4. Calculate delta X = targetX - sourceX  \n5. Get current Y position of source unit via Ordinal_10329 (D2Common.GetUnitY)\n6. Calculate delta Y = targetY - sourceY\n7. Get approximate distance to target coordinates\n8. If distance is 0, set to 1 (prevent divide by zero)\n9. Calculate normalized velocity X = sourceX + (deltaX * 2) / distance\n10. Calculate normalized velocity Y = sourceY + (deltaY * 2) / distance\n11. Zero-initialize 0x16 (22) dwords of projectile parameter structure\n12. Set projectile type = 3\n13. Set projectile mode = 0xDA (218)\n14. Set owner unit pointer\n15. Set starting X/Y position to calculated velocity\n16. Set trajectory delta = delta * 5 for X and Y components\n17. Store projectile ID parameter\n18. Call InitializeAndAllocateProjectile with parameter structure\n19. If projectile created successfully, get direction to target\n20. Set projectile direction to face target\n\nParameters:\n  pSourceUnit - UnitAny* in ECX, the unit launching the projectile\n  dwProjectileId - uint in EDX, identifier for projectile type/behavior\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Returns early if CalculateUnitCoordinates fails\n  - Distance clamped to minimum of 1 to prevent divide-by-zero\n  - Projectile direction only set if allocation succeeds\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x16 (22) - Number of dwords to zero in projectile param structure\n  0x3 - Projectile type identifier\n  0xDA (218) - Projectile mode/behavior identifier\n  0x38 - Offset to unit pointer in projectile structure\n\nOrdinal References:\n  Ordinal_10326 - D2Common.GetUnitX\n  Ordinal_10329 - D2Common.GetUnitY",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_StatList", "STRUCT_Path", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PARAM_2", "PROP_NOCALLER", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
    },
