      "comment": "Copy dimensional properties from source context to target context\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get target handle from context using D2COMMON Ordinal 10323\n2. Retrieve source context structure from context using FUN_6fb63760\n3. Validate source context is not null, return 0 if null\n4. Check source context state using D2COMMON Ordinal 11021\n5. If state check returns 0, get global context value and compare with input context\n6. If context matches global value, return 0 (no copy needed)\n7. Get first dimension value from source using D2COMMON Ordinal 10326\n8. Set first dimension on target using D2COMMON Ordinal 10980\n9. Get second dimension value from source using D2COMMON Ordinal 10329\n10. Set second dimension on target using D2COMMON Ordinal 10981\n11. Get third value from source context field at offset +4\n12. Set third value on target using D2COMMON Ordinal 10982\n13. Return 1 (success)\n\nParameters:\n  nContext - Context identifier or handle for dimension copy operation\n\nReturns:\n  1 - Dimensional properties successfully copied\n  0 - Source context null, or context matches global context (no copy needed)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If source context pointer is null, returns 0 immediately without error\n  - If context matches global context value from FUN_6fb62880, skips copy and returns 0\n  - State validation via Ordinal_11021 determines if global context check is needed",
