      "comment": "Execute skill animation sequence with associated sound effects and position tracking.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Read and modify unit flags at offset 0xe8, setting bit 0x40 (animation active flag)\n2. Initialize sound parameter array with flags 0x2021 and unit pointers\n3. Calculate end coordinates by adding tile offsets to target coordinates using Ordinal_10918\n4. Store initial start coordinates and skill ID in local parameters\n5. Retrieve skill data structure from skill level using Ordinal_10582\n6. Check byte at offset 0x2f5 in skill data for multi-directional flag:\n   - If set: Use angle index 0, iteration count 1, sound type 0x73\n   - If clear: Check byte at offset 0x2f4:\n     * If clear: Update animation frames (2,2), set sound type 0x15, use angle 1, 3 iterations\n     * If set: Update animation frames (3,3), set sound type 0x14, use angle 2, 4 iterations\n7. Call UpdateAnimationFrameOffsets with calculated angle index and iteration count\n8. Reset coordinates to target position in sound parameters\n9. Set sound type to 0x2a and create first sound source via FUN_6fb77720\n10. Set delay to 2, change sound type to 0x97, create second sound source\n11. Attach sound to event 0x99a using FUN_6fb8d210 with created source pointer\n\nParameters:\n  pUnit - Pointer to UnitAny structure representing the unit performing the skill\n  dwSkillId - Skill identifier for animation lookup\n  nTargetX - Target X coordinate in world/tile space\n  nTargetY - Target Y coordinate in world/tile space\n  dwSkillLevel - Skill level affecting animation behavior and sound parameters\n\nReturns:\n  void - Function performs animation setup and sound creation as side effects\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Skill data offsets 0x2f4 and 0x2f5 control animation complexity and direction count\n- Multiple sound sources created with different types (0x2a, 0x97) for layered effects\n- Tile offset adjustments via Ordinal_10918 ensure proper world coordinate alignment\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0xe8 (232 dec) - Offset to unit flags field in UnitAny structure\n  0x40 (64 dec) - Animation active flag bit in unit flags\n  0x2021 (8225 dec) - Sound parameter flags (bits: spatial=1, use_unit_pos=5, delay=13)\n  0x2f4 (756 dec) - Offset to multi-frame animation flag in skill data\n  0x2f5 (757 dec) - Offset to multi-directional animation flag in skill data\n  0x73 (115 dec) - Simple skill sound type identifier\n  0x15 (21 dec) - Standard skill animation sound type\n  0x14 (20 dec) - Advanced skill animation sound type\n  0x2a (42 dec) - Primary skill execution sound type\n  0x97 (151 dec) - Secondary skill effect sound type\n  0x99a (2458 dec) - Skill execution sound event identifier\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset  Size  Field Name         Type      Description\n------  ----  ----------------   -------   -----------\n0x00    4     dwFlags           uint      Sound parameter control flags (0x2021)\n0x04    4     pSourceUnit       UnitAny*  Unit initiating the sound/animation\n0x08    4     pTargetUnit       UnitAny*  Unit target (same as source for self-cast)\n0x0c    4     nEndX             int       Calculated end X coordinate with tile offset\n0x10    4     nStartX           int       Initial X coordinate (target position)\n0x14    4     nEndY             int       Calculated end Y coordinate with tile offset\n0x18    4     nStartY           int       Initial Y coordinate (target position)\n0x1c    4     dwDelay           uint      Sound delay parameter (set to 2 in step 10)\n0x20    4     dwSoundType       uint      Sound type identifier (varies: 0x73/0x15/0x14/0x2a/0x97)",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_StatList", "STRUCT_Path", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "STRUCT_Skill", "PARAM_5", "STRUCT_Room1", "STRUCT_ItemData", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
