      "comment": "Validates and executes a skill action for a unit with target coordinates\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Retrieve skill handle from unit using Ordinal_10323 (GetSkillHandleFromUnit)\n2. If skill handle is NULL, log fatal error and terminate process\n3. Extract skill level from skill handle using Ordinal_10978 (GetSkillLevel)\n4. Extract target Y coordinate from skill handle using Ordinal_10977 (GetSkillTargetY)\n5. Extract target X coordinate from skill handle using Ordinal_10976 (GetSkillTargetX)\n6. Execute skill animation and sound effect with all extracted parameters\n\nParameters:\n  pUnit - Pointer to UnitAny structure representing the entity performing the skill\n  dwSkillId - Skill identifier (matches skill enumeration from D2COMMON)\n\nReturns:\n  void - Function does not return a value\n  NOTE: Terminates process with exit code 0xFFFFFFFF if skill handle validation fails\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If Ordinal_10323 returns NULL (skill handle not found), function logs error \n    \"Skill handle error\" via Ordinal_10023 and calls FUN_6fb9a10f(-1) which \n    terminates the process without returning\n  - Error message references source file path and line 0xB8 (184 decimal)\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0xB8 (184) - Source line number for error reporting\n  0xFFFFFFFF (-1) - Process exit code indicating fatal skill validation failure",
