      "comment": "Initializes a game object with type 0x76 configuration and sets control flag bit 0x40.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Set flag bit 0x40 at offset 0xe8 in the game object structure using bitwise OR operation\n2. Retrieve control flags by calling Ordinal_10590 with object type parameter 0x76\n3. Initialize game object by calling InitializeGameObject with the following parameters:\n   - Object ID: pGameObject (pointer used as identifier)\n   - Data reference: pGameObject (same pointer for ordinal data lookups)\n   - Class type: 0x76 (specific game object class)\n   - Mode selector: 0xffff (special value that bypasses array copying in InitializeGameObject)\n   - Additional data: dwAdditionalData (caller-provided configuration data)\n   - Control flags: dwControlFlags (ordinal result from step 2)\n4. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\n- pGameObject (ECX): Pointer to GameObjectWithFlags structure to initialize; used both as object\n  identifier and data reference for initialization\n- dwAdditionalData (EDX): Additional configuration data passed to InitializeGameObject\n\nReturns:\n- void (no return value)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Magic Number 0x76 (118): Object type/class identifier used for ordinal lookup and initialization\n- Magic Number 0x40 (64): Control flag bit set at offset 0xe8 before initialization; likely enables\n  specific behavior for type 0x76 objects\n- Magic Number 0xffff (65535): Mode selector value that causes InitializeGameObject to skip\n  configuration array copying and pass NULL pointer instead\n- Offset 0xe8 (232 decimal): Location of control flags field within GameObjectWithFlags structure\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset | Size | Field Name         | Type | Description\n-------|------|-------------------|------|-------------\n0xe8   | 4    | dwControlFlags    | uint | Control/status flags; bit 0x40 set by this function",
