      "instructions": ["0x23340|PUSH|ESI", "0x23341|PUSH|EDI", "0x23342|MOV|EDI, ECX", "0x23344|PUSH|EDI", "0x23345|CALL|0x6fb983c2", "0x2334A|MOV|ECX, EDI", "0x2334C|MOV|ESI, EAX", "0x2334E|CALL|0x6fb63760", "0x23353|TEST|ESI, ESI", "0x23355|MOV|EDI, EAX", "0x23357|JNZ|0x6faf3377", "0x23359|PUSH|0xd7", "0x2335E|PUSH|0x6fbb1958", "0x23363|PUSH|0x6fbb0bec", "0x23368|CALL|0x6fb99a7a"],
      "comment": "Validates and updates target coordinates for Necromancer summoning skills (Raise Skeleton/Revive).\n\nAlgorithm:\n\n1. Retrieve skill handle from unit using Ordinal_10323 (GetSkillFromUnit)\n2. Retrieve control unit (cursor target) using FUN_6fb63760\n3. Validate skill handle exists, assert if null (error: \"hSkill\")\n4. Get skill type using Ordinal_10963 (SkillsGetType)\n5. Validate skill is SKILL_RAISESKELETON (0x46) or SKILL_REVIVE (0x50)\n6. Assert if neither skill type matches (error: assertion string at 0x6fbb1994)\n7. Check control unit valid using Ordinal_11017 with parameter 0\n8. Check control unit command type field at offset +0xc equals 0xc (weapon swap command)\n9. If both conditions true:\n   a. Get X coordinate from control unit using Ordinal_10326\n   b. Set skill X coordinate using Ordinal_10980\n   c. Get Y coordinate from control unit using Ordinal_10329\n   d. Set skill Y coordinate using Ordinal_10981\n   e. Return 1 (success)\n10. Return 0 (no update)\n\nParameters:\n\npUnit - UnitAny * - Player unit containing the active skill\n\nReturns:\n\n1 (0x1) - Skill target coordinates successfully updated\n0 (0x0) - Control unit invalid or command type not weapon swap (0xc)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n- 0x46 (70) - SKILL_RAISESKELETON skill type ID\n- 0x50 (80) - SKILL_REVIVE skill type ID\n- 0xc (12) - Weapon swap command type (UnitAny field at offset +0xc)\n- 0xd7 (215) - Source line number for skill handle assertion\n- 0xd9 (217) - Source line number for skill type assertion\n- 0xffffffff (-1) - Fatal error exit code passed to FUN_6fb9a10f\n\nError Handling:\n\nFunction uses assertion-based validation with fatal termination:\n- If skill handle is null, asserts with error \"hSkill\" at SkillsNec.cpp:215\n- If skill type is not Raise Skeleton or Revive, asserts at SkillsNec.cpp:217\n- Both assertions call FUN_6fb9a10f(0xffffffff) which does not return\n\nStructure Layout:\n\nUnitAny structure field access:\nOffset | Size | Field Name      | Type  | Description\n-------|------|-----------------|-------|----------------------------------\n+0xc   | 4    | dwCommandType   | uint  | Active command type (0xc = weapon swap/skill use)",
