      "comment": "Configures skill targeting based on mercenary position data.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Find skill node by ID 0x56 (likely a specific skill type)\n2. Get mercenary position data for the unit\n3. If no position data exists, return early\n4. Set skill owner type from position data [+0x0]\n5. Set skill target X coordinate from position data [+0x8]\n6. Calculate missile target coordinates with type 0x93\n\nParameters:\n  pUnit (ECX) - UnitAny pointer, the unit whose skill is being configured\n  dwUnused (EDX) - Passed to CalculateMissileTargetCoordinates as 3rd param\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value (return value 1 at 0x6faf3676 is ignored)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Returns early if GetMercenaryPosition returns NULL\n- Assembly shows EAX=1 before return but function is void\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x56 - Skill info node ID for FindInfoNodeById\n- 0x93 - Missile target calculation type\n- 0x8 - Offset to target X in mercenary position data\n\nMercenary Position Structure (inferred):\n  Offset  Size  Field       Description\n  0x0     4     dwOwnerType Owner type for skill\n  0x4     4     unknown     (not used here)\n  0x8     4     dwTargetX   X coordinate for targeting",
