      "comment": "Initialize handle with configuration from context state.\n\nAlgorithm:\n\n1. Create/acquire handle from context using Ordinal_10323\n2. Retrieve state object from context via FUN_6fb63760\n3. Validate state object is non-null\n4. Validate state object using Ordinal_11021\n5. Extract first configuration value from state via Ordinal_10326\n6. Apply first configuration to handle using Ordinal_10980\n7. Extract second configuration value from state via Ordinal_10329\n8. Apply second configuration to handle using Ordinal_10981\n9. Apply third configuration from state field offset +0x4 using Ordinal_10982\n10. Return success (1) if all validations pass\n\nParameters:\n\npContext - Pointer to context object containing initialization state\n           (Generic void* type - specific structure type unknown without D2Client context)\n\nReturns:\n\n1 - Success, handle initialized with all configuration values from state\n0 - Failure, state object null or validation failed\n\nSpecial Cases:\n\nIf FUN_6fb63760 returns null, function immediately returns 0 without further processing.\nIf Ordinal_11021 validation fails, function returns 0 without applying configuration.\nFunction uses SSA temporary variable (uVar1) for second config value - optimized by decompiler.\n\nStructure Layout:\n\nState object structure (offset +0x4 accessed):\n  Offset | Size | Field Name      | Type | Description\n  ------ | ---- | --------------- | ---- | -----------\n  +0x0   | ?    | Unknown         | ?    | Not accessed\n  +0x4   | 4    | dwConfigValue3  | uint | Third configuration value",
