      "api_calls": ["UNITS_GetSummonOwnerUnitId", "FogAssert", "GetSkillTargetY", "GetSkillTargetX", "GetSkillOwnerType", "GetMonsterInitStatsPtr"],
      "instructions": ["0x236F0|SUB|ESP, 0x5c", "0x236F3|PUSH|EBX", "0x236F4|PUSH|EBP", "0x236F5|PUSH|ESI", "0x236F6|MOV|EBX, ECX", "0x236F8|PUSH|EDI", "0x236F9|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x10], EDX", "0x236FD|PUSH|EBX", "0x236FE|CALL|0x6fb983c2", "0x23703|MOV|ESI, EAX", "0x23705|TEST|ESI, ESI", "0x23707|JNZ|0x6faf3727", "0x23709|PUSH|0x1f6", "0x2370E|PUSH|0x6fbb1958", "0x23713|PUSH|0x6fbb0bec"],
      "comment": "Creates summon projectiles for necromancer skills.\n\nThis function is a necromancer skill handler that creates two projectiles \n(modes 0x74 and 0x98) for summoning effects. It retrieves skill information,\nvalidates the skill pointer, gets target coordinates and owner type, then\ninitializes projectile data structures.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call Ordinal_10323 (D2Common.GetSkillFromUnit) to get skill pointer (returned in EAX)\n2. Assert skill pointer is not NULL - fatal error if invalid\n3. Get skill target Y coordinate (used as monster type ID)\n4. Get skill target X coordinate\n5. Get skill owner type from skill\n6. Get monster init stats pointer using target Y as type ID\n7. If monster stats exist:\n   a. Zero-initialize 88-byte (0x58) projectile init structure\n   b. Set projectile flags to 0x2001\n   c. Set skill ID, owner type, target X, and target param\n   d. Create first projectile with mode 0x74\n   e. Create second projectile with mode 0x98 and param=2\n   f. If first projectile created successfully:\n      - Initialize skill charge table with value 0xD9\n      - Initialize game object properties with ID 0x99A\n\nParameters:\n  dwSkillId (ECX) - Skill identifier passed to projectile init\n  dwTargetParam (EDX) - Target parameter, stored in projectile init structure\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - NULL skill pointer causes assertion failure and application exit\n  - If monster init stats not found (GetMonsterInitStatsPtr returns 0), \n    no projectiles are created\n  - Second projectile created regardless of first projectile success\n  - Game object properties only initialized if first projectile succeeded\n\nSSA Temporaries (decompiler-generated, cannot be renamed):\n  pSkill (Skill*) - Return value from Ordinal_10323 in EAX\n  iVar1 (int) - Reused: targetY then monsterStatsPtr then loop counter\n  iVar2 (int) - targetX coordinate\n  dVar3 (dword) - ownerType from GetSkillOwnerType\n  nMode (void*) - First projectile pointer from InitializeAndAllocateProjectile\n  puVar4 (uint*) - Loop iterator for structure zero-initialization\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x2001 - Projectile flags (summon type flags)\n  0x74   - First projectile mode\n  0x98   - Second projectile mode\n  0xD9   - Skill charge table initialization value (217 decimal)\n  0x99A  - Game object property ID (2458 decimal)\n  0x1F6  - Assert line number (502 decimal) in SkillsNec.cpp\n\nProjectile Init Structure Layout (88 bytes):\n  Offset  Size  Field              Description\n  0x00    4     dwFlags            Projectile flags (0x2001)\n  0x04    4     dwSkillId          Skill identifier\n  0x10    4     dwMode             Projectile mode (0x74/0x98)\n  0x14    4     dwOwnerType        Owner type from skill\n  0x18    4     nTargetX           Target X coordinate\n  0x2C    4     dwTargetParam      Target parameter",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PARAM_2", "PROP_NOCALLER", "UI_SKILLS", "STRUCT_ItemData", "SRC_SkillsNec.cpp", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
