      "instructions": ["0x237D0|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [ESP + 0xc]", "0x237D4|SUB|ESP, 0x58", "0x237D7|PUSH|EBX", "0x237D8|PUSH|ESI", "0x237D9|MOV|ESI, EDX", "0x237DB|MOV|EBX, ECX", "0x237DD|PUSH|EAX", "0x237DE|CALL|0x6fb98206", "0x237E3|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0x237E5|JZ|0x6faf3866", "0x237E7|MOV|EDX, dword ptr [ESP + 0x68]", "0x237EB|PUSH|EDI", "0x237EC|MOV|ECX, 0x16", "0x237F1|XOR|EAX, EAX", "0x237F3|LEA|EDI, [ESP + 0xc]"],
      "comment": "Send skill request to game server\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate target ID using Ordinal_10582 (D2COMMON.DLL)\n2. If validation fails, return immediately without action\n3. Initialize 88-byte skill request structure by zeroing 22 dwords (0x58 bytes)\n4. Populate request structure fields:\n   - Set request type to 0x2001 (skill request identifier)\n   - Copy player ID to offset +0x4\n   - Copy skill ID to dwParameter field\n   - Copy target X coordinate to dwCoordX\n   - Copy target Y coordinate to dwCoordY\n   - Set initial operation code to 0x74 (116)\n5. Send first request with operation code 0x74 via FUN_6fb77720\n6. Update structure for second request:\n   - Change dwParameter to 2 (request mode change)\n   - Change operation code to 0x98 (152)\n7. Send second request with updated parameters via FUN_6fb77720\n8. If first request returned valid skill handle:\n   - Call FUN_6fb6f9a0 with skill handle and code 0xd9 (217)\n   - Call FUN_6fb8d210 with code 0x99a (2458), skill handle, and zero float parameters\n\nParameters:\n  dwPlayerId - Player unit identifier (ECX register)\n  dwSkillId - Skill identifier to activate (EDX register)\n  dwTargetX - Target X coordinate for skill targeting\n  dwTargetY - Target Y coordinate for skill targeting\n  dwTargetId - Target entity ID, validated before processing\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value, operates via side effects\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If target validation fails (Ordinal_10582 returns 0), function exits without sending request\n  - If FUN_6fb77720 returns NULL, skip skill handle processing (steps 8)\n  - Two-phase request protocol: initial request (0x74) followed by confirmation (0x98)\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x2001 (8193) - Skill request type identifier\n  0x74 (116) - Initial skill operation code\n  0x98 (152) - Confirmation skill operation code\n  0xd9 (217) - Skill activation parameter for FUN_6fb6f9a0\n  0x99a (2458) - Skill effect code for FUN_6fb8d210\n  0x16 (22) - Structure size in dwords (88 bytes total)\n  2 - Request mode parameter (confirmation phase)\n\nStructure Layout (88 bytes):\n  Offset  Size  Field Name        Type   Description\n  +0x00   4     dwRequestType     uint   Request type (0x2001)\n  +0x04   4     dwPlayerIdField   uint   Player unit identifier\n  +0x08   4     (unknown)         uint   Reserved/padding\n  +0x0c   4     dwParameter       uint   Skill ID / mode parameter\n  +0x10   ... (remaining fields not fully documented)\n  +0x1c   4     dwOperationCode   uint   Operation code (0x74 or 0x98)\n  +0x20   4     dwCoordX          uint   Target X coordinate\n  +0x24   4     dwCoordY          uint   Target Y coordinate",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Inventory", "PARAM_5", "STRUCT_Room1", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
