      "globals": ["0xFFFFFFFF90530000||", "0xFFFFFFFF90530008||", "0xFFFFFFFF9052FFA8||", "0xFFFFFFFF9053001C||", "0xFFFFFFFF9052FFAC||", "0xFFFFFFFF9052FFB0||", "0xFFFFFFFF9052FFD4||", "0xFFFFFFFF9052FFB8||"],
      "api_count": 3,
      "api_calls": ["GetMonsterArmorType", "CanMonsterUseInferno", "GetMonsterInitStatsPtr"],
      "instructions": ["0x23980|SUB|ESP, 0x58", "0x23983|PUSH|EBX", "0x23984|PUSH|EBP", "0x23985|PUSH|ESI", "0x23986|MOV|EBP, EDX", "0x23988|MOV|EBX, ECX", "0x2398A|CALL|0x6fb63760", "0x2398F|MOV|ESI, EAX", "0x23991|TEST|ESI, ESI", "0x23993|JZ|0x6faf3a51", "0x23999|CMP|dword ptr [ESI], 0x1", "0x2399C|JNZ|0x6faf3a51", "0x239A2|PUSH|ESI", "0x239A3|CALL|0x6fb985e4", "0x239A8|CMP|EAX, 0x4e"],
      "comment": "Spawns an inferno-type projectile for a mercenary unit.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get mercenary unit from owner via GetMercenaryPosition\n2. Validate mercenary exists and is type 1 (monster)\n3. Check armor type is not 0x4e (78) - excludes certain armor classes\n4. Verify mercenary can use inferno via CanMonsterUseInferno\n5. Validate unit state conditions via ValidateUnitStateConditions\n6. Get monster init stats and read byte at offset 0x19a for projectile class\n7. Select projectile type ID based on class byte:\n   - 1 -> 0x10c (268)\n   - 2 or default -> 0x10d (269)\n   - 3 -> 0x10e (270)\n8. Zero 0x58 bytes (22 dwords) of projectile config structure\n9. Populate projectile config:\n   - [0x00] flags = 0x2000 (skill seed flag)\n   - [0x04] source unit = pOwnerUnit\n   - [0x08] mercenary unit = pMercenaryUnit\n   - [0x10] projectile type ID\n   - [0x2c] skill level\n10. Call InitializeAndAllocateProjectile with config\n11. If projectile created, call InitializeGameObjectProperties(0x9ac)\n12. Return 1 on success, 0 on validation failure\n\nParameters:\npOwnerUnit - UnitAny pointer to the owner/caster unit (ECX, __fastcall)\nnSkillLevel - Skill level modifier for projectile damage (EDX, __fastcall)\n\nReturns:\n1 if projectile was successfully spawned\n0 if any validation check failed (null merc, wrong type, armor type 0x4e,\n  cannot use inferno, invalid state conditions)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x4e (78) - Excluded armor type\n0x19a (410) - Offset in monster stats for projectile class byte\n0x10c (268) - Inferno projectile type 1\n0x10d (269) - Inferno projectile type 2 (default)\n0x10e (270) - Inferno projectile type 3\n0x2000 - Projectile flag for skill seed initialization\n0x9ac (2476) - Game object property ID for projectile effects\n0x58 (88) - Size of projectile config structure (22 dwords)",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Inventory", "PARAM_2", "PROP_NOCALLER", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
