      "comment": "Processes Necromancer raise/summon skill activation for skeleton and golem summoning.\n\nAlgorithm:\n\n1. Validate unit pointer by calling Ordinal_10323(pUnit)\n2. Calculate skill index by subtracting 0x42 from nSkillId\n3. Validate skill index is in valid range [0, 0x1E) (0-29, covering 30 Necromancer skills)\n4. If out of range, assert with \"nSkillId >= 0 && nSkillId < NUM_NECROMANCER_SKILLS\" and terminate\n5. If validation failed (result == 0), exit early\n6. Calculate table index: nSkillIndex * 0x14 (20-byte stride for skill descriptor table)\n7. Check if missile target ID at g_aNecromancerSkillTable[nSkillIndex] is not 0xFFFF\n8. If valid target, call CalculateMissileTargetCoordinates(pUnit, dwTargetId, dwParam)\n9. Set delay/pending flag 0x40 in pUnit->dwFlags at offset 0xE8\n10. Check if callback function pointer at g_apfnNecromancerSkillCallbacks[nSkillIndex] exists\n11. If callback exists, invoke callback(pUnit, dwParam) [__fastcall convention]\n12. If no callback, set delay flag 0x40 again (redundant safety set)\n13. Retrieve audio context for unit with Ordinal_10958(pUnit, 0)\n14. If audio context exists, remove it from list with RemoveAudioContextFromList(pAudioContext)\n15. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\n\npUnit (UnitAny *) - Pointer to the unit (player/monster) activating the skill\nnSkillId (int) - Skill ID from game skill system (range 0x42-0x5F for Necromancer raise/summon skills)\ndwParam (uint) - Additional parameter passed to skill callback (context-dependent, often target coordinates or flags)\n\nIMPLICIT: ESI and EDI preserved across call (saved/restored by function prologue/epilogue)\n\nReturns:\n\nvoid - Function does not return a value\nSide effect: Modifies pUnit->dwFlags bit 0x40 (delay/pending flag)\nSide effect: May invoke skill-specific callback function\nSide effect: Removes audio context from active list\n\nSpecial Cases:\n\nSkill ID Validation:\n- Valid range: 0x42 (66) to 0x5F (95) inclusive\n- Converts to array index: nSkillId - 0x42 = [0, 29]\n- Out of range triggers assertion failure and FUN_6fb9a10f(-1) termination\n\nEarly Exit Conditions:\n- Validation function Ordinal_10323 returns 0 (unit invalid)\n- No action taken, function returns immediately\n\nMissile Target Handling:\n- Table entry 0xFFFF means \"no missile target\" (skip CalculateMissileTargetCoordinates)\n- Valid target IDs trigger missile trajectory calculation\n- Delay flag 0x40 set regardless of target validity\n\nCallback Function Invocation:\n- NULL function pointer (0x0) means \"no callback\" (skip callback invocation)\n- Non-NULL callback invoked with __fastcall convention (ECX=pUnit, EDX=dwParam)\n- Delay flag set in both callback and no-callback paths\n\nAudio Context Cleanup:\n- Audio context lookup may return NULL (no context exists)\n- Non-NULL context removed from audio system's active context list\n- Always performed regardless of skill success/failure\n\nStructure Layout:\n\nNecromancer Skill Descriptor (20 bytes, stride 0x14):\n\nOffset | Size | Field Name             | Type  | Description\n-------|------|------------------------|-------|------------------------------------------\n+0x00  |  4   | dwMissileTargetId      | uint  | Target ID for missile calculation (0xFFFF = none)\n+0x04  | 16   | (remaining fields)     | ?     | Unknown structure continuation\n\nFunction Pointer Table (4 bytes per entry, stride 0x4 but accessed as [index*5]):\n\nOffset | Size | Field Name             | Type              | Description\n-------|------|------------------------|-------------------|------------------------------\n+0x00  |  4   | pfnSkillCallback       | function pointer  | Skill-specific handler or NULL\n\nUnitAny Extended Structure (at least 236 bytes based on offset 0xE8):\n\nOffset | Size | Field Name             | Type  | Description\n-------|------|------------------------|-------|------------------------------------------\n+0xE8  |  4   | dwFlags                | uint  | Unit state flags (bit 0x40 = delay/pending)\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n\n0x42 (66 decimal) - Minimum Necromancer raise/summon skill ID\n0x1E (30 decimal) - Number of Necromancer raise/summon skills in table\n0x14 (20 decimal) - Byte stride for skill descriptor table entries\n0x5 (5 decimal) - Function pointer table multiplier (appears to index 20-byte aligned pointers)\n0xFFFF (65535 decimal) - Sentinel value for \"no missile target\"\n0x40 (64 decimal, bit 6) - Delay/pending flag in unit flags at offset 0xE8\n0xE8 (232 decimal) - Byte offset to dwFlags field in UnitAny structure\n0x332 (818 decimal) - Assertion line number in SkillsNec.cpp\n\nError Handling:\n\nAssertion Failure Path:\n- Invalid skill ID (< 0x42 or >= 0x60) triggers assertion\n- Calls Ordinal_10023 with assertion string, source file, line number\n- Assertion message: \"nSkillId >= 0 && nSkillId < NUM_NECROMANCER_SKILLS\"\n- Source file: \"C:\\Projects\\Diablo2\\Source\\D2Client\\Skills\\SkillsNec.cpp\"\n- Line number: 0x332 (818)\n- Terminates execution with FUN_6fb9a10f(0xFFFFFFFF) [does not return]\n\nValidation Failure:\n- Ordinal_10323 returns 0 (unit pointer invalid or failed validation)\n- Function returns immediately without taking any action\n- No error logged, silent failure mode\n\nGlobal Data References:\n\ng_aNecromancerSkillTable @ 0x6fba7e8c - Array of 30 skill descriptors (20 bytes each)\ng_apfnNecromancerSkillCallbacks @ 0x6fba7e90 - Array of 30 function pointers (4 bytes each, stride anomaly)\n\nNote: Function pointer table stride calculation uses multiplier 5 ([index*5]*4 bytes) instead of 1,\nsuggesting either 20-byte alignment requirement or table contains additional metadata between pointers.",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Inventory", "PROP_NOCALLER", "UI_SKILLS", "PARAM_3", "SRC_SkillsNec.cpp", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control"]
