      "global_count": 18,
      "globals": ["0xFFFFFFFF9052FFEC||", "0xFFFFFFFF9052FFE4||", "0xFFFFFFFF9052FFD8||", "0xFFFFFFFF9052FFE8||", "0xFFFFFFFF9052FFCC||", "0xFFFFFFFF90530004||", "0xFFFFFFFF90530000||", "0xFFFFFFFF9052FFF0||", "0xFFFFFFFF9052FFE0||", "0xFFFFFFFF9052FFFC||", "0xFFFFFFFF9052FFC4||", "0xFFFFFFFF9052FFDC||", "0xFFFFFFFF9052FFF8||", "0xFFFFFFFF9052FFD4||", "0xFFFFFFFF9052FFD0||", "0xFFFFFFFF9052FFF4||", "0xFFFFFFFF9052FFC0||", "0xFFFFFFFF9052FFC8||"],
      "api_count": 12,
      "api_calls": ["GetUnitLevel", "GetUnitX", "GetUnitTargetCoords", "GetExpansionModeIfInitialized", "UNITS_GetSummonOwnerUnitId", "FogAssert", "GetSkillsTxtId", "FogAssert", "GetSkillTargetY", "STATLIST_GetUnitOwnerType", "...+2 more"],
      "instructions": ["0x23BD0|SUB|ESP, 0x40", "0x23BD3|PUSH|EBX", "0x23BD4|PUSH|EBP", "0x23BD5|PUSH|ESI", "0x23BD6|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0x23BD8|PUSH|EDI", "0x23BD9|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x3c], EDX", "0x23BDD|PUSH|ESI", "0x23BDE|CALL|0x6fb981d0", "0x23BE3|PUSH|ESI", "0x23BE4|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x38], EAX", "0x23BE8|CALL|0x6fb981ca", "0x23BED|LEA|ECX, [ESP + 0x28]", "0x23BF1|XOR|EBP, EBP", "0x23BF3|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x38], EAX"],
      "comment": "Renders animated charge skill effect along trajectory between source and target\n\nAlgorithm:\n\n1. Retrieve source coordinates using Ordinal_10333 and Ordinal_10334\n2. Calculate delta vector (nDeltaX, nDeltaY) using Ordinal_10141\n3. Validate direction flag: if nDirection == 0, require nDeltaY < 0 (moving up), else require nDeltaY >= 0 (moving down)\n4. Calculate Manhattan-based distance metric: max(abs(nDeltaX), abs(nDeltaY)) + 2 * min(abs(nDeltaX), abs(nDeltaY))\n5. Normalize delta to step size by dividing by distance/2, then multiply by 15 (0xf) for animation speed\n6. Extract animation frame from pControl[0x14] upper 24 bits (>> 8)\n7. Get skill handle from Ordinal_10323, validate type == 0x6b (SKILL_CHARGE)\n8. Get segment count from Ordinal_10978 (determines number of effect instances along trajectory)\n9. For each segment, decrement animation frame with wraparound (0 to 7)\n10. If game mode active, apply viewport transform using Ordinal_10330, Ordinal_10327, Ordinal_10067, GetRelativeViewportX, GetViewportYOffsetAdjusted\n11. Calculate render position: if nDirection == 0, use accumulated position (forward), else use reversed position (backward)\n12. Render segment at calculated position using FUN_6fb91fe0\n13. Advance accumulator by step values (nAccumX += nStepX, nAccumY += nStepY)\n14. Restore original animation frame to pControl[0x14] after loop\n\nParameters:\n\n  pControl - UI control structure pointer, offset +0x14 contains animation frame and flags (upper 24 bits = frame index 0-7)\n  dwCellFile - Cell file handle for rendering charge effect graphics\n  nDirection - Direction flag: 0 = Render from source to target (charge forward), 1 = Render from target to source (charge backward)\n\nReturns:\n\n  void - No return value, terminates on error via FUN_6fb9a10f(0xffffffff)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n\n  Early Exit: If delta validation fails (wrong sign for direction), return without rendering\n  Zero Distance: If both nDeltaX and nDeltaY are zero, set distance to 1 to avoid division by zero\n  Skill Type Validation: Function asserts skill type == 0x6b (SKILL_CHARGE), calls error handler for other types\n  Missing Skill Handle: Calls error handler with g_szSkillHandleError if Ordinal_10323 returns NULL\n\nMagic Numbers:\n\n  0xf (15) - Animation speed multiplier for trajectory step calculation\n  0x6b (107) - SKILL_CHARGE type constant from SkillsGetType\n  0x60 (96) - Parameter for Ordinal_10067 viewport transform\n  0x14 (20) - Offset to animation frame field in control structure\n  0x97 (151) - Alternative skill type handled by RenderControlWithTransparency\n  0x12 (18) - Control type check value in caller (param_1[3] == 0x12)\n  0xe (14) - Alternative control type check value in caller (param_1[3] == 0x0e)\n\nError Handling:\n\n  Missing Skill: If Ordinal_10323 returns NULL, push g_szSkillHandleError and call FUN_6fb9a10f(-1)\n  Invalid Skill Type: If skill type != 0x6b, push \"SkillsGetType (hSkill) == SKILL_CHARGE\" error and call FUN_6fb9a10f(-1)\n  Both errors use Ordinal_10023 to format error with file path and line numbers 0x3d (61) or 0x3e (62)\n\nDistance Calculation:\n\n  Step 1: Take absolute values of nDeltaX and nDeltaY\n  Step 2: Compare abs values, identify larger and smaller\n  Step 3: distance = larger + (smaller * 2), favors diagonal movement\n  Step 4: Divide by 2 for final metric, ensures minimum distance of 1\n\nAnimation Frame Cycling:\n\n  Frame stored in bits 8-31 of pControl[0x14] (extracted via >> 8)\n  Each segment decrements frame: nAnimFrame = (nAnimFrame - 1) & 0x7 (wraps 7 -> 0)\n  Frame restored to original value after all segments rendered\n  Provides smooth animation as charge effect travels along trajectory",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "STRUCT_Room2", "STRUCT_ItemData", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData", "STRUCT_StatList", "PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Path", "SRC_SkillsPal.cpp", "UI_SKILLS", "PARAM_3", "STRUCT_Skill"]
