      "instructions": ["0x23E00|SUB|ESP, 0x8", "0x23E03|PUSH|EBX", "0x23E04|PUSH|EBP", "0x23E05|PUSH|ESI", "0x23E06|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0x23E08|PUSH|EDI", "0x23E09|PUSH|ESI", "0x23E0A|CALL|0x6fb983c2", "0x23E0F|MOV|EDI, EAX", "0x23E11|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [ESI + 0x38]", "0x23E14|TEST|EDI, EDI", "0x23E16|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x14], EDI", "0x23E1A|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x10], EAX", "0x23E1E|JNZ|0x6faf3e3b", "0x23E20|PUSH|0x69"],
      "comment": "Executes a corpse-targeting skill (Find Item, Grim Ward, or similar).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Retrieve skill handle from unit via Ordinal_10323\n2. Assert skill handle is valid (fatal error if null)\n3. Get mercenary/target position from unit\n4. If unit is Player (type 0) and target exists and is visible:\n   - Call InitializeItemStats and return result early\n5. Based on unit type, initialize game object properties:\n   - Player (type 0): Object ID 0x948 (Find Item skill effect)\n   - Monster (type 1): Check armor type for skill variant:\n     - Armor 0x1B4: Object ID 0x8AC (Grim Ward variant)\n     - Armor 0x1B9: Object ID 0x6D5 (alternate variant)\n6. Set skill owner type based on target:\n   - If target exists and not in state 0x36: use target's type\n   - Otherwise: set owner type to 6 (no target)\n7. Set skill target coordinates from target unit\n8. Set skill target GUID to 7\n9. Get animation rate multiplier:\n   - Player: byte at character slot + 0x41 (shifted to high byte)\n   - Monster: dword at monster stats + 0x1A0 (shifted left 8)\n   - Special case: monster ID 0xD3 sets target GUID to 0xF\n10. Calculate animation rate: (stat 0x43 * rate * 256 / 100) * field_F0[0x6B] / 100\n11. Set animation rate and calculate path to target\n12. If target exists, validate unit and process global data\n13. Set skill client function to 0x1001\n14. Set skill target Y to 0\n15. Process unit ability and return 1 (success)\n\nParameters:\n  pUnit (ECX): Pointer to the unit executing the skill\n\nReturns:\n  int: Result from InitializeItemStats on early exit, or 1 on success\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Monster ID 0xD3 (Baal?) gets special target GUID 0xF\n- Monster animation uses SetCellDirectionCount with value 0x1E (30)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x948: Find Item skill object ID\n- 0x8AC: Grim Ward skill object ID (armor type 0x1B4)\n- 0x6D5: Alternate skill object ID (armor type 0x1B9)\n- 0x36: Unit state flag for target validity\n- 0x43: Stat ID for skill rate calculation\n- 0x6B: Monster data field index for rate modifier\n- 0x1001: Skill client function identifier\n- 0xD3: Special monster ID (Baal)",
