      "comment": "ProcessMonsterSkillTargeting - Updates monster skill targeting and animation based on monster type\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call Ordinal_10323 (D2Common - skill/unit state initialization)\n2. Get unit flags via GetUnitFlags and skill flags via GetSkillFlags\n3. Check if unit is player (type 0) and has skill mode 3 - apply aura effect and return\n4. If unit is monster (type 1), check monster armor type for special handling:\n   - 0xD3: If animation frame is 5, apply aura effect with mode 1\n   - 0x1B9: If animation frame is 16, initialize game object properties (0x8AC)\n5. Set animation parameters based on monster armor type:\n   - 0x1B4: max_frame=29(0x1D), max_anim=10\n   - 0x49: max_frame=14(0xE), max_anim=7\n   - 0xD3: max_frame=31(0x1F), max_anim=14\n   - 0x1B9: max_frame=22(0x16), max_anim=14\n6. Get skill owner type and target X (unit ID) from skill data\n7. If owner type is not 6, find target unit in hash table\n8. Branch based on unit flags bit 0:\n   - If bit 0 clear: Clear skill targeting, calculate remaining frames, find new target\n   - If bit 0 set: Check visibility and update animation or find new target\n\nParameters:\n  pUnit (ECX) - UnitAny * - Pointer to the unit to process (monster or player)\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nMonster Armor Type Constants:\n  0x49 (73) - Sand Maggot type\n  0xD3 (211) - Unraveler/Mummy type\n  0x1B4 (436) - Act Boss type 1\n  0x1B9 (441) - Act Boss type 2\n\nFlag Bits:\n  0x01 - Unit targeting active\n  0x02 - Unit searching for target\n  0x40 - Animation state flag (cleared at unit offset 0xE8)\n\nOrdinal Functions:\n  Ordinal_10323 - D2Common skill/unit state initialization\n  Ordinal_10326 - D2Common GetUnitX coordinate helper\n  Ordinal_10329 - D2Common GetUnitY coordinate helper\n\nSSA Temporaries (cannot be renamed):\n  bVar1 (bool) - fVisibilityResult: Result of CheckTargetVisibility\n  dVar2 (dword) - dwUnitFlags: Unit flags from GetUnitFlags\n  iVar3 (int) - nMonsterType: Monster armor type from GetMonsterArmorType\n  iVar5 (int) - nMaxFrame: Maximum animation frame counter\n  pUVar4 (UnitAny_conflict*) - pTargetUnit: Target unit found by search\n  puVar6 (uint*) - pSearchBuffer: Pointer for zeroing search structure\n  extraout_var/extraout_var_00 (undefined3) - SSA return value padding\n\nStack Variables:\n  local_30: dwMaxAnimFrame - Maximum animation frame count for monster type\n  local_20: dwSearchFlags - Target search flags (3 = search mode)\n  local_1c: pSourceUnit - Source unit for target search\n  local_18: dwTargetUnitId - Target unit ID (0xFFFFFFFF = any)\n  local_c: dwSearchMode - Search mode (3 = standard)",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PROP_NOCALLER", "STRUCT_Room2", "STRUCT_ItemData", "PARAM_1", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData", "STRUCT_StatList", "STRUCT_MonsterData", "PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Path", "STRUCT_Skill"]
