      "comment": "Error handler for ability type 0x6b, manages ability state flags before dispatching error notification.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Retrieve current ability handle using Ordinal_10950 (GetAbilityHandle)\n2. Query ability state flags from handle using Ordinal_10985 (GetAbilityFlags)\n3. Test bit 0 (0x01) in flags for error processing enable state\n4. If bit 0 set, clear bit 0 and set bit 1 (0x02) using Ordinal_10984 (SetAbilityFlags)\n5. Report error code 0x36 to error handler using Ordinal_10486 (ReportAbilityError)\n\nParameters:\npAbilityData (uint *): Pointer to ability data structure passed from HandleAbilityErrorByType\n\nIMPLICIT:\nECX: Contains pAbilityData on entry per __fastcall convention\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Function performs state flag modification and error notification, no return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Bit 0 clear: Skip flag modification, proceed directly to error reporting\n- Bit 0 set: Transition state by clearing bit 0 and setting bit 1 before error report\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x6b (decimal 107): Ability type code for this specialized error handler\n0x01 (bit 0): Error processing enable flag tested for state transition\n0x02 (bit 1): Error processed flag set during state transition\n0x36 (decimal 54): Error code identifier reported to error handling system\n0xfffffffe: Bitmask used to clear bit 0 (AND mask for all bits except bit 0)\n\nFlag Bits:\nBit 0 (0x01): Error processing enable - triggers state transition when set\nBit 1 (0x02): Error processed marker - set after processing error for type 0x6b\n\nError Handling:\nFunction performs unconditional error reporting with code 0x36 regardless of flag state.\nFlag modification only affects internal ability state tracking, not error propagation.\n\nState Transition:\nThe function implements a state machine for error processing:\nState 1: Bit 0 set (0x01) - Error processing enabled, transition to State 2\nState 2: Bit 1 set (0x02) - Error processed, bit 0 cleared\nThis prevents duplicate error processing for the same ability instance.",
      "tags": ["PARAM_1", "PROP_SMALL"]
