      "instructions": ["0x24380|PUSH|ESI", "0x24381|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0x24383|CALL|0x6fb984d6", "0x24388|MOV|EDX, EAX", "0x2438A|MOV|ECX, ESI", "0x2438C|CALL|0x6fb868b0", "0x24391|SUB|EAX, 0x3", "0x24394|MOV|ECX, 0x0", "0x24399|SETS|CL", "0x2439C|DEC|ECX", "0x2439D|PUSH|0x0", "0x2439F|AND|EAX, ECX", "0x243A1|PUSH|0x0", "0x243A3|PUSH|EAX", "0x243A4|MOV|EDX, ESI"],
      "comment": "Apply skill stat modifier with clamped value adjustment.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call Ordinal_10365 from D2COMMON.DLL to retrieve raw stat value\n2. Call FUN_6fb868b0 with unit pointer and raw value to process/adjust value\n3. Subtract 3 from adjusted value\n4. Clamp result to minimum of 0 using bit manipulation\n5. Call FUN_6fb8d210 with stat ID 0x955, unit pointer, clamped float value, 0.0, and 0\n6. Return success code 1\n\nParameters:\n  pUnit (UnitAny *) - Pointer to game entity/unit structure passed in ECX register\n\nReturns:\n  int - Always returns 1 indicating successful application of stat modifier\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x955 (2389 decimal) - Stat or skill identifier passed to FUN_6fb8d210\n  0x3 (3 decimal) - Adjustment offset subtracted from raw value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  If adjusted value is less than 3, result is clamped to 0 before conversion to float\n  The clamping uses bitwise: (value - 3) & (((int)(value - 3) < 0) - 1)\n    When negative: mask = 0xFFFFFFFF, result ANDed becomes 0\n    When positive: mask = 0x00000000, result passes through unchanged",
      "tags": ["PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_1"]
