      "instructions": ["0x243C0|SUB|ESP, 0x40", "0x243C3|PUSH|EDI", "0x243C4|MOV|EDI, ECX", "0x243C6|OR|dword ptr [EDI + 0xe8], 0x40", "0x243CD|CALL|0x6fb63760", "0x243D2|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0x243D4|JZ|0x6faf44bd", "0x243DA|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [EDI + 0x38]", "0x243DD|PUSH|EBX", "0x243DE|PUSH|EBP", "0x243DF|PUSH|ESI", "0x243E0|PUSH|EAX", "0x243E1|CALL|0x6fb985c0", "0x243E6|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0x243E8|JZ|0x6faf43fa"],
      "comment": "Creates a scatter projectile from a mercenary unit with random directional variance.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Set graphics flag 0x40 on unit's dwGfxFrame (offset 0xe8) to mark projectile pending\n2. Get mercenary position data - exit early if null\n3. Check if unit has a valid room (GetRoomNext on pMemPool at offset 0x38):\n   - If room exists: get unit direction via Ordinal_10457, divide by 8 for 8-way index\n   - If no room: get random direction index 0-7\n4. Add random scatter (-1 to +1) to base direction, wrap to 0-7\n5. Build direction offset lookup table on stack:\n   - X offsets [0]: 0, -1, -2, -1, 0, 1, 2, 1 (indices 0-7)\n   - Y offsets [8]: 2, 1, 0, -1, -2, -1, 0, 1 (indices 8-15)\n6. Get unit X coordinate via Ordinal_10326\n7. Add X offset from table[direction_index]\n8. Get unit Y coordinate via Ordinal_10329\n9. Add Y offset from table[direction_index + 8]\n10. Get random missile type variation (0-2) and add 0x12 (base missile ID 18-20)\n11. Create projectile at calculated position via CreateProjectileFromUnit\n\nParameters:\n  pUnit (ECX) - UnitAny* - Source unit (mercenary) creating the projectile\n\nReturns: void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Early exit if GetMercenaryPosition returns NULL\n- Direction index calculation handles negative values via signed modulo\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x40: Graphics flag for projectile pending\n- 0xe8: Offset to dwGfxFrame field in UnitAny\n- 0x38: Offset to pMemPool/pRoom in UnitAny\n- 8: Number of cardinal/ordinal directions\n- 3: Random scatter range and missile type variation count\n- 0x12 (18): Base missile type ID for scatter projectiles\n\nCalled Ordinals:\n- Ordinal_10457: D2Common.GetUnitDirection - returns 0-255 direction\n- Ordinal_10326: D2Common.GetUnitX - get unit X coordinate\n- Ordinal_10329: D2Common.GetUnitY - get unit Y coordinate",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_StatList", "STRUCT_Path", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PROP_NOCALLER", "STRUCT_Skill", "STRUCT_Room2", "PARAM_1", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
