      "comment": "Apply stat value with negative clamping to game entity\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Retrieve base stat value from D2COMMON Ordinal_10365\n2. Process stat value with context parameter via FUN_6fb868b0\n3. Calculate clamped adjustment: subtract 3 from processed value\n4. Apply negative clamping: if (value - 3) >= 0, set to 0; else keep (value - 3)\n5. Convert clamped value to float and apply via FUN_6fb8d210 with stat ID 0x957\n6. Return success code 1\n\nParameters:\n- nContextParam (int): Context parameter passed to stat processing functions\n  IMPLICIT: this in ECX (__fastcall)\n\nReturns:\n- int: Always returns 1 (success)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- When processed value >= 3: Clamped to 0 (no negative adjustment)\n- When processed value < 3: Applies negative adjustment (value - 3)\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n- 0x957 (2391 decimal): Stat ID for the stat being modified\n- 0x3 (3 decimal): Threshold value for clamping calculation\n- 0.0: Secondary float parameter to FUN_6fb8d210 (unused)\n- 0: Fifth parameter to FUN_6fb8d210 (flags or options)\n\nNote: Function uses register-optimized variables - uVar1 exists only in decompiler view\nand is held in EAX throughout execution. No stack-allocated local variables.",
