      "instructions": ["0x24650|PUSH|ESI", "0x24651|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0x24653|CMP|dword ptr [ESI], 0x0", "0x24656|JNZ|0x6faf4671", "0x24658|PUSH|0x0", "0x2465A|PUSH|0x0", "0x2465C|PUSH|0x4", "0x2465E|MOV|EDX, 0x5", "0x24663|CALL|0x6fb86850", "0x24668|MOV|ECX, EAX", "0x2466A|MOV|EDX, ESI", "0x2466C|CALL|0x6fb8d210", "0x24671|CMP|dword ptr [ESI], 0x1", "0x24674|JNZ|0x6faf46b5", "0x24676|CMP|dword ptr [ESI + 0x4], 0xd3"],
      "comment": "Plays sound effects based on state transitions and values.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if state is 0 (initialization state)\n2. If state 0: Validate hit class 5, play sound with ID 4 (0x4) and delay\n3. Check if state is 1 (active state)\n4. If state 1 and value is 0xd3 (211): Validate hit class 5, play sound with ID 6 (0x6) and delay\n5. If state 1 and value is 0x1ac (428): Play sound with ID 0x300 (768) immediately\n6. Return success (1)\n\nParameters:\n  pStateDesc - Pointer to StateDescriptor containing state and value fields\n    pStateDesc->dwState: State identifier (0 = initialization, 1 = active)\n    pStateDesc->dwStateValue: State-specific value (0xd3 or 0x1ac for state 1)\n\nReturns:\n  Always returns 1 (success)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  State 0: Triggers sound ID 4 with delay 5.60519e-45 (reinterpreted as int 0x4)\n  State 1, Value 0xd3: Triggers sound ID 6 with delay 8.40779e-45 (reinterpreted as int 0x6)\n  State 1, Value 0x1ac: Triggers sound ID 0x300 immediately with no delay\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x4 (4) - Sound ID for initialization state (reinterpreted from float 5.60519e-45)\n  0x6 (6) - Sound ID for state 1 value 0xd3 (reinterpreted from float 8.40779e-45)\n  0x300 (768) - Sound ID for state 1 value 0x1ac\n  0xd3 (211) - State value threshold for first sound trigger\n  0x1ac (428) - State value threshold for second sound trigger\n  5 - Hit class validation parameter\n\nStructure Layout:\n  StateDescriptor (8 bytes):\n  Offset | Size | Field Name      | Type | Description\n  -------|------|-----------------|------|----------------------------------\n  0x0    | 4    | dwState         | uint | State identifier (0 or 1)\n  0x4    | 4    | dwStateValue    | uint | State-specific value (0xd3, 0x1ac)",
      "tags": ["PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_1"]
    },
