      "instructions": ["0x24780|PUSH|EBX", "0x24781|PUSH|EBP", "0x24782|PUSH|ESI", "0x24783|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0x24785|PUSH|EDI", "0x24786|PUSH|ESI", "0x24787|CALL|0x6fb983c2", "0x2478C|MOV|EDI, EAX", "0x2478E|PUSH|EDI", "0x2478F|CALL|0x6fb9845e", "0x24794|MOV|EBP, EAX", "0x24796|TEST|EBP, EBP", "0x24798|JLE|0x6faf483c", "0x2479E|PUSH|EDI", "0x2479F|CALL|0x6fb98458"],
      "comment": "Consume a protection item from inventory and apply its damage reduction effect to the unit.\n\nAlgorithm:\n\n1. Retrieve inventory/skill handle from unit using Ordinal_10323\n2. Get current item count from handle using Ordinal_10976\n3. Validate item count is positive, return if zero or negative\n4. Get item type identifier using Ordinal_10977\n5. Get query parameter using Ordinal_10978\n6. Search for item in inventory using FUN_6fb60e10 with query parameters\n7. If item not found, perform fallback search using BuildAndExecuteItemQuery with query flags 0x4 (type filter) on all inventory (target 0xFFFFFFFF)\n8. Return early if no item found in either search\n9. Decrement item count in handle using Ordinal_10980 (count - 1)\n10. Validate decremented count is still positive\n11. Query for target item using BuildAndExecuteItemQuery with found item's pMemPool field as target\n12. Return early if target item query fails\n13. Extract property values from target item using Ordinal_10329 and Ordinal_10326\n14. Apply properties to unit field at offset 0x38 using Ordinal_10216 with flags 0x0\n15. Update handle with target item's dwUnitType field using Ordinal_10981\n16. Update handle with target item's pMemPool field using Ordinal_10982\n17. Retrieve updated handle value using Ordinal_10963\n18. Calculate damage reduction value using Ordinal_10991\n19. Apply damage reduction effect to unit using ApplyDamageReduction\n20. Trigger state update using FUN_6fb87e60 with unit's dwUnitId and flag 0x1\n\nParameters:\n\npUnit - Pointer to UnitAny structure representing the player/entity consuming the item\n\nReturns:\n\nvoid - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n\nIf item count is zero or negative, function returns immediately without processing\nIf item not found in primary or fallback search, function returns without consuming\nIf decremented count becomes zero or negative, function skips effect application\nIf target item query fails, function returns without applying effects\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n\n0xFFFFFFFF (4294967295) - Wildcard target for inventory-wide item search\n0x4 (4) - Query type flag indicating item type filtering\n0x1 (1) - State update flag for FUN_6fb87e60\n0x0 (0) - Default flags value for property application\n0x38 (56) - Byte offset to UnitAny field used for property application (pUnit[1].pMemPool in 32-bit pointer arithmetic = pUnit + 0x38 bytes)\n0xC (12) - Byte offset to dwUnitId field in UnitAny structure",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Inventory", "PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_1"]
    },
