      "instructions": ["0x24850|SUB|ESP, 0x60", "0x24853|PUSH|EBX", "0x24854|PUSH|EBP", "0x24855|PUSH|ESI", "0x24856|MOV|EBX, ECX", "0x24858|PUSH|EDI", "0x24859|PUSH|EBX", "0x2485A|CALL|0x6fb98164", "0x2485F|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0x24861|JZ|0x6faf499c", "0x24867|PUSH|EAX", "0x24868|CALL|0x6fb98416", "0x2486D|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0x2486F|JNZ|0x6faf499c", "0x24875|PUSH|0x1"],
      "comment": "Executes monster skill 0x77 (119) - spawns multiple projectiles in a circular nova pattern.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get the unit's room via UNITS_GetRoom\n2. Validate DRLG subtype allows skill execution (returns early if invalid)\n3. Find skill node by ID 0x77 and get skill level\n4. Get monster skill damage value via GetMonsterSkillId\n5. Get monster data field F0 (base damage divisor) via GetMonsterDataFieldF0\n6. Calculate projectile count: (damage^2 / fieldF0^2) / (random(0-17) + 1)\n7. Initialize 0x58-byte projectile parameters struct (zero 0x16 dwords)\n8. Set projectile flags to 0x2001, skill ID to 0x39 (57)\n9. Loop for each projectile to spawn:\n   a. Generate random X offset in range [-damage, +damage]\n   b. Generate random Y offset in range [-damage, +damage]\n   c. Check if offset is within circular radius (X^2 + Y^2 < damage^2)\n   d. If within radius: get unit X/Y coords via Ordinal_10326/10329\n   e. Set target position = unit position + offset + 2\n   f. Create projectile via InitializeAndAllocateProjectile\n   g. Set random direction (0-63) on created projectile\n\nParameters:\n  pUnit (ECX) - UnitAny* - Monster unit executing the skill\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Returns immediately if unit has no room\n  - Returns immediately if DRLG subtype validation fails\n  - Skips projectile if random offset falls outside circular radius\n  - Uses circular distribution (not square) for natural spread pattern\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x77 (119) - Skill ID being executed\n  0x39 (57)  - Projectile skill ID\n  0x2001     - Projectile flags (spawner flags)\n  0x12 (18)  - Random divisor range for count calculation\n  0x40 (64)  - Direction range (0-63 for 64 directions)\n  0x2c       - Offset to unit's RNG seed (pUnit + 0x2c)\n  0x38       - Offset to projectile's unit pointer",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_MonsterData", "PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_1", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
    },
