      "comment": "Initialize resource context by obtaining existing handle or creating new resource.\n\nAlgorithm:\n\n1. Attempt to obtain existing resource handle via Ordinal_10480(pContext, 0xc)\n2. If handle obtained successfully (hResource != 0):\n   a. Configure context via Ordinal_10372(pContext, 8)\n   b. Set context configuration flag at offset 0x54 to 0x500\n   c. Configure resource handle via Ordinal_10476(hResource, 6)\n   d. Return success (1)\n3. If no existing handle, create new resource via Ordinal_10470(0, 2, 0x14, *pContext, pContext[2])\n   - Resource size: 0x14 (20 bytes)\n   - Uses context data at offsets 0x0 and 0x8\n4. If resource creation fails (hResource == 0):\n   a. Return failure (0)\n5. Otherwise, initialize newly created resource:\n   a. Associate resource with context via Ordinal_10475(pContext, hResource)\n   b. Set resource callback to ResourceCallbackThunk via Ordinal_10477\n   c. Configure resource with value 0xc via Ordinal_10478\n   d. Finalize context initialization via Ordinal_10486(pContext, 0xc, 1)\n   e. Return success (1)\n\nParameters:\n\npContext - Pointer to resource context structure (min size 0x58 bytes)\n           Accessed offsets: 0x0, 0x8 (input), 0x54 (output)\n\nIMPLICIT: ECX contains pContext pointer (__fastcall convention)\n\nReturns:\n\n1 (0x1) - Resource context successfully initialized (existing or new)\n0 (0x0) - Resource creation failed\n\nSpecial Cases:\n\n- Function handles both reuse of existing resources and creation of new ones\n- No callers detected - may be unused initialization path\n- Context structure offsets: [0x0]=data, [0x8]=data, [0x54]=config flag\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n\n0xc (12) - Resource type or configuration identifier (used in multiple ordinals)\n0x14 (20) - Resource allocation size in bytes\n0x500 (1280) - Context configuration flag value set at offset 0x54\n0x8 (8) - Context configuration parameter\n0x6 (6) - Resource handle configuration value\n0x2 (2) - Resource creation flag/mode parameter\n0x1 (1) - Finalization enable flag for Ordinal_10486",
