      "comment": "Calculate and apply scaled stat value based on range divisor\n\nAlgorithm:\n\n1. Retrieve stats data pointer from game object field at offset +0x4 via Ordinal_10589\n2. Validate stats pointer is non-null, abort with assertion if null (ptStats)\n3. Validate range parameter is non-zero, abort with assertion if zero (nRange)\n4. Read byte value from stats data structure at offset +0x58 (88 decimal)\n5. Scale byte value by shifting left 8 bits to multiply by 256\n6. Perform signed division of scaled value by range parameter\n7. Apply calculated proportional result to game object via Ordinal_10377\n\nParameters:\n\npGameObject - Pointer to game object structure containing event type at offset +0x4\nnRange - Range divisor for scaling calculation, must be non-zero to avoid assertion\n\nReturns:\n\nvoid - Function does not return a value\nAborts execution if stats pointer is null or range parameter is zero\n\nSpecial Cases:\n\nIf stats pointer retrieved from Ordinal_10589 is null, triggers assertion failure\nwith \"ptStats\" identifier at source line 0x56 and aborts with exit code -1\n\nIf nRange parameter is zero, triggers assertion failure with \"nRange\" identifier\nat source line 0x57 and aborts with exit code -1 to prevent division by zero\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n\n0x4 (offset) - Offset to event type field in GameObject structure passed to lookup\n0x58 (offset, 88 decimal) - Offset to byte stat value in stats data structure\n0x56 (86 decimal) - Source line number for ptStats null pointer assertion\n0x57 (87 decimal) - Source line number for nRange zero value assertion\n256 (0x100) - Scale factor applied to byte value via left shift by 8 bits\n0xffffffff (-1) - Exit code passed to abort function FUN_6fb9a10f on assertion\n\nStats Data Structure Layout:\n\nOffset | Size | Field Name    | Type  | Description\n-------|------|---------------|-------|----------------------------------\n+0x58  | 1    | byStatValue   | byte  | Raw stat byte used in calculation",
