      "instructions": ["0x24C90|SUB|ESP, 0x60", "0x24C93|LEA|EAX, [ESP + 0x4]", "0x24C97|PUSH|EBX", "0x24C98|PUSH|ESI", "0x24C99|MOV|ESI, EDX", "0x24C9B|PUSH|EDI", "0x24C9C|MOV|EBX, ECX", "0x24C9E|PUSH|EAX", "0x24C9F|LEA|EDX, [ESP + 0x10]", "0x24CA3|CALL|0x6fae96a0", "0x24CA8|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0x24CAA|JNZ|0x6faf4cb5", "0x24CAC|POP|EDI", "0x24CAD|POP|ESI", "0x24CAE|POP|EBX"],
      "comment": "Creates a missile projectile with range scaled based on skill stats and distance calculation\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate source unit coordinates using CalculateUnitCoordinates\n2. Return NULL if coordinate calculation fails\n3. Check missile spread mode with Ordinal_10918\n4. If spread mode disabled, use nTargetY parameter instead of nSkillLevel for calculations\n5. Call Ordinal_10996 to calculate base range from skill parameters\n6. Initialize local missile data structure (zeroing 0x16 dwords starting at offset)\n7. Calculate scaled range by dividing base range by 2 (SAR instruction)\n8. Populate missile parameter structure with coordinates and skill data\n9. Set missile flags to 0x8020 in structure\n10. Call FUN_6fb77720 to create missile object from parameter structure\n11. If missile creation succeeds, validate missile stats pointer with Ordinal_10589\n12. If stats invalid, trigger assertion failure with ptStats error\n13. If scaled range is zero, trigger assertion failure with nRange error\n14. Calculate missile speed: (stat_byte[0x58] << 8) / nScaledRange\n15. Set missile speed using Ordinal_10377\n16. Check if source unit has state flag 0xc with Ordinal_10487\n17. If flag set and unit type is 1 (player), check if unit class is 0x167 (Amazon)\n18. For Amazon class, adjust unit field at offset 0x50 by subtracting 0x200\n19. For other classes with flag, remove state 8 with Ordinal_10372 and set field 0x54 to 0x500\n20. Return missile pointer\n\nParameters:\n  pSourceUnit - Source unit firing the missile (UnitAny structure pointer)\n  nSkillId - Skill identifier for missile type\n  nSkillLevel - Skill level affecting missile properties\n  nTargetX - Target X coordinate for missile destination\n  nTargetY - Target Y coordinate for missile destination\n\nIMPLICIT:\n  EBX - Preserved unit pointer used throughout function\n\nReturns:\n  Pointer to created missile object (void *)\n  NULL if coordinate calculation fails\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  Missile spread mode affects whether nSkillLevel or nTargetY is used for parameter\n  Range scaling divides calculated range by 2 for balance\n  Amazon class (0x167) receives special offset adjustment to field 0x50\n  Zero scaled range triggers assertion to prevent division by zero in speed calculation\n  Missing missile stats pointer triggers assertion failure\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x8020 - Missile flags set in parameter structure\n  0xc - State flag checked on source unit\n  0x1 - Player unit type constant\n  0x167 - Amazon character class identifier\n  0x50 - Unit field offset for Amazon-specific adjustment\n  0x200 - Value subtracted from Amazon field 0x50\n  0x8 - State flag removed for non-Amazon classes\n  0x54 - Unit field offset set to 0x500\n  0x500 - Value written to unit field 0x54\n  0x58 - Stat structure byte offset for missile speed calculation\n  0x56 - Assertion line number for missing ptStats\n  0x57 - Assertion line number for zero nRange\n\nError Handling:\n  Coordinate calculation failure returns NULL immediately\n  Invalid missile stats pointer triggers Ordinal_10023 assertion with file/line info\n  Zero scaled range triggers Ordinal_10023 assertion to prevent division by zero\n  Both assertion failures call FUN_6fb9a10f with -1 to terminate process\n\nString References:\n  \"ptStats\" (0x6fbb1418) - Assertion variable name for stats pointer check\n  \"nRange\" (0x6fbb1b00) - Assertion variable name for range check\n  \"C:\\\\Projects\\\\Diablo2\\\\Source\\\\D2Cli...\" (0x6fbb1b08) - Source file path for assertions",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "STRUCT_Room1", "STRUCT_ItemData", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData", "STRUCT_MonsterData", "STRUCT_Path", "UI_SKILLS", "STRUCT_Skill", "PARAM_5", "STRUCT_Other", "SRC_SkillsSor.cpp"]
