      "comment": "Configures text control with value clamping and rendering properties.\n\nAlgorithm:\n\n1. Validate text control context pointer (null check)\n2. Query current value from text control (Ordinal_11122)\n3. Check if value exceeds maximum threshold (0x4E = 78)\n4. If exceeds threshold, clamp value to maximum (0x4D = 77)\n   - Set text control value to 77 (Ordinal_11121)\n   - Set text control position to 77 (Ordinal_11123)\n5. Retrieve text control handle from context at offset +0x38\n6. Initialize text control rendering (Ordinal_10175)\n7. Perform text control setup operation (Ordinal_10913)\n8. Set text control mode to 10 (Ordinal_10185)\n9. Set text control display value (Ordinal_10188 with clamped value)\n10. Finalize text control configuration with context offset +0x2C (Ordinal_10142)\n\nParameters:\n\npTextControlContext (TextControlContext *) - Pointer to text control context structure\n  +0x2C: Control data region used in final configuration\n  +0x38: Text control handle (void *) for rendering operations\nnOffset (int) - Offset value added to context base during configuration\n  IMPLICIT EDX: Used in address calculation [context + 0x2C] + nOffset\n\nReturns:\n\nvoid - Function performs configuration with no return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n\n- Null context pointer: Function returns immediately without operations\n- Value > 77 (0x4D): Value is clamped to maximum 77 before rendering\n- Maximum threshold is 78 (0x4E) exclusive, 77 (0x4D) inclusive\n\nMagic Numbers:\n\n0x4E (78) - Maximum value threshold for comparison (exclusive upper bound)\n0x4D (77) - Maximum clamped value applied to text control\n0x38 (56) - Offset to text control handle in context structure\n0x2C (44) - Offset to control data region in context structure\n10 (0xA) - Text control rendering mode parameter\n\nError Handling:\n\n- No explicit error handling beyond null check\n- Assumes ordinal functions succeed without validation\n- No return value to indicate success/failure",
