      "comment": "Periodically create tooltip with randomized position every 10th invocation\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get random/counter object from Ordinal_10950()\n2. If object is NULL, return NULL (no tooltip created)\n3. Get current counter value from object via Ordinal_10976()\n4. Increment counter and store back via Ordinal_10980()\n5. Calculate trigger condition: counter / 10 (integer division)\n6. Check if counter is divisible by 10 (counter % 10 == 0)\n7. If divisible by 10 (every 10th call):\n   a. Get base X coordinate from unit via Ordinal_10326()\n   b. Get first random offset via Ordinal_10918()\n   c. Get base Y coordinate from unit via Ordinal_10329()\n   d. Get second random offset via Ordinal_10918()\n   e. Get third random value via Ordinal_10918()\n   f. Call FUN_6fb77e50 to create tooltip with:\n      - Unit pointer\n      - Message type 0xd4 (212 decimal)\n      - Calculated X position: baseX - 5 + randomOffset1\n      - Calculated Y position: baseY - 5 + randomOffset2\n      - Display flag: 1 (show tooltip)\n      - Random value for additional positioning/variation\n8. Return result pointer from tooltip creation or counter/10 value\n\nParameters:\n  pUnit - UnitAny * - Game entity containing coordinate information\n\nReturns:\n  void * - Pointer to created tooltip object on 10th call, otherwise counter/10 value cast to pointer\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Returns NULL if Ordinal_10950() fails to get counter object\n  - Tooltip only created every 10th invocation (modulo 10 check)\n  - On non-trigger calls (not divisible by 10), returns counter/10 as pointer\n  - Coordinate offsets use -5 adjustment plus random value for positioning variance\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0xd4 (212 decimal) - Tooltip message type identifier\n  10 - Invocation period (tooltip created every 10 calls)\n  -5 - Base coordinate offset applied before adding random offset\n  1 - Tooltip display flag (show/enable)\n\nError Handling:\n  - Returns NULL if counter object unavailable\n  - No error checking on coordinate or random value functions\n  - Assumes FUN_6fb77e50 handles NULL unit pointer internally",
