      "comment": "Plays a sound effect associated with a unit based on game difficulty.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate unit has valid path handle (offset +0x38)\n2. Retrieve unit sound ID and validate unit position\n3. Get unit coordinates (X, Y) and path handle\n4. Check path collision status - exit if collision detected\n5. Initialize 88-byte sound request structure (22 dwords) with zeroes\n6. Set request header: flags (0x21), unit pointer, coordinates, sound ID\n7. Query current game difficulty level (0=Normal, 1=Nightmare, 2=Hell)\n8. Map difficulty to sound type code: Normal→0x68, Nightmare→0x69, Hell→0x45\n9. Submit sound request to audio playback system via FUN_6fb77720\n\nParameters:\n  pUnit - Pointer to UnitAny structure requesting sound effect\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If unit path handle is NULL (offset +0x38), function returns without action\n  - If path collision is detected (Ordinal_10082), sound is suppressed\n  - Default difficulty 0 maps to sound type 0x68 if difficulty query fails\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x21 (33) - Sound request structure identifier/flags\n  0x68 (104) - Normal difficulty sound type code\n  0x69 (105) - Nightmare difficulty sound type code  \n  0x45 (69) - Hell difficulty sound type code\n  0x16 (22) - Number of dwords in sound request structure (88 bytes total)\n  0x38 (56) - Offset to pPath field in UnitAny structure\n\nSound Request Structure Layout:\nOffset | Size | Field Name      | Type    | Description\n-------|------|-----------------|---------|------------------------------------------\n0x00   | 4    | dwRequestFlags  | uint    | Request flags/identifier (0x21)\n0x04   | 4    | pUnit           | uint    | Pointer to requesting UnitAny\n0x08   | 4    | dwSoundType     | uint    | Sound type code (0x68/0x69/0x45)\n0x0C   | 4    | dwCoordX        | uint    | Unit X coordinate\n0x10   | 4    | dwCoordY        | uint    | Unit Y coordinate\n0x14   | 4    | dwSoundIdFinal  | uint    | Final sound identifier\n0x18   | 72   | Reserved        | byte[]  | Additional sound parameters\n\nError Handling:\n  - NULL path handle → Silent return (no sound played)\n  - Path collision detected → Silent return via Ordinal_10082 check\n  - Invalid difficulty (>2) → Falls through to default case (0x68)",
