      "comment": "Execute skill effect handler for unit with missile calculation and audio cleanup.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate unit state using Ordinal_10323\n2. Calculate skill table index by subtracting base skill ID (0x24 = 36)\n3. Validate skill index is within valid range (0 to 0x1E = 30)\n4. If out of range, trigger assertion with skill ID bounds message and terminate\n5. If unit validation passed, check missile target ID from skill params table\n6. If missile target is valid (not 0xFFFF), calculate missile target coordinates\n7. Set unit flag 0x40 at offset 0xE8 (dwGfxFrame in UnitAny[4])\n8. Retrieve skill effect callback function pointer from params table offset +4\n9. If callback is NULL, set unit flag 0x40 again\n10. If callback exists, invoke skill effect callback with indirect call\n11. Retrieve audio context for unit using Ordinal_10958\n12. If audio context exists, remove it from active audio list\n13. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\n  pUnit - Pointer to UnitAny executing the skill effect\n  nSkillId - Skill ID to execute (valid range 0x24 to 0x42, base 36 to 66 decimal)\n  dwFlags - Flags passed to missile calculation\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value (terminates process on invalid skill ID)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Skill ID must be in range [0x24, 0x42] or assertion triggers\n  - Adjusted index must be [0, 0x1E] (30 entries in params table)\n  - If unit validation fails, function returns early without executing effect\n  - Missile target ID 0xFFFF indicates no missile calculation needed\n  - Callback function pointer can be NULL, indicating no custom effect handler\n  - Unit flag 0x40 set multiple times suggests \"effect processed\" state\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x24 (36) - Base skill ID offset for table indexing\n  0x1E (30) - Maximum skill index, table size is 30 entries\n  0x14 (20) - SkillParams structure size in bytes\n  0xFFFF - Invalid missile target ID sentinel value\n  0x40 (bit 6) - Unit flag indicating skill effect processed\n  0xE8 (232) - Offset to dwGfxFrame field in UnitAny structure\n  0x2B4 (692) - Source line number for assertion message\n  0xFFFFFFFF - Error code passed to termination function\n\nError Handling:\n  - Out of range skill ID triggers Ordinal_10023 assertion\n  - Assertion displays: \"nSkillId >= 0 && nSkillId < NUM_SKILLS\"\n  - Assertion includes source file path and line number 0x2B4\n  - FUN_6fb9a10f called with 0xFFFFFFFF to terminate process\n  - No graceful recovery, process termination is fatal\n\nStructure Layout:\n  SkillParams (20 bytes, 0x14):\n    Offset  Size  Field Name       Type    Description\n    +0x00   4     dwSkillId        uint    Missile target ID or skill parameter (0xFFFF = none)\n    +0x04   4     dwParam1         uint    Function pointer to skill effect callback\n    +0x08   12    (unknown)        byte[]  Additional parameters (not accessed in this function)\n\nGlobal Data:\n  g_aSkillEffectParams @ 0x6fba833c - Array of 30 SkillParams entries for skills 0x24-0x42",
