      "api_count": 2,
      "api_calls": ["UNITS_SetStatInfoValue", "FogAssert"],
      "instructions": ["0x25530|PUSH|ESI", "0x25531|PUSH|EDI", "0x25532|SUB|EDX, 0x24", "0x25535|MOV|EDI, ECX", "0x25537|JS|0x6faf55dd", "0x2553D|CMP|EDX, 0x1e", "0x25540|JGE|0x6faf55dd", "0x25546|LEA|ESI, [EDX + EDX*0x4]", "0x25549|SHL|ESI, 0x2", "0x2554C|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [ESI + 0x6fba8338]", "0x25552|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0x25554|JZ|0x6faf558e", "0x25556|MOV|EDX, dword ptr [ESP + 0xc]", "0x2555A|CALL|EAX", "0x2555C|TEST|EAX, EAX"],
      "comment": "Processes skill-specific effects and audio for skills in range 0x24-0x41.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate skill index by subtracting 0x24 from skill ID\n2. Validate skill index is within bounds 0-0x1D (0-29 decimal), abort if out of range\n3. Look up skill parameters in g_SkillParamsTable using (nSkillId - 7) as index\n4. If dwTargetParam function pointer exists, call validation callback\n5. If validation returns 0 (failure), clear active skill and update audio state\n6. If audio source state is 0, set to 1 via FUN_6fb86790\n7. Early return if audio source state != 1 after state check\n8. If dwParam2 is non-zero, apply skill effect via FUN_6fb8d210\n9. If dwParam3 is not 0xFFFFFFFF, apply visual effect via FUN_6fb931f0\n10. Look up audio effect ID in skill audio table at DAT_6fba833c + (nSkillIndex * 0x14)\n11. If audio effect ID is 0xFFFF (sentinel), skip audio initialization\n12. Otherwise call InitializeAudioLightingEffect with audio effect ID\n\nParameters:\npAudioSource - Pointer to audio source data structure for skill sound effects\nnSkillId     - Skill identifier (must be in range 0x24-0x41, 36-65 decimal)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Function performs side effects on audio system and skill state\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Skills outside range 0x24-0x41 cause assertion failure and process termination\n- Audio effect ID 0xFFFF indicates no audio for this skill (silent skills)\n- Validation callback returning 0 triggers skill cancellation and state reset\n- dwParam3 value 0xFFFFFFFF indicates no visual effect for this skill\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x24     - Minimum valid skill ID offset (36 decimal) - skill range start\n0x1D     - Maximum skill index (29 decimal) - covers 30 skills total\n0x41     - Maximum valid skill ID (65 decimal) - skill range end  \n0x07     - SkillParams table base offset adjustment\n0x14     - Audio table stride (20 bytes per entry)\n0xFFFF   - Sentinel value for missing audio effect ID\n\nStructure Layout:\nSkillParams Structure (via g_SkillParamsTable):\nOffset | Size | Field Name      | Type | Description\n0x00   | 4    | dwSkillId       | uint | Skill identifier value\n0x04   | 4    | dwParam1        | uint | General purpose parameter 1\n0x08   | 4    | dwParam2        | uint | Skill effect parameter (0=none)\n0x0C   | 4    | dwParam3        | uint | Visual effect ID (0xFFFFFFFF=none)\n0x10   | 4    | dwTargetParam   | uint | Function pointer for validation callback\n\nAudioSourceData Structure (param pAudioSource):\nOffset | Size | Field Name | Type | Description\n0x00   | 4    | dwState    | uint | Audio source state (0=idle, 1=active)",
      "tags": ["PARAM_2", "UI_SKILLS", "SRC_SkillsSor.cpp"]
