      "instructions": ["0x25600|SUB|ESP, 0x58", "0x25603|PUSH|EBX", "0x25604|PUSH|EBP", "0x25605|PUSH|ESI", "0x25606|PUSH|EDI", "0x25607|MOV|ESI, EDX", "0x25609|MOV|EDI, ECX", "0x2560B|CALL|0x6fb60ef0", "0x25610|MOV|EBX, EAX", "0x25612|PUSH|0x14", "0x25614|PUSH|ESI", "0x25615|CALL|0x6fb986a4", "0x2561A|TEST|EBX, EBX", "0x2561C|MOV|EBP, EAX", "0x2561E|JZ|0x6faf56b2"],
      "comment": "Process item equipment special effects for player character.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Retrieve player/owner unit from unit pointer\n2. Validate item has stat property 0x14\n3. Verify player pointer and stat property are valid\n4. Check if player can equip the item\n5. Retrieve configuration data from unit class ID\n6. Check configuration flag at offset 0x72 for effect processing enabled\n7. Initialize 88-byte effect parameter structure (0x58 bytes = 22 DWORDs)\n8. Set structure size field to 0x20\n9. Store item pointers in structure (offsets 0x04 and 0x08)\n10. Retrieve stat data from stat property with parameter 0xa8\n11. Set effect type to 0x108\n12. Get player X coordinate from player unit\n13. Get player Y coordinate from player unit\n14. Call effect creation function with structure\n15. Trigger item effect with event 0x2c and type 2\n\nParameters:\n  pUnit - UnitAny * - Unit equipping the item (player character)\n  pItem - UnitAny * - Item being equipped\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value (side effects only)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Returns early if player/owner unit retrieval fails\n  - Returns early if item lacks stat property 0x14\n  - Returns early if player cannot equip item\n  - Returns early if configuration flag at offset 0x72 is disabled\n  - Effect only triggered when all validation passes\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x14 (20) - Stat property ID for equipment validation\n  0x72 (114) - Configuration offset for effect processing enabled flag\n  0x16 (22) - DWORD count for initialization loop (88 bytes / 4)\n  0x20 (32) - Structure size field value\n  0xa8 (168) - Parameter for stat data retrieval\n  0x108 (264) - Effect type identifier\n  0x2c (44) - Item effect event ID\n  0x02 (2) - Effect trigger type\n\nStructure Layout:\nThe 88-byte (0x58) stack-allocated effect parameter structure:\n\nOffset | Size | Field Name   | Type       | Description\n-------|------|--------------|------------|------------\n  0x00 |   4  | dwStructSize | uint       | Structure size (0x20)\n  0x04 |   4  | pItemRef1    | UnitAny *  | Item pointer reference 1\n  0x08 |   4  | pItemRef2    | UnitAny *  | Item pointer reference 2\n  0x10 |   4  | dwEffectType | uint       | Effect type (0x108)\n  0x1C |   4  | dwStatData   | uint       | Stat data from property\n  0x20 |   4  | dwPlayerX    | uint       | Player X coordinate\n  0x2C |   4  | dwPlayerY    | uint       | Player Y coordinate",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_MonsterData", "STRUCT_Path", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PARAM_2", "STRUCT_Skill", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
