      "instructions": ["0x256C0|PUSH|ESI", "0x256C1|MOV|ESI, dword ptr [ESP + 0x8]", "0x256C5|PUSH|0x0", "0x256C7|PUSH|0x0", "0x256C9|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [ESI]", "0x256CB|PUSH|0x10", "0x256CD|PUSH|EAX", "0x256CE|CALL|dword ptr [0x6fba6214]", "0x256D4|MOV|dword ptr [ESI + 0x18], 0x0", "0x256DB|MOV|dword ptr [ESI + 0x1c], 0x0", "0x256E2|POP|ESI", "0x256E3|RET|0x4"],
      "comment": "Closes a window by sending WM_CLOSE and resets both state flags to zero.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load window handle (HWND) from offset 0x00 of context structure\n2. Send WM_CLOSE (0x10) message to the window via SendMessageA\n3. Clear closed flag at offset 0x18 to 0\n4. Clear active flag at offset 0x1C to 0\n\nParameters:\n  pdwWindowContext - Pointer to window context structure containing:\n    +0x00: HWND hWindow - Handle to the window to close\n    +0x18: uint dwClosedFlag - Cleared to 0 (reset closed state)\n    +0x1C: uint dwActiveFlag - Cleared to 0 (reset active state)\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- No callers found; likely a callback or cleanup function for deallocating window contexts\n- No error checking on SendMessageA return value\n- Unlike CloseWindowAndSetClosedState (which sets dwClosedFlag=1), this resets both flags to 0\n- Used for full window context reset, possibly before reuse or deallocation\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x10 - WM_CLOSE message constant\n  0x18 - Offset to closed state flag (field index 6)\n  0x1C - Offset to active state flag (field index 7)",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Inventory", "PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_1", "STRUCT_Control", "PROP_SMALL", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
