      "comment": "Calculate and set window border offsets for windowed graphics mode.\n\nAlgorithm:\n\n1. Check if fullscreen is enabled (g_dwFullscreenEnabled) OR nEnable parameter is non-zero\n2. If neither condition is true, return 0 (no borders calculated)\n3. Call FUN_6faf57b0() to apply window settings\n4. Retrieve graphics mode from g_dwGraphicsMode and check if mode - 1 == 0 (mode is 1)\n5. If mode is not 1, clear border offsets (g_dwWindowBorderX = 0, g_dwWindowBorderY = 0)\n6. If mode is 1 (windowed mode), calculate centered border offsets:\n   - g_dwWindowBorderX = (g_dwScreenWidth / 3 - g_dwWindowBaseX - 0x10)\n   - g_dwWindowBorderY = (g_dwScreenHeight / 3 - g_dwWindowBaseY - 0x10)\n7. Return mode - 1 (0 for mode 1, non-zero for other modes)\n\nParameters:\n\nnEnable (int): Enable flag for border calculation (0 = skip unless fullscreen enabled, non-zero = force calculation)\n\nReturns:\n\nint: Graphics mode minus 1 (0 if mode is 1, non-zero otherwise), or 0 if calculation was skipped\n\nSpecial Cases:\n\nWhen both g_dwFullscreenEnabled is 0 and nEnable is 0, function returns immediately with 0\nGraphics mode 1 triggers border calculation, all other modes zero the borders\nBorder calculation uses division by 3 (multiply by 0x55555556 magic constant with shift)\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n\n0x55555556 (1431655766 decimal): Magic multiplier for division by 3 (signed)\n0x10 (16 decimal): Border padding offset subtracted from calculated position",
