      "comment": "Initialize viewport coordinates based on screen dimensions and display mode\n\nAlgorithm:\n\n1. Call FUN_6fb06470() to get current state flag\n2. Check if state has changed by comparing DAT_6fbf4328 with FUN_6fb06470 result\n3. If state unchanged, check if DAT_6fbf432c equals DAT_6fbf431c\n4. If equal, determine viewport origin based on DAT_6fbf431c value:\n   - If DAT_6fbf431c is 0: Set origin X to 2/3 screen width, Y to 0x4e (78)\n   - If DAT_6fbf431c is nonzero: Set origin X to 0, Y to 0x60 (96) or 0 based on FUN_6fb06470\n5. Store origin coordinates to _DAT_6fbf42fc and _DAT_6fbf4300\n6. Calculate viewport bounds based on DAT_6fbf428c mode flag:\n   - If DAT_6fbf428c is not 1: Full screen viewport (0xfffffff0 to screen dimensions)\n   - If DAT_6fbf428c is 1: Scaled viewport (origin + 1/3 screen dimensions minus 8 pixel offset)\n7. If state changed, update DAT_6fbf4328 or DAT_6fbf432c and recursively reinitialize\n8. Calculate and store final dimensions to DAT_6fbf42c4 and DAT_6fbf42c8\n9. Return calculated value based on screen height or mode\n\nParameters:\n\nNone\n\nReturns:\n\nint - Viewport dimension calculation result:\n  - 0xfffffff0 (-16) when mode is not 1\n  - Sign-extended screen height MSB when mode is 1 (typically 0 or -1)\n  - Mode-1 value when not windowed\n  - Scaled height product (g_dwScreenHeight * 0x55555556) for windowed mode\n\nSpecial Cases:\n\n- Recursive call to self when global state variables change\n- CONCAT31 operations merge FUN_6fb06470 boolean result with upper 24 bits for 32-bit comparison\n- Uses fixed offsets 0x4e (78) and 0x60 (96) for Y coordinate positioning\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n\n0x4e (78 decimal) - Default Y offset when DAT_6fbf431c is 0\n0x60 (96 decimal) - Alternate Y offset when condition is met\n0xfffffff0 (-16 decimal) - Default X/Y coordinate for full screen mode\n0x55555556 (1431655766 decimal) - Multiplier for height calculation (approximately 1/3 in fixed-point)\n-8 (0xfffffff8) - Pixel of