      "comment": "Updates automap fade state based on current mode and parameters.\n\nAlgorithm:\n\n1. Check if automap mode is active (g_dwAutomapMode == 1)\n2. Check if fade state is in initial state (g_dwAutomapFadeState == 1)\n3. If both conditions met, compute new fade state from g_dwAutomapFadeParam\n4. Computation: NEG/SBB idiom produces 0 if param is 0, -1 (0xFFFFFFFF) if param is non-zero\n5. Mask with 0xFFFFFFFE: 0 remains 0, 0xFFFFFFFF becomes 0xFFFFFFFE\n6. Add 2: 0 becomes 2, 0xFFFFFFFE becomes 0 (with overflow)\n7. Store computed value to g_dwAutomapFadeState (result is 2 if param==0, else 0)\n\nParameters:\n\nNone\n\nReturns:\n\nvoid - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n\nMagic Number Reference:\n- 0x1 (1) - Active automap mode flag\n- 0x1 (1) - Initial fade state value  \n- 0x2 (2) - Target fade state when param is zero\n- 0x0 (0) - Alternate fade state when param is non-zero\n- 0xFFFFFFFE (4294967294) - Mask used in NEG/SBB computation\n\nState Machine:\n\nState 1: g_dwAutomapMode != 1 OR g_dwAutomapFadeState != 1 - No state update, return immediately\nState 2: g_dwAutomapMode == 1 AND g_dwAutomapFadeState == 1 - Update g_dwAutomapFadeState based on g_dwAutomapFadeParam\n\nAutomap Fade States (observed from xrefs):\n- State 1: Initial/transitioning state\n- State 2: Fully visible/active state  \n- State 3: Alternative display mode (referenced in FUN_6faf82c0)\n\nGlobal Variables:\n- g_dwAutomapMode @ 0x6fbf428c: Automap display mode flag\n- g_dwAutomapFadeState @ 0x6fbf42e4: Current fade/visibility state\n- g_dwAutomapFadeParam @ 0x6fbf42e8: Parameter controlling state transition",
