      "comment": "Configure automap fade transition mode and persist setting to INI file.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if g_dwAutomapMode equals 1 (0x1) and dwFadeMode equals 1 (0x1)\n2. If both conditions true, set g_dwAutomapFadeState to 1 (0x1)\n3. Calculate alternate fade mode: if g_dwAutomapFadeParam is zero, use 2 (0x2), otherwise use 0 (0x0)\n4. Write fade mode value to INI file section \"AutoMapFade\" in \"Diablo II\" configuration via Ordinal_426\n5. Store fade mode in g_dwAutomapFadeParam global variable\n6. Store fade mode in g_dwAutomapFadeState global variable\n7. Return the final fade mode value\n\nParameters:\n  dwFadeMode - uint - Automap fade mode value (0-4, validated by caller)\n\nReturns:\n  uint - The fade mode value applied (may differ from input if special conditions met)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  When g_dwAutomapMode == 1 and dwFadeMode == 1, function toggles between fade modes 0 and 2 based on current g_dwAutomapFadeParam state. This implements fade mode cycling behavior.\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x1 - Automap mode check value and fade mode trigger\n  0x2 - Alternate fade mode when toggling from zero state\n  0x0 - Alternate fade mode when toggling from non-zero state\n  0xfffffffe - Bit mask (-2) used in toggle calculation (NEG + SBB + AND sequence)\n\nOrdinal_426 Parameters:\n  Param 1: \"Diablo II\" - INI file section name (const char *)\n  Param 2: \"AutoMapFade\" - INI key name (const char *)\n  Param 3: 0 - Unknown flag or index\n  Param 4: dwFadeMode - Value to write to INI",
      "tags": ["UI_AUTOMAP", "PARAM_1"]
    },
