      "instructions": ["0x259E0|PUSH|ESI", "0x259E1|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0x259E3|PUSH|ESI", "0x259E4|PUSH|0x0", "0x259E6|PUSH|0x6fbb1d3c", "0x259EB|PUSH|0x6fbae148", "0x259F0|CALL|0x6fb99c4e", "0x259F5|MOV|dword ptr [0x6fbf4320], ESI", "0x259FB|MOV|dword ptr [0x6fbf4324], ESI", "0x25A01|MOV|dword ptr [0x6fbf431c], ESI", "0x25A07|MOV|EAX, ESI", "0x25A09|POP|ESI", "0x25A0A|RET|"],
      "comment": "Initializes the \"AutoMap Left\" configuration setting in registry/config file.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call STORM.DLL Ordinal_426 (SGSetValue) to write config value to registry\n2. Pass \"Diablo II\" as application/section name\n3. Pass \"AutoMap Left\" as configuration key name\n4. Store the input value to g_dwAutomapLeftState (current state flag)\n5. Store the input value to g_dwAutomapLeftPrevious (previous state for comparison)\n6. Store the input value to g_dwAutomapLeftTarget (target state for transitions)\n7. Return the input value unchanged\n\nParameters:\n  dwValue: uint - Configuration value to set (0 = disabled, 1 = enabled)\n           Passed via ECX register (__fastcall calling convention)\n\nReturns:\n  uint: The input value (dwValue) unchanged, returned via EAX register\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Called during automap initialization in FUN_6faf9170\n  - Value persists across game sessions via STORM.DLL registry system\n  - Affects viewport scrolling behavior in FUN_6faf7ca0\n  - All three global variables are always set to the same value simultaneously",
