      "comment": "Allocate and initialize an automap sprite entry from paged memory pool\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Read current allocation counter (g_dwAutomapSpriteAllocCount)\n2. Calculate target page index via division by 512 (>> 9 shift)\n3. Calculate slot index within page via modulo 512 (& 0x1ff mask)\n4. Increment global allocation counter\n5. Traverse linked list of pages to find target page\n6. If target page doesn't exist, allocate new 10244-byte page:\n   - Call Ordinal_10042(0x361, 0) to allocate memory (865 dwords = 3460 bytes requested, but allocates 10244 bytes)\n   - Zero entire page (0xa01 dwords = 2561 dwords)\n   - Link new page into list: if previous page exists, set its next pointer; otherwise update global head\n7. Update global page list head pointer\n8. Calculate sprite entry address: page base + (slot index * 5 dwords = 20 bytes)\n9. Zero 5 dwords (20 bytes) of sprite entry\n10. Return pointer to initialized sprite entry\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\nAutomapSprite * - Pointer to zeroed 20-byte sprite entry within page pool\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset  Size  Field Name     Type   Description\n------  ----  -------------  -----  ------------------------------------\n0x00    4     dwType         uint   Sprite type/flags\n0x04    2     sCelNum        short  Cel/frame number for sprite\n0x06    2     sPixelX        short  X pixel coordinate\n0x08    2     sPixelY        short  Y pixel coordinate\n0x0A    10    abReserved     byte[] Reserved/unknown fields\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x1ff (511 decimal) - Page slot mask for modulo 512 calculation\n0x800001ff - Sign-extended mask for negative modulo handling\n0xfffffe00 - Two's complement adjustment mask\n0x9 (9 decimal) - Right shift count for divide by 512\n0xa00 (2560 decimal) - Offset to next page pointer in dwords (2560 * 4 = 10240 bytes)\n0x361 (865 decimal) - Allocation size parameter (actual allocation is larger)\n0xa01 (2561 decimal) - Number of dwords to zero (includes next pointer)\n0x5 (5 decimal) - Dwords per sprite entry (20 bytes)\n\nMemory Layout:\nEach page is 10244 bytes structured as:\n- 512 sprite entries × 20 bytes = 10240 bytes\n- 1 next page pointer = 4 bytes\n- Total: 10244 bytes\n\nPage List Structure:\ng_pAutomapSpritePageList -> Page0[10240 bytes data + 4 byte next ptr] -> Page1[...] -> NULL\n\nSSA Temporary Variables:\nFunction uses 6 register-allocated SSA temporaries optimized away by decompiler.\nThese cannot be renamed through HighVariable interface (not in get_function_variables output):\n- iVar2 (nTotalIndex): Combined page+slot index for target calculation\n- puVar3 (pCurrentPage): Pointer to current page during list traversal\n- iVar4 (nPageIndex): Current page counter in list traversal (0, 1, 2...)\n- uVar5 (dwSlotIndex): Slot index within page (0-511)\n- puVar6 (pPageOrTemp): Multipurpose temporary pointer for page operations\n- pAVar1 (pSprite): Pointer to allocated sprite entry (return value)\n\nActual Renameable Variables:\n- pNextPageField (uint *): Pointer to previous page's next-pointer field (only real stack variable)",
