      "comment": "Update client node tracking based on cursor position.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if update is temporarily disabled (DAT_6fbf42e0 counter)\n2. If counter non-zero, decrement and return early (throttling mechanism)\n3. Get current unit handle via FUN_6fb62880, abort on failure\n4. Query cursor X/Y coordinates (Ordinal_10333, Ordinal_10334)\n5. Calculate Manhattan distance from stored position (DAT_6fbf4330, DAT_6fbf4334)\n6. Compute weighted distance: shorter axis + (longer axis * 2)\n7. If distance threshold exceeded (> 0x4f = 79 pixels):\n   a. Update stored position to current cursor coordinates\n   b. Get enumeration handle from FUN_6fb634e0\n   c. Enumerate units at cursor via Ordinal_10035\n   d. Get unit ID from first enumerated unit\n   e. Search existing client node list (DAT_6fbf429c) for matching ID\n   f. If not found, allocate new ClientNode (28 bytes), initialize, prepend to list\n   g. If client node changed (piVar2 != DAT_6fbf42a0):\n      - Serialize active binary trees via SerializeActiveBinaryTrees\n      - Clear automap sprite page list and reset allocation count\n      - Clear fields at offsets +8, +12, +16, +20 in previous client node\n      - Update current client node pointer (DAT_6fbf42a0)\n      - Refresh display via FUN_6faf6650\n   h. Iterate through all enumerated units, call FUN_6faf71e0 for matching IDs\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If DAT_6fbf42e0 throttle counter active, function returns immediately\n- If FUN_6fb62880 returns NULL handle, triggers fatal assertion with file/line info\n- Distance threshold prevents excessive updates during minor cursor movement\n- Client node list uses intrusive linked list (next pointer at offset +24)\n- Allocation size 0x5f1 (1521 bytes) suggests ClientNode followed by buffer\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x4f (79 decimal) - Distance threshold in pixels for cursor movement detection\n0x5f1 (1521 decimal) - Allocation size: 28-byte ClientNode + 1493-byte data buffer\n0x2800 (10240 decimal) - Offset to next pointer in automap sprite page structure\n0x522 (1314 decimal) - Ordinal for cleanup/deallocation function\n0x69a (1690 decimal) - Line number for assertion failure in hUnit validation\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset | Size | Field Name | Type        | Description\n-------|------|------------|-------------|------------------------------------\n0x00   | 4    | dwUnitId   | uint        | Unit identifier for client tracking\n0x04   | 4    | dwField04  | uint        | Reserved/unknown field\n0x08   | 4    | dwField08  | uint        | Cleared on client node switch\n0x0C   | 4    | dwField0C  | uint        | Cleared on client node switch\n0x10   | 4    | dwField10  | uint        | Cleared on client node switch\n0x14   | 4    | dwField14  | uint        | Cleared on client node switch\n0x18   | 4    | pNext      | ClientNode* | Intrusive linked list next pointer\n\nDistance Calculation:\nUses Manhattan distance variant: min(dx, dy) + 2*max(dx, dy)\nThis weights diagonal movement more heavily than axis-aligned movement.\nExample: dx=10, dy=30 → distance = 10 + (30*2) = 70 pixels",
      "tags": ["SRC_automap.cpp", "UI_AUTOMAP", "MOD_UI", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "TBL_automap", "PARAM_0", "PROP_LOOPHEAVY", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
