      "comment": "Serialize active binary trees to save file buffer.\n\nThis function traverses up to 4 binary tree structures (stored in slots 2-5 of the\nactive context) and serializes their contents to a save file format. Each tree is\ncounted, allocated a buffer, serialized, and then finalized with save markers.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if global active context pointer (g_pActiveTreeContext) is null, return if so\n2. Zero-initialize local tree count array (40 bytes = 10 dwords)\n3. Copy context ID and secondary ID from active context to local variables\n4. Load rendering system flags from g_pRenderingContext+4 into count array\n5. For tree slot 2 (if not null):\n   a. Count bytes needed for left subtree (pLeftChild) into adwTreeCounts[2]\n   b. If root node dwType == 0, add 6 bytes to count (leaf node overhead)\n   c. Count bytes needed for right subtree (pRightChild) into same counter\n6. For tree slot 3 (if not null):\n   a. Count bytes for left/right subtrees into adwTreeCounts[3]\n   b. Add 6-byte overhead if dwType == 0\n7. For tree slot 4 (if not null):\n   a. Count bytes for left/right subtrees into nTree4Count\n   b. Add 6-byte overhead if dwType == 0\n8. For tree slot 5 (if not null):\n   a. Count bytes for left/right subtrees into nTree5Count\n   b. Add 6-byte overhead if dwType == 0\n9. Conditionally serialize trees based on non-zero byte counts:\n   a. If tree 2 count > 0: Allocate buffer (0x4ee bytes), serialize tree 2\n   b. If tree 3 count > 0: Allocate buffer (0x4f5 bytes), serialize tree 3\n   c. If tree 4 count > 0: Allocate buffer (0x4fc bytes), serialize tree 4\n   d. If tree 5 count > 0: Allocate buffer (0x503 bytes), serialize tree 5\n10. Call SaveMapFileSizeTable with context structure\n11. Finalize each allocated tree buffer with Ordinal_10043 markers (0x50d-0x510)\n\nParameters:\nNone (implicitly uses global g_pActiveTreeContext at 0x6fbf42a0)\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nIMPLICIT:\ng_pActiveTreeContext - Global pointer to TreeContextArray structure at 0x6fbf42a0\ng_pwSerializationCursor - Global ushort pointer tracking write position in save buffer (0x6fbf4290)\ng_pRenderingContext - Global rendering context pointer at 0x6fbe9288\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If g_pActiveTreeContext is null, function returns immediately without serialization\n- Only trees with non-zero byte counts are serialized (empty trees skipped)\n- dwType == 0 indicates leaf node type, requires additional 6-byte overhead\n- Buffer allocation sizes are fixed per tree slot (0x4ee, 0x4f5, 0x4fc, 0x503)\n- Finalization markers are sequential (0x50d, 0x50e, 0x50f, 0x510) per tree slot\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x4ee (1262 decimal) - Buffer allocation size for tree slot 2\n0x4f5 (1269 decimal) - Buffer allocation size for tree slot 3\n0x4fc (1276 decimal) - Buffer allocation size for tree slot 4\n0x503 (1283 decimal) - Buffer allocation size for tree slot 5\n0x50d (1293 decimal) - Finalization marker for tree 2 buffer\n0x50e (1294 decimal) - Finalization marker for tree 3 buffer\n0x50f (1295 decimal) - Finalization marker for tree 4 buffer\n0x510 (1296 decimal) - Finalization marker for tree 5 buffer\n6 - Byte overhead added for leaf nodes (dwType == 0)\n\nStructure Layout (BinaryTreeNode - 20 bytes):\nOffset | Size | Field Name    | Type              | Description\n-------|------|---------------|-------------------|---------------------------\n     0 |    4 | dwType        | uint              | Node type flag (0 = leaf)\n     4 |    4 | dwValue1      | uint              | First node value\n     8 |    4 | dwValue2      | uint              | Second node value\n    12 |    4 | pLeftChild    | BinaryTreeNode *  | Left child pointer\n    16 |    4 | pRightChild   | BinaryTreeNode *  | Right child pointer\n\nGlobal Data Access:\ng_pActiveTreeContext[0] - Context ID (copied to dwContextId)\ng_pActiveTreeContext[1] - Secondary ID (copied to adwTreeCounts[0])\ng_pActiveTreeContext[2] - Tree slot 2 root pointer\ng_pActiveTreeContext[3] - Tree slot 3 root pointer\ng_pActiveTreeContext[4] - Tree slot 4 root pointer\ng_pActiveTreeContext[5] - Tree slot 5 root pointer",
