      "comment": "Update map file size tracking table with indexed file size entry.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Open map file handle via file opening routine\n2. If file handle invalid (0xffffffff), return immediately\n3. Initialize 100-DWORD file size table to zero (400 bytes total)\n4. Read existing file size table from map file (400 bytes)\n5. If read operation returned less than 400 bytes:\n   - Re-initialize table to zero\n   - Seek to beginning of file\n   - Write initialized 400-byte table to file\n6. Retrieve existing size value at indexed position from table\n7. Get actual file size via GetFileSize API\n8. If table entry at index is zero (uninitialized):\n   - Store actual file size in table at indexed position\n9. Else if table entry at index is non-zero (already initialized):\n   - Enter wait loop: repeatedly seek to beginning and read 4 bytes until condition clears\n   - Seek to beginning after loop exits\n   - Write 4-byte placeholder to file\n10. Seek to beginning of file\n11. Write updated 400-byte file size table to file\n12. Seek to beginning of file and write zero DWORD\n13. Write eight 4-byte entries to file (purpose unclear - padding or metadata)\n14. If context nDataSize1 field (offset 0xc) non-zero, write that many bytes from pDestBuffer1\n15. If context nDataSize2 field (offset 0x10) non-zero, write that many bytes from pDestBuffer2\n16. If context nDataSize3 field (offset 0x14) non-zero, write that many bytes from pDestBuffer3\n17. If context nDataSize4 field (offset 0x18) non-zero, write that many bytes from pDestBuffer4\n18. Close map file handle\n\nParameters:\npContext - Pointer to SaveFileContext structure containing:\n           - nFileIndex (offset 0x0): Index into 100-entry file size table\n           - nDataSize1 (offset 0xc): Optional data block 1 size in bytes\n           - nDataSize2 (offset 0x10): Optional data block 2 size in bytes\n           - nDataSize3 (offset 0x14): Optional data block 3 size in bytes\n           - nDataSize4 (offset 0x18): Optional data block 4 size in bytes\n           - pDestBuffer1 (offset 0x1c): Pointer to data block 1 buffer\n           - pDestBuffer2 (offset 0x20): Pointer to data block 2 buffer\n           - pDestBuffer3 (offset 0x24): Pointer to data block 3 buffer\n           - pDestBuffer4 (offset 0x28): Pointer to data block 4 buffer\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If file handle is invalid (0xffffffff), function returns without any operations\n- If file size table read returns partial data, table is reinitialized and written\n- Non-zero table entry at index triggers synchronization wait loop\n- Optional data blocks only written if size fields are non-zero\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x190 (400 decimal) - File size table byte count (100 DWORDs * 4 bytes)\n0x4 (4 decimal) - DWORD size in bytes\n0xffffffff (-1) - Invalid file handle constant\n\nStructure Layout:\n\nSaveFileContext (44 bytes):\nOffset | Size | Field Name      | Type | Description\n-------|------|-----------------|------|------------------------------------------\n0x00   | 4    | nFileIndex      | int  | Index into 100-entry file size table\n0x04   | 4    | field_0x4       | int  | Unknown field\n0x08   | 4    | field_0x8       | int  | Unknown field\n0x0c   | 4    | nDataSize1      | int  | Optional data block 1 size in bytes\n0x10   | 4    | nDataSize2      | int  | Optional data block 2 size in bytes\n0x14   | 4    | nDataSize3      | int  | Optional data block 3 size in bytes\n0x18   | 4    | nDataSize4      | int  | Optional data block 4 size in bytes\n0x1c   | 4    | pDestBuffer1    | int  | Pointer to data block 1 buffer\n0x20   | 4    | pDestBuffer2    | int  | Pointer to data block 2 buffer\n0x24   | 4    | pDestBuffer3    | int  | Pointer to data block 3 buffer\n0x28   | 4    | pDestBuffer4    | int  | Pointer to data block 4 buffer\n\nOrdinal Functions:\nOrdinal_10110 - Read data from file into buffer (3 params: size, buffer, flags)\nOrdinal_10111 - Write data from buffer to file (3 params: size, buffer, flags)\nOrdinal_10112 - Seek to file position (2 params: offset, origin)\nOrdinal_10109 - Close file handle (0 params)",
