      "comment": "Recursively count total byte size required for binary tree leaf node serialization.\n\nAlgorithm:\n\n1. Check if current tree node pointer is NULL, return immediately if so\n2. Enter traversal loop processing current node and all right siblings\n3. Recursively process left subtree (offset +0xc from node base)\n4. Check if current node is a leaf node (first field at offset +0x0 equals 0)\n5. If leaf node, add 6 bytes to accumulator (3 shorts: value, flags, data)\n6. Move to right sibling node (offset +0x10 from current node)\n7. Repeat until no more siblings (right pointer is NULL)\n\nParameters:\n\n- pTreeNode: Pointer to BinaryTreeNode to begin traversal from (can be NULL)\n- pnByteCount: Pointer to integer accumulator for total byte count (modified in-place)\n\nReturns:\n\n- void (result accumulated in *pnByteCount)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n\n- NULL tree node: Function returns immediately without modifying counter\n- Leaf nodes identified by first field (offset +0x0) being 0\n- Each leaf contributes exactly 6 bytes to total (3 ushort fields)\n- Traversal order: left subtree depth-first, then current, then right siblings\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n\n- 0x0 (decimal 0): Leaf node indicator value at node offset +0x0\n- 0x6 (decimal 6): Byte size per leaf node (3 × 2-byte shorts)\n- 0xc (decimal 12): Offset to left child pointer in BinaryTreeNode\n- 0x10 (decimal 16): Offset to right sibling pointer in BinaryTreeNode\n\nStructure Layout:\n\nBinaryTreeNode (20 bytes):\nOffset | Size | Field Name      | Type             | Description\n-------|------|-----------------|------------------|---------------------------\n+0x0   | 4    | dwLeafIndicator | uint             | 0 if leaf node, non-zero otherwise\n+0x4   | 4    | dwValue         | uint             | Node value/data\n+0x8   | 4    | dwFlags         | uint             | Node flags/attributes\n+0xc   | 4    | pLeftChild      | BinaryTreeNode * | Left child/subtree pointer\n+0x10  | 4    | pRightSibling   | BinaryTreeNode * | Right sibling pointer",
