      "instructions": ["0x265F0|PUSH|ESI", "0x265F1|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0x265F3|TEST|ESI, ESI", "0x265F5|JZ|0x6faf664d", "0x265F7|MOV|ECX, dword ptr [ESI + 0xc]", "0x265FA|CALL|0x6faf65f0", "0x265FF|CMP|dword ptr [ESI], 0x0", "0x26602|JNZ|0x6faf6646", "0x26604|MOV|ECX, dword ptr [0x6fbf4290]", "0x2660A|MOV|AX, word ptr [ESI + 0x4]", "0x2660E|MOV|word ptr [ECX], AX", "0x26611|MOV|EAX, [0x6fbf4290]", "0x26616|ADD|EAX, 0x2", "0x26619|MOV|[0x6fbf4290], EAX", "0x2661E|MOV|DX, word ptr [ESI + 0x6]"],
      "comment": "Recursively traverse and serialize a binary tree in-order, writing node data to global buffer\n\nAlgorithm:\n\n1. Null pointer check - Return immediately if pNode is NULL\n2. Recursive left traversal - Call self on pNode->pLeftChild (offset 0xC)\n3. Node type check - If pNode->dwType == 0, serialize node data:\n   a. Write pNode->dwValue1 (offset 0x4) as 16-bit word to buffer\n   b. Advance buffer pointer by 2 bytes\n   c. Write lower 16 bits of dwValue2 (offset 0x6) to buffer\n   d. Advance buffer pointer by 2 bytes\n   e. Write pNode->dwValue2 (offset 0x8) as 16-bit word to buffer\n   f. Advance buffer pointer by 2 bytes\n4. Iterative right traversal - Loop through pNode->pRightChild chain (offset 0x10)\n5. Repeat steps 2-4 for each right sibling until NULL\n\nParameters:\n\npNode - Pointer to current BinaryTreeNode to serialize (passed in ECX via __fastcall)\n\nIMPLICIT:\ng_pwSerializeBufferPtr @ 0x6fbf4290 - Global pointer to current position in serialization buffer\n\nReturns:\n\nvoid - No return value, operates on global buffer pointer\n\nSpecial Cases:\n\n- Nodes with dwType != 0 are skipped (not serialized)\n- Only nodes with dwType == 0 contribute 6 bytes to output (3 words)\n- Left subtree fully traversed recursively before processing current node\n- Right siblings processed iteratively to avoid deep recursion\n- Global buffer pointer advanced by serialization, caller must initialize\n\nStructure Layout:\n\nOffset | Size | Field Name   | Type    | Description\n-------|------|--------------|---------|----------------------------------\n  0x0  |  4   | dwType       | uint    | Node type, 0 = serialize\n  0x4  |  4   | dwValue1     | uint    | First value (serialized as word)\n  0x8  |  4   | dwValue2     | uint    | Second value (serialized as word)\n  0xC  |  4   | pLeftChild   | void *  | Pointer to left child node\n 0x10  |  4   | pRightChild  | void *  | Pointer to right sibling node\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n\n0x0 (decimal 0) - dwType value indicating node should be serialized\n0x4 (decimal 4) - Offset to dwValue1 field\n0x6 (decimal 6) - Offset to lower 16 bits of dwValue2\n0x8 (decimal 8) - Offset to full dwValue2 field\n0xC (decimal 12) - Offset to pLeftChild pointer\n0x10 (decimal 16) - Offset to pRightChild pointer\n0x2 (decimal 2) - Byte increment per word written (16-bit values)",
