      "comment": "Load automap sprite data from binary storage for the current level\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Verify global automap state pointer DAT_6fbf42a0 is non-null and file handle is valid (FUN_6faf62f0() returns != -1)\n2. Initialize 100-element level offset table adwLevelFileOffsets[] to zero\n3. Read 400-byte header from storage to determine all level offsets (Ordinal_10110)\n4. Verify full header was read (dwBytesRead == 400), abort if incomplete\n5. Load current level's offset from table using level ID at *DAT_6fbf42a0 as index\n6. If current level has no data (dwCurrentLevelOffset == 0), close file and return\n7. Enter main loop to process sprite layers for current level:\n   a. Save previous level offset in dwNextLevelOffset for continuation logic\n   b. Zero-initialize 10-element layer size array anLayerSizes[4]\n   c. Seek to level's data offset (Ordinal_10112)\n   d. Read 8x 4-byte layer headers into anLayerSizes[] (nLevelId, field, dwFloorSize, dwWallsSize, dwUnitsLayerSize, dwExtraLayerSize, etc)\n   e. Validate nLevelId matches current level (*DAT_6fbf42a0), break if mismatch (invalid level data)\n   f. Process floor sprites if dwFloorSize > 0 (anLayerSizes[2])\n   g. Process wall sprites if dwWallsSize > 0 (anLayerSizes[3])\n   h. Process unit sprites if dwUnitsLayerSize > 0 AND level ID matches DAT_6fbe9288+4\n   i. Process extra sprites if dwExtraLayerSize > 0 (anLayerSizes[0] used as layer-specific limit check)\n8. After processing all layers, load next level if dwCurrentLevelOffset != 0, else close file and return\n9. On sprite limit breach (cel num >= DAT_6fbf42b4), seek backwards and exit early\n\nParameters:\nIMPLICIT EBX: Not preserved across file I/O ordinal calls\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\nIf level ID mismatch (nLevelId != *DAT_6fbf42a0) at step 7e, function aborts layer loading, seeks to handle next level or invalid state\nUnit sprites (step 7h) only loaded if level ID matches DAT_6fbe9288+4 (likely difficulty-specific level data filter)\nSprite limit breach uses different seek sizes: 400 bytes if first level (dwNextLevelOffset==0), 4 bytes if subsequent levels\nError messages reference source file paths: C:\\Projects\\Diablo2\\Source\\D2Client\\*.cpp with line numbers 0x57e, 0x593, 0x5ab, 0x5c6\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x579 (1401 dec) - Ordinal for floor sprite memory allocation\n0x57e (1406 dec) - Error line number for floor data read failure\n0x58a (1418 dec) - Ordinal to free floor sprite buffer\n0x58e (1422 dec) - Ordinal for wall sprite memory allocation\n0x593 (1427 dec) - Error line number for wall data read failure\n0x59f (1439 dec) - Ordinal to free wall sprite buffer\n0x5a6 (1446 dec) - Ordinal for unit sprite memory allocation\n0x5ab (1451 dec) - Error line number for unit data read failure\n0x5b7 (1463 dec) - Ordinal to free unit sprite buffer\n0x5c1 (1473 dec) - Ordinal for extra sprite memory allocation\n0x5c6 (1478 dec) - Error line number for extra data read failure\n0x5d2 (1490 dec) - Ordinal to free extra sprite buffer\n400 (0x190 dec) - Header size in bytes containing level offset table\n4 (0x4 dec) - Size of each layer header field in bytes\n1 (0x1 dec) - dwType value assigned to all automap sprites (standard type)\n100 (0x64 dec) - Maximum number of levels in offset table\n10 (0xA dec) - Number of 4-byte layer fields per level\n3 (0x3 dec) - Stride for sprite data array (3 shorts: celNum, pixelX, pixelY)\n\nError Handling:\nRead size validation after each Ordinal_10110() - if dwBytesRead != expected, calls Ordinal_10023 (log error) then FUN_6fb9a10f(0xffffffff) to terminate process\nSprite limit checking: if sprite cel number >= DAT_6fbf42b4, seek backwards and abort layer\nFile handle validation: if FUN_6faf62f0() returns -1, entire function returns immediately\n\nStructure Layout:\nAutomapSprite (20 bytes):\nOffset  Size  Field Name  Type    Description\n0x00    2     sCelNum     short   Sprite cel/frame number from data\n0x02    2     sPixelX     short   X pixel coordinate on automap\n0x04    4     dwType      uint    Sprite category (always 1 in this function)\n0x08    2     sPixelY     short   Y pixel coordinate on automap\n\nBinary Storage Format:\nHeader (400 bytes): 100 dword offsets, one per level (adwLevelFileOffsets[100])\nLevel Data Record:\n  +0x00: nLevelId (int) - Level identifier\n  +0x04: unknown field (int)\n  +0x08: dwFloorSize (int) - Floor sprite data size in bytes\n  +0x0C: dwWallsSize (int) - Wall sprite data size in bytes\n  +0x10: dwUnitsLayerSize (int) - Unit sprite data size in bytes\n  +0x14: dwExtraLayerSize (int) - Extra sprite data size in bytes\n  +0x18-0x1F: Additional fields (2x int, purpose unclear)\n  Followed by variable-length sprite data arrays\n\nSprite Data Array Format (each layer):\nEach sprite = 3 shorts (6 bytes total):\n  [0]: sCelNum - sprite frame number\n  [1]: sPixelX - X coordinate\n  [2]: sPixelY - Y coordinate",
      "tags": ["MOD_UI", "SRC_automap.cpp", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "TBL_automap", "STRUCT_Room2", "STRUCT_ItemData", "PARAM_0", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData", "STRUCT_StatList", "PROP_LARGE", "UI_AUTOMAP", "STRUCT_Path", "STRUCT_Skill", "PROP_LOOPHEAVY"]
