      "api_calls": ["FogAssert", "FogAssert", "FogAssert", "FogAssert", "FogAssert", "FogAssert", "FogAssert", "FogAssert"],
      "instructions": ["0x26DB0|SUB|ESP, 0x8", "0x26DB3|PUSH|EBX", "0x26DB4|PUSH|ESI", "0x26DB5|MOV|ESI, dword ptr [EDX]", "0x26DB7|XOR|EBX, EBX", "0x26DB9|CMP|ESI, EBX", "0x26DBB|PUSH|EDI", "0x26DBC|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x10], EDX", "0x26DC0|JZ|0x6faf7100", "0x26DC6|MOVSX|EDX, word ptr [ESI + 0x8]", "0x26DCA|MOVSX|EAX, word ptr [ECX + 0x8]", "0x26DCE|SUB|EAX, EDX", "0x26DD0|JNZ|0x6faf6e05", "0x26DD2|MOVSX|EDX, word ptr [ESI + 0x6]", "0x26DD6|MOVSX|EAX, word ptr [ECX + 0x6]"],
      "comment": "Insert AutomapSprite into balanced binary search tree with rebalancing\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if current tree node is NULL (empty tree/leaf position found)\n2. If NULL, initialize sprite tree fields to zero and return 1 (inserted)\n3. Compare sprite coordinates with current node (sPixelY, sPixelX, then sCelNum via lookup table at 0x6fbf228c)\n4. If comparison result is 0, sprites are equal - update tree root pointer and return 0 (already exists)\n5. If comparison < 0, recursively insert into left subtree (ptLess)\n6. If comparison > 0, recursively insert into right subtree (ptMore)\n7. After recursive insertion, check if rebalancing is needed based on child's sBalance value\n8. Perform tree rotations (single or double) to maintain balance:\n   - Left rotation via RotateAutomapTreeLeft (0x6faf7120)\n   - Right rotation via RotateAutomapTreeRight (0x6faf7180)\n9. Update balance factors after rotations (-1 = left-heavy, 0 = balanced, 1 = right-heavy)\n10. Return 1 if tree height increased, 0 if tree was rebalanced\n\nParameters:\npSprite       - Pointer to AutomapSprite to insert into tree\nppTreeRoot    - Pointer to tree root pointer (updated if tree structure changes)\n\nReturns:\n1 = Sprite inserted and tree height increased (may need parent rebalancing)\n0 = Tree rebalanced or sprite already exists (no height change)\n\nStructure Layout:\nAutomapSprite (20 bytes):\nOffset | Size | Field Name | Type              | Description\n-------|------|------------|-------------------|---------------------------\n0x00   | 4    | dwType     | uint              | Sprite type/category\n0x04   | 2    | sCelNum    | short             | Cel/frame number\n0x06   | 2    | sPixelX    | short             | X pixel coordinate\n0x08   | 2    | sPixelY    | short             | Y pixel coordinate\n0x0A   | 2    | sBalance   | short             | Tree balance factor (-1, 0, 1)\n0x0C   | 4    | ptLess     | AutomapSprite *   | Left child (smaller coords)\n0x10   | 4    | ptMore     | AutomapSprite *   | Right child (larger coords)\n\nBalance Values:\n0xFFFF (-1) = Left subtree is one level deeper (left-heavy)\n0x0000 (0)  = Subtrees have equal depth (balanced)\n0x0001 (1)  = Right subtree is one level deeper (right-heavy)\n\nComparison Order:\n1. sPixelY (primary sort key)\n2. sPixelX (secondary sort key)\n3. sCelNum via lookup table at 0x6fbf228c (tertiary sort key, -1 = ignore)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Empty tree: Initializes sprite as root with balance 0, ptLess=NULL, ptMore=NULL\n- Duplicate sprite: Returns 0 without inserting\n- Assertion failures trigger Ordinal_10023 + FUN_6fb9a10f(0xffffffff) for NULL pointer errors\n\nError Handling:\n- Validates pointers are non-NULL before dereferences\n- Uses assertion messages: \"ptRoot == NULL\", \"ptRoot->ptLess == NULL\", \"ptRoot->ptMore == NULL\"\n- Validates balance values match expected states during rotations\n- File reference: \"C:\\\\Projects\\\\Diablo2\\\\Source\\\\D2Client\\\\Automap.cpp\"",
