      "comment": "Perform left rotation on binary tree root node\n\nAlgorithm:\n\n1. Validate root node pointer - Dereference ppRootNode to get pRoot, assert non-NULL\n2. Validate right child exists - Get pRoot->pRightChild as pNewRoot, assert non-NULL\n3. Rotate tree structure:\n   a. Move pNewRoot's left child to become pRoot's right child\n   b. Set pRoot as pNewRoot's left child\n   c. Update ppRootNode to point to pNewRoot (new root)\n4. Return - Tree rotation complete\n\nParameters:\n\nppRootNode - Pointer to pointer to current root BinaryTreeNode, updated to new root after rotation\n\nReturns:\n\nvoid - No return value, modifies tree structure through ppRootNode\n\nSpecial Cases:\n\n- Assertion failure if pRoot is NULL (error: \"ptRoot != NULL\")\n- Assertion failure if pNewRoot is NULL (error: \"ptRoot->ptMore != NULL\")\n- Both assertions call Ordinal_10023 with file/line info then abort via FUN_6fb9a10f(-1)\n- This is a standard left rotation used in self-balancing binary trees (AVL/Red-Black)\n\nStructure Layout:\n\nOffset | Size | Field Name   | Type              | Description\n-------|------|--------------|-------------------|----------------------------------\n  0x0  |  4   | dwType       | uint              | Node type identifier\n  0x4  |  4   | dwValue1     | uint              | First data value\n  0x8  |  4   | dwValue2     | uint              | Second data value\n  0xC  |  4   | pLeftChild   | BinaryTreeNode *  | Pointer to left child node\n 0x10  |  4   | pRightChild  | BinaryTreeNode *  | Pointer to right child node\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n\n0x237 (decimal 567) - Source line number for \"ptRoot != NULL\" assertion\n0x238 (decimal 568) - Source line number for \"ptRoot->ptMore != NULL\" assertion\n0xFFFFFFFF (decimal -1) - Exit code passed to abort function\n0xC (decimal 12) - Offset to pLeftChild pointer\n0x10 (decimal 16) - Offset to pRightChild pointer",
