      "comment": "Perform left rotation on binary tree node\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate root node pointer is non-null (assert ptRoot != NULL at line 0x248)\n2. Load current root node from ppRoot into pRoot\n3. Validate left child exists (assert ptRoot->ptLess != NULL at line 0x249)\n4. Load left child node from pRoot->pLeftChild into pLeftChild\n5. Reattach pLeftChild's right subtree as pRoot's new left child\n6. Make original pRoot the right child of pLeftChild\n7. Update ppRoot to point to pLeftChild (new root after rotation)\n\nParameters:\n  ppRoot - Pointer to pointer to BinaryTreeNode root being rotated\n           IMPLICIT: ECX register contains ppRoot value\n\nReturns:\n  void - Updates tree structure in-place through pointer indirection\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If *ppRoot is NULL, triggers assertion failure at 0x248 and terminates\n  - If (*ppRoot)->pLeftChild is NULL, triggers assertion failure at 0x249 and terminates\n  - Both conditions result in call to Ordinal_10023 (assertion handler) followed by FUN_6fb9a10f(-1) exit\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x248 (584 decimal) - Source line number for \"ptRoot != NULL\" assertion\n  0x249 (585 decimal) - Source line number for \"ptRoot->ptLess != NULL\" assertion\n  0xffffffff (-1) - Exit code passed to termination function\n  0xc (12 decimal) - Offset to pLeftChild field in BinaryTreeNode structure\n  0x10 (16 decimal) - Offset to pRightChild field in BinaryTreeNode structure\n\nStructure Layout:\n  BinaryTreeNode (20 bytes):\n  Offset | Size | Field Name    | Type              | Description\n  -------|------|---------------|-------------------|----------------------------------\n  0x00   | 2    | sYear         | short             | Year component for tree ordering\n  0x02   | 2    | sMonth        | short             | Month component for ordering\n  0x04   | 2    | sDay          | short             | Day component for ordering\n  0x06   | 2    | sHour         | short             | Hour component for ordering\n  0x08   | 2    | sMinute       | short             | Minute component for ordering\n  0x0a   | 2    | sBalance      | short             | AVL balance factor (-1, 0, +1)\n  0x0c   | 4    | pLeftChild    | BinaryTreeNode *  | Pointer to left subtree (less)\n  0x10   | 4    | pRightChild   | BinaryTreeNode *  | Pointer to right subtree (more)\n\nRotation Visualization:\n  Before:          After:\n      pRoot           pLeftChild\n      /   \\           /        \\\n  pLeft   C    =>    A        pRoot\n   / \\                         /   \\\n  A   B                       B     C\n\nAlgorithm Verification:\n  Step 5 maps to: pRoot->pLeftChild = pLeftChild->pRightChild (address 0x6faf71ca-0x6faf71cd)\n  Step 6 maps to: pLeftChild->pRightChild = pRoot (address 0x6faf71d0)\n  Step 7 maps to: *ppRoot = pLeftChild (address 0x6faf71d3)",
      "tags": ["SRC_automap.cpp", "UI_AUTOMAP", "MOD_UI", "TBL_automap", "PARAM_1", "STRUCT_Other"]
