      "comment": "ProcessUnitSkillsAndFlags - Process and render skill effects for all units with flag updates\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize loop counter and count variable to zero\n2. Store copies of input parameters in local variables\n3. Get automap sprite context pointer via Ordinal_10007\n4. Retrieve player skill list via Ordinal_10030 and iterate through skills\n5. Check skill flags (bit 3 disabled, bit 17 visible) and rendering conditions\n6. Render player skills to automap sprite buffer at pOutputContext+8\n7. Retrieve monster skill list via Ordinal_10031 and iterate with same logic\n8. Render monster skills to automap sprite buffer at pOutputContext+0xC\n9. Retrieve unit linked list head from pClient structure at offset 0x2C\n10. Iterate through units checking flags and processing based on type\n11. For player units (type 1), check txt 0x1B3 and call skill callback\n12. For monster units (type 2), apply special case filtering then call callback\n13. Advance to next unit via pointer at offset 0x10C and repeat\n\nParameters:\n  pClient (void *) - Pointer to client/game context with unit list at +0x2C\n  nForceUpdate (int) - Force rendering flag bypassing visibility checks\n  pOutputContext (void *) - Pointer to output with sprite buffers at +8, +0xC, +0x10\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value, processes units until NULL encountered\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Global flag DAT_6fbf42dc bypasses all checks when non-zero\n  - Skill bit 3 (0x08) = disabled, bit 17 (0x20000) = visible\n  - Unit bit 28 (0x10000000) = pending, bit 29 (0x20000000) = processed\n  - Monster 0x10B requires Nightmare/Hell difficulty (2 or 3)\n  - Monster 0x16E requires mode 2 state\n  - Monster 0x192 requires client state 0x4A\n  - Player unit 0x1B3 has special skill effect rendering",
