      "instructions": ["0x273B0|SUB|ESP, 0xc", "0x273B3|PUSH|EBX", "0x273B4|PUSH|EBP", "0x273B5|PUSH|ESI", "0x273B6|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0x273B8|PUSH|EDI", "0x273B9|MOV|EDI, EDX", "0x273BB|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [ESI + 0x14]", "0x273BE|TEST|EAX, 0x40000", "0x273C3|JNZ|0x6faf74e1", "0x273C9|OR|EAX, 0x40000", "0x273CE|MOV|dword ptr [ESI + 0x14], EAX", "0x273D1|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [EDI]", "0x273D3|MOV|ECX, dword ptr [EAX + 0x4]", "0x273D6|PUSH|ECX"],
      "comment": "Renders an automap cell to a sprite and inserts it into the automap sprite tree.\n\nAlgorithm:\n\n1. Check if cell has already been rendered (flag 0x40000 in dwReserved field)\n2. If not rendered yet, mark as rendered by setting flag 0x40000\n3. Load cell file handle from pCell->pParent using D2GFX ordinals\n4. Calculate cel number from cell file (returns -1 if not found)\n5. If cel found (nCelNum != -1):\n   a. Allocate new AutomapSprite structure\n   b. Calculate pixel coordinates: base position (pCell->dwHeight, pCell->dwXOffset) + offsets\n   c. Transform coordinates using Ordinal_10110 (likely screen/world coordinate conversion)\n   d. Scale coordinates by dividing by 10\n   e. Validate nPixelX is within signed 16-bit range (-32768 to 32767)\n   f. Validate nPixelY is within signed 16-bit range (-32768 to 32767)\n   g. Validate nCelNum is within signed 16-bit range (-32768 to 32767)\n   h. If layer number > 15, adjust nPixelY by adding 0x18 (24 pixels)\n   i. Set sprite fields: sCelNum, sPixelX, sPixelY\n   j. Insert sprite into binary tree via InsertAutomapSpriteIntoTree\n\nParameters:\n\npCell (GfxCell *) - Pointer to graphics cell containing rendering info and parent reference\npOffsets (int *) - Pointer to offset array with base coordinates [0]=unknown, [1]=X offset, [2]=Y offset\nppSpriteList (AutomapSprite **) - Pointer to pointer to root of automap sprite binary tree\n\nReturns:\n\nvoid - No return value; fatal errors trigger assertions and exit\n\nSpecial Cases:\n\n- If 0x40000 flag already set, function returns immediately without processing\n- nCelNum == -1 means cel not found in file, sprite allocation skipped\n- Layer numbers > 15 (0xF) get +24 pixel Y adjustment for vertical positioning\n- Coordinate overflow triggers assertion with source file/line info then exits\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n\n0x40000 (262144 decimal) - \"Cell already rendered\" flag bit in dwReserved field\n-1 (0xFFFFFFFF) - \"Cel not found\" sentinel value from Ordinal_10011\n-0x8000 (-32768 decimal) - SHRT_MIN, minimum signed 16-bit value\n0x7FFF (32767 decimal) - SHRT_MAX, maximum signed 16-bit value\n10 (0xA) - Coordinate scaling divisor for pixel conversion\n15 (0xF) - Layer number threshold for Y-adjustment\n0x18 (24 decimal) - Pixel Y adjustment for layers > 15\n0x395 (917 decimal) - Assertion line number for nPixelX overflow\n0x396 (918 decimal) - Assertion line number for nPixelY overflow\n0x397 (919 decimal) - Assertion line number for nCelNum overflow\n\nError Handling:\n\n- Coordinate overflow (X, Y, or cel number outside -32768 to 32767):\n  * Calls Ordinal_10023 with assertion message, source file, and line number\n  * Calls FUN_6fb9a10f(0xffffffff) which does not return (likely exit/abort)\n- Fatal errors prevent sprite insertion but do not return error codes\n\nStructure Layout:\n\nGfxCell (param_1):\nOffset  Size  Field          Type     Description\n------  ----  -------------  -------  ----------------------------------\n0x00    4     dwFlags        uint     Cell flags\n0x04    4     dwWidth        uint     Cell width in pixels\n0x08    4     dwHeight       uint     Cell height (used as Y base coordinate)\n0x0C    4     dwXOffset      uint     Cell X offset (used as X base coordinate)\n0x10    4     dwYOffset      uint     Cell Y offset\n0x14    4     dwReserved     uint     Reserved field with 0x40000 render flag\n0x18    4     pParent        void*    Pointer to parent cell file handle\n0x1C    4     dwLength       uint     Length field (layer number check)\n0x20    1     bCols          byte     Column count\n\nAutomapSprite (allocated):\nOffset  Size  Field          Type     Description\n------  ----  -------------  -------  ----------------------------------\n0x00    2     sCelNum        short    Cel number in cell file\n0x02    2     sPixelX        short    Screen X coordinate\n0x04    2     sPixelY        short    Screen Y coordinate\n\nFlag Bits:\n\nBit(s)    Hex       Name              Description\n--------  --------  ----------------  ------------------------------------\n18        0x40000   CELL_RENDERED     Cell already processed and rendered",
      "tags": ["SRC_automap.cpp", "UI_AUTOMAP", "MOD_UI", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "TBL_automap", "PARAM_3", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
