      "comment": "Creates an automap sprite with validated pixel coordinates and inserts it into the sprite tree.\n\nAlgorithm:\n\n1. Allocate new AutomapSprite structure via AllocateAutomapSprite\n2. Convert dwCoordinate to pixel X coordinate using Ordinal_10333 (divide by 10, add 1)\n3. Convert dwCoordinate to pixel Y coordinate using Ordinal_10334 (divide by 10, subtract 3)\n4. Validate nPixelX is within signed short range (-32768 to 32767)\n5. If nPixelX out of range, log assertion error and call fatal exit with code -1\n6. Validate nCalculatedPixelY is within signed short range (-32768 to 32767)\n7. If nCalculatedPixelY out of range, log assertion error and call fatal exit with code -1\n8. Validate nCelNumber is within signed short range (-32768 to 32767)\n9. If nCelNumber out of range, log assertion error and call fatal exit with code -1\n10. Assign nCelNumber to sprite sCelNum field (offset +0x4)\n11. Assign nPixelX to sprite sPixelX field (offset +0x6)\n12. Assign nCalculatedPixelY to sprite sPixelY field (offset +0x8)\n13. Insert sprite into binary tree via InsertAutomapSpriteIntoTree\n\nParameters:\n\ndwCoordinate - World/tile coordinate to convert to pixel position\nnCelNumber - Sprite cel/frame number for rendering\npSpriteList - Pointer to AutomapSprite tree root for insertion\n\nReturns:\n\nvoid - Function does not return on validation failure (calls FUN_6fb9a10f(-1))\n\nSpecial Cases:\n\nCoordinate conversion applies scale factor of 1/10 with fixed offsets (+1 for X, -3 for Y)\nAll three values must fit in signed 16-bit range to prevent truncation\nValidation failures trigger assertion logs followed by fatal exit\nError logging includes source file path and line numbers for debugging\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n\n0x66666667 (1717986919 decimal) - Magic multiplier for division by 10 optimization\n0x8000 (32768 decimal) - SHRT_MIN absolute value for range checking\n0x7fff (32767 decimal) - SHRT_MAX for upper bound validation\n0x3c9 (969 decimal) - Source line number for nPixelX assertion\n0x3ca (970 decimal) - Source line number for nPixelY assertion\n0x3cb (971 decimal) - Source line number for nCelNumber assertion\n0xffffffff (-1 decimal) - Fatal error exit code\n\nError Handling:\n\nOrdinal_10023 logs assertion failure with format string, source file, and line number\nFUN_6fb9a10f terminates process with exit code -1 (does not return)\nThree separate validation checkpoints for X coordinate, Y coordinate, and cel number\nError strings reference C:\\Projects\\Diablo2\\Source\\D2Client source paths\n\nStructure Layout:\n\nAutomapSprite (20 bytes total):\nOffset | Size | Field Name | Type   | Description\n-------|------|------------|--------|----------------------------------\n+0x0   | 4    | (unknown)  | void*  | Likely tree node pointer or flags\n+0x4   | 2    | sCelNum    | short  | Sprite cel/frame number\n+0x6   | 2    | sPixelX    | short  | Pixel X coordinate on automap\n+0x8   | 2    | sPixelY    | short  | Pixel Y coordinate on automap\n+0xa   | 10   | (unknown)  | byte[10] | Remaining structure fields",
