      "comment": "Set automap cursor update throttle to skip next 2 frames\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Set g_dwAutomapUpdateThrottle to 2 (0x2)\n2. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\nThis function sets a frame-skip throttle counter used by UpdateClientNodeFromCursor\nto reduce CPU usage by skipping automap cursor position updates for the next 2 frames.\nThe UpdateClientNodeFromCursor function checks this counter at entry, and if non-zero,\ndecrements it and returns early without processing cursor position or updating the\nautomap client node list.\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n- 0x2 (2) - Number of frames to skip for automap update throttling\n\nCross-Reference Usage:\nCalled from FUN_6fb61180 at 0x6fb6138e after conditional check (TEST EAX, JNZ).\nThe throttle mechanism prevents excessive automap updates when cursor position\nchanges rapidly, improving performance during fast mouse movement.",
