      "globals": ["0xFFFFFFFF9052FFA0||", "0xFFFFFFFF9052FF98||", "0xFFFFFFFF90530000||", "0xDE0E4|g_dwScreenWidth|0x280", "0xE1D10|g_dwSubtileDivisor|0xa", "0x1242D4|g_nAutomapOriginX|0x0", "0xFFFFFFFF9053001C||", "0xFFFFFFFF9052FFA4||", "0x1242D8|g_nAutomapOriginY|0x0", "0xFFFFFFFF90530018||", "0xFFFFFFFF9052FF9C||", "0xFFFFFFFF9052FFB8||", "0xFFFFFFFF9052FF94||", "0xFFFFFFFF9052FFBC||", "0x12428C|g_dwLastError|0x0", "0x1242E4|g_dwAutomapFadeState|0x0", "0xFFFFFFFF9052FFC0||", "0xFFFFFFFF9052FFC4||", "0x1242E8|g_dwAutomapFadeParam|0x0", "0x1242A4|DAT_6fbf42a4|0x0"],
      "api_count": 1,
      "api_calls": ["GfxInterface_CallMethod0x98"],
      "instructions": ["0x282C0|SUB|ESP, 0x6c", "0x282C3|PUSH|EBX", "0x282C4|PUSH|EBP", "0x282C5|PUSH|ESI", "0x282C6|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0x282C8|MOV|EBP, EDX", "0x282CA|PUSH|EDI", "0x282CB|TEST|ESI, ESI", "0x282CD|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x1c], EBP", "0x282D1|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x14], ESI", "0x282D5|JZ|0x6faf8591", "0x282DB|JMP|0x6faf82e1", "0x282DD|MOV|ESI, dword ptr [ESP + 0x14]", "0x282E1|XOR|EBX, EBX", "0x282E3|CALL|0x6fae4fd0"],
      "comment": "Recursively renders automap objects (sprites/symbols) with fade effects and clipping.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if node pointer is null, return if empty (early termination)\n2. Query scroll window mode to compute horizontal scroll offset adjustment\n3. Convert node world coordinates (pixelX, pixelY) to screen coordinates using subtile divisor\n4. Check if screen Y coordinate is within vertical render bounds (pRenderBounds[3] <= Y <= pRenderBounds[4])\n5. Recursively process left subtree (ptLess) if Y coordinate is above minimum bound\n6. If Y coordinate is below minimum bound, return early (subtree pruning)\n7. Check if screen X coordinate is within horizontal render bounds (pRenderBounds[1] <= X <= pRenderBounds[2])\n8. Initialize 18-element render parameter array, zero all elements using REP STOSD pattern\n9. Set render parameters: layer index, cel number, initial flags\n10. Compute fade level (0-5) based on automap fade state and distance from player\n11. Apply fade state transitions: Normal (1) -> Fading (2) when parameter changes, stay at level 1 for state 2\n12. For fade state 3, check game mode at offset +0x14 for visibility override (modes 0 or 2)\n13. Compute viewport clipping rectangle based on graphics mode (3D or 2D)\n14. For 3D mode: Set automap panel bounds (left or right side), query inventory state to adjust Y offset\n15. For 2D mode: Use full screen dimensions minus 1 pixel border\n16. Call Ordinal_10077 to render sprite with computed parameters and fade level\n17. Check if Y coordinate exceeds maximum bound, return if beyond visible region\n18. Advance to next sibling node (ptMore) and repeat traversal\n19. Return when ptMore is null (end of linked list)\n\nParameters:\n  pNode - Pointer to current AutomapSprite node in binary tree structure\n  pRenderBounds - Pointer to 7-element int array defining render region:\n    [0] = Layer index or rendering context ID\n    [1] = Minimum X coordinate (left edge of visible region)\n    [2] = Maximum X coordinate (right edge of visible region)\n    [3] = Minimum Y coordinate (top edge of visible region)\n    [4] = Maximum Y coordinate (bottom edge of visible region)\n    [5] = Player X offset for distance calculation (fade computation)\n    [6] = Player Y offset for distance calculation (fade computation)\n\nReturns:\n  void - Function performs rendering side effects, no return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Function is tail-recursive on ptMore traversal, processes ptLess via recursive call\n  - Early termination occurs when Y coordinate falls outside vertical bounds [3] to [4]\n  - Horizontal bounds [1] to [2] filter which objects render but don't prune tree traversal\n  - Fade level computation only applies in specific fade states and graphics modes\n  - 3D mode (g_dwGraphicsMode == 1) uses panel-relative coordinates, 2D mode uses full screen\n  - Inventory state affects Y offset in 3D mode when automap is on left side\n  - extraout_var is CONCAT31 high bytes from FUN_6fb06470 boolean return (compiler artifact)\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x0 = Null pointer check, fade state normal (no fading)\n  0x1 = Left scroll mode, fade state normal, 3D graphics mode, fade level bright\n  0x2 = Right scroll mode, fade state transitioning, 2D graphics mode, fade level medium-bright\n  0x3 = Fade state active (visibility override check), array element offset\n  0x4 = Array element offset (max Y bound), divide-by-4 right shift count\n  0x5 = Initial fade level (dimmest), array element offset (player X offset)\n  0x6 = Array element offset (player Y offset)\n  0xa = Decimal 10, subtile coordinate multiplier in 2D mode (DAT_6fbb1d10)\n  0x12 = Decimal 18, render parameter array element count (loop counter)\n  0x14 = Decimal 20, offset to game mode byte in structure returned by FUN_6fb62880\n  0x32 = Decimal 50, inner fade distance threshold (pixels from player)\n  0x39 = Decimal 57, 3D mode top clip Y offset when automap on right\n  0x60 = Decimal 96, conditional Y offset adjustment for inventory state\n  0x64 = Decimal 100, middle fade distance threshold\n  0x82 = Decimal 130, maximum Y distance from viewport center for fade computation\n  0x8c = Decimal 140, maximum X distance from screen center for fade computation\n  0x96 = Decimal 150, outer fade distance threshold\n  0xe1 = Decimal 225, 3D mode clip height (bottom = top + 0xe1)\n  0x117 = Decimal 279, 3D mode clip width (right = left + 0x117)\n  0x119 = Decimal 281, 3D mode left clip X when automap on right (screenWidth - 0x119)\n  0xffffff4c = Signed -180, 3D mode left clip X for large automap variant\n  0xffffff56 = Signed -170, 3D mode top clip Y for large automap variant\n  0xffffff60 = Signed -160, 3D mode left clip X for large automap variant 2\n  0xffffff78 = Signed -136, 3D mode left clip X for medium automap variant\n  0xffffff9c = Signed -100, 3D mode top clip Y for large automap variant 2\n  0xffffffa6 = Signed -90, 3D mode top clip Y for medium automap variant\n  0xffffffe0 = Signed -32, 2D mode top clip Y initial value\n  0xffffffef = Signed -17, conditional Y offset adjustment base\n  0xfffffff0 = Signed -16, 2D mode left clip X initial value\n  0xfffffffe = Mask for setting fade state to 2 when fade param non-zero\n\nFade Distance Computation:\n  - Calculates Manhattan-like distance with dominant axis weighted 2x\n  - deltaX = abs(screenCenterX - objectX + scrollOffset)\n  - deltaY = abs(viewportCenterY - 10 - objectY)\n  - distance = (smallerDelta + largerDelta * 2) / 2\n  - Fade levels: 0 (< 50px), 1 (< 100px), 2 (< 150px), 5 (>= 150px)\n\nStructure Layout:\n  AutomapSprite (20 bytes):\n    Offset  Size  Field Name     Type            Description\n    +0x0    2     sCelNum        short           Sprite cel number (frame index)\n    +0x2    2     (padding)      short           Alignment padding\n    +0x4    2     sPixelX        short           World X coordinate in subtile units\n    +0x6    2     (reserved)     short           Reserved/unused field\n    +0