      "comment": "Renders player and party member markers on the automap with optional name labels.\n\nAlgorithm:\n\n1. Initialize player iteration starting from first player slot node\n2. Get current player context and query entity list from game state  \n3. Iterate through all entity slots in the entity list array\n4. For each slot, traverse the linked list of entities at offset 0x2c\n5. Check entity type: 0 = player, 1 = party member, 2 = special marker (0x10b class)\n6. Validate entity should be displayed based on party mode and player state\n7. Call ValidateAutomapMarkerDisplay() to get color and display validation\n8. Get entity world coordinates via Ordinal_10333/10334 (X/Y positions)\n9. Convert world coordinates to automap coordinates using subtile divisor\n10. Apply automap origin offset and +8/-8 pixel adjustment for centering\n11. Perform viewport bounds check against automap viewport rectangle\n12. If entity type 0 (player): Call RenderAutomapPlayerIcon() with color\n13. If entity type 1 (party member): Draw custom icon using line data table\n14. If entity type 2 (class 0x10b): Render either icon or special text marker\n15. If g_fShowAutomapPartyNames enabled and not local player: Render player name above marker\n16. Advance to next entity in linked list via offset 0x10c\n17. After main loop, check for duplicate player IDs across remote players\n18. For duplicate players in same act: Render additional markers at their coordinates\n\nParameters:\n\nIMPLICIT EBX: Unknown context register (preserved across function)\nIMPLICIT EDI: Byte value passed to RenderTextWithFont() for rendering flags\n\nReturns:\n\nvoid - No return value (renders directly to automap buffer)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n\n- If g_dwAutomapPartyMode == 0: Only render local player marker (not party members)\n- If g_fShowAutomapPartyNames == 0: Suppress name labels above markers  \n- If g_dwGraphicsMode == 1: Apply coordinate adjustment for alternate rendering mode\n- Party member markers (type 1) use g_AutomapPlayerIconLineData for custom icon shape\n- Special class 0x10b with names enabled uses different text rendering path\n- Duplicate player ID check handles remote players in same game session/act\n\nNote: Function uses 12 SSA temporary variables optimized away by decompiler (extraout_var, unaff_EDI, uVar1, uVar2, uVar9, dVar3, iVar7, piVar4, piVar8, pUVar5, pvVar6 - compiler optimization artifacts appearing in decompiled view but not renameable)\n\nCoordinate Transformation:\n\nWorldX / g_dwSubtileDivisor - g_nAutomapOriginX + 8 = AutomapX\nWorldY / g_dwSubtileDivisor - g_nAutomapOriginY - 8 = AutomapY\n\nViewport Bounds:\ng_nAutomapViewportLeft <= AutomapX <= g_nAutomapViewportRight\ng_nAutomapViewportTop <= AutomapY <= g_nAutomapViewportBottom\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n\n0x00 - Entity type: Player\n0x01 - Entity type: Party member  \n0x02 - Entity type: Special marker\n0x07 - Parameter to Ordinal_10487() for party flag check\n0x10b (267) - Special class ID for alternate marker rendering\n0x10c (268) - Offset to next entity pointer in linked list\n0x2c (44) - Offset to entity list head pointer in slot structure\n0x2fb (763) - Offset to name string null terminator check\n0xff (255) - Alpha value for line drawing (fully opaque)\n\nStructure Layout:\n\nEntity/UnitAny offsets:\nOffset | Size | Field Name | Type | Description\n0x00   | 4    | dwUnitType | uint | Entity type (0=player, 1=party, 2=special)\n0x04   | 4    | dwClassId  | uint | Class identifier (0x10b for special rendering)\n0x10c  | 4    | pNext      | ptr  | Next entity in linked list\n(Other fields accessed via helper functions)\n\nSlot structure offsets:\nOffset | Size | Field Name     | Type | Description  \n0x2c   | 4    | pEntityListHead| ptr  | Head of entity linked list\n\ng_AutomapPlayerIconLineData format:\nArray of int[2] coordinate pairs for line segments (x1, y1, x2, y2 pattern)\nTerminated when pointer exceeds UNK_6fba861f (end marker)",
