      "comment": "Validates whether a unit should be displayed on the automap and determines its marker type.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Read unit type from pUnit->dwUnitType\n2. If unit type is Player (0):\n   a. If unit ID is not Town Portal (0x11):\n      i. Check if unit is the current player - return SelfPlayer marker\n      ii. Get current player unit and compare area IDs\n      iii. If areas match, return SameParty marker\n      iv. Otherwise return OtherArea marker\n   b. If unit ID is Town Portal (0x11):\n      i. Check if portal owner matches unit's memory pool ID\n      ii. If match, return PartyMember marker\n3. If unit type is Monster (1):\n   a. If unit ID is not Diablo (0xc):\n      i. Check flags at offset 0xe8 for bit 0x200000 (hidden) - return false if set\n      ii. Check flags for bit 0x200 (super unique) - return Monster marker if set\n      iii. Get monster stats and check if boss flag at offset 0x2fb is clear\n      iv. If boss flag clear, validate player connection status:\n          - Status 0 or 3: return false (don't display)\n          - Status 1: return Monster marker\n          - Status 2: return Connection marker\n      v. Check if class ID is minion (0x219, 0x21a, 0x21b) - return false if so\n      vi. Otherwise return Hostile marker\n4. If unit type is Object (2):\n   a. If class ID is waypoint (0x3b), return Object marker\n   b. If class ID is shrine (0x3c):\n      i. Get level ID and check if in restricted list (0x6f-0x70, 0x75, 0x7d-0x7f)\n      ii. If restricted, return false (don't display)\n      iii. Otherwise return Object marker\n   c. If class ID is quest marker (0x10b), return marker type 0\n5. Return false for all other cases (don't display)\n\nParameters:\n  pUnit: Pointer to UnitAny structure being validated for automap display\n  pbMarkerType: Output pointer to receive the marker type byte if unit should be displayed\n\nReturns:\n  1 (true) if unit should be displayed on automap with marker type written to *pbMarkerType\n  0 (false) if unit should not be displayed on automap\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Hidden monsters (flag 0x200000) are never displayed\n  - Diablo boss (unit ID 0xc) is never displayed\n  - Minion monsters (0x219-0x21b) are never displayed  \n  - Shrines in specific restricted levels are hidden\n  - Town portals only display if owned by party member\n  - Connection validation determines if remote players are shown\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x11 (17): Town Portal unit ID\n  0xc (12): Diablo boss unit ID\n  0x200000: Hidden unit flag bit\n  0x200: Super unique monster flag bit\n  0x2fb: Boss flag offset in monster stats\n  0x3b (59): Waypoint object class ID\n  0x3c (60): Shrine object class ID\n  0x10b (267): Quest marker object class ID\n  0x219-0x21b (537-539): Minion monster class IDs\n  0x6f-0x70 (111-112), 0x75 (117), 0x7d-0x7f (125-127): Restricted level IDs for shrines\n\nSSA Variables (Decompiler-Generated):\n  uVar1: Unit type from pUnit->dwUnitType (uint)\n  sVar2, sVar3: Area ID comparison results (short)\n  uVar4: Return value from Ordinal_10342 (uint)\n  iVar5: Temporary for connection validation and level checks (int)\n  pvVar6: Portal owner from Ordinal_10293 (void *)\n  pUVar7: Current player unit pointer (UnitAny *)\n  piVar8: Current player unit for area comparison (int *)\n  \nNote: Function uses 8 SSA temporary variables optimized by decompiler. These variables\nrepresent intermediate calculation results and cannot be renamed through standard tools.\n\nError Handling:\n  Returns 0 (false) for invalid unit types or conditions where display is not appropriate\n  No explicit error codes - binary success/failure based on validation logic",
