      "comment": "Renders text string using specified font size with Unicode conversion.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate length of input text string using manual strlen loop\n2. Return early if string is empty (length == 0)\n3. Clamp font size to maximum value of 0xc (12) if exceeds limit\n4. Initialize Unicode buffer (48 characters) with default constructors\n5. Zero-initialize Unicode buffer using STOSD/STOSW instructions\n6. Convert ASCII/ANSI text to Unicode using toUnicode function\n7. Calculate adjusted X position by subtracting 10 from nX parameter\n8. Call D2WIN font rendering functions (Ordinal_10121, Ordinal_10117)\n9. Cleanup font resources with final Ordinal_10127 call\n\nParameters:\n  this (void *) - Pointer to null-terminated ASCII/ANSI text string to render (passed in ECX via __thiscall convention, cast to char*)\n  nX (int) - X coordinate for text rendering position\n  byFontSize (byte) - Font size index (0-12), clamped to maximum of 0xc\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Empty strings (length 0) skip all rendering operations\n  - Font size values > 12 (0xc) are clamped to 0 for safety\n  - Unicode buffer fixed at 48 characters (0x17 = 23 wide chars)\n  - X coordinate adjusted by -10 before passing to rendering functions\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0xc (12) - Maximum valid font size index\n  0x17 (23) - Unicode buffer capacity in wide characters\n  48 - Total Unicode array size (23 * 2 bytes + null terminator)\n  -10 - X coordinate adjustment offset\n  -2 - Empty string detection sentinel (strlen loop result)",
