      "comment": "Initialize video playback Unicode string buffers and format strings for display.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize local Unicode string arrays\n   - Call Unicode constructor 0x19 (25) times for wszLocalBuffer[52]\n   - Call Unicode constructor 0x32 (50) times for second Unicode buffer[100]\n2. Retrieve validated global string pointer via GetValidatedGlobalString()\n3. Retrieve video playback filename via GetVideoPlaybackFilename()\n4. Check if either string pointer is valid (not NULL)\n5. If validated global string exists:\n   - Format string using g_szStringFormatSpecifier (\"%s\") with lpszValidatedString\n   - Convert formatted ASCII string to Unicode using toUnicode() with max length 0x19\n   - Get string resource ID 0x1055 via Ordinal_10004\n   - Copy and concatenate Unicode strings using strcpy/strcat\n   - Allocate video string buffer via Ordinal_10121 with size 4 bytes at offset 0\n   - Write concatenated string to buffer via Ordinal_10117\n   - Advance g_dwVideoStringBufferPointer by 0x10 (16 bytes)\n6. If video playback string exists via GetVideoPlaybackString():\n   - Format string using g_szStringFormatSpecifier (\"%s\") with retrieved string\n   - Convert formatted ASCII string to Unicode with max length 0x19\n   - Get string resource ID 0x1056 via Ordinal_10004\n   - Copy and concatenate Unicode strings\n   - Allocate video string buffer via Ordinal_10121 with size 4 bytes at offset 0\n   - Write concatenated string to buffer via Ordinal_10117\n   - Advance g_dwVideoStringBufferPointer by 0x10 (16 bytes)\n7. Return\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nIMPLICIT:\n  ESI - lpszSourceString: Pointer to source Unicode string for copy operations\n  EDI - lpszDestString: Pointer to destination Unicode string for copy operations\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If both GetValidatedGlobalString() and GetVideoPlaybackFilename() return NULL, function returns immediately\n- Unicode buffers initialized to size 52 (wszLocalBuffer) and 100 (se