      "comment": "Process automap rendering state with video string buffer manipulation\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize 100-byte Unicode buffer by calling default constructor 50 times (50 × 2-byte Unicode = 100 bytes)\n2. Call Ordinal_10004 (D2WIN.DLL) to perform video initialization or state setup\n3. Copy Unicode string data from implicit source to implicit destination via Unicode::strcpy\n4. Read current video string buffer position from g_dwVideoStringBufferPointer\n5. Call Ordinal_10121 (D2COMMON.DLL) with buffer position, size value 4, and zero parameter\n6. Call Ordinal_10117 (D2WIN.DLL) with saved buffer position, size value 4, and zero parameter\n7. Advance global buffer pointer by 0x10 (16 bytes) for next rendering operation\n\nParameters:\nIMPLICIT ESI (char *) - Source Unicode string pointer for copy operation\nIMPLICIT EDI (char *) - Destination Unicode string pointer for copy operation\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Unicode buffer initialization requires 50 iterations because each Unicode character is 2 bytes\n- Loop counter 0x32 (50 decimal) decrements until zero, initializing 100-byte buffer\n- Buffer pointer advancement of 0x10 (16 bytes) suggests fixed-size string slots\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x32 (50 decimal) - Number of Unicode characters to initialize (100 bytes total)\n0x2 - Unicode character size in bytes, iterator advances by 2 each loop\n0x4 (4 decimal) - Size parameter passed to ordinal functions\n0x10 (16 bytes) - Buffer pointer advancement for next string slot\n\nGlobal Data References:\ng_dwVideoStringBufferPointer @ 0x6fbf42f8 - Current position in video string buffer, advanced by 0x10 after processing",
