      "comment": "Initializes and clears a 4-byte video buffer entry for string rendering\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check render context validity via GetRenderContextHandle\n2. If context invalid (0), return immediately without processing\n3. Get D2COMMON context handle from render context using Ordinal_10057\n4. Calculate video buffer address offset using FUN_6fb5dad0\n5. Store current buffer pointer position from g_dwVideoStringBufferPointer\n6. Clear 4-byte buffer entry at current position using Ordinal_10121(buffer, 4, 0)\n7. Initialize buffer metadata using Ordinal_10117(buffer, 4, 0)\n8. Advance global buffer pointer g_dwVideoStringBufferPointer by 0x10 (16 bytes)\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If render context is NULL (FUN_6fb634e0 returns 0), function returns early\n- Buffer pointer increments by 16 bytes (0x10) even though only 4 bytes are cleared\n- This suggests 16-byte aligned buffer entries with 4-byte data + 12-byte metadata\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x10 (16 decimal) - Buffer entry stride/alignment, advances pointer after initialization\n4 - Size of video buffer entry in bytes being cleared\n0 - Clear value used to initialize buffer entry\n\nGlobal Data References:\ng_dwVideoStringBufferPointer @ 0x6fbf42f8 - Current write position in video string buffer (dword)\n\nExternal Functions:\nFUN_6fb634e0 - GetRenderContextHandle, returns current render context or 0 if invalid\nOrdinal_10057 (D2COMMON) - Context conversion, transforms render context to D2COMMON handle\nFUN_6fb5dad0 - CalculateBufferAddress, computes video buffer address from context handle\nOrdinal_10121 (D2COMMON) - Buffer clear operation, fills buffer with specified value\nOrdinal_10117 (D2COMMON) - Buffer metadata initialization",
