      "comment": "Renders the automap version string to the video buffer.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize Unicode object array by calling default constructor for 100 Unicode objects\n2. Get current game instance interface pointer via GetCurrentInstance()\n3. If instance exists, call instance method at offset 0x5c to retrieve version data\n4. Format version string using \"v %d.%02d\" template with major/minor version components\n5. Calculate major version by dividing result by 100 (value / 100)\n6. Calculate minor version using modulo operation (value % 100)\n7. Convert formatted ASCII string to Unicode character array\n8. Call Ordinal_10121() to set rendering state/context\n9. Call Ordinal_10117() to render Unicode text at current buffer position with mode 4\n10. Increment global video string buffer pointer by 0x10 for next string position\n\nParameters:\n  None - Function takes no parameters\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If GetCurrentInstance() returns NULL, skip rendering and only increment buffer pointer\n  - Version calculation uses magic constant 0x51eb851f for fast division approximation\n  - Unicode array allocated as 200 elements (100 wide chars * 2 bytes each)\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x5c (92) - Offset to GetVersion method in instance vtable\n  0x64 (100) - Number of Unicode objects to initialize, also max string length\n  0x51eb851f - Magic multiplier for fast integer division by 100\n  0x10 (16) - Buffer pointer increment for next string slot\n  4 - Rendering mode parameter for Ordinal_10117\n\nStructure Access:\n  Instance+0x5c - Virtual method pointer to GetVersion() function\n  Returns version as integer (major*100 + minor)",
