      "api_calls": ["ValidateStringId", "ValidateStringId", "FogAssert", "ValidateStringId", "ValidateStringId", "SumCharacterValues", "RenderUnicodeTextWithLineHeight"],
      "instructions": ["0x29080|SUB|ESP, 0x258", "0x29086|PUSH|EBX", "0x29087|CALL|0x6fadb930", "0x2908C|AND|EAX, 0xff", "0x29091|DEC|EAX", "0x29092|JZ|0x6faf90a2", "0x29094|DEC|EAX", "0x29095|JNZ|0x6faf9161", "0x2909B|MOV|EBX, 0x1422", "0x290A0|JMP|0x6faf90a7", "0x290A2|MOV|EBX, 0x1423", "0x290A7|PUSH|ESI", "0x290A8|PUSH|EDI", "0x290A9|LEA|ESI, [ESP + 0xc]", "0x290AD|MOV|EDI, 0x12c"],
      "comment": "Renders video frame count overlay text on automap display\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check video frame count mode via GetVideoFrameCount()\n2. If mode is 1 or 2, initialize Unicode string buffer (300 chars)\n3. Initialize each Unicode character with default constructor in loop\n4. Determine string resource ID based on mode: 0x1422 for mode 1, 0x1423 for mode 2\n5. Retrieve two localized strings via StrGetStringByIndex (D2LANG Ordinal_10004)\n6. Calculate combined string length with format overhead (+3 bytes)\n7. Validate buffer capacity (299 chars max) to prevent overflow\n8. If overflow detected, trigger assertion and terminate (-1 exit code)\n9. Format combined string using Unicode::sprintf with resource strings\n10. Build video text entry structure at buffer offsets: [0]=g_dwVideoStringBufferPointer, [1]=4 (flags), [2]=0 (terminator)\n11. Queue text entry for rendering via D2WIN Ordinal_10117\n12. Commit rendering queue via D2COMMON Ordinal_10121\n13. Advance global video string buffer pointer by 0x10 (16 bytes)\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nIMPLICIT:\nEDI - lpszFormatString: Pointer to format string buffer used by string retrieval functions\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value, function modifies global rendering state\n\nSpecial Cases:\nVideo frame count modes:\n- 1 (0x01): Use string resource 0x1422 - likely \"Frame %d\" or \"FPS: %d\"\n- 2 (0x02): Use string resource 0x1423 - alternate frame display format\n- Other: Early return without rendering overlay\n\nBuffer overflow protection:\n- Maximum Unicode buffer capacity: 300 characters (600 bytes)\n- Length check threshold: 299 characters\n- Includes format string overhead (+3 bytes)\n- Overflow triggers assertion at source location 0xb10 in D2Client\n\nVideo text entry structure (12 bytes):\nOffset | Size | Field Name                | Type | Description\n-------|------|---------------------------|------|------------------------------------------\n0x00   | 4    | dwBufferPointer           | uint | Global video string buffer position\n0x04   | 4    | dwFlags                   | uint | Rendering flags (always 4)\n0x08   | 4    | dwTerminator              | uint | Structure terminator (always 0)\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x1422 (5154 decimal) - String resource ID for video mode 1\n0x1423 (5155 decimal) - String resource ID for video mode 2\n300 (0x12c) - Unicode buffer capacity in characters\n299 (0x12b) - Maximum allowed string length for overflow check\n0x10 (16 decimal) - Video string buffer pointer increment\n0xb10 (2832 decimal) - Source line number for assertion\n4 - Video text rendering flags value\n0 - Structure terminator value\n\nError Handling:\n- Buffer overflow: Calls Ordinal_10023 (assertion handler) with file, line number\n- Assertion triggers FUN_6fb9a10f(-1) terminating process\n- No recovery path - overflow is fatal error condition\n\nGlobal Data References:\ng_dwVideoStringBufferPointer @ 0x6fbf42f8 - Current position in video text rendering buffer",
      "tags": ["SRC_automap.cpp", "UI_AUTOMAP", "MOD_UI", "STRUCT_Inventory", "TBL_automap", "PARAM_0", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control"]
