      "instructions": ["0x29620|MOV|EAX, ECX", "0x29622|CMP|EAX, dword ptr [0x6fbf428c]", "0x29628|JZ|0x6faf96b2", "0x2962E|MOV|[0x6fbf428c], EAX", "0x29633|DEC|EAX", "0x29634|MOV|dword ptr [0x6fbb1d10], 0xa", "0x2963E|JNZ|0x6faf964a", "0x29640|MOV|dword ptr [0x6fbb1d10], 0x14", "0x2964A|CALL|0x6faf9280", "0x2964F|CALL|0x6faf57b0", "0x29654|MOV|EAX, [0x6fbf428c]", "0x29659|DEC|EAX", "0x2965A|JZ|0x6faf9669", "0x2965C|XOR|EAX, EAX", "0x2965E|MOV|[0x6fbf42c4], EAX"],
      "comment": "Sets the automap graphics mode and recalculates window border offsets.\n\nAlgorithm:\n\n1. Check if the requested graphics mode differs from current mode\n   - If modes match, return immediately (no changes needed)\n2. Set subtile divisor based on graphics mode\n   - Mode 0 (normal): Set divisor to 10 (0xA)\n   - Mode 1 (high-res): Set divisor to 20 (0x14)\n3. Update global graphics mode variable to new mode value\n4. Reload automap sprite resources for the new graphics mode\n   - Loads different sprite files based on resolution\n5. Reinitialize viewport coordinates for new display mode\n6. Calculate window border offsets based on graphics mode\n   - Mode 0: Reset borders to zero (no offset needed)\n   - Mode 1: Calculate borders from screen dimensions\n     * X border = (screen_width / 3 - window_base_x) - 16\n     * Y border = (screen_height / 3 - window_base_y) - 16\n7. Return the graphics mode value (or intermediate calculation for mode 1)\n\nParameters:\n\nnGraphicsMode - Graphics mode to set (0 = normal resolution, 1 = high resolution)\n\nReturns:\n\nGraphics mode value on success\nIntermediate calculation value (screen_height * 0x55555556) if mode 1 and changes applied\n\nSpecial Cases:\n\nMode values other than 0 or 1 are treated as mode 0 (normal resolution)\nIf current mode already matches requested mode, function returns immediately without reloading resources\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n\n0x0A (10) - Subtile divisor for normal resolution mode\n0x14 (20) - Subtile divisor for high resolution mode\n0x55555556 - Magic number for division by 3 using multiplication\n             Formula: (value * 0x55555556) >> 32 = value / 3\n             Used to calculate window borders as 1/3 of screen dimensions\n0x10 (16) - Border offset adjustment in pixels\n            Subtracted from calculated border position",
      "tags": ["PARAM_1"]
    },
