      "comment": "Renders centered text within a horizontal boundary using D2WIN text drawing.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate text width by calling Ordinal_10121 (D2COMMON text measurement)\n2. Compute available horizontal space: nRightX - nLeftX + 1\n3. If text width < available space, calculate centering offset\n   - Subtract text width from available space\n   - Divide offset by 2 (right shift 1)\n   - Add offset to left X coordinate\n4. Call Ordinal_10117 (D2WIN DrawText) with centered position and flags\n\nParameters:\n  nLeftX - Left boundary X coordinate for text centering\n  nYPos - Y screen coordinate for text baseline\n  nRightX - Right boundary X coordinate for text centering\n  pwszText - Pointer to wide character (Unicode) text string\n  dwFlags - Text rendering flags (color, alignment, font attributes)\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If text width >= available space, renders at left boundary without centering\n  - Text measurement includes null terminator (+1 to width)\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x1 (decimal 1) - Added to width calculation for null terminator or spacing",
