      "comment": "Parse Unicode string and split at first newline character.\\n\\nAlgorithm:\\n1. Initialize output pointer to NULL (zero ppwszNextLine)\\n2. Get length of input string buffer via Unicode::strlen\\n3. Scan Unicode string character by character searching for newline (0x000A)\\n4. If null terminator (0x0000) encountered before newline, return false (not found)\\n5. When newline found, null-terminate string at that position\\n6. Validate remaining buffer: if no characters after newline, return false\\n7. Set output pointer to character immediately after newline\\n8. Return true indicating successful line split\\n\\nParameters:\\n  pwszLine (ushort *) - Unicode string buffer to parse and modify (null-terminated)\\n  ppwszNextLine (ushort **) - Output pointer to receive address of next line after newline\\n  IMPLICIT: EDI (char *) - ASCII string buffer used for length validation\\n\\nReturns:\\n  true (1) - Successfully found newline and split string\\n  false (0) - No newline found, or newline at end of buffer with no next line\\n\\nSpecial Cases:\\n  Newline at buffer boundary: Returns false if newline is last valid character\\n  Null-terminated before newline: Returns false, leaves string unmodified\\n  String modification: Original string is modified (newline replaced with null)\\n\\nMagic Numbers:\\n  0x000A (10) - Unicode newline character (LF)\\n  0x0000 (0) - Unicode null terminator",
      "tags": ["PARAM_2"]
