      "api_calls": ["GfxInterfaceCall84", "GfxInterfaceCall84", "GfxInterfaceCall84", "GfxInterfaceCall84", "ValidateStringId", "InitializeStringBuffer", "GetUnitStatById", "GfxInterfaceCall84", "SetActiveFont", "ValidateStringId", "...+82 more"],
      "instructions": ["0x29BA0|SUB|ESP, 0x374", "0x29BA6|PUSH|EBX", "0x29BA7|PUSH|EBP", "0x29BA8|PUSH|ESI", "0x29BA9|PUSH|EDI", "0x29BAA|CALL|0x6fb62880", "0x29BAF|MOV|EDX, dword ptr [0x6fbfd800]", "0x29BB5|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x1c], EAX", "0x29BB9|MOV|ECX, 0x12", "0x29BBE|XOR|EAX, EAX", "0x29BC0|LEA|EDI, [ESP + 0x34]", "0x29BC4|XOR|ESI, ESI", "0x29BC6|STOSD.REP|ES:EDI", "0x29BC8|MOV|EAX, [0x6fbf8f9c]", "0x29BCD|MOV|ECX, dword ptr [0x6fbae0e8]"],
      "comment": "Renders player statistics overlay on game screen displaying attributes and status information.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize display context and zero out 18 dwords for UI state structure\n2. Set up four screen position overlays at calculated screen coordinates relative to g_dwScreenHeight\n3. Initialize 50 Unicode character buffers for text rendering\n4. Check mouse coordinates for hover detection in specific UI regions (0x80-0xA0 X, height-based Y ranges)\n5. If quest flag set (Ordinal_10521 returns non-zero), render quest indicator with formatted quest count\n6. Render attribute modification indicators from table at 0x6fbb23c4 (5 entries, 14 bytes each)\n7. Process multi-line text blocks from 0x6fbb2148 table, rendering each line with proper Y offset on line breaks\n8. Calculate player experience percentage from current/total XP and difficulty multipliers\n9. Determine render mode based on mouse hover regions: 0=off-left panel, 1=right panel hover\n10. Render selected attribute display box with 155x30px dimensions at table-defined coordinates\n11. Format and display selected stat value from player statistics structure\n12. Process stat comparison display if hovering over level requirement region\n13. Render player name if target data available using GetPlayerTargetDataByInfo\n14. Iterate through stat display table at 0x6fbb2268, rendering each stat with color coding based on stat state\n15. Apply special processing for stats 0x06-0x0B (enhanced stats with shift operations)\n16. Handle resistance stats (0x25-0x2D) with difficulty-based penalties and cap checks\n17. Render experience stat (0x1F) with quest/penalty modifiers and special formatting\n18. Display mana/life regeneration stats (0x0D/0x1E) with special string formatting\n\nParameters:\nNone (accesses global state directly)\n\nIMPLICIT:\nESI - preserved size value for strncpy operations\nEDI - preserved text pointer for Unicode operations\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\nIf player stats pointer null (Ordinal_10582 returns 0), calls error handler at 0x17A/0x1EA\nIf difficulty level > 2, calls error handler at 0x175\nColor coding: 0=normal, 1=enhanced, 3=penalty/reduced, 4=capped at maximum\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x80 (128) - X offset for hover region start\n0xA0 (160) - X offset for hover region end  \n0x100 (256) - X offset increment between UI elements\n0x9B (155) - Width of stat display box in pixels\n0x1E (30) - Height of stat display box in pixels\n0xE0 (224) - Y offset from screen bottom for top elements\n0x30 (48) - Y offset from screen bottom for bottom elements\n0x5F (95) - Maximum stat level cap\n0x5 (5) - Minimum stat level floor\n0x244 (580) - Offset to difficulty stat table in player stats structure\n0x26C (620) - Offset to alternate difficulty stat table\n0x294 (660) - Offset to tertiary difficulty stat table\n0x1C4 (452) - Offset to difficulty multiplier array\n0x3C (60) - Offset to stat array in statistics structure\n\nStructure Layout:\nPlayer Statistics Structure (from Ordinal_10582):\nOffset  Size  Field Name                Type      Description\n+0x1C4  1     byDifficultyMultiplier    byte      XP multiplier per difficulty\n+0x244  4     dwDifficultyStat1         uint      Primary difficulty-based stat\n+0x26C  4     dwDifficultyStat2         uint      Secondary difficulty-based stat  \n+0x294  4     dwDifficultyStat3         uint      Tertiary difficulty-based stat\n\nUI State Structure (local_350 base):\nOffset  Size  Field Name                Type      Description\n+0x00   4     nScreenY                  int       Current Y screen coordinate\n+0x04   4     pnUiDataPtr               int*      Pointer to UI data table\n+0x08   4     dwOverlayState            uint      Current overlay render state (0-3)\n\nStat Table Entry Format (at 0x6fbb2268):\nOffset  Size  Field Name                Type      Description\n+0x00   4     dwStatId                  uint      Stat identifier (6-0x2D range)\n+0x04   4     nYOffset                  int       Y coordinate offset from base\n+0x08   4     nXOffset                  int       X coordinate offset from base\n+0x0C   4     dwFlags                   uint      Display flags\n+0x10   4     nReserved                 int       Reserved field\n(20 bytes per entry, repeats until >= 0x6fbb23ce)\n\nFlag Bits:\nBit 0 (0x01) - Use Ordinal_10519 instead of Ordinal_10521 for stat fetch\nBit 1 (0x02) - Alternate render mode\nBit 2 (0x04) - Enable color coding\nBit 3 (0x08) - Enhanced stat display (shift value right 8 bits)",
      "tags": ["MOD_UI", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "STRUCT_Room2", "STRUCT_Room1", "STRUCT_ItemData", "PARAM_0", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "SRC_char.cpp", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData", "STRUCT_StatList", "STRUCT_MonsterData", "PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Path", "UI_CHAR", "STRUCT_Skill", "STRUCT_Other", "PROP_LOOPHEAVY"]
