      "api_calls": ["FogAssert", "GetMonsterInitStatsPtr", "FogAssert", "GetCharacterSlotAddress", "FogAssert", "GetTotalStatValue"],
      "instructions": ["0x2ABA0|SUB|ESP, 0x8", "0x2ABA3|PUSH|EBX", "0x2ABA4|PUSH|EBP", "0x2ABA5|PUSH|ESI", "0x2ABA6|PUSH|EDI", "0x2ABA7|MOV|EDI, ECX", "0x2ABA9|TEST|EDI, EDI", "0x2ABAB|JNZ|0x6fafabb7", "0x2ABAD|POP|EDI", "0x2ABAE|POP|ESI", "0x2ABAF|POP|EBP", "0x2ABB0|XOR|EAX, EAX", "0x2ABB2|POP|EBX", "0x2ABB3|ADD|ESP, 0x8", "0x2ABB6|RET|"],
      "comment": "Calculates alpha transparency value (0-95) for player statistics overlay rendering.\n\nAlgorithm:\n\n1. Validate input - return 0 if nOffensiveStatValue is 0\n2. Get player context pointer via FUN_6fb62880()\n3. Get current difficulty level (0=Normal, 1=Nightmare, 2=Hell) from GetVideoFrameCount()\n4. Validate difficulty level < 3, abort if invalid (prevents array out-of-bounds)\n5. Get PlayerStatistics structure pointer via GetPlayerStatistics()\n6. Get stats structure pointer via Ordinal_10582(), validate not NULL\n7. Read defensive resistance value from stats structure at offset 0x1ac + (difficulty * 4)\n8. If player context first field is 0, get alternate stats structure via Ordinal_10581()\n9. If alternate structure exists, read bonus value at offset 0x3c and add to nOffensiveStatValue\n10. Normalize negative values - if defense < 0, transfer to offense and set defense to 0\n11. Normalize negative values - if offense < 0, transfer to defense and set offense to 0\n12. Calculate offense/defense ratio percentage - if defense is 0, use 100%\n13. Calculate offense/defense ratio percentage - if offense is 0, use 0%\n14. Calculate ratio percentage: (offense * 100) / (defense + offense)\n15. Get character level modifier via Ordinal_10519(context, 0xc)\n16. Read difficulty scaling byte from stats structure at offset 0x1c4 + difficulty\n17. Apply weighted formula: (level * ratio * 2) / (scaling_byte + level)\n18. Clamp result to minimum of 5\n19. Clamp result to maximum of 95 (0x5f)\n20. Return clamped alpha transparency value\n\nParameters:\n\nnOffensiveStatValue (int) - Offensive statistic value from player (attack, offense, damage stat)\n\nReturns:\n\nint - Alpha transparency value clamped to range [5, 95]\n     - 5 minimum transparency (mostly opaque)\n     - 95 maximum transparency (mostly transparent)\n     - 0 if input value is 0 (early return)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n\n- If difficulty level >= 3, triggers assertion and aborts execution\n- If PlayerStatistics pointer is NULL, triggers assertion and aborts execution\n- If stats structure pointer is NULL, triggers assertion and aborts execution\n- If alternate stats structure is NULL when needed, triggers assertion and aborts\n- Negative resistance values are normalized by transferring to opposite stat\n- Division by zero prevented - if both offense and defense become 0, ratio defaults to 100%\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n\n0x1ac (428 decimal) - Offset to defensive resistance array base in stats structure\n0x1c4 (452 decimal) - Offset to difficulty scaling byte array in stats structure\n0x3c (60 decimal) - Offset to bonus value in alternate stats structure\n0xc (12 decimal) - Parameter to Ordinal_10519() to get character level modifier\n0x5f (95 decimal) - Maximum alpha transparency value (mostly transparent)\n0x5 (5 decimal) - Minimum alpha transparency value (mostly opaque)\n0x2 (2 decimal) - Multiplier in weighted formula for ratio adjustment\n0x13e (318 decimal) - Line number for difficulty level assertion\n0x143 (323 decimal) - Line number for PlayerStatistics NULL assertion\n0x126 (294 decimal) - Line number for alternate stats structure assertion\n\nStructure Layout (PlayerStatistics):\n\nOffset  | Size | Field Name              | Type  | Description\n--------|------|-------------------------|-------|------------------------------------------\n0x1ac   | 12   | defensive_resistances   | int[3]| Defensive stats indexed by difficulty (Normal/Nightmare/Hell)\n0x1c4   | 3    | difficulty_scaling      | byte[3]| Scaling factors indexed by difficulty level\n0x3c    | 4    | bonus_value             | int   | Bonus value added to offensive stat (in alternate structure)",
      "tags": ["MOD_UI", "UI_CHAR", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PARAM_1", "STRUCT_Other", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "SRC_char.cpp", "STRUCT_Control"]
