      "instructions": ["0x2ACE0|MOV|EAX, [0x6fbfd7fc]", "0x2ACE5|PUSH|EBX", "0x2ACE6|PUSH|EBP", "0x2ACE7|PUSH|ESI", "0x2ACE8|PUSH|EDI", "0x2ACE9|MOV|EDI, dword ptr [ESP + 0x14]", "0x2ACED|MOV|EBP, dword ptr [0x6fbae0e8]", "0x2ACF3|XOR|EBX, EBX", "0x2ACF5|MOV|ESI, dword ptr [EDI + 0xc]", "0x2ACF8|MOV|BX, word ptr [EDI + 0xc]", "0x2ACFC|LEA|ECX, [EAX + 0x80]", "0x2AD02|SHR|ESI, 0x10", "0x2AD05|CMP|EBX, ECX", "0x2AD07|MOV|ECX, dword ptr [0x6fbfd800]", "0x2AD0D|JL|0x6fafad5d"],
      "comment": "Handles mouse click events on the player statistics panel UI.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract click coordinates from pClickEvent structure (X in low word, Y in high word at offset +0x0C)\n2. Check if click is in Level Up button region (X: UIOffset+0x80 to +0xA0, Y: ScreenHeight-0x5C to -0x3C)\n   - If so, set g_dwStatsLevelUpButtonFlag=1, mark handled, call InitializeGameObjectProperties(4,...), cache widget\n3. Check if click is in left stat panel region (X: UIOffset to ScreenWidth/2, Y: UIOffset to ScreenHeight-0x31)\n   - Get player stat points via GetUnitStatById(unit, 4)\n   - If stat points available, iterate through 4 stat button regions in g_aStatButtonRegions (14-byte stride)\n   - For each button: check if click within button bounds (40x22 pixel region)\n   - If button clicked, set g_adwStatButtonActiveFlags entry, call ValidateScreenStateTransition, mark handled\n   - If no button hit but in panel, just mark handled and cache widget\n4. Otherwise call Ordinal_10005 (D2Win.GetScreenState)\n   - If screen state is 2, call ValidateCoordinateInBounds\n   - If bounds valid and click in left half of screen below UI, check GetScreenState\n   - If screen state is 6, call SendResourceUpdate\n   - Mark handled and cache widget\n5. If none of the above, mark click as not handled (pClickEvent[6] = 0)\n\nParameters:\npClickEvent - Pointer to click event structure containing:\n  +0x0C: Packed X/Y screen coordinates (low word=X, high word=Y)\n  +0x18: Click handled flag (1=handled, 0=not handled)\n  +0x1C: Secondary result flag (cleared to 0 on handled clicks)\n\nReturns:\nvoid (sets handled flag in pClickEvent structure)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Level Up button only visible/clickable when stat points available\n- Stat buttons (Str/Dex/Vit/Nrg) only process clicks if stat points > 0\n- Screen state 2 enables additional click handling with bounds validation\n- Screen state 6 triggers SendResourceUpdate for resource syncing\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x80 (128) - X offset from UI origin to Level Up button start\n0xA0 (160) - X offset from UI origin to Level Up button end\n0x5C (92) - Y offset below screen height for button top\n0x3C (60) - Y offset below screen height for button bottom\n0x31 (49) - Y margin from screen height for stat panel bottom\n0x1F6 (502) - Y offset for stat button top boundary calculation\n0x1E0 (480) - Y offset for stat button bottom boundary calculation\n0x28 (40) - Width of each stat button in pixels\n0x0E (14) - Stride size of stat button region table entries\n0x2F (47) - Y margin for bounds check in screen state 2\n\nStructure Layout:\nStat Button Region Entry (at g_aStatButtonRegions, 14 bytes each):\nOffset  Size  Field           Type  Description\n+0x00   4     nXOffset        int   X offset from UI origin\n+0x04   4     nYOffset        int   Y offset from screen height\n+0x08   4     dwActiveFlag    uint  Active/highlight flag (stored at g_adwStatButtonActiveFlags)\n+0x0C   2     wReserved       word  Reserved/padding\n\nOrdinal References:\nOrdinal_10005 - D2Win.GetScreenState (returns current screen/dialog state)",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PROP_NOCALLER", "STRUCT_Skill", "PARAM_1", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
