      "instructions": ["0x2AEC0|PUSH|ECX", "0x2AEC1|PUSH|EBX", "0x2AEC2|PUSH|EBP", "0x2AEC3|MOV|EBP, dword ptr [ESP + 0x10]", "0x2AEC7|PUSH|ESI", "0x2AEC8|PUSH|EDI", "0x2AEC9|XOR|EDI, EDI", "0x2AECB|MOV|ESI, dword ptr [EBP + 0xc]", "0x2AECE|MOV|DI, word ptr [EBP + 0xc]", "0x2AED2|PUSH|EBP", "0x2AED3|SHR|ESI, 0x10", "0x2AED6|CALL|0x6fb8f010", "0x2AEDB|MOV|EAX, [0x6fbfd7fc]", "0x2AEE0|MOV|EBX, dword ptr [0x6fbae0e8]", "0x2AEE6|MOV|dword ptr [0x6fbf4348], 0x0"],
      "comment": "Handles mouse clicks on the character stats panel UI.\n\nClassification: Callback/Handler - invoked when mouse is clicked in stat panel region\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract click coordinates from UIObject (X = low word, Y = high word of textWidth field at offset +0xC)\n2. Initialize screen state for the UI object\n3. Clear the level-up button flag (g_dwStatsLevelUpButtonFlag = 0)\n4. Check if click is on \"Level Up\" button region:\n   - X: g_dwUIXOffset + 0x80 to g_dwUIXOffset + 0xA0 (128-160 pixel range)\n   - Y: g_dwUIYOffset + screenHeight - 0x5C to screenHeight - 0x3C\n   - If yes: call ProcessUIStateChange(2, 1, 0) and return\n5. Check if click is outside valid stat panel region:\n   - X outside [g_dwUIXOffset, screenWidth/2 - 1]\n   - Y outside [g_dwUIYOffset, g_dwUIYOffset + screenHeight - 0x31]\n   - If outside: call Ordinal_10005 (clear state), check screen state 2 conditions, handle UI caching\n6. If click is within stat button area:\n   - Get player unit via GetGameContext()\n   - Get stat points available via GetUnitStatById(pUnit, 4) where 4 = STAT_STATPTS\n   - If stat points > 0, iterate through stat button regions (4 buttons at 0x6fbb23c4)\n7. For each stat button (14-byte stride):\n   - Calculate button Y bounds: base Y + g_dwUIYOffset + screenHeight - 0x1F6 to -0x1E0\n   - Calculate button X bounds: base X + g_dwUIXOffset to + 0x28 (40 pixels wide)\n   - If click matches button region:\n     - Get total stat points via GetTotalStatValue(pUnit, 4)\n     - Check if Shift key held (VK_SHIFT = 0x10)\n     - If Shift held: apply all stat points; otherwise apply 1\n     - Call LogEventData(0x3A, statId) for each point applied\n     - Break out of loop\n8. Call ClearTargetingState() to reset UI targeting\n9. Mark UIObject as processed (unknown_0 = 1, textWidth = 0)\n10. Insert UIObject into cache via InsertCacheNodeWithCookie()\n\nParameters:\n  pUIObject (UIObject *) - UI object containing click coordinates\n    - Offset +0xC (textWidth field of index 1): packed coordinates (X in low word, Y in high word)\n    - Offset +0x18 (unknown_0 field of index 3): processing flag\n    - Offset +0x1C (textWidth field of index 3): cleared on process\n\nReturns: void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Level up button click (region 128-160 x -92 to -60 from bottom): triggers ProcessUIStateChange\n  - Click outside panel: checks Ordinal_10005 return for state 2, may update cache\n  - Shift+click on stat button: applies ALL available stat points at once\n  - No stat points available: loops through buttons but takes no action\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x80, 0xA0 - Level up button X bounds relative to UI offset (128, 160)\n  0x5C, 0x3C - Level up button Y offsets from screen bottom (92, 60)\n  0x31 - Stats panel Y offset from screen bottom (49)\n  0x1F6, 0x1E0 - Stat button Y bounds offsets (502, 480 from top)\n  0x28 - Stat button width (40 pixels)\n  0x0E - Stat button descriptor stride (14 bytes)\n  0x10 - VK_SHIFT virtual key code\n  0x3A - Log event ID for stat point allocation (58)\n  4 - STAT_STATPTS stat ID for available stat points\n\nStat Button Array (g_aStatButtonRegions at 0x6fbb23c0):\n  Each entry is 14 bytes:\n    Offset -4: X offset from g_dwUIXOffset\n    Offset  0: Y offset base value\n    Offset +4: Active flag (cleared each iteration)\n    Offset +C: Stat ID (ushort) - which stat to increment\n\nOrdinal References:\n  Ordinal_10005 - D2Client.ClearMouseClickState - clears pending click state",
      "tags": ["PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PROP_NOCALLER", "STRUCT_Skill", "PARAM_1", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
