      "comment": "Initialize string length table for 15 predefined Unicode strings.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize pointer to start of string length table at 0x6fbb2156\n2. Loop through 15 entries (18 bytes each) until reaching end at 0x6fbb2264\n3. For each entry:\n   a. Load entry code/index from offset -0x2 (ushort at offset 0x00 of structure)\n   b. Call Ordinal_10004 dispatch function with code in CX register\n   c. Call Unicode::strlen on current string (implicit EDI register parameter)\n   d. Store returned string length at entry offset +0x2 (dwStringLength field)\n   e. Advance pointer by 0x12 (18 bytes) to next entry\n4. Return when all 15 entries processed\n\nParameters:\n  IMPLICIT lpwszCurrentString (wchar_t * in EDI) - Pointer to Unicode string being measured\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Function relies on Ordinal_10004 setting up the string pointer in EDI\n  - Each call to Ordinal_10004 must update EDI to point to the next string\n  - Total 15 iterations hardcoded by end address comparison\n\nStructure Layout:\n  Offset | Size | Field Name       | Type   | Description\n  -------+------+------------------+--------+------------------------------\n  0x00   | 2    | wCodeOrIndex     | ushort | Code passed to Ordinal_10004\n  0x02   | 4    | dwStringLength   | uint   | Computed string length stored here\n  0x06   | 4    | dwField1         | uint   | Unknown field\n  0x0A   | 4    | dwField2         | uint   | Unknown field\n  0x0E   | 4    | dwField3         | uint   | Unknown field\n  Total: 18 bytes (0x12)\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x6fbb2156 (start) - Beginning of StringLengthEntry array\n  0x6fbb2264 (end)   - End of array (15 entries * 18 bytes = 270 bytes)\n  0x12 (stride)      - Size of each StringLengthEntry structure\n  15                 - Number of string entries in table",
