      "comment": "Initializes the global chat input buffer by calling the Unicode default constructor on each element.\n\nClassification: Initialization function\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Set pointer ESI to start of g_abChatInputBuffer (0x6fbf4350)\n2. Set loop counter EDI to 0x101 (257 elements)\n3. Loop: Call Unicode::_default_constructor_closure_ with ESI as this pointer\n4. Advance ESI by 2 bytes (size of Unicode element)\n5. Decrement counter EDI\n6. Repeat until counter reaches 0\n7. Return\n\nParameters: None\n\nReturns: void\n\nMemory Model:\n- Operates on global buffer g_abChatInputBuffer at 0x6fbf4350\n- Buffer size: 257 elements × 2 bytes = 514 bytes (0x202)\n- Each element is a 2-byte Unicode character slot\n- Called from initialization table at 0x6fbae014\n\nCalled Functions:\n- Unicode::_default_constructor_closure_ (MSVCP60.dll ordinal) - Initializes each Unicode element\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Loop count 0x101 (257) provides space for 256 characters + null terminator\n- Buffer is used by RenderChatInputInterface, InitializeChatInputBuffer, and other chat functions",
