      "instructions": ["0x2B190|SUB|ESP, 0x108", "0x2B196|MOV|ECX, 0x32", "0x2B19B|XOR|EAX, EAX", "0x2B19D|PUSH|EBX", "0x2B19E|PUSH|EBP", "0x2B19F|PUSH|EDI", "0x2B1A0|LEA|EDI, [ESP + 0x4c]", "0x2B1A4|STOSD.REP|ES:EDI", "0x2B1A6|CALL|0x6fb9922c", "0x2B1AB|PUSH|EAX", "0x2B1AC|CALL|0x6fb99c96", "0x2B1B1|MOV|EBP, EAX", "0x2B1B3|XOR|EBX, EBX", "0x2B1B5|CMP|EBP, EBX", "0x2B1B7|JZ|0x6fafb391"],
      "comment": "Processes IME (Input Method Editor) composition messages for CJK text input.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize 200-byte ANSI buffer (szAnsiBuffer) to zeros using REP STOSD\n2. Call GetInitFlag() to retrieve HWND for IME context\n3. Obtain IME context via ImmGetContext(hWnd)\n4. If no IME context, skip to step 14\n5. Initialize 64-element wchar_t buffer (awszWideBuffer) using Unicode default constructor\n6. Check if GCS_RESULTSTR flag (0x800) is set in message lParam (offset 0xc):\n   a. Query composition string length via ImmGetCompositionStringA(GCS_RESULTSTR)\n   b. Clamp buffer length to 199 bytes max\n   c. Retrieve composition result string into szAnsiBuffer\n   d. Convert ANSI to Unicode via MultiByteToWideChar\n   e. Concatenate to global input buffer if combined length < 127 chars\n   f. Update g_dwStateFlags with string length\n   g. Clear g_dwImeSecondaryState and g_awImeCompositionBuffer\n7. Check if GCS_COMPSTR flag (0x8) is set in message lParam:\n   a. Verify IME is open via ImmGetOpenStatus\n   b. Query composition string length\n   c. If length > 0, re-clear both buffers\n   d. Clamp to 199 bytes and retrieve composition string\n   e. Convert to Unicode via MultiByteToWideChar\n   f. If converted length < 31, null-terminate at that position\n   g. If length < 32, copy to g_awImeCompositionBuffer via strcpy\n   h. Otherwise, truncate copy to 31 chars and call InitializeGameObjectProperties\n8. Call GetInitFlag() again to get HWND\n9. Release IME context via ImmReleaseContext\n10. Set pMsgContext[0x18] = 1 (message handled flag)\n11. Set pMsgContext[0x1c] = 0 (clear secondary status)\n12. Call InsertCacheNodeWithCookie to queue message context\n\nParameters:\n  pMsgContext - Pointer to message context structure containing:\n    +0x0c: LPARAM flags (GCS_RESULTSTR=0x800, GCS_COMPSTR=0x8)\n    +0x18: Handled flag (set to 1 on completion)\n    +0x1c: Secondary status (cleared to 0)\n  IMPLICIT ESI - Pointer to source Unicode buffer (g_dwImeInputBuffer at 0x6fbf4554)\n  IMPLICIT EDI - Pointer to destination Unicode buffer (g_dwInputStateFlags at 0x6fbf4350)\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If ImmGetContext returns NULL, skips all IME processing\n  - Buffer overflow protection: composition strings clamped to 199 bytes\n  - Unicode buffer limited to 32 wide characters (64 bytes)\n  - Global buffer concatenation limited to 127 characters total\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x800 - GCS_RESULTSTR: Final composition result string\n  0x8 - GCS_COMPSTR: Current composition string being edited\n  0xc7 - 199: Maximum ANSI buffer size minus null terminator\n  0x7f - 127: Maximum combined Unicode string length\n  0x1f - 31: Maximum composition buffer length minus null\n  0x20 - 32: Unicode buffer element count\n  0x32 - 50: Loop counter for clearing 200-byte buffer (50 * 4 = 200)\n\nGlobal Variables:\n  g_dwStateFlags (0x6fbf55f4) - Accumulated string length counter\n  g_dwImeSecondaryState (0x6fbf4554) - IME secondary state flag\n  g_awImeCompositionBuffer (0x6fbf55a8) - Unicode composition buffer\n  g_dwInputStateFlags (0x6fbf4350) - Input state tracking buffer\n  g_wImeCompositionTerminator (0x6fbf55e6) - Composition terminator word",
      "tags": ["PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_1", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
