      "comment": "Initializes IME (Input Method Editor) state to default values and registers a node in the cache system.\n\nClassification: Initialization function\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Set IME open status flag to 1 (enabled)\n2. Clear IME composition buffer to 0\n3. Clear IME secondary state to 0\n4. If language ID is English (9), set conversion mode to 4 (alphanumeric)\n5. Set node field at offset +0x18 to 1 (active flag)\n6. Set node field at offset +0x1c to 0 (clear state)\n7. Call InsertCacheNodeWithCookie to register node\n\nParameters:\n  dwNodeHandle - Handle/pointer to node structure to initialize and register\n                 Node structure fields:\n                   +0x18: uint - Active flag (set to 1)\n                   +0x1c: uint - State field (cleared to 0)\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nGlobals Modified:\n  g_dwImeOpenStatus (0x6fbf55e8) - Set to 1\n  g_awImeCompositionBuffer (0x6fbf55a8) - Cleared to 0\n  g_dwImeSecondaryState (0x6fbf4554) - Cleared to 0\n  g_dwImeConversionMode (0x6fbf55fc) - Set to 4 if English\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Language ID 9 (English) triggers alphanumeric conversion mode (0x4)\n  - Other languages retain existing conversion mode\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  9 - LANG_ENGLISH language ID\n  4 - Alphanumeric IME conversion mode\n  0x18, 0x1c - Node structure field offsets",
