      "comment": "Resets IME (Input Method Editor) state and inserts a cache node with a cookie value.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Clear IME composition buffer (first word set to 0)\n2. Clear IME secondary state flag\n3. Set chat cursor position to 0xFFFFFFFE (invalid/reset state)\n4. If language ID is 6 (Korean), clear IME open status flag\n5. Set cache node field at offset +0x18 to 1 (mark active/valid)\n6. Set cache node field at offset +0x1C to 0 (clear secondary field)\n7. Call InsertCacheNodeWithCookie to insert node into cache\n\nParameters:\n  dwCookieValue - Cookie/identifier value for the cache node; also used as\n                  base address for setting fields at offsets +0x18 and +0x1C\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Korean language (ID 6) receives additional IME open status reset\n  - Cursor position 0xFFFFFFFE indicates no active cursor/reset state\n\nStructure Layout (Cache Node accessed via dwCookieValue):\n  Offset  Size  Field           Type    Description\n  0x18    4     dwActiveFlag    uint    1 = active, 0 = inactive\n  0x1C    4     dwSecondary     uint    Secondary field, cleared on reset\n\nGlobal State Modified:\n  g_awImeCompositionBuffer (0x6fbf55a8) - First word cleared\n  g_dwImeSecondaryState (0x6fbf4554) - Cleared to 0\n  g_dwChatCursorPosition (0x6fbf55f8) - Set to 0xFFFFFFFE\n  g_dwImeOpenStatus (0x6fbf55e8) - Cleared if Korean language",
