      "instructions": ["0x2B460|SUB|ESP, 0x8", "0x2B463|PUSH|EBX", "0x2B464|PUSH|EBP", "0x2B465|PUSH|ESI", "0x2B466|MOV|ESI, dword ptr [ESP + 0x18]", "0x2B46A|PUSH|EDI", "0x2B46B|MOV|EDI, 0x1", "0x2B470|XOR|EBX, EBX", "0x2B472|PUSH|ESI", "0x2B473|MOV|dword ptr [ESI + 0x18], EDI", "0x2B476|MOV|dword ptr [ESI + 0x1c], EBX", "0x2B479|CALL|0x6fb99c36", "0x2B47E|CALL|0x6fb9922c", "0x2B483|PUSH|EAX", "0x2B484|CALL|0x6fb99c96"],
      "comment": "ProcessImeNotification - Handle IME notification messages for input method state changes\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize context flags: set pImeContext[6]=1 (processed), pImeContext[7]=0 (no error)\n2. Insert context into cache via InsertCacheNodeWithCookie\n3. Get active window handle via GetInitFlag\n4. Acquire IME context via ImmGetContext; exit early if NULL\n5. Switch on notification type (pImeContext[2] - 2):\n   - Case 2 (IMN_SETOPENSTATUS): Query keyboard layout, check if IME active, set conversion mode\n   - Case 3 (IMN_OPENCANDIDATE): Get candidate list count and size for Japanese (lang=9)\n   - Case 4 (IMN_CLOSECANDIDATE): Release candidate list allocation if present\n   - Case 5 (IMN_CHANGECANDIDATE): Update candidate list - allocate, retrieve, validate\n   - Case 6 (IMN_SETCONVERSIONMODE): Check conversion status for Chinese (7) or Korean (12)\n   - Case 8 (IMN_SETSENTENCEMODE): Check open status for Simplified Chinese (6) or Japanese (9)\n6. Release IME context via ImmReleaseContext before returning\n\nParameters:\n- pImeContext: uint * - Pointer to IME context structure (24+ bytes)\n  - [+0x08] (offset 2): Notification type code\n  - [+0x18] (offset 6): Processed flag (set to 1)\n  - [+0x1C] (offset 7): Error/result flag (set to 0)\n\nReturns: void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Early exit if ImmGetContext returns NULL\n- Language-specific handling based on g_dwLanguageId:\n  - 6 = Simplified Chinese (zh-CN)\n  - 7 = German/Chinese Traditional (zh-TW)\n  - 9 = Japanese (ja-JP)\n  - 12 = Korean (ko-KR)\n- Candidate list with dwStyle=2 and dwCount=1 is released (single-char completion)\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n- 0x02: IMN_SETOPENSTATUS notification\n- 0x03: IMN_OPENCANDIDATE notification\n- 0x04: IMN_CLOSECANDIDATE notification\n- 0x05: IMN_CHANGECANDIDATE notification\n- 0x06: IMN_SETCONVERSIONMODE notification\n- 0x08: IMN_SETSENTENCEMODE notification\n- 0xDD (221): Line number for release allocation (before alloc)\n- 0xDF (223): Line number for FogMemAlloc\n- 0xE4 (228): Line number for release on single-char\n- 0x13E (318): Line number for close candidate release\n\nGlobals Accessed:\n- g_dwLanguageId (0x6fbf55ec): Current IME language identifier\n- g_dwImeOpenStatus (0x6fbf55e8): IME open/active status byte\n- g_dwImeConversionMode (0x6fbf55fc): Current conversion mode (0-4)\n- g_pCandidateList (0x6fbf5600): Pointer to allocated CANDIDATELIST\n\nConversion Mode Values:\n- 0: IME closed/disabled\n- 1: Native input mode (Chinese/Korean)\n- 3: Simplified Chinese open\n- 4: Japanese IME open",
      "tags": ["SRC_chat.cpp", "UI_CHAT", "PROP_LARGE", "MOD_UI", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_1", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
