      "instructions": ["0x2B6D0|SUB|ESP, 0x8", "0x2B6D3|PUSH|ESI", "0x2B6D4|PUSH|EDI", "0x2B6D5|PUSH|0x4", "0x2B6D7|CALL|0x6fb9922c", "0x2B6DC|MOV|ECX, EAX", "0x2B6DE|MOV|EDX, 0x6fbb2468", "0x2B6E3|CALL|0x6fad25b0", "0x2B6E8|CALL|0x6fb99822", "0x2B6ED|CMP|EAX, 0x6", "0x2B6F0|MOV|[0x6fbf55ec], EAX", "0x2B6F5|JZ|0x6fafb70a", "0x2B6F7|CMP|EAX, 0x9", "0x2B6FA|JZ|0x6fafb70a", "0x2B6FC|CMP|EAX, 0x7"],
      "comment": "Initialize IME (Input Method Editor) for current language environment\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Send initial message table (4 entries) to main window\n2. Query active language configuration via Ordinal_10007\n3. Validate language is IME-supported (6=Japanese, 7=Korean, 9=Chinese Traditional, 0xC=Korean Extended)\n4. Initialize global IME state flags to 0\n5. For Chinese Traditional (language 9):\n   - Verify system language is 0x404 (Taiwan) or 0xC04 (Hong Kong)\n   - If not IME-capable layout, simulate IME toggle hotkey (0x70)\n   - Open IME context and set conversion mode to 4 (full-width)\n6. For other languages (6, 7, 0xC):\n   - Verify keyboard layout has IME capability\n   - For Japanese (0x411): Open IME, set mode 3, send 7-message table\n   - For Korean (0x412/0x812): Open IME, read/set conversion status, update mode flags\n7. Send setup message table (7 entries) for confirmed IME languages\n8. Release IME context handle\n\nParameters:\nIMPLICIT EBX: Window handle (retrieved via Ordinal_10027)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Updates global IME state flags\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Early return if language not IME-supported (6, 7, 9, 0xC)\n- Early return if IME context acquisition fails\n- Japanese mode sets g_dwImeConversionMode to 3 on success, 0 on failure\n- Korean mode sets g_dwImeConversionMode to 0 or 1 based on conversion status bit 0\n- Chinese mode sets g_dwImeConversionMode to 4\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x6 (6) - Japanese language ID\n0x7 (7) - Korean language ID (variant 1)\n0x9 (9) - Chinese Traditional language ID\n0xC (12) - Korean language ID (variant 2)\n0x404 (1028) - Taiwan Chinese LANGID\n0xC04 (3076) - Hong Kong Chinese LANGID\n0x411 (1041) - Japanese LANGID\n0x412 (1042) - Korean LANGID\n0x812 (2066) - Korean Extended LANGID\n0x70 (112) - IME toggle hotkey ID\n0x1 (1) - Conversion mode: Native input enabled\n0x3 (3) - IME mode: Hiragana (Japanese)\n0x4 (4) - IME mode: Full-width characters (Chinese)\n\nGlobal State Updates:\ng_dwActiveLanguageId - Set to Ordinal_10007 result (language configuration)\ng_dwImeInitialized - Set to 1 after successful IME initialization\ng_dwImeGlobalState - Reset to 0 at function start\ng_dwImeSecondaryState - Reset to 0 at function start\ng_dwImeOpenStatus - Set to 1 if IME opened successfully, 0 on failure\ng_dwImeConversionMode - Language-specific mode (0, 1, 3, or 4)\n\nMessage Tables:\ng_ImeInitMessageTable[4] - Initial 4-entry message sequence\ng_ImeSetupMessageTable[7] - Setup 7-entry message sequence for IME activation",
      "tags": ["PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PARAM_0", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control"]
    },
