      "comment": "Disables IME (Input Method Editor) and clears input state when transitioning UI modes\n\nAlgorithm:\n\n1. Send basic UI initialization messages (4 messages from g_MessageArrayBasicUiInit)\n2. If full UI mode enabled (g_bFullUiModeEnabled != 0):\n   a. Send full UI initialization messages (7 messages from g_MessageArrayFullUiInit)\n   b. Obtain IME context handle from window\n   c. If IME context valid:\n      - Disable IME open status\n      - For Japanese (0x07) or Korean (0x0C) language IDs:\n        * Get current conversion and sentence modes\n        * Clear conversion mode to 0 (disable all IME conversion)\n      - Release IME context handle\n   d. Clear input state flags (g_dwInputStateFlags = 0)\n   e. Clear IME composition state (g_dwImeCompositionState = 0)\n   f. If timer active (g_dwTimerActive != 0):\n      - Kill timer 600\n      - Clear timer active flag\n\nParameters:\n\nNone (void function)\n\nReturns:\n\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n\nLanguage ID 0x07 (Japanese) and 0x0C (Korean) require IME conversion mode reset\nTimer ID 600 is killed only when g_dwTimerActive flag is set\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n\n0x07 - Japanese language ID (LANG_JAPANESE)\n0x0C - Korean language ID (LANG_KOREAN)\n600 - Timer identifier for IME-related periodic events\n0 - ImmSetOpenStatus FALSE parameter (disable IME)\n0 - ImmSetConversionStatus mode parameter (clear all conversion modes)\n\nError Handling:\n\nNo error return - operates silently\nIf ImmGetContext returns NULL, IME operations skipped\nMessageArray processing errors handled by ProcessMessageArray callee",
      "tags": ["SRC_chat.cpp", "UI_CHAT", "MOD_UI", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PARAM_0"]
