      "instructions": ["0x2B9E0|SUB|ESP, 0x284", "0x2B9E6|PUSH|EBX", "0x2B9E7|PUSH|EBP", "0x2B9E8|PUSH|ESI", "0x2B9E9|PUSH|EDI", "0x2B9EA|MOV|ECX, 0xd", "0x2B9EF|CALL|0x6fb99a02", "0x2B9F4|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x28], EAX", "0x2B9F8|MOV|AL, [0x6fbf5604]", "0x2B9FD|TEST|AL, AL", "0x2B9FF|JZ|0x6fafbc4a", "0x2BA05|LEA|ESI, [ESP + 0x2c]", "0x2BA09|MOV|EDI, 0x14", "0x2BA0E|MOV|ECX, ESI", "0x2BA10|CALL|dword ptr [0x6fba5c30]"],
      "comment": "Renders the in-game chat input interface with multilingual text support and cursor animation\n\nAlgorithm:\n\n1. Check if chat interface is enabled via DAT_6fbf5604; if disabled, skip to frame counter update\n2. Initialize Unicode text buffers for input mode indicator (20 ushorts)\n3. Switch on language setting (DAT_6fbf55fc) to display appropriate input mode text:\n   - Case 0 (English): Convert \"Alphanumeric\" string to Unicode, position at screen height - 0x80\n   - Case 1 (Korean): Set hardcoded Unicode for Korean input mode (0xd55c)\n   - Case 2/3 (Japanese): Set hardcoded Unicode for Japanese input mode (0x65e5, 0x672c, 0x8a9e)\n   - Case 4 (Chinese): Set Chinese character (0x6f22), then render line history if available\n4. For Chinese mode with line history (DAT_6fbf5600 != NULL):\n   - Calculate visible line range from history buffer (fields at +0x8, +0x10, +0x14, +0x18)\n   - Limit display to 20 lines maximum (0x14)\n   - Loop through visible lines and render each with 15-pixel vertical spacing (0xf)\n   - Convert multibyte strings to wide characters using MultiByteToWideChar\n   - Format line numbers using \"%d: \" template from 0x6fbb2578\n   - Stop rendering when vertical offset exceeds 0x118 pixels\n5. Render main chat input box at coordinates (0x7f, screen_height - 0x67) with dimensions (width - 0xff, 0x2f)\n6. Check if game system is enabled; if so, call FUN_6fb5d370(5, 1, 0)\n7. Process input string if present (from implicit EDI register parameter):\n   - Convert to Unicode in 512-ushort buffer\n   - Word-wrap text using Ordinal_10199 with max width (screen_width - 0x109)\n   - Render each wrapped line with 15-pixel (0xf) vertical spacing at Y = screen_height - 0x58\n   - If final line and cursor display enabled (DAT_6fbf55e8), draw cursor at offset +0x83\n8. Update cursor blink animation using GetTickCount:\n   - Compare elapsed time against blink interval (stored in DAT_6fbb24f0 low word)\n   - Toggle cursor visibility state (DAT_6fbb24ec) between 0 and 1\n   - Use 100ms interval when cursor visible, 500ms when hidden\n9. Increment frame counter (DAT_6fbf55f8)\n\nParameters:\n\nIMPLICIT ESI (uint cbInputStringLength): Length of input string in bytes\nIMPLICIT EDI (char * lpszInputString): Pointer to current input string being typed\n\nReturns:\n\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n\n- If DAT_6fbf5604 is 0 (chat disabled), function only increments frame counter\n- Chinese mode (case 4) is the only language that renders historical chat lines\n- Line history buffer structure at DAT_6fbf5600 has fields:\n  +0x08: Total line count\n  +0x10: Start index for visible window\n  +0x14: End index for visible window  \n  +0x18: Array of int pointers to line strings\n- Word wrapping stops after 3 lines maximum (iStack_284 clamped to 2)\n- Cursor animation uses alternating intervals: 500ms hidden, 100ms visible\n- All screen coordinates are relative to global g_dwScreenWidth and g_dwScreenHeight\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n\n0x80 (128 decimal): Y-offset from bottom of screen for input mode indicator\n0x67 (103 decimal): Y-offset from bottom for chat input box top edge\n0xff (255 decimal): X-offset from right edge for chat input box width\n0x2f (47 decimal): Height of chat input box in pixels\n0xf (15 decimal): Vertical spacing between text lines\n0x58 (88 decimal): Y-offset from bottom for first line of input text\n0x83 (131 decimal): X-offset for cursor position\n0x14 (20 decimal): Maximum lines in input mode buffer and line history display\n0x170 (368 decimal): Y-offset from bottom for chat history rendering start\n0x118 (280 decimal): Maximum vertical offset for chat history rendering\n0x109 (265 decimal): X-offset from right edge for word wrap width calculation\n0x101 (257 decimal): Buffer size for wide character conversion (including null)\n100 (0x64): Cursor visible duration in milliseconds\n500 (0x1f4): Cursor hidden duration in milliseconds\n\nGlobal Data References:\n\nDAT_6fbf5604: Chat interface enable flag (byte)\nDAT_6fbf55fc: Language/region selector (0=English, 1=Korean, 2/3=Japanese, 4=Chinese)\nDAT_6fbf5600: Pointer to chat line history buffer structure (Chinese mode only)\nDAT_6fbf55f8: Frame counter incremented each call\nDAT_6fbf55e8: Cursor display enable flag\nDAT_6fbf5608: Last tick count for cursor blink timing (DWORD)\nDAT_6fbb24ec: Cursor visibility state (0=hidden, 1=visible)\nDAT_6fbb24f0: Cursor blink interval in milliseconds (low word)\ng_dwScreenWidth: Current screen width in pixels\ng_dwScreenHeight: Current screen height in pixels\ns_Alphanumeric_6fbb2580: \"Alphanumeric\" ASCII string for English input mode",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "STRUCT_Room2", "STRUCT_ItemData", "PARAM_0", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData", "STRUCT_StatList", "PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Path", "STRUCT_Skill", "PROP_LOOPHEAVY"]
