      "api_calls": ["SumCharacterValues", "RenderUnicodeTextWithLineHeight", "SumCharacterValues", "RenderUnicodeTextWithLineHeight", "ValidateStringId", "RenderUnicodeTextWithLineHeight"],
      "instructions": ["0x2BEC0|PUSH|ECX", "0x2BEC1|PUSH|EBX", "0x2BEC2|PUSH|EBP", "0x2BEC3|PUSH|ESI", "0x2BEC4|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0x2BEC6|PUSH|EDI", "0x2BEC7|MOV|ECX, 0x6fbf4554", "0x2BECC|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x10], EDX", "0x2BED0|XOR|EBX, EBX", "0x2BED2|MOV|EDI, EDX", "0x2BED4|CALL|dword ptr [0x6fba5c44]", "0x2BEDA|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0x2BEDC|JZ|0x6fafbf1c", "0x2BEDE|MOV|ECX, 0x6fbf4554", "0x2BEE3|CALL|0x6fb999fc"],
      "comment": "Render blinking cursor at specified position for IME text input.\n\nAlgorithm:\n\n1. Calculate initial text width by calling strlen on implicit text parameter (EDI)\n2. If text exists (length > 0):\n   a. Get text width from Ordinal_10121\n   b. Check if text extends beyond right screen boundary (g_dwScreenWidth - 0x109)\n   c. If overflow detected, reset X position to 0x83 and advance Y by 0xf (15 pixels)\n   d. Set render position with Ordinal_10117(nTextYPos, 4, 0)\n3. Calculate second text width measurement with Ordinal_10121\n4. Call strlen again to verify text length\n5. If text still exists:\n   a. Perform second boundary check with accumulated widths\n   b. If overflow, advance Y position by 0xf\n   c. Set render position again with Ordinal_10117\n6. If global blink state flag (DAT_6fbb24ec) is 1:\n   a. Call Ordinal_10004 to render cursor glyph\n   b. Call Ordinal_10117 to finalize rendering\n7. Get current system tick count with GetTickCount\n8. Compare elapsed time against blink interval (DAT_6fbb24f0 & 0xffff):\n   a. If interval expired:\n      - Update last tick timestamp (DAT_6fbf5608)\n      - Toggle blink state and update interval\n      - If currently visible (DAT_6fbb24ec == 1): Hide cursor, set interval to 100ms\n      - If currently hidden (DAT_6fbb24ec == 0): Show cursor, set interval to 500ms\n\nParameters:\n\nnTextXPos (ECX) - Horizontal pixel position for text/cursor rendering\nnTextYPos (EDX) - Vertical pixel position for text/cursor rendering\n\nIMPLICIT:\nlpszText (EDI) - Pointer to text string for width calculation (char *)\n\nReturns:\n\nvoid - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n\n- If text string is empty (length 0), skips boundary checking and positioning\n- Cursor blink uses asymmetric timing: 500ms visible, 100ms hidden\n- Screen boundary constant 0x109 (265 decimal) represents right margin offset\n- X position 0x83 (131 decimal) is left margin after line wrap\n- Y increment 0xf (15 decimal) is line height for wrapping\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n\n0x83 (131) - Left margin X coordinate after text wrap\n0xf (15) - Line height increment for Y position advancement\n0x109 (265) - Right screen boundary margin offset from g_dwScreenWidth\n100 - Cursor hidden interval in milliseconds\n500 - Cursor visible interval in milliseconds\n\nGlobal Variables:\n\nDAT_6fbb24ec - Cursor visibility state flag (1 = visible, 0 = hidden)\nDAT_6fbb24f0 - Packed blink timing value (low word = interval in ms)\nDAT_6fbf5608 - Last tick timestamp for blink timing comparison\ng_dwScreenWidth - Screen width in pixels for boundary checking",
      "tags": ["PARAM_2"]
