      "comment": "Check if UI element exceeds screen bounds and deactivate inventory panel.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Read UI element Y position from offset +0xc (high word via >> 16)\n2. Calculate visible screen threshold (g_dwScreenHeight - 0x31)\n3. If element Y position > threshold, call ProcessUIStateChange(5, 1, 0) to deactivate inventory\n4. Return without action if bounds check passes\n\nParameters:\npUIElement - Pointer to UI element structure with Y position at offset +0xc (high word)\n\nStructure Layout (offset +0xc):\nOffset  Size  Field       Type   Description\n0x0c    4     dwPosition  uint   Packed position (low word = X, high word = Y)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x31 (49) - Bottom screen margin reserved for UI chrome\n5 - UI element ID for inventory panel (nUIId parameter to ProcessUIStateChange)\n1 - Deactivate state (nUIState parameter)\n0x10 - Shift count to extract high word (Y coordinate)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value; conditionally triggers ProcessUIStateChange",
