      "instructions": ["0x2C020|PUSH|ESI", "0x2C021|MOV|ESI, dword ptr [ESP + 0x8]", "0x2C025|PUSH|EDI", "0x2C026|PUSH|ESI", "0x2C027|MOV|dword ptr [ESI + 0x18], 0x1", "0x2C02E|MOV|dword ptr [ESI + 0x1c], 0x0", "0x2C035|CALL|0x6fb99c36", "0x2C03A|TEST|dword ptr [ESI + 0xc], 0x40000000", "0x2C041|JNZ|0x6fafc14b", "0x2C047|MOV|ESI, dword ptr [ESI + 0x8]", "0x2C04A|SUB|ESI, 0x26", "0x2C04D|JZ|0x6fafc0d4", "0x2C053|SUB|ESI, 0x2", "0x2C056|JNZ|0x6fafc14b", "0x2C05C|MOV|EAX, [0x6fbf4594]"],
      "comment": "Navigates chat history buffer in response to Up/Down arrow key presses.\n\nClassification: Worker function - handles UI input for chat history navigation\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Set cache node fields: node+0x18 = 1 (active), node+0x1c = 0 (clear)\n2. Call InsertCacheNodeWithCookie to register the node\n3. Check flag at node+0xc for bit 0x40000000 - if set, skip navigation and exit\n4. Read keycode from node+0x8:\n   - 0x26 (VK_UP): Navigate to NEXT entry in history (older)\n   - 0x28 (VK_DOWN): Navigate to PREVIOUS entry in history (newer)\n5. For VK_UP (0x26):\n   a. Copy history entry at g_dwChatHistoryIndex to g_abChatInputBuffer (0x202 bytes = 257 wchar_t)\n   b. Update g_dwChatInputLength with strlen of copied string\n   c. Increment history index with wraparound: if >= 8, wrap to 0; if < 0, wrap to 7\n   d. Check boundary: if g_wChatHistoryCount < 7 AND (8 - newIndex) > count, restore original index\n6. For VK_DOWN (0x28):\n   a. Decrement history index with wraparound (same logic as increment)\n   b. Check boundary condition\n   c. Copy history entry to input buffer\n   d. Update input length\n7. Update g_dwChatHistoryIndex with final calculated index\n\nParameters:\n   pCacheNode - Pointer to cache node structure containing:\n      +0x08: uint dwKeycode - Virtual key code (0x26=Up, 0x28=Down)\n      +0x0C: uint dwFlags - Control flags, bit 0x40000000 disables navigation\n      +0x18: uint dwActive - Set to 1 on entry\n      +0x1C: uint dwReserved - Cleared to 0 on entry\n\nReturns: void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n   - Flag 0x40000000 at node+0xc bypasses all navigation (early exit)\n   - Keycodes other than 0x26 or 0x28 cause early exit with no navigation\n   - Circular buffer of 8 entries (indices 0-7) with wraparound\n   - Boundary check prevents navigation past valid history entries\n\nMagic Numbers:\n   0x26 - VK_UP (Windows virtual key code for Up arrow)\n   0x28 - VK_DOWN (Windows virtual key code for Down arrow)\n   0x40000000 - Control flag that disables history navigation\n   0x202 - History entry size in bytes (257 wchar_t = 514 bytes, 0x202 hex)\n   0x80 - DWORD count for REP MOVSD (128 DWORDs = 512 bytes)\n   8 - Maximum history entries in circular buffer\n\nGlobal Data:\n   g_dwChatHistoryIndex (0x6fbf4594) - Current position in circular history buffer\n   g_awszChatHistoryBuffer (0x6fbf4598) - Array of 8 wide string history entries\n   g_abChatInputBuffer (0x6fbf4350) - Current chat input buffer (copied to/from)\n   g_wChatHistoryCount (0x6fbf55f0) - Number of valid entries in history\n   g_dwChatInputLength (0x6fbf55f4) - Length of current input string",
