      "comment": "Parse Battle.net chat command prefix from input text.\n\nThis function scans the input string for known chat command prefixes (/, !, SHOUT, etc.)\nand extracts the command type and optional formatted output. It supports both exact-match\nand prefix-match modes based on a command table with match type flags.\n\nAlgorithm:\n\n1. Verify server connection is active via GetCurrentServerPort()\n2. Copy input text to local buffer (256 bytes max)\n3. Calculate input string length\n4. Iterate through command prefix table (10-byte entries):\n   a. Get prefix string pointer and match type flag at offset +4\n   b. Calculate prefix length\n   c. If match type == 3 (exact match):\n      - Check input length >= prefix length\n      - Compare strings case-insensitively (Ordinal_509)\n      - If exact match found, extract command type and return success\n   d. If match type != 3 (prefix match):\n      - Check input length > prefix length\n      - Compare prefix case-insensitively\n      - If match and next character is not null:\n        * Advance input pointer past prefix\n        * Check if format string exists at offset +6\n        * If format exists: Apply format template with <BattleNet>: prefix\n        * If no format: Advance input text pointer\n        * Extract command type from table\n        * Return success\n5. Return failure (0) if no command matches\n\nParameters:\n\n  pplpszInputText - Pointer to input text pointer (updates on match to skip prefix)\n  pbCommandType - Output byte receiving command type from table offset +0\n  pbOutputBuffer - Output buffer for formatted command text (16 byte max)\n\n  IMPLICIT ECX - pplpszInputText pointer-to-pointer\n  IMPLICIT EDX - pbCommandType output byte pointer\n  IMPLICIT [ESP+0x21c] - pbOutputBuffer on stack\n\nReturns:\n\n  1 (true) - Command prefix matched and parsed successfully\n  0 (false) - No matching prefix found or server port unavailable\n\nSpecial Cases:\n\n  - Returns 0 immediately if GetCurrentServerPort() returns 0\n  - Skips table entries where prefix match succeeds but remaining string is empty\n  - Format buffer limited to 16 bytes (0x10) including null terminator\n  - Input buffer limited to 256 bytes (0x100)\n  - Format buffer size 260 bytes (0x104) for expanded output\n\nCommand Table Structure (10 bytes per entry):\n\n  Offset +0x0 (4 bytes): char * - Pointer to prefix string\n  Offset +0x4 (2 bytes): short - Match type flag (3 = exact, other = prefix)\n  Offset +0x6 (4 bytes): int * - Format string pointer (0 = none)\n\nTable Traversal:\n\n  - Base address: g_ChatCommandPrefixTable (0x6fbb24f8)\n  - End address: 0x6fbb252a\n  - Entry size: 10 bytes (0xa)\n  - Iteration: ADD EDI, 0xa / INC EBX\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n\n  0x100 (256) - Input buffer size limit for strncpy\n  0x104 (260) - Format buffer size for expanded output\n  0x10 (16) - Maximum formatted output length check\n  0xa (10) - Command table entry size in bytes\n  0x4 (4) - Offset to match type flag within entry\n  0x6 (6) - Offset to format string pointer within entry\n  0x3 (3) - Match type value indicating exact match required\n  0x6fbb24f8 - Base address of command prefix table\n  0x6fbb252a - End address for table iteration bounds check\n  0x6fbb24fc - Base address of command type table (offset +0)\n  0x6fbb24fe - Base address of format string pointer table (offset +6)\n  0x7fffffff - Maximum string copy length for Ordinal_501\n\nFlag Bits:\n\n  Match Type Flag (offset +0x4, 2 bytes):\n    0x0003 - Exact match required (compare full input length)\n    Other  - Prefix match (partial match at start of string)\n\nString Functions:\n\n  Ordinal_506 - Calculate string length (like strlen)\n  Ordinal_509 - Case-insensitive string comparison (like strnicmp)\n  Ordinal_501 - String copy to buffer (like strcpy with length check)\n  Ordinal_504 - Format string with template (like sprintf)\n  _strncpy    - Copy fixed-length string to buffer\n\nNote:\n\nSSA variables (iVar3, iVar5, uVar4,