      "comment": "Parse and execute BattleNet chat command with case-insensitive prefix matching\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate length of lpszCommandName using manual strlen loop\n2. Calculate length of pbInputBuffer using manual strlen loop  \n3. Verify lpszCommandName length is less than or equal to pbInputBuffer length\n4. Perform case-insensitive character-by-character comparison of prefix\n5. Check character after prefix is space (0x20) or null terminator\n6. Tokenize remaining input using space delimiter (0x0020 from g_wSpaceDelimiter)\n7. Verify exactly one token remains after command name\n8. If valid, call GetGameInterface and execute function pointer at offset +0x14\n9. If invalid token count, format error message with correct usage template\n10. Copy error message to secondary buffer and call message display function\n\nParameters:\n  pbInputBuffer (byte *) - Input chat command buffer to parse\n  lpszCommandName (char *) - Expected command name for prefix matching\n\nIMPLICIT:\n  ECX - pbInputBuffer passed in ECX register (__fastcall)\n  EDX - lpszCommandName passed in EDX register (__fastcall)\n\nReturns:\n  1 (true) - Command matched prefix and was processed (success or error displayed)\n  0 (false) - Command prefix did not match lpszCommandName\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Returns 0 if lpszCommandName longer than pbInputBuffer\n  - Returns 0 if case-insensitive comparison fails at any character\n  - Returns 0 if character after prefix is not space or null\n  - Returns 1 even if error message displayed (command was recognized)\n  - Tokenization allows maximum 2 tokens total (command + 1 argument)\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x20 (32) - ASCII space character for delimiter and validation\n  0x0020 - Word-sized space delimiter loaded from g_wSpaceDelimiter at 0x6fbb25d8\n  0xFFFFFFFF - Initial value for strlen countdown loop\n  0x14 (20) - Offset to function pointer in GameInterface structure\n  0x40 (64) - Loop counter for 256-byte buffer copy (64 dwords = 256 bytes)\n  0x6fbb25f8 - Address of error message template \"<BattleNet>: Correct usage is: %s\"\n  0x4 - Message priority value for error display\n  0x3 - Message flags value for error display\n\nError Handling:\n  - If tokenization yields 0 tokens or >1 tokens, displays usage error\n  - Error message formatted with lpszCommandName as parameter\n  - Error display uses FUN_6fb9a261 (sprintf-like) and FUN_6fb58150 (message display)\n  - Function returns 1 after displaying error (command was recognized)",
