      "comment": "Conditionally initialize game mode when system is inactive.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call IsGameSystemEnabled() to check if game system is active\n2. If enabled (non-zero), exit immediately without initialization\n3. Call IsGameInMenuState() to check if game is in menu state (0x11)\n4. If in menu state (true), exit without initialization\n5. Tail-call InitializeGameMode(1) to initialize with mode parameter 1\n\nParameters:\n  None\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Initialization only occurs when BOTH conditions are met:\n  a) Game system is disabled (IsGameSystemEnabled returns 0)\n  b) Game is NOT in menu state (IsGameInMenuState returns false)\n- Uses tail-call optimization: JMP to InitializeGameMode instead of CALL+RET\n- Parameter 1 passed to InitializeGameMode via ECX register\n\nDecompiler Discrepancies:\n- extraout_var and CONCAT31 are artifacts from decompiler treating bool as 32-bit\n- Actual logic is simple: if (EAX != 0) return; applied twice\n- The tail-call shows as nested if in decompiler but is actually sequential checks\n\nClassification: Conditional Initializer - guards initialization behind state checks",
