      "comment": "Toggles the automap party member display state.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call GetAutomapShowParty to retrieve current party display state (returns in EAX)\n2. Invert the boolean value using NEG/SBB/INC idiom: (value == 0) ? 1 : 0\n3. Tail-call to SetAutomapPartyMode with inverted value in ECX\n\nParameters:\n  None\n\nReturns:\n  void - Function tail-calls SetAutomapPartyMode which returns the new mode value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Uses optimized x86 boolean inversion: NEG+SBB+INC converts non-zero to 0, and 0 to 1\n- Tail-call optimization: JMP instead of CALL+RET reduces stack overhead\n- Decompiler shows extraout_EAX - this is the return value from GetAutomapShowParty\n\nAssembly Idiom Explanation:\n  MOV ECX,EAX    ; Copy GetAutomapShowParty result\n  NEG ECX        ; Sets CF=1 if ECX was non-zero, CF=0 if zero\n  SBB ECX,ECX    ; ECX = 0 - CF = (0 or -1)\n  INC ECX        ; ECX = (1 or 0) - inverted boolean\n\nRelated Functions:\n  GetAutomapShowParty (0x6faf5a10) - Getter for party display state\n  SetAutomapPartyMode (0x6faf5a20) - Setter for party display state",
