      "comment": "Toggles the automap left-side panel state between enabled and disabled.\n\nClassification: Thunk/Wrapper - combines getter and setter to implement toggle logic.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call GetAutomapLeftState() to retrieve current state from g_dwAutomapLeftState\n2. Compute inverted value: if state == 0 then 1, else 0\n   - Uses NEG/SBB/INC sequence for branchless boolean inversion\n3. Tail-call SetAutomapLeftConfig() with inverted value\n   - Persists new value to registry via STORM.DLL SGSetValue\n   - Updates g_dwAutomapLeftState, g_dwAutomapLeftPrevious, g_dwAutomapLeftTarget\n\nParameters: None\n\nReturns: void (SetAutomapLeftConfig return value discarded via tail call)\n\nCaller Analysis:\n- No direct xrefs found - likely called via function pointer or hotkey handler table\n- Part of automap UI control system with GetAutomapLeftState/SetAutomapLeftConfig\n\nAssembly Implementation:\n- Uses tail-call optimization (JMP instead of CALL+RET)\n- Branchless boolean NOT: NEG ECX; SBB ECX,ECX; INC ECX\n  - If EAX=0: NEG 0=0 (CF=0), SBB 0,0,0=0, INC 0=1\n  - If EAX!=0: NEG n=-n (CF=1), SBB 0,0,1=-1, INC -1=0\n\nRelated Functions:\n- GetAutomapLeftState (0x6faf59d0): Returns current state\n- SetAutomapLeftConfig (0x6faf59e0): Sets state and persists to registry",
