      "comment": "Handles left mouse click on skill slot UI element.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if game system is enabled - if enabled, return early (no action during loading/transition)\n2. Check if game is in menu state - if in menu, return early (no skill selection in menus)\n3. Get skill UI resource (ID=3) to determine UI context\n4. If UI resource exists, trigger OnSkillButtonClicked(0) for button click behavior\n5. If UI resource not found, trigger SelectSkillSlot(0) for direct slot selection\n\nParameters: None (void)\n\nReturns: void\n\nSSA Temporaries (decompiler-generated, not renameable):\n- uVar2: uint return from IsGameSystemEnabled() (EAX)\n- bVar1: bool return from IsGameInMenuState() (EAX)\n- extraout_var: undefined3 artifact from bool widening (ignore)\n- dVar3: dword return from GetUIResourceByIdWithValidation() (EAX)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Early exit if game system enabled (loading/transition state)\n- Early exit if game in menu state\n- UI resource ID 3 determines click vs select behavior\n\nNotes:\n- No direct callers (likely registered as UI callback handler)\n- Both tail calls pass 0 as the skill/slot index (left slot)\n- GetUIResourceByIdWithValidation checks if skill button panel is visible",
