      "comment": "Handles input action for skill slot 10 (hotkey or button press).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if game system is enabled via IsGameSystemEnabled()\n2. If enabled, exit early (no skill input during system-enabled state)\n3. Check if game is in menu state via IsGameInMenuState()\n4. If in menu state, exit early (no skill input during menus)\n5. Get global system state via GetGlobalSystemState() (returns state in EAX)\n6. If system state is 0/invalid, exit early\n7. Get UI resource ID 3 via GetUIResourceByIdWithValidation(3)\n8. If UI resource exists, tail-call OnSkillButtonClicked(10)\n9. If UI resource doesn't exist, tail-call SelectSkillSlot(10)\n\nParameters:\n  None (callback function)\n\nReturns:\n  void (tail-calls to handler functions)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Function uses tail-calls (JMP) to OnSkillButtonClicked/SelectSkillSlot\n  - Skill slot index is hardcoded as 10 (0x0A)\n  - UI resource ID 3 determines which handler receives the action\n  - No callers found - likely registered as UI callback or input handler\n\nControl Flow:\n  Entry -> IsGameSystemEnabled -> (if enabled) -> Exit\n                               -> IsGameInMenuState -> (if in menu) -> Exit\n                               -> GetGlobalSystemState -> (if state == 0) -> Exit\n                               -> GetUIResourceByIdWithValidation(3)\n                               -> (if resource) -> OnSkillButtonClicked(10)\n                               -> (if no resource) -> SelectSkillSlot(10)",
