      "comment": "Toggle inventory panel UI with state validation and initialization.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call IsAnyDialogActive() to check if dialogs block panel toggle\n2. If dialog active, return immediately (no-op)\n3. Call IsItemListAvailable() to check if item list blocks panel\n4. If item list available, return immediately (panel already showing items)\n5. Call GetUIResourceByIdWithValidation(9) to get game state UI resource\n6. If game state UI exists (non-zero), call ProcessUIStateTransitions(1) and return\n7. Otherwise call ProcessUIStatesByResourceBuffer(0, 1) to process states\n8. If state processing returns 0 (no changes), call InitializePanelMode(1, 0) to init panel\n\nParameters:\n(none) - __stdcall with no parameters\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value, modifies global UI state\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Early exit if any dialog active (loading, character select, server, talk, etc.)\n- Early exit if item list already initialized/visible\n- Two initialization paths: state transition vs full panel mode init\n\nControl Flow:\n- Entry -> Dialog check -> Item check -> UI resource check\n- If UI resource exists: transition path (ProcessUIStateTransitions)\n- If no UI resource: init path (ProcessUIStatesByResourceBuffer -> InitializePanelMode)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 9 (0x9): Game state UI resource index\n- 1: Active state / initialization flag for panel mode\n- 0: Inactive state / normal panel mode\n\nRelated Functions:\n- IsAnyDialogActive: Blocks toggle if dialogs showing\n- IsItemListAvailable: Blocks toggle if item list visible\n- GetUIResourceByIdWithValidation: Gets UI resource state by index\n- ProcessUIStateTransitions: Handles state transitions for all UI elements\n- ProcessUIStatesByResourceBuffer: Processes UI states by buffer values\n- InitializePanelMode: Initializes panel configuration",
