      "comment": "Navigate skill slot selection if game state allows interaction.\n\nClassification: Thunk/Wrapper - Guards ProcessSkillSlotNavigation with state checks.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if game system is enabled via IsGameSystemEnabled()\n2. If enabled, exit early (no navigation during system activity)\n3. Check if game is in menu state via IsGameInMenuState()\n4. If in menu, exit early (no navigation during menus)\n5. If both checks pass, tail-call ProcessSkillSlotNavigation(-1) to cycle slots\n\nParameters:\n  None\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nCallees:\n  IsGameSystemEnabled (0x6fadb800) - Returns non-zero if game system active\n  IsGameInMenuState (0x6fb62890) - Returns true if in menu state (0x11)\n  ProcessSkillSlotNavigation (0x6fb53d30) - Cycles skill slots with -1 direction\n\nControl Flow:\n  Entry -> IsGameSystemEnabled -> [if != 0] -> RET (early exit)\n                               -> [if == 0] -> IsGameInMenuState\n  IsGameInMenuState -> [if != 0] -> RET (early exit)\n                    -> [if == 0] -> JMP ProcessSkillSlotNavigation (tail call)\n\nDecompiler Discrepancies:\n  - bVar1, uVar2, extraout_var are phantom variables from decompiler\n  - Actual code uses EAX for both return value checks\n  - CONCAT31 artifact is false - assembly shows simple TEST EAX,EAX\n  - No local variables exist - all logic is in register and tail call\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0xffffffff (-1) - Direction parameter for ProcessSkillSlotNavigation (cycle mode)",
