      "comment": "Processes idle state transition for player unit when stationary.\n\nClassification: Callback/Handler - invoked by game loop or event system\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Clear global DWORD value to 0 (SetGlobalDwordValue(0))\n2. Retrieve game context pointer (GetGameContext)\n3. If no game context, exit early\n4. Check always-run setting (GetAlwaysRunSetting)\n5. If always-run is enabled (EAX != 0), exit early\n6. Check unit type at offset +0x00, must be 0 (player type)\n7. Check unit state at offset +0x0C, must be 3 (idle state)\n8. If all conditions met:\n   a. Call ClearUnitStateAndProcessTransition(pUnit, 2) - transition type 2\n   b. Call QuerySystemInfoAndIncrementCounters with counter ID 0x54\n\nParameters: None (void)\n\nReturns: void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Early exit if game context is NULL\n- Early exit if always-run setting is enabled\n- Early exit if unit type is not 0 (non-player unit)\n- Early exit if unit state is not 3 (not in idle state)\n\nStructure Layout (Unit at ESI):\nOffset  Size  Field         Type  Description\n0x00    4     dwUnitType    uint  Unit type identifier (0 = player)\n0x0C    4     dwUnitState   uint  Current unit state (3 = idle)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0: SetGlobalDwordValue parameter (clear value)\n- 2: Transition type for ClearUnitStateAndProcessTransition\n- 3: Idle state identifier in unit state field\n- 0x54: Counter ID for QuerySystemInfoAndIncrementCounters",
