      "comment": "Load and validate keyboard command bindings from registry or fallback file.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Attempt to open registry key with FUN_6fafdf60(0x80000000, 3) - HKEY_CURRENT_USER\n2. If registry accessible, initialize local keybinding table (114 entries, 10 bytes each)\n3. Read registry value with Ordinal_10110(0x476, &nReadSize, 0) - expects 1142 bytes\n4. Call Ordinal_10109() to process registry data into local buffer\n5. Validate registry data: check size (0x476 = 1142 bytes) and entry count (0x25 = 37 entries)\n6. Verify all command IDs 0-56 (0x39) are present in table (loop checks for duplicates)\n7. Verify no duplicate key codes across 114 (0x72) entries (nested loop comparison)\n8. If validation passes, initialize global keybinding table at g_KeyBindingTable+4 with 0xFFFF\n9. Copy validated keybindings to g_KeyBindingTable (1141 bytes = 0x11d dwords)\n10. Call InitializeMouseButtonCallbacks() to register mouse event handlers\n11. If registry fails or validation fails, build path \"%s\\\\CMD\\\\%s\\\\default.key\"\n12. Load default.key file from disk using FUN_6fb994dc() \n13. Validate file header: magic 0x5357 (SW), count 0x25 (37), size 0x47a (1146)\n14. Copy file data to g_DefaultKeyBindingTable (1141 bytes)\n15. Report result with Ordinal_10043(0x51c=success or 0x521=failure, 0)\n16. Initialize global table with 0xFFFF then copy from default table\n17. Call InitializeMouseButtonCallbacks() and FUN_6fafe090()\n18. Call FUN_6faff390(1, 0) for final initialization\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Function always completes, falling back to default keybindings if registry unavailable\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If registry read fails (nReturnCode == -1), falls through to file load path\n- If registry data size != 1142 bytes, validation fails and uses file fallback\n- If registry entry count != 37, validation fails and uses file fallback\n- If duplicate command IDs found in range 0-56, validation fails\n- If duplicate key codes found across 114 entries (excluding -1/0xFFFF), validation fails\n- File header validation requires exact matches: 0x5357, 0x0025, 0x047a\n- Global table initialization uses 0xFFFF as \"unbound\" sentinel value\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x80000000 - HKEY_CURRENT_USER registry root key\n0x476 (1142) - Expected size of keybinding data in bytes\n0x25 (37) - Expected count of keybinding entries in header\n0x39 (57) - Maximum command ID to validate (range 0-56)\n0x72 (114) - Total keybinding table entries to process\n0x11d (285) - Number of dwords to copy (1140 bytes / 4)\n0xFFFF - Sentinel value for unbound keybinding entries\n0x5357 - File magic number \"SW\" (little-endian)\n0x47a (1146) - Expected file data size in bytes\n0x50e (1294) - Ordinal code parameter for file load\n0x51c (1308) - Ordinal code for successful key load\n0x521 (1313) - Ordinal code for failed key load validation\n\nKeyBinding Structure Layout:\nOffset  Size  Field Name    Type    Description\n------  ----  ----------    ----    -----------\n0x00    4     dwCommandId   uint    Game command/action identifier (0-56)\n0x04    2     wKeyCode      ushort  Keyboard scan code or virtual key\n0x06    2     wModifiers    ushort  Modifier keys (Shift, Ctrl, Alt)\n0x08    2     wFlags        ushort  Binding flags and state",
