      "comment": "Initialize mouse button callback function pointers by scanning key binding table.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Clear all mouse button callback globals (buttons 3, 4, 5 down/lift)\n2. Initialize pointer to key binding table at 0x6fbf5628\n3. Iterate through key binding entries (10-byte stride) until end at 0x6fbf5a9c\n4. For each entry, check if button type ID > 0xDF and key code < 0x39\n5. Calculate button type offset by subtracting 0x100 from button type ID\n6. Use offset (0-4) as switch index to determine which button callbacks to set\n7. Each case validates button availability then assigns callbacks from lookup table\n8. Set appropriate global function pointer pair based on button type offset\n9. Continue iteration until end of key binding table\n\nParameters:\n  None (implicit: Key binding table at 0x6fbf5628)\n\nIMPLICIT:\n  Key binding table at 0x6fbf5628 with 10-byte stride entries\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Button type IDs <= 0xDF are skipped (not mouse buttons 3/4/5)\n  - Key codes >= 0x39 (57 decimal) are skipped (out of valid range)\n  - Switch covers offsets 0-4 mapping to buttons: 0=Mouse3, 1=Mouse4, 2=Mouse5, 3=Unknown, 4=Unknown\n  - Jump tables at 0x6fafdef4, 0x6fafdf08, 0x6fafdf1c, 0x6fafdf30, 0x6fafdf44 contain validation routines\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0xDF (223): Minimum button type ID threshold for mouse buttons 3/4/5\n  0x100 (256): Base offset subtracted from button type ID to get switch index\n  0x39 (57): Maximum valid key code value\n  0x6fbf5628: Start address of key binding table\n  0x6fbf5a9c: End address of key binding table (1140 bytes = 114 entries)\n  0x6fbb2ad8: Base address of callback function pointer lookup table\n  10 (0xA): Stride between key binding entries\n\nKey Binding Entry Structure:\n  Offset | Size | Field Name      | Type   | Description\n  -------|------|-----------------|--------|----------------------------------\n  0x00   | 4    | dwKeyCode       | uint   | Key code for binding\n  0x0