      "comment": "Save current keyboard bindings to registry and optionally to default.key file.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Open registry key for keybinding data using FUN_6fafdf60(0x40000000, 2) - write access\n2. If registry open fails (returns -1), exit without saving\n3. Initialize local binding buffer (285 dwords = 1140 bytes) to zero\n4. Set binding count header to 0x25 (37 entries)\n5. Initialize all 114 key entry slots to 0xFFFF (unbound sentinel)\n6. Copy current keybindings from g_KeyBindingTable to local buffer (285 dwords)\n7. Write 0x476 bytes (1142) to registry via Ordinal_10111\n8. Close registry handle via Ordinal_10109\n9. Get base path string via Ordinal_10116 into szFilePath\n10. Calculate length of \"default.key\" filename string\n11. Find end of szFilePath string (strlen)\n12. Append \"default.key\" to szFilePath (memcpy in dword+byte chunks)\n13. Open/create file handle via Ordinal_10107(0, 0, 2, 0x80, 0)\n14. If file open fails (returns -1), skip file write\n15. Set file header: wFileMagic=0x5357 (\"SW\"), wEntryCount=0x25, wDataSize=0x47a\n16. Write 6-byte header to file via Ordinal_10111\n17. Write 0x474 bytes (1140) binding data via Ordinal_10111\n18. Close file handle via Ordinal_10109\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Function completes silently, errors handled by early returns\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x40000000 - HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE registry root (passed to FUN_6fafdf60)\n0x11d (285) - Number of dwords in keybinding table (1140 bytes / 4)\n0x25 (37) - Expected number of keybinding entries in header\n0x72 (114) - Total keybinding slots (114 entries x 10 bytes stride)\n0xFFFF - Sentinel value for unbound/empty keybinding slot\n0x476 (1142) - Total bytes to write to registry (6 header + 1136 data)\n0x5357 - File magic \"SW\" (little-endian) identifying key binding file\n0x47a (1146) - File data size indicator in header\n0x474 (1140) - Actual binding data bytes written to file\n0x80 - File creation flags for Ordinal_10107\n2 - Write mode flag for FUN_6fafdf60 and Ordinal_10107\n\nRelated Functions:\n- LoadKeyboardBindings() - Caller that loads bindings before this saves them\n- FUN_6fafdf60() - Opens registry key with specified access mode\n- Ordinal_10107 - Creates/opens file handle for keybinding file\n- Ordinal_10109 - Closes registry/file handle\n- Ordinal_10111 - Writes data buffer to registry/file\n- Ordinal_10116 - Gets game path string for building file path",
