      "instructions": ["0x2E1E0|SUB|ESP, 0x588", "0x2E1E6|LEA|EAX, [ESP]", "0x2E1EA|PUSH|ESI", "0x2E1EB|PUSH|EDI", "0x2E1EC|PUSH|0x0", "0x2E1EE|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0x2E1F0|PUSH|EAX", "0x2E1F1|CALL|0x6fb9980a", "0x2E1F6|TEST|ESI, ESI", "0x2E1F8|JZ|0x6fafe2b2", "0x2E1FE|PUSH|EBP", "0x2E1FF|MOV|EDX, 0xdc", "0x2E204|LEA|ECX, [ESP + 0x14]", "0x2E208|CALL|0x6fb99a8c", "0x2E20D|MOV|EDI, 0x6fbb2ed8"],
      "comment": "Loads keyboard binding configuration from file or data file archive.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get current locale string for localization\n2. If nLoadFromFile is non-zero (load from file):\n   a. Get install path and append \"default.key\" filename\n   b. Open the file with CreateFileWrapper (GENERIC_READ, OPEN_EXISTING)\n   c. Read 0x47a (1146) bytes into local buffer\n   d. If read successful and size matches, allocate pool memory and copy data\n   e. Jump to validation step\n3. If nLoadFromFile is zero or file read failed:\n   a. Format path using \"%s\\CMD\\%s\\default.key\" pattern\n   b. Call GetDataFilePath() and ReadAndProcessFileData() to load from archive\n4. Validate loaded key data:\n   a. Check magic signature: 0x5357 (\"WS\") at offset 0\n   b. Check version marker: 0x25 (37) at offset 2\n   c. Check data size: 0x47a (1146) at offset 4\n   d. If valid, copy 0x11d (285) dwords to g_DefaultKeyBindingTable\n5. Release pool allocation if data was loaded\n6. Initialize g_aKeyBindingTable: set 0xFFFF at start of each 10-byte entry\n   Loop from 0x6fbf562c to 0x6fbf5aa0 (stride 10, ~114 entries)\n7. Copy g_DefaultKeyBindingTable to g_KeyBindingTable (0x11d dwords = 285 entries)\n8. Call InitializeMouseButtonCallbacks() to set up mouse input\n\nParameters:\n  nLoadFromFile (ECX): int - Non-zero to load from \"default.key\" file in install dir,\n                             zero to load from data file archive\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - File not found or wrong size: falls back to loading from data archive\n  - Invalid magic/version/size: skips copy to default table, still initializes tables\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x47a (1146) - Expected key binding file size\n  0x5357 - Magic signature \"WS\" (little-endian)\n  0x25 (37) - Version marker\n  0x11d (285) - Number of dword entries to copy\n  0x11e (286) - Dwords in buffer copy (285 + 1 word)\n  10 (0x0a) - Stride of key binding table entries\n  0xFFFF - Default/unbound key value\n\nGlobal Data:\n  g_DefaultKeyBindingTable (0x6fbb2660): Template key bindings loaded from file\n  g_KeyBindingTable (0x6fbf5628): Active key bindings used at runtime\n  g_aKeyBindingTable (0x6fbf562c): Extended binding table with 10-byte stride\n  szDefaultKeyFilename (0x6fbb2ed8): \"default.key\"\n  g_szDefaultKeyPathFmt (0x6fbb2eb4): \"%s\\CMD\\%s\\default.key\"\n  g_szCmdTblSourceFile (0x6fbb2df0): Source file for allocation tracking",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "SRC_CmdTbl.cpp", "STRUCT_Skill", "PARAM_1", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
