      "api_count": 0,
      "api_calls": [],
      "instructions": ["0x2E370|PUSH|ESI", "0x2E371|XOR|ESI, ESI", "0x2E373|MOV|EAX, 0x6fbf562e", "0x2E378|CMP|ECX, dword ptr [EAX + -0x6]", "0x2E37B|JNZ|0x6fafe381", "0x2E37D|CMP|EDX, dword ptr [EAX]", "0x2E37F|JZ|0x6fafe392", "0x2E381|ADD|EAX, 0xa", "0x2E384|INC|ESI", "0x2E385|CMP|EAX, 0x6fbf5aa2", "0x2E38A|JL|0x6fafe378", "0x2E38C|OR|AX, 0xffff", "0x2E390|POP|ESI", "0x2E391|RET|", "0x2E392|LEA|EAX, [ESI + ESI*0x4]"],
      "comment": "Lookup virtual key code for a command binding in the keybinding table.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize table pointer to g_adKeyBindingTypes (offset +6 in entry)\n2. Initialize entry index counter to 0\n3. Loop: Compare nCommandId with entry's command ID (at pointer - 6)\n4. If command ID matches, compare nBindingType with entry's type (at pointer)\n5. If both match, return keycode from g_awKeyBindingKeyCodes[index * 5]\n6. Advance pointer by 10 bytes (entry stride) and increment index\n7. Continue until pointer exceeds 0x6fbf5aa1 (end of table)\n8. Return 0xFFFF if no matching binding found\n\nParameters:\nnCommandId - Game command identifier to look up (e.g., 0x22 for keyboard config)\nnBindingType - Binding type/slot index (primary=1, secondary=2, etc.)\n\nReturns:\nushort - Virtual key code if binding found, 0xFFFF if unbound\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x6fbf562e - Start of keybinding types field in table\n0x6fbf5aa1 - End boundary of keybinding table (114 entries * 10 bytes)\n0xFFFF - Sentinel value indicating unbound/not found\n\nKeyBinding Entry Structure (10 bytes stride):\nOffset | Size | Field        | Type   | Description\n-------|------|--------------|--------|---------------------------\n+0x00  | 4    | dwCommandId  | uint   | Game command identifier\n+0x04  | 4    | dwBindingType| uint   | Binding slot (1=primary)\n+0x08  | 2    | wKeyCode     | ushort | Virtual key code (VK_*)",
      "tags": ["PARAM_2", "PROP_LEAF", "PROP_SMALL"]
