      "comment": "Validates whether a virtual key code can be used for key binding assignment.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract lower 16 bits of key code (mask with 0xFFFF)\n2. Check if key code is less than 0x2B:\n   a. If exactly 0x2A (VK_PRINT): Return TRUE (valid)\n   b. If in range 0x01-0x29, use switch table at PTR_caseD_5_6fafe410:\n      - Valid (return 1): VK_TAB(0x09), VK_CLEAR(0x0C), VK_RETURN(0x0D), VK_SHIFT(0x10),\n        VK_CONTROL(0x11), VK_MENU(0x12), VK_PAUSE(0x13), VK_CAPITAL(0x14),\n        VK_SPACE(0x20), VK_PRIOR(0x21), VK_NEXT(0x22), VK_END(0x23), VK_HOME(0x24)\n      - Ignored (fall through): VK_BACK(0x08), VK_CANCEL(0x03), VK_HELP(0x2F)\n      - Invalid (return 0): Default cases\n3. Check if key code >= 0x2B using switch table at 0x6fafe440:\n   a. Invalid (return 0): VK_ADD(0x2B), VK_LWIN(0x5B), VK_RWIN(0x5C), VK_APPS(0x5D), VK_NUMLOCK(0x90)\n   b. Valid (return 1): VK_SEPARATOR(0x2C) through VK_DIVIDE(0x2F), VK_NUMPAD0-9(0x60-0x69),\n      VK_MULTIPLY(0x6A), VK_ADD(0x6B), VK_SEPARATOR(0x6C), VK_SUBTRACT(0x6D), VK_DECIMAL(0x6E),\n      VK_DIVIDE(0x6F), VK_F1-F24(0x70-0x87), VK_SCROLL(0x91), VK_OEM keys(0xBA-0xC0, 0xDB-0xDE),\n      Extended keys(0x100-0x104)\n4. For unhandled key codes, check virtual key type flags:\n   a. Call FUN_6fb9aafb with mask 0x103 - check if VK has valid modifier/extended flags\n   b. If non-zero, return TRUE (valid)\n5. Call FUN_6fb9ab29 with mask 0x04 - check if VK is control character\n   a. If non-zero, return TRUE (valid)\n   b. Otherwise return FALSE (invalid)\n\nParameters:\n  wKeyCode - Virtual key code to validate (lower 16 bits used)\n\nReturns:\n  1 - Key code is valid and can be assigned to a key binding\n  0 - Key code is invalid or reserved (Windows keys, NumLock, etc.)\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x2A - VK_PRINT (Print Screen)\n  0x2B - VK_ADD / VK_EXECUTE (reserved, invalid)\n  0x5B - VK_LWIN (Left Windows key, reserved)\n  0x5C - VK_RWIN (Right Windows key, reserved)\n  0x5D - VK_APPS (Applications key, reserved)\n  0x90 - VK_NUMLOCK (reserved, invalid)\n  0x103 - Modifier/extended key flag mask\n  0x04 - Control character flag mask",
      "tags": ["PARAM_0"]
    },
