      "comment": "Copies key binding table to backup location and reinitializes mouse button callbacks.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Save ESI and EDI registers to stack\n2. Set copy count ECX = 0x11d (285 DWORDs = 1140 bytes)\n3. Set source ESI = 0x6fbf5628 (g_KeyBindingTable)\n4. Set destination EDI = 0x6fbf5aa0 (g_KeyBindingTableBackup)\n5. Execute REP MOVSD to copy table in DWORD increments\n6. Restore ESI and EDI registers\n7. Jump to InitializeMouseButtonCallbacks to rescan and setup callbacks\n\nParameters:\n  None\n\nReturns:\n  void (does not return directly, tail-calls InitializeMouseButtonCallbacks)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Uses REP MOVSD for efficient block copy (4 bytes per iteration)\n- Tail-call optimization to InitializeMouseButtonCallbacks via JMP\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x11d (285): Number of DWORDs to copy (1140 bytes total)\n  0x6fbf5628: Source address (g_KeyBindingTable)\n  0x6fbf5aa0: Destination address (g_KeyBindingTableBackup)\n\nRelated Functions:\n- InitializeMouseButtonCallbacks() - Called via tail-jump after copy\n- LoadKeyboardBindings() - References both source and destination tables",
