      "comment": "Clears key bindings matching the specified type pair by setting their key code to 0xFFFF.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize pointer to g_adKeyBindingTypes array (offset +6 to point at second int field)\n2. Loop through all 114 entries in the key binding table (10 bytes each)\n3. For each entry, compare first int field (at offset -6) with nKeyType1\n4. If match, compare second int field (at offset 0) with nKeyType2\n5. If both match, set the key code field (at offset -2) to 0xFFFF (unbound)\n6. Advance pointer by 10 bytes to next entry\n7. Continue until pointer reaches 0x6fbf5aa2 (end of table)\n\nParameters:\n- nKeyType1 (int, ECX): First type identifier to match against entry offset +0\n- nKeyType2 (int, EDX): Second type identifier to match against entry offset +6\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nStructure Layout (KeyBindingEntry, 10 bytes):\nOffset  Size  Field         Type    Description\n------  ----  -----------   ------  -----------\n0x00    4     nType1        int     First type identifier\n0x04    2     wKeyCode      ushort  Virtual key code (0xFFFF = unbound)\n0x06    4     nType2        int     Second type identifier\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n- 0xFFFF (65535): Unbound key code value\n- 0x0A (10): Size of KeyBindingEntry structure in bytes\n- 0x6fbf562e: Start of g_adKeyBindingTypes array (offset +6)\n- 0x6fbf5aa2: End of key binding table",
