      "instructions": ["0x2EE50|PUSH|ESI", "0x2EE51|PUSH|EDI", "0x2EE52|MOV|EDI, EDX", "0x2EE54|XOR|ESI, ESI", "0x2EE56|MOV|EAX, 0x6fbf562e", "0x2EE5B|CMP|ECX, dword ptr [EAX + -0x6]", "0x2EE5E|JNZ|0x6fafee64", "0x2EE60|CMP|EDI, dword ptr [EAX]", "0x2EE62|JZ|0x6fafeea2", "0x2EE64|ADD|EAX, 0xa", "0x2EE67|INC|ESI", "0x2EE68|CMP|EAX, 0x6fbf5aa2", "0x2EE6D|JL|0x6fafee5b", "0x2EE6F|MOV|EAX, 0xffff", "0x2EE74|AND|EAX, 0xffff"],
      "comment": "Returns a string ID for a key binding based on command and type.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize search index to 0, pointer to g_adKeyBindingTypes (0x6fbf562e)\n2. Loop through key binding table entries (10 bytes each, up to 0x6fbf5aa2):\n   a. Compare nBindingCommand with entry's command (at pointer - 6)\n   b. Compare nBindingType with entry's type (at pointer)\n   c. If both match, retrieve string ID from g_aKeyBindingTable[index * 5]\n   d. If no match, advance pointer by 10 bytes, increment index\n3. If table exhausted without match, use value 0xFFFF\n4. Mask string ID to 16 bits, subtract 8 to get switch index\n5. If switch index > 0xFC (252), fall through to LookupKeyBindingStringId\n6. Use jump table (switchdataD_6faff024) indexed by byte table (switchdataD_6faff0a4)\n7. Each case loads a specific string resource ID (0xF15-0xF4A) into ECX\n8. Call Ordinal_10004 (D2Lang.GetStringFromIndex) with resource ID\n9. Return string pointer from Ordinal_10004\n\nParameters:\n- nBindingCommand (ECX): Key binding command identifier to look up\n- nBindingType (EDX): Key binding type (primary/secondary)\n\nReturns:\n- ushort: String resource ID for the key binding, or result from fallback lookup\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n- 0x6fbf562e: Start of g_adKeyBindingTypes array (type field of entries)\n- 0x6fbf5aa2: End boundary of key binding table search\n- 0x0A (10): Stride of key binding table entries\n- 0xFFFF: Sentinel value indicating no binding found\n- 0xFC (252): Maximum valid switch table index\n- 0xF15-0xF4A: String resource IDs for various key names\n\nRelated Functions:\n- LookupKeyBindingStringId (0x6fafe760): Fallback for complex string lookups\n- Ordinal_10004: D2Lang.GetStringFromIndex - retrieves localized string",
