      "comment": "Searches key binding table for a matching key code and executes the associated action handler.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize loop index to 0 and pointer to g_KeyBindingTable (0x6fbf5628)\n2. Read key code from input event at offset +0x8\n3. For each binding entry (10-byte stride):\n   a. Compare binding key code (ushort at offset +4) with input key code\n   b. Read command ID (dword at offset 0)\n   c. Skip if command ID is 0xFFFF (invalid)\n   d. Skip if command ID >= 0x39 (57, out of valid action range)\n   e. Skip if command ID > 0xDF (223, secondary range check)\n   f. Look up action handler at g_apRemoteSessionActionTable[commandId*0xC]\n   g. Skip if handler is NULL\n4. Exit if binding pointer exceeds 0x6fbf5a9b (end of table)\n5. If g_dwRemoteSessionMode == 2, verify action allowed via g_adwKeyActionValidationTable\n6. Validate handler with IsBadCodePtr to prevent crash\n7. If validation fails, call assertion (Ordinal_10023) with source location\n8. Call the action handler function via indirect call\n9. Set input event processed flag at offset +0x18 to 1\n10. Clear input event consumed flag at offset +0x1c to 0\n11. Call Ordinal_511 to finalize input event processing\n\nParameters:\n  nInputEvent - Pointer to input event structure containing key code at +0x8\n\nReturns:\n  void - Returns after executing bound action or if no binding found\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x6fbf5628 - g_KeyBindingTable base address\n  0x6fbf5a9b - End of key binding table\n  0x6fbb2adc - g_apRemoteSessionActionTable base (action handler pointers)\n  0x6fbb2ae0 - g_adwKeyActionValidationTable (remote session validation)\n  0x0A (10)  - Key binding entry stride in bytes\n  0x0C (12)  - Action table entry stride in bytes\n  0xFFFF     - Invalid command ID marker\n  0x39 (57)  - Maximum command ID for primary range\n  0xDF (223) - Maximum command ID for secondary range\n  0x7F6 (2038) - Source line number for assertion",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Inventory", "PROP_NOCALLER", "SRC_CmdTbl.cpp", "PARAM_1", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
