      "comment": "Manages panel message state transitions based on session mode (active/inactive).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Store session mode value in global state variable g_dwRemoteSessionMode\n2. If session mode disabled (nSessionMode == 0):\n   - Check if previously enabled: if DAT_6fbf5f24 == 1 (was enabled)\n   - Mark messages as disabled: set DAT_6fbf5f24 = 0\n   - Get main window handle from Ordinal_10027 (D2Win.GetHwnd)\n   - Process 4 message array entries from main message table (DAT_6fbb2d88)\n   - If caller requested message display (fShowMessages != 0) and disabled mode not set:\n     - Process 2 message entries from secondary message table (DAT_6fbb2db8)\n     - Mark secondary messages as enabled: set DAT_6fbf5f28 = 1\n3. If session mode enabled (nSessionMode != 0):\n   - Check if previously disabled: if DAT_6fbf5f24 == 0 (was disabled)\n   - Mark messages as enabled: set DAT_6fbf5f24 = 1\n   - If caller requested message display (fShowMessages != 0) and secondary messages active:\n     - Process 2 message entries from secondary message table (DAT_6fbb2db8)\n     - Mark secondary messages as disabled: set DAT_6fbf5f28 = 0\n   - Process 4 message array entries from main message table (DAT_6fbb2d88)\n\nParameters:\n- nSessionMode: Session mode flag (ECX: 0 = disable messages, non-zero = enable messages)\n- fShowMessages: Boolean flag (EDX: non-zero = show secondary messages if applicable)\n\nReturns:\n- void: No return value; modifies global state variables DAT_6fbf5f24 and DAT_6fbf5f28\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Early exit if session state unchanged (if param already matches current state)\n- DAT_6fbf5f28 tracks secondary message panel visibility independent of session mode\n- DAT_6fbf5f24 tracks whether messages are currently enabled (0=enabled, 1=disabled)\n\nRelated Functions:\n- ProcessMessageArray() - Processes array of main message entries\n- ProcessMessageEntryArray() - Processes array of secondary message entries\n- Ordinal_10027 (D2Win.GetHwnd) - Retrieves main window handle for message dispatch",
