      "comment": "Searches item list for entry matching target coordinates.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate input: check if nItemBase is not null\n2. Initialize: nItemIndex = 0, nOffsetAccum = 0, iVar3 = 0\n3. Extract target X coordinate from upper 16 bits of nCoordStruct offset 0xc\n4. Extract target Y coordinate from low 16 bits of nCoordStruct offset 0xc\n5. Load item count from nItemBase offset 0x50\n6. If item count <= 0, return -1 (no items to search)\n7. Loop through item list starting at nItemBase + 0x158 (stride 0x110)\n8. Check item active flag: pnCurrentItem[7] must equal 1\n9. Check Y bounds: nItemBase[0x2c] + 0xf <= Y < nItemBase[0x34] - 0xf + nItemBase[0x2c]\n10. Calculate item coordinate: nItemCoord = *pnCurrentItem + nItemBase[0x30] + nOffsetAccum\n11. Check X bounds: nItemCoord - 0xb <= X < nItemCoord + 0x4\n12. If all checks pass, return nItemIndex (found match)\n13. Add current item size to accumulator: nOffsetAccum += *pnCurrentItem\n14. Increment item counter and advance pointer: nItemIndex++, move to next 0x110-byte entry\n15. Continue looping until all items checked or match found\n16. Return -1 if no matching item found\n\nParameters:\nnItemBase - Pointer to dialog/item manager structure containing item array\nnCoordStruct - Pointer to quest/dialog structure with coordinates at offset 0xc\n\nReturns:\nint - Zero-based item index if match found, -1 (0xFFFFFFFF) if no match\n\nSpecial Cases:\nNote: Function uses 1 SSA temporary variable (uVar1) optimized away by decompiler during analysis.",
