      "comment": "Process dialog input event and perform associated callbacks.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load global dialog state pointer from g_pCurrentDialog\n2. Extract event code (low 16 bits) and event data (high 16 bits) from dialog parameter at offset 0xc\n3. Call validation functions to check if event is valid (FUN_6fb5d340 with 0x15, FUN_6fb38320 with event code and data)\n4. If validation fails, initialize dialog failure state at offsets 0x18=1 and 0x1c=0\n5. Call ordinal cleanup function (Ordinal_511) with dialog parameter\n6. Verify global state pointer is valid, otherwise abort with fatal error (Ordinal_10023 + FUN_6fb9a10f)\n7. If global state[0x10] is already set, skip processing\n8. Check global state[0x4] flag to determine callback path:\n   - If flag==1 (timer-based processing): Get current tick count, check timeout condition against global state[0]\n   - Call FUN_6faff510 to calculate index\n   - If index valid and callback exists at calculated offset, invoke callback at global state[index*0x44+0x5c]\n   - If callback returns non-zero, return immediately\n   - Reset state[0x4] flag\n   - If flag!=1 (list-based processing): Iterate linked list at global state[0x2c2]\n   - For each node, invoke callback at [*node].field_0x10\n   - Continue until callback returns 1 or list exhausted\n\nParameters:\n- pDialog (dword): Pointer to dialog structure containing event data at offset 0xc\n  IMPLICIT: g_pCurrentDialog - Global dialog state structure pointer\n\nReturns:\n- void: No return value, modifies dialog and global state\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Handles null global state pointer (fatal error path)\n- Validates callback pointers before invocation to prevent null dereference\n- Supports both timer-based (state[4]==1) and list-based callback mechanisms\n- Clears processing flag (state[0x10]) to prevent re-entry\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x15: Validation code passed to FUN_6fb5d340\n- 0xc: Offset in dialog structure containing event code/data\n- 0x18, 0x1c: Dialog failure state offsets\n- 0x4: Global state flag controlling callback mode (timer vs list)\n- 0x50: Timeout offset in global state\n- 0x12, 0x14: Index bounds checking offsets in global state\n- 0x11: Index multiplier offset in global state\n- 0x44: Stride for index*0x44 calculation\n- 0x5c: Callback function pointer offset within stride\n- 0x2c2: Linked list pointer offset in global state\n- 0x10: Processing flag offset in global state\n- 0x48, 0x50: State management offsets for index validation\n\nRelated Functions:\n- FUN_6faff510: Calculates current event index based on timing\n- FUN_6fb5d340: Primary event validation function\n- FUN_6fb38320: Secondary event validation with code/data check\n- Ordinal_511: Dialog cleanup/finalization routine\n- GetTickCount: Windows API for timing\n- Ordinal_10023: Fatal error reporting\n- FUN_6fb9a10f: Process termination",
