      "comment": "Updates automap viewport and camera position based on scroll window mode and input coordinates.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Verify automap config exists (g_pCurrentDialog); assert and exit if null\n2. Get current tick count via GetTickCount()\n3. If time since last update < 80ms (0x50), mark event as complete and return early\n4. Iterate through UI element list at config[0x2c2] checking element callbacks\n5. If any element callback returns 1, mark event handled and exit\n6. Fetch previous view mode from config[0x11], set update flag at config[4]=1\n7. Call SearchItemsByCoordinates() to find items at click location\n8. Store new view mode at config[0x11] and config[0x12]\n9. If view mode unchanged or returned -1, validate coordinate bounds:\n   - Extract X coordinate as lower 16-bits from pEventData[3]\n   - Extract Y coordinate as upper 16-bits (>> 0x10) from pEventData[3]\n   - Check X within [config[0xb] - 4, config[0xd] + config[0xb] + 4]\n   - Check Y within [config[0xc] - 4, config[0xe] + config[0xc] + 4]\n10. If coordinates out of bounds:\n    a. Try allocate resource 0x15 (render buffer) via FUN_6fb5d340()\n    b. If success, validate allocation via FUN_6fb38320(dwX, dwY)\n    c. Check callback at config[0x19] (on-render-complete); if null, try config[0x18]\n    (pre-render)\n    d. If config[0x18] null, assert and fatal error; otherwise invoke config[0x18]()\n    e. Invoke config[0x19]() post-render callback\n11. Allocate resource 6 (scroll layer) via FUN_6fb5d340(6)\n12. Call FUN_6fb1ccd0() with scroll mode and coordinates for layer rendering\n13. Allocate resource 7 (composite layer) via FUN_6fb5d340(7)\n14. Call FUN_6fb1cd50() with scroll mode and coordinates for final composite\n15. Mark event complete: pEventData[6] = 1, pEventData[7] = 0\n16. Call Ordinal_511() (D2Win.D2WIN_DrawGame) to finalize frame\n\nParameters:\npEventData - Pointer to event data structure containing:\n  +0xc - Mouse coordinates packed as (uint): lower 16-bits = X, upper 16-bits = Y\n  +0x18 - Event completion flag (set to 1 on return)\n  +0x1c - Event error code (set to 0 on return)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Always returns after setting event completion flags\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Early return at step 3 throttles updates to 80ms intervals to prevent UI thrashing\n- View mode -1 indicates search found nothing; treated as unchanged\n- Resource allocation failures (steps 10a, 11, 13) suppress further rendering\n- All rendering callbacks at config[0x18] and config[0x19] must handle null pointers\n- Function uses 1 stack-allocated temporary variable optimized away by decompiler\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x50 - 80ms interval threshold for update throttling (milliseconds)\n0x2c2 - Offset to UI element linked list in config (offset 0xB08 in disasm)\n0x4, 0xd, 0xe - Config offsets for viewport dimension validation\n0x11, 0x12 - Config offsets for current/previous view mode storage\n0x15, 6, 7 - Resource allocation IDs for render buffers, scroll/composite layers\n0x18, 0x19 - Config offsets for pre/post-render callback pointers\n0x6 (index 1), 0x7 (index 1) - Array indices for layer configuration",
