      "comment": "Inserts a cache node into the dialog system and conditionally triggers a callback.\n\nWorker function that manages dialog cache node registration. Checks if the dialog\nsystem is ready before insertion, saves previous state, then conditionally invokes\nthe dialog callback if the previous state was empty.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load g_pCurrentDialog global pointer\n2. Check if dialog offset +0x20 is zero (dialog not ready)\n3. If not ready, call GetUIResourceByIdWithValidation(5) - if found, exit early\n4. Save previous state from dialog offset +0x1c (used to determine callback trigger)\n5. Initialize cache node: set offset +0x18 to 1 (active flag), offset +0x1c to 0\n6. Call InsertCacheNodeWithCookie to register the node\n7. If previous state was 0 (first insertion):\n   a. Assert dialog pointer is valid\n   b. Check dialog type at offset +0x54 > 4 (callback-capable type)\n   c. If callback pointer at offset +0x60 exists, invoke it\n   d. Call UpdateTimeoutValue to refresh timeout\n\nParameters:\n  pCacheNode (uint *) - Pointer to cache node structure to insert\n    Offset +0x18: Active/ready flag (set to 1)\n    Offset +0x1c: State field (cleared to 0)\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Early exit if dialog offset +0x20 is 0 and UI resource 5 is available\n  - Asserts if g_pCurrentDialog is NULL when callback would be triggered\n  - Only triggers callback on first insertion (when previous +0x1c was 0)\n\nDialog Structure Layout (partial):\n  Offset  Size  Field         Type       Description\n  +0x1c   4     dwPrevState   uint       Previous state value\n  +0x20   4     dwReadyFlag   uint       Dialog ready indicator\n  +0x54   4     dwDialogType  uint       Dialog type (>4 = callback capable)\n  +0x60   4     pfnCallback   code *     Optional callback function pointer\n\nSSA Temporaries:\n  iVar1: int - Cached g_pCurrentDialog pointer and previous state value\n  dVar2: dword - Return value from GetUIResourceByIdWithValidation\n\nSource: C:\\Projects\\Diablo2\\Source\\D2Client\\UI\\dialog.cpp line 0x1c0 (448)",
