      "comment": "Processes mouse wheel scroll input to navigate dialog slots.\n\nHandler/Callback function registered in dialog vtable (no direct callers).\nConverts wheel delta into slot navigation direction and cycles through active slots.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Cache g_pCurrentDialog pointer for later use\n2. Extract wheel delta from pInputEvent[2] high word (signed 16-bit)\n3. If delta is zero, skip to step 11 (mark handled and return)\n4. Calculate scroll units: delta / 0x78 (120 decimal - standard wheel notch)\n   Uses signed division with sign extension for negative values\n5. If scroll units is zero (small movement), skip to step 11\n6. Assert g_pCurrentDialog != NULL, exit with -1 on failure\n7. Iterate dialog handler list at [dialog+0xB08]:\n   - For each handler node, call vtable[2] method (OnWheelScroll)\n   - If handler returns 1, event was consumed - return immediately\n8. If scroll units > 0 (scroll up/backward):\n   - Require at least 2 slots ([dialog+0x4C] >= 2)\n   - Start from current slot [dialog+0x44], decrement with wraparound\n   - Loop until finding active slot (non-zero at slot*0x110+0x174)\n9. If scroll units <= 0 (scroll down/forward):\n   - Same slot count requirement\n   - Increment slot index with wraparound\n   - Loop until finding active slot\n10. Call InitializeGameObjectProperties(1, 0, 0.0, 0.0, 0) and update [dialog+0x44]\n11. Mark event handled: pInputEvent[6] = 1, pInputEvent[7] = 0\n12. Call InsertCacheNodeWithCookie to queue event for processing\n\nParameters:\n  pInputEvent (dword*) - Pointer to input event structure\n    [+0x08]: Wheel delta in high word (signed, 120 units per notch)\n    [+0x18]: Handled flag (set to 1)\n    [+0x1C]: Result code (set to 0)\n\nReturns:\n  void - Event marked as handled via pInputEvent fields\n\nDialog Structure Offsets:\n  +0x44: Current slot index (int)\n  +0x4C: Total slot count (int)\n  +0x50: Max slot index (int)\n  +0x174: Slot array base (stride 0x110 bytes per slot)\n  +0xB08: Handler list head pointer\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Zero wheel delta: Event still marked handled but no navigation\n  - Single slot dialog (count < 2): No navigation possible\n  - All slots inactive: Loop terminates when active slot found (may infinite loop if none)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x78 (120): Windows standard wheel delta per notch\n  0x110 (272): Slot entry stride in bytes\n  0x174 (372): Offset to first slot in dialog structure\n  0xB08 (2824): Offset to handler list in dialog structure\n  0x1F7 (503): Assert line number in dialog.cpp",
