      "comment": "Inserts a cache node and processes dialog timeout callback.\n\nWorker function that sets cache node state flags, inserts the node into\nthe cache system, and conditionally invokes the dialog timeout callback\nwhen the dialog has been active past its grace period.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Cache g_pCurrentDialog pointer locally\n2. If dialog exists, get current tick count\n3. If within 80ms (0x50) grace period after dialog start time, perform\n   early return path (steps 4-5) to avoid timeout callback\n4. Set cache node active flag (offset +0x18) to 1\n5. Clear cache node secondary flag (offset +0x1c) to 0\n6. Call InsertCacheNodeWithCookie to insert node\n7. If dialog is NULL, assert failure and exit application\n8. If dialog state (offset +0x54) > 4 and callback (offset +0x60) exists,\n   invoke the timeout callback\n9. Call UpdateTimeoutValue to refresh timeout tracking\n\nParameters:\n  pCacheNode - uint * - Pointer to cache node structure\n      +0x18: Active flag (set to 1)\n      +0x1c: Secondary flag (cleared to 0)\n\nReturns: void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Early return: If current time < dialog start time + 80ms, inserts node\n    and returns without processing timeout callback\n  - NULL dialog assertion: Fails with code 0x1c0 in dialog.cpp if\n    g_pCurrentDialog is NULL after cache node insertion\n  - Callback guard: Only invokes callback if dialog state > 4 AND callback\n    pointer is non-NULL\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x50 (80) - Grace period in milliseconds before timeout callback fires\n  0x1c0 (448) - Assert line number in dialog.cpp\n  0x54 - Dialog state field offset (index 0x15 = 21, *4 = 0x54)\n  0x60 - Dialog timeout callback pointer offset (index 0x18 = 24, *4 = 0x60)\n\nFile: C:\\Projects\\Diablo2\\Source\\D2Client\\UI\\dialog.cpp",
