      "comment": "Initialize dialog event handlers by dispatching to handler callback chain.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Set enabled flag (offset +0x18) to 1, set mode field (offset +0x1c) to 0\n2. Call Ordinal_511(pDialog) for dialog initialization\n3. Load current dialog from global g_pCurrentDialog\n4. Verify dialog is non-NULL, terminate if NULL\n5. Retrieve event handler list head from dialog+0xb08\n6. Loop through handler nodes via ppnNode[1] (next pointer)\n7. For each node: check if ppnNode and **ppnNode are non-NULL\n8. Call handler callback at vftable(**ppnNode)+0x24 with pDialog parameter\n9. If callback returns 1 (event handled), exit and return\n10. Move to next handler node\n11. When handler chain exhausted: check if slot cycling available (count > 1)\n12. Cycle to previous slot: read current from dialog+0x44, decrement\n13. Validate slot in range: wrap if negative, reset if past maximum\n14. Loop until active slot found (slot active flag at dialog+0x174+(slot*0x110))\n15. Call FUN_6fb8d210(1,0,0.0,0.0,0) to update graphics\n16. Store selected slot back to dialog+0x44\n\nParameters:\npDialog - DialogStruct pointer to dialog structure; fields accessed:\n  +0x18 dwEnabled - enable flag (set to 1)\n  +0x1c nMode - mode field (set to 0)  \n  +0x44 nSlotIdx - current slot index (read/write)\n  +0x4c nSlotCount - number of available slots\n  +0x50 nMinSlot - minimum slot index\n  +0xb08 ppHandlers - head of event handler linked list\n\nReturns:\nvoid; modifies dialog state and triggers graphics update if cycling slots",
