      "comment": "Process dialog UI slots sequentially, finding the next active slot with valid handler.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize input dialog flags at pDialog+0x18=1 and pDialog+0x1c=0\n2. Call Ordinal_511 (validation) with pDialog parameter\n3. Retrieve g_pCurrentDialog global, exit if null (error handler at 0x6faffbe6)\n4. Get slot list head from pDialog+0xb08 into pSlotNode\n5. Loop through slot linked list: check each node for non-null vtable, call virtual method at offset 0x28\n6. If virtual method returns 1, exit function (slot handled successfully)\n7. Otherwise advance to next slot via pSlotNode+0x4\n8. If no slots matched or list empty, check if slot count at pDialog+0x4c > 1\n9. If count valid, get current index from pDialog+0x44, increment and wrap (max is pDialog+0x50)\n10. Calculate offset as (nSlotIndex * 0x110) + 0x174, loop until finding active slot\n11. Call FUN_6fb8d210 with parameters (1, 0, 0.0, 0.0, 0) to trigger UI update\n12. Store updated slot index back to pDialog+0x44\n\nParameters:\npDialog (DialogStruct *): Dialog object containing slot list and management fields\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Handles null dialog pointer with exception handler\n- Implements circular slot index wraparound\n- Stride between slots is fixed at 0x110 bytes\n- Note: One phantom variable (iVar1) optimized by decompiler",
