      "comment": "Initialize dialog inventory display and validate active slot selection.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Set inventory display flag at offset 0x18 to 1\n2. Clear inventory counter at offset 0x1c to 0\n3. Call Ordinal_511(pDialog) to validate dialog\n4. Retrieve current dialog pointer from g_pCurrentDialog global\n5. If g_pCurrentDialog is NULL, log error and terminate application\n6. Load slot linked list from dialog offset 0xb08\n7. Iterate through each slot in the linked list:\n   - Check if current slot node is NULL, if so exit iteration\n   - Verify slot object pointer is valid (non-NULL at offset 0)\n   - Call slot's virtual method at offset 0x1c with pDialog parameter\n   - If method returns 1, exit function immediately\n   - Advance to next slot (offset 0x4 contains next pointer)\n8. If no slots exist in list, proceed to validation logic\n9. Check if slot count exceeds 1 (at dialog offset 0x4c)\n10. Locate current slot index from dialog offset 0x44\n11. Decrement index to find previous active slot\n12. Validate index is within valid range using min value at offset 0x50\n13. If index below minimum, wrap to maximum slot index minus 1\n14. Check if slot at calculated offset is active (non-zero value)\n15. Repeat steps 11-14 until active slot found\n16. Call FUN_6fb8d210(1, 0, 0.0, 0.0, 0) to update rendering\n17. Store validated slot index back to dialog offset 0x44\n\nParameters:\npDialog - Pointer to Dialog structure containing inventory/slot management data\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Modifies dialog state directly via structure pointer side effects",
