      "comment": "Initializes dialog control list and activates first available control.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize dialog structure fields at offset 0x18 to 1 and offset 0x1c to 0\n2. Call Ordinal_511 with dialog parameter (dialog initialization)\n3. Load global g_pCurrentDialog pointer into pCurrentDialogPtr\n4. Validate g_pCurrentDialog is not null; assert if null and call FUN_6fb9a10f to exit\n5. Load control list head pointer from pDialog->controlListHead (offset 0xb08)\n6. While control list not exhausted (ppControlListNode != NULL):\n   a. Dereference node vtable pointer at offset 0\n   b. If vtable exists (not null), call virtual method at [vtable + 0x20] with pDialog parameter\n   c. If method returns 1, exit loop (control activated successfully)\n   d. Move to next control node via offset 0x4 pointer\n7. If control list was empty or all methods returned non-1:\n   a. Check if pCurrentDialogPtr->controlCountField > 1 (multiple controls available)\n   b. If true, enter control cycling mode:\n      - Load current index from pCurrentDialogPtr->currentControlIndex\n      - Increment index by 1\n      - If index >= pCurrentDialogPtr->maxControlCount, wrap to 0\n      - If index < 0, wrap to maxControlCount - 1\n      - Check if control at (index * 0x110 + 0x174) offset is enabled\n      - Repeat until finding enabled control\n   c. Call FUN_6fb8d210(1, 0, 0.0, 0.0, 0) to update rendering\n   d. Store selected nCycleIndex in pCurrentDialogPtr->currentControlIndex\n\nParameters:\npDialog - Pointer to Dialog structure containing control list, control count, and enabled flags\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If g_pCurrentDialog is NULL, triggers assertion and calls exit function\n- Control stride is 0x110 bytes (272 bytes per control descriptor)\n- Virtual method dispatch allows different control types to handle activation differently\n- Index wrapping handles circular list of controls for keyboard navigation",
