      "instructions": ["0x2FE00|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [ESP + 0x4]", "0x2FE04|PUSH|ESI", "0x2FE05|PUSH|EAX", "0x2FE06|MOV|dword ptr [EAX + 0x18], 0x1", "0x2FE0D|MOV|dword ptr [EAX + 0x1c], 0x0", "0x2FE14|CALL|0x6fb99c36", "0x2FE19|MOV|EAX, [0x6fbf5f34]", "0x2FE1E|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0x2FE20|MOV|ESI, EAX", "0x2FE22|JNZ|0x6faffe42", "0x2FE24|PUSH|0x2c6", "0x2FE29|PUSH|0x6fbb3034", "0x2FE2E|PUSH|0x6fbb3024", "0x2FE33|CALL|0x6fb99a7a", "0x2FE38|ADD|ESP, 0xc"],
      "comment": "Processes dialog control input and updates dialog state based on key bindings or user selection.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize dialog flags (offset 0x18 = 1, offset 0x1c = 0)\n2. Perform initialization (call Ordinal_511)\n3. Validate current dialog exists (g_pCurrentDialog != NULL); abort with error if NULL\n4. Check if dialog control count > 4 (offset 0x54)\n5. If dialog focus flag (offset 0x20) == 0, check key bindings:\n   - Test for key binding 5,1 (PREV_PANEL); if active and key==0xd, return\n   - Test for key binding 5,0 (NEXT_PANEL); if active and key==0xd, return\n6. Get current selected index from dialog (offset 0x44)\n7. Validate index: if < 0 or >= max_controls (offset 0x50), find first non-NULL control:\n   - Iterate through controls at offset 0x174 (stride 0x110 = 272 bytes)\n   - Set selected index to first control with non-NULL function pointer\n8. If valid index, retrieve control callback function pointer at offset [index*0x110 + 0x170]\n9. Call callback and check return value (== 1 indicates process dialog)\n10. If callback returns 1, call FUN_6fb5d9c0() and return\n11. Otherwise return normally\n\nParameters:\npDialog (DialogStruct *) - Dialog structure containing control list, selection state, and callbacks\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Function updates dialog state in-place; no return value\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x18 - Offset to unknown flag field (set to 1)\n0x1c - Offset to unknown field (cleared to 0)\n0x20 - Offset to focus flag (non-zero when dialog has focus elsewhere)\n0x44 - Offset to currently selected control index\n0x50 - Offset to total control count\n0x54 - Offset to effective control count (minimum 5 for processing)\n0x110 - Control structure stride/size (272 bytes)\n0x174 - Offset to control array start\n0xd - Key code for ENTER/RETURN\n5 - Dialog/control type identifier\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If no current dialog exists, function terminates process\n- If dialog has < 5 controls, function returns without processing\n- If current selected index out of bounds, function searches for first valid control\n- If callback not found (NULL pointer), function returns without calling\n- Key binding check (5,1) and (5,0) allow pre-dialog exit on ENTER key\n\nNote: Function uses 2 phantom variables (extraout_var, extraout_var_00) optimized away by decompiler from CONCAT31 macro operations in key binding checks; these do not appear in decompiled variable list.",
