      "comment": "Processes keyboard input events for the active dialog system.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate g_pCurrentDialog is not NULL (assert and exit if NULL)\n2. Iterate through dialog control handler list at offset 0xB08 (linked list)\n3. For each handler node, call handler function at vtable+0x18 with input event\n4. If any handler returns non-zero, input was consumed - return immediately\n5. Get key code from input event at offset +0x8\n6. Check if dialog is in special mode (offset +0x20 != 0) - skip key binding checks\n7. If not special mode, check if key binding command 5 (primary) is active\n8. If primary binding active, lookup bound key and compare to input key code\n9. If match found, return (key consumed by binding)\n10. Repeat binding check for secondary slot (command 5, slot 0)\n11. If key code is 0x0D (Enter), call ProcessDialogControlInput and return\n12. If key code is 0x1B (Escape):\n    a. Check if dialog pointer valid and timeout not elapsed (tickcount check)\n    b. If timeout elapsed or no dialog: set event handled flags, queue event\n    c. Validate g_pCurrentDialog again (assert if NULL)\n    d. If dialog state >= 5 and callback at offset +0x60 exists, call it\n    e. Call UpdateTimeoutValue and return\n13. If key code is other and dialog mode (offset +0x18) != 1, return\n14. Otherwise set event handled flags and queue input event\n\nParameters:\npInputEvent - DialogStruct pointer containing input event data\n  +0x08: uint dwKeyCode - virtual key code\n  +0x18: uint dwHandled - set to 1 when processed\n  +0x1C: uint dwResult - set to 0 when processed\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Enter key (0x0D) always delegates to ProcessDialogControlInput\n- Escape key (0x1B) has 80ms timeout before allowing close\n- Key binding command 5 can intercept input before dialog processing\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x0D - VK_RETURN (Enter key)\n0x1B - VK_ESCAPE (Escape key)\n0x50 - 80 decimal, timeout in milliseconds for escape handling\n0x2C2 - Offset 0xB08 / 4, index to control handler list in dialog\n5 - Key binding command ID for dialog interaction",
