      "instructions": ["0x30070|MOV|EAX, [0x6fbf5f38]", "0x30075|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0x30077|JZ|0x6fb000ae", "0x30079|PUSH|0xe", "0x3007B|CALL|0x6fb9922c", "0x30080|MOV|ECX, EAX", "0x30082|MOV|EDX, 0x6fbb2f58", "0x30087|CALL|0x6fad2670", "0x3008C|CALL|0x6fadaa70", "0x30091|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0x30093|JZ|0x6fb000a8", "0x30095|PUSH|0x1", "0x30097|CALL|0x6fb9922c", "0x3009C|MOV|ECX, EAX", "0x3009E|MOV|EDX, 0x6fbb3000"],
      "comment": "Processes messages for dialogs and iterates through dialog chain.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if automap initialization flag is set (g_dwAutomapInitFlag)\n2. If set, get window handle via Ordinal_10027() (GetWindowHandle)\n3. Process 14 (0x0E) messages from first message array (g_aMessageArray1)\n4. Check if remote session is supported via IsRemoteSessionSupported()\n5. If remote session supported, process 1 message from second array (g_aMessageArray2)\n6. Decrement message processor counter (g_nMessageProcessorCounter)\n7. Load current dialog pointer from global (g_pCurrentDialog)\n8. If no current dialog, clear global and return\n9. Iterate through dialog linked list:\n   - Load next dialog from offset 0xb0c (dialog structure field)\n   - Call Ordinal_10043(0x334, 0) for each dialog node\n   - Continue while dialog pointer is non-null\n10. Store final dialog pointer (null) back to g_pCurrentDialog\n\nParameters: None (uses global state)\n\nReturns: void\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x0E (14): Count of messages in first array\n- 0x01 (1): Count of messages in second array\n- 0x334 (820): Parameter for Ordinal_10043()\n- 0xB0C (2828): Offset to next dialog pointer in dialog structure\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Dialog list traversal: function assumes dialog structure with valid next pointer at offset 0xB0C\n- Both message arrays (g_aMessageArray1, g_aMessageArray2) processed via ProcessMessageArray() with different counts\n- Remote session check controls which message array is processed\n- Note: Function uses 1 phantom SSA variable (extraout_var) that was optimized away by decompiler - not renameable",
