      "comment": "Appends a generic node to a linked list structure maintained in a container.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate list base pointer is not NULL; if NULL, call error handler\n2. Retrieve current tail node pointer from container at offset +0xb08\n3. Allocate new linked list node via Ordinal_10042 with allocation ID 0x35a\n4. Update container's tail pointer at offset +0xb08 to new allocated node\n5. Link previous tail node to new node by storing old tail at new_node[+0x4]\n6. Store node data value at new_node[+0x0]\n7. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\n  pListBase (LinkedListNode * in ECX) - Pointer to list container structure with:\n    - Offset +0xb08: Current tail pointer to last node in chain\n  pNewNode (void * in EDX) - Generic data value or pointer to store in new node's data field.\n    Intentionally void* to support polymorphic node types (dialogs, player slots, sprites, etc.)\n\nReturns:\n  void - No explicit return value; updates list in place through side effects\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  NULL pointer validation triggers error path\n  Preserves entire chain during append operation\n  New node becomes new tail after append\n  Supports any pointer type through void* parameter design\n\nDesign Note:\n  This function uses void* parameters to implement a generic linked list append operation.\n  The actual node types vary by caller context (dialogs, UI components, game entities)\n  but all follow the same 52-byte LinkedListNode structure with data at [0] and next at [+4].",
