      "comment": "Initializes game state dialog structure with resource data and UI configuration.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate game state parameter is non-zero and initialization flags are valid\n2. Increment global dialog initialization counter\n3. Allocate 2844-byte (0x2c4 × 4-byte elements) dialog state structure via Ordinal_10042\n4. Clear entire structure with 2844 DWORD zero writes\n5. Save previous dialog state pointer to structure offset 0xb0c (2851)\n6. Clear second 2844-DWORD region within structure\n7. Initialize dialog state metadata fields (dimensions, position, mode flags)\n8. Set game state and map data parameters at offsets 0x60, 0x64\n9. Query system tick count and store as dialog creation timestamp\n10. Configure key bindings via Ordinal_10037 and Ordinal_10038 for command 0x26 (camera control)\n11. Load dialog resource file path and concatenate with base UI path\n12. Load resource data via Ordinal_10036 (resource loader)\n13. Validate resource load succeeded; fatal error if failed\n14. Extract width and height from resource data using Ordinal_10037/Ordinal_10038\n15. Store game unit/inventory references at structure offsets 0x28, 0x24, 0x2c, 0x30\n16. Set dialog mode indicator and global mode tracking\n17. Check key binding availability for command 0x26 option 1 (map rotation key)\n18. If available and valid (< 0xdf), store key code in DAT_6fbb2f5c\n19. Check key binding availability for command 0x26 option 0 (alternate mapping)\n20. If available and valid (< 0xdf), store key code in DAT_6fbb2f68\n21. Query ordinal 10027 for interface context and process 14 message entries for main dialog UI\n22. Check if remote session supported (network play)\n23. If remote session enabled, query ordinal 10027 again and process 1 message entry for network options\n24. Increment dialog state counter and verify initialization not re-entrant\n25. Return pointer to initialized dialog structure; fatal error on re-entrancy\n\nParameters:\n  dwUnitAny (ECX, DWORD) - Unit/entity reference for game context\n  dwInventoryData (EDX, DWORD) - Inventory or unit data component\n  dwGameState (Stack[4], DWORD) - Game state identifier (validated non-zero)\n  dwMapData (Stack[8], DWORD) - Map or terrain data reference\n  nInitFlags (Stack[12], int) - Initialization flags (validated <= 0)\n  dwGameMode (Stack[16], DWORD) - Game mode identifier (difficulty, play type)\n\nReturns:\n  DWORD * - Pointer to initialized 2844-DWORD dialog structure (0x2c4 elements)\n  NULL (return 0x0) if dwGameState is zero or nInitFlags > 0 (validation failed)\n  Note: Function uses 3 phantom SSA temporaries optimized away by decompiler (extraout_var_00, extraout_var, extraout_var_01) - these are carry-through values from conditional branches\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Re-entrancy check: If dialog already initialized (DAT_6fbf5f3c != 1), triggers fatal error at 0x3cc\n  - Resource load failure: If Ordinal_10036 returns zero, triggers fatal error at 0x3b4\n  - Key binding lookup: Skips if key code is 0xffff or >= 0xe0 (invalid range)\n  - Network mode: Message processing only if remote session supported\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x397 - Resource allocation size (919 × 4 bytes = 3676 total, includes metadata)\n  0x2c4 - Loop count (708 × 4-byte elements = 2832 bytes for main dialog array)\n  0x12 - Second loop count (18 × 4-byte elements = 72 bytes for temporary array)\n  0xb0c - Offset to previous dialog pointer in structure (2828 bytes)\n  0x26 - Command ID for map rotation/camera control key binding\n  0xffff - Invalid key code marker\n  0xdf (223) - Maximum valid key code threshold\n  0xe - Number of main UI message entries (14)\n  1 - Number of network UI message entries\n  DAT_6fbf5f3c - Global dialog initialization counter (must equal 1 for re-entrancy check)\n  DAT_6fbf5f2c - Global dialog state counter (incremented each initialization)\n  DAT_6fbf5f34 - Previous dialog structure pointer chain\n  DAT_6fbf5f38 - Mode tracking flag (set to 1 for current dialog)\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset  Size  Field Name                Type    Description\n0x0     4     dwTickCount              uint    System tick count at creation\n0x4     4     dwResourceData           uint    Loaded resource file reference\n0x8     4     dwResourceHandle         uint    Resource handle from loader\n0xc     4     dwInitFlag               uint    Initialization state (1 = initialized)\n0x10    4     dwMessageResult          uint    Message processing result\n0x14    4     dwUnused14               uint    Unused padding\n0x18    4     dwGameState              uint    Game state parameter (non-zero)\n0x1c    4     dwMapData                uint    Map data parameter reference\n0x24    4     dwUnitRef                uint    Game unit reference (param_1)\n0x28    4     dwUnitRef2               uint    Game unit reference duplicate\n0x2c    4     dwInventoryRef           uint    Inventory reference (param_2)\n0x30    4     dwInventoryRef2          uint    Inventory reference duplicate\n0x34    4     dwWidth                  uint    Dialog width from resource\n0x38    4     dwHeight                 uint    Dialog height from resource\n0x44    4     dwNegativeOne            uint    Constant 0xffffffff\n0x48    4     dwNegativeOne2           uint    Constant 0xffffffff\n0x50    4     dwZero50                 uint    Zero padding\n0x5c    4     dwModeFlag               uint    Mode indicator (2 = current)\n0x60    4     dwGameStateStore         uint    Game state copy (param_3)\n0x64    4     dwMapDataStore           uint    Map data copy (param_4)\n0xb08   4     dwZeroB08                uint    Zero padding\n0xb0c   4     pPreviousDialog          DWORD*  Linked list pointer to previous dialog\n\nRelated Functions:\n  - Ordinal_10042() - Memory allocator for dialog structures\n  - Ordinal_10036() - Resource file loader (validates file exists)\n  - Ordinal_10037() - Query width from resource metadata\n  - Ordinal_10038() - Query height from resource metadata\n  - IsKeyBindingActive() - Check if key binding defined for command ID\n  - LookupKeyBindingByCommandId() - Get current key code for binding\n  - ProcessMessageEntryArray() - Route UI messages to handlers\n  - IsRemoteSessionSupported() - Determine if network play enabled",
