      "comment": "Initialize dialog structure with 11 parameters.\\n\\nAlgorithm:\\n1. Initialize internal systems (FUN_6fb5e340, FUN_6fb18910)\\n2. Call InitializeTargetingSystem()\\n3. Return NULL if dwParam3 is zero (invalid dialog ID)\\n4. Increment initialization counter g_dwDialogInitCount\\n5. Allocate new dialog structure (0xb10 bytes = 2832 bytes)\\n6. Save previous dialog pointer in structure offset 0xb0c\\n7. Set new dialog as g_pCurrentDialog\\n8. Clear all structure fields with memset (2820 dwords)\\n9. Populate dialog fields from parameters:\\n   - dwParam1 -> offsets 0x24, 0x2c (appears twice)\\n   - dwParam2 -> offsets 0x28, 0x30\\n   - dwParam3 -> offset 0x60\\n   - dwParam4 -> offset 0x64\\n   - dwParam5 -> offset 0x34\\n   - dwParam6 -> offset 0x58\\n   - dwParam7 -> offset 0x14\\n   - dwParam8 -> offset 0x18\\n   - dwParam9 -> offset 0x38\\n   - dwParam10 -> offset 0x20\\n   - dwParam11 -> offset 0x1c\\n10. Initialize remaining fields with defaults:\\n    - offset 0x00 = current tick count from GetTickCount()\\n    - offset 0x44, 0x48 = 0xffffffff\\n    - offset 0x5c = 0x02 (initial state)\\n    - offset 0xb08 = 0x00\\n11. Check key binding 0x26 (first variant):\\n    - If active, lookup binding and store at g_dwKeyBinding0x26Var1 if valid\\n12. Check key binding 0x26 (second variant):\\n    - If active, lookup binding and store at g_dwKeyBinding0x26Var2 if valid\\n13. Process 14 message entries from g_MessageEntryArray1\\n14. Check if remote session supported\\n15. If supported, process 1 message entry from g_MessageEntryArray2\\n16. Increment g_DialogProcessCount\\n17. Verify initialization count is 1 (only one dialog init allowed)\\n18. If count != 1, call error handler with file/line info and terminate\\n\\nParameters:\\n- dwParam1 (ECX): Dialog parameter 1 (stored at offset 0x24, 0x2c)\\n- dwParam2 (EDX): Dialog parameter 2 (stored at offset 0x28, 0x30)\\n- dwParam3 [ESP+4]: Dialog ID (must be non-zero)\\n- dwParam4 [ESP+8]: Dialog parameter