      "comment": "Shuts down and closes the active dialog window, cleaning up resources and message handlers.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Decrement global dialog initialization counter (g_dwDialogInitCount)\n2. If counter reaches zero, proceed with shutdown; otherwise exit immediately\n3. Call FUN_6fb5e340(1) to prepare for dialog closure\n4. Query current window handle via Ordinal_10027() (D2Win.GetWindowHandle)\n5. Post 14 (0xe) messages from g_aMessageArray1 to dialog window\n6. Check if in remote session via IsRemoteSessionSupported()\n7. If remote session active, post 1 message from g_aMessageArray2\n8. Call FUN_6fb18910(1) to finalize dialog closure\n9. Call CopyConfigurationData(NULL) to persist current config state\n10. Load current dialog pointer from g_pCurrentDialog\n11. Clear automap initialization flag (g_dwAutomapInitFlag = 0)\n12. Traverse linked list of dialogs starting at offset 0xb08\n13. For each dialog in chain, post message 0x42e (WM_APP equivalent)\n14. Check parent dialog state at offsets 0xc and 0x8\n15. If both conditions true, report validation error via ReportValidationError()\n16. Load next dialog pointer from offset 0xb0c\n17. Post message 0x439 to complete cleanup\n18. Update global current dialog pointer to next dialog\n19. Restore registers and return\n\nParameters:\nNone (void function)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Early exit if dialog init count not zero (function has multiple active dialogs)\n- Remote session message block only posts if IsRemoteSessionSupported() returns non-zero\n- Dialog linked list iteration continues until NULL pointer encountered\n- Validation error check skips reporting if either parent state field is zero\n- IMPLICIT: EDI register used as dialog pointer throughout (loaded from g_pCurrentDialog)\n- IMPLICIT: ESI register used as linked list iterator",
