      "comment": "Renders all dialog elements to the display surface.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate pDialog parameter is not NULL; if NULL, log error and abort\n2. Initialize local render buffer array (18 elements) to zero\n3. Load starting coordinates (nStartY, nStartX) from dialog structure\n4. Calculate bounding coordinates (nMaxX, nMaxY) from structure fields\n5. Increment dialog reference counter\n6. Check dialog rendering mode: if direct mode, call RenderDirectToSurface\n7. If cached mode and texture buffer exists, call RenderCachedTile\n8. Process callback list: iterate linked list and invoke each callback\n9. Begin main loop through dialog elements (count from structure)\n10. For each element: load offset data and coordinates\n11. Check if element matches current layer; if match, apply color mode\n12. Render element to display at calculated coordinates\n13. Update iteration counters and advance to next element\n14. Call final display commit\n\nParameters:\npDialog - Pointer to DialogStruct containing rendering data and element array\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value; function terminates or aborts on NULL input",
