      "comment": "Validates and sets the current selectable line index in a dialog.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate pDialog is not NULL; fail if NULL (assertion)\n2. Load NumLines field from dialog structure at offset +0x50\n3. Validate nLineIndex < NumLines; fail if out of bounds (assertion)\n4. Handle special case: if nLineIndex == -1, set current index to -1 and return\n5. Initialize loop counter nCurrentIdx = 0\n6. Loop through line entries while nCurrentIdx < NumLines:\n   a. Load line pointer from offset [pDialog + 0x174 + (nCurrentIdx * 0x110)]\n   b. If nCurrentIdx == nLineIndex (target line found):\n      i. Check if line is selectable (*pLinePtr != 0); fail if not (assertion)\n      ii. Set current index field [pDialog + 0x44] = nLineIndex\n      iii. If nLineIndex >= 1, accumulate line widths: loop nLineIndex times loading width from offset +0x158\n      iv. Return after width calculation\n   c. Increment nCurrentIdx and continue loop\n7. If loop completes without finding nLineIndex, fail (assertion)\n\nParameters:\n- pDialog (ECX): Pointer to dialog structure; contains NumLines at +0x50, current index at +0x44, line array at +0x174\n- nLineIndex (EDX): Line index to select; -1 for special clear case\n\nReturns:\n- void; sets dialog current index field as side effect\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- nLineIndex = -1: Clear selection (set current index to -1xFFFFFFFF) without validation\n- Line stride: 0x110 bytes (272 decimal) per line entry in array at offset +0x174\n- Width field: Line width at offset +0x158 within each line structure\n- Assertions on NULL dialog, out-of-bounds index, unselectable line indicate defensive programming",
