      "comment": "Sets a field value in a dialog structure at offset 0x5c.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if dialog pointer is null (test ECX, ECX)\n2. If null, jump to error handler (JNZ to success path skips error)\n3. Call Ordinal_10023 with error parameters (pointer, filepath, error code 0x527)\n4. Call FUN_6fb9a10f with 0xffffffff to terminate the application on error\n5. If dialog valid (non-null), proceed to store value\n6. Store dwValue parameter at [pDialog + 0x5c]\n7. Return from function\n\nParameters:\npDialog (Dialog *) - Pointer to dialog structure in ECX; if NULL triggers fatal error termination\ndwValue (dword) - Value to store at dialog field offset 0x5c in EDX\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value; on null pointer error, calls fatal terminator FUN_6fb9a10f\n\nSpecial Cases:\nNull dialog pointer is fatal error condition that terminates entire application\nOffset 0x5c stores critical dialog state value (observed as 1 in all callers)",
