      "comment": "Adds a new line to a dialog box with text, color, and positioning settings.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Retrieve current line count from this+0x50\n2. Assert if line count > 10 (max dialog lines exceeded)\n3. Increment line count and store at this+0x50\n4. Calculate line storage offset: nLineIndex * 0x110 (288 bytes per line slot)\n5. Clear display flags at offset+0x15c to 0\n6. Store dwBaseColor at offset+0x158\n7. Store dwExtraColor at offset+0x164\n8. Store dwColorValue at offset+0x168\n9. If nColorType==3 and this+0x5c==1, assert (invalid color combination)\n10. Store nColorType at offset+0x16c\n11. Store dwUnknown at offset+0x170\n12. Store nAddMode at offset+0x174\n13. Call Unicode::strlen (via 0x6fba5c44) to get text length\n14. Clamp text length to max 0x77 (119 characters)\n15. Call Unicode::strncpy (via 0x6fba5c50) to copy text to offset+0x68\n16. Clear terminator word in text buffer\n17. If nAddMode!=0, increment selection counter at this+0x4c\n18. If this+0x58==0, calculate line display position via Ordinal calls\n19. Otherwise call FUN_6fb00b60 for positioned display\n20. Load configuration values from this+0x2c/0x30/0x34/0x38 offsets\n21. Call CopyConfigurationData with configuration parameters\n22. Check selection index at this+0x44\n23. If selected with nAddMode!=0, call SetDialogLineIndex\n24. Return void\n\nParameters:\n- this (ECX): Pointer to dialog structure containing line array and settings\n- dwBaseColor: Base text color value (stored at line offset 0x158)\n- dwExtraColor: Secondary color or effects flag (stored at line offset 0x164)\n- nColorType: Color mode/type value (3=special, stored at offset 0x16c)\n- dwColorValue: Color palette value (stored at line offset 0x168)\n- dwUnknown: Additional flag/mode value (stored at line offset 0x170)\n- nAddMode: Selection/display mode (0=no select update, non-zero=update counter)\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Maximum 10 lines per dialog (assertion failure if exceeded)\n- Text length