      "comment": "Calculates optimal dialog panel dimensions based on content items and screen constraints.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Verify dialog item count exists at pDialogPanel->itemCount; error if zero or invalid\n2. Initialize maximum width tracker, empty slot counter, and accumulated field dimension accumulators\n3. Iterate through all panel items (stride 0x44 bytes starting at itemFieldPtr offset):\n   a. Call Ordinal_10121 to get item text width\n   b. Track maximum width across all items; update nMaxWidth if larger\n   c. Count empty slots by testing if item pointer is zero\n   d. Accumulate field dimensions by reading value at item_ptr - 0x1c\n4. Apply padding: add 0x14 to maximum width, add 0xf to total accumulated height\n5. Calculate x-offset: nCalcXOffset = screenCenterX - (maxWidth / 2)\n6. Calculate y-offset based on mode flag:\n   - If yOffsetMode == 0: nCalcYOffset = screenCenterY - (totalHeight / 3)\n   - Else: nCalcYOffset = screenCenterY + (emptySlotCount * -0x15)\n7. Validate calculated width against screen boundaries\n8. Validate calculated height against screen boundaries\n9. Apply boundary clamps and enforce minimum dimension (0xb pixels) thresholds\n10. Store final dimensions in contentWidth and contentHeight fields\n11. Second pass: For each item, calculate optimal centered x-position offset\n12. Return void\n\nParameters:\npDialogPanel (DialogPanel*): Dialog panel structure containing:\n  yOffsetMode (offset 0x14): Mode flag (0=divide height by 3, nonzero=use empty slots)\n  screenCenterX (offset 0x24): Panel horizontal center coordinate\n  screenCenterY (offset 0x28): Panel vertical center coordinate\n  itemCount (offset 0x50): Number of items in the panel\n  itemFieldPtr (offset 0x174): Array of item structure pointers (0x44-byte stride)\nOutput:\n  calcXOffset (offset 0x2c): Calculated x-offset position\n  calcYOffset (offset 0x30): Calculated y-offset position\n  contentWidth (offset 0x34): Total content width after padding\n  contentHeight (offset 0x38): Total content height after padding\n\nReturns:\nvoid - modifies pDialogPanel structure in-place with calculated dimensions\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If pDialogPanel->itemCount == 0 or invalid: Calls error handler routine (Ordinal_10023)\n- Width exceeds screen maximum: Error handling and termination\n- Height exceeds screen maximum: Error handling and termination",
