      "comment": "Returns a dword value from offset 0x44 within a unit structure.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if pUnit parameter (passed in ECX) is NULL\n2. If NULL, set EAX to 0xFFFFFFFF (all bits set) and return\n3. If non-NULL, dereference pUnit + 0x44 and load dword into EAX\n4. Return the loaded dword value\n\nParameters:\n- pUnit (UnitAny *): Pointer to unit structure containing the field; passed via ECX register (__fastcall convention)\n\nReturns:\n- dword: Value at offset 0x44 within the unit structure if pUnit is valid; 0xFFFFFFFF (-1) if pUnit is NULL\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- NULL Pointer Handling: Function gracefully handles NULL input by returning sentinel value 0xFFFFFFFF instead of crashing\n- Offset 0x44: Fixed field offset (68 decimal bytes) within UnitAny structure\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n- 0x44: Field offset within unit structure (decimal: 68)\n- 0xFFFFFFFF: Error/sentinel value (-1 as unsigned dword)",
