      "comment": "Initializes slider/spin control UI object with range, display, and height parameters.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Setup exception handling and allocate 0x12c bytes for locals\n2. Load UI slider path template string for resource loading\n3. Build full path using ConcatenatePathAndWriteFile, store at object+0x52\n4. Calculate display buffer size = (wNumCharacters * 2) + 2\n5. Create first display buffer via Ordinal_10042(0x5b), store at object+0x28\n6. Create second display buffer via Ordinal_10042(0x5c), store at object+0x2c\n7. Zero-fill first buffer with REP STOSD/STOSB\n8. Zero-fill second buffer with REP STOSD/STOSB\n9. Store control parameters: wNumCharacters at object+0x34, dwInitialValue at object+0x30, dwMaximumValue at object+0x4e\n10. Store calculated values: (nMinValue+1) at object+0x10, 1 at object+0x20 and object+0x4a\n11. Copy 11 bytes initialization data from szInitialSliderValues to stack buffer\n12. Initialize Unicode string array (11 elements) via default_constructor_closure loop\n13. Call Ordinal_10127 for unicode initialization\n14. Convert ASCII init values to Unicode via win2Unicode\n15. If nHeightPixels < 1: calculate height = (CharacterWidth/10) * (wNumCharacters+2)\n16. If nHeightPixels >= 1: use explicit value\n17. If nDefaultHeightPixels < 1: set default height=1, flag at object+0x56\n18. If nDefaultHeightPixels >= 1: use explicit value, clear flag\n19. Zero-init final fields at object+0x24 and object+0x4\n20. Restore exception list and return control pointer\n\nParameters:\n  pSliderControl: Slider control object to initialize (SliderControl*)\n  nMinValue: Minimum slider value (int)\n  nColumnPosition: X column position (int)\n  nHeightPixels: Explicit height; auto-calculated if <1 (int)\n  nDefaultHeightPixels: Default height; set to 1 if <1 (int)\n  dwInitialValue: Initial slider value (dword)\n  wNumCharacters: Display character count (ushort)\n  dwMinimumValue: Minimum range value (dword)\n  dwMaximumValue: Maximum range value (dword)\n\nReturns:\n  SliderControl*: Pointer to initialized control object\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  Auto-height uses 0x66666667 magic constant for division-by-10\n  Both buffers must be pre-allocated before this call\n  Unicode initialization via Ordinal_10127 and win2Unicode\n  Character width via Ordinal_10121 for auto mode\n  Assembly temporaries optimized away during decompilation\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x5b: First buffer ordinal parameter\n  0x5c: Second buffer ordinal parameter  \n  0x0b: Initialization data size and Unicode array length\n  0x66666667: Muldiv constant for efficient /10",
