      "comment": "Cleanup resources from a UnitAny object before destruction.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Setup SEH (Structured Exception Handling) frame for exception safety\n2. Set object vtable pointer to cleanup handler vtable\n3. Initialize local flag variable to 0\n4. Check if slot [+0x28] (destructor callback slot) is active\n5. If active, call ordinal 0x8C with parameter 0 (release/cleanup operation code)\n6. Clear slot [+0x28] to NULL\n7. Check if slot [+0x2C] (secondary destructor callback slot) is active\n8. If active, call ordinal 0x91 with parameter 0 (cleanup operation code)\n9. Clear slot [+0x2C] to NULL\n10. Read validation/error field from offset [+0x52]\n11. Call ReportValidationError to report any accumulated errors\n12. Set flag to 0xFFFFFFFF (cleanup complete marker)\n13. Call FUN_6fb1de50 for additional cleanup operations specific to this unit type\n14. Restore exception list pointer to previous value\n15. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\npUnit (UnitAny *): Pointer to game unit object to clean up before destruction\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No explicit return value; cleanup is performed as side effect\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Destructor callback slots (offsets 0x28, 0x2C) may be NULL - slots are only called if non-NULL\n- Validation error field (offset 0x52) is always read and reported, even if NULL\n- Function uses SEH for exception safety - any exception will trigger cleanup\n- Called exclusively from the Destructor function; always precedes actual object deallocation",
