      "comment": "Renders a text input control with blinking cursor support.\n\nClassification: Worker function - renders UI text input with scrolling and line wrapping\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Increment frame counter (nCtrlPtr+0x46) for cursor blink timing\n2. If background visible flag (nCtrlPtr+0x56) set, draw background sprite offset by (-10, -16)\n3. Set active font from control (nCtrlPtr+0x4e)\n4. Initialize cursor character buffer with '_' underscore character\n5. Initialize temp buffer (400 Unicode chars) for wrapped text\n6. Convert cursor char to Unicode via win2Unicode\n7. Update cursor blink state:\n   - If cursor visible: toggle every 20 frames (0x14)\n   - If cursor hidden: toggle every 10 frames\n   - Store blink state at nCtrlPtr+0x4a\n8. Branch on render mode (nCtrlPtr+0x1c):\n   - Mode 1: Single-line rendering with horizontal scroll\n   - Other modes: Multi-line wrapped text rendering\n\nSingle-line mode (nCtrlPtr+0x1c == 1):\n9. Calculate text width via SumCharacterValues\n10. If text width > max width (nCtrlPtr+0x18), find scroll offset\n11. Render text starting from scroll offset\n12. Check if cursor should be drawn (position < text length, blink on, position valid)\n13. If cursor visible, calculate X position and render cursor char\n\nMulti-line mode:\n14. Call WrapUnicodeText to split text into lines\n15. Loop through wrapped lines:\n    a. Render each line at Y offset (0x14 per line)\n    b. Track cumulative character offset\n    c. When cursor position found on this line, render cursor\n    d. Release pool allocations for wrapped line data\n16. If no lines rendered but cursor visible, render cursor at origin\n\nParameters:\n- nCtrlPtr (int, ECX): Pointer to TextInputControl structure (cast as int)\n\nTextInputControl Structure Layout:\nOffset  Size  Field                Description\n0x10    4     nX                   X coordinate for rendering\n0x14    4     nY                   Y coordinate for rendering\n0x18    4     nMaxWidth            Maximum text width in pixels\n0x1c    4     nRenderMode          1=single-line, other=multi-line\n0x28    4     pwszText             Pointer to text Unicode string\n0x2c    4     pwszDisplayBuf       Display buffer pointer\n0x34    2     wTextLen             Current text length\n0x36    4     nCursorPos           Cursor position in text\n0x3a    4     nMaxCursorPos        Maximum valid cursor position\n0x46    4     dwFrameCounter       Frame counter for blink timing\n0x4a    4     fCursorVisible       Cursor visibility flag (blink state)\n0x4e    4     nFontId              Font ID for text rendering\n0x56    4     fShowBackground      Background visibility flag\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x14 (20): Line height in pixels, cursor blink fast rate (frames)\n- 0x0a (10): Cursor blink slow rate (frames)\n- 0xc7 (199): Max string length for wrapped line copy\n- 0x12 (18): Background sprite Y source offset\n- 10, 16: Background sprite position offsets\n\nRelated Functions:\n- DrawSpriteWithSourceOffset: Draws control background\n- SetActiveFont: Activates font for rendering\n- SumCharacterValues: Calculates text pixel width\n- WrapUnicodeText: Splits text into wrapped lines\n- RenderUnicodeTextWithLineHeight: Renders Unicode text\n- ReleasePoolAllocation: Frees wrapped line allocations",
