      "comment": "Formats a numeric value into a string buffer and converts it to Unicode for display in a text control.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Format nFormatValue into local ANSI buffer using FormatStringToBuffer with \"%d\" format\n2. Calculate string length using inline strlen (SCASB.REPNE pattern)\n3. Read max buffer length from control structure at offset +0x34 (ushort)\n4. If string length exceeds max length, truncate by null-terminating at max position\n5. Convert ANSI string to Unicode via win2Unicode, storing at buffer pointer from +0x28\n6. Get Unicode string length via Unicode::strlen\n7. Store result length at both +0x36 and +0x3a in control structure\n\nParameters:\n  pTextControl (ECX) - Pointer to text control structure containing:\n    +0x28: Unicode * - Pointer to Unicode output buffer\n    +0x34: ushort   - Maximum string length\n    +0x36: uint     - Current string length (output)\n    +0x3a: uint     - Display string length (output)\n  nFormatValue (stack+4) - Integer value to format as string\n\nReturns: void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - String truncation occurs silently if formatted string exceeds wMaxLength\n  - Both length fields (+0x36, +0x3a) are set to same value\n\nCalled By: Function pointer table at 0x6fba86f4\nCalls: FormatStringToBuffer, Unicode::win2Unicode, Unicode::strlen",
