      "comment": "Validates UTF-8 text control content length and processes it via buffer conversion.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get Unicode string buffer from text control structure at offset +0x28\n2. Call strlen on the Unicode buffer to check if it has content\n3. If buffer is empty (length 0), return 0 immediately (early exit)\n4. Convert Unicode buffer to UTF-8 using toUtf into local 100-byte stack buffer\n   - Pass Unicode pointer from +0x28 and max length from +0x34 (ushort)\n5. Call ProcessUtf8TextBuffer to parse the UTF-8 buffer\n6. Compare parsed result (extraout_EAX) against max length at +0x30\n7. Return result value, masked to 0 if it exceeds max length\n\nParameters:\n  pTextControl (ECX) - Pointer to TextControlContext structure containing:\n    +0x28: Unicode * - Pointer to Unicode string buffer\n    +0x30: int      - Maximum allowed result value\n    +0x34: ushort   - Maximum string length for conversion\n\nReturns:\n  uint - Parsed integer result from UTF-8 buffer, or 0 if:\n         - Input buffer is empty\n         - Result exceeds maximum value at +0x30\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Empty string check prevents unnecessary conversion work\n  - Result clamping uses branchless mask: value & (max < value) - 1\n    If result > max, mask becomes 0, otherwise 0xFFFFFFFF\n  - Local stack buffer is 100 bytes (acStack_64)\n\nDecompiler Notes:\n  - unaff_ESI appears in decompiler but is actually the Unicode buffer pointer\n  - extraout_EAX carries return value from ProcessUtf8TextBuffer\n  - ESI register preserves pTextControl across function calls",
