      "comment": "Clears text selection state in a TextControlContext structure.\n\nClassification: Cleanup - resets selection-related fields to zero\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load selection start value from this+0x3e into EDX\n2. Set EAX to 0 (will be used for clearing and return value)\n3. Compare selection start against 0\n4. If selection start is 0 (no selection), skip to step 7\n5. Clear selection end field at this+0x46 to 0\n6. Clear selection start field at this+0x3e to 0\n7. Return 0\n\nParameters:\n  this (ECX) - TextControlContext * pointer to text control structure\n    +0x3e: int dwSelectionStart - text selection start position (0 = no selection)\n    +0x46: int dwSelectionEnd - text selection end position\n  pTextControl (Stack+4) - TextControlContext * UNUSED, matches vtable signature\n\nReturns:\n  int - Always returns 0\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If dwSelectionStart is already 0, no modifications are made\n  - Both fields are cleared together to maintain selection consistency\n  - Stack parameter pTextControl is unused but required for vtable compatibility\n\nRelated Functions:\n  - FUN_6fb01470: Keyboard input handler that sets selection state\n  - FUN_6fb017a0: Move cursor right (affects +0x36)\n  - FUN_6fb017c0: Move cursor left (affects +0x36)\n\nCalled From:\n  - Function pointer table at g_apfnTextControlHandlers (0x6fba86c8)",
