      "comment": "Processes keyboard input events for a text input control widget.\n\nClassification: Worker function - handles keyboard-based text editing for UI controls\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if control accepts input (pTextControl+0x24 != 0 or input flags 0x40000000 not set)\n2. Extract keycode from input message (pInputMsg->wFlags at offset +0x8)\n3. If keycode >= 0x80 (non-ASCII), skip to event completion\n4. Determine input processing mode:\n   a. If custom handler (pTextControl+0x4) exists, call it\n   b. Else if validation mode (pTextControl+0x20) set, call CheckKeyCodeControlFlag\n   c. Else call CheckBitFlagIndex for standard key processing\n5. Handle special keys Enter (0x0D) and Escape (0x1B) via callback at pTextControl+0x42\n6. Process key by type:\n   - Backspace (0x08): Delete character before cursor, shift remaining text left\n   - Delete (0x2E): Delete character at cursor position, shift text left\n   - Space/Enter/Escape with dwKeyResult==0: Return without character insertion\n   - Normal char: Insert character at cursor position, shift existing text right\n7. If text modified, validate line wrapping via WrapUnicodeText\n8. If wrapped lines exceed max (pTextControl+0x1c), truncate last character\n9. Update text length (pTextControl+0x3a) and cursor position (pTextControl+0x36)\n10. If validation mode enabled, convert to UTF-8 and process through validation\n11. Mark input message as processed (dwProcessed=1, dwResult=0)\n12. Queue processed input message via InsertCacheNodeWithCookie\n\nParameters:\npTextControl (TextControlContext *, ECX) - Pointer to text input control structure:\n  +0x04: pfnCustomHandler - Custom input handler callback (code *)\n  +0x18: nMaxWidth - Maximum text width in pixels for line wrapping\n  +0x1c: nMaxLines - Maximum number of wrapped lines allowed\n  +0x20: fValidationMode - Enable UTF-8 validation processing flag\n  +0x24: fAcceptInput - Control accepts keyboard input flag\n  +0x28: pwszTextBuffer - Pointer to Unicode text buffer (ushort *)\n  +0x30: dwMaxLength - Maximum UTF-8 text length for validation\n  +0x34: wBufferCapacity - Text buffer capacity in characters (ushort)\n  +0x36: nCursorPosition - Current cursor position in text\n  +0x3a: nTextLength - Current text length in characters\n  +0x42: pfnSpecialKeyCallback - Callback for Enter/Escape key handling\n  +0x4e: nFontId - Font ID for text width calculation\n\npInputMsg (UIInputMessage *, Stack[0x4]) - Input message structure:\n  +0x08: wFlags/keycode - Virtual keycode of pressed key\n  +0x0C: dwInputFlags - Input flags (0x40000000 = special input mode)\n  +0x18: dwProcessed - Set to 1 when message has been handled\n  +0x1C: dwResult - Processing result code (0 = success)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Input message marked as processed via dwProcessed field\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Keys with code >= 0x80 are ignored (non-ASCII characters)\n- Space (0x20), Enter (0x0D), Escape (0x1B) with dwKeyResult==0 cause early return\n- Text is truncated if line wrapping exceeds nMaxLines limit\n- Validation mode truncates text if UTF-8 length exceeds dwMaxLength\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x08 - Backspace keycode (VK_BACK)\n0x0D - Enter/Return keycode (VK_RETURN)\n0x1B - Escape keycode (VK_ESCAPE)\n0x20 - Space keycode (VK_SPACE)\n0x2E - Delete keycode (VK_DELETE)\n0x80 - ASCII range boundary (keys >= 0x80 are ignored)\n0x40000000 - Special input mode flag in pInputMsg->dwInputFlags\n\nRelated Functions:\n- CheckBitFlagIndex: Validates standard key acceptance\n- CheckKeyCodeControlFlag: Validates key in control/validation mode\n- WrapUnicodeText: Splits text into wrapped lines for width check\n- SetActiveFont: Activates font for width calculations\n- ProcessUtf8TextBuffer: Validates UTF-8 encoded text content\n- FormatStringToBuffer: Formats validation error message\n- InsertCacheNodeWithCookie: Queues processed input message",
