      "comment": "Advances text control cursor position by one if not at maximum.\n\nClassification: Callback/Handler - Text control cursor movement handler\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load current cursor position from pTextControl+0x36\n2. Load maximum position from pTextControl+0x3a\n3. Compare current position against maximum\n4. If current < max, increment cursor position by 1\n5. Return 1 (success)\n\nParameters:\npTextControl (TextControlContext *) - ECX, pointer to text control context\n  +0x36 (int): nCursorPosition - current cursor/caret position\n  +0x3a (int): nMaxPosition - maximum allowed cursor position (buffer length)\n\nReturns:\nint - Always returns 1 (TRUE) indicating operation completed\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Cursor at max position: No change, returns 1\n- No bounds checking for null pointer (assumes valid context)\n\nRelated Functions:\nFUN_6fb017c0 - Decrements cursor position (move backward)\n\nCalled Via:\ng_apfnTextControlHandlers function pointer table at 0x6fba86c8",
