      "comment": "Iterates through game data table and processes valid entries matching conditions.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize pointer to data table base at 0x6fbf5f63\n2. Load entry at current position (26-byte stride elements)\n3. Check if entry has field at offset +5 not equal zero (validation check)\n4. Check if byte at offset -1 is not space (0x20) - signature byte validation\n5. Check if byte at offset +0 is not -0xAC (character validation)\n6. If all conditions pass, call FUN_6fb03f10 with three parameters from entry\n7. Advance pointer by 0x1a (26 bytes) to next entry\n8. Continue until pointer reaches end boundary at 0x6fbf62a3 (ESI < boundary)\n9. Exit and return\n\nParameters:\n(none)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value. Function performs side effects via FUN_6fb03f10 calls.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Entry validation uses three separate condition checks that must ALL be true\n- Offset -1 check uses space (0x20) as invalid marker\n- Offset +0 uses byte 0xAC as invalid marker\n- Offset +5 contains validation flag (any non-zero value passes)\n- Table stride is 26 bytes per entry\n- Table boundary is hardcoded at 0x6fbf62a3\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x6fbf5f63 - Base address of data table (26-byte stride)\n0x6fbf62a3 - Upper boundary of data table iteration (exclusive)\n0x1a (26) - Stride between consecutive entries\n0x20 (32) - Space character used as invalid marker at offset -1\n0xAC (172) - Byte value marking invalid entry at offset +0\n+5 offset - Position of validation flag within entry",
