      "instructions": ["0x31B70|XOR|EAX, EAX", "0x31B72|PUSH|EBX", "0x31B73|MOV|[0x6fbf66d4], EAX", "0x31B78|MOV|[0x6fbf66d8], EAX", "0x31B7D|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [ESP + 0x8]", "0x31B81|PUSH|EBP", "0x31B82|PUSH|ESI", "0x31B83|PUSH|EDI", "0x31B84|MOV|EBP, dword ptr [EAX + 0xc]", "0x31B87|XOR|EDI, EDI", "0x31B89|MOV|DI, word ptr [EAX + 0xc]", "0x31B8D|MOV|ECX, 0x6fbf62a4", "0x31B92|SHR|EBP, 0x10", "0x31B95|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [ECX + -0x4]", "0x31B98|CMP|EDI, EAX"],
      "comment": "Processes mouse click events on a button grid UI panel.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Clear button grid state flags (g_dwButtonGridState1, g_dwButtonGridState2)\n2. Extract click X coordinate from low word of pClickEventData[3]\n3. Extract click Y coordinate from high word of pClickEventData[3]\n4. Iterate through button bounds array (stride 0x15 bytes, 21-byte entries):\n   a. Check if click X is within button X bounds (minX < X < minX + 0x1a)\n   b. Check if click Y is within button Y bounds (maxY - 0x1a < Y < maxY)\n   c. If within bounds and entry pointer < 0x6fbf6362:\n      - Store button column from entry offset +0xd to g_dwSelectedButtonColumn\n      - Update all button state entries where flag at offset +6 is non-zero\n   d. If within bounds and entry pointer >= 0x6fbf6362:\n      - Store button row from entry offset +0xd to g_dwSelectedButtonRow\n      - Update all button row state entries where flag at offset +5 is non-zero\n5. Iterate through button entry array (stride 0x1a bytes, 26-byte entries):\n   a. Check if click is within expanded bounds (X: +0x30, Y: -0x40 to current)\n   b. Search primary button flags array for first non-zero entry (indices 0-9)\n   c. Search secondary button flags array for first non-zero entry (indices 10+)\n   d. If primary index found: clear button state array to space (0x20)\n   e. If secondary index found: set button row state to 0xAC\n   f. Update entry field at offset +4 or +5 if entry flag at +10 is set\n6. Check if click in \"Cancel\" region (X: 0x18-0x36, Y: 0x158-0x176):\n   - Call ProcessUIStateChange(0x20, 2, 0) and (0x1b, 0, 0) to close UI\n7. Check if click in \"Confirm\" region (X: 0x245-0x263, Y: 0x158-0x176):\n   a. Search for active button entry with valid state flags\n   b. Get button value from index table or use default\n   c. Call ProcessUIStateChange to prepare UI\n   d. Call CompressThreeByteValue with button value and adjusted coordinates\n   e. Set g_dwGameInitializedFlag = 1\n   f. Call ProcessUIStateChange to finalize\n8. Set event handled flag: pClickEventData[6] = 1, pClickEventData[7] = 0\n9. Insert event into cache via InsertCacheNodeWithCookie\n\nParameters:\n  pClickEventData - Pointer to click event structure:\n    +0x0C: Packed coordinates (low word = X, high word = Y)\n    +0x18: Event handled flag (set to 1)\n    +0x1C: Secondary flag (set to 0)\n\nReturns: void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Click outside any button bounds: no state change, event still cached\n  - Cancel button clicked: closes UI without game initialization\n  - Confirm button clicked: triggers game initialization with selected button value\n\nButton Entry Structure (0x1a bytes / 26 bytes):\n  Offset  Size  Field         Description\n  -0x04   4     nMinX         Minimum X coordinate\n  +0x00   4     nMaxY         Maximum Y coordinate  \n  +0x04   1     bColumnValue  Button column identifier\n  +0x05   1     bRowValue     Button row identifier\n  +0x06   4     dwActiveFlag  Non-zero if entry is active\n  +0x0A   4     dwUpdateFlag  Non-zero to allow state update\n  +0x0D   4     dwDataValue   Associated data value\n\nButton Bounds Entry (0x15 bytes / 21 bytes):\n  Offset  Size  Field       Description\n  -0x04   4     nMinX       Minimum X bound\n  +0x00   4     nMaxY       Maximum Y bound\n  +0x04   1     bValue      Associated byte value\n  +0x0D   4     dwData      Associated data value\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x1a (26) - Button entry stride and X range size\n  0x15 (21) - Button bounds entry stride\n  0x30 (48) - Extended X range for entry matching\n  0x40 (64) - Extended Y range for entry matching\n  0x20 (32) - Space character, button cleared state\n  0xAC (172) - Row state marker value (-0x54 signed)\n  0x17-0x37 - Cancel button X range (23-55)\n  0x157-0x177 - Cancel/Confirm button Y range (343-375)\n  0x244-0x264 - Confirm button X range (580-612)",
      "tags": ["PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PROP_NOCALLER", "STRUCT_Skill", "PARAM_1", "PROP_LOOPHEAVY", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
