      "comment": "Initialize a cache node for UI state tracking and insert it into the cache system.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Toggle UI element 0x20 (scroll mode) to state 2 (toggle) via ProcessUIStateChange\n2. Activate UI element 0x1b (panel state) by setting state to 0 (activate)\n3. Set cache node field at +0x18 to 1 (active flag)\n4. Clear cache node field at +0x1c to 0 (state/cookie field)\n5. Insert the initialized node into the cache via InsertCacheNodeWithCookie\n\nParameters:\npCacheNode - Pointer to cache node structure to initialize\n  +0x18: dwActiveFlag - Set to 1 to mark node as active\n  +0x1c: dwStateValue - Cleared to 0\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- No callers found - likely a callback or function pointer target\n- Function is a leaf worker that delegates to InsertCacheNodeWithCookie\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x20 - UI element ID for scroll/panel mode\n0x1b - UI element ID for panel state\n0x18 - Offset to active flag in cache node\n0x1c - Offset to state value in cache node",
