      "comment": "Initialize all game dialogs, UI elements, and rendering surfaces.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate 0x11A0 bytes for function working buffer via FUN_6fb9af30()\n2. Zero-initialize local buffer region (18 dwords)\n3. Return early if g_pGameState is null (no game state available)\n4. Initialize 6 dialog surfaces with Ordinal_10072() calls (indices 0-5), each 0x102 bytes\n5. Get current texture surface from FUN_6fb8ed80()\n6. If texture surface exists:\n   - Allocate and initialize 512 Unicode strings (0x200 * sizeof(Unicode) = 2 bytes each)\n   - Load surface from Ordinal_11163() via Unicode::toUnicode()\n   - Call three ordinal functions (10127, 10121, 10117) - likely texture setup\n   - Check if game initialized with IsGameInitialized()\n   - If NOT initialized, setup alternate dialog with g_dwGameId, else ProcessDataTableWithConditionCheck()\n7. Process first alternate dialog surface (Ordinal_11164):\n   - Load as Unicode string, measure length\n   - Trim trailing zeros if output exceeds 0x104 bytes\n8. Process second alternate dialog surface (Ordinal_11166):\n   - Load as Unicode string\n   - Iterate through linked list from Ordinal_10199() calling display functions\n9. Get frame/timer value via Ordinal_11173() (64-bit), convert to decimal string via FUN_6fb9ae77()\n10. Get second timer value via Ordinal_11176():\n    - Check if equals 1600000 (special case: ~26.7 minutes)\n    - If different and non-zero, repeat string conversion step\n11. Process scroll bar surfaces (indices 3-5) with layout calculations\n12. Call FUN_6fb16490(3) - final UI initialization\n13. Get current UI layout from FUN_6fb5e380()\n14. Update base offset with g_dwBaseOffset + 0x0A via Ordinal_10072()\n15. If g_pAdditionalConfig exists, setup additional rendering surfaces\n16. If g_fInitialized is false, call FUN_6fb00d70() to validate initialization\n17. Get mouse coordinates via FUN_6fb8f680() (X) and FUN_6fb8f690() (Y)\n18. Increment g_nFrameCounter\n19. Handle left panel scroll (if g_fLeftPanelEnabled and frame % 8 == 0):\n    - Bounds check against mouse position and g_nScrollPosition\n    - Calculate scroll bar position: (g_nScrollPosition * 0xF8) / (g_nDialogCount - 1)\n20. Handle right panel scroll (if g_fRightPanelEnabled):\n    - Increment g_nScrollPosition with similar bounds checking\n    - Recalculate scroll bar position\n21. Mouse region detection - trigger UI actions when mouse in specific areas:\n    - Region 1 (0x10E-0x136, 0x180-0x1A8): Call Ordinal_10004(), 10121(), 10129()\n    - Region 2 (0x1A-0x12C, 0x15B-0x171): Call ordinals if g_pAdditionalConfig set\n    - Region 3 (0x1A-0x4B, 0x41-0x87): Another UI region trigger\n    - Region 4 (0x1A-0x12C, 0xE2-0x140): Extended region trigger\n    - Region 5 (0x95-0x12D, 0x49-0x5A): Call ordinals and return\n    - Region 6 (0x12D, 0x77-0x9B): Alternate region, also returns\n    - Region 7 (0xD7-0x12E, 0xAC-0xBA): Final region, call ordinals\n\nParameters:\nNone. Function uses only global variables accessed via DAT_ references.\n\nReturns:\nvoid. Modifies numerous global state variables controlling dialog layout, scrolling, and UI rendering.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Timer value 1600000 (0x186A00) treated as special case with conditional logic\n- If g_pGameState is null, function exits immediately without initialization\n- Scroll calculations use division by (g_nDialogCount - 1) to avoid division by zero\n- Mouse coordinate regions are mutually exclusive and trigger different UI actions\n- Frame counter with modulo 8 check provides debouncing for scroll operations\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x11A0 - Function working buffer size (4512 bytes)\n0x12 - Buffer initialization count (18 dwords)\n0x102 - Dialog surface unit size (258 bytes)\n0x200 - Unicode string array count (512 items)\n0x104 - Maximum length threshold for string truncation\n0x1B2, 0x1A3, 0x1A4, 0x16B, 0x66, 0xFF, 0x259 - Dialog IDs and resource indices\n0x258, 0x267, 0x6F, 0x79 - Mouse coordinate range checks\n0x1600000 - Special timer constant (~26.7 minutes in game ticks)\n0x0A - Offset increment for layout\n0x0E, 0x12D, 0x4B, 0x1A - Mouse region boundaries (X coordinates)\n0x41, 0x87, 0x15B, 0x171, 0x49, 0x5A, 0x77, 0x9B, 0xAC, 0xBA - Mouse region boundaries (Y coordinates)\n0xF8 - Scroll bar calculation multiplier\n0xE1, 0x52 - Additional ordinal IDs",
