      "instructions": ["0x32B50|SUB|ESP, 0xcac", "0x32B56|PUSH|EBX", "0x32B57|PUSH|EBP", "0x32B58|PUSH|ESI", "0x32B59|PUSH|EDI", "0x32B5A|LEA|EAX, [ESP + 0x24]", "0x32B5E|MOV|EDI, ECX", "0x32B60|PUSH|EAX", "0x32B61|MOV|EBX, EDX", "0x32B63|PUSH|EDI", "0x32B64|CALL|0x6fb98788", "0x32B69|XOR|EAX, EAX", "0x32B6B|PUSH|EDI", "0x32B6C|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x14], EAX", "0x32B70|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x18], EAX"],
      "comment": "Convert text input to Unicode and render with various display modes and settings. Text object is obtained from context object passed as parameter (likely a game UI text widget or D2Common text context).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize local variables: set fIsHighQuality and byDisplayMode flags to false/0\n2. Call Ordinal_11197 to extract text pointer from pTextObject into lpszTextBuffer\n3. Query text mode via Ordinal_11200(pTextObject), set byDisplayMode if mode==1, set fIsHighQuality if mode==2\n4. Query text variant via Ordinal_11199(pTextObject), store in dwModeValue (used in switch for variants 1-4)\n5. Initialize Unicode buffer awUnicodeBuffer[64] with 32 Unicode::default_constructor calls (zeros)\n6. Convert lpszTextBuffer to Unicode in awUnicodeBuffer using Unicode::toUnicode(awUnicodeBuffer, lpszTextBuffer, 0x20)\n7. Call Ordinal_10004 to prepare/reset rendering state\n8. Call Ordinal_10121 to set up rendering parameters\n9. If fIsHighQuality is true (mode==2):\n   - Call Ordinal_10117(0x58, 7, 0) twice to set high-quality rendering parameters\n   - Initialize large Unicode buffer with 0x400 (1024) Unicode::default_constructor calls (zeros)\n   - Call FUN_6fb9ae77 to process color/palette data\n   - Convert buffer to Unicode\n   - Call Ordinal_10117(0x58, 7, 0) once more and return\n10. If fIsHighQuality is false (normal mode):\n    - Calculate byColorMask: = -(nFlags != 0) & 3 (sets to 3 if nFlags != 0, else 0)\n    - Call Ordinal_10117(dwDisplayAddress, byColorMask, 0) twice to set display mode/color\n    - Calculate dwDisplayAddress = g_dwDisplayStride * nIndex + g_dwBaseOffsetX + g_dwBaseOffsetY\n    - Initialize large Unicode buffer with 0x400 (1024) Unicode::default_constructor calls (zeros)\n    - Call FUN_6fb9ae77 to process color/palette data\n    - Convert buffer to Unicode\n    - Call Ordinal_10117(dwDisplayAddress, byColorMask, 0) once more\n    - Initialize array adStackArray[18] with 0x12 (18) DWORD elements set to 0\n    - Set adStackArray[2] = byDisplayMode, adStackArray[1] = g_dwDisplayFormat, adStackArray[3] = 0\n    - Call Ordinal_10072 with adStackArray and calculated parameters to render text\n\nParameters:\npTextObject (ECX, void *) - Text context/object pointer; passed to Ordinal_11197, Ordinal_11200, Ordinal_11199 for text and mode extraction. Type is internal text widget structure from game UI/D2Common system. Remains opaque in this function as it's only passed to ordinal functions.\nnIndex (EDX, int) - Display table/grid index; multiplied by g_dwDisplayStride to calculate display coordinate (e.g., row in text grid)\nnFlags (Stack, int) - Display flags; if != 0, enables color masking (byColorMask = 3), likely for text highlighting or special rendering\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No explicit return value; function side effects (rendering/display to screen buffer via ordinal calls)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Mode 2 (fIsHighQuality=true) takes early exit path after high-quality rendering setup\n- Mode 1 (byDisplayMode) sets flag but continues to normal rendering with byDisplayMode stored in config\n- nFlags parameter affects color masking calculation via signed extension -(nFlags != 0) and AND with 3\n- Arrays and buffers are initialized via repeated Unicode::default_constructor calls (1024+ iterations)\n- Note: SSA temporary variable iVar1 optimized away during decompilation (not visible in high-level code)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x20 (32 decimal) - Unicode buffer element count for small buffer\n0x400 (1024 decimal) - Unicode buffer element count for large buffer\n0x12 (18 decimal) - Configuration array element count\n0x58 - Base rendering parameter/palette base (passed to Ordinal_10117)\n0x7 - Color/quality level (passed to Ordinal_10117)\n0xffffffff - Max iterator value (passed to Ordinal_10072 as iteration limit)\n0xf, 0x38, 0xe6, 0xbd - Offset constants into display configuration table (g_pDisplayConfigBase)\n0x3 - Bitmask for color flags in byColorMask calculation\n\nGlobal Data References:\ng_dwDisplayStride (0x6fbb31f0) - Display stride/scaling factor (multiplied by nIndex)\ng_dwBaseOffsetX (0x6fbb31ec) - Base display offset X coordinate\ng_dwBaseOffsetY (0x6fbb31e4) - Base display offset Y coordinate\ng_pDisplayConfigBase (0x6fbb31e8) - Display configuration table base address\ng_dwDisplayFormat (0x6fbf6704) - Display palette/format identifier\n\nOrdinal Functions Called:\nOrdinal_11197(pTextObject, *lpszTextBuffer) - Extract text string from object\nOrdinal_11200(pTextObject) - Get text display mode (1=normal, 2=high-quality)\nOrdinal_11199(pTextObject) - Get text variant (1-4, used in switch/jump table)\nOrdinal_10004() - Reset/prepare rendering state\nOrdinal_10121() - Configure rendering parameters\nOrdinal_10117(dwAddress, byLevel, 0) - Set rendering parameters at address with level\nOrdinal_10072(adConfig[], nOffset, dwAddress, 0xffffffff, 5, 0) - Render with configuration array\n\nRelated Functions:\n- Called by: FUN_6fb01e50 (higher-level UI text rendering coordinator)\n- Calls: Ordinal_10004, Ordinal_10117, Ordinal_10121, Ordinal_10072 (rendering system)\n- Cooperates with: FUN_6fb9ae77 (color/palette processing), Unicode class (constructor/conversion)",
