      "comment": "Initialize player game state and targeting system after state transition.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if game state 0x1b (player initialization state) is ready via FUN_6fb5d370\n2. If not ready, return immediately\n3. If ready, check if a game resource (possibly difficulty/mode setup) was successfully loaded via FUN_6fb8ed80\n4. If load failed, mark state 0x1b as complete and send packet 0x4f (game ready) to game server\n5. If load succeeded, zero-initialize 12 global game state variables (camera position, targeting mode, scroll offsets, panel state, render state)\n6. Call InitializeTargetingSystem to setup player targeting/combat system\n7. Check if state 0x0a is ready (likely quest/objective system)\n8. If state 0x0a ready, mark it complete via state transition\n9. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\nVOID - No parameters; operates on global game state\n\nReturns:\nVOID - No return value; modifies global state\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Function called during state machine case 0x19 (likely server-side player join/spawn sequence)\n- Two exit paths: early return if state 0x1b not ready, or full initialization on ready\n- Magic constant 0x1b represents player initialization state\n- Magic constant 0x0a represents quest/objective verification state\n- Packet 0x4f signals game server that player is ready to play\n- All globals are zeroed to clear any previous game state (preventing state bleed between sessions)",
