      "comment": "Initializes UI panel images and configures UI state for game launch.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Clear game ready flag\n2. Retrieve parent window handle from system initialization\n3. Return early if initialization failed (parent window = NULL)\n4. If steelstone background image not loaded, construct path and load image via ConcatenatePathAndWriteFile\n5. If medium button blank image not loaded, construct path and load image\n6. If click box image not loaded, construct path and load image\n7. If scroll bar image not loaded, construct path and load image\n8. If panel icon 01 image not loaded, call LoadImage helper function\n9. Set UI color mask to 0xFFFFFFFF (all bits set)\n10. Clear UI offset X and Y coordinates\n11. Call GetCurrentUnitType to retrieve player unit\n12. Call Ordinal_10424 on unit (window transformation)\n13. Call Ordinal_11196 to configure UI display for unit\n14. If configuration succeeds, call Ordinal_11200 to get display mode\n15. Set g_dwUIMode flag: 1 if display mode equals 2, 0 otherwise\n16. Return 0 (success)\n\nParameters:\nvoid (takes no parameters)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value. Modifies global UI image pointers and mode flag.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Images may already be loaded (pointers non-zero) - function skips re-loading\n- Game initialization may fail, triggering early exit at step 3\n- Display mode check uses (display_mode == 2) to determine g_dwUIMode flag\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x104: Local buffer size for file path construction (260 bytes max path)\n- 0xFFFFFFFF: UI color mask initial value (all bits enabled)\n- 0x2: Display mode comparison value determining g_dwUIMode setting",
