      "comment": "Sends network packet to server or local connection by compressing packet data and routing through appropriate channel.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get connection ID from FUN_6fb8ed80()\n2. Check if g_pServerConnection is active (non-NULL)\n3. If server connection exists:\n   a. Invoke server connection initialize function (offset +0x3c)\n   b. Build packet string on stack at [ESP+0xc]\n   c. Calculate string length using REPNE SCASB (string scan)\n   d. If length valid (iVar3 != -2), set field separator byte to 0x00\n   e. Call CompressStringPacket with field separator 0x00 and packet buffer\n   f. Send compressed packet to server via Ordinal_11165(connectionId, buffer)\n   g. Invoke server connection cleanup function if exists\n   h. Clear server connection pointer to NULL and return\n4. Otherwise, process local connection:\n   a. Invoke local connection initialize function (offset +0x3c)\n   b. Build packet string on stack at [ESP+0xc]\n   c. Calculate string length using REPNE SCASB\n   d. If length valid (iVar3 != -2), set field separator byte to 0x01\n   e. Call CompressStringPacket with field separator 0x01 and packet buffer\n   f. Send compressed packet locally via Ordinal_11167(connectionId, buffer)\n   g. Invoke local connection cleanup function if exists\n   h. Clear local connection pointer to NULL and return\n\nParameters:\n(none - uses global connection pointers g_pServerConnection and g_pLocalConnection)\nIMPLICIT: Returns uint connection ID via EAX (result of FUN_6fb8ed80)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - always returns normally after processing connection\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Buffer allocated: [ESP] to [ESP+0x103] (260 bytes) for packet data\n- String scan uses REPNE SCASB with ECX=0xFFFFFFFF, sets byte at offset to 0x00 or 0x01\n- Two separate code paths: server connection (higher priority) vs local connection\n- Both paths follow identical packet building and transmission pattern\n- Early return via JZ 0x6fb03569 if server connection not active",
