      "comment": "Activate a cache node entry and initialize game state if needed.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Set cache node active flag at offset +0x18 to 1\n2. Clear cache node secondary flag at offset +0x1c to 0\n3. Insert node into cache via InsertCacheNodeWithCookie\n4. Check if game initialization flag (g_fInitialized) is clear\n5. If not initialized:\n   a. Process UI state change for element 0x1b (waypoint panel) with activate state\n   b. Check if game ready flag (g_dwGameReadyFlag) is clear\n   c. If not ready, send game ready packet (type 0x4f, subtype 0x1b)\n   d. Set game ready flag to prevent resending\n   e. Flush any pending validation errors\n6. Reset cache node active flag at offset +0x18 to 1\n7. Clear cache node secondary flag at offset +0x1c to 0\n8. Re-insert node into cache via InsertCacheNodeWithCookie\n\nParameters:\npCacheNode - Pointer to cache node structure to activate\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Steps 6-8 duplicate steps 1-3, possibly intentional double-registration\n- Game initialization only occurs on first call when g_fInitialized == 0\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x18 - Offset to cache node active state field (1 = active)\n0x1c - Offset to cache node secondary state field (cleared to 0)\n0x1b - UI element ID for waypoint/quest panel\n0x4f - Packet type for game ready notification\n\nRelated Functions:\n- InsertCacheNodeWithCookie: Registers node in game cache\n- ProcessUIStateChange: Updates UI element visibility/state\n- SendPackedData: Transmits network packet to server\n- FlushPendingValidationErrors: Clears queued error states",
