      "comment": "Initializes cache node fields and inserts into the cache system.\n\nClassification: Worker function - initializes dialog/cache node state\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check g_fInitialized flag - if not set, skip to step 5\n2. Check g_pDialogConfig2 - if set, call its vtable handler at offset 0x24\n3. If Config2 is NULL, check g_pDialogConfig1 - if set, call its handler\n4. If handler returns non-zero, node was processed - exit early\n5. Set node field at offset 0x18 to 1 (active/valid flag)\n6. Set node field at offset 0x1c to 0 (clear state/counter)\n7. Call InsertCacheNodeWithCookie to add node to cache\n\nParameters:\n  dwCacheNodePtr - uint: Pointer to cache node structure to initialize\n    - Offset 0x18: DWORD - Set to 1 (validity/active flag)\n    - Offset 0x1c: DWORD - Set to 0 (state/counter field)\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If system not initialized (g_fInitialized == 0), bypasses dialog handlers\n- If both dialog configs are NULL, proceeds directly to cache insertion\n- Handler returning non-zero indicates node was processed externally\n\nGlobals Referenced:\n  g_fInitialized (0x6fbf6738) - System initialization flag\n  g_pDialogConfig2 (0x6fbf6750) - Primary dialog config handler\n  g_pDialogConfig1 (0x6fbf6754) - Secondary dialog config handler\n\nNote: No callers found - likely called via function pointer table",
