      "comment": "Initializes Unicode string buffer and computes length adjustment.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate 200-byte stack buffer for 100 Unicode characters\n2. Call Ordinal_10004 in loop 100 times to initialize each Unicode character\n3. Increment buffer pointer by 2 bytes per iteration (Unicode char size)\n4. Call Ordinal_10004 for Unicode string constructor\n5. Call strcpy with source and destination string pointers\n6. Call Ordinal_10121 to get current Unicode string length in bytes\n7. Calculate adjusted length: nLength - (Ordinal_10121_result / 2)\n8. Return adjusted length in EAX\n\nParameters:\npBuffer (int *): Input/output buffer pointer passed in ECX\nnLength (int): Base length value in EDX to be adjusted\n\nReturns:\nint: Adjusted length = nLength - (length_in_bytes / 2)\n     Represents final character count after Unicode processing\n\nSpecial Cases:\nFunction uses implicit string parameters in ESI and EDI registers\nUnicode characters are 2 bytes; division by 2 converts byte counts to character counts\nStack buffer sized for exactly 100 Unicode characters (200 bytes)",
