      "comment": "Initialize automap viewport panels with default configuration and rendering parameters.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate 18-element panel configuration array (72 bytes)\n2. Zero-initialize entire configuration array using REP STOSD\n3. Set game state manager reference at offset +4 (index 1)\n4. Create viewport panel 0: X=0, Y=0, W=0x100, H=0x100\n5. Create viewport panel 1: X=0x100, Y=0, W=0x100, H=0x100\n6. Create viewport panel 2: X=0, Y=(screen_height-0x30), W=0x100, H=0x100\n7. Create viewport panel 3: X=0x100, Y=(screen_height-0x30), W=0x100, H=0x100\n8. Create viewport panel 4: X=0x140, Y=0, W=0x100, H=0x100\n9. Create viewport panel 5: X=0x240, Y=0, W=0x100, H=0x100\n10. Create viewport panel 6: X=0x140, Y=(screen_height-0x30), W=0x100, H=0x100\n11. Create viewport panel 7: X=0x240, Y=(screen_height-0x30), W=0x100, H=0x100\n\nParameters:\nNone (no explicit parameters; function uses global state)\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\nScreen height is fetched from global g_dwScreenHeight; panels positioned relative to screen resolution.\nAll viewport panels created with full opacity (0xffffffff) and priority level 5.\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x30 = Panel height adjustment from screen bottom (48 pixels)\n0x100 = Standard viewport panel dimension (256 pixels)\n0x140 = Column 2 offset (320 pixels)\n0x240 = Column 3 offset (576 pixels)\n0xffffffff = RGBA fully opaque white color\n5 = Rendering priority/z-order\n\nRelated Functions:\n- InitializeAutomapRendering() - Calls this function during automap subsystem initialization\n- Ordinal_10072() - Creates individual viewport/widget with specified configuration",
