      "comment": "Initializes viewport rendering context for non-game states (menu, cinematics, etc.).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate local buffer anRenderContext (18 dwords = 72 bytes)\n2. Initialize all array elements to 0 via repeated STOSD\n3. Call FUN_6fb5e380() to retrieve viewport coordinate data\n4. Store viewport handle in anRenderContext[1]\n5. Set anRenderContext[3] = 0 (reserved)\n6. Calculate panel variant mode: set anRenderContext[2] = 10 + (g_dwPanelVariantFlag ? 1 : 0)\n   - If g_dwPanelVariantFlag set: mode = 11 (0x0b)\n   - If g_dwPanelVariantFlag clear: mode = 10 (0x0a)\n7. Call Ordinal_10005() to verify game state\n8. If state == 2 (normal game): exit immediately via early return\n   - This function should only execute when state != 2\n9. Call Ordinal_10072() twice with viewport sprite parameters:\n   - Sprite offset varies based on state verification:\n     - If verification passed (JNZ): use 0x20d (fallback viewport)\n     - If verification failed: use 0x2ad (alternate viewport)\n   - Size: 0x38 bytes\n   - Alpha mask: 0xffffffff\n   - Priority: 5\n   - Frame: 0\n10. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\nNone (uses global state: g_pViewportData, g_dwPanelVariantFlag)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Initializes viewport context in-place\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Function is only called when game state is not 2 (non-game states: menu, cinematics, transitions)\n- The initial game state check serves as sanity verification and controls sprite offset selection\n- Note: Function uses 1 SSA temporary variable optimized away by decompiler (iVar1)\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x12 = 18 elements in context array (0x12 * 4 = 0x48 bytes)\n0x2ad = Alternate viewport sprite offset for verification failure branch\n0x20d = Fallback viewport sprite offset for non-game state path\n0x38 = 56 bytes, typical sprite structure size\n0xffffffff = Full alpha blending mask\n5 = Priority level for viewport sprites\n\nStructure Layout:\nanRenderContext[] - Viewport rendering initialization structure (18 dwords):\nOffset  Size  Field Name    Type      Description\n0x0     4     reserved0     int       (cleared to 0)\n0x4     4     handle        int       Viewport coordinate handle from FUN_6fb5e380()\n0x8     4     mode          int       Panel variant mode (10 or 11)\n0xc     4     reserved1     int       (cleared to 0)\n...     ...   ...           ...       (remaining 14 dwords cleared)\n\nRelated Functions:\n- FUN_6fb5e380() - Retrieves viewport coordinate data handle\n- Ordinal_10005() - GetGameState (returns 2 for active game, other values for menu/cinematics)\n- Ordinal_10072() - D2Common sprite/layer initialization\n- InitializeAutomapRendering() - Caller function (invokes this for non-game states)",
