      "comment": "Handles mouse-down events within the panel variant hotspot region.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract click X coordinate (low word) and Y coordinate (high word) from event data offset +0x0C\n2. Call Ordinal_10005 (GetResolutionMode) to determine screen resolution mode\n3. If mode == 2 (high resolution 800x600):\n   - Check if X is in range [685, 717] (0x2AD-0x2CD)\n4. Else (low resolution 640x480):\n   - Check if X is in range [525, 557] (0x20D-0x22D)\n5. If X in valid range AND Y in range [24, 56] (0x18-0x38):\n   - Set g_dwPanelVariantFlag = 1 (panel variant mode active)\n   - Set event processed flag at offset +0x18 = 1\n   - Clear pending flag at offset +0x1C = 0\n   - Call InsertCacheNodeWithCookie to queue event completion\n6. Else (click outside hotspot):\n   - Call ClearTargetingState to reset targeting system\n   - Set event processed/pending flags as above\n   - Call InsertCacheNodeWithCookie to queue event completion\n\nParameters:\npMouseEvent - Pointer to mouse event structure containing:\n  +0x0C: packed coordinates (low word=X, high word=Y)\n  +0x18: event processed flag (set to 1 on completion)\n  +0x1C: event pending flag (cleared to 0 on completion)\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Resolution-dependent hotspot regions accommodate different screen sizes\n- The hotspot corresponds to a UI panel element (likely minimap toggle or similar)\n- Paired with HandlePanelVariantMouseUp (FUN_6fb05fa0) which handles release\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x2AD (685) = High-res panel hotspot X minimum\n0x2CD (717) = High-res panel hotspot X maximum (range width: 32 pixels)\n0x20D (525) = Low-res panel hotspot X minimum\n0x22D (557) = Low-res panel hotspot X maximum (range width: 32 pixels)\n0x18 (24) = Panel hotspot Y minimum (both resolutions)\n0x38 (56) = Panel hotspot Y maximum (range height: 32 pixels)\n\nRelated Functions:\n- FUN_6fb05fa0: Mouse-up handler for panel variant\n- ClearTargetingState: Resets targeting globals on outside clicks\n- InsertCache