      "comment": "Process mouse click events in the panel region to toggle UI elements.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract X coordinate from pClickEvent[3] low word, Y from high word\n2. If g_dwPanelVariantFlag is 0, skip UI toggle logic\n3. Call Ordinal_10005 (D2GFX.GetResolutionMode) to get current resolution\n4. If resolution mode == 2 (800x600):\n   - Check if X in range [0x2AD, 0x2CD] (685-717) and Y in range [0x18, 0x38] (24-56)\n5. If resolution mode != 2 (640x480):\n   - Check if X in range [0x20D, 0x22D] (525-557) and Y in range [0x18, 0x38] (24-56)\n6. If click is in valid region:\n   - Call ProcessUIStateChange(0x21, 2, 0) to toggle UI element 0x21\n   - If g_dwAutomapInitialized != 0, deactivate automap (0x15, 1, 0) and clear flag\n7. If click not in region or flag was 0:\n   - Clear g_dwPanelVariantFlag to 0\n   - Call ClearTargetingState() to reset targeting\n8. Mark click event as processed: pClickEvent[6] = 1, pClickEvent[7] = 0\n9. Insert event into cache via InsertCacheNodeWithCookie\n\nParameters:\npClickEvent - Pointer to click event structure:\n  +0x0C: Packed coordinates (low word = X, high word = Y)\n  +0x18: Processing flag (set to 1 when handled)\n  +0x1C: Result code (set to 0 when handled)\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- No callers found - likely registered as callback handler\n- Resolution mode determines which coordinate range is valid\n- UI element 0x21 appears to be a panel toggle button\n- Automap (0x15) is conditionally deactivated when panel toggled\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x2AD-0x2CD (685-717) - X range for 800x600 resolution\n0x20D-0x22D (525-557) - X range for 640x480 resolution\n0x18-0x38 (24-56) - Y range for both resolutions\n0x21 - UI element ID for panel toggle\n0x15 - UI element ID for automap",
