21. Call Ordinal_10072 again with updated screen height (nScreenHeight-0xA4) and mode flag\n\nParameters:\nNone (void function)\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Resource validation short-circuits on first failure - early exit prevents further initialization\n- Key binding lookups return 0xffff if not configured - skips string formatting for missing bindings\n- Two separate Unicode string buffers (400 and 30 elements) suggest help text split between main and secondary text\n- Screen layout calculations subtract fixed offsets from global dimensions (height -0xC5/-0xA0/-0xA4, width -0x4B/-0x48) indicating UI border/frame sizes\n- Mode flag (SETNZ) converts zero/nonzero to boolean 0/1 for screen rendering\n- Function uses 9 phantom variables (SSA temporaries): iVar2, uVar3, pUVar4, puVar5, auStack_1d8[4], auStack_1c8[4] optimized away by decompiler\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x4, 0x3, 0x1, 0xC, 0x17, 0x19 - Resource IDs for validation\n0x22 - Error code for menu load failure\n0xC8 (200) - Element count for first Unicode array (aUStack_190)\n0x1E (30) - Element count for second Unicode array (stack buffers)\n0x12 (18) - Dword array size for buffer zeroing\n0xF (15) - Dword array size for key binding buffer\n0x1051, 0x1052 - String IDs for key binding lookups\n0xFFFF - Invalid/missing key binding indicator\n0xC5 - Vertical offset subtraction for screen layout\n0xA0, 0xA4 - Screen height adjustments\n0x4B, 0x48 - Screen width adjustments\n0xffffffff - Text color parameter (full white)\n5 - Screen rendering mode parameter\n\nRelated Functions:\n- FUN_6fb5d340 - Resource validator (called 6 times for dependency checking)\n- FUN_6fb5d370 - Error handler (called on menu load failure with error code)\n- Ordinal_423 - Load help menu file/resource\n- Ordinal_10004 - Initialize/get string resources\n- Ordinal_10121 - Display/render help menu to screen\n- Ordinal_10072 - Screen/window rendering with parameters (called twice)\n- LookupKeyBindingByCommandId - Get key binding for comman