      "comment": "Initialize key binding help text for two command sequences (primary and alternate).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Zero-initialize 18 DWORD slots on stack (72 bytes)\n2. Construct 200 Unicode string objects on stack\n3. Construct 30 Unicode string objects for parameter buffers\n4. Call Ordinal_10004 to reset Unicode buffer context\n5. Copy ESI to EDI using Unicode string copy\n6. Look up primary key binding ID for command type 6, action 1\n7. If key binding exists (result != 0xffff):\n   - Zero-initialize 15 pointer slots for string array\n   - Get string resource ID for primary key binding\n   - Call Ordinal_10004 with string resource ID to get Unicode string\n   - Format primary key binding text into primary buffer using sprintf\n   - Append primary suffix to primary buffer using strcat\n8. Look up alternate key binding ID for command type 6, action 0\n9. If alternate key binding exists (result != 0xffff):\n   - Zero-initialize 15 pointer slots for alternate string array\n   - Get string resource ID for alternate key binding\n   - Call Ordinal_10004 with resource ID to get Unicode string\n   - Format alternate key binding text into alternate buffer using sprintf\n   - Append alternate suffix to alternate buffer using strcat\n10. Call Ordinal_10121 to finalize UI element\n11. Call Ordinal_10117 to set vertical position (screen height - 197 pixels)\n12. Configure and apply first dialog element with Ordinal_10072:\n    - Load config value from g_dwScreenHeight - 197\n    - Width = screen width - 75\n    - Height = screen height - 160\n    - Color = 0xffffffff (white)\n    - Frame type = 5\n13. Load alternate config value from g_dwScreenHeight - 197\n14. Set active flag based on whether alternate config is loaded (non-zero)\n15. Configure and apply second dialog element with Ordinal_10072:\n    - Width = screen width - 72\n    - Height = screen height - 164\n    - Color = 0xffffffff (white)\n    - Frame type = 5\n\nParameters:\n- lpszPrimaryBuffer (char *): Outpu