      "comment": "Initialize hireable/mercenary icon data and configuration for all unit types.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Copy Amazon icon path from data to local buffer (local_5a0, 21 bytes)\n2. Copy Sorceress icon path to local buffer (local_580 array, 6 dwords)\n3. Copy Barbarian icon path to buffer (local_560, 6 dwords)\n4. Copy Paladin icon path to buffer (local_540, 5 dwords + word)\n5. Copy Necromancer icon path to buffer (local_520, 6 dwords + word)\n6. Copy Rogue icon path to buffer (local_500, 5 dwords)\n7. Copy Act 2 Hireable icon path (local_4e0, 6 dwords + word + byte)\n8. Copy Act 3 Hireable icon path (local_4c0, 6 dwords + word + byte)\n9. Copy Skeleton icon path (local_4a0, 5 dwords + word + byte)\n10. Copy Skeleton Mage icon (local_480, 6 dwords + word + byte)\n11. Copy Revived/Resurrected icon (local_460, 5 dwords + word)\n12. Copy Earth Golem icon path (local_440, 25 bytes)\n13. Copy Blood Golem icon path (local_420, 25 bytes)\n14. Copy Metal Golem icon path (local_400, 25 bytes)\n15. Copy Fire Golem icon path (local_3e0, 6 dwords)\n16. Copy Valkyrie icon path (local_3c0, 5 dwords + word + byte)\n17. Copy Assassin icon path (local_3a0, 5 dwords + word + byte)\n18. Copy Druid icon path (local_380, 5 dwords)\n19. Copy Raven, Wolf, Bear spirit paths from string data with byte-sized copies\n20. Copy Plague Poppy and Cycle of Life paths (5 dwords + word each)\n21. Copy Vines, Spirit of Barbs, Heart of Wolverine paths\n22. Copy Oak Sage and Shadow Assassin paths (6+ bytes)\n23. Copy Barbarian Hireable icon path (6 dwords + word + byte)\n24. Initialize global data array g_adHireableIconData (128 dwords) to zero\n25. Clear global configuration at g_pdwHireableConfig (29 dwords) to zero\n26. For each of 16 icon path buffers, call FUN_6fb5a050 to process path and store result in g_adHireableIconData\n27. Check if custom mercenary filtering enabled via Ordinal_10227 (D2Common.IsExpansionAct or quest flag check)\n28. If enabled, process Assassin icon through loop, count valid paths, load into g_pdwHireableConfig\n29. Return after initialization complete\n\nParameters:\n(none - __stdcall, no parameters)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value, function initializes global state\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Icon paths are stored as strings in string constant area\n- Byte-sized copies (MOVSB) used for 3-byte data segments\n- Word-sized copies (MOVSW) used for 2-byte data segments\n- Function uses REP MOVSD for bulk 4-byte copies\n- Global arrays must be initialized first before configuration loop\n- Configuration loop only runs if Ordinal_10227 returns non-zero (expansion enabled)\n- String length validation: stops at first null terminator, returns early if no valid path found\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n- 0x80 (128): Size of g_adHireableIconData array in dwords (512 bytes total)\n- 0x1d (29): Size of g_pdwHireableConfig array in dwords (116 bytes total)\n- 0x10 (16): Number of icon paths to process in main loop\n- 0x20 (32): Stride/size of each icon path buffer (bytes)\n- 0xe (14): Offset of null terminator character in some string structures\n- 0x5-0x6: Loop counts for copying different-sized buffers\n\nRelated Functions:\n- FUN_6fb5a050(char* pszIconPath) - Process icon path and return configuration value\n- Ordinal_10227() - D2Common function, check if expansion/act enabled\n- Global callers: FUN_6fb5a0b0 - Likely initialization of mercenary system",
