      "comment": "Clears validation error codes from a global array by reporting and zeroing each non-zero entry.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize ESI pointer to start of validation error array (0x6fbf6778)\n2. Load first dword entry from current pointer position\n3. Test if entry is non-zero (validation error present)\n4. If zero, skip to step 6\n5. If non-zero, report error code via ReportValidationError() and clear entry to zero\n6. Advance pointer to next dword (add 4 bytes)\n7. Compare pointer against array end boundary (0x6fbf67ec)\n8. If pointer less than boundary, repeat from step 2\n9. Return when all entries processed\n\nParameters:\n(none - __stdcall, no parameters)\nIMPLICIT: ESI register used as loop pointer\n\nReturns:\nvoid - no return value\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x6fbf6778 - Array start address (validation error buffer)\n0x6fbf67ec - Array end boundary address\n0x4 - Dword stride between entries\n0x109 - Total entries in array ((0x6fbf67ec - 0x6fbf6778) / 4)\n\nError Handling:\nReportValidationError() called for each non-zero error code found. Entry cleared after reporting to prevent duplicate reports on next iteration.\n\nNote:\nFunction uses one register variable (ESI) optimized away by decompiler into piVar1. Cannot set type on this phantom variable in decompiled view - it exists only in assembly.\n\nRelated Functions:\n- ReportValidationError() - Reports validation error code to error log\n- FUN_6fb5a220() - Caller in game shutdown sequence",
