      "comment": "Initialize palette color lookup tables.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if initialization flag is 0 (first-time init)\n2. If flag is 0, check initialization flag variable (DAT_6fbf67f3)\n3. If already initialized, return early\n4. Set initialization flag to prevent redundant initialization\n5. Call Ordinal_10034 with parameters (0, 0x80, 0) and store AL result in g_bPaletteBlue\n6. Call Ordinal_10034 with parameters (0xc0, 0xc0, 0) and store AL result in g_bPaletteGreen\n7. Call Ordinal_10034 with parameters (0xff, 0, 0) and store AL result in g_bPaletteRed\n8. Return\n\nParameters:\ndwInitFlag - Initialization control flag (ECX register). Value 0 checks first-init flag; non-zero skips first-init check\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Function performs initialization side-effects, no return value\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x80 - Blue channel component value\n0xc0 - Green channel component value\n0xff - Red channel component value\n\nNotes:\nFunction uses conditional logic to prevent re-initialization. When dwInitFlag is non-zero, initialization is performed unconditionally. When dwInitFlag is 0, function checks a static guard variable to execute initialization only once.",
