      "comment": "Updates player roster dialog and manages associated UI elements in response to roster changes.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize search context and UI state variables\n2. Check scroll window mode (2=inactive, 3=inactive) and return if necessary\n3. Verify UI state conditions (flag 9 and 11 must be clear, inventory state not 2)\n4. Call FUN_6fb644b0 to get player ID and store in search key\n5. If player ID invalid (-1) or inventory active, jump to cleanup\n6. Loop through player nodes: Get next player, extract ID and unit field\n7. For matching player IDs, retrieve unit type and select corresponding data array (validation errors, item stats, etc.)\n8. If table found, calculate display offset using division formula (index * 0x2e) / 100\n9. Initialize palette colors, select color index based on player index thresholds (0x50 vs 0x19)\n10. Call Ordinal_10055 twice to render sprite and clear overlay area\n11. Process roster field, build UI structures, populate array with 18 dwords\n12. Call Ordinal_10072 to render UI element, set bVar2=true\n13. Move to next player node, repeat until end of list\n14. If no player matched, skip to next section\n15. Search for node by criteria (type 7, value 0)\n16. If found, get linked list value and map to local_2d8 table index (0x167->7, 0x10f->5, 0x152->6, 0x230/0x231->2)\n17. Call FUN_6fb07180 to process found node\n18. Get field pointer from search result\n19. If pointer valid, initialize 29-dword buffer, call FUN_6fb638b0\n20. Copy string data, process field display\n21. Store source and current pointers to global variables DAT_6fbf67f8/f4\n22. Call FUN_6fb07ae0 through FUN_6fb073d0 for fields 2,3,4,5,6,10,11,12,15,16\n23. If all field checks return 0 and no player/dialog found, call error handler FUN_6fb5d370(0x13,1,0)\n24. Check hiring dialog state (0x6fbf6804) and trigger popup if needed\n25. If roster changed flag set, initialize Unicode buffer and build message string\n26. Call Ordinal_10004 three times to get key binding strings\n27. Use GetKeyBindingStringId to retrieve action key ID\n28. Call sprintf to format message with retrieved strings\n29. Call strcat twice to append to dialog buffer\n30. Call Ordinal_10129 to update UI element at offset 0x24\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Function processes up to 18-element UI arrays per roster update\n- Color selection uses nested thresholds: default (0xf0), 0x32+ (0xf1), 0x19+ (0xf2)\n- Division formula (index*0x2e)/100 calculates UI positioning with specific stride\n- Multiple ordinal function calls (Ordinal_10055, 10072, 10004, 10129) handle rendering and UI updates\n- Unicode string formatting includes key binding lookups for user display",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_StatList", "PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Path", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "STRUCT_Skill", "STRUCT_Room1", "STRUCT_ItemData", "PARAM_0", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
