      "instructions": ["0x37180|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [ESP + 0x4]", "0x37184|PUSH|EBX", "0x37185|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0x37187|PUSH|ESI", "0x37188|MOV|EBX, EDX", "0x3718A|JZ|0x6fb07193", "0x3718C|CALL|0x6fae1780", "0x37191|JMP|0x6fb07198", "0x37193|CALL|0x6fae0730", "0x37198|MOV|ESI, EAX", "0x3719A|TEST|ESI, ESI", "0x3719C|JZ|0x6fb0725c", "0x371A2|LEA|ECX, [ESI + ESI*0x2]", "0x371A5|MOV|EAX, 0x51eb851f", "0x371AA|SHL|ECX, 0x3"],
      "comment": "Render skill level indicator bars on automap display for a player slot.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Determine player slot data lookup method based on nSearchNode (0=by player ID, else=by packed value)\n2. Retrieve player slot index using FindPlayerSlotDataByPlayerId or SearchLinkedListForPackedValue\n3. If player slot not found (index is 0), return without rendering\n4. Calculate Y coordinate as (nPlayerSlotIndex * 46) / 100 + nX (health bar scaling)\n5. Initialize palette colors on first call: bPaletteColorsInitialized = 1\n6. Call Ordinal_10034 three times to retrieve RGB color palette entries:\n   - Medium health (50-99%): 0x80 green (R=128, G=128, B=0)\n   - Low health (25-49%): 0xC0 cyan (R=192, G=192, B=0)\n   - Critical health (0-24%): 0xFF yellow (R=255, G=0, B=0)\n7. Select health color based on slot index threshold:\n   - If nPlayerSlotIndex >= 50 (0x32): use medium color\n   - If nPlayerSlotIndex >= 25 (0x19): use low color\n   - If nPlayerSlotIndex < 25: use critical color\n8. Render two line segments with Ordinal_10055 (draw line):\n   - First segment: from nX to nYCoord with width 0xE, length 0x13, color selected, style 5\n   - Second segment: from nYCoord to nX+46, width 0xE, length 0x13, color 0, style 5\n\nParameters:\nnPlayerId (ECX) - Player ID to look up slot data for\nnX (EDX) - Base X pixel coordinate for bar rendering\nnSearchNode (stack) - Search context: 0 for direct lookup, non-zero for packed value lookup\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Function performs rendering side effects only\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x2E - 46 bytes: player slot data structure size or health bar pixel length\n0x32 - 50 decimal: health percentage threshold for medium color selection\n0x19 - 25 decimal: health percentage threshold for low/critical color selection\n0x80 - RGB green palette entry (medium health indicator)\n0xC0 - RGB cyan palette entry (low health indicator)\n0xFF - RGB yellow palette entry (critical health indicator)\n0x0E - 14: line width or bar dimension\n0x13 - 19: line length or bar dimension\n5 - line style constant (solid or dash pattern)\n\nRelated Functions:\n- FindPlayerSlotDataByPlayerId() - Retrieve slot data by player ID (direct lookup)\n- SearchLinkedListForPackedValue() - Search packed value list (indirect lookup)\n- Ordinal_10034() - D2Common.GetPalette (retrieve color from palette)\n- Ordinal_10055() - D2Win.DrawLine (render line segment on screen)",
      "tags": ["PARAM_3"]
    },
