      "comment": "Initializes Unicode string buffer from ANSI input with configuration processing.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate 58-element Unicode character array on stack (116 bytes)\n2. Initialize Unicode elements via default constructor loop, 0x3c iterations with 2-byte stride\n3. Call Unicode::toUnicode to convert ANSI input string to Unicode with 0x3c count\n4. Call Ordinal_10127 for initialization setup\n5. Fetch counter from Ordinal_10121\n6. Loop: while counter > 0x42, decrement buffer pointer, zero ushort value\n7. Call Ordinal_10121 again for state check\n8. Calculate offset: sign-extend, modulo 2, SAR by 1, add 0x16\n9. Clamp result to zero if negative\n10. Call Ordinal_10117 with nFlags parameter and two zero values\n11. Call Ordinal_10127 again for cleanup\n12. Return\n\nParameters:\n- this: ANSI input string pointer (__thiscall implicit parameter)\n- nFlags: Configuration flags passed to Ordinal_10117\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No explicit return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Fixed 0x3c (60) element capacity\n- Cleanup loop terminates at counter <= 0x42\n- Arithmetic adjustment value clamped to >= 0\n- Ordinal functions provide stateful processing\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x3c: 60 elements (Unicode array capacity)\n- 0x42: 66 decimal (loop threshold)\n- 0x16: 22 decimal (offset constant)\n- 0x78: 120 decimal (stack allocation)",
