      "comment": "Apply delta adjustment to a value, either subtracting an existing delta or adding a default increment.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load the delta value from pnDelta\n2. If delta is zero (no existing delta):\n   a. Set delta to 10\n   b. Add 10 to the value at pnValue\n   c. Return\n3. If delta is non-zero (existing delta to apply):\n   a. Subtract delta from the value at pnValue\n   b. Clear the delta by setting pnDelta to 0\n   c. Return\n\nParameters:\npnValue: Pointer to the integer value to be adjusted (passed in ECX). Can be increased by 10 or decreased by the stored delta value.\npnDelta: Pointer to the delta value (passed in EDX). If zero, delta is set to 10; if non-zero, its value is subtracted from pnValue then cleared.\n\nReturns:\nvoid. Both input values are modified in-place through pointers.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- When pnDelta is 0, adds 10 to pnValue and stores 10 in pnDelta\n- When pnDelta is non-zero, subtracts delta from pnValue and clears pnDelta to 0\n- Uses ESI register for temporary storage during subtraction operation\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x0a (10): Default delta increment and value added when no delta exists",
      "tags": ["PARAM_2", "PROP_LEAF", "PROP_SMALL"]
