      "comment": "Validates node in search context and renders palette-based data visualization.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Find node by search criteria in context using nNodeType\n2. Return 0 immediately if node not found (ID = 0xFFFFFFFF)\n3. Validate nNodeType and set dwTypeConstant based on value (0x02->0x0F, 0x0F->0x14, 0x10->0x1B)\n4. Retrieve search result data (nSearchResult) by node ID\n5. Initialize palette rendering if not already done (set g_bPaletteRenderingFlag, create color table)\n6. Select palette color based on nSearchResult thresholds (0x32, 0x19)\n7. Render visualization bars (two bars with height 0x13, width 0x0E)\n8. Initialize local string buffer (58 Unicode chars) and populate via constructor\n9. Execute type-specific processing based on nNodeType (cases 2-6, 10-16)\n10. Process string data via Ordinal_10004, strcpy, Ordinal_10127 sequence\n11. Loop reading buffer content until <= 0x42 bytes\n12. Flush remaining buffer via additional Ordinal_10127 call\n13. Adjust position counters (if pnPosZ zero: set 10 and increment pnPosY; else decrement pnPosY by pnPosZ)\n14. Initialize 18-element data array with zeros\n15. Set array[1] to validation error value from g_adValidationErrorArray[dwTypeConstant]\n16. Call Ordinal_10072 to display validation data\n17. Increment pnPosX by 0x38\n18. Return 1 (success)\n\nParameters:\n- pSearchContext: Pointer to search context structure (ECX register, __fastcall)\n- nNodeType: Type selector value (EDX register): 0x02=TypeA, 0x0F=TypeB, 0x10=TypeC\n- pnPosX: Pointer to X position (stack param), incremented by result\n- pnPosY: Pointer to Y position (stack param), adjusted by displacement\n- pnPosZ: Pointer to Z value (stack param), temporary offset used for calculation\n\nReturns:\n- 1: Success - validation and rendering completed\n- 0: Failure - invalid node type or node not found",
