      "comment": "Process skill display with validation and rendering.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get skill usage limit for unit and skill ID\n2. Return 0 if limit is 0 (skill not available)\n3. Map skill ID to display index using switch\n4. If limit == 1 and valid ID, find player node by search\n5. Get player slot data or packed list value\n6. Calculate display value: (value * 46) / 100 + index\n7. Initialize palette if first call\n8. Select color based on value thresholds\n9. Render filled and empty bars\n10. Initialize Unicode buffers\n11. Zero error array\n12. Load strings from config\n13. Convert to Unicode format\n14. Copy to buffer with strncpy\n15. Trim if exceeds max length\n16. Render ordinals and set parameters\n17. Build skill name from switch table\n18. Display final text\n19. Update display offset\n\nParameters:\npUnit - Unit performing skill (ECX)\ndwSkillId - Skill ID (EDX)\npnPrimaryIndex - Bar position\npnDisplayObject - Display surface\npnDisplayOffset - Offset counter\n\nReturns:\n1 on success\n0 if skill unavailable",
