      "comment": "Validates if a hit position falls within the dialog bounds and sets validation flags.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call GetGlobalSystemState to check if system is active\n2. If system inactive (returns 0), exit immediately\n3. Clear hit result field at pHitInfo->dwResultState\n4. Initialize both validation flags (g_fEntityValidationFlag, g_fNodeFoundFlag) to 0\n5. Extract X coordinate from low 16 bits of pHitInfo->dwPackedCoords\n6. Extract Y coordinate from high 16 bits of pHitInfo->dwPackedCoords\n7. If inventory state is 2 (busy/locked), clear flags and exit\n8. If X < g_nDialogMinX (left bound), clear flags and exit\n9. If X > g_nDialogMinX + 0x2e (right bound), clear flags and exit\n10. If Y < 0x18 (top bound), clear flags and exit\n11. If Y >= 0x3d (bottom bound), clear flags and exit\n12. Position is within dialog bounds - proceed with validation\n13. Get game context; if valid, get inventory owner from offset 0x84\n14. If no game context or no inventory owner:\n    a. Search for node with criteria type 7, value 0\n    b. If node found (result != -1), set g_fNodeFoundFlag = 1\n15. Call ValidateEntityProperties(0)\n16. If entity validation succeeds, set g_fEntityValidationFlag = 1\n\nParameters:\npHitInfo (DialogHitInfo *) - Pointer to hit test info structure:\n    +0x0c dwPackedCoords: uint - packed coordinates (low 16 = X, high 16 = Y)\n    +0x18 dwResultState: uint - result/state field (cleared by this function)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Results communicated via global flags:\n    g_fEntityValidationFlag - Set to 1 if ValidateEntityProperties succeeds\n    g_fNodeFoundFlag - Set to 1 if dialog node found via FindNodeBySearchCriteria\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Inventory state 2 causes immediate exit with flags cleared\n- Dialog bounds: X in [g_nDialogMinX, g_nDialogMinX+0x2e], Y in [0x18, 0x3c]\n- Node search only performed when no inventory owner exists\n- Both flags cleared on any bounds check failure\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x2e (46) - Dialog width in pixels\n0x18 (24) - Dialog top Y bound\n0x3c (60) - Dialog bottom Y bound (exclusive, check uses < 0x3d)\n0x84 - Offset to inventory pointer in game context\n7 - Search criteria type for dialog node lookup",
