      "comment": "Update inventory dialog state machine based on server connectivity.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Read current state from g_dwInventoryState (0=closed, 1=opening, 2=open)\n2. If state == 0 (closed):\n   a. Check server connectivity via GetCurrentServerPort()\n   b. If connected (non-zero): transition to state 1, notify UI deactivate (0x23, 0)\n   c. If not connected: transition to state 2, notify UI activate (0x23, 1)\n3. If state == 1 (opening):\n   a. Check server connectivity via GetCurrentServerPort()\n   b. If still connected: transition to state 2, notify UI activate (0x23, 1)\n   c. If disconnected: transition to state 0, notify UI deactivate (0x23, 0)\n4. If state >= 2 (open or any other):\n   a. Reset to state 0, notify UI deactivate (0x23, 0)\n\nParameters:\nNone - uses global state\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nState Machine:\nState 0 (Closed) + Server Connected -> State 1 (Opening) + UI Deactivate\nState 0 (Closed) + No Server -> State 2 (Open) + UI Activate\nState 1 (Opening) + Server Connected -> State 2 (Open) + UI Activate\nState 1 (Opening) + No Server -> State 0 (Closed) + UI Deactivate\nState 2+ (Open/Other) -> State 0 (Closed) + UI Deactivate\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x23 - UI element ID for inventory/hireling dialog system\n0, 1, 2 - State values: closed, opening, open\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- No callers in xref analysis - likely called via function pointer table\n- Uses g_dwInventoryState at 0x6fbf67ec shared with inventory UI functions\n- ProcessUIStateChange second param: 0=deactivate, 1=activate",
