      "comment": "Renders the copyright/credits screen during game startup.\n\nDisplays Blizzard copyright text and either expansion or classic credits\ndepending on whether the Lord of Destruction MPQ files are present.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call Ordinal_10026 to check if game window is minimized/inactive\n2. If inactive (EAX != 0), exit early\n3. Call RenderScene to render base scene\n4. If render fails (EAX == 0), exit early\n5. Initialize graphics interface (GfxInterface_CallMethod0xC4)\n6. Clean up palette state (ProcessPaletteCleanup)\n7. Zero-initialize 72-byte GFX render info structure (18 DWORDs)\n8. Set render info fields: DC handle = popup background, frame = 0\n9. Draw left background panel at (UIXOffset + 0xBC, 0x148 - UIYOffset)\n10. Draw right background panel at (UIXOffset + 0x1BC, 0x148 - UIYOffset)\n11. Save current font, set font ID 1 (copyright font)\n12. Validate and draw first copyright string (ID 0x1430) centered\n13. Check if expansion MPQ exists (CheckExpansionMpqExists)\n14. If expansion: validate string 0x5578 (LoD credits)\n    Else: validate string 0x1431 (classic credits)\n15. Draw credits string centered below copyright\n16. Restore previous font\n17. Zero-initialize render info again for OK button\n18. Set render info: DC = OK button handle, frame = button frame index\n19. Draw OK button at (UIXOffset + 0x110, 0x13E - UIYOffset)\n20. Set font 1, validate string 0x13EE (OK text)\n21. Draw OK text centered on button\n22. Restore font, finalize screen drawing, reinitialize GFX interface\n\nParameters: None\n\nReturns: void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Early exit if game window minimized (Ordinal_10026 returns non-zero)\n- Early exit if RenderScene fails\n- Different copyright text for expansion vs classic\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x1430 - String ID: Blizzard copyright notice\n0x1431 - String ID: Classic D2 credits\n0x5578 - String ID: Lord of Destruction credits  \n0x13EE - String ID: \"OK\" button text\n0xBC (188) - Left panel X offset from UI base\n0x1BC (444) - Right panel X offset from UI base\n0x148 (328) - Panel Y position base\n0xBE (190) - First text line Y position base\n0xCD (205) - Second text line Y position base\n0x84 (132) - Half-width offset for centering\n0x1C4 (452) - Text right boundary offset\n0x110 (272) - OK button X offset\n0x13E (318) - OK button Y position base\n0x136 (310) - OK text Y position base\n0x170 (368) - OK text right boundary offset\n\nStructure Layout (adGfxRenderInfo - 72 bytes):\nOffset  Size  Field           Type    Description\n0x00    4     dwUnknown0      uint    Reserved/flags\n0x04    4     nDcHandle       uint    DC/surface handle\n0x08    4     nFrameIndex     uint    Animation frame\n0x0C    4     dwUnknown3      uint    Always 0 in this function\n0x10-0x44     dwReserved[14]  uint    Reserved fields\n\nSSA Variables (decompiler-generated, cannot rename):\niVar2 (nPreviousFontId): Saved font ID before changing to font 1\npuVar3 (pdwRenderInfoPtr): Iterator for zeroing render info array\nuVar4 (dwColorFlags): Color flags parameter (always 0)\nwszText, wszText_00, wszText_01: Wide string pointers from ValidateStringId\nextraout_EAX: Return values from Ordinal_10026 and RenderScene\nfExpansionExists: Boolean result from CheckExpansionMpqExists",
      "tags": ["PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PROP_NOCALLER", "STRUCT_ItemData", "PARAM_0", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
