      "comment": "Displays a popup OK dialog used for informational messages in the main menu system.\n\nClassification: Initialization/Public API - Creates and manages popup dialog lifecycle.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Clear dialog result flag (g_fPopupDialogResult = 0)\n2. Initialize cleanup timer with disabled state (false parameter)\n3. Load popup background texture from Data\\Global\\UI\\Bigmenu\\popupok path twice:\n   - First load stored to g_nPopupBackgroundDcHandle\n   - Second load stored to g_nSecondaryBackgroundDcHandle (duplicate for mirrored rendering)\n4. Load OK/Cancel button texture from Data\\Global\\UI\\Menu\\okcancelbtn path\n   - Result stored to g_nOkButtonDcHandle\n5. Compare palette buffers for consistency\n6. Set active pointer index to 1 (dialog cursor mode)\n7. Get initialization flag and register 4 message handlers from g_aPopupOkMessageEntries\n8. Enter message pump loop with RenderPopupOkDialog callback\n   - Loop continues until user clicks OK button or closes dialog\n9. Unregister message handlers (ProcessMessageArray with same entry array)\n10. Reset active pointer index to 0 (normal cursor mode)\n11. Cleanup loaded textures:\n    - Free g_nPopupBackgroundDcHandle if non-zero, then clear\n    - Free g_nSecondaryBackgroundDcHandle if non-zero, then clear\n    - Free g_nOkButtonDcHandle if non-zero, then clear\n12. Reload palettes to restore graphics state\n13. Return 1 (EAX) on completion\n\nParameters:\n  None - Function takes no parameters.\n\nReturns:\n  int - Always returns 1 (success) after dialog closes\n\nCross-References:\n  Called from PlayVideoById at 3 locations (0x6fad18a2, 0x6fad19de, 0x6fad1b7f)\n  Used as data reference, likely in message handler or callback table\n\nGlobals Used:\n  g_fPopupDialogResult (0x6fbf6824) - Dialog result flag, set by OK button handler\n  g_nPopupBackgroundDcHandle (0x6fbf680c) - DC handle for popup background texture\n  g_nOkButtonDcHandle (0x6fbf6810) - DC handle for OK button texture\n  g_nSecondaryBackgroundDcHandle (0x6fbf6814) - Secondary DC handle for mirrored background\n  g_aPopupOkMessageEntries (0x6fbb3640) - Message handler entry array (4 entries)\n  g_szPopupOkBackgroundPath (0x6fbb36c0) - Path string for popup background\n  g_szOkCancelButtonPath (0x6fbb36a0) - Path string for button texture\n\nCallees:\n  InitializeCleanupTimer - Initializes/disables cleanup timer\n  ConcatenatePathAndWriteFile - Loads texture resources by path\n  ComparePaletteBuffers - Validates palette consistency\n  SetActivePointerIndex - Sets cursor mode (0=normal, 1=dialog)\n  GetInitFlag - Gets initialization state flag\n  ProcessMessageEntryArray - Registers message handlers\n  ProcessMessagePumpWithCallback - Main message loop with render callback\n  ProcessMessageArray - Unregisters message handlers\n  ReportValidationError - Frees texture DC handles\n  LoadPalettes - Restores palette state\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0 - Normal cursor mode / false initialization flag\n  1 - Dialog cursor mode / success return value\n  4 - Number of message handler entries in g_aPopupOkMessageEntries",
