      "comment": "Displays a popup OK dialog for informational messages (alternate entry point).\n\nClassification: Initialization/Public API - Duplicate implementation of DisplayPopupOkDialog.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Clear dialog result flag (g_fPopupDialogResult = 0)\n2. Initialize cleanup timer with disabled state (ECX=0)\n3. Load popup background texture from Data\\Global\\UI\\Bigmenu\\popupok path twice:\n   - First load result stored to g_nPopupBackgroundDcHandle\n   - Second load result stored to g_nPopupBackgroundDcHandleAlt (mirrored rendering)\n4. Load OK/Cancel button texture from Data\\Global\\UI\\Menu\\okcancelbtn path\n   - Result stored to g_nOkButtonDcHandle\n5. Compare palette buffers for consistency\n6. Set active pointer index to 1 (dialog cursor mode)\n7. Get initialization flag and register 4 message handlers from g_aPopupOkMessageEntries\n8. Enter message pump loop with RenderPopupOkDialog callback\n9. Unregister message handlers (ProcessMessageArray with same entry array)\n10. Reset active pointer index to 0 (normal cursor mode)\n11. Cleanup loaded textures:\n    - Free g_nPopupBackgroundDcHandle if non-zero, then clear\n    - Free g_nPopupBackgroundDcHandleAlt if non-zero, then clear\n    - Free g_nOkButtonDcHandle if non-zero, then clear\n12. Reload palettes to restore graphics state\n13. Return 1 (success)\n\nParameters:\n  None - Function takes no parameters.\n\nReturns:\n  int - Always returns 1 (success) after dialog closes\n\nCross-References:\n  Called from PlayVideoById at 0x6fad1b77\n\nGlobals Used:\n  g_fPopupDialogResult (0x6fbf6824) - Dialog result flag\n  g_nPopupBackgroundDcHandle (0x6fbf680c) - DC handle for popup background\n  g_nPopupBackgroundDcHandleAlt (0x6fbf6814) - Secondary DC handle for mirrored background\n  g_nOkButtonDcHandle (0x6fbf6810) - DC handle for OK button texture\n  g_aPopupOkMessageEntries (0x6fbb3640) - Message handler entry array (4 entries)\n  g_szPopupOkBackgroundPath (0x6fbb36c0) - Path: Data\\Global\\UI\\Bigmenu\\popupok\n  g_szOkCancelButtonPath (0x6fbb36a0) - Path: Data\\Global\\UI\\Menu\\okcancelbtn\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0 - Normal cursor mode / false initialization flag / zero DC handle\n  1 - Dialog cursor mode / success return value\n  4 - Number of message handler entries\n\nNote: This function is a duplicate of DisplayPopupOkDialog (0x6fb088b0) with identical implementation.",
