      "comment": "Handles OK button click detection for UI dialogs.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load UI screen offset from g_dwUIXOffset and g_dwUIYOffset globals\n2. Calculate button bounding box:\n   - X bounds: [UIXOffset + 0x110, UIXOffset + 0x170] (272 to 368 pixels relative)\n   - Y bounds: [-UIYOffset + 0x116, -UIYOffset + 0x136] (278 to 310 pixels relative)\n3. Get current mouse position via GetCurrentResourceID() (X) and GetResourceFlags() (Y)\n4. If mouse position within button bounds:\n   a. Set g_nOkButtonFrameIndex = 1 (pressed frame)\n   b. Set g_fOkButtonPressed = 1 (button state flag)\n   c. Call InitializeGameObjectProperties(4, 0, 0.0, 0.0, 0) to setup button response\n   d. Set message handled flag at [dwUIMessagePtr + 0x18] = 1\n   e. Set message result at [dwUIMessagePtr + 0x1c] = 0\n   f. Insert message into cache via InsertCacheNodeWithCookie\n5. If mouse outside button bounds:\n   a. Call ClearTargetingState() to reset targeting system\n   b. Set message handled flag at [dwUIMessagePtr + 0x18] = 1\n   c. Set message result at [dwUIMessagePtr + 0x1c] = 0\n   d. Insert message into cache via InsertCacheNodeWithCookie\n\nParameters:\n  dwUIMessagePtr (uint) - Pointer to UI message structure (passed as uint)\n    +0x18: dwHandled - Message handled flag (set to 1 on completion)\n    +0x1c: dwResult - Message result code (set to 0)\n\nReturns:\n  void - Message structure modified in place\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Button bounds are relative to UI screen offset which varies by resolution\n  - Both click inside and outside button paths mark message as handled\n  - ClearTargetingState called only when click is outside button bounds\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x110 (272) - Button left edge offset from UI origin\n  0x170 (368) - Button right edge offset from UI origin\n  0x116 (278) - Button top edge offset from UI origin\n  0x136 (310) - Button bottom edge offset from UI origin\n  0x18 - UIMessage dwHandled field offset\n  0x1c - UIMessage dwResult field offset",
      "tags": ["PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_1", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
