      "comment": "Handles mouse button release on popup OK dialog button.\n\nClassification: Callback - UI event handler for popup dialog OK button release.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Reset OK button frame index to 0 (unpressed visual state)\n2. Check if button was pressed (g_fOkButtonPressed != 0)\n3. If not pressed, skip to step 8 (clear targeting state)\n4. Calculate OK button bounding box from UI offsets\n5. Get current mouse position via GetCurrentResourceID (X) and GetResourceFlags (Y)\n6. If mouse within button bounds: set dialog result, clear pressed flag, mark handled, return\n7. If mouse outside bounds, fall through to step 8\n8. Call ClearTargetingState to reset UI state\n9. Mark message as handled and insert into cache\n\nParameters:\n  pUIMessage (UIInputMessage *) - Pointer to UI message structure\n    +0x18: fHandled - Message handled flag (set to 1)\n    +0x1c: dwResult - Message result (set to 0)\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nGlobals Used:\n  g_dwUIXOffset (0x6fbfd7fc) - UI horizontal centering offset\n  g_dwUIYOffset (0x6fbfd800) - UI vertical centering offset\n  g_nOkButtonFrameIndex (0x6fbf681c) - Button animation frame\n  g_fOkButtonPressed (0x6fbf6818) - Flag indicating button was pressed\n  g_fPopupDialogResult (0x6fbf6824) - Dialog confirmation result\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x110 (272) - OK button left edge X offset\n  0x170 (368) - OK button right edge X offset\n  0x116 (278) - OK button top edge Y offset\n  0x136 (310) - OK button bottom edge Y offset",
