      "comment": "Confirms and dismisses the popup OK dialog, marking the UI message as handled.\n\nClassification: Callback - UI event handler for forced dialog dismissal.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Set g_fPopupDialogResult to 1 (confirmed state triggers message pump exit)\n2. Set g_fOkButtonPressed to 0 (clear button pressed state)\n3. Call ClearTargetingState to reset UI targeting system variables\n4. Set pUIMessage->dwProcessed to 1 (mark message as handled)\n5. Set pUIMessage->dwResult to 0 (no error result)\n6. Call InsertCacheNodeWithCookie to queue message for cache processing\n7. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\n  pUIMessage (UIInputMessage *) - Pointer to UI input message structure\n    +0x18 dwProcessed: Set to 1 to mark message handled\n    +0x1c dwResult: Set to 0 (success/no error)\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value\n\nGlobals Modified:\n  g_fPopupDialogResult (0x6fbf6824) - Set to 1 to signal dialog confirmation\n  g_fOkButtonPressed (0x6fbf6818) - Cleared to 0 to reset button state\n\nCallees:\n  ClearTargetingState - Resets g_fTargetingEnabled, g_fTargetingActive, g_dwUICommandPending\n  InsertCacheNodeWithCookie - Queues message structure for cache node processing\n\nRelated Functions:\n  HandleOkButtonRelease - Similar handler that validates mouse position first\n  DisplayPopupOkDialog - Creates popup that this function dismisses\n  RenderPopupOkDialog - Returns true when g_fPopupDialogResult != 0",
