      "api_calls": ["GfxUpdateWindowVisibility", "RenderScene", "GfxInterface_CallMethod0xC4", "ProcessPaletteCleanup", "GfxInterfaceCall84", "GfxInterfaceCall84", "SetActiveFont", "ValidateStringId", "ValidateStringId", "SetActiveFont", "...+7 more"],
      "instructions": ["0x38E90|SUB|ESP, 0x48", "0x38E93|CALL|0x6fb992c2", "0x38E98|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0x38E9A|JNZ|0x6fb090e6", "0x38EA0|PUSH|EAX", "0x38EA1|PUSH|EAX", "0x38EA2|PUSH|EAX", "0x38EA3|PUSH|0x1", "0x38EA5|CALL|0x6fb992b6", "0x38EAA|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0x38EAC|JZ|0x6fb090e6", "0x38EB2|PUSH|ESI", "0x38EB3|PUSH|EDI", "0x38EB4|PUSH|0x0", "0x38EB6|CALL|0x6fb992b0"],
      "comment": "Renders the video options confirmation dialog with OK/Cancel buttons.\n\nCalled from function pointer table (DATA xref at 0x6fbaf3e8) as UI callback handler.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call Ordinal_10026 to check if dialog should be displayed\n2. If result is non-zero, exit early (dialog not needed)\n3. Call RenderScene with g_InvalidTooltipMarker to check render state\n4. If render state fails (returns 0), exit early\n5. Initialize graphics interface (GfxInterface_CallMethod0xC4, ProcessPaletteCleanup)\n6. Clear 18-element draw params array (72 bytes) via REP STOSD\n7. Draw left popup background panel at (UIXOffset + 0xBC, 0x148 - UIYOffset)\n8. Draw right popup background panel at (UIXOffset + 0x1BC, 0x148 - UIYOffset)\n9. Set font to ID 1, save previous font ID\n10. Validate and draw title text (StringId 0x1430) centered at (screenWidth/2 - 0x84, 0xBE - UIYOffset)\n11. Select subtitle StringId based on g_dwCurrentVideoId (0x1432 if 0, 0x5578 otherwise)\n12. Validate and draw subtitle text centered at (screenWidth/2 - 0x84, 0xCD - UIYOffset)\n13. Restore previous font\n14. Cache g_nCancelButtonFrameIndex for Cancel button\n15. Clear draw params array again\n16. Draw OK button at (UIXOffset + 0xCE, 0x13E - UIYOffset) using g_nOkButtonDcHandle\n17. Draw Cancel button at (UIXOffset + 0x152, 0x13E - UIYOffset) using cached frame index\n18. Set font to ID 1 again, save previous font\n19. Validate and draw OK button label (StringId 0x13EE) at button position\n20. Validate and draw Cancel button label (StringId 0x13EF) at button position\n21. Restore font\n22. Call ProcessScreenResourceDrawing and GfxInitializeInterface to finalize\n\nParameters: None (void)\n\nReturns: void\n\nGlobals Used:\n  g_InvalidTooltipMarker - Marker for invalid tooltip state check\n  g_nPopupBackgroundDcHandleAlt - DC handle for popup background panels\n  g_dwUIXOffset - Horizontal UI offset for positioning\n  g_dwUIYOffset - Vertical UI offset for positioning\n  g_dwScreenWidth - Screen width for centering calculations\n  g_dwCurrentVideoId - Video mode ID (determines subtitle string)\n  g_nOkButtonDcHandle - DC handle for OK button graphic\n  g_nOkButtonFrameIndex - Frame index for OK button animation\n  g_nCancelButtonFrameIndex - Frame index for Cancel button animation\n\nString IDs:\n  0x1430 - Dialog title text\n  0x1432 - Subtitle when video ID is 0\n  0x5578 - Subtitle when video ID is non-zero\n  0x13EE - OK button label\n  0x13EF - Cancel button label\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x12 (18) - Draw params array element count\n  0xBC (188) - Left panel X offset from UIXOffset\n  0x1BC (444) - Right panel X offset from UIXOffset\n  0x148 (328) - Panel Y base position\n  0xBE (190) - Title text Y position\n  0xCD (205) - Subtitle text Y position\n  0xCE (206) - OK button X offset\n  0x152 (338) - Cancel button X offset\n  0x13E (318) - Button Y base position\n  0x136 (310) - Button label Y position\n  0x12E (302) - OK button label right boundary\n  0x1B2 (434) - Cancel button label right boundary\n  0x1C4 (452) - Text right boundary\n  0x84 (132) - Half-width offset for centering",
      "tags": ["PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PROP_NOCALLER", "STRUCT_ItemData", "PARAM_0", "STRUCT_Control"]
