      "api_count": 2,
      "api_calls": ["InsertCacheNodeWithCookie", "InsertCacheNodeWithCookie"],
      "instructions": ["0x391E0|MOV|EAX, [0x6fbfd7fc]", "0x391E5|MOV|EDX, dword ptr [0x6fbfd800]", "0x391EB|PUSH|EBX", "0x391EC|PUSH|ESI", "0x391ED|MOV|ESI, 0x136", "0x391F2|PUSH|EDI", "0x391F3|SUB|ESI, EDX", "0x391F5|LEA|EDI, [EAX + 0xce]", "0x391FB|CALL|0x6fb8f680", "0x39200|MOV|EBX, EAX", "0x39202|CALL|0x6fb8f690", "0x39207|CMP|EBX, EDI", "0x39209|JL|0x6fb0922a", "0x3920B|ADD|EDI, 0x60", "0x3920E|CMP|EBX, EDI"],
      "comment": "Handles mouse click events for dialog OK/Cancel buttons.\n\nChecks if click position (from GetCurrentResourceID/GetResourceFlags) falls within\nOK button bounds or Cancel button bounds, sets appropriate frame index and pressed\nstate, then finalizes event context.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load UI offset globals (g_dwUIXOffset, g_dwUIYOffset)\n2. Calculate OK button bounds: X=[xOffset+0xCE, xOffset+0x12E], Y=[-yOffset+0x116, -yOffset+0x136]\n3. Get current mouse position via GetCurrentResourceID (X) and GetResourceFlags (Y)\n4. If mouse within OK button bounds:\n   a. Set g_nOkButtonFrameIndex = 1\n   b. Jump to step 8\n5. Recalculate Cancel button bounds: X=[xOffset+0x152, xOffset+0x1B2], Y=[-yOffset+0x116, -yOffset+0x136]\n6. Get mouse position again\n7. If mouse NOT within Cancel button bounds:\n   a. Call ClearTargetingState to reset UI state\n   b. Set event context fields and call InsertCacheNodeWithCookie\n   c. Return early\n8. Set g_nCancelButtonFrameIndex = 1 (if Cancel hit)\n9. Set g_fOkButtonPressed = 1 (button press acknowledged)\n10. Call InitializeGameObjectProperties(4, 0, 0.0, 0.0, 0)\n11. Set event context offset +0x18 = 1 (processed flag)\n12. Set event context offset +0x1C = 0 (result code)\n13. Call InsertCacheNodeWithCookie to queue event\n\nParameters:\n  dwEventContext - Pointer to event context structure passed as uint\n                   Fields: +0x18 = processed flag, +0x1C = result code\n\nReturns:\n  void - Results communicated via event context structure\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Click outside both buttons: clears targeting state and returns\n  - Click on OK button: sets OK frame index, processes as button press\n  - Click on Cancel button: sets Cancel frame index, processes as button press\n\nButton Bounds (relative to UI offsets):\n  OK Button:     X=[+0xCE, +0x12E] (96 pixels wide), Y=[0x116, 0x136] (32 pixels tall)\n  Cancel Button: X=[+0x152, +0x1B2] (96 pixels wide), Y=[0x116, 0x136] (32 pixels tall)",
      "tags": ["PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_1", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
    },
