      "comment": "Process OK/Cancel button mouse release event for popup dialogs\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Reset button frame indices to 0 (no hover state)\n2. Check if OK button was in pressed state (g_fOkButtonPressed)\n3. If not pressed, call ClearTargetingState and skip hit-testing\n4. If pressed, compute OK button bounding rect:\n   - X: [UIXOffset + 0xCE, UIXOffset + 0x12E] (width = 0x60 = 96 pixels)\n   - Y: [0x116 - UIYOffset, 0x136 - UIYOffset] (height = 0x20 = 32 pixels)\n5. Get current mouse position via GetCurrentResourceID (X) and GetResourceFlags (Y)\n6. If mouse within OK button bounds, set g_fOkConfirmedFlag = 1, clear pressed state\n7. Compute Cancel button bounding rect:\n   - X: [UIXOffset + 0x152, UIXOffset + 0x1B2] (width = 0x60 = 96 pixels)\n   - Y: [0x116 - UIYOffset, 0x136 - UIYOffset] (same Y range as OK)\n8. If mouse within Cancel button bounds, set g_fCancelConfirmedFlag = 1, clear pressed\n9. Mark UI event node as processed (offset +0x18 = 1, +0x1C = 0)\n10. Queue event node via InsertCacheNodeWithCookie\n\nParameters:\npUIEventNode - Pointer to UI event structure. Fields:\n  +0x18 (dword): Event processed flag, set to 1\n  +0x1C (dword): Event result/status, set to 0\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If g_fOkButtonPressed is 0, function clears targeting state without hit-testing\n- Both buttons share same Y coordinate range (vertically aligned)\n- Button confirmation flags persist for caller to check dialog result\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0xCE (206) - OK button left edge offset from UI origin\n0x12E (302) - OK button right edge offset\n0x152 (338) - Cancel button left edge offset  \n0x1B2 (434) - Cancel button right edge offset\n0x116 (278) - Button top edge (inverted Y)\n0x136 (310) - Button bottom edge (inverted Y)\n0x60 (96) - Button width in pixels\n0x20 (32) - Button height in pixels",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Inventory", "PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_1", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
