      "instructions": ["0x39500|MOV|EAX, 0x1090", "0x39505|CALL|0x6fb9af30", "0x3950A|PUSH|EBX", "0x3950B|PUSH|EBP", "0x3950C|MOV|EBP, dword ptr [ESP + 0x10a0]", "0x39513|PUSH|ESI", "0x39514|TEST|EBP, EBP", "0x39516|PUSH|EDI", "0x39517|JZ|0x6fb097fb", "0x3951D|LEA|ESI, [ESP + 0x100]", "0x39524|MOV|EDI, 0x7d0", "0x39529|MOV|ECX, ESI", "0x3952B|CALL|dword ptr [0x6fba5c30]", "0x39531|ADD|ESI, 0x2", "0x39534|DEC|EDI"],
      "comment": "Parse bracketed resource strings with indexed values, initializing storage and locating positions.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize all cleared Unicode storage buffers [ESP+0x100] for up to 2000 wide chars\n2. Count active data entries in input structure, storing result in [ESP+0x1c]\n3. Search for colon (':') in input string, returning pointer or NULL\n4. Search for opening bracket ('[') in input string, storing pointer at [ESP+0x18]\n5. If bracket found, extract row index (N): search for \"[msdn]\" pattern, get digit at +0x2, subtract 0x30\n6. If bracket found, extract column index (M): search for \"[ms]\" pattern (different marker), get digit at +0x2, subtract 0x30\n7. Both row and column must be valid (not -1); proceed with resource lookup if both present\n8. Calculate buffer offsets: row_buffer = 0x100 + (row*5*5*16), col_buffer = 0x100 + (col*5*5*16)\n9. Copy marker pattern \"[ms]\" to temp storage at [ESP+0x2c]\n10. Load data from row buffer at calculated offset, verify 0x5b marker, append 0x4 bytes\n11. Locate substring within data string, calculate length delta, perform structured copy\n12. Return pointer offset from row buffer start + 0x2, or column buffer equivalent\n13. After loop: reset all cleared buffers, then iterate active entries and call ReplaceFormatSpecifier for each\n\nParameters:\nnDataHandle (int) - Opaque resource data structure handle\nszInputString (char *) - Null-terminated input string to parse\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value; modifies data structures in place\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If no bracket found, operate without offset transformation\n- If row index invalid (-1), skip this data pair and use column offset only if col valid\n- If column index invalid (-1), skip and use row offset only if row valid\n- If both indices invalid, return without modification\n- Cleared buffers store Unicode data in wide-char format (2-byte aligned)\n- Note: Function uses 2 stack-allocated temporaries optimized away (iVar2, pszTempBuffer)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x100: Base offset for Unicode buffer storage (256 decimal)\n- 0x1090: Stack allocation size (4240 bytes) for all buffers\n- 2000: Number of wide characters in each cleared buffer (2000 * 2 = 4000 bytes)\n- 0x30: ASCII offset to convert digit character to numeric value ('0' = 0x30)\n- 0x5b: Opening bracket marker '[' (91 decimal)\n- 0x6d: Character 'm' in pattern \"[msdn]\" (109 decimal)\n- 0x73: Character 's' in pattern \"[msdn]\" (115 decimal)\n- 0x6e: Character 'n' in pattern \"[msdn]\" (110 decimal)\n- 0x61: Character 'a' in pattern \"[ms]\" (97 decimal)\n- 5 * 5 * 16 = 400: Stride for buffer offset calculation per row/column\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset | Size | Field Name | Type | Description\n0x100  | 4000 | abClearedData0 | byte[2000] | First wide-char resource buffer (Unicode)\n0x1100 | 4000 | abClearedData1 | byte[2000] | Second wide-char resource buffer\n0x2100 | 4000 | abClearedData2 | byte[2000] | Third wide-char resource buffer\n0x3100 | 4000 | abClearedData3 | byte[2000] | Fourth wide-char resource buffer\n0x10   | 2    | wTempMarker    | ushort     | Temporary marker storage\n0x18   | 4    | pDataEntry     | void *     | Found data entry pointer\n0x1c   | 4    | nEntryCount    | int        | Active entry count\n0x2c   | 10   | abPattern      | byte[5]    | Pattern buffer for search\n\nRelated Functions:\n- ReplaceFormatSpecifier() - Called for each active data entry to process format strings\n- FUN_6fb9af30() - Stack initialization/setup function",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_StatList", "STRUCT_MonsterData", "PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Path", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PARAM_2", "STRUCT_Skill", "PROP_LOOPHEAVY", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
