      "comment": "Load and parse game configuration data from a resource.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call FUN_6fb9af30() to initialize configuration state\n2. Allocate three Unicode buffer arrays (0x1220 bytes each) via constructor calls\n3. Load primary and secondary configuration resource strings via Ordinal_10614, Ordinal_10701\n4. Check if primary configuration exists; if NULL, display error dialog and exit\n5. Load second configuration resource via Ordinal_10701, initialize structure via Ordinal_578\n6. Detect configuration mode via first character check (Ordinal_10725): string mode (char type 0x7) vs binary mode\n7. For string mode: Parse source string, build ASCII/wide character tables, process placeholders\n8. For binary mode: Load raw binary data, call Ordinal_10614 for string formatting, invoke ProcessBracketedStringData\n9. For types 0x12, 0x16, 0x28: Load config ID, add offset, invoke string formatter\n10. Generate output string via repeated string operations, append to output buffer\n11. Validate output size against reserved buffer (0x1e24 bytes); error if overflow detected\n12. Call Ordinal_10003, Ordinal_10007 to release resources and cleanup\n\nParameters:\nnResourceId - Configuration resource identifier (int, stack +4)\npbConfigData - Output buffer for parsed configuration data (byte *, stack +8)\nIMPLICIT - Return address (stack +0)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Function has no explicit return; side effect is writing parsed config to pbConfigData buffer. Calls FUN_6fb9a10f(0xffffffff) on error which terminates.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Empty primary configuration string: Error dialog displayed, function terminates\n- Configuration type validation failure (type > 7): Error branch execution, function terminates\n- Output size exceeds 0x1e24: Fatal error with FUN_6fb9a10f(0xffffffff), function terminates\n- Types 0x12, 0x16: Special resource type handling with ordinal function calls\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x1220 - Unicode buffer allocation size for temporary string storage\n0x200 - Loop count for double-word initialization (represents 0x400 bytes per 0x200 iterations)\n0x1e10 - Total stack frame size (ESP adjustment at function end)\n0x1e24 - Maximum allowed output buffer size for pbConfigData\n0xf9b, 0xf9e - Configuration resource IDs for primary and secondary configs\n0x717, 0x735 - Error line numbers in configuration parser\n0x5b, 0x5d - ASCII '[' (0x5b) and ']' (0x5d) for bracketed string delimiter detection\n0xe8 - Offset into configuration structure for resource name string field\n0x80 - Offset into configuration structure for configuration ID field\n0x40 - Offset for configuration string base address calculation",
      "tags": ["UI_INVENTORY", "MOD_UI", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData", "STRUCT_StatList", "STRUCT_MonsterData", "PROP_LARGE", "PARAM_2", "STRUCT_Skill", "SRC_inv.cpp", "STRUCT_Other", "PROP_LOOPHEAVY"]
