      "comment": "Initialize rendering modes for all quality levels and object rendering.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if current graphics quality level matches cached level\n2. If quality level changed, reset render mode flags and rebuild modes\n3. Get current graphics quality flag from global state\n4. For each quality mode 0, 13, 6-12: Initialize rendering lists with three render mode variants\n5. For each quality level, configure 10 rendering slots (slots 0-9) with ordinal 10637\n6. Set render mode initialization flag to 1\n7. Check if object data available and ready flag not set\n8. If ready, retrieve object data index from FUN_6fb29fe0\n9. Apply object rendering modes for quality level 0\n10. Mark object rendering initialization complete\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Function initializes global graphics state without return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Graphics quality flag changed: Resets both render mode and object render flags\n- Object rendering only initialized if object data available (g_dwObjectDataAvailable != 0)\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n- 0x0, 0x1-0x9: Rendering mode slot indices (10 total slots per quality level)\n- 0xd (13): Special quality level with additional modes\n- 0x6, 0x7, 0x8, 0xc (12), 0x9, 0xa (10), 0xb (11): Additional quality levels\n\nGlobal Variables:\ng_dwGraphicsQualityFlag - Current graphics quality level\ng_dwLastQualityLevel - Cached quality level for change detection\ng_dwRenderModeInitialized - Flag indicating render modes initialized\ng_dwObjectRenderInitialized - Flag indicating object rendering initialized\ng_dwObjectDataAvailable - Flag indicating object data is available\ng_pRenderModeList_* - Rendering mode list pointers for each quality level",
