      "comment": "Renders the game viewport with selected display mode (normal, object data, or inventory).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize graphics rendering modes based on global config\n2. Determine render mode list based on display mode value (0=normal modes, 1=object data, 2=inventory)\n3. Get viewport unit root from global state and retrieve list size\n4. If units exist, iterate through linked list of units\n5. For each active unit with matching character class:\n   - If unit is selected player: render with special handling (palette frames, checks for animations)\n   - Otherwise: validate unit rendering (immunity checks, passability) and render with conditional palettes\n6. After unit pass, process object layer rendering:\n   - Validate cursor position within game boundaries for current mode\n   - Retrieve cursor object and verify passability\n   - If passable and within hover viewport: render object with palette\n   - Otherwise: attempt alternate hover object selection from dynamic list\n   - On success: render alternate with different palette (0x3)\n\nParameters:\npState: uint* - Pointer to display state array [mode, secondary_index, ...0x21: unit_list_root]\n  Bit 0: Display mode (0=normal, 1=object data, 2=inventory)\n  Offset 1: Secondary index for mode 2 (0x152=item stash, 0x153=item inventory)\n  Offset 0x21: Root of unit linked list for rendering\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value. Modifies global render state and palette buffers via side effects.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Mode 0 (normal): Selects render mode based on global video config (mode 1-4)\n- Mode 1 (objects): Returns early if unit list is empty\n- Mode 2 (inventory): Returns if inventory type invalid or inventory unavailable\n- Only renders selected player (DAT_6fbf8a68) with enhanced effects (animation checks)\n- Non-selected units skip animation rendering; hover objects use alt sprite mode\n- Cursor bounds validation differs per game mode (Act varies bounds, specific modes have overrides)",
      "tags": ["UI_INVENTORY", "MOD_UI", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "STRUCT_ItemData", "PARAM_1", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData", "PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Path", "STRUCT_Skill", "SRC_inv.cpp", "SRC_CmnItems.h"]
