      "comment": "Renders sprite tiles to the game viewport with palette-based color mapping.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate ending X: nEndX = nStartX + (dwWidthCount & 0xFF)\n2. Calculate ending Y: nEndY = nStartY + (dwHeightCount & 0xFF)\n3. Return if nStartX >= nEndX (invalid width range)\n4. Iterate rows from nStartY to nEndY-1\n5. For each row, iterate columns from nStartX to nEndX-1\n6. Load sprite width stride from [nSpriteInfo + 0x14]\n7. Load sprite height stride from [nSpriteInfo + 0x15]\n8. Calculate pixel X: nPixelX = (width_stride * nIterY) + [nSpriteInfo + 0x4]\n9. Calculate pixel Y: nPixelY = (height_stride * nCurrentY) + [nSpriteInfo + 0xC]\n10. Validate: 0 <= nPixelX < g_dwBackBufferHeight AND 0 <= nPixelY < g_dwViewportHeight\n11. Call RenderPixelWithPalette with palette lookup [nPaletteIndex + g_bPaletteRedComponent]\n\nParameters:\n- nSpriteInfo (ECX): Pointer to sprite structure with stride and offset fields\n- nStartY (EDX): Starting Y coordinate in sprite space\n- nStartX: Starting X coordinate in sprite space\n- dwHeightCount: Row count (masked to 8-bit, max 255)\n- dwWidthCount: Column count (masked to 8-bit, max 255)\n- nPaletteIndex: Index into palette lookup table for color conversion\n\nReturns:\n- void (no return value)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Empty width (nStartX >= nEndX) returns immediately without rendering\n- Out-of-bounds pixel coordinates are skipped\n- Palette lookup concatenates high byte of nPaletteIndex with palette red component\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset | Size | Field Name | Type | Description\n0x4    | 4    | pixelOffsetX | int | Base X pixel offset\n0xC    | 4    | pixelOffsetY | int | Base Y pixel offset\n0x14   | 1    | strideX      | byte| Width stride multiplier\n0x15   | 1    | strideY      | byte| Height stride multiplier",
