      "comment": "Render complete game UI including inventory, skills, character stats, quests, experience, and game-specific UI elements.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize local Unicode string buffers (multiple 1KB and 2KB buffers for UI text rendering)\n2. Check game initialization state - return if configuration missing\n3. Check mouse position against UI panel boundaries to detect interaction\n4. Handle skill button press actions if mouse clicks detected\n5. Load game object type and validate (1-9 valid objects, 0=items, others skip rendering)\n6. Render main inventory panel with FUN_6fb5a3a0 using buffer offsets for each UI element\n7. Process special item properties and render UI based on object type\n8. Handle monster data rendering with position, life, mana calculations\n9. Render quest log if available (Ordinal_10707 check)\n10. Render character stats with formatting (experience via Ordinal_10520, life/mana calculations)\n11. Check object affinity flags and render special skill markers (Ordinal_10737/Ordinal_10739)\n12. Load final UI configuration via LoadGameConfiguration(0x100) and display\n\nParameters:\n(none - void function, uses global game state)\n\nReturns:\nvoid (UI rendered in global display buffers via LoadGameConfiguration calls)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x6fbf8a68 = global game object pointer (pGameObject)\n0x6fbf8a64 = global object type identifier (dwObjectType)\n0x6fbfd7fc = UI panel X coordinate global (dwUIXOffset)\n0x6fbfd800 = UI panel Y coordinate global (dwUIYOffset)\n0x6fbae0e8 = screen height global\n0x6fbae0e4 = screen width global\n0x87fc = stack allocation size (34812 bytes for Unicode buffers)\n0x400 = 1024 byte buffer count for initialization loops\n0x200 = 512 byte buffer count for initialization loops\n0x100 = 256 byte buffer count for initialization loops\n\nNote: Function allocates 34812 bytes (0x87fc) on stack for temporary Unicode string buffers. Contains 22+ undefined variables with generic compiler-generated names (iVar4-iVar13, uV