      "comment": "Formats and displays item stat ranges with property modifiers, color codes, and difficulty adjustments.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize Unicode buffers (512 chars min/max, 256 chars format, 256 chars ANSI)\n2. Get difficulty level (0=Normal, 1=Nightmare/Hell)\n3. Check if item is unique/set (property 0x26)\n4. If NOT unique/set (normal/magic item):\n   a. Get current and max stat values for item type (Ordinal_10569, Ordinal_10568)\n   b. Get base multiplier from difficulty table (Ordinal_10519, value 0x0C)\n   c. For property 0xDA (requirement stat):\n      - Get stat value from item (Ordinal_10519)\n      - Get definition table and shift bits (Ordinal_10598 + offset 0x1E)\n      - Calculate: (stat_value * multiplier) >> shift_bits\n      - Add to max value\n   d. For property 0xDB (bonus stat):\n      - Get stat value and definition bits\n      - Get requirement bonus from definition (Ordinal_10521, param 0x16)\n      - Add difficulty adjustment if present (pItemStats offset +7 vs +3)\n      - Calculate weighted bonus: ((stat * multiplier) >> bits) * (requirement + adjustment) / 100\n   e. Ensure max >= min+1, format as Unicode \"min-max\" with color codes\n5. If IS unique/set (special item):\n   a. Get unique definition pointer (Ordinal_10760)\n   b. Get definition fields: base damage (0xB0), type (0xA8), quality (0xAC)\n   c. For type 5 (quest), divide by quest level factor (offset 0xC0/25)\n   d. Apply shift and scale: ((base + quality) << shift) >> 8\n   e. Format damage range with appropriate color code\n6. For charged items (properties 0x12, 0x11, 0x9F, 0xA0):\n   a. Calculate charge damage/quantity range similar to step 4c-d\n   b. Format with charge indicator colors\n\nParameters:\nthis - Item structure pointer (ECX implicit, __thiscall)\npItemStats - Pointer to item stat expansion data (Stack[0x4])\nnStatPropertyCount - Number of properties to display (Stack[0x8])\n\nReturns:\nVoid. Modifies output buffer (unaff_EDI) with formatted Unicode stat strings via strcpy/strcat.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Magic items with property bonuses (0xDA, 0xDB) receive color codes (see FUN_6fb5a3a0 color param meanings: 0=white, 1=gold, 2=green, 3=red)\n- Unique/set items use stored definition pointers instead of dynamic calculation\n- Quest items (type 5) divide max level by 25 (0x19)\n- Unaffected registers ESI, EDI hold string pointers; register EAX/EBP reused for temporaries\n- Magic numbers: 0x1E=shift bit offset in definition, 0xC0=quest divisor location, 0x1F=bit mask for shift count\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x1E - Byte offset in stat definition table pointing to right-shift bit count\n0x1F - Mask for bit count validation (ensure <= 31 bits)\n0xC0 - Offset within unique definition for quest level divisor\n0x19 - Quest level divisor constant (25 decimal)\n0xDA - Stat property ID for requirement modifier\n0xDB - Stat property ID for damage bonus modifier\n0x12, 0x11 - Socketed gem properties for damage\n0x15, 0x16, 0x17, 0x18 - Gem/rune socket properties\n0x9F, 0xA0 - Charged skill properties for mana/charges\n0x26 - Unique/set flag property\n\nStructure Layout (Item Statistics):\nNote: Function uses register-based string pointers (ESI, EDI) and multiple temporary Unicode buffers allocated on stack.\n",
      "tags": ["UI_INVENTORY", "MOD_UI", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "STRUCT_ItemData", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData", "STRUCT_StatList", "STRUCT_MonsterData", "PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Path", "PARAM_3", "STRUCT_Skill", "SRC_inv.cpp", "STRUCT_Other", "PROP_LOOPHEAVY"]
    },
