      "instructions": ["0x41710|SUB|ESP, 0x260", "0x41716|PUSH|EBX", "0x41717|PUSH|EBP", "0x41718|PUSH|ESI", "0x41719|PUSH|EDI", "0x4171A|PUSH|0x14", "0x4171C|MOV|EBP, EDX", "0x4171E|PUSH|ECX", "0x4171F|CALL|0x6fb9826c", "0x41724|MOV|EDI, EAX", "0x41726|CALL|0x6fb62880", "0x4172B|MOV|ESI, EAX", "0x4172D|TEST|ESI, ESI", "0x4172F|JZ|0x6fb11780", "0x41731|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [ESI + 0x4]"],
      "comment": "Renders formatted Unicode text to game UI display with width constraints\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Retrieve base text width value from pThis->textWidth (offset 0x14) via Ordinal_10519\n2. Query current game viewport state with FUN_6fb62880()\n3. If viewport is NULL, use base width only; otherwise accumulate viewport width\n4. Fetch viewport state descriptor at [viewport + 0x4] and load byte at [descriptor + 0x49]\n5. Add descriptor byte value to accumulated width\n6. Query modifier flags by calling Ordinal_10949(0xFFFFFFFF)\n7. If modifier flags are non-NULL, check if viewport supports modifier flag 0x65\n8. Fetch modifier width scaling via Ordinal_10968(viewport, modifierFlags, 1)\n9. Extract final width adjustment from scaling result via Ordinal_11036(scalingResult, 0x75)\n10. Accumulate modifier width adjustment to total width\n11. Clamp final width to maximum of 0x4B (75 decimal)\n12. If final width is 0, return early\n13. Initialize two Unicode string arrays (64 and 512 wide chars) via default constructors\n14. Format ANSI string using Ordinal_578 with format template, width parameter to szFormatBuffer\n15. Convert formatted ANSI string to Unicode via win2Unicode to aUnicodeText buffer\n16. Compare calculated width against threshold at nTextId parameter[0x19]\n17. If width exceeds threshold, apply rendering mode 3 via FUN_6fb5a3a0\n18. Flush game rendering state via Ordinal_10004\n19. Copy resulting Unicode text to output buffer szOutputBuffer\n20. Apply rendering mode 0 for finalization\n21. Copy text to secondary output buffer\n22. Concatenate additional text fragments to final output\n\nParameters:\n- pThis: UIObject pointer; contains text width field at offset 0x14\n- nTextId: Integer text identifier; byte at [nTextId + 0x19] contains width threshold for rendering mode selection\n\nReturns:\n- void; function performs in-place text buffer construction and rendering state updates\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Null viewport (FUN_6fb62880 returns NULL): width calculation skips modifier checks\n- Width overflow: clamped to 0x4B to prevent buffer overrun\n- Zero width: triggers early exit before buffer initialization\n- Modifier flags NULL: width adjustment is skipped entirely",
      "tags": ["PARAM_3"]
