      "comment": "Format item attribute display strings (position X/Y in UI panel).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize local Unicode buffer with 20 default-constructed Unicode characters via loop\n2. Extract X coordinate from dwCoordRecord[2] as byte value\n3. Extract Y coordinate from dwCoordRecord[3] as byte value  \n4. Call FUN_6fb62880 to retrieve item/dimension handle\n5. Call Ordinal_10949(0xffffffff) to get active dimension data handle\n6. Check dimension validity - if NULL, skip dimension adjustments\n7. Call Ordinal_10487 with 0x65 flag to verify dimension available\n8. If available, get dimension bounds: Ordinal_10968 to fetch handle, Ordinal_11002 to get X width, Ordinal_11003 to get Y height\n9. Accumulate adjusted X/Y coordinates into local variables\n10. Call Ordinal_10731(pPanel, 0x33) to validate panel control type\n11. On validation failure (result == 0), call Ordinal_10025 to log error with line reference 0xb56\n12. Format X coordinate value to ASCII using Ordinal_578 (sprintf equivalent) into acStack_20 buffer\n13. Convert formatted ASCII to Unicode using win2Unicode function\n14. Append formatted X to output ESI string via strcat (3 consecutive appends)\n15. Repeat steps 12-14 for Y coordinate value\n16. Return with output string fully constructed\n\nParameters:\npPanel (ECX/IMPLICIT): void * - UI panel object managing display context\ndwCoordRecord (Stack[0x4]): dword - Pointer to coordinate record [X@+2, Y@+3]\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Modifies ESI output string with formatted X/Y display text\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Dimension lookup may return NULL (dimension_handle check at 0x118a7)\n- Panel type validation failure triggers error logging\n- Unicode buffer allocated on stack [ESP+0x28], size 20 chars\n- Format buffer acStack_20 reused for both X and Y conversions (pattern repeated)",
