      "comment": "Render game UI status line text for a unit.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize 20 Unicode string buffers (local_14[0..19])\n2. Call Ordinal_10004 twice (unknown game state operations)\n3. Call Ordinal_10519(nUnitId, 0x46) to query unit attribute 0x46\n4. If result < 1, call Ordinal_10795(nUnitId) as fallback\n5. If both fail (result < 1), return early\n6. Call Ordinal_10004 (game state operation)\n7. Copy base string from unaff_ESI to unaff_EDI (Unicode::strcpy)\n8. Query Ordinal_10519(nUnitId, 0x46) again for value\n9. Call Ordinal_578(szTemp[12], 10, szFmtLongDecimal, dwValue) - format long decimal to temp buffer\n10. Convert szTemp ANSI to Unicode in local_14 via win2Unicode(local_14, szTemp, 9)\n11. Append three copies of string from local_14 to unaff_EDI via strcat (3x)\n\nParameters:\nnUnitId (uint): Unit identifier in ECX, used with Ordinal queries (0x46 = stat code)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Modifies Unicode string buffer pointed to by unaff_EDI\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Returns early if both Ordinal_10519 and Ordinal_10795 queries return < 1 (unit not found/invalid)\n- Magic number 0x46: Unit attribute code (possibly experience/level stat)\n- Magic number 10: ANSI buffer size (szTemp[12] formatted as 10 chars)\n- Magic number 9: Characters to convert from ANSI to Unicode\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x46 - Unit attribute code for stat query (Ordinal_10519/10795)\n10 - Ordinal_578 format buffer size parameter\n9 - Character count for ANSI-to-Unicode conversion\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset | Size | Field Name | Type | Description\n0 | 1 | local_14[0] | Unicode | Unicode string array, 20 elements (40 bytes total)\n0x14 | 12 | szTemp[12] | char | Temporary ANSI format buffer for number conversion",
