      "comment": "Render resource skill text to game UI based on resource type\nChecks resource/skill type and appends appropriate localized text display strings to Unicode buffer\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize resource lookup state via Ordinal_10004 calls (twice)\n2. Read resource type value from (param + 0x78 offset)\n3. If type is 0x08 (Mana) or 0x09 (Stamina), copy/concatenate base resource strings\n4. Otherwise, iterate through g_dwResourceTableCount entries in g_pResourceTableStart table\n5. For each entry, check if table resource ID matches lookup type\n6. When match found, initialize 20 wchar_t buffer with destructors (10 iterations)\n7. Calculate table offset = counter * 0x0C, check flag at offset+0x6fbb3958\n8. If flag clear (0x00), get unsigned resource value, apply Ordinal_10842 transform\n9. If flag set (!0x00), get signed resource value, apply Ordinal_10841 transform\n10. Format resource value to decimal string via Ordinal_578 (szFmtLongDecimal format)\n11. Convert formatted ASCII to Unicode via win2Unicode, append string concatenations to output\n12. Return after exhausting table or finding match\n\nParameters:\nnResourceType: int - Value at caller's base+0x78 (8=Mana, 9=Stamina, others=lookup in table)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Modifies global Unicode string buffer via unaff_EDI string operations\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Types 0x08 and 0x09 take fast path (no table lookup)\n- Empty table (g_dwResourceTableCount==0) exits without match\n- Unmatched type returns early at loop end\n- String operations use imported Unicode class methods (strcpy, strcat, win2Unicode)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x78 - Offset into base structure for resource type field\n0x08, 0x09 - Type constants for Mana and Stamina resources\n0x0C - Table entry size (12 bytes per resource entry)\n0x6fbb3958 - Offset within entry for flag indicating signed/unsigned\n0x6fbb3954 - Offset within entry for resource value",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PARAM_1", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control"]
