      "comment": "Searches for a unit matching specified filter criteria within a linked list structure.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get initial node from first parameter (pUnit)\n2. Loop through linked list nodes:\n   a. Return 0 if node is NULL (end of list)\n   b. Extract data from node using Ordinal_10305\n   c. Check if data type equals 5 using Ordinal_10695\n   d. Verify data state is valid (0x00, 0x03, 0x04, or 0xFF) using Ordinal_10719\n   e. Check if node flags (1, 3, or 4) using Ordinal_10307\n   f. Validate first search parameter matches using Ordinal_10732\n   g. Validate second search parameter matches using Ordinal_10746\n   h. If all conditions met, return extracted data; otherwise continue to next node\n3. Get next node using Ordinal_10304 and repeat\n\nParameters:\npUnit (void *): IMPLICIT EBX - Initial node/starting point for list traversal\nnSearchParam2 (int): IMPLICIT EDX - First filter value to match\nnSearchParam3 (int): Stack - Second filter value to match\n\nReturns:\nvoid *: Matching data structure if all filter conditions are satisfied, 0 if no match found\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x05 - Target data type constant\n0x00, 0x03, 0x04, 0xFF - Valid data state values\n1, 3, 4 - Valid node flag values\n\nRelated Ordinals:\nOrdinal_10277: Get first node (D2Common)\nOrdinal_10305: Extract data from node (D2Common)\nOrdinal_10695: Get data type (D2Common)\nOrdinal_10719: Check data state (D2Common)\nOrdinal_10307: Get node flags (D2Common)\nOrdinal_10732: Get first filter field (D2Common)\nOrdinal_10746: Get second filter field (D2Common)\nOrdinal_10304: Get next node in list (D2Common)",
