      "comment": "Builds and renders a tooltip string for the currently selected game unit, displaying unit properties based on type.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize wsLocalBuffer Unicode buffer (126 chars) with null values via STOSD/STOSW (31 dwords + 1 word)\n2. Initialize aUStack_100 Unicode buffer (256 chars) via loop calling _default_constructor_closure_ (0x3f iterations, 2 bytes per Unicode char)\n3. Call Ordinal_10004() - String locale/resource initialization\n4. Copy selected unit string to output buffer via strcpy(lpszOutputBuffer, lpszInputString)\n5. Check g_dwObjectType == 4 (OBJECT_MONSTER):\n   a. If true, call Ordinal_10707(g_pSelectedUnit, 0x400000, 0xce1, szPath) - Fetch monster-specific properties string\n   b. If success (return != 0), initialize aUStack_100 buffer (0x80 = 128 iterations)\n   c. Call Ordinal_10004() again for second string locale lookup\n   d. Apply strcpy + strcat operations to build extended text\n   e. Call FUN_6fb5a3a0(aUStack_100, 1) - Render/display tooltip text\n   f. Call strcat to append separator\n6. Call FUN_6fb29640(g_pSelectedUnit, g_pUIPanel, &iStack_184, &wNumChars, 0x40) - Fetch unit stats/properties\n7. If FUN_6fb29640 returns success:\n   a. If wNumChars != 0, append separator via strcat\n   b. Append final separator via strcat\n   c. Return early (exit function)\n8. If FUN_6fb29640 returns failure or object not type 4:\n   a. Initialize aUStack_100 (0x40 = 64 iterations)\n   b. Call Ordinal_10004() for third string locale operation\n   c. Copy+concatenate strings for alternative unit type display\n   d. Call FUN_6fb5a3a0(aUStack_100, 1) - Render alternate tooltip\n   e. Call strcat for final separator\n   f. Return\n\nParameters:\n- IMPLICIT ECX (unaff_ESI): Pointer to input string buffer [register preserved by caller]\n- IMPLICIT EDX (unaff_EDI): Pointer to output tooltip buffer [register preserved by caller]\n\nReturns:\n- void (no return value, result stored in output buffer via strcat operations)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If FUN_6fb29640 succeeds, function returns early at 0x6fb1214f (happy path)\n- If FUN_6fb29640 fails or object type != 4, alternative path handles non-monster/non-playable unit rendering\n- Two distinct buffer sizes used: 0x80 (128 chars) for monsters, 0x40 (64 chars) for other units\n- Multiple calls to Ordinal_10004() suggest resource string loading for different tooltip sections\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x6fbb3c08: String resource/file path constant\n- 0xce1: Resource ID/magic constant for Ordinal_10707 query\n- 0x400000: Lookup flag parameter for Ordinal_10707\n- 0x3f (63): Loop count for initializing 126 char Unicode buffer\n- 0x80 (128): Buffer size for monster tooltip (256 chars / 2 bytes per char)\n- 0x40 (64): Buffer size for other unit tooltips (128 chars / 2 bytes per char)\n- 0x4: OBJECT_MONSTER type constant (matches g_dwObjectType)",
      "tags": ["UI_INVENTORY", "MOD_UI", "STRUCT_Inventory", "SRC_inv.cpp", "PARAM_0", "PROP_LOOPHEAVY", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
