      "comment": "Processes item placement into character body equipment slots.\n\nHandles item equip/unequip operations based on screen state and body slot compatibility.\nCalled when user attempts to place an item in an equipment slot (weapon, armor, etc.).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get item owner from inventory container via INVENTORY_GetOwner\n2. Get slot 5 data (cursor item) and slot 4 data (target slot) from array container\n3. Check screen state - if trading screen (6), send trade packet 0x27\n4. If screen state 8, send packet 0x4c for alternate mode\n5. Call CanPlaceItemInBodySlot to determine placement result (0-7)\n6. Switch on placement result:\n   - Case 0: Item cannot be placed - check alternate slot, play error sound 0x12 or 0x13\n   - Case 1: Direct equip - send packet 0x1a with item GUID\n   - Case 2: Swap items - send packet 0x1b, initialize both item resources\n   - Case 3: Special object type handling - check g_dwObjectType for valid types (0,1,2,0xb,0xc,0xe,0xf,0x13)\n   - Case 4: Belt/inventory placement - send packet 0x1c with slot 4\n   - Case 5: Unequip to cursor - send packet 0x1d with item GUID\n   - Case 6: Move between slots - send packet 0x21 unless object type 0xb\n   - Case 7: Triple resource swap - send packet 0x1e, initialize all three resources\n7. For multiplayer, throttle actions with 400ms delay via g_dwLastInteractionTime\n8. Set g_dwInteractionState = 1 on successful operations\n\nParameters:\n  pUnit - Player unit performing the action (ECX, __fastcall)\n  pInventoryContainer - Inventory array container with item slots (EDX, __fastcall)\n  dwBodySlotId - Target body slot index (stack)\n\nReturns:\n  1 on successful operation or handled case\n  0 if operation blocked (game paused, throttled, or invalid state)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x27 - Trade screen item packet\n  0x4c - Alternate mode item packet\n  0x1a - Direct equip packet\n  0x1b - Item swap packet\n  0x1c - Belt/inventory packet\n  0x1d - Unequip to cursor packet\n  0x1e - Triple swap packet\n  0x21 - Move between slots packet\n  0x12 - Error sound: cannot place\n  0x13 - Error sound: alternate slot available\n  400 (0x190) - Multiplayer throttle delay in milliseconds\n  0x191 - Throttle comparison value (401ms)\n\nGlobals Used:\n  g_dwLastInteractionTime - Tick count for multiplayer action throttling\n  g_dwInteractionState - Set to 1 on successful placement\n  g_dwObjectType - Current object interaction type\n  g_dwInteractionParam0, g_dwInteractionParam1 - Interaction parameters for ProcessUnitInteraction",
      "tags": ["PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_3", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
    },
