      "comment": "Handle mouse input events and process game interactions\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if game system is enabled; return early if already processing\n2. Extract mouse coordinates from input event (X, Y position)\n3. Check screen width constraints; set error flag if out of bounds\n4. Query viewport state and validate coordinate ranges\n5. Check for UI mode interactions (modes 0x0, 0xb, 0xc, 0xe, 0xf, 0x11)\n6. For UI modes: process button clicks, inventory interactions, skill selections\n7. For game view: validate object placement using GetGameObject; iterate through hotspot regions\n8. For each valid hotspot: verify click point, get game object, validate placement\n9. If server port is local (0 or 1): send action packet immediately\n10. If server port is remote: check action throttle (400ms cooldown); resend if needed\n11. Handle special cases: item interactions, unit targeting, spell casting\n12. Clear global game state on exit (pGameStateConfig, dwUIFlag1, pSelectedUnit)\n\nParameters:\n  pMouseEvent (DWORD *): Pointer to mouse input event data\n    [0]: Flags/status field\n    [3]: Contains Y coordinate (upper 16-bits) and X coordinate (lower 16-bits)\n    [6]: Output status flag\n    [7]: Output result flag\n\nReturns:\n  void - Updates game state through pointer parameter and globals\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Early exit if IsGameSystemEnabled() returns true\n  - Mode 0xb: Weapon slot interactions (limited area)\n  - Mode 0xc: Armor/skill slot interactions (screen-dependent)\n  - Mode 0xf: Inventory grid interactions with drag calculations\n  - Mode 0x11: Spell book interactions\n  - Server throttling: 400ms minimum between remote server actions\n  - Coordinates validated against multiple panel regions and hotspot arrays\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x80 - Hotspot region size/stride\n  0x28 - Packet type for direct object interaction\n  0x2c - Hotspot region field offset\n  0x400 - Throttle time 400ms in GetTickCount units\n  0x191 - Throttle time 401ms alternate value",
