      "instructions": ["0x44EC0|SUB|ESP, 0x8", "0x44EC3|PUSH|EBX", "0x44EC4|PUSH|EBP", "0x44EC5|PUSH|ESI", "0x44EC6|PUSH|EDI", "0x44EC7|CALL|0x6fadb800", "0x44ECC|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0x44ECE|JNZ|0x6fb1550d", "0x44ED4|CALL|0x6fb62890", "0x44ED9|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0x44EDB|JNZ|0x6fb1550d", "0x44EE1|MOV|EAX, [0x6fbb36e0]", "0x44EE6|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0x44EE8|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [ESP + 0x1c]", "0x44EEC|JNZ|0x6fb14eff"],
      "comment": "Handles UI mouse click events and processes them based on current game mode.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if game system enabled or if processing is blocked (FUN_6fb62890) - exit with result 0 if so\n2. Check if main data array (DAT_6fbb36e0) is initialized - exit with result 0 if not\n3. Extract mouse screen X from pClickEvent[0xc] (lower 16 bits) into dwScreenX\n4. Extract mouse screen Y from pClickEvent[0xc] (upper 16 bits) into dwScreenY (EDI)\n5. Get render state (nRenderState) via FUN_6fb62880, call InitializeGraphicsRenderingModes\n6. Get viewport position via FUN_6fb300a0 (return in EAX)\n7. Validate mouse in main viewport bounds - if yes, process as game world click:\n   a. Set result[0x18] = 1, result[0x1c] = 0\n   b. Check if in special UI panel bounds (DAT_6fbf686c etc.) - if yes, process UI panel click via FUN_6fb15530\n   c. Otherwise iterate through panel array at DAT_6fbf8ad4 (stride 20 bytes = 5 dwords)\n   d. Test panel bounds: piVar9[-1] <= X < piVar9[0], piVar9[1] <= Y <= piVar9[2]\n   e. Find matching panel slot, retrieve target unit via Ordinal_10262/10291/10257\n   f. Check unit immunities (0x23, 0x1b) and select target unit\n   g. Store panel index in DAT_6fbf8a98, selected unit in g_pSelectedUnit\n8. If not in main viewport, check game mode (g_dwObjectType):\n   a. Mode 0xB (mode 11): Check bounds DAT_6fbf6954-6960, call FUN_6fb15530 with mode list 6 or 7\n   b. Mode 0xC (mode 12): Check bounds based on global state, call FUN_6fb15530 with mode list 8 or 12\n   c. Mode 0xE (mode 14): Check bounds DAT_6fbf6a24-30, call FUN_6fb15530 with mode list 9\n   d. Mode 0xF (mode 15): Check bounds DAT_6fbf69e4-f0, require state from FUN_6fb8ed80/Ordinal_11181, call FUN_6fb15530 with mode list 10\n   e. Otherwise: Check result from FUN_6fb5d340(0x24), set result[0x18] = 0 and exit\n9. Final state: Restore original game mode (uVar3), clear UI globals if no panel processed, set g_pUIPanel = 1\n\nParameters:\n  pClickEvent: Pointer to event structure containing mouse coordinates at offset 0xc (X=lower word, Y=upper word)\n\nReturns:\n  void (updates pClickEvent[0x18] with result: 1 = processed in viewport, 0 = not processed)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Multiple mode paths depending on g_dwObjectType value\n  - Temporary game mode changes during render operations (modes 1, 2, 3, 4, 0)\n  - Panel iteration with bounds check and stride of 20 bytes per panel entry\n  - Unit immunity checks for properties 0x23 and 0x1b during target selection\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x18 - Event result offset in pClickEvent\n  0x1c - Additional result offset\n  0xc - Mouse coordinate offset in pClickEvent\n  0x10 - Y coordinate shift (16 bits)\n  0x23, 0x1b - Unit immunity property IDs\n  0x24 - Memory allocation size\n  0xB, 0xC, 0xE, 0xF - Game mode IDs\n  DAT_6fbf8ad4 - Panel array base address\n  20 - Panel entry stride (5 dwords * 4 bytes)\n  0x84 - Offset in render state structure for data pointer",
      "tags": ["PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PARAM_1", "PROP_LOOPHEAVY", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
