      "instructions": ["0x45530|SUB|ESP, 0x10", "0x45533|PUSH|EBX", "0x45534|PUSH|EBP", "0x45535|PUSH|ESI", "0x45536|PUSH|EDI", "0x45537|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x14], EDX", "0x4553B|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0x4553D|CALL|0x6fadb920", "0x45542|PUSH|EAX", "0x45543|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [ESP + 0x38]", "0x45547|PUSH|EAX", "0x45548|PUSH|ESI", "0x45549|CALL|0x6fb9884e", "0x4554E|MOV|ECX, EAX", "0x45550|XOR|EBX, EBX"],
      "comment": "Transform viewport coordinates for game rendering. Converts world coordinates to screen coordinates based on viewport configuration, handling scaling and offset calculations.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call GetGlobalSystemState() to fetch current system state context\n2. Obtain viewport unit scale from system state via Ordinal_10409\n3. Calculate scaled coordinates: (inputCoord - baseOffset) / pixelScale\n4. If output buffer NULL: generate new coordinates via Ordinal_10252\n5. If result zero: clear game state (set flags to 0)\n6. Else: update selected entity and viewport coordinates via Ordinal calls\n7. If buffer provided: apply viewport constraints and compute adjusted coordinates\n8. Check coordinate bounds against viewport dimensions\n9. Write final screen coordinates (dwX, dwY) to globals if valid\n\nParameters:\nnGameState - Game state handle (ECX register)\ndwInputFlags - Viewport/input flags controlling coordinate transformation behavior\npdwOutputBuffer - Optional output buffer for computed coordinates (NULL for new allocation)\ndwParam4 - Input X coordinate in world space\ndwParam5 - Input Y coordinate in world space\npbViewportConfig - Pointer to viewport configuration structure (contains scaling factors and base offsets)\ndwUnitsPerPixelX - Scaling parameter for coordinate transformation\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Updates global variables: g_dwCursorScreenX, g_dwCursorScreenY, g_dwViewportX, g_pSelectedEntity\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If pdwOutputBuffer is NULL, allocates new coordinate buffer via Ordinal_10252\n- Coordinate bounds validation: if calculated position exceeds viewport dimensions, returns without update\n- Handles signed/unsigned conversion for coordinate calculations (JNS/DEC pattern for signed extension)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x14, 0x15 - Viewport configuration offsets for pixel scale factors\n0x5fd - Ordinal call parameter (likely size or flag constant)\n0xFF - Byte mask for coordinate component extraction\n0x01 - Flag bit check for viewport mode\n\nGlobal Variables Modified:\n- g_dwCursorScreenX: Final X coordinate for screen rendering\n- g_dwCursorScreenY: Final Y coordinate for screen rendering  \n- g_dwViewportX: Intermediate viewport X calculation result\n- g_pSelectedEntity: Current selected game entity handle\n",
