      "comment": "Validates game entity screen coordinates against viewport bounds and triggers actions.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Verify game system is enabled via IsGameSystemEnabled()\n2. Check rendering subsystem via FUN_6fb62890 to ensure no render errors\n3. If either check fails, mark validation as invalid (0x18 = 0) and return\n4. Extract X coordinate from entity offset 0x0C (lower 16 bits)\n5. Extract Y coordinate from entity offset 0x0C (upper 16 bits via SHR 16)\n6. Load current system mode via FUN_6fb62880 and retrieve render state\n7. Validate entity structure via FUN_6fb300a0\n8. Confirm X coordinate within bounds: X >= g_dwMinScreenX_Left AND X < g_dwMaxScreenX_Right\n9. Confirm Y coordinate within bounds: Y >= g_dwMinScreenY_Top AND Y < g_dwMaxScreenY_Bottom\n10. If out of bounds, mark invalid (0x18 = 0) and return\n11. Mark valid (0x18 = 1) and clear offset 0x1c\n12. Check viewport-specific bounds using local region variables\n13. If outside viewport, reset 0x18 = 0, otherwise call FUN_6fb159d0 for pixel processing\n14. If object type in range [2,4], reset g_adwObjectTypeData array and call Ordinal_10262 (GetUnitMode)\n15. Check game input mode via FUN_6fb8f780: mode 6=special render, mode 8=log packet\n16. Handle each mode with Ordinal_511 (InitializeLinkedNodeThreadSafe) for state synchronization\n\nParameters:\npUnit (void *) - Pointer to game entity with coordinate pair at offset 0x0C and status flags at 0x18/0x1C\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Sets entity->offset_0x18 to 0 (invalid) or 1 (valid); modifies offset_0x1c on success\n\nRelated Functions:\n- FUN_6fb159d0: Pixel lookup at coordinates\n- FUN_6fb62880: Get system rendering mode\n- FUN_6fb8f780: Get input/event mode\n- Ordinal_10262 (D2Common.GetUnitMode): Query entity state mode\n- Ordinal_511 (Storm.InitializeLinkedNodeThreadSafe): Notify state change",
