      "comment": "Process screen click event and dispatch to entity click handler.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get current game system state (2D/isometric)\n2. Call Ordinal_10409 to validate and process click state\n3. Determine grid coordinates based on state:\n   - If flags == 0: Use DAT_6fbf686c baseline (state 0)\n   - Else if GetGlobalSystemState() == 0: Use g_dwMinScreenX_Mode12 baseline (mode 12)\n   - Else: Use g_dwMinScreenX_NoState baseline (alternate state)\n4. Lookup entity at grid coordinates via Ordinal_10252\n5. If entity found:\n   a. Check if entity is selected (Ordinal_10262) - if yes, skip selection logic\n   b. Attempt selection with Ordinal_10825:\n      - If success: Verify with FUN_6fb6e180, log packet 0x4c, return 1\n      - If invalid: Return 0\n   c. Check if entity is structure (Ordinal_10771):\n      - If NOT structure: Check if object (Ordinal_10772)\n        * If object: Check type [offset+0x80] for skill/book/knowledge flags\n        * If type matches 0x20737274/0x20736b62/0x20646b62: Call FUN_6fb58e40\n        * Return 1\n      - If structure: Get X,Y coords via Ordinal_10326/10329\n        * Verify with FUN_6fb6e180\n        * Check throttle: GetCurrentServerPort() must be valid\n        * Check rate limit: 0x191ms (401ms) cooldown via _g_dwLastInteractionTime\n        * Send 0x20 subcommand, call FUN_6fb6e120\n        * Call FUN_6fb6bc60 to get viewport param, call FUN_6fb8d210\n        * Clear g_pGameStateConfig, return 1\n6. Return 0 if entity not found\n\nParameters:\n  nGameState (ECX) - Game display state/mode (2D mode ID)\n  nEntityId (EDX) - Entity/object unique identifier\n  nScreenX (Stack+4) - Mouse X coordinate in screen space\n  nScreenY (Stack+8) - Mouse Y coordinate in screen space\n  nFlags (Stack+C) - Click flags/modifiers (0=state0, !=0=alternate state)\n\nReturns:\n  1 - Click processed successfully (entity found and handled)\n  0 - Click rejected (invalid entity, rate limited, or no entity)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x191 - 401 decimal, rate limit cooldown in milliseconds\n  0x20737274 - 'trs ' skill type marker\n  0x20736b62 - 'bks ' book/knowledge type marker\n  0x20646b62 - 'bkd ' knowledge type marker\n  0x80 - Offset in entity structure containing type flags\n  0x24, 0x1c, 0x20 - Stack frame offsets for parameters\n  0x4c - Packet type for interaction logging\n\nRelated Functions:\n  GetGlobalSystemState - Returns current display mode (2D/isometric)\n  Ordinal_10252 - D2Common entity lookup by grid coordinates\n  Ordinal_10409 - Validate and normalize click state\n  FUN_6fb6e180 - Verify entity validity\n  SendPacketWithSubcommand - Send 0x20 interaction packet to server",
