      "comment": "Validate and select available rarity mode for item filter display\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate initial mode index (0-4) by clearing high bytes if > 4\n2. Check if filter database is initialized (DAT_6fbf8a7c == 0)\n3. Initialize filter by calling FUN_6fb29fe0 with mode parameter\n4. Retrieve inventory items for mode via FUN_6fb60e10, verify items exist\n5. Count items by rarity type (0-4) using Ordinal calls\n6. Build rarity count array [anRarityCount] with counts for each rarity\n7. Scan up to DAT_6fbb3a78 items, store rarity per item\n8. Mark rarity modes as \"available\" if count > 0 at DAT_6fbb3a3e offset table\n9. If initial mode has no items, find next available mode (0-4) by cycling\n10. Store selected mode index (0-255) and update view marker at DAT_6fbb3a3a\n\nParameters:\nnInitialMode (ECX, dword) - Preferred display mode (0=rarity0, 1=rarity1... 4=rarity4, >4 clears high bytes)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Updates global mode indicator (byte at 0x6fbf8a78) and availability flags at DAT_6fbb3a3e\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If DAT_6fbf8a7c != 0, exit early (filter already initialized)\n- If inventory lookup fails, exit early\n- If preferred mode has no items, scan modes 0-4 up to 4 attempts before cycling\n- Mode value cycles at 0xff boundary or exceeds DAT_6fbf8a80\n\nNote: Function uses 4 stack-allocated temporaries optimized away (phantom locals)",
