      "comment": "Initializes game mode state and object type configuration tables based on unit mode.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Clear global state variables (dwUIMode1Flag, dwInteractionState, dwObjectType)\n2. Zero-fill object type configuration array based on dwObjectTypeCount count\n3. Query primary unit type via FUN_6fb2a5e0 and FUN_6fb29fe0\n4. Retrieve unit type ID via FUN_6fb60e10 at offset +4\n5. Switch on unit type ID (0x93, 0x9a, 0xfc, 0xfd, 0x101, 0x195, 0x1ff-0x201):\n   - Types 0x93,0x94,0xb1,0xc7,0xca,0xfc,0xfe,0xff,0x100,0x200: Set config mode 0\n   - Types 0x9a,0xb2,0x101,0x195,0x1ff,0x201: Set config mode 1 with extended parameters\n   - Other types: Return with dwObjectTypeState1 = 0\n6. Populate global configuration parameter table (g_wConfigId1-g_wConfigParam9)\n7. Zero global object type data array (g_adwObjectTypeData)\n8. Query secondary unit type via second FUN_6fb29fe0 call\n9. Switch on secondary unit type, set g_chCurrentMode (0, 1, or 3)\n10. Call SelectAvailableItemRarityMode with mode value\n11. If mode was set (fModeSet true), set timer dwModeUpdateTimer to current tick + 500ms\n\nParameters:\n(none - void function)\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\nNote: Function uses SSA temporaries optimized away by compiler (uVar1, iVar3, puVar2, piVar4, iVar6, extraout_ECX cannot be renamed)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x12: Object type entry stride (18 bytes)\n- 0xd07, 0xd08, 0xd0a: Configuration mode IDs\n- 0x1030, 0x276e: Item rarity IDs\n- 500: Millisecond tick timeout for mode update\n- 0x14 (20): Object type data array stride",
