      "comment": "Initialize inventory object data and set object type to player inventory.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate object type is 5 (object type expected before initialization)\n2. If type is not 5, log error message with actual type value and raise fatal assertion error\n3. Clear all object data by iterating from g_adwObjectTypeData with stride of 5 dwords, setting each to 0\n4. Set g_dwObjectType to 1 (player inventory type)\n5. Call GetInventoryClassInfo() to retrieve object class information\n6. Extract object identifier from class info at offset 0x84\n7. Pass identifier to InitializeObjectFromIdentifier() for final setup\n8. Return void\n\nParameters:\n  None - operates on global inventory state (g_dwObjectType, g_adwObjectTypeData)\n\nReturns:\n  void - initializes global state, no return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Function asserts g_dwObjectType must be 5 on entry (validates caller state)\n  - Object data clearing loop uses pointer arithmetic [0x6fbf6904 .. 0x6fbf6954) with 20-byte stride\n  - Assertion failure terminates with exit code 0xffffffff\n  - Class info lookup must succeed for initialization to proceed\n  - Note: Function returns temporary from FUN_6fb62880() (iVar1) optimized away by compiler\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x5 - expected object type value for assertion\n  0x1 - player inventory object type constant\n  0x84 - offset within class info structure for object identifier\n  0x14 - dword stride (5 dwords) in object data array\n  0x6fbf6904 - start address of object data array\n  0x6fbf6954 - end address of object data array (80 bytes total)",
