      "comment": "Validates that object type is 5, or terminates with error if not, then sets type to 6.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if g_dwObjectType is not equal to 5\n2. If type mismatch (not 5):\n   - Call Ordinal_10023 with inventory mode verification string, source file path, and error code 0x1ec0\n   - Call FUN_6fb9a10f(-1) to abort/terminate process\n   - (Does not return on failure)\n3. If type is 5:\n   - Skip error handling block (JZ to line 7)\n4. Set g_dwObjectType to 6 (new state)\n5. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\n(none) - Uses implicit global g_dwObjectType at 0x6fbf8a64\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value on success. Function terminates process on validation failure.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If g_dwObjectType != 5 at entry, function calls abort routine (FUN_6fb9a10f) which does not return\n- Error code 0x1ec0 suggests inventory mode validation error\n- Global g_dwObjectType transitions from state 5 to state 6 on success",
