      "comment": "Validates that current object type is 6, and transitions to object type 7.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Compare global g_dwObjectType with value 0x6 (6)\n2. If equal, skip validation (jump to end at 0x6fb163e7)\n3. If not equal, call Ordinal_10023 with error message parameters to log assertion failure\n4. Call FUN_6fb9a10f with parameter 0xffffffff (likely fatal exit)\n5. Set g_dwObjectType to 0x7 (7) as final state\n6. Return\n\nParameters:\n(none) - operates on global state\n\nReturns:\nvoid - function terminates process on validation failure via FUN_6fb9a10f\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- No return on validation failure (FUN_6fb9a10f does not return)\n- On success (type == 6), sets type to 7 and returns normally\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x6 - expected object type value (6 - likely OBJECT_NORMAL or similar)\n0x7 - final object type value (7 - likely OBJECT_TRANSITION or next state)\n0x1ee7 - error code/line number passed to Ordinal_10023\n0xffffffff - fatal exit code (-1)",
