      "comment": "Initialize object type data array by zeroing all entries.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if current object type (g_dwObjectType) equals 7 (inventory/buy-sell mode)\n2. If NOT in mode 7, display assertion error with file/line info and exit via FUN_6fb9a10f\n3. Clear object type data array: iterate from g_adwObjectTypeData to 0x6fbf6954\n4. Zero each dword (4-byte) entry and advance pointer by 5 dwords per iteration\n5. Set g_dwObjectType to 1 (default/active state)\n6. Call FUN_6fb62880 to get object data reference\n7. Read dword at offset 0x84 within returned data\n8. Pass this dword value to Ordinal_10262 for processing\n9. Call FUN_6fb8f0c0 with processed value, then return\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value. Exits via FUN_6fb9a10f on assertion failure.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Function asserts g_dwObjectType must equal 7 on entry (inventory mode validation)\n- Loop clears 0x6fbf6954 / (0x6fbf6904 + 5*4) entries ≈ 130 dwords\n- Loop advances by 5 dwords (20 bytes) per iteration, not contiguous memory\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x7 - Object type identifier (inventory/buy-sell mode check)\n0x84 - Offset within FUN_6fb62880 return value to extract\n0x1 - Default object type state after initialization\n0x6fbf6954 - Loop boundary address (array end)",
