      "api_calls": ["SetActiveFont", "GetTotalStatValue", "GetTotalStatValue", "ValidateStringId", "InitializeStringBuffer", "GetTotalStatValue", "GetTotalStatValue", "GetGuildFlags", "GetTotalStatValue", "ValidateStringId", "...+16 more"],
      "instructions": ["0x46490|SUB|ESP, 0x120", "0x46496|PUSH|EBX", "0x46497|PUSH|EBP", "0x46498|MOV|EBP, ECX", "0x4649A|PUSH|ESI", "0x4649B|PUSH|EDI", "0x4649C|MOV|ECX, 0x1", "0x464A1|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x24], EBP", "0x464A5|CALL|0x6fb99a02", "0x464AA|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x30], EAX", "0x464AE|LEA|ESI, [ESP + 0xb8]", "0x464B5|MOV|EDI, 0x3c", "0x464BA|MOV|ECX, ESI", "0x464BC|CALL|dword ptr [0x6fba5c30]", "0x464C2|ADD|ESI, 0x2"],
      "comment": "Renders UI dialog frame for gold coin trading panel with input region detection.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize two Unicode string buffers (120 chars each) using default constructors\n2. Initialize array of 18 uint values to zero (auStack_fc parameter buffer)\n3. Switch based on nPanelId (0-4 or invalid):\n   - Case 0: Retrieve frame color 0x0f, calculate position based on screen state\n     - Check GetGlobalSystemState to determine UI Y offset (0xf2 or 0x1b6 from base)\n     - Detect mouse hover over gold coin button: x in [XOffset+0x49, XOffset+0x5d], y within range\n     - If hovered, clear dialog frame with Ordinal_10004(yPos, 0, 0)\n   - Case 1: Use frame color 0x0e, position at (ScreenWidth - XOffset - 0xed, offset -0x48)\n   - Case 2: Same as default, clears panel and calls Ordinal_10121\n   - Case 3: Render with both frame colors (0x0f and 0x0e), use yPos = ScreenHeight - 0xdf\n   - Case 4: Retrieve panel handle from FUN_6fb8ed80, use frame color from Ordinal_11177\n4. Initialize second Unicode string buffer (40 chars x 2 bytes) for localized text\n5. Call Ordinal_578 to format localization string into char buffer (20 bytes)\n6. Convert ASCII to Unicode using win2Unicode\n7. Dispatch to sub-handler based on nPanelId via computed switch table (offset 0x6fb16a10):\n   - Handler at 0x6fb16891: Render gold panel (iVar9 incremented if g_dwUIMode1Flag set)\n   - Handler at 0x6fb168d2: Render with stash visibility check (g_fPanelStashVisibility)\n   - Handler at 0x6fb16916: Render with render state check, call FUN_6fb32640\n   - Handler at 0x6fb16978: Render with cube visibility (g_fPanelCubeVisibility), offset uVar5 by 4\n   - Handler at 0x6fb169c6: Default - clear dialog with Ordinal_10004\n8. Call Ordinal_10117 to finalize rendering with calculated offsets\n9. Call Ordinal_10127 to cleanup/commit UI changes\n\nParameters:\n- nPanelId (ECX:4): Panel type selector (0=gold, 1=items, 2=stats, 3=special, 4=quest, 5+=invalid)\n\nReturns: void (no return value)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- nPanelId >= 5: Executes default case, skips computed dispatch\n- g_dwUIMode1Flag check: Adjusts vertical position for alternate UI layout\n- g_fPanelStashVisibility/g_fPanelCubeVisibility: Conditional vertical position adjustment\n- Mouse hover detection only active for Case 0\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x0f, 0x0e: Frame color palette IDs\n- 0x49, 0x5d: X-axis boundaries for mouse hit detection\n- 0xf2, 0xf4, 0x1b6, 0x1b8: Y-axis offsets based on UI state\n- 0x14, 0x13: String buffer sizes (20, 19 characters)\n- 0xffffffff: Color parameter (fully opaque white)\n- 5: Ordinal_10072 stack depth parameter\n\nRelated Functions:\n- GetGlobalSystemState: Determines UI layout variant (0=normal, non-zero=expanded)\n- FUN_6fb8f680, FUN_6fb8f690: Retrieve mouse X/Y coordinates\n- FUN_6fb62880: Get sprite handle for frame rendering\n- FUN_6fb32640: Get current panel button reference\n- FUN_6fb8ed80: Get active panel handle for Case 4\n- Ordinal_10519: Retrieve frame palette from sprite\n- Ordinal_10127: Initialize/cleanup UI rendering state\n- Ordinal_10004, Ordinal_10129: Clear/hide dialog frame\n- Ordinal_10072: Draw dialog panel component\n- Ordinal_10117: Finalize panel rendering\n- Ordinal_578: Format localized string\n- Ordinal_10121: Reset panel focus\n- win2Unicode: Convert ANSI to UTF-16LE\n- Ordinal_11177: Extract panel type from handle (Case 4)",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_StatList", "PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Path", "STRUCT_Inventory", "STRUCT_Skill", "STRUCT_Room1", "STRUCT_ItemData", "PARAM_1", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
