      "instructions": ["0x46A30|PUSH|EBX", "0x46A31|PUSH|EBP", "0x46A32|PUSH|ESI", "0x46A33|PUSH|EDI", "0x46A34|CALL|0x6fb62880", "0x46A39|MOV|EBX, EAX", "0x46A3B|CALL|0x6fadb800", "0x46A40|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0x46A42|JNZ|0x6fb16e9a", "0x46A48|TEST|EBX, EBX", "0x46A4A|JZ|0x6fb16e9a", "0x46A50|CALL|0x6fb62890", "0x46A55|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0x46A57|JNZ|0x6fb16e9a", "0x46A5D|MOV|EBP, dword ptr [ESP + 0x14]"],
      "comment": "Processes game input messages including click events and screen coordinate validation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get current game state (nGameState = FUN_6fb62880)\n2. Check if game system is enabled (return if enabled)\n3. Return if game state is 0\n4. Check if processing flag (fIsProcessing) is set (return if set)\n5. Extract screen coordinates from input data (dwScreenX, dwScreenY)\n6. Validate coordinates against initial viewport boundaries\n7. If out of bounds, check game mode (0x06, 0x08, 0x0c, 0x0e) and apply mode-specific boundaries\n8. For mode 0x0c: load viewport bounds based on GetGlobalSystemState\n9. For mode 0x0e: use mode-specific boundaries (g_dwMinScreenX_Mode14, etc.)\n10. For modes 1-2: apply altmode boundaries (g_dwMinScreenX_Alt, g_dwMaxScreenX_Alt2, etc.)\n11. If coordinates within altmode bounds: validate and exit\n12. If coordinates outside all bounds: check object type validation\n13. For valid objects: set object data array to 0, validate with ordinal check\n14. For selected unit: validate with FUN_6fb29fe0, get unit data with FUN_6fb60e10\n15. Call HandleScreenClickEvent if all validations pass\n16. Finalize by setting input data fields (offset +0x18 = 1, +0x1c = 0)\n17. Call Ordinal_511(pInputData) to cleanup\n\nParameters:\n- pInputData (uint): Pointer to input message data structure containing:\n    Offset +0x0c: Screen coordinates (X in low word, Y in high word)\n    Offset +0x08: Additional input flags\n    Offset +0x18, +0x1c: Fields set to 1 and 0 respectively\n\nReturns:\n- void: No return value, modifies global state and input structure in-place\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If game system enabled or game state = 0: returns immediately\n- If processing flag set: returns without processing\n- Screen coordinate mode depends on g_dwObjectType value\n- Ordinal_10262 is used to check game state validity\n- Ordinal_511 is called for input finalization at both entry and exit paths\n\nNote: Function uses 2 stack-allocated temporaries (temp_79f87974120, temp_79fb2594d69) optimized away by compiler",
