      "comment": "Process mouse click events for main game viewport modes (0-4).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check g_dwObjectType is 0, 1, 2, 3, or 4 (main game modes) - exit if not\n2. Extract mouse X from pClickEvent[3] lower 16 bits into dwScreenX\n3. Extract mouse Y from pClickEvent[3] upper 16 bits into dwScreenY\n4. Store coordinates in g_dwInteractionParam0/1 globals\n5. Call GetInitializationFlag to check if system initialized\n6. If initialized AND coordinates within viewport bounds (g_pRenderModeList_ObjectData to g_nMaxViewportX/Y) - exit early (already handled)\n7. If g_dwObjectType == 0 - delegate to HandleUIMouseClickEvent\n8. Call InitializeGameState to get game context\n9. If game state valid, call FindUnitInHashTable to get player unit\n10. If player unit found, get dwInputFlags from unit offset 0x84\n11. Validate coordinates against outer viewport bounds (g_pRenderModeList_ObjectData to g_nMaxViewportX/Y)\n12. If valid, set pClickEvent[6]=1 (processed), pClickEvent[7]=0 (no error)\n13. Validate coordinates against inner screen bounds (g_nMinScreenX/Y to g_nMaxScreenX/Y)\n14. If within inner bounds, call TransformCoordinatesForViewport with unit data\n15. Set pClickEvent[6]=1, pClickEvent[7]=0, clear g_pUIPanel, return\n16. If any validation fails, delegate to HandleUIMouseClickEvent\n\nParameters:\n  pClickEvent - Pointer to click event structure\n    [3] (0x0C): Mouse coordinates (X in low word, Y in high word)\n    [6] (0x18): Result flag (1=processed, 0=not processed)\n    [7] (0x1C): Error code (0=success)\n\nReturns:\n  void - Updates pClickEvent result fields and global state\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Only handles game modes 0-4 (main gameplay)\n  - Modes 5+ delegated to HandleUIMouseClickEvent\n  - Coordinates must pass two-stage validation (outer then inner bounds)\n  - g_dwObjectType==0 always delegates to HandleUIMouseClickEvent\n\nGlobal Variables:\n  g_dwObjectType (0x6fbf8a64) - Current game/UI mode\n  g_dwInteractionParam0/1 - Cached click coordinates\n  g_pRenderModeList_ObjectData (0x6fbf6840) - Min viewport X\n  g_nMaxViewportX (0x6fbf6844) - Max viewport X\n  g_nMinViewportY (0x6fbf6848) - Min viewport Y\n  g_nMaxViewportY (0x6fbf684c) - Max viewport Y\n  g_nMinScreenX/Y, g_nMaxScreenX/Y - Inner screen bounds\n  g_pUIPanel (0x6fbb36e4) - UI panel state\n  g_chCurrentMode (0x6fbf8a78) - Current rendering mode",
