      "instructions": ["0x470B0|SUB|ESP, 0x8c", "0x470B6|MOV|EAX, [0x6fbf8a64]", "0x470BB|PUSH|EBX", "0x470BC|MOV|EBX, dword ptr [ESP + 0x94]", "0x470C3|PUSH|EBP", "0x470C4|PUSH|ESI", "0x470C5|PUSH|EDI", "0x470C6|MOV|EDI, dword ptr [EBX + 0xc]", "0x470C9|XOR|EBP, EBP", "0x470CB|XOR|ESI, ESI", "0x470CD|MOV|SI, word ptr [EBX + 0xc]", "0x470D1|SHR|EDI, 0x10", "0x470D4|CMP|EAX, EBP", "0x470D6|JZ|0x6fb17109", "0x470D8|CMP|EAX, 0x1"],
      "comment": "Processes mouse click events across multiple UI regions and dispatches to appropriate handlers.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract mouse X (low word) and Y (high word) from pMouseEvent[3]\n2. Validate g_dwObjectType is in valid range (0-4); if not, mark event handled and return\n3. Check if click is in close button region (ScreenWidth-0x12E to ScreenWidth-0x10E, ScreenHeight-0x60 to ScreenHeight-0x40)\n   - If yes, set g_dwUIMode2Flag=1, call InitializeGameObjectProperties(4,...) and return\n4. If initialization flag set and coordinate validation returns 1, clear object type data array and reset to inventory mode\n5. If initialization flag set and coordinates within screen bounds:\n   - Check screen state; if 6 (loading), return\n   - Get unit from hash table, build tooltip text\n   - Call ProcessUnitInteraction with coordinates and delay\n   - Reset game state\n6. If click in skill bar region (UIXOffset to ScreenWidth/2-1, ScreenHeight-0x1DF to ScreenHeight-0x1C1):\n   - Check skill slot regions at +0x50, +0xA0, +0xF0, +0x140 pixel intervals\n   - If slot enabled and not current mode, call InitializeGameObjectProperties(6,...) and SelectAvailableItemRarityMode\n7. If click in belt slot region (g_pRenderModeList_ObjectData to g_nMaxViewportX, ScreenHeight-0x6D to g_nMaxViewportY):\n   - Iterate belt slots checking if mouse within slot bounds (+0x2D width)\n   - Update slot selection state and g_dwUIColorFlag\n   - Handle inventory owner via GetGameContext and INVENTORY_GetOwner\n8. If click in viewport region with object type 1 or 2:\n   - Call ProcessMouseClickGameObject with unit data and current mode\n9. All other clicks: delegate to HandleMouseInputEvents\n10. Mark event handled (pMouseEvent[6]=1, pMouseEvent[7]=0) and call InsertCacheNodeWithCookie\n\nParameters:\n  pMouseEvent - Pointer to mouse event structure:\n    [0]: Event type\n    [2]: Delay/timing value (dwInitDelay)\n    [3]: Packed coordinates (low word=X, high word=Y)\n    [6]: Handled flag (set to 1 when processed)\n    [7]: Result code (set to 0 on success)\n\nReturns: void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Screen state 6 (loading): Early return without processing\n  - Invalid object type (not 0-4): Mark handled and return immediately\n  - Null unit from hash table: Early return\n\nUI Regions (pixel offsets from UIXOffset):\n  Skill Slot 0: 0x00-0x50\n  Skill Slot 1: 0x50-0xA0\n  Skill Slot 2: 0xA0-0xF0\n  Skill Slot 3: 0xF0-0x140\n  Belt Slot Width: 0x2D (45 pixels)\n\nGlobal State Modified:\n  g_dwObjectType, g_dwUIMode2Flag, g_dwUIColorFlag, g_dwModeUpdateTimer_renamed, g_adwObjectTypeData",
      "tags": ["PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_1", "PROP_LOOPHEAVY", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
