      "comment": "Activates inventory UI (element 5) and inserts a cache node for processing.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if UI element 5 (inventory) is already active via GetUIResourceBufferElement(5)\n2. If inventory UI is active, exit early (already displayed)\n3. Check if any modal dialogs are active via IsAnyDialogActive()\n4. If dialogs active, exit (cannot activate inventory while dialog shown)\n5. Check cache node flags at offset 0x0C - if 0x40000000 bit NOT set:\n   a. Call ProcessUIStateChange(5, 0, 0) to activate inventory UI\n6. Set cache node field at offset 0x18 to 1 (mark as active/ready)\n7. Set cache node field at offset 0x1C to 0 (clear state/counter)\n8. Insert the cache node via InsertCacheNodeWithCookie for further processing\n\nParameters:\npCacheNode - Pointer to cache node structure with layout:\n             Offset 0x0C: dwFlags (dword) - 0x40000000 bit controls UI activation skip\n             Offset 0x18: dwActiveState (dword) - set to 1 on activation\n             Offset 0x1C: dwStateCounter (dword) - cleared to 0 on activation\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Early exit if inventory UI already active (g_dwUIResourceBuffer[5] != 0)\n- Early exit if any dialog is active (prevents UI conflicts)\n- Skip ProcessUIStateChange if cache node flag 0x40000000 is set\n\nClassification: Worker function - called to activate inventory display and queue cache node",
