      "api_calls": ["INVENTORY_GetOwner", "INVENTORY_GetOwner"],
      "instructions": ["0x47B50|PUSH|ECX", "0x47B51|MOV|EAX, [0x6fbf8a64]", "0x47B56|PUSH|ESI", "0x47B57|CMP|EAX, 0x1", "0x47B5A|PUSH|EDI", "0x47B5B|JZ|0x6fb17b70", "0x47B5D|CMP|EAX, 0x2", "0x47B60|JZ|0x6fb17b70", "0x47B62|CMP|EAX, 0x4", "0x47B65|JZ|0x6fb17b70", "0x47B67|CMP|EAX, 0x3", "0x47B6A|JNZ|0x6fb17cac", "0x47B70|CALL|0x6fb62880", "0x47B75|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [EAX + 0x84]", "0x47B7B|PUSH|EAX"],
      "comment": "Process object type state transitions and validate viewport coordinates for selected game object\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Verify object type is valid (1, 2, 3, or 4 = Monster/Player/Object/Item)\n2. Call FUN_6fb62880() to get object state reference\n3. Call Ordinal_10262() with object state at offset 0x84 - check if object is invalid/gone\n4. If valid, call FUN_6fb8f780() to get current game state mode (1=Game, 4=Menu, 7=InGame)\n5. If mode matches (1, 4, or 7), clear all g_adwObjectTypeData array (5-dword entries, 0x50 bytes total)\n6. Reset g_dwObjectType to 1 (Monster type)\n7. Re-query object state through Ordinal_10262, call FUN_6fb8f0c0() with object state\n8. Load g_wCurrentConfigId into ECX, iterate array at 0x6fbf6904 (20-byte stride)\n9. For each entry, compare word at [entry+10] with g_wCurrentConfigId - set 1 if match, 0 otherwise\n10. Get current config ID from array, update g_dwObjectType and call FUN_6fb8f090() with new config\n11. Call FUN_6fb29fe0() to get selected item slot\n12. If slot valid, call FUN_6fb60e10(slot, 1) to fetch game state for that item\n13. If game state found, get screen coordinates from FUN_6fb8f680/FUN_6fb8f690\n14. Validate coordinates are within viewport bounds: g_nMinScreenX <= X <= g_nMaxScreenX, g_nMinScreenY <= Y <= g_nMaxScreenY\n15. If in bounds, call TransformCoordinatesForViewport() with game state, coordinates, render mode\n16. Clear g_pUIPanel to 0 on success\n\nParameters:\n(void) - No parameters. Uses global state: g_dwObjectType, g_adwObjectTypeData, g_wCurrentConfigId, viewport bounds\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Modifies global state (g_dwObjectType, g_adwObjectTypeData, g_pUIPanel), may trigger TransformCoordinatesForViewport()\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Exits early if object type invalid (not 1-4)\n- Exits early if Ordinal_10262 returns nonzero (object invalid/stale)\n- Exits early if current mode not in (1, 4, 7)\n- Exits early if FUN_6fb29fe0 returns zero (no selected item)\n- Exits early if game state not found for selected slot\n- Exits early if viewport coordinates out of bounds\n- Uses CONCAT31 to combine extraout_ECX with g_chCurrentMode for render mode parameter",
      "tags": ["PARAM_0"]
