      "comment": "Validates mouse click position against screen boundaries and routes to UI handler.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract low 16-bits of input packet offset 0xc as X coordinate\n2. Extract high 16-bits of input packet offset 0xc as Y coordinate\n3. Verify X >= g_dwMinScreenX_Alt AND X < g_dwMaxScreenX_Alt2\n4. Verify Y >= g_dwMaxScreenY AND Y <= g_dwMaxScreenY_Alt2\n5. If all bounds checks pass, route click to HandleUIMouseClickEvent\n6. Return 1 for valid click within bounds, 0 for out of bounds\n\nParameters:\npInputPacket - Pointer to input event structure; contains packed coordinates at offset 0xc\n\nReturns:\n1 if mouse click is within valid screen bounds and handler was called\n0 if mouse click is outside bounds (no handler invoked)\n\nStructure Layout (Input Packet):\nOffset | Size | Field Name    | Type  | Description\n+0x0c  | 2    | nX            | short | Mouse X coordinate (low word)\n+0x0e  | 2    | nY            | short | Mouse Y coordinate (high word)",
