      "instructions": ["0x47D10|PUSH|EBX", "0x47D11|PUSH|ESI", "0x47D12|PUSH|EDI", "0x47D13|MOV|EDI, dword ptr [ESP + 0x10]", "0x47D17|XOR|ESI, ESI", "0x47D19|PUSH|EDI", "0x47D1A|MOV|EBX, dword ptr [EDI + 0xc]", "0x47D1D|MOV|SI, word ptr [EDI + 0xc]", "0x47D21|SHR|EBX, 0x10", "0x47D24|MOV|dword ptr [0x6fbf69f8], ESI", "0x47D2A|MOV|dword ptr [0x6fbf6a00], EBX", "0x47D30|MOV|dword ptr [EDI + 0x18], 0x1", "0x47D37|MOV|dword ptr [EDI + 0x1c], 0x0", "0x47D3E|CALL|0x6fb99c36", "0x47D43|CMP|ESI, dword ptr [0x6fbf6a40]"],
      "comment": "Validates mouse coordinates against screen bounds and processes input if valid.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract lower word of panel data[3] as screen X coordinate (dwScreenX)\n2. Extract upper word of panel data[3] as screen Y coordinate (dwScreenY)\n3. Store extracted coordinates in global interaction parameters (g_dwInteractionParam0/1)\n4. Set panel fields [6]=1, [7]=0 (initialization flags)\n5. Call Ordinal_511 (unknown validation/preprocessing function)\n6. Check if dwScreenX within [g_dwMinScreenX_Alt, g_dwMaxScreenX_Alt2) bounds\n7. Check if dwScreenY within [g_dwMaxScreenY, g_dwMaxScreenY_Alt2] bounds\n8. If ALL bounds checks pass, call HandleMouseInputEvents(pPanelData) and return 1 (success)\n9. Otherwise return 0 (out of bounds)\n\nParameters:\npPanelData (dword *): Panel/viewport data structure, offsets used: [3]=coords, [6],[7]=flags\n\nReturns:\n1 - Mouse coordinates valid and input processed\n0 - Mouse coordinates out of screen bounds\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Ordinal_511 purpose unknown - may validate/preprocess panel state\n- Bounds validation uses global screen limit variables, not hardcoded values\n- Coordinates extracted from single DWORD as: lower WORD=X, upper WORD=Y\n- Global parameters used: g_dwInteractionParam0 (X), g_dwInteractionParam1 (Y)",
