      "instructions": ["0x47D80|PUSH|EBX", "0x47D81|PUSH|EBP", "0x47D82|PUSH|ESI", "0x47D83|PUSH|EDI", "0x47D84|MOV|EDI, dword ptr [ESP + 0x14]", "0x47D88|XOR|ESI, ESI", "0x47D8A|XOR|EBP, EBP", "0x47D8C|PUSH|EDI", "0x47D8D|MOV|EBX, dword ptr [EDI + 0xc]", "0x47D90|MOV|SI, word ptr [EDI + 0xc]", "0x47D94|SHR|EBX, 0x10", "0x47D97|MOV|dword ptr [0x6fbf69f8], ESI", "0x47D9D|MOV|dword ptr [0x6fbf6a00], EBX", "0x47DA3|MOV|dword ptr [EDI + 0x18], 0x1", "0x47DAA|MOV|dword ptr [EDI + 0x1c], EBP"],
      "comment": "Process interaction click event and update UI state.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract screen coordinates from unit structure: X = lower 16 bits of [pUnit+0xc], Y = upper 16 bits of [pUnit+0xc]\n2. Store coordinates in global interaction parameters: g_dwInteractionParam0 = X, g_dwInteractionParam1 = Y\n3. Initialize unit interaction fields: [pUnit+0x18] = 1, [pUnit+0x1c] = 0\n4. Call Ordinal_511 to notify interaction event handler (Storm.dll ordinal)\n5. Validate screen coordinates are within valid bounds:\n   - Check X >= g_dwMinScreenX_Alt AND X < g_dwMaxScreenX_Alt2\n   - Check Y >= g_dwMaxScreenY AND Y <= g_dwMaxScreenY_Alt2\n6. If bounds valid, check for UI inventory panel click:\n   - Calculate panel X range: (g_dwScreenWidth - g_dwUIXOffset - 0x12e) to (g_dwScreenWidth - g_dwUIXOffset - 0x10e)\n   - Calculate panel Y range: (g_dwUIYOffset + g_dwScreenHeight - 0x60) to (g_dwUIYOffset + g_dwScreenHeight - 0x40)\n   - If click within panel AND g_dwUIMode2Flag != 0: reinitialize fields, call Ordinal_511, invoke HandleUIInventoryClick\n7. Clear UI mode flag: g_dwUIMode2Flag = 0\n8. Return 1 if coordinates valid, 0 if out of bounds\n\nParameters:\n  pUnit (UnitAny*) - Pointer to unit/interaction structure with screen coordinates and state fields\n\nReturns:\n  1 if click coordinates within valid screen bounds, 0 if coordinates out of bounds\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  Magic number 0x12e (302 decimal) = left boundary of inventory UI panel\n  Magic number 0x10e (270 decimal) = right boundary of inventory UI panel\n  Magic number 0x60 (96 decimal) = top boundary of inventory UI panel\n  Magic number 0x40 (64 decimal) = bottom boundary of inventory UI panel\n  g_dwUIMode2Flag controls whether inventory panel click processing is active",
