      "comment": "Checks if a screen point falls within the UI viewport panel bounds.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract X coordinate (lower 16 bits) and Y coordinate (upper 16 bits) from param struct\n2. Set initial state fields (offset 0x18=1, 0x1C=0) and call Ordinal_511 (Storm.dll viewport refresh)\n3. Check X bounds: (ScreenWidth - UIXOffset - 0x12E) <= X <= (ScreenWidth - UIXOffset - 0x10E)\n4. Check Y bounds: (UIYOffset - 0x60 + ScreenHeight) <= Y <= (UIYOffset - 0x40 + ScreenHeight)\n5. If both bounds satisfied, set g_dwUIMode2Flag=1, reset state fields, call Ordinal_511, return 1\n6. Otherwise return 0\n\nParameters:\nnUIPanel (int): Pointer to UI panel structure containing X/Y coordinates at offset 0xC\n\nReturns:\n1 if point is within viewport bounds\n0 if point is outside bounds\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x12E = 302 (decimal) - Right bound offset from screen width\n0x10E = 270 (decimal) - Left bound offset from screen width\n0x60 = 96 (decimal) - Top bound offset from screen height\n0x40 = 64 (decimal) - Bottom bound offset from screen height\nOrdinal_511 = Storm.dll InvalidateViewport - refresh screen viewport after state changes",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Inventory", "PARAM_1", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
