      "api_count": 1,
      "api_calls": ["InitializeStringBuffer"],
      "instructions": ["0x480E0|MOV|EAX, [0x6fbf8a64]", "0x480E5|PUSH|ESI", "0x480E6|CMP|EAX, 0xb", "0x480E9|JNZ|0x6fb181d1", "0x480EF|MOV|EDX, dword ptr [ESP + 0x8]", "0x480F3|MOV|ESI, dword ptr [0x6fbf6a40]", "0x480F9|XOR|EAX, EAX", "0x480FB|MOV|ECX, dword ptr [EDX + 0xc]", "0x480FE|MOV|AX, word ptr [EDX + 0xc]", "0x48102|SHR|ECX, 0x10", "0x48105|CMP|EAX, ESI", "0x48107|MOV|[0x6fbf69f8], EAX", "0x4810C|MOV|dword ptr [0x6fbf6a00], ECX", "0x48112|JL|0x6fb18136", "0x48114|CMP|EAX, dword ptr [0x6fbf6a44]"],
      "comment": "Validates click event coordinates against three UI regions when object type is 0xb (inventory/interface mode).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if g_dwObjectType == 0xb (UI interaction mode)\n2. Extract screen X coordinate from low word of pClickEvent[3]\n3. Extract screen Y coordinate from high word of pClickEvent[3]\n4. Store coordinates in g_dwInteractionParam0 (X) and g_dwInteractionParam1 (Y)\n5. Check Region 1 (Alt screen bounds): g_dwMinScreenX_Alt <= X < g_dwMaxScreenX_Alt2 AND g_dwMaxScreenY <= Y <= g_dwMaxScreenY_Alt2\n6. If in Region 1, call HandleUIMouseClickEvent and return\n7. Check Region 2 (Mode11 bounds): g_dwMinScreenX_Mode11 < X < g_dwMaxScreenX_Mode11 AND g_dwMinScreenY_Mode11 <= Y <= g_dwMinScreenY\n8. If in Region 2, call HandleUIMouseClickEvent and return\n9. Check Region 3: g_dwMinScreenX_Region3 < X < g_dwMaxScreenX_Region3 AND g_dwMinScreenY_Region3 <= Y <= g_dwMaxScreenY_Region3\n10. If in Region 3, call HandleUIMouseClickEvent and return\n11. If click outside all regions, reset UI state: set viewport/cursor to -1, clear selection pointers\n12. Call InitializeStringBuffer with null/reset parameters\n\nParameters:\n    pClickEvent (dword *) - Pointer to click event structure; pClickEvent[3] contains packed screen coordinates (low word = X, high word = Y)\n\nReturns:\n    void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n    - Only processes events when g_dwObjectType == 0xb\n    - Click outside all regions triggers full UI state reset\n    - Multiple globals reset to 0xffffffff indicating invalid/cleared state\n\nGlobals Modified:\n    g_dwInteractionParam0 - Set to click X coordinate\n    g_dwInteractionParam1 - Set to click Y coordinate  \n    g_dwViewportX, g_dwUIState - Reset to 0xffffffff on miss\n    g_dwCursorScreenX, g_dwCursorScreenY - Reset to 0xffffffff on miss (set twice, likely legacy)\n    g_pGameStateConfig, g_dwUIFlag1 - Cleared to 0 on miss\n    g_pSelectedUnit, g_pSelectedEntity - Cleared to 0 on miss",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Inventory", "PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_1"]
    },
