      "instructions": ["0x481E0|MOV|EAX, [0x6fbf8a64]", "0x481E5|PUSH|EBX", "0x481E6|PUSH|EBP", "0x481E7|PUSH|ESI", "0x481E8|CMP|EAX, 0xb", "0x481EB|PUSH|EDI", "0x481EC|JNZ|0x6fb1848c", "0x481F2|MOV|ESI, dword ptr [ESP + 0x14]", "0x481F6|XOR|EBX, EBX", "0x481F8|MOV|ECX, ESI", "0x481FA|MOV|EDI, dword ptr [ESI + 0xc]", "0x481FD|MOV|BX, word ptr [ESI + 0xc]", "0x48201|SHR|EDI, 0x10", "0x48204|MOV|dword ptr [0x6fbf69f8], EBX", "0x4820A|MOV|dword ptr [0x6fbf6a00], EDI"],
      "comment": "Handles mouse click events on UI panel buttons based on screen coordinates.\n\nClassification: Callback handler - registered to process UI click events when g_dwObjectType == 0xb\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Early exit if g_dwObjectType != 0xb (not in correct UI mode)\n2. Extract click coordinates from pClickEvent[3]: X = low 16 bits, Y = high 16 bits\n3. Store coordinates in g_dwInteractionParam0 (X) and g_dwInteractionParam1 (Y)\n4. Check if click is in minimap close button region (screen right side, offset -0x12e to -0x10e, Y offset -0x60 to -0x40)\n   - If yes: Set g_dwUIMode2Flag = 1, mark event handled, call InitializeGameObjectProperties\n5. Check bounds via ValidateCoordinateInBounds - if returns 1, exit (already handled)\n6. Check if click in Alt screen region (g_dwMinScreenX_Alt to g_dwMaxScreenX_Alt2, g_dwMaxScreenY to g_dwMaxScreenY_Alt2)\n   - If yes: Call HandleMouseInputEvents and return\n7. Check if click in Mode11 screen region (Mode11 bounds)\n   - If yes: Call HandleMouseInputEvents and return\n8. Get game context and inventory owner via GetGameContext/INVENTORY_GetOwner\n9. If owner exists: Clear all UI flags, call SendGameStatePacket\n10. If no owner, check multiple button regions:\n    a. Panel button 1 (UIXOffset+0xdf to +0xff): Toggle g_dwUIPanelFlag, handle refresh\n    b. Panel button 2 (UIXOffset+0x113 to +0x133): Set visibility flags\n    c. Mode1 button (screen right -0xed to -0xd9, Y -0x57 to -0x45): Set g_dwUIMode1Flag\n11. Mark click event as handled: pClickEvent[6] = 1, pClickEvent[7] = 0\n12. Call InsertCacheNodeWithCookie to queue the processed event\n\nParameters:\n  pClickEvent - Pointer to click event structure:\n    [0x0C] (offset 3): Packed coordinates (low word = X, high word = Y)\n    [0x18] (offset 6): Handled flag (set to 1 when processed)\n    [0x1C] (offset 7): Reserved (set to 0)\n\nReturns: void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Returns immediately if g_dwObjectType != 0xb\n- Returns after ValidateCoordinateInBounds returns 1\n- Different code paths based on whether inventory owner exists\n\nUI Button Regions (relative to screen/UI offsets):\n- Minimap close: (ScreenWidth - UIXOffset - 0x12e) to (- 0x10e), Y: -0x60 to -0x40\n- Panel button 1: UIXOffset + 0xdf to + 0xff\n- Panel button 2: UIXOffset + 0x113 to + 0x133\n- Mode1 button: (ScreenWidth - UIXOffset - 0xed) to (- 0xd9), Y: -0x57 to -0x45\n\nGlobal State Modified:\n- g_dwInteractionParam0, g_dwInteractionParam1: Click coordinates\n- g_dwUIMode1Flag, g_dwUIMode2Flag: UI mode toggles\n- g_dwUIPanelFlag, g_dwUIRefreshFlag, g_dwUIColorFlag, g_dwUIUpdateFlag, g_dwUIVisibilityFlag",
      "tags": ["PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Act", "PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_1", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
    },
