      "instructions": ["0x48790|CMP|dword ptr [0x6fbf8a64], 0xb", "0x48797|JNZ|0x6fb187c4", "0x48799|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [ESP + 0x4]", "0x4879D|PUSH|EAX", "0x4879E|MOV|dword ptr [EAX + 0x18], 0x1", "0x487A5|MOV|dword ptr [EAX + 0x1c], 0x0", "0x487AC|CALL|0x6fb99c36", "0x487B1|MOV|ECX, 0x5", "0x487B6|CALL|0x6fb5d970", "0x487BB|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0x487BD|JNZ|0x6fb187c4", "0x487BF|CALL|0x6fb596c0", "0x487C4|RET|0x4"],
      "comment": "Process monster cache node and conditionally transition to menu state.\n\nClassification: Worker function (conditional cache insertion with state transition)\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if g_dwObjectType equals 0xb (monster object type)\n2. If not monster type, return immediately (no-op)\n3. Set cache node state flag at offset +0x18 to 1 (active/valid)\n4. Set cache node counter at offset +0x1c to 0 (reset)\n5. Insert cache node into system via InsertCacheNodeWithCookie\n6. Query UI resource buffer element at index 5\n7. If element 5 is zero, call TransitionGameState to enter menu (state 7)\n\nParameters:\npCacheNode - Pointer to cache node structure to process\n             Structure offsets:\n             +0x18: dword - State/active flag (set to 1)\n             +0x1c: dword - Counter/index (reset to 0)\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0xb (11) - Monster object type identifier\n0x18 - Offset to state flag field in cache node\n0x1c - Offset to counter field in cache node\n5 - UI resource buffer index for transition check\n1 - Active state value\n0 - Reset counter value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Function is a no-op if object type is not monster (0xb)\n- State transition only occurs if UI resource element 5 is zero\n- No callers found via xrefs - likely referenced via function pointer table",
