      "instructions": ["0x487D0|MOV|EAX, [0x6fbf8c90]", "0x487D5|PUSH|ESI", "0x487D6|PUSH|EDI", "0x487D7|MOV|EDI, ECX", "0x487D9|MOV|ECX, dword ptr [0x6fbf8c94]", "0x487DF|MOV|ESI, EDX", "0x487E1|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0x487E3|JNZ|0x6fb187e9", "0x487E5|TEST|ECX, ECX", "0x487E7|JZ|0x6fb187f5", "0x487E9|TEST|EDI, EDI", "0x487EB|JZ|0x6fb18822", "0x487ED|TEST|ESI, ESI", "0x487EF|JZ|0x6fb18822", "0x487F1|TEST|EAX, EAX"],
      "comment": "Conditionally update UI item and state flags based on current state.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. If both current flags are 0 (initial state), proceed to step 6\n2. If either input flag is 0, reset display (call FUN_6fb8d210 with mode 3) and update flags, then return\n3. If item flag is already 0, go back to step 6\n4. If state flag is 0 or current state is set, update flags and return\n5. If state flag is set, proceed to step 7\n6. If item flag is non-zero, fall through to step 7\n7. Call FUN_6fb8d210 with mode 1 (update display)\n8. Update both flags to input values and return\n\nParameters:\n- dwItemFlag (uint, ECX): Item selection flag; 0 clears selection\n- dwStateFlag (uint, EDX): Item state flag; 0 clears state\n\nReturns:\n- void (modifies global state and display via FUN_6fb8d210)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- When either input is 0, resets display before updating flags\n- Skips update if item and state flags haven't changed from current state\n- Calls FUN_6fb8d210 in mode 1 for most transitions, mode 3 for full reset",
      "tags": ["PARAM_2"]
