      "comment": "Normalize object type based on current object type value.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize normalization flag to 0\n2. If current object type is 0x0D (13 decimal):\n   - Set object type to 0x0C (12 decimal)\n   - Return\n3. If current object type is 0x10 (16 decimal):\n   - Set object type to 0x0F (15 decimal)\n4. Return\n\nParameters:\nNone. Uses global g_dwObjectType.\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Magic values 0x0D and 0x10 appear to represent specific object types that need normalization\n- Normalization decrements the type value by 1 in both cases\n- Flag initialization may indicate a state tracker for downstream processing\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n- 0x0D: Source object type requiring normalization to 0x0C\n- 0x0C: Normalized target type\n- 0x10: Secondary source type requiring normalization to 0x0F\n- 0x0F: Secondary normalized target type\n- g_dwObjectTypeNormalizationFlag: State flag (initialized to 0 each call)",
