      "comment": "Normalize object type identifiers to canonical values.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Set g_dwObjectTypeNormalizationFlag = 1 (indicates normalization in progress)\n2. Load g_dwObjectType from global address 0x6fbf8a64\n3. If g_dwObjectType == 0x0d (uninitialized SuperUnique):\n   - Normalize to 0x0c (canonical SuperUnique)\n   - Call handler with parameters (5, 1, 0)\n   - Return\n4. Else if g_dwObjectType == 0x10 (alternate Boss type):\n   - Normalize to 0x0f (canonical Boss)\n5. Call handler with parameters (5, 1, 0) for all types\n6. Return\n\nParameters:\nNone (void function)\n\nReturns:\nvoid (modifies globals g_dwObjectType and g_dwObjectTypeNormalizationFlag)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Type 0x0d -> 0x0c: SuperUnique normalization (early return path)\n- Type 0x10 -> 0x0f: Boss type normalization (falls through to common handler)\n- All other types: Handler called without type modification\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x0d: Source type for SuperUnique (uninitialized state)\n- 0x0c: Canonical SuperUnique identifier\n- 0x10: Source type for Boss (alternate encoding)\n- 0x0f: Canonical Boss identifier\n- 0x5: Handler operation code (normalization handler)\n- 0x1: Handler flag parameter (always 1)\n- 0x0: Handler data parameter (always 0)",
