      "comment": "Initializes or clears game state based on dialog state parameter.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Store nDialogState value into g_nCurrentDialogState global\n2. If nDialogState == 0: Clear all UI and viewport state\n   - Set g_pGameStateConfig to NULL\n   - Set all viewport coordinates (g_dwViewportX) to 0xFFFFFFFF (uninitialized)\n   - Set all screen cursor coordinates (g_dwCursorScreenX, g_dwCursorScreenY) to 0xFFFFFFFF\n   - Set UI flags and selection pointers to NULL\n3. If nDialogState != 0: Only update g_nCurrentDialogState, exit without clearing state\n\nParameters:\nnDialogState: int - Dialog state identifier; 0 = clear all state, non-zero = update and preserve state\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- State clearing is guarded by equality check with 0; any non-zero value skips reset\n- Duplicate cursor coordinate assignments in assembly indicate possible field reuse or register reuse optimization\n- Magic value 0xFFFFFFFF used for uninitialized coordinates (representing \"no valid value\")",
