      "comment": "Validates mouse click coordinates against screen bounds and dispatches to UI handler.\n\nThis callback/event handler processes mouse click events for object types 0xC (12) and 0xD (13).\nExtracts X/Y coordinates from the event structure, validates against multiple screen boundary\nregions based on global system state, and either processes the click or resets UI state.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check g_dwObjectType equals 0xC or 0xD (inventory/interaction modes), exit if neither\n2. Extract packed coordinates from pMouseEvent+0xC: low word = X, high word = Y\n3. Store coordinates in g_dwInteractionParam0 (X) and g_dwInteractionParam1 (Y)\n4. First bounds check: validate X in [g_dwMinScreenX_Alt, g_dwMaxScreenX_Alt2)\n   and Y in [g_dwMaxScreenY, g_dwMaxScreenY_Alt2]\n5. If outside first bounds, call GetGlobalSystemState to determine active region\n6. Based on system state (EAX): select Mode12 bounds (state=0) or NoState bounds (state!=0)\n7. Second bounds check against selected region\n8. If inside bounds: delegate to HandleUIMouseClickEvent(pMouseEvent)\n9. If outside all bounds: clear UI state (g_pGameStateConfig, g_dwUIFlag1,\n   g_pSelectedUnit, g_pSelectedEntity = 0) and call InitializeStringBuffer to reset\n\nParameters:\n  pMouseEvent - Pointer to mouse event structure\n                Offset +0xC: Packed coordinates (low word = X, high word = Y)\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - No direct callers found - likely registered as callback in UI event system\n  - Object type must be 0xC or 0xD for any processing to occur\n  - Multiple screen boundary regions handle different UI modes/states\n\nGlobals Accessed:\n  g_dwObjectType (0x6fbf8a64) - Current interaction object type\n  g_dwMinScreenX_Alt (0x6fbf6a40) - Primary region min X\n  g_dwMaxScreenX_Alt2 (0x6fbf6a44) - Primary region max X\n  g_dwMaxScreenY (0x6fbf6a48) - Primary region min Y\n  g_dwMaxScreenY_Alt2 (0x6fbf6a4c) - Primary region max Y\n  g_dwMinScreenX_Mode12 (0x6fbf6884) - Mode12 region min X\n  g_dwMaxScreenX_Mode12 (0x6fbf6888) - Mode12 region max X\n  g_dwMinScreenY_Mode12 (0x6fbf688c) - Mode12 region min Y\n  g_dwMaxScreenY_Mode12 (0x6fbf6890) - Mode12 region max Y\n  g_dwMinScreenX_NoState (0x6fbf68bc) - NoState region min X\n  g_dwMaxScreenX_NoState (0x6fbf68c0) - NoState region max X\n  g_dwMinScreenY_Alt (0x6fbf68c4) - NoState region min Y\n  g_dwMaxScreenY_NoState (0x6fbf68c8) - NoState region max Y\n  g_dwInteractionParam0 (0x6fbf69f8) - Stored click X coordinate\n  g_dwInteractionParam1 (0x6fbf6a00) - Stored click Y coordinate\n  g_pGameStateConfig (0x6fbf8a58) - Game state config pointer (cleared on invalid)\n  g_dwUIFlag1 (0x6fbf8a5c) - UI state flag (cleared on invalid)\n  g_pSelectedUnit (0x6fbf8a68) - Selected unit pointer (cleared on invalid)\n  g_pSelectedEntity (0x6fbf8a6c) - Selected entity pointer (cleared on invalid)",
      "tags": ["PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_1"]
