      "instructions": ["0x48A40|MOV|EAX, [0x6fbf8a64]", "0x48A45|PUSH|EBX", "0x48A46|PUSH|EBP", "0x48A47|PUSH|ESI", "0x48A48|CMP|EAX, 0xc", "0x48A4B|PUSH|EDI", "0x48A4C|JZ|0x6fb18a57", "0x48A4E|CMP|EAX, 0xd", "0x48A51|JNZ|0x6fb18f9b", "0x48A57|MOV|EDI, dword ptr [ESP + 0x14]", "0x48A5B|XOR|EBP, EBP", "0x48A5D|MOV|EBX, dword ptr [EDI + 0xc]", "0x48A60|MOV|BP, word ptr [EDI + 0xc]", "0x48A64|SHR|EBX, 0x10", "0x48A67|MOV|dword ptr [0x6fbf69f8], EBP"],
      "comment": "Processes UI mouse click events and routes to appropriate UI region handlers.\n\nClassification: Worker function - UI input router\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Early exit if g_dwObjectType is not 0xC (inventory mode) or 0xD (stash mode)\n2. Extract mouse X coordinate from low word of pMouseEvent[3] (uVar9)\n3. Extract mouse Y coordinate from high word of pMouseEvent[3] (uVar8)\n4. Store coordinates in g_dwInteractionParam0/g_dwInteractionParam1\n5. Check if game state active and coordinates valid via ValidateCoordinateInBounds\n6. If inactive/invalid, check if click is in skill bar region (right side, 0x12E-0x10E from right edge)\n   - If in skill bar Y range (0x60-0x40 from bottom), set g_dwUIMode2Flag=1, handle event\n7. Call GetGlobalSystemState to determine UI layout mode\n8. Check stash panel region based on state (Y: -0x1C7 to -0x1B6 if state, else -0x103 to -0xF2)\n   - X range: UIXOffset+0x49 to UIXOffset+0x96\n   - If hit, set g_fPanelStashVisibility=1, handle event\n9. Check inventory panel close button region (X: UIXOffset+0x110/0x113 to +0x138, Y: near bottom)\n   - If hit, set inventory flags and handle event\n10. If ValidateCoordinateInBounds returns 1, clear all UI flags and return\n11. Check primary screen bounds (g_dwMinScreenX_Alt to g_dwMaxScreenX_Alt2, etc.)\n    - If hit, call HandleMouseInputEvents and cache event\n12. Check secondary screen bounds based on GetGlobalSystemState (Mode12 vs NoState bounds)\n    - If hit, call HandleMouseInputEvents and cache event\n13. Get game context, check if inventory has owner via INVENTORY_GetOwner\n14. If no owner and click in help button region (-0x57 to -0x45 Y, -0xED to -0xD9 X from right)\n    - Set g_dwUIMode1Flag=1, clear other flags, handle event\n15. Re-check stash panel region (same as step 8) with different flag clearing\n16. Check render mode list bounds (g_pRenderModeList_8/12 regions)\n    - If hit, clear all flags, cache event and return\n17. Call Ordinal_10005, if result != 2, clear flags and return\n18. Additional ValidateCoordinateInBounds check, return if non-zero\n19. Check if Y below screen bottom - 0x30, return if so\n20. GetScrollWindowMode checks for modes 1 and 3 with left-half screen filtering\n21. If GetScreenState returns 6, call SendResourceUpdate\n22. Final fallback: set pMouseEvent[6]=1, clear g_pGameStateConfig/g_dwUIFlag1\n23. Cache event via InsertCacheNodeWithCookie, clear inventory/panel flags\n\nParameters:\n  pMouseEvent (uint *) - Pointer to mouse event structure\n    [3] - Low word: X coordinate, High word: Y coordinate\n    [6] - Event handled flag (set to 1 when processed)\n    [7] - Event continuation flag (set to 0 when handled)\n\nReturns: void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Exits immediately if object type not 0xC or 0xD (inventory/stash modes)\n- Multiple overlapping region checks with priority ordering\n- State-dependent coordinate bounds (GetGlobalSystemState affects thresholds)\n- Scroll window mode affects left-half screen click filtering\n\nGlobals Modified:\n- g_dwInteractionParam0/1 - Mouse coordinates\n- g_dwUIMode1Flag, g_dwUIMode2Flag - UI mode indicators\n- g_fPanelStashVisibility - Stash panel visibility\n- g_dwUIPanelFlag, g_dwUIRefreshFlag, g_dwUIColorFlag - UI state flags\n- g_dwGameObjectCount, g_dwInventoryItemCount - Object counts\n- g_pGameStateConfig, g_dwUIFlag1 - Game state config\n\nCallees:\n- IsGameStateActive, ValidateCoordinateInBounds, GetGlobalSystemState\n- HandleMouseInputEvents, GetGameContext, INVENTORY_GetOwner\n- InitializeGameObjectProperties, InsertCacheNodeWithCookie\n- Ordinal_10005, GetScrollWindowMode, GetScreenState, SendResourceUpdate",
      "tags": ["PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_1", "PROP_LOOPHEAVY", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
