      "instructions": ["0x48FB0|MOV|EAX, [0x6fbf8a64]", "0x48FB5|PUSH|EBX", "0x48FB6|PUSH|EBP", "0x48FB7|PUSH|ESI", "0x48FB8|CMP|EAX, 0xc", "0x48FBB|PUSH|EDI", "0x48FBC|JZ|0x6fb18fd4", "0x48FBE|CMP|EAX, 0xd", "0x48FC1|JZ|0x6fb18fd4", "0x48FC3|POP|EDI", "0x48FC4|POP|ESI", "0x48FC5|POP|EBP", "0x48FC6|MOV|dword ptr [0x6fbf8d20], 0x0", "0x48FD0|POP|EBX", "0x48FD1|RET|0x4"],
      "comment": "Handles mouse click events on inventory/stash UI panels.\n\nProcesses click coordinates from message structure and determines which UI region\nwas clicked, then triggers appropriate UI state changes or panel initializations.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check g_dwObjectType for 0xC (inventory mode) or 0xD (stash mode)\n2. If neither mode active, clear g_dwUIColorFlag and return early\n3. Extract click coordinates from pMsg[3]: low word = X, high word = Y\n4. Clear UI mode flags and store coordinates in g_dwInteractionParam0/1\n5. Get game context and player inventory pointer at offset +0x84\n6. Check if game state active and validate coordinates in bounds\n7. If no inventory owner and click in close button region (right side):\n   - X: screenWidth - UIXOffset - 0x12E to - 0x10E (302 to 270 from right)\n   - Y: screenHeight + UIYOffset - 0x60 to - 0x40 (96 to 64 from bottom)\n   - Call ProcessUIStateChange(0x19, 1, 0) to close panel\n8. Check belt slot region based on GetGlobalSystemState():\n   - X: UIXOffset + 0x110/0x113 to + 0x138/0x13B (40 pixel width)\n   - Y: screenHeight + UIYOffset - 0x64 to - 0x3C\n   - If clicked and g_dwGameObjectCount != 0, send packet 0x4F/0x12\n9. Set pMsg[6] = 1 (handled), pMsg[7] = 0 and call InsertCacheNodeWithCookie\n10. Check character panel button region (lower left):\n    - X: UIXOffset + 0x49 to + 0x96 (73 to 150 from left)\n    - Y varies by GetGlobalSystemState() return\n    - Call InitializeGameStatePanel(3) for skills, (4) for quests\n11. Final ValidateCoordinateInBounds check - if returns 1, clear panel flags\n12. Handle UI color flag reset and refresh flag management\n13. Always mark message as handled before returning\n\nParameters:\n  pMsg - Pointer to UI message structure:\n         +0x00: Message type\n         +0x0C: Packed coordinates (low word = X, high word = Y)\n         +0x18: Handled flag (set to 1 when processed)\n         +0x1C: Result code (set to 0)\n\nReturns:\n  void - Modifies global UI state flags and message structure\n\nGlobals Modified:\n  g_dwUIColorFlag, g_dwUIMode2Flag, g_dwUIMode3Flag, g_dwGameObjectCount,\n  g_dwInventoryItemCount, g_dwUIPanelFlag, g_dwUIRefreshFlag,\n  g_fPanelStashVisibility, g_dwUIMode1Flag, g_dwInteractionParam0/1\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Returns early if g_dwObjectType not 0xC or 0xD\n  - Close button detection uses screen-relative coordinates\n  - Belt slot and panel regions use UI offset-adjusted coordinates\n  - GetGlobalSystemState() affects coordinate calculations by 1 pixel",
      "tags": ["PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PROP_NOCALLER", "STRUCT_Skill", "PARAM_1", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
