      "comment": "Resets UI state and clears selection when object type matches expected value (0xC)\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if g_dwObjectType equals 0xC (specific game mode/object type)\n2. If not matching, exit immediately (early return)\n3. Set cache node flags at offset +0x18 to 1 (active flag)\n4. Set cache node flags at offset +0x1C to 0 (clear secondary flag)\n5. Insert cache node with cookie value into cache system\n6. Get UI resource buffer element at index 5\n7. If UI resource element is non-zero, exit (resource still active)\n8. If UI resource element is zero, perform full UI state reset:\n   a. Process UI state change with parameters (0x19, 1, 0)\n   b. Send packed data packet (0x4F, 0x12, 0, 0) to notify server\n   c. Clear g_pGameStateConfig to NULL\n   d. Set viewport/cursor coordinates to -1 (0xFFFFFFFF) indicating invalid\n   e. Clear g_dwUIFlag1 to 0\n   f. Clear g_pSelectedUnit and g_pSelectedEntity to NULL\n\nParameters:\ndwCacheNodeCookie - Pointer to cache node structure with flags at +0x18 and +0x1C\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Object type 0xC appears to be a specific game mode requiring UI cleanup\n- UI resource buffer element 5 acts as a guard; reset only occurs when zero\n- Multiple globals are set to -1 as sentinel values for invalid coordinates\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0xC (12) - Object type that triggers this cleanup routine\n5 - UI resource buffer index checked for cleanup condition\n0x19 (25) - UI state change type parameter\n0x4F (79) - Packed data message type\n0x12 (18) - Packed data subtype\n0xFFFFFFFF (-1) - Invalid/uninitialized coordinate sentinel value\n\nGlobal Variables Modified:\ng_pGameStateConfig - Cleared to NULL\ng_dwViewportX (0x6fbb36e8) - Set to -1\ng_dwUIState (0x6fbb36ec) - Set to -1  \ng_dwCursorScreenX (0x6fbb36f0, 0x6fbb36f8) - Set to -1\ng_dwCursorScreenY (0x6fbb36f4, 0x6fbb36fc) - Set to -1\ng_dwUIFlag1 - Cleared to 0\ng_pSelectedUnit - Cleared to NULL\ng_pSelectedEntity - Cleared to NULL",
