      "instructions": ["0x493C0|PUSH|ESI", "0x493C1|MOV|ESI, dword ptr [ESP + 0x8]", "0x493C5|TEST|dword ptr [ESI + 0xc], 0x40000000", "0x493CC|JNZ|0x6fb193d3", "0x493CE|CALL|0x6fafd540", "0x493D3|PUSH|ESI", "0x493D4|MOV|dword ptr [ESI + 0x18], 0x1", "0x493DB|MOV|dword ptr [ESI + 0x1c], 0x0", "0x493E2|CALL|0x6fb99c36", "0x493E7|POP|ESI", "0x493E8|RET|0x4"],
      "comment": "Initialize a cache node and insert it into the cache system.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if UI screen flag (bit 0x40000000) is clear at offset +0xc\n2. If flag clear, call EnableUIScreen31() to enable UI screen 31\n3. Set node state at offset +0x18 to 1 (mark as active/inserted)\n4. Set node state at offset +0x1c to 0 (clear secondary state)\n5. Call InsertCacheNodeWithCookie to add node to cache\n\nParameters:\npCacheNode - Pointer to CacheNode structure (passed as uint)\n  +0x0c: dwFlags - Node flags (bit 0x40000000 = UI already enabled)\n  +0x18: dwActiveState - Active/insertion state (1 = active)\n  +0x1c: dwSecondaryState - Secondary state field (cleared to 0)\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- EnableUIScreen31 is skipped if UI flag 0x40000000 is already set\n- No callers found in code (likely called via function pointer or external)\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x40000000 - UI screen enabled flag in node flags field\n0x0c - Offset to flags field in CacheNode structure\n0x18 - Offset to active state field in CacheNode\n0x1c - Offset to secondary state field in CacheNode\n1 - Active/inserted state value\n0 - Clear/reset state value",
