      "comment": "Initializes expansion resources and inserts cache node into system.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if global system state is active (GetGlobalSystemState)\n2. Early exit if system state is inactive (EAX == 0)\n3. Check cache node flags at offset +0x0C for 0x40000000 bit\n4. If flag not set, check UI resource buffer element 5\n5. If UI resource is 0, verify expansion MPQ exists\n6. If expansion exists and system state active:\n   a. Initialize game object properties (mode 1)\n   b. Query system info and increment counters\n   c. Get game context and extract resource array at offset +0x84\n   d. Get array element 4 and initialize if non-null\n   e. Get array element 5 and initialize if non-null\n7. Set cache node field +0x18 to 1 (initialized flag)\n8. Set cache node field +0x1C to 0 (clear state)\n9. Insert cache node via InsertCacheNodeWithCookie\n\nParameters:\npCacheNode (dword *) - Pointer to cache node structure\n  +0x0C: Flags field (bit 30 = 0x40000000 skip expansion init)\n  +0x18: Initialization status (1 = initialized)\n  +0x1C: State field (cleared to 0)\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Exits early without inserting if global system state is 0\n- Skips expansion initialization if flag 0x40000000 is set at +0x0C\n- Skips expansion initialization if UI resource element 5 is non-zero\n- Always sets +0x18=1, +0x1C=0 and inserts node if system state active\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x40000000 - Bit 30 flag: Skip expansion resource initialization\n0x5 - UI resource buffer index for expansion check\n0x84 - Offset in game context to resource array pointer\n0x4, 0x5 - Array indices for resources to initialize\n0x18 - Cache node offset for initialization flag\n0x1C - Cache node offset for state field",
