      "comment": "Processes pending object state transitions and reports accumulated validation errors.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load current object type from g_dwObjectType\n2. Check if object type is 0xc (12) or 0xd (13) indicating portal/waypoint objects\n3. If match found:\n   a. Reset g_dwObjectType to 0\n   b. Call FUN_6fb5d370 with parameters (0x19, 1, 0) to process object-specific logic\n   c. Call SendPackedData(0x4f, 0x12, 0, 0) to transmit state update packet\n4. Check g_pCharacterBankStorage for pending validation error code\n   a. If non-zero error: Call ReportValidationError() to handle error\n   b. Clear error code by writing 0 to g_pCharacterBankStorage\n5. Check g_pCharacterTradeStashStorage for pending validation error code\n   a. If non-zero error: Call ReportValidationError() to handle error\n   b. Clear error code by writing 0 to g_pCharacterTradeStashStorage\n6. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\n(none) - Function operates on global state only\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value; side effects modify global state and may transmit packets\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If g_dwObjectType is neither 0xc nor 0xd: Skip object type processing, proceed to error reporting\n- Zero error codes: Validation error checks skip ReportValidationError() calls\n- Multiple errors: Both error globals are checked independently; order of reporting is g_pCharacterBankStorage then g_pCharacterTradeStashStorage\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0xc (12): Portal object type ID\n0xd (13): Waypoint object type ID\n0x19 (25): Object processing command passed to FUN_6fb5d370\n0x4f (79): Packet command for state update transmission\n0x12 (18): Packet subtype for state update\n0: Success/reset value written to error tracking globals",
