      "api_count": 1,
      "api_calls": ["InitializeStringBuffer"],
      "instructions": ["0x49630|MOV|EAX, [0x6fbf8a64]", "0x49635|PUSH|ESI", "0x49636|CMP|EAX, 0xe", "0x49639|JNZ|0x6fb196ca", "0x4963F|MOV|EDX, dword ptr [ESP + 0x8]", "0x49643|MOV|ESI, dword ptr [0x6fbf6a40]", "0x49649|XOR|EAX, EAX", "0x4964B|MOV|ECX, dword ptr [EDX + 0xc]", "0x4964E|MOV|AX, word ptr [EDX + 0xc]", "0x49652|SHR|ECX, 0x10", "0x49655|CMP|EAX, ESI", "0x49657|MOV|[0x6fbf69f8], EAX", "0x4965C|MOV|dword ptr [0x6fbf6a00], ECX", "0x49662|JL|0x6fb1967c", "0x49664|CMP|EAX, dword ptr [0x6fbf6a44]"],
      "comment": "Processes mouse click events for game mode 14 (type 0xE).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if g_dwObjectType equals 0xE (mode 14), return immediately if not\n2. Extract X coordinate from pClickEvent[3] (lower 16 bits) into g_dwInteractionParam0\n3. Extract Y coordinate from pClickEvent[3] (upper 16 bits via SHR 0x10) into g_dwInteractionParam1\n4. Check click coordinates against primary viewport bounds (g_dwMinScreenX_Alt to g_dwMaxScreenX_Alt2, g_dwMaxScreenY to g_dwMaxScreenY_Alt2)\n5. If within primary bounds, forward to HandleUIMouseClickEvent for processing\n6. If outside primary bounds, check secondary bounds (g_dwMinScreenX_Mode14 to g_dwMaxScreenX, g_dwMinScreenX_Mode14 to g_dwMaxScreenY_Mode14)\n7. If within secondary bounds, forward to HandleUIMouseClickEvent\n8. If outside all valid regions, clear UI state:\n   - Set g_pGameStateConfig = 0\n   - Set g_dwUIFlag1 = 0\n   - Set g_pSelectedUnit = 0\n   - Set g_pSelectedEntity = 0\n   - Call InitializeStringBuffer with null/reset parameters\n\nParameters:\n  pClickEvent - Pointer to click event structure\n    [+0x0C] (dword) - Packed mouse coordinates (X in lower 16 bits, Y in upper 16 bits)\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Function returns early if object type is not 0xE\n  - Uses dual-region boundary validation (primary and secondary viewport regions)\n  - Resets all UI interaction globals when click is out of bounds\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x0E - Game mode 14 object type identifier\n  0x10 - Bit shift amount for Y coordinate extraction (16 bits)",
