      "api_count": 4,
      "api_calls": ["INVENTORY_GetOwner", "INVENTORY_GetOwner", "InsertCacheNodeWithCookie", "InsertCacheNodeWithCookie"],
      "instructions": ["0x49A90|MOV|EAX, [0x6fbf8a64]", "0x49A95|PUSH|EBX", "0x49A96|PUSH|EBP", "0x49A97|PUSH|ESI", "0x49A98|CMP|EAX, 0xe", "0x49A9B|PUSH|EDI", "0x49A9C|JZ|0x6fb19aaf", "0x49A9E|POP|EDI", "0x49A9F|POP|ESI", "0x49AA0|POP|EBP", "0x49AA1|MOV|dword ptr [0x6fbf8d20], 0x0", "0x49AAB|POP|EBX", "0x49AAC|RET|0x4", "0x49AAF|MOV|EBX, dword ptr [ESP + 0x14]", "0x49AB3|XOR|EDI, EDI"],
      "comment": "Handles UI region click interactions based on mouse coordinates and game state.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if g_dwObjectType == 0x0E (UI interaction mode); if not, clear g_dwUIMode1Flag and exit\n2. Extract mouse X coordinate from low word and Y from high word of dwEventData+0x0C\n3. Store coordinates in g_dwInteractionParam0 (X) and g_dwInteractionParam1 (Y)\n4. Clear g_dwUIMode2Flag and g_dwUIMode3Flag\n5. Call GetGameContext() and get inventory pointer at offset +0x84\n6. Call IsGameStateActive(); if active, skip to secondary region checks\n7. Call INVENTORY_GetOwner(pInventory); if owner exists, skip to secondary checks\n8. Calculate X bounds: g_dwScreenWidth - g_dwUIXOffset + offsets (-302 to -270)\n9. Calculate Y bounds: g_dwUIYOffset + g_dwScreenHeight + offsets (-96 to -64)\n10. If click in primary region (minimap area), call ProcessUIStateChange(0x1A, 1, 0) and exit\n11. Check secondary region (X: +275 to +315, Y: -100 to -60) for menu button\n12. If in menu region and g_dwMenuState != 0, clear states and call SendPackedData(0x4F, 0x17, 0, 0)\n13. Check third region (X: +144 to +184, Y: -223 to -183) for targeting button\n14. If in targeting region and g_dwTargetingMode != 0, clear and call SendPackedData(0x4F, 0x18, 0, 0)\n15. Call ValidateCoordinateInBounds with event pointer; if returns 1, clear flags and exit\n16. Re-validate inventory owner; check fourth region bounds for panel interaction\n17. If in panel region and g_dwObjectTypeNormalizationFlag == 0, call InitializeGameStatePanel(1)\n18. Process final UI state updates based on g_dwUIMode1Flag\n19. Clear panel mode flags based on current state\n20. Set event data fields +0x18 = 1, +0x1C = 0, call InsertCacheNodeWithCookie\n\nParameters:\n  dwEventData - Pointer to event structure containing mouse coordinates at +0x0C\n                (low word = X, high word = Y), output fields at +0x18, +0x1C\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Early exit if g_dwObjectType != 0x0E (not in UI interaction mode)\n  - Multiple mutually exclusive UI regions checked in priority order\n  - Panel state flags cleared based on hierarchical state machine\n\nGlobals Modified:\n  g_dwUIMode1Flag (0x6fbf8cb0), g_dwUIMode2Flag (0x6fbf8d10), g_dwUIMode3Flag (0x6fbf8d14)\n  g_dwInteractionParam0 (0x6fbf69f8), g_dwInteractionParam1 (0x6fbf6a00)\n  g_dwMenuState (0x6fbf8cc0), g_dwPanelMode (0x6fbf8cc4)\n  g_dwTargetingMode (0x6fbf8cc8), g_dwPanelNpcMode (0x6fbf8ccc)\n  g_dwUIPanelFlag (0x6fbf8ca0), g_dwUIRefreshFlag (0x6fbf8c98)\n  g_dwGameStateFlags (0x6fbf8a88)\n\nUI Region Bounds (relative to screen offsets):\n  Region 1 (Minimap): X [-302, -270], Y [-96, -64] from adjusted screen coords\n  Region 2 (Menu): X [+275, +315], Y [-100, -60]\n  Region 3 (Targeting): X [+144, +184], Y [-223, -183]\n  Region 4 (Panel): X [-87, -69], Y [-237, -213]",
      "tags": ["PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_1", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
