      "comment": "Resets UI state when the global object type equals 0xE (14).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if g_dwObjectType == 0xE, exit early if not\n2. Set cache node flags: pCacheNode[6] = 1 (active), pCacheNode[7] = 0 (cleared)\n3. Call InsertCacheNodeWithCookie to add node to cache system\n4. Get UI resource ID 1 via GetUIResourceByIdWithValidation\n5. If resource not found (NULL), reset all UI state globals:\n   - g_pGameStateConfig = NULL\n   - g_dwViewportX, g_dwUIState = -1 (invalid)\n   - g_dwCursorScreenX, g_dwCursorScreenY = -1 (both pairs)\n   - g_dwUIFlag1 = 0\n   - g_pSelectedUnit, g_pSelectedEntity = NULL\n6. Get UI resource buffer element 5 via GetUIResourceBufferElement\n7. If buffer element not found (NULL):\n   - Clear g_dwGameStateFlags = 0\n   - Call ProcessUIStateChange(0x1A, 1, 0) to transition UI state\n   - Call SendPackedData(0x4F, 0x17, 0, 0) to send network packet\n\nParameters:\n  pCacheNode - Pointer to cache node structure, fields at +0x18 and +0x1C modified\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Function exits immediately if g_dwObjectType != 0xE\n  - No callers found - likely called via function pointer table\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0xE (14) - Object type triggering reset\n  0x18, 0x1C - Cache node flag offsets\n  1 - UI resource ID for validation check\n  5 - UI resource buffer element index\n  0x1A (26) - UI state change identifier\n  0x4F (79) - Network packet type\n  0x17 (23) - Network sub-command",
