      "instructions": ["0x4A330|MOV|EAX, [0x6fbf8a64]", "0x4A335|PUSH|EBX", "0x4A336|PUSH|EBP", "0x4A337|PUSH|ESI", "0x4A338|CMP|EAX, 0xf", "0x4A33B|PUSH|EDI", "0x4A33C|JZ|0x6fb1a354", "0x4A33E|CMP|EAX, 0x10", "0x4A341|JZ|0x6fb1a354", "0x4A343|POP|EDI", "0x4A344|POP|ESI", "0x4A345|POP|EBP", "0x4A346|MOV|dword ptr [0x6fbf8d20], 0x0", "0x4A350|POP|EBX", "0x4A351|RET|0x4"],
      "comment": "Handle mouse click events on inventory panel UI elements.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if g_dwObjectType is 0xF (stash) or 0x10 (cube) - exit early if neither\n2. Extract click coordinates from mouse event structure at offset +0xc\n   - X coordinate: lower 16 bits (ushort)\n   - Y coordinate: upper 16 bits (shift right 16)\n3. Reset UI mode flags (g_dwUIMode2Flag, g_dwUIMode3Flag)\n4. Store click coordinates in g_dwInteractionParam0/1 for later processing\n5. Get game context and player inventory pointer at context+0x84\n6. Check if game state is active and inventory has no owner:\n   - If click is in panel close button region (right side, -0x12E to -0x10E from screen right edge):\n     - Call ProcessUIStateChange(0x1C, 1, 0) to close panel\n     - Return immediately\n7. Check if click is in scroll button region (X: offset+0x110 to +0x138, Y: -100 to -0x3C from bottom):\n   - If g_dwUIScrollOffsetY was set, reset it and send close packet (0x4F, 0x1F)\n   - Reset scroll offsets and color flag\n   - Set mouse event result fields (+0x18=1, +0x1C=0)\n   - Insert into cache node and return\n8. Reset scroll offsets for general area click\n9. If game state inactive and no inventory owner:\n   - Check for click in gold pickup region: call InitializeGameStatePanel(6)\n10. Check for click in left panel button region: call InitializeGameStatePanel(7)\n11. Call ValidateCoordinateInBounds to check if click is within valid UI area\n12. If bounds validation fails (result != 1):\n    - Hide cube panel visibility flag\n    - Reset UI mode flag\n    - Clear UI color flag and handle panel/scroll state cleanup\n    - Set mouse event result and insert into cache\n\nParameters:\n- pMouseEvent (dword): Pointer to mouse event structure containing:\n  +0x0C: Packed click coordinates (low 16-bit=X, high 16-bit=Y)\n  +0x18: Result/handled flag (set to 1 when processed)\n  +0x1C: Secondary result flag (set to 0 when processed)\n\nReturns:\n- void (modifies global UI state flags and mouse event structure)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Object type check: Only processes clicks when type is 0xF (stash) or 0x10 (cube)\n- Panel close button: Right side of panel, triggers ProcessUIStateChange\n- Scroll region: Triggers packet send and UI state reset\n- Gold pickup: Left panel button (panel index 6)\n- Additional button: Left panel button (panel index 7)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x0F: Object type for stash panel\n- 0x10: Object type for cube panel\n- 0x1C: UI state ID for inventory close action\n- 0x4F: Packet type for UI action\n- 0x1F: Packet subtype for close/reset\n- 0x12E: X offset from right edge for close button min\n- 0x10E: X offset from right edge for close button max\n- 0x60, 0x40: Y offsets from bottom for close button region\n- 0x110, 0x138: X offsets for scroll button region\n- 0x57, 0x45: Y offsets for gold pickup button region\n- 0xED, 0xD9: X offsets for gold pickup button region\n- 0x14D, 0x13C: Y offsets for left panel button region\n- 0x32, 0x7F: X offsets for left panel button region",
      "tags": ["PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_1", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
