      "comment": "Filters mouse click events for object types 0xF (mode 15) and 0x10 (mode 16).\nValidates click coordinates against two screen regions before delegating to handler.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check g_dwObjectType - only process if 0xF or 0x10, else exit early\n2. Extract X coordinate from pClickEvent[3] lower 16 bits into g_dwInteractionParam0\n3. Extract Y coordinate from pClickEvent[3] upper 16 bits into g_dwInteractionParam1\n4. Check primary bounds: g_dwMinScreenX_Alt <= X < g_dwMaxScreenX_Alt2 AND\n   g_dwMaxScreenY <= Y <= g_dwMaxScreenY_Alt2\n5. Check secondary bounds (mode 15): g_dwMinScreenX_Mode15 <= X < g_dwMaxScreenX_Mode15 AND\n   g_dwMinScreenY_Mode15 <= Y <= g_dwMaxScreenY_Mode15\n6. If click within EITHER region, call HandleUIMouseClickEvent(pClickEvent)\n7. If click outside BOTH regions, clear UI state:\n   - g_pGameStateConfig = 0\n   - g_dwUIFlag1 = 0\n   - g_pSelectedUnit = NULL\n   - g_pSelectedEntity = NULL\n   - Call InitializeStringBuffer(NULL, -1, -1, 0, 0)\n\nParameters:\n  pClickEvent: Pointer to click event structure\n               - Offset 0xC: Mouse coordinates (low word=X, high word=Y)\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Function has no callers (orphaned or callback registration)\n  - Two separate screen regions define valid click areas\n  - Mode 15/16 specific filtering for UI panels\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0xF (15) - First valid object type\n  0x10 (16) - Second valid object type\n  0xC - Offset to mouse coordinates in event structure\n  0x10 - Bit shift for Y extraction (16 bits)",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Inventory", "PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_1"]
    },
