      "comment": "Activates a cache node and sends UI/network updates when object type is 15 (0xf).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if g_dwObjectType equals 0xf (object type 15)\n2. If not type 15, return immediately without action\n3. Set cache node field at offset 0x18 to 1 (activation flag)\n4. Set cache node field at offset 0x1c to 0 (clear secondary flag)\n5. Call InsertCacheNodeWithCookie to register the node in cache\n6. Call ProcessUIStateChange(0x1c, 1, 0) to update UI panel state\n7. Call SendPackedData(0x4f, 0x1f, 0, 0) to send network packet\n\nParameters:\n  pCacheNode: Pointer to CacheNode structure to activate\n    - Field at +0x18 (uint): Activation flag, set to 1\n    - Field at +0x1c (uint): Secondary flag, cleared to 0\n\nReturns:\n  void: No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Early exit if g_dwObjectType != 0xf (object type 15)\n  - Object type 0xf appears to be a specific UI panel mode\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  - 0xf (15): Object type for this specific UI panel mode\n  - 0x18: Offset to activation flag in CacheNode\n  - 0x1c: Offset to secondary flag in CacheNode (also UI ID for ProcessUIStateChange)\n  - 0x4f (79): Network packet opcode\n  - 0x1f (31): Network packet data value",
