      "comment": "Handles mouse click events on UI hotspot regions.\n\nClassification: Callback/Handler - invoked by UI input system for click events\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Early exit if object type != 0x11 (specific UI mode), clearing UI color flag\n2. Extract mouse X/Y coordinates from event structure (offset 0xC, packed as low/high word)\n3. Clear UI mode flags and store coordinates in global interaction params\n4. Get game context and extract inventory pointer at offset 0x84\n5. Check if game state is active - if active, skip special hotspot handling\n6. Get inventory owner - if owner exists, skip special hotspot handling\n7. Check if click is in \"help\" hotspot region (screen right edge):\n   - X bounds: (screenWidth - UIXOffset - 0x12E) to (screenWidth - UIXOffset - 0x10E)\n   - Y bounds: (UIYOffset + screenHeight - 0x60) to (UIYOffset + screenHeight - 0x40)\n   - If in bounds: trigger UI state change (mode 0x1D=help) and return\n8. Check if click is in \"cancel targeting\" hotspot region (bottom center):\n   - X bounds: (UIXOffset + 0x110) to (UIXOffset + 0x138)\n   - Y bounds: (UIYOffset + screenHeight - 0x64) to (UIYOffset + screenHeight - 0x3C)\n   - If in bounds and targeting active: clear targeting, send cancel packet (0x4F, 0x24)\n   - Mark event handled and insert into cache\n9. Clear targeting state, validate click coordinates via ValidateCoordinateInBounds\n10. If validation returns 1: clear panel flag and targeting flags, return\n11. If UI color flag clear: mark event handled, insert cache, clear refresh flag\n12. Otherwise clear UI state flags based on panel/refresh state, insert cache\n\nParameters:\n  pMouseEvent - Pointer to mouse event structure (dword *):\n    +0x0C (offset 3): Packed coordinates (low word = X, high word = Y)\n    +0x18 (offset 6): Event handled flag (set to 1 when processed)\n    +0x1C (offset 7): Event result (set to 0)\n\nReturns: void\n\nLocal Variables (SSA temporaries - cannot be renamed):\n  bVar1 (fGameActive): bool - Result of IsGameStateActive() call\n  pvVar2 (pGameContext): void* - Game context pointer from GetGameContext()\n  pUVar3 (pInventoryOwner): UnitAny* - Unit owning the inventory, NULL if none\n  iVar4 (nBoundsResult): int - Return value from ValidateCoordinateInBounds()\n  uVar5 (dwMouseY): uint - Mouse Y coordinate (high 16 bits of packed value)\n  uVar6 (dwMouseX): uint - Mouse X coordinate (low 16 bits of packed value)\n  extraout_var: undefined3 - High bytes from bool return (ignored)\n  pInventory: Inventory* - Player inventory from game context + 0x84\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Object type != 0x11: Clears color flag and returns immediately\n- Game state active or inventory has owner: Falls through to coordinate validation\n- Help hotspot click: Triggers UI state 0x1D without processing event further\n- Cancel targeting click: Sends network packet to cancel current targeting\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x11: UI mode for hotspot processing\n- 0x1D: Help panel UI state identifier\n- 0x4F: Packet type for targeting cancel\n- 0x24: Packet subtype for targeting cancel\n- 0x12E/0x10E: Help button X offset range (302-270 pixels from right)\n- 0x60/0x40: Help button Y offset range (96-64 pixels from bottom)\n- 0x110/0x138: Cancel button X offset range (272-312 pixels)\n- 0x64/0x3C: Cancel button Y offset range (100-60 pixels from bottom)",
      "tags": ["PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_1", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
    },
