      "comment": "Processes mouse click events when game is in mode 0x11 (17).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if g_dwObjectType equals 0x11 (mode 17) - exit immediately if not\n2. Extract X coordinate from lower 16 bits of pClickEvent[3] into g_dwInteractionParam0\n3. Extract Y coordinate from upper 16 bits of pClickEvent[3] into g_dwInteractionParam1\n4. Validate coordinates against primary screen bounds (g_dwMinScreenX_Alt to g_dwMaxScreenX_Alt2,\n   g_dwMaxScreenY to g_dwMaxScreenY_Alt2) - if within bounds, delegate to HandleUIMouseClickEvent\n5. Validate coordinates against secondary mode 17 bounds (g_dwMinScreenX_Mode17 to \n   g_dwMaxScreenX_Mode17, g_dwMinScreenY_Mode17 to g_dwMaxScreenY_Mode17)\n6. If within secondary bounds, delegate to HandleUIMouseClickEvent\n7. If outside both bounds, clear UI state: g_pGameStateConfig=0, g_dwUIFlag1=0,\n   g_pSelectedUnit=0, g_pSelectedEntity=0, then call InitializeStringBuffer to reset\n\nParameters:\n  pClickEvent - Pointer to click event structure with mouse coords at offset 0xC\n                (lower word = X, upper word = Y)\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Only processes when g_dwObjectType == 0x11 (mode 17)\n  - Two separate valid screen regions checked in sequence\n  - Coordinates stored in g_dwInteractionParam0/1 before validation\n  - UI state cleared if click outside valid regions\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x11 - Mode 17 object type\n  0xC (pClickEvent+3) - Offset to packed X/Y coordinates\n  0x10 - Bit shift for Y coordinate extraction",
