      "comment": "Handles Enter key input on automap slider control to send chat message.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check input event byte at offset +8 for carriage return (0x0D) or newline (0x0A)\n2. If neither CR nor LF detected, return 1 (event not consumed)\n3. Call slider control vtable method at +0x3C to get current text content into buffer\n4. Send network message via SendNetworkMessage with text buffer content\n5. Reset game object properties via InitializeGameObjectProperties(2, 0, 0.0, 0.0, 0)\n6. Call slider control vtable method at +0x34 with g_pdwBasePropertyString to clear text\n7. Return 0 (event consumed successfully)\n\nParameters:\n  pSliderControl (SliderControl*) - ECX: Pointer to slider control (unused, uses g_pAutomapSliderControl)\n  nInputEvent (int) - EDX: Pointer to input event structure, byte at offset +8 contains key code\n\nReturns:\n  int - 0 if Enter key was handled (event consumed), 1 if not Enter key (pass through)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Both CR (0x0D) and LF (0x0A) are treated as Enter key input\n  - Function ignores pSliderControl parameter, always uses global g_pAutomapSliderControl\n  - Message is sent regardless of text content (could send empty message)\n  - 256 byte local buffer allocated on stack for text content\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x0D (13): Carriage return ASCII character\n  0x0A (10): Line feed ASCII character\n  0x3C (60): Vtable offset for GetText method\n  0x34 (52): Vtable offset for SetText/Clear method\n  0x100 (256): Text buffer size in bytes\n  2: Game object property mode parameter for reset\n\nGlobals Used:\n  g_pAutomapSliderControl - Global slider control instance pointer\n  g_pdwBasePropertyString - Base property string used for slider text reset",
