      "comment": "Activates a cache object and sends UI/network notifications when object type is 0x12.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if global object type (g_dwObjectType) equals 0x12\n2. If not 0x12, exit early without action\n3. Set activation flag at object offset +0x18 to 1 (active state)\n4. Reset counter/state at object offset +0x1c to 0\n5. Insert object into cache via InsertCacheNodeWithCookie\n6. Notify UI system via ProcessUIStateChange(0x1E=30, 1=deactivate, 0)\n7. Send network packet via SendPackedData(0x4F=79, 0x27=39, 0, 0)\n\nParameters:\npCacheObject - Pointer to cache object structure with activation fields at +0x18 and +0x1c\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Function is orphan (no callers found) - may be registered as callback or called via pointer\n- Only processes objects when g_dwObjectType == 0x12 (specific game mode/state)\n- UI state change uses element ID 0x1E (30) with deactivate state\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x12 - Object type check value (specific game object type)\n0x18 - Offset to activation flag in cache object\n0x1C - Offset to state counter in cache object\n0x1E (30) - UI element ID for ProcessUIStateChange\n0x4F (79) - Network packet opcode for SendPackedData\n0x27 (39) - Network packet data value",
