      "comment": "Initialize game state for specified mode (Single Player or Multi-Player)\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Query current game handle state via FUN_6fb2a190\n2. If mode is Single Player (0x20747368 \"hst \"):\n   - Validate game handle exists (return if NULL)\n   - Call Ordinal_11107(handle, 10, 0x0b) to set Single Player mode\n   - Return on validation failure\n3. Else if mode is Multi-Player (0x20326671 \"1fq \"):\n   - Validate game handle exists (return if NULL)\n   - Call Ordinal_11107(handle, 0x12, 0x0b) to set Multi-Player mode\n   - Return on validation failure\n4. Call Ordinal_11108 to finalize mode configuration\n5. Set global game state flags to active (0x01)\n6. Reset game state counter to 0\n7. Record initialization timestamp via GetTickCount\n8. If game data file not yet initialized (g_dwGameDataFileHandle == 0):\n   - Call Ordinal_578 to build config file path in local buffer\n   - Write initialized file data via ConcatenatePathAndWriteFile\n\nParameters:\n- nGameModeId (dword in ECX): Game mode identifier\n  - 0x20747368 = Single Player mode (\"hst \")\n  - 0x20326671 = Multi-Player mode (\"1fq \")\n\nReturns:\n- void (no return value)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Function returns silently if game handle is NULL\n- Invalid mode causes early exit after validation failure\n- File initialization only occurs once per session\n- Note: Function uses 1 stack-allocated temporary (uVar1) optimized away in decompilation\n\nRelated Functions:\n- FUN_6fb2a190 - Query game session handle\n- FUN_6fb667e0 - Caller, initiates mode initialization\n- Ordinal_578 - Path construction\n- Ordinal_11107 - Channel validation/assignment\n- Ordinal_11108 - Mode finalization\n- ConcatenatePathAndWriteFile - File initialization",
