      "comment": "Initialize UI interaction state and validate game object selection.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Clear all global UI/interaction flags (color, object type, parameters)\n2. Get current UI selection context via FUN_6fb62880()\n3. If no selection, abort with FUN_6fb8f0c0(0)\n4. Load object instance pointer from selection context offset +0x84\n5. Validate object instance via Ordinal_10262 (Storm.dll validator)\n6. If validation fails, abort with FUN_6fb8f0c0(0)\n7. If validation succeeds, return (caller performs further UI updates)\n\nParameters:\n(none)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Side effects: g_dwUIColorFlag, g_dwObjectType, g_dwInteractionParam0/1 set to 0; FUN_6fb8f0c0 called on error paths\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- No UI selection context: fails at step 3\n- Invalid object instance: fails at step 5\n- Both failure paths call FUN_6fb8f0c0(0) for cleanup\n\nNote: Function uses 1 temporary SSA variable (nResult) optimized away in register EAX.\n\nRelated Functions:\n- FUN_6fb62880() - Retrieve current UI selection context\n- FUN_6fb8f0c0() - Error handler/UI state reset\n- Ordinal_10262 - Object instance validator (Storm.dll)",
