      "comment": "Renders viewport tiles within visible bounds.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get current viewport tile array pointer and count via Ordinal_10262\n2. If tile count > 0, iterate through tile array (0x14 bytes per entry)\n3. For each tile: load bounds (nMinY, nMaxY, nMinX, nMaxX from offsets -0x9, -0x5, -0xd, -0x11)\n4. Get current viewport coordinates via FUN_6fb8f680 (X) and FUN_6fb8f690 (Y)\n5. Check if viewport point is within tile bounds: min_x <= view_x <= max_x AND min_y <= view_y <= max_y\n6. If bounds valid: call Ordinal_10749 to extract palette indices\n7. Call Ordinal_10758 to check tile visibility\n8. If visible, call FUN_6fb1b570 to process tile rendering parameters\n9. Call Ordinal_10756 to validate rendering state\n10. Check final pixel coordinates against back buffer height (g_dwBackBufferHeight) and viewport height (g_dwViewportHeight)\n11. Select color palette component: green (0x6fbf68d0) or red (0x6fbf68d1) based on rendering path\n12. Call FUN_6fb92980 to render tile with pixel values and color\n13. Loop to next tile (increment by 0x14 bytes) until end of array (0x6fbf8c9d)\n\nParameters:\nNone - function uses global viewport tile array g_pViewportTileArray\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If tile count is 0, function returns immediately\n- Viewport bounds checks prevent out-of-bounds rendering\n- Two rendering paths: error case uses red component, success uses green component\n- Tile array iteration uses pointer arithmetic (pTile + 0x14)\n- Note: Function uses 2 stack-allocated byte temporaries optimized away (local_19, local_1a)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x84 - offset in viewport data structure to tile count field\n0x14 - tile entry size in bytes\n0x5fd - palette index size constant for Ordinal_10749\n0x6fbf8bc1 - global viewport tile array base address (g_pViewportTileArray)\n0x6fbf8c9d - viewport tile array end address\n0x6fbf68d0, 0x6fbf68d1 - palette component addresses (green, red)\n\nStructure Layout - Tile Entry (0x14 bytes):\nOffset | Size | Field Name    | Type   | Description\n-------|------|---------------|--------|---------------------\n-0x11  | 4    | nMinX         | int    | Minimum X coordinate\n-0xd   | 4    | nMaxX         | int    | Maximum X coordinate  \n-0x9   | 4    | nMinY         | int    | Minimum Y coordinate\n-0x5   | 4    | nMaxY         | int    | Maximum Y coordinate\n+0x0   | 1    | byPixelLo     | byte   | Pixel value (low byte)\n-0x1   | 1    | byPixelHi     | byte   | Pixel value (high byte)",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Inventory", "PARAM_0", "SRC_CmnItems.h", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
