      "comment": "Validate entity skill attribute requirements for game entity\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize output flag to 0\n2. Check global system state - return 0 if system not initialized\n3. Test entity attribute 0x3012 with key 0x10 - return 0 if invalid\n4. Test entity attribute 0x3015 with key 0x100 - return 0 if test passes\n5. Check attributes 3 and 0x25 - set flag 1 if either present\n6. Load entity type from parameter 1 + offset 8\n7. Route by entity type (0x0F=111, 0x67=103, 0x30=48, 0x31=49, others):\n   - Type 0x0F (111): Check attributes 2, 0x1E, 0x47\n   - Type 0x67 (103): Check attributes 0x21, 0x1E, 0x1C with 0x47 fallback\n   - Type 0x30 (48): Check attribute 0x1C and fallback attribute 0x47\n   - Type 0x31 (49): Check attributes 0x1E, 0x1C with 0x47 fallback\n   - Default path: Skip further validation\n8. Set match flag and output to 1 when validation conditions met\n9. Call final ordinal function with entity ID and fixed parameters\n10. Return match flag, or 0 if final validation fails\n\nParameters:\n  pEntityNode (int IMPLICIT ECX) - Pointer to entity structure with type at offset +8\n  dwEntityId (dword IMPLICIT EDX) - Entity unique identifier\n  pOutFlags (dword*) - Output pointer to receive validation flags\n\nReturns:\n  Non-zero on validation success, 0 on failure\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Output flag may be set multiple times before final return\n  - Multiple attribute checks per entity type path\n  - Function returns early on system state or initial attribute failures\n  - Final ordinal call determines ultimate success/failure\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x10, 0x100 - Attribute keys for initial validation\n  0x3012, 0x3015 - Attribute values/states\n  0x3, 0x25, 0x2, 0x1E, 0x1C, 0x21, 0x47 - Entity attributes being validated\n  0x0F (15) - Entity type constant 1\n  0x67 (103) - Entity type constant 2\n  0x30 (48) - Entity type constant 3\n  0x31 (49) - Entity type constant 4\n  0x230 (560) - Large entity type boundary\n  0x231 (561) - Another entity type boundary\n  0x168 (360) - Mid-range entity type boundary\n\nRelated Functions:\n  GetGlobalSystemState() - Check system initialization\n  FindLinkedListNodeValue() - Retrieve entity type value\n  Ordinal_10707, Ordinal_10731, Ordinal_10765 - Attribute checking functions\n  Ordinal_10756 - Final validation function",
