      "api_calls": ["SetActiveFont", "GetTotalStatValue", "GetUnitStatById", "GetTotalLifeBonusFromInventory", "FormatString", "GetTotalStatValue", "GetTotalStatValue", "GetTotalStatValue", "GetArrayElementPtr", "GetTotalStatValue", "...+37 more"],
      "instructions": ["0x4BB10|SUB|ESP, 0x1dc", "0x4BB16|PUSH|ESI", "0x4BB17|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0x4BB19|TEST|ESI, ESI", "0x4BB1B|JZ|0x6fb1c0fd", "0x4BB21|PUSH|EBX", "0x4BB22|PUSH|EBP", "0x4BB23|PUSH|EDI", "0x4BB24|XOR|ECX, ECX", "0x4BB26|CALL|0x6fb99a02", "0x4BB2B|MOV|EBP, 0x6fbb3ad4", "0x4BB30|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x30], EAX", "0x4BB34|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x24], EBP", "0x4BB38|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x14], 0x0", "0x4BB40|LEA|EDI, [ESP + 0x6c]"],
      "comment": "Renders stat lines for item display in inventory/equipment screen.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if pStatUnit is valid (non-null parameter check)\n2. Call Ordinal_10127 to save display state\n3. Initialize pCurrentEntry pointer to g_pStatLineInfoTable\n4. For each entry in stat table (loop until entry + 0x10 >= table end):\n   a. Initialize 256-character Unicode buffer with default constructors\n   b. Query stat presence via Ordinal_10519 (presence check)\n   c. Query stat value via Ordinal_10521 and compare values\n   d. Set dwCurrentColor = 3 if stat values mismatch (different bases)\n   e. Extract X offset (offset -0xc) and Y offset (offset -0x4)\n   f. Switch on stat type (offset 0) with cases: 0x6, 0x15, 0x1f, 0x27, 0x29, 0x2b, 0x2d\n5. Type 0x6 (Damage): Calculate from base via Ordinal_10564, format with Ordinal_578\n6. Type 0x15 (Attributes): Sum base + bonuses + equipment effects, query Ordinal_10257\n7. Type 0x1f (Requirement): Query Ordinal_10431, check Ordinal_10539 requirement\n8. Types 0x27+ (Charges): Query frame count, apply adjustments, cap value at 0x5f\n9. Format all values to Unicode buffer via Unicode::toUnicode\n10. Render output based on position flags or call specialized render functions\n\nParameters:\npStatUnit (int, IMPLICIT ECX): Pointer to unit/item structure with stat data\n\nReturns: void (renders to screen via Ordinal_10121 or DrawCenteredText)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Position X=0: use Ordinal_10121; X=0 with Y!=0: use Ordinal_10117\n- Frame 1 adjusts -0x14, Frame 2 by -0x32\n- Color codes: 1=bonus (green), 2=penalty (red), 3=normal (gray), 4=capped (orange)\n\nNote: Function uses 8 stack-allocated temporary arrays (uStack_1a0-1c0) for bonus calculations optimized away. These are assembly-only temporaries initialized inline and cannot be renamed in decompiled view.",
