      "comment": "Checks if a mouse click occurred within the snow button UI region and enables snow mode if so.\n\nClassification: Worker function - Handles snow mode toggle via UI button click detection\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get game context via GetGameContext()\n2. Search for player unit using FindNodeBySearchCriteria with type 7\n3. If search returns -1 (not found), call ProcessUIStateChange(0x24, 2, 0) and exit\n4. Look up unit in hash table with FindUnitInHashTable(unitId, 1)\n5. If unit not found, call ProcessUIStateChange(0x24, 2, 0) and exit\n6. Initialize pUIState[6] (clicked flag) to 0\n7. Calculate screen bounds: maxY = screenHeight - 49, halfWidth = screenWidth / 2\n8. Get cursor position via GetCurrentResourceID() (X) and GetResourceFlags() (Y)\n9. First bounds check: cursor must be within (0 to halfWidth, 0 to maxY)\n10. If outside first bounds, return without updating UI state\n11. Calculate snow button region:\n    - X bounds: UIXOffset + 272 to UIXOffset + 304\n    - Y bounds: UIYOffset + screenHeight - 95 to UIYOffset + screenHeight - 63\n12. Get cursor position again for second bounds check\n13. If cursor is within snow button region:\n    - Set g_fSnowModeEnabled = 1\n    - Set pUIState[6] = 1 (clicked in snow button)\n    - Set pUIState[7] = 0\n    - Initialize snow effect via InitializeGameObjectProperties(4, 0, 0.0, 0.0, 0)\n    - Insert UI state into cache via InsertCacheNodeWithCookie\n14. If cursor in screen bounds but outside button region:\n    - Set pUIState[6] = 1\n    - Set pUIState[7] = 0\n    - Insert UI state into cache\n\nParameters:\n  pUIState - Pointer to UI state structure\n    +0x18 (index 6): BOOL clicked - Set to 1 if click processed\n    +0x1C (index 7): uint reserved - Always set to 0\n\nReturns: void\n\nGlobals Used:\n  g_dwScreenHeight (0x6fbae0e8) - Screen height in pixels\n  g_dwScreenWidth (0x6fbae0e4) - Screen width in pixels\n  g_dwUIYOffset (0x6fbfd800) - UI Y coordinate offset\n  g_dwUIXOffset (0x6fbfd7fc) - UI X coordinate offset\n  g_fSnowModeEnabled (0x6fbf8d28) - Snow mode enabled flag (1=enabled)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x31 (49) - Bottom margin offset for clickable area\n  0x130 (304) - Snow button right edge X offset from UIXOffset\n  0x110 (272) - Snow button left edge X offset from UIXOffset\n  0x3F (63) - Snow button top edge Y offset from bottom\n  0x5F (95) - Snow button bottom edge Y offset from bottom\n  7 - Search criteria type for player unit\n  1 - Unit type for hash table lookup\n  0x24 - UI element ID for ProcessUIStateChange\n  4 - Game object type for snow effect",
      "tags": ["PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_1", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
    },
