      "comment": "Performs hit testing for NPC shop inventory grid slots.\n\nDetermines if the cursor is hovering over a valid NPC shop inventory slot\nand updates selection state globals accordingly. Used when player opens\nNPC shop interface to track which slot the mouse cursor is over.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get game context and find player unit via FindNodeBySearchCriteria(type=7)\n2. Look up player unit in hash table with FindUnitInHashTable\n3. If no player found, trigger UI state change (0x24=close shop, mode=2)\n4. Clear pUIContext[6] (interaction state offset 0x18)\n5. Calculate valid cursor bounds: X in [0, screenWidth/2], Y in [0, screenHeight-0x31]\n6. Get current cursor position via GetCurrentResourceID/GetResourceFlags\n7. If cursor out of bounds, exit early\n8. If snow mode enabled, check cursor against snow region bounds:\n   - X bounds: [UIXOffset+0x110, UIXOffset+0x130]\n   - Y bounds: [UIYOffset+screenHeight-0x5f, UIYOffset+screenHeight-0x3f]\n   - Disable snow mode if cursor outside region\n9. Get inventory data from player unit at offset 0x84 (piVar4[0x21])\n10. If inventory data exists, reset all selection globals to -1/NULL\n11. Get inventory owner via INVENTORY_GetOwner\n12. If no owner (player viewing NPC shop), iterate shop display table:\n    - Table at g_pNpcShopDisplayTable (0x6fbf8bb0), 11 entries of 20 bytes each\n    - Entry format: [minX, maxX, minY, maxY, unused] (5 DWORDs)\n    - For each valid entry (minX > 0):\n      a. Get cursor position\n      b. Check if cursor within entry bounds\n      c. If within bounds and slot valid, update selection globals:\n         - g_dwUIFlag1 = 1\n         - g_dwViewportX = horizontal center of slot\n         - g_dwUIState = minY of slot\n         - g_dwCursorScreenX/Y = slot coordinates\n         - g_pSelectedUnit/Entity = slot unit pointer\n13. Return\n\nParameters:\n  pUIContext - Pointer to UI context structure. Offset 0x18 (index 6) is cleared.\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If player unit not found: calls ProcessUIStateChange(0x24, 2, 0) to close shop\n  - If inventory owner exists: skips shop slot iteration (player inventory mode)\n  - Snow mode region check prevents selection in decoration area\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x7     - Search criteria type for player unit\n  0x1     - Unit type for hash table lookup\n  0x24    - UI state: close shop dialog\n  0x31    - Bottom margin offset (49 pixels)\n  0x3f    - Snow region upper Y offset (63 pixels)\n  0x5f    - Snow region lower Y offset (95 pixels)\n  0x110   - Snow region left X offset (272 pixels)\n  0x130   - Snow region right X offset (304 pixels)\n  0x84    - Inventory data offset in unit structure\n  0x14    - Shop entry stride (20 bytes = 5 DWORDs)\n\nStructure Layout - Shop Display Entry (20 bytes):\n  Offset  Size  Field    Type   Description\n  0x00    4     minX     int    Left boundary of slot\n  0x04    4     maxX     int    Right boundary of slot\n  0x08    4     minY     int    Top boundary of slot\n  0x0C    4     maxY     int    Bottom boundary of slot\n  0x10    4     (unused) int    Reserved\n\nGlobal Variables Modified:\n  g_dwViewportX        - Horizontal center of selected slot\n  g_dwUIState          - Top Y coordinate of selected slot\n  g_dwCursorScreenX/Y  - Selected slot coordinates\n  g_pSelectedUnit      - Pointer to unit in selected slot\n  g_pSelectedEntity    - Same as g_pSelectedUnit\n  g_dwUIFlag1          - Set to 1 when slot selected\n  g_pGameStateConfig   - Reset to 0\n  g_fSnowModeEnabled   - Cleared if cursor outside snow region",
      "tags": ["PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_1", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
    },
