      "comment": "Validate resource position within screen bounds and insert cache node if valid.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate max Y bound as screen height minus 49 (0x31) pixels\n2. Calculate max X bound as half screen width (screen center)\n3. Get current resource X position via GetCurrentResourceID()\n4. Get current resource Y position via GetResourceFlags()\n5. Validate X position: must be >= 0 and <= half screen width\n6. Validate Y position: must be >= 0 and <= adjusted screen height\n7. If both coordinates valid:\n   a. Trigger UI state change with element ID 0x25, state 1 (deactivate), scroll param 0\n   b. Clear targeting state to reset targeting system\n   c. Set cache node flag at offset 0x18 to 1 (active/valid)\n   d. Clear cache node flag at offset 0x1c to 0 (pending cleared)\n   e. Insert cache node into system via InsertCacheNodeWithCookie()\n\nParameters:\npCacheNode - Pointer to cache node structure. Structure has fields at:\n             +0x18: dword - Active flag (set to 1)\n             +0x1c: dword - Pending flag (cleared to 0)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value. Side effects occur only if position valid.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Position check uses signed comparison (JL/JG instructions)\n- Returns early without action if position out of bounds\n- The 0x31 offset accounts for UI panel/border height\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x25 - UI element ID for this cache operation\n0x31 - Vertical offset subtracted from screen height (49 pixels)\n0x18 - Structure offset for active flag\n0x1c - Structure offset for pending flag\n\nGlobal Dependencies:\ng_dwScreenHeight (0x6fbae0e8) - Current screen height in pixels\ng_dwScreenWidth (0x6fbae0e4) - Current screen width in pixels",
