      "comment": "Validate item type state and update UI panels for item type filters.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check state 0x0B (item type validation enabled) - if set, return early\n2. Get current item data via FUN_6fb62880\n3. Validate state 0x06 (primary check):\n   - If 0x06 clear: Check item type code 0x04 via Ordinal_10521\n     * If pass (result == 0): Set state 0x06 to 0, update panel\n     * If fail: Return early\n   - If 0x06 set: Check item type code 0x04 via Ordinal_10521\n     * If fail (result != 0): Return early, else set dwItemTypeState=1\n   - Call FUN_6fb5d370(0x06, dwItemTypeState, 0)\n4. Validate state 0x07 (secondary check):\n   - If 0x07 clear: Check item type code 0x05 via Ordinal_10521\n     * If pass: Check state 0x04\n       - If clear: Call FUN_6fb5d370(0x07, 0, 0)\n   - If 0x07 set: Check item type code 0x05 via Ordinal_10521\n     * If pass: Call FUN_6fb5d370(0x07, 1, 0), return\n     * If fail: Check state 0x04, if clear call FUN_6fb5d370(0x07, 0, 0)\n\nParameters:\n(none) - Uses global item context via FUN_6fb62880\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Updates UI panel states via FUN_6fb5d370\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Early exit if state 0x0B already set\n- State 0x06 tracks item type filter status (0=fail, 1=pass)\n- State 0x07 tracks alternate item type filter status\n- Ordinal_10521 appears to validate item type codes (0x04, 0x05)\n\nNote: Function uses SSA temporaries optimized away by compiler (register-only temporaries)",
      "tags": ["PARAM_0"]
