      "instructions": ["0x4CCD0|PUSH|ESI", "0x4CCD1|CMP|ECX, 0x2", "0x4CCD4|MOV|ESI, EDX", "0x4CCD6|JNZ|0x6fb1cd13", "0x4CCD8|MOV|EAX, [0x6fbae0e4]", "0x4CCDD|CDQ|", "0x4CCDE|SUB|EAX, EDX", "0x4CCE0|SAR|EAX, 0x1", "0x4CCE2|LEA|ECX, [EAX + 0x28]", "0x4CCE5|CMP|ESI, ECX", "0x4CCE7|JLE|0x6fb1cd40", "0x4CCE9|ADD|EAX, 0x4a", "0x4CCEC|CMP|ESI, EAX", "0x4CCEE|JGE|0x6fb1cd40", "0x4CCF0|MOV|EAX, [0x6fbae0e8]"],
      "comment": "Checks if point (X, Y) falls within UI panel boundaries.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if panel type equals 2 (centered panel mode)\n   - If panel=2: calculate offset from screen center (g_dwScreenWidth/2)\n   - Y bounds: (ScreenHeight - 0x8b, ScreenHeight - 0x66)\n   - X bounds: (Center + 0x28, Center + 0x4a)\n2. If panel != 2 (edge panel mode)\n   - Fixed X bounds: (0x28, 0x4a)\n   - Y bounds: (ScreenHeight - 0x8b, ScreenHeight - 0x66)\n3. Return 1 if point inside bounds, 0 otherwise\n\nParameters:\nnPanelType - int: Panel layout mode (2=centered, other=edge)\nnX - int: X coordinate to validate\nnY - int: Y coordinate to validate\n\nReturns:\n1 if point is within panel boundaries, 0 otherwise\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Panel type 2 offsets X range by screen width/2 (for centered layout)\n- Y bounds are identical regardless of panel type\n- Height offset 0x8b (139) from bottom, 0x66 (102) inset\n- Width offset 0x28 (40) from edge, 0x4a (74) inset\n- All coordinates inclusive on upper bound, exclusive on lower bound\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x28 - 40: Left X bound offset\n0x4a - 74: Right X bound offset  \n0x8b - 139: Top Y bound offset from screen height\n0x66 - 102: Bottom Y bound offset\ng_dwScreenWidth - Global screen width (used for centered panel calc)\ng_dwScreenHeight - Global screen height (used for Y bound calc)",
