      "comment": "Check if coordinates are within automap scroll panel bounds\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. If nScrollMode == 1 (left panel):\n   a. Calculate panel width as (ScreenWidth - ScreenWidth/2)\n   b. Check if nX in range [panelWidth - 0x49, panelWidth - 0x28]\n   c. Check if nY in range [ScreenHeight - 0x8a, ScreenHeight - 0x66]\n   d. Return 1 if both conditions met, otherwise continue to return 0\n2. If nScrollMode != 1 (right panel):\n   a. Check if nX in range [ScreenWidth - 0x49, ScreenWidth - 0x28]\n   b. Check if nY in range [ScreenHeight - 0x8a, ScreenHeight - 0x66]\n   c. Return 1 if both conditions met\n3. Return 0 if no bounds check passed\n\nParameters:\nnScrollMode - Scroll window mode (1=left panel, other=right panel)\nnX - X coordinate to validate\nnY - Y coordinate to validate\n\nReturns:\n1 if coordinates are within panel bounds, 0 otherwise\n\nSpecial Cases:\nMagic Numbers (Automap Panel Dimensions):\n0x49 (73) - Left boundary offset from panel edge\n0x28 (40) - Right boundary offset from panel edge\n0x8a (138) - Top boundary offset from screen top\n0x66 (102) - Bottom boundary offset from screen top",
