      "comment": "Validates UI element positioning and visibility within screen bounds.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract X-coordinate (lower 16 bits) and Y-coordinate (upper 16 bits) from nUIElement offset 0xc\n2. Check frame delta time - if equals 2, verify game is ready via FUN_6fb5d340(9), return on error\n3. Query current scroll window mode (0=normal, 2=scroll enabled)\n4. If scroll mode: Get X/Y screen positions via FUN_6fb8f680/FUN_6fb8f690\n5. For scroll mode: validate X in [screen_width/2 + 0x28, screen_width/2 + 0x4a] AND Y in [screen_height - 0x8b, screen_height - 0x66]\n6. For normal mode: validate X in [0x28, 0x4a] AND Y in [screen_height - 0x8b, screen_height - 0x66]\n7. On bounds validation success: set g_dwUIValidationFlag=1, call FUN_6fb8d210(4,0,0.0,0.0,0), call FUN_6fb8ef90\n8. If scroll mode available: call FUN_6fb2a560() to verify scroll state, abort if returns 0\n9. Set nUIElement[0x18]=1 (visible) on validation success or 0 (hidden) on bounds violation\n10. Call Ordinal_511(nUIElement) to finalize state, set nUIElement[0x1c]=0\n\nParameters:\n  nUIElement (int) - UI element structure pointer, field offsets: +0xc=packed XY coords, +0x18=visibility flag, +0x1c=render flags\n\nReturns:\n  void - Modifies element state via nUIElement pointer\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  Frame delta 2 is frame trigger - early return preserves previous state\n  Scroll mode uses centered bounds, normal mode uses left-edge bounds\n  Y bounds consistent between modes but X bounds differ\n  Magic hex: 0x28=40, 0x4a=74, 0x8b=139, 0x66=102, 0xce=206, 0xef=239, 0x2a=42, 0x8=8",
