      "comment": "Validate panel position against screen bounds and activate if within valid region.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract X coordinate (low word at offset 0xC) and Y (high word at offset 0xC) from pPanel\n2. Call Ordinal_10005() to determine window mode (returns 2 for expanded, else normal)\n3. Branch on window mode:\n   - Mode 2: Validate X in range [0x233, 0x255] and Y in range [screen_height-0x2a, screen_height-8]\n   - Mode Normal: Read screen width, adjust for scroll mode (subtract width/2 if mode=1)\n     Validate X in range [width-0x49, width-0x28] and Y in range [screen_height-0x8a, screen_height-0x66]\n4. If bounds check passes: set g_dwPanelBoundsExceeded=1, clear buffer via FUN_6fb8d210, redraw via FUN_6fb8ef90\n5. If scroll mode is 1: validate with FUN_6fb2a560, exit if non-zero\n6. Set pPanel[0x18]=1 (active flag), pPanel[0x1c]=0\n7. Call Ordinal_511(pPanel) to register panel state with engine\n8. If bounds check fails: set pPanel[0x18]=0 (inactive) and return\n\nParameters:\npPanel - Pointer to panel structure; offset 0xC contains packed X,Y coordinates as ushort|ushort, offsets 0x18 and 0x1c are status fields\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Modifies panel structure fields in-place (0x18 and 0x1c)\n\nSpecial Cases:\nScreen bounds use pixel offsets: 0x49, 0x28, 0x8a, 0x66, 0x2a, 0x8 - these represent margin pixels from edges\nWindow mode determines which bounds validation path to execute\nScroll mode=1 adds secondary validation through FUN_6fb2a560",
