      "comment": "Validates window scroll position and viewport coordinates against screen bounds.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract window X coordinate (lower word) and Y coordinate (upper word) from window data at offset 0xc\n2. Call Ordinal_10005 (GetCurrentGameState) to get current game state/mode\n3. If state == 2 and FUN_6fb5d340(9) returns non-zero, early exit (state validation failed)\n4. Call FUN_6fb8f010(nWindowData) to initialize/update window\n5. Check game state again via Ordinal_10005\n6. If state == 2 (town/menu mode): Check g_dwUIValidationFlag for active UI validation, get mouse position, verify coordinates, set viewport modes, call Ordinal_511\n7. If state != 2 (game mode): Validate window X coordinate based on scroll mode, validate window Y in range, set viewport modes if valid\n8. If any validation fails: Clear flag, set window field [0x18]=0\n\nParameters:\n- nWindowData (int): Pointer to window structure with coordinates at offset 0xc and state fields at 0x18, 0x1c\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nNote: Function uses stack-allocated temporaries optimized away in decompilation (visible only in assembly)",
