      "instructions": ["0x4D210|PUSH|EBX", "0x4D211|PUSH|EBP", "0x4D212|PUSH|ESI", "0x4D213|PUSH|EDI", "0x4D214|MOV|EDI, dword ptr [ESP + 0x14]", "0x4D218|XOR|ESI, ESI", "0x4D21A|MOV|EBX, dword ptr [EDI + 0xc]", "0x4D21D|MOV|SI, word ptr [EDI + 0xc]", "0x4D221|SHR|EBX, 0x10", "0x4D224|CALL|0x6fb9921a", "0x4D229|CMP|EAX, 0x2", "0x4D22C|JNZ|0x6fb1d23c", "0x4D22E|MOV|ECX, 0x9", "0x4D233|CALL|0x6fb5d340", "0x4D238|TEST|EAX, EAX"],
      "comment": "Validates UI element position against screen bounds and clears drag mode if out of range.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call Ordinal_10005 to query system state - if != 2 OR FUN_6fb5d340(9) succeeds, continue\n2. Call FUN_6fb8f010 with element node for pre-processing\n3. Call Ordinal_10005 again to check if state == 2 (minimap mode)\n4. If state == 2: validate cursor X in [0x233, 0x255], Y in [dwHeight-0x2a, dwHeight-8]\n5. If state != 2: call GetScrollWindowMode to get layout mode, adjust width if mode==1 (half-screen: dwWidth/2)\n6. Validate cursor X in [dwWidth-0x49, dwWidth-0x28], Y in [dwHeight-0x8a, dwHeight-0x66]\n7. If bounds valid: clear drag flag, call FUN_6fb5d370(7,1,0) then FUN_6fb5d370(4,0,0), set element fields +0x18=1, +0x1c=0\n8. Call Ordinal_511 to notify element of coordinate change and return\n9. If bounds invalid or state==2: clear drag flag, set element +0x18=0, clear global, return\n\nParameters:\n  pElementNode - GameDataElement* UI element node with coordinates packed at +0x0c (X: low16, Y: high16)\n\nReturns:\n  void - modifies element structure and clears global g_bAutomapUIDragActive\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  Ordinal_10005 = Get game state (2=minimap visible)\n  Ordinal_511 = Notify coordinate change to element\n  GetScrollWindowMode returns 1 for half-screen, 0 for full-screen layout\n  Magic X bounds: 0x233-0x255 (minimap), dwWidth-0x49 to dwWidth-0x28 (regular)\n  Magic Y bounds: height-0x2a to height-0x8 (minimap), height-0x8a to height-0x66 (regular)\n  Note: Compiler optimizations create ephemeral SSA temporaries (iVar3, uVar2, uVar4, iVar5) visible only in assembly",
