      "comment": "Render game UI panel when screen configuration is active.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call Ordinal_10005 to determine screen configuration mode\n2. If configuration mode equals 2:\n   a. Initialize local buffer (adUIBuffer) to 72 bytes of zeros via REP STOSD\n   b. Set buffer field [1] to global screen config value (g_dwScreenConfig2)\n   c. Set buffer field [2] to mode value 2\n   d. Fetch current viewport coordinates: nScreenX and nScreenY\n   e. Check if cursor is within viewport bounds (0xCE < X < 0xF0, Y between margin)\n   f. If within bounds, request UI resource (type 9)\n   g. If resource obtained, set event type to 0x226 and trigger event notification\n   h. Render UI panel at position (0xCE, screenHeight-8) with specific dimensions\n3. Return void\n\nParameters:\n(none) - No parameters. Uses global state: g_dwScreenConfig2, g_dwScreenHeight\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Magic numbers: 0x226 = event ID, 0xCE = X coordinate, 0xF0 = max X, 0x2A = top margin, 0x8 = bottom margin, 18 = buffer size in dwords\n- Function returns early if screen mode != 2\n- Rendering always occurs regardless of viewport check (separate code path)\n- Note: Decompiler generates temporary SSA variables (uVar3, puVar2) optimized by compiler; these cannot be renamed independently\n\nRelated Functions:\n- Ordinal_10005() - Fetch screen configuration\n- FUN_6fb8f680() - Get viewport X coordinate\n- FUN_6fb8f690() - Get viewport Y coordinate\n- FUN_6fb5d340() - Request UI resource by type\n- Ordinal_10004() - Initialize event\n- Ordinal_10129() - Trigger event notification\n- Ordinal_10072() - Render UI panel with buffer",
