      "comment": "Render and handle interactive UI automap panel with mouse interaction detection.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get scroll window mode (normal/compact/fullscreen)\n2. Check if window is already open (Ordinal_10005 returns 2 if open)\n3. Validate UI prerequisites: Check states via FUN_6fb5d340 with params 0x02, 0x16, 0x01, 0x04, 0x0c\n4. Calculate X offset: 0x28 base + (screen_width/2) if mode 2 (compact), else 0x28\n5. Initialize panel array (18 dwords) with zeros except: [1]=g_dwScreenConfig1, [3]=0\n6. Call Ordinal_10036 (create panel), Ordinal_10037 (draw panel), Ordinal_10004 (render UI)\n7. If not mode 2: Display alternate viewport at calculated position with dimensions\n8. Prepare second panel array with [1]=g_dwScreenConfig2\n9. Check mouse coordinates (FUN_6fb8f680/FUN_6fb8f690) against region bounds\n10. If in bounds and validation enabled: Set [2]=1 (selected), else [2]=0\n11. Render second panel and handle final mouse click if in viewport region\n\nParameters: None (uses global UI state and screen dimensions)\n\nReturns: void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Window state 2: Mode 2 uses screen_width/2 offset for compact layout\n- Mouse click in region 0xCE-0xF0 X, (height-0x2A) to (height-0x08) Y: Marks selection with [2]=1\n- If validation disabled: Mouse clicks ignored\n- Mode check at 0x6fb1d4d1 calculates: (screen_width / 2) >> 1, adds 0x28\n- Magic constant 0xF92: Panel resource ID for Automap\n- Magic constant 0x226: Hotspot coordinate constant\n\nStructure Layout - Panel Array [18 dwords]:\n| Offset | Size | Field Name | Type | Description |\n|--------|------|-----------|------|-------------|\n| 0x00 | 4 | dwType | uint | Panel type identifier (0) |\n| 0x04 | 4 | dwConfig | uint | Screen config reference |\n| 0x08 | 4 | dwSelected | uint | Selection state (0/1) |\n| 0x0c | 4 | dwReserved | uint | Unused padding |\n| 0x10-0x44 | 52 | reserved | uint[13] | Unused panel fields |\n\nRelated Functions:\n- FUN_6fb5d340 - Validates UI components and prerequisites\n- GetScrollWindowMode - Returns display mode (0=normal, 2=compact, 3=fullscreen)\n- FUN_6fb8f680 - Get current mouse X coordinate\n- FUN_6fb8f690 - Get current mouse Y coordinate",
      "tags": ["PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "STRUCT_Skill", "PARAM_0", "PROP_LOOPHEAVY", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
