      "comment": "Initialize and draw the AutoMap overlay panel.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if GetUnitX (Ordinal_10005) returns 2 (valid mode indicator)\n2. If valid:\n   a. Allocate 18-element UI structure array (local_48)\n   b. Initialize first 18 elements to 0 using REP STOSD\n   c. Set structure[1] = screen config from g_dwScreenConfig2\n   d. Set structure[2] = 2 (panel type/flag)\n   e. Get current mouse X coordinate via FUN_6fb8f680()\n   f. Get current mouse Y coordinate via FUN_6fb8f690()\n3. Validate mouse is within AutoMap panel bounds:\n   a. X must be between 0x233 (563) and 0x255 (597)\n   b. Y must be between (ScreenHeight - 42) and (ScreenHeight - 8)\n4. If within bounds:\n   a. Call FUN_6fb5d340(9) to check panel resource/state\n   b. If check succeeds (returns 0):\n      i. Set flags: x=0x226, flag=1\n      ii. Call Ordinal_10004 (D2Client.GetDifficulty) with params\n      iii. Call Ordinal_10129 to register panel with UI system\n5. Always call Ordinal_10072 (D2Common.GetUnitInventory) with panel config array\n6. Return void\n\nParameters: None\n\nReturns: void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Function only activates if initial mode check returns 2\n- Panel bounds are hardcoded screen coordinates\n- Mouse coordinate calls (FUN_6fb8f680/FUN_6fb8f690) checked against screen dimensions\n- Ordinal_10004 magic value 0xf93 appears to be UI state ID\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x12 (18) - UI structure array size\n0x233 (563) - Panel X minimum bound\n0x255 (597) - Panel X maximum bound\n0x226 (550) - Panel X coordinate constant\n0x2a (42) - Panel Y offset from screen height\n0x8 (8) - Panel Y offset margin\n0xffffffff (-1) - Flag parameter to Ordinal_10004\n0xf93 (3987) - Magic ID for Ordinal_10004 lookup\n0x242 (578) - Secondary coordinate for Ordinal_10129\n\nRelated Functions:\n- FUN_6fb8f680() - Get current mouse X position\n- FUN_6fb8f690() - Get current mouse Y position\n- FUN_6fb5d340(dwPanelId) - Check/validate panel resource state",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PARAM_0", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
