      "comment": "Render the automap UI with mouse interaction handling\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if game is in valid screen mode via GetScrollWindowMode/Ordinal_10005\n2. If screen mode is not 2 and other UI checks fail, disable automap drag and return\n3. Calculate screen X offset based on scroll mode (full or half-width)\n4. Initialize 72-byte UI structure array (18 uint slots)\n5. Configure structure with screen parameters and render first UI element\n6. If not in cinema mode, render additional UI layer with offset calculations\n7. Configure second UI structure with g_dwScreenConfig2\n8. Check drag mode and mouse position boundaries:\n   - In cinema mode: check if mouse is in zone (0x233-0x255 X, height-0x2a to height-0x8 Y)\n   - In normal mode: check if mouse is in zone (screen_x to screen_x+0x21 X, height-0x8a to height-0x66 Y)\n   - In wide screen mode: calculate adjusted boundary (width/2 - 0x49)\n9. Set drag flag in UI structure based on position\n10. Render second UI element with structure\n11. In cinema mode: check mouse on special zone (0x233-0x255 X) and call FUN_6fb5d340(9)\n12. Render final UI element with adjusted coordinates\n\nParameters: (none)\n\nReturns: void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Screen mode 2 is cinema/fullscreen mode with different coordinate calculations\n- Scroll mode 1 uses half-width screen calculation (width - width/2)\n- Magic coordinates: 0x233, 0x255 (cinema zone), 0x8e, 0x89, 0x69, 0x66 (height offsets)\n- Array local_48 reused for multiple UI structure configurations\n- Three separate Ordinal calls (10036, 10037, others) for UI rendering pipeline\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x233 (563): Cinema mode X boundary low\n- 0x255 (597): Cinema mode X boundary high\n- 0x49 (73): X offset adjustment\n- 0x2a (42): Height offset for cinema zone\n- 0x8e (142): Primary height offset\n- 0x69 (105): Secondary height offset\n- 0x8a (138): Tertiary height offset\n- 0x66 (102): Quaternary height offset\n- 0xf93: Configuration parameter constant\n- 0xffffffff: Color parameter (white)\n- 0x5: Render layer/type parameter",
