      "comment": "Clears room tile arrays by zeroing 6 word values per entry in a tile data structure.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if room tile count at offset 0x12e08 is zero, if so skip loop\n2. Calculate base pointer to first tile entry at offset 0x198\n3. For each tile entry up to count:\n   a. Clear word at entry offset -0x190 (relative -200 words)\n   b. Clear word at entry base (offset 0)\n   c. Clear word at entry offset +0x190 (relative +200 words)\n   d. Clear word at entry offset +0x320 (relative +400 words)\n   e. Clear word at entry offset +0x4b0 (relative +600 words)\n   f. Clear word at entry offset +0x640 (relative +800 words)\n   g. Advance pointer by stride 0x96e (2414 bytes per entry)\n4. Reset tile count field to zero\n\nParameters:\n  pRoomData (ECX) - Pointer to room data structure containing tile arrays\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value\n\nStructure Layout (RoomData tile portion):\n  Offset   Size  Field              Description\n  0x0198   2     First tile word    Base of tile entry array\n  0x12e08  2     wTileCount         Number of active tile entries\n\nMemory Model:\n  - Each tile entry is 2414 bytes (0x96e stride)\n  - 6 word values cleared per entry at fixed offsets\n  - Offsets relative to entry base: -0x190, 0, +0x190, +0x320, +0x4b0, +0x640\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If tile count is 0, function still writes 0 to count field (no-op optimization)\n\nCalled from: Function pointer table at 0x6fba9164 (room cleanup vtable)",
