      "instructions": ["0x4E120|PUSH|EBX", "0x4E121|PUSH|EBP", "0x4E122|PUSH|ESI", "0x4E123|PUSH|EDI", "0x4E124|XOR|EDI, EDI", "0x4E126|XOR|EDX, EDX", "0x4E128|MOV|DI, word ptr [ECX + 0x12e08]", "0x4E12F|XOR|EAX, EAX", "0x4E131|TEST|EDI, EDI", "0x4E133|JLE|0x6fb1e1c7", "0x4E139|MOV|ESI, dword ptr [ECX + 0x12dd4]", "0x4E13F|MOV|EBX, dword ptr [ECX + 0x12df0]", "0x4E145|LEA|EBP, [ESI + -0x14]", "0x4E148|LEA|ESI, [ECX + 0x198]", "0x4E14E|CMP|EAX, EBX"],
      "comment": "Counts active tile properties within valid range and accumulates weights.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load tile count from base+0x12e08 into EDI\n2. Initialize accumulators: EDX=0 (sum), EAX=0 (index)\n3. Exit if tile count is 0 or negative\n4. For each tile from min_valid_index to tile_count:\n   a. Load min_valid_index from base+0x12df0, compare with current index\n   b. If current index >= min_valid_index AND current index < tile_count:\n      - Check 6 tile property flags at offsets -200, 0, 200, 400, 600, 800 relative to pTileData\n      - For each non-zero flag, add weight from base+0x12e26 to accumulator\n      - Always add fixed weight from base+0x12e2a\n   c. Check if accumulator > (max_memory_limit - 0x14)\n   d. If true and (index - min_index) > 0, return EDI (failure/abort)\n5. Increment index, advance pTileData by 0x4b7 bytes\n6. Continue loop until index >= tile_count\n7. Return EDI (0 on success from initial XOR)\n\nParameters:\n- pTileBasePtr (ECX, __fastcall): Base pointer to tile structure containing:\n  - +0x12e08: ushort - tile count\n  - +0x12df0: int - minimum valid tile index\n  - +0x12dd4: int - maximum memory allocation limit\n  - +0x12e26: int - per-property weight value\n  - +0x12e2a: int - base weight per tile\n  - +0x198: short* - base pointer to tile data array\n\nReturns:\n- EDI register: 0 on success (tile properties within limit), 1 on early abort/failure (memory limit exceeded)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If tile_count == 0, function returns immediately without processing\n- Early abort occurs when accumulated weight exceeds limit by more than 0x14 bytes\n- Tile indices outside [min_index, tile_count) are skipped\n- Property flags are checked at fixed 2-byte intervals (+200, +400, +600, +800 elements = 2-byte words)",
