      "comment": "Processes viewport scroll events with boundary constraints. Returns 1 if scroll processed, 0 if invalid.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract Y coordinate from event (param_1 + 0xc, right-shifted 16 bits) = nSelectedY\n2. Read viewport state: scroll position (0x12df8), item height (0x12e0e), size (0x12e08)\n3. Validate: size != 0, scroll <= size, coordinate delta positive, min != max bounds\n4. Calculate bounds: LEA EDI,[EDI + EDI*0x2] then LEA EDI,[EBP + EDI*0x4 + 0xd] for min/max Y\n5. If Y < minY: scroll = max(0, scroll - itemHeight)\n6. If Y > maxY: scroll += itemHeight, clamp to (0, size-1), validate remainder\n7. If scroll > 0x1f: decrement and apply sign extension mask\n8. Store final scroll to backup field (0x12df0) and call FUN_6fb8d210(1,0,0,0,0)\n9. Final bounds check: ensure min_scroll <= final <= max_scroll + itemHeight\n10. Return 1 on success, 0 on any validation failure\n\nParameters:\npViewportData: void* - Viewport object with scroll/bounds fields at offsets 0x12df8/0x12e0e/0x12e08/0x12e12/0x12e16/0x12df0\npEventData: void* - Event structure with Y coordinate at offset 0xc (high word of 32-bit dword)\n\nReturns:\n1 - Scroll processed successfully\n0 - Validation failed (size=0, bounds invalid, coordinate out of range)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If min_bounds == max_bounds, returns 0 (no scroll possible)\n- Scroll position clamped to [0, size-1]\n- Height adjustment uses sign extension: ((value < 1) - 1) & value\n- Magic number 0xd: Base offset for item render area\n- Magic number 0x1f: Maximum scroll position sentinel (32 items)",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Inventory", "PARAM_3", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control"]
