      "comment": "Process unit animation state transitions based on direction parameter.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract direction flags from pUnit->dwFlags (bit 16+)\n2. If direction > 0: set dwField_12df8 = dwField_12df0, call virtual method at this[0x1c]\n3. If direction < 0: calculate dwField_12df8 = dwField_12e0e + dwField_12df0 - 1, call virtual method at this[0x20]\n4. Set pUnit->dwField_18 = 1 (animation active flag)\n5. Set pUnit->dwField_1c = 0 (animation offset)\n6. Call Ordinal_511(pUnit) for animation state finalization\n7. Return 1 (success)\n\nParameters:\n- pThis (void*): this pointer to animation controller\n- pUnit (void*): unit data structure with animation state fields\n\nReturns:\n1 (success)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Direction >= 0: forward animation path (0x1c handler)\n- Direction < 0: backward animation path (0x20 handler)\n- Virtual method calls depend on controller implementation\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x12df8: animation frame counter offset\n- 0x12e0e: animation end marker offset\n- 0x12df0: animation start offset\n- 0x20: virtual method offset for backward animation\n- 0x1c: virtual method offset for forward animation\n- 0x18: animation active flag offset in pUnit\n- 0x1c: animation offset field offset in pUnit\n- 0x8: direction flags offset in pUnit\n- 0x10: bit shift for direction flags extraction",
