      "comment": "Check if screen coordinate falls within viewport and active regions.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract X (lower 16 bits) and Y (upper 16 bits) from nCoord\n2. Check viewport bounds: X in [minX, minX+widthX], Y in [minY, minY+heightY]\n3. If out of bounds, return 0\n4. If within bounds: set viewport active flag (offset 0x12ddc)\n5. Check three nested regions in sequence:\n   a. Primary: X in [baseX, baseX+0x10], Y in [yBase-0xc, yBase]\n   b. Secondary: X in [baseX, baseX+0x10], Y with count offset at 0x12e22\n   c. Tertiary: X in [baseX, baseX+0x10], Y at remaining range\n6. If region matches: set region flag, clear skip flag (0x12e2e), return 1\n7. If no region match and handler exists (0x12e0a): call FUN_6fb1f390 for additional processing\n8. Return 1 for in-bounds, 0 for out-of-bounds\n\nParameters:\n- this (ECX): Viewport/panel structure pointer with 16 offsets\n- nCoord: Packed coordinate where low word = X, high word = Y\n\nReturns:\n- 1 if coordinate in viewport bounds\n- 0 if coordinate out of bounds",
