      "instructions": ["0x4F110|PUSH|ESI", "0x4F111|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0x4F113|XOR|EAX, EAX", "0x4F115|PUSH|EDI", "0x4F116|CMP|dword ptr [ESI + 0x12ddc], EAX", "0x4F11C|JNZ|0x6fb1f132", "0x4F11E|MOV|dword ptr [ESI + 0x12df4], 0xffffffff", "0x4F128|POP|EDI", "0x4F129|MOV|EAX, 0x1", "0x4F12E|POP|ESI", "0x4F12F|RET|0x4", "0x4F132|MOV|ECX, dword ptr [ESI + 0x12de0]", "0x4F138|MOV|EDI, 0x1", "0x4F13D|CMP|ECX, EDI", "0x4F13F|MOV|dword ptr [ESI + 0x12ddc], EAX"],
      "comment": "Process viewport mouse click event and dispatch to appropriate handler.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if viewport is inactive (offset 0x12ddc == 0), if so set status to -1 and return 1\n2. Clear inactive flag (0x12ddc = 0)\n3. If mode is button1-down (0x12de0 == 1):\n   a. Clear flag\n   b. Extract Y coordinate from high word of event data (+0xc >> 16)\n   c. Validate X coordinate within range [viewport_x, viewport_x+0x10)\n   d. Validate Y coordinate within range [viewport_y-0xc, viewport_y)\n   e. If valid, call virtual function at offset 0x1c with event data\n4. Else if mode is button2-down (0x12de4 == 1):\n   a. Clear flag\n   b. Extract Y coordinate from high word of event data\n   c. Validate X coordinate within range [viewport_x, viewport_x+0x10)\n   d. Validate Y coordinate within calculated range [viewport_y-0xc, viewport_y + count*0xc)\n   e. If valid, call virtual function at offset 0x20, set status to -1, return 0\n5. Else if mode is button3-down (0x12de8 == 1):\n   a. Clear flag\n   b. Extract Y coordinate from high word of event data\n   c. Validate X coordinate within range [viewport_x, viewport_x+0x10)\n   d. Validate Y coordinate within calculated range [viewport_y, viewport_y + count*0xc - 0xc)\n   e. If valid, call ProcessViewportScrolling with event, set status to -1, return 0\n6. Else if callback handler exists (0x12e0a != 0):\n   a. Call FUN_6fb1f390 to process event\n   b. Compare result with current status at 0x12df4\n   c. If status is -1, return 0\n   d. If match, set status to -1, call handler at 0x12e0a, return 1\n7. Set status to -1 and return 0 for any unhandled path\n\nParameters:\n  this - void * pointer to viewport structure (implicit ECX parameter, __thiscall)\n  nEventData - int containing packed event data with X coordinate (low word) and Y coordinate (high word)\n\nReturns:\n  1 if event processed, 0 if not processed or error\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  Coordinates extracted as: X = low word, Y = high word (bits 16-31)\n  Function uses SSA temporaries optimized away: nYCoord (register value), dwYCoord (shifted Y)\n  Bounds validation includes boundary checks for element arrays with stride 0xc (12 bytes)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x12ddc - Viewport inactive flag offset\n  0x12de0 - Button 1 mode flag offset\n  0x12de4 - Button 2 mode flag offset\n  0x12de8 - Button 3 mode flag offset\n  0x12df4 - Current viewport status offset\n  0x12e0a - Callback handler pointer offset\n  0x12e1a - Viewport X coordinate offset\n  0x12e1e - Viewport Y coordinate offset\n  0x12e22 - Viewport height/element count offset\n  0x1c - Virtual function offset for button 1 handler\n  0x20 - Virtual function offset for button 2 handler\n  0xffffffff - Status value for unhandled/processed state\n  0x10 - X coordinate range width\n  0xc - Y coordinate boundary offset (0xc bytes), element stride for arrays",
