      "comment": "Increment viewport slot index, maintain visible window bounds.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load maximum slot count from nViewportData[0x12e08] and subtract 1 for upper bound\n2. Load current slot index from nViewportData[0x12df8]\n3. Compare current slot against upper bound\n4. If current >= bound, exit (already at maximum)\n5. Increment current slot index by 1\n6. Write updated slot back to nViewportData[0x12df8]\n7. Call display refresh FUN_6fb8d210(1,0,0.0,0.0,0) to redraw viewport\n8. Load updated current slot into nCurrentSlot for bounds checking\n9. Compare current against minimum bound nViewportData[0x12df0]\n10. If current < minimum, update minimum to current (constrain lower bound)\n11. Load minimum and window size nViewportData[0x12e0e]\n12. Calculate visible range end: minimum + window_size\n13. Compare current against range end\n14. If current < range_end, no panning required\n15. If current >= range_end, increment minimum by 1 (pan window forward)\n16. Return 1 (success or boundary condition)\n\nParameters:\nnViewportData (int) - Viewport state structure containing offset fields:\n  0x12df0 = minimum displayed slot index\n  0x12df8 = current selected slot index\n  0x12e08 = maximum slot count (total slots)\n  0x12e0e = visible window size in slots\n\nReturns:\n1 - Always returns 1 (operation completed or boundary reached)",
