      "comment": "Calculate accumulated grid value with neighbor influence checks.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate input coordinate index is within valid range (subtract 0xf offset for bounds check)\n2. Verify data structure is initialized (check pointer validity at offset 0x12e0a)\n3. Extract high 16-bits of coordinate parameter as target coordinate value\n4. Load current slot index from object state (offset 0x12df0)\n5. Iterate through active slots (while slot_index < max_slots from 0x12e08):\n   a. Load slot data pointer with stride calculation (slot_index * 0x96e + 0x198)\n   b. Check 6 neighbor positions (offsets at -200, 0, 200, 400, 600, 800 words from slot pointer)\n   c. For each non-zero neighbor, accumulate stride value (0x12e26 offset per neighbor)\n   d. Check if target coordinate falls within valid range for this slot:\n      - Min bound: base_value (0x12dcc + 0xc) + nAccumulator (accumulated from neighbors)\n      - Max bound: base_value + nTempValue (modified accumulator)\n   e. If coordinate >= min_bound AND coordinate < max_bound, exit loop with valid index\n   f. Advance to next slot iteration by incrementing slot_index\n6. Return slot index (-1 if not found, else valid index)\n7. Store result in object state (offset 0x12df8)\n\nParameters:\n  this (void*) - Object pointer containing grid/slot configuration [auto-parameter, __thiscall]\n  pCoordIndex (void*) - Coordinate parameter structure with coord value at offset +0xc\n\nReturns:\n  int - Slot index if coordinate found in valid range, -1 if not found or out of bounds\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Returns -1 immediately if coordinate value < 0xf (boundary condition)\n  - Returns -1 if pointer at 0x12e0a is zero (uninitialized data)\n  - No slots checked if slot_index >= max_slots at entry\n  - Neighbor stride multiplier stored at offset 0x12e26\n  - Slot stride offset: 0x96e bytes per slot, pointer base at 0x198\n  - Neighbor word offsets from slot pointer: -200 (0xfffffe70), 0, +200 (0x190), +400 (0x320),