      "comment": "Validates coordinate bounds before calculating grid value.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract X coordinate from low word of pCoordData+0xc\n2. Extract Y coordinate from high word of pCoordData+0xc (shift right 16)\n3. Check if X > nGridMinX (this+0x12dc8)\n4. Check if X < nGridMinX + nGridWidth (this+0x12dc8 + this+0x12dd0)\n5. Check if Y > nGridMinY (this+0x12dcc)\n6. Check if Y < nGridMinY + nGridHeight (this+0x12dcc + this+0x12dd4)\n7. If all bounds checks pass, call CalculateGridValueWithNeighbors\n\nParameters:\n  this (ECX) - Grid context structure with boundary fields at +0x12dc8\n  pCoordData - Coordinate data structure, packed X|Y at offset +0xc\n  IMPLICIT EDI - Pass-through parameter for CalculateGridValueWithNeighbors\n\nReturns:\n  void - Result stored by callee in grid context\n\nStructure Layout (this pointer):\n  Offset    Size  Field         Description\n  0x12dc8   4     nGridMinX     Grid minimum X boundary\n  0x12dcc   4     nGridMinY     Grid minimum Y boundary  \n  0x12dd0   4     nGridWidth    Grid width extent\n  0x12dd4   4     nGridHeight   Grid height extent\n\nCoordinate Packing (pCoordData+0xc):\n  Bits 0-15:  X coordinate (low word)\n  Bits 16-31: Y coordinate (high word)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Returns immediately if coordinates outside grid bounds\n  - EDI register passed through to callee without modification",
