      "comment": "Validates game state and initializes state data fields.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if game state handler is initialized at offset 0x12e0a\n2. If handler exists:\n   - Set pStateData[0x18] = 1 (activation flag)\n   - Set pStateData[0x1c] = 0 (reset value)\n   - Call Ordinal_511(pStateData) to apply state changes\n   - Check if global counter at offset 0x12e32 >= 2\n   - If counter >= 2:\n     * Verify saved state index at offset 0x12df8 != -1\n     * Verify pStateData[0x8] == 0xd (type validation)\n     * If both conditions true: invoke function pointer at offset 0x12e0a\n   - Return 1 (success)\n3. If handler not initialized or counter < 2: Return 0 (failure)\n\nParameters:\nthis - Game state object (void* - structure with handlers at 0x12e0a, 0x12df8, 0x12e32)\npGameState - Unused, passed through stack\npStateData - State data structure to initialize (fields: [0x8]=type, [0x18]=activation, [0x1c]=value)\n\nReturns:\n1 if state initialization successful and counter >= 2\n0 if handler not initialized or counter < 2\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Index validation (0x12df8) may be -1 when state not yet saved\n- Type field (0x8) must be exactly 0xd for function invocation\n- Handler function pointer at 0x12e0a is indirectly called via (*FuncPtr)()",
