      "comment": "Retrieves entry data from a listbox widget at a specified selection index.\n\nVirtual function in listbox vtable. Validates selection index bounds before\ncomputing entry data offset using complex stride calculation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get nSelectionIndex from stack parameter\n2. Load pListboxData from this+0x8\n3. If nSelectionIndex < 0, goto error validation\n4. Load wNumEntries from pListboxData+0x12e08\n5. If nSelectionIndex >= wNumEntries, goto error validation  \n6. If nSelectionIndex >= LISTBOX_MAX_ENTRIES (0x20), goto error validation\n7. Calculate entry offset: index * 0x252 (stride = 594 bytes per entry)\n   Computed as: ((idx*32 + idx)*2 + idx)*9*2 + idx = idx * 594\n8. Return dword at pListboxData + nSelectionIndex*2 + 0x96a\n\nError Validation (runs assertion checks before fatal exit):\n9. Assert wNumEntries < LISTBOX_MAX_ENTRIES (0x20) at line 0x45d\n10. Assert wNumEntries < nSelectionIndex at line 0x45e  \n11. Assert nSelectionIndex >= 0 at line 0x45f\n12. Return 0 (never reached - ExitApplicationWithCode terminates)\n\nParameters:\n  this (ECX)        - Pointer to listbox widget object\n  nSelectionIndex   - Zero-based index of entry to retrieve (must be 0-31)\n\nReturns:\n  dword entry data from listbox entry array on success\n  0 on error (after fatal assertion - never returns normally)\n\nConstants:\n  LISTBOX_MAX_ENTRIES = 0x20 (32) - Maximum entries in listbox\n  LISTBOX_DATA_OFFSET = 0x8 - Offset to data pointer in listbox\n  NUM_ENTRIES_OFFSET = 0x12e08 - Offset to entry count (ushort)\n  ENTRY_ARRAY_BASE = 0x96a - Base offset for entry data array\n  ENTRY_STRIDE = 0x252 (594 bytes) - Size of each listbox entry\n\nSource: D2Client/Source - Line 0x45d-0x45f",
