      "comment": "Process gem/socket modifier table entry and synchronize string resource.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call Ordinal_10855 (D2Common initialize) with gem handle and 0x2/0x0 params to bind context\n2. Initialize loop counter to 0, load base table pointer from param_2 + 0x30\n3. Check entry type at [base_ptr]: if value equals 0xf2, branch to string concatenation\n4. Otherwise increment counter, advance pointer by 0x10 bytes (entry stride)\n5. Repeat until counter reaches 3 or 0xf2 entry found\n6. Call Ordinal_10004 (D2Common.AllocateString) to create new string buffer\n7. Call Unicode::strcat to append ESI content to EDI buffer\n8. Call FUN_6fb21640 with resource ID param_5 and flags param_6\n9. Call Ordinal_10483 (D2Common.GetUnitStat) with 0x40 flags to retrieve stat value\n10. If stat retrieved (return non-zero), call Ordinal_10474 (D2Common.SetUnitStat) with flags\n11. Load string length via function pointer call (strlen)\n12. Check if character at [buffer + (length*2) - 2] equals 0x0a (newline)\n13. If newline present, replace with 0x0000 null terminator\n\nParameters:\n- dwGemHandle: Gem unit handle identifier (dword, ECX)\n- pGemTable: Pointer to gem property table array (int*, EDX)\n- dwTableIndex: Index/type identifier for processing (dword, stack)\n- nEntryFlags: Modification behavior flags for SetUnitStat (int, stack)\n- nStringResourceId: Resource ID to initialize string content (dword, stack)\n- nStringFlags: String handling flags (int, stack)\n\nReturns: void (no return value)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Loop executes 0-1 iterations: early exit if 0xf2 found, skips concatenation if not found\n- Newline stripping assumes null terminator after 0x0a character\n- Note: Function uses 3 SSA temporaries optimized away (iVar3, sVar2, piVar1) and 2 unaffected registers (unaff_ESI, unaff_EDI) for string pointers - compiler optimization prevents renaming\n- Ordinal_10855 initialization is critical for subsequent stat operations\n\nMagic Numbers: 0xf2 (gem type), 0x30