      "comment": "Constructs formatted gem/socket property string for item display.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize 512-byte Unicode character buffer (256 ushort elements)\n2. Validate item handle exists (stat 0x35 check)\n3. Retrieve item stats table pointer and validate non-null\n4. Check for unique properties (stat 0x14) vs gem properties (stat 0x4a)\n5. Load gem modifiers table (offset 0x7c) and validate\n6. Initialize string building with strcat_exref pointer\n7. Build property string by calling FormatItemProperties 4 times with different gem types:\n   - Gem type 2 (highest priority gems)\n   - Gem type 1 (medium priority gems - called twice)\n   - Gem type 0 (lowest priority gems)\n8. Each iteration: reset buffer, format properties, append to output\n9. Finalize string with final strcat calls\n10. Return with success, or exit with error code -1 if validation fails\n\nParameters:\nnItemHandle (in ECX): Item pointer/handle for stat lookup\npwOutputBuffer (in EDX): Pointer to output buffer for formatted property string\ndwChardataTable (Stack[0x4]): Chardata table index for property lookup\n\nReturns:\nvoid - String written to pwOutputBuffer, or process terminates if validation fails\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If item lacks 0x35 stat (required), terminates with assertion\n- If item lacks 0x4a stat (no gems), early return without string building\n- If gem modifiers table is null, terminates with assertion\n- Constructs strings in 512-byte Unicode buffer before copying to output",
