      "comment": "Format item description string with multiple components\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize ordinal result codes via three Ordinal_10004() calls\n2. Loop nCount times through item pointers (incrementing by 4 bytes)\n3. For each iteration:\n   a. Get item stat via Ordinal_10466(dwItemId, *szItemPointer)\n   b. Extract stat components via Ordinal_10845() into nItemHandle2, dwItemStat, dwOrdinal3\n   c. If nItemHandle2 != 0:\n      - Initialize 256-char Unicode buffer with default constructor (0x80 = 256 wide chars)\n      - Call FUN_6fb38b50 to process item handle\n      - Get final ordinal result via Ordinal_10004()\n      - If pnResult != 0 AND nUnknown2 == 0: concatenate strings to szDestStr twice\n      - Set *pnResult = 1 (success flag)\n      - Format result via sprintf: szOutput = formatted string with dwItemStat, dwOrdinal3, etc.\n      - Concatenate szDefPrefix to szItemPointer\n      - If in_stack_00000028 != 0: concatenate szDefPrefix again\n4. Loop continues until nLoopCount reaches 0, advancing szItemPointer by 4 each iteration\n5. Return void\n\nParameters:\ndwItemId (ECX) - Item/resource identifier\nszDefPrefix - Prefix string buffer\nszOutput - Formatted output string buffer\nszItemPointer - Pointer to item data array (incremented by 4 per iteration)\nnCount - Number of items to process\ndwUnknown - Unknown code parameter passed to sprintf\npnResult - Output success flag (set to 1 on success)\nnUnknown2 - Conditional flag (controls string concatenation)\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Item handle of 0 skips processing for that iteration\n- Ordinal calls appear to fetch game resource data (D2Common functions)\n- Unicode buffer size is hardcoded to 256 wide characters\n- Multiple ordinal results stored but actual usage unclear from decompilation",
