      "comment": "Formats unit stat values from stat data table and appends to output buffer.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize stat lookup values by calling Ordinal_10004 (GetStatValue) 5 times\n2. Set data table pointer to &g_pUnitStatDataTable (array of stat indices)\n3. Loop through stat data table entries:\n   a. Call Ordinal_10466 to get stat reference from unit handle and current table entry\n   b. Call Ordinal_10846 to extract stat properties (4 dword values from stat)\n   c. Check if nResultCount > 0 (stat exists)\n   d. If found, initialize Unicode buffers (local_280[256], aUStack_180[256])\n   e. Check conditional: if (*pResultCounter != 0) AND (nExtraParam == 0)\n      - Call Unicode::strcat twice\n   f. Set *pResultCounter = 1\n   g. Call Unicode::strcat twice more\n   h. Format stat string to szFormatBuffer using Ordinal_578 with &g_szFormatTemplate\n   i. Convert to Unicode and concatenate to output\n   j. Call FUN_6fb38b50 with stat count\n   k. Format final output using sprintf with stat values\n   l. Concatenate formatted output to szOutputBuffer\n4. Increment data table pointer and continue until pointer >= 0x6fba9268\n\nParameters:\n- dwUnitHandle (ECX): Unit handle to extract stats from\n- szOutputBuffer (EDX): Output buffer for formatted stat strings\n- dwFlags (Stack+0x4): Flags controlling stat formatting/filtering\n- pResultCounter (Stack+0x8): Pointer to result counter, set to 1 if stat found\n- nExtraParam (Stack+0xc): Extra parameter controlling conditional concatenation\n\nReturns:\n- void: Modifies szOutputBuffer and pResultCounter\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If nResultCount == 0, skips stat formatting for that entry\n- Conditional logic based on (*pResultCounter != 0) AND (nExtraParam == 0) determines additional concatenation\n- Uses Unicode string operations (strcat, sprintf) for output formatting\n- Iterates through predefined stat table at 0x6fba9240-0x6fba9268\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x80: Unicode buffer size (256 Unicode characters = 0x100 bytes