      "comment": "Processes unit rendering data across all units in global tables\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Loop through all available units (0-0x145)\n2. For each unit, retrieve unit data from Ordinal_10598(unit_index)\n3. Check if unit is active by verifying offset +0x1f != '\\0'\n4. If active, call Ordinal_10466 to validate unit type against dwUnitType parameter\n5. If valid unit type, call Ordinal_10933 to get rendering context handle\n6. Call Ordinal_10843 to process rendering data with context, storing results in local buffers\n7. Clamp rendering value to range [0, 3]\n8. Call Ordinal_10004 to mark processing complete\n9. Invoke Unicode string concatenation operations twice (unaff_EDI, unaff_ESI)\n10. If g_dwUnitDataCount > 0, iterate through g_pUnitDataTable matching unit data at offset +0x18\n11. For matching entries, initialize 512-element Unicode buffer and call FUN_6fb20710\n12. Break loop on successful match (FUN_6fb20710 returns non-zero)\n13. If param_5 (nLoopCount) != 0, perform additional string concatenation\n14. Continue loop until unit index reaches 0x145\n\nParameters:\nIMPLICIT ECX: dwUnitType - Unit type identifier to filter units for processing\nIMPLICIT EDX: dwRenderMode - Rendering mode/flags for data processing  \nStack[0x4]: nParam3 - Additional processing parameter\nStack[0x8]: nParam4 - Additional processing parameter\nStack[0xc]: nLoopCount - Loop iteration count (0=skip extra operations, non-0=perform additional operations)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Results written to global rendering buffers and string outputs\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If unit data pointer is NULL, skips validation and processing\n- If g_hRenderContext is NULL, uses alternative rendering result from local_20c\n- Value clamping ensures rendering value never exceeds 3\n- Empty units (offset +0x1f == '\\0') are skipped without processing",
