      "comment": "Formats an item stat value to a display string with proper modifiers and formatting.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize Unicode string buffers (256-char array, 10-char array)\n2. Clear output string pointers\n3. Retrieve stat configuration data (type, modifier info) from global tables\n4. Apply stat scaling factor if configured (check bit 0x1d, shift by byte at 0x1e)\n5. Based on stat type (g_adStatTypeTable[nStatId]), apply type-specific scaling:\n   - Types 0x06-0x0b, 0xd8-0xd9: Right-shift base value by 8 bits\n   - Type 0x27 (special): Format and return early if nModifier set\n   - Types 0x29, 0x2b, 0x2d (percentage): Return 0 if nModifier set\n   - Type 0x53 (charge): Skip processing if nParam5 set\n   - Types 0x54-0x57, 0xb3-0xb4 (stack effects): Return 0 if nParam5 set\n   - Type 0x7a (special bonus): Add 0x32 if condition check (param_1 != NULL && *param_1 == 4 && Ordinal_10731 succeeds)\n   - Type 0x79 (base value): Add 0x64 (100 decimal)\n6. Format base value to string using sprintf with g_szFormatTemplate\n7. Convert formatted string to Unicode using toUnicode\n8. Based on display mode (g_adStatDisplayTable[nStatId*16]), apply formatting rules:\n   - Cases 0,5: Append strings based on value <1 check and modifier count (1-2 appends)\n   - Cases 1,6: Conditionally append strings (1-3 appends) based on modifier count\n   - Cases 2,7: Append 2 strings if modifier==1, else 2 if modifier==2, else 1\n   - Case 3: Handle negative values by clearing output, then append based on modifier\n   - Cases 4,8: Divide base by 0x80 (128 decimal) for display, append 1-4 strings based on modifier\n   - Case 9 (special ratio): If value <1 append 1 string with 0x19, else divide 0x9c4 by value and append with count/0x19\n9. Final suffix handling: If display mode in range [5,8), format and append additional string\n10. Return 1 (success)\n\nParameters:\n- pStatInfo (int *): IMPLICIT in ECX - pointer to item data or NULL\n- nStatId (uint): IMPLICIT in EDX - stat identifier (index into global tables)\n- nBaseValue (int): Stack[0x4] - base stat value (scaled per type)\n- nModifier (int): Stack[0x8] - modifier flag affecting string formatting\n- nParam5 (int): Stack[0xc] - parameter controlling stat processing\n- pszOutput (char *): Stack[0x10] - Unicode output string buffer (2-char min capacity)\n\nReturns:\n- EAX = 1 (success/value formatted)\n- EAX = 0 (skipped due to param_4/param_5 conditions)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Type 0x27, 0x53: Early return to LAB_6fb2085c if conditions met\n- Type 0x7a: Special handling when pStatInfo is valid, dereferenced, and Ordinal_10731 check passes\n- Ordinal calls (10004, 10598, 10519, 10731, 578): External library functions for stat processing\n- Unicode handling: Input/output use Unicode class methods (sprintf, strcpy, strcat, toUnicode)\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n- 0x100: Unicode buffer element count (256 characters)\n- 0x10: Stride for table indexing (param_2 * 0x10)\n- 0x1d, 0x1e: Offsets within stat config for scaling flags and shift amount\n- 0x0b, 0xd8, 0xd9: Stat type boundaries for shift-by-8 handling\n- 0x27, 0x29, 0x2b, 0x2d, 0x53: Stat type boundaries for special cases\n- 0x54-0x57, 0xb3-0xb4: Stat types for param_5 return-0 handling\n- 0x7a, 0x79: Stat types for bonus adjustments\n- 0x39: Magic value passed to Ordinal_10731 for bonus check\n- 0x32, 0x64: Bonus adjustments (50 decimal, 100 decimal)\n- 0x80, 0x9c4: Constants for ratio division (128 decimal, 2500 decimal)\n- 0x19: Divisor for final value (25 decimal)\n- 0x64: Comparison value for ratio check (100 decimal)\n\nGlobal Data Layout:\n- g_adStatTypeTable (0x6fbb4168): Indexed by nStatId - stat type identifiers\n- g_adStatDisplayTable (0x6fbb416c): Indexed by nStatId*16 - display mode flags\n- g_adStatModifierTable (0x6fbb4174): Indexed by nStatId*16 - modifier count/flags\n- g_szFormatTemplate (0x6fbb2458): Format string for stat value",
      "tags": ["PARAM_6", "PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PROP_LOOPHEAVY", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
