      "comment": "Build detailed description of a game unit with stats, items, and status information\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize Unicode buffers for base text (256 chars), output (256 chars)\n2. Get unit type via Ordinal_10751(); if special unit (0x0b), handle special case\n3. Special case: Initialize two 128-element Unicode buffers; get unit handle via Ordinal_10732()\n4. Iterate through unit stat table DAT_6fbb4b80 (count in DAT_6fbb4be0)\n5. For each matching unit type, call Ordinal_10519() to get stat value, right-shift for types 6-7, 8-9, 10-11\n6. Format stat with Ordinal_578() (snprintf equivalent), convert to Unicode via toUnicode()\n7. Validate table entry at offset 0x4 != 0 (required field check)\n8. Append formatted strings to output text multiple times via strcat references\n9. If not special case, extract unit handle via Ordinal_10470() with unit slot\n10. Call Ordinal_10484() twice to apply param5 and param6 modifiers to unit handle\n11. Ordinal_10573() applies modifications to actual unit\n12. Walk unit inventory chain (Ordinal_10277 -> Ordinal_10304/10305) for unit type 4 (player)\n13. BuildGameStateText/BuildCoordinateMapping for map info\n14. Process skill/ability slots checking bits 0x27,0x29,0x2b,0x2d (all equal?) and 0x53,0x54,0x55,0x56,0x57,0xb3,0xb4\n15. Call FUN_6fb21450() to initialize stat lookup array aiStack_18c[]\n16. Iterate through description slots DAT_6fbb4168[] (count in DAT_6fbb4b78)\n17. Call FUN_6fb20710() for each slot returning formatted description string\n18. Call FormatUnitStats, FormatItemDescription (3x for DAT_6fba9210/9220/9230), FUN_6fb20570\n19. Special final check: if unit type 4 with valid inventory, format additional text\n20. Return via Ordinal_10485() (cleanup/release unit)\n\nParameters:\npUnit (int *): ECX - pointer to unit structure\npOutputText (char *): EDX - output buffer for formatted text\npItemText (char *): Stack[4] - secondary text buffer\nnParams (int): Stack[8] - parameter/slot count\nnParam5 (int): Stack[12] - modifier 1 value\nnParam6 (int): Stack[16] - modifier 2 value  \nnParam7 (int): Stack[20] - modifier/flag value\nnParam8 (int): Stack[24] - flag parameter (controls formatting)\n\nReturns: void (output written to pOutputText buffer)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Unit type 0x0b: special unit with stat table iteration loop\n- Unit type 4: player unit with inventory chain walking\n- param8 != 0: affects conditional string concatenation behavior\n- Magic numbers: 0x47 (stat query type), 0x39/0x7a (property flags), stat array offsets 0x27-0x2d/0x53-0xb4\n\nStructure Layout (Unit structure context):\nOffset | Size | Field | Type | Purpose\n0x0    | 4    | type  | uint | Unit type code (4=player, 0x0b=special)\n0x4    | 4    | class | int  | Unit subtype/class\n0x8    | 4    | x     | int  | Position X\n0x10   | 4    | y     | int  | Position Y\n0x84   | 4    | inv   | void*| Inventory head pointer\n\nNote: Function uses stack temporaries for Unicode text building (aUStack_4ac, auStack_48c, auStack_38c, auStack_38c arrays optimized away)",
      "tags": ["MOD_UI", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "STRUCT_Room2", "STRUCT_ItemData", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "SRC_mods.cpp", "STRUCT_PlayerData", "PROP_LARGE", "PARAM_8", "STRUCT_Path", "STRUCT_Skill", "PROP_LOOPHEAVY"]
