      "comment": "Initialize skill stat information array from global stat definitions.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Clear output array (0x23 dwords = 35 int elements)\n2. Iterate through global skill stat info array (g_adwSkillStatInfoIds)\n3. For each stat ID, call Ordinal_10466 (D2Common.GetUnitStat) to retrieve value\n4. Store result in appropriate output array index based on stat ID:\n   - 0x11 (param_type_skill_physical_damage) -> output[6]\n   - 0x12 (param_type_skill_magic_damage) -> output[5]\n   - 0x15 (param_type_skill_base_attack_speed) -> output[0], fallback to 0x17 if zero\n   - 0x16 (param_type_skill_level_dependent_attack_speed) -> output[1], fallback to 0x18 if zero\n   - 0x30-0x3b (additional skill parameters) -> output[20-27]\n5. Post-process output array: For 7 groups of 5-element slots, set slot[3]=1 if both slot[0]>0 and slot[1]>0 (validation)\n\nParameters:\n  dwUnitId (dword) - IMPLICIT in ECX, unit identifier for stat lookup\n  pStatArray (int *) - Output array of 35 integer values to populate\n\nReturns:\n  void (result in output array)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Fallback handling: 0x15 tries 0x17 if first call returns 0; 0x16 tries 0x18 if first returns 0\n  - Output array index mapping uses both array offsets [N] and hex offsets [0xN]\n  - Validation loop only operates on first 7 slot groups (indices 3, 8, 13, 18, 23, 28, 33)",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PARAM_2", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
