      "instructions": ["0x51640|SUB|ESP, 0x808"],
      "comment": "Process Unicode string and format with line breaks\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize local Unicode buffer (0x400 dwords, 0x800 bytes)\n2. Call FUN_6fb20ce0 to fill buffer with formatted output\n3. If bInsertNewlines equals 0, return without newline insertion\n4. Get string length via Unicode::strlen for length validation\n5. If length is 0, return empty result with formatting strings\n6. Calculate search start position as (length - 2)\n7. Scan backwards through buffer looking for newline (0x0A)\n8. When newline found and position > 0:\n   - Call Ordinal_10004 twice (D2Lang.GetLocaleId context)\n   - Null-terminate string at newline position\n   - Append szFormat string 3 times for spacing\n   - Check last character for trailing newline and remove if present\n   - Append szFormat string 3 more times for final padding\n9. If no newline found, append szFormat 2 times and return\n\nParameters:\n- pThis (void *): Unicode object context pointer (ECX register)\n- nBufferSize (int): Buffer allocation size (0x400 dwords)\n- nInsertNewlines (int): Insertion control flag\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Formatted string built via Unicode::strcat in szOutput buffer\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Handles zero-length strings\n- Removes duplicate trailing newlines\n- Calls D2Lang function for locale-specific formatting",
      "tags": ["PROP_TINY", "PARAM_3", "PROP_LEAF"]
    },
