      "comment": "Process unit description by type filter matching.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if unit type is 5 (class/type) via Ordinal_10695 - return if not\n2. Get unit mode via Ordinal_10732\n3. Loop through g_anUnitTypeFilter array searching for matching type\n   - Call Ordinal_10480(pUnit, filter_value) to check unit\n   - If non-zero, call Ordinal_10466(result, 0x47) to extract type bits\n   - Compare result to unit mode, break if matches\n   - Increment array pointer and counter, check boundary at 0x6fba9284\n4. Call BuildUnitDescription with matched filter index\n\nParameters:\npUnit: Unit structure pointer to process\ndwUnitGUID: Unit unique identifier/GUID\nszDestBuffer: Output buffer for formatted string\nszDestBuffer2: Secondary output buffer\n\nReturns:\nvoid - modifies output buffers via BuildUnitDescription\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Returns early if unit type is not 5\n- Returns if filter array bounds exceeded (0x6fba9284)\n- Magic number 0x47 extracts specific type bits from ordinal result\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n- 0x5: Unit class/type identifier (check with GetUnitType)\n- 0x47: Bit mask for type filtering (type bits in positions 0x47)\n- 0x6fba926c: g_anUnitTypeFilter array start address\n- 0x6fba9283: g_anUnitTypeFilter boundary check value",
      "tags": ["PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_4"]
