      "comment": "Query and return unit property values based on property ID.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize local Unicode buffer (512 chars) with constructors\n2. Clear first 128 dwords of buffer memory\n3. Switch on dwPropertyId:\n   - 0x11: Return unit[8] (basic stat)\n   - 0x12: Format and concatenate multiple Unicode strings using Ordinal_10004/578\n   - 0x15-0x17: Conditional processing - check unit[4], validate unit[3]/unit[1]\n   - 0x18: Return unit[4] flag if set, else unit[3]\n   - 0x30-0x3b: Various property lookups using Ordinal_10004 for formatting\n4. Return iVar3 (result flag) or direct unit field values\n\nParameters:\npUnit (int *): Pointer to unit structure (array of dwords)\ndwPropertyId (dword): Property/stat identifier in range 0x11-0x3b\n\nReturns:\nDword value from unit structure at offset based on dwPropertyId\n0 if unit field is null/disabled\n1 if specific condition met (case 0x18)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Multiple string concatenation operations in case 0x12 (Unicode handling)\n- Fixed multiplier 0x51eb851f used in case 0x39 (fixed-point math)\n- Offset 0x80 added before right-shift by 8 bits (rounding adjustment)\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x11, 0x12, 0x15-0x17, 0x18, 0x30-0x3b: Property ID constants\n0x80: Rounding constant for fixed-point math\n0x100: Buffer size for Unicode operations\n0x51eb851f: Fixed-point multiplier (1/25 approximation)\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset | Size | Field Name | Type | Description\n0x00   | 0x04 | field_0x00 | int  | Value A (used in comparisons)\n0x04   | 0x04 | field_0x04 | int  | Value B (used in comparisons)\n0x08   | 0x04 | field_0x08 | int  | Basic stat (returned by 0x11)\n0x0c   | 0x04 | field_0x0c | int  | Enabled flag or status\n0x10   | 0x04 | field_0x10 | int  | Property flag\n0x14   | 0x04 | field_0x14 | int  | Min/current value (property-dependent)\n0x15   | 0x04 | field_0x15 | int  | Max value (property-dependent)\n...",
