      "comment": "Processes game state updates and synchronizes NPC data structures\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Clear NPC data buffer (0x6fbf8ddd to 0x6fbf8e7d) to zero\n2. Retrieve current game state object pointer\n3. Check if game state object changed during operation\n4. If changed, log mismatch error via Ordinal_10029\n5. Retrieve player entity data structure via FUN_6fb60e10\n6. Process timed skill list:\n   - Get first timed skill via Ordinal_10277\n   - For each timed skill in list:\n     - Retrieve next node via Ordinal_10304\n     - Get skill data via Ordinal_10305\n     - Process skill effects via FUN_6fb60ff0\n   - Release skill list via Ordinal_10279, Ordinal_10251\n7. Check timed event flag (g_dwTimedEventFlag)\n8. If set, process timed event data via FUN_6fb8d060\n9. Clear timed event flag and data pointer\n10. Set entity flag 0x02 (entity active bit) in player data offset 0xe8\n11. Send game state packet (type 0x30) to all clients via SendPacketData\n12. Initialize UI state via FUN_6fb58710\n13. Clear game state initialized flag\n14. Trigger UI refresh with event type 8\n15. If entity valid, update quest journal and player state\n16. Trigger final UI refresh with event type 8\n\nParameters:\nNone (void function, operates on global game state)\n\nReturns:\nNone (void)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Function uses multiple Ordinal calls which are Storm/D2Common API wrappers\n- Timed event processing only occurs if g_dwTimedEventFlag is non-zero\n- NPC data buffer clearing loop from 0x6fbf8ddd to 0x6fbf8e7d (160 bytes)\n- Entity flag update at offset 0xe8 sets bit 0x02 for active state",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Inventory", "PARAM_0"]
    },
