      "instructions": ["0x51F60|PUSH|ECX", "0x51F61|PUSH|EBX", "0x51F62|PUSH|ESI", "0x51F63|XOR|EBX, EBX", "0x51F65|PUSH|EDI", "0x51F66|MOV|dword ptr [0x6fbf8dbb], EBX", "0x51F6C|CALL|0x6fb15c00", "0x51F71|MOV|EDI, dword ptr [0x6fbf8e75]", "0x51F77|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0xc], EDI", "0x51F7B|CALL|0x6fb62880", "0x51F80|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0x51F82|JZ|0x6fb21f90", "0x51F84|CALL|0x6fb62880", "0x51F89|MOV|ECX, EAX", "0x51F8B|CALL|0x6fb86710"],
      "comment": "Transitions game state, clears unit processing, and finalizes game status.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Clear pending state flag\n2. Initialize game UI state\n3. Cache current game state\n4. Validate NPC IDs - fetch player slot, verify no state change occurred\n5. If NPC ID mismatch detected, log error via Ordinal_10029\n6. Fetch game player unit at slot 1\n7. If player exists:\n   - Clear unit processing buffer (g_adwGameUnitArray[0..N])\n   - Iterate skill chains: get first skill (Ordinal_10277), loop next (Ordinal_10304), get data (Ordinal_10305)\n   - For each skill node: call FUN_6fb60ff0 to process\n   - Release skill chain (Ordinal_10279, Ordinal_10251)\n8. Check pending unit flag - if set, finalize pending unit via FUN_6fb8d060\n9. Clear pending unit tracking globals\n10. Fetch player unit again, set flag 0x02 at offset 0x3a\n11. Send game state packet (0x30) to client\n12. Call FUN_6fb58710 (unknown finalization)\n13. Clear g_dwGameStateInitialized flag\n14. Call FUN_6fb5d370(8, 1, 0)\n15. If player exists: set scroll window mode (0x8) and clear inventory via FUN_6fb86790\n16. Call FUN_6fb5d370(8, 1, 0) again\n\nParameters:\nNone - function operates on global state\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If no player unit exists, skips unit processing and scroll/inventory operations\n- Uses Diablo II ordinal imports for skill iteration (D2Common)\n- Double call to FUN_6fb5d370 brackets player finalization\n\nNote: Function uses 1 stack-allocated temporary optimized away (local_4)",
