      "comment": "Closes NPC dialog and transitions game state based on initialization status.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if g_dwGameStateInitialized is zero\n2. If uninitialized (or player unit not found): execute full cleanup path\n   a. Clear g_fInventoryDialogOpen flag to 0\n   b. Call InitializeGameUIState to reset UI\n   c. Get game context and clear unit inventory slots if context exists\n   d. Log warning if NPC ID mismatch detected\n   e. Find unit in hash table and process linked list cleanup\n   f. If pending unit flag set, initialize inventory item state for pending unit\n   g. Clear pending unit flag and pointer\n   h. Find unit again, set flag bit 0x02 at offset 0xE8 (mark unit processed)\n   i. Send packet 0x30 to server with unit ID\n   j. Process game shutdown and reinitialize game state\n   k. Process UI state change (type 8, enable, no extra)\n   l. If unit found, modify word flags and clear unit state\n   m. Process UI state change again\n3. If initialized with valid player unit: execute dialog transition path\n   a. Close existing server socket dialog if present\n   b. Set g_fInventoryDialogOpen to 1\n   c. Search g_aUnitSlotArray for matching g_dwGameState (stride 0x16)\n   d. Calculate slot pointer: g_aUnitSlotArray + nSlotIndex * 0x16\n   e. Store in g_pGameDifficultyConfig\n   f. Call InitializeTalkDialog with found slot index\n\nParameters:\n(void) - no parameters\n\nReturns:\nvoid - modifies global dialog and game state\n\nGlobals Modified:\n- g_fInventoryDialogOpen (0x6fbf8dbb): Set to 0 (cleanup) or 1 (dialog transition)\n- g_dwPendingUnitFlag (0x6fbf8f00): Cleared to 0\n- g_pPendingUnit (0x6fbf8f04): Cleared to 0\n- g_pServerSocketDialog (0x6fbf8ebb): Cleared to 0 if dialog closed\n- g_pGameDifficultyConfig (0x6fbf8dcd): Set to slot array pointer\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x16 - Stride of unit slot array entries (22 bytes per slot)\n0x30 - Packet type for NPC dialog close notification\n0xE8 - Offset in unit structure for state flags\n0x02 - Flag bit to set at unit offset 0xE8 (processed state)\n0x1C - Offset in unit structure for word flags pointer\n0x08 - UI state change type (dialog state)\n0x3A - Array index for unit state flags (offset 0xE8 / 4 = 58 = 0x3A)",
