      "instructions": ["0x52250|TEST|ECX, ECX", "0x52252|JZ|0x6fb22270", "0x52254|MOV|dword ptr [0x6fbf8e79], 0x1", "0x5225E|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [ECX + 0x8]", "0x52261|MOV|[0x6fbf8e75], EAX", "0x52266|MOV|ECX, dword ptr [ECX + 0x4]", "0x52269|MOV|dword ptr [0x6fbf8e7d], ECX", "0x5226F|RET|", "0x52270|MOV|dword ptr [0x6fbf8e79], 0x0", "0x5227A|RET|"],
      "comment": "Initialize game state from configuration structure or reset to uninitialized state.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Test if pGameStateConfig pointer is non-NULL using TEST ECX, ECX\n2. If non-NULL branch:\n   - Set g_dwGameStateInitialized flag to 1 (indicates initialized state)\n   - Load pGameStateConfig->pGameStateObject (offset +8) into g_pGameStateObject\n   - Load pGameStateConfig->dwGameState (offset +4) into g_dwGameState\n3. If NULL branch:\n   - Set g_dwGameStateInitialized flag to 0 (indicates uninitialized state)\n4. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\n- pGameStateConfig (GameStateConfig *): Pointer to game state configuration structure containing state value and object pointer. Pass NULL to reset to uninitialized state. IMPLICIT: Parameter passed in ECX register (__fastcall).\n\nReturns:\n- void: No return value. Function updates three global variables to reflect new state.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- NULL pointer: Clears initialization flag and leaves state unchanged\n- Non-NULL: Loads both state value and state object from structure offsets\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset | Size | Field Name       | Type        | Purpose\n0x0    | 4    | dwPad0          | uint        | Reserved/padding\n0x4    | 4    | dwGameState     | uint        | Game state value identifier\n0x8    | 4    | pGameStateObject| void*       | Pointer to active game state object",
