      "comment": "Close talk dialog and reset game UI state.\n\nCallback handler invoked when user closes NPC talk dialog menu or selects \"Done\" option.\nRegistered as handler in InitializeTalkDialog at address 0x6fb225c0.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check g_abGameStateFlags byte at offset 1 - if non-zero, return 0 (early exit during state transition)\n2. Check if g_pCurrentTalkDialog exists (non-null pointer)\n3. If dialog exists:\n   a. Call CloseDialogAndCleanup() to destroy dialog UI and free resources\n   b. Call InitializeGameObjectProperties(1, 0, 0.0, 0.0, 0) to reset game object state\n   c. Clear g_pCurrentTalkDialog to NULL\n   d. Call InitializeInventoryDialogFrame() to reinitialize inventory UI frame\n4. Return 1 (success)\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\ndword - 0 if game state prevents closing (early exit), 1 on successful close or no dialog to close\n\nGlobals Accessed:\ng_abGameStateFlags (0x6fbf8db8) - Game state flags array, byte[1] checked for transition lock\ng_pCurrentTalkDialog (0x6fbf8ebf) - Pointer to current talk dialog structure\n\nCallees:\nCloseDialogAndCleanup (0x6fb005c0) - Destroys dialog UI elements\nInitializeGameObjectProperties (0x6fb8d210) - Resets game object rendering state\nInitializeInventoryDialogFrame (0x6fb249e0) - Reinitializes inventory panel\n\nCallers:\nInitializeTalkDialog - Registers this as close handler and \"Done\" button action",
