      "comment": "Close NPC talk dialog and cleanup associated game state.\n\nCallback handler invoked when player ends NPC interaction dialog.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check g_abGameStateFlags byte 1; if non-zero (game state invalid), return 0\n2. Check g_pCurrentTalkDialog; if null (no active dialog), skip to return 1\n3. Call CloseDialogAndCleanup() to close dialog UI\n4. Clear g_pCurrentTalkDialog and g_fInventoryDialogOpen (ram0x6fbf8dbb)\n5. Call InitializeGameUIState() to reset UI\n6. Save current g_pGameStateObject as nUnitId for validation\n7. Get game context; if valid, call ClearUnitInventorySlots() on player unit\n8. Validate nUnitId matches g_pGameStateObject; log mismatch if different\n9. Find unit in hash table for nUnitId with type=1 (player)\n10. If unit found:\n    a. Clear g_adwGameUnitArray (160 bytes at 0x6fbf8ddd in 16-byte chunks)\n    b. Get inventory pointer from unit offset +0x84\n    c. If inventory exists, iterate inventory nodes:\n       - For each node, get next node and field data\n       - Remove item from hash table using unit ID and type\n    d. Call ClearInventory() and ClearInventoryData() on inventory\n11. If g_dwPendingUnitFlag set, call InitializeInventoryItemState(g_pPendingUnit)\n12. Clear g_dwPendingUnitFlag and g_pPendingUnit\n13. Find unit again in hash table; if found, set flag 0x2 at offset +0xE8\n14. Send packet 0x30 (close NPC dialog) with unit ID\n15. Call ProcessGameShutdown() for shutdown processing\n16. Clear g_dwGameStateInitialized\n17. Call ProcessUIStateChange(8, 1, 0) to update UI state\n18. If unit found, call ModifyWordFlags() at offset +0x70 with (8, 0)\n19. Call ClearUnitStateAndProcessTransition(unit, 1)\n20. Call ProcessUIStateChange(8, 1, 0) again\n21. Return 1 (success)\n\nParameters:\nNone - uses global state (g_pCurrentTalkDialog, g_pGameStateObject)\n\nReturns:\nint - 1 on success (dialog closed), 0 if game state invalid\n\nSSA Variables (decompiler temporaries - no storage):\n- nUnitId (dword): Saved g_pGameStateObject for validation, stored in EDI\n- pvVar1 (void *): GetGameContext() return value, check result\n- pUnit_00 (UnitAny *): Player unit from GetGameContext() for inventory clear\n- piVar2 (int *): FindUnitInHashTable() result, player unit pointer\n- pNode (InventoryData *): Current inventory node during iteration\n- pIVar3 (InventoryData *): Next inventory node from GetInventoryNodeNext()\n- pUnit_01 (uint *): Player unit pointer from second hash lookup\n- puVar4 (undefined4 *): Loop pointer for clearing g_adwGameUnitArray\n- pUnit (UnitAny_conflict *): Inventory pointer from unit +0x84\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Returns 0 immediately if g_abGameStateFlags byte 1 is non-zero\n- Returns 1 without action if no dialog is active\n- Logs \"mismatch npc ids\" if unit ID changes during processing\n\nMemory Cleanup:\n- Clears 160-byte g_adwGameUnitArray in 16-byte chunks (loop 0x6fb22692-0x6fb2269d)\n- Iterates and removes all inventory items from hash table\n- Clears pending unit state\n\nNetwork:\n- Sends packet type 0x30 (end NPC dialog) to server",
