      "comment": "End NPC conversation dialog and perform cleanup/state transition.\n\nCalled as callback from \"End Conversation\" dialog option in InitializeTalkDialog.\nHandles two distinct paths based on game state.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Save difficulty config offset +0xd to iVar3 (level/area index)\n2. Check if g_dwGameStateInitialized != 0 AND FindUnitInHashTable returns valid unit\n3. PATH A - Dialog active with valid unit (skip to step 11 if false):\n   a. Set g_abGameStateFlags byte 1 = 1 (conversation ending flag)\n   b. Call InitializeStateCallbackAndData with LAB_6fb22a20 callback, param 0\n   c. Call CloseDialogAndCleanup to close current dialog\n   d. Clear g_pCurrentTalkDialog = 0\n   e. Set difficulty config byte +0x11 = 1 (area transition flag)\n4. If g_abGameStateFlags byte 2 == 0 (unit slots not validated):\n   a. Loop through g_aUnitSlotArray (stride 0x16 bytes)\n   b. Call ValidateUnitSlot for each slot, i < g_dwMaxUnitSlots\n   c. Set g_abGameStateFlags byte 2 = 1 (slots validated)\n   d. Reload iVar3 from config +0xd\n5. Re-fetch unit from hash table (may be NULL if state cleared)\n6. Calculate area index: iVar3 % config[+9] -> multiply by 0xF stride\n7. Read short from config[+5] + calculated offset\n8. Call InitializeGameAfterLoad(pUnit, areaShort) and return\n\n9. PATH B - No dialog or invalid unit (cleanup path):\n10. Clear ram0x6fbf8dbb = 0\n11. Call InitializeGameUIState\n12. Save g_pGameStateObject to nUnitId\n13. Get game context; if valid, clear unit inventory slots\n14. If nUnitId != g_pGameStateObject, log \"mismatch npc ids\" warning\n15. Find unit in hash table; if found, call ClearGameUnitsAndProcessLinkedList\n16. If g_dwPendingUnitFlag != 0, call InitializeInventoryItemState(g_pPendingUnit)\n17. Clear g_dwPendingUnitFlag and g_pPendingUnit to 0\n18. Re-find unit; if valid, set unit[0xE8] |= 0x2 (state transition flag)\n19. Send packet 0x30 (conversation end) with params (1, nUnitId)\n20. Call ProcessGameShutdown\n21. Call InitializeGameState(NULL)\n22. Call ProcessUIStateChange(8, 1, 0)\n23. If unit valid: ModifyWordFlags at unit[0x1C], clear flags 8\n24. Call ClearUnitStateAndProcessTransition(pUnit, 1)\n25. Call ProcessUIStateChange(8, 1, 0) again\n26. Return 1\n\nParameters:\nNone (uses globals for state)\n\nReturns:\nint - Always returns 1 on success\n\nDecompiler Variables (SSA artifacts - cannot be renamed):\n- piVar1 (pUnit): Pointer to unit from FindUnitInHashTable result\n- pvVar2 (pGameContext): Void pointer from GetGameContext\n- iVar3 (nAreaIndex): Area/level index counter, reused as loop counter\n- nSlotIndex (pSlotEntry): Pointer iterating through unit slot array\n- pUnit: UnitAny pointer for inventory operations\n- pUnit_00 (pTargetUnit): Unit pointer for state transition operations\n- nUnitId (dwSavedGameState): Saved copy of g_pGameStateObject\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Path A: Quick exit when dialog state valid - validates slots and transitions area\n- Path B: Full cleanup when no active dialog - processes shutdown and resets state\n- Unit slot validation loop uses 0x16 (22) byte stride per slot entry\n- Packet 0x30 signals server that conversation has ended\n- Unit offset 0xE8: state flags, bit 1 = transitioning\n- Unit offset 0x1C: pointer to word flags for UI state\n- Unit offset 0x3A (as dword index): state flags at byte offset 0xE8",
