      "comment": "Handle \"No Talk\" dialog option selection for NPC interaction menu.\n\nClassification: Callback/Handler - Invoked when player selects \"No Talk\" option in NPC dialog.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get game context and extract current game mode from offset +0x4\n2. Check if game state initialized (g_dwGameStateInitialized != 0)\n3. Find player unit in hash table via FindUnitInHashTable(g_pGameStateObject, 1)\n4. If player found, extract dialog state code from unit offset +0x4\n5. Switch on dialog state code:\n   - 0x201: If game mode == 4, validate unit slots and initialize with config mode 0xf\n   - 0x202: If game mode == 2, validate slots and call InitializeGameAfterLoad with index 0xb\n   - 0x203: If game mode == 3, validate slots and initialize with config mode 0xa\n6. If no state matches, check if game mode matches difficulty config offset +0x1a\n7. If matches, get current game state object:\n   - If null: call ProcessGameInitialization\n   - If valid: validate slots and initialize with config mode 0x1\n8. If game mode doesn't match, call ProcessGameStateTransition(0, false)\n9. For successful paths: calculate config index as (mode % divisor) * 0xf, read config value\n\nCommon State Setup (steps 5.x, 7):\na. Set g_abGameStateFlags[1] = 1 (mark state transition active)\nb. InitializeStateCallbackAndData(0x6fb22a20, 0) - register callback\nc. CloseDialogAndCleanup() - close current dialog\nd. Clear g_pCurrentTalkDialog\ne. Set difficulty config flag at offset +0x11\nf. If g_abGameStateFlags[2] == 0, validate unit slots then set flag to 1\n\nFallback Path (LAB_6fb22c22):\n- Clear g_fInventoryDialogOpen (0x6fbf8dbb)\n- InitializeGameUIState()\n- InitializeGameObjects(g_pGameStateObject)\n- ProcessUIStateChange(8, 1, 0)\n\nParameters:\nNone - Uses global state for context\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Modifies global game state and UI\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Dialog state 0x201/0x202/0x203 are distinct NPC interaction modes\n- Unit slot validation loop iterates g_dwMaxUnitSlots times with 0x16-byte stride\n- Config mode calculation: index = (mode % g_pGameDifficultyConfig[9]) * 0xf\n- Config value read from: g_pGameDifficultyConfig[5] + (index * 0xf)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x201, 0x202, 0x203: Dialog state codes for different NPC interaction types\n- 0xf, 0xa, 0x1, 0xb: Config mode indices for InitializeGameAfterLoad\n- 0x16: Unit slot structure stride (22 bytes)\n- 0x11: Offset in difficulty config for state flag",
