      "comment": "Initialize game session and validate unit slots based on game phase transition.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if game is currently initializing (g_dwGameStateInitialized != 0)\n2. If initializing, mark game state ready and proceed to unit validation loop\n3. Validate each unit slot by calling ValidateUnitSlot() for slot count iterations\n4. Set game state ready flag in g_abGameStateFlags\n5. Query game unit pointer from g_pGameStateObject\n6. Apply difficulty-based resource indexing using nGamePhase parameter\n7. Check if game object changed; if so, validate NPC IDs match with Ordinal_10029 (D2Client.LogMessage)\n8. Clean up any pending unit state before new game session\n9. Set unit active flag (field 0x3a |= 0x02) before transmission\n10. Send game state packet (0x30) to notify other clients\n11. Initialize UI state and refresh viewport with visibility flags\n\nParameters:\nnGamePhase: Game phase index or difficulty-based resource index (int, implicit ECX)\ncSkipUnitValidation: Boolean flag; if non-zero, skip unit validation loop (char, implicit DL)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Function modifies global game state, unit slots, and network packet transmission\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Game not initialized: Performs full initialization including unit slot validation\n- Game object changes between calls: Validates NPC ID consistency as safety check\n- Pending unit exists: Cleans up old unit before processing new game state\n- Unit validation loop: Only executes if cSkipUnitValidation is 0 and g_dwMaxUnitSlots > 0\n- Note: Function uses 1 stack-allocated temporary (local_EAX_109) optimized away by compiler",
