      "comment": "Handles the shop action dialog option when user selects trading in NPC talk menu.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if game state is initialized (g_dwGameStateInitialized != 0)\n2. If not initialized, exit early returning 1\n3. Find player unit in hash table via FindUnitInHashTable(g_pGameStateObject, 1)\n4. If player unit not found, exit early returning 1\n5. Re-check game state and re-fetch player unit (defensive check)\n6. Call InitializeGameAfterLoad(pPlayerUnit, 0xfe) to reinitialize game for shop mode\n7. Set dialog selection flag: g_abGameStateFlags[1] = 1\n8. Register callback via InitializeStateCallbackAndData(LAB_6fb22a20, 0)\n9. Close current dialog via CloseDialogAndCleanup()\n10. Clear talk dialog pointer: g_pCurrentTalkDialog = 0\n11. Return 1 (success)\n\nParameters:\nNone (void) - callback invoked by dialog system\n\nReturns:\nEAX = 1 always (success indicator for dialog callback)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Double-fetch of player unit with intervening state check appears redundant but may\n  guard against race condition where game state changes between checks\n- Called only when g_dwGameState == 0xc9 (SHOPPING mode) per InitializeTalkDialog\n- 0xfe config mode passed to InitializeGameAfterLoad initializes shop UI\n\nRelated Functions:\n- InitializeTalkDialog: Registers this as callback for shop action option\n- InitializeGameAfterLoad: Reinitializes game state for shopping\n- InitializeStateCallbackAndData: Sets up state transition callback\n- CloseDialogAndCleanup: Closes NPC talk dialog\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0xfe - Shop mode configuration value for InitializeGameAfterLoad\n0x1 - Unit type parameter for FindUnitInHashTable (player unit)",
      "tags": ["PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_0"]
