      "comment": "Handle dialog callback for \"Open Box\" option in NPC trade dialog.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if game state is initialized (g_dwGameStateInitialized != 0)\n2. Find player unit in hash table via FindUnitInHashTable(g_pGameStateObject, 1)\n3. If player unit found, re-fetch player unit (redundant state consistency check)\n4. Initialize game after load with config mode 0x152 (box opening mode)\n5. Set game state transition flag (g_abGameStateFlags byte at +1 = 1)\n6. Register state callback LAB_6fb22a20 with InitializeStateCallbackAndData\n7. Close current dialog via CloseDialogAndCleanup()\n8. Clear global talk dialog pointer (g_pCurrentTalkDialog = 0)\n9. Return 1 indicating success (EAX = 1 in disassembly)\n\nParameters:\nNone (void)\n\nReturns:\nint - Always returns 1 (success); return value set in EAX at 0x6fb23290\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Early exit if game state not initialized (returns without action)\n- Early exit if player unit not found in hash table\n- Redundant FindUnitInHashTable call appears to be defensive coding pattern\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x152 - Config mode for box opening game state (338 decimal)\n1 - Unit type for player unit in FindUnitInHashTable\n\nCaller Context:\n- Registered as callback in InitializeTalkDialog when g_dwGameState is in\n  trading states (0x109, 0xf4, 0xf5, 0x208, 0xf6) and player inventory\n  contains item with property 0x20786f62 (\"box \" reversed)\n- String ID 0x8b7 (2231) displayed for this option",
