      "comment": "Initialize inventory dialog. Allocates Dialog/DialogPanel, builds Unicode strings from equipment slots, formats with resource IDs, calls viewport render function.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if dialog already exists - if yes, close via CloseDialogAndCleanup\n2. Create Dialog struct (0x1ea x 0x15e pixels) centered on screen using screen dimensions\n3. Initialize 300-element Unicode buffer on stack for main display string\n4. Get resource string IDs 0xf and 0xe, sum them, format title via Ordinal_10004\n5. Add dialog header line (type 0x15) and background color line (0x13b) to dialog\n6. Allocate viewport panel (0x1ea x 0x118) via Ordinal_401, position below title\n7. Loop 10 times through equipment slots [puStack_68c + offset]:\n   a. Check if slot has item via [puStack_68c + 4] != 0\n   b. Call Ordinal_11086 to notify system, get video frame via Ordinal_11082\n   c. Initialize 6 Unicode string buffers (300/40/300/20 elements each)\n   d. Format display string by concatenating resource strings 0xf9b/0xf9c/0xf9d\n   e. Format 4 numeric values (dwValue0-3) via wsprintfA(\"%d\") and win2Unicode\n   f. If Ordinal_11085 returns nonzero, append hex format via ProcessBracketedStringData\n   g. Call viewport->vtable[0x30] with formatted strings and render\n8. After loop, check if nItemsFound == 0; if yes, display empty message\n9. Set dialog line focus to -1, return success (1)\n\nParameters:\n  (none explicitly - uses global dialog state via EBX)\n\nReturns:\n  1 on success (dialog initialized and rendered)\n  0 on failure (allocation failed or existing dialog error)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Dialog is 490x350 pixels centered on screen with 195-pixel Y offset\n  - Viewport is 280 pixels tall, positioned 160 pixels below center\n  - String buffers total 1280+ Unicode chars allocated on stack\n  - Equipment slot loop runs exactly 10 iterations (index 0-9)\n  - Three numeric output values formatted via \"%d\" format string\n  - Hex-formatted string built only if Ordinal_11085 condition met",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "STRUCT_Room2", "STRUCT_ItemData", "PARAM_1", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData", "STRUCT_StatList", "PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Path", "STRUCT_Skill", "PROP_LOOPHEAVY"]
