      "comment": "Reset character dialog state and reinitialize inventory dialog frame.\n\nClassification: Cleanup/Initialization hybrid - closes existing dialog before reinitializing\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if g_pCharacterDialogState is non-zero (dialog exists)\n2. If dialog exists:\n   a. Call CloseDialogAndCleanup to tear down current dialog\n   b. Check if g_pDialogCallback is non-null\n   c. If callback exists, invoke vtable[0] destructor with param 1\n   d. Clear g_pDialogCallback to NULL\n   e. Clear g_pCharacterDialogState to 0\n3. Call InitializeInventoryDialogFrame to set up fresh dialog frame\n4. Return 1 (success)\n\nParameters:\n  None - Function takes no explicit parameters\n\nReturns:\n  1 - Always returns success after reset (EAX set to 1)\n\nGlobal State Modified:\n  g_pCharacterDialogState (0x6fbf8ec3) - Cleared to 0\n  g_pDialogCallback (0x6fbf8ecf) - Cleared to NULL\n\nCallers:\n  InitializeCharacterInventoryDialog - Called as cleanup callback (function pointer)\n  Used as callback passed to InitializeDialogStructure at 0x6fb23a60\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If no dialog exists (g_pCharacterDialogState == 0), skips cleanup and only initializes\n  - Callback destructor invoked with argument 1 before clearing pointer\n  - Dialog callback uses vtable dispatch via *g_pDialogCallback then [EAX]",
