      "comment": "Initialize a dialog box with computed coordinates from game state.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Send initial packet with current resource ID to server\n2. Check and close any previously open dialog if flag set\n3. Initialize dialog position variables (X=0, Y=0)\n4. If game state active: fetch game state object, extract viewport coordinates\n5. Calculate dialog position: apply viewport offsets and ensure minimum Y coordinate (0x14)\n6. Create new dialog structure with computed coordinates, default template resource\n7. Set dialog timeout to current time + 60000ms\n8. Initialize dialog field with default value (0)\n9. Queue dialog line with default color settings (base=0xF, extra=0, mode=0, value=1)\n\nParameters:\n  void (no parameters)\n\nReturns:\n  void (modifies global dialog state)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Minimum Y coordinate enforced at 0x14 (20 pixels)\n  - Dialog position offset: Y -= (0x96 + rect.top), X = local_28 - rect.left\n  - Uses game state for coordinate calculation only if g_dwGameStateInitialized != 0\n  - Ordinal_10004 called during initialization (Storm.dll function)\n  - Ordinal_10335 called to update dialog position (D2Common function)",
