      "instructions": ["0x53D20|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [ECX]", "0x53D22|PUSH|EBX", "0x53D23|MOV|[0x6fbf8ed3], EAX", "0x53D28|MOV|EDX, dword ptr [ECX + 0x4]"],
      "comment": "Processes network validation data and handles game state transitions.\n\nClassification: Worker function - handles network validation state machine\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Copy 15-byte NetValidationData structure to global storage (g_dwNetValidationField0-E)\n2. Get game context and calculate total stat value for stat ID 0xE (energy)\n3. Check g_byGameStateMode:\n   - If mode != 5 and mode == 10: Initialize character selection dialog, return\n   - If mode != 5: Return immediately (no processing)\n4. Get player inventory from game context offset 0x84\n5. If g_byNetValidationFlag > 6 (error conditions):\n   a. Close any active server connection dialog\n   b. Select error string ID based on validation flag:\n      - 7,8: 0xD1E (connection error)\n      - 10: 0xD1C (realm error)\n      - 11: 0xD20 (character error)\n      - 12: 0xD22 (game full)\n      - 15: 0xD23 (level restriction)\n      - 16: 0xD1D (game does not exist)\n      - default: 0xD21 (generic error)\n   c. Transition state from 5 to 6\n   d. Validate and initialize error dialog with callback FUN_6fb252c0\n   e. Add error message line and OK button\n   f. Return\n6. If g_byNetValidationFlag == 0 (success):\n   a. Initialize game object with g_dwLastPacketTime\n   b. Reset g_dwLastPacketTime to 0\n   c. Find unit in hash table using validation parameter\n   d. If not found, set g_dwGameStatusFlags = 1 and return\n7. If g_byNetValidationFlag == 1 (alternate success):\n   a. Initialize game object with 0xDD\n   b. Find unit in hash table\n   c. If found, set g_dwGameStatusFlags = 1 and return\n8. If g_byNetValidationFlag == 5: Open hireling dialog\n9. Set g_dwGameStatusFlags = 0 (success)\n10. Close server connection dialog if active\n11. Clear unit selection state\n12. Reset initialization counters and network state\n13. Set g_byGameStateMode = 3 (in-game state)\n14. Initialize object type array and validate viewport\n\nParameters:\npNetValidationData (ECX) - Pointer to 15-byte NetValidationData structure containing:\n  dwField0 (0x00): First validation DWORD\n  dwField4 (0x04): Second validation DWORD\n  dwField8 (0x08): Third validation DWORD\n  wFieldC (0x0C): Validation WORD\n  byFieldE (0x0E): Final validation byte\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value; modifies global state\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Function body truncated in Ghidra (only 10 bytes defined); full logic extends to ~0x6fb24000\n- Multiple exit points based on validation flag value\n- Error paths call FogAssert and ExitApplicationWithCode(-1)\n- g_byGameStateMode values: 3=in-game, 5=validating, 6=error dialog, 10=character select\n\nError String IDs (from D2Lang):\n0xD1C: Realm down error\n0xD1D: Game does not exist\n0xD1E: Connection error\n0xD20: Character error\n0xD21: Generic error\n0xD22: Game is full\n0xD23: Level restriction\n\nGlobals Modified:\ng_dwNetValidationField0-E: Cached validation data\ng_dwReservedViewportData: Stat value result\ng_byGameStateMode: State machine mode\ng_dwGameStatusFlags: Operation result\ng_fServerConnecting: Connection dialog flag\ng_byInitAttemptCounter: Reset to 0\ng_dwNetworkStateFlag: Reset to 0\ng_nInteractionData: Reset to 0\ng_pCharacterSelectionDialog: Error dialog handle",
      "tags": ["PARAM_1", "PROP_LEAF", "PROP_SMALL"]
