      "comment": "Handles game exit or server disconnect by cleaning up pending units, dialogs, and game state.\n\nClassification: Worker function - handles cleanup and state transition during game exit\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if pending unit operation flag is set (g_dwPendingUnitFlag)\n2. If pending unit exists, call InitializeInventoryItemState to finalize it\n3. Clear pending unit pointer and flag\n4. Check if server socket dialog is active (g_pServerSocketDialog)\n5. If dialog active, close it via CloseDialogAndCleanup and clear pointer\n6. Find player unit (type 1) in hash table using g_pGameStateObject\n7. If player found AND player has active state (offset 0x84 != 0):\n   a. Set game mode to 3 (exit pending)\n   b. Clear game state flags\n   c. Trigger UI state change (mode 0xC = exit dialog)\n   d. Send packet 0x38 (disconnect request) to server\n   e. Store current game context in g_pCurrentPlayerSlot\n   f. Clear status word at 0x6fbf8f24\n   g. Return early (graceful disconnect path)\n8. Otherwise (forced exit path):\n   a. Set game mode to 0 (cleanup)\n   b. Initialize game UI state\n   c. Get game context and clear player inventory slots\n   d. Initialize game unit arrays for cleanup\n   e. Find player unit again and set flag bit 0x02 at offset 0xE8\n   f. Send packet 0x30 (game exit) to server\n   g. Call ProcessGameShutdown\n   h. Clear g_dwGameStateInitialized\n   i. Trigger UI state change (mode 8)\n   j. If player unit exists, modify word flags and clear unit state\n\nParameters: None (void)\n\nReturns: void (implicitly returns 1 in EAX on exit)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Two distinct exit paths: graceful (player has active state) vs forced (immediate cleanup)\n- Graceful path sends packet 0x38 and returns early\n- Forced path performs full cleanup sequence\n\nDecompiler Variables (SSA temporaries - cannot be renamed):\n- piVar1: Player unit pointer from FindUnitInHashTable (type int*)\n- pvVar2: Temporary for GetGameContext result check (type void*)\n- pUnit: UnitAny pointer for ClearUnitInventorySlots\n- pUnit_00: Player unit as uint* for flag manipulation\n- dwGameStateId: Copy of g_pGameStateObject for function calls\n\nGlobals Modified:\n- g_dwPendingUnitFlag: Cleared to 0\n- g_pPendingUnit: Cleared to 0 after processing\n- g_pServerSocketDialog: Cleared to 0 after closing\n- ram0x6fbf8dbb: Set to 3 (graceful) or 0 (forced)\n- g_dwGameStateFlags: Cleared on graceful exit\n- g_pCurrentPlayerSlot: Set to current game context on graceful exit\n- g_dwGameStateInitialized: Cleared on forced exit\n\nFlag Bits:\n- Unit offset 0x84: Non-zero indicates active player state\n- Unit offset 0xE8: Bit 0x02 set during forced exit (marks unit for cleanup)\n- Word flags parameter 0x08: Passed to ModifyWordFlags during cleanup\n\nCross-References:\n- Called from function pointer table at 0x6fbb64ce and 0x6fbb68c4\n- Likely triggered by game exit menu option or server disconnect event",
