      "comment": "Initialize game UI state and process active dialog rendering for server connection and character selection workflow.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if initial game state setup is complete (FUN_6fb62890 return value)\n2. If setup incomplete, validate game state initialized flag (g_dwGameStateInitialized)\n3. Retrieve game state object at index 1 using FUN_6fb60e10\n4. Verify state object type field [+0xc] equals 0xc\n5. If validation passes, enter character selection dialog path (LAB_6fb24556)\n6. If validation fails, initialize game UI (InitializeGameUIState, FUN_6fb29ff0, FUN_6fb5d370)\n7. At LAB_6fb24556: Check active dialogs in priority order:\n   - If g_fGameNpcIdValidation active, render it\n   - Else if g_pServerSocketDialog active, render it\n   - Else if g_pCharacterSelectionDialog not set:\n     * If g_fServerConnecting flag set:\n       - Check game state object field [+0x4] == 0x202 (character selection state)\n       - If DAT_6fbf8f08 not set, initialize timeout (g_fLoadingDialogInitialized = 1, calculate expiry)\n       - Compare current tick with timeout; if expired, display loading dialog (FUN_6fb8d210)\n     * Check server connection status via GetCurrentServerPort and timeout\n     * If timeout expired, cleanup and initialize object type arrays\n     * Else validate server state change time; if past limit, configure server and enable game system\n   - Else if g_pLoadingProgressDialog active, check load status via Ordinal_10262 and FUN_6fb8f100\n     * If load complete, initialize object configs and update attempt counter\n   - Else render g_pConnectionErrorDialog or g_pUIStateDialog if set\n\nParameters:\nNone (function reads global UI state variables)\n\nReturns:\nvoid (no return value; modifies global UI state)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Function uses nested conditionals for dialog prioritization\n- Server connection timeout uses tick-based countdown calculation\n- Character selection state verification uses magic constant 0x202\n- Ordinal_10262 called with structure field offset (+0x84) parameter\n- GetTickCount called 4 times for time-based state transitions\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0xc - Expected game state object type field value\n0x1 - Game state object index parameter\n0x4 - Character selection state field offset in game state object\n0x202 - Game state type code for character selection\n0x84 - Field offset in data structure passed to Ordinal_10262\n0x11d0 - Dialog identifier constant for FUN_6fb8d210\n5 - Multiplier for tick count calculation (iVar3 * 5 + 600)\n200 - Second multiplier for timeout calculation ((iVar3 * 5 + 600) * 200)\n600 - Base tick offset for timeout calculation\n0x258 - Address constant for timeout calculation\n3 - State value written to g_dwLastInitializationTime for object type initialization",
