      "comment": "Initializes game exit state if the global system state is active.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call GetGlobalSystemState to check if game system is running\n2. If system state is non-zero (active):\n   a. Set g_dwGameExitMode to 3 (game exit mode)\n   b. Set g_pfnGameExitHandler to FUN_6fb257d0 (ProcessGameExitAndCleanup)\n   c. Set g_wPanelExitState to 0x58d2 (exit panel state identifier)\n3. Return 1 (always succeeds)\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\nint - Always returns 1\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If GetGlobalSystemState returns 0, no state changes occur (game not active)\n- The exit handler FUN_6fb257d0 handles full game disconnect: closes dialogs, \n  clears inventory, sends shutdown packets, and processes UI state changes\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x3 - Game exit mode flag value\n0x58d2 - Panel exit state identifier\n0x6fbb67ef - g_dwGameExitMode address\n0x6fbb6801 - g_pfnGameExitHandler address (function pointer)\n0x6fbb67f5 - g_wPanelExitState address\n\nClassification: Initialization function - Sets up callback state for game exit",
