      "instructions": ["0x549E0|MOV|EAX, [0x6fbf8ebb]", "0x549E5|SUB|ESP, 0x500", "0x549EB|PUSH|EBX", "0x549EC|XOR|EBX, EBX", "0x549EE|PUSH|EBP", "0x549EF|PUSH|ESI", "0x549F0|CMP|EAX, EBX", "0x549F2|PUSH|EDI", "0x549F3|JZ|0x6fb24a13", "0x549F5|PUSH|0xc07", "0x549FA|PUSH|0x6fbb6c70", "0x549FF|PUSH|0x6fbb6d40", "0x54A04|CALL|0x6fb99a7a", "0x54A09|ADD|ESP, 0xc", "0x54A0C|PUSH|-0x1"],
      "comment": "Initializes the NPC dialog frame with character/inventory-related options.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if dialog already initialized; if so, report error and exit\n2. If game state uninitialized, initialize UI state, game state, and set ground pickup flag\n3. Extract viewport coordinates and calculate dialog position offsets\n4. Create dialog structure with InitializeDialogStructure at calculated position\n5. Initialize Unicode string buffer (160 chars) for dialog text\n6. Look up player unit in game state\n7. Iterate through NPC dialog options (max 39 lines):\n   - Check line type (0x1507=stat, 0xd09=skill, 0xfb4=quest, else=special)\n   - For stat lines: get stat value from player unit, format and add to dialog\n   - For skill lines: check skill availability, format skill level with percentage\n   - For quest lines: check quest status flags, conditionally enable based on flags\n   - Set dialog line color and visibility based on conditions\n8. Add final dialog separator line\n9. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\n(void) - no parameters; uses global g_pGameStateObject for player reference\n\nReturns:\nvoid - modifies global g_dwGameNpcDialogFlags with dialog handle\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Dialog position auto-adjusts if calculated offset < 20 pixels from screen top (min y=0x14)\n- Skill lines disabled (iStack_4ec=0) if skill percentage == 0\n- Quest lines conditional on quest status flag values (0xfc, 0xc6, 0x203, 0x96)\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x14 - Minimum dialog Y coordinate (20 pixels from top)\n0x1507 - Line type ID for stat display\n0xd09 - Line type ID for skill display\n0xfb4 - Line type ID for quest display\n0x50 - Character count for Unicode array initialization (160 chars / 4 per iteration)\n0x200 - Character count for large Unicode buffer (1024 chars / 4 per iteration)\n0x27 - Byte stride for dialog option table (39 bytes per entry)\n0x3a - Offset for player state flags in unit structure\n0x1c - Offset for unit pointer in state structure\n2 - Flag value for setting player active state\n3 - Quest dialog option value\n0x421 - Magic value compared against DAT_6fbb4d04 (season/difficulty flag)",
      "tags": ["MOD_UI", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "STRUCT_Room2", "STRUCT_ItemData", "PARAM_0", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData", "STRUCT_StatList", "PROP_LARGE", "SRC_npcmenu.cpp", "STRUCT_Path", "UI_DIALOG", "STRUCT_Skill", "PROP_LOOPHEAVY"]
