      "instructions": ["0x55150|PUSH|ECX", "0x55151|MOV|ECX, dword ptr [0x6fbf8ebb]", "0x55157|PUSH|EBX", "0x55158|XOR|EBX, EBX", "0x5515A|PUSH|ESI", "0x5515B|CMP|ECX, EBX", "0x5515D|JZ|0x6fb2516a", "0x5515F|CALL|0x6fb005c0", "0x55164|MOV|dword ptr [0x6fbf8ebb], EBX", "0x5516A|PUSH|EDI", "0x5516B|MOV|dword ptr [0x6fbf8dbb], EBX", "0x55171|CALL|0x6fb15c00", "0x55176|MOV|EDI, dword ptr [0x6fbf8e75]", "0x5517C|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0xc], EDI", "0x55180|CALL|0x6fb62880"],
      "comment": "Closes the NPC dialog and resets game state for dialog transition.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. If server socket dialog exists, close it and clear pointer\n2. Reset game state mode flag to 0\n3. Initialize game UI state\n4. Save current game state object ID for validation\n5. Get game context; if valid, clear unit inventory slots\n6. Validate game state ID unchanged; log mismatch if changed\n7. Find player unit in hash table by saved ID\n8. If player found, clear game unit array (0x6fbf8ddd to 0x6fbf8e7d in 16-byte strides)\n9. Get player inventory pointer from offset 0x84\n10. If inventory exists, iterate through inventory nodes:\n    - Get next node before processing current\n    - Get node field data; if valid, remove unit from hash table\n11. Clear inventory and inventory data for player\n12. If pending unit flag set, initialize pending unit inventory state\n13. Clear pending unit flag and pointer globals\n14. Find player unit again and set active flag (OR 0x2 at offset 0xE8)\n15. Send packet 0x30 (dialog close notification) to server\n16. Process game shutdown\n17. Clear game state initialized flag\n18. Process UI state change (state=8, flag=1, param=0)\n19. If player found, modify word flags and clear unit state\n20. Final UI state change processing\n\nParameters:\n(void) - No parameters; uses global g_pGameStateObject for player reference\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Modifies multiple global state variables\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Game state ID validated before and after context operations\n- Array clearing uses 16-byte stride (clears 10 DWORDs spaced 16 bytes apart)\n- Inventory iteration saves next pointer before processing to handle removal\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x6fbf8ddd - Start of game unit array\n0x6fbf8e7d - End of game unit array (160 bytes total)\n0x84 - Offset to inventory pointer in unit structure (0x21 * 4)\n0xE8 - Offset to unit state flags (0x3A * 4)\n0x70 - Offset to word flags pointer (0x1C * 4)\n0x30 - Packet ID for dialog close notification\n0x2 - Active unit flag bit\n0x8 - UI state parameter for dialog mode",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Inventory", "PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_0"]
    },
