      "comment": "Cleans up game session state and exits to character selection menu\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Clear current unit selection state via ClearUnitSelectionState\n2. Reset game object properties via InitializeGameObjectProperties(1,0,0,0,0)\n3. Close active dialog via CloseDialogAndCleanup\n4. Store current game state object ID and clear character selection dialog pointer\n5. Check game state mode (g_byGameStateMode at 0x6fbf8dbb):\n   - If mode == 0x0C (in-game) and g_dwUnknownState == 5: proceed to cleanup\n   - If mode == 0x0C and g_dwUnknownState != 5: call InitializeInventoryDialogFrame and return\n   - If mode == 0x06: Assert failure and exit with code -1\n   - If mode == 0x08: Assert failure and exit with code -1\n   - Otherwise: Set mode to 0x03 and call InitializeObjectTypeData\n6. Get game context and clear unit inventory slots if context exists\n7. Log warning if game state object ID changed during cleanup (NPC ID mismatch)\n8. Find player unit in hash table by stored ID\n9. If unit found, initialize game unit array\n10. Get unit's inventory pointer at offset 0x84\n11. Iterate through inventory nodes, removing each unit from hash table\n12. Clear inventory and inventory data for the unit\n13. If pending unit flag set, initialize pending unit's inventory item state\n14. Clear pending unit flag and pointer globals\n15. Re-find unit and set flag bit 0x02 at offset 0xE8 (mark for cleanup)\n16. Send exit packet (type 0x30, value 1, with unit ID)\n17. Call ProcessGameShutdown and clear game state initialized flag\n18. Process UI state change (type 8, value 1, param 0)\n19. If unit still valid, modify word flags at offset 0x70 and clear unit state\n\nParameters:\n(none) - void function with no parameters\n\nReturns:\nvoid - always returns after completing cleanup sequence\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Early exit if game state mode is 0x0C but unknown state != 5\n- Assert failures trigger application exit for states 0x06 and 0x08\n- Handles case where game state object changes during cleanup (logs warning)\n- Pending unit cleanup occurs regardless of main unit existence\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x0C: In-game state mode\n- 0x05: Expected unknown state for normal cleanup\n- 0x06, 0x08: Invalid states causing assert\n- 0x03: State mode set before InitializeObjectTypeData\n- 0x30: Exit game packet type\n- 0x84: Offset to inventory pointer in unit structure\n- 0xE8: Offset to unit flags (bit 0x02 = cleanup flag)\n- 0x70: Offset to word flags in unit structure\n- 0x1C: Offset to word flags pointer (pUnit_01[0x1c])\n- 0x3A: Offset to unit flags dword (pUnit_01[0x3a] at byte offset 0xE8)\n\nGlobal Variables:\n- g_byGameStateMode (0x6fbf8dbb): Current game state mode\n- g_dwUnknownState (0x6fbf8e81): Secondary state flag\n- g_pGameStateObject (0x6fbf8e75): Current game state object ID\n- g_pCharacterSelectionDialog (0x6fbf8eb3): Character selection dialog pointer\n- g_dwPendingUnitFlag (0x6fbf8f00): Flag for pending unit operation\n- g_pPendingUnit (0x6fbf8f04): Pointer to pending unit\n- g_dwGameStateInitialized (0x6fbf8e79): Game state initialization flag",
