      "comment": "Cleanup game session state when exiting a game or logging out.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Close server socket dialog if open and clear g_pServerSocketDialog\n2. Reset g_dwInteractionState (ram0x6fbf8dbb) to 0\n3. Call InitializeGameUIState to reset UI state\n4. Save current g_pGameStateObject (player unit ID) for later comparison\n5. Get game context and clear player unit inventory slots if context valid\n6. Log \"mismatch npc ids\" warning if g_pGameStateObject changed during operation\n7. Find player unit in hash table using saved unit ID (type=1 for player)\n8. If player unit found:\n   a. Zero out g_adwGameUnitArray (10 DWORDs at 0x6fbf8ddd-0x6fbf8e7d, stride 0x10)\n   b. Get inventory pointer from unit offset +0x84\n   c. Iterate inventory linked list via GetUnitStat/GetInventoryNodeNext\n   d. For each inventory item, remove from hash table using RemoveUnitFromHashTable\n   e. Call ClearInventory and ClearInventoryData on inventory\n9. If pending unit exists (g_dwPendingUnitFlag != 0), call InitializeInventoryItemState\n10. Clear g_dwPendingUnitFlag and g_pPendingUnit\n11. Find player unit again and set flag bit 0x02 at offset +0xE8 (cleanup marker)\n12. Send packet 0x30 (game exit notification) with player ID\n13. Call ProcessGameShutdown for core shutdown\n14. Clear g_dwGameStateInitialized\n15. Call ProcessUIStateChange(8, 1, 0) to update UI state\n16. If player unit valid, clear word flag bit 8 at unit offset +0x70\n17. Call ClearUnitStateAndProcessTransition on player unit with transition type 1\n18. Call ProcessUIStateChange(8, 1, 0) again\n19. Send packet 0x38 (subcommand) with data 0x28 and player ID\n\nParameters:\nNone - operates on global state variables\n\nReturns:\nvoid - cleanup function with no return value\n\nGlobal Variables:\ng_pServerSocketDialog (0x6fbf8ebb) - Server socket dialog handle\ng_dwInteractionState (0x6fbf8dbb) - NPC interaction state flag\ng_pGameStateObject (0x6fbf8e75) - Current player unit ID\ng_adwGameUnitArray (0x6fbf8ddd) - Array of 10 unit slot DWORDs (stride 0x10)\ng_dwPendingUnitFlag (0x6fbf8f00) - Flag indicating pending unit operation\ng_pPendingUnit (0x6fbf8f04) - Pending unit pointer/ID\ng_dwGameStateInitialized (0x6fbf8e79) - Game initialization state flag\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x84 - Offset to inventory pointer in unit structure\n0xE8 - Offset to cleanup flags in unit structure\n0x70 - Offset to word flags in unit structure\n0x30 - Packet ID for game exit notification\n0x38 - Packet ID for subcommand with data\n0x28 - Subcommand parameter for exit packet\n0x02 - Cleanup marker flag bit\n0x08 - Word flag bit for UI state\n\nStructure Offsets (UnitAny):\n+0x21*4 = +0x84: pInventory - Inventory data pointer\n+0x3A*4 = +0xE8: dwCleanupFlags - Unit cleanup state flags\n+0x1C*4 = +0x70: pwWordFlags - Word-sized flag array pointer",
