      "comment": "Handles full game exit cleanup when disconnecting from a game session.\n\nCalled as exit handler callback set by SetupGameExitStateIfActive when exiting game.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Close server socket dialog if open, set g_pServerSocketDialog to 0\n2. Reset NPC dialog state (g_byNpcDialogState = 0)\n3. Initialize game UI state via InitializeGameUIState\n4. Save current game state object ID for consistency check\n5. Get game context and clear unit inventory slots if context valid\n6. Log error if game state object changed unexpectedly during cleanup\n7. Find player unit in hash table by saved ID\n8. If player unit found:\n   a. Zero out g_adwGameUnitArray (160 bytes at 0x6fbf8ddd, stride 16)\n   b. Get unit's inventory pointer at offset 0x84\n   c. Iterate inventory nodes, removing each item from hash table\n   d. Clear inventory and inventory data structures\n9. If pending unit flag set, initialize pending unit's inventory item state\n10. Clear pending unit flag and pointer\n11. Re-lookup player unit in hash table\n12. If found, set unit flags at offset 0xE8 with bit 0x2 (disconnect flag)\n13. Send game exit packet (type 0x30, param 1, unit ID)\n14. Call ProcessGameShutdown for server-side cleanup\n15. Set g_dwGameStateInitialized = 0\n16. Process UI state change (mode 8, param 1, 0)\n17. If player unit valid:\n    a. Modify word flags at unit offset 0x70 (flags 8, 0)\n    b. Clear unit state and process transition\n18. Process UI state change again (mode 8, param 1, 0)\n19. Send subcommand packet (type 0x38, 0, game state object, 0x6D)\n\nParameters:\nNone (void)\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Server socket dialog may already be closed (check before CloseDialogAndCleanup)\n- Game context may be NULL (skip inventory clear)\n- Player unit may not exist in hash table (skip unit cleanup)\n- Pending unit flag controls whether pending unit cleanup occurs\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x84 - Unit inventory pointer offset\n0xE8 - Unit flags offset (disconnect flag at bit 1)\n0x70 - Unit word flags offset\n0x30 - Game exit packet type\n0x38 - Subcommand packet type\n0x6D - Exit subcommand value\n0x2 - Disconnect flag bit\n0x8 - UI state mode for exit\n\nStructure Layout (UnitAny relevant offsets):\nOffset  Size  Field           Description\n0x70    4     pWordFlags      Pointer to word flags array\n0x84    4     pInventory      Pointer to inventory data\n0xE8    4     dwUnitFlags     Unit state flags\n\nClassification: Cleanup/Destructor - Full game session teardown handler",
