      "instructions": ["0x55950|PUSH|ECX", "0x55951|MOV|ECX, dword ptr [0x6fbf8ebb]", "0x55957|PUSH|EBX", "0x55958|XOR|EBX, EBX", "0x5595A|PUSH|ESI", "0x5595B|CMP|ECX, EBX", "0x5595D|JZ|0x6fb2596a", "0x5595F|CALL|0x6fb005c0", "0x55964|MOV|dword ptr [0x6fbf8ebb], EBX", "0x5596A|PUSH|EDI", "0x5596B|MOV|dword ptr [0x6fbf8dbb], EBX", "0x55971|CALL|0x6fb15c00", "0x55976|MOV|EDI, dword ptr [0x6fbf8e75]", "0x5597C|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0xc], EDI", "0x55980|CALL|0x6fb62880"],
      "comment": "Performs complete game session cleanup and state reset on exit.\n\nCalled when player exits the current game session. Closes dialogs, clears unit\nhash tables, processes inventory cleanup for the player's NPC/mercenary, resets\npending unit state, sends exit packets to server, and reinitializes UI state.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. If server socket dialog is open, close it and clear the global pointer\n2. Reset NPC dialog state flag (ram0x6fbf8dbb) to 0\n3. Initialize game UI state via InitializeGameUIState()\n4. Save current g_pGameStateObject as nUnitId for validation\n5. Get game context; if valid, clear unit inventory slots\n6. Verify g_pGameStateObject hasn't changed (log mismatch if it has)\n7. Find player unit in hash table by nUnitId\n8. If player unit found:\n   a. Clear g_adwGameUnitArray (160 bytes from 0x6fbf8ddd to 0x6fbf8e7d)\n   b. Get unit's inventory pointer at offset +0x84\n   c. If inventory exists, iterate all inventory nodes:\n      - Get next node before processing\n      - Get inventory item from current node\n      - Remove item from hash table using item's type and ID\n   d. Clear inventory and inventory data for the unit\n9. If pending unit flag is set, initialize inventory item state for pending unit\n10. Clear pending unit flag and pending unit pointer\n11. Re-find player unit in hash table\n12. If player unit valid, set flag bit 0x02 at unit offset +0xE8\n13. Send exit packet 0x30 with player ID\n14. Call ProcessGameShutdown()\n15. Clear g_dwGameStateInitialized flag\n16. Process UI state change (type=8, param1=1, param2=0)\n17. If player unit valid:\n    a. Modify word flags at unit offset +0x70 (clear flag 8)\n    b. Clear unit state and process transition\n18. Process UI state change again (type=8)\n19. Send packet 0x38 with subcommand 0x28 and player ID\n\nReturns:\n  int - Always returns 1 (EAX set to 1 before RET)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If server socket dialog not open, skip dialog cleanup\n  - If game context is null, skip inventory slot clearing\n  - If player unit not found in hash table, skip unit cleanup entirely\n  - If unit has no inventory (offset +0x84 is null), skip inventory iteration\n  - If pending unit flag is 0, skip pending unit cleanup\n\nMemory Access Patterns:\n  Unit structure offsets:\n    +0x70  - Word flags pointer (passed to ModifyWordFlags)\n    +0x84  - Inventory pointer (InventoryData *)\n    +0xE8  - Unit state flags (OR'd with 0x02 on cleanup)\n\n  Inventory node structure offsets:\n    +0x00  - Item type/mode\n    +0x08  - Item unit ID\n\nGlobal State Modified:\n  - g_pServerSocketDialog: Set to 0\n  - ram0x6fbf8dbb: Set to 0 (NPC dialog state)\n  - g_adwGameUnitArray: All 160 bytes cleared to 0\n  - g_dwPendingUnitFlag: Set to 0\n  - g_pPendingUnit: Set to 0\n  - g_dwGameStateInitialized: Set to 0\n\nPackets Sent:\n  - 0x30: Game exit notification (1 byte header + unit ID)\n  - 0x38: Subcommand packet with 0x28 and unit ID",
