      "comment": "Cleans up game session state, player inventory, and units on game exit.\n\nClassification: Cleanup/Destructor - Called during game session termination.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Close server socket dialog if open, set g_pServerSocketDialog to NULL\n2. Clear NPC dialog state flag (g_byNpcDialogState = 0)\n3. Initialize game UI state to default\n4. Save current unit ID from g_pGameStateObject for validation\n5. Get game context and clear player unit inventory slots if valid\n6. Log warning if unit ID changed during processing (race condition check)\n7. Find player unit in hash table by saved unit ID\n8. If player unit found:\n   a. Clear g_adwGameUnitArray (loop: 0x6fbf8ddd to 0x6fbf8e7d, stride 0x10)\n   b. Get inventory owner from unit offset +0x84\n   c. Iterate inventory nodes, remove each from hash table\n   d. Clear inventory and inventory data for owner\n9. If pending unit exists (g_dwPendingUnitFlag != 0):\n   a. Initialize inventory item state for pending unit\n   b. Clear pending unit flag and pointer\n10. Find player unit again to get current reference\n11. If unit valid, set flag bit 0x02 at offset +0xE8\n12. Send exit packet (0x30) with unit ID\n13. Call ProcessGameShutdown\n14. Clear g_dwGameStateInitialized\n15. Process UI state change (type 8, mode 1, param 0)\n16. If unit valid:\n    a. Modify word flags at offset +0x70 (value 8, clear mode 0)\n    b. Clear unit state and process transition\n17. Process UI state change again (type 8)\n18. Send packet with subcommand (0x38) for final cleanup\n\nParameters:\n  None - Function takes no parameters\n\nReturns:\n  int - Always returns 1 (success)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Server socket dialog cleanup is conditional on dialog existing\n- Unit ID mismatch logs warning but continues (defensive check)\n- Pending unit cleanup is conditional on pending flag\n- Unit flag modifications only occur if unit reference valid\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x84: Offset to inventory owner pointer in UnitAny\n- 0xE8: Offset to unit state flags (bit 0x02 set on exit)\n- 0x70: Offset to word flags field for modification\n- 0x30: Exit game packet type\n- 0x38: Subcommand packet type for final cleanup\n- 0x10: Stride for clearing game unit array\n- 8: UI state type for game exit processing",
