      "comment": "Clears game unit array and processes linked list of game objects.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize pointer to start of g_adwGameUnitArray at 0x6fbf8ddd\n2. Loop: Clear each DWORD (4 bytes) by setting to 0, advance by 0x10 bytes until reaching 0x6fbf8e7d\n3. Validate pGameObject is non-null (if null, skip linked list processing)\n4. Retrieve list head at offset 0x84 from pGameObject\n5. If list head is valid:\n   a. Call Ordinal_10277 (D2Common.GetFirstNode) to get first node\n   b. Loop through linked list:\n      - Call Ordinal_10304 (D2Common.GetNextNode) to get next node\n      - Call Ordinal_10305 (D2Common.GetNodeData) to extract node data\n      - If data pointer is valid, call FUN_6fb60ff0(pNodeData[2], pNodeData[0])\n      - Advance to next node\n   c. Call Ordinal_10279 to free iterator\n   d. Call Ordinal_10251 to cleanup linked list\n\nParameters:\npGameObject (int *) - IMPLICIT in ECX; pointer to game object containing linked list head at offset 0x84; NULL to skip linked list processing\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value; performs in-place modification\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If pGameObject is NULL, skips all linked list processing but array is still cleared\n- Array cleared spans 0x6fbf8ddd to 0x6fbf8e7d (256 bytes total)\n- Node data validation: only processes nodes where pNodeData != NULL\n- Note: Function uses SSA temporaries (iVar2, piVar3, puVar1) optimized away; cannot rename assembly-only intermediates\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x84 - Offset to linked list head within game object structure\n0x6fbf8ddd - Start of game unit array\n0x6fbf8e7d - End boundary of game unit array\n0x10 - Stride for clearing array (4-byte words, advancing 16 bytes per iteration)",
