      "comment": "Initialize game unit arrays and manage pending unit state.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Verify game state object ID matches current global state (g_pGameStateObject)\n2. Retrieve unit data pointer from game state using Ordinal_10277 (D2Common.GetUnitInventory)\n3. Zero-initialize the global unit array (g_adwGameUnitArray, 0x6fbf8ddd to 0x6fbf8e7d)\n4. Iterate through unit inventory chain using Ordinal_10304 (D2Common.GetNextUnit) and Ordinal_10305 (D2Common.GetPreviousUnit)\n5. For each item in inventory, initialize with FUN_6fb60ff0\n6. Clean up unit references using Ordinal_10279 and Ordinal_10251\n7. Clear pending unit flag and pending unit pointer to NULL\n\nParameters:\nIMPLICIT ECX (EAX) - dwGameStateId: Pointer to game state object for validation\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Exits early if game state ID does not match global g_pGameStateObject\n- Skips unit inventory processing if unit pointer is NULL\n- Handles empty inventory lists gracefully",
