      "comment": "Validate and process game state attribute flag\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load state value from game state structure at offset +0x4\n2. Invoke Ordinal_10582 (D2Common.GetUnitStat) to retrieve state table entry address\n3. Load attribute flag byte from state table entry at offset 0x2ad\n4. Test if attribute flag is non-zero (0x00 = unset, !0x00 = set)\n5. If attribute flag is set: call FUN_6fb93500(pGameState, 0x48) for attribute processing\n6. If attribute flag is unset: return without further processing\n7. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\npGameState: Pointer to GameState structure containing state identifier at offset +0x4\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No explicit return value; attribute processing via FUN_6fb93500 occurs conditionally\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If attribute flag byte at offset 0x2ad is zero, processing path is skipped\n- Processing flag 0x48 is constant for all invocations\n- Uses __fastcall convention with pGameState in ECX, flag value in EDX\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x04: Offset within game state to state identifier value\n0x2ad: Offset within state table entry to attribute flag byte (0 = unset, non-zero = set)\n0x48: Attribute processing flag constant (decimal 72)\n\nRelated Functions:\n- FUN_6fb93500 - Conditional attribute processor (called if flag set)\n- Ordinal_10582 - D2Common.GetUnitStat (state table lookup)\n- FUN_6fb26660 - Caller that manages game state initialization flow",
