      "comment": "Initialize game state and unit data structures during game startup\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Clear unit data array (16-byte strides from 0x6fbf8ddd to 0x6fbf8e7d)\n2. Initialize game UI state via InitializeGameUIState()\n3. Get current game state object pointer\n4. Validate game state consistency - log error if mismatch\n5. Obtain game state root node (player context)\n6. Iterate through all child units in linked list:\n   - Get next unit pointer via Ordinal_10304 (linked list traversal)\n   - Get unit data via Ordinal_10305 (unit structure access)\n   - Call FUN_6fb60ff0 with unit ID and unit data pointer\n7. Cleanup unit linked list head via Ordinal_10279 and Ordinal_10251\n8. Process pending unit flag: call FUN_6fb8d060 if flag set, then clear\n9. Clear pending unit references\n10. Get game state again and set bit 0x02 in field +0x3a (flags/state)\n11. Send initialization packet (0x30) with state object\n12. Run post-init sequence: clear flag, call FUN_6fb5d370, FUN_6fb796e0, FUN_6fb86790\n13. Final FUN_6fb5d370 cleanup call\n\nParameters:\n  None - void function\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Handles game state mismatch (logs error but continues)\n  - Skips unit iteration if state pointer is NULL\n  - Skips pending unit processing if flag not set\n  - Skips final operations if game state becomes NULL\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x6fbf8dbb - Flag cleared at start (game init state marker)\n  0x6fbf8ddd - Start of unit data array (16-byte aligned)\n  0x6fbf8e7d - End of unit data array (array size: 160 bytes / 0xa0)\n  0x21 - Offset in game state to linked list head\n  0x84 - Offset in game state object  \n  0x3a - Offset in unit structure for flags field\n  0x70 - Offset in unit structure (pointer to substructure)\n  0xe8 - Offset in unit structure for state flags\n  0x1c - Offset in unit structure for secondary data\n  0x30 - Packet type ID for game initialization\n  0x02 - Flag bit set in unit state field (+0xe8)\n  0x08 - Parameter constant for cleanup calls",
