      "comment": "Clean up unit slots after game state transition.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if provided unit type matches current game unit type via FUN_6fb62880()\n2. If mismatch, skip entire cleanup process\n3. If match, iterate through all g_dwMaxUnitSlots unit slots:\n   - Check g_abUnitSlotActive[slot] for active flag (0x01)\n   - If active, clear flag to 0x00\n   - Verify unit still valid via FUN_6fb62880() (must return 0)\n   - Call ValidateUnitSlot() to perform slot validation\n   - Set g_abUnitSlotActive[slot + 4] = 0x01 (next slot flag)\n   - Increment slot counter and advance pointer by 0x16 bytes\n4. Check g_dwGameStateInitialized and g_pGameStateObject validity\n5. If valid game state, call InitializeGameUIState()\n6. Clear and reinitialize unit lists via Ordinal calls (10277, 10304, 10305, 10279, 10251)\n7. Clear pending unit via g_dwPendingUnitFlag and g_pPendingUnit\n8. Set game state flags (0xe8 offset = 0x02)\n9. Send state packet (0x30) and clear initialized flag\n10. Cleanup viewport via FUN_6fb796e0() and unit references\n\nParameters:\nnUnitType (ECX): Unit type to match against current game unit type\n\nReturns:\nvoid - performs side effects on game state globals\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If nUnitType != current unit type, entire function is skipped\n- If unit validation fails (FUN_6fb62880() returns 0), triggers error path and fatal exit\n- Game state pointer comparison checks for state corruption during cleanup\n\nNote: Function uses 2 stack-allocated temporaries (local_EAX_212, local_EDI_25) optimized away in decompilation.",
