      "comment": "Processes interaction stop command based on unit type and current interaction state.\n\nCalled by ProcessInteractionStopCommand when SCMD_INTERACTION_STOP is received.\nHandles cleanup of NPC/object interactions, menu dialogs, and game state transitions.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. If byUnitType < 6, look up the unit in hash table by dwUnitId and byUnitType\n2. Switch on byUnitType:\n   - Case 1: Player unit - proceed to interaction state check\n   - Case 2,4,6: Call ProcessUIStatesByResourceBuffer(1,0) then return\n   - Default: Return immediately (no-op for other unit types)\n3. If found unit exists, set unit flag [0xE8] |= 0x2 (mark interaction stopped)\n4. Check g_dwInteractionState:\n   - State 1 (Menu active): Log menu stop, reset UI, clear inventory, reinit arrays,\n     set player flags, send packet 0x30, shutdown game, clear init flag, change UI state\n   - State 3-6 (Dialog states): UI state change 0xC, reset UI, clear inventory,\n     reinit arrays, set player flags, packet 0x30, shutdown, reinit game state,\n     modify word flags, clear unit state, reinit UI interaction, log, close dialogs\n   - State 7 (Message state): Process game message transition, close dialogs\n   - State 0 with text flag: Log text stop, reset UI, clear inventory, check NPC mismatch,\n     clear linked list, handle pending unit, reinit game state, set flags\n5. Clear player word flags (offset 0x70, flag 0x8) and process transition if player valid\n6. Close all dialogs and reset g_dwInteractionState to 0\n\nParameters:\n  byUnitType (CL): Unit type code (1=Player, 2=NPC, 4=Object, 6=Item)\n  dwUnitId (EDX): Unit identifier for hash table lookup\n\nReturns: void\n\nInteraction States (g_dwInteractionState):\n  0 - No interaction (may have text flag set)\n  1 - Menu interaction active\n  3-6 - Dialog/trade interaction states\n  7 - Message/waypoint interaction\n\nUnit Flag Bits (offset 0xE8):\n  0x02 - Interaction stop flag\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - NPC ID mismatch logged if g_pGameStateObject changes during text interaction\n  - Pending unit inventory handled if g_dwPendingUnitFlag set\n  - Different cleanup paths for menu vs dialog vs text interactions",
      "tags": ["PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PARAM_2", "STRUCT_Skill", "NET_SCMD"]
    },
