      "comment": "Initialize game load sequence for character/difficulty selection\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. If difficulty == 6: Write slot data (0x60 bytes) to base address via Ordinal_11113, return\n2. Lookup GameStateConfig by class/difficulty via FUN_6fb60e10\n3. If config not found (NULL):\n   - Get current viewport via FUN_6fb62880\n   - Call viewport handler via FUN_6fb86710\n   - Send LoadComplete packet (0x30) with (difficulty & 0xFF, class)\n   - Validate game object match; if mismatch, log warning\n   - Clear all units from class 1 via ClearGameUnitsAndProcessLinkedList\n   - Clear pending unit flag and pointer\n   - Return (early exit path)\n4. If config found:\n   - Install state checking callback via FUN_6fb63810(CheckGameStateAttribute)\n   - Set game state flag 0x2 (in-game)\n   - Initialize UI panels: set state=2 for panels 0xF, 0x2B, 0x15\n   - Reset internal dialog/panel state variables to 0\n   - If special panel pointer matches LAB_6fb272f0, set sub-state to 3\n   - Send game create packet (0x2F) with difficulty and class\n   - Initialize targeting system\n5. Check if already in-game (g_abGameStateFlags bit 0):\n   - If YES: Set initialized flag, save state, clear flags, return\n   - If NO: Continue to step 6\n6. Get game text/message list via FUN_6fb586b0:\n   - If list invalid/closed: Log error \"hTextList____NULL\" at 0xfc7, abort\n7. Get first valid unit by difficulty via Ordinal_10907(list, 0)\n8. Get game state object pointer via Ordinal_10582(dwGameState)\n9. Check for special game types (0x219, 0x21A, 0x21B, 0x20F):\n   - If NOT special type and has content at offset 0x2FB: Call FUN_6fb63360\n10. Check if multiplayer/PvP via Ordinal_10262:\n    - If multiplayer mode active: Initialize multiplayer game state, return\n11. Multiplayer check failed; process single-player path:\n12. If first unit valid (not 0xFFFF):\n    - Clear targeting\n    - For unit=first down to -1, lookup in table/regenerate as needed\n    - Set selected unit, call targeting init\n    - If game state invalid: Call viewport init, return error\n    - Else: Setup main game viewport, initialize features\n13. If first unit invalid (0xFFFF):\n    - Get quest list state via FUN_6fb586b0\n    - Check if difficulty is 0x20F (special):\n      - If NO: Call state validation FUN_6fb633b0\n    - Check if extended data (offset 0x38) exists:\n      - If YES: Process external data via Ordinal_10153\n    - Get previous unit via Ordinal_10908(list, 0):\n      - If -1: Check special types (offset 0x2FB content)\n        - If special: Load validation data via FUN_6fb26db0\n          - If validation OK: Initialize UI, reset viewport, process state, return\n          - If validation FAIL: Initialize main game state, continue\n      - If valid (>= 0): Load unit's target info, initialize multi-step quest/town load\n\nParameters:\nbyte bGameDifficulty  - Game difficulty (0=Normal, 1=Nightmare, 2=Hell, 6=TownReset)\nuint dwPlayerGameClass - Player class enum (0=Barbarian, 1=Sorceress, 2=Necromancer, 3=Paladin, 4=Druid, 5=Assassin)\nuint dwSlotIndex - Character slot/save file identifier\nuint dwUnknown - Additional parameter (unused/reserved)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value; all state changes via globals (g_dwGameStateInitialized, g_pGameStateObject, etc.)",
      "tags": ["PROP_LARGE", "SRC_npcmenu.cpp", "MOD_UI", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "STRUCT_Skill", "PARAM_4", "PROP_LOOPHEAVY", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "UI_MENU", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
