      "comment": "Check if game state code is an exception/special state that requires different handling.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Compare dwGameState against hardcoded set of exception state codes\n2. If dwGameState matches ANY of the exception codes, return 1 (true)\n3. Otherwise return 0 (false)\n\nException codes checked: 0x92, 0x20f, 0x219, 0x21a, 0x21b, 0x209, 0x10a, 0x17a, 0xfb, 0x179, 0x14b, 0x196, 0x198\n\nParameters:\n  dwGameState (uint) - Game state code to validate\n\nReturns:\n  1 (byte=true) - State code is an exception that requires special handling\n  0 (byte=false) - State code is normal, proceed with standard initialization\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  Uses hardcoded constants for exception detection\n  Called during game load initialization to determine initialization path",
