      "comment": "Initialize dialog option state for a specific slot.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate byte offset from slot index: offset = nSlotIndex * 0x27 (39 bytes per slot)\n2. Set state field to 3 (active/visible state)\n3. Clear displayed flag (word) to 0\n4. Clear clickable flag (dword) to 0\n\nParameters:\nnSlotIndex (int) - Dialog slot index to initialize\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n0x27 (39) is the size of a dialog option state structure. Each slot gets initialized with active state (3).\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x27 (39 decimal) - Size of dialog option state structure per slot\n0x3 (3 decimal) - Active/visible dialog option state value\n0x6fbb64bc - Base address of dialog option state array (g_anDialogOptionStateArray)\n0x6fbb64c6 - Offset to displayed flags array within state region\n0x6fbb64d6 - Offset to clickable flags array within state region",
