      "instructions": ["0x57830|PUSH|ECX", "0x57831|MOV|ECX, dword ptr [0x6fbf8ec7]", "0x57837|PUSH|EBX", "0x57838|XOR|EBX, EBX", "0x5783A|PUSH|ESI", "0x5783B|CMP|ECX, EBX", "0x5783D|JZ|0x6fb27860", "0x5783F|CALL|0x6fb005c0", "0x57844|MOV|EDX, dword ptr [0x6fbf8e75]", "0x5784A|XOR|EAX, EAX", "0x5784C|MOV|AX, [0x6fbf8dc7]", "0x57852|MOV|CL, 0x31", "0x57854|PUSH|EAX", "0x57855|MOV|dword ptr [0x6fbf8ec7], EBX", "0x5785B|CALL|0x6fadd2e0"],
      "comment": "Cleans up game state when closing the Game Load dialog\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. If UI dialog exists, close it and send cancel packet (0x31)\n2. Clear game load dialog active flag, initialize game UI state\n3. Save current unit ID from game state object\n4. If game context valid, clear unit inventory slots\n5. Verify unit ID consistency (log mismatch if detected)\n6. Find player unit in hash table\n7. If player unit found, clear game unit array (16 slots, 16 bytes each)\n8. Get inventory unit at offset 0x84 of player unit\n9. Loop through inventory nodes:\n   - Get next node via GetInventoryNodeNext\n   - Get node field data via GetInventoryNodeField\n   - Remove unit from hash table using unit type and ID\n10. Clear inventory and inventory data for inventory unit\n11. If pending unit flag set, initialize pending unit's inventory state\n12. Clear pending unit flag and pointer\n13. Find player unit again, set flag bit 0x02 at offset 0xE8\n14. Send close interaction packet (0x30) with unit ID\n15. Call ProcessGameShutdown\n16. Clear game state initialized flag\n17. Process UI state change (mode 8, flag 1)\n18. If player unit valid, modify word flags and clear unit state\n\nParameters: None (callback function)\n\nReturns: void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Unit ID mismatch logs warning via QueueLogMessage\n- Inventory loop handles empty inventory (null check)\n- Pending unit only processed if flag is set\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x31 - Cancel interaction packet type\n0x30 - Close interaction packet type\n0x84 - Offset to inventory unit in player structure\n0xE8 - Offset to unit flags in player structure\n0x02 - Flag bit set during cleanup\n0x1C - Offset to word flags pointer\n0x6fbf8ddd - Start of game unit array\n0x6fbf8e7d - End of game unit array (160 bytes, 10 slots x 16 bytes)\n8 - UI state mode for game load/transition",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Inventory", "PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_0"]
    },
