      "api_calls": ["QueueLogMessage", "GetUnitStat", "GetInventoryNodeNext", "GetInventoryNodeField", "ClearInventory", "ClearInventoryData"],
      "instructions": ["0x579B0|PUSH|ECX", "0x579B1|MOV|ECX, dword ptr [0x6fbf8ec7]", "0x579B7|PUSH|EBX", "0x579B8|XOR|EBX, EBX", "0x579BA|PUSH|ESI", "0x579BB|CMP|ECX, EBX", "0x579BD|JZ|0x6fb279e0", "0x579BF|CALL|0x6fb005c0", "0x579C4|MOV|EDX, dword ptr [0x6fbf8e75]", "0x579CA|XOR|EAX, EAX", "0x579CC|MOV|AX, [0x6fbf8dc7]", "0x579D2|MOV|CL, 0x31", "0x579D4|PUSH|EAX", "0x579D5|MOV|dword ptr [0x6fbf8ec7], EBX", "0x579DB|CALL|0x6fadd2e0"],
      "comment": "Cleanup callback for Game Load Dialog - handles dialog closure and game state reset\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. If UI dialog exists, close it and send cancel packet (0x31) to server\n2. Clear game load dialog active flag (g_bGameLoadDialogActive = 0)\n3. Initialize game UI state via InitializeGameUIState()\n4. Save current unit ID for consistency verification\n5. If game context valid, clear unit inventory slots\n6. Verify unit ID unchanged (log warning if mismatch detected)\n7. Find player unit in hash table by saved unit ID\n8. If player found, clear game unit array (10 slots x 16 bytes from 0x6fbf8ddd to 0x6fbf8e7d)\n9. Get inventory unit at player offset 0x84 (pUnit[0x21])\n10. Loop through inventory nodes:\n    - Get next node via GetInventoryNodeNext\n    - Get field data via GetInventoryNodeField\n    - Remove unit from hash table using type (offset 0x8) and ID (offset 0x0)\n11. Clear inventory and inventory data for NPC\n12. If pending unit flag set, initialize pending unit inventory state\n13. Clear pending unit flag and pointer\n14. Find player unit again, set flag bit 0x02 at offset 0xE8\n15. Send close interaction packet (0x30) with unit ID\n16. Call ProcessGameShutdown to terminate game session\n17. Clear game state initialized flag\n18. Process UI state change (mode 8, reset)\n19. If player valid, modify word flags and clear unit state\n\nParameters: None (dialog callback)\n\nReturns: void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Unit ID mismatch: logs warning via QueueLogMessage but continues\n- Empty inventory: loop exits immediately on null node\n- Pending unit: only processed if g_dwPendingUnitFlag != 0\n- Player not found: skips inventory cleanup and flag setting\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x31 - Cancel interaction packet type\n0x30 - Close interaction packet type  \n0x84 - Offset to inventory unit in UnitAny (piVar1[0x21] = offset/4)\n0xE8 - Offset to state flags in UnitAny (pUnit[0x3a] = offset/4)\n0x02 - State flag bit set during cleanup\n0x1C - Offset to word flags pointer (pUnit[0x1c] = offset/4)\n0x6fbf8ddd - Start of g_adwGameUnitArray\n0x6fbf8e7d - End of game unit array (160 bytes total)\n8 - UI state mode for game load/transition",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Inventory", "PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_0"]
