      "api_calls": ["GetTotalStatValue", "QueueLogMessage", "IsNpcTradeFlagSet", "IsNpcTradeFlagSet", "GetTotalStatValue", "QueueLogMessage", "GetUnitStat", "GetInventoryNodeNext", "GetInventoryNodeField", "ClearInventory", "...+1 more"],
      "instructions": ["0x57CB0|SUB|ESP, 0x8", "0x57CB3|PUSH|EBX", "0x57CB4|PUSH|EBP", "0x57CB5|PUSH|ESI", "0x57CB6|PUSH|EDI", "0x57CB7|MOV|ESI, EDX", "0x57CB9|MOV|EDI, ECX", "0x57CBB|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x14], ESI", "0x57CBF|CALL|0x6fadb810", "0x57CC4|XOR|EBX, EBX", "0x57CC6|CMP|EDI, EBX", "0x57CC8|JNZ|0x6fb27cf8", "0x57CCA|MOV|dword ptr [0x6fbf8dbb], EBX", "0x57CD0|CALL|0x6fb15c00", "0x57CD5|MOV|ECX, dword ptr [0x6fbf8e75]"],
      "comment": "Initializes the game client state and game unit context in Diablo II\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call InitializeTargetingSystem to set up targeting data\n2. If pGameUnit is NULL, reset game state flags and UI, then return early\n3. Set up initial slot reservation and game state flags\n4. Call FUN_6fb62880 to get current frame data\n5. Set viewport reserved data via Ordinal_10519\n6. Initialize frame data via FUN_6fb5d910\n7. Branch on nInitMode:\n   - Mode 0: Check if current unit matches existing game unit, reset if mismatch\n   - Mode 1: Verify pGameUnit matches current game unit context\n8. Set global game state and unit references from pGameUnit array\n9. Clear unit state flag 0x02 (0xfffffffd mask)\n10. Iterate through slot handler array (g_dwSlotHandlerArray):\n    - For each slot matching current unit state, call Ordinal_11107\n    - Invoke slot handler callback [offset +8] if condition is met\n11. Clear pending unit if flag is set\n12. Dispatch on unit game mode value (0xfc, 0x96, 0xc6, 0x16f, 0x203)\n13. Call FUN_6fb280d0 with computed dialog index and difficulty flag\n14. Call FUN_6fb5d370(8,0,0) to check panel state\n15. If panel closed (return 0):\n    - Reset game state and send 0x30 packet\n    - Iterate through game unit links via Ordinal_10277/10304/10305\n    - Clear unit array memory and destroy unit links\n16. If panel open:\n    - Initialize inventory dialog\n    - Find matching unit in g_aUnitSlotArray\n    - If found, adjust dialog state flags\n    - Call FUN_6fb7dcc0 to get next UI element\n    - Create pending unit via FUN_6fb8d210\n    - If flag=2, log event 0x4d and set pending unit flag\n\nParameters:\npGameUnit: Pointer to game unit structure (contains mode at offset 4, data at offset 8)\nnInitMode: Initialization mode (0=check mode, non-zero=strict mode with verification)\n\nReturns: void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If pGameUnit is NULL, function returns immediately after UI reset\n- Slot handler iteration depends on g_dwSlotHandlerCount > 0\n- Game mode dispatch includes handlers for modes 0xfc, 0x96, 0xc6, 0x16f, 0x203\n- Difficulty flag (0xffff check) affects dialog initialization\n- Panel state affects downstream unit link processing\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x02: Unit state flag to clear (UI visibility flag)\n0xfffffffd: Mask to clear flag 0x02\n0xe: Initial UI reservation value\n0xd45: Character dialog resource ID\n0xfc, 0x96, 0xc6, 0x16f, 0x203: Game mode constants\n0x30: Packet type for game state change\n0x4d: Event log code for unit state change",
      "tags": ["PROP_LARGE", "SRC_npcmenu.cpp", "MOD_UI", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PARAM_2", "STRUCT_Skill", "PROP_LOOPHEAVY", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
