      "instructions": ["0x580D0|PUSH|EBX", "0x580D1|PUSH|ESI", "0x580D2|PUSH|EDI", "0x580D3|MOV|EDI, EDX", "0x580D5|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0x580D7|CALL|0x6fb99a9e", "0x580DC|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0x580DE|JZ|0x6fb28268", "0x580E4|CALL|0x6fadb920", "0x580E9|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0x580EB|JZ|0x6fb28268", "0x580F1|TEST|EDI, EDI", "0x580F3|JZ|0x6fb281f3", "0x580F9|LEA|EAX, [ESI + ESI*0x4]", "0x580FC|XOR|EDX, EDX"],
      "comment": "Adds or removes dialog options from a dialog option list.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call Ordinal_10227 to verify system initialization state\n2. Call GetGlobalSystemState to verify system is operational\n3. Return 0 if either check fails (system not initialized)\n4. If nAppendMode == 1 (add option):\n   a. Calculate dialog offset as (nDialogIndex * 39 * 8 - nDialogIndex)\n   b. Get option count for this dialog from g_abDialogOptionState\n   c. Search dialog option array for InitializeCharacterInventoryDialog handler\n   d. If handler found, shift all entries after it right by 1 position\n   e. Copy values using memmove-like pattern for both pointers and indexes\n   f. Increment option count in g_abDialogOptionState\n   g. Store marker pointer 0x6fb272f0 at found position\n   h. Store marker value 0x1507 at found position\n   i. Return 1 on success\n5. If nAppendMode == 0 (remove option):\n   a. Calculate dialog offset as (nDialogIndex * 39 * 8 - nDialogIndex)\n   b. Get option count from g_abDialogOptionState\n   c. Search dialog option array for 0x6fb272f0 marker\n   d. If marker found, shift entries left to close gap (remove slot)\n   e. Decrement option count in g_abDialogOptionState\n   f. Return 1 on success\n\nParameters:\n  nDialogIndex: Dialog index (passed in ECX); used to calculate offset into dialog arrays\n  nAppendMode: Operation mode; 1 to add option, 0 to remove option (passed in EDX)\n\nReturns:\n  1: Dialog option successfully added or removed\n  0: Operation failed due to system not initialized\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Returns 0 immediately if Ordinal_10227 or GetGlobalSystemState returns 0\n  - Uses 0x6fb272f0 as marker for empty/removed dialog option slots\n  - Uses 0x1507 as constant identifier value for dialog options\n  - Array operations use direct pointer arithmetic rather than memcpy\n  - Dialog offset is calculated as: (nDialogIndex * 39) * 8 - nDialogIndex = scaled index\n\nStructure Layout:\n  Offset   | Size | Field Name              | Type     | Description\n  ---------|------|-------------------------|----------|--------------------------------------------\n  +0x00    | 4    | g_abDialogOptionState   | dword    | Count of options in current dialog\n  +0x04    | 4    | PTR_LAB_6fbb64ca        | dword*   | Pointer array to option handlers\n  +0x08    | 4    | PTR_LAB_6fbb64ce        | dword*   | Alternate option data array\n  +0x0c    | 2    | g_anDialogSlotIndexArray| word     | Dialog option index values",
      "tags": ["PARAM_2", "PROP_LOOPHEAVY"]
