      "instructions": ["0x583E0|MOV|EAX, [0x6fbf8dbb]", "0x583E5|PUSH|EBX", "0x583E6|XOR|EBX, EBX", "0x583E8|PUSH|ESI", "0x583E9|CMP|EAX, 0x1", "0x583EC|PUSH|EDI", "0x583ED|JNZ|0x6fb2847b", "0x583F3|MOV|byte ptr [0x6fbf8db9], BL", "0x583F9|MOV|dword ptr [0x6fbf8dbb], EBX", "0x583FF|CALL|0x6fb15c00", "0x58404|MOV|EDI, dword ptr [0x6fbf8e75]", "0x5840A|CALL|0x6fb62880", "0x5840F|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0x58411|JZ|0x6fb2841f", "0x58413|CALL|0x6fb62880"],
      "comment": "Handle game state transitions (load, join, reset, exit sequences).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check ram0x6fbf8dbb for state code (1=load, 2-6=join, 7=reset/exit)\n2. If state==1: Clear flags, reset UI/units, initialize player data, mark player flag 0x2\n3. If state in 2-6: Warn (0xc alert), then same init sequence with extra cleanup\n4. If state==7: Quick exit sequence (call FUN_6fb5ec60)\n5. Otherwise: Validate game state consistency, reset pending unit data, reinit player\n6. All paths: Send 0x30 packet, trigger UI refresh, close dialogs, reset state\n\nParameters:\n(none) - uses global ram0x6fbf8dbb (game state code), g_pGameStateObject\n\nReturns:\nvoid - modifies global game state, initializes arrays, sends network packets\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- State validation at offset 0x6fbf8db9 (flag), ram0x6fbf8dbb (code)\n- Player data accessed at offset 0xe8 (flag), 0x70 (subfield ptr), 0x1c (related data)\n- State code change detected and logged via Ordinal_10029\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x1: Initial load state\n- 0x2-0x6: Join/transition states (0xc=warn code, 0x8=refresh code)\n- 0x7: Exit/reset state\n- 0x30: Packet type for player init\n- 0xe8: Player flag offset (OR 0x2)\n- 0x70: Subdata ptr offset in player object\n- 0x1c: Related offset in subdata\n- Ordinal_10029: GetLevel/logging (D2Common ordinal)",
      "tags": ["PROP_LARGE", "PARAM_0"]
    },
