      "comment": "Sends player/unit data packet to game server for inventory or trading operations\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if initialization attempted (g_byInitAttemptCounter)\n2. Determine packet type based on game state (0x32, 0x33, or 0x35)\n3. If init mode is 0, validate object type; else set object type to 6\n4. Retrieve player unit data using GetGameState and FUN_6fb60e10\n5. For packet type 0x32: shift flags left 16 bits, OR with 0x2 if game state active\n6. Check fields 0x16 and 0x4c; if non-zero and dwFlags has 0x4, OR result with 0x80000000\n7. Compress and send packet with CompressPackedData\n8. For packet types 0x33/0x35: similar flag processing with different conditions\n9. If dialog not created: calculate viewport coordinates and create dialog with InitializeDialogStructure\n10. Add dialog lines and configure UI state\n\nParameters:\nnInitMode (ECX): 0 = validate object type, non-zero = set object type\ndwFlags (EDX): 0x4 bit indicates special flag handling\n\nReturns:\nvoid; updates global g_fServerConnecting with dialog reference\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Early returns on initialization failure (g_byInitAttemptCounter == 0)\n- Invalid game state sets g_dwUnknownState to 3 and returns\n- Null player unit triggers error logging and counter increment\n- Dialog creation includes viewport boundary checks with 0x14 minimum\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x1073 - error line number\n0x32 - packet type for mode 1\n0x33 - packet type for mode 2\n0x35 - packet type for mode 3\n0xf - initial field value\n0x16, 0x4c - field offsets for flag checking\n0x80000000 - high-bit flag\n0x2 - state-active flag\n0x10 - bit shift count\n0x14 - viewport minimum bound\n0xea60 (60000) - timeout milliseconds\n0xd19 - dialog line count\n\nStructure Layout (tagRECT):\nOffset | Size | Field Name | Type | Description\n0x00   | 4    | left       | int  | Left coordinate\n0x04   | 4    | top        | int  | Top coordinate\n0x08   | 4    | right      | int  | Right coordinate\n0x0c   | 4    | bottom     | int  | Bottom coordinate\n\nRelated Functions:\n- ProcessUnitInteraction() - Calls this function on unit click\n- GetGameState() - Returns current game state for packet mode selection\n- CompressPackedData() - Encodes and sends the actual packet\n- InitializeDialogStructure() - Creates server connection dialog UI",
