      "comment": "Validates network initialization prerequisites and establishes server connection timeout.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if game status flags set, network validation flag active, and parameter matches validation key\n2. Get current tick count and calculate elapsed time since last initialization attempt\n3. If elapsed time < 1000ms: calculate timeout = tickCount + (attemptCount*5 + 150)*100 (capped at 10 attempts)\n4. If elapsed time >= 1000ms: calculate timeout = tickCount + 100\n5. Clear game status flags\n6. If init attempt counter is 0, log debug message via Ordinal_10029 (D2Common.ErrorLog)\n7. Reset init attempt counter and network state flag to 0\n8. Reset interaction data to 0\n9. Query current server port:\n   - If port is 0 (not connected): close server dialog, reset connection flag, set status=3, reinitialize object types and viewport, clear selection\n   - If port != 0: exit normally\n\nParameters:\n- dwValidationParameter: Validation token to match against g_dwValidationParameter (ECX register in __fastcall)\n\nReturns:\nvoid (no return value)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Only executes if all three conditions met: game status set, net validation enabled, parameter valid\n- Port 0 indicates disconnected state, triggers full reinitialization chain\n- Attempt counter capped at 10 to prevent timeout scaling beyond 10 attempts\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x3e8 = 1000 decimal, timeout calculation threshold in milliseconds\n- 0x96 = 150 decimal, base timeout offset constant\n- 0x5 = 5 decimal, multiplier for per-attempt timeout increment\n- 0x64 = 100 decimal, millisecond timeout when elapsed >= 1000ms\n- 0xa = 10 decimal, maximum initialization attempts cap\n- 0x1200 = 4608 decimal, log buffer size for debug message\n\nNote: Function uses 3 SSA temporaries optimized away (DVar1, dVar2, uVar3).",
