      "comment": "Validate network connection and initialize server connection state.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check validation flags: game status active, network validation enabled, parameter matches expected\n2. Get current tick count (GetTickCount)\n3. Calculate elapsed time since last initialization\n4. If elapsed time < 1000ms: calculate timeout as 100ms + (attempts * 500 + 150) * 100ms (capped at 10 attempts)\n   Otherwise: set timeout to current ticks + 100ms\n5. Clear game status flags\n6. If init attempt counter = 0: call Ordinal_10029 (D2Common.GetLevel) with string parameters for logging\n7. Reset init attempt counter and network state flag\n8. Get server port (0x6fadb8c0)\n9. If server port = 0 (disconnected):\n   a. If server connecting flag set: close dialog and clear flag\n   b. Set init state to 3\n   c. Call InitializeObjectTypeArray, ProcessObjectTypeAndValidateViewport, ClearUnitSelectionState\n\nParameters:\nnValidationParameter (int) - IMPLICIT ECX - Expected validation token to match stored parameter\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Function checks g_byNetValidationFlag for 0x01 (validation enabled)\n- Timeout calculation scales with initialization attempt count (min 5 attempts, max 10)\n- Server port check (0 = disconnected) triggers reconnection cleanup\n\nRelated Functions:\n- ProcessObjectTypeAndValidateViewport() - Viewport validation\n- InitializeObjectTypeArray() - Object array setup\n- ClearUnitSelectionState() - Selection cleanup\n- GetCurrentServerPort() - Port query (0x6fadb8c0)",
