      "comment": "Validate game state initialization status and initialize viewport if conditions met.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Verify game status is active (g_dwGameStatusFlags != 0)\n2. Verify no network validation in progress (g_byNetValidationFlag == 0)\n3. Verify validation parameter matches expected value (nValidationParameter == g_dwValidationParameter)\n4. Get current system time via GetTickCount()\n5. Check if elapsed time since last init < 1000ms (0x3e9):\n   - If yes: Calculate timeout as (attempt_count * 5 + 150) * 100 milliseconds (cap attempt count at 10)\n   - If no: Calculate timeout as 100 milliseconds\n6. Clear game status flag and network state flag\n7. Log initialization attempt via Ordinal_10029 (D2Common.LogEvent) if first attempt (g_byInitAttemptCounter == 0)\n8. Reset all state flags and counters\n9. Get current server port via GetCurrentServerPort()\n10. If server port is 0 (not connected):\n    - Close dialog if server connecting flag is set\n    - Reset server connecting flag\n    - Set state to error code 3\n    - Initialize object type arrays\n    - Validate and process viewport\n    - Clear unit selection state\n\nParameters:\n- nValidationParameter (int, implicit ECX): Validation code to match against expected value\n\nReturns:\n- void (no return value)\n\nOrdinal Calls:\n- Ordinal_10029: D2Common.LogEvent - Log initialization debug message with file/line location\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Function validates initialization only when multiple flags are set (prevents double initialization)\n- Timeout calculation uses exponential backoff based on attempt count\n- Network initialization can only proceed when server port is established\n- Initial attempt logs via Ordinal_10029 system call\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x3e9 = 1001 milliseconds (elapsed time threshold)\n- 0x96 = 150 decimal (timeout base offset)\n- 0x1200 = 4608 decimal (Ordinal_10029 parameter)\n- 0x3 = 3 (error state code)\n- 100 = timeout milliseconds (fast path)",
