      "comment": "Validates game initialization state and configures server connection timeout.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if game status flags set, network validation flag clear, and param matches stored validation param\n2. Get current tick count via GetTickCount()\n3. If time since last initialization < 1001ms (0x3e9), calculate timeout with retry backoff:\n   - Clamp attempt count to max 10 (0xa)\n   - Calculate multiplier: (attemptCount * 5 + 150) * 100ms\n   - Add to current tick count\n4. Else set timeout to current tick + 100ms\n5. Clear game status flags (0x6fbf8ee2)\n6. Log initialization diagnostic if attempt counter clear: call Ordinal_10029 with diagnostic strings\n7. Clear attempt counter (0x6fbf8d50)\n8. Clear network state flag (0x6fbf8d51)\n9. Clear interaction data (0x6fbf8d55)\n10. Get current server port via GetCurrentServerPort()\n11. If server port is 0:\n    - Close dialog if connecting flag set\n    - Initialize object type array\n    - Process object types and validate viewport\n    - Clear unit selection state\n\nParameters:\nnValidationValue (int, ECX): Validation token compared against stored validation parameter\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nRelated Ordinals:\nOrdinal_10029 (GetLevel) - Used for initialization diagnostic logging; unknown usage pattern\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x3e9 = 1001ms, initialization timeout threshold\n0x96 = 150 decimal, base retry multiplier constant\n0x5 = 5, attempt count multiplier\n0x3 = 3, game state code for initialization\n0x1200 = 4608 decimal, diagnostic buffer size\n0xa = 10, maximum attempt count clamp",
