      "comment": "Initialize game state and validate server connection with retry timeout logic.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate conditions: game status active, network validation flag clear, token matches stored parameter\n2. Get current tick count for timeout calculation\n3. If time since last initialization < 1001ms: calculate timeout with exponential backoff based on attempt count (5-10 attempts capped)\n4. Otherwise: set timeout to current time + 100ms\n5. Clear game status flags and increment attempt counter\n6. Call logging/debug function if attempt counter was 0 (Ordinal_10029 = debug logging)\n7. Reset attempt counter, network state flag, interaction data\n8. Check current server port: if 0 (disconnected):\n   - Close dialog if server was connecting\n   - Clear server connection flag\n   - Reinitialize object type arrays\n   - Process object types and validate viewport rendering\n   - Clear unit selection state\n\nParameters:\nnValidationToken (ECX) - int - Game validation token, must match g_dwValidationParameter\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Skips execution if game not active or network validation in progress\n- Exponential backoff: attempt count capped at 10, timeout = current_time + (count*5 + 150)*100ms\n- Server disconnection triggers full UI and data reinitialization",
