      "comment": "Validates game state and resource handle, clears UI selection on match\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Retrieve validated resource handle via GetValidatedResourceHandle()\n2. Verify handle is valid (not NULL) and game state is initialized (g_dwGameStateInitialized != 0)\n3. Retrieve game state object via FUN_6fb60e10(g_pGameStateObject, 1)\n4. If state object valid, check resource type matches 0x4 (first field)\n5. If resource ID matches (third field == nResourceId parameter), clear selection and reinitialize UI\n\nParameters:\nnResourceId (int) - Resource ID to match against resource handle at offset +0x8\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value, modifies game state via side effects\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Returns silently if any validation check fails (handle NULL, state not initialized, state object NULL, type/ID mismatch)\n- Magic number 0x4: Resource type identifier at resource handle +0x0\n- Resource ID stored at resource handle +0x8\n\nRelated Functions:\n- GetValidatedResourceHandle() - Obtains resource handle\n- FUN_6fb60e10() - Retrieves game state object\n- ClearUnitSelectionState() - Deselects current unit\n- InitializeGameUIState() - Reinitializes UI state",
