      "instructions": ["0x59470|MOV|ECX, dword ptr [0x6fbf8eb7]", "0x59476|TEST|ECX, ECX", "0x59478|JZ|0x6fb29489", "0x5947A|CALL|0x6fb005c0", "0x5947F|MOV|dword ptr [0x6fbf8eb7], 0x0", "0x59489|MOV|AL, [0x6fbf8ed5]", "0x5948E|PUSH|ESI", "0x5948F|CMP|AL, 0x5", "0x59491|JZ|0x6fb295a1", "0x59497|CMP|AL, 0x6", "0x59499|JZ|0x6fb295a6", "0x5949F|CMP|AL, 0x3", "0x594A1|JZ|0x6fb295a6", "0x594A7|XOR|ECX, ECX", "0x594A9|MOV|CL, AL"],
      "comment": "Initializes the Character Selection dialog based on network validation state.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if server connection flag (g_fServerConnecting) is set, if so close dialog and clear flag\n2. Process network validation flag (g_byNetValidationFlag):\n   - If 0x05: Open hireling dialog and return\n   - If 0x06 or 0x03: Skip to character selection initialization\n   - For other values (0x07-0x10): Set dialog text resource ID based on flag value\n3. If character selection dialog exists, call Ordinal_10023 with error message resources and exit\n4. Initialize dialog structure with default parameters:\n   - Retrieve dialog dimensions via FUN_6fb8f690/FUN_6fb8f680\n   - Create dialog with width and height\n   - Add first dialog line with state 0x15 (21)\n   - Call Ordinal_10004 before adding line\n   - Add second dialog line with state 0x0f (15) and code pointer\n5. If game state initialized and level is valid (0xf4-0xf6 or 0x109 or 0x208):\n   - Set 5 dialog visibility flags to 0x2 (enabled)\n6. Initialize inventory dialog frame and return\n\nParameters:\n  None\n\nReturns:\n  void (None)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x05, 0x06, 0x03 - Network validation flag values for state machine\n  0x136d - Dialog line type constant\n  0x15, 0x0f - Dialog state codes\n  0xc - Dialog mode flag (0xc = 12)\n  0x109, 0x208, 0xf4, 0xf6 - Level/state ID values for dialog configuration\n  0x2 - Dialog visibility flag value (enabled/visible)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If g_pCharacterSelectionDialog already exists, calls non-returning function FUN_6fb9a10f(0xffffffff)\n  - Function uses multiple undocumented Ordinal calls (Storm/Fog DLL functions)\n  - 5 global dialog visibility flags set atomically on valid level state",
