      "comment": "Build tooltip text for an item based on its type and game state. Returns success/failure status with formatted tooltip text.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate item is not NULL and not already fully processed (type != 4)\n2. If mode is 0 (normal tooltip):\n   - Determine game state flags and get slot data\n   - Call Ordinal_10775 to build base tooltip ID\n3. If mode is non-zero (detailed tooltip):\n   - Check game state is initialized\n   - Get item type and validate against multiple type ranges\n   - For monster/special items (type 0xff-0x109, 0x1ff, etc.):\n     - If not monster, check item is valid and set result flags\n     - Otherwise check item properties and call Ordinal_10775\n   - For equipment items (type 0xf4-0xf5, 0x109):\n     - Check item properties and return success\n   - For other types (0xfc, 0x93-0xca):\n     - Call Ordinal_10775 with appropriate flags\n4. Append tooltip text to buffer with localization string\n5. Return success (1) or failure (0)\n\nParameters:\n  pItem (ECX, int) - Pointer to item structure  \n  nMode (EDX, int) - Tooltip mode (0=normal, non-0=detailed)\n  pnTooltipId (Stack[0x4], int*) - Output tooltip ID value\n  pwBuffer (Stack[0x8], short*) - Unicode output buffer for tooltip text\n  nBufferSize (Stack[0xc], int) - Maximum buffer size in bytes\n\nReturns:\n  1 - Success, tooltip text appended to buffer\n  0 - Failure, item invalid or buffer too small\n\nNote: Function uses SSA temporaries optimized away by compiler (psVar2, pdVar1, bVar4, etc).\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x4 - Item type field offset\n  0xc - Slot data mask value for Ordinal_10519\n  0x10,0x13d7,0x932 - Ordinal_10707 validation type codes\n  0xfc,0xfd,0xfe,0xff,0x101,0x109 - Item type ranges\n  0x1ff,0x195,0x200-0x202 - Special item type cases\n  0x46,0x48 - Field offsets for property checks\n  0xa - Buffer size adjustment for localization string",
