      "comment": "HandleUIStateTransitionForDialog - Callback handler for UI state transitions\n\nHandles UI state transitions based on g_dwUnknownState and g_dwUIState globals.\nUsed as a callback from InitializeItemDisplayDialog (referenced as function pointer).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if g_dwUnknownState == 5 (graphic action verification state)\n2. If state 5:\n   a. Close loading progress dialog if open (set g_pLoadingProgressDialog = 0)\n   b. Call InitializeDialogWithCoordinates to show new dialog\n3. Else check if g_dwUIState == 4 (loading/transaction state)\n4. If state 4:\n   a. Close loading progress dialog if open\n   b. Call SendPlayerDataPacket(0, 0) to send empty data\n   c. Return immediately\n5. Otherwise call ClearUnitSelectionState to clear selections\n6. Re-check g_dwUIState == 4 after clearing (race condition guard)\n7. If state became 4, assert failure and exit application\n\nParameters:\n  None (callback with no parameters)\n\nReturns:\n  EAX = 1 on success (implicit, set before RET)\n  Does not return if assertion fails (ExitApplicationWithCode)\n\nState Values:\n  g_dwUnknownState = 5: UIStateGraphicVerifyingAction\n  g_dwUIState = 4: Loading/Transaction state\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Assertion failure exits application with code -1 (0xFFFFFFFF)\n  - Assert message: \"sgUIState.CurrentState != UIStateGraphicVerifyingAction\"\n  - Source file: C:\\Projects\\Diablo2\\Source\\D2Client\\..., line 0x1458 (5208)\n\nCallees:\n  CloseDialogAndCleanup - Closes current dialog\n  InitializeDialogWithCoordinates - Opens dialog at specified coordinates\n  SendPlayerDataPacket - Sends player data to server\n  ClearUnitSelectionState - Clears unit selection state\n  FogAssert - Assertion handler\n  ExitApplicationWithCode - Terminates application",
      "tags": ["SRC_npcmenu.cpp", "MOD_UI", "PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_0"]
