      "comment": "Transitions from loading dialog to appropriate inventory dialog based on interaction state.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Close current dialog via CloseDialogAndCleanup()\n2. Clear loading progress dialog pointer (g_pLoadingProgressDialog = 0)\n3. Check dialog interaction state (g_dwDialogInteractionState)\n4. If state == 5 (buy/sell verification mode):\n   - Call InitializeCharacterInventoryDialog to show character stats\n   - Return 1\n5. Else (normal inventory mode):\n   - Call InitializeInventoryObjects to initialize inventory data\n   - Set UI state to 3 (g_dwUIState = 3, inventory active)\n   - Call ClearUnitSelectionState to reset selection flags\n   - Return 1\n\nParameters:\n  None - operates on global dialog state\n\nReturns:\n  1 (EAX) - Always returns success\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - State 5 triggers character inventory dialog (buy/sell verification screen)\n  - All other states trigger standard inventory objects initialization\n  - Function is stored in function pointer table and called from InitializeItemDisplayDialog\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  5 - Buy/sell verification dialog state (triggers InitializeCharacterInventoryDialog)\n  3 - UI state for active inventory mode\n  0 - Null pointer for cleared dialog\n\nCross-References:\n  - Called from InitializeItemDisplayDialog via function pointer at 0x6fb29c10 and 0x6fb29e9e",
