      "comment": "Initialize game objects for the current game state.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get current viewport scroll state (FUN_6fb62880)\n2. Update viewport display if scroll state changed (FUN_6fb86710)\n3. Validate game state matches expected object\n4. Get game state object pointer via FUN_6fb60e10\n5. Clear all unit array entries ([0x6fbf8ddd] to [0x6fbf8e7d])\n6. Iterate through linked list at offset 0x84 via Ordinal_10277/10304/10305\n   - For each list node, extract data pointers and call FUN_6fb60ff0\n7. Clean up list iteration (Ordinal_10279, Ordinal_10251)\n8. Check pending unit flag (g_dwPendingUnitFlag)\n9. If pending unit exists, finalize it (FUN_6fb8d060)\n10. Clear pending unit flag and pointer\n11. Set unit state flag 0x02 at offset 0xe8 of game state object\n12. Send packet 0x30 to server (SendPacketData)\n13. Reset game state initialized flag (g_dwGameStateInitialized = 0)\n14. Trigger UI/dialog update (FUN_6fb5d370)\n15. Update viewport viewport coordinates (FUN_6fb796e0)\n16. Finalize unit display (FUN_6fb86790)\n\nParameters:\n  dwGameState (ECX): Game state identifier passed to lookup functions\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If game state mismatch, logs error string 's_mismatch_npc_ids'\n  - If FUN_6fb60e10 returns NULL, skips unit array initialization\n  - If pending unit flag set, calls cleanup before resetting\n  \nRelated Functions:\n  - InitializeGameClient() - calls this function at game init\n  - InitializeGameLoad() - alternate initialization path\n  - InitializeGameUIAndProcessDialogStates() - UI initialization flow",
