      "instructions": ["0x5A170|MOV|EAX, 0x6fbf8ddd", "0x5A175|MOV|dword ptr [EAX], 0x0", "0x5A17B|ADD|EAX, 0x10", "0x5A17E|CMP|EAX, 0x6fbf8e7d", "0x5A183|JL|0x6fb2a175", "0x5A185|RET|"],
      "comment": "Initialize game unit array by zeroing all unit slots.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Set pdwSlotPointer to base of g_adwGameUnitArray (0x6fbf8ddd)\n2. Write zero dword to current slot pointer\n3. Increment pointer by 16 bytes (one unit slot size)\n4. Repeat until reaching array end (0x6fbf8e7d)\n5. Return\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Array spans 0x6fbf8ddd to 0x6fbf8e7d (160 bytes total = 10 unit slots @ 16 bytes each)\n- Each unit slot initialized to zero\n- No error handling\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset | Size | Field Name | Type | Description\n0x00   | 0xa0 | g_adwGameUnitArray | uint[40] | Game unit array (10 slots × 16 bytes)",
