      "comment": "Initialize game state, dialogs, paths, and UI resources for a new game session.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Set game difficulty flag to 0xFFFF (invalid/unset)\n2. Shutdown existing game session and dialogs\n3. Clear loading dialog state (initialized, displayed flags, timeout)\n4. Clear global game state flags (dword)\n5. Zero 0x57 dwords (87 dwords = 348 bytes) starting at g_abGameStateFlags\n6. Allocate slot data base via Ordinal_11111 - OS memory allocation (malloc/HeapAlloc)\n7. Allocate validation magic via Ordinal_11111 - OS memory allocation (malloc/HeapAlloc)\n8. Clear validation magic storage (ram0x6fbf8dbb = 0)\n9. Build UI buysell panel path and store pointer\n10. Build UI gold button path and store pointer\n11. Clear initialization counter and attempt tracking\n12. Clear last init time stamps\n13. Clear game state flags byte at offset 2\n14. Initialize dialog state flags for all unit slots (0x16 bytes per slot)\n\nParameters:\n  None\n\nReturns:\n  void (no return value)\n\nOrdinals:\n  Ordinal_11111 - OS memory allocation function (appears to be malloc or HeapAlloc variant)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Ordinal_11111 called twice for slot data and validation magic allocation\n  - Loop at offset 0x285 processes g_dwMaxUnitSlots slots, clearing 2 consecutive bytes per slot\n  - If g_dwMaxUnitSlots <= 0, dialog initialization loop skipped\n  - Uses REP STOSD for bulk zeroing (more efficient than individual writes)\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0xFFFF - Difficulty unset sentinel value\n  0x57 - 87 dwords to zero in game state\n  0x16 - Offset/stride for dialog state per slot\n  0x104 - Local stack buffer size (260 bytes)",
