      "instructions": ["0x5A3F0|PUSH|ECX", "0x5A3F1|MOV|EAX, [0x6fbf8e75]", "0x5A3F6|PUSH|EBP", "0x5A3F7|PUSH|ESI", "0x5A3F8|PUSH|EDI", "0x5A3F9|MOV|EDI, ECX", "0x5A3FB|CMP|EDI, EAX", "0x5A3FD|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0xc], EDI", "0x5A401|JZ|0x6fb2a41a", "0x5A403|PUSH|0x6fbb6c70", "0x5A408|PUSH|0x15ce", "0x5A40D|PUSH|0x6fbb6fd4", "0x5A412|CALL|0x6fb99a80", "0x5A417|ADD|ESP, 0xc", "0x5A41A|CALL|0x6fb62880"],
      "comment": "Cleanup and reset game state after unit processing complete\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate game state object ID matches expected value (assert check)\n2. Call unit list flush function, handle any returned state value\n3. Clear any NPC ID mismatches\n4. Fetch game unit by ID; if valid:\n   a. Zero-initialize global unit array (g_adwGameUnitArray)\n   b. Iterate NPC list from unit[0x21] offset\n   c. For each NPC node, retrieve next pointer and unit reference\n   d. Call function to register unit-associated resource IDs\n5. Clear pending unit flag and pending unit pointer if set\n6. Add flag 0x02 to unit[0x3a] (unknown state flag)\n7. Send game state packet (type 0x30) to remote party\n8. Flush any pending game state updates\n9. Clear game state initialized flag\n10. Process pending resource cleanup\n11. Apply final flags and deallocate old unit reference\n\nParameters:\nnUnitId (dword, implicit ECX): Game state object/unit ID to process\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value; function performs side effects\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Phantom variable: local_4 (optimized away by compiler)\n- Function uses implicit register parameter (ECX contains nUnitId)\n- Multiple validation checks for game state consistency\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x21 - Offset to NPC list head in unit structure\n0x3a - Offset to unit state flags in unit structure\n0x1c - Offset to active skills/abilities in unit structure\n0x02 - Flag value set in unit[0x3a]\n0x30 - Packet type for game state update\n8    - Game state cleanup event type\n0x6fbf8e7d - Upper boundary address for unit array clearing loop",
