      "api_calls": [],
      "instructions": ["0x5A5F0|PUSH|EBX", "0x5A5F1|PUSH|EBP", "0x5A5F2|PUSH|ESI", "0x5A5F3|MOV|ESI, dword ptr [0x6fbb64b4]", "0x5A5F9|PUSH|EDI", "0x5A5FA|LEA|EDX, [ECX + 0x2]", "0x5A5FD|MOV|EDI, 0xc", "0x5A602|CMP|word ptr [EDX], 0x23f", "0x5A607|JZ|0x6fb2a629", "0x5A609|TEST|ESI, ESI", "0x5A60B|JLE|0x6fb2a629", "0x5A60D|MOV|EAX, 0x6fbb60d2", "0x5A612|MOV|ECX, ESI", "0x5A614|MOV|EBP, dword ptr [EAX + -0x12]", "0x5A617|XOR|EBX, EBX"],
      "comment": "Marks dialog slot flags as active for matching dialog IDs.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load max dialog slot count from g_dwMaxUnitSlots\n2. For each of 12 dialog IDs in the input array:\n   a. If current dialog ID is not 0x23f (invalid marker):\n      i. Iterate through all active dialog slots (nMaxSlots)\n      ii. Compare each slot's ID with current dialog ID\n      iii. If match found, set corresponding slot flag to 1 (active)\n   b. Move to next dialog ID in array\n3. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\n- pSlotData: Pointer to dialog slot data array (base + 2 to start reading ushort dialog IDs)\n\nReturns:\n- void: Modifies g_abDialogStateFlags array in-place\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Dialog ID 0x23f indicates slot is invalid/empty (skipped)\n- If nMaxSlots is 0 or negative, entire inner loop is skipped\n- Function processes exactly 12 dialog IDs from input array\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x23f: Invalid dialog ID marker (567 decimal)\n- 0xc: Number of dialog IDs to process (12 decimal)\n- 0x2: Offset in param_1 where dialog ID array begins\n- 0x12: Offset for reading slot ID from g_abDialogStateFlags structure (-18 decimal)\n- 0x16: Structure stride for g_abDialogStateFlags entries (22 decimal)\n\nStructure Layout - g_abDialogStateFlags:\nOffset | Size | Field Name | Type | Description\n0x00   | 1    | dwActive   | byte | Active flag (0=inactive, 1=active)\n-0x12  | 2    | wSlotId    | ushort | Dialog slot ID for comparison\n(stride: 0x16 = 22 bytes per entry)",
      "tags": ["PARAM_1", "PROP_LEAF"]
    },
