      "comment": "Manages character dialog state transitions and cleanup\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if dialog callback pointer (g_pDialogCallback) is valid\n2. If callback exists, verify character dialog state is active (g_pCharacterDialogState != 0)\n3. If state active: close current dialog and cleanup resources via CloseDialogAndCleanup()\n4. Re-verify callback still exists after cleanup (defensive check)\n5. If callback still valid, invoke callback with parameter 0x1 (completion/success flag)\n6. Clear dialog callback and state globals (reset to NULL/0)\n7. Jump to InitializeInventoryDialogFrame() to setup new inventory frame\n8. If callback initially invalid or after cleanup, return early\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Dialog callback may be cleared during CloseDialogAndCleanup() - post-cleanup null check prevents crash\n- InitializeInventoryDialogFrame() invoked unconditionally when callback valid (critical initialization)\n- Global state cleanup (steps 6) prevents stale dialog references in subsequent operations\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x1: Callback completion flag (success/ready status)\n0x6fbf8ecf: Global dialog callback function pointer (code** type)\n0x6fbf8ec3: Global character dialog state flag (0=inactive, non-zero=active)\n\nRelated Functions:\n- CloseDialogAndCleanup() - Performs actual dialog teardown, may modify callback\n- InitializeInventoryDialogFrame() - Prepares inventory UI after transition\n- FUN_6fb5eaa0() - Parent caller, initiates dialog state changes",
      "tags": ["PARAM_0"]
    },
