      "instructions": ["0x5A6F0|MOV|EAX, [0x6fbdc010]", "0x5A6F5|ADD|EAX, 0xfffffe5c", "0x5A6FA|CDQ|", "0x5A6FB|SUB|EAX, EDX", "0x5A6FD|SAR|EAX, 0x1", "0x5A6FF|ADD|EAX, 0x2f", "0x5A702|MOV|[0x6fbf8f28], EAX", "0x5A707|RET|"],
      "comment": "Calculates the vertical Y position for centering menu panels on screen.\n\nClassification: Leaf function (no calls), Initialization utility\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Read current viewport height from g_dwViewportHeight\n2. Subtract menu panel height (0x1A4 = 420 pixels)\n3. Divide by 2 to center vertically (signed division with rounding)\n4. Add top margin offset (0x2F = 47 pixels)\n5. Store result to g_dwMenuPositionY global\n\nFormula: g_dwMenuPositionY = (g_dwViewportHeight - 420) / 2 + 47\n\nParameters: None (reads global state)\n\nReturns: void (stores result to g_dwMenuPositionY)\n\nGlobals Used:\n  g_dwViewportHeight (0x6fbdc010) - Current viewport height in pixels [READ]\n  g_dwMenuPositionY (0x6fbf8f28) - Calculated menu Y position [WRITE]\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x1A4 (420) - Menu panel height in pixels\n  0x2F (47) - Top margin/offset in pixels\n\nCalled From: Function pointer table at 0x6fbae030 (screen resolution change handlers)",
      "tags": ["PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_0", "PROP_LEAF", "PROP_SMALL"]
