      "comment": "Initialize game UI state and input bindings during startup sequence.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call InitializeInputSystemBindings() to save keyboard bindings and set up mouse callbacks\n2. Call ProcessUIStateChange(0xB, 1, 0) to activate UI element 0xB (likely quest/party panel)\n3. Tail-call ProcessUIStateTransitions(1) to iterate all UI elements and reset states\n\nParameters:\n  None\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nClassification: Initialization\nEntry point for game UI and input system initialization. Called during game startup\nto configure input bindings (keyboard/mouse) and establish initial UI element states.\nNo direct callers visible - likely invoked via function pointer table or export.\n\nCallees:\n- InitializeInputSystemBindings: Saves keybindings to registry, sets up mouse callbacks\n- ProcessUIStateChange: Updates UI element state (element 0xB activated with state 1)\n- ProcessUIStateTransitions: Iterates UI state table to reset/initialize all elements\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0xB (11): UI element ID being activated (quest/party panel based on context)\n- 0x1: Active state for ProcessUIStateChange and full-table flag for ProcessUIStateTransitions\n- 0x0: Scroll parameter (no viewport adjustment)",
