      "comment": "Initialize configuration values based on current system state.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call GetGlobalSystemState() to determine current state\n2. If state is active (non-zero):\n   - Set g_pConfigurationDataPointer to active configuration buffer at 0x6fbb71f8\n   - Set g_dwConfigValue1 to 0x3e (62 decimal, active config threshold)\n   - Set g_dwConfigValue2 to 5 (active mode count)\n   - Set g_dwConfigValue3 to 0x2f (47 decimal, active config secondary threshold)\n3. If state is inactive (zero):\n   - Set g_pConfigurationDataPointer to inactive configuration buffer at 0x6fbb6ff8\n   - Set g_dwConfigValue1 to 0x33 (51 decimal, inactive config threshold)\n   - Set g_dwConfigValue2 to 6 (inactive mode count)\n   - Set g_dwConfigValue3 to 0x24 (36 decimal, inactive config secondary threshold)\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\nUses GetGlobalSystemState() to determine active/inactive state.\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x3e = 62 decimal - Active configuration threshold value\n0x2f = 47 decimal - Active configuration secondary threshold\n0x33 = 51 decimal - Inactive configuration threshold value\n0x24 = 36 decimal - Inactive configuration secondary threshold\n\nInline Comments:\nAll magic numbers are documented in-line with their decimal equivalents and semantic meanings. Configuration values 5 and 6 represent counts/modes for active and inactive states respectively.",
