      "instructions": ["0x5A970|CMP|ECX, -0x1", "0x5A973|PUSH|ESI", "0x5A974|JGE|0x6fb2a98f", "0x5A976|TEST|ECX, ECX", "0x5A978|JGE|0x6fb2aa39", "0x5A97E|NEG|ECX", "0x5A980|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0x5A982|OR|ECX, 0xffffffff", "0x5A985|CALL|0x6fb2a970", "0x5A98A|DEC|ESI", "0x5A98B|JNZ|0x6fb2a982", "0x5A98D|POP|ESI", "0x5A98E|RET|", "0x5A98F|CMP|ECX, 0x1", "0x5A992|JLE|0x6fb2a9ad"],
      "comment": "Adjusts UI menu value with recursive processing and bounds clamping.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. If nDirection < -1: Negate value, recursively call with -1 for negated count iterations\n2. If nDirection == -1: Return early (base case for negative recursion)\n3. If nDirection > 1: Recursively call with 1 for nDirection count iterations, decrementing\n4. If nDirection == 0: Calculate base offset value (g_dwConfigValue1 decrement loop, max 0xf iterations)\n5. Adjust g_dwUIMenuUpdateFlag: clamp between 0 and calculated offset, increment/decrement based on direction\n6. Calculate final menu Y position: formula combines config scaling, update flag, viewport height\n7. Store result in g_dwMenuPositionY\n\nParameters:\nnDirection: Direction indicator - negative/positive for decrease/increase, 0 for neutral, absolute value indicates iteration count\n\nReturns:\nvoid (modifies global g_dwUIMenuUpdateFlag and g_dwMenuPositionY)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Negative direction: negate param, call recursively\n- Positive direction: decrement loop counter\n- Zero direction: neutral positioning with offset calculation\n- Bounds: g_dwUIMenuUpdateFlag clamped to [0, calculated_offset]",
      "tags": ["PARAM_1", "PROP_LOOPHEAVY"]
    },
