      "comment": "Initialize session mode and configure UI based on remote/local context.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize base configuration values for current game state\n2. Check if remote session mode (nSessionMode != 0):\n   - If LOCAL MODE (nSessionMode == 0):\n     a. Test g_dwRemoteSessionMode flag\n     b. If NOT in remote session (flag == 0):\n        - Configure UI panels for local session mode\n        - Initialize remote session message handlers\n        - Clear player unit selection state\n   - If REMOTE MODE (nSessionMode != 0):\n     a. Test g_dwRemoteSessionMode flag\n     b. If NOT in remote session (flag == 0):\n        - Backup and reinitialize key bindings\n        - Configure UI panels for remote session mode\n        - Process remote session messages\n        - Validate current unit selection with NULL context\n     c. Clear UI menu update flags\n     d. Clear UI menu state flags\n3. Execute post-initialization cleanup routine\n4. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\nnSessionMode (int): Session mode flag, 0 for local mode, non-zero for remote mode\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If g_dwRemoteSessionMode is non-zero, initialization is skipped for mode-dependent operations\n- UI state is always cleared at end when entering remote mode\n- Both local and remote paths call FUN_6fb2a8b0 for post-init cleanup",
