      "comment": "Render automap display with viewport coordinates and sprite rendering.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get current tick count and viewport state\n2. Check if viewport state changed from last render\n3. If state changed, update viewport configuration\n4. Iterate through display items (0xF passes)\n5. For each item, calculate screen coordinates from game coordinates\n6. Query item bitmap and render sprite data\n7. Repeat for secondary item pass if needed\n8. Render UI elements, status text, and labels\n9. Update frame counter and return\n\nParameters:\nNone (void function, uses globals for viewport state)\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Viewport change handling resets coordinate calculations\n- Multiple passes render different display layers (background items, decorations)\n- Screen coordinate transformation uses fixed math operations\n- Magic numbers: 0xd, 0x171, 0xf - rendering layer indices\n- Note: Function uses 21 SSA temporaries optimized away by compiler (iVar*, uVar*, extraout_*)\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset | Size | Field | Type | Description\n0x40   | 4    | dwFrameCount   | uint | Current frame number in sequence\n0x44   | 4    | (reserved)     | uint | Padding\n0x48   | 4    | dwViewportX    | uint | Viewport X coordinate\n0x4c   | 4    | dwViewportY    | uint | Viewport Y coordinate\n0x50   | 4    | dwOffsetX      | uint | Horizontal offset for rendering\n0x54   | 4    | dwOffsetY      | uint | Vertical offset for rendering\n0x58   | 4-7c | (stack temps)  | uint | Temporary calculation spaces\n\nRelated Functions:\n- FUN_6fb2b2c0 - Update viewport configuration on state change\n- FUN_6fb92980 - Render sprite data\n- FUN_6fb5b7d0 - Calculate viewport bounds\n- FUN_6fb8f680 - Get viewport state (Ordinal_10121)\n- FUN_6fb8f690 - Get secondary viewport parameter (Ordinal_10127)",
