      "comment": "Process mouse click input in menu UI, dispatching clicks to appropriate menu regions\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if menu is locked (g_pMenuLockState != 0), return if locked\n2. Calculate menu region boundaries based on screen and viewport dimensions\n3. Detect which of 6 menu regions contains click (fRegion1Hit through fRegion6Hit)\n4. Region 1: Top panel (y-offset 0x28 to 0x136)\n5. Region 2: Left side region (y-offset 0x23 to 0x2f)\n6. Region 3: Middle region (y-offset 0x125 to 0x131)\n7. Region 4: Below scroll area (y-offset 0x2f to menu Y boundary)\n8. Region 5: Scroll region (within dynamically calculated bounds)\n9. Region 6: Below Region 5 (to end of menu bounds)\n10. Query menu state array g_pMenuRegion1State..g_pMenuRegion6State\n11. If no regions hit and nMenuResult == 3, clear menu state\n12. If Region 1 hit, handle up/down navigation, menu item selection\n13. If Region 2 hit with debounce (32ms), adjust menu -1\n14. If Region 3 hit with debounce (32ms), adjust menu +1\n15. If Region 4 hit with debounce (32ms), adjust menu -14 (page up)\n16. If Region 5 hit, track scroll origin and adjust menu based on drag movement\n17. If Region 6 hit with debounce (32ms), adjust menu +14 (page down)\n18. Check clicked bounds against menu panel table (g_pMenuPanelBoundsTable)\n\nParameters:\nint nScreenX - X coordinate of mouse click (ECX, __fastcall)\nint nScreenY - Y coordinate of mouse click (EDX, __fastcall)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Modifies global menu state variables as side effects\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- When menu locked (g_pMenuLockState set), function returns immediately\n- Debounce timer: 50ms (0x32) between repeated actions on same region\n- Menu item count limits: g_dwConfigValue1 (max items), g_dwConfigValue2 (rows per page)\n- Scroll calculation uses g_dwConfigValue3 + 1 as multiplier\n- Bounds checking: Validates click within calculated menu area before processing\n- Note: Function uses 7 compiler-optimized temporaries not visible in decompiled code (stack-allocated values optimized away by compiler)\n\nRelated Functions:\n- FUN_6fb2b9f0 - GetMenuClickResult (returns current menu item selected)\n- FUN_6fb2b920 - AdjustMenuNavigation (handles up/down arrow navigation)\n- AdjustMenuValue - Adjusts selected menu item by offset (-14 to +14)\n- GetTickCount - Win32 API for debounce timer\n\nStructure Layout (Menu Region State Array):\nOffset | Size | Field Name | Description\n0      | 4    | Element 0  | Region 1 state pointer\n4      | 4    | Element 1  | Region 2 state pointer\n8      | 4    | Element 2  | Region 3 state pointer\n12     | 4    | Element 3  | Region 4 state pointer\n16     | 4    | Element 4  | Region 5 state pointer\n20     | 4    | Element 5  | Region 6 state pointer\n24     | 4    | End marker | Array terminator (0x6fbf8f5c)",
