      "comment": "Adjust UI menu state based on delta. Handles positive/negative adjustments with bounds checking.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. If nDelta is 0, return early (no adjustment needed)\n2. If nDelta < -1, recursively call with -1 for |nDelta| iterations (decrement menu state)\n3. If nDelta > 1, recursively call with 1 for nDelta iterations (increment menu state)\n4. For nDelta = -1: Decrement g_dwUIMenuStateFlags (clamp to 0)\n5. For nDelta = 1: Increment g_dwUIMenuStateFlags (clamp to g_dwConfigValue1)\n6. If g_dwUIMenuStateFlags <= g_dwUIMenuUpdateFlag, update menu display\n7. Otherwise adjust update flag and call AdjustMenuValue(0) to refresh display\n\nParameters:\n- nDelta (int): Direction/magnitude of adjustment (-1 to decrement, 1 to increment, or batch values)\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- nDelta = 0: Early return (NOP)\n- nDelta between -1 and 1 (exclusive): Return without state change\n- Bounds checked: g_dwUIMenuStateFlags constrained to [0, g_dwConfigValue1]\n- Recursive calls optimize batch adjustments via loop unrolling",
