      "comment": "Find menu panel index by screen coordinates.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize panel index counter to 0\n2. Start at first menu panel bounds entry in g_pMenuPanelBoundsTable\n3. Loop through bounds table:\n   - Check if screen coordinates fall within current bounds rectangle (left, right, top, bottom)\n   - If coordinates match, exit loop and return current index\n   - Advance to next bounds entry (offset 0x1a bytes per entry)\n   - Increment panel index counter\n   - Check if end of table reached; if so, return current index\n4. Return panel index if match found, else return 3 (no match)\n\nParameters:\nnScreenX: Screen X coordinate (from mouse click/input)\nnScreenY: Screen Y coordinate (from mouse click/input)\n\nReturns:\nPanel index (0-based) if coordinates match a menu panel\n3 if no matching panel found\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Return value 3 used as \"no match\" sentinel\n- Bounds comparison uses piVar2[-1] for left, [0] for right, [1] for top, [2] for bottom\n- Table entries are 0x1a bytes apart containing 4 DWORD bounds values\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset | Size | Field Name      | Type  | Description\n-----------------------------------------------------\n0x00   | 4    | dwMinX/dwLeft   | uint  | Minimum X coordinate\n0x04   | 4    | dwMaxX/dwRight  | uint  | Maximum X coordinate\n0x08   | 4    | dwMinY/dwTop    | uint  | Minimum Y coordinate\n0x0C   | 4    | dwMaxY/dwBottom | uint  | Maximum Y coordinate\n0x10   | 10   | (unused)        | byte  | Padding/reserved\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x1a (26): Stride between menu panel bound entries\n0x03 (3): Sentinel return value for no match",
      "tags": ["PARAM_2", "PROP_LEAF", "PROP_SMALL"]
