      "comment": "Process automap menu click event from UI message cache node.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if game system is currently enabled via IsGameSystemEnabled()\n2. If enabled (non-zero), mark cache node inactive (fActive = 0) and return early\n3. If disabled (zero), set g_pAutomapRenderCache to 1 (render flag)\n4. Extract X coordinate from low word of dwFlags (bits 0-15)\n5. Extract Y coordinate from high word of dwFlags (bits 16-31)\n6. Dispatch click to ProcessMenuInputClick with extracted coordinates\n7. Mark cache node as active (fActive = 1)\n8. Clear pending flag (dwPending = 0)\n9. Insert cache node into UI system via InsertCacheNodeWithCookie\n\nParameters:\nCacheNode * pCacheNode - Pointer to UI cache node containing click coordinates\n  - dwFlags (offset 0x0C): Packed coordinates (low word = X, high word = Y)\n  - fActive (offset 0x18): Set to 0 if ignored, 1 if processed\n  - dwPending (offset 0x1C): Cleared to 0 after processing\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Modifies cache node state as side effect\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Early exit when game system enabled: Sets fActive = 0 without processing click\n- Coordinate packing: X/Y stored in single DWORD, unpacked via shift/mask\n- g_pAutomapRenderCache set to 1 triggers automap render update\n\nRelated Functions:\n- IsGameSystemEnabled: Returns non-zero if game system active\n- ProcessMenuInputClick: Dispatches click to 6 menu regions\n- InsertCacheNodeWithCookie: Inserts node into cache system",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Inventory", "PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_1", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
