      "comment": "Get menu item index from Y-coordinate. Finds which menu item (if any) corresponds to the given Y-coordinate by checking against stored base Y position and item height.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. If current menu index >= max items, return adjusted index or max-1\n2. Calculate base Y position: (viewport_height - 0x1a4) / 2 + 0x3a\n3. Iterate from current menu index checking if Y-coordinate <= item Y position\n4. Each item is spaced 0x12 pixels apart\n5. If more than 14 items (0xe) checked and coordinate still beyond range, break loop\n6. Return matched item index or max-1 if coordinate out of range\n\nParameters:\n- nYCoord (ECX, int): Y-coordinate to search for in menu\n\nReturns:\n- EAX (int): Menu item index (0-based), or max-1 if no match found\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If max items (g_dwConfigValue1) is 0 or negative, returns -1\n- Item height constant: 0x12 pixels (18 pixels)\n- Menu base Y offset: 0x3a (58 pixels)\n- Viewport height adjustment: 0x1a4 (420 pixels)\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n- 0x1a4: 420 - viewport height adjustment\n- 0x3a: 58 - menu base Y position offset\n- 0x12: 18 - menu item height in pixels\n- 0xe: 14 - maximum items to check in loop\n- 0xfffffe5c: -420 - used in division to calculate base Y",
      "tags": ["PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_1", "PROP_LEAF"]
    },
