      "instructions": ["0x5BDE0|CALL|0x6fadb800", "0x5BDE5|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0x5BDE7|JZ|0x6fb2bdf7", "0x5BDE9|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [ESP + 0x4]", "0x5BDED|MOV|dword ptr [EAX + 0x18], 0x0", "0x5BDF4|RET|0x4", "0x5BDF7|PUSH|ESI", "0x5BDF8|MOV|ESI, dword ptr [0x6fbf8f68]", "0x5BDFE|MOV|ECX, 0x1", "0x5BE03|CALL|0x6fb2b920", "0x5BE08|MOV|EAX, [0x6fbf8f68]", "0x5BE0D|MOV|EDX, dword ptr [0x6fbb7464]", "0x5BE13|LEA|ECX, [EAX + EAX*0x4]", "0x5BE16|CMP|dword ptr [EDX + ECX*0x2], 0x39", "0x5BE1A|JZ|0x6fb2bdfe"],
      "comment": "Activates a UI menu widget by advancing to a valid menu state.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if game system is enabled via IsGameSystemEnabled()\n2. If system enabled: Set widget disabled flag (offset +0x18 = 0), return early\n3. If system disabled: Save current menu state index\n4. Loop: Call AdjustUIMenuState(1) to advance menu position\n5. Continue loop while menu entry type at current index equals 0x39 (separator/disabled)\n6. If menu state changed: Call InitializeGameObjectProperties to reinitialize display\n7. Set widget enabled flag (offset +0x18 = 1)\n8. Clear widget state (offset +0x1c = 0)\n9. Insert widget into cache via InsertCacheNodeWithCookie\n\nParameters:\n- pUIWidget (dword): Pointer to UI widget structure\n  +0x18: dwEnabled - Widget activation state (0=disabled, 1=enabled)\n  +0x1c: dwState - Widget state flags (cleared to 0)\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If game system already enabled, widget is immediately disabled\n- Loop skips menu entries of type 0x39 (separator/inactive items)\n- Menu state only triggers reinitialization if it actually changed\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n- 0x39: Menu entry type indicating separator or disabled item\n- 0x18: Offset to widget enabled flag\n- 0x1c: Offset to widget state flags\n- 10 (0xA): Stride of menu configuration entries (* 10 = entry size)\n\nGlobal References:\n- g_dwUIMenuStateFlags (0x6fbf8f68): Current menu state index\n- g_pConfigurationDataPointer (0x6fbb7464): Pointer to menu configuration table",
      "tags": ["PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_1", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
