      "comment": "Prepares a UI cache node for menu interaction processing\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if game system is enabled via IsGameSystemEnabled()\n2. If enabled, set cache node field at offset 0x18 to 0 (disabled state) and return early\n3. Check if menu hit region mask equals 1 (pending menu action)\n4. If mask is 1, clear it to 0 and call InitializeGameObjectProperties to reset game object state\n5. Set cache node field at offset 0x18 to 1 (enabled/active state)\n6. Set cache node field at offset 0x1c to 0 (initialize secondary field)\n7. Insert cache node into system via InsertCacheNodeWithCookie()\n\nParameters:\ndword * pCacheNode - Pointer to cache node structure (32+ bytes minimum)\n  +0x18: dword - Active state flag (0=disabled, 1=enabled)\n  +0x1c: dword - Secondary state field (initialized to 0)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Modifies cache node fields as side effect\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Early exit when game system enabled: Only clears active flag, skips cache insertion\n- Menu transition: Clears g_dwMenuHitRegionMask and reinitializes game object when mask==1\n\nRelated Functions:\n- IsGameSystemEnabled - Checks if core game system is running\n- InitializeGameObjectProperties - Resets game object state during menu transitions\n- InsertCacheNodeWithCookie - Adds node to internal cache system\n\nGlobal Dependencies:\n- g_dwMenuHitRegionMask (0x6fbb74b8) - Menu hit region tracking flag",
      "tags": ["PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_1", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
    },
