      "comment": "Processes UI menu panel input messages based on game system and remote session state.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if game system is enabled via IsGameSystemEnabled\n2. If enabled, set pInputMessage->dwResult to 0 (handled) and return early\n3. If g_dwUIMenuInitialized is 0, set it to 1 (first-time initialization)\n4. Otherwise check input flags and menu state:\n   a. If flags bit 0x40000000 is set, skip panel processing\n   b. If current menu state is 0x39 (exit state), skip panel processing\n5. Set g_dwRemoteSessionMode to 1\n6. Dispatch game state 0xB via ProcessGameStateHandler\n7. Process 6 menu panel messages via ProcessMessageEntryArray\n8. If IsRemoteSessionActive returns true, process 1 remote session message\n9. If IsValidRemoteDesktopSession returns true, process 1 remote desktop message\n10. If IsRemoteSessionSupported returns true, process 1 remote support message\n11. Call InitializeGameObjectProperties with mode 2 and zero coordinates\n12. Set g_dwUIMenuInitialized to 0 (processing complete)\n13. Set pInputMessage->dwResult to 1 (success)\n14. Set pInputMessage->dwError to 0\n15. Call InsertCacheNodeWithCookie to queue the message\n\nParameters:\npInputMessage (UIInputMessage *) - Pointer to input message structure containing:\n  +0x0C: dwFlags - Input flags (bit 0x40000000 = skip processing)\n  +0x18: dwResult - Output result code (0 = handled by system, 1 = success)\n  +0x1C: dwError - Output error code (0 = no error)\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If game system enabled, message is marked handled (dwResult=0) without panel processing\n- Menu state 0x39 (exit state) bypasses all panel processing\n- Flag bit 0x40000000 bypasses all panel processing\n- Uses g_dwUIMenuInitialized as reentrancy guard\n\nGlobal Variables:\ng_dwUIMenuInitialized (0x6fbb74bc) - Initialization/reentrancy flag\ng_dwUIMenuStateFlags (0x6fbf8f68) - Current UI menu state index\ng_pConfigurationDataPointer (0x6fbb7464) - Config data array pointer\ng_dwRemoteSessionMode (0x6fbf8f70) - Remote session mode flag",
