      "comment": "Processes keyboard binding registration for menu panel operations and updates UI state.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if game system is enabled via IsGameSystemEnabled\n2. If enabled, set cache node field +0x18 to 0 and return early (system busy)\n3. Initialize key code output buffer to zero\n4. Calculate configuration pointer using g_dwUIMenuStateFlags * 10 as index into g_pConfigurationDataPointer\n5. Call RegisterKeyboardBinding with config entry, hit region mask, 0x100 flag, and output buffer\n6. If binding registration returns 0 (new binding created):\n   a. If output key code is non-zero, store it in g_wLastBoundKeyCode\n   b. Update g_dwLastRenderTick with current tick count\n7. If binding registration returns non-zero (updated existing binding):\n   a. Get init flag and process 6 messages from g_aMenuPanelsEnd array\n   b. If remote session is supported, process 1 message from g_aRemoteSessionSupportedPanels\n   c. If valid remote desktop session, process 1 message from g_aRemoteDesktopPanels\n   d. If remote session is active, process 1 message from g_aRemoteSessionActivePanels\n   e. Call ProcessRemoteSessionMessageState to update session handling\n   f. Clear g_dwRemoteSessionMode to 0\n8. Set cache node field +0x18 to 1 (processing complete)\n9. Set cache node field +0x1C to 0 (clear status)\n10. Insert cache node into UI cache via InsertCacheNodeWithCookie\n\nParameters:\npCacheNode - Pointer to UI cache node structure; fields at +0x18 and +0x1C are updated\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Early return if game system is enabled (field +0x18 set to 0)\n- Key code stored only if non-zero after binding registration\n- Remote session panels only processed when respective session checks pass\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x18 (24) - Cache node offset for completion status flag\n0x1C (28) - Cache node offset for secondary status\n0x100 (256) - Key code flag passed to RegisterKeyboardBinding\n6 - Message count for main menu panels array\n1 - Message count for remote session panel arrays",
