      "comment": "Processes keyboard binding requests and updates menu panel state.\n\nHandles two key binding types (0x101 and 0x102) based on message code in cache node.\nIf game system is enabled, skips processing and marks node as empty.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if game system is enabled via IsGameSystemEnabled()\n2. If enabled, set cache node offset +0x18 to 0 and return early\n3. Extract message code from cache node offset +0x8, shift right 16 bits\n4. If code == 1 (0x101 binding):\n   a. Call RegisterKeyboardBinding with 0x101 flag\n   b. If binding fails (returns 0), update g_wLastBoundKeyCode and g_dwLastRenderTick\n   c. If binding succeeds, process 6 menu panels via ProcessMessageArray\n   d. Check IsRemoteSessionSupported, process 1 remote session panel if true\n   e. Check IsValidRemoteDesktopSession, process 1 remote desktop panel if true\n   f. Check IsRemoteSessionActive, process 1 active session panel if true\n5. If code == 2 (0x102 binding):\n   a. Same sequence as code 1 but with 0x102 flag\n6. If code neither 1 nor 2, skip to finalization\n7. After panel processing, call ProcessRemoteSessionMessageState\n8. Clear g_dwRemoteSessionMode to 0\n9. Set cache node offset +0x18 to 1 (success)\n10. Set cache node offset +0x1c to 0\n11. Call InsertCacheNodeWithCookie to queue the cache node\n\nParameters:\n  pCacheNode - Pointer to cache node structure\n    +0x08: uint dwMessageCode (high word is binding type: 1=0x101, 2=0x102)\n    +0x18: uint dwStatus (0=empty, 1=success)\n    +0x1c: uint dwErrorCode (always set to 0)\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nGlobals Referenced:\n  g_pConfigurationDataPointer (0x6fbb7464) - Config data table base\n  g_dwUIMenuStateFlags (0x6fbf8f68) - Menu state index for config lookup\n  g_dwMenuHitRegionMask (0x6fbb74b8) - Hit region mask for binding\n  g_wLastBoundKeyCode (0x6fbf8f7c) - Last bound key code (word)\n  g_dwLastRenderTick (0x6fbf8f80) - Tick count when key was bound\n  g_dwRemoteSessionMode (0x6fbf8f70) - Remote session mode flag\n  g_aMenuPanelsEnd (0x6fbb74c0) - Menu panels message array\n  g_aRemoteSessionSupportedPanels (0x6fbb7528) - Remote supported panels\n  g_aRemoteDesktopPanels (0x6fbb7518) - Remote desktop panels\n  g_aRemoteSessionActivePanels (0x6fbb7508) - Active session panels\n\nSSA Temporary Variables (decompiler artifacts):\n  sVar1 (wKeyCode): short - Previous key code value from g_wLastBoundKeyCode\n  sVar2 (wNewKeyCode): short - New captured key code from binding output\n  bVar3 (fSessionCheck): bool - Remote session check result\n  uVar4 (dwPanelCount): uint - Panel count for ProcessMessageArray (6 or 1)\n  iVar5 (nBindingResult): int - Return value from RegisterKeyboardBinding\n  extraout_var*: undefined3 - High bytes from bool return value expansion (compiler artifact)\n  dwCookieValue: uint* - Saved copy of pCacheNode pointer\n  hWnd*: HWND - Unused return values from GetInitFlag (decompiler artifact)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x101 - Key binding type 1\n  0x102 - Key binding type 2\n  0x10 - Bit shift to extract binding type from message code\n  0x6 - Panel count for main menu panels\n  0x1 - Panel count for remote session panels",
