      "comment": "Load inventory panel UI assets and initialize image pointers\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load panel button base image (normal state)\n2. Check character type: if class between 5-9 (exclusive), handle special case:\n   - Call inventory source check\n   - If result nonzero, use expanded inventory image path (6-char UI)\n   - Otherwise use standard inventory image path\n   - Load selected inventory image and write to buffer file\n   - Jump to asset initialization\n3. For non-special classes:\n   - Call inventory source check\n   - If zero, load standard inventory image (4-char panel)\n   - If nonzero, check system state:\n     - If state nonzero, load expanded inventory image (6-char panel)\n     - If state zero, load standard inventory image (4-char panel)\n4. Initialize all panel UI asset pointers by calling load function for each:\n   - Arrow, warning, durability socket, gem socket, belt panel\n   - Health/mana bar, overlap, menu button, menu panel\n   - Skill points, run button, hostile picture\n5. Clear 12 dwords (0x0C) starting at global slot reservation\n\nParameters: None\n\nReturns: void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Character class IDs 6-8 (Sorceress, Necromancer, Druid) have special inventory UI\n- System state determines variant selection for some panels\n- Buffer uses local stack allocation for path construction (260 bytes)",
      "tags": ["UI_INVENTORY", "UI_SKILLS", "PARAM_0", "UI_PANEL"]
