      "comment": "Render game window elements for both inventory and character panels.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Query game state objects (viewport 1) via Ordinal_10321/10966\n2. Get inventory panel render target via FUN_6fb50af0\n3. Check inventory state: if < 6 (active), use default layout; else use extended layout\n4. If panel is inactive (byte at offset 0xe9 == 0), check Ordinal_10082 flag and set active flag\n5. Call Ordinal_10955 to update position/size values for panel bounds\n6. Render inventory panel via FUN_6fb50ce0 with calculated positions\n7. If extended layout and state_check fails, render alternate content via Ordinal_10968\n8. Finalize rendering via FUN_6fb50b80\n9. Repeat same process for character panel: query state via Ordinal_10322/10966\n10. Character panel checks: if < 6 OR (0xd8-0xdc range), use default; else extended\n11. Final render calls FUN_6fb50b80 to present both panels\n\nParameters:\nNone (void) - reads global screen dimensions (g_dwScreenWidth, g_dwScreenHeight)\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Magic numbers: 0xa5 (width offset), 0x75 (default Y position), 0xd8-0xdc (character panel state range)\n- Character panel height = screen height; width = screen width - 0xa5\n- Panel content source changes based on state flags (Ordinal_10082 result)\n- Extended layout uses Ordinal_10968 for alternate render content\n- Note: Function uses 6 SSA temporaries optimized away (uVar6, iVar3, uVar2, iVar5, uVar4, piVar1)\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0xa5 = 165 decimal, panel width offset from right edge\n0x75 = 117 decimal, default panel Y position from top\n0xd8 = 216 decimal, character panel state range start\n0xdd = 221 decimal, character panel state range end\n0xe9 = 233 decimal, panel inactive flag offset within state structure",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_StatList", "PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Path", "STRUCT_Inventory", "STRUCT_Skill", "PARAM_0", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
