      "comment": "Maps game mode state value to return code for game state handling\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Read global game mode state variable (g_dwGameMode)\n2. Switch on mode value:\n   - Modes 0, 5: Return 3 (mode class A)\n   - Modes 1, 4: Return 2 (mode class B)\n   - Mode 2: Return 1 (mode class C)\n   - All others: Return 4 (mode class D/invalid)\n3. Return mapped value to caller\n\nParameters:\nNone - reads global game mode state from g_dwGameMode\n\nReturns:\nuint - Mode code (1-4): 1=mode_class_c, 2=mode_class_b, 3=mode_class_a, 4=mode_class_d_invalid\n\nSpecial Cases:\nMultiple input modes map to same output (0,5→3; 1,4→2); modes 6+ default to 4\nUsed by ~20 functions for conditional game state routing",
