      "comment": "Manages player skill slot display and rendering across active game elements.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize skill slot display flags (g_abSkillSlotFlags) and reset counters\n2. Retrieve active game context via Ordinal_10719 and validate texture resources\n3. Verify availability of skill display surfaces (Ordinal_10257, Ordinal_10781, Ordinal_10731)\n4. If primary display unavailable, check alternate display surface\n5. Allocate and initialize skill array with header info (type=2) and skill error code\n6. Allocate viewport and set Y coordinate based on slot index\n7. Check player condition (CheckPlayersForCondition) to adjust Y offset (+0x1e if true)\n8. Render skill array via Ordinal_10072 (Storm display function)\n9. Iterate through skill list (g_aSkillTypeList) up to g_dwSkillTypeCount times\n10. For each skill type, retrieve and validate unit skill data\n11. Calculate total skill level by summing matching skills from all players\n12. Compare with thresholds (g_aSkillListData offsets) and select appropriate display level\n13. Update skill array with correct skill level and re-render if threshold exceeded\n14. Continue to next skill type\n\nParameters:\nIMPLICIT EBP: Game data context pointer\nIMPLICIT ECX: Window context (saved/restored from g_dwScreenWidth)\n\nReturns:\nvoid (no return value, state updated via globals)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Handles 6 maximum skill display slots via g_abSkillSlotFlags\n- Supports 3-tier skill level display (uVar8, +1, +2)\n- Skill display fails silently if textures unavailable (Ordinal_10257 returns 0)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x37: Screen width offset adjustment\n0x28: Slot width (per-slot spacing in pixels)\n0x9b: Base Y coordinate for first slot\n0xc6: Alternate Y coordinate when condition met\n0x1e: Y offset adjustment for condition met\n0x80: Skill field offset for comparison\n0x46: Skill parameter code (Ordinal_10519 parameter)\n0x6: Maximum slot iterations",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_StatList", "PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Path", "STRUCT_Inventory", "STRUCT_Skill", "STRUCT_Room1", "STRUCT_ItemData", "PARAM_0", "PROP_LOOPHEAVY", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
