      "comment": "Display error/warning messages for all player classes in the party.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get game state and unit context via FUN_6fb62880()\n2. Scan player class array g_aPlayerClassIds starting from index 0\n3. For each class, fetch unit via Ordinal_10257() with game state ID\n4. Skip if unit not found OR unit state invalid (Ordinal_10811 == 0)\n5. Skip if unit is reserved/hidden (Ordinal_10767 returns 1)\n6. Calculate error level (0=severe 1%, 1=warning 5-20%, 2=critical <1%)\n7. Determine visual severity based on class type and internal state flags\n8. Populate message buffer [0]=type, [1]=error code, [2]=severity, [3..]=flags\n9. Call Ordinal_10072() to render message at screen position (width-60, Y-offset)\n10. Move to next player class, repeat until boundary reached or error\n\nParameters:\n(void)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Messages displayed directly to screen buffer\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If scan reaches boundary 0x6fbb760c, function exits cleanly\n- Error severity calculation uses formula: (quality_stat * 100) / total_stat\n- Message buffer size fixed at 72 bytes (18 dword elements)\n- Y coordinate computed as g_dwScreenWidth - 0x3c or offset by 0x8c on error\n\nOrdinal Mapping:\n- Ordinal_10257: D2Common.GetUnit() - Retrieve unit by class ID\n- Ordinal_10811: D2Common.IsUnitAllocated() - Check unit validity\n- Ordinal_10767: D2Common.IsUnitReserved() - Check if hidden/reserved\n- Ordinal_10567: D2Common.GetUnitLife() - Get health/state\n- Ordinal_10731: D2Common.GetUnitStat() - Query unit stat (0x33=mana)\n- Ordinal_10783: D2Common.GetUnitExtraData() - Fetch profession/type\n- Ordinal_10519: D2Common.GetUnitData() - Get primary data (0x48=experience)\n- Ordinal_10072: D2Common.DisplayString() - Render text on screen",
