      "comment": "Render slider control template with position validation and formatting.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get current slider template pointer and screen coordinates\n2. Initialize two Unicode string buffers (200 chars each)\n3. Check if coordinates are within valid range (0x1e-0x6e X, screen_height-0x4b to screen_height-0xf Y)\n4. If out of bounds: return immediately\n5. If in bounds (normal case):\n   - Get color value from position (mode 6: 0x80-centered)\n   - Call Ordinal_10564 to get slider resource\n   - Check unit data: validate (*[0] == 0) && ([12] != 0x11) && (-1 < color < 2)\n   - If validation passes, set color to 1\n6. Initialize third Unicode string buffer\n7. Get alternate color value (mode 8: 0x100-offset)\n8. Call Ordinal_10004 with color values\n9. Format Unicode string using sprintf\n10. Concatenate with in-stack string\n11. Call Ordinal_10121 (render/draw operation)\n12. Call Ordinal_10117 with calculated Y offset and zeros\n\nParameters:\nNone - uses global screen dimensions and slider control template\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nOrdinal Functions Called:\n- Ordinal_10565 (address 0x6fb2d763): Get slider template/resource handle\n- Ordinal_10564 (address 0x6fb2d763): Get slider resource length/size  \n- Ordinal_10004 (address 0x6fb2d7a6): Format color/position value to packed integer\n- Ordinal_10121 (address 0x6fb2d7b8): Render slider control to screen\n- Ordinal_10117 (address 0x6fb2d7da): Position slider with vertical offset\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Coordinate validation uses screen dimensions from g_dwScreenHeight and g_dwScreenWidth\n- Magic number 0x4b (75) is top margin, 0xf (15) is bottom margin, 0x1e (30) is left, 0x6e (110) is right\n- Two rendering paths: out-of-bounds returns immediately, in-bounds renders slider\n- Unicode string operations suggest wide-character rendering\n- Stack-based temporary buffers (aUStack_190, aUStack_c8) for string formatting\n- Note: Function uses stack-allocated temporaries optimized away in decompilation\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x1e (30) - minimum X coordinate\n0x6e (110) - maximum X coordinate  \n0x4b (75) - top margin from screen height\n0xf (15) - bottom margin from screen height\n0x6f (111) - left boundary check offset\n0x1f (31) - right boundary check offset\n0x11 (17) - unit data validation constant\n0x5f (95) - final Y offset calculation\n100 - Unicode string buffer initialization count\n6 - color mode for normal rendering (0x80-centered)\n8 - color mode for alternate rendering (0x100-offset)",
