      "comment": "Validates and updates panel animation frame counter with timing constraints.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get frame data pointer (Ordinal_10519)\n2. Determine panel type: 6=Inventory(fIsType6=false), 8=Character(fIsType6=true), 10=Spells\n3. Fetch frame limit via appropriate ordinal (Ordinal_10564/10565/10566)\n4. Return 0 if frame limit is 0 (invalid panel)\n5. If frame counter < 2 (initial setup): initialize both current and previous frame values\n6. If frame changed and count difference < frame_limit/8: update timestamp, store previous frame\n7. Calculate frame range (7-15 frames) based on elapsed time\n8. Apply animation interpolation if frame available and elapsed time < frame_range\n9. Validate result (0 to frame_limit inclusive)\n10. Return interpolated or constrained frame number\n\nParameters:\nnPanelType (ECX) - Panel type: 6=Inventory, 8=Character, 10=Spells\nIMPLICIT dwFrameDataPtr (EAX) - Frame data base pointer from GetUnitData\n\nReturns:\nint - Validated frame number (0 to nFrameLimit), or 0 on error\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x10 - Offset stride for panel data structures (16 bytes per panel)\n0x6fbf8fe0 - Base address of current frame values array\n0x6fbf8fd8 - Base address of previous frame values array\n0x6fbf8fe4 - Base address of frame update timestamps\n0x6fbf8fdc - Base address of last frame change timestamps\n0x03 - Mask for CDQ sign extension (rounding adjustment)\n0x03 - Shift amount for frame limit division (divide by 8)\n0x07 - Minimum frame range (7 frames)\n0x0f - Maximum frame range (15 frames)\n\nRelated Functions:\n- FUN_6fb62880() - Retrieves game unit/frame data\n- Ordinal_10519() - D2Common frame index lookup\n- Ordinal_10564() - Inventory frame limit\n- Ordinal_10565() - Character frame limit\n- Ordinal_10566() - Spells frame limit\n- GetGlobalFrameCounter() - Gets current game frame counter",
