      "comment": "Render main game screen with panels based on active game state.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check game type (Ordinal_10003 = GetGameType) - set dwExtraOffset=1 if type 3, else 0\n2. Get scroll window mode (Ordinal_10005 = GetScrollWindowMode) - determines which panels to render (1=weather, 2=object, 3=both)\n3. If scroll mode 2 or 3:\n   a. Initialize anPanelData array (18 dwords, cleared to 0)\n   b. Get or initialize ItemError panel resource using FUN_6fb5a050\n   c. Render 5 item panels via Ordinal_10072 at positions (0,0), (0x100,0), (0,0x1e4), (0,0x229), (0x100,0x229)\n4. If scroll mode 1 or 3:\n   a. Render 5 weather panels via Ordinal_10072 at positions (400,0x3f), (0x220,0xfd), (0x2c9,0x1e4), (0x220,0x229), (400,0x229)\n5. For weather/object panels based on scroll mode:\n   a. If scroll mode 2: render object panels at bottom using g_dwScreenHeight adjusted by dwExtraOffset\n   b. If not mode 2: render weather panels, report/clear errors from g_dwWeatherError, g_dwObjectError, g_dwItemError if set\n6. Get mouse position (FUN_6fb8f680=GetMouseX, FUN_6fb8f690=GetMouseY) - returns nMouseX in EBX, nMouseY in EBP\n7. Check always-run mode (GetAlwaysRunSetting):\n   a. If disabled (0): check g_dwAlwaysRunModeEnabled for sprint state, set nRunMode=1 if enabled\n   b. If enabled (!0): check g_dwAlwaysRunModeEnabled inverted, set nRunMode=2 or 3\n8. Render movement mode indicator at bottom center via Ordinal_10072\n9. Check if mouse in button hotzone [(ScreenWidth/2-0x91), (ScreenWidth/2-0x80)] x [(ScreenHeight-0x1c), (ScreenHeight-8)]\n   - If yes: call FUN_6fb2e490 (handle button click)\n10. Call UI rendering functions: FUN_6fb2dff0, FUN_6fb2e180, FUN_6fb2e2d0, RenderGameWindowElements, FUN_6fb2ef90, FUN_6fb2f200, FUN_6fb2f230\n\nParameters:\n(none)\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Panel array initialized to 0 before each panel type (local_110 is 18 dwords = 72 bytes)\n- Array field [1] holds error code/panel ID, field [2] holds panel type indicator (0-9)\n- Screen position adjustments account for resolution via g_dwScreenHeight and g_dwScreenWidth globals\n- Magic number 0x91 and 0x80 define button hotspot left/right bounds on screen\n- Magic number 0x1c and 0x8 define button hotspot top/bottom bounds from screen bottom\n- Note: Function uses stack-allocated temporary abRenderBuffer[200] bytes optimized away in disassembly\n\nStructure Layout:\nanPanelData is 18-element int array used as parameter block for Ordinal_10072 rendering:\n| Offset | Size | Field | Type | Description |\n|--------|------|-------|------|-------------|\n| 0      | 4    | [0]   | int  | Reserved (always 0) |\n| 4      | 4    | [1]   | int  | Error code or panel ID |\n| 8      | 4    | [2]   | int  | Panel type index (0-9) |\n| 12     | 4    | [3]   | int  | Reserved (always 0) |\n| 16-68  | 52   | [4-17]| int  | Coordinates/flags passed to Ordinal_10072 |\n\nRelated Functions:\n- FUN_6fb5a050() - Load panel resource by name\n- FUN_6fb2e490() - Handle panel click event\n- FUN_6fb2dff0() - Render viewport/map display\n- FUN_6fb2e180() - Render character stats\n- FUN_6fb2e2d0() - Render inventory items\n- RenderGameWindowElements() - Render window frame/decorations\n- FUN_6fb2ef90() - Render equipment display",
      "tags": ["PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Path", "STRUCT_Inventory", "STRUCT_Skill", "PARAM_0", "UI_PANEL", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
