      "comment": "Render experience and loot progress bars on main game screen.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get current screen mode from FUN_6fb62880()\n2. Update panel animation frame using UpdatePanelAnimationFrameWithValidation(6)\n3. Query experience bar display status from Ordinal_10564()\n4. If experience bar enabled, calculate bar height from frame count and divisor\n5. Initialize panel data buffer (adwPanelData[18]) with values\n6. Set panel color 0x1c (green) for experience bar\n7. Query loot bar display status from Ordinal_10487(dwPanelMode, 100)\n8. If loot bar enabled, calculate bar width from bar divisor 0x4a\n9. Draw loot bar using Ordinal_10074() with color 0x1c or 0x1d based on mode\n10. Draw experience bar using Ordinal_10074() if bar height nonzero\n11. Query NPC damage status from Ordinal_10487(dwPanelMode, 2)\n12. Draw NPC damage bar using Ordinal_10072()\n13. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\nNone - operates on global screen state and panel variables\n\nReturns:\nvoid - modifies game display buffers\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Experience bar color varies by mode (0x1c for mode 6, 0x1d otherwise)\n- Loot bar drawn only if width > height calculation result\n- Panel uses fixed screen height offset -0xd (13 pixels from bottom)\n- Color modes: 0x1c=green, 0x1d=blue",
