      "comment": "Render slider gauge indicator on main game screen.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Query viewport object via FUN_6fb62880 and retrieve width/height from offsets 0xc-0xd\n2. Extract viewport values: current value at 0xc, max value at 0xd, min value at 0xc\n3. Calculate bar span: barEndPos = current - (current - 1), gives range of values\n4. Compute offset: rangeValue = max < currentValue ? (max - currentValue) : 0\n5. Initialize wchar_t buffer (100 characters) with Unicode constructor loop\n6. Query mouse position: nMouseXPos = FUN_6fb8f680(), nMouseYPos = FUN_6fb8f690()\n7. Validate mouse bounds: X in [width/2 - 0x92, width/2 - 0x17], Y in [height - 0x2b, height - 0x22]\n8. If in bounds: format display string via Ordinal_10004, sprintf to buffer, draw label via Ordinal_10129\n9. Check bar length nonzero, if yes continue to gauge rendering\n10. For overflow check: if rangeValue > 0x226b901 then shift right by 7 bits\n11. Calculate bar pixels: (rangeValue * 0x77) / barLength, clamp max to 0x77\n12. Query slider width via Ordinal_10629, verify mouse within parameter bounds\n13. Draw gauge lines: two horizontal white (0xff,0xff) lines at Y=(height-0x26) and Y=(height-0x25)\n\nParameters:\n(implicit) viewport data via FUN_6fb62880 return - EAX contains viewport handle\n(implicit) g_dwScreenWidth global - screen width for bound checks\n(implicit) g_dwScreenHeight global - screen height for positioning\n\nReturns:\nvoid - renders gauge to backbuffer, modifies screen pixels\n\nSpecial Cases:\nEmpty range: barLength == 0 skips gauge rendering\nOverflow: rangeValue > 0x226b901 triggers bit shift scaling\nClamped: bar pixels > 0x77 reset to 0 to prevent overflow\nMouse out of bounds: conditional rendering skipped\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x92, 0x17 - horizontal offsets from screen center for bounds\n0x2b, 0x22 - vertical offsets from screen height for bounds\n0x33 - vertical offset for label positioning\n0x90 - alternate horizontal offset in gauge draw path\n0x25, 0x26 - gauge line Y coordinates relative to height\n0x77 - maximum bar pixel width (119)\n0x226b901 - overflow threshold requiring bit shift\n0xff - white color value for gauge lines\n0x7 - bit shift count for scaling",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "STRUCT_Skill", "PARAM_0", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
