      "comment": "Build display strings for active key bindings in game UI\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize Unicode output buffer (szOutputBuffer) with 400 Unicode characters\n2. Initialize temporary stack buffer (dwTemp) with 30 Unicode characters\n3. Call Ordinal_10004 (likely GetStringPrefix) to get prefix string\n4. Copy prefix into szOutputBuffer via Unicode::strcpy\n5. Lookup primary keybind ID for command 0x23 via LookupKeyBindingByCommandId\n6. If keybind exists (wKeyBindId != 0xffff):\n   - Clear temporary buffer via REP STOSD loop\n   - Get string ID for keybind via GetKeyBindingStringId\n   - Call Ordinal_10004 with string ID to get localized key name\n   - Format into temporary buffer via Unicode::sprintf\n   - Concatenate to main output via Unicode::strcat\n7. Setup secondary keybind lookup (EDX=0, ECX=0x23)\n8. Lookup secondary keybind ID via LookupKeyBindingByCommandId\n9. If secondary keybind exists (wKeyBindId != 0xffff):\n   - Clear buffer achTempBuffer via REP STOSD\n   - Get string ID for secondary keybind\n   - Call Ordinal_10004 with string ID\n   - Format via Unicode::sprintf into achTempBuffer\n   - Concatenate via Unicode::strcat\n10. Calculate Y position: screen height - 0x17 (23 pixels from bottom)\n11. Call Ordinal_10129 to render key binding display at calculated position\n12. Return void\n\nParameters:\n(none - implicit parameters via ESI/EDI unaffected registers)\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If primary keybind not found (0xffff), skips first binding display\n- If secondary keybind not found, skips second binding display\n- Uses both Unicode and ANSI string operations for compatibility\n- Stack layout includes 0x1cc bytes allocated for Unicode buffers",
