      "comment": "Determines if screen coordinates fall within the center game panel area.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load g_dwScreenWidth and calculate center panel horizontal bounds\n2. Calculate left bound: (screen_width / 2) - 0x91\n3. Calculate right bound: (screen_width / 2) - 0x80\n4. Check if nScreenX >= left bound AND nScreenX <= right bound\n5. Load g_dwScreenHeight and calculate vertical bounds\n6. Calculate top bound: screen_height - 0x1C\n7. Calculate bottom bound: screen_height - 0x8\n8. Check if nScreenY >= top bound AND nScreenY <= bottom bound\n9. Return 1 (true) if all four bounds satisfied, else return 0 (false)\n\nParameters:\n  int nScreenX: Screen X coordinate (ECX in __fastcall)\n  int nScreenY: Screen Y coordinate (EDX in __fastcall)\n\nReturns:\n  bool: 1 if coordinates are within center panel bounds, 0 otherwise\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Center panel position depends on runtime screen resolution\n  - Bounds are fixed offsets from screen dimensions\n  - Used for UI click detection\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x91 (145 decimal): Pixel offset for left edge of center panel\n  0x80 (128 decimal): Pixel offset for right edge of center panel\n  0x1C (28 decimal): Pixel offset for top edge of center panel\n  0x8 (8 decimal): Pixel offset for bottom edge of center panel\n\nStructure Layout:\n  (Screen-space coordinates)\n  Offset | Size | Field Name | Type | Description\n  N/A    | N/A  | nScreenX   | int  | Horizontal position in screen pixels\n  N/A    | N/A  | nScreenY   | int  | Vertical position in screen pixels",
      "tags": ["PARAM_2", "PROP_LEAF"]
