      "comment": "Renders game state indicator panel positioned near screen center\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize parameter array (18 dwords) with zeros and game error state\n2. Check if key state is set (FUN_6fb5d340)\n3. If key set: Check mouse in button region relative to screen center\n   - Valid region: [screen_width/2-8, screen_width/2+5] x [height-39, height-13]\n   - If in region: state=3 (hover), else state=2 (out of region)\n4. If key not set: Same mouse check, state=1 (active) if in region, else state=0 (inactive)\n5. Call Ordinal_10072 to render panel with calculated position and state\n\nParameters: None (uses global screen dimensions)\n\nReturns: void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Panel position: screen_width/2-8, screen_height-16 (top-left corner)\n- Mouse region check applied regardless of key state\n- State values: 0=idle, 1=active_hover, 2=inactive, 3=key_active_hover\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x12 (18): Parameter array size\n- 0x15: Key state constant\n- 0x8, 0x5: Mouse region width adjustment (-8 to +5)\n- 0x27 (39): Offset from bottom for region top\n- 0xd (13): Offset from bottom for region bottom\n- 0x10 (16): Vertical padding from bottom\n- 0xffffffff: Color parameter (opaque white/no tint)\n- 5: Unknown parameter (possibly layer/priority)",
