      "comment": "Render active game panels and unit/monster selection displays.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize Storm/rendering subsystem with Ordinal_10127\n2. Retrieve current game status handle via FUN_6fb62880\n3. Extract game unit handle from status structure at offset 0x84\n4. Validate unit handle with Ordinal_10257(handle, 8) - returns non-zero if valid\n5. If invalid, set g_dwGameMode = 2 and return\n6. If valid, verify unit type with Ordinal_10751 == 0x13\n7. Check unit quality with Ordinal_10367 - abort if < 0 (invalid state)\n8. Check input state flags FUN_6fb5d340(0x1f) and FUN_6fb5d340(0x9)\n9. Set g_dwGameStateFlags based on game mode switch (modes 0-5)\n10. Initialize local panel array [18] with zero-fill using REP STOSD\n11. Set panel colors: red/green/blue/yellow to 0x80 via Ordinal_10034\n12. Loop through 3 panels: if active in state flags, render label via Ordinal_10072\n13. Query viewport dimensions from g_dwScreenWidth, g_dwScreenHeight\n14. Query panel format with Ordinal_10638(gameMode, quality, format)\n15. For each slot in viewport (count from local_104):\n    - Get unit pointer via Ordinal_10271(gameHandle, index)\n    - Validate unit with Ordinal_10707, Ordinal_10771, FUN_6fb6e180\n    - If special monster (pdwCurrentUnit match), use alternate palette\n    - Render panel with FUN_6fb92980 and unit data with FUN_6fb91bf0\n    - If unit keybindable, lookup keybinding with LookupKeyBindingByCommandId\n    - Format and display key binding string in local_1d0 (Unicode)\n16. Check if special monster selected (g_dwSelectedMonsterIndex >= 0)\n17. If selected and visible, fetch with Ordinal_10271\n18. Validate special monster with Ordinal_10768\n19. Render special monster with alternate palette\n\nParameters:\n   None - void function, reads global game state\n\nReturns:\n   None - void function\n\nSpecial Cases:\n   Game mode validation: Validates mode between 0-5 with switch statement\n   Palette colors: Uses Ordinal_10034 to create 8-bit palette entries from 24-bit RGB\n   Key binding truncation: Limits Unicode string to 0x1c (28) characters\n   Monster selection: Special rendering for g_dwSelectedMonsterIndex if >= 0\n   Stack arrays: Local arrays use 0x250 (592 bytes) of local stack space\n\nMagic Numbers:\n   0x84 - Game status structure unit handle offset\n   0x8 - Slot validation parameter for Ordinal_10257\n   0x13 - Expected unit type value from Ordinal_10751\n   0x1f - Input state check code\n   0x9 - Game state flag check code\n   0x2 - Game mode for inactive state\n   0x80 - RGB component value (128 decimal) for palette\n   0x5 - Maximum game mode value\n   0x12 - Panel data array element count (18)\n   0x20 - Y-offset increment per panel (32 pixels)\n   0x1c - Max key binding string length (28 chars)\n   0x1d - Panel display width/height (29 pixels)\n   0x29 - Y-offset base value\n   0x250 - Total stack frame size (592 bytes)",
      "tags": ["MOD_UI", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "STRUCT_Room2", "PARAM_0", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData", "PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Path", "STRUCT_Skill", "SRC_panel.cpp", "PROP_LOOPHEAVY"]
