      "comment": "Handle minimap/panel button click detection and triggering.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get current mouse coordinates via FUN_6fb8f680 (X) and FUN_6fb8f690 (Y)\n2. Calculate button region bounds: center screen ±8 pixels X, bottom area (height-0x27 to height-0x0d) Y\n3. Check if mouse is within button click region\n4. If within bounds, call FUN_6fb5d340(0x15) to check button state (0x15 likely button ID)\n5. If button active (non-zero return), call Ordinal_10004 with Y offset -0x27, then Ordinal_10129\n6. If button inactive (zero return), skip step 5 calls\n7. Both paths push dwMode1=0 and dwMode2=1 as parameters before conditional calls\n\nParameters:\nNone - reads screen state from global variables\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Button region: screen center X ±8 pixels (-8 to +5), screen height-0x27 to height-0x0d Y\n- Magic values: 0x15 (button ID), 0x27 (button Y offset), 0x0d (button height offset)\n- Two ordinal calls (10004, 10129) likely handle button rendering/state update\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n- 0x15: Button ID (likely minimap expand/collapse)\n- 0x27: Y offset for button bottom edge (39 pixels from screen height)\n- 0x0d: Button height adjustment (13 pixels)\n- 0x08, 0x05: X bounds tolerance (±8/-5 pixels from center)",
      "tags": ["PARAM_0"]
    },
