      "comment": "Validates and adjusts viewport position to stay within screen boundaries.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check IsGameSystemEnabled - if enabled, mark processed and return\n2. Validate viewport via FUN_6fb62890 - if invalid, return early\n3. Extract X (bits 0-15) and Y (bits 16-31) from element offset 0x0c\n4. Call FUN_6fb300a0 to validate bounds - if failed, set update flag and return\n5. If Y exceeds screen_height - 0x30, mark processed and return\n6. Check if X or Y violates screen boundaries (X < 0x75, X != 0xa5, Y > screen_height)\n7. Adjust position based on screen region: center, left/right, or bottom\n8. Set UI update flag and call Ordinal_511 to trigger viewport refresh\n\nParameters:\npUIElement - UIObject pointer; position coords at offset 0x0c, flags at 0x18-0x1c\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Updates element position in-place; sets global UI state flags\n\nSpecial Cases:\nEarly return if game disabled or viewport invalid; handles coordinates outside visible screen area",
