      "api_count": 2,
      "api_calls": ["InsertCacheNodeWithCookie", "InsertCacheNodeWithCookie"],
      "instructions": ["0x5F440|CALL|0x6fadb800", "0x5F445|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0x5F447|JNZ|0x6fb2f8e1", "0x5F44D|CALL|0x6fb62890", "0x5F452|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0x5F454|JNZ|0x6fb2f8e1", "0x5F45A|PUSH|EBX", "0x5F45B|PUSH|EBP", "0x5F45C|PUSH|ESI", "0x5F45D|PUSH|EDI", "0x5F45E|CALL|0x6fb62880", "0x5F463|MOV|EBP, dword ptr [ESP + 0x14]", "0x5F467|MOV|EBX, EAX", "0x5F469|MOV|EAX, [0x6fbf902c]", "0x5F46E|XOR|ESI, ESI"],
      "comment": "Processes mouse clicks on the lower UI panel (belt/skill bar area).\n\nHandles click events in different screen zones:\n- Center belt toggle button (UI ID 0x15)\n- Left skill button zone (X: 0x75-0xA5, bottom 48 pixels)\n- Right skill button zone (screenWidth-0xA5 to screenWidth-0x75, bottom 48 pixels)\n- Always-Run toggle button (center-0x91 to center-0x80, bottom 28-8 pixels)\n- Viewport interaction zone (center+0x17 to center+0x91, bottom 39-10 pixels)\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Early exit if game system disabled (IsGameSystemEnabled) or in menu state (IsGameInMenuState)\n2. Extract click coordinates from event structure: X from low word, Y from high word at offset +0xC\n3. Clear UI state change flags (g_dwUIStateChange, g_dwUIRefreshFlag)\n4. Branch based on g_dwUIUpdateFlag and g_dwGameActive:\n   a. If g_dwUIUpdateFlag set AND g_dwGameActive set:\n      - Validate click coordinates (ValidateCoordinateInBounds)\n      - If valid: send resource update based on screen state (6=SendResourceUpdate, 8=LogFiveBytePacket)\n      - Call ValidateViewportAndSendPacket, mark event processed, insert cache node\n   b. If g_dwUIUpdateFlag set but g_dwGameActive not set:\n      - Check various UI zones and toggle appropriate UI elements\n      - Toggle belt state via g_dwBeltToggleState\n   c. If g_dwUIUpdateFlag not set:\n      - Only handle left/right skill button zones\n5. Clear flags: g_dwUIUpdateFlag, g_dwGameStateFlag, g_dwAlwaysRunModeEnabled\n6. Set event result at offset +0x18 (1=processed, 0=ignored)\n\nParameters:\n  pClickEvent - Pointer to click event structure:\n    +0x0C: LOWORD=X coordinate, HIWORD=Y coordinate\n    +0x18: Result flag (set to 1 if click processed, 0 if ignored)\n    +0x1C: Secondary result (set to 0 on success)\n\nReturns:\n  void (results stored in pClickEvent structure)\n\nUI Zone Constants:\n  0x15 - Belt toggle button UI ID\n  0x03 - Skill button UI ID\n  Screen state 6 - Resource update mode\n  Screen state 8 - Packet logging mode\n  0x4C - Packet type for five-byte packet\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Returns immediately with result=0 if game disabled or in menu\n  - Multiple overlapping zones checked with priority order\n  - Always-run toggle inverts current setting via GetAlwaysRunSetting/SetAlwaysRunFlag",
      "tags": ["PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_1", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
    },
