      "comment": "Validates and processes player item state for slot management with renderer initialization\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if item type is already allocated via Ordinal_10262 - if so, return early\n2. Call FUN_6fb5d340 to check memory availability (param 9)\n3. Get system state via GetGlobalSystemState\n4. Query item unit pointer via Ordinal_10409 and apply graphics quality flag via Ordinal_10636 to local_18 buffer\n5. Retrieve item unit data via Ordinal_10271(itemType, itemId) - store in pItemUnitData\n6. If item unit exists:\n   a. Validate item stat exists via Ordinal_10600(itemStat[1]) - log critical error and terminate via FUN_6fb9a10f if NULL\n   b. Check equippable flags at offsets 0x29 and 0x2a - if set, process equip action via FUN_6fb58e40 and return\n   c. Check identify flag at offset 0x25 - if NOT set, send error (0x13) via FUN_6fb88d60 and return\n   d. Get item renderer state via FUN_6fb6e180 - if already initialized, skip processing\n   e. Initialize new renderer:\n      - Get player stat ID via Ordinal_10329(playerIndex)\n      - Get player unit ID via Ordinal_10326(playerIndex)\n      - Send network packet type 0x26 with item data via SendPacketWithSubcommand\n      - Clean up existing renderer via FUN_6fb6e120\n      - Initialize flCoordX and flY to 0.0 (coordinate placeholders)\n      - Query monster visibility data via FUN_6fb6bc60\n      - Process item rendering via FUN_6fb8d210 with zero coordinates\n      - Clear global monster visibility flag (g_dwMonsterVisible = 0)\n\nParameters:\n  nPlayerId (int, IMPLICIT ECX) - Player unit index in active roster, used for stat/ID queries\n  dwItemType (dword, IMPLICIT EDX) - Item type enumeration from D2Common item table\n  dwItemId (dword, stack at +0x4) - Item instance ID from unit memory system\n\nReturns: void (all paths return without value)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Critical item stat missing: logs error details and terminates process via FUN_6fb9a10f(0xFFFFFFFF)\n- No system memory available (FUN_6fb5d340 check fails): early return without processing\n- Item type already initialized (Ordinal_10262 returns non-zero): early return without processing\n- Invalid item flags (offset 0x25 not set): error code 0x13 sent via FUN_6fb88d60, return early\n- Renderer already initialized (FUN_6fb6e180 returns non-zero): skip initialization, return early\n- Equippable item (flags 0x29 or 0x2a set): special equip processing via FUN_6fb58e40, return early\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x29, 0x2a - Equippable/usable item flag offsets in D2Common.UnitAny structure (byte-sized flags, 0x01 = true)\n  0x25 - Identify flag offset in item unit structure (0x01 = identified item, required for processing)\n  0x26 - Network packet subcommand type for item state update packet\n  0x13 - Error code for invalid item state, passed to FUN_6fb88d60\n  0x4 - Stack cleanup on return (RET 0x4 - remove 4-byte parameter from stack)\n  0x18 - Local stack allocation (24 bytes for graphics buffer)",
