      "comment": "Processes player item state when game system is inactive and not in menu.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if game system is enabled via IsGameSystemEnabled\n2. If enabled, return early (do nothing when system active)\n3. Check if game is in menu state via IsGameInMenuState\n4. If in menu state, return early (do nothing in menus)\n5. Check global flag g_byItemProcessingEnabled == 1\n6. If flag not set, return early\n7. Get game context pointer via GetGameContext\n8. Extract item type from game context at offset +0x84\n9. Call ProcessPlayerItemState with context, item type, and constant 1\n\nParameters:\n  None (void function)\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - All three conditions must pass: system disabled, not in menu, flag enabled\n  - Offset 0x84 in game context appears to be default/current item type\n  - Third parameter to ProcessPlayerItemState is always 1 (item ID or mode)\n  - extraout_var (phantom): Decompiler artifact for high 24 bits of EAX after bool return;\n    IsGameInMenuState returns bool but CONCAT31 shows full EAX treatment - ignore this variable\n\nCallees:\n  IsGameSystemEnabled - Returns non-zero if game system active\n  IsGameInMenuState - Returns true if in menu state (0x11) or NULL context\n  GetGameContext - Returns pointer to global game context structure\n  ProcessPlayerItemState - __fastcall(nPlayerId in ECX, dwItemType in EDX, dwItemId on stack)\n\nGlobal References:\n  g_byItemProcessingEnabled (0x6fbf9039) - Byte flag, must be 1 to allow processing",
