      "comment": "Conditionally triggers player item state processing if game is active\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if game system is enabled via IsGameSystemEnabled - if enabled, return early\n2. Check if game is in menu state via IsGameInMenuState - if in menu, return early\n3. Check g_fItemProcessingEnabled flag (must equal 0x01) - if not set, return early\n4. Get game context pointer via GetGameContext\n5. Extract item type from context+0x84 offset (player inventory slot type)\n6. Call ProcessPlayerItemState with player context, item type, and mode 2\n\nParameters:\n  (none - uses global state)\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Game system enabled: Immediate return, no processing\n  - Game in menu state (0x11): Immediate return, no processing\n  - Item processing flag not set: Immediate return, no processing\n  - All checks pass: Processes player item with mode 2 (inventory update)\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x84 - Offset of inventory slot type field in game context structure\n  0x01 - Required value of g_fItemProcessingEnabled for processing\n  2 - Item processing mode parameter (inventory state update)\n\nGlobals Used:\n  g_fItemProcessingEnabled (0x6fbf903a) - Item processing enable flag (byte)\n\nFunction Classification: Thunk/Wrapper - validates preconditions before calling ProcessPlayerItemState",
