      "comment": "Attempts to process player item state with mode 3 if all preconditions are met.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call IsGameSystemEnabled to check if game system is active\n2. If system enabled (non-zero), exit early - no item processing during system events\n3. Call IsGameInMenuState to check if game is in menu state (0x11)\n4. If in menu state (non-zero), exit early - no item processing in menus\n5. Check g_fItemProcessingEnabled flag at 0x6fbf903b for value 0x01\n6. If flag not set (not 0x01), exit early - item processing disabled\n7. Get game context pointer via GetGameContext\n8. Extract player item type from game context at offset +0x84\n9. Call ProcessPlayerItemState(pGameContext, dwItemType, 3) with mode 3\n\nParameters:\n  None (void)\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Early exit if game system is enabled (IsGameSystemEnabled returns non-zero)\n- Early exit if game is in menu state (IsGameInMenuState returns true)\n- Early exit if g_fItemProcessingEnabled != 0x01\n- Only called via thunk at 0x6fafd5b0\n- ProcessPlayerItemState called with hardcoded mode 3 (item state processing)\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x6fbf903b - g_fItemProcessingEnabled: byte flag controlling item processing (0x01 = enabled)\n0x84 - Offset in game context structure to player item type field\n0x3 - Item processing mode passed to ProcessPlayerItemState\n\nCalling Convention:\n__stdcall with no parameters, called via JMP thunk",
