      "instructions": ["0x600A0|SUB|ESP, 0x108", "0x600A6|MOV|EDX, dword ptr [0x6fbb7548]", "0x600AC|LEA|EAX, [ESP]", "0x600B0|PUSH|ESI", "0x600B1|XOR|ESI, ESI", "0x600B3|MOV|SI, word ptr [ECX + 0xc]", "0x600B7|PUSH|EDI", "0x600B8|MOV|EDI, dword ptr [ECX + 0xc]", "0x600BB|MOV|ECX, dword ptr [0x6fbdc018]", "0x600C1|PUSH|EAX", "0x600C2|PUSH|ECX", "0x600C3|PUSH|EDX", "0x600C4|SHR|EDI, 0x10", "0x600C7|CALL|0x6fb98aa6", "0x600CC|MOV|EAX, [0x6fbf9020]"],
      "comment": "Validate if screen coordinates are within active game or UI bounds.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract X coordinate (lower 16-bit) and Y coordinate (upper 16-bit) from coordinate pointer + 0xc\n2. Call Ordinal_10638 with game mode and graphics quality flags to prepare render data\n3. Check if game is active (g_dwGameActive == 0 indicates menu/UI screen)\n   - If INACTIVE: Validate coordinates against menu UI bounds (hardcoded offsets)\n     - Min X: g_dwScreenWidth/2 + 0x17, Max X: g_dwScreenWidth/2 + 0x91\n     - Min Y: g_dwScreenHeight - 0x30, Max Y: g_dwScreenHeight - 0x27\n   - If ACTIVE: Validate against game UI panel bounds\n     - Panel index = (dwMode & 0xff) - 4 \n     - Bounds loaded from aiStack_100 array: [MinX, unused, MinY, MaxY]\n     - X: aiStack_100[index*4] <= X <= local_cc\n     - Y: aiStack_100[index*4+2] <= Y <= local_c4\n4. Return 1 if coordinates within bounds, 0 otherwise\n\nParameters:\n- nCoordPtr (int, __fastcall ECX): Pointer to coordinate structure (X at +0xc offset as packed shorts)\n\nReturns:\n- 1: Coordinates are within valid bounds\n- 0: Coordinates are outside bounds\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Coordinate encoding: X in lower 16-bit, Y in upper 16-bit of 32-bit value\n- Menu bounds use hardcoded offsets relative to screen dimensions\n- Game bounds array index calculated as (mode & 0xFF) - 4 for up to 13 panels",
