      "comment": "Initialize game viewport configuration state by invoking Storm.dll function.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Push three zero parameters (context flags, reserved, flags) onto stack\n2. Call Ordinal_10034 (Storm.GetDisplayMode - retrieves display configuration)\n3. Store AL register result (display mode byte) to global g_byViewportConfigState\n4. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\nNone (void function)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Updates g_byViewportConfigState with display mode configuration from Storm.dll\n\nSpecial Cases:\nFunction always called before viewport rendering initialization (InitializeViewportRendering).\nResult stored as single byte despite EAX return value (upper 3 bytes discarded).\nZero parameters to Storm.GetDisplayMode indicate query-only operation (no flags set).\n\nRelated Functions:\n- InitializeViewportRendering() - Caller; uses this function to initialize display state first\n- RenderPlayerStatisticsOverlay() - References g_byViewportConfigState indirectly via rendering logic\n- Ordinal_10034() - Storm.dll display mode query function (3 parameters: reserved, reserved, flags)",
