      "comment": "Traverse and process linked list nodes, calling Ordinal_10043 for each entry.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load linked list head pointer from g_pLinkedListHead\n2. If list is empty (NULL), zero the global and return\n3. Loop: Get next node pointer from current node at offset 0xcd\n4. Call Ordinal_10043(0x107, 0) for processing each node\n5. Continue until next pointer is NULL\n6. Store final pointer value to g_pLinkedListHead and return\n\nParameters:\n(none)\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Empty list: Returns immediately after zeroing g_pLinkedListHead\n- List structure: Next pointer at offset 0xcd (205 bytes from node start)",
