      "comment": "Constructs linked list of player slot structures. Iterates through player roster, allocates memory for each slot, initializes slot data with player attributes and configuration values.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Clear existing linked list (walk through g_pLinkedListHead chain, deallocate each node)\n2. Initialize cursor base offset to 0x5a, get first player roster entry\n3. Loop through player roster:\n   - Return if end of roster and player count >= 9\n   - Allocate 0x14c bytes for new slot structure (via Ordinal_10042)\n   - Zero initialize allocated buffer (52 dwords + 1 byte)\n   - Set slot structure header fields (ID, type flags, base offset)\n   - Query player slot status checks (access privilege, board status, slot status)\n   - Set slot structure status fields based on privilege checks (result & 0x2 + base value)\n   - Copy player roster name to slot structure (src GetRosterFieldAt0x66, dst puVar7+0xa0)\n   - Set player unit type and field data (unit type, field 0x20, field 0x24)\n   - Insert new slot structure into linked list tail\n   - Increment cursor base offset by 0x26, advance to next roster entry\n\nParameters:\n  (void) - Operates on globals: g_pLinkedListHead (linked list head), roster entry state\n\nReturns:\n  void - Modifies global player slot list structure\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x5a - Initial slot cursor offset value\n  0x14c - Size of allocated slot structure buffer\n  0x34 - Count of dwords to zero (slot structure initialization)\n  0x107, 0x14c - Ordinal parameters (memory management calls)\n  0xcd - Offset within slot/node structure for linked list pointer\n  0xc9 - Offset for cursor position within slot structure\n  0xa0 - Offset for player name buffer within slot structure",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "STRUCT_Room2", "STRUCT_Room1", "STRUCT_ItemData", "PARAM_0", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData", "PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Path", "STRUCT_Skill", "PROP_LOOPHEAVY"]
