      "comment": "Render the character creation screen with UI frames and player slot information.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize 4 UI frame positions for character selection class display (top-left, top-right, bottom-left, bottom-right)\n2. Retrieve current player character data via GetPlayerTargetDataByInfo()\n3. If player name exists, convert to Unicode and display centered at top (max width 0xb)\n4. Initialize linked list head for player slots\n5. For each of 8 player slots: fetch node, validate player ID with CheckPlayerIdDuplicate()\n   a. Compare current vs first player ID to detect duplicates (sets status code 0x2)\n   b. Check unit identifiers with CompareUnitIdentifiers() for conflicts (status 0x1)\n   c. Set status 0x8 for normal valid slots\n   d. Render frame data, field indicators, skills with FUN_6fb309e0/FUN_6fb30b10/FUN_6fb308f0\n   e. If duplicate flag set and slot has special flag, render extra data via FUN_6fb30e00\n   f. Advance to next player slot in linked list\n6. Display \"SELECT\" button frame at bottom right (position 0x116, 0x1a5)\n7. If button clicked via FUN_6fb31020(), render zoom animation with Ordinal_10129()\n\nParameters:\nNone (uses global UI state and player slot data via GetPlayerNodeNext, GetPlayerTargetDataByInfo)\n\nReturns:\nNone (renders to screen)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- First player ID (-1) skipped in loop, slots 2-9 processed\n- Character name truncated if wider than 0xb (width 0xc triggers Ordinal_10127)\n- Button click triggers animation parameters: Y offset 0x182 (adjusted for UI offset)\n- Hardcore mode flag (g_bHardcoreFlagEnabled) affects secondary frame display",
      "tags": ["PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Path", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "STRUCT_Skill", "PARAM_0", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
