      "comment": "Display unit inventory at screen coordinates with color key.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize 18-element DWORD buffer (adwItemBuffer) on stack to zero\n   - Use EDI pointer arithmetic and REP STOSD for efficient zeroing\n   - Clears 0x12 (18) elements = 72 bytes total\n2. Set buffer[3] = 0 (terminator/padding field)\n3. Set buffer[2] = dwColor (color override key passed to renderer)\n4. Set buffer[1] = dwUnitId (unit identifier/reference)\n5. Retrieve X offset from global g_dwUIXOffset\n6. Retrieve Y offset from global g_dwUIYOffset\n7. Call D2Common.GetUnitInventory (Ordinal_10072) with:\n   - Buffer address (pointer to adwItemBuffer)\n   - Adjusted X = g_dwUIXOffset + nScreenX\n   - Adjusted Y = nScreenY - g_dwUIYOffset\n   - Color key 0xffffffff (no override)\n   - Priority 5 (standard UI layer)\n   - Flags 0 (default behavior)\n8. Inventory items rendered by callee, function returns immediately\n\nParameters:\ndwUnitId (dword): Unit ID/entity pointer in ECX register\nnScreenX (int): Viewport X coordinate in EDX register\nnScreenY (int): Viewport Y coordinate on stack [ESP+0x58]\ndwColor (dword): Color key for rendering on stack [ESP+0x54]\n\nReturns:\nvoid - All work delegated to D2Common.GetUnitInventory ordinal call\nInventory structure populated in-place and rendered by callee\n\nSpecial Cases:\nBuffer layout: 18 DWORDs (72 bytes) for inventory item display\nMagic numbers: 0x12 = 18 items, 0xffffffff = no color override, 5 = UI priority\nScreen coordinate adjustment required due to viewport offset globals",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PARAM_4", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
