      "comment": "Constructs a formatted UI label string and displays it on the interface at specified coordinates.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize 100 Unicode characters in stack buffer at [ESP + 0x24]\n2. Initialize 10 Unicode characters in stack buffer at [ESP + 0x10]\n3. Call Ordinal_10004 (UI resource lock/reference)\n4. Call strncpy to copy label text to destination\n5. Call Ordinal_10004 twice to format and concatenate strings\n6. Call wsprintfA to format dwLabelId as decimal string using format string g_szFormatPercent\n7. Call win2Unicode to convert formatted ANSI string to Unicode (max 9 chars)\n8. Call strcat to concatenate Unicode string to display buffer\n9. Call Ordinal_10117 (D2UI.TakeScreenCoord) with adjusted Y coordinate (dwYOffset - g_dwUIYOffset) and widget ID\n10. Call display function through ESI to render label on screen\n\nParameters:\n- dwLabelId (uint, ECX): Label resource ID to format and display\n- dwYOffset (int, EDX): Y coordinate offset for label placement\n- dwWidgetId (uint, Stack[0x4]): Widget identifier for the UI control\n\nReturns:\n- None (void)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Magic number 0x140 (320 bytes) is total stack allocation for three buffers\n- Unicode buffers: 200 chars (0x18c bytes) + 20 chars (0x28 bytes)\n- ANSI buffer: 100 chars (0x64 bytes)\n- Y coordinate is offset by g_dwUIYOffset, indicating screen coordinate system correction\n- The function performs UI coordinate transformation before calling display routine\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n- 0x140 (320): Total stack allocation size\n- 0x64 (100): ANSI formatting buffer size in characters\n- 100: Count of Unicode characters to initialize (200-byte buffer = 100 wide chars)\n- 10: Count of Unicode characters for temporary buffer (20-byte buffer = 10 wide chars)\n- 0x9 (9): Maximum characters for number formatting\n- 0x10a (266): UI coordinate offset constant\n- 0x14 (20): Lock/reference count for ordinal call\n- 0xd28, 0xf9d, 0xf9b: Internal ordinal parameters\n\nRelated Functions:\n- Ordinal_10004 (UI resource management)\n- Ordinal_10117 (D2UI screen coordinate handling)\n- wsprintfA (ANSI string formatting)\n- Unicode string operations (initialization, copying, concatenation)",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PARAM_3", "STRUCT_Skill", "STRUCT_ItemData", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
