      "comment": "Processes input Unicode string with character filtering based on mode\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize 98-character Unicode buffer (aUnicodeBuffer) with constructor calls\n2. Convert input string szInput to Unicode in buffer (toUnicode call, max 100 chars)\n3. Initialize 5-character temp buffer (aUStack_d8) with constructors\n4. Load config value from g_szEllipsisString into dwConfig\n5. Branch on nHighFilter: if zero, use threshold 0x88; else use 0x60\n6. Call Ordinal_10121 (character generation) repeatedly\n7. Filter loop: while character > threshold, move backward and write 0x0000 (null wide char)\n8. Convert config bytes to Unicode (5 chars max)\n9. Concatenate temp buffer to output using strcat (unaff_EDI, unaff_ESI from caller)\n10. Calculate final Y offset by subtracting g_dwUIYOffset and decrementing by 2\n11. Call Ordinal_10117 (output rendering) with offset, length, and zero flag\n\nParameters:\nszInput (char *) - IMPLICIT ECX: pointer to source ANSI string to convert\nnMaxLen (int) - IMPLICIT EDX: maximum length for buffer (100 chars)\nnOutputLen (int) - Stack[4]: length parameter for output operation\nnHighFilter (int) - Stack[8]: filter mode flag (0=use 0x88 threshold, non-zero=use 0x60)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - function modifies global state and output strings via strcat/ordinal calls\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Early exit at LAB_6fb30ad0 if character code below threshold on first check\n- Padding flag bPadding (byte) initialized but not used (compiler optimization)\n- unaff_ESI and unaff_EDI are preserved caller registers, not renamed (unaffected registers)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x88 - High filter threshold character code (136 decimal)\n0x60 - Low filter threshold character code (96 decimal)\n0x64 - Buffer size constant (100 decimal, 100 Unicode chars = 0xc8 bytes)\n0x5 - Temp buffer size (5 wide chars maximum)\n0x2 - Offset adjustment for Y coordinate calculation\n0x0 - Null wide character terminator for buffer clearing",
