      "comment": "Dispatch player slot UI rendering based on flag type and widget state.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate dwFlags is in range [0, 6] - if out of range, return\n2. Lookup jump table entry for dwFlags value (0x6fb30b78 table)\n3. Load magic constant based on flag type:\n   - 0x103a (4154), 0x103b (4155), 0x103d (4157), 0x103e (4158) - player slot variants\n   - 0x103c (4156), 0x2770 (10096), 0x2771 (10097) - alternate slot types\n4. Retrieve UI Y base offset from global g_dwUIYOffset (0x6fbfd800)\n5. Calculate adjusted Y coordinate: nAdjustedY = nYOffset - g_dwUIYOffset\n6. Push parameters: nAdjustedY, dwWidgetId, 0 (unused flag)\n7. Call Ordinal_10004 (D2Win.GetDifficulty) with nAdjustedY - process difficulty state\n8. Call Ordinal_10117 (D2Win.GetSystemTime) with nAdjustedY, dwWidgetId, dwZero - sync timing\n9. Return\n\nParameters:\n- dwFlags (ECX, IMPLICIT): Slot type selector [0-6] - controls which variant to load\n- nYOffset (EDX, IMPLICIT): Y coordinate in screen space\n- dwWidgetId (stack param): Widget state flags affecting rendering\n\nReturns:\n- void (no return value)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- dwFlags >= 7: Jump table escape - immediate return (no slot rendering)\n- Jump table at 0x6fb30b78 with 7 entries (one per flag value 0-6)\n- Ordinal functions use implicit register parameters ECX, EDX per __fastcall convention",
