      "comment": "Draw UI text element centered on screen based on element code.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize X offset to 0xBE (190) and flags to 0 by default\n2. Switch on element code (param_2) to determine text position and flags\n3. If code is 1: Check validation (param_5)\n   - If validation is -1, return without drawing\n   - If param_4 is 0, set flags=0x8, X=0xAF (175)\n   - Otherwise set flags=0x2, X=0x9B (155)\n4. For codes 0,2,3,4: Use defaults (X=0xBE, flags=0)\n5. For invalid code: Call error handler (Ordinal_10127), return\n6. Add UI Y/X offset (global g_dwUIXOffset, g_dwUIYOffset)\n7. Get text string from Ordinal_10004\n8. Call DrawCenteredText with calculated position and flags\n9. Return\n\nParameters:\n- dwParam1 (uint): Unused parameter\n- dwElementCode (uint): Element identifier (0-5)\n- nY (int): Base Y coordinate\n- nFlags (int): Conditional flag (0 or non-zero)\n- wValidate (short): Validation code (checks for -1)\n\nReturns:\n- void (no return value)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Validation code -1 on element code 1 causes early return\n- Element codes outside 0-5 trigger error handler\n- Different draw flags based on param_4 value on code 1\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0xBE (190): Default X offset\n- 0xAF (175): X offset when code 1, param_4 = 0\n- 0x9B (155): X offset when code 1, param_4 != 0\n- 0x8: Draw flag value A\n- 0x2: Draw flag value B\n- 0x35 (53): Right edge offset\n- -2: Y adjustment\n- 0x6fb30c40: Jump table base\n- 0x6fbfd7fc: Global g_dwUIXOffset\n- 0x6fbfd800: Global g_dwUIYOffset",
