      "comment": "Render character selection slots with validation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize local slot array (18 integers, 72 bytes)\n2. Iterate through 5 character slots starting at dialog base + 8\n3. For each slot, validate slot type (1-4) with bounds checking:\n   - Type 1: Character class (levels 4-7)\n   - Type 2: Experience class (levels 0xC-0xF), check video flag\n   - Type 3: Difficulty (levels 0-3)\n   - Type 4: Experience difficulty (levels 8-0xB)\n4. For slots with type=1 (character):\n   - Validate unit stat < 9\n   - Check player skill resource availability\n   - Set viewport state if valid or error condition met\n5. Call rendering function for each slot with UI coordinates\n\nParameters:\n- IMPLICIT ECX (nDialogPtr): Pointer to dialog structure base\n  Offset + 8: Slot data array (5 slots × 32 bytes)\n  Offset + 0xBD: Unit stat field\n  Offset + 0xC5: Resource reference field\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Slot type != 1 OR field[4] == 1: Skip rendering call\n- Video flag check (type 2): Early exit if flag clear\n- Character validation: Checks multiple failure conditions (unit stat, skill resources)\n- Bounds clamping: Invalid level values clamped to defaults (type 1→4, type 2→0xC, type 4→8)\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n- 0x5: Number of slots to iterate (5 slots)\n- 0x12: Array initialization loop count (18 dwords)\n- 0x8: Offset to first slot data\n- 0x1C: Size per field at offset [ESP + 0x1C]\n- 0xBD: Dialog offset for unit stat field\n- 0xC5: Dialog offset for resource field\n- 0x9: Unit stat threshold\n- 0x13: UI Y coordinate adjustment\n- 0x14: Render box dimensions (20×20 pixels)",
