      "comment": "Validate duplicate player slot IDs and display error messages for conflicts.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize slot IDs table (g_anPlayerSlotIds) with 0xffff sentinel values (8 entries)\n2. Iterate player slot nodes via GetPlayerNodeNext, store each node's duplicate check result\n3. Loop through filled slots, compare adjacent slot IDs for duplicates\n4. If duplicate found (slot[i] != slot[i+1] and slot[i] != 0xffff):\n   - Initialize local UI buffer array (18 dwords) with zeros\n   - Copy UI asset ID (g_dwUIAssetId) to buffer[1]\n   - Call Ordinal_10072 to render UI element 1 at position (g_dwUIXOffset+0x0c, Y)\n   - Set buffer[2] to 1, call Ordinal_10072 to render UI element 2 at position (g_dwUIXOffset+0x10b, Y)\n   - Y position increments by 0x26 pixels per slot iteration\n\nParameters:\n  None - uses global player slot array at g_anPlayerSlotIds (8 slots max)\n  Global dependencies: g_dwUIXOffset, g_dwUIYOffset, g_dwUIAssetId\n\nReturns:\n  void - no return value, side effects render UI error messages for duplicate detection\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Empty player list: skips duplicate check loop\n  - All empty slots (0xffff): skips error UI rendering\n  - First call with no duplicates: initializes slot array only",
