      "comment": "Test if current mouse cursor is within a UI rectangle.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get current mouse X coordinate via FUN_6fb8f680()\n2. Get current mouse Y coordinate via FUN_6fb8f690()\n3. Check if mouse X is within [rectX + g_dwUIXOffset, rectX + g_dwUIXOffset + rectWidth]\n   - If mouse X < minimum or > maximum, return 0 (not in rect)\n4. Check if mouse Y is within [rectY - g_dwUIYOffset - rectHeight, rectY - g_dwUIYOffset]\n   - If mouse Y < minimum or > maximum, return 0 (not in rect)\n5. All bounds validated, return 1 (point is inside rectangle)\n\nParameters:\n- nRectX (ECX, dword): X offset of rectangle in UI coordinate system\n- nRectY (EDX, dword): Y offset of rectangle in UI coordinate system\n- nRectWidth (Stack[0x4], dword): Width of rectangle in pixels\n- nRectHeight (Stack[0x8], dword): Height of rectangle in pixels\n\nReturns:\n- EAX = 1 if mouse cursor is within rectangle bounds\n- EAX = 0 if mouse cursor is outside rectangle bounds\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Uses global offsets g_dwUIXOffset and g_dwUIYOffset for coordinate system translation\n- Rectangle bounds are inclusive on all sides\n- Y-axis may be inverted from typical screen coordinates\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x6fbfd7fc: Address of g_dwUIXOffset global\n- 0x6fbfd800: Address of g_dwUIYOffset global",
