      "comment": "Initializes and calculates viewport dimensions for UI panel display\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize local Unicode string buffer aUnicodeBuffer1 (200-element Unicode array)\n2. Call Ordinal_10004() - Unknown, appears to initialize or modify state (documented as unknown ordinal)\n3. Copy string data using strcpy from szSourceBuffer to szDestBuffer\n4. Call Ordinal_10121() - Unknown, appears to retrieve frame type/dimension information (documented as unknown ordinal)\n5. If wFrameIndex is non-zero, initialize second Unicode buffer (aUStack_c8) and repeat steps 2-4\n6. Determine viewport dimensions based on nOffsetY (panel mode):\n   - If nOffsetY == 0: use width 0x23 (35 pixels), height 0x1e (30 pixels)\n   - Else: use width 0x2a (42 pixels), height 0xf (15 pixels)\n7. Select effective height: max(iVar1, iVar6) from ordinal return values\n8. Extract high byte from effective height via arithmetic right shift by 8\n9. Call FUN_6fb92980() to render viewport with calculated coordinates and dimensions\n\nParameters:\n- dwPanelHandle (ECX): Panel identifier/handle\n- wFrameIndex (DX): Frame index selector (0=single frame, non-zero=multi-frame variant)\n- nOffsetX (stack +0x4): Horizontal offset adjustment\n- nOffsetY (stack +0x8): Vertical offset adjustment / panel mode selector\n\nReturns:\n- void (modifies UI viewport state through FUN_6fb92980 call)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- szSourceBuffer, szDestBuffer (EDI, ESI) must be initialized by caller\n- Unknown ordinals Ordinal_10004 and Ordinal_10121 not in D2 reference (need further analysis)\n- Magic width values: 0x23 (standard), 0x2a (alternate)\n- Magic height values: 0x1e (standard), 0xf (alternate)\n- Function uses __fastcall convention: dwPanelHandle in ECX, wFrameIndex in DX",
