      "comment": "Render character selection panel with interactive buttons and character validation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize 3x Unicode buffers for character display data\n2. Load initial player node and current game state\n3. Check game unit stat availability via Ordinal_10342 (D2Common.GetUnitStat)\n4. Loop through player roster nodes, fetching stored field data\n5. For each roster position, test mouse coordinates against 5 button regions\n6. On button hit: validate player access, validate character slot state, check roster availability\n7. Build character info strings (name, level, experience) via Unicode::toUnicode/sprintf\n8. Validate character data integrity (compare unit identifiers, check access privileges)\n9. Render text strings at calculated positions using Ordinal_10117/Ordinal_10121 (UI frame management)\n10. Return after processing entire roster or on access validation failure\n\nParameters:\n(none - uses global state: g_pLinkedListHead, g_dwUIXOffset, g_dwUIYOffset, g_byViewportConfigState)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - renders directly to screen buffer, modifies global viewport state\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If roster name is unavailable, substitutes s_ERROR_PLAYER_NAME_6fbb7818 (\"ERROR\")\n- Phantom variables (local_38X) are compiler-optimized temporaries, not visible in decompiled code\n- Mouse hit tests use bounding boxes: X=[offset+0x24, offset+0x8c], Y=[offset-0x1a, offset]\n- Button states: 1=create, 2=play, 3=delete, 4=exit\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x0c9 - PlayerSlotNode field offset for Y coordinate\n0x0cd - PlayerSlotNode field offset for next node link\n0x0bd - Roster array base field offset  \n0xbd - Character level/stat data field\n0x24, 0x8c - Viewport X-axis button boundaries (relative to g_dwUIXOffset)\n0x1a - Viewport Y-axis button top boundary offset\n0x14 - Button height (pixels)\n0x80 - Buffer capacity (Unicode chars for name display)\n0x28, 0x34 - Button array stride for iteration (5 buttons max)",
