      "comment": "Initializes the character selection display with viewport dimensions and renders UI panels.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if nMode is 0 (initial setup mode)\n2. Call CalculateViewportDimensions to adjust viewport size based on mode\n3. Initialize Unicode string buffer (200 characters) by calling Unicode constructors (100 iterations)\n4. Call Ordinal_10004 to set initial state\n5. Call Unicode::strcpy to copy string data from szSource to szDest\n6. Call Ordinal_10121 to finalize string setup\n7. Calculate Y offset: nYOffset = nBaseY (or nAltY if mode != 0) - g_dwUIYOffset\n8. Call Ordinal_10004 with Y offset and extra parameter\n9. Call Ordinal_10117 to render the UI panel at calculated coordinates\n10. If mode != 0, repeat steps 3-9 with nAltY instead of nBaseY\n\nParameters:\n  nViewportHandle (ECX, dword): Viewport/UI element handle\n  nMode (DX, short): Display mode (0=base, non-zero=alternate)\n  nX (Stack[0x4], int): Base X coordinate\n  dwOffset (Stack[0x8], dword): Coordinate offset value\n  nBaseY (Stack[0xc], int): Primary Y coordinate\n  nAltY (Stack[0x10], int): Alternate Y coordinate (used when nMode != 0)\n  dwExtra (Stack[0x14], dword): Extra parameter passed to rendering ordinals\n\nReturns:\n  void - Function returns after configuring viewport and rendering\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - When nMode == 0: Only base Y coordinate is used, single initialization pass\n  - When nMode != 0: Both base and alternate Y coordinates are processed in sequence\n  - Unicode buffer sized exactly 200 characters (0x64 = 100 * 2 bytes)\n  - Y offset calculation uses arithmetic right shift (SAR) by 1 bit (division by 2)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x64 (100): Loop iteration count for Unicode buffer initialization\n  0x2: Unicode character size increment\n  0x1: Mode check flag (zero = false, non-zero = true)\n  0xcc: Stack frame size allocation\n  SAR by 0x1: Y coordinate adjustment (divide by 2)",
