      "instructions": ["0x620A0|SUB|ESP, 0x214", "0x620A6|PUSH|EBX", "0x620A7|PUSH|EBP", "0x620A8|PUSH|ESI", "0x620A9|PUSH|EDI", "0x620AA|CALL|0x6fb8f680", "0x620AF|XOR|ECX, ECX", "0x620B1|MOV|ESI, EAX", "0x620B3|CALL|0x6fadf290", "0x620B8|MOV|EBX, dword ptr [0x6fbf9094]", "0x620BE|XOR|EBP, EBP", "0x620C0|MOV|EDI, EAX", "0x620C2|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x14], EBX", "0x620C6|MOV|dword ptr [0x6fbf90b0], EBP", "0x620CC|CALL|0x6fb62880"],
      "comment": "Handles mouse click events on the party panel UI for multiplayer games.\nProcesses button clicks for close, options, and player slot interactions.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get current cursor position and first player node\n2. Store linked list head and reset hardcore flag\n3. Get game context for later validation\n4. Early exit: If cursor X >= screen center, mark event as unhandled (offset +0x18 = 0)\n5. Check close button bounds (g_dwUIXOffset + 0x116 to +0x136, Y: 0x185 to 0x1a5 adjusted)\n   - If clicked: ProcessUIStateChange(0x16,1,0), clear targeting, mark handled\n6. Check options button bounds (g_dwUIXOffset + 0xe3 to +0x118, Y: 0x18 to 0x23 adjusted)\n   - If clicked and player ID valid: ProcessPlayerDisconnection(), mark handled\n7. If g_bSlotInteractionFlag == 0: Reset interaction state for all slots in linked list\n8. Otherwise iterate player nodes and slot entries (5 slots per node, 0x20 stride):\n   - For each slot, check if cursor within button bounds\n   - Switch on button type (piVar13[1]):\n     Case 1: Party invite - ProcessPlayerRemovalRequest, CheckPlayerSlotAccess\n     Case 2: Loot toggle - ProcessUnitForNetworkSync, ValidatePlayerSlotStatus  \n     Case 3: Hostile toggle - ProcessEntityNetworkUpdate, CheckPlayerAccessPrivilege\n     Case 4: Squelch toggle - Build \"/squelch \" or \"/unsquelch \" + player name command\n9. If action successful, increment slot state by 2\n10. Clear targeting state and mark event as handled\n\nParameters:\n  dwInputEventPtr - Pointer to input event structure\n    +0x18: Event handled flag (1=handled, 0=not handled)\n    +0x1c: Reserved/secondary flag (set to 0)\n\nReturns:\n  void - Results stored in input event structure\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Screen width check prevents interaction when cursor on right half\n  - Level 9+ required for party invite actions\n  - Room and DRLG validation required for party invites\n  - Squelch command built as \"/squelch [playername]\" or \"/unsquelch [playername]\"\n  - FogAssert triggered if linked list entry lookup fails\n\nLinked List Node Layout (stride 0x20 per slot, 5 slots):\n  +0x00: Interaction flag\n  +0x04: Button X position  \n  +0x08: Button Y position\n  +0x10: Base pointer for slot data\n  +0x14: Button type (1=invite, 2=loot, 3=hostile, 4=squelch)\n  +0x18: Slot state value\n  +0xc5: Secondary node link\n  +0xcd: Next node pointer",
      "tags": ["PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_1", "STRUCT_Other", "PROP_LOOPHEAVY", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
