      "comment": "Initializes static coordinate bounds for the stats/character panel UI.\n\nClassification: Initialization function - sets up UI layout coordinates\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Read g_dwScreenWidth and g_dwScreenHeight global screen dimensions\n2. Calculate vertical bounds relative to screen bottom:\n   - Right bound: screenHeight - 0x69 (105 pixels from bottom)\n   - Top bound: screenHeight - 0x8C (140 pixels from bottom)\n   - Bottom bound: screenHeight - 0x8F (143 pixels from bottom)\n   - Inner top: screenHeight - 0xA0 (160 pixels from bottom)\n   - Header top: screenHeight - 0xC3 (195 pixels from bottom)\n   - Title top: screenHeight - 0xC6 (198 pixels from bottom)\n3. Calculate horizontal center offsets:\n   - Center X: (screenWidth / 2) + 0x28 (40 pixels right of center)\n   - Center X2: (screenWidth / 2) + 0x4B (75 pixels right of center)\n4. Store fixed horizontal offsets: 0x28 (40) and 0x4B (75)\n5. Write all calculated values to paired global coordinate arrays\n\nParameters: None (void)\n\nReturns: void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Screen width divided by 2 uses signed division (CDQ/SAR pattern)\n- Coordinates stored in duplicate pairs (primary and secondary arrays)\n\nMemory Model:\n- Reads: g_dwScreenWidth (0x6fbae0e4), g_dwScreenHeight (0x6fbae0e8)\n- Writes: 18 global coordinate values at 0x6fbb78b0-0x6fbb78f4\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x69 (105): Right panel vertical offset from screen bottom\n- 0x8C (140): Top boundary offset\n- 0x8F (143): Bottom boundary offset  \n- 0xA0 (160): Inner panel top offset\n- 0xC3 (195): Panel header top offset\n- 0xC6 (198): Panel title top offset\n- 0x28 (40): Left horizontal offset from center\n- 0x4B (75): Right horizontal offset from center",
      "tags": ["PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_0", "PROP_LEAF"]
