      "comment": "Clears validation error codes from global error code tracking variables\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if g_dwValidationError1 is non-zero, report error if present, clear to zero\n2. Check if g_dwValidationError2 is non-zero, report error if present, clear to zero\n3. Check if g_dwValidationError3 is non-zero, report error if present, clear to zero\n4. Check if g_dwValidationError4 is non-zero, report error if present, clear to zero\n5. Check if g_dwValidationError5 is non-zero, report error if present, clear to zero\n6. Loop through g_adwValidationErrorArray from base address to g_dwValidationErrorArrayEnd:\n   - Load error code from current array element\n   - If non-zero, report error and clear element to zero\n   - Advance to next element (4-byte stride)\n   - Continue while pointer < array end boundary\n\nParameters:\n(none) - Function operates on global validation error code variables\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Function clears all pending error codes but does not return status\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Array iteration uses pointer arithmetic; loop condition uses pointer comparison against end boundary\n- All individual error code dwords are zeroed after reporting\n- Array elements are cleared using indirect pointer dereference (MOV dword ptr [ESI], 0)",
