      "comment": "Render main UI panel with game state, slots, and interactive elements\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize slot buffer array (23 elements)\n2. Call FUN_6fb62890() to check initialization status\n3. If initialization failed or other error flags set, reset state and return\n4. Call IsVideoInitializationEnabled() - if true, skip to error cleanup\n5. If DAT_6fbf9115 is uninitialized, call FUN_6fb33ee0() and FUN_6fb33ce0()\n6. Set up 4 render targets with Ordinal_10072() calls at different screen coordinates\n7. If DAT_6fbf9119 is active, iterate through 5 slot positions:\n   a. Check system state via Ordinal_10227() and GetGlobalSystemState()\n   b. Set slot graphics index based on position (cases 1-4 have switch logic)\n   c. Call Ordinal_11107() to get slot data\n   d. Call Ordinal_10072() to render slot at calculated coordinates\n8. Clear DAT_6fbf91e9 buffer (6 iterations of 0x39f bytes each)\n9. Main slot rendering loop (up to 6 slots, 42 iterations max):\n   a. Validate slot data pointer, count, and type constraints\n   b. For each valid slot, execute switch on slot type (0-3):\n      - Type 0: Regular slot - increment animation frame, check timing, render\n      - Type 1: Special slot - check highlight state, render with offset\n      - Type 2: Bonus slot - render with standard frame\n      - Type 3: Feature slot - check reel position, conditional highlight\n   c. Increment slot counter, check loop limits\n10. If animation flag set and slot 5 active, render special overlay at position (0x6e, 0x6e offset)\n11. Handle slot selection highlights via Ordinal_10127/10004 calls\n12. For selected slots with valid state, render border/highlight via Ordinal_10121/10117\n13. Call IsVideoInitializationEnabled() and check mouse input coordinates\n14. If mouse in bounds, call interactive handlers Ordinal_10129()\n15. Final cleanup and return\n\nParameters: None (void function)\n\nReturns: void (no return value)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- DAT_6fbf90d8 == 0x2 triggers buffer resets (lines resetting to 0)\n- Mouse coordinate calculation: (X - dwUIXOffset, Y + dwUIYOffset)\n- Slot animation: frame counter incremented every 100ms (GetTickCount check)\n- Coordinate offsets: 0xe0, 0x30, 0x1c0 (vertical spacing), 0x100, 0x6e (horizontal)\n- Slot type switch uses jump table at 0x6fb3333c (4 entries)\n- Frame data array indexed via (dwSlotIndex * 0x26a offset calculation)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x5: Number of slot positions (indices 1-5)\n- 0x6: Maximum slot count in DAT_6fbf91e9\n- 0x12: Array initialization loop count (18 elements)\n- 0x39f: Buffer size per slot in DAT_6fbf91e9 (927 bytes)\n- 0x26a: Slot record size in bytes (618)\n- 0x39f: Total buffer size (6 * 0x39f)\n- 0x64 (100): Animation frame timing threshold in milliseconds\n- 0x1a: Maximum animation frame value\n- 0x3a0: Special reel position check (928)\n- 0x116/0x13a: Mouse X bounds for button 1 (278-314)\n- 0x187/0x1aa: Mouse Y bounds for button 1 (391-426)\n- 0xe5/0x104: Mouse X bounds for button 2 (229-260)\n- 0x186/0x1a8: Mouse Y bounds for button 2 (390-424)",
      "tags": ["SRC_QuestLog.cpp", "MOD_UI", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "STRUCT_Room2", "STRUCT_ItemData", "PARAM_0", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "UI_QUEST", "STRUCT_PlayerData", "STRUCT_StatList", "PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Path", "STRUCT_Skill", "PROP_LOOPHEAVY"]
