      "comment": "Process and cache menu configuration state for UI rendering.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check system state validity with Ordinal_10227() and GetGlobalSystemState()\n2. Return early if param_1==4 (special case) or system not initialized\n3. Load menu configuration bounds from DAT_6fbb80c8[param_1] to DAT_6fbb80cc[param_1]\n4. For each config slot, load cached path from DAT_6fbf9121[index]\n5. If cache empty, generate path via FUN_6fb9a261() + ConcatenatePathAndWriteFile()\n6. Process config entries (max 0x29 entries from DAT_6fbb80f1) matching menu_id\n7. For each matching entry, initialize Unicode buffer and call FUN_6fb33360() \n8. Validate result and track selected state in dwSelectedState\n9. If param_2 (fResetState) set, reset global config pointers to 0xffffffff\n10. Return final state in DAT_6fbf90f9\n\nParameters:\n  nMenuId (ECX) - Menu configuration index (0-3, special handling for 4)\n  fResetState (EDX) - If non-zero, reset all config pointers to -1 on exit\n\nReturns:\n  void - Updates globals DAT_6fbf90f9, DAT_6fbf90c0-d0 with cache/state info\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Menu ID 4 causes immediate return (hardcoded exit condition)\n  - Config bounds checked: if min > max, skip processing\n  - Unicode buffer (sz PathBuffer) sized for 602 Unicode chars (1204 bytes)\n  - File path buffer (szFileBuffer) sized for 260 chars\n  - Max 0x29 entries processed; loop exits early if nLoopIndex >= 0x29\n  - Entry validation: type check (< 0x1b), cache existence, menu_id match, enable flag",
