      "globals": ["0xFFFFFFFF90530004||", "0xFFFFFFFF90530000||", "0xDE0E4|g_dwScreenWidth|0x280", "0xDE0E8|g_dwScreenHeight|0x1e0", "0x12D7FC|g_dwUIXOffset|0x0", "0x12D800|g_dwUIYOffset|0x0", "0x1290F3|g_bGameInitFlag5|0x0", "0xFFFFFFFF9053001C||", "0x12A095|g_dwSlotArraySize|0x0", "0x1290E0|g_dwSlotCount|0x0", "0x1291EA|g_pSlotDataStart+1|", "0xFFFFFFFF90530018||", "0x12944F|DAT_6fbf944f|0x0", "0x1296B9|DAT_6fbf96b9|0x0", "0x1290F1|g_bGameInitFlag1|0x0", "0x1290F2|g_bGameInitFlag2|0x0", "0x1290F0|g_bGameInitFlag3|0x0", "0x1290F5|g_dwGameValue1|0x0", "0x1290F4|g_bGameInitFlag4|0x0", "0x12A09D|g_bGameFlag1|0x0"],
      "api_count": 7,
      "api_calls": ["GetGameState", "CheckExpansionMpqExists", "CheckExpansionMpqExists", "SetBitInArray2D", "InsertCacheNodeWithCookie", "FogAssert", "InsertCacheNodeWithCookie"],
      "instructions": ["0x64040|PUSH|EBX", "0x64041|PUSH|EBP", "0x64042|MOV|EBP, dword ptr [ESP + 0xc]", "0x64046|PUSH|ESI", "0x64047|PUSH|EDI", "0x64048|XOR|EDI, EDI", "0x6404A|MOV|EBX, dword ptr [EBP + 0xc]", "0x6404D|MOV|DI, word ptr [EBP + 0xc]", "0x64051|SHR|EBX, 0x10", "0x64054|CALL|0x6fad1c00", "0x64059|TEST|AL, AL", "0x6405B|JNZ|0x6fb34222", "0x64061|MOV|EAX, [0x6fbae0e4]", "0x64066|CDQ|", "0x64067|SUB|EAX, EDX"],
      "comment": "Processes mouse click events on the quest log UI panel.\n\nClassification: Callback/Handler - UI event handler invoked on mouse click\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract mouse X coordinate (low word of offset 0xC) and Y coordinate (high word)\n2. Check if video initialization is enabled - return early if true\n3. Validate X coordinate is within left half of screen (X <= screenWidth/2)\n4. Call Ordinal_10005 to get display mode, calculate Y boundary (screenHeight - 0x2F or 0x31)\n5. Validate Y coordinate is within bounds\n6. Adjust coordinates by UI offsets (X -= g_dwUIXOffset, Y += g_dwUIYOffset)\n7. If g_bGameInitFlag5 is set, skip to event finalization\n8. Check if click is within quest slot region (0 <= Y < 0x1C, 0 <= X < 0x140)\n9. Determine slot width based on expansion mode (0x40 for expansion, 0x50 for classic)\n10. Calculate which slot index was clicked by iterating through slot boundaries\n11. If valid slot selected and not current slot, process slot change:\n    - Iterate through active slots and clear their bit flags\n    - Call InitializeGameSlots with new slot index\n    - Call ProcessMenuConfigurationState to update menu\n    - Reset all game init flags and values\n12. If click in button region (X: 0x116-0x139, Y: 0x188-0x1A9), set g_bGameInitFlag2\n13. If click in alternate button region (X: 0xE6-0x103, Y: 0x187-0x1A7), set g_bGameInitFlag4\n14. Mark mouse event as handled (offset 0x18 = 1, offset 0x1C = 0)\n15. Insert event into cache via InsertCacheNodeWithCookie\n\nParameters:\n  pMouseEvent - Pointer to mouse event structure:\n    +0x0C: dword - packed coordinates (low word = X, high word = Y)\n    +0x18: dword - event handled flag (set to 1)\n    +0x1C: dword - event result (set to 0)\n\nReturns: void\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x140 (320) - Quest log panel width in pixels\n  0x1C (28) - Quest slot region height\n  0x50 (80) - Slot width in classic mode (320/4 slots)\n  0x40 (64) - Slot width in expansion mode (320/5 slots)\n  0x38 (56) - Button hit-test width\n  0x34 (52) - Button hit-test height\n  0x116-0x139 - Right button X bounds (278-313)\n  0x188-0x1A9 - Button Y bounds (392-425)\n  0xE6-0x103 - Left button X bounds (230-259)\n  0x26A (618) - Stride between quest slot data entries\n\nGlobals Accessed:\n  g_dwScreenWidth, g_dwScreenHeight - Screen dimensions\n  g_dwUIXOffset, g_dwUIYOffset - UI coordinate offsets\n  g_bGameInitFlag1-5 - Game initialization state flags\n  g_dwSlotCount - Number of active quest slots\n  g_dwSlotArraySize - Current slot array size\n  g_dwGameValue1 - Selected game value (-1 = none)",
      "tags": ["SRC_QuestLog.cpp", "MOD_UI", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_1", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "UI_QUEST", "STRUCT_PlayerData", "PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Path", "PROP_LOOPHEAVY"]
    },
