      "comment": "Clear game state callback and initialize with data value.\n\nClassification: Initialization - Sets up state for callback system\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Clear g_bGameInitFlag5 to 0 (reset game init state)\n2. Call InitializeStateCallbackAndData with NULL callback and passed data value\n3. Return 0 via XOR EAX,EAX (stdcall cleanup)\n\nParameters:\ndwStateData (ECX, __fastcall) - Game state data value to pass to InitializeStateCallbackAndData\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No meaningful return (EAX cleared to 0)\n\nCaller Context:\n- Called from FUN_6fb344c0 via function pointer table\n- Used as callback target for InitializeStateCallbackAndData\n- When invoked as callback, clears the callback registration (sets to NULL)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Always passes NULL (0x0) as callback parameter, effectively clearing registration\n- The cleared g_bGameInitFlag5 prevents re-entry into certain init paths",
