      "instructions": ["0x64B10|PUSH|ECX", "0x64B11|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [ESP + 0x8]", "0x64B15|PUSH|EBX", "0x64B16|PUSH|EBP", "0x64B17|XOR|EBP, EBP", "0x64B19|MOV|EBX, dword ptr [EAX + 0xc]", "0x64B1C|MOV|BP, word ptr [EAX + 0xc]", "0x64B20|PUSH|EDI", "0x64B21|SHR|EBX, 0x10", "0x64B24|CALL|0x6fae4fd0", "0x64B29|MOV|ECX, 0x6", "0x64B2E|MOV|EDI, EAX", "0x64B30|CALL|0x6fb5d340", "0x64B35|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0x64B37|JZ|0x6fb34bbf"],
      "comment": "Handle panel bounds click detection and initialize game mode if within bounds.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract click coordinates from pEventData[3] - low word is X, high word is Y\n2. Get current scroll window mode via GetScrollWindowMode()\n3. Check UI resource state for elements 6 (waypoint) and 2 (inventory)\n4. Call Ordinal_10005 to get current game mode for panel selection\n5. Calculate panel index multiplier (0, 0x14, or 0x28) based on mode\n6. If scroll mode == 2, calculate center offset as (screenWidth - 0x280) / 2\n7. Look up panel bounds from g_adwPanelLeftBounds/TopBounds/WidthBounds/RightBounds tables\n8. Verify click X is within [leftBound + offset, widthBound + offset)\n9. Verify click Y is within [topBound + screenHeight - 0x1e0, rightBound + screenHeight - 0x1e0)\n10. If within bounds and g_bGameInitFlag3 is set:\n    a. Call ProcessUIStateChange(0x11, 1, 0) to deactivate UI element 0x11\n    b. Call InitializeGameMode(0) to reset game mode\n    c. Clear g_bGameInitFlag3\n    d. Set pEventData[6] = 1 (click handled flag)\n    e. Set pEventData[7] = 0\n    f. Call InsertCacheNodeWithCookie to queue event\n11. If not within bounds or flag not set:\n    a. Clear g_bGameInitFlag3\n    b. Set pEventData[6] = 0 (click not handled)\n\nParameters:\n  pEventData (dword *) - Pointer to event data structure:\n    +0x0C (pEventData[3]): Click coordinates - low word = X, high word = Y\n    +0x18 (pEventData[6]): Output - click handled flag (1 = handled, 0 = not)\n    +0x1C (pEventData[7]): Output - reserved/cleared to 0\n\nReturns:\n  void - Results returned via pEventData structure fields\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Scroll mode 2 applies horizontal center offset for 640-width panel\n  - Panel bounds tables are indexed by mode * 0x14 (20 bytes per entry)\n  - Magic 0x280 (640) is legacy panel width for centering calculation\n  - Magic 0x1e0 (480) is legacy screen height offset for Y bounds\n  - UI element 0x11 (17) is deactivated on successful click detection\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x280 (640) - Legacy panel width for center offset calculation\n  0x1e0 (480) - Legacy screen height for Y coordinate adjustment\n  0x14 (20) - Panel bounds table stride per mode entry\n  0x11 (17) - UI element ID deactivated on click detection\n  6 - UI resource ID for waypoint panel check\n  2 - UI resource ID for inventory panel check",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_1", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
    },
