      "instructions": ["0x64C90|SUB|ESP, 0x58", "0x64C93|PUSH|ESI", "0x64C94|CALL|0x6fb62890", "0x64C99|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0x64C9B|JZ|0x6fb34cd1", "0x64C9D|PUSH|0x0", "0x64C9F|MOV|EDX, 0x1", "0x64CA4|MOV|ECX, 0x11", "0x64CA9|CALL|0x6fb5d370", "0x64CAE|CMP|dword ptr [0x6fbf90d8], 0x1", "0x64CB5|JNZ|0x6fb34fa4", "0x64CBB|MOV|byte ptr [0x6fbf90f0], 0x0", "0x64CC2|MOV|dword ptr [0x6fbf90d8], 0x0", "0x64CCC|POP|ESI", "0x64CCD|ADD|ESP, 0x58"],
      "comment": "Render main viewport window with panel configuration based on game mode.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if game initialization is cancelled via FUN_6fb62890\n2. If cancelled, notify UI (0x11 message) and reset game state, return\n3. Get current scroll window mode (0=fullscreen, 2=windowed, 3=minimized)\n4. If minimized, return immediately\n5. Validate UI button state with FUN_6fb5d340(0xf) - if pressed, return\n6. Initialize adwWindowConfig[18] array to zeros\n7. Set default screen configuration: adwWindowConfig[1] = g_dwScreenConfig1, adwWindowConfig[3] = 0\n8. Validate UI state: FUN_6fb5d340(6) OR FUN_6fb5d340(2)\n9. Determine viewport panel configuration:\n   - If menu/button blocked, check window mode\n   - Mode 2 (windowed): Check Ordinal_10005() for mode 2 response\n   - Assign dwWindowMode: 1 (left panel), 2 (center), or 3 (right panel)\n10. Call Ordinal_10036(adwWindowConfig) - apply window config\n11. Call Ordinal_10037, Ordinal_10004, Ordinal_10121 - render initialize\n12. Calculate viewport Y offset: nConfigIndex*20 offsets into DAT_6fbb78b8 table\n13. Calculate screen X/Y positions accounting for 0x1e0 offset and screen height\n14. Render viewport panel with coordinates via Ordinal_10072\n15. Update adwWindowConfig[1] = g_dwScreenConfig2\n16. If game initialized (g_bGameInitFlag3):\n    a. Get current mouse coordinates via FUN_6fb8f690/FUN_6fb8f680\n    b. Recalculate panel config with current mouse position\n    c. Check if mouse within viewport bounds:\n       - nMouseY must be between panel's X range\n       - nMouseX must be between panel's top/bottom Y range\n       - If all conditions met, set adwWindowConfig[2] = 1 (hit)\n    d. Otherwise set adwWindowConfig[2] = 0 (no hit)\n17. Render second viewport panel with adjusted coordinates\n\nParameters:\n(none - no parameters, called from FUN_6fb5ba40)\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If game init cancelled, resets g_bGameInitFlag3 and g_dwGameModeFlag\n- Windowed mode applies horizontal offset correction: (g_dwScreenWidth - 0x280) / 2\n- Multiple Ordinal calls ensure proper UI state synchronization\n- Panel configuration recalculated for both initial render and mouse detection\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x11: UI cancel notification code\n0xf: Button state check code (0xf = 15)\n0x6: Menu state check code\n0x2: Alternative state check code\n0x12: Array initialization loop count (18 elements)\n0x14: Panel config offset stride (20 bytes)\n0x1e0: Y offset adjustment constant (480 decimal)\n0x280: Windowed mode width constant (640 decimal)\n0xffffffff: Color value (white, no transparency)\n5: Ordinal_10072 panel render type parameter\n\nRelated Functions:\n- FUN_6fb62890(): Check if game init cancelled\n- FUN_6fb5d340(): UI state validator\n- GetScrollWindowMode(): Get current window display mode\n- Ordinal_10005(): Get current viewport panel mode\n- Ordinal_10036(): Apply window configuration\n- Ordinal_10072(): Render viewport panel\n- FUN_6fb8f690(): Get current mouse X coordinate\n- FUN_6fb8f680(): Get current mouse Y coordinate\n- FUN_6fb5ba40(): Caller - main game loop renderer",
      "tags": ["PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Path", "STRUCT_Inventory", "STRUCT_Skill", "STRUCT_Room2", "PARAM_0", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
