      "comment": "Hash table unit callback that clears render flag bit 1 for units of type 0x92.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if unit type field at offset +0x4 equals 0x92 (146 decimal)\n2. If match, clear bit 1 (0x02) from flags field at offset +0xe8\n3. Return (no action if type mismatch)\n\nParameters:\n- pUnit (ECX): Pointer to unit structure in hash table\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Only affects units with dwType == 0x92; all other units pass through unchanged\n- Called from ProcessUnitHashTableWithCallback during game state transitions\n- Bit 1 (0x02) likely controls render visibility or update flag\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x92 (146): Unit type identifier being filtered\n- 0x4: Offset to unit type field (dwType)\n- 0xe8 (232): Offset to unit flags field (dwFlags)\n- 0xfd: Bitmask to clear bit 1 (AND with 0xfffffffd)\n\nStructure Layout (inferred unit offsets):\nOffset  Size  Field         Type  Description\n0x04    4     dwType        uint  Unit type identifier\n0xe8    4     dwFlags       uint  Unit state flags (bit 1 = render flag)",
