      "comment": "Iterate over game objects with X,Y offsets and store object data reference.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if g_bGameFlag3 is set (game active flag)\n2. Call FUN_6fb62880() to initialize/get game state\n3. Call Ordinal_10918() [D2Common.RandSeed] to get object count\n4. Add 2 to count (boundary adjustment)\n5. Loop from 0 to (count+2): For each index nIterator\n   a. Compute normalized index: nIndex = (nIterator & 0x80000001) with sign adjustment\n   b. Calculate X offset: nBaseX + nIndex\n   c. Calculate Y offset: nBaseY + nIndex\n   d. Call FUN_6fb621c0(0x95, X_offset, Y_offset, 1, 1) to get object reference\n   e. Extract dword at offset +0x8 from result and store in g_dwLastObjectData\n   f. Set g_bGameFlag4 = 1 (processing complete flag)\n\nParameters:\nIMPLICIT ECX: nBaseX - Base X coordinate offset\nIMPLICIT EDX: nBaseY - Base Y coordinate offset\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Updates globals g_dwLastObjectData and g_bGameFlag4 as side effects\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If g_bGameFlag3 is 0, function returns immediately without processing\n- Boundary adjustment (+2) may represent padding or sentinel objects\n- Modulo arithmetic (0x80000001) normalizes negative indices\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x80000001: Modulo mask for index normalization (handles negative indices)\n- 0x95: Object type/flag parameter to FUN_6fb621c0\n- +0x8: Offset into result structure for data extraction",
