      "comment": "Closes a dialog window and resets all UI element states to inactive.\n\nClassification: Cleanup/Destructor - UI teardown handler\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Reset global state to 0 via SetGlobalState(0)\n2. Send WM_CLOSE (0x10) message to window handle from phWnd\n3. Set initialization flag to 1 via SetInitializationFlag(1)\n4. Get minimap UI resource (ID 9) via GetUIResourceByIdWithValidation\n5. If minimap resource valid, activate it via ProcessUIStateChange(9, 1, 0)\n6. Initialize loop: dwUIIndex = 0, ESI = g_pUIStateTable (0x6fbb8628)\n7. Loop through UI state table entries (stride 0xC = 12 bytes per entry):\n   a. If current entry's first DWORD is non-zero (element active)\n   b. Deactivate element via ProcessUIStateChange(dwUIIndex, 0, 0)\n   c. Advance ESI by 12 bytes (3 DWORDs), increment dwUIIndex\n   d. Continue while ESI < g_pPanelDataSingleplayerEnd (0x6fbb87f0)\n8. Return (void)\n\nParameters:\nIMPLICIT (ECX): dwUnused - unused parameter (always 0 in typical usage)\nIMPLICIT (EDX): phWnd - pointer to HWND to close\n\nReturns: void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- No callers found - likely registered as callback or event handler\n- Activates minimap (ID 9) before deactivating other elements\n- Loop count: (0x6fbb87f0 - 0x6fbb8628) / 0xC = 39 entries maximum\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x10 - WM_CLOSE Windows message\n9 - UI element ID for minimap\n0xC - Stride of UI state table entries (3 DWORDs)\n\nGlobal Data:\ng_pUIStateTable (0x6fbb8628) - Array of UI state entries, 12 bytes each\ng_pPanelDataSingleplayerEnd (0x6fbb87f0) - End boundary for UI state table",
