      "comment": "Deactivate all UI panels except minimap which is first activated then deactivated.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if minimap (UI element 9) resource exists via GetUIResourceByIdWithValidation\n2. If minimap exists, call ProcessUIStateChange(9, 1, 0) to activate it first\n3. Initialize loop counter (EDI=0) and pointer (ESI=g_pUIStateTable at 0x6fbb8628)\n4. Loop through UI state table entries (stride 12 bytes, 50 entries):\n   a. Check if current entry's first dword is non-zero (panel active)\n   b. If active, call ProcessUIStateChange(index, 0, 0) to deactivate panel\n   c. Advance pointer by 12 bytes (ESI += 0xC)\n   d. Increment index counter (EDI++)\n   e. Continue while ESI < g_pPanelDataSingleplayerEnd (0x6fbb87f0)\n5. Restore saved registers and return\n\nParameters:\nNone (void function)\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Minimap (UI 9) is explicitly activated before the deactivation loop, then deactivated\n  in the loop like other panels - ensures proper minimap state transition\n- Loop bounds: g_pUIStateTable (0x6fbb8628) to g_pPanelDataSingleplayerEnd (0x6fbb87f0)\n- Stride: 12 bytes per entry (0xC)\n- Entry count: 50 entries ((0x87f0 - 0x8628) / 0xC = 0x1C8 / 0xC = 50)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x9 - Minimap UI element ID\n0xC (12) - UI state table entry stride in bytes\n0x6fbb8628 - g_pUIStateTable start address\n0x6fbb87f0 - g_pPanelDataSingleplayerEnd boundary address",
