      "instructions": ["0x65810|SUB|ESP, 0x8", "0x65813|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [ECX + 0x120]", "0x65819|MOV|ECX, dword ptr [ECX + 0x124]", "0x6581F|DEC|EAX", "0x65820|MOV|dword ptr [ESP], EAX", "0x65824|XOR|EAX, EAX", "0x65826|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x4], EAX", "0x6582A|FILD|qword ptr [ESP]", "0x6582E|MOV|dword ptr [ESP], ECX", "0x65832|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x4], EAX", "0x65836|FDIVR|float ptr [0x6fba62f8]", "0x6583C|FIMUL|dword ptr [ESP]", "0x65840|CALL|0x6fb9a480", "0x65845|MOV|ECX, EAX", "0x65847|CALL|0x6fb998ac"],
      "comment": "Calculates and applies music volume from slider settings object.\n\nClassification: Worker function (thiscall method on settings object)\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Read current slider value from [ECX + 0x120] (this->dwSliderValue)\n2. Decrement slider value by 1 (slider is 1-based, volume is 0-based)\n3. Read maximum volume from [ECX + 0x124] (this->dwMaxVolume)\n4. Convert (sliderValue - 1) to floating point via qword stack buffer\n5. Divide by 100.0f (g_flVolumePercentDivisor) to normalize to 0.0-1.0 range\n6. Multiply by maxVolume to scale to actual volume range\n7. Convert result back to integer via __ftol\n8. Call SetMusicVolume with calculated volume\n\nParameters:\n  pThis (ECX, IMPLICIT) - Pointer to settings object containing:\n    +0x120: dwSliderValue (uint) - Current slider position (1-based)\n    +0x124: dwMaxVolume (uint) - Maximum volume value for scaling\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Slider value 1 produces volume 0 (minimum after decrement)\n- Uses FPU for smooth volume scaling calculation\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x120: Offset to slider value in settings object\n- 0x124: Offset to max volume in settings object\n- 100.0f: Percentage divisor for normalizing slider to 0.0-1.0 range\n\nCalled by: Function pointer at g_pfnApplyMusicVolumeFromSlider (0x6fbbbe64)\nCalls: __ftol (float to long conversion), SetMusicVolume",
