      "comment": "Load blended shadows setting from Windows registry into config structure.\n\nClassification: Initialization helper - reads single registry value into config.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate pointer to shadow mode field at pConfig + 0x124\n2. Query registry key \"Diablo II\\Blended Shadows\" with default value 0\n3. Store result directly into config field at offset 0x124\n4. Call Ordinal_10014 (D2Win.UpdateUIState) to refresh shadow rendering\n\nParameters:\npConfig (ECX): Pointer to graphics configuration structure\n  - Offset 0x124: Shadow mode setting (DWORD)\n  - 0 = disabled, non-zero = enabled\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Registry value stored directly in config structure\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Uses __fastcall: pConfig passed in ECX\n- If registry key missing, default value 0 (disabled) is used\n- Always calls Ordinal_10014 regardless of registry read success\n\nRelated Functions:\n- SetBlendedShadowsMode: Writes shadow setting to registry (inverse operation)\n- QueryRegistryUlong: Registry access wrapper (Ordinal import)\n- Ordinal_10014: D2Win.UpdateUIState - refreshes graphics state",
