      "comment": "Initializes graphics resolution mode from registry setting.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Read \"Resolution\" value from registry key \"Diablo II\" into pConfigStruct+0x124\n2. Default graphics mode to 0 (640x480 low resolution)\n3. If registry value equals 1, set graphics mode to 2 (800x600 high resolution)\n4. Tail-call SetGraphicsModeConfiguration with selected mode\n\nParameters:\n  pConfigStruct (void * in ECX): Pointer to configuration structure\n    - Offset +0x124: Stores resolution registry value (ulong)\n\nReturns:\n  void: Function configures graphics mode and returns via tail call\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  Registry value 0 or missing: Uses mode 0 (640x480)\n  Registry value 1: Uses mode 2 (800x600)\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x124: Offset in config struct for resolution setting\n  0: Graphics mode for 640x480 resolution\n  1: Registry value indicating high resolution\n  2: Graphics mode for 800x600 resolution\n\nStructure Layout:\n  Offset   Size   Field                  Type    Description\n  0x124    4      dwResolutionSetting    ulong   Registry resolution value",
      "tags": ["PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_1", "PROP_SMALL"]
