      "comment": "Loads perspective mode setting from Windows registry and initializes viewport.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate address of perspective flag at pGameConfig+0x124\n2. Query registry value \"Perspective\" from \"Diablo II\" key into perspective flag\n3. Call D2GFX.Ordinal_10007 to check if perspective mode is supported\n4. If perspective supported (EAX != 0):\n   a. Write current perspective value back to registry\n   b. Set toggle state for perspective rendering mode\n   c. Initialize viewport rectangles with current display dimensions\n5. If not supported: clear perspective flag to 0\n\nParameters:\npGameConfig (void *) - Pointer to game configuration structure. Offset 0x124 holds\n                       the perspective mode flag (DWORD)\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Registry query uses key \"Diablo II\" and value \"Perspective\"\n- If D2GFX perspective check fails, perspective flag is forced to 0\n- Viewport initialization uses global display dimensions (g_dwBackBufferHeight, g_dwViewportHeight)\n\nOrdinal References:\n- Ordinal_10007: D2GFX - Check if perspective rendering is supported (returns 0 if not)\n\nRelated Functions:\n- InitializeGameDisplaySettings: Similar setup without registry query\n- QueryRegistryUlong: Storm registry wrapper\n- SetRegistryDword: Storm registry wrapper",
