      "comment": "Saves the contrast setting from slider control to Windows registry.\n\nCalculates the contrast value from slider position and max value, scales it\nusing floating point arithmetic, and persists to registry. Updates graphics\nsettings and refreshes the display.\n\nClassification: Worker function - saves slider state to registry\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Read slider position from this+0x120\n2. Read slider max value from this+0x124  \n3. Compute normalized contrast: ((position - 1) / 100.0) * maxValue\n4. Convert float result to integer via __ftol\n5. Save contrast value to registry under \"Contrast\" key\n6. Call ResetGraphicsSettings with display parameter (EDX=maxValue, ECX=0xB)\n7. Call D2GFX.Ordinal_10018 to refresh display\n\nParameters:\n  this (ECX, IMPLICIT): Pointer to slider control structure\n    +0x120: Current slider position (int)\n    +0x124: Slider maximum value (int)\n\nReturns: void\n\nCallees:\n  __ftol - Convert ST(0) float to 32-bit integer in EAX\n  SetRegistryDword - Save DWORD value to registry\n  ResetGraphicsSettings - Update graphics subsystem (EDX=value, ECX=settingId)\n  Ordinal_10018 - D2GFX display refresh\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  100.0f (0x6fba62f8) - Divisor for slider normalization\n  0xB - Graphics setting ID for ResetGraphicsSettings\n\nRegistry:\n  Key: DiabloII\n  Value: Contrast (DWORD)",
