      "comment": "Calculates and applies contrast setting based on slider position.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call GetWindowMode to determine current display mode (result in EAX)\n2. If window mode != 4 (not Direct3D), use default contrast of 100; else use 0\n3. Query registry for saved \"Contrast\" value, overwriting default if present\n4. Read current slider max value from pOptionsControl+0x120, decrement by 1\n5. Increment contrast value by 1 for FPU calculation base\n6. Convert both values to 64-bit floats for precision calculation\n7. Multiply slider position by max value, then by 0.01 scale factor\n8. Call __ftol to convert float result to integer\n9. Divide 100.0 by intermediate result for inverse scaling\n10. Store calculated contrast at pOptionsControl+0x124\n11. Multiply by stored integer and convert back via __ftol\n12. Save final contrast value to registry under \"Contrast\" key\n13. Call ResetGraphicsSettings to apply new contrast\n14. Call Ordinal_10018 (D2Gfx.RefreshScreen) to update display\n\nParameters:\n- pOptionsControl (ECX): Pointer to options/slider control structure\n  - +0x120: Slider maximum value (int)\n  - +0x124: Calculated contrast output (int)\n\nReturns: void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Window mode 4 (Direct3D) starts with contrast 0 vs 100 for other modes\n- Registry value overrides the window-mode-based default\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x64 (100): Default contrast for non-D3D modes\n- 0x120: Offset to slider max value in control struct\n- 0x124: Offset to contrast result in control struct\n- 0.01 (0x6fba9384): FPU scale factor for percentage conversion\n- 100.0 (g_flVolumePercentDivisor): Divisor for inverse calculation",
