      "comment": "Validate and configure automap display mode, clamping value to valid range [0,2].\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Compare current mode value at offset 0x124 against maximum (0x2)\n2. If mode exceeds 2, clamp to 0 (invalid modes reset to default)\n3. Call SetAutomapGraphicsMode with validated mode to apply graphics settings\n4. Call Ordinal_426 (D2Client.SetAutomapSettings or similar) with global config pointer and mode value\n\nParameters:\npMode (IMPLICIT in ECX): Pointer to configuration structure containing:\n  +0x124: uint - Automap display mode (0=Normal, 1=Expanded, 2=Max; >2 invalid)\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Mode value >2 is automatically clamped to 0 (default mode)\n- Ordinal_426 call updates persistent automap settings\n- Configuration structure pointer remains in ECX throughout function\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x124: Offset to mode field within config structure (292 bytes from base)\n- 0x02: Maximum valid automap mode value (3 total modes: 0,1,2)\n- 0x00: Reset/default mode when validation fails",
