      "comment": "Initialize automap display mode from Windows registry and apply to config structure.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize local mode value from parameter's current mode field at offset 0x124\n2. Call QueryRegistryUlong to read \"AutoMapMode\" from \"Diablo II\" registry key\n3. Validate registry value: if mode > 2, clamp to 0 (default mode)\n4. Call SetAutomapGraphicsMode with validated mode to configure display\n5. Call GetGraphicsMode to retrieve actual graphics mode applied\n6. Store returned graphics mode at config structure offset 0x124\n\nParameters:\npConfig (IMPLICIT in ECX): Pointer to configuration structure containing:\n  +0x124: uint - Automap display mode destination (0=Normal, 1=Expanded, 2=Full)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Mode stored directly into config structure at offset 0x124\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Registry value > 2 is automatically clamped to 0 (invalid modes reset to default)\n- Initial value at pConfig+0x124 used as default if registry read fails\n- No callers found - likely called from initialization table or computed jump\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x124: Offset to automap mode field within config structure (292 bytes)\n- 0x02: Maximum valid automap mode (3 modes: 0, 1, 2)\n- 0x00: Default/reset mode when validation fails\n\nCallees:\n- QueryRegistryUlong: Read DWORD from Windows registry\n- SetAutomapGraphicsMode: Apply automap graphics settings\n- GetGraphicsMode: Retrieve current graphics mode value",
