      "comment": "Handle mouse down event on panel UI element.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract X coordinate from low word of event data at offset +0xc\n2. Extract Y coordinate from high word of event data at offset +0xc (shift right 16)\n3. Call FindPanelAtYCoordinate to locate panel at mouse Y position\n4. If panel found (result != -1), update g_nCurrentPanelIndex with new panel index\n5. Call HandlePanelMouseInteraction with extracted X,Y coordinates\n6. Set g_fMouseDown flag to 1 indicating mouse button is pressed\n7. Set event structure field at +0x18 to 1 (handled flag)\n8. Set event structure field at +0x1c to 0 (clear state)\n9. Call InsertCacheNodeWithCookie with event data pointer\n\nParameters:\n  dwMouseEventData (uint) - Pointer to mouse event structure:\n    +0x0c: Packed coordinates (low word = X, high word = Y)\n    +0x18: Handled flag (set to 1)\n    +0x1c: State field (cleared to 0)\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Panel index only updated when FindPanelAtYCoordinate returns valid index (!= -1)\n  - No callers found - likely registered as callback in function pointer table\n\nGlobals Modified:\n  g_nCurrentPanelIndex (0x6fbfa158) - Active panel index\n  g_fMouseDown (0x6fbfa168) - Mouse button state flag",
