      "comment": "Find UI panel at given Y coordinate\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Retrieve global panel count (g_nPanelCount) and half-height offset for viewport\n2. Check if Y coordinate falls within viewport bounds (centered on screen, ±half-height)\n3. Iterate through panel array (g_pPanelArray) to find matching entry at target Y\n4. Calculate panel offset from array base (stride 0x550 bytes per entry)\n5. For found panel, load optional callback from offset 0x44\n6. If callback exists, invoke it; if returns 0, panel is active\n7. Return found panel index or -1 if not found or callback fails\n\nParameters:\nint nYCoord - Y coordinate to test against panel positions\n\nReturns:\nint - Panel index if found (0+), -1 if no matching panel found or callback failed\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Panels outside viewport bounds return -1 immediately\n- Callback result (0=active, non-zero=inactive) determines return\n- Array stride: 0x550 bytes per panel entry\n- Callback pointer stored at offset 0x44 within panel structure\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset | Size | Field Name | Type | Description\n0x00   | 4    | dwPanelId  | uint | Panel identifier or state flag\n0x44   | 4    | pfnCallback| void*| Optional callback function pointer",
