      "comment": "Handle mouse interaction with the active UI panel scrollable region.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if interaction is already being processed (g_fPanelInteractionActive != 0) or find panel at mouse Y coordinate\n2. If found panel matches current active panel (g_nCurrentPanelIndex), proceed to interaction\n3. Retrieve current panel offset: g_nCurrentPanelIndex * 0x550 + g_pPanelDataBase\n4. Get callback handler at offset +0x110 and invoke if not null\n5. Check if panel type at offset +0x0 equals 2 (scrollable panel)\n6. Calculate screen center: g_dwScreenWidth / 2\n7. If panel flag at offset +0x53c is set, adjust bounds to narrower range (0x90/0x91) else default (0x3b/0x3c)\n8. Validate mouse X within calculated bounds; if not within bounds and not force-interacting, skip processing\n9. Update panel scroll position based on mouse X:\n   - If X < right bound + 0xc: set scroll to 0 (top)\n   - If X > right bound + 0x115: set scroll to max-1 (bottom)\n   - Else: calculate proportional scroll using floating-point interpolation\n10. Mark interaction as processed (g_fPanelInteractionActive = 1)\n11. If panel scroll position changed, invoke change callback at offset +0x114\n12. Call FUN_6fb8d210 to update UI rendering\n\nParameters:\n  nMouseX (int) - IMPLICIT ECX: Mouse X coordinate, used to determine scroll position\n  nMouseY (int) - IMPLICIT EDX: Mouse Y coordinate, passed to panel finder\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Function uses SSA temporaries (pfnCallback) that are compiler-optimized register reuses\n  - Floating-point calculations for smooth scroll interpolation across panel width\n  - Dual callback pattern: initialization callback on panel activation, change callback on scroll change\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x550 - Panel structure size in bytes\n  0x124 - Offset of current scroll position field\n  0x110 - Offset of initialization callback pointer\n  0x114 - Offset of change callback pointer\n  0x120 - Offset of max scroll value field\n  0x53c - Offset of panel type/flags field\n  0x3b, 0x3c - Default scroll bounds offset from center\n  0x90, 0x91 - Narrow scroll bounds offset from center\n  0x121 - Full scroll width (289 pixels)\n  0xc - Right button area boundary\n  0x115 - Left button area boundary (277 pixels right of center)",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PARAM_2", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
