      "comment": "Handles mouse button release event for panel UI system.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if mouse was previously down (g_fMouseDown != 0)\n2. If mouse was down, extract Y coordinate from input event (pInputEvent[3] >> 16)\n3. Find panel at that Y coordinate via FindPanelAtYCoordinate\n4. If found panel matches current active panel (g_nCurrentPanelIndex), process state update\n5. Always: call InitializeTargetingSystem to reset targeting state\n6. Clear mouse down flag (g_fMouseDown = 0)\n7. Clear panel interaction flag (g_fPanelInteractionActive = 0)\n8. Mark input event as handled (pInputEvent[6] = 1)\n9. Clear secondary result (pInputEvent[7] = 0)\n10. Insert event into cache via InsertCacheNodeWithCookie\n\nParameters:\npInputEvent - Pointer to input event structure\n  [3] (offset 0x0C): Mouse coordinates (high word = Y, low word = X)\n  [6] (offset 0x18): Handled flag (set to 1 on return)\n  [7] (offset 0x1C): Secondary result (set to 0 on return)\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If mouse was not down, skips panel lookup but still resets state\n- Panel state update only occurs if release is on same panel as initial press\n\nGlobals Modified:\n- g_fMouseDown: Cleared to 0\n- g_fPanelInteractionActive: Cleared to 0",
