      "comment": "Processes state updates for the current panel, executing type-specific callbacks.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Retrieve onRender callback for current panel and invoke if non-null\n2. If callback returned success (0), check panel state type:\n   - State 0: Invoke onLeave callback and reset panel state to inactive (type 2)\n   - State 1: Increment visit counter, validate counter against max visits\n     If counter exceeds max, reset to 0. Invoke onRender callback and update state (type 1)\n3. If callback returned failure or no callback exists, return without state change\n\nParameters:\nNone (uses global panel index g_dwCurrentPanelIndex)\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Panel without callbacks: transitions states without execution\n- Counter overflow: automatically resets to 0 when exceeding max\n- Null callback: skips execution but continues state transition\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x550: Panel record stride in bytes (sizeof PanelData)\n- 0x110: Offset to onRender callback pointer\n- 0x114: Offset to second callback pointer\n- 0x120: Offset to visit counter\n- 0x124: Offset to visit counter max\n- 0x45: Array index to onLeave callback (offset 0x45*4 from panel base)\n- 0x49: Array index to counter (offset 0x49*4 from panel base)",
