      "instructions": ["0x66560|MOV|ECX, dword ptr [0x6fbfa158]", "0x66566|DEC|ECX", "0x66567|MOV|dword ptr [0x6fbfa158], ECX", "0x6656D|JNS|0x6fb3657d", "0x6656F|MOV|EAX, [0x6fbfa15c]", "0x66574|MOV|ECX, dword ptr [EAX]", "0x66576|DEC|ECX", "0x66577|MOV|dword ptr [0x6fbfa158], ECX", "0x6657D|MOV|EAX, ECX", "0x6657F|SHL|EAX, 0x4", "0x66582|ADD|EAX, ECX", "0x66584|LEA|EDX, [EAX + EAX*0x4]", "0x66587|MOV|EAX, [0x6fbfa160]", "0x6658C|SHL|EDX, 0x4", "0x6658F|ADD|EAX, EDX"],
      "comment": "Selects the previous valid panel in the panel list with wraparound.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Decrement g_nCurrentPanelIndex\n2. If index goes negative, wrap to (*g_nPanelCount - 1)\n3. Calculate panel address: g_pPanelDataBase + index * 0x550\n4. Check if panel ID at offset 0x00 equals -1 (invalid) - if so, loop back to step 1\n5. Check if callback function pointer at offset 0x110 exists\n6. If callback exists, call it - if returns 0, loop back to step 1\n7. If no callback or callback returns non-zero, panel is valid\n8. Call InitializeGameObjectProperties(1, 0, 0.0, 0.0, 0) to reset display state\n9. Set pMessage[0x18/4] = 1 (result/status flag)\n10. Set pMessage[0x1c/4] = 0 (secondary result)\n11. Call InsertCacheNodeWithCookie(pMessage) to requeue message\n\nParameters:\n  pMessage (uint *) - Message structure to update with selection result\n    Offset 0x18: Set to 1 on successful panel selection\n    Offset 0x1c: Set to 0 on successful panel selection\n\nReturns:\n  void - Results communicated via pMessage structure\n\nGlobals Accessed:\n  g_nCurrentPanelIndex (0x6fbfa158) - Current panel index, modified\n  g_nPanelCount (0x6fbfa15c) - Pointer to panel count, read\n  g_pPanelDataBase (0x6fbfa160) - Base of panel data array, read\n\nPanel Data Structure (stride 0x550 bytes):\n  Offset 0x000: Panel ID (-1 = invalid/empty slot)\n  Offset 0x110: Callback function pointer for panel validation\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Wraps index from -1 to last panel (circular navigation)\n  - Skips panels with ID = -1 (empty slots)\n  - Skips panels where validation callback returns 0",
