      "comment": "HandlePanelScrollUp - Handles upward scrolling in panel list UI\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get current panel data structure (0x550 byte stride per panel)\n2. Save current selection index from offset 0x124\n3. Check pre-scroll callback at offset 0x110 - abort if returns 0\n4. Based on scroll mode (offset 0x0):\n   - Mode 1: Decrement index, clamp to (max_items - 1)\n   - Mode 2: Decrement index, wrap to 0 if below minimum\n5. If selection changed, call post-scroll callback at offset 0x114\n6. Mark cache node as processed and insert into callback cache\n\nParameters:\n  pCacheNode - Callback cache node pointer (flags set at +0x18, +0x1c)\n\nReturns: void\n\nPanel Data Structure Offsets:\n  +0x000: Scroll mode (1=clamp, 2=wrap)\n  +0x110: Pre-scroll validation callback\n  +0x114: Post-scroll notification callback\n  +0x120: Max items count\n  +0x124: Current selection index",
      "tags": ["PROP_NOCALLER", "PROP_TINY", "PARAM_1", "PROP_LEAF"]
