      "comment": "Processes configuration/menu items and writes cached data to files.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate parameters: Ensure pnCount pointer is not NULL (fails with Ordinal_10023)\n2. Validate nCount > 0: Exit with error if count is zero\n3. Initialize 256-byte local buffer (local_103) with zero values using REP STOSD\n4. Call Ordinal_10006 with local buffer (initialization)\n5. For each configuration item (0 to nCount-1):\n   - Get configuration item at offset 0x550 * loop_index\n   - Check if item is disabled (offset -8 == 0) or call Ordinal_10227\n   - If item has non-empty name (offset 0x0):\n     * Copy item to local buffer via FUN_6fb9a261\n     * Call ConcatenatePathAndWriteFile to process item\n     * If item has -0xc field == 1: Process choice files\n   - Call optional callback at offset 0x10c if present\n6. Return when all items processed\n\nParameters:\npnCount: int * - Pointer to count of configuration items (__fastcall ECX parameter)\npConfig: int * - Pointer to configuration data/array start (__fastcall EDX parameter)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- NULL pnCount pointer: Fatal error (Ordinal_10023 abort)\n- nCount == 0: Fatal error (Ordinal_10023 abort)\n- dwChoiceCount > 4: Fatal error (Ordinal_10023 abort)\n- Empty choice file name: Fatal error (Ordinal_10023 abort)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x550: Configuration item stride (size of each config entry)\n0x150: Initial loop counter value\n0x154: Loop counter increment per item\n0x8: Offset to item enabled flag (negative from base, relative -8)\n0xc: Offset to choice count field\n0xc: Offset to item name string\n0x10c: Offset to callback function pointer\n0x114: Offset to choice count in item\n0x120: Offset to choice file names array in item\n0x530: Offset to write result storage\n0x104: Choice file entry stride in array\n0x40: Loop count for initializing 256-byte buffer (64 dwords)",
