      "comment": "Initialize all 6 panel configuration arrays and compute maximum value count.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call FUN_6fb36890 six times to initialize different panel configurations (OptBar, OptBarC, OptSkull, and three others)\n2. Copy base property string pointer to local buffer\n3. Clear local buffer space (64 dwords for 256 bytes)\n4. Process three UI widget configuration files: OptBar, OptBarC, OptSkull\n   - For each file: call FUN_6fb9a261 to build path, then ConcatenatePathAndWriteFile to write/validate\n   - Store resulting pointers in DAT_6fbfa170, DAT_6fbfa174, DAT_6fbfa178\n5. Initialize panel data array (18 elements) and get total panel count via FUN_6fb5d980\n6. Store count in adwPanelData[1]\n7. Loop through all panels (0 to count-1):\n   - Call Ordinal_10036 to get panel value\n   - Call Ordinal_10037 to extract numeric property\n   - Track maximum value encountered\n8. Store maximum value in DAT_6fbfa17c\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Initializes global panel configuration state\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Panel count from FUN_6fb5d980 may be 0, loop conditionally executed\n- Maximum value initialized to 0, updated only if greater values found",
