      "comment": "Initializes panel mode configuration and optionally resets panel structure data.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. If nInitializeFlag is non-zero:\n   - Iterate through panel structures starting at g_pPanelDataSingleplayer\n   - For each panel entry (3 dwords per entry, 12 bytes stride):\n     a. Clear current entry to 0x00\n     b. Check if parent panel ([-2] offset) is active\n     c. If parent active AND child panel ([-1] offset) exists:\n        - Call FUN_6fb5d340 to get unit stat and store in entry\n     d. Call FUN_6fb5d340 again to check panel state\n     e. If result non-zero, call FUN_6fb5d370 to reset panel with mode 1\n   - Continue loop while pPanelEntry < g_pPanelDataSingleplayerEnd (32 panel entries total)\n2. Call FUN_6fb5d370(9, 0, 0) to finalize previous mode cleanup\n3. Switch on nPanelMode (0-5):\n   - Mode 0: Set g_nPanelCount = g_pPanelCountNormalUI, g_pPanelArray = g_ppPanelArrayNormalUI\n   - Mode 1: Set g_nPanelCount = g_pPanelCountEtherealUI, g_pPanelArray = g_ppPanelArrayEtherealUI\n   - Mode 2: Set g_nPanelCount = g_pPanelCountExpandedUI, g_pPanelArray = g_ppPanelArrayExpandedUI\n   - Mode 3: Call Ordinal_10227() to check condition, set arrays based on return:\n     * If return == 0: use g_pPanelCountSingleplayerMode3 and g_ppPanelArraySingleplayerMode3\n     * Otherwise: use g_pPanelCountMultiplayerMode3 and g_ppPanelArrayMultiplayerMode3\n   - Mode 4: Set g_nPanelCount = g_pPanelCountMode4, g_pPanelArray = g_ppPanelArrayMode4\n4. Set g_dwCurrentPanelIndex = *g_nPanelCount - 1\n5. If nPanelMode == 5, override g_dwCurrentPanelIndex to 1\n\nParameters:\nnInitializeFlag (int, ECX) - Non-zero to initialize panel structures; 0 to skip initialization\nnPanelMode (int, EDX) - Panel mode selector (0-5) determining which panel array configuration to activate\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Modifies global panel configuration variables (g_nPanelCount, g_pPanelArray, g_dwCurrentPanelIndex)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Mode 3 has conditional logic based on Ordinal_10227 (likely D2Common.IsSingleplayer or similar)\n- Mode 5 overrides panel index calculation regardless of array count\n- Panel iteration uses 12-byte stride (3 consecutive dwords per panel entry)\n\nRelated Functions:\n- FUN_6fb5d340: Get/check panel state for unit\n- FUN_6fb5d370: Reset/update panel configuration\n- Ordinal_10227: Singleplayer mode check",
