      "instructions": ["0x66F10|MOV|EAX, [0x6fbfa15c]", "0x66F15|SUB|ESP, 0xc8", "0x66F1B|PUSH|EBP", "0x66F1C|XOR|EBP, EBP", "0x66F1E|CMP|EAX, EBP", "0x66F20|JNZ|0x6fb36f40", "0x66F22|PUSH|0x695", "0x66F27|PUSH|0x6fbc5340", "0x66F2C|PUSH|0x6fbc53cc", "0x66F31|CALL|0x6fb99a7a", "0x66F36|ADD|ESP, 0xc", "0x66F39|PUSH|-0x1", "0x66F3B|CALL|0x6fb9a10f", "0x66F40|CMP|dword ptr [0x6fbfa160], EBP", "0x66F46|JNZ|0x6fb36f66"],
      "comment": "Renders all UI panels and handles mouse interactions with dynamic scrolling.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate g_nPanelCount and g_pPanelDataBase are initialized; abort with error 0xffffffff if missing\n2. Get current mouse coordinates via FUN_6fb8f680/FUN_6fb8f690\n3. If mouse position changed from g_dwLastMouseX/g_dwLastMouseY, update globals and either:\n   - Call FindPanelAtYCoordinate if g_fMouseDown == 0 (mouse released)\n   - Call HandlePanelMouseInteraction if mouse held (g_fMouseDown != 0)\n4. Loop through each panel in g_pPanelDataBase:\n   a. Clear panel's Y-offset field at +0x08\n   b. Check if panel enabled (field +0x04) via Ordinal_10227 validation\n   c. If enabled, invoke optional panel-specific callback at +0x110, then +0x11c\n   d. Compute centered Y position: (screen_height - 0x50) / 2 - (panel_grid_height) / 2\n   e. Switch on panel type (offset +0x00):\n      - Type 0x00, 0xFFFFFFFF: Draw border via Ordinal_10134 (cLineHeight=1)\n      - Type 0x01: Draw border via Ordinal_10134 twice (top/bottom borders, cLineHeight=1)\n      - Type 0x02: Complex rendering:\n        * Check field at +0x53c (panel state)\n        * Render optional top border if state non-zero\n        * Calculate scroll viewport width based on panel state\n        * Call FUN_6fb92980 twice to fill left/right viewport regions\n        * Render center button via Ordinal_10134\n        * Initialize auStack_48 array (18 DWORDs) with g_pValidationError3 at [1]\n        * Call Ordinal_10072 to render scrollable text content\n5. After panels, initialize local_90 array (18 DWORDs)\n6. Set local_90[1] = FUN_6fb5d980() (animation frame value)\n7. Set local_90[2] = (g_dwScrollAnimCounter == 0) ? 0 : 8 - g_dwScrollAnimCounter\n8. Call Ordinal_10072 twice for left/right scroll indicators at fixed X offsets\n9. Increment g_dwScrollAnimCounter with wrap-around: (counter + 1) & 0x80000007, then SAR 31 adjustment\n10. Return void\n\nParameters: None\n\nReturns: void (no return value)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If g_nPanelCount is NULL or g_pPanelDataBase is 0, call Ordinal_10023 (debug assertion) then FUN_6fb9a10f exit\n- Panel type 0x02 uses conditional logic for dual viewports based on state field +0x53c\n- Magic number 0x550 = size of each panel structure entry\n- Magic number 0x80000007 = bitmask for counter wrap-around (mod 8 with sign extension)\n- __ftol converts FP to int (division result for viewport positioning)\n- NEG/SBB pattern implements sign extension for counter modulo\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x550: Panel structure stride (1360 bytes)\n- 0xc8: Stack frame size (200 bytes)\n- 0x50: Y-offset adjustment (80 pixels)\n- 0x90, 0x3c: X-position offsets for dual viewport modes\n- 0x1e: Line height constant (30 pixels)\n- 0x121, 0xe6: Viewport width calculations (289, 230 pixels)\n- 0xf9, 0x0f9: Scroll indicator X-offset (249 pixels)\n- 0x80000007: Counter modulo 8 bitmask\n- 0xffffffff: Sentinel color value (opaque white in 0xARGB)\n\nRelated Functions:\n- FindPanelAtYCoordinate() - Locate panel under mouse cursor\n- HandlePanelMouseInteraction() - Process mouse drag on active panel\n- Ordinal_10023 - Debug assertion output (Storm.dll)\n- Ordinal_10072, Ordinal_10134 - Rendering primitives (Fog.dll)\n- Ordinal_10227 - Panel validation check\n- FUN_6fb8f680/FUN_6fb8f690 - Get mouse X/Y coordinates\n- FUN_6fb92980 - Fill rectangle primitive\n- FUN_6fb5d980 - Get animation frame counter\n- FUN_6fb5e930 - Check for animation update trigger",
      "tags": ["MOD_UI", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "STRUCT_Room2", "STRUCT_ItemData", "PARAM_0", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData", "STRUCT_StatList", "SRC_Restart.cpp", "PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Path", "STRUCT_Skill"]
