      "api_calls": ["GfxInterfaceCall84", "GfxInterfaceCall84"],
      "instructions": ["0x67440|SUB|ESP, 0x48", "0x67443|MOV|ECX, 0x17", "0x67448|PUSH|EBX", "0x67449|PUSH|EBP", "0x6744A|PUSH|ESI", "0x6744B|PUSH|EDI", "0x6744C|XOR|EDI, EDI", "0x6744E|XOR|ESI, ESI", "0x67450|CALL|0x6fb5d340", "0x67455|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0x67457|MOV|EBP, 0x1", "0x6745C|JNZ|0x6fb37542", "0x67462|MOV|ECX, 0x19", "0x67467|CALL|0x6fb5d340", "0x6746C|TEST|EAX, EAX"],
      "comment": "Update game UI state and render mode based on game state and mode flags\nValidates multiple game state conditions and adjusts UI rendering modes accordingly\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check all 14 core game state validity flags (checks performed via FUN_6fb5d340 with various state indices)\n2. If all core state flags pass (return 0), set g_fGameStateInitialCheckFailed = 0\n3. Otherwise, set flag = 1 indicating state validation failure\n4. Check additional state flag 0x24; if set, mark g_fGameStateInitialCheckFailed = 1\n5. Validate secondary state flags (different indices); if any set (non-zero), set g_fGameModeWarningActive = 1\n6. Check flag 0x1f; if set OR game state inactive (IsGameStateActive), mark warning active\n7. Check game mode via GetGameModeFlag; if mode > 1, mark warning active\n8. Check flags 1 and 4; if both clear (zero), clear g_fGameModeWarningActive; otherwise set to 1\n9. Branch logic:\n   - If fGameStateCheckFailed AND fGameModeWarning: disable all UI panels (call Update functions with 0), set render mode = 1\n   - If fGameStateCheckFailed only: initialize UI buffer, place window at calculated screen position, disable panel 3, render button array, set render mode = 0\n   - If fGameModeWarning only: disable all panels (call functions with 1), set render mode = 0\n   - If neither flag set: initialize UI buffer, place window at alternate position, disable panel 2, disable panel 1, set render mode = 0\n\nParameters:\n(none)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Updates global UI state flags and triggers UI rendering updates\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Screen position calculations depend on g_fResolutionMode flag (normal vs expanded resolution)\n- UI button array (g_aUIButtonArray) processed conditionally based on render mode\n- Button iteration uses dynamic count (7 or 8) based on resolution mode\n- Button offset calculation adds +1 if field [0x10] equals 1\n\nRelated Functions:\n- FUN_6fb5d340 - Check game state flag\n- IsGameStateActive - Query if game is active\n- GetGameModeFlag - Get current game mode\n- FUN_6fb377e0 - Update UI panel (call with 0, 1, or disable)\n- FUN_6fb37910 - Update button panel\n- FUN_6fb379f0 - Update text/help panel\n- FUN_6fb37aa0 - Update status panel\n- FUN_6fb378d0 - Render button at position",
      "tags": ["PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PARAM_0", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
