      "instructions": ["0x678D0|SUB|ESP, 0x48", "0x678D3|PUSH|ESI", "0x678D4|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0x678D6|PUSH|EDI", "0x678D7|MOV|ECX, 0x12", "0x678DC|XOR|EAX, EAX", "0x678DE|LEA|EDI, [ESP + 0x8]", "0x678E2|STOSD.REP|ES:EDI", "0x678E4|MOV|ECX, dword ptr [ESP + 0x54]", "0x678E8|MOV|EAX, [0x6fbfa18c]", "0x678ED|PUSH|0x0", "0x678EF|PUSH|0x5", "0x678F1|PUSH|-0x1", "0x678F3|PUSH|ECX", "0x678F4|PUSH|EDX"],
      "comment": "Render a game UI element at the specified screen coordinates.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize 72-byte (18 dword) buffer on stack\n2. Set buffer[1] to UI element configuration table pointer\n3. Set buffer[2] to element index nElementIndex\n4. Call Ordinal_10072 (rendering function) with:\n   - Buffer as first parameter (contains configuration)\n   - X coordinate (dwX)\n   - Y coordinate (dwY)\n   - Color mask (0xFFFFFFFF = white)\n   - Drawing mode (5)\n   - Reserved flag (0)\n\nParameters:\nnElementIndex (ECX) - Element table index to render\ndwX (EDX) - Screen X coordinate for element placement\ndwY (Stack+4) - Screen Y coordinate for element placement\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value, updates screen buffer via Ordinal_10072 call\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Always uses 0xFFFFFFFF (white) color mask\n- Drawing mode fixed at 5 (standard UI drawing)\n- Buffer must be zeroed before configuration (REP STOSD)",
