      "instructions": ["0x67910|PUSH|ECX", "0x67911|PUSH|EBX", "0x67912|MOV|EBX, dword ptr [0x6fbfa1a0]", "0x67918|PUSH|EBP", "0x67919|XOR|EBP, EBP", "0x6791B|PUSH|ESI", "0x6791C|PUSH|EDI", "0x6791D|CMP|EBX, EBP", "0x6791F|MOV|EDI, 0x8", "0x67924|JZ|0x6fb3792b", "0x67926|MOV|EDI, 0x7", "0x6792B|CMP|ECX, EBP", "0x6792D|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x10], EBP", "0x67931|JZ|0x6fb379e3", "0x67937|MOV|EAX, [0x6fbae0e4]"],
      "comment": "Initialize panel slot positions and related data based on screen dimensions and panel configuration.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Read panel configuration flag from g_dwPanelConfig\n2. Calculate number of slot rows: 8 rows if config=0, 7 rows if config!=0\n3. Calculate base X position: screen_width/2 - offset, adjusted for panel type and config\n   - Type 1: offset = 0xCA (left side)\n   - Type 3 with config=0: offset = 0x23 (far right)\n   - Type 3 with config!=0: offset = 0x39 (right)\n   - Other: offset = 0x54 (right), or 0x4A if config!=0\n4. Calculate base Y position: screen_height - 0x32\n5. Initialize array headers g_aPanelSlotXPositions[0] and g_aPanelSlotYPositions[0] with base positions\n6. For each slot row (1 to uRowCount-1):\n   - Calculate X position: add 0x15 (21 pixels) per row to base X\n   - Store in g_aPanelSlotXPositions[row] and g_aPanelSlotYPositions[row]\n   - If config=0 (disabled): slot indices = row, slot values = row*2\n   - If config!=0 (enabled): slot indices = accumulator + row, slot values = penalty + row*2\n     - Penalty increases by 2 every 3 rows, accumulator increments once every 3 rows\n   - Store calculated indices/values in g_aPanelSlotIndices and g_aPanelSlotValues\n\nParameters:\nnPanelType (int, ECX) - Panel type identifier (0=default, 1=left variant, 3=right variant)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Function modifies global arrays\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If nPanelType=0, no initialization occurs (early return)\n- Panel configuration affects both positioning and slot mapping\n- Slot penalty system only applies when config!=0",
      "tags": ["PARAM_1", "PROP_LEAF"]
    },
