      "instructions": ["0x679F0|SUB|ESP, 0x90", "0x679F6|MOV|EAX, 0x8", "0x679FB|TEST|ECX, ECX", "0x679FD|JZ|0x6fb37a93", "0x67A03|MOV|ECX, dword ptr [0x6fbfa1a0]", "0x67A09|TEST|ECX, ECX", "0x67A0B|JZ|0x6fb37a12", "0x67A0D|MOV|EAX, 0x7", "0x67A12|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0x67A14|JLE|0x6fb37a93", "0x67A16|PUSH|EBX", "0x67A17|PUSH|ESI", "0x67A18|PUSH|EDI", "0x67A19|MOV|ESI, 0x6fbfa138", "0x67A1E|MOV|EBX, EAX"],
      "comment": "Process UI slot rendering queue with conditional initialization.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize maximum slot count (8 or 7) based on DAT_6fbfa1a0 flag\n2. If slot count is zero, return early\n3. For each available slot (iterate nMaxSlots times):\n   - Check if slot is active (piVar3[-8] == 1)\n   - If active: Initialize aRenderData1 with incremented slot index and global value\n   - If inactive: Initialize aRenderData2 with current slot index and global value\n   - Call Ordinal_10072 to render the buffer\n   - Advance slot pointer by 4 bytes\n\nParameters:\n- nSlotCount (ECX): Number of UI slots to process; if 0, function returns immediately\n- Implicit globals: DAT_6fbfa1a0 (flag), DAT_6fbfa138 (slot array base), DAT_6fbfa18c (config value)\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If nSlotCount is 0, function exits without processing\n- Maximum slot count is reduced to 7 if DAT_6fbfa1a0 is non-zero\n- Stack arrays are cleared before use (18 dwords each)",
