      "comment": "Process panel slot mouse hit detection and key binding display\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get current mouse position (screen coordinates)\n2. Adjust X coordinate based on button parameter (-0x76 for button 1, 0x77 for button 3)\n3. Check if mouse is within right-side panel boundaries (Y: screen_height-0x45 to -0x2f, X: adjusted ± 0x59)\n4. If resolution mode flag set (DAT_6fbfa1a0 != 0), slot count = 7, else 8\n5. Iterate through panel slot array (g_aPanelSlots), checking each slot X position\n6. If slot X in range [slot_x, slot_x+0x14):\n   a. Get command ID from slot offset +0x10\n   b. Clear 400-char Unicode buffer (local_190)\n   c. Call Ordinal_10004 (unknown, likely preprocessing)\n   d. Copy base string to destination\n   e. If valid command ID (not 0x39):\n      - Look up primary key binding (slot offset +0x8)\n      - If key exists (wKeyCode != 0xffff):\n        * Clear 60-char Unicode buffer (aUStack_1cc)\n        * Get key binding string and format into buffer via Ordinal_10004\n        * Concatenate formatted key string to destination\n      - Look up secondary key binding\n      - Same process as primary if key exists\n   f. Trigger panel update via Ordinal_10129 (slot_offset-0x1a, 0, 1)\n\nParameters:\n  nMouseButton (ECX): Mouse button identifier (0=left, 1=middle, 3=right); used to adjust X offset\n\nReturns:\n  void; updates UI panel display as side effect\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Button 0: no X offset adjustment\n  - Button 1: offset -0x76 pixels\n  - Button 3: offset +0x77 pixels\n  - Other buttons: no special handling\n  - 0x39 is sentinel command ID indicating no key binding display\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x54: X offset bounds lower (-84 decimal)\n  0x59: X offset bounds upper (+89 decimal)\n  0x45: Y coordinate bottom boundary (69 decimal)\n  0x2f: Y coordinate top boundary (47 decimal)\n  0x14: Slot width (20 decimal)\n  0x1a: Offset adjustment for panel update (26 decimal)\n  0x76: Button 1 X offset magnitude (118 decimal, negative)\n  0x77: Button 3 X offset magnitude (119 decimal)\n  0xffff: Invalid key code sentinel\n  0x39: Invalid command ID sentinel\n  0xc8: Unicode buffer size (200 elements)\n  0x1e: Small key binding buffer size (30 elements)",
      "tags": ["PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "STRUCT_Skill", "STRUCT_ItemData", "PARAM_1", "PROP_LOOPHEAVY", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
