      "comment": "Processes a panel slot click event by checking cursor position against UI panel slots.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get game context and check if panel click is pending (g_fPanelClickPending)\n2. Clear pending flag and validate game context has valid inventory owner\n3. If inventory owner is null (no unit selected), proceed with click processing\n4. Get screen state; if not state 7, call SetGameStateForUnit(0)\n5. Determine slot count based on resolution mode (8 for 640x480, 7 for 800x600+)\n6. If UI render mode is active, skip processing\n7. Extract cursor X (low word) and Y (high word) from pClickEvent[3]\n8. Clear UI element state array (g_adwUIElementState)\n9. Calculate panel center X position with adjustments:\n   - Base: g_dwScreenWidth / 2\n   - If game state active and mode > 1: subtract 0x76 (118px)\n   - If warning active: subtract additional 0x76\n   - If initial check failed: add 0x77 (119px)\n10. Check if cursor is within panel bounds:\n    - X: (center - 0x54) to (center + 0x59)\n    - Y: (screenHeight - 0x45) to (screenHeight - 0x2f)\n11. If within bounds, iterate through panel slots:\n    - Check if cursor X is within slot X position + 0x14 (20px width)\n    - Check slot index == 7 OR (game state[0] == 0 AND state[3] != 0x11)\n    - Dispatch to HandlePanelModeDispatcher with slot index\n12. Call InitializeTargetingSystem and ClearTargetingState\n13. Set event handled flag (pClickEvent[6] = 1) and cache the event\n14. If cursor outside bounds, set pClickEvent[6] = 0\n\nParameters:\n  pClickEvent - Pointer to click event structure:\n    +0x0C: Packed cursor position (low word = X, high word = Y)\n    +0x18: Event handled flag (1 = handled, 0 = not handled)\n    +0x1C: Reserved (set to 0 on success)\n\nReturns: void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Returns early if g_fPanelClickPending is 0\n  - Returns early if game context is null\n  - Returns early if inventory pointer is null\n  - Returns early if inventory has valid owner (unit selected)\n  - Skips slot processing if g_fUIRenderMode is non-zero\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  - 0x84: Offset to inventory pointer in game context\n  - 7: Screen state for panel mode / slot index for special handling\n  - 8/7: Slot count for 640x480 / 800x600+ resolutions\n  - 0x54 (84): Left panel boundary offset from center\n  - 0x59 (89): Right panel boundary offset from center\n  - 0x45 (69): Top panel boundary offset from screen bottom\n  - 0x2f (47): Bottom panel boundary offset from screen bottom\n  - 0x14 (20): Panel slot width in pixels\n  - 0x76 (118): Panel position adjustment for game mode\n  - 0x77 (119): Panel position adjustment for failed state\n  - 0x11 (17): Game state value that blocks slot interaction",
