      "comment": "Dispatches handler code based on panel mode index (0-7).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Compare nPanelMode with 7 (bounds check)\n2. If nPanelMode > 7, return immediately\n3. Jump to handler via jump table at [nPanelMode * 4 + 0x6fb3808c]\n4. Each handler (0-5) calls FUN_6fb5d340 with mode index to check availability\n5. Based on result (0 = unavailable, non-zero = available), call FUN_6fb5d370 with appropriate status code (1=available, 2=unavailable)\n6. Handler 6: Output debug string \"Panel_quest_log_toggle\", call InitializeGameMode(0)\n7. Handler 7: Execute shutdown sequence - call FUN_6fb5d910, FUN_6fb5d9a0, InitializePanelMode, FUN_6fb5d9b0, FUN_6fb5d9c0\n\nParameters:\nnPanelMode (ECX register) - dword: Panel mode identifier (0=panel0, 1=panel1, 2=panel2, 3=server, 4=panel4, 5=combined, 6=quest, 7=shutdown)\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Mode 3 (server): Only executes if GetCurrentServerPort() returns non-zero\n- Mode 5: First checks FUN_6fb5d340(0x1f), then FUN_6fb5d340(0x18) and returns after both checks\n- All modes except 6 and 7 use same pattern: check availability via FUN_6fb5d340, then call FUN_6fb5d370 with status\n- Note: Function uses 1 stack-allocated temporary (iVar2 result) optimized away by compiler",
