      "comment": "Processes a mouse click event on the bottom panel slot region.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Determine max slot count based on screen resolution mode (8 for 640x480, 7 otherwise)\n2. Get game context and validate inventory owner exists\n3. Call INVENTORY_GetOwner - if owner exists (non-null), exit early\n4. Check g_fUIRenderMode flag - if set, exit early\n5. Extract click X coordinate (low word) and Y coordinate (high word) from pClickEvent+0xc\n6. Calculate horizontal center offset based on game state flags:\n   - If IsGameStateActive() and GetGameModeFlag() > 1: offset = -0x76 (-118)\n   - If g_fGameModeWarningActive: offset -= 0x76 (-118)\n   - If g_fGameStateInitialCheckFailed: offset += 0x77 (+119)\n7. Calculate panel center: g_dwScreenWidth/2 + offset\n8. Validate X coordinate is within panel bounds (center-84 to center+89)\n9. Validate Y coordinate is within screen bottom region (height-69 to height-47)\n10. Iterate through g_aPanelSlotXPositions array to find slot containing click X\n11. If slot found and g_aPanelSlotIndices[slot] != 7 (not skill slot):\n    - Check game context state and UI resource availability\n    - Apply slot restrictions based on server port and slot index\n12. Set g_adwUIElementState[slot] = 1 to mark slot as active\n13. Call InitializeGameObjectProperties(4, 0, 0.0, 0.0, 0)\n14. Set g_fPanelClickPending = 1 and update pClickEvent result fields\n15. Call InsertCacheNodeWithCookie to queue click event\n\nParameters:\n  pClickEvent - Pointer to click event structure:\n    +0x0C: uint - Packed coordinates (low word=X, high word=Y)\n    +0x18: uint - Result flag (set to 1 on success)\n    +0x1C: uint - Secondary result (set to 0)\n\nReturns: void\n\nLocal Variables (SSA temporaries):\n  nMaxSlotCount (local_8) - Maximum slot count (7 or 8 based on resolution)\n  uVar1 (dwPackedCoords) - Packed X/Y coordinates from pClickEvent[3]\n  uVar10 (wClickX) - Click X coordinate (low word of packed coords)\n  uVar1 >> 16 (wClickY) - Click Y coordinate (high word of packed coords)\n  pvVar3 (pGameContext) - Game context pointer from GetGameContext()\n  pUVar4 (pInventoryOwner) - Inventory owner from INVENTORY_GetOwner\n  piVar5 (pGameState) - Second game context pointer for state checks\n  piVar8 (pSlotXPos) - Pointer to current slot X position in array\n  iVar9 (nSlotIndex) - Current slot index during iteration\n  bVar2 (fGameActive) - Result from IsGameStateActive()\n  uVar6 (dwGameMode) - Result from GetGameModeFlag()\n  dVar7 (dwResourceResult) - Result from UI resource/server port calls\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Exit early if game context is NULL\n- Exit early if inventory at context+0x84 is NULL\n- Exit early if INVENTORY_GetOwner returns non-NULL (has owner)\n- Exit early if g_fUIRenderMode is set\n- Exit early if click coordinates outside panel bounds\n- Slot 7 (skill slot) bypasses UI resource validation\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x54 (84): Panel left bound offset from center\n- 0x59 (89): Panel right bound offset from center\n- 0x45 (69): Panel top bound offset from screen bottom\n- 0x2f (47): Panel bottom bound offset from screen bottom\n- 0x14 (20): Panel slot width in pixels\n- 0x76 (118): Horizontal offset adjustment for game mode\n- 0x77 (119): Horizontal offset adjustment for state check failed\n- 0x11 (17): Special UI state value at context+0xC\n\nGlobals Referenced:\n- g_dwScreenResolutionMode: Screen resolution mode flag\n- g_fUIRenderMode: UI render mode flag\n- g_fGameModeWarningActive: Game mode warning state\n- g_fGameStateInitialCheckFailed: Initial state check failure flag\n- g_dwScreenWidth: Screen width in pixels\n- g_dwScreenHeight: Screen height in pixels\n- g_aPanelSlotXPositions: Array of panel slot X positions\n- g_aPanelSlotIndices: Array of slot type indices (7=skill slot)\n- g_adwUIElementState: Array of UI element active states\n- g_fPanelClickPending: Panel click pending flag",
