      "comment": "Check if screen coordinates fall within automap interaction bounds.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Read global screen width (g_dwScreenWidth) and height (g_dwScreenHeight)\n2. Calculate horizontal center: width / 2\n3. Calculate left bound: center - 0x4a (74 pixels)\n4. Calculate right bound: center + 0x47 (71 pixels)\n5. Calculate top bound: height - 0x45 (69 pixels)\n6. Calculate bottom bound: height - 0x32 (50 pixels)\n7. Check if nX in range [left_bound, right_bound) AND nY in range (top_bound, bottom_bound)\n8. Return 1 (true) if all conditions met, 0 (false) otherwise\n\nParameters:\n- nX (ECX, dword): X-coordinate on screen\n- nY (EDX, dword): Y-coordinate on screen\n\nReturns:\n- 1: Coordinates are within automap bounds\n- 0: Coordinates are outside automap bounds\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Bounds are asymmetric (74px left margin vs 71px right margin)\n- Vertical bounds depend on screen height\n- Used for click detection in automap UI window",
      "tags": ["PARAM_2", "PROP_LEAF"]
    },
