      "api_count": 0,
      "api_calls": [],
      "instructions": ["0x68390|PUSH|EBX", "0x68391|PUSH|EDI", "0x68392|CALL|0x6fb8f680", "0x68397|MOV|EDI, EAX", "0x68399|CALL|0x6fb8f690", "0x6839E|MOV|ECX, 0x14", "0x683A3|MOV|EBX, EAX", "0x683A5|CALL|0x6fb5d340", "0x683AA|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0x683AC|JZ|0x6fb38416", "0x683AE|MOV|ECX, 0x15", "0x683B3|CALL|0x6fb5d340", "0x683B8|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0x683BA|JZ|0x6fb38416", "0x683BC|MOV|EAX, [0x6fbae0e4]"],
      "comment": "Checks if a mouse point is within an active UI inventory slot region\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get current mouse X coordinate via FUN_6fb8f680\n2. Get current mouse Y coordinate via FUN_6fb8f690\n3. Check if item is in slot 0x14 (upper slot), abort if not present\n4. Check if item is in slot 0x15 (lower slot), abort if not present\n5. Calculate slot origin X based on g_dwUISlotExtendedFlag\n   - If flag is clear: originX = (ScreenWidth / 2) + 0x23\n   - If flag is set: originX = (ScreenWidth / 2) + 0x38\n6. Determine slot width (column count) based on g_dwUISlotExtendedFlag\n   - If flag is clear: width = 8 columns\n   - If flag is set: width = 7 columns\n7. Calculate slot height in pixels: height = width * 0x14 (20 pixels per column)\n8. Calculate Y bounds: minY = ScreenHeight - 0x4c (332), maxY = ScreenHeight - 0x32 (366)\n9. Validate point is within bounds:\n   - X in range [originX, originX + height)\n   - Y in range [minY, maxY)\n10. Return 1 if point in region, else 0\n\nParameters:\n(implicit) g_dwUISlotExtendedFlag - Flag controlling extended UI mode\n(implicit) g_dwScreenWidth - Current screen width\n(implicit) g_dwScreenHeight - Current screen height\n\nReturns:\n1 if mouse coordinates are within the slot region\n0 if outside region or slot items not present\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Returns immediately if either slot 0x14 or 0x15 is empty\n- UI dimensions scale based on g_dwUISlotExtendedFlag (extended vs compact)\n- Height calculation uses stride of 0x14 (20 decimal) pixels per column\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x14 (20 decimal) - Pixels per slot column (height stride)\n0x23 (35 decimal) - Base X offset for compact UI mode\n0x38 (56 decimal) - Base X offset for extended UI mode\n0x4c (76 decimal) - Y offset subtracted from screen height (minY = height - 76)\n0x32 (50 decimal) - Y offset subtracted from screen height (maxY = height - 50)",
      "tags": ["PARAM_0"]
    },
