      "comment": "Initializes the collision unit data array by calling a constructor on each element.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load pointer to g_abCollisionUnitData (0x6fbfa1bc) into ESI\n2. Set loop counter EDI to 32 (0x20 elements)\n3. Loop: Call CallFunctionOnRange with current element pointer\n   - Parameters: element pointer, stride=2, count=0x80 (128), constructor callback\n4. Advance pointer by 0x120 (288) bytes to next element\n5. Decrement counter and repeat until all 32 elements initialized\n\nParameters:\n  None (uses globals)\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nStructure Layout (Collision Unit Data Element):\n  Size: 0x120 (288) bytes per element\n  Total array: 32 elements × 288 bytes = 9216 bytes\n  Base: g_abCollisionUnitData (0x6fbfa1bc)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Each element contains 128 sub-elements (stride 2, count 0x80)\n  - Constructor callback from g_pfnUnicodeConstructor (0x6fba5c30)\n\nCalled From:\n  - Function pointer table at 0x6fbae03c (initialization table)",
