      "instructions": ["0x68450|SUB|ESP, 0x8", "0x68453|MOV|EAX, [0x6fbae0e8]", "0x68458|PUSH|EBX", "0x68459|PUSH|EBP", "0x6845A|ADD|EAX, -0x30", "0x6845D|MOV|EBP, EDX", "0x6845F|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x8], EAX", "0x68463|MOV|EDX, dword ptr [ECX]", "0x68465|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [ESP + 0x24]", "0x68469|PUSH|ESI", "0x6846A|CMP|EDX, EAX", "0x6846C|PUSH|EDI", "0x6846D|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x14], EBP", "0x68471|JGE|0x6fb38487", "0x68473|MOV|EDI, dword ptr [ESP + 0x1c]"],
      "comment": "Validates and adjusts a viewport rectangle against collision boundaries.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load screen height and calculate maximum Y coordinate (screen_height - 48)\n2. Validate minimum X: if MinX < nMinX, adjust MaxX and set MinX to minimum threshold\n3. Validate minimum Y: if MinY < 6, adjust MaxY and set MinY to 6\n4. Validate maximum X: if MaxX >= nItemWidth, reduce MaxX and MinX by (MaxX - nItemWidth + 1)\n5. Validate maximum Y: if MaxY >= screen_max_y, clamp MaxY to screen_max_y\n6. Check collision rect count: if count > 31, raise assertion failure\n7. Iterate collision rectangles: for each collision rect, test both X and Y bounds\n8. X-bounds check: piVar6[2] >= MinX AND MaxX >= piVar6[0]\n9. Y-bounds check: piVar6[3] >= MinY AND MaxY >= piVar6[1]\n10. If both checks pass: adjust viewport based on nItemWidth and calculate final position\n11. Return 0 on successful collision adjustment, return 1 if no collision detected\n\nParameters:\npMinX - Pointer to minimum X coordinate of viewport (adjusted in-place)\npMinY - Pointer to minimum Y coordinate of viewport (adjusted in-place)\npMaxX - Pointer to maximum X coordinate of viewport (adjusted in-place)\npMaxY - Pointer to maximum Y coordinate of viewport (adjusted in-place)\nnItemWidth - Item width threshold for maximum X boundary\nnItemHeight - Unused parameter (reserved for height threshold)\nnMinX - Minimum X coordinate threshold for validation\n\nReturns:\n0 - Viewport successfully adjusted for collision\n1 - No collision detected or viewport out of bounds\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x30 (48) - Screen height offset\n0x6 (6) - Minimum Y coordinate threshold\n0x20 (32) - Collision rect count limit (assertion check at 31+)\n0x48 (72) - Collision rect structure stride\n0x120 (288) - Collision rect structure entry size in array\n\nStructure Layout - Collision Rectangle (72 bytes):\nOffset | Size | Field Name | Type | Description\n0x0    | 4    | left       | int  | Rect left boundary\n0x4    | 4    | bottom     | int  | Rect bottom boundary\n0x8    | 4    | right      | int  | Rect right boundary\n0xc    | 4    | top        | int  | Rect top boundary\n0x10   | 52   | reserved   | byte | Unused padding\n\nRelated Functions:\n- FUN_6fb38640() - Calls this function\n- Ordinal_10023() - Error handler for collision rect validation",
      "tags": ["PARAM_7", "MOD_UI", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "SRC_showitems.cpp", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
