      "api_calls": ["GetExpansionModeIfInitialized", "UNITS_GetRoom", "ExtractRoomTileList", "FindPaletteIndexForColor", "UNITS_GetUnitX", "STATLIST_GetUnitOwnerType", "ValidateCoordinateRange", "GfxIsDisplayTypeAccelerated", "GetUnitLevel", "GetUnitX", "...+10 more"],
      "instructions": ["0x68640|SUB|ESP, 0x48", "0x68643|PUSH|ESI", "0x68644|CALL|0x6fb99256", "0x68649|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x34], EAX", "0x6864D|CALL|0x6fb62880", "0x68652|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0x68654|JZ|0x6fb38af4", "0x6865A|PUSH|EAX", "0x6865B|CALL|0x6fb98164", "0x68660|MOV|ESI, EAX", "0x68662|TEST|ESI, ESI", "0x68664|JZ|0x6fb38af4", "0x6866A|PUSH|EDI", "0x6866B|CALL|0x6fae52a0", "0x68670|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x4c], EAX"],
      "comment": "Process viewport units and build collision rect table for rendering.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get current center unit from game state (Ordinal_10010)\n2. Get selected unit (FUN_6fb62880) and its data (Ordinal_10342)\n3. Get viewport dimensions and resource context\n4. Retrieve main unit from resource handle (GetValidatedResourceHandle)\n5. Get viewport bounds (Ordinal_10035) - extract min Y and room count\n6. For each room (0 to dwRoomCount): \n   a. Get first unit in room chain from room data\n   b. Walk unit linked list (pUnit[0x43] = next unit)\n   c. Check if unit visible: (flags & 0x80) != 0 AND type == 4 (monster)\n   d. If visible and room count < 0x20: store unit in collision table\n7. Calculate screen position based on center unit type:\n   - If center unit: use viewport offset from GetRelativeViewportX/GetViewportYOffsetAdjusted\n   - Otherwise: use Ordinal_10327/10330 for isometric coords, apply scroll window offset\n8. For each valid unit, check if screen position within bounds\n9. Build collision rectangle using FUN_6fb5a690 (get unit bounds)\n10. Call ProcessViewportCollision up to 0xc times to resolve collisions\n11. Store collision rect in arrays (left/bottom/right/top)\n12. Determine unit color/palette based on type and flags (switch on Ordinal_10695)\n13. Render collision rects via Ordinal_10132\n14. Clear unit selection if no units processed (local_30 = 0)\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Color palette depends on unit type: demon (3), undead (2), boss (9), superunique (4), champion (8), other (5)\n- Center unit displayed with selected color (5) if within viewport\n- Non-center units use type-specific palette or flag-based colors (0x800/0x400000)\n- Scroll window offset applied for split screen modes (modes 1-2)\n- Collision checking limited to 0xc attempts per unit\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x3b: Unit flags offset within unit structure\n- 0x80: Unit visibility flag bit\n- 0x2c: Room unit list pointer offset\n- 0x43: Unit next pointer offset (in dwords)\n- 0x48: Collision rect entry stride in arrays\n- 0x20: Maximum collision rects\n- 0x90: Unit data stride for rendering\n- 0x40/0x80: Color palette selection flags\n- 0xc: Max collision resolution attempts\n- 0x2a: Character name offset in inventory\n- 0x80 (at offset 0x80): Magic number check in inventory\n\nData Structures:\nUnits are processed from room data structures. Unit type 4 = monsters.\nCollision rectangles stored in arrays with 0x48 byte stride:\n  Offset | Size | Field          | Type     | Purpose\n  0x0    | 4    | nLeft          | int      | Left edge screen X\n  0x4    | 4    | nBottom        | int      | Bottom edge screen Y  \n  0x8    | 4    | nRight         | int      | Right edge screen X\n  0xc    | 4    | nTop           | int      | Top edge screen Y\n  0x10.. | ...  | unitData       | byte[..] | Unit rendering data",
      "tags": ["MOD_UI", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "STRUCT_Room2", "STRUCT_ItemData", "PARAM_0", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData", "STRUCT_StatList", "PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Path", "STRUCT_Skill", "SRC_showitems.cpp", "PROP_LOOPHEAVY"]
