      "comment": "Initializes the global BattleNet format buffer array with 8 Unicode objects.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Set pointer to start of g_szBattleNetFormatBuffer (0x6fbfc5ac)\n2. Set loop counter to 8\n3. Call Unicode::_default_constructor_closure_ for current element\n4. Advance pointer by 2 bytes to next Unicode element\n5. Decrement counter and repeat until all 8 elements initialized\n6. Return\n\nParameters: None (void)\n\nReturns: void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Called from initialization function pointer table at 0x6fbae044\n- Array contains 8 Unicode objects at 2-byte stride (16 bytes total)\n- Each Unicode object is default-constructed via virtual dispatch\n\nStructure Layout:\ng_szBattleNetFormatBuffer at 0x6fbfc5ac:\n  Offset  Size  Field           Type      Description\n  0x00    2     Unicode[0]      Unicode   First format buffer element\n  0x02    2     Unicode[1]      Unicode   Second format buffer element\n  ...\n  0x0E    2     Unicode[7]      Unicode   Eighth format buffer element\n\nRegister Usage:\n  ESI - Pointer to current Unicode element (preserved)\n  EDI - Loop counter 8..0 (preserved)\n  ECX - this pointer for constructor call",
