      "comment": "Calculate skill stat table offset based on skill ID and base offset.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. If skill ID < 0x9C (156): Calculate offset as nBaseOffset + (nSkillId * 4) + 0x27C7\n   - Convert skill ID to offset using 4-byte stride\n   - Check if battle net format initialized via Ordinal_10004 call\n   - If format strings don't match (strcmp != 0), use 0x1115 offset\n2. If skill ID in range 0xDD-0x118 (221-280): Return nBaseOffset + (nSkillId * 4) + 0x52A2\n3. If skill ID in range 0xD9-0xDC (217-220): Return nBaseOffset + (nSkillId * 4) + 0x1021\n4. Default: Return 0x1115\n\nParameters:\nnSkillId: Skill ID value (0-0x118)\nnBaseOffset: Base offset for calculation (usually loaded from game state)\n\nReturns:\nCalculated stat offset for skill properties lookup",
