      "comment": "Format and concatenate localized Unicode strings for display.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize Unicode string buffer (64 elements, 2 bytes each = 128 bytes)\n2. Read formatting parameters from structure at param_3 (offsets 0xe0, 0xe4, 0xdc)\n3. If both params at 0xe0 and 0xe4 are zero, return 0 (invalid/empty)\n4. If param_5 is non-zero (alternate format mode):\n   - Call Ordinal_10004 four times (initialization sequence)\n   - Initialize 16-element Unicode buffer\n   - Call Ordinal_578 with format string and param_5\n   - Convert result from ANSI to Unicode\n   - Append to output string via strcat (EDI register) 4 times\n5. Else (standard format mode):\n   - Calculate value: dwValue = ((param_4 - 1) * param_3[0xe4] + param_3[0xe0]) << shift\n   - If param_2 == 6: clamp dwValue to 0 if negative\n   - Else: clamp dwValue to minimum 0x100\n   - If depth=8 OR param_3[0xe4]<<shift > 0x100 OR dwValue > 0xc00 (large format):\n     a. Calculate high nibble: iHigh = dwValue >> 8\n     b. Format to string using g_szLocalizationConfig with iHigh\n     c. Convert to Unicode, call Ordinal_10004, append to output\n   - Else (normal format):\n     a. Extract low byte and scale: iCounter = (dwValue & 0xff) * 10 >> 8\n     b. Calculate iHigh = dwValue >> 8\n     c. If iCounter == 0: format with just iHigh parameter\n     d. Else: format with both iHigh and iCounter parameters\n     e. Convert result to Unicode, call Ordinal_10004, append to output\n6. Call strcat_exref function pointer (stored in EBX/pfnStrcat)\n7. Call Ordinal_10004 again\n8. Call strcat_exref one final time\n9. Return 1 (success)\n\nParameters:\n- nIndex (dword): Resource or string index/selector passed in ECX\n- nParam2 (int): Mode selector (0x6 = special handling, 0xdd = alternate path)\n- nParam3 (int): Pointer to configuration structure with offsets:\n                 +0xdc: shift amount (usually 8)\n                 +0xe0: base height/scale value\n                 +0xe4: multiplier or divisor\n- nParam4 (int): Height or scaling factor (typically decremented for calculation)\n- nParam5 (int): Alternate format parameter when non-zero (bitmask or index)\n\nReturns:\n- 0 if parameters invalid (both config values at 0xe0/0xe4 are zero)\n- 1 if formatting and concatenation successful\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Magic value 0x100: minimum threshold for small formats\n- Magic value 0xc00: threshold triggering large format path\n- Ordinal_10004: Called multiple times, likely for string pool/reference management\n- Ordinal_578: Unknown ordinal, called with format string for alternate format\n- strcat_exref: Function pointer stored in global (likely Unicode::strcat)\n- unaff_ESI, unaff_EDI: Unaffected registers containing source/destination strings\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x20 (32 decimal): Size of initialization loops for Unicode buffers\n- 0xdc: Stack frame size\n- 0xe0, 0xe4: Offsets into parameter structure\n- 0xc: Return stack cleanup (5 parameters * 2 + 1)\n- 0x100: Minimum threshold (256 decimal)\n- 0xc00: Large format threshold (3072 decimal)\n- 0x6: Special mode indicator\n- 0xdd: Alternate format mode indicator\n- 0x109f, 0x5511, 0x5300-0x5305: Resource/string pool identifiers",
