      "comment": "Calculates adjusted screen coordinates for item text rendering and draws range text.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize position (nPosX, nPosY) and flags to zero\n2. Call CalcImageCoordinates to get base coordinates from item record\n3. Read scale factor from pItemRecord+0x129 (byte field)\n4. If scale factor is non-zero:\n   a. Get item inventory dimensions via GetItemInventorySize\n   b. Apply dimension adjustments via CalculateAdjustedDimensions\n   c. Calculate X offset: (nParam3 * dwScaleFactor) / 8 (with signed rounding)\n   d. Calculate Y offset: (nAdjustedHeight * dwScaleFactor) / 8 (with signed rounding)\n   e. Add offsets to base positions\n5. Call DrawRangeText with final coordinates\n\nParameters:\n  pnItemCode (ECX) - Pointer to item code/identifier used for size lookup\n  pItemRecord (EDX) - Pointer to item record structure (byte at +0x129 is scale factor)\n  nParam3 - Image index passed to CalcImageCoordinates\n  nTextParam1 - First text parameter passed to DrawRangeText\n  nTextParam2 - Second text parameter passed to DrawRangeText\n  nTextParam3 - Third text parameter passed to DrawRangeText\n\nReturns: void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If scale factor at pItemRecord+0x129 is 0, skips dimension adjustment entirely\n  - Division by 8 uses signed rounding: (val + (val>>31 & 7)) >> 3\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x129 - Offset to scale factor byte in item record\n  0x7 (7) - Mask for signed division rounding correction\n  0x3 - Shift amount for divide-by-8",
