      "comment": "Calculate image coordinates with zoom and modifier effects.\n\nNote: Function uses 4 stack-allocated temporaries optimized away (uVar3, uVar4, iVar1, iVar2 reused across statements).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get base delta value via Ordinal_11045 (D2Common.GetUnitStat)\n2. Check image mode flag at offset 0x50 (value 0x05 for scaled mode)\n3. If scaled mode:\n   - Set output mode to 2\n   - Get multiplier via Ordinal_11046 (D2Common.GetUnitStat)\n   - Multiply by param_2-1, add offset at 0x56\n   - Fetch base X/Y at offsets 0x51, 0x52, add delta\n   - Left shift by scale factor at 0x4a (masked to 0x1f bits)\n   - Multiply by multiplier, right shift by 8 (divide by 256)\n4. If standard mode:\n   - Fetch base X/Y, add delta\n   - Right shift by (8 - scale factor), masked to 0x1f bits\n5. Check image type at offset 0x00 (0x14, 0x31, 0x35)\n   - If special types, set output X to 1\n6. Query game state via FUN_6fb62880 (get world/game context)\n   - If state flag at offset +4 == 1:\n     - Get skill effect 0x47 via Ordinal_10487 (D2Common.IsSkillActive)\n     - If enabled and pImageData null or byte at 0x35 == 0x01:\n       - Get party modifier via Ordinal_10949 (query), Ordinal_10968 (apply), Ordinal_10996 (percentage)\n       - Apply percentage increase (modifier * result / 100)\n     - Repeat for effect 0x48 with offset 0x35 == 0x02\n\nParameters:\n- pImageData: Image/entity structure pointer (nullable for party effects)\n- nValue: Dimension/scale parameter (usually width/height)\n- pOutX: Output X coordinate (modified by zoom/modifiers)\n- pOutY: Output Y coordinate (modified by zoom/modifiers)\n- pOutMode: Output mode indicator (2 for scaled, 1 for special types, other for standard)\n\nReturns:\n- Last percentage modifier applied, or undefined on standard path\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- NULL pImageData bypasses entity checks (applies global party modifiers)\n- Scale factor (offset 0x4a) masked to 5 bits (0-31 valid values)\n- Magic values 0x14, 0x31, 0x35 identify special unit types (monst/merc/summon)\n- Two skill effects applied in sequence (0x47, 0x48) with conditional party modifiers\n- 0x51eb851f constant used for fixed-point division (magic multiplier)",
