      "comment": "Calculate item inventory grid dimensions based on item properties, base size, and special modifiers.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate input: If nSkillId is 0, log error\n2. Get item stat record from game state\n3. Determine base dimensions:\n   - If nItemParam7 non-zero: fetch from item-specific stat record\n   - If nItemParam8 non-zero: get property-based dimensions\n   - Otherwise: use default dimensions (0x15, 0x16) with adjustments\n4. Apply minimum constraints: width >= 1, height >= 2\n5. Add base width and height offsets (0x19, 0x12, 0x11)\n6. Calculate width total: add display offset height calculation\n7. Check for special effects (0xfe overlay) and add if present\n8. If item has properties: add dimensional modifiers for stat 0 and stat 2 (percentage-based)\n9. Get bonus property (0x6f) and add to height\n10. Check special state flags and set pFlags appropriately\n11. Apply final formulas: scale by base dimensions with +100 offset, add bonuses\n\nParameters:\npWidth - output pointer for final grid width (cells)\npHeight - output pointer for final grid height (cells)\npFlags - output pointer for overlay flags (1=Unique, 3=Unique+Quest)\nnBaseWidth - base width offset (usually 0)\nnBaseHeight - base height offset (usually 0)\nnSkillId - skill ID for lookup (0 triggers error)\nnItemParam7 - item parameter 7 (non-zero uses property lookup)\nnItemParam8 - item parameter 8 (non-zero uses default dimensions)\n\nReturns:\n(void) - outputs via pointer parameters\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If nSkillId=0: logs error and returns default dimensions\n- Ordinal_10966 = D2Common.GetCursorInfo - get cursor object reference\n- Ordinal_10807 = D2Common.GetStatValue - property stat 0 (physical damage)\n- Ordinal_10808 = D2Common.GetStatValue - property stat 2 (elemental damage)\n- Ordinal_10258 = D2Common.GetItemDataRecord - fetch item skill lookup\n- Ordinal_10600 = D2Common.ValidateStat - verify item stat exists\n- Ordinal_10023 = Storm.Assert - assertion failure handler\n- Ordinal_10025 = Storm.Assert - assertion failure handler\n- Ordinal_10520 = D2Common.GetItemProperty - fetch bonus property\n- Ordinal_10466 = D2Common.GetInventoryImage - get tile overlay spec\n- Ordinal_10481 = D2Common.GetAnimationData - fetch animation info\n- Ordinal_10996 = D2Common.CalculateDisplayDimension - calculate rendering bounds\n- Ordinal_10545 = D2Common.IsItemUnique - check item quality\n- Ordinal_10568 = D2Common.GetItemHeight - property height accessor\n- Ordinal_10569 = D2Common.GetItemWidth - property width accessor\n- Ordinal_10538 = D2Common.IsQuestItem - check quest property\n- Ordinal_10968 = D2Common.ApplyOverlay - apply display effect\n- Ordinal_10519 = D2Common.GetGameConstant - get constant values (0x11, 0x12, 0x15, 0x16, 0x17, 0x18, 0x19)\n- Ordinal_10949 = D2Common.GetCurrentColor - get effect color\n- Ordinal_10291 = D2Common.GetItemCategory - determine item type\n- Ordinal_11023 = D2Common.CalculateBufferSize - calculate dimensional requirements\n- Note: Phantom locals at Stack[-0x4,-0x8,-0x10] from compiler optimization",
      "tags": ["MOD_UI", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "STRUCT_ItemData", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData", "STRUCT_StatList", "STRUCT_MonsterData", "PROP_LARGE", "PARAM_8", "STRUCT_Path", "UI_SKILLS", "SRC_SkillDesc.cpp", "STRUCT_Skill", "TBL_skilldesc", "STRUCT_Other"]
