      "api_calls": ["GetTotalStatValue", "GetTotalStatValue", "GetTotalStatValue", "GetTotalStatValue", "GetTotalStatValue", "SKILLS_GetSkillId", "GetStatListByFlags", "GetStatListValue", "GetUnitSkillById", "GetSkillLevel", "...+8 more"],
      "instructions": ["0x69490|SUB|ESP, 0xc", "0x69493|PUSH|EBX", "0x69494|PUSH|EBP", "0x69495|PUSH|ESI", "0x69496|PUSH|EDI", "0x69497|MOV|EBP, EDX", "0x69499|MOV|EBX, ECX", "0x6949B|CALL|0x6fb62880", "0x694A0|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x10], EAX", "0x694A4|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x14], 0x6fba93e0", "0x694AC|MOV|ESI, 0x6fba93c4", "0x694B1|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [ESI + -0x4]", "0x694B4|MOV|ECX, dword ptr [ESP + 0x10]", "0x694B8|PUSH|EAX", "0x694B9|PUSH|ECX"],
      "comment": "Calculate adjusted width and height dimensions for a game unit based on damage/resistance adjustments.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get current game state handle via FUN_6fb62880()\n2. Loop through damage adjustment table (g_adDamageAdjustment):\n   - Fetch adjustment values at current and previous indices via Ordinal_10519\n   - Take minimum of both values\n   - Accumulate to pWidth and pHeight\n   - Update pDimensionType if non-zero adjustment found\n3. Apply additional adjustments from properties 0x39, 0x3a, 0x3b:\n   - Get property 0x3a (multiplier present flag)\n   - If set, fetch properties 0x39 (multiplicand) and 0x3b (multiplier)\n   - Calculate scaled adjustment: (multiplier * property) >> 8\n   - Accumulate to dimensions and set pDimensionType = 2\n4. Clamp pWidth minimum to 1\n5. Ensure pHeight > pWidth (increment if needed)\n6. If pLookupTable provided, apply special resistance table adjustments:\n   - Check game state for valid unit via Ordinal_10966()\n   - Verify unit has resistance flag (byte at +0xEB != 0)\n   - Loop through resistance adjustment table (g_adResistanceAdjustment):\n     - Check if property exists via Ordinal_10466\n     - If exists, calculate bonus via Ordinal_11004/11005\n     - Accumulate bonuses and set pDimensionType = 3\n7. Check for missile properties (Ordinal_10487):\n   - If param4 = 0, call Ordinal_10258 with missile data\n   - Apply missile adjustment via Ordinal_11038\n8. Check for aura presence via Ordinal_10538, set pDimensionType = 3 if found\n9. Check for curse via Ordinal_10545, set pDimensionType = 1 if found\n\nParameters:\n- pWidth (ECX): Pointer to width value, accumulated with adjustments\n- pHeight (EDX): Pointer to height value, accumulated with adjustments\n- pDimensionType (Stack[0x4]): Output dimension type flag (1=curse, 2=property-scaled, 3=aura/resistance)\n- nParam4 (Stack[0x8]): Missile parameter flag (0=skip missile prep, !0=process missile)\n- pLookupTable (Stack[0xC]): Optional lookup table pointer for special adjustments (may be NULL)\n\nReturns: void (modifies pWidth, pHeight, pDimensionType via pointers)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If pWidth < 1, forced to 1 (minimum dimension)\n- If pHeight <= pWidth, forced to pWidth + 1\n- Resistance table only processed if pLookupTable != NULL\n- Magic constants: 0x39, 0x3a, 0x3b are unit property IDs for scaling calculations\n- Adjustment tables are fixed global arrays; may represent base stat modifications\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset | Size | Field Name | Type | Description\n-------|------|------------|------|-------------\n0x0    | 4    | (parameter) | int* | Pointer to width accumulator\n0x4    | 4    | (parameter) | int* | Pointer to height accumulator\n0x8    | 4    | (parameter) | uint*| Pointer to dimension type flag\n0xC    | 4    | (parameter) | int  | Missile parameter flag\n0x10   | 4    | (parameter) | uint*| Optional lookup table pointer",
