      "comment": "Draws a formatted range text display at specified screen coordinates.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize Unicode string buffer (64 wide chars) with default constructors\n2. Build range text: if min == max use single value format, else use \"min-max\" format\n3. Convert formatted ANSI text to Unicode representation\n4. Call Ordinal_10131 with paint data structure pointer\n5. Calculate text centering: align within available width\n6. Determine vertical position offset based on range bounds\n7. Call Ordinal_10127 to prepare rendering context\n8. Call DrawCenteredText with calculated coordinates and formatted Unicode text\n\nParameters:\nnMinRange (int ECX) - Minimum value of range display\nnMaxRange (int EDX) - Maximum value of range display\ndwColorCode (dword Stack[0x4]) - UI color/style code for text rendering\nnXOffset (int Stack[0x8]) - Horizontal offset from base screen position\nnYOffset (int Stack[0xc]) - Vertical offset from base screen position\nnWidth (int Stack[0x10]) - Available width in pixels for centering calculation\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value, modifies UI rendering state\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Single value display (min == max): Uses single-value format string\n- Range display (min != max): Uses format string with both values\n- Centering calculation uses complex fixed-point math (0x92492493 magic constant)\n- Text height adjusted based on range extent difference\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x92492493 - Fixed-point multiplier for text width calculation (dividing by 13)\n0x1e0 (480) - Offset for UI Y-coordinate base\n0x20 (32) - Unicode buffer element count for loop iteration\n0x2 - Unicode character stride (2 bytes per wide char)",
