      "instructions": ["0x697C0|SUB|ESP, 0x8", "0x697C3|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [ESP + 0xc]", "0x697C7|PUSH|EBX", "0x697C8|PUSH|EBP", "0x697C9|PUSH|ESI", "0x697CA|MOV|ESI, EDX", "0x697CC|MOV|EBP, ECX", "0x697CE|PUSH|EDI", "0x697CF|PUSH|EAX", "0x697D0|MOV|ECX, dword ptr [ESI]", "0x697D2|PUSH|ECX", "0x697D3|CALL|0x6fb98ae2", "0x697D8|MOV|EDI, dword ptr [ESI + 0x12c]", "0x697DE|MOV|EBX, dword ptr [ESI + 0x130]", "0x697E4|XOR|EDX, EDX"],
      "comment": "Calculates damage range values from monster data and displays them as text.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get base min damage via GetMonsterMinDamage(pMonsterData[0], dwSkillId)\n2. Extract adjustment factor from offset 0x129 of monster data\n3. Calculate shift amount: 8 - pMonsterData[0x4a] (bit precision control)\n4. Compute min range: (pMonsterData[0x4b] + baseDamage) >> shiftAmount\n5. Compute max range: (pMonsterData[0x4c] + baseDamage) >> shiftAmount\n6. If adjustment factor != 0:\n   a. Get item inventory size via GetItemInventorySize\n   b. Adjust dimensions via CalculateAdjustedDimensions\n   c. Add scaled width to min range: (width * factor + rounding) >> 3\n   d. Add scaled height to max range: (height * factor + rounding) >> 3\n7. Call DrawRangeText to display the computed range\n\nParameters:\n  pItemInfo (ECX) - Pointer to item information structure for inventory size\n  pMonsterData (EDX) - Pointer to monster data structure containing damage values\n    [0x000] Base monster ID for damage lookup\n    [0x128] Bit precision value (byte)\n    [0x129] Inventory adjustment factor (byte)\n    [0x12C] Min damage offset value (dword at [0x4b])\n    [0x130] Max damage offset value (dword at [0x4c])\n  dwSkillId - Skill ID for damage calculation\n  nTextX - X coordinate for text display\n  nTextY - Y coordinate for text display\n  nTextColor - Color for text display\n\nReturns: void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If adjustment factor at 0x129 is zero, inventory size adjustment is skipped\n  - Division by 8 (>>3) includes signed rounding correction\n\nCalled by: UI tooltip/stat display functions (5 xrefs)",
