      "comment": "Get item grid dimensions with damage/resistance adjustments applied.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call GetItemInventorySize to calculate base item dimensions from stat tables\n2. Call CalculateAdjustedDimensions to apply damage and resistance modifiers\n3. Return modified dimensions via output pointers\n\nParameters:\npnWidth (ECX) - Output pointer for final grid width in cells\npnHeight (EDX) - Output pointer for final grid height in cells\npdwDimensionType (Stack[0x4]) - Output dimension type flag (1=curse, 2=scaled, 3=aura/resist)\nnBaseWidth (Stack[0x8]) - Base width offset (usually 0)\nnBaseHeight (Stack[0xC]) - Base height offset (usually 0)\npLookupTable (Stack[0x10]) - Optional lookup table for resistance adjustments (may be NULL)\nnItemParam (Stack[0x14]) - Item parameter for dimension calculation\n\nReturns: void - outputs via pointer parameters\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- This is a thin wrapper combining two dimension calculation functions\n- Used by DrawItemDamageText and DisplayUnitDamageRange for rendering\n- pLookupTable controls whether resistance table adjustments are applied\n\nRelated Functions:\n- GetItemInventorySize: Calculates base dimensions from item stats\n- CalculateAdjustedDimensions: Applies damage/resistance modifiers",
