      "instructions": ["0x69FE0|SUB|ESP, 0xc0", "0x69FE6|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [ESP + 0xe0]", "0x69FED|PUSH|EBX", "0x69FEE|PUSH|EBP", "0x69FEF|PUSH|ESI", "0x69FF0|PUSH|EDI", "0x69FF1|XOR|EDI, EDI", "0x69FF3|CMP|EAX, EDI", "0x69FF5|MOV|ESI, EDX", "0x69FF7|MOV|EBX, ECX", "0x69FF9|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x24], EDI", "0x69FFD|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x14], EDI", "0x6A001|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x18], EDI", "0x6A005|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x20], EDI", "0x6A009|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x10], EDI"],
      "comment": "Renders damage range text with dual-range coordinate transformation and internationalization support.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize all coordinate/range variables to zero\n2. If screen row offset provided, calculate image-relative coordinates via CalcImageCoordinates\n3. Extract zoom factor from coordinate table[0x129]\n4. Validate damage range pointer (fatal error if null)\n5. Query damage sprite dimensions and adjust ranges via FUN_6fb3a340\n6. Apply zoom transformation if both min/max ranges non-zero: result = (value * zoom + rounding) >> 3 + offset\n7. Apply zoom transformation to alternate range similarly\n8. Branch based on valid range pairs:\n   - Both ranges (0,0): draw alternate coordinates\n   - Alternate ranges (0,0): draw primary coordinates\n   - Both valid: format text strings and draw both centered\n9. Format damage text: if min == max, single value; else min-max range\n10. Convert ASCII to Unicode via toUnicode\n11. Initialize display offset via Ordinal_10127 (D2Common.InitTimingOffset)\n12. If offset not set, query game time via Ordinal_10007 and set offset (-6 if time < 6, -7 if time > 9)\n13. Draw primary damage text at calculated Y position\n14. Draw alternate damage text with secondary offset\n\nParameters:\ndwFlagsMask (ECX) - Drawing flags for text rendering\npCoordinateTable (EDX) - Ptr to coordinate/zoom table containing array at offset 0x129\nnZoom - Additional zoom/scale factor\npDamageRange - Ptr to damage range array [min_width, min_height, max_width, max_height]\ndwMinDamage - Minimum damage value (32-bit)\ndwMaxDamage - Maximum damage value (32-bit)\nnBaseX - Base X screen coordinate\nnBaseY - Base Y screen coordinate\nnMaxWidth - Maximum text width pixels\nnRowOffset - Screen row offset for Y positioning\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nNote: Function contains 4 SSA variables optimized away by compiler (pUVar2, iVar3, uVar1, local_80 - Unicode array iteration counters and zoom calculation temporaries).\n\nOrdinal Calls:\n- Ordinal_10023 (0x6fb3a033): D2Common.AssertFailure - logs assertion with filename, source module, line number\n- Ordinal_10127 (0x6fb3a064): D2Common.InitTimingOffset - initializes display offset timing system\n- Ordinal_10007 (0x6fb3a0e6): D2Common.GetGameTick - queries current game clock time (6-9 threshold determines offset)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x129 - Offset within coordinate table for zoom factor\n0x5c4 - Error code (assertion line number)\n0x20 - Text width in Unicode characters (32)\n0x3 - SAR shift count for divide-by-8 scaling\n0x7 - Modulo mask for rounding\n0x6, 0x9 - Time thresholds for offset calculation\n-0x1e0 - Screen height constant offset (-480)\n0x1ff - XOR mask (possibly alpha channel)",
      "tags": ["MOD_UI", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "STRUCT_ItemData", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData", "PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Path", "UI_SKILLS", "SRC_SkillDesc.cpp", "TBL_skilldesc", "PARAM_10"]
