      "comment": "Activate secondary weapon slot by validating and switching equipped items.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate unit exists using Ordinal_10462 (GetUnitState)\n2. Get unit's secondary item reference from offset +0x84\n3. Retrieve secondary item data with Ordinal_10258 (GetItemData)\n4. Get item type code using Ordinal_10689 (GetItemType)\n5. Check if type is 0x04 (dual-wield): set dwWeaponType=5, else 4\n6. Equip item with weapon type using Ordinal_10257 (EquipItem)\n7. If equipment fails, log error with Ordinal_10023 and exit via FUN_6fb9a10f\n8. Check item flag 0x2D using Ordinal_10731 (CheckItemFlag)\n9. Validate primary item exists with Ordinal_10839 (GetItemData)\n10. Set primary item owned with Ordinal_10524 (SetItemOwned)\n11. Set primary item slot 0 with Ordinal_10523 (SetSlotIndex)\n12. Validate secondary item exists with Ordinal_10839 (GetItemData)\n13. Set secondary item owned with Ordinal_10524 (SetItemOwned)\n14. Set secondary item slot 1 with Ordinal_10523 (SetSlotIndex)\n15. Return secondary item ID on success\n\nParameters:\nnUnit (int) - Unit pointer, passed in ECX register (fastcall)\n\nReturns:\nSecondary item ID (handle) on successful activation\n0 on validation failure or equipment errors\n-1 on critical error (exits process)\n\nSpecial Cases:\nItem type 0x04 designates dual-wield weapons (uses weapon type 5)\nItem type other than 0x04 uses weapon type 4\nFlag 0x2D must be present for valid equipment setup\nOne stack-allocated temporary optimized away during compilation\n\nNote: Function uses 1 stack-allocated temporary optimized away.",
