      "instructions": ["0x6A550|PUSH|EBX", "0x6A551|PUSH|ESI", "0x6A552|MOV|EBX, ECX", "0x6A554|PUSH|EDI", "0x6A555|PUSH|EBX", "0x6A556|CALL|0x6fb983fe", "0x6A55B|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0x6A55D|JZ|0x6fb3a5f5", "0x6A563|MOV|ESI, dword ptr [EBX + 0x84]", "0x6A569|PUSH|ESI", "0x6A56A|CALL|0x6fb98ad0", "0x6A56F|MOV|EDI, EAX", "0x6A571|TEST|EDI, EDI", "0x6A573|JZ|0x6fb3a5ef", "0x6A575|PUSH|EDI"],
      "comment": "Validate and process player inventory item state changes\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Ordinal_10462: GetPlayerValid(nPlayer) - Validate player exists, return 0 if invalid\n2. Load inventory buffer pointer from player+0x84 into dwItemBuf\n3. Ordinal_10258: GetItemFromBuffer(dwItemBuf) - Retrieve item from buffer into nResult\n4. If nResult==0, return 0 (no item)\n5. Ordinal_10689: GetItemQuality(nResult) - Get quality byte into cQuality\n6. Compare cQuality==0x04, set dwItemType=0x05 if true, else 0x04\n7. Ordinal_10257: SetItemType(dwItemBuf, dwItemType) - Assign type, store in nItem\n8. If nItem==0, log error and abort via Ordinal_10023 + FUN_6fb9a10f(0xFFFFFFFF)\n9. Ordinal_10731: HasProperty(nItem, 0x2d) - Check for property flag 0x2d into nHasProperty\n10. If nHasProperty!=0, proceed to property application:\n11.    Ordinal_10839: ValidateItem(nItem) - Validate secondary item\n12.    If validation ok, Ordinal_10524: BeginPropertyApplication(nPlayer, nItem)\n13.    Then Ordinal_10523: ApplyProperty(nPlayer, nItem, 0)\n14.    Ordinal_10839: ValidateItem(nResult) - Validate primary item from step 3\n15.    If primary validation ok, Ordinal_10524: BeginPropertyApplication(nPlayer, nResult)\n16.    Then Ordinal_10523: ApplyProperty(nPlayer, nResult, 1)\n17. Return nResult (item handle, or 0 if property check failed)\n\nParameters:\n- nPlayer (int, ECX): Player unit handle to validate and process\n\nReturns:\n- Item handle (int) if successful validation and processing\n- 0 if player invalid, no item, or property check failed\n- Terminates via FUN_6fb9a10f(0xFFFFFFFF) on SetItemType failure (never returns)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Quality 0x04 triggers type 0x05, other qualities use type 0x04\n- Property 0x2d initiates dual-item validation and property application chain\n- SetItemType failure is fatal - calls error handler\n- Both primary and secondary items must validate if property exists",
      "tags": ["MOD_UI", "UI_SKILLS", "SRC_SkillDesc.cpp", "TBL_skilldesc", "PARAM_1"]
