      "comment": "Allocate and validate skill resource values based on resource type and state conditions.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Query current game state handle via FUN_6fb62880()\n2. Check if state is initialized using Ordinal_10462 (Storm validation - returns non-zero if ready)\n3. If initialized (non-zero):\n   a. Call ValidateAndProcessStateChange() with resource parameters and current state handle\n   b. Return after state validation completes\n4. If not initialized (zero):\n   a. Query state handle again via FUN_6fb62880()\n   b. Load resource configuration from state offset 0x84 via Ordinal_10258 (Storm config accessor)\n   c. Clear resource value and flags pointers to 0x00000000\n   d. Calculate skill resource allocation using CalculateSkillResourceValue()\n   e. Return with allocated values\n\nParameters:\n- pThis: SkillAllocator instance (implicit ECX in __thiscall)\n- nResourceType: Resource type identifier for skill allocation\n- pdwResourceValue: Output pointer to allocated resource value\n- pdwResourceFlags: Output pointer to resource flags configuration\n- pdwResourceMask: Output pointer to resource mask value\n- pdwResultFlags: Output pointer to result status flags\n\nReturns:\n- void (result passed through pointer parameters)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- State validation via Ordinal_10462 gates between initialized and uninitialized paths\n- Offset 0x84 contains resource configuration structure reference\n- Both execution paths converge on CalculateSkillResourceValue() with different initial parameters\n- Resource value and flags cleared to zero before calculation in uninitialized path",
