      "instructions": ["0x6A680|PUSH|ESI", "0x6A681|MOV|ESI, EDX", "0x6A683|CALL|0x6fb62880", "0x6A688|MOV|CL, byte ptr [ESI + 0x128]", "0x6A68E|MOV|ESI, dword ptr [ESI + 0x12c]", "0x6A694|SUB|ECX, 0x8", "0x6A697|PUSH|0x89", "0x6A69C|PUSH|EAX", "0x6A69D|SHL|ESI, CL", "0x6A69F|CALL|0x6fb983bc", "0x6A6A4|ADD|ESI, EAX", "0x6A6A6|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [ESP + 0x14]", "0x6A6AA|MOV|ECX, dword ptr [ESP + 0x10]", "0x6A6AE|MOV|EDX, dword ptr [ESP + 0xc]", "0x6A6B2|PUSH|EAX"],
      "comment": "Draws fire damage stat value on UI using stat descriptor data.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get player unit context via GetGameContext()\n2. Read shift amount from stat descriptor at offset 0x128 (char)\n3. Read base damage value from stat descriptor at offset 0x12c (int)\n4. Get fire damage minimum stat (ID 0x89) from player unit via GetStatValue\n5. Calculate display value: (baseValue << (shiftAmount - 8)) + fireMinStat\n6. Call DrawRangeText with calculated value as both min and max for single value display\n\nParameters:\nnUnused (int ECX) - Unused fastcall register parameter, passed through calling convention\npStatDescriptor (void* EDX) - Pointer to stat descriptor structure containing:\n  +0x128: char cShiftAmount - Shift amount for damage calculation\n  +0x12c: int nBaseValue - Base damage value before scaling\nnUnused2 (int Stack[0x4]) - Unused stack parameter from caller\nnXOffset (int Stack[0x8]) - Horizontal screen offset for text placement\nnYOffset (int Stack[0xc]) - Vertical screen offset for text placement\nnWidth (int Stack[0x10]) - Available width for text centering calculation\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value, renders text directly to UI via DrawRangeText\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Uses same value for min and max in DrawRangeText to display single value\n- Color code 0 passed to DrawRangeText for default text color\n- Shift calculation uses (shiftAmount - 8) with mask 0x1F to limit shift range\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x89 (137) - Fire damage minimum stat ID in D2 stat system\n0x128 (296) - Offset to shift amount byte in stat descriptor\n0x12c (300) - Offset to base damage int in stat descriptor\n0x8 - Adjustment subtracted from shift amount\n0x1F - Mask to limit shift to valid range (0-31)",
