      "comment": "Calculate base and enhanced weapon damage with enchantments, auras, and mastery bonuses.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize output values (*pMinDamage = 0, *pMaxDamage = 0)\n2. Retrieve game state (nGameState = FUN_6fb62880)\n3. Validate weapon handle: if nWeapon == 0, attempt to get from state 0x84 offset\n4. Check weapon is equipped (Ordinal_10759 - GetUnitMode): if not equipped, return early\n5. Check weapon type (Ordinal_10731 with 0x26 parameter): if type 0x26 is set, process as special case\n6. Standard weapon damage path (if not special):\n   a. Get damage modifiers (dwAura & 0xff for aura, dwEnchantBonus & 0xff for bonus)\n   b. Retrieve skill mastery bonuses (Ordinal_10519): multiply by modifier percentage, divide by 100\n   c. Check augmentation flag (0x4e): if set, apply divine damage (Ordinal_11023)\n   d. Get base damage values from weapon (Ordinal_10520: 0x9f for min, 0xa0 for max)\n   e. Apply damage bonus: (*pMinDamage * nDamageBonus) / 100 + *pMinDamage\n   f. Check enhancement flag (0x10): if set, mark special type = 1\n   g. Normalize with Ordinal_11038\n7. Special weapon damage path (if 0x26 type is set):\n   a. Get weapon subtype (Ordinal_10760)\n   b. Retrieve subtype damage table (Ordinal_10589)\n   c. Initialize character buffer (512 Unicode chars)\n   d. Extract offset values from damage table (+0xb0, +0x98, +0xac, +0x94)\n   e. Switch on damage type field (+0xa8): determines special type (1/2/3/4)\n   f. For type 5 (special): calculate scaled damage based on +0xc0 field / 0x19 (25)\n   g. Compute final min/max: scale by bit shift amount at +0x8c, arithmetic right shift by 8\n\nParameters:\n  pMinDamage (int *) - Output minimum damage value\n  pMaxDamage (int *) - Output maximum damage value\n  pSpecialType (uint *) - Output special damage type (0=normal, 1/2/3/4=special, set if 0x10 flag present)\n  dwAura (uint) - Aura effect flags (bits 0-7 contain percentage modifier)\n  dwEnchantBonus (uint) - Enchantment bonus flags (bits 0-7 contain percentage modifier)\n  dwMastery (uint) - Mastery skill level/bonus\n  nWeapon (int) - Weapon handle/ID\n\nReturns:\n  void - Results written to pMinDamage, pMaxDamage, pSpecialType pointers\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If nWeapon == 0 at start and state 0x84 is also 0, logs error and returns early\n  - If weapon not equipped (Ordinal_10759 returns 0), returns early\n  - Special weapon types (0x26 flag set) follow alternative calculation path\n  - Type 5 special weapons include divisor check: if divisor < 1, force to 1\n  - Damage scaling uses magic constant 0x51eb851f (division optimization constant)\n  - Final min/max clamped by comparison: if max < min, use max as both\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x26 - Special weapon type flag identifier\n  0x84 - Offset in game state to default weapon\n  0x9f, 0xa0 - Offsets for min/max base damage\n  0x4e - Augmentation/divine damage flag\n  0x10 - Enhancement flag for special type marking\n  0x8c - Bit shift amount offset (for damage scaling)\n  0xb0, 0x98, 0xac, 0x94 - Damage table offset values\n  0xa8 - Damage type field in weapon subtype\n  0xc0 - Scaling divisor offset\n  0x19 (25) - Base scale divisor\n  0x51eb851f - Magic multiplication constant for division (approximately 1/100)\n  0xff - Mask to extract flags byte\n  0x1f - Bit mask for shift amount validity\n  8 - Right shift for final damage normalization\n\nRelated Functions:\n  - FUN_6fb62880 - Get game state pointer\n  - Ordinal_10759 (D2Common.GetUnitMode) - Check if weapon equipped\n  - Ordinal_10731 (D2Common.GetUnitStat) - Query weapon property\n  - Ordinal_10807/10808 (D2Common.GetUnitStat) - Get aura/bonus flags\n  - Ordinal_10519 (D2Common.GetUnitStat) - Get mastery bonus\n  - Ordinal_11023 (D2Common.CalcDamage) - Calculate divine damage\n  - Ordinal_10520 (D2Common.GetUnitStat) - Get base damage\n  - Ordinal_11038 (D2Common.NormalizeDamage) - Finalize damage values\n  - Ordinal_10760 (D2Common.GetUnitProperty) - Get weapon subtype\n  - Ordinal_10589 (D2Common.GetDataTable) - Retrieve damage table",
      "tags": ["PARAM_7", "PROP_LARGE", "MOD_UI", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "UI_SKILLS", "SRC_SkillDesc.cpp", "TBL_skilldesc", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
