      "comment": "Displays secondary weapon damage as a formatted range text on screen.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize damage output variables (nMinDamage=0, nMaxDamage=0, dwSpecialType=0)\n2. Get game context via GetGameContext()\n3. Activate secondary weapon slot via ActivateSecondaryWeaponSlot to get weapon handle\n4. Check if weapon exists (nWeaponHandle != 0)\n5. If no weapon in secondary slot, exit early (skip damage display)\n6. Calculate weapon damage via CalculateWeaponDamage passing output pointers\n7. Process player inventory state via ProcessPlayerInventoryState\n8. Draw formatted damage range text via DrawRangeText at specified screen coordinates\n\nParameters:\n  this (void *) - ECX __thiscall implicit, mastery/skill data pointer passed to CalculateWeaponDamage\n  nUnused (int) - Unused parameter, reserved for future use\n  nXOffset (int) - Horizontal screen offset for text placement\n  nYOffset (int) - Vertical screen offset for text placement\n  nWidth (int) - Available width in pixels for text centering\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value, renders UI text directly to screen\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Early exit if ActivateSecondaryWeaponSlot returns 0 (no secondary weapon equipped)\n  - Damage values passed by reference to CalculateWeaponDamage for output\n  - dwSpecialType indicates damage type (0=physical, 1-4=elemental/special types)\n  - The 'this' pointer is passed as dwMastery to CalculateWeaponDamage for skill bonuses",
