      "comment": "Wrapper function to display weapon damage range text using CalculateWeaponDamage callback.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Pass all parameters through to DrawDamageRangeText\n2. Set pDamageRange to CalculateWeaponDamage function pointer (0x6fb3a790)\n3. Set dwMinDamage=0, dwMaxDamage=0 (unused, damage calculated by callback)\n4. Set nRowOffset=1 to enable screen row coordinate calculation\n\nParameters:\n  dwFlags (ECX) - Drawing flags for text rendering\n  pCoordinates (EDX) - Ptr to coordinate/zoom table with scale factor at +0x129\n  nZoom - Additional zoom/scale factor for coordinate calculation\n  nBaseX - Base X screen coordinate\n  nBaseY - Base Y screen coordinate\n  nMaxWidth - Maximum text width in pixels\n\nReturns:\n  void - Renders weapon damage range text directly to screen\n\nClassification: Thunk/Wrapper\nWraps: DrawDamageRangeText with CalculateWeaponDamage callback\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x6fb3a790 - CalculateWeaponDamage function pointer (damage calculation callback)\n  1 - nRowOffset value enabling image-relative coordinate calculation\n  0 - dwMinDamage/dwMaxDamage placeholders (actual damage from callback)",
