      "comment": "Calculates and displays a skill's damage range text in the UI.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get the skill's txt record ID via GetSkillsTxtId(pSkill)\n2. Get monster-leveled stat value using skill ID and monster level\n3. Calculate base damage dimensions via GetItemInventorySize()\n4. Apply damage adjustments via CalculateAdjustedDimensions()\n5. Render the min-max range text at specified screen position\n\nParameters:\n- this (ECX): Skill * - Skill pointer (cannot retype via API, documented here)\n- nMonsterLevel: Monster level for stat calculations\n- nXOffset: Horizontal screen offset for text\n- nYOffset: Vertical screen offset for text  \n- nWidth: Available width for text centering\n\nReturns: void\n\nLocal Variables:\n- nMinDamage (int): Minimum damage value (output from GetItemInventorySize)\n- dwColorCode (uint): Color/style code for text rendering (initialized to 0)\n- iVar1: SSA temporary holding skill ID then monster stat value\n\nClassification: Worker function - coordinates damage calculation and text rendering\n\nCallees:\n- GetSkillsTxtId: Gets skill record ID from skill pointer\n- GetMonsterLeveledStat: Calculates stat value based on monster level\n- GetItemInventorySize: Computes base damage range dimensions\n- CalculateAdjustedDimensions: Applies damage modifiers\n- DrawRangeText: Renders formatted min-max damage range text",
