      "comment": "Calculate and display skill damage range text based on player stats and weapon.\n\nClassification: Worker function - Called from function pointer table at 0x6fbc5ba8 for skill UI rendering.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize damage range variables (nMinDamage, nMaxDamage, dwColorCode) to zero\n2. Call GetItemInventorySize to get base damage range from skill ID (this param in ECX)\n3. Get current game context (player unit pointer) via GetGameContext\n4. Get skill damage modifier from GetMonsterSkillId(0x6f, nSkillLevel) where stat 0x6f is skill damage bonus\n5. Get player attack weapon using GetUnitAttackWeapon with transform check flag=1\n6. Branch based on weapon availability:\n   6a. If no weapon (NULL): Get base min damage (stat 0x15) and max damage (stat 0x16) from player stats\n   6b. If weapon exists: Get inventory status, check if two-handed (status==2), get weapon damage range\n7. Apply minimum damage constraints: nMinDamage >= 1, nMaxDamage >= 2\n8. Scale damage by skill bonus: damage += (base_damage * skill_bonus * 3) / 100\n9. Call CalculateAdjustedDimensions to apply final scaling with color code\n10. Call DrawRangeText to render formatted min-max damage text at UI coordinates\n\nParameters:\nthis (ECX) - Skill ID for damage calculation lookup (int cast to void* by __thiscall)\nnSkillLevel (int) - Current skill level for bonus calculation\nnXOffset (int) - Horizontal offset for text positioning in pixels\nnYOffset (int) - Vertical offset for text positioning in pixels\nnWidth (int) - Available width for text centering in pixels\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Renders damage text directly to screen, no return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Unarmed combat uses player base stats (0x15/0x16) instead of weapon damage\n- Two-handed weapon detection via inventory status comparison to 2\n- Damage scaling formula: (base * skillBonus * 3) / 100 = 3% damage increase per skill bonus point\n- Minimum constraints prevent display of 0-0 or negative damage ranges\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x6f - Skill damage bonus stat ID passed to GetMonsterSkillId\n0x15 - Minimum physical damage stat ID for GetTotalStatValue\n0x16 - Maximum physical damage stat ID for GetTotalStatValue\n0x2 - Two-handed weapon inventory status code\n0x3 - Skill damage percentage multiplier (3% per point)\n0x64 (100) - Percentage divisor for damage calculation\n0x84 - Inventory offset in player unit structure for weapon lookup\n\nOrdinal References:\nGetItemInventorySize @ 0x6fb391c0 - Get base skill damage range from skill ID\nGetGameContext @ 0x6fb62880 - Get current player unit pointer\nGetMonsterSkillId @ 0x6fb984e8 - D2Common skill stat lookup for damage bonus\nGetUnitAttackWeapon @ 0x6fb983ce - D2Common get equipped weapon unit\nGetInventoryEntryStatus @ 0x6fb98854 - D2Common check weapon hand type\nGetUnitVitalityOrEnergy @ 0x6fb988ea - D2Common get minimum weapon damage\nGetItemMaxDamage @ 0x6fb988e4 - D2Common get maximum weapon damage\nGetTotalStatValue @ 0x6fb9826c - D2Common get unit stat value\nCalculateAdjustedDimensions @ 0x6fb39490 - Apply UI scaling to damage values\nDrawRangeText @ 0x6fb396a0 - Render formatted damage range text string",
