      "instructions": ["0x6B2A0|SUB|ESP, 0x68", "0x6B2A3|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [ESP + 0x74]", "0x6B2A7|PUSH|EBX", "0x6B2A8|PUSH|EBP", "0x6B2A9|MOV|EBP, dword ptr [ESP + 0x74]", "0x6B2AD|PUSH|ESI", "0x6B2AE|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0x6B2B0|MOV|ECX, dword ptr [ESP + 0x7c]", "0x6B2B4|PUSH|EDI", "0x6B2B5|PUSH|EAX", "0x6B2B6|MOV|EBX, EDX", "0x6B2B8|PUSH|ECX", "0x6B2B9|PUSH|EBP", "0x6B2BA|MOV|ECX, ESI", "0x6B2BC|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x20], EBX"],
      "comment": "Formats monster damage statistics for display, including skill-based damage bonuses.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call FormatLocalizationString with base parameters for initial formatting\n2. Initialize 32-element Unicode buffer (local_40) with default constructors\n3. Get treasure class via GetMonsterTreasureClass for monster type and difficulty\n4. Calculate treasure value = treasureClass * (difficulty-1) + pStatRecord+0x158\n5. If treasure value non-zero and stat record type is 0x04 or 0x05, format resource string\n6. Get base max damage via GetMonsterMaxDamage for monster type and difficulty\n7. Calculate min damage = pStatRecord+0x144 + baseDamage\n8. Calculate max damage = pStatRecord+0x148 + baseDamage\n9. If any damage values non-zero, apply shift from pStatRecord+0x128 then right-shift by 8\n10. For monster types 0x14, 0x31, 0x35 (special monsters), set min damage to 1\n11. Check for Concentration aura (state 0x47): if player has aura and stat type is 0x01,\n    apply skill 0x3D bonus as percentage increase to both min/max damage\n12. Check for Might aura (state 0x48): if player has aura and stat type is 0x02,\n    apply skill 0x3F bonus as percentage increase to both min/max damage\n13. Call FormatLocalizationString with calculated damage values and stat type\n14. Call FormatResourceStatString to add additional stat formatting\n15. Calculate level-scaled value = pStatRecord+0x124 * (difficulty-1) + pStatRecord+0x120\n16. If level-scaled value non-zero, format with + or - prefix and append localized strings\n17. Return 1\n\nParameters:\n  pOutputBuffer (ECX) - Output Unicode buffer for formatted string\n  nMonsterType (EDX) - Monster type ID (0x14=special1, 0x31=special2, 0x35=special3)\n  pStatRecord - Pointer to monster stat record structure\n  nDifficultyLevel - Game difficulty level (1=Normal, 2=Nightmare, 3=Hell)\n  nUnused - Unused parameter, repurposed as loop counter\n\nReturns:\n  Always returns 1\n\nStructure Offsets (pStatRecord):\n  +0x0D4 (1 byte) - Stat type for aura check (0x01=Concentration, 0x02=Might)\n  +0x120 (4 bytes) - Base level-scaled value\n  +0x124 (4 bytes) - Per-difficulty level-scaled multiplier\n  +0x128 (1 byte) - Damage shift amount (masked to 5 bits)\n  +0x140 (1 byte) - Resource type (0x04, 0x05 trigger resource formatting)\n  +0x144 (4 bytes) - Base minimum damage\n  +0x148 (4 bytes) - Base maximum damage\n  +0x158 (4 bytes) - Treasure class base value\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x14, 0x31, 0x35 - Special monster type IDs that force min damage to 1\n  0x47 - STATE_CONCENTRATION (Paladin aura)\n  0x48 - STATE_MIGHT (Paladin aura)\n  0x3D - SKILL_CONCENTRATION\n  0x3F - SKILL_MIGHT\n  0x10A6, 0x10B3, 0xF9E - Localization string IDs for damage display",
      "tags": ["PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_5", "STRUCT_Room1", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
