      "instructions": ["0x6B570|SUB|ESP, 0x64", "0x6B573|PUSH|EBX", "0x6B574|PUSH|EBP", "0x6B575|PUSH|ESI", "0x6B576|PUSH|EDI", "0x6B577|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x10], EDX", "0x6B57B|MOV|EBP, ECX", "0x6B57D|LEA|ESI, [ESP + 0x34]", "0x6B581|MOV|EDI, 0x20", "0x6B586|MOV|ECX, ESI", "0x6B588|CALL|dword ptr [0x6fba5c30]", "0x6B58E|ADD|ESI, 0x2", "0x6B591|DEC|EDI", "0x6B592|JNZ|0x6fb3b586", "0x6B594|MOV|ECX, dword ptr [ESP + 0x78]"],
      "comment": "Formats a time interval resource string into a localized display format\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize Unicode string buffer auUnicodeBuffer (array of 64 Unicode characters)\n2. Calculate quotient and remainder: quotientTicks = nResourceId / 0x19, remainderTicks = (nResourceId % 0x19) * 10 / 0x19\n3. If both quotient and remainder are 0, return 0 (empty string)\n4. If remainder is 0 and quotient is non-zero, format using single-value format string from global (varies by nSuffixType parameter)\n5. Otherwise, format using dual-value format string (0x6fbc62d0 or 0x6fbc635c based on nSuffixType)\n6. Convert formatted ANSI string to Unicode format using toUnicode()\n7. Call Ordinal_10004() to acquire resource lock\n8. Concatenate result strings to output pointers pszOutput1 and pszOutput2 (multiple concatenations)\n9. Return 1 (success)\n\nParameters:\n- nResourceId (int): Input time value in ticks/units to format (0x19 = 25 decimal, appears to be frame count)\n- nSuffixType (int): Suffix mode selection - 0 for standard format, non-zero for alternative format\n\nReturns:\n- 0 if input is empty/zero\n- 1 if formatting and concatenation succeeded\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- 0x19 (25 decimal) is the division constant used to convert ticks to display units\n- Two separate resource format strings are referenced based on nSuffixType parameter\n- Phantom variable: local_64 (undefined4) is stack-allocated temporary optimized away\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n- 0x19 (25): Time conversion denominator for tick-to-unit scaling\n- 0x20 (32): Unicode buffer size in elements\n- 0x51eb851f: Magic multiplier constant used in signed division optimization (IMUL constant for fast integer division)\n- 0x1: Success return code, 0: Failure/empty return",
