      "comment": "Format and process localized string data with Unicode conversion.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize 64-element Unicode buffer (local_40) with default constructors\n2. Validate param_5 is zero and param_4 is within valid mode range (1-6)\n3. Based on param_2/param_3 values, format string into stack buffer using wsprintfA\n4. Convert formatted string to Unicode via toUnicode() with 0x20 character limit\n5. Call Ordinal_10004 (Storm locale notification) multiple times\n6. Concatenate strings via Unicode::strcat operations\n7. Return success (1) or failure (0)\n\nParameters:\npContext (void *) - Localization context object passed in ECX\nnParam2 (int) - First parameter for string format\nnParam3 (int) - Second parameter for conditional logic  \ndwMode (dword) - Mode selector (0x1-0x6) determining string processing path\nsParam5 (short) - Validation flag; function returns 0 if non-zero\n\nReturns:\n1 - Success, string formatted and processed\n0 - Failure, invalid mode or parameters\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If sParam5 != 0, returns 0 immediately (validation failure)\n- If dwMode < 1 or dwMode > 6, returns 0 (invalid mode)\n- If nParam2 == 0 and nParam3 == 0, uses default format string from g_szLocalizationConfig\n- If nParam2 == nParam3, also uses default format string\n\nNote: Function uses compiler-generated 'this' parameter (Unicode*) from constructor closure calls",
