      "comment": "Formats a scaled monster stat with bonus damage display for UI tooltips.\n\nClassification: Worker function - Formats stat values with level-based scaling\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call FormatLocalizationString with base parameters to initialize output\n2. Get monster leveled stat via GetMonsterLeveledStat(nMonsterLevel, nStatIndex)\n3. Append formatted stat value using FormatAndAppendStringValue\n4. Calculate scaled value from stat record (offsets +0xF0, +0xF4)\n5. Initialize Unicode buffer (64 chars) via default constructor loop (32 iterations, 2 bytes each)\n6. If scaled value is non-zero (negated result):\n   a. Format negative value to ANSI using wsprintfA with \"%d\" format\n   b. Convert ANSI to Unicode via toUnicode\n   c. Append localized string ID 0x10B5 (separator/label)\n   d. Append formatted Unicode buffer\n   e. Append localized string ID 0x0F9E (suffix)\n7. Get final monster level scaled value with flag=0\n8. Format final resource string via FormatResourceString\n\nParameters:\n  pOutputBuffer (ECX) - Unicode output buffer for formatted string\n  nMonsterLevel (EDX) - Monster level for stat scaling\n  pStatRecord (Stack+0x4) - Pointer to stat record structure\n    +0xF0: int - Base scaling factor\n    +0xF4: int - Additional scaling factor\n  nStatIndex (Stack+0x8) - Index of stat to format\n  pBaseString (Stack+0xC) - Base Unicode string input\n\nReturns: void (output via pOutputBuffer)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Scaled value of 0 skips bonus string append (lines 6a-6e)\n  - Buffer initialized with 32 Unicode default constructors\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x10AE - String ID for FormatAndAppendStringValue\n  0x10B5 - String ID for bonus separator/label\n  0x0F9E - String ID for suffix\n  0x20   - Loop count for buffer init (32 iterations)\n  0xF0, 0xF4 - Stat record offsets for scaling factors\n\nCallees: FormatLocalizationString, GetMonsterLeveledStat, FormatAndAppendStringValue,\n         CalculateScaledValue, ValidateStringId, wsprintfA, toUnicode, strcat,\n         GetMonsterLevelScaledValue, FormatResourceString",
