      "comment": "Format a numeric value and append localized string representation to output buffer.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize local 64-wchar Unicode array (awOutput)\n2. Calculate format quotient: (nValue * 0x14) / 3, then divide by 10 for first digit\n3. Calculate remainder: modulo 10 of calculated value for second digit\n4. Ensure quotient is at least 1 (minimum threshold)\n5. Format ANSI string: if remainder is 0, use single digit format \"%d\"; otherwise use two-digit format \"%d_%d\"\n6. Convert ANSI formatted string to Unicode via toUnicode()\n7. Lock data via Ordinal_10004 (D2Common.AcquireCriticalSection) - see inline comments\n8. Concatenate formatted Unicode string to output buffer (unaff_EDI) twice\n9. Unlock via Ordinal_10004 (D2Common.ReleaseCriticalSection) - see inline comments\n10. If quotient is 1, append resource ID 0x10c0; otherwise append 0x10b6\n11. Load resource and concatenate to output\n12. Append resource ID 0xf9e and concatenate\n13. Return success (1)\n\nParameters:\nnValue (dword): Numeric value to format and localize\nIMPLICIT ESI (unaff_ESI): Preserved char* parameter, source string pointer\nIMPLICIT EDI (unaff_EDI): Preserved char* parameter, destination string pointer\n\nReturns:\n1 on success\n\nCompiler Notes:\n- iVar1: Phantom variable (optimized away by compiler)\n- unaff_ESI, unaff_EDI: Preserved register parameters from calling convention\n- Ordinal_10004: D2Common critical section lock/unlock (documented via inline comments)",
