      "comment": "Formats and displays monster skill statistics in localized string format.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call FormatLocalizationString to format base stat string from configuration\n2. Call GetMonsterLeveledStat to get leveled stat value for monster\n3. Call FormatAndAppendStringValue to format and append the stat value\n4. Call GetMonsterSkillId to retrieve monster's skill identifier\n5. Initialize 64-element Unicode buffer for skill name formatting\n6. If skill ID is non-zero:\n   a. Format skill ID to ANSI string using g_szLocalizationConfig format\n   b. Convert ANSI to Unicode via toUnicode\n   c. Validate string ID 0x10e1 (skill name prefix)\n   d. Concatenate skill name to output buffer twice\n   e. Validate string ID 0x10b3 (skill suffix)\n   f. Concatenate suffix to output buffer\n   g. Validate string ID 0xf9e (standard delimiter)\n   h. Concatenate delimiter to output buffer\n7. Call GetMonsterLevelScaledValue to get scaled damage/value\n8. Call FormatResourceString with nSuffixType=0 for standard format\n\nParameters:\n- nOutputBuffer (dword, ECX): Destination buffer for formatted output string\n- nMonsterIndex (int, EDX): Monster record index for stat lookup\n- nStatType (int, Stack+0x4): Stat type selector for configuration\n- nLevel (int, Stack+0x8): Monster level for scaled calculations\n- nReserved (int, Stack+0xc): Reserved parameter (used as loop counter internally)\n\nReturns:\n- void (formatted string written to output buffer via strcat calls)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If GetMonsterSkillId returns 0, skill name formatting is skipped entirely\n- unaff_ESI and unaff_EDI are preserved register parameters for Unicode::strcat\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x20 (32): Unicode buffer size in elements / loop iteration count\n- 0x10e1: String resource ID for skill name prefix\n- 0x10b3: String resource ID for skill suffix\n- 0xf9e: String resource ID for standard delimiter\n- 0x10ae: String resource ID passed to FormatAndAppendStringValue\n- 0x10b0: String resource ID for FormatResourceString",
