      "comment": "Format localization string and append monster skill ID if present.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call FormatLocalizationString with all parameters to format base string\n2. Get monster skill ID for skill slot 12 (0xc) at nSkillSlot position\n3. Initialize Unicode buffer (64 elements) via default constructor loop\n4. If skill ID is zero, return base format result unchanged\n5. Format skill ID as decimal string using \"%d\" format into ANSI buffer\n6. Convert ANSI buffer to Unicode (32 chars max)\n7. Append skill string to output via strcat (EDI=dest, ESI=src)\n8. Validate and append string ID 0x10a5 (skill name separator)\n9. Validate and append string ID 0xf9e (skill suffix/terminator)\n10. Return base result + 1 to indicate skill was appended\n\nParameters:\n- dwIndex (dword, ECX): Localization string index/selector\n- nParam2 (int, EDX): Format mode selector passed to FormatLocalizationString\n- nParam3 (int, Stack+0x4): Configuration structure pointer\n- nSkillSlot (int, Stack+0x8): Skill slot index for monster skill lookup\n- nParam5 (int, Stack+0xc): Alternate format parameter\n\nReturns:\n- dword: Result from FormatLocalizationString if no skill\n- dword: Result + 1 if skill ID was appended\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If GetMonsterSkillId returns 0, no skill formatting occurs\n- Skill slot 12 (0xc) is hardcoded for monster skill type lookup\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0xc (12): Monster skill type/category\n- 0x20 (32): Loop iterations for Unicode buffer init (64 elements)\n- 0x10a5: String ID for skill name separator\n- 0xf9e: String ID for skill suffix/terminator\n\nGlobals:\n- g_szLocalizationConfig: Format string \"%d\" for skill ID",
