      "comment": "Format and display an entity's field value at offset 0xf0.\n\nClassification: Thunk/Wrapper - Extracts value from structure and delegates to FormatAndAppendStringValue.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load pDataSource parameter from stack [ESP+0x4]\n2. Extract dword value at offset 0xf0 from pDataSource structure\n3. Load string resource ID 0x10ae into EDX\n4. Call FormatAndAppendStringValue with extracted value\n5. Return 1 (success)\n\nParameters:\npDataSource (void *): Pointer to data structure containing value at offset 0xf0\nIMPLICIT ESI: Preserved source string pointer (passed through to callee)\nIMPLICIT EDI: Preserved destination buffer pointer (passed through to callee)\n\nReturns:\ndword: Always returns 1 (success)\n\nCalled From:\nFunction pointer table at 0x6fbc56a4 (formatting callback array)\n\nCallees:\nFormatAndAppendStringValue(dword nValue): Formats numeric value with localization\n\nStructure Access:\nOffset 0xf0 (240): dword value passed to formatter - likely a stat/attribute value\n\nNotes:\nRET 0xc indicates 12 bytes popped (3 params including implicit ESI/EDI preservation)\nPart of UI formatting callback system for entity display",
