      "instructions": ["0x6D390|PUSH|ECX", "0x6D391|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [ESP + 0x10]", "0x6D395|PUSH|EBX", "0x6D396|MOV|EBX, dword ptr [ESP + 0xc]", "0x6D39A|PUSH|EBP", "0x6D39B|PUSH|ESI", "0x6D39C|MOV|ESI, dword ptr [ESP + 0x18]", "0x6D3A0|PUSH|EDI", "0x6D3A1|PUSH|EAX", "0x6D3A2|MOV|EDI, ECX", "0x6D3A4|PUSH|ESI", "0x6D3A5|MOV|EBP, EDX", "0x6D3A7|PUSH|EBX", "0x6D3A8|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x1c], EDI", "0x6D3AC|CALL|0x6fb38bf0"],
      "comment": "Formats monster damage range with player skill bonus modifiers for display.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Format initial localization string with monster parameters\n2. Get monster treasure class and format resource string\n3. Get base monster max damage and calculate min/max from offsets +0x144, +0x148\n4. Apply shift modifier from offset +0x128 (scale by 256)\n5. Special case: undead monsters (0x14, 0x31, 0x35) set min damage to 1\n6. Check Amplify Damage state (0x47) - apply percentage bonus from skill 0x3D\n7. Check Lower Resist state (0x48) - apply percentage bonus from skill 0x3F\n8. Format final string with calculated damage and element type from +0x140\n\nParameters:\npDisplayContext (void*) - Display context for string formatting (ECX)\nnMonsterId (int) - Monster type identifier (EDX)\npMonsterData (void*) - Pointer to monster data structure\nnDifficulty (int) - Game difficulty level\nnParam5 (int) - Additional formatting parameter\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x14/0x31/0x35 - Undead monster types (Skeleton/Horror/Mummy)\n0x3D/0x3F - Amplify Damage/Lower Resist skill IDs\n0x47/0x48 - Amplify Damage/Lower Resist state flags",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_5", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
    },
