      "comment": "Builds a monster skill tooltip string with stat information and skill name.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call FormatLocalizationString to format base localization with stat parameters\n2. Get monster leveled stat value for stat index 0x28 (40 decimal) at given level\n3. Format the stat value as resource string (suffix type 0)\n4. Get monster level-scaled value for same stat index at given level\n5. Format the scaled value as resource string (suffix type 0)\n6. Get monster skill ID for stat index 0x28 at given level\n7. Initialize Unicode buffer (32 elements) with default constructors\n8. If skill ID is non-zero:\n   a. Format skill ID using \"%d\" format string into ANSI buffer\n   b. Convert ANSI buffer to Unicode (max 32 chars)\n   c. Get localized string 0x10BB and concatenate to output\n   d. Concatenate skill name Unicode string to output\n   e. Get localized string 0x10B3 and concatenate to output\n   f. Get localized string 0x0F9E (newline/separator) and concatenate to output\n9. Return 1 (success)\n\nParameters:\n- pOutputBuffer (ECX, ushort*): Unicode output buffer to append tooltip text to\n- nStringId (EDX, int): Base localization string ID for tooltip format\n- nStatParam (stack+0, int): Stat parameter value for localization formatting\n- nMonsterLevel (stack+4, int): Monster level for stat scaling calculations\n- nStatIndex (stack+8, int): Stat index parameter for localization\n\nReturns:\n- 1: Always returns success\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If GetMonsterSkillId returns 0, skill name section is skipped entirely\n- String IDs: 0x10BB (skill label prefix), 0x10B3 (skill separator), 0x0F9E (line terminator)\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n- 0x28 (40): Monster stat index constant used for all stat queries\n- 0x20 (32): Unicode buffer size in elements\n- 0x10BB (4283): Localized string ID for skill label\n- 0x10B3 (4275): Localized string ID for skill separator\n- 0x0F9E (3998): Localized string ID for line terminator/newline\n\nDecompiler Discrepancies:\n- unaff_ESI/unaff_EDI are phantom variables - ESI actually holds pOutputBuffer throughout\n- The decompiler incorrectly shows separate ESI/EDI params for strcat calls",
