      "comment": "Formats a difficulty indicator string for game UI display.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract difficulty level from game state structure at offset +0xFC\n2. Initialize 64-element Unicode buffer with default constructors (32 iterations, 2 bytes each)\n3. If difficulty is 0, return 0 (no indicator needed)\n4. Format difficulty number as ANSI string using wsprintfA with \"%d\" format\n5. Convert ANSI buffer to Unicode using toUnicode (max 32 chars)\n6. Retrieve localized string ID 0x10BD via ValidateStringId\n7. Append retrieved string to destination using Unicode::strcat\n8. Append formatted difficulty Unicode buffer to destination\n9. Retrieve localized string ID 0x10B3 via ValidateStringId\n10. Append retrieved string to destination\n11. Retrieve localized string ID 0x0F9E via ValidateStringId\n12. Append retrieved string to destination\n13. Return 1 indicating success\n\nParameters:\n  pGameState - Pointer to game state structure containing difficulty at +0xFC\n  IMPLICIT ECX - Destination Unicode buffer pointer (preserved in ESI)\n\nReturns:\n  0 - Difficulty is 0, no string formatted\n  1 - Success, difficulty indicator string built\n\nString IDs (Localization Table):\n  0x10BD (4285) - Difficulty prefix text\n  0x10B3 (4275) - Difficulty separator/suffix\n  0x0F9E (3998) - Final difficulty suffix\n\nStack Layout:\n  [ESP+0x00..0x2F] - aCStack_60: ANSI format buffer (32 bytes)\n  [ESP+0x30..0xAF] - awszDifficultyBuffer: Unicode buffer (128 bytes, 64 wchar_t)\n\nCalling Convention: __stdcall with implicit ECX register parameter",
