      "instructions": ["0x6DFC0|PUSH|ECX", "0x6DFC1|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [ESP + 0x10]", "0x6DFC5|PUSH|EBX", "0x6DFC6|MOV|EBX, dword ptr [ESP + 0xc]", "0x6DFCA|PUSH|EBP", "0x6DFCB|PUSH|ESI", "0x6DFCC|MOV|ESI, dword ptr [ESP + 0x18]", "0x6DFD0|PUSH|EAX", "0x6DFD1|PUSH|ESI", "0x6DFD2|MOV|EBP, EDX", "0x6DFD4|PUSH|EBX", "0x6DFD5|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x18], ECX", "0x6DFD9|CALL|0x6fb38bf0", "0x6DFDE|PUSH|ESI", "0x6DFDF|PUSH|EBP"],
      "comment": "Calculates and formats monster damage with elemental mastery skill bonuses.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call FormatLocalizationString with initial parameters for base formatting\n2. Get base maximum damage via GetMonsterMaxDamage(nDamageType, nSkillType)\n3. Calculate minDamage = pMonsterData->minDamageBonus + baseDamage (offset +0x144)\n4. Calculate maxDamage = pMonsterData->maxDamageBonus + baseDamage (offset +0x148)\n5. If all damage values are zero, return early (no damage to display)\n6. Apply shift scaling: damage = (damage << shiftFactor) >> 8 using byte at +0x128\n7. For special damage types (0x14, 0x31, 0x35), force minDamage to 1\n8. Get player game context and check if unit type is 1 (player)\n9. Check Fire Mastery state (flag 0x47) and element type (0x01 at +0xD4)\n10. If Fire Mastery active: get skill 0x3D level, calculate bonus percentage, apply\n11. Check Lightning Mastery state (flag 0x48) and element type (0x02 at +0xD4)\n12. If Lightning Mastery active: get skill 0x3F level, calculate bonus percentage, apply\n13. Format final localization string with calculated min/max damage and display type\n\nParameters:\n  pOutputBuffer - Output string buffer for formatted damage text\n  nDamageType - Damage type identifier (0x14=Fire, 0x31=Lightning, 0x35=Cold)\n  pMonsterData - Pointer to monster data structure containing damage offsets\n  nSkillType - Skill type for damage calculation lookup\n  nUnused - Unused parameter (passed through to initial format call)\n\nReturns:\n  void (implicitly returns 1 via EAX but return value is not used by callers)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Returns early if all damage values (min, max, base) are zero\n  - Forces minimum damage to 1 for special damage types (Fire/Lightning/Cold)\n  - Mastery bonuses only applied if player has corresponding mastery state flag set\n  - Element type at +0xD4 must match mastery type (0x01=Fire, 0x02=Lightning)\n\nMonster Data Structure Offsets:\n  Offset  Size  Field                 Description\n  +0x128  byte  shiftFactor           Damage shift scaling factor\n  +0x140  byte  displayType           Display type for localization\n  +0x144  int   minDamageBonus        Minimum damage bonus to add\n  +0x148  int   maxDamageBonus        Maximum damage bonus to add\n  +0xD4   byte  elementType           Element type (0x01=Fire, 0x02=Lightning)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x14 (20) - Fire damage type\n  0x31 (49) - Lightning damage type\n  0x35 (53) - Cold damage type\n  0x47 (71) - Fire Mastery state flag\n  0x48 (72) - Lightning Mastery state flag\n  0x3D (61) - Fire Mastery skill ID\n  0x3F (63) - Lightning Mastery skill ID\n  0x51eb851f - Division by 100 magic multiplier (reciprocal approximation)\n\nMastery Bonus Formula:\n  adjustedDamage = baseDamage + (masteryPercent * baseDamage) / 100",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_5", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
