      "comment": "Formats monster damage tooltip with min/max damage and mastery bonus calculations.\n\nClassification: Worker function - UI tooltip formatting for monster damage display\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize 64-char Unicode buffer (local_80) with default constructors\n2. Call FormatLocalizationString with initial parameters to format base tooltip\n3. If nMonsterId == 0x2c (special monster type):\n   a. Initialize secondary buffer (aUStack_40)\n   b. Get treasure class via GetMonsterTreasureClass(0x2c, nDifficulty)\n   c. Calculate offset: treasureClass * (nDifficulty - 1) + pMonsterStats[0x158]\n   d. If offset != 0 and damageType is 4 or 5, format resource string\n4. Get max damage via GetMonsterMaxDamage(nMonsterId, nDifficulty)\n5. Read damage type from pMonsterStats+0x140\n6. Calculate scaled min/max damage:\n   - minDamage = (pMonsterStats[0x144] + maxDamage) << shiftAmount >> 8\n   - maxDamage = (pMonsterStats[0x148] + maxDamage) << shiftAmount >> 8\n7. Select localization string ID based on damage type:\n   - 0x02 (physical) -> 0x10a3\n   - 0x04 (fire/cold) -> 0x10a2\n   - 0x05 (lightning) -> 0x10a4\n   - Other types -> early return\n8. Get player unit via GetGameContext()\n9. If player is type 1 and has state 0x48 (Critical Strike mastery active):\n   a. Get mastery skill (skill ID 0x3f) via GetUnitSkillById\n   b. Get skill level via GetSkillLevel\n   c. Get bonus percentage via GetMonsterSkillId\n   d. Apply bonus: damage += (bonus * damage) / 100\n10. Call FormatLocalizationString with final min/max damage values\n\nParameters:\n  pOutputBuffer (ECX) - Unicode buffer to receive formatted tooltip string\n  nMonsterId (EDX) - Monster type ID (0x2c triggers treasure class handling)\n  pMonsterStats (Stack+4) - Pointer to monster stats structure\n  nDifficulty (Stack+8) - Game difficulty level (1=Normal, 2=Nightmare, 3=Hell)\n  nStringId (Stack+C) - Base localization string ID\n\nMonster Stats Structure Offsets:\n  +0x128 - byte shift amount for damage scaling\n  +0x140 - byte damage type (2=phys, 4=fire/cold, 5=lightning)\n  +0x144 - int base minimum damage\n  +0x148 - int base maximum damage\n  +0x158 - int treasure class offset\n  +0xd4  - byte mode flag (checked for value 2)\n\nReturns: void (output written to pOutputBuffer)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x2c - Special monster type requiring treasure class lookup\n  0x3f - Critical Strike/Mastery skill ID\n  0x48 - Unit state flag for mastery active\n  0x10a2 - Fire/Cold damage localization string\n  0x10a3 - Physical damage localization string\n  0x10a4 - Lightning damage localization string",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_5", "STRUCT_ItemData", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
