      "instructions": ["0x6E6B0|SUB|ESP, 0x68", "0x6E6B3|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [ESP + 0x74]", "0x6E6B7|PUSH|EBX", "0x6E6B8|MOV|EBX, dword ptr [ESP + 0x70]", "0x6E6BC|PUSH|EBP", "0x6E6BD|PUSH|ESI", "0x6E6BE|PUSH|EDI", "0x6E6BF|MOV|EDI, dword ptr [ESP + 0x80]", "0x6E6C6|PUSH|EAX", "0x6E6C7|PUSH|EDI", "0x6E6C8|MOV|EBP, EDX", "0x6E6CA|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0x6E6CC|PUSH|EBX", "0x6E6CD|CALL|0x6fb38bf0", "0x6E6D2|PUSH|0x44"],
      "comment": "Format display dimension values for viewport rendering with localization support.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call FormatLocalizationString to initialize localization context with resource and grid params\n2. Calculate height spacing: (aspect_ratio_c * (gridSize - 1) + aspect_ratio_o) * 2 / 3\n3. Initialize 64-element wchar array with default constructor calls (loops 32 times, 2 bytes per element)\n4. If height spacing != 0: format as decimal string, convert to Unicode, append formatted strings with resource labels (0x10b6, 0xf9e)\n5. Query viewport state via Ordinal_11045 and Ordinal_10589 calls\n6. Calculate scaled dimensions: dimY = (coord_y + offset_y) << shift_bits; dimX = (coord_x + offset_x) << shift_bits\n7. Apply 75x multiplier via multiply-and-shift: LEA EDX,[EDX + EDX*0x2]; LEA EDX,[EDX + EDX*0x4] (multiply by 15, then >> 8)\n8. Get effect modifier via Ordinal_10589(0x45): check if value 0x1 at offset 0x4\n9. If modifier found and validation flags set: retrieve modifier value with Ordinal_10949, Ordinal_10968, Ordinal_10996\n10. Calculate percentage increase: (modifier * dimension / 100); apply to both dimY and dimX\n11. Clear wchar array again with 32 loop iterations\n12. Compare final dimensions: if equal, format single value; if different, format as \"X - Y\" range\n13. Call Ordinal_10004 multiple times between string concatenations (appears to be accumulator reset)\n14. Return 1 (success status)\n\nParameters:\n- dwResourceId: Resource identifier for localization lookup (ECX fastcall)\n- nPositionX: Grid X coordinate for dimension calculation (EDX fastcall)\n- nPositionY: Screen Y coordinate (stack param)\n- nGridSize: Grid cell count, used to calculate base spacing (stack param)\n- pszDestBuffer: Destination Unicode string buffer for formatted output (stack param)\n\nReturns:\n- 1 on success\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Height spacing calculation uses signed fractional arithmetic: (aspect_c * (gridSize-1) + aspect_o) * 2 / 3\n- Dimensions adjusted via bit-shift scaling based on zoom/aspect byte at param_3 + 0x128\n- Modifier application: percentage-based multiplier applied via 32-bit signed IMUL with magic constant 0x51eb851f\n- Format string selection: single value (0x6fbb0de4) vs range format (0x6fbb40a0) based on dimension equality\n- Multiple resource ID lookups (0x44, 0x45, 0x47) for different aspect/modifier data tables\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x20: Array size constant (32 wchar elements, 2 bytes each = 64 bytes)\n- 0x44: Resource ID for aspect ratio table lookup\n- 0x45: Resource ID for modifier table lookup\n- 0x47: Property flags check in modifier structure\n- 0x55555556: Division magic for calculating height spacing (divides by 3)\n- 0x1: Modifier enabled flag at offset +0x4 in effect structure\n- 0xffffffff: Default modifier parameter (unsigned max = -1 in signed)\n- 0x3d: Property type/ID constant for modifier lookup\n- 0x51eb851f: Magic constant for percentage multiplication (100x scale factor)\n- 0x4b: Scaling factor for dimension calculations (75 decimal)\n- 0xff1f: Bit mask for bit-shift count (0x1f = 31, masks to valid shift range)\n- 0xd4: Validation flag offset in structure (checks for 0x01)\n- Resource IDs in string table: 0x10f0 (main), 0x10b6, 0xf9e, 0x10e2, 0x10a1, 0x10be (label strings)",
      "tags": ["PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_5", "STRUCT_Room1", "STRUCT_ItemData", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
