      "comment": "Append formatted stat value to a string output buffer\nRetrieves a stat data structure via Ordinal_10589, accesses field at offset +0x78, and formats it into a string buffer.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call Ordinal_10589(0x3e) to retrieve stat data structure pointer\n2. Load dword at [stat_data + 0x78] (field offset within structure)\n3. Push value and this pointer (ECX) as parameters\n4. Call FormatAndAppendStringValue to append formatted value to output string\n\nParameters:\nECX (implicit, IMPLICIT): this pointer - output string buffer context\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Stat data structure returned by Ordinal_10589 assumed to be valid (no NULL check)\n- Offset 0x78 is a fixed field within stat data structure\n- Returns void with stdcall stack cleanup pattern (return addr + 3 dwords)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x3e (62 decimal) - Stat type identifier passed to Ordinal_10589\n0x78 (120 decimal) - Field offset within stat data structure containing value to format",
