      "instructions": ["0x6F050|PUSH|ECX", "0x6F051|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [ESP + 0x10]", "0x6F055|PUSH|EBX", "0x6F056|MOV|EBX, dword ptr [ESP + 0xc]", "0x6F05A|PUSH|EBP", "0x6F05B|PUSH|ESI", "0x6F05C|PUSH|EDI", "0x6F05D|MOV|EDI, dword ptr [ESP + 0x1c]", "0x6F061|PUSH|EAX", "0x6F062|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0x6F064|PUSH|EDI", "0x6F065|MOV|EBP, EDX", "0x6F067|PUSH|EBX", "0x6F068|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x1c], ESI", "0x6F06C|CALL|0x6fb38bf0"],
      "comment": "Format unit stat values with percentage-based property bonuses.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call FormatLocalizationString to get base stat formatted value\n2. Call Ordinal_10997(0x37) to retrieve resource stat property flag value\n3. Call Ordinal_11045 to get per-stat modifier adjustment\n4. Load X offset from pUnit[0x144] and Y offset from pUnit[0x148]\n5. Add the stat modifier to both X and Y offsets\n6. Check if all values (X, Y, modifier) are zero - if so return early (base + resource)\n7. Retrieve bit shift count from pUnit[0x128] masked with 0x1f\n8. Apply left shift then arithmetic right shift by 8 to both X and Y offsets (normalize)\n9. For specific stat types (0x14, 0x31, 0x35): override X offset to 1\n10. Call FUN_6fb62880 to get party/game state information\n11. For property 0x47 (fire): if active and unit allows (pUnit[0xd4] == 0x01), call Ordinal_10949(0xffffffff) to get resistance, Ordinal_10968 to calculate damage bonus, Ordinal_10996(0x3d) to get fire percentage bonus, apply (bonus * X)/100 and (bonus * Y)/100\n12. For property 0x48 (cold): repeat step 11 with 0x02 flag and 0x3f percentage value\n13. Call FormatLocalizationString again with adjusted X/Y offsets and pUnit[0x140] as modifier byte\n14. Return final format value + base value + resource value\n\nParameters:\n  pFormatString: void * - Format template for stat display string\n  nStatId: int - Stat type ID (0x14, 0x31, 0x35 receive special handling)\n  pUnit: UnitAny * - Pointer to unit structure containing stat data at offsets 0x128, 0x140, 0x144, 0x148, 0xd4\n  nSubordinalValue: int - Secondary stat parameter passed to ordinals\n  nFlag: int - Unused/reserved flag parameter\n\nReturns:\n  int: Combined formatted value (base + adjusted offsets + resource), or zero if calculation fails\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Magic numbers: 0x37 (stat flag), 0x47/0x48 (fire/cold), 0x3d/0x3f (fire/cold bonuses), 0x01/0x02 (property flags)\n  - Offsets 0x144/0x148 are signed and can be negative\n  - Bit shift masked with 0x1f limits to 31-bit max\n  - Ordinal functions are D2Common engine lookups for game stat data",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PROP_NOCALLER", "STRUCT_Skill", "PARAM_5", "STRUCT_ItemData", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
