      "comment": "Formats monster damage values with skill bonuses for UI display.\n\nClassification: Worker function - formats damage text with mastery bonuses\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call FormatLocalizationString with base parameters for initial formatting\n2. Get base monster max damage via GetMonsterMaxDamage(nMonsterType, nSkillLevel)\n3. Calculate nDamageMin = pMonsterData[0x144] + nBaseDamage\n4. Calculate nDamageMax = pMonsterData[0x148] + nBaseDamage\n5. If any damage values non-zero:\n   a. Apply shift from pMonsterData[0x128]: nDamageMin = (nDamageMin << shift) >> 8\n   b. Apply same shift to nDamageMax\n   c. If nMonsterType is 0x14, 0x31, or 0x35: override nDamageMin to 1\n6. Get game context (player unit) via GetGameContext()\n7. If player type == 1 (Player unit):\n   a. Check for Fire Mastery (state 0x47):\n      - If active AND (pMonsterData null OR pMonsterData[0xd4] == 1):\n      - Get Fire Mastery skill (0x3d) and level\n      - Calculate bonus percentage via GetMonsterSkillId\n      - Apply bonus: damage = damage + (bonus * damage) / 100\n   b. Check for Lightning Mastery (state 0x48):\n      - If active AND (pMonsterData null OR pMonsterData[0xd4] == 2):\n      - Get Lightning Mastery skill (0x3f) and level\n      - Apply same percentage bonus formula\n8. Format final damage values via FormatLocalizationString with shift byte from [0x140]\n9. Get skill display ID via GetMonsterSkillId\n10. Format resource string with skill ID\n\nParameters:\n- pOutputBuffer (ECX): Destination buffer for formatted string\n- nMonsterType (EDX): Monster type ID (0x14=special1, 0x31=special2, 0x35=special3)\n- pMonsterData (Stack+4): Pointer to monster data structure with fields:\n    +0x128: Shift amount for damage scaling\n    +0x140: Formatting byte\n    +0x144: Base minimum damage\n    +0x148: Base maximum damage\n    +0xd4: Element type (1=fire, 2=lightning)\n- nSkillLevel (Stack+8): Skill level for damage calculation\n- nDifficultyLevel (Stack+C): Difficulty level modifier\n\nReturns: void (outputs to pOutputBuffer)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x14, 0x31, 0x35: Special monster types requiring min damage = 1\n- 0x47: Fire Mastery state flag\n- 0x48: Lightning Mastery state flag\n- 0x3d: Fire Mastery skill ID\n- 0x3f: Lightning Mastery skill ID\n- 100: Percentage divisor for bonus calculation\n- 8: Right shift amount (divides by 256)",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_5", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
