      "comment": "Formats monster skill duration text for UI display.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call FormatLocalizationString to initialize the output buffer with base skill text\n2. Call CalculateScaledValue with skill level and config values at offsets +0xf8 and +0xfc to compute the duration in frames/ticks\n3. Initialize Unicode buffer (64 elements) via default constructor loop (32 iterations)\n4. If scaled duration is non-zero:\n   a. Format duration value to ANSI string using \"%d\" format (g_szLocalizationConfig)\n   b. Convert ANSI to Unicode via toUnicode()\n   c. ValidateStringId(0x10c4) - Get \"Lasts \" prefix string\n   d. Concatenate prefix to output\n   e. Concatenate duration value\n   f. ValidateStringId(0x10b3) - Get \" seconds\" suffix string\n   g. Concatenate suffix to output\n   h. ValidateStringId(0xf9e) - Get newline separator string\n   i. Concatenate separator to output\n5. Call GetMonsterSkillId to get the skill ID for this monster/slot\n6. Call FormatResourceString with skill ID to append final resource text\n\nParameters:\n- pOutputBuffer (dword, ECX): Pointer to Unicode output buffer for formatted text\n- nMonsterId (int, EDX): Monster unit ID for skill lookup\n- pSkillConfig (dword, stack): Pointer to skill configuration structure\n  - Offset +0xf8: nMinDuration - Minimum duration value\n  - Offset +0xfc: nMaxDuration - Maximum duration value\n- nSkillLevel (int, stack): Current skill level for scaling calculations\n- nSkillSlot (int, stack): Skill slot index\n- IMPLICIT unaff_ESI (char *): Source string pointer for strcat operations\n- IMPLICIT unaff_EDI (char *): Destination string pointer for strcat operations\n\nReturns:\n- void (no return value, output via pOutputBuffer)\n- Sets EAX to 1 at end (success indicator) but return type is void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Duration of 0 skips the \"Lasts X seconds\" text entirely\n- Uses implicit ESI/EDI registers for Unicode::strcat source/destination\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x20 (32): Loop count for Unicode buffer initialization\n- 0xf8, 0xfc: Skill config structure offsets for duration values\n- 0x10c4: String ID for duration prefix (\"Lasts \")\n- 0x10b3: String ID for time unit suffix (\" seconds\")\n- 0xf9e: String ID for newline/separator",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_5", "STRUCT_Room1", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
