      "instructions": ["0x6F7C0|PUSH|ECX", "0x6F7C1|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [ESP + 0x10]", "0x6F7C5|PUSH|EBX", "0x6F7C6|MOV|EBX, dword ptr [ESP + 0xc]", "0x6F7CA|PUSH|EBP", "0x6F7CB|PUSH|ESI", "0x6F7CC|MOV|ESI, dword ptr [ESP + 0x18]", "0x6F7D0|PUSH|EDI", "0x6F7D1|PUSH|EAX", "0x6F7D2|MOV|EDI, ECX", "0x6F7D4|PUSH|ESI", "0x6F7D5|MOV|EBP, EDX", "0x6F7D7|PUSH|EBX", "0x6F7D8|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x1c], EDI", "0x6F7DC|CALL|0x6fb38bf0"],
      "comment": "Formats skill damage text with aura bonus calculations for UI display.\n\nClassification: Worker function - formats damage info with aura skill bonuses.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call FormatLocalizationString with initial parameters for base text setup\n2. Get missile template record for ID 0x9E (158 - elemental damage missile)\n3. Assert if missile record is null, exit with error code -1 on failure\n4. Calculate resource string offset: [missile+0xC] * nDamageType + [missile+0x8]\n5. Call FormatResourceString with calculated offset for element name\n6. Get base monster max damage via GetMonsterMaxDamage(nSkillId, nDamageType)\n7. Add skill desc offsets +0x144 (min damage) and +0x148 (max damage) to base\n8. Early exit if all damage values (min, max, base) are zero\n9. Apply shift scaling: damage << [desc+0x128] >> 8 (fixed-point to integer)\n10. For specific skills (0x14=Smite, 0x31=Zeal, 0x35=Vengeance), force min=1\n11. Get game context and check if player unit (field_4 == 1)\n12. Check Holy Fire aura (state 0x47): if active and element type 0x01 (fire):\n    - Get skill 0x3D (Holy Fire) at level, get bonus percent from GetMonsterSkillId\n    - Add bonus: damage += (bonus * damage) / 100\n13. Check Holy Freeze aura (state 0x48): if active and element type 0x02 (cold):\n    - Get skill 0x3F (Holy Freeze) at level, get bonus percent from GetMonsterSkillId\n    - Add bonus: damage += (bonus * damage) / 100\n14. Format final damage string with min, max, and element type byte from +0x140\n\nParameters:\n  pOutputBuffer (ECX): Output buffer for formatted damage string\n  nSkillId (EDX): Skill ID determining damage type and special handling\n  pSkillDescRecord (Stack+0x4): Pointer to skill description record structure\n  nDamageType (Stack+0x8): Damage type index for element calculation\n  nSkillLevel (Stack+0xC): Skill level for scaling\n\nReturns: void (formats to output buffer)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Skills 0x14, 0x31, 0x35 force minimum damage to 1\n- Holy Fire applies only to fire element (0x01 at offset +0xD4)\n- Holy Freeze applies only to cold element (0x02 at offset +0xD4)\n- Null pSkillDescRecord allows aura bonus without element check\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x9E (158) - Missile template ID for elemental damage reference\n0x47 (71) - Unit state flag for Holy Fire aura active\n0x48 (72) - Unit state flag for Holy Freeze aura active  \n0x3D (61) - Skill ID for Holy Fire\n0x3F (63) - Skill ID for Holy Freeze\n0x14 (20) - Smite skill ID\n0x31 (49) - Zeal skill ID\n0x35 (53) - Vengeance skill ID\n\nSkill Desc Record Offsets:\n+0x8: Base damage offset in missile data\n+0xC: Damage scale factor per level\n+0xD4: Element type byte (1=fire, 2=cold)\n+0x128: Shift amount for fixed-point conversion\n+0x140: Element type for display formatting\n+0x144: Minimum damage bonus\n+0x148: Maximum damage bonus",
      "tags": ["MOD_UI", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PROP_NOCALLER", "UI_SKILLS", "SRC_SkillDesc.cpp", "PARAM_5", "TBL_skilldesc", "STRUCT_Other", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
