      "instructions": ["0x6FBD0|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [ESP + 0x8]", "0x6FBD4|SUB|ESP, 0x60", "0x6FBD7|PUSH|EBX", "0x6FBD8|PUSH|EBP", "0x6FBD9|PUSH|ESI", "0x6FBDA|PUSH|EDI", "0x6FBDB|PUSH|EAX", "0x6FBDC|MOV|EDI, ECX", "0x6FBDE|PUSH|EDX", "0x6FBDF|CALL|0x6fb984e8", "0x6FBE4|MOV|EBP, EAX", "0x6FBE6|LEA|ESI, [ESP + 0x30]", "0x6FBEA|MOV|EBX, 0x20", "0x6FBEF|MOV|ECX, ESI", "0x6FBF1|CALL|dword ptr [0x6fba5c30]"],
      "comment": "Builds a Unicode tooltip string for a monster's skill modifier.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get the skill ID from the monster using GetMonsterSkillId(nMonsterId, nSkillSlot)\n2. Initialize a local Unicode buffer of 64 characters (32 iterations x 2 bytes each)\n3. If skill ID is 0 (no skill), return false immediately\n4. Select format string based on skill ID sign:\n   - Negative skill ID: use \"%d\" format (g_szResourceFormatPlain)\n   - Positive skill ID: use \"+%d\" format (g_szResourceFormatPlus)\n5. Format the skill ID into an ANSI buffer using wsprintfA\n6. Convert the ANSI skill string to Unicode using toUnicode\n7. Fetch localized string 0x10A1 via ValidateStringId and concatenate to output\n8. Concatenate the skill ID string to output\n9. Fetch localized string 0x10B3 via ValidateStringId and concatenate to output\n10. Fetch localized string 0x0F9E via ValidateStringId and concatenate to output\n11. Return true (success)\n\nParameters:\n  pOutputBuffer (ECX): Unicode* - Output buffer to receive the formatted tooltip string\n  nMonsterId (EDX): int - Monster type identifier used to look up skill\n  nUnused (Stack+0x4): int - Unused parameter (preserved for calling convention)\n  nSkillSlot (Stack+0x8): int - Skill slot index to query (0-based)\n\nReturns:\n  bool - true if skill tooltip was built successfully, false if monster has no skill\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Returns false (EAX=0) if GetMonsterSkillId returns 0\n  - Negative skill IDs are formatted without plus sign prefix\n  - Positive skill IDs are formatted with plus sign prefix (\"+%d\")\n\nString IDs:\n  0x10A1 - Skill label prefix localization\n  0x10B3 - Skill value separator localization  \n  0x0F9E - Skill suffix localization\n\nCalled Functions:\n  GetMonsterSkillId - Retrieves skill ID for monster at specified slot\n  Unicode::_default_constructor_closure_ - Initializes Unicode character\n  wsprintfA - Formats skill ID as ANSI string\n  Unicode::toUnicode - Converts ANSI to Unicode\n  ValidateStringId - Fetches localized string by ID\n  Unicode::strcat - Concatenates Unicode strings",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_4", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control"]
