      "comment": "Appends monster skill description text to a Unicode string buffer.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call GetMonsterSkillId(nMonsterId, nSkillSlot) to retrieve skill ID\n2. Initialize local Unicode buffer (64 chars) via constructor loop (32 iterations, 2 bytes each)\n3. If skill ID is zero, return early with success (1)\n4. Select format string based on skill ID sign:\n   - Negative: g_szResourceFormatNegative (\"%d\")\n   - Positive: g_szResourceFormatPlus (\"+%d\")\n5. Format skill ID into ANSI buffer using wsprintfA\n6. Convert ANSI buffer to Unicode via toUnicode\n7. Validate and concatenate string ID 0x10A3 to destination\n8. Concatenate formatted skill ID buffer to destination\n9. Validate and concatenate string ID 0x10B3 to destination\n10. Validate and concatenate string ID 0x0F9E to destination\n11. Return success (1)\n\nParameters:\n  pDestString (ECX) - Unicode string buffer to append skill description to\n  nMonsterId (EDX) - Monster type ID for skill lookup\n  nUnused (Stack+0x4) - Unused parameter\n  nSkillSlot (Stack+0x8) - Skill slot index (0-7 typically)\n\nReturns:\n  int - Always returns 1 (success)\n\nString IDs Referenced:\n  0x10A3 - Skill prefix text (e.g., \"Skills: \")\n  0x10B3 - Skill separator text\n  0x0F9E - Skill suffix text\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Returns early if GetMonsterSkillId returns 0 (no skill in slot)\n  - Negative skill IDs formatted without '+' sign\n  - Uses __fastcall: first two params in ECX/EDX, rest on stack\n\nStack Frame:\n  [ESP+0x00..0x0F] - Saved registers (EBX, EBP, ESI, EDI)\n  [ESP+0x10..0x2F] - szSkillIdBuffer (32 bytes ANSI)\n  [ESP+0x30..0x6F] - awSkillBuffer (64 Unicode chars, 128 bytes)",
