      "comment": "Formats curse skill description text for UI display.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call FormatLocalizationString with all parameters to format base localization\n2. Get scaled monster level value via GetMonsterLevelScaledValue(nMonsterId, nSkillSlot)\n3. Get current difficulty level via GetVideoFrameCount (returns difficulty byte)\n4. Get difficulty record via GetDifficultyLevelRecord(difficulty)\n5. Assert that ptDifficultyLevel->nMonsterAICurseDivisor != 0 (offset 0x1c)\n6. If divisor is zero, trigger FogAssert and exit with code -1\n7. Calculate curse duration: nScaledValue / ptDifficultyLevel->nMonsterAICurseDivisor\n8. Format resource string with calculated duration via FormatResourceString\n9. Get monster skill ID via GetMonsterSkillId(nMonsterId, nSkillSlot)\n10. Format and append skill value string via FormatAndAppendStringValue\n11. Return sum of all three formatting results\n\nParameters:\n- dwSkillIndex (dword, ECX): Skill index/selector for localization lookup\n- nMonsterId (int, EDX): Monster type identifier\n- nParam3 (int, stack+0x4): Configuration structure pointer\n- nSkillSlot (int, stack+0x8): Skill slot index\n- nParam5 (int, stack+0xc): Additional format parameter\n\nReturns:\n- Sum of three formatting function results (locale + resource + skill string)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Division by zero protection: asserts nMonsterAICurseDivisor != 0\n- Exit code -1 (0xffffffff) on assertion failure\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x1c: Offset to nMonsterAICurseDivisor field in DifficultyLevelRecord\n- 0x87: Line number in SkillDesc.cpp for assertion\n- 0x10b0: Resource string ID passed to FormatResourceString\n- 0x10ae: Resource string ID passed to FormatAndAppendStringValue\n\nSource File: C:\\Projects\\Diablo2\\Source\\D2Client\\UI\\SkillDesc.cpp",
      "tags": ["MOD_UI", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PROP_NOCALLER", "UI_SKILLS", "SRC_SkillDesc.cpp", "PARAM_5", "TBL_skilldesc", "STRUCT_Other", "AI_MONSTER", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
