      "comment": "BuildMonsterResurrectModeString - Builds formatted string showing monster resurrect mode value\n\nClassification: Worker function - called to format resurrect mode for display\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call GetMonsterResurrectMode(0x48) to get current monster resurrect mode value\n2. Initialize Unicode buffer (32 elements) via default constructor loop\n3. If resurrect mode is 0, return early with EAX=0 (no resurrect mode active)\n4. Negate resurrect mode value for display formatting\n5. Format negated value as decimal string using wsprintfA with \"%d\" format\n6. Convert ANSI formatted string to Unicode via toUnicode\n7. Validate and retrieve localized string ID 0x10c2\n8. Concatenate result to destination buffer (via ECX/ESI)\n9. Concatenate local Unicode buffer to destination\n10. Validate and retrieve localized string ID 0x10b3\n11. Concatenate result to destination buffer\n12. Validate and retrieve localized string ID 0xf9e\n13. Concatenate result to destination buffer\n14. Return EAX=1 (success)\n\nParameters:\n  IMPLICIT ECX: Unicode* pDestBuffer - destination buffer for concatenated result\n\nReturns:\n  EAX: 0 if no resurrect mode active, 1 if string was built successfully\n\nLocals:\n  nResurrectMode (int): Return value from GetMonsterResurrectMode, negated for display\n  nLoopCounter (int): Loop counter for Unicode buffer initialization (32 iterations)\n  local_40 (ushort[32]): Local Unicode buffer for formatted resurrect mode value\n  aCStack_60 (char[32]): ANSI buffer for wsprintfA intermediate result\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x48 - Monster index parameter for GetMonsterResurrectMode\n  0x20 - Loop count (32 Unicode characters) and toUnicode max length\n  0x10c2 - String ID for resurrect mode prefix text\n  0x10b3 - String ID for resurrect mode middle text\n  0xf9e - String ID for resurrect mode suffix text\n\nCalled Functions:\n  GetMonsterResurrectMode - D2Common ordinal, gets monster resurrect mode by index\n  Unicode::_default_constructor_closure_ - Initializes Unicode character\n  wsprintfA - Windows API, formats integer as ANSI string\n  Unicode::toUnicode - Converts ANSI to Unicode\n  ValidateStringId - Retrieves localized string by ID\n  Unicode::strcat - Concatenates Unicode strings",
