      "comment": "Builds formatted stat modifier text for character stats UI display.\n\nUses string IDs to build localized stat bonuses with +/- formatting based on sign.\nAccesses stat descriptor structure at offsets +0xF0 and +0xF4 for stat values.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Append opening bracket (string ID 0x10FE)\n2. Calculate first stat value = nModifier * pStatInfo[0xF4]\n3. If value != 0, format with \"+%d\" (positive) or \"%d\" (negative)\n4. Append stat name (0x10A0), value, separator (0x10B3), suffix (0xF9E)\n5. Append bracket (0x10FE)\n6. Calculate second stat value = pStatInfo[0xF0] * nModifier\n7. If value != 0, format and append label (0x10C6), value, separator, suffix\n8. If nModifier > 1, append plural indicator (0x10FD), level text (0x10C7), suffix\n9. Append closing bracket (0x10FC)\n10. Repeat steps 2-4 for first stat\n11. Append closing bracket (0x10FC)\n12. Repeat steps 6-7 for second stat\n\nParameters:\n  this (ECX)     - Unicode string builder object (implicit __thiscall)\n  pStatInfo      - Pointer to stat descriptor structure with +0xF0 and +0xF4 fields\n  nModifier      - Multiplier for stat values (typically character level or count)\n\nReturns:\n  1 always (success)\n\nString IDs:\n  0x10FE - Opening bracket / section start\n  0x10FC - Closing bracket / section end\n  0x10A0 - First stat label\n  0x10B3 - Separator between value and suffix\n  0x10C6 - Second stat label\n  0x10C7 - Level/count text\n  0x10FD - Plural indicator\n  0x0F9E - Suffix/newline\n\nFormat Strings:\n  0x6FBC6358 - \"+%d\" (positive values)\n  0x6FBB0DE4 - \"%d\"  (negative values)",
      "tags": ["PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_3", "STRUCT_Room1", "PROP_LOOPHEAVY", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
