      "instructions": ["0x70B70|SUB|ESP, 0x60", "0x70B73|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [ESP + 0x6c]", "0x70B77|PUSH|EBX", "0x70B78|MOV|EBX, dword ptr [ESP + 0x68]", "0x70B7C|PUSH|EBP", "0x70B7D|PUSH|ESI", "0x70B7E|PUSH|EDI", "0x70B7F|MOV|EDI, dword ptr [ESP + 0x78]", "0x70B83|PUSH|EAX", "0x70B84|PUSH|EDI", "0x70B85|MOV|ESI, EDX", "0x70B87|MOV|EBP, ECX", "0x70B89|PUSH|EBX", "0x70B8A|CALL|0x6fb38bf0", "0x70B8F|PUSH|EDI"],
      "comment": "Formats monster stat tooltip displaying level difference and damage range.\n\nWorker function that builds a localized string for monster tooltips showing:\n- Level difference relative to player (with +/- prefix)\n- Min/max damage values scaled by difficulty\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call FormatLocalizationString with initial parameters\n2. Get monster level stat via GetMonsterLevelStat\n3. Initialize 32-element Unicode buffer (64 bytes) with default constructors\n4. If level stat is non-zero:\n   a. Select format string: \"+%d\" for positive, \"%d\" for negative\n   b. Format level stat to ANSI string via wsprintfA\n   c. Convert ANSI to Unicode via toUnicode\n   d. Append localization strings 0x10b2, 0x10b3, 0xf9e via strcat\n5. Get treasure class via GetMonsterTreasureClass\n6. Calculate resource ID: (treasureClass * difficulty) + pMonsterStats[0x56]\n7. Get max damage via GetMonsterMaxDamage\n8. Read damage parameters from MonsterStats structure:\n   - nMinBaseDamage from offset 0x144 (index 0x51)\n   - byDamageShift from offset 0x128 (index 0x4a)\n   - nMaxBaseDamage from offset 0x148 (index 0x52)\n9. Format resource string for damage display\n10. Calculate scaled damage: ((baseDmg + maxDmg) << shift) * resourceId >> 8\n11. Call FormatLocalizationString with calculated min/max damage\n\nParameters:\n  pOutputBuffer (ECX): Unicode output buffer for formatted string\n  nMonsterClassId (EDX): Monster class identifier\n  pMonsterStats (Stack+0x4): Pointer to MonsterStats structure\n  nDifficultyLevel (Stack+0x8): Current game difficulty (0=Normal, 1=NM, 2=Hell)\n  nAreaLevel (Stack+0xC): Area level for scaling calculations\n\nReturns: void\n\nStructure Offsets (MonsterStats):\n  Offset  Size  Field           Description\n  0x128   1     byDamageShift   Bit shift for damage scaling\n  0x144   4     nMinBaseDamage  Minimum base damage value\n  0x148   4     nMaxBaseDamage  Maximum base damage value\n  0x158   4     nResourceBase   Base resource ID offset\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x10b2 - String ID for level stat prefix\n  0x10b3 - String ID for level stat suffix\n  0xf9e  - String ID for damage format\n  0x20   - Unicode buffer element count (32 characters)\n  0x5    - Damage format type parameter",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_5", "STRUCT_Room1", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
