      "comment": "Formats and renders localized game text with viewport scaling and text positioning.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get frame display configuration from Ordinal_10582(0x121) base address\n2. Query current video frame count via GetVideoFrameCount() - masked 0xff\n3. Initial text format via FormatLocalizationString(pWidget, param2, param3, param4, param5)\n4. Load X scale factor from config[frame_index*4 + 0x22c]\n5. Load Y scale factor from config[frame_index*4 + 0x238]  \n6. Retrieve viewport scale from pLayoutParams+0xf4, calculate (scale*(sizeScale-1))\n7. Apply first FormatLocalizationString with scaled dimensions: ((scale*X)/100 + X), ((scale*Y)/100 + Y)\n8. Query blend/tint mode via Ordinal_10990(0x4f), apply Ordinal_10968 to blend modes\n9. Fetch color palette from Ordinal_10582 at offset 0x180/0x174 indexed by frame count\n10. Calculate final text position: (colorPos + (colorPos * (tint * blendMode + scale * (sizeScale-1))) / 100)\n11. If position != 0: Convert to wide-char string via wsprintfA+Unicode::toUnicode\n12. Apply decorations via Ordinal_10004(), concatenate result 3x to widget buffer\n13. Return 1 (success)\n\nParameters:\n- pWidget (void *): Text widget/string buffer to render into - IMPLICIT in ECX (fastcall)\n- nBaselineY (int): Base Y coordinate for text layout - IMPLICIT in EDX (fastcall)\n- nLayoutParams (int): Pointer to structure with viewport scale factors at offsets 0xf0/0xf4\n- nSizeScale (int): Scale factor multiplier for sizing calculations relative to layout\n- nUnused (int): Unused/reserved parameter, passed for alignment\n\nReturns:\n1 on successful text formatting and decoration application\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Frame count masked 0xff selects config row from arrays indexed by 4-byte strides\n- Magic constant 0x51eb851f used for fixed-point percentage scaling (IMUL technique)\n- Position = 0 skips decoration phase entirely \n- Unicode string constructed as 64-element wide-char stack array\n- Text concatenated to buffer 3 times consecutively",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PROP_NOCALLER", "STRUCT_Skill", "PARAM_5", "STRUCT_Room1", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
