      "comment": "Formats monster damage text for UI display based on animation frame.\n\nClassification: Worker function - builds damage text string for monster stats display\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get current video frame count (animation frame index)\n2. Get monster init stats pointer for monster ID 0x16C (364)\n3. If stats pointer is null, return 1 (success with no output)\n4. Read min damage from offset +0x174 indexed by frame\n5. Read max damage from offset +0x180 indexed by frame\n6. Calculate average damage: (min + max) / 2\n7. If average is zero, return 1 (success with no output)\n8. Initialize 32-element Unicode buffer with default constructors\n9. Format average damage as decimal string using wsprintfA with \"%d\"\n10. Convert ANSI string to Unicode via toUnicode\n11. Get string ID 0x10C6 (damage label prefix)\n12. Concatenate prefix string to output buffer (2x)\n13. Get string ID 0x0F9E (damage label suffix)\n14. Concatenate suffix string to output buffer\n15. Return 1 (success)\n\nParameters:\n  wszOutputBuffer (ECX, IMPLICIT) - wchar_t* output buffer pointer for result string\n\nReturns:\n  int - Always returns 1 (success)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Returns early if monster stats pointer is null\n- Returns early if calculated average damage is zero\n- String IDs 0x10C6 and 0x0F9E are localized damage labels\n\nStructure Layout (MonsterInitStats at nAvgDamage):\n  Offset  Size  Field               Type    Description\n  +0x174  4     anMinDamage[frame]  int[]   Min damage array by frame\n  +0x180  4     anMaxDamage[frame]  int[]   Max damage array by frame\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x16C (364) - Monster ID parameter for GetMonsterInitStatsPtr\n  0x20 (32)   - Unicode buffer element count\n  0x10C6      - String ID for damage label prefix\n  0x0F9E      - String ID for damage label suffix",
