      "comment": "Formats a localized string with count-based singular/plural suffix.\n\nClassification: Worker function - called by localization formatting system\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call FormatLocalizationString with all parameters to get base formatted count\n2. If nCount == 1 (singular):\n   a. Initialize 32-element Unicode buffer with default constructors\n   b. Format count as ANSI string using \"%d\" format (g_szLocalizationConfig)\n   c. Convert ANSI to Unicode\n   d. Append singular suffix (StringId 0x10C9) to output\n   e. Append delimiter (StringId 0x0F9E) to output\n   f. Return base count + 1\n3. If nCount == 0:\n   a. Initialize Unicode buffer (unused but required for control flow)\n   b. Return base count unchanged (no suffix appended)\n4. If nCount > 1 (plural):\n   a. Initialize 32-element Unicode buffer with default constructors\n   b. Format count as ANSI string using \"%d\" format\n   c. Convert ANSI to Unicode\n   d. Append plural suffix (StringId 0x10CA) to output\n   e. Append delimiter (StringId 0x0F9E) to output\n   f. Return base count + 1\n\nParameters:\n  pOutputBuffer (ECX) - Pointer to Unicode output buffer for formatted result\n  pSourceString (EDX) - Source Unicode string to format\n  nBaseStringId (Stack+0x4) - Base string ID for localization lookup\n  nCount (Stack+0x8) - Count value for singular(1)/plural(>1)/none(0) selection\n  nMaxLength (Stack+0xc) - Maximum length of output buffer\n\nReturns:\n  uint - Total formatted string count (base count, or base+1 if suffix added)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  nCount == 0: No suffix appended, returns base count only\n  nCount == 1: Uses singular suffix (StringId 0x10C9)\n  nCount > 1: Uses plural suffix (StringId 0x10CA)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x20 (32) - Unicode buffer element count for initialization loop\n  0x10C9 (4297) - Singular form string ID\n  0x10CA (4298) - Plural form string ID\n  0x0F9E (3998) - Delimiter string ID\n\nGlobals Accessed:\n  g_szLocalizationConfig (0x6fbb0de4) - Format stri