      "comment": "Format and display monster damage statistics for tooltip display.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call FormatLocalizationString with initial parameters to format context\n2. Get monster treasure class via GetMonsterTreasureClass(nMonsterId, nDifficulty)\n3. Calculate resource ID: dwTreasureClass * nDifficulty + pMonsterRecord[0x56]\n4. Get monster max damage via GetMonsterMaxDamage(nMonsterId, nDifficulty)\n5. Read base min damage from pMonsterRecord[0x51] (offset 0x144)\n6. Read damage shift factor from pMonsterRecord+0x128 (byte)\n7. Read base max damage from pMonsterRecord[0x52] (offset 0x148)\n8. Call FormatResourceString with calculated resource ID\n9. Calculate scaled min damage: (nBaseMinDamage + nMaxDamage) << bShift * nResourceId >> 8\n10. Calculate scaled max damage: (nBaseMaxDamage + nMaxDamage) << bShift * nResourceId >> 8\n11. Call FormatLocalizationString with scaled damage values, mode 5\n12. Return 1 (always succeeds)\n\nParameters:\npContext (void *) - ECX: Localization context buffer for string output\nnMonsterId (int) - EDX: Monster type/index identifier\npMonsterRecord (int *) - Stack[0x4]: Pointer to monster data record structure\n  +0x128: bDamageShift - Bit shift factor for damage scaling\n  +0x144: nBaseMinDamage - Base minimum damage value\n  +0x148: nBaseMaxDamage - Base maximum damage value\n  +0x158: nDamageBonus - Additional damage bonus for resource calculation\nnDifficulty (int) - Stack[0x8]: Game difficulty level (Normal/Nightmare/Hell)\nnParam5 (int) - Stack[0xC]: Additional format parameter passed to localization\n\nReturns:\n1 - Always returns success (implicit EAX=1 at 0x6fb4172e)\n\nStructure Layout (pMonsterRecord offsets):\nOffset  Size  Field           Type    Description\n0x128   1     bDamageShift    byte    Bit shift amount for damage scaling\n0x144   4     nBaseMinDamage  int     Base minimum damage before scaling\n0x148   4     nBaseMaxDamage  int     Base maximum damage before scaling\n0x158   4     nDamageBonus    int     Bonus added to treasure class calculation\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x56 (86): Array index for damage bonus in monster record (0x158/4)\n0x51 (81): Array index for base min damage (0x144/4)\n0x52 (82): Array index for base max damage (0x148/4)\n0x4a (74): Byte offset for damage shift (0x128/4, then byte access)\n0x5: Mode parameter for FormatLocalizationString (damage display mode)\n0x8: Right shift for damage scaling (divide by 256)\n\nCalling Convention: __fastcall\n- ECX: pContext\n- EDX: nMonsterId\n- Stack: pMonsterRecord, nDifficulty, nParam5\n- Callee cleanup: RET 0xC (3 stack params)",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Inventory", "PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_5", "STRUCT_Control"]
