      "comment": "Formats Vengeance skill tooltip damage value for display\n\nClassification: Worker function - Skill UI tooltip builder\nCaller Analysis: No direct callers found (likely registered as callback)\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize skill level to 0\n2. Get game context (player unit) via GetGameContext()\n3. If player unit valid:\n   a. Get Vengeance skill (ID 0x4f=79) via GetUnitSkillById\n   b. If skill found, get its level via GetSkillLevel\n4. Get monster damage modifier via GetMonsterDataFieldF0(0x4f)\n5. Get video frame count (animation index) via GetVideoFrameCount\n6. Get monster init stats pointer via GetMonsterInitStatsPtr(0x124)\n7. If stats pointer valid:\n   a. Read min damage from [stats + 0x174 + frameIndex*4]\n   b. Read max damage from [stats + 0x180 + frameIndex*4]\n   c. Calculate base damage = (min + max) / 2\n   d. Calculate bonus = (base * modifier * skillLevel) / 100\n   e. Add bonus to base damage\n8. If final damage non-zero:\n   a. Initialize Unicode buffer (32 wchars)\n   b. Format damage as \"%d\" string via wsprintfA\n   c. Convert ANSI to Unicode via toUnicode\n   d. Append localized string 0x10c6 via ValidateStringId/strcat\n   e. Append damage value via strcat\n   f. Append localized string 0xf9e (suffix) via ValidateStringId/strcat\n9. Return 1 (always succeeds)\n\nParameters:\n  pOutputBuffer: Unicode* - Destination buffer for formatted tooltip text\n  nUnknownParam1: int - Stack parameter (purpose undetermined)\n  nUnknownParam2: int - Stack parameter (purpose undetermined)\n\nReturns:\n  int - Always returns 1 (success)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Returns early if game context null\n  - Returns early if monster stats pointer null\n  - Returns early if calculated damage is zero\n  - Animation frame selects damage range from table\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x4f (79) - Vengeance skill ID\n  0x124 (292) - Monster type for stats lookup\n  0x174 - Offset to min damage array in stats\n  0x180 - Offset to max damage array in stats\n  0x10c6 (4294) - String table ID for damage prefix\n  0xf9e (3998) - String table ID for damage suffix\n  0x20 (32) - Unicode buffer length in wchars",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_3", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control"]
