      "comment": "Formats Iron Golem bonus tooltip for monster stat displays.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get player unit context via GetGameContext\n2. If no player unit, skip to step 10\n3. Get Iron Golem skill (0x45) from player unit\n4. If skill exists, get skill level\n5. If skill level > 0:\n   a. Get monster base ID for Iron Golem (0x45)\n   b. Calculate bonus = baseId * skillLevel\n   c. Initialize Unicode buffer (32 wchar_t)\n   d. Format bonus as \"+%d\" (positive) or \"%d\" (negative)\n   e. Convert to Unicode and append:\n      - String ID 0x10A0 (Iron Golem bonus label)\n      - Formatted value\n      - String ID 0x10B3 (separator)\n      - String ID 0x0F9E (stat suffix)\n6. Get monster data field F0 for input monster\n7. If player has Iron Golem skill:\n   a. Get field F0 for Iron Golem\n   b. Add (fieldF0_golem * skillLevel) to base value\n8. Reinitialize Unicode buffer\n9. If combined F0 value != 0:\n   a. Format as \"+%d\" or \"%d\"\n   b. Append string IDs 0x10C6, 0x10B3, 0x0F9E\n10. Get monster level scaled value\n11. Format resource string with scaled value\n\nParameters:\n  wszOutputBuffer [ECX] - Unicode output buffer for tooltip text\n  nMonsterId [EDX] - Monster type ID to get base stats for\n  wszLabelBuffer [Stack+0x4] - Unicode buffer for labels (unused directly)\n  nMonsterLevel [Stack+0x8] - Monster level for scaling calculations\n\nReturns: void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If no player context, only formats monster field F0 and level bonus\n  - If no Iron Golem skill, skips golem-specific bonus calculation\n  - Negative values use plain \"%d\" format, positive use \"+%d\"\n\nString IDs:\n  0x10A0 - Iron Golem bonus label\n  0x10B3 - Stat separator  \n  0x0F9E - Stat suffix\n  0x10C6 - Monster F0 field label\n\nCalled By: None detected (may be callback/vtable)\n\nImplicit Registers:\n  EDI - Destination Unicode buffer pointer (unaff_EDI)\n  ESI - Source string pointer (unaff_ESI)\n  EBP - strcat function pointer from 0x6fba5c40",
