      "comment": "Formats a scaled stat bonus value as a Unicode string with localized labels.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate scaled value using CalculateScaledValue with nLevel and min/max from pStatDescriptor (+0xf0, +0xf4)\n2. Initialize 64-element Unicode buffer via default constructor loop (32 iterations, 2 bytes per element)\n3. If scaled value is zero, return 0 (no bonus to display)\n4. Select format string based on sign: \"+%d\" (g_szResourceFormatPlus) for positive, \"%d\" (g_szLocalizationConfig) for negative\n5. Format value to ANSI string via wsprintfA\n6. Convert ANSI to Unicode via Unicode::toUnicode\n7. Concatenate localized strings using ValidateStringId and Unicode::strcat:\n   - String 0x10d4 (first label)\n   - Formatted value from local buffer\n   - String 0x10b3 (second label)\n   - String 0xf9e (third label)\n8. Return 1 on success\n\nParameters:\n  pStatDescriptor (void*): Pointer to stat descriptor structure\n    - Offset +0xf0: nMinValue (int) - minimum stat value\n    - Offset +0xf4: nMaxValue (int) - maximum stat value\n  nLevel (int): Current level for scaling calculation\n  IMPLICIT ECX: Preserved as EDI - destination Unicode buffer for output\n  IMPLICIT ESI/EDI: Used by Unicode::strcat for source/destination\n\nReturns:\n  int: 1 on success (value formatted), 0 if scaled value is zero\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Zero scaled value returns early with 0 (no string generated)\n  - Negative values use \"%d\" format (no plus sign)\n  - Positive values use \"+%d\" format\n\nString IDs:\n  0x10d4 - First localized label\n  0x10b3 - Second localized label  \n  0xf9e  - Third localized label\n\nGlobals Referenced:\n  g_szResourceFormatPlus (0x6fbc6358): \"+%d\" format string\n  g_szLocalizationConfig (0x6fbb0de4): \"%d\" format string\n  0x6fba5c30: Unicode::_default_constructor_closure_ vtable\n  0x6fba5c34: Unicode::toUnicode vtable\n  0x6fba5c40: Unicode::strcat vtable",
