      "comment": "Formats the Find Item skill bonus percentage for display in skill tooltip.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get monster init stats pointer for monstats index 0x123 (291)\n2. Get current video frame count for animation-based selection\n3. Format base localization string using string IDs from stats table\n4. Get game context (player unit)\n5. If player exists, get Find Item skill (skill ID 0x4F = 79)\n6. If skill exists, get current skill level\n7. Get monster data field F0 for Find Item skill (base bonus percentage)\n8. Calculate average of two stat values at offsets 0x174 and 0x180\n9. Apply skill level bonus: basePercent + (basePercent * multiplier * skillLevel) / 100\n10. If bonus is non-zero, initialize Unicode buffer (32 elements)\n11. Format bonus as decimal string using wsprintfA with \"%d\" format\n12. Convert ANSI string to Unicode\n13. Append string ID 0x10C6 (bonus label), the formatted bonus, and string ID 0x0F9E (percent sign)\n\nParameters:\npDestBuffer - Unicode destination buffer to append formatted bonus text (ECX, __fastcall)\n\nReturns:\nAlways returns 1 (EAX) - success indicator\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If player unit is NULL, skill bonus calculation is skipped\n- If Find Item skill not found, bonus remains 0\n- If calculated bonus is 0, string formatting is skipped entirely\n\nConstants:\n0x4F (79)  - Find Item skill ID\n0x123 (291) - Monster stats table index for skill data\n0x10A0     - Base localization string ID\n0x10C6     - Bonus label string ID\n0x0F9E     - Percent sign string ID\n0x174      - Offset to min stat value in monster init stats\n0x180      - Offset to max stat value in monster init stats\n0x22C      - Offset to string ID array in monster init stats\n0x238      - Offset to secondary string ID array",
