      "comment": "Format monster skill information for tooltip display.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call FormatLocalizationString to format base localization text\n2. If nSkillCount > 1 (monster has multiple skills):\n   a. Get monster skill ID for the (nSkillCount-1) slot\n   b. Initialize 64-element Unicode buffer with default constructors\n   c. If skill ID is valid (non-zero):\n      - Format skill ID using g_szLocalizationConfig (\"%d\" format)\n      - Convert ANSI to Unicode via toUnicode\n      - Append skill name string (ValidateStringId 0x10d5)\n      - Append separator string (ValidateStringId 0xf9e)\n   d. Append skill type string (ValidateStringId 0x110d)\n   e. Append final separator string (ValidateStringId 0xf9e)\n3. Return 1 (always succeeds)\n\nParameters:\n- pOutputBuffer (dword): ECX - Pointer to output Unicode buffer\n- nMonsterId (int): EDX - Monster ID for skill lookup\n- nSkillLevel (int): Stack+0x4 - Skill level parameter\n- nSkillCount (int): Stack+0x8 - Number of skills (if > 1, formats additional info)\n- nUnused (int): Stack+0xc - Unused parameter\n\nReturns:\n- Always returns 1\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If nSkillCount <= 1, only base localization is formatted\n- If skill ID is 0 (invalid), skill name section is skipped\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x20 (32): Loop count for Unicode buffer initialization\n- 0x10d5: String ID for skill name localization\n- 0xf9e: String ID for separator/delimiter\n- 0x110d: String ID for skill type/category\n\nNote: Uses unaffected registers unaff_EBP and unaff_EDI from caller for strcat operations",
