      "comment": "Builds a monster description string by concatenating monster data with localized text.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize 32-element Unicode buffer array (64 bytes) by calling default constructor for each element\n2. Get monster data field 0xF8 for monster index 0x60\n3. Format monster data as decimal string using wsprintfA with \"%d\" format\n4. Convert ANSI string to Unicode using toUnicode (max 32 chars)\n5. Concatenate formatted monster data to output buffer (via ECX this pointer)\n6. Get localized string for ID 0x10B3 and concatenate to output\n7. Get localized string for ID 0x10CD and concatenate to output\n8. Get localized string for ID 0xF9E and concatenate to output\n9. Return 1 (success)\n\nParameters:\n  IMPLICIT ECX: Unicode* - Destination buffer for concatenated string result\n  Note: RET 0xC cleans 12 bytes but no stack params appear used in assembly\n\nReturns:\n  int - Always returns 1 (success)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x60 - Monster index for data lookup\n  0x20 - Unicode buffer element count (32 chars)\n  0x10B3 - Localized string ID\n  0x10CD - Localized string ID\n  0xF9E - Localized string ID\n\nStack Frame:\n  [ESP+0x00..0x0B] - aCStack_60: ANSI char buffer for wsprintfA (32 bytes)\n  [ESP+0x2C..0x6B] - awUnicodeBuffer: Unicode array (64 bytes, 32 wchars)\n\nCalled From: Function pointer table at 0x6FBC5AB4",
