      "comment": "Format monster skill bonus text with level-scaled values for UI display.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call FormatLocalizationString to format base localization string\n2. Get monster skill ID for monster type 0x61 at given level\n3. Clamp skill ID to maximum 0xFA (250)\n4. Format skill resource string using FormatResourceString\n5. Get level-scaled bonus value via GetMonsterLevelScaledValue for monster 0x61\n6. Initialize 64-element Unicode buffer with default constructors\n7. If scaled value is zero, return sum of base format + resource format results\n8. Select format string: g_szLocalizationConfig (\"%d\") for negative, g_szResourceFormatPlus (\"+%d\") for positive\n9. Format scaled value to ANSI string via wsprintfA\n10. Convert ANSI to Unicode via toUnicode\n11. Validate and concatenate string IDs 0x10a0, 0x10b3, 0xf9e with Unicode::strcat\n12. Return base + resource + 1 (indicating bonus text was appended)\n\nParameters:\n- dwStringBuilder (uint, ECX): String builder context handle\n- nStringParam (int, EDX): String parameter selector\n- nSkillTableOffset (int, Stack+0x4): Offset into skill table\n- nMonsterLevel (int, Stack+0x8): Monster level for scaling calculations\n- nDisplayFlags (int, Stack+0xc): Display formatting flags\n\nReturns:\n- dwBaseFormatResult + dwResourceFormatResult if no scaled bonus (nScaledValue == 0)\n- dwBaseFormatResult + dwResourceFormatResult + 1 if bonus text appended\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x61: Monster type ID (97 decimal)\n- 0xFA: Maximum skill ID cap (250 decimal)\n- 0x20: Unicode buffer element count (32 decimal)\n- 0x10a0, 0x10b3, 0xf9e: Localization string IDs for bonus formatting\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Negative scaled value uses \"%d\" format (shows negative number)\n- Positive scaled value uses \"+%d\" format (shows with plus sign)\n- Zero scaled value skips bonus text entirely\n\nGlobals Referenced:\n- g_szLocalizationConfig @ 0x6fbb0de4: \"%d\" format string\n- g_szResourceFormatPlus @ 0x6fbc6358: \"+%d\" format string",
