      "comment": "Formats complete monster level bonus tooltip by combining localization, scaled value, and skill info.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call FormatLocalizationString with all parameters to get base localization result\n2. Call GetMonsterLevelScaledValue(nMonsterIndex, nLevel) to get scaled bonus value\n3. Initialize Unicode buffer (64 elements, 128 bytes) via default_constructor_closure loop\n4. If scaled value is zero, set result contribution to 0\n5. If scaled value non-zero:\n   a. Select format string: g_szLocalizationConfig (\"%d\") if negative, g_szResourceFormatPlus (\"+%d\") if positive\n   b. Format scaled value to ANSI string via wsprintfA\n   c. Convert ANSI to Unicode via toUnicode\n   d. Load resource string 0x10d0 via ValidateStringId\n   e. Append strings via Unicode::strcat (called twice)\n   f. Load resource string 0xf9e via ValidateStringId\n   g. Append final string via Unicode::strcat\n   h. Set result contribution to 1\n6. Call GetMonsterSkillId(nMonsterIndex, nLevel) to get skill identifier\n7. Call FormatAndAppendStringValue with skill ID (uses resource 0x10ae internally)\n8. Return sum of all three result contributions\n\nParameters:\n- nIndex (dword, ECX): Resource or string index selector for localization\n- nMonsterIndex (int, EDX): Monster type or configuration index\n- nParam3 (int, Stack+0x4): Configuration structure pointer (passed to FormatLocalizationString)\n- nLevel (int, Stack+0x8): Monster level for scaling calculations\n- nParam5 (int, Stack+0xc): Alternate format parameter (passed to FormatLocalizationString)\n- IMPLICIT ESI: Source string pointer for Unicode::strcat operations\n- IMPLICIT EDI: Destination string pointer for Unicode::strcat operations\n\nReturns:\n- Sum of three result contributions (0-3 range typical)\n- 0 if all formatting steps produce zero results\n- Higher values indicate more text segments were appended\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x20 (32): Unicode buffer element count (loop iterations)\n- 0x10d0: Resource string ID for level bonus prefix/suffix\n- 0xf9e: Resource string ID for separator or suffix\n- 0x10ae: Resource string ID used by FormatAndAppendStringValue\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Negative scaled value uses \"%d\" format (no plus sign)\n- Positive scaled value uses \"+%d\" format (explicit plus sign)\n- Zero scaled value skips all formatting, contributes 0 to result",
