      "comment": "Builds a skill damage tooltip string for monster/player skills.\n\nClassification: Worker function - formats skill damage range text with Holy Fire/Freeze bonuses.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize Unicode buffer (64 wchars) with default constructor for each element\n2. Call FormatLocalizationString with base params to begin tooltip line\n3. Get skill ID from GetMonsterSkillId(nSkillId, nSkillLevel)\n4. Get scaled skill level from GetMonsterLevelScaledValue(nSkillId, nSkillLevel)\n5. Format skill ID and level as \"%d-%d\" string\n6. Convert to Unicode and append to output buffer\n7. Append localized string 0x10D0 (separator) via strcat\n8. Append converted skill ID/level string via strcat\n9. Append localized string 0x0F9E (damage label) via strcat\n10. Get base max damage from GetMonsterMaxDamage(nSkillId, nSkillLevel)\n11. Calculate minDamage = pSkillDescEntry->field_144 + maxDamage\n12. Calculate maxDamage = pSkillDescEntry->field_148 + maxDamage\n13. If all damage values zero, return early (nLineCount + 1)\n14. Apply damage shift: min/max << (pSkillDescEntry->field_128 & 0x1F) >> 8\n15. For skills 0x14/0x31/0x35 (special melee), force minDamage = 1\n16. Check Holy Fire bonus (state 0x47, skill 0x3D):\n    a. If player has Holy Fire state and skill matches damage type 1\n    b. Get Holy Fire skill level and bonus percent\n    c. Apply bonus: damage += (bonus * damage) / 100\n17. Check Holy Freeze bonus (state 0x48, skill 0x3F):\n    a. If player has Holy Freeze state and skill matches damage type 2\n    b. Get Holy Freeze skill level and bonus percent\n    c. Apply bonus: damage += (bonus * damage) / 100\n18. Format final damage range and return combined line count\n\nParameters:\n  pOutput (ECX): Unicode output buffer for tooltip text\n  nSkillId (EDX): Skill identifier (0x14=melee1, 0x31=melee2, 0x35=melee3)\n  pSkillDescEntry (Stack+4): Pointer to skill descriptor structure\n    +0xD4: byDamageType (1=fire, 2=cold)\n    +0x128: byDamageShift - bit shift for damage scaling\n    +0x140: byDisplayMode - damage display formatting mode\n    +0x144: nMinDamageBonus - added to calculated min damage\n    +0x148: nMaxDamageBonus - added to calculated max damage\n  nSkillLevel (Stack+8): Skill level for damage calculation\n  nLineCount (Stack+C): Current tooltip line count\n\nReturns:\n  int - Updated line count (nLineCount + lines added)\n  Typically returns nLineCount + 1 for early exit, or nLineCount + 2 for full format\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Returns early if minDamage, maxDamage, and baseDamage all zero\n  - Skills 0x14, 0x31, 0x35 force minimum damage to 1 (prevents 0-X display)\n  - Holy Fire (state 0x47) bonus applied when pSkillDescEntry->field_D4 == 1\n  - Holy Freeze (state 0x48) bonus applied when pSkillDescEntry->field_D4 == 2\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x10D0 - Localization string ID for damage separator\n  0x0F9E - Localization string ID for damage label\n  0x47 - Unit state flag for Holy Fire aura active\n  0x48 - Unit state flag for Holy Freeze aura active\n  0x3D - Skill ID for Holy Fire (61)\n  0x3F - Skill ID for Holy Freeze (63)\n  0x14 - Skill ID 20 (special melee)\n  0x31 - Skill ID 49 (special melee)\n  0x35 - Skill ID 53 (special melee)\n\nVariable Reference:\n  dVar1 (nResultLines): Return value from first FormatLocalizationString\n  iVar2 (nMaxDamage): Calculated max damage with bonuses\n  iVar7 (nMinDamage): Calculated min damage with bonuses\n  iVar8 (nBonusPercent): Holy Fire/Freeze bonus percentage\n  pUVar3 (pPlayer): Player unit from GetGameContext\n  uVar4 (dwStateFlag): State flag check result\n  pSVar5 (pSkill): Skill pointer for aura lookup\n  dVar6 (nExtraLines): Lines added by final format call",
      "tags": ["PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_5", "STRUCT_Room1", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
