      "api_count": 4,
      "api_calls": ["GetMonsterMaxDamage", "ValidateStringId", "ValidateStringId", "GetMonsterSkillId"],
      "instructions": ["0x72C00|SUB|ESP, 0xcc", "0x72C06|PUSH|EBX", "0x72C07|PUSH|EBP", "0x72C08|PUSH|ESI", "0x72C09|PUSH|EDI", "0x72C0A|MOV|EDI, EDX", "0x72C0C|MOV|EBP, ECX", "0x72C0E|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x18], EDI", "0x72C12|LEA|ESI, [ESP + 0x9c]", "0x72C19|MOV|EBX, 0x20", "0x72C1E|MOV|ECX, ESI", "0x72C20|CALL|dword ptr [0x6fba5c30]", "0x72C26|ADD|ESI, 0x2", "0x72C29|DEC|EBX", "0x72C2A|JNZ|0x6fb42c1e"],
      "comment": "Formats monster damage range string for display in UI.\n\nCreates a localized damage display showing min-max damage range with optional\ndecimal precision for fractional damage values. Uses 8.8 fixed-point format\nwhere bit 7 (0x80) indicates decimal precision is needed.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize 64-element Unicode buffer for damage string\n2. Call FormatLocalizationString with monster/difficulty parameters\n3. Get base max damage from GetMonsterMaxDamage(monsterClass, difficulty)\n4. Calculate scaled min damage: (MonsterData+0x144 + baseDamage) << shiftAmount\n5. Calculate scaled max damage: (MonsterData+0x148 + baseDamage) << shiftAmount\n6. Copy damage separator string \"-\" from global to local buffer\n7. Convert separator to Unicode and append to output\n8. Validate string ID 0x10A1 (damage separator localization)\n9. Append separator to output buffer\n10. Initialize temp Unicode buffer for min damage formatting\n11. Check if min damage has decimal (bit 0x80 set): use \"%d.5\" else \"%d\"\n12. Format min damage value (value >> 8) using wsprintfA\n13. Convert formatted min damage to Unicode and append\n14. Append damage string to output\n15. Re-initialize temp buffer for max damage formatting\n16. Check if max damage has decimal (bit 0x80 set): use format accordingly\n17. Format max damage value (value >> 8) using wsprintfA\n18. Convert formatted max damage to Unicode and append\n19. Validate string ID 0x0F9E and append\n20. Get monster skill ID and append via FormatAndAppendStringValue(0x10AE)\n21. Return 1 (success)\n\nParameters:\n  pOutputBuffer (ECX): Pointer to Unicode output buffer for result string\n  nMonsterClass (EDX): Monster class/type identifier\n  pMonsterData (stack): Pointer to monster stats structure\n    +0x128: Damage shift amount (byte)\n    +0x144: Base minimum damage (int)\n    +0x148: Base maximum damage (int)\n  nDifficulty (stack): Game difficulty level (Normal/Nightmare/Hell)\n  nUnused (stack): Unused parameter\n\nReturns:\n  int: Always returns 1 (success)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - 0x80 flag in scaled damage indicates 8.8 fixed-point format\n  - When flag set, displays as \"N.5\" for half-point damage\n  - String IDs: 0x10A1 (separator), 0x0F9E (suffix), 0x10AE (skill format)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x80 - Fixed-point decimal flag (bit 7)\n  0x144 - Offset to min damage in monster data\n  0x148 - Offset to max damage in monster data\n  0x128 - Offset to damage shift amount\n  0x20 (32) - Unicode buffer element count",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_5", "STRUCT_Room1", "PROP_LOOPHEAVY", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
    },
