      "comment": "Format monster skill level information for tooltip display.\n\nClassification: Worker function - formats and appends monster skill data to output buffer.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call GetMonsterLevelScaledValue(nMonsterIndex, nSkillSlot) to get scaled level value\n2. Initialize local Unicode buffer (64 wchars) via constructor loop (32 iterations, 2 bytes each)\n3. If scaled value is non-zero:\n   a. Format scaled value as ANSI string using wsprintfA with \"%d\" format\n   b. Convert ANSI to Unicode via toUnicode()\n   c. Concatenate formatted Unicode to output buffer\n   d. Append resource string 0x10d5 (skill level label)\n   e. Concatenate to output buffer\n   f. Append resource string 0xf9e (separator/suffix)\n   g. Concatenate to output buffer\n4. Call GetMonsterSkillId(nMonsterIndex, nSkillSlot) to get skill identifier\n5. Call FormatAndAppendStringValue(dwSkillId) to format and append skill info\n\nParameters:\npOutput (ushort *): Destination Unicode buffer for formatted tooltip text [ECX, __fastcall]\nnMonsterIndex (int): Monster identifier for skill lookup [EDX, __fastcall]\npSource (ushort *): Source Unicode string for concatenation [Stack+0x4]\nnSkillSlot (int): Skill slot index (0-based) [Stack+0x8]\nIMPLICIT EDI: Preserved destination pointer (unaff_EDI) - actual strcat destination\nIMPLICIT ESI: Preserved source pointer (unaff_ESI) - actual strcat source\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Output written to pOutput buffer via concatenation\n\nResource IDs:\n0x10d5: Skill level label string\n0xf9e: String separator/suffix\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If scaled value is 0, skill level formatting block is skipped entirely\n- Unicode buffer initialized with 32 constructor calls (64 wchars total)\n\nCompiler Notes:\n- unaff_EDI/unaff_ESI are callee-preserved registers from calling convention\n- local_40/awLocalBuffer is stack-allocated Unicode[64] array",
