      "instructions": ["0x73420|SUB|ESP, 0x64", "0x73423|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [ESP + 0x68]", "0x73427|PUSH|EBX", "0x73428|PUSH|EBP", "0x73429|PUSH|ESI", "0x7342A|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0x7342C|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0xc], EDX", "0x73430|MOV|ECX, dword ptr [EAX + 0xfc]", "0x73436|MOV|EDX, dword ptr [EAX + 0xf8]", "0x7343C|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [ESP + 0x78]", "0x73440|PUSH|EDI", "0x73441|PUSH|ECX", "0x73442|PUSH|EDX", "0x73443|PUSH|EAX", "0x73444|CALL|0x6fb98b18"],
      "comment": "Format extra damage text for monster skill tooltip display.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate scaled damage value from skill descriptor min/max damage (offsets 0xF8/0xFC) at monster level\n2. Initialize 64-element Unicode buffer with default constructors (32 iterations, 2 bytes each)\n3. If scaled damage is non-zero:\n   a. Format damage as ANSI string using wsprintfA with \"%d\" format\n   b. Convert ANSI to Unicode via toUnicode()\n   c. Validate and append string ID 0x10E8 (damage label)\n   d. Append formatted damage value\n   e. Validate and append string ID 0x10B3 (unit separator)\n   f. Validate and append string ID 0x0F9E (suffix)\n4. Get monster skill ID from skill row and level via GetMonsterSkillId()\n5. Format skill ID value via FormatAndAppendStringValue() with string ID 0x10AE\n6. Return sum of format result and damage-present flag (0 or 1)\n\nParameters:\npOutputBuffer (Unicode *, ECX): Destination buffer for formatted Unicode text\nnSkillRow (int, EDX): Skill table row index for GetMonsterSkillId lookup\npSkillDesc (void *, Stack[0x4]): Pointer to skill descriptor structure\n  - Offset 0xF8: Min extra damage value (int)\n  - Offset 0xFC: Max extra damage value (int)\nnMonsterLevel (int, Stack[0x8]): Monster level for damage scaling\nIMPLICIT ESI: Source string pointer for Unicode::strcat operations\nIMPLICIT EDI: Destination string pointer for Unicode::strcat operations\n\nReturns:\nint: Count of formatted elements (0-2 typically)\n  - 0: No damage and FormatAndAppendStringValue returned 0\n  - 1: Either damage formatted OR FormatAndAppendStringValue returned 1\n  - 2+: Damage formatted AND FormatAndAppendStringValue returned 1+\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If CalculateScaledValue returns 0, damage formatting is skipped entirely\n- The function always calls GetMonsterSkillId and FormatAndAppendStringValue regardless of damage\n\nString IDs Used:\n0x10E8: Damage prefix/label string\n0x10B3: Unit separator string\n0x0F9E: Suffix/terminator string\n0x10AE: Used by FormatAndAppendStringValue for skill formatting\n\nCalled Functions:\nCalculateScaledValue(level, min, max): Scale damage by monster level\nGetMonsterSkillId(skillRow, level): Get skill identifier for formatting\nFormatAndAppendStringValue(skillId): Format skill value with localization",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_4", "STRUCT_Room1", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
