      "comment": "Appends monster level stat information to a Unicode tooltip buffer.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get monster level stat value from GetMonsterLevelStat(nMonsterIndex, nStatLevel)\n2. Initialize local Unicode buffer (32 chars) via constructor loop\n3. If stat value is 0, return 0 (no tooltip needed)\n4. Select format string: \"+%d\" for positive values, \"%d\" for negative\n5. Format stat value to ANSI string via wsprintfA\n6. Convert ANSI to Unicode via Unicode::toUnicode\n7. Validate and append string ID 0x10BA to destination\n8. Append local stat buffer to destination\n9. Validate and append string ID 0x10B3 to destination\n10. Validate and append string ID 0x0F9E to destination\n11. Return 1 indicating success\n\nParameters:\n  pDestBuffer - Destination Unicode buffer for tooltip text (ECX, __fastcall)\n  nMonsterIndex - Monster type index for stat lookup (EDX, __fastcall)\n  unused - Unused parameter (stack)\n  nStatLevel - Level parameter for stat calculation (stack)\n\nReturns:\n  0 - Stat value is 0, no text appended\n  1 - Tooltip text successfully appended\n\nString IDs:\n  0x10BA - Monster level stat label prefix\n  0x10B3 - Delimiter or separator string\n  0x0F9E - Suffix or closing string\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  Zero stat value causes early return without modifying destination buffer",
