      "comment": "Formats monster skill and treasure class information into localized strings.\n\nClassification: Worker function - called to format monster stats for display.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call FormatLocalizationString to format base monster localization data\n2. Call GetMonsterSkillId to retrieve skill ID for monster at given difficulty\n3. Initialize Unicode buffer (64 elements) for skill string construction\n4. If skill ID is non-zero:\n   a. Select format string: g_szFmtIntegerValue for negative, g_szResourceFormatPlus for positive\n   b. Format skill ID to ANSI temp buffer using wsprintfA\n   c. Convert temp buffer to Unicode using toUnicode\n   d. Call ValidateStringId(0x10e9) for Skill label string resource\n   e. Append skill string via Unicode strcat (4 concatenations total)\n   f. Call ValidateStringId(0x10b3) for additional separator string\n   g. Call ValidateStringId(0xf9e) for closing bracket separator\n   h. Set nSkillId result to 1 (indicates skill was formatted)\n5. Re-initialize Unicode buffer for treasure class formatting\n6. Call GetMonsterTreasureClass to retrieve treasure class value\n7. Calculate treasure offset: dwTreasureClass * (nDifficulty - 1) + nMonsterDataPtr[0x158]\n8. If treasure offset is non-zero:\n   a. Check monster type at nMonsterDataPtr[0x140]\n   b. If type is not 4 or 5 return early with dwLocalizationResult + nSkillId\n   c. Call FormatResourceString(nTreasureOffset, 0) to format treasure class\n9. Return combined result: dwResourceFormatResult + dwLocalizationResult + nSkillId\n\nParameters:\n- dwIndex (dword, ECX): Resource or string index for localization\n- nMonsterId (int, EDX): Monster ID for skill and treasure lookups\n- nMonsterDataPtr (int, Stack+0x4): Pointer to monster data structure with fields:\n    +0x140: Monster type (byte) where 4 is champion and 5 is unique\n    +0x158: Base treasure class offset (int)\n- nDifficulty (int, Stack+0x8): Difficulty level (1 is Normal 2 is Nightmare 3 is Hell)\n- nParam5 (int, Stack+0xC): Additional format parameter passed to FormatLocalizationString\n- IMPLICIT: unaff_ESI and unaff_EDI are source and destination string pointers for strcat\n\nReturns:\n- Combined formatting result from FormatLocalizationString plus skill format (0 or 1) plus treasure format\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Skill ID of 0 skips skill string formatting entirely\n- Negative skill IDs use plain format (debuffs) while positive use plus format (bonuses)\n- Monster types 4 (champion) and 5 (unique) get treasure class formatting\n- Other monster types skip treasure class and return early\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x20 (32): Unicode buffer element count for initialization loops\n- 0x10e9: String resource ID for Skill label\n- 0x10b3: String resource ID for separator\n- 0xf9e: String resource ID for closing bracket\n- 0x140: Offset to monster type byte in monster data\n- 0x158: Offset to treasure class base value in monster data\n- 0x04 and 0x05: Monster type values (4 is champion and 5 is unique)",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_5", "STRUCT_Room1", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
