      "instructions": ["0x73A70|SUB|ESP, 0xc4", "0x73A76|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [ESP + 0xcc]", "0x73A7D|PUSH|EBX", "0x73A7E|PUSH|EBP", "0x73A7F|MOV|EBP, dword ptr [ESP + 0xd0]", "0x73A86|PUSH|ESI", "0x73A87|PUSH|EDI", "0x73A88|CMP|EBP, EAX", "0x73A8A|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x10], EDX", "0x73A8E|MOV|EDI, ECX", "0x73A90|JNZ|0x6fb43b1e", "0x73A96|LEA|ESI, [ESP + 0x54]", "0x73A9A|MOV|EBX, 0x20", "0x73A9F|MOV|ECX, ESI", "0x73AA1|CALL|dword ptr [0x6fba5c30]"],
      "comment": "Builds a Unicode tooltip string for a resource with optional formatting.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize two Unicode arrays (64 elements each) for primary/secondary tooltips\n2. Check if nResourceId matches nResourceTarget (same ID mode):\n   a. If true, enter primary mode: format nResourceId using g_szLocalizationConfig or g_szResourceFormatPlus based on nPrefixMode\n   b. Call Ordinal_10004 (memory/state management)\n   c. Convert formatted string to Unicode using toUnicode()\n   d. Concatenate to destination string using strcat\n   e. Call pfnStrcat (function pointer concatenation)\n3. If IDs don't match (different ID mode):\n   a. Initialize secondary tooltip array\n   b. Call Ordinal_10004 (memory/state management)\n   c. Concatenate using strcat\n   d. Select format string based on nPrefixMode (0x6fbc639c or 0x6fbb40a0)\n   e. Call wsprintfA to format both IDs to secondary buffer\n   f. If bIncludeExtra != 0, call Ordinal_10004() and concatenate additional data\n4. Final concatenation of tooltip strings to destination buffer\n5. Final Ordinal_10004() call for state finalization\n6. Return 1 on success, 0 if nResourceId is 0\n\nParameters:\nnResourceId (int) - Primary resource ID to format\nnResourceTarget (int) - Target resource ID for comparison\nnPrefixMode (int) - Format mode: 0 = standard format, 1 = plus format\nnIncludeExtra (int) - Flag: if non-zero, include additional data\n\nReturns:\n1 - Success (tooltip string built)\n0 - Failure (nResourceId was 0)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If nResourceId == 0, returns immediately without processing\n- Multiple Ordinal_10004 calls throughout (likely Storm.dll state management)\n- Uses two separate tooltip buffers for different code paths\n- Function parameters passed via unaffected registers (ESI=source, EDI=dest suggest register-based calling)",
