      "comment": "Format a configuration value as Unicode string for localization display.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Query localization data (Ordinal_11033) with config offsets [0xf8] and [0xfc]\n2. Initialize 64-element Unicode array (128 bytes) with default constructors\n3. If query result non-zero (valid ID found):\n   - Convert result to ANSI string via wsprintfA with localization format\n   - Convert ANSI to Unicode using toUnicode()\n   - Append string values via three strcat() calls (Ordinal_10004 between calls)\n4. Process formatting (Ordinal_10996, FormatAndAppendStringValue)\n5. Return formatted value + 1 if result was valid, else formatted value\n\nParameters:\n- pConfigData (ECX): Source data context/handle\n- nValueId (EDX): Configuration value identifier\n- pConfigStruct (stack[4]): Pointer to config structure containing offsets 0xf8, 0xfc\n- nResourceId (stack[8]): Resource identifier for lookup\n\nReturns:\n- int: Formatted string value + 1 if valid ID, else formatted value + 0\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If Ordinal_11033 returns 0, skips localization (no string appends)\n- Localization config stored at global g_szLocalizationConfig\n- Uses hardcoded magic numbers: 0x10eb, 0x10b3, 0xf9e for resource IDs\n\nStructure Layout:\n| Offset | Size | Field Name | Type | Description |\n|--------|------|-----------|------|-------------|\n| 0xf8   | 4    | field_f8  | dword| Config data 1 |\n| 0xfc   | 4    | field_fc  | dword| Config data 2 |\n\nRelated Functions:\n- Ordinal_11033() - Localization data lookup\n- FormatAndAppendStringValue() - Final formatting pipeline\n- toUnicode() - ANSI-to-Unicode conversion",
