      "comment": "Format monster combat statistics (Attack Rating, Defense, Damage) for display.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get monster's scaled Attack Rating via GetMonsterLevelScaledValue(nMonsterIndex, nMonsterLevel)\n2. Initialize 64-wchar Unicode buffer awUnicodeTemp using default constructors\n3. If Attack Rating != 0:\n   a. Select format string: \"+%d\" for positive values, \"%d\" for negative\n   b. Format value to ANSI buffer via wsprintfA\n   c. Convert to Unicode via toUnicode()\n   d. Validate and append string ID 0x10e3 (Attack Rating label)\n   e. Append formatted value twice (stat name + value)\n   f. Append string ID 0x10b3 (separator/units)\n   g. Append string ID 0xf9e (newline/terminator)\n   h. Set nFormattedSections = 1\n4. Get monster's scaled Defense via GetMonsterLevelScaledValue (second call)\n5. Reinitialize Unicode buffer\n6. If Defense != 0: format and append with string ID 0x10e5 (Defense label)\n7. Accumulate formatted section count\n8. Get monster's scaled Damage via GetMonsterScaledDamage(nMonsterLevel, nMonsterIndex)\n9. If Damage != 0: format and append with string ID 0x10f7 (Damage label)\n10. Get skill ID via GetMonsterSkillId and format via FormatAndAppendStringValue\n11. Return total count of formatted stat sections\n\nParameters:\npOutputBuffer (Unicode *, ECX): Output buffer for formatted Unicode strings (IMPLICIT - not used directly)\nnMonsterIndex (int, EDX): Monster type/class index in data tables\nnUnused (int, Stack[0x4]): Unused parameter (legacy or reserved)\nnMonsterLevel (int, Stack[0x8]): Monster level for stat scaling calculations\nIMPLICIT ESI (unaff_ESI): Source string pointer for Unicode::strcat operations\nIMPLICIT EDI (unaff_EDI): Destination string pointer for Unicode::strcat operations\n\nReturns:\nint: Total count of successfully formatted stat sections (0-4, counting Attack Rating, Defense, Damage, Skill)\n\nString ID Reference:\n0x10e3 - Monster Attack Rating label\n0x10e5 - Monster Defense label  \n0x10f7 - Monster Damage label\n0x10b3 - Stat separator/units\n0xf9e  - Line terminator/newline\n\nFormat String Selection:\ng_szResourceFormatPlus (0x6fbc6358): \"+%d\" - positive stat bonus display\ng_szLocalizationConfig (0x6fbb0de4): \"%d\" - negative/neutral stat display\n\nCompiler Notes:\n- iVar1: Reused for Attack Rating, Defense values, and accumulated count\n- iVar3: Loop counter in init loops, then reused for Damage value\n- pUVar4: Iterator pointer for Unicode array initialization\n- pCVar5: Format string pointer selected based on sign\n- iStack_64: Formatted sections counter (accumulates)\n- iStack_68: Array initialization loop counter\n- aCStack_60: 32-byte ANSI buffer for wsprintfA formatting\n- local_40: 64-wchar Unicode buffer for stat value conversion\n- unaff_ESI, unaff_EDI: Preserved caller registers for string concatenation",
      "tags": ["PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_4", "STRUCT_Room1", "PROP_LOOPHEAVY", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
