      "comment": "Formats monster damage statistics with Holy Freeze/Shock aura bonuses for UI display.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize 64-element Unicode buffer array\n2. Get base damage from GetMonsterMaxDamage(nSkillRowId, nAreaLevel)\n3. Calculate damage range from MonsterRecord offsets +0x144 (min) and +0x148 (max) plus base\n4. Scale damage by shift amount from MonsterRecord offset +0x128, then divide by 256\n5. Override minimum damage to 1 for specific skill types (0x14, 0x31, 0x35)\n6. Check if player has Holy Freeze aura (state 0x47) and appropriate damage type (+0xD4 == 1)\n   - If so, apply Cold Mastery skill (0x3D) bonus percentage to damage range\n7. Check if player has Holy Shock aura (state 0x48) and appropriate damage type (+0xD4 == 2)\n   - If so, apply Lightning Mastery skill (0x3F) bonus percentage to damage range\n8. Call FormatLocalizationString to output damage range with element type (+0x140)\n9. Get level-scaled value and format as \"1-%d\" level string\n10. Concatenate localized strings for UI labels (string IDs: 0x10A3, 0x2744, 0xF9E)\n11. Append skill ID value using string ID 0x10AE\n\nParameters:\n  pOutputBuffer (ECX): Output Unicode buffer for formatted damage string\n  nSkillRowId (EDX): Skill row ID (20=specific damage type, 49/53=override min to 1)\n  pMonsterRecord (Stack+4): Pointer to monster record structure\n  nAreaLevel (Stack+8): Area level for damage scaling\n\nReturns:\n  Always returns 1 (EAX = 1)\n\nMonsterRecord Structure Offsets:\n  +0x0D4 (1 byte): Damage element type (1=cold, 2=lightning)\n  +0x128 (1 byte): Damage shift amount\n  +0x140 (1 byte): Element type for display\n  +0x144 (4 bytes): Minimum damage modifier\n  +0x148 (4 bytes): Maximum damage modifier\n\nState Flags:\n  0x47: Holy Freeze aura active\n  0x48: Holy Shock aura active\n\nSkill IDs:\n  0x3D (61): Cold Mastery\n  0x3F (63): Lightning Mastery\n\nString IDs:\n  0x10A3 (4259): UI label separator\n  0x2744 (10052): Level label\n  0xF9E (3998): Stat label\n  0x10AE (4270): Skill value format",
      "tags": ["PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_4", "STRUCT_Room1", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
