      "api_calls": ["GetMonsterMaxDamage", "GetUnitStateFlag", "GetUnitSkillById", "GetSkillLevel", "GetMonsterSkillId", "GetUnitStateFlag", "GetUnitSkillById", "GetSkillLevel", "GetMonsterSkillId", "GetMissileTemplateRecord", "...+1 more"],
      "instructions": ["0x748C0|SUB|ESP, 0x8", "0x748C3|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [ESP + 0x14]", "0x748C7|PUSH|EBX", "0x748C8|MOV|EBX, dword ptr [ESP + 0x10]", "0x748CC|PUSH|EBP", "0x748CD|PUSH|ESI", "0x748CE|MOV|ESI, dword ptr [ESP + 0x1c]", "0x748D2|PUSH|EDI", "0x748D3|PUSH|EAX", "0x748D4|MOV|EBP, EDX", "0x748D6|PUSH|ESI", "0x748D7|PUSH|EBX", "0x748D8|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x20], EBP", "0x748DC|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x1c], ECX", "0x748E0|CALL|0x6fb38bf0"],
      "comment": "Formats damage display string with difficulty modifiers applied.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Format base damage/defense string using FormatLocalizationString\n2. Get base value modifier from difficulty ID and minimum damage via Ordinal_11045\n3. Add modifier to item node fields at offsets 0x144 and 0x148\n4. If any offset has non-zero value, apply bit-shift scaling using byte at offset 0x128\n5. Check difficulty ID for special cases (0x14, 0x31, 0x35) - set scaled min to 1\n6. Get state configuration via FUN_6fb62880\n7. For first modifier (0x47): If enabled and item node passes validation (offset 0xd4 == 0x01):\n   - Get area ID via Ordinal_10949(0xffffffff)\n   - Get file handle via Ordinal_10968\n   - Look up modifier value via Ordinal_10996(0x3d, ...)\n   - Apply percentage increase to scaled min/max: value += (modifier * value) / 100\n8. For second modifier (0x48): If enabled and item node passes validation (offset 0xd4 == 0x02):\n   - Repeat modifier lookup and percentage calculation with Ordinal_10996(0x3f, ...)\n9. If any modification applied, format final string with scaled values\n10. Get base stat table via Ordinal_10589(0xea)\n11. Get parameter offset from stat table via Ordinal_11220(0xea, nMinDamage)\n12. Load table fields at offsets 0xac and 0xb0, add offset from step 11\n13. If difficulty ID between 0x22 and 0x23 inclusive, set scaled value to 1, otherwise apply bit-shift at offset 0x8c\n14. Format final defense string with scaled value and base table at offset 0xa8\n15. Return 1 (success)\n\nParameters:\npBuffer (void *) - IMPLICIT ECX - Destination buffer for formatted string\nnDifficultyId (dword) - IMPLICIT EDX - Difficulty/mode identifier (checked against 0x14, 0x31, 0x35)\npItemNode (void *) - Stack - Item/equipment node structure with offsets: 0x128 (shift), 0x140 (color), 0x144 (field1), 0x148 (field2), 0xd4 (validation flags)\nnMinDamage (dword) - Stack - Minimum damage value (used with Ordinal_11045)\nnMaxDamage (dword) - Stack - Maximum damage value (used as offset parameter)\n\nReturns:\n1 (success/complete)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If nDifficultyId is 0x14, 0x31, or 0x35: scaled minimum forced to 1\n- If pItemNode is NULL: modifier validation skipped (only nDifficultyId check performed)\n- If stat field at offset 0xac or 0xb0 is zero and offset is zero: no final formatting\n- Modifiers 0x47 and 0x48 use 0x01 and 0x02 validation flags respectively\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x128 - Bit shift amount stored as byte (shift count for scaling)\n0x140 - Color/appearance field (low byte extracted as uint)\n0x144 - First damage modifier field\n0x148 - Second damage modifier field\n0x8c - Bit shift amount for stat table (byte, masked 0x1f)\n0xac - Base stat table field 1 offset\n0xb0 - Base stat table field 2 offset\n0xa8 - Color/format field in stat table\n0xd4 - Validation flags (0x01, 0x02)\n0x47 - First modifier type ID\n0x48 - Second modifier type ID\n0x3d - First modifier lookup key\n0x3f - Second modifier lookup key\n0x22, 0x23 - Difficulty ID range for forced scaling (inclusive)\n0xffffffff - Special marker for Ordinal_10949 (current area ID)\n0x10f9 - Format string ID for defense stat\n\nRelated Ordinals:\n- Ordinal_11045 - Get base modifier value from difficulty/damage parameters\n- Ordinal_10949 - Get area/map ID (0xffffffff = current)\n- Ordinal_10968 - Get file handle for resource with modifier flag\n- Ordinal_10996 - Look up modifier percentage value\n- Ordinal_10487 - Check modifier enabled state\n- Ordinal_10589 - Get base stat table\n- Ordinal_11220 - Get offset within stat table\n\nRelated Functions:\n- FormatLocalizationString - Format damage/defense display strings",
      "tags": ["PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_5", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
