      "comment": "Formats monster stat modifier strings for display in the UI.\n\nBuilds localized text showing monster life bonus, damage reduction, and skill information\nbased on area level scaling. The function concatenates multiple string components from\nthe localization table to form complete stat descriptions.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get monster level-scaled life bonus value via GetMonsterLevelScaledValue\n2. Initialize 64-character Unicode buffer (loop 32 iterations, 2 bytes per char)\n3. If life bonus is non-zero:\n   a. Format integer as ANSI string using \"%d\" format\n   b. Convert ANSI to Unicode\n   c. Append string 0x571b (life bonus label)\n   d. Append formatted value\n   e. Append string 0x10b3 (delimiter/suffix)\n   f. Append string 0x0f9e (percentage or unit marker)\n4. Calculate damage reduction from MonsterData offsets +0x100 and +0x104\n5. Reinitialize Unicode buffer\n6. If damage reduction is non-zero (negated value):\n   a. Format negated integer as ANSI string\n   b. Convert ANSI to Unicode\n   c. Append string 0x10b1 (damage reduction label)\n   d. Append formatted value\n   e. Append string 0x10b3 (delimiter/suffix)\n   f. Append string 0x0f9e (percentage marker)\n7. Get monster skill ID via GetMonsterSkillId\n8. Format and append skill string value via FormatAndAppendStringValue\n9. Return 1 (success)\n\nParameters:\n  pOutputString (ECX, void*): Target Unicode string buffer to append formatted text\n  nMonsterId (EDX, int): Monster identifier for stat lookup\n  pMonsterData (Stack+0x4, void*): Pointer to monster data structure\n    - Offset +0x100: Damage reduction min value\n    - Offset +0x104: Damage reduction max value\n  nAreaLevel (Stack+0x8, int): Current area level for scaling calculations\n\nReturns:\n  int: Always returns 1 indicating success\n\nString IDs Referenced:\n  0x571b - Monster life bonus label\n  0x10b1 - Damage reduction label\n  0x10b3 - Stat delimiter/suffix\n  0x0f9e - Percentage/unit marker\n  0x10ae - Skill description (via FormatAndAppendStringValue)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Life bonus of 0 skips life bonus string formatting entirely\n  - Damage reduction of 0 skips damage reduction formatting entirely\n  - Values are negated for display (showing reduction as positive number)\n\nClassification: Worker function - formats monster stat text for UI display",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_4", "STRUCT_Room1", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
    },
