      "comment": "Formats stat bonus tooltip text showing level-scaled base value and per-level bonus.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize 256-char Unicode buffer for output text\n2. Calculate scaled stat value: CalculateScaledValue(nLevel, 0, 0x19)\n3. Get base stat string (StringId 0x5510) and format with scaled value\n4. Append localized separator (StringId 0xf9e)\n5. Calculate stat bonus: GetStatCostByLevel(nLevel, nStatGroupId, 1)\n6. If bonus non-zero:\n   a. Format with \"+%d\" (positive) or \"%d\" (negative)\n   b. Convert to Unicode\n   c. Append \"stat bonus\" label (StringId 0x10b2)\n   d. Append formatted bonus value (StringId 0x10b3)\n   e. Append separator (StringId 0xf9e)\n7. Calculate base stat cost: GetStatCostByLevel(nLevel, pOutputBuffer, 0)\n8. If base cost non-zero:\n   a. Format with \"+%d\" (positive) or \"%d\" (negative)\n   b. Convert to Unicode\n   c. Append \"stat cost\" label (StringId 0x10a0)\n   d. Append formatted cost value (StringId 0x10b3)\n   e. Append separator (StringId 0xf9e)\n9. Return 1\n\nParameters:\n  nUnused (ECX) - Unused parameter\n  pOutputBuffer (EDX) - Unicode * - Output buffer for tooltip text\n  nStatGroupId (Stack+4) - int - Stat group identifier\n  nLevel (Stack+8) - int - Character/skill level for scaling\n\nReturns:\n  int - Always returns 1 (success)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x5510 - Base stat description string ID\n  0xf9e  - Newline/separator string ID\n  0x10b2 - \"Bonus per level\" label string ID\n  0x10b3 - Numeric value placeholder string ID\n  0x10a0 - \"Base stat cost\" label string ID\n  0x19   - Max scaling value (25)\n  0x80   - Unicode buffer size (128 chars)\n  0x20   - Temp buffer size (32 chars)\n\nStack Layout:\n  [ESP+0x78] - Unicode[128] aLocalBuffer - Main output text buffer\n  [ESP+0x38] - Unicode[32] aTempBuffer - Temp buffer for bonus formatting\n  [ESP+0x18] - char[32] aCFormatBuffer - ANSI format buffer for wsprintf",
