      "comment": "Format bonus stat string with optional scaled value suffix.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call FormatLocalizationString to format base localized string with parameters\n2. Calculate scaled value from nCharLevel and config offsets 0xf0/0xf4\n3. Initialize 64-element Unicode buffer (loop 32 iterations, 2 bytes each)\n4. If scaled value is 0, return base format result\n5. Format scaled value as ANSI string using \"%d\" format\n6. Convert ANSI to Unicode buffer (max 32 chars)\n7. Append formatted value to output via strcat (unaff_EDI target)\n8. Validate and append string ID 0x10b4 (bonus label)\n9. Validate and append string ID 0xf9e (suffix/unit)\n10. Return base result + 1 to indicate additional content added\n\nParameters:\n- dwStringIndex (ECX): Resource string index for localization lookup\n- nFormatMode (EDX): Format mode selector passed to FormatLocalizationString\n- pStatConfig (Stack+0x4): Pointer to stat config structure\n  +0xf0: nMinValue for scaling calculation\n  +0xf4: nMaxValue for scaling calculation\n- nCharLevel (Stack+0x8): Character level for value scaling\n- nAltParam (Stack+0xc): Alternate parameter for FormatLocalizationString\n- IMPLICIT unaff_EDI: Destination Unicode string buffer\n- IMPLICIT unaff_ESI: Source Unicode string for strcat operations\n\nReturns:\n- dwFormatResult: Result from FormatLocalizationString if nScaledValue == 0\n- dwFormatResult + 1: If scaled value appended (indicates extra content)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Zero scaled value: Early return with just base format result\n- Non-zero scaled value: Appends formatted number plus two string IDs\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x20 (32): Loop iterations for Unicode buffer init (64 bytes / 2)\n- 0x10b4: String ID for bonus label text\n- 0xf9e: String ID for suffix/unit text\n- 0xf0, 0xf4: Config structure offsets for min/max values",
