      "comment": "Format and display a localized monster stat value scaled by level.\n\nClassification: Worker function - orchestrates three localization calls.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call FormatLocalizationString with all parameters to set up localization context\n2. Call GetMonsterLevelScaledStat(nLevel, nMonsterId) to calculate the stat scaled by monster level\n3. Call FormatAndAppendStringValue with scaled stat and string resource ID 0x10ae\n4. Return 1 (success)\n\nParameters:\n- dwStringIndex (dword, ECX): String resource index for localization formatting\n- nMonsterId (int, EDX): Monster identifier for stat lookup\n- pConfig (void*, Stack+0x4): Pointer to configuration structure with offsets 0xdc, 0xe0, 0xe4\n- nLevel (int, Stack+0x8): Monster level for stat scaling calculation\n- nParam5 (int, Stack+0xc): Additional format parameter passed to FormatLocalizationString\n\nReturns:\n- 1: Always returns success\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x10ae: String resource ID passed to FormatAndAppendStringValue (MOV EDX, 0x10ae at 6fb45524)\n\nCallee Functions:\n- FormatLocalizationString: Sets up Unicode localization string buffer\n- GetMonsterLevelScaledStat: Calculates level-scaled stat value\n- FormatAndAppendStringValue: Formats numeric value and appends to output",
