      "comment": "Format localization string with optional monster level stat appended.\n\nWrapper function that extends FormatLocalizationString by appending monster\nlevel statistics when the monster has a level stat value.\n\nClassification: Wrapper function\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call FormatLocalizationString with all 5 parameters to get base result\n2. Call GetMonsterLevelStat(nMonsterIndex, nMonsterLevel) to get level stat\n3. Initialize Unicode buffer (64 elements) via constructor loop (32 iterations, 2 bytes each)\n4. If nMonsterLevelStat == 0, return base result unchanged\n5. Format monster level stat as ANSI string using wsprintfA with \"%d\" format\n6. Convert ANSI buffer to Unicode via toUnicode\n7. ValidateStringId(0x10a6) - validate first string resource\n8. Append string via strcat (2 calls)\n9. ValidateStringId(0x10b3) - validate second string resource  \n10. Append string via strcat\n11. ValidateStringId(0xf9e) - validate third string resource\n12. Append string via strcat\n13. Return base result + 1\n\nParameters:\n- dwIndex (ECX): Localization string index/selector\n- nMonsterIndex (EDX): Monster type/index for stat lookup\n- nParam3 (Stack+0x4): Configuration structure pointer\n- nMonsterLevel (Stack+0x8): Monster level for stat calculation\n- nParam5 (Stack+0xc): Additional format parameter\n\nReturns:\n- dwBaseResult: Original FormatLocalizationString result if no monster stat\n- dwBaseResult + 1: If monster level stat was appended\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x20 (32): Loop iterations for Unicode buffer initialization\n- 0x10a6: String resource ID for first append\n- 0x10b3: String resource ID for second append\n- 0xf9e: String resource ID for third append\n\nCallees:\n- FormatLocalizationString: Base localization formatting\n- GetMonsterLevelStat: Retrieve monster stat by index and level\n- wsprintfA: Format integer to ANSI string\n- Unicode::toUnicode: Convert ANSI to Unicode\n- ValidateStringId: Validate string resource existence\n- Unicode::strcat: Ap