      "comment": "Formats monster skill and level-scaled stats for tooltip display.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call FormatLocalizationString to initialize base localization formatting\n2. Get monster skill ID via GetMonsterSkillId(nMonsterId, nSkillSlot)\n3. Initialize 64-element Unicode buffer (128 bytes) using default constructors\n4. If skill ID is non-zero:\n   a. Format skill ID as decimal string using g_szFmtDecimal (\"%d\")\n   b. Convert ANSI string to Unicode\n   c. Validate and append string ID 0x10D7 (skill prefix)\n   d. Call strcat twice (append formatted value)\n   e. Validate and append string ID 0x10B3 (separator)\n   f. Validate and append string ID 0x0F9E (skill suffix)\n   g. Increment count\n5. Get level-scaled value via GetMonsterLevelScaledValue(nMonsterId, nSkillSlot)\n6. Re-initialize Unicode buffer\n7. If level-scaled value is non-zero:\n   a. Format value as decimal string\n   b. Convert to Unicode\n   c. Validate and append string ID 0x10C2 (level prefix)\n   d. Call strcat twice (append formatted value)\n   e. Validate and append string ID 0x10B3 (separator)\n   f. Validate and append string ID 0x0F9E (level suffix)\n   g. Increment count and return\n\nParameters:\n- pOutput (ECX): Output Unicode string buffer pointer\n- nMonsterId (EDX): Monster type/record identifier\n- nParam3 (Stack+0x4): Configuration or mode parameter\n- nSkillSlot (Stack+0x8): Monster skill slot index\n- nMonsterLevel (Stack+0xC): Monster level for scaling calculation\n\nReturns:\n- Number of stats formatted (0, 1, or 2)\n- 0 if no skill and no level-scaled value\n- 1 if either skill or level-scaled value formatted\n- 2 if both skill and level-scaled value formatted\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x20 (32): Loop count for Unicode buffer initialization (64 chars / 2)\n- 0x10D7: String ID for skill stat prefix\n- 0x10C2: String ID for level-scaled stat prefix\n- 0x10B3: String ID for separator/delimiter\n- 0x0F9E: String ID for stat suffix\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If skill ID is 0, skill formatting is skipped\n- If level-scaled value is 0, level formatting is skipped\n- unaff_ESI and unaff_EDI are implicit string parameters from caller context",
