      "comment": "Build monster skill level bonus tooltip string by combining localization, resource, and skill data.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call FormatLocalizationString with all parameters to get base localization result\n2. Initialize suffix type to 0 (standard format)\n3. Call GetMonsterLevelScaledValue(nMonsterId, nLevel) to get scaled level value\n4. Call FormatResourceString with scaled value and suffix type 0 to format resource portion\n5. Call GetMonsterSkillId(nMonsterId, nSkillSlot) to retrieve skill ID for this monster/slot\n6. Initialize Unicode buffer (64 elements) via 32-iteration constructor loop\n7. If skill ID is 0 (no skill): return sum of localization + resource results (early exit)\n8. If skill ID < 0: use negative format string (g_szLocalizationConfig = \"%d\")\n9. Else (skill ID > 0): use positive format string (g_szResourceFormatPlus = \"+%d\")\n10. Format skill ID into ANSI temp buffer using wsprintfA\n11. Convert ANSI to Unicode via toUnicode into local_40 buffer\n12. ValidateStringId(0x10b1) - validate skill prefix string\n13. Append strings via strcat (twice)\n14. ValidateStringId(0x10b3) - validate skill suffix string  \n15. Append string via strcat\n16. ValidateStringId(0xf9e) - validate separator string\n17. Append final string via strcat\n18. Return localization + resource + 1 (success with skill component)\n\nParameters:\n- dwStringIndex (dword, ECX): String table index for localization lookup\n- nMonsterId (int, EDX): Monster type identifier for stat lookups\n- nSkillSlot (int, Stack+0x4): Skill slot index on monster\n- nLevel (int, Stack+0x8): Monster level for scaled value calculation\n- nParam5 (int, Stack+0xc): Additional parameter passed to FormatLocalizationString\n\nReturns:\n- Sum of component results if no skill (dwLocalizationResult + dwResourceResult)\n- Sum + 1 if skill component was appended (indicates skill info added)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Skill ID 0: No skill bonus - returns early without skill formatting\n- Skill ID < 0: Uses negative format without plus sign\n- Skill ID > 0: Uses positive format with plus sign prefix\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x20 (32): Loop counter for Unicode buffer initialization (64 bytes / 2)\n- 0x10b1: String ID for skill prefix text\n- 0x10b3: String ID for skill suffix text\n- 0xf9e: String ID for separator/delimiter text\n\nImplicit Parameters:\n- unaff_ESI: Source string pointer for strcat operations\n- unaff_EDI: Destination buffer pointer for strcat operations",
