      "comment": "FormatMonsterSkillAndLevelTooltip - Formats monster skill and level bonus information for tooltip display\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call FormatLocalizationString with all parameters to initialize base tooltip text\n2. Get monster skill ID via GetMonsterSkillId(nMonsterDataId, nLevelMode)\n3. Cap skill ID at 250 (0xfa) maximum\n4. Format resource string with skill ID using string ID 0x10b0\n5. Get monster level stat via GetMonsterLevelStat(nMonsterDataId, nLevelMode)\n6. Initialize 32-element Unicode buffer array (64 bytes) with default constructors\n7. If level stat is non-zero:\n   a. Select format string: \"+%d\" if nLevelMode != 0 AND level >= 0, else \"%d\"\n   b. Format level stat value to ANSI string buffer\n   c. Convert ANSI to Unicode\n   d. Append localized strings: 0x10b2 (open bracket), level value, 0x10b3 (close bracket), 0xf9e (suffix)\n\nParameters:\n  pDestBuffer (ECX) - Destination Unicode buffer pointer for formatted tooltip text\n  nMonsterDataId (EDX) - Monster data identifier for stat lookups\n  nSkillParam (Stack+0x4) - Skill parameter passed to FormatLocalizationString\n  nLevelMode (Stack+0x8) - Level mode: 0 = use plain format, non-zero = use plus format for positive values\n  nUnused (Stack+0xc) - Unused parameter passed through to FormatLocalizationString\n\nReturns:\n  int - Always returns 1 (success)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Skill ID capped at 250 to prevent out-of-bounds access\n  - Level stat of 0 skips all level bonus formatting\n  - Negative level values always use plain \"%d\" format regardless of nLevelMode\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0xfa (250) - Maximum skill ID value\n  0x10b0 - String ID for skill resource formatting\n  0x10b2 - String ID for opening bracket/prefix\n  0x10b3 - String ID for closing bracket/suffix\n  0xf9e - String ID for final suffix text\n  0x20 (32) - Unicode buffer element count\n\nCallees:\n  FormatLocalizationString - Initializes base localization text\n  GetMonsterSkillId - Retrieves skill ID for monster\n  FormatResourceString - Formats skill resource string\n  GetMonsterLevelStat - Retrieves level stat bonus\n  Unicode::_default_constructor_closure_ - Initializes Unicode elements\n  wsprintfA - Formats integer to ANSI string\n  Unicode::toUnicode - Converts ANSI to Unicode\n  ValidateStringId - Validates and retrieves localized string\n  Unicode::strcat - Concatenates Unicode strings",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Inventory", "PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_5", "STRUCT_Room1", "STRUCT_ItemData", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control"]
