      "comment": "Appends monster skill bonus text to Unicode destination buffer.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get monster skill ID for specified monster and skill slot via GetMonsterSkillId\n2. Initialize 64-element Unicode buffer (32 iterations, 2 bytes each)\n3. If skill ID is 0 (invalid/no skill), return 0 (failure)\n4. Format skill ID as string:\n   - Negative skill ID: use \"%d\" format (g_szLocalizationConfig at 0x6fbb0de4)\n   - Positive skill ID: use \"+%d\" format (g_szResourceFormatPlus at 0x6fbc6358)\n5. Convert ANSI skill ID string to Unicode via toUnicode (max 32 chars)\n6. ValidateStringId(0x10e5) - Get skill bonus prefix string\n7. Concatenate prefix to destination buffer (EDI)\n8. Concatenate converted skill ID Unicode string\n9. ValidateStringId(0x10b3) - Get skill bonus suffix string\n10. Concatenate suffix to destination buffer\n11. ValidateStringId(0xf9e) - Get delimiter/separator string\n12. Concatenate separator to destination buffer\n13. Return 1 (success)\n\nParameters:\n- pDestBuffer (Unicode *): ECX - Destination buffer for formatted text\n- nMonsterId (int): EDX - Monster type ID for skill lookup\n- pSourceText (Unicode *): Stack+0x4 - IMPLICIT: passed via EDI/ESI for strcat\n- nSkillSlot (int): Stack+0x8 - Skill slot index to query\n\nReturns:\n- 0: Skill ID was 0 (no skill for this slot)\n- 1: Successfully appended skill bonus text\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Negative skill IDs formatted without plus sign\n- Positive skill IDs formatted with leading plus sign\n- unaff_EDI and unaff_ESI are implicit register parameters from caller\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x20 (32): Loop iterations for Unicode buffer init (64 bytes / 2)\n- 0x10e5: String table ID for skill bonus prefix\n- 0x10b3: String table ID for skill bonus suffix  \n- 0xf9e: String table ID for separator/delimiter\n\nCalled By:\n- Data reference at 0x6fbc5d80 (function pointer table)",
