      "comment": "Append monster level-scaled stat value to a localized string.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call FormatLocalizationString with all parameters to format base string\n2. Call GetMonsterLevelScaledStat(nParam4, nParam2) to get scaled stat value\n3. Initialize 64-element Unicode buffer (32 iterations, 2 bytes each)\n4. If scaled stat value is non-zero:\n   a. Format stat value as decimal string using wsprintfA with g_szLocalizationConfig (\"%d\")\n   b. Convert ANSI string to Unicode via toUnicode\n   c. Concatenate Unicode buffer to output string\n   d. Append string ID 0x10b4 (likely separator/prefix)\n   e. Concatenate again\n   f. Append string ID 0xf9e (likely suffix/formatting)\n   g. Final concatenation\n5. Return (always returns 1 via EAX at function end)\n\nParameters:\n- nIndex (dword, ECX): Resource or string index for localization lookup\n- nParam2 (int, EDX): Monster ID or stat type selector, passed to GetMonsterLevelScaledStat\n- nParam3 (int, Stack+0x4): Configuration structure pointer for FormatLocalizationString\n- nParam4 (int, Stack+0x8): Monster level, passed to GetMonsterLevelScaledStat\n- nParam5 (int, Stack+0xc): Alternate format parameter for FormatLocalizationString\n- IMPLICIT unaff_ESI: Source Unicode string for strcat operations\n- IMPLICIT unaff_EDI: Destination Unicode string for strcat operations\n\nReturns:\n- Always returns 1 (success) via MOV EAX, 1 before RET\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If GetMonsterLevelScaledStat returns 0, stat formatting is skipped entirely\n- Function relies on caller setting ESI/EDI for Unicode concatenation\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x20 (32): Loop iteration count for Unicode buffer initialization\n- 0x10b4: String ID for separator/prefix localization\n- 0xf9e: String ID for suffix/formatting localization\n- 0xc: Stack cleanup for 3 stack parameters (RET 0xc)",
