      "comment": "Appends monster level-based stat bonuses to tooltip text output.\n\nFormats both the base level stat and scaled stat value bonuses for monster tooltips.\nUses localized format strings to properly display positive (+%d) or negative (%d) values.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call FormatLocalizationString to initialize base formatting\n2. Get monster level stat via GetMonsterLevelStat(nMonsterIndex, nMonsterLevel)\n3. Initialize 64-element Unicode buffer (awUnicodeBuffer) via constructor loop\n4. If level stat is non-zero:\n   a. Select format string: \"+%d\" (g_szResourceFormatPlus) if positive, \"%d\" (g_szLocalizationConfig) if negative\n   b. Format stat value to ANSI string via wsprintfA\n   c. Convert ANSI to Unicode via toUnicode\n   d. Append string ID 0x10B2 label to output\n   e. Append formatted value to output\n   f. Append string ID 0x10B3 separator\n   g. Append string ID 0x0F9E suffix\n5. Get scaled value via GetMonsterLevelScaledValue(nMonsterIndex, nMonsterLevel)\n6. Re-initialize Unicode buffer (same loop as step 3)\n7. If scaled value is non-zero:\n   a. Select format string based on sign (same as step 4a)\n   b. Format and convert to Unicode (same as steps 4b-4c)\n   c. Append string ID 0x10A0 label (scaled value label)\n   d. Append formatted value\n   e. Append string ID 0x10B3 separator\n   f. Append string ID 0x0F9E suffix\n8. Return 1 (success)\n\nParameters:\n  pOutputBuffer (ECX) - Unicode buffer to append formatted text to\n  nMonsterIndex (EDX) - Monster type index for stat lookup\n  nStatId (Stack+0x04) - Stat identifier\n  nMonsterLevel (Stack+0x08) - Monster level for stat scaling\n  nDifficulty (Stack+0x0C) - Game difficulty level\n\nReturns:\n  int - Always returns 1 (success)\n\nString IDs:\n  0x10B2 - Level stat label\n  0x10B3 - Stat separator/delimiter\n  0x0F9E - Stat suffix/terminator\n  0x10A0 - Scaled value label\n\nGlobals:\n  g_szResourceFormatPlus (0x6FBC6358) - \"+%d\" format for positive values\n  g_szLocalizationConfig (0x6FBB0DE4) - \"%d\" format for negative values",
