      "comment": "Format monster stat bonus strings for tooltip display.\n\nBuilds localized Unicode strings for monster skill ID, level stat, and level-scaled values.\nEach non-zero stat appends formatted text with sign prefix and string IDs.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call FormatLocalizationString to format base localization text\n2. Get monster skill ID via GetMonsterSkillId(nMonsterId, nSkillSlot)\n3. Initialize 64-element Unicode buffer (128 bytes)\n4. If skill ID non-zero:\n   a. Format with \"+%d\" (positive) or \"%d\" (negative) into ANSI buffer\n   b. Convert ANSI to Unicode via toUnicode\n   c. Append string IDs 0x10a0, 0x10b3, 0xf9e via strcat\n   d. Set result flag to 1\n5. Get monster level stat via GetMonsterLevelStat(nMonsterId, nSkillSlot)\n6. Re-initialize Unicode buffer\n7. If level stat non-zero:\n   a. Format with sign prefix into ANSI buffer\n   b. Convert to Unicode\n   c. Append string IDs 0x10b2, 0x10b3, 0xf9e\n   d. Set result flag to 1\n8. Accumulate total: localization result + skill result + stat result\n9. Get scaled value via GetMonsterLevelScaledValue(nMonsterId, nSkillSlot)\n10. Re-initialize Unicode buffer\n11. If scaled value non-zero:\n    a. Format with sign prefix\n    b. Convert to Unicode\n    c. Append string IDs 0x10b1, 0x10b3, 0xf9e\n    d. Increment total by 1\n12. Return total count of formatted stat strings\n\nParameters:\n- dwIndex (uint, ECX): Resource or string index passed to FormatLocalizationString\n- nMonsterId (int, EDX): Monster identifier for stat lookups\n- nParam3 (int, Stack+0x4): Additional parameter passed to FormatLocalizationString\n- nSkillSlot (int, Stack+0x8): Skill slot index for monster stat queries\n- nParam5 (int, Stack+0xc): Additional parameter passed to FormatLocalizationString\n- IMPLICIT unaff_ESI: Source string pointer for strcat operations\n- IMPLICIT unaff_EDI: Destination string pointer for strcat operations\n\nReturns:\n- int: Count of stat strings formatted (0-4), sum of base + skill + stat + scaled contributions\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x20 (32): Loop counter for Unicode buffer initialization (64 elements * 2 bytes)\n- 0x10a0: String ID for skill bonus label\n- 0x10b1: String ID for scaled value label\n- 0x10b2: String ID for level stat label\n- 0x10b3: String ID for separator/delimiter\n- 0xf9e: String ID for newline/terminator\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Zero stat values skip formatting entirely (no string appended)\n- Negative values use \"%d\" format, positive use \"+%d\" format\n- Unicode buffer re-initialized before each stat section",
