      "comment": "Formats monster skill ID into tooltip string with localization.\n\nRetrieves the skill ID for a monster's skill slot and formats it as a tooltip \nstring with positive (+N) or negative (N) notation. Appends two localization \nstrings (0x10b3 and 0xf9e) to complete the tooltip.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get monster skill ID from GetMonsterSkillId(nMonsterId, nParam4)\n2. Initialize 32-element Unicode buffer (64 bytes) with default constructors\n3. If skill ID is 0, return 0 (no skill)\n4. Select format string: g_szFmtPositiveSkillId (\"+%d\") for positive IDs, \n   g_szFmtSkillId (\"%d\") for negative IDs\n5. Format skill ID to ANSI string via wsprintfA\n6. Convert ANSI to Unicode via Unicode::toUnicode\n7. Concatenate skill ID Unicode to destination buffer\n8. Get localization string 0x10b3, concatenate to destination\n9. Get localization string 0xf9e, concatenate to destination\n10. Return 1 (success)\n\nParameters:\n  pDestBuffer (ECX): Unicode destination buffer for tooltip string\n  nMonsterId (EDX): Monster ID to look up skill for\n  nSkillSlot (Stack+4): Skill slot index (passed to GetMonsterSkillId)\n  nParam4 (Stack+8): Additional parameter passed to GetMonsterSkillId\n\nReturns:\n  int - 1 on success (skill found and formatted), 0 if no skill (ID was 0)\n\nGlobals:\n  g_szFmtPositiveSkillId (0x6fbc6358): \"+%d\" format string for positive skill IDs\n  g_szFmtSkillId (0x6fbb0de4): \"%d\" format string for negative skill IDs\n  0x6fba5c30: Unicode::_default_constructor_closure_\n  0x6fba5c34: Unicode::toUnicode\n  0x6fba5c40: Unicode::strcat\n  0x6fba6210: wsprintfA import\n\nString IDs:\n  0x10b3 (4275): Localization string appended after skill ID\n  0xf9e (3998): Localization string appended last",
