      "comment": "Formats monster stat tooltip strings with leveled stats and scaled values.\n\nClassification: Worker function - Called via function pointer to format monster stat displays\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call FormatLocalizationString with all 5 parameters to set base formatting\n2. Get monster leveled stat via GetMonsterLeveledStat(nMonsterIndex, nLevel)\n3. Initialize Unicode buffer (64 elements) with default constructors\n4. If leveled stat is non-zero:\n   a. Format stat value to ANSI string using wsprintfA with \"%d\" format\n   b. Convert ANSI to Unicode via toUnicode\n   c. Validate string ID 0x10a0 (leveled stat label)\n   d. Append formatted string via strcat (called twice)\n   e. Validate string ID 0x10b3 (separator)\n   f. Append separator\n   g. Validate string ID 0xf9e (terminator/suffix)\n   h. Append terminator\n5. Get monster level scaled value via GetMonsterLevelScaledValue(nMonsterIndex, nLevel)\n6. Re-initialize Unicode buffer for second stat\n7. If scaled value is non-zero:\n   a. Format value to ANSI string\n   b. Convert to Unicode\n   c. Validate string ID 0x10b1 (scaled stat label)\n   d. Append formatted string (twice)\n   e. Validate string ID 0x10b3 (separator)\n   f. Append separator\n   g. Validate string ID 0xf9e (terminator)\n   h. Append terminator\n8. Get monster skill ID via GetMonsterSkillId(nMonsterIndex, nLevel)\n9. Format skill resource string with nSuffixType=0\n10. Return (void)\n\nParameters:\n- dwStringIndex (dword, ECX): String table index for base localization\n- nMonsterIndex (int, EDX): Monster type/index for stat lookup\n- nParam3 (int, Stack+0x4): Additional parameter passed to FormatLocalizationString\n- nLevel (int, Stack+0x8): Monster level for scaled calculations\n- nLoopCounter (int, Stack+0xC): Loop iteration parameter (re-used as loop counter internally)\n- IMPLICIT unaff_ESI: Source string pointer for strcat operations\n- IMPLICIT unaff_EDI: Destination string pointer for strcat operations\n\nReturns: void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If GetMonsterLeveledStat returns 0, section 4 is skipped entirely\n- If GetMonsterLevelScaledValue returns 0, section 7 is skipped entirely\n- nParam5 is re-used as loop counter (0x20 iterations) for buffer initialization\n- strcat operations use implicit ESI/EDI registers from caller context\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x20 (32): Loop counter for Unicode buffer initialization (64 bytes / 2 bytes per Unicode)\n- 0x10a0: String ID for leveled stat label\n- 0x10b1: String ID for scaled value label\n- 0x10b3: String ID for separator between stat sections\n- 0xf9e: String ID for terminator/suffix\n- 0x10b0: String ID passed to FormatResourceString for skill formatting\n\nDecompiler Notes:\n- unaff_ESI/unaff_EDI appear as unaffected registers but are actually implicit\n  parameters set by the caller before invoking this function via pointer\n- The double strcat calls (lines 4d, 7d) appear redundant but may be\n  intentional for specific formatting requirements",
