      "comment": "Formats monster stat comparison text for UI display.\n\nCompares monster stats at specified level vs level 1, displaying experience,\ndamage, level stat modifier, and skill ID differences with +/- indicators.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call FormatLocalizationString with base parameters\n2. Get experience at nMonsterLevel and level 1, format difference with string 0x10B3\n3. Get scaled damage at nMonsterLevel and level 1, format difference with string 0x10B3\n4. Get monster level stat modifier via GetMonsterLevelStat\n5. If level stat != 0:\n   a. Initialize Unicode buffer (64 wchar_t) via default constructor loop\n   b. Format stat as \"+%d\" (positive) or \"%d\" (negative) using wsprintfA\n   c. Convert to Unicode via toUnicode\n   d. Concatenate strings: ValidateStringId(0x10B2) + stat + ValidateStringId(0x10B3) + ValidateStringId(0xF9E)\n6. Get monster skill ID via GetMonsterSkillId\n7. If skill ID != 0:\n   a. Initialize Unicode buffer (64 wchar_t)\n   b. Format skill ID as \"+%d\" or \"%d\"\n   c. Convert to Unicode\n   d. Concatenate strings: ValidateStringId(0x10A0) + skillId + ValidateStringId(0x10B3) + ValidateStringId(0xF9E)\n8. Return (implicit EAX = 1)\n\nParameters:\n  pOutputBuffer (ECX): Unicode* - Output buffer for formatted text\n  nMonsterClassId (EDX): int - Monster class/type identifier\n  nParam3 (Stack+0x4): int - Additional parameter passed to FormatLocalizationString\n  nMonsterLevel (Stack+0x8): int - Monster level for stat comparison\n  nUnused (Stack+0xC): int - Unused, repurposed as loop counter internally\n\nReturns:\n  void (but EAX = 1 on return)\n\nString IDs:\n  0x10B3 - Separator/formatting string (used between values)\n  0x10B2 - Level stat label\n  0x10A0 - Skill ID label\n  0x0F9E - Suffix/terminator string\n\nFormat Strings:\n  g_szFmtPositive (0x6FBC6358): \"+%d\" - For positive values\n  g_szFmtInteger (0x6FBB0DE4): \"%d\" - For negative/zero values\n\nLocals:\n  aCStack_60 [32]: char buffer for wsprintfA\n  local_40 