      "comment": "Initialize and format Unicode strings with parameter substitution for localization.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize Unicode output array (64 elements) using default constructors\n2. Check if nStartParam equals nEndParam:\n   a. If equal and nStartParam == 0: return 0 (no formatting needed)\n   b. If equal and nStartParam != 0: format single parameter into local_80\n3. If nStartParam != nEndParam: format range into local_40\n4. Select format string based on nFormatMode: 0x6fbc639c if set, 0x6fbb40a0 if clear\n5. Call strcat_exref to concatenate strings (repeated 3 times with ordinal separators)\n6. Call Ordinal_10004() between each concatenation (likely flush/sync operation)\n7. Return 1 on success\n\nParameters:\n- nStringId: string identifier/index for localization lookup\n- nStartParam: starting parameter index for formatting\n- nEndParam: ending parameter index for formatting range\n- nFormatMode: selects format template (0=template_A, non-zero=template_B)\n\nReturns:\n- 0 if nStartParam == nEndParam and nStartParam == 0 (no-op condition)\n- 1 on successful formatting and concatenation\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Function initializes both local_80 and local_40 arrays but only uses one based on parameter comparison\n- Ordinal_10004() called multiple times (Storm.dll import, likely cache invalidation/flush)\n- unaff_ESI/unaff_EDI are unaffected register parameters (ESI=output dest, EDI=source)\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset | Size | Field Name | Type | Description\n   0x0 | 0x80 | local_80   | Unicode[64] | Primary Unicode output buffer\n  0x80 | 0x80 | local_40   | Unicode[64] | Secondary Unicode buffer for range formatting\n  0xc0 | 0x20 | aCStack_a0 | char[32]    | ANSI format buffer\n  0xc0 | 0x20 | aCStack_c0 | char[32]    | ANSI format buffer (overlaps with aCStack_a0)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x20 (32): Unicode array element count\n- 0x80 (128): Byte offset for secondary buffer (0x40 elements * 2 bytes per Unicode char)\n- 0xc4 (196): Total stack frame siz