      "comment": "Formats a scaled stat modifier value with localized prefix/suffix strings.\n\nWorker function that calculates a level-scaled stat value from a StatTable\nstructure and formats it as a Unicode string with sign prefix (+/-) and\nlocalized stat name components.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract min/max scaling values from StatTable at offsets +0xF0 and +0xF4\n2. Call CalculateScaledValue(nLevel, nMinValue, nMaxValue) to compute scaled result\n3. Initialize 64-element Unicode buffer array by calling default constructor 32 times\n4. If scaled value is 0, return 0 (no modifier to display)\n5. Select format string: \"%d\" for negative values, \"+%d\" for positive values\n6. Format scaled value to ANSI string using wsprintfA\n7. Convert ANSI buffer to Unicode using toUnicode(buffer, source, 32)\n8. Append localized strings via ValidateStringId and Unicode::strcat:\n   - String ID 0x10F7: First stat component\n   - Append formatted numeric value\n   - String ID 0x10B3: Middle stat component  \n   - String ID 0x0F9E: Final stat component\n9. Return 1 indicating success\n\nParameters:\n  pStatTable - StatTable* - Pointer to stat table structure containing:\n    +0xF0: nMinValue (int) - Minimum scaling value\n    +0xF4: nMaxValue (int) - Maximum scaling value\n  nLevel - int - Level value for scaling calculation\n  IMPLICIT ECX: Destination Unicode string pointer (saved to EDI)\n\nReturns:\n  0 - Scaled value was zero, no string generated\n  1 - Successfully formatted stat modifier string\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  Zero scaled value causes early return without string modification.\n  Negative values use plain \"%d\" format (shows minus sign).\n  Positive values use \"+%d\" format (explicit plus sign).\n\nString Format References:\n  0x6FBC6358: g_szResourceFormatPlus = \"+%d\"\n  0x6FBB0DE4: g_szLocalizationConfig = \"%d\"\n\nRelated String IDs:\n  0x10F7 (4343): Stat name prefix\n  0x10B3 (4275): Stat name separator\n  0x0F9E (3998): Stat name suffix",
