      "comment": "Formats a monster skill bonus tooltip with level-scaled stat values.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call FormatLocalizationString with input parameters to initialize base string\n2. Get level-scaled value via GetMonsterLevelScaledValue(nMonsterRecord, nMonsterLevel)\n3. Initialize 64-character Unicode buffer (loop 0x20 times calling default_constructor_closure)\n4. If scaled value is non-zero:\n   a. Format scaled value as ANSI string using wsprintfA with \"%d\" format\n   b. Convert ANSI to Unicode buffer via toUnicode\n   c. Validate and append string ID 0x1102 (skill stat label)\n   d. Append Unicode buffer (formatted value)\n   e. Validate and append string ID 0x10b3 (separator/colon)\n   f. Validate and append string ID 0xf9e (newline/delimiter)\n5. Reinitialize Unicode buffer\n6. If scaled value is non-zero:\n   a. Repeat formatting with string ID 0x1101 (second skill stat label)\n7. Reinitialize Unicode buffer\n8. If scaled value is non-zero:\n   a. Repeat formatting with string ID 0x1103 (third skill stat label)\n9. Get monster skill ID via GetMonsterSkillId(nMonsterRecord, nMonsterLevel)\n10. Call FormatResourceString with skill ID to append skill name\n11. Return 1 (success)\n\nParameters:\n  pOutputBuffer (ECX): Pointer to Unicode output buffer for tooltip text\n  nMonsterRecord (EDX): Monster record/data index\n  nSkillIndex (Stack+0x4): Skill slot index for the monster\n  nMonsterLevel (Stack+0x8): Monster level for stat scaling\n  pInputString (Stack+0xC): Input Unicode string for localization\n\nReturns:\n  Always returns 1 (success)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If GetMonsterLevelScaledValue returns 0, all three stat blocks are skipped\n  - Function uses ESI/EDI internally via unaff_ decompiler artifacts for strcat operations\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x1102 - First skill stat localization string ID\n  0x1101 - Second skill stat localization string ID\n  0x1103 - Third skill stat localization string ID\n  0x10b3 - Separator/colon localization string ID\n  0