      "instructions": ["0x76C80|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [ESP + 0x4]", "0x76C84|SUB|ESP, 0x60", "0x76C87|MOV|EDX, dword ptr [EAX + 0xf0]", "0x76C8D|PUSH|EBX", "0x76C8E|PUSH|EBP", "0x76C8F|PUSH|ESI", "0x76C90|PUSH|EDI", "0x76C91|MOV|EDI, ECX", "0x76C93|MOV|ECX, dword ptr [EAX + 0xf4]", "0x76C99|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [ESP + 0x78]", "0x76C9D|PUSH|ECX", "0x76C9E|PUSH|EDX", "0x76C9F|PUSH|EAX", "0x76CA0|CALL|0x6fb98b18", "0x76CA5|MOV|EBP, EAX"],
      "comment": "Formats a stat modifier value as a signed display string for UI rendering.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate scaled stat value using CalculateScaledValue with pStatData fields at offsets 0xF0 and 0xF4\n2. Initialize a 32-element Unicode buffer by calling default constructor 32 times\n3. If scaled value is 0, return 0 (no display needed)\n4. Select format string based on sign: \"+%d\" for positive, \"%d\" for negative\n5. Format value to ANSI string buffer using wsprintfA\n6. Convert ANSI to Unicode buffer using toUnicode\n7. Append string ID 0x10F8 to output buffer\n8. Append formatted value string to output buffer\n9. Append string ID 0x10B3 to output buffer\n10. Append string ID 0x0F9E to output buffer\n11. Return 1 (success)\n\nParameters:\n  pStatData - Pointer to stat data structure with scale factors at offsets 0xF0 and 0xF4\n  nStatValue - Raw stat value to scale and format\n  IMPLICIT ECX - Output Unicode buffer pointer (stored in EDI)\n\nReturns:\n  1 - Success, formatted string written to output buffer\n  0 - Scaled value was zero, no output generated\n\nString IDs:\n  0x10F8 - First prefix string (concatenated before value)\n  0x10B3 - Middle string (concatenated after value)\n  0x0F9E - Suffix string (concatenated at end)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Negative values use plain \"%d\" format (shows minus sign naturally)\n  - Positive values use \"+%d\" format (adds explicit plus sign)\n  - Zero values cause early return with no string output",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PARAM_2", "PROP_NOCALLER", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control"]
