      "comment": "Formats a complete monster skill display string by combining localization, resource, and stat strings.\n\nClassification: Worker function - called to compose full skill tooltip/display text\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call FormatLocalizationString to format base localized text with pConfig structure data\n2. Call GetMonsterSkillId to retrieve skill ID based on monster and skill slot\n3. Clamp skill ID to maximum of 250 (0xfa) - prevents out-of-bounds resource lookup\n4. Call FormatResourceString with clamped skill ID and suffix type 0 (standard format)\n5. Call FormatResourceStatString to append damage/stat values to display\n6. Return combined total length of all three formatted components\n\nParameters:\n  pStringContext (ECX, dword): String buffer context/handle passed to all formatters\n  nMonsterId (EDX, int): Monster type ID for skill lookup\n  pConfig (Stack[0x4], void *): Configuration structure pointer with stat offsets:\n    +0xdc: Bit shift amount for scaling\n    +0xe0: Base stat value\n    +0xe4: Stat multiplier\n    +0x128-0x130: Stat delta offsets\n  nSkillSlot (Stack[0x8], int): Skill slot index (0-based)\n  nFormatFlags (Stack[0xc], int): Format mode flags for localization string\n\nReturns:\n  int: Combined character count from all three format operations\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0xfa (250): Maximum valid skill resource ID (prevents overflow)\n  0x0: Standard suffix mode passed to FormatResourceString\n\nCross-References:\n  FormatLocalizationString - formats base localized text with scaling\n  GetMonsterSkillId - retrieves skill resource ID from monster tables\n  FormatResourceString - formats time/resource interval display\n  FormatResourceStatString - formats damage/stat range display\n\nNote: extraout_EAX captures FormatResourceStatString return value despite void declaration",
      "tags": ["PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_5", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
    },
