      "comment": "Format monster skill damage tooltip with level-scaled values.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call FormatLocalizationString to initialize base tooltip text\n2. Get monster skill ID using GetMonsterSkillId(0x128, nMonsterLevel)\n3. Format and append skill value using FormatAndAppendStringValue\n4. Get level-scaled monster value via GetMonsterLevelScaledValue\n5. Initialize 64-element Unicode buffer (loop 32 iterations, 2 bytes each)\n6. If scaled value is non-zero:\n   a. Format integer to string using wsprintfA with \"%d\" format\n   b. Convert ANSI to Unicode via toUnicode\n   c. Append string using strcat, validate string ID 0x10D5\n   d. Append separator, validate string ID 0xF9E\n7. Read damage multiplier from pMonsterStats+0xF0\n8. Get current video frame index via GetVideoFrameCount\n9. Get monster init stats pointer for monster ID 0x1A6\n10. If init stats pointer valid:\n    a. Read damage values from init stats at offsets 0x180 and 0x174 indexed by frame\n    b. Calculate average: (stats[0x180+frame*4] + stats[0x174+frame*4]) / 2\n    c. Apply level scaling: damage += (damage * multiplier * (level-1)) / 100\n    d. If calculated damage non-zero:\n       - Reinitialize Unicode buffer\n       - Format damage value to string\n       - Convert to Unicode\n       - Validate string ID 0x10C6, append formatted string\n       - Append separator, validate string ID 0xF9E\n11. Return 1 (success)\n\nParameters:\n- pOutputBuffer (dword, ECX): Pointer to Unicode output buffer for tooltip text\n- nMonsterIndex (int, EDX): Monster type/index for skill lookup\n- pMonsterStats (int, Stack+4): Pointer to monster stats structure\n  +0xF0: Damage multiplier value\n- nMonsterLevel (int, Stack+8): Monster level for scaling calculations\n- nParam5 (int, Stack+C): Additional formatting parameter\n\nReturns:\n- 1: Always returns success\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x128: Monster skill ID constant for GetMonsterSkillId\n- 0x1A6: Monster init stats ID (422 decimal)\n- 0x10D5: String ID for skill damage label (4309 decimal)\n- 0x10C6: String ID for calculated damage label (4294 decimal)\n- 0xF9E: String ID for separator/newline (3998 decimal)\n- 0xF0: Offset to damage multiplier in monster stats\n- 0x174: Offset to min damage array in init stats\n- 0x180: Offset to max damage array in init stats\n- 0x20: Unicode buffer element count (32)\n- 100: Percentage divisor for level scaling\n\nStructure Layout (pMonsterStats):\nOffset  Size  Field              Type   Description\n0xF0    4     nDamageMultiplier  int    Level-based damage scaling factor\n\nStructure Layout (MonsterInitStats at 0x1A6):\nOffset  Size  Field              Type   Description\n0x174   4*N   anMinDamage[]      int[]  Min damage values indexed by frame\n0x180   4*N   anMaxDamage[]      int[]  Max damage values indexed by frame\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If GetMonsterLevelScaledValue returns 0, skill damage section skipped\n- If GetMonsterInitStatsPtr returns NULL, damage calculation skipped\n- If calculated damage is 0, damage tooltip section skipped\n- Frame index from GetVideoFrameCount used to select damage variant",
