      "comment": "Format monster skill bonus text and append to tooltip string buffer.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get monster skill ID via GetMonsterSkillId(dwUnitId, dwFlags)\n2. Initialize 64-element Unicode buffer (32 wide chars) using default constructor\n3. If skill ID is non-zero:\n   a. Select format string: \"%d\" for negative, \"+%d\" for positive skill values\n   b. Format skill ID to ANSI buffer using wsprintfA\n   c. Convert ANSI to Unicode via toUnicode (max 32 chars)\n   d. Append localized string 0x10a0 to output\n   e. Append skill value Unicode string to output\n   f. Append localized string 0x10b3 to output\n   g. Append localized string 0xf9e (line separator) to output\n4. Append localized string 0x550d to output (unconditional)\n5. Append localized string 0xf9e (line separator) to output\n6. Call CalcViewportCoordinates to compute display position\n7. Return 1 (success)\n\nParameters:\n  dwRenderContext (ECX) - Render context or display object handle\n  dwUnitId (EDX) - Unit/monster identifier for skill lookup\n  pOutputCoords (Stack+4) - Pointer to output coordinate buffer\n  dwFlags (Stack+8) - Flags controlling skill ID retrieval\n\nReturns:\n  int = 1 (always succeeds)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x20 (32) - Unicode buffer element count (64 bytes / 2 = 32 wide chars)\n  0x10a0 - Localized string ID (skill bonus prefix)\n  0x10b3 - Localized string ID (skill bonus suffix)\n  0xf9e - Localized string ID (line separator/newline)\n  0x550d - Localized string ID (unconditional tooltip text)\n\nDecompiler Notes:\n  unaff_ESI/unaff_EDI are implicit registers used by Unicode::strcat\n  for destination/source string pointers set by ValidateStringId calls",
