      "api_calls": ["GetMonsterTreasureClass", "GetMonsterMaxDamage", "GetMonsterLevelStat", "ValidateStringId", "ValidateStringId", "ValidateStringId"],
      "instructions": ["0x77C60|SUB|ESP, 0x68", "0x77C63|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [ESP + 0x74]", "0x77C67|PUSH|EBX", "0x77C68|MOV|EBX, dword ptr [ESP + 0x70]", "0x77C6C|PUSH|EBP", "0x77C6D|MOV|EBP, dword ptr [ESP + 0x78]", "0x77C71|PUSH|ESI", "0x77C72|PUSH|EDI", "0x77C73|PUSH|EAX", "0x77C74|PUSH|EBP", "0x77C75|PUSH|EBX", "0x77C76|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x20], EDX", "0x77C7A|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x1c], ECX", "0x77C7E|CALL|0x6fb38bf0", "0x77C83|MOV|ECX, dword ptr [EBX]"],
      "comment": "Formats monster damage and level bonus statistics into a tooltip string.\n\nClassification: Worker function - formats monster stats for UI tooltip display\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call FormatLocalizationString with initial parameters for base formatting\n2. Get monster treasure class via GetMonsterTreasureClass(baseStatId, difficultyLevel)\n3. Calculate scaled resource ID: treasureClass * difficultyLevel + pMonsterStats[0x56]\n4. Get max damage via GetMonsterMaxDamage(baseStatId, difficultyLevel)\n5. Read min damage stat from pMonsterStats[0x51] (offset 0x144)\n6. Read shift value byte from pMonsterStats[0x4a] (offset 0x128)\n7. Read max damage stat from pMonsterStats[0x52] (offset 0x148)\n8. Call FormatResourceString with scaled resource ID\n9. Calculate scaled min damage: ((minDamageStat + maxDamage) << shiftValue) * resourceId >> 8\n10. Calculate scaled max damage: ((maxDamageStat + maxDamage) << shiftValue) * resourceId >> 8\n11. Call FormatLocalizationString with scaled min/max damage values\n12. Get monster level stat via GetMonsterLevelStat(monsterType, difficultyLevel)\n13. Initialize Unicode buffer array (64 elements, loop 32 times with 2-byte stride)\n14. If level stat is non-zero:\n    a. Select format string: \"+%d\" if positive, \"%d\" if negative\n    b. Format level stat to ANSI buffer via wsprintfA\n    c. Convert ANSI to Unicode via toUnicode\n    d. Append localized strings 0x10b2, level value, 0x10b3, and 0xf9e\n\nParameters:\n  pOutputBuffer (ECX) - void * - Output buffer for formatted string\n  nMonsterType (EDX) - int - Monster type identifier for level stat lookup\n  pMonsterStats (Stack+0x4) - int * - Pointer to monster stats structure:\n    +0x000: Base stat ID (dword)\n    +0x128: Shift value (byte) for damage scaling\n    +0x144: Min damage stat (dword)\n    +0x148: Max damage stat (dword)\n    +0x158: Treasure class offset (dword)\n  nDifficultyLevel (Stack+0x8) - int - Game difficulty level\n  nDisplayFlags (Stack+0xC) - int - Display flags for formatting\n\nReturns:\n  Always returns 1 (success)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If level stat is 0, skips level bonus formatting entirely\n  - Negative level stats use \"%d\" format (shows minus sign)\n  - Positive level stats use \"+%d\" format (explicit plus sign)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x51 (81) - Array index for min damage stat field (offset 0x144)\n  0x52 (82) - Array index for max damage stat field (offset 0x148)\n  0x56 (86) - Array index for treasure class offset field (offset 0x158)\n  0x4a (74) - Array index for shift value byte (offset 0x128)\n  0x1f (31) - Mask for shift value (limits to 0-31 bits)\n  0x10b2 (4274) - String ID for level bonus prefix\n  0x10b3 (4275) - String ID for level bonus middle\n  0xf9e (3998) - String ID for level bonus suffix\n  0x20 (32) - Unicode buffer size / loop count\n\nDecompiler Discrepancies:\n  - unaff_ESI and unaff_EDI appear uninitialized in decompiler but are likely\n    set by the calling convention or previous function context\n  - The Unicode::strcat calls use these registers as source/destination",
