      "comment": "Formats and combines three stat display strings for UI rendering.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call FormatLocalizationString with all five parameters for base localization\n2. Load resource ID from pConfig+0xf4 structure offset\n3. Call FormatResourceString with resource ID and standard suffix mode (0)\n4. Call FormatResourceStatString with nIndex, nFormatMode, pConfig, nScaleFactor\n5. Return 1 indicating all formatting operations completed successfully\n\nParameters:\n  nIndex (ECX, dword): Resource or string index selector for localization lookup\n  nFormatMode (EDX, int): Mode selector - 0x6 for special handling, 0xdd for alternate path\n  pConfig (Stack+0x4, void*): Pointer to configuration structure containing:\n      +0xdc: shift amount for scaling calculations\n      +0xe0: base height or scale value\n      +0xe4: multiplier for height calculations\n      +0xf4: resource ID passed to FormatResourceString\n      +0x128: bit shift amount for stat scaling (max 0x1f)\n      +0x12c: primary stat offset in stat table\n      +0x130: secondary stat offset in stat table\n  nScaleFactor (Stack+0x8, int): Height or scaling factor used in calculations\n  nAlternateParam (Stack+0xc, int): Alternate format parameter bitmask or index\n\nReturns:\n  1: Always returns success after completing all three formatting calls\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  Referenced from function pointer table at 0x6fbc5fa8\n  All three sub-functions may modify shared Unicode string buffers\n  RET 0xc cleans up 3 stack parameters (stdcall-style cleanup)",
