      "comment": "Builds a configuration tooltip string by formatting a numeric value and appending localized strings.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract configuration value from pConfigContext+0x100\n2. Initialize 64-element Unicode array using default constructor loop (32 iterations, 2 bytes each)\n3. If configuration value is non-zero:\n   a. Format value as decimal string using wsprintfA with \"%d\" format\n   b. Convert ANSI string to Unicode (max 32 chars)\n   c. Append localized string 0x10A0 to output buffer via ValidateStringId\n   d. Append formatted Unicode value to output buffer via Unicode::strcat\n   e. Append localized string 0x10B3 to output buffer via ValidateStringId\n   f. Append localized string 0x0F9E to output buffer via ValidateStringId\n4. Return 1 (success)\n\nParameters:\n- pConfigContext: Pointer to configuration context structure\n  - Offset +0x100: Configuration value to format (int)\n- IMPLICIT ECX: Pointer to destination Unicode buffer (this pointer for strcat calls)\n\nReturns:\n- int: Always returns 1 indicating success\n\nString IDs Referenced:\n- 0x10A0: Prefix localized string\n- 0x10B3: Separator localized string\n- 0x0F9E: Suffix localized string\n\nCalled From:\n- Function pointer table at 0x6fbc5fcc (tooltip handler callback)",
