      "comment": "Formats monster damage stat text with skill bonus modifiers from active auras.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call FormatLocalizationString with initial parameters to format base damage text\n2. Get base monster max damage via GetMonsterMaxDamage(nStatId, nMonsterLevel)\n3. Calculate damage range by adding base damage to pbMonsterStatData offsets 0x144 and 0x148\n4. If all damage values are zero, skip damage formatting and jump to step 12\n5. Apply shift modifier from pbMonsterStatData[0x128] and scale damage values right by 8\n6. For stat IDs 0x14, 0x31, 0x35 force nDamageMin to 1 as minimum damage floor\n7. Get player unit via GetGameContext to check for active auras\n8. If player unit type is 1 (Player) check Concentration aura state 0x47 with skill 0x3d\n9. If Concentration active and aura type matches apply percentage bonus to damage values\n10. Check Fanaticism aura state 0x48 with skill 0x3f and apply bonus if active\n11. Call FormatLocalizationString with final damage range and display mode byte from offset 0x140\n12. Call FormatResourceStatString to append resource stat formatting\n13. Get final skill ID via GetMonsterSkillId and call FormatResourceString with ID 0x10ce\n\nParameters:\n- wszOutputBuffer (ECX): Output Unicode buffer for formatted damage text\n- nStatId (EDX): Stat identifier where 0x14 0x31 0x35 are special cases with minimum floor\n- pbMonsterStatData (Stack+4): Pointer to monster stat structure with damage offsets\n- nMonsterLevel (Stack+8): Monster level for damage calculation scaling\n- nParam5 (Stack+C): Additional parameter passed to format functions\n\nReturns:\n- void with damage string written to wszOutputBuffer\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Stat IDs 0x14 0x31 0x35 force minimum damage to 1\n- Concentration aura 0x47 applies to aura type 1 monsters\n- Fanaticism aura 0x48 applies to aura type 2 monsters\n- Division by 100 uses optimized multiply-shift with magic constant 0x51eb851f\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x47: Concentration aura state flag\n- 0x48: Fanaticism aura state flag\n- 0x3d: Concentration skill ID (61 decimal)\n- 0x3f: Fanaticism skill ID (63 decimal)\n- 0x14 0x31 0x35: Special stat IDs with minimum damage floor\n- 0x10ce: Resource string ID for FormatResourceString",
