      "api_calls": ["GetMonsterSkillId", "ValidateStringId", "ValidateStringId", "ValidateStringId", "GetMonsterInitStatsPtr", "ValidateStringId", "ValidateStringId"],
      "instructions": ["0x78650|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [ESP + 0xc]", "0x78654|SUB|ESP, 0x60", "0x78657|PUSH|EBX", "0x78658|MOV|EBX, dword ptr [ESP + 0x6c]", "0x7865C|PUSH|EBP", "0x7865D|PUSH|ESI", "0x7865E|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0x78660|PUSH|EDI", "0x78661|MOV|ECX, dword ptr [ESP + 0x74]", "0x78665|PUSH|EAX", "0x78666|PUSH|EBX", "0x78667|PUSH|ECX", "0x78668|MOV|EDI, EDX", "0x7866A|MOV|ECX, ESI", "0x7866C|CALL|0x6fb38bf0"],
      "comment": "Append monster skill ID and scaled damage statistics to tooltip string.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call FormatLocalizationString to initialize output with base formatting\n2. Get monster skill ID for the specified skill slot\n3. Initialize 64-element Unicode buffer (128 bytes) via constructor loop\n4. If skill ID is non-zero:\n   a. Select format string: \"%d\" for negative IDs, \"+%d\" for positive IDs\n   b. Format skill ID value to ANSI buffer using wsprintfA\n   c. Convert ANSI to Unicode via toUnicode\n   d. Validate and append string IDs 0x10c6, 0x10b3, 0xf9e via strcat\n5. Read damage modifier from pMonsterStats+0xf0\n6. Get current difficulty level via GetVideoFrameCount\n7. Get monster init stats pointer for index 0x1a8\n8. If stats pointer valid:\n   a. Calculate base damage: avg of values at offsets 0x174 and 0x180 indexed by difficulty\n   b. Scale damage: base + (base * damageModifier * (skillSlot-1)) / 100\n   c. If scaled damage non-zero:\n      - Re-initialize Unicode buffer\n      - Format damage value with \"%d\" format\n      - Convert to Unicode, validate string 0x10c6\n      - Append damage strings via strcat with string 0xf9e\n9. Return 1 (always succeeds)\n\nParameters:\n- pOutputBuffer (ECX): Pointer to Unicode output string buffer\n- nMonsterId (EDX): Monster type identifier for skill lookup\n- pMonsterStats (Stack+4): Pointer to monster stats structure (offset 0xf0 = damage modifier)\n- nSkillSlot (Stack+8): Skill slot index (1-based, decremented for calculation)\n- nMonsterLevel (Stack+C): Monster level (passed to FormatLocalizationString)\n\nReturns:\n- 1: Always returns success\n\nStructure Layout (pMonsterStats):\nOffset | Size | Field              | Type | Description\n0xf0   | 4    | nDamageModifier    | int  | Base damage scaling percentage\n\nStructure Layout (MonsterInitStats at 0x1a8):\nOffset | Size | Field              | Type | Description\n0x174  | 4*N  | anMinDamage[]      | int  | Minimum damage per difficulty\n0x180  | 4*N  | anMaxDamage[]      | int  | Maximum damage per difficulty\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x20 (32): Unicode buffer element count (64 elements / 2 bytes each = init loop)\n- 0x1a8 (424): Monster index for damage lookup table\n- 0x10c6: String ID for skill display prefix\n- 0x10b3: String ID for skill separator\n- 0xf9e: String ID for tooltip suffix/terminator\n- 0xf0: Offset to damage modifier in monster stats\n- 0x174, 0x180: Offsets to min/max damage arrays in init stats\n- 100: Divisor for percentage scaling calculation\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Negative skill IDs use \"%d\" format (no plus sign)\n- Positive skill IDs use \"+%d\" format (shows plus prefix)\n- Zero skill ID skips skill portion entirely\n- Zero calculated damage skips damage portion\n- unaff_ESI, unaff_EDI: Unaffected registers used by Unicode::strcat as src/dst",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_5", "STRUCT_Room1", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control"]
