      "instructions": ["0x787F0|SUB|ESP, 0x64", "0x787F3|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [ESP + 0x70]", "0x787F7|PUSH|EBX", "0x787F8|MOV|EBX, dword ptr [ESP + 0x70]", "0x787FC|PUSH|EBP", "0x787FD|PUSH|ESI", "0x787FE|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0x78800|MOV|ECX, dword ptr [ESP + 0x74]", "0x78804|PUSH|EDI", "0x78805|PUSH|EAX", "0x78806|PUSH|EBX", "0x78807|MOV|EDI, EDX", "0x78809|PUSH|ECX", "0x7880A|MOV|ECX, ESI", "0x7880C|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x1c], EDI"],
      "comment": "Formats and appends monster level scaling statistics to a localization output buffer.\nThis function builds a complete monster stat tooltip by combining scaled values,\nbase stats, and resource information with proper +/- formatting.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call FormatLocalizationString to initialize base output with all parameters\n2. Get monster level scaled value via GetMonsterLevelScaledValue(nMonsterLevel, nLevelIndex)\n3. Initialize 64-element Unicode buffer with default constructors (loop 0x20 iterations)\n4. If scaled value is non-zero:\n   a. Select format string: g_szResourceFormatPlus (+%d) if positive, g_szLocalizationConfig (%d) if negative\n   b. Format value to ANSI string via wsprintfA\n   c. Convert ANSI to Unicode via toUnicode\n   d. Append localization strings 0x10A0, formatted value, 0x10B3, and 0x0F9E via strcat\n5. Get monster level stat via GetMonsterLevelStat(nMonsterLevel, nLevelIndex)\n6. Re-initialize Unicode buffer (loop 0x20 iterations)\n7. If stat value is non-zero:\n   a. Select format string based on sign (same as step 4a)\n   b. Format and convert to Unicode\n   c. Append localization strings 0x10BA, formatted value, 0x10B3, and 0x0F9E\n8. Call FormatResourceStatString to append resource stat information\n9. Calculate final level: pStatData[0x100] + nLevelIndex - 1, clamped to pStatData[0x104] max\n10. Re-initialize Unicode buffer (loop 0x20 iterations)\n11. If final level is non-zero:\n    a. Format as plain integer (always uses %d format)\n    b. Convert to Unicode\n    c. Append formatted value, localization string 0x10A7, and 0x0F9E\n12. Return 1 (success)\n\nParameters:\n  pOutputBuffer (ECX) - Pointer to Unicode output buffer for formatted result\n  nMonsterLevel (EDX) - Monster level used for stat calculations\n  pStatData (Stack+0x4) - Pointer to stat data structure with fields at +0x100 and +0x104\n  nLevelIndex (Stack+0x8) - Level index for scaling calculations\n  nStatParam (Stack+0xC) - Additional stat parameter (passed to FormatLocalizationString)\n  IMPLICIT EDI - Unicode strcat function pointer loaded from [0x6fba5c40]\n  IMPLICIT ESI - Preserved as output buffer pointer throughout\n\nReturns:\n  int - Always returns 1 (success)\n\nLocalization String IDs:\n  0x10A0 - Scaled value label prefix\n  0x10B3 - Stat separator/delimiter\n  0x0F9E - Line/section terminator\n  0x10BA - Monster level stat label prefix\n  0x10A7 - Final level label prefix\n\nStructure Layout (pStatData):\n  Offset  Size  Field           Type  Description\n  0x100   4     nBaseLevelValue int   Base level value for calculation\n  0x104   4     nMaxLevelValue  int   Maximum allowed level value (clamp)",
      "tags": ["PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_5", "STRUCT_Room1", "PROP_LOOPHEAVY", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
