      "comment": "Formats monster skill slot text for UI display.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract skill value from pSkillData at offset 0xf8 (index 0x3e)\n2. Call FormatAndAppendStringValue to format the skill value with localized string\n3. Call GetMonsterSkillId to get the skill resource ID for the monster/slot\n4. Call FormatResourceString to format the skill name with suffix type 0 (standard)\n5. Return 1 (success)\n\nParameters:\n- pOutputBuffer (void *, ECX): Output buffer context for formatted string\n- nMonsterId (int, EDX): Monster type ID for skill lookup\n- pSkillData (int *, Stack+0x4): Pointer to skill data structure, field at offset 0xf8 contains skill value\n- nSkillSlot (int, Stack+0x8): Skill slot index (0-based) for monster skill lookup\n\nReturns:\n- 1: Always returns success\n\nClassification: Callback - Referenced from function pointer table at 0x6fbc603c\n\nStructure Access:\n- pSkillData[0x3e] (offset 0xf8): Skill value passed to FormatAndAppendStringValue\n\nCallees:\n- FormatAndAppendStringValue: Formats numeric skill value to localized string\n- GetMonsterSkillId: Retrieves skill ID for monster at given slot (D2Common ordinal)\n- FormatResourceString: Formats skill resource string with suffix type",
