      "comment": "Formats and applies game state modifiers (potions/skill bonuses) to a localization string.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call FormatLocalizationString with initial parameters to set up string\n2. Get stat modification value via Ordinal_11045 based on nStatType and nValueX\n3. Load character state offsets at 0x144 and 0x148, add modification value\n4. Return 1 if all values zero (no modifiers needed)\n5. Shift and normalize values using scale factor at offset 0x128\n6. Override value to 1 for special stat types (0x14 Strength, 0x31 Dexterity, 0x35 Vitality)\n7. Process first enchantment (0x47): Get current game state, check if available\n8. Validate character state at offset 0xd4 equals 0x01, or pCharState is NULL\n9. If enchantment active, get bonus flags from Ordinal_10949, apply via Ordinal_10968 and Ordinal_10996\n10. Multiply values by bonus percentage 0x3d, divide by 100, accumulate results\n11. Process second enchantment (0x48): Same logic with offset 0x02 check and percentage 0x3f\n12. Load character stat value from offset 0x140, call FormatLocalizationString with final values\n\nParameters:\nszString (char *) - Pointer to localization string buffer\nnStatType (int) - Stat identifier for modification lookup\npCharState (int *) - Pointer to character state structure containing offsets\nnValueX (int) - Primary value for stat lookup (x-coordinate)\nnValueY (int) - Secondary value (y-coordinate)\n\nReturns:\n1 - Always returns success\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If pCharState NULL, bypasses character state offset checks\n- Special stat types (0x14, 0x31, 0x35) force value to 1 regardless\n- Bonus application skipped if character state flag doesn't match enchantment type\n- Uses 0x51eb851f magic constant for fixed-point percentage calculation\n\nStructure Offsets (pCharState):\nOffset | Size | Field Name | Type | Description\n0x128  | 1    | nScaleFactor | byte | Shift amount for value scaling\n0x140  | 1    | nStatFlags | byte | Final stat value flags\n0x144  | 4    | nOffsetX | int | X offset modifier\n0x148  | 4    | nOffsetY | int | Y offset modifier\n0xd4   | 1    | nEnchantType | byte | Enchantment type flag (0x01 or 0x02)",
