      "comment": "Appends monster skill level bonus text to tooltip buffer.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get monster skill ID from level and skill parameter\n2. Format resource string using skill ID\n3. Get level-scaled value for monster stat modifier\n4. Initialize Unicode buffer array (32 elements)\n5. If scaled value is non-zero:\n   a. Select format string: \"%d\" for negative, \"+%d\" for positive\n   b. Format value into ANSI buffer with wsprintfA\n   c. Convert ANSI to Unicode\n   d. Append localization strings using string IDs:\n      - 0x1101: Skill bonus prefix\n      - 0x10b3: Level modifier separator\n      - 0x0f9e: Tooltip suffix\n6. Return success (always 1)\n\nParameters:\n  pDestBuffer (ECX): Pointer to destination Unicode tooltip buffer\n  nMonsterLevel (EDX): Monster level for scaling calculations\n  nUnused (Stack+4): Unused parameter (reserved)\n  nSkillParam (Stack+8): Skill parameter for lookup\n\nReturns:\n  int: Always returns 1 (success)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If scaled value is 0, function exits early without appending text\n- Negative values use \"%d\" format (shows minus sign)\n- Positive values use \"+%d\" format (explicit plus sign)\n\nClassification: Worker function - Formats and appends monster skill bonus text to UI tooltips",
