      "comment": "Formats monster experience and level stat bonus strings for tooltip display.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call FormatLocalizationString to initialize base localization\n2. Get monster experience value via GetMonsterExperienceByLevel(nMonsterLevel, nMonsterClassId)\n3. Initialize 64-element Unicode buffer (wchar_t[64]) by calling default constructor closure 32 times\n4. If experience value is non-zero:\n   a. Select format string: \"+%d\" for positive, \"%d\" for negative\n   b. Format experience value to ANSI string via wsprintfA\n   c. Convert ANSI to Unicode via toUnicode\n   d. Append localized strings: Experience label (0x1107), value, separator (0x10B3), newline (0xF9E)\n5. Get monster level stat bonus via GetMonsterLevelStat(nMonsterClassId, nMonsterLevel)\n6. Re-initialize Unicode buffer (same 32-iteration loop)\n7. If level stat value is non-zero:\n   a. Select format string: \"+%d\" for positive, \"%d\" for negative\n   b. Format level stat to ANSI string via wsprintfA\n   c. Convert ANSI to Unicode via toUnicode\n   d. Append localized strings: Level label (0x10A6), value, separator (0x10B3), newline (0xF9E)\n8. Return 1 (TRUE) indicating success\n\nParameters:\n  pDestBuffer (ECX) - Destination Unicode string buffer for formatted output\n  nMonsterClassId (EDX) - Monster class/type identifier for stat lookup\n  nDifficulty (Stack+0x4) - Game difficulty level (Normal/Nightmare/Hell)\n  nMonsterLevel (Stack+0x8) - Monster level for experience calculation\n  nUnused (Stack+0xc) - Unused parameter (passed through to FormatLocalizationString)\n\nReturns:\n  int - Always returns 1 (TRUE)\n\nString IDs:\n  0x1107 - Experience bonus label\n  0x10A6 - Level stat bonus label  \n  0x10B3 - Separator/delimiter string\n  0x0F9E - Newline/line terminator\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Zero experience/level values skip formatting (no text appended)\n  - Negative values use \"%d\" format (shows minus sign)\n  - Positive values use \"+%d\" format (explicit plus sign)",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_5", "STRUCT_Room1", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
