      "comment": "Formats monster damage and life leech statistics into a localized Unicode string.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call FormatLocalizationString to initialize output buffer with base formatting\n2. Get scaled monster damage via GetMonsterScaledDamage(nLevel, nMonsterClassId)\n3. Initialize 64-element Unicode buffer awUnicodeBuffer with default constructors\n4. If scaled damage is non-zero:\n   a. Format damage as decimal string using wsprintfA with \"%d\"\n   b. Convert ANSI to Unicode via toUnicode\n   c. Append localized string 0x10D0 (damage label)\n   d. Append formatted damage value\n   e. Append localized string 0x10B3 (separator)\n   f. Append localized string 0x0F9E (newline/suffix)\n5. Read base life leech value from pMonsterStats+0xF8\n6. Get video frame count for animation timing\n7. Get monster init stats for stat ID 0x1AA (life leech)\n8. If init stats exist:\n   a. Calculate base leech from stats at offsets 0x180 and 0x174 indexed by frame\n   b. Average the two values: (val1 + val2) / 2\n   c. Scale by level: leech += (leech * baseLeech * (nDifficulty-1)) / 100\n   d. If calculated leech is non-zero, format and append with localized strings\n9. Return\n\nParameters:\n  pOutputBuffer (ECX): Unicode string buffer to append formatted text\n  nMonsterClassId (EDX): Monster class ID for damage lookup\n  pMonsterStats (stack+0x4): Pointer to monster stats structure with leech at +0xF8\n  nLevel (stack+0x8): Monster level for damage scaling\n  nDifficulty (stack+0xc): Difficulty level (1-based) for leech scaling\n  IMPLICIT ESI: Source string pointer for strcat operations\n  IMPLICIT EDI: Function pointer to Unicode::strcat (loaded from 0x6fba5c40)\n\nReturns:\n  void - Output written to pOutputBuffer via strcat\n\nString IDs:\n  0x10D0 - Damage label\n  0x10B3 - Separator\n  0x10C6 - Life leech label\n  0x0F9E - Newline/suffix\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Returns early if both scaled damage and calculated leech are zero\n  - Magic constant 0x51eb851f used for fast division by 100",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_5", "STRUCT_Room1", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control"]
