      "comment": "Formats duration value from stat descriptor for UI display\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Read duration ticks from pStatDescriptor at offset 0xf0\n2. Push 0 as suffix type (standard format mode)\n3. Call FormatResourceString with tick value and suffix type\n4. Set EAX to 1 (success return value)\n5. Return, cleaning 12 bytes from stack (vtable callback convention)\n\nParameters:\n- pStatDescriptor (int *): Pointer to stat descriptor structure containing duration field at offset 0xf0\n\nReturns:\n- 1: Always returns success (EAX = 0x1)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- RET 0xc indicates 12 bytes stack cleanup despite single parameter\n- Function is callback handler invoked via function pointer table at 0x6fbc5f2c\n- Extra stack slots are unused padding for uniform callback signature\n\nStructure Access:\nOffset  Size  Field            Description\n0xf0    4     dwDurationTicks  Time value in game ticks to format\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x10b0: Resource string ID loaded into EDX (unused by FormatResourceString path taken)\n- 0xf0: Offset to duration ticks field in descriptor structure",
