      "comment": "Wrapper function for formatting localized and resource strings in a single call.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call FormatLocalizationString with all 5 parameters to format the primary localized text\n2. Extract resource ID from config structure at offset +0xfc\n3. Call FormatResourceString with extracted resource ID and suffix type 0 (standard format)\n4. Return 1 (success)\n\nParameters:\n- nIndex (dword, ECX): Resource or string index/selector for localization lookup\n- nMode (int, EDX): Mode selector controlling formatting behavior (0x6=special, 0xdd=alternate)\n- pConfig (void*, Stack+0x4): Pointer to configuration structure containing:\n    +0xdc: shift amount for value calculation\n    +0xe0: base scale value\n    +0xe4: multiplier value\n    +0xfc: secondary resource ID for FormatResourceString\n- nScale (int, Stack+0x8): Height/scaling factor for value calculation\n- nAltFormat (int, Stack+0xc): Alternate format parameter (0=standard, non-zero=alternate path)\n\nReturns:\n- Always returns 1 (success)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- This is a thin wrapper combining two formatting operations\n- Referenced via function pointer table at 0x6fbc5f3c\n- FormatLocalizationString handles the complex formatting logic\n- FormatResourceString uses suffix type 0 (standard format)\n\nStructure Layout (pConfig):\nOffset  Size  Field       Type  Description\n0xdc    4     nShift      int   Bit shift amount for calculations\n0xe0    4     nBaseValue  int   Base height/scale value\n0xe4    4     nMultiplier int   Multiplier for scaling\n0xfc    4     nResourceId int   Secondary resource ID for FormatResourceString",
