      "comment": "Format Maul skill damage text for UI display.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call GetMonsterLevelStat to get level-based stat modifier\n2. Initialize Unicode buffer array (64 elements) with default constructors\n3. If level stat modifier is non-zero:\n   a. Select format string based on sign (negative: \"%d\", positive: \"+%d\")\n   b. Format modifier value with wsprintfA to ANSI string\n   c. Convert ANSI to Unicode via toUnicode\n   d. Validate and concatenate string IDs 0x10b2, 0x10b3, 0xf9e with strcat\n4. Call SKILLS_GetMaulSkillParam1 to get Maul skill parameter\n5. Format damage range string using pSkillData[0x3E] (base damage) and calculated scaled value\n6. Call GetMonsterScaledDamage twice with different base values for damage range\n7. Format final coordinate string with FormatCoordinateString\n8. Return 1 (always succeeds)\n\nParameters:\n- pOutputBuffer (ECX): Pointer to Unicode output buffer for formatted text\n- nMonsterIndex (EDX): Monster index for level stat lookup\n- pSkillData (Stack+0x4): Pointer to skill data structure, accesses field at offset 0xF8 (0x3E * 4)\n- nSkillLevel (Stack+0x8): Skill level for damage calculation\n\nReturns:\n- 1 always (success)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If level stat modifier is 0, skips modifier text formatting but continues damage formatting\n- unaff_ESI/unaff_EDI are implicit Unicode buffer parameters preserved from caller\n- String IDs: 0x10b2 (damage prefix), 0x10b3 (damage range separator), 0xf9e (damage suffix)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x20 (32): Unicode array element count\n- 0x3E (62): Offset index into pSkillData for base damage (actual byte offset 0xF8)\n- 0xE9 (233): Damage scaling type identifier for GetMonsterScaledDamage\n- 0x10b2, 0x10b3, 0xf9e: Localization string IDs\n\nGlobals Referenced:\n- g_szLocalizationConfig: Format string \"%d\" for negative values\n- g_szResourceFormatPlus: Format string \"+%d\" for positive values",
