      "comment": "Format 2D coordinate values into a Unicode display string with fractional tenth components.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize Unicode array buffer (local_40) with 64 wchar_t elements\n2. Extract coordinate whole and fractional (tenth) parts:\n   - nXWhole = param_1 / 0x19 (25)\n   - nXDecimalTenth = ((param_1 % 25) * 10) / 25\n   - nYWhole = param_2 / 0x19 (25)\n   - nYDecimalTenth = ((param_2 % 25) * 10) / 25\n3. Check for zero-value optimization:\n   - If all parts zero (nXWhole=0, nXDecimalTenth=0, nYWhole=0, nYDecimalTenth=0): return 0\n   - If nXWhole=0 and nXDecimalTenth=0: format as \"%d.%d\" with Y values only\n4. Format coordinate string using wsprintfA with either 2-value or 4-value format string\n5. Convert formatted ANSI string to Unicode using toUnicode (buffer size 0x20=32)\n6. Concatenate formatted Unicode string to unaffected ESI/EDI string buffers via Ordinal_10004()\n7. Return 1 (success)\n\nParameters:\n  int nXCoordinate - X coordinate value (scaled by 25, contains whole and fractional parts)\n  int nYCoordinate - Y coordinate value (scaled by 25, contains whole and fractional parts)\n\nReturns:\n  1 on success (formatted and concatenated)\n  0 if all coordinate parts are zero (no-op case, zero optimization)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  Zero Optimization: Returns 0 without formatting when all coordinate components equal zero\n  Format String Selection: Uses 2-part format \"%d.%d\" when both X parts are zero, else uses 4-part format \"%d.%d.%d.%d\"\n  Magic Numbers: 0x19 (25) - divisor for coordinate normalization, 0x20 (32) - Unicode buffer size\n\nStructure Layout:\n  Offset | Size | Field Name | Type | Description\n  --------|------|------------|------|-----\n  -0x40 | 128 | local_40 | wchar_t[64] | Unicode output buffer for formatted coordinate string\n  -0x60 | 32 | aCStack_60 | char[32] | ANSI temporary buffer for formatted string before Unicode conversion",
