      "comment": "Appends monster skill information to a localized string buffer.\n\nClassification: Worker function - formats and appends skill tooltip text\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call FormatLocalizationString to initialize base string with monster info\n2. Get monster skill ID from GetMonsterSkillId(nMonsterId, nSkillSlot)\n3. Initialize 64-element Unicode buffer (awszSkillName) via constructor loop\n4. If skill ID is non-zero:\n   a. Format skill ID as decimal string into stack buffer using wsprintfA\n   b. Convert ANSI buffer to Unicode using toUnicode\n   c. Append space separator (string ID 0x10c4)\n   d. Append skill name Unicode buffer\n   e. Append skill level header (string ID 0x2712)\n   f. Append skill level suffix (string ID 0x0f9e)\n\nParameters:\n  wszBuffer (ECX) - Destination Unicode string buffer to append to\n  nMonsterId (EDX) - Monster type identifier for skill lookup\n  nParam3 (Stack+4) - Passed to FormatLocalizationString\n  nSkillSlot (Stack+8) - Skill slot index (0-based) for GetMonsterSkillId\n  nParam5 (Stack+C) - Passed to FormatLocalizationString\n\nReturns:\n  int - Always returns 1 (success)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If GetMonsterSkillId returns 0, skill info is not appended (early exit)\n  - Unicode buffer initialized with 32 constructor calls (64 wchar_t elements)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x20 - Loop counter for 32 Unicode constructor calls (64 bytes / 2)\n  0x10c4 (4292) - Localized string ID for space/separator\n  0x2712 (10002) - Localized string ID for skill level header\n  0x0f9e (3998) - Localized string ID for skill level suffix\n\nRegister Usage:\n  ESI - Preserved destination buffer pointer (wszBuffer)\n  EDI - Initially Unicode iterator, then strcat function pointer\n  EBP - Skill ID result, reused as loop counter\n\nDecompiler Discrepancies:\n  - unaff_ESI and unaff_EDI shown in decompiler are artifacts\n  - ESI actually holds wszBuffer, EDI becomes strcat function pointer after loop",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_5", "STRUCT_Room1", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control"]
