      "api_calls": ["GetMonsterMaxDamage", "GetUnitStateFlag", "GetUnitSkillById", "GetSkillLevel", "GetMonsterSkillId", "GetUnitStateFlag", "GetUnitSkillById", "GetSkillLevel", "GetMonsterSkillId"],
      "instructions": ["0x79D70|PUSH|ECX", "0x79D71|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [ESP + 0x10]", "0x79D75|PUSH|EBX", "0x79D76|MOV|EBX, dword ptr [ESP + 0xc]", "0x79D7A|PUSH|EBP", "0x79D7B|PUSH|ESI", "0x79D7C|MOV|ESI, dword ptr [ESP + 0x18]", "0x79D80|PUSH|EAX", "0x79D81|PUSH|ESI", "0x79D82|MOV|EBP, EDX", "0x79D84|PUSH|EBX", "0x79D85|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x18], ECX", "0x79D89|CALL|0x6fb38bf0", "0x79D8E|PUSH|ESI", "0x79D8F|PUSH|EBP"],
      "comment": "Formats skill bonus string with damage/defense modifiers\nApplies affixes (elemental/physical) based on skill and equipment state.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Format initial string with basic parameters\n2. Calculate skill offset modifiers (x/y) from equipment stats at +0x144, +0x148\n3. Apply bit shift scaling from mask at +0x128\n4. Check for special skills (0x14, 0x31, 0x35) - force x-offset to 1\n5. Query context state [+0x4] == 0x1\n6. If elemental affix flag (0x47):\n   - Get affix level via Ordinal_10949 (GetAreaId)\n   - Apply Ordinal_10968 (GetFileHandle) affix evaluation\n   - Query stat 0x3d via Ordinal_10996\n   - Add (stat% * offset / 100) to x/y\n7. Repeat for physical affix flag (0x48) with stat 0x3f\n8. Format final string with adjusted offsets\n\nParameters:\npszBuffer (void*) - string pointer for formatting\ndwSkillId (dword) - skill identifier to check against special list\npData (void*) - equipment/unit structure with stat offsets [+0x140, +0x144, +0x148, +0x128, +0xd4]\nnX (int) - (unused, overridden by calculations)\nnY (int) - (unused, overridden by calculations)\n\nReturns:\n0 always (void return)\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset | Size | Field | Type | Description\n+0x128 | 1    | scale | byte | bit shift scale for damage calc\n+0x140 | 1    | alpha | byte | alpha/opacity value\n+0x144 | 4    | offX  | int  | x-offset contribution\n+0x148 | 4    | offY  | int  | y-offset contribution\n+0xd4  | 1    | flags | byte | affix state (0x01=elemental, 0x02=physical)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x128 - shift amount mask (& 0x1f)\n0x144/0x148 - stat offset fields (skill modifier sources)\n0x140 - alpha/opacity field\n0xd4 - affix flag field\n0x47, 0x48 - affix type identifiers\n0x3d, 0x3f - stat indices (0x3d=elemental%, 0x3f=physical%)\n0x51eb851f - magic constant for fixed-point division\n\nNote: Function uses 5-6 stack-allocated temporaries optimized away by compiler (phantom variables)",
