      "comment": "Appends monster skill ID and level-scaled value bonus text to a localization string.\n\nThis function extends a formatted localization string by appending bonus values\nfor monster skill IDs and level-scaled stats. Positive values display with \"+\"\nprefix, negative values display with \"-\" prefix.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call FormatLocalizationString to initialize base output string\n2. Get monster skill ID via GetMonsterSkillId(nMonsterIndex, nStatType)\n3. Initialize 64-element Unicode buffer with default constructors\n4. If skill ID is non-zero:\n   a. Select format string: \"+%d\" for positive, \"%d\" for negative\n   b. Format skill ID to ANSI buffer via wsprintfA\n   c. Convert ANSI to Unicode via toUnicode\n   d. Append localized string 0x10b2 (skill bonus label)\n   e. Append formatted skill ID value\n   f. Append localized string 0x10b3 (separator/suffix)\n   g. Append localized string 0x0f9e (closing bracket/suffix)\n5. Get monster level-scaled value via GetMonsterLevelScaledValue\n6. Re-initialize Unicode buffer with default constructors\n7. If level-scaled value is non-zero:\n   a. Select format string based on sign\n   b. Format value to ANSI buffer\n   c. Convert to Unicode\n   d. Append localized string 0x10a0 (level bonus label)\n   e. Append formatted value\n   f. Append localized string 0x10b3 (separator)\n   g. Append localized string 0x0f9e (closing)\n8. Return 1 (success)\n\nParameters:\n  pUnicodeOutput (ECX): Destination Unicode string buffer to append to\n  nMonsterIndex (EDX): Monster table index for stat lookup\n  nDifficultyLevel: Game difficulty level (Normal/Nightmare/Hell)\n  nStatType: Stat type identifier for bonus calculation\n  nAreaLevel: Area level for scaling calculations\n\nReturns:\n  int: Always returns 1 (success)\n\nString ID Reference:\n  0x10b2: Skill bonus label text\n  0x10b3: Separator/suffix text  \n  0x0f9e: Closing bracket/suffix\n  0x10a0: Level bonus label text\n\nGlobals Referenced:\n  g_szFmtPositiveNumber (0x6fbc6358): \"+%d\" format string\n  g_szFmtSignedNumber (0x6fbb0de4): \"%d\" format string\n  [0x6fba5c40]: Unicode::strcat function pointer\n  [0x6fba5c30]: Unicode::_default_constructor_closure_ function pointer\n  [0x6fba5c34]: Unicode::toUnicode function pointer\n\nDecompiler Notes:\n  unaff_ESI/unaff_EDI shown in decompiler are artifacts - ESI holds\n  pUnicodeOutput throughout, EDI holds strcat function pointer from vtable.",
