      "comment": "Format explosive missile skill description for skill tooltip.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get missile template record for missile ID 0x185 (389 - explosive arrow/bolt)\n2. Initialize Unicode buffer local_80 with 64 default-constructed Unicode chars\n3. Call FormatLocalizationString to build base skill description\n4. Call GetMonsterMaxDamage to get base damage for skill level\n5. Extract missile damage multiplier from template offset +0x0C\n6. Extract missile base offset from template offset +0x08\n7. Assert pSkillDesc->nParam2 (offset +0xF4) is non-zero\n8. Calculate synergy bonus: (nEffectLevel - 1) / pSkillDesc[0xF4] + pSkillDesc[0xF0]\n9. Calculate damage low: (pSkillDesc[0x144] + baseDamage) << shift >> 8\n10. Calculate damage high: (pSkillDesc[0x148] + baseDamage) << shift >> 8\n11. Format damage string: if low==high use \"%d\", else use \"%d-%d\"\n12. Convert damage string to Unicode\n13. Append string IDs 0x10A3, 0x10BE, 0xF9E for localized text parts\n14. Calculate resource string index: multiplier * (nEffectLevel - 1) + baseOffset\n15. Call FormatResourceString with calculated index\n16. Initialize second Unicode buffer aUStack_40 (64 chars)\n17. If synergy bonus non-zero, format and append synergy text with string ID 0x5707\n18. Return 1 (success)\n\nParameters:\n- pUnicodeBuffer (dword *): Output Unicode string buffer passed in ECX\n- nSkillLevel (int): Skill level for damage calculation passed in EDX\n- pSkillDesc (int): Pointer to skill description structure with offsets:\n    +0xF0: synergy base value\n    +0xF4: synergy divisor (asserted non-zero)\n    +0x128: shift amount for damage scaling\n    +0x144: minimum damage modifier\n    +0x148: maximum damage modifier\n- nEffectLevel (int): Effect level for calculations\n- nUnused (int): Unused parameter\n\nReturns:\n- 1: Always returns success\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x185: Missile template ID (389 decimal - explosive missile)\n- 0x20: Buffer size (32 Unicode chars for initialization loop)\n- 0x10A3: String ID for damage label\n- 0x10BE: String ID for separator\n- 0xF9E: String ID for newline/spacing\n- 0x5707: String ID for synergy bonus text\n- 0x1702: Line number for assertion (5890 decimal)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- FogAssert triggered if pSkillDesc[0xF4] is zero (division by zero protection)",
