      "comment": "Callback handler for formatting monster skill display strings.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Forward all parameters to FormatLocalizationString to format the base localized string\n2. Call GetMonsterSkillId with nMonsterId and nSkillSlot to retrieve the skill resource ID\n3. Call FormatResourceString with the skill ID and suffix type 0 (standard format)\n4. Return 1 (success)\n\nParameters:\n- dwIndex (dword, ECX): String context or resource index for localization lookup\n- nMonsterId (int, EDX): Monster type identifier for skill lookup\n- pConfig (void*, Stack+0x4): Pointer to configuration structure with format parameters\n- nSkillSlot (int, Stack+0x8): Skill slot index (0-based) to retrieve skill ID\n- nFormatParam (int, Stack+0xc): Additional format parameter passed to localization\n\nReturns:\n- 1: Always returns success (EAX = 1)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- This function is a callback referenced from function pointer table at 0x6fbc60bc\n- Always returns 1 regardless of callee return values\n- Suffix type is hardcoded to 0 (standard format without plus sign)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x10b0: Resource string ID passed to FormatResourceString (EDX at 0x6fb4a286)\n- 0x0: Suffix type for standard formatting (pushed at 0x6fb4a27d)\n- 0xc: Stack cleanup for 3 stack parameters (RET 0xc)",
