      "comment": "Format monster level-scaled statistics into a localized display string.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call FormatLocalizationString with all parameters to initialize formatting context\n2. Call GetMonsterLevelScaledValue(nMonsterIndex, nScaleFactor) to get resource identifier\n3. Call FormatResourceString with resource ID and suffix type 0 (EDX=0x10b0)\n4. Call GetMonsterLevelScaledStat(nScaleFactor, nMonsterIndex) to compute scaled stat value\n5. Call FormatAndAppendStringValue with stat value (EDX=0x10d6) to append formatted result\n6. Return 1 (success)\n\nParameters:\n- pOutputContext (dword, ECX): Pointer to output string buffer/formatting context\n- nMonsterIndex (int, EDX): Monster type index for stat lookup\n- nStatLevel (int, stack+0x4): Base level value for stat scaling\n- nScaleFactor (int, stack+0x8): Scaling factor applied to stat calculation\n- nFormatMode (int, stack+0xc): Format mode selector passed to localization\n\nReturns:\n- 1: Always returns success\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- This is a worker function that orchestrates multiple string formatting calls\n- Uses __fastcall: first two params in ECX/EDX, rest on stack\n- Stack cleanup: RET 0xc (3 stack parameters × 4 bytes)\n- EDI, ESI, EBX preserved across calls via PUSH/POP\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n- 0x10b0: Resource string ID passed via EDX to FormatResourceString\n- 0x10d6: Resource string ID passed via EDX to FormatAndAppendStringValue\n- 0x0: Suffix type parameter (nSuffixType=0 for standard format)",
