      "comment": "Formats a scaled damage reduction/bonus value into a Unicode tooltip string.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call GetMonsterScaledDamage(nLevel, nMonsterClassId) to compute scaled damage\n2. Initialize 64-character Unicode buffer with default constructors (32 iterations x 2 chars)\n3. Negate the scaled damage value (damage reduction displayed as positive)\n4. If negated value is zero, skip formatting and return 1\n5. Select format string: \"+%d\" if original negative, \"%d\" if positive\n6. Format negated damage value using wsprintfA into ANSI buffer\n7. Convert ANSI buffer to Unicode via Unicode::toUnicode\n8. Validate and append string ID 0x10B1 to output buffer\n9. Append the formatted damage value to output buffer\n10. Validate and append string ID 0x10B3 to output buffer\n11. Validate and append string ID 0xF9E to output buffer\n12. Return 1 (success)\n\nParameters:\nlpwszOutputBuffer - Output Unicode string buffer to append tooltip text (ECX)\nnMonsterClassId - Monster class identifier for damage lookup (EDX)\nnUnused - Unused parameter reserved for future use (Stack+4)\nnLevel - Monster level for damage scaling calculation (Stack+8)\n\nReturns:\nint - Always returns 1 indicating success\n\nSpecial Cases:\nWhen scaled damage is zero, function exits early without modifying output buffer.\nPositive damage (bonus) displays with \"+\" prefix using g_szFmtPlusNumber.\nNegative damage (reduction) displays without prefix using g_szFmtNumber.\n\nString IDs Used:\n0x10B1 - Tooltip label prefix\n0x10B3 - Tooltip separator/suffix\n0x0F9E - Tooltip terminator\n\nDecompiler Discrepancies:\nunaff_ESI and unaff_EDI are decompiler artifacts. Assembly shows ESI holds\nUnicode::strcat function pointer from [0x6fba5c40]. Actual strcat arguments\nare (ECX=lpwszOutputBuffer, EDX=ValidateStringId result).",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_4", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control"]
