      "comment": "Appends monster stat bonus strings (level, skill multipliers) to localized output.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get monster level stat value from GetMonsterLevelStat(nMonsterId, nStatIndex)\n2. Get monster skill ID from GetMonsterSkillId(nMonsterId, nStatIndex)\n3. Call FormatLocalizationString to initialize base output string\n4. Initialize 64-character Unicode buffer with zero values (32 iterations, 2 bytes each)\n5. If level stat value is non-zero:\n   a. Format level value as \"+%d\" (positive) or \"%d\" (negative)\n   b. Append string ID 0x10b2 (level stat label)\n   c. Append formatted level value string\n   d. Append string ID 0x10b3 (separator)\n   e. Append string ID 0x0f9e (line terminator)\n6. Calculate skillId * 3 for triple skill bonus display\n7. Re-initialize Unicode buffer, then if triple bonus is non-zero:\n   a. Format bonus value with sign prefix\n   b. Append string ID 0x5714, value, 0x571a separator, 0x0f9e terminator\n8. Calculate skillId * 2 for double skill bonus display\n9. Re-initialize Unicode buffer, then if double bonus is non-zero:\n   a. Append string ID 0x5713, value, 0x571a separator, 0x0f9e terminator\n10. Re-initialize Unicode buffer, then if single skill bonus (skillId) is non-zero:\n    a. Append string ID 0x5712, value, 0x571a separator, 0x0f9e terminator\n11. Return 1 (success)\n\nParameters:\n  pOutputString (ECX) - Unicode string buffer to append formatted stat strings to\n  nMonsterId (EDX) - Monster type identifier for stat lookup\n  nStatType (Stack+0x4) - Stat category type passed to FormatLocalizationString\n  nStatIndex (Stack+0x8) - Stat index within category for GetMonsterLevelStat/GetMonsterSkillId\n  nUnused (Stack+0xc) - Reused as loop counter internally\n\nReturns:\n  1 - Always returns success (EAX = 1)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Zero stat values are skipped entirely (no string appended)\n  - Negative values use \"%d\" format string (shows minus sign naturally)\n  - Positive values use \"+%d\" format string (explicit plus sign)\n  - Unicode buffer is re-initialized to zero before each stat section\n\nString ID Reference:\n  0x10b2 - Level stat label text\n  0x10b3 - Level stat separator\n  0x5712 - Single skill multiplier label (x1)\n  0x5713 - Double skill multiplier label (x2)\n  0x5714 - Triple skill multiplier label (x3)\n  0x571a - Skill bonus separator\n  0x0f9e - Line terminator (shared across sections)\n\nGlobal References:\n  g_szResourceFormatPlus (0x6fbc6358) - \"+%d\" format for positive values\n  g_szLocalizationConfig (0x6fbb0de4) - \"%d\" format for negative values",
