      "comment": "Formats monster level stat value with localization strings and appends attribute bonuses.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call GetMonsterLevelStat to retrieve monster level stat value for given stat parameter\n2. Call FormatLocalizationString to format base localization with provided parameters\n3. Initialize Unicode buffer array (64 elements, 32 iterations with stride 2)\n4. If monster level stat is non-zero:\n   a. Select format string: \"+%d\" for positive values, \"%d\" for negative values\n   b. Format stat value to ANSI string buffer using wsprintfA\n   c. Convert ANSI to Unicode with toUnicode (max 32 chars)\n   d. Append localization string 0x10B2 (stat prefix) to output\n   e. Append formatted Unicode stat value to output\n   f. Append localization string 0x10B3 (stat suffix) to output\n   g. Append localization string 0x0F9E (level indicator) to output\n5. Append attribute value for ID 0x239 (experience bonus)\n6. Append attribute value for ID 0x238 (damage bonus)\n7. Append attribute value for ID 0x233 (defense bonus)\n8. Return (always returns 1 in EAX)\n\nParameters:\n  pOutputBuffer (ECX): Unicode string buffer to append formatted stats\n  nMonsterData (EDX): Monster data for stat lookup\n  nLocalizationParam (Stack+4): Localization string parameter\n  dwStatParam (Stack+8): Stat parameter ID for GetMonsterLevelStat\n  nExtraParam (Stack+C): Extra parameter passed to FormatLocalizationString\n\nReturns:\n  void (implicit EAX=1 on success)\n\nString IDs:\n  0x10B2 (4274): Monster level stat prefix\n  0x10B3 (4275): Monster level stat suffix  \n  0x0F9E (3998): Level indicator string\n\nAttribute IDs:\n  0x239 (569): Experience bonus attribute\n  0x238 (568): Damage bonus attribute\n  0x233 (563): Defense bonus attribute\n\nFormat Strings:\n  g_szResourceFormatPlus (0x6FBC6358): \"+%d\" - positive stat format\n  g_szLocalizationConfig (0x6FBB0DE4): \"%d\" - negative stat format",
