      "instructions": ["0x7AA00|SUB|ESP, 0x60", "0x7AA03|PUSH|EBX", "0x7AA04|PUSH|EBP", "0x7AA05|PUSH|ESI", "0x7AA06|PUSH|EDI", "0x7AA07|MOV|EBX, EDX", "0x7AA09|MOV|EBP, ECX", "0x7AA0B|LEA|ESI, [ESP + 0x30]", "0x7AA0F|MOV|EDI, 0x20", "0x7AA14|MOV|ECX, ESI", "0x7AA16|CALL|dword ptr [0x6fba5c30]", "0x7AA1C|ADD|ESI, 0x2", "0x7AA1F|DEC|EDI", "0x7AA20|JNZ|0x6fb4aa14", "0x7AA22|PUSH|EBX"],
      "comment": "Format skill/spell attribute value into Unicode string with stat modifiers\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize 64-element Unicode array (128 bytes) for output buffer\n2. Retrieve stat data record via Ordinal_10589(dwValue) \n3. If stat record found:\n   a. Get base stat value via Ordinal_11220(dwValue, nParam3)\n   b. Calculate displayed stat = (record[0xac] + base) << shift >> 8\n   c. If record[0xa8] == 2, override displayed stat to 1\n   d. Format as ANSI string via wsprintfA using format \"%d/%d\"\n   e. Convert ANSI string to Unicode via toUnicode\n   f. Use switch statement to select stat prefix strings based on dwValue\n   g. Call Ordinal_10004 to acquire lock, concatenate strings via strcat\n   h. Unlock via subsequent Ordinal_10004 call\n4. Return 1 (success)\n\nParameters:\nnStatType (ECX, 32-bit): Index/ID of stat type (0x22e, 0x22f, 0x233, 0x238, 0x239)\ndwValue (EDX, 32-bit): Skill/spell ID for looking up stat data record\nnParam3 (Stack +0x4, 32-bit): Parameter value used in calculation\n\nReturns:\n1 - Function always returns 1 (success indicator)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If stat record lookup fails (Ordinal_10589 returns 0), skips formatting and returns\n- Special handling for stat type 0x238+ with different prefix strings\n- Shift amount extracted from record[0x8c] bits 0-4\n- Display stat clamped to 1 if record[0xa8] == 2\n- Note: Function uses 3 unaffected registers (unaff_ESI, unaff_EDI, Unicode pointer this) optimized away by compiler",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Inventory", "PARAM_3", "STRUCT_Room1"]
