      "instructions": ["0x7B9A0|SUB|ESP, 0x14", "0x7B9A3|PUSH|EBX", "0x7B9A4|PUSH|EBP", "0x7B9A5|PUSH|ESI", "0x7B9A6|MOV|ESI, dword ptr [EDX]", "0x7B9A8|PUSH|EDI", "0x7B9A9|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x18], ECX", "0x7B9AD|CALL|0x6fb62880", "0x7B9B2|MOV|EBX, dword ptr [ESP + 0x28]", "0x7B9B6|MOV|EDI, EAX", "0x7B9B8|PUSH|EBX", "0x7B9B9|PUSH|EDI", "0x7B9BA|PUSH|ESI", "0x7B9BB|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x1c], 0x0", "0x7B9C3|CALL|0x6fb98932"],
      "comment": "Render damage/resistance values at screen coordinates with visual adjustments\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Retrieve light level from viewport (FUN_6fb62880)\n2. Calculate base damage X-Y: invoke GetDamageX(light, baseVal, nTargetX), GetDamageY(light, baseVal, nTargetX)\n3. Resolve missile type: invoke GetMissileResistance to fetch from resistance table\n4. If missile exists: multiply base damage by missile resistance factor, store render mode 0x03\n5. Fetch adjustment bonuses: invoke GetResistanceBonus(3 offsets: 0x19, 0x12, 0x11)\n6. Calculate angle adjustment: (bonusX + bonusY_component) * damageFactor / 100\n7. Enumerate resistance table (0x6fba93a8..0x6fba93c0): for each entry:\n   - Check if resistance index exists\n   - Accumulate resistance X/Y contributions\n   - Store render mode 0x03 if any resistance found\n8. Invoke DrawRangeText with final X, Y coordinates, render mode, color parameters\n\nParameters:\nnMissileType (ECX) - missile ID for damage type lookup\npDamageBaseValue (EDX) - pointer to base damage value\nnTargetX (stack) - screen X coordinate\nnTargetY (stack) - screen Y coordinate\nnDisplayMode (stack) - visual display flags\nnColor (stack) - text color index\n\nReturns:\nvoid - directly invokes DrawRangeText to render text on screen\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If missile resistance check fails, skip missile damage calculation\n- If no resistance entries found, render with mode 0x00 instead of 0x03\n- Resistance table iteration uses pointer increments by 8 bytes (dword pairs)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x10 - resistance table entry flag mask\n0x13e - resistance index offset constant\n0xfe - color/display adjustment factor\n0xffffffff - light level default mask\n0x19, 0x12, 0x11 - resistance bonus offset indices\n0x51eb851f - magic constant for fixed-point division (0.31622776...)\n0x6fba93a8 - start of resistance adjustment table\n0x6fba93c0 - end of resistance adjustment table",
      "tags": ["PARAM_6", "STRUCT_Path", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PROP_NOCALLER", "STRUCT_Skill", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
