      "comment": "Calculate viewport coordinate transformation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call GetKeyModifiers to determine offset for key code and panel reference.\n2. Load base X/Y coordinates from configuration structure at offsets 0x144, 0x148.\n3. Add modifier offset to both coordinates.\n4. If all coordinates and offset are zero return success immediately.\n5. Apply bit shift scaling using configuration byte at offset 0x128.\n6. Override X coordinate to 1 if key code is 0x14, 0x31, or 0x35.\n7. Get viewport mode via GetViewportMode function.\n8. If mode is active check first modifier (0x47) and apply damage scaling.\n9. Check second modifier (0x48) and apply damage scaling similarly.\n10. Call FormatLocalizationString to output formatted coordinates to buffer.\n11. Return success code 1.\n\nParameters:\n- szBuffer: Character array for formatted coordinate output.\n- nKeyCode: Key identifier for coordinate override logic.\n- pPanelConfig: Pointer to configuration struct with coordinate and modifier fields.\n- dwPanelRef: Panel reference value passed to modifier functions.\n\nReturns:\n- uint: Always returns 1 indicating successful formatting.",
