      "comment": "FormatMonsterDamageWithAuraBonus - Formats monster damage output with aura bonuses applied.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call FormatLocalizationString with initial parameters\n2. Get base monster max damage and combine with MonStats record offsets +0x144/+0x148\n3. Return early if all damage values are zero\n4. Apply damage shift from offset +0x128 and scale by 256\n5. Override to 1 for certain damage types (0x14=poison, 0x31, 0x35)\n6. Check player for Holy Fire aura (state 0x47, skill 0x3D) and apply percentage bonus\n7. Check player for Holy Freeze aura (state 0x48, skill 0x3F) and apply percentage bonus\n8. Format final damage range with element type to output buffer\n\nParameters:\n  pOutputBuffer - Output buffer for formatted damage string\n  nDamageType - Damage type identifier (0x14=poison, etc.)\n  pMonStatsRecord - Pointer to monster stats record with damage offsets\n  nParam4 - Additional formatting parameter\n  nParam5 - Additional formatting parameter\n\nReturns: void (outputs via pOutputBuffer)",
