      "comment": "Format and apply game effects to display values (width/height)\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call FormatLocalizationString to initialize output buffer with base parameters\n2. Query game state info: Get property values for X (offset 0x144) and Y (offset 0x148)\n3. Calculate base scaled dimensions: shift values by precision bits (offset 0x128), right-shift 8 bits\n4. Check for override conditions: if type is 0x14, 0x31, or 0x35, force X scaling to 1\n5. Retrieve current game context (FUN_6fb62880)\n6. First effect pass: Check if effect flag 0x47 is enabled in game state\n   - If enabled and conditions met (state=0x01 or no state), apply +3D% bonus to scaled dimensions\n7. Second effect pass: Check if effect flag 0x48 is enabled in game state\n   - If enabled and conditions met (state=0x02 or no state), apply +3F% bonus to scaled dimensions\n8. Format final result: Call FormatLocalizationString with adjusted dimensions and alpha (offset 0x140)\n9. Return success (always 1)\n\nParameters:\npBuffer (void *) - IMPLICIT ECX; Output buffer for formatted result\nnType (int) - IMPLICIT EDX; Property/element type identifier (compared against 0x14, 0x31, 0x35)\nnX (int) - Stack[0x4]; X-coordinate or width component\nnOffsetY (int) - Stack[0x8]; Y-offset or scaling parameter\nnY (int) - Stack[0xC]; Y-coordinate or height component\n\nReturns:\ndword - Always returns 1 (success)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Early exit if X=0 AND Y=0 AND offset=0: returns 1 without processing\n- Type override: Resets X scaling to 1 for types 0x14, 0x31, 0x35 (special rendering modes)\n- Conditional effect application depends on state byte at offset 0xD4 (0x01=effect47, 0x02=effect48, 0x00=always apply)\n- Constants 0x3D and 0x3F represent percentage modifiers for each effect\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x144 - Offset for X property value in structure\n0x148 - Offset for Y property value in structure\n0x128 - Offset for scale/precision bits in structure\n0xD4 - Offset for state/effect filter byte\n0x140 - Offset for alpha/transparency value\n0x14, 0x31, 0x35 - Special type identifiers for forced X=1 scaling\n0x3D - Effect 0x47 percentage modifier (61%)\n0x3F - Effect 0x48 percentage modifier (63%)\n0x47, 0x48 - Effect flag identifiers for game state queries\n-0x1 - Wildcard parameter for ordinal calls (match any)\n0x51eb851f - Fixed-point conversion multiplier for division\n0x5 - Right-shift count for fixed-point precision (32 bits)",
