      "comment": "FormatMonsterStatBonusStrings - Formats localized strings showing monster stat bonuses for difficulty levels.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call FormatLocalizationString for base formatting\n2. If difficulty > Normal, calculate scaled stat bonuses from monster data\n3. Format resistance bonus string (offset 0xF8) with +/- prefix\n4. Format damage bonus string (offset 0xF4) with +/- prefix  \n5. Calculate life bonus from monster init stats using frame count\n6. Apply percentage modifier and append life bonus string\n\nParameters:\n  pOutputBuffer - Unicode buffer to receive formatted string\n  nLocStringId - Base localization string ID\n  pMonsterData - Pointer to monster data structure with stat offsets\n  nDifficultyLevel - Game difficulty (1=Normal, 2=Nightmare, 3=Hell)\n  nUnused - Unused parameter\n\nReturns: void (modifies output buffer in place)",
