      "comment": "Builds Unicode skill description string from stat table lookup.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate skill ID against DAT_6fbc5e70 threshold\n2. Compute pointer to skill descriptor table (DAT_6fbc54b0 or PTR_LAB_6fbc5e78)\n3. Check if descriptor table pointer valid, return if NULL\n4. Initialize output Unicode buffer (1320 chars) with default constructor\n5. Initialize temp Unicode buffer (64 chars) for intermediate strings\n6. Query quest completion status via Ordinal_10949/Ordinal_10968\n7. Copy initial skill description to output buffer\n8. For each skill stat (using function pointers in descriptor):\n   - Call stat getter function with skill ID and index\n   - Convert result to localized string via Ordinal_10004/strcat\n   - Append to output buffer\n9. Include quest requirement strings if fQuestActive detected\n10. Finalize description and return\n\nParameters:\n  nSkillId (ECX): skill ID index into descriptor table\n  nParam2 (EDX): parameter for stat level computation\n  dwParam3 (stack): flags or config parameter\n  dwParam4 (stack): additional flags parameter\n  nParam5 (stack): offset adjustment for final quest flag\n\nReturns:\n  void (result written to persistent Unicode buffer via unaffected registers)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Skill ID >= DAT_6fbc5e70: alternate descriptor table via PTR_LAB_6fbc5e78\n  - nParam2=0: skips certain stat lookups\n  - fQuestActive: includes quest requirement strings in output",
