      "comment": "Validate skill effect level configurations across defined ranges.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call FUN_6fb62880 to retrieve active effect configuration\n2. Check global flag g_fSkillEffectValidated - if set, return 1\n3. If no configuration available, return 0\n4. Iterate through skill effect levels 0x6 to 0x9b (6-155 decimal)\n   - Call Ordinal_10949 with -0x1 to select effect by level\n   - If effect found, call Ordinal_10968 to validate effect configuration\n   - If validation succeeds, set g_fSkillEffectValidated flag and return 1\n5. Iterate through skill effect levels 0xdd to 0x118 (221-280 decimal)\n   - Repeat effect selection and validation as steps 4\n   - If validation succeeds, set flag and return 1\n6. Return 0 if all validations fail\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\n1 if valid effect configuration found and validated, flag set\n0 if no valid configuration found after checking all ranges\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Global flag g_fSkillEffectValidated acts as early exit\n- Effect level ranges: [6-155] primary, [221-280] secondary\n- Ordinal calls represent D2Common DLL interactions",
