      "comment": "Build a skill tooltip string in Unicode format for display.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate skill ID against bounds (< 0xdd or mapped table)\n2. If invalid, check range 0xd9-0xdc for special skills, delegate to specific handlers\n3. If valid, allocate local Unicode buffers (aUnicodeBuffer 2640 bytes, aUnicodeTemp 400 bytes)\n4. Initialize all local Unicode strings via default constructor loop\n5. Retrieve skill stat count via Ordinal_10594(nSkillId)\n6. Retrieve player/character data pointer via FUN_6fb62880()\n7. Call skill handler function pointers (*ppFunc[0] and *ppFunc[1]) with (stat_count, nParam3, nParam4)\n8. Build localization format string using wsprintfA with nParam3 as parameter\n9. Append formatted strings to output buffer via repeated strcat/toUnicode calls\n10. If special case (nSkillId == 0), append additional strings\n11. Append stat offset descriptions via GetSkillStatOffset(nSkillId, {0,1})\n12. Query screen metrics via Ordinal_10131 to calculate tooltip Y offset\n13. Render tooltip at final position via Ordinal_10129\n\nParameters:\n- nSkillId (ECX, int): Skill identifier, validated against table bounds\n- pBuffer (EDX, void*): Output buffer for tooltip text (Unicode)\n- nParam3 (stack, int): Skill-specific parameter (format/category identifier)\n- nParam4 (stack, int): Skill-specific parameter (sub-category or index)\n- nParam5 (stack, int): Skill-specific parameter (reserved/unused in main path)\n- nYOffset (stack, int): Y-axis offset for tooltip positioning\n\nReturns:\n- void: Modifies pBuffer in place with formatted skill tooltip text\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Skills 0xd9-0xdc (217-220): Special skill handlers with dedicated formatting\n- Skill ID 0: Additional string appended for base skill\n- Skill IDs >= 0xdd (221+): Mapped to alternate table with bounds check\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0xdd (221): Skill ID boundary for table mapping\n- 0xd8 (216): Lower bound for special skill range\n- 0xd9 (217): First special skill (skill type A)\n- 0xda (218): Second special skill (skill type B)\n- 0xdb (219): Third special skill (skill type C)\n- 0xdc (220): Fourth special skill (skill type D)\n- 0x294 (660): Loop count for aUnicodeBuffer initialization\n- 0x20 (32): Loop count for aUnicodeTemp initialization\n- 0x34 (52): Pixel offset for tooltip positioning (g_dwScreenHeight - 0x34)\n\nStructure Layout:\n- DAT_6fbc54b0: Skill handler function pointer table (base for IDs < 0xdd)\n- PTR_LAB_6fbc5e78: Alternate handler table (base for mapped IDs)\n- DAT_6fbc5e70: Threshold value for skill ID table selection\n- DAT_6fbc6238: Size of alternate handler table\n\nRelated Functions:\n- GetSkillStatOffset(nSkillId, nParam): Retrieve stat definition offset\n- FUN_6fb62880(): Get current player/character context\n- FUN_6fb53a20/80/ae0/b40(): Special skill formatters\n- Ordinal_10594(nSkillId): Get skill stat count\n- Ordinal_10129(y, x, flags): Render tooltip at position\n- Ordinal_10131(array): Query screen dimensions",
