      "comment": "Initialize slider control template with localized text and properties.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate 100 Unicode characters (0xc8 bytes) on stack\n2. Initialize each Unicode character (2 bytes) to zero using loop (100 iterations)\n3. Call Ordinal_10004 (GetDifficulty) to retrieve current game difficulty\n4. Format difficulty string into Unicode buffer using sprintf with template\n5. Call Ordinal_10004 again (second call appears to validate or consume result)\n6. Concatenate property string 1 to Unicode buffer\n7. Concatenate property string 2 to Unicode buffer  \n8. Call Ordinal_10129 with adjusted screen height (g_dwScreenHeight - 0x34) and 0x0, 0x1 parameters\n9. Return void\n\nParameters:\n- dwTemplateId (ECX, uint): Ordinal ID or control template identifier\n- dwProperty (EDX, uint): Additional property/property pointer for slider configuration\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Unicode string initialized to zero before use (memset equivalent via loop)\n- Double Ordinal_10004 call suggests validation or state consumption\n- Screen height offset 0x34 (52 pixels) suggests UI positioning adjustment\n- Calls stdcall functions (strcat, sprintf) compatible with Unicode strings\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n- 0xc8 (200 decimal): Stack allocation size for 100 Unicode chars\n- 0x64 (100 decimal): Loop count for Unicode initialization\n- 0x34 (52 decimal): Vertical offset from screen height for positioning\n- 0x1058: Constant passed to internal function at 0x6fb9981c\n- 0xf9e: Constant passed to internal function at 0x6fb9981c\n\nOrdinals Called:\n- Ordinal_10004: GetDifficulty - Get current game difficulty level (called twice)\n- Ordinal_10129: Unknown - Screen positioning or UI update (y_offset, 0x0, 0x1)",
