      "comment": "Process skill effect string generation and validation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Resolve skill table entry from nSkillId (either standard or extended table)\n2. Validate table pointer is not NULL\n3. Call Ordinal_10594 to get skill index from nSkillId\n4. Initialize Unicode buffers: awSkillString (660 wchars), aUStack_5a8 (64 wchars)\n5. If skill function pointer exists:\n   - If nLevel == 0: Call skill function with level 1, then with level 0 if handler exists\n   - If nLevel != 0: Call skill function with nLevel, then with param_2 if handler exists\n   - For non-zero level: Format level string via wsprintfA + toUnicode\n   - Append strings to szOutputBuffer via strcat\n6. Call GetViewportInfo() to get viewport state\n7. If viewport invalid or scroll mode check fails:\n   - Get skill stat offset + nLevel\n   - Call CallFunctionOnRange on aUStack_568\n   - If computed value non-zero: Format and append string\n8. Append statistical output strings via GetSkillStatOffset(nSkillId, 1) and (nSkillId, 0)\n9. Validate skill effects via ValidateSkillEffectSettings()\n10. Call Ordinal_10131 and Ordinal_10129 to finalize output\n\nParameters:\nIMPLICIT nSkillId (ECX) - uint - Skill ID (< 0xdd = standard, >= 0xdd = extended)\nIMPLICIT nLevel (EDX) - uint - Skill level to process (0-N)\nIMPLICIT pInOutData (Stack[0x4]) - uint * - Pointer to input/output data buffer\nIMPLICIT pOutBuffer (Stack[0x8]) - uint * - Pointer to output buffer\nIMPLICIT nQuality (Stack[0xc]) - uint - Quality level affecting computation\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value, all output via pointer parameters\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Skill ID validation: Returns early if standard table index >= g_dwSkillTableSize\n- Extended table bounds: Only checks extended if ID >= 0xdd\n- NULL handler check: Skips function call if ppfnHandler is NULL\n- Level == 0 path: Calls with level 1 first, then 0 if secondary handler exists\n- Viewport bounds: If viewport invalid, uses alternate computation path\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0xdd: Skill ID threshold for extended table lookup\n- 0x294: Buffer size for awSkillString initialization (0x294 * 2 bytes = 1320 bytes)\n- 0x20: Buffer size for Unicode init loops (64 wchars)\n- 0x10: Skill entry size in standard table (4 pointers)\n- 0x4: Extended table entry stride\n- 0x98: Offset within skill data for stat lookup\n- 0x14: Minimum threshold for viewport validity check\n- 0xf9e, 0x10ad, 0x105b, 0xf9e, 0x1111, 0x1114: Ordinal string IDs (D2Common localization)",
      "tags": ["PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PARAM_5", "STRUCT_ItemData", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
