      "comment": "Renders skill damage and stat information overlay for player character display\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize damage text display offset if needed (random between -6 and -7)\n2. Get current skill ID from game state\n3. Retrieve skill charge amount for current slot\n4. Loop through skill table rows:\n   a. Get skill definition pointer (from base table or extended table based on skill index)\n   b. Check if skill has damage stat (check ppSkillTable[2] != NULL)\n   c. Check if skill has additional stat (check ppSkillTable[3] != NULL)\n   d. If damage stat present, format and display damage value with color\n   e. If extended stat present, call stat handler (ppSkillTable[3]) to format/display\n   f. If both stats present, display formatted damage and additional values\n   g. Handle damage text Y-offset initialization (sets g_nDamageDisplayYOffset)\n5. Advance to next skill row (increment pointers by 0x24 bytes)\n6. Exit when X position reaches boundary (0x6fbc62d8)\n\nParameters:\n(none)\n\nReturns:\n(void)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- First initialization: randomly selects damage display Y offset between -6/-7 based on game tick\n- Skill index > 0xDD requires extended skill table lookup with bounds checking\n- Double pointer dereference for skill definition (ppSkillTable[2], ppSkillTable[3])\n- Skill charge amount 0 skips damage display for non-primary skills\n- Damage text color varies by skill index (0=default, color stored in dwChargeAmount)\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x02, 0x04, 0x06, 0x08 - Skill types requiring damage display\n0xDD (221) - Skill table size threshold, triggers extended table lookup\n0xFFF9/-7, 0xFFFA/-6 - Y offset adjustments for damage text positioning\n0x1E0 (480) - Screen offset baseline for UI positioning\n0x24 (36) - Size of skill row entry in display array\n0x20 (32) - Unicode string buffer size\n0xC8 (200) - Display buffer capacity\n",
      "tags": ["MOD_UI", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "STRUCT_ItemData", "PARAM_0", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData", "STRUCT_StatList", "PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Path", "UI_SKILLS", "SRC_SkillDesc.cpp", "STRUCT_Skill", "TBL_skilldesc", "PROP_LOOPHEAVY"]
