      "instructions": ["0x7E9C0|SUB|ESP, 0x10", "0x7E9C3|PUSH|EBX", "0x7E9C4|PUSH|EBP", "0x7E9C5|PUSH|ESI", "0x7E9C6|PUSH|EDI", "0x7E9C7|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0x7E9C9|CALL|0x6fb62880", "0x7E9CE|MOV|EDI, EAX", "0x7E9D0|TEST|ESI, ESI", "0x7E9D2|PUSH|EDI", "0x7E9D3|JZ|0x6fb4e9dc", "0x7E9D5|CALL|0x6fb98a88", "0x7E9DA|JMP|0x6fb4e9e1", "0x7E9DC|CALL|0x6fb98a82", "0x7E9E1|MOV|ESI, EAX"],
      "comment": "Retrieves skill table record for a given skill type or ID (Ordinal_10321=GetPlayerData, Ordinal_10322=GetMonsterData, Ordinal_10963=GetSkillData, Ordinal_10966=ResourceInit, Ordinal_10968=GetFileHandle)\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get base unit pointer via GetSkillData()\n2. Branch on skillType parameter to select skill lookup method\n   - param == 0: Call GetMonsterData for class-based lookup\n   - param != 0: Call GetPlayerData for inventory-based lookup\n3. Initialize graphics/sound system via ResourceInit ordinal\n4. Transform skill with GetFileHandle() passing unit, skill ID, and flag 1\n5. Get skill table index via GetSkillData()\n6. Branch on table index value:\n   - If index < g_dwSkillTableSize: use main skill table at g_pSkillTableBase + index*16\n   - Else: subtract 0xDD from index, check extended table\n     - If result < 0 or >= g_dwSkillExtendedCount: set ppSkillTable = NULL\n     - Else: use extended table PTR_LAB_6fbc5e78 + index*4\n7. If table pointer valid and callback function (ppSkillTable[3]) present:\n   - Call callback with transformed unit, dwParam1 ptr, abTempBuffer1 array, dwParam2 ptr\n   - Return abTempBuffer2 buffer pointer\n8. If no valid callback, return NULL\n\nParameters:\n  skillType (ECX): Skill type/ID selector (0=class-based, non-zero=inventory-based) IMPLICIT\n\nReturns:\n  void *: Pointer to skill record buffer or NULL if table/callback not found\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Multiple ordinal calls to Storm.dll for skill lookup and initialization\n  - Extended skill table with 0xDD offset mapping between ID ranges\n  - Stack-allocated temp buffers passed to callback function\n  \nMagic Numbers:\n  0xDD (221 dec): Offset between primary and extended skill table index ranges\n  0x10 (16 dec): Size of skill table entry\n  0x4 (4 dec): Size of extended table pointer entry",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PARAM_1", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
