      "comment": "Validate and process current skill tree slot data.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load current skill slot index from g_byCurrentSkillSlot\n2. Calculate offset into skill tree chart (index * 0x2a bytes per slot)\n3. Check if skill tree chart entry exists at calculated offset\n4. If NULL (skill not initialized):\n   a. Call Ordinal_10023 (Storm assertion) with error location\n   b. Terminate process with FUN_6fb9a10f(-1)\n5. If valid:\n   a. Call FUN_6fb5a050 to process the skill slot data\n   b. Store processed result in g_aSkillTreeSlots at same slot offset\n\nParameters:\nNone (uses global g_byCurrentSkillSlot)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - terminates process on assertion failure, otherwise returns after storing result\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Function has no return on assertion path (non-returning branch via FUN_6fb9a10f)\n- Slot offset calculation: (index * 8 - index) * 3 = index * 21 = index * 0x15 (simplified to index * 0x2a in pointer context)\n- Magic number 0x2a: size of skill tree slot structure",
