      "comment": "Clear the error state flag for the current slot.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load current slot index from g_byCurrentSlotIndex (byte value)\n2. Calculate array offset: (index * 8) - index = index * 7, then multiply by 2 for dword offset\n3. Read error code from g_pSlotErrorArray at calculated offset\n4. If error code is non-zero, call ReportValidationError to log error\n5. Clear error code to 0 at same offset\n\nParameters:\n  (none)\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nNotes:\n  - Slot error array uses stride of 0x2A (42) bytes per entry (calculated from assembly as (index*7)*2 = 14x offset, scaled in context)\n  - Uses byte-load optimization in assembly (MOV CL, byte) to avoid zero-extending full dword\n  - Function is called when validating/finalizing slot states",
