      "instructions": ["0x7EB30|SUB|ESP, 0x20", "0x7EB33|PUSH|EBX", "0x7EB34|PUSH|EBP", "0x7EB35|PUSH|ESI", "0x7EB36|PUSH|EDI", "0x7EB37|CALL|0x6fb62880", "0x7EB3C|MOV|EBX, EAX", "0x7EB3E|LEA|ESI, [ESP + 0x1c]", "0x7EB42|MOV|EDI, 0xa", "0x7EB47|MOV|ECX, ESI", "0x7EB49|CALL|dword ptr [0x6fba5c30]", "0x7EB4F|ADD|ESI, 0x2", "0x7EB52|DEC|EDI", "0x7EB53|JNZ|0x6fb4eb47", "0x7EB55|PUSH|0x5"],
      "comment": "Initializes and processes game object attributes based on quest mode\nValidates each game object against current quest mode and applies appropriate\nstate and flag values for rendering and interaction\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call FUN_6fb62880 to get active source/entity ID\n2. Extract field at offset 5 from source via Ordinal_10521 (D2Common.GetUnitStat)\n3. Convert extracted value to Unicode string using wsprintfA and toUnicode\n4. Check graphics mode (g_dwGraphicsMode) to determine render mode (0x80 flag)\n5. Iterate through 0x1E (30) objects from g_pObjectArray\n6. For each object, validate dwCurrentQuestMode matches object's quest field at +0xD4\n7. If modes match:\n   - Call Ordinal_10988 (D2Common.ProcessObjectState) for base attributes\n   - If failed (0): Set state[idx]=0xFFFFFFFF, flags[idx]=5\n   - Call Ordinal_10949 (D2Common.GetObjectHandle) to check state validity\n   - Apply Ordinal_10968 (D2Common.HandleOperation) or Ordinal_10989 as needed\n   - If passed: Validate handle via Ordinal_10949, apply appropriate modification\n8. Call FUN_6fb4ed10 with computed state/flags for each object\n\nParameters:\n(void) - No explicit parameters; uses global data:\n  g_dwScreenHeight, g_dwUIYOffset - Viewport dimensions for offset calculation\n  g_dwGraphicsMode - Rendering mode selector (0=software, else=hardware)\n  g_pObjectArray - Array of game object pointers\n  g_dwCurrentQuestMode - Current quest mode (mode selector)\n  g_adObjectState - Array of object state values (32-bit each)\n  g_adObjectFlags - Array of object flag values (32-bit each)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No explicit return value; modifies global object state/flags arrays\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Objects not matching quest mode are skipped (no state modification)\n- Invalid source ID (0) returns graphics mode check only, no object processing\n- Invalid graphics mode selector causes early return before processing\n- State value 0xFFFFFFFF indicates uninitialized/error state\n- Flag value 5 indicates pending/error condition requiring retry\n\nNote: Function uses 3 stack-allocated temporaries optimized away (iVar1, iVar2, uVar3)",
