      "instructions": ["0x7F010|SUB|ESP, 0x20", "0x7F013|PUSH|EBX", "0x7F014|PUSH|EBP", "0x7F015|PUSH|ESI", "0x7F016|PUSH|EDI", "0x7F017|CALL|0x6fb62880", "0x7F01C|MOV|EBP, EAX", "0x7F01E|MOV|EAX, [0x6fbfc8c8]", "0x7F023|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0x7F025|JNZ|0x6fb4f096", "0x7F027|LEA|ESI, [ESP + 0x1c]", "0x7F02B|MOV|EDI, 0xa", "0x7F030|MOV|ECX, ESI", "0x7F032|CALL|dword ptr [0x6fba5c30]", "0x7F038|ADD|ESI, 0x2"],
      "comment": "Initialize and process quest objects to synchronize game state.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get server ID for object synchronization from GetGameServerID()\n2. If quest objects not yet initialized (g_nQuestObjectInitialized == 0):\n   a. Initialize 10 Unicode string buffers for object names (local_14[10])\n   b. Format localization config string with wsprintfA\n   c. Convert formatted string to Unicode with toUnicode()\n   d. Draw centered text at calculated screen position\n3. Iterate through all 30 objects (0x1e = 30):\n   a. Get object data pointer from g_pObjectArray[nIdx] via Ordinal_10594\n   b. Check if object's mode matches current quest mode\n   c. If match:\n      - Initialize object state to 0xFFFFFFFF and flags to 5\n      - Query object animation state with Ordinal_10949(0xFFFFFFFF)\n      - If animation exists (nObjectID != 0):\n        * Fetch animation update data via Ordinal_10968(dwServerID, nObjectID, 1)\n        * If result > 0: reset state to 0, flags to 0\n      - Call ProcessQuestObjectAnimation() to handle update\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Initialization flag checked on first call prevents redundant UI display\n- Magic value 0xFFFFFFFF used to query animation state validity\n- 30-object iteration hardcoded (0x1e), assumes fixed array size\n- Object mode comparison at offset +0xD4 requires specific object structure\n- Flags reset (5 -> 0) only if animation update succeeds\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x1E (30) - number of quest objects to process\n0xD4 (212) - offset of quest mode field in object structure\n0xFFFFFFFF - sentinel value for animation state query\n5 - initial object flags value\n-0x41 (65 decimal) - X-axis offset for centered text\n-0x19 (25 decimal) - width adjustment for centered text\n-400 - Y-axis offset relative to screen height",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PARAM_0", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
