      "api_count": 13,
      "api_calls": ["SetActiveFont", "GfxInterfaceCall84", "GfxInterfaceCall84", "GfxInterfaceCall84", "GfxInterfaceCall84", "GfxInterfaceCall84", "GfxInterfaceCall84", "GfxInterfaceCall84", "GfxInterfaceCall84", "GetUnitStatById", "...+3 more"],
      "instructions": ["0x7F150|SUB|ESP, 0x48", "0x7F153|PUSH|EBX", "0x7F154|PUSH|EBP", "0x7F155|PUSH|ESI", "0x7F156|PUSH|EDI", "0x7F157|CALL|0x6fb62880", "0x7F15C|MOV|ECX, 0x1", "0x7F161|MOV|EBX, EAX", "0x7F163|CALL|0x6fb99a02", "0x7F168|MOV|ECX, 0x12", "0x7F16D|XOR|EAX, EAX", "0x7F16F|LEA|EDI, [ESP + 0x10]", "0x7F173|MOV|EDX, dword ptr [0x6fbae0e8]", "0x7F179|STOSD.REP|ES:EDI", "0x7F17B|XOR|ECX, ECX"],
      "comment": "Render the quest mode skill tree UI with four main skill slots and quest-specific mode indicators.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize local 18-int array for UI slot parameters\n2. Clear array with REP STOSD (0x12 dwords)\n3. Set UI rendered flag (g_bSkillUIRendered = 1)\n4. Populate slot array with skill tree data from g_aSkillTreeSlots\n5. Call Ordinal_10072 four times to render main skill slots at specific screen offsets\n6. Multiply quest mode by 4 for skill offset calculation\n7. Render four quest-mode-specific slots via Ordinal_10072\n8. Load object array pointers from g_aSkillTreeObjectSizes and calculate array end\n9. Call RenderQuestObjectContainer() to setup quest object rendering\n10. Query active quest state via Ordinal_10521 (returns bit flags)\n11. Branch based on quest state: inactive zeros g_bActiveQuestObjectRenderer, active sets to 1\n12. Call appropriate handler (ProcessGameObjectAttributes or RenderDefaultObjects)\n13. Load quest UI mode from g_dwQuestUIMode table indexed by quest/slot\n14. Compare mode (-0x95, -0xdc, -0x131) to update mode state\n15. Clear array again and load cursor context via FUN_6fb5e380\n16. Calculate UI element position based on g_bQuestModeUIActive flag (add 10 or 11)\n17. Render cursor context at offset position\n18. Branch on quest UI mode: 1=bounds check, 2-3=collision test via FUN_6fb53330\n19. If bounds/collision pass: fetch colors via Ordinal_10004/Ordinal_10129, render cursor\n20. If all branches fail: skip rendering (jump to LAB_6fb4f5f5)\n21. Call FUN_6fb4fd90 with current quest mode to finalize rendering\n22. Return\n\nParameters:\n(none - void, uses global game state exclusively)\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Phantom stack temporaries: local_3c, local_40, local_44 optimized away\n- Array-based UI model: slot parameters in array[0-3] = slot index, array[1] = skill offset, array[2] = mode, array[3] = reserved\n- Magic values: 0x140, 0x40, 0x30, 0xe0, 0x3f, 0x62 are pixel offsets for UI positioning\n- Quest mode values: -0x95=mode1, -0xdc=mode2, -0x131=mode3, mapped via g_dwQuestUIMode\n- Cursor bounds: 0x95 pixels wide, 0x22 pixels tall, positioned relative to quest mode UI\n\nRelated Functions:\n- ProcessGameObjectAttributes() - handles active quest object rendering\n- FUN_6fb4f010() - handles inactive quest state\n- FUN_6fb5e380() - loads cursor position context\n- FUN_6fb53330() - performs collision/bounds testing\n- FUN_6fb4fd90() - finalizes quest mode UI rendering",
      "tags": ["PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Path", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "STRUCT_Skill", "PARAM_0", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
