      "instructions": ["0x7FD50|MOV|EAX, [0x6fbdc014]", "0x7FD55|PUSH|ESI", "0x7FD56|MOV|ESI, dword ptr [0x6fbfd7fc]", "0x7FD5C|PUSH|0x0", "0x7FD5E|SUB|EAX, ESI", "0x7FD60|MOV|ESI, dword ptr [0x6fbfd800]", "0x7FD66|PUSH|ECX", "0x7FD67|MOV|ECX, dword ptr [0x6fbae0e8]", "0x7FD6D|ADD|ESI, ECX", "0x7FD6F|PUSH|EAX", "0x7FD70|LEA|ECX, [EAX + -0x5a]", "0x7FD73|LEA|EDX, [ESI + EDX*0x1 + 0xfffffe20]", "0x7FD7A|CALL|0x6faf9b10", "0x7FD7F|POP|ESI", "0x7FD80|RET|"],
      "comment": "Draw a centered UI text line at the specified vertical offset.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Retrieve current back buffer height from global g_dwBackBufferHeight\n2. Retrieve UI X offset from global g_dwUIXOffset\n3. Calculate X coordinate: (g_dwBackBufferHeight - g_dwUIXOffset) - 0x5a\n4. Retrieve UI Y offset from global g_dwUIYOffset\n5. Retrieve screen height from global g_dwScreenHeight\n6. Calculate Y coordinate: g_dwUIYOffset + g_dwScreenHeight - 0x1e0 + nYOffset\n7. Retrieve width from global g_dwBackBufferHeight - g_dwUIXOffset\n8. Call DrawCenteredText with calculated position, width, text, and flags (0)\n\nParameters:\nlpszText (wchar_t*) - Wide string containing the text to display\nnYOffset (int) - Vertical offset to add to the calculated Y position\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Nothing returned\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Y coordinate calculation uses magic number 0x1e0 (480 decimal) for UI baseline offset\n- X coordinate uses 0x5a (90 decimal) for center adjustment\n- Text always drawn with flags=0 (no special formatting)\n- Relies on global variables for positioning (UI coordinate system)",
      "tags": ["PARAM_2", "PROP_SMALL"]
    },
