      "instructions": ["0x7FD90|SUB|ESP, 0x78", "0x7FD93|PUSH|EBX", "0x7FD94|PUSH|EBP", "0x7FD95|PUSH|ESI", "0x7FD96|PUSH|EDI", "0x7FD97|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x20], ECX", "0x7FD9B|CALL|0x6fb8f680", "0x7FDA0|MOV|EBX, EAX", "0x7FDA2|CALL|0x6fb8f690", "0x7FDA7|MOV|ESI, EAX", "0x7FDA9|LEA|EDI, [ESP + 0x24]", "0x7FDAD|MOV|EBP, 0x32", "0x7FDB2|MOV|ECX, EDI", "0x7FDB4|CALL|dword ptr [0x6fba5c30]", "0x7FDBA|ADD|EDI, 0x2"],
      "comment": "Perform hit detection for quest mode skill panel UI at current mouse position.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize local Unicode string buffer (100 wide characters) for text operations\n2. Query current mouse screen coordinates via FUN_6fb8f680/FUN_6fb8f690\n3. Call Ordinal_10034 (Storm dll) to get UI button display state\n4. Validate X coordinate: verify mouse is within right edge boundary (screen_width - ui_offset - 0x59)\n5. Based on nMode parameter (1/2/3), check mouse Y coordinate against mode-specific panel bounds:\n   - Mode 1 (main skill panel): Y in range [ui_offset-0x108+height, ui_offset-0x9c+height]\n   - Mode 2 (alternate panel 2): Y in range [ui_offset-0x174+height, ui_offset-0x108+height] OR [ui_offset-0x30+height, ui_offset-0x9c+height]\n   - Mode 3 (alternate panel 3): Y in range [ui_offset-0x9c+height, ui_offset-0x30+height]\n6. Set corresponding boolean flags (fIsSkillMode, fIsSpellMode, fIsSpecialMode) and store Y offset in iVar7\n7. Call Ordinal_10127 (cleanup call)\n8. If fHasTarget (any mode matched):\n   - Draw background panel at calculated position via FUN_6fb92980\n   - For each active mode flag, call Ordinal_10004 (retrieve mode text) and render via DrawCenteredText\n9. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\nnMode (int, ECX): Panel mode selector (1=Skill, 2=Alternate, 3=Special)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Function performs UI rendering as side effect\n\nSpecial Cases:\nMagic number 0x59: panel width offset\nMagic number 0x9c: Y offset for skill panel top bound (negative from ui_offset)\nMagic number 0x108: Y offset for skill panel bottom bound (negative)\nMagic number 0x174: Y offset for alternate panel 2 bottom (negative)\nMagic number 0x30: Y offset for alternate panel 3 boundary (negative)\nMagic number 0x5a: panel width in pixels (90)\nMagic number 0x14: text row height (20 pixels)",
      "tags": ["PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PARAM_1", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
    },
