      "comment": "Process mouse input for quest UI panel interaction and skill UI\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract X,Y coordinates from event data (word at +0xC for X, bits 16-31 for Y)\n2. Get resource handle via FUN_6fb62880()\n3. Process event coordinates via FUN_6fb8f010()\n4. Validate coordinates via ValidateCoordinateInBounds() - if result != 0, invalid\n5. Check g_bSkillUIRendered: if 0, clear targeting state, set flags, return\n6. Check g_bQuestModeUIActive: if 0, check X coordinate >= screen_width/2\n   - Call Ordinal_10521 to query resource value\n   - Iterate 30 object slots, retrieve each via Ordinal_10594\n   - Match current quest mode, validate panel Y position (modes 1-6 use different offsets)\n   - Validate panel X bounds based on panel type (Ordinal_10487)\n   - If click hits panel: call FUN_6fb5d370(4,2,0), trigger graphics update\n7. If g_bQuestModeUIActive: check quest UI mode (1/2/3) versus panel bounds\n   - Call FUN_6fb8f680/FUN_6fb8f690 to get mouse coords\n   - Compare against hardcoded X/Y offsets per mode\n   - If OUT OF BOUNDS: call FUN_6fb5d370(4,2,0)\n8. Set event flags at +0x18=1, +0x1C=0\n9. Call Ordinal_511() finalizer\n10. Return void\n\nParameters:\npEventData (EventData *) - Input event structure, contains:\n  [+0xC] = Packed coordinates (word X, word Y from bits 16-31)\n  [+0x18] = Event status flags (set to 1 on success)\n  [+0x1C] = Result code (set to 0 on success)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Returns via early exit if validation fails\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Quest panel Y offsets vary by type: 0x1a2, 0x15e, 0x11a, 0xd6, 0x91, 0x4d\n- Panel X offsets also vary: 0x131, 0xec, 0xa7\n- State arrays reset after successful panel click (g_adObjectState, g_adObjectFlags)\n- Multiple quest UI modes require separate bounds checking (1/2/3)",
      "tags": ["PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PROP_NOCALLER", "STRUCT_Skill", "PARAM_1", "PROP_LOOPHEAVY", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
