      "instructions": ["0x809B0|PUSH|EDI", "0x809B1|MOV|ECX, 0x6fbc66a0", "0x809B6|CALL|0x6fb5a050", "0x809BB|MOV|[0x6fbfce14], EAX", "0x809C0|XOR|EAX, EAX", "0x809C2|MOV|AL, [0x6fbe9194]", "0x809C7|MOV|ECX, EAX", "0x809C9|SHL|ECX, 0x4", "0x809CC|ADD|ECX, EAX", "0x809CE|LEA|ECX, [ECX*0x2 + 0x6fbc65b4]", "0x809D5|CALL|0x6fb5a050", "0x809DA|XOR|ECX, ECX", "0x809DC|MOV|EDI, 0x6fbfcd00", "0x809E1|MOV|CL, byte ptr [0x6fbe9194]", "0x809E7|MOV|EDX, ECX"],
      "comment": "Initialize skill UI state by caching skill icon and clearing render buffers.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load main window render target from skill icon sprite sheet\n2. Load current skill icon based on selected skill slot\n3. Cache skill icon in global array indexed by slot\n4. Clear four 0x10-sized render target arrays to 0xFFFFFFFF (transparent)\n5. Clear main state buffer (0xF1 dwords) to 0x00 (zero), then final byte\n6. Clear skill UI render target array (0x3C dwords) to 0xFFFFFFFF\n7. Zero four state flag values\n\nParameters:\n(none)\n\nReturns:\n(void)\n\nSpecial Cases:\nNote: Function uses 2 stack-allocated temporaries optimized away (SSA variables regenerated at decompilation).\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x22: Skill slot stride for array indexing\n- 0x10: Size of render target arrays (16 dwords = 64 bytes)\n- 0xF1: Main state buffer size (241 dwords + 1 byte = 965 bytes)\n- 0x3C: Skill UI render target size (60 dwords = 240 bytes)\n- 0xFFFFFFFF: Default render target fill value (transparent)\n- 0x00: Clear state value (zero)",
