      "comment": "Retrieves cached skill icon data from the skill icon cache array.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. If pSkillId is NULL, calculate slot index from g_byCurrentSkillSlot (multiply by 0x22 bytes per entry)\n2. If pSkillId is provided, call Ordinal_11008 (D2Common.GetSkillInfo) to get skill index\n3. Validate skill index is in range [0, 7)\n4. Calculate cache entry offset: index * 0x22 (34 bytes per skill entry)\n5. Check if cache entry is initialized (zero means uninitialized)\n6. If not cached, load icon data from skill table offset 0x6fbc65b4 + offset\n7. Store loaded data in cache g_aSkillIconCache + offset\n8. Return cached icon data\n\nParameters:\npSkillId (dword *) - Optional pointer to skill ID; if NULL uses current skill slot\nIMPLICIT ECX (const/input register) - param_1 input in __fastcall\n\nReturns:\ndword - Cached skill icon data (color or texture ID), or g_pMainWindowRenderTarget if skill index out of range\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Invalid skill index: returns g_pMainWindowRenderTarget as fallback\n- NULL parameter triggers use of g_byCurrentSkillSlot (global current skill selection)\n- Cache is lazily populated on first access\n- Note: Function uses 2 stack-allocated temporaries optimized away by compiler\n\nOrdinals:\n- Ordinal_11008 (D2Common.GetSkillInfo) - Validates and returns skill index\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x22 (34 decimal) - Bytes per skill entry in cache\n0x6fbc65b0 - Base address of g_aSkillIconCache array\n0x6fbc65b4 - Base address of skill icon source table (offset +4 from cache base)\n0x7 (7 decimal) - Maximum valid skill index (0-6 allowed, 7 invalid)",
      "tags": ["UI_SKILLS", "PARAM_1"]
    },
