      "comment": "Validate panel state and translate ordinal return codes to UI status codes.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call Ordinal_10964 with panel state and sub-state parameters\n2. Store ordinal return value in nResult\n3. Test if ordinal returned 0 (success case)\n4. If nResult is 0, return 0 (panel state valid)\n5. If nResult is non-zero (error case), perform code translation\n6. Subtract 6 from nResult to check if equal to zero\n7. Negate result and sign-extend to conditional flag\n8. AND with 0xFD bitmask for translation logic\n9. Add 4 to produce final error code\n10. Return translated error code (4 for nResult==6, 6 for others)\n\nParameters:\n  dwPanelState: Panel type/index (passed to Ordinal_10964 via ECX register)\n  dwSubState: Panel sub-state value (passed to Ordinal_10964 via EDX register)\n\nReturns:\n  int: 0 if panel state valid, 4 if ordinal returned 6, 6 if ordinal returned other error code\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Error translation: Ordinal_10964 returns 6 gets translated to UI code 4\n  - Generic error: Any non-6 return translates to code 6\n  - Success path: Zero return passes through unchanged\n  - Uses fastcall convention with parameters in ECX/EDX registers",
