      "comment": "Validates cursor position against bounding rectangle and conditionally renders tooltip.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call FUN_6fb8f680 to get current cursor X coordinate, store in nCursorX\n2. Call FUN_6fb8f690 to get current cursor Y coordinate, store in nCursorY\n3. Check if cursor outside bounding box: if (nCursorX < nMinX || nCursorX > nMinX+0x30 || nCursorY < nMinY-0x30 || nCursorY > nMinY)\n4. If outside bounds: pbResult = pointer to DAT_00000001 (invalid/null marker)\n5. If inside bounds: pbResult = (nCheckMode == 1) ? 1 : 0 (cast to byte pointer)\n6. Call FUN_6fb8f680 again to verify cursor X coordinate\n7. Call FUN_6fb8f690 again to verify cursor Y coordinate\n8. Check if cursor within validated bounds: if (nMinX <= nCursorX <= nMinX+0x30 AND nMinY-0x30 <= nCursorY <= nMinY)\n9. If within bounds, call BuildSkillTooltip with pPanelData dereference, pbResult flag, dwValue1, dwValue2, nMinX, nMinY\n10. Return void\n\nParameters:\npPanelData (int *) - Pointer to panel data structure containing skill/tooltip information\nnCheckMode (int) - Flag indicating check mode (1 = validate, other = clear)\ndwValue1 (uint) - First parameter passed to BuildSkillTooltip if validation succeeds\ndwValue2 (uint) - Second parameter passed to BuildSkillTooltip if validation succeeds\nnMinX (int) - Minimum X coordinate of bounding rectangle\nnMinY (int) - Minimum Y coordinate of bounding rectangle\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Magic number 0x30 (48 decimal): bounding box height/width tolerance in pixels\n- Function performs two validation passes with cursor re-read for consistency\n- pbResult is a flag pointer that indicates validation status to BuildSkillTooltip\n- DAT_00000001 address used as sentinel value for out-of-bounds condition\n- BuildSkillTooltip called only when both validation passes succeed\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x30 = 48 decimal, bounding box offset/tolerance in pixels",
