      "comment": "Initialize keybinding text display by copying binding string to Unicode buffer and applying width constraints.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Query keybinding for command ID 1 via LookupKeyBindingByCommandId\n2. If binding exists (not 0xFFFF), initialize 200-element Unicode array with default constructors\n3. Retrieve keybinding string ID and copy to destination buffer\n4. Calculate string length after copy\n5. Get width measurement via Ordinal_10121\n6. If width exceeds 0x28 (40), backfill from string end with nulls until width fits\n7. Call Ordinal_10121 final check\n8. Execute Ordinal_10117 (system time) with dwUnknown1, dwUnknown2, 0\n\nParameters:\n- this: Keybinding configuration object (IMPLICIT in ECX, cannot be renamed - __thiscall auto-parameter)\n- dwUnknown1: First parameter passed to Ordinal_10117\n- dwUnknown2: Second parameter passed to Ordinal_10117\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If keybinding not found (0xFFFF), function returns early without processing\n- Width constraint is 0x28 (40 units); excess text is truncated from end\n- Unicode strings use 2-byte element size\n- Unaffected register parameters (unaff_ESI, unaff_EDI) are from calling function context\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0xFFFF: Invalid/not-found keybinding sentinel\n- 100: Number of Unicode elements to initialize (200 byte buffer / 2)\n- 0x28: Width constraint threshold (40)\n- 0x1: Command ID being queried (hardcoded)\n\nRelated Functions:\n- LookupKeyBindingByCommandId: Validate keybinding exists\n- GetKeyBindingStringId: Retrieve string resource ID\n- Ordinal_10121: Width measurement (likely GetTextWidth)\n- Ordinal_10117: System time operation",
