      "instructions": ["0x80CE0|SUB|ESP, 0x178", "0x80CE6|PUSH|EBX", "0x80CE7|MOV|EBX, EDX", "0x80CE9|XOR|EAX, EAX", "0x80CEB|PUSH|EBP", "0x80CEC|MOV|AL, byte ptr [EBX + 0xd7]", "0x80CF2|PUSH|ESI", "0x80CF3|PUSH|EDI", "0x80CF4|MOV|EBP, ECX", "0x80CF6|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x10], EAX", "0x80CFA|CALL|0x6fb8f680", "0x80CFF|MOV|ESI, EAX", "0x80D01|CALL|0x6fb8f690", "0x80D06|MOV|ECX, dword ptr [ESP + 0x198]", "0x80D0D|CMP|ESI, ECX"],
      "comment": "Render an inventory item (cursor drag support).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load item state byte from inventory node at offset 0xd7\n2. Get current mouse coordinates via FUN_6fb8f680/FUN_6fb8f690\n3. Check if mouse is within rendering region (param_6±0x30 x param_7±0x30)\n4. Adjust render mode based on nParam (0=normal, 1=keep, other=mode 4)\n5. Initialize 18-dword structure for Ordinal_10073 call with item ID and state\n6. Call Ordinal_10073 (D2Common rendering API) with structure, coordinates, flags\n7. Branch on nUseAltRender: 0=normal FUN_6fb51940, 1=alternate FUN_6fb50f20\n8. Get current game state from FUN_6fb62880\n9. If game state valid:\n   - Check inventory type (*pInventoryNode):\n     - Type 2: Query item via Ordinal_10258/10759/10767, get property 0x46\n     - Type 4: Query dual items via Ordinal_10257, select valid path, get property 0x46\n10. Initialize Unicode buffer (200 chars) via loop with constructor closure\n11. If dwParam > 0:\n    - Convert param value to ANSI string via FUN_6fb9adee(dwParam, szAnsiBuffer, 10)\n    - Convert ANSI to Unicode via toUnicode\n    - Get Unicode string length via Ordinal_10121\n    - If string length > 0x28: truncate from end via loop\n12. Calculate final string position (nOffsetY - 1) at x-coord 3\n13. Call Ordinal_10117 Unicode rendering with calculated position and 0 flag\n\nParameters:\n  dwItemId (ECX) - Inventory item identifier/index\n  pInventoryNode (EDX) - Pointer to inventory structure; +0xd7 = item state byte\n  nScreenX (stack) - Screen X coordinate baseline\n  dwParam (stack) - Item property value (converted to decimal string if >0)\n  nParam (stack) - Render mode modifier (0/1 normal, 4 alternate)\n  nOffsetX (stack) - Base X coordinate for rendering region\n  nOffsetY (stack) - Base Y coordinate for rendering region  \n  nUseAltRender (stack) - Branch flag: 0=normal render, nonzero=alternate render\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If nParam is 0 or 1: mode unchanged; else normalized to 4\n  - If game state unavailable: dwParam unchanged\n  - If dwParam is 0 or negative: Unicode buffer only constructor initialized (no string)\n  - If Unicode length > 0x28 (40 dec): string truncated from end to fit\n  - Inventory type 2 vs 4: different property query chains (one vs dual items)\n  - Note: Function uses 5 SSA temporaries (puVar5, pcVar2, pUVar4, sVar3, iVar1) optimized away by compiler\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0xd7 - Offset of item state byte in inventory node\n  0x30 - Pixel tolerance for region boundary check (±48 pixels from base coords)\n  18 - Count of dwords in rendering structure (adStructArray)\n  200 - Unicode buffer element count (szUnicodeBuffer)\n  100 - ANSI buffer size (szAnsiBuffer)\n  0x46 - Item property ordinal (typically color/visual attribute)\n  0x2d - Validation check ordinal (0x2d = 45 decimal, likely state/validity flag)\n  0x28 - String length limit (40 decimal) before truncation\n  10 - Radix for decimal conversion (FUN_6fb9adee)\n  5, 0xffffffff - Ordinal_10073 constant parameters\n\nRelated Functions:\n  FUN_6fb51940 - Normal render path for inventory item\n  FUN_6fb50f20 - Alternate render path for inventory item\n  FUN_6fb62880 - Get current game state/world pointer\n  FUN_6fb9adee - Convert integer to decimal string\n  Ordinal_10073 - D2Common rendering initialization\n  Ordinal_10258 - Query primary item from container\n  Ordinal_10759, 10767 - Validation checks on item\n  Ordinal_10519 - Get item property value\n  Ordinal_10257 - Query item by index\n  Ordinal_10731 - Validation check\n  RenderGameWindowElements - Calling function",
