      "comment": "Initialize UI element text displays for key binding commands.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check viewport coordinates (pViewportX, nViewportY) against registered viewport IDs\n2. If viewport ID matches and element active flag (DAT_6fbfc8e4 = 1), retrieve key binding command code\n3. Look up Unicode string for key binding using GetKeyBindingStringId(commandId, 1)\n4. Copy key binding text to awKeyText buffer via Unicode::strcpy, determine text length with strlen\n5. Validate text length against threshold (0x28 = 40 chars) using Ordinal_10121\n6. If text exceeds threshold, truncate by overwriting trailing characters with null (0x0000) via Ordinal_10117\n7. Repeat for 8 viewport element mappings (viewport IDs: 0x0e-0x0f, 0x10-0x15, 0x2e, 0x2f-0x35)\n\nParameters:\npViewportX (int *) - Pointer to viewport X coordinate value to compare against registered viewports\nnViewportY (int) - Viewport Y coordinate value to compare against registered viewports  \nnPanelId (uint) - Panel/element ID for validation\nnOffsetBase (int) - Base offset for element index calculations\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value; modifies UI element text display in place\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Phantom variables local_cc and local_d0 are compiler stack temporaries (optimized away)\n- Key binding code 0xffff indicates no binding configured, operation skipped\n- Text truncation prevents buffer overrun in 200-char Unicode array\n\nRelated Functions:\n- GetKeyBindingStringId() - Retrieves Unicode string for key binding\n- LookupKeyBindingByCommandId() - Looks up key binding by command ID\n- InitializeKeyBindingDisplayText() - Alternative single-element initialization\n- Ordinal_10121() - UI dimension query function\n- Ordinal_10117() - UI text truncation function",
