      "comment": "Initialize and update key binding display text for skill command UI elements.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. For each supported command ID (0x0E-0x0F, 0x10-0x15, 0x2E-0x35):\n   a. Check if pImageIds[0] matches expected control ID (DAT_* global comparisons)\n   b. Check if nImageHeight matches expected value (DAT_* global comparisons)\n   c. Verify control ID != -1 (enabled state)\n   d. Check state flag (DAT_* global) equals 0 (not yet initialized)\n   e. Look up key binding string for command ID with variant 0x01\n   f. If binding found (result != 0xFFFF), initialize display text\n2. For commands 0x0E-0x15, 0x2E:\n   a. Allocate 100-element Unicode buffer on stack\n   b. Initialize each buffer element to null\n   c. Get key binding string ID and copy to buffer\n   d. Calculate string length\n   e. Get pixel width via Ordinal_10121 (Unicode::strlen)\n   f. Pad/trim text to fit within 0x28 (40) pixels\n   g. Call Ordinal_10117 (UpdateUIElement) with offset (param_4 - 0x23) and size 4\n3. For commands 0x2F-0x35:\n   a. Call InitializeKeyBindingDisplayText directly with command ID and buffer pointer\n\nParameters:\npImageIds (int*) - Array of control/image IDs to check in conditions\nnImageHeight (int) - Secondary identifier for matching control states\ndwUnknown (uint) - Unknown purpose, not used in visible logic\npBaseControl (int*) - Base pointer for relative offset calculations (param_4 - 0x23)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value; modifies global state and control display text\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Commands 0x0E, 0x0F, 0x10, 0x11, 0x12, 0x13, 0x14, 0x15, 0x2E use stack allocation and manual pixel calculation\n- Commands 0x2F, 0x30, 0x31, 0x32, 0x33, 0x34, 0x35 use direct InitializeKeyBindingDisplayText\n- Magic number 0x28 (40) is pixel width limit for text truncation\n- Magic number 0x23 (35) is offset subtracted from pBaseControl\n- Magic number 0x64 (100) is buffer element count\n\nOrdinals:\n- Ordinal_10121 @ 0x6fb999fc (Unicode::strlen) - Get pixel width of text\n- Ordinal_10117 @ 0x6fb999f6 (UpdateUIElement) - Update control display with buffer\n\nRelated Functions:\n- GetKeyBindingStringId - Retrieves key binding text for command\n- LookupKeyBindingByCommandId - Checks if binding exists (returns != 0xFFFF)\n- InitializeKeyBindingDisplayText - Alternative path for commands 0x2F-0x35",
