      "instructions": ["0x82360|SUB|ESP, 0x180", "0x82366|PUSH|EBX", "0x82367|PUSH|EBP", "0x82368|MOV|EBP, ECX", "0x8236A|PUSH|ESI", "0x8236B|PUSH|EDI", "0x8236C|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x14], EDX", "0x82370|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [EBP]", "0x82373|PUSH|EAX", "0x82374|CALL|0x6fb98b66", "0x82379|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0x8237B|JL|0x6fb523b2", "0x8237D|CMP|EAX, 0x7", "0x82380|JGE|0x6fb523b2", "0x82382|MOV|ESI, EAX"],
      "comment": "Configure and display key binding UI with rendered icon/resource.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get skill icon index from slot pointer, validate range [0-6]\n2. If valid: scale offset (multiply by 0x22) to access skill icons array\n3. Load or cache skill icon resource from s_Spells_AmSkillicon array\n4. Extract slot status byte from offset 0xd7 of slot structure\n5. Query current screen coordinates via FUN_6fb8f680/6fb8f690\n6. If coords within bounds (X: [nScreenX, nScreenX+0x30], Y: [nScreenY-0x30, nScreenY]):\n   - Normalize nDisplayMode: 0→0, 1→1, other→calculated (-(val!=4)&0xfd)+4\n7. Initialize display params array (18 dwords) with zeros\n8. Set params: [1]=icon_resource, [2]=bySlotStatus, [3]=0\n9. Call Ordinal_10073 with display params and normalized mode\n10. Branch on bUseAlternateDisplay:\n    - If 0: Call ProcessKeyBindingDisplayUpdates\n    - If non-zero: Call InitializeKeyBindingDisplayTexts\n11. Initialize Unicode text buffer (200 wide chars) with constructors\n12. If nDisplayFlags > 0:\n    - Convert flag to string via FUN_6fb9adee\n    - Convert ANSI to Unicode via toUnicode\n    - Get string length, check available space (0x28 limit)\n    - Fill remaining space with null terminators if needed\n    - Call Ordinal_10117 with adjusted coordinates\n\nParameters:\npSlotIndex - Pointer to skill slot index (validated 0-6)\nnSlotId - Skill slot ID for display\nnDisplayFlags - Numeric value to display as string (if > 0)\nnDisplayMode - Display mode: 0=default, 1=alt1, 4=alt2, other=calculated\nnScreenX - Base X coordinate (min bounds check)\nnScreenY - Base Y coordinate (max bounds check)\nbUseAlternateDisplay - 0=update mode, non-zero=initialize mode\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Modifies display state and UI elements\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Invalid slot index (< 0 or > 6): Uses g_pMainWindowRenderTarget instead\n- Coordinates out of bounds: Uses original nDisplayMode without normalization\n- Empty nDisplayFlags: Skips string conversion and Unicode initialization\n- String exceeds 0x28 chars: Pads with null terminators to fit\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x22 - Skill icon array entry stride (34 bytes per entry)\n0xd7 - Offset in slot structure for status byte\n0x30 - Bounding box extension (48 pixels)\n0x12 - Display params array size (18 dwords)\n0x28 - Maximum string/display width (40 decimal)\n0x64 - Unicode buffer size (100 wide chars)\n0xfffffffd - Bitmask for mode calculation\n\nRelated Functions:\n- ProcessKeyBindingDisplayUpdates - Update existing key binding display\n- InitializeKeyBindingDisplayTexts - Initialize new key binding display\n- FUN_6fb8f680 - Get current screen X coordinate\n- FUN_6fb8f690 - Get current screen Y coordinate\n- FUN_6fb5a050 - Load/allocate skill icon resource\n- Ordinal_10073 - Render display with params (Storm/Fog)\n- Ordinal_10117 - Position/adjust display coordinates\n- Ordinal_10121 - Query display dimension/bounds\n",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_StatList", "PARAM_7", "STRUCT_Path", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "UI_SKILLS", "STRUCT_Skill", "STRUCT_ItemData", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
