      "comment": "Renders skill UI slot display with up to 5 active skill slots arranged in columns.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Return immediately if game state not zero (game not running)\n2. Get viewport handle via Ordinal_10966() /* D2Common.GetUnitStat */ to access unit record data\n3. Initialize position tracking (local_30 holds base X position, nScreenPosY holds base Y)\n4. Set skill slot counter to 0, clear bit flags (bVar4=dagger/claw flag, bVar3=axe flag)\n5. Loop through skill inventory:\n   - Get next skill via Ordinal_10320() /* D2Common.GetNextInventoryItem */\n   - Get skill record properties via Ordinal_10947() /* D2Common.GetItemProperty */\n   - Check skill requirements: null terminator at offset 0x3b, skill type != 1 and != 5\n   - Query min/max values via Ordinal_10955() /* D2Common.GetItemMinMaxValue */ (results in nMinValue, dwMaxValue)\n   - Verify skill is available via Ordinal_11011() /* D2Common.GetUnitInventorySize */ - must return > 0\n   - Check if skill class in range 0xd8-0xdc (allows special class skills)\n   - Validate slot count <= 4 or slot index doesn't match current dwCurrentSlot\n6. For valid skills:\n   - Get skill color via Ordinal_10964() /* D2Common.GetItemQuality */ with result in nScreenPosY temp\n   - Compute color flags based on skill type (dagger=0x01, other=0x04)\n   - Update Y position by -0x30 if slot count changed\n   - Get skill effect via Ordinal_10963() /* D2Common.GetItemEffectiveLevel */\n   - Switch on dwSlotIndex to position in column 0-4:\n     * Case 0-3: Positions in columns at X = local_30/local_2c/local_28/local_24\n     * Case 4: Special handling for dagger (0xd9) and axe (0xdb), X = local_20\n   - Call ConfigureKeyBindingDisplay() if nDisplayMode==0 to setup key bindings\n   - Store position and skill data in UI state arrays (g_abSkillUIStateBuffer, g_adSkillUIPositionsY, g_adSkillUIRenderTargets)\n   - Decrement X position by 0x30 for next skill in column\n   - Increment dwSlotIndex for next iteration\n7. Loop until dwSlotIndex >= 5\n\nParameters:\ndwDisplayMode (uint) - 0=configure key bindings, non-zero=skip key binding setup\n\nReturns:\nvoid - no return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Function silently returns if g_dwGameState != 0 (game not active)\n- Dagger skills (0xd9) and axe skills (0xdb) limited to once per UI render to avoid duplicate slots\n- Color calculation via ordinal result: if result==6 then 0x04, else 0xFFFFFFFD|0x04 = 0xFFFFFFFD|0x04\n- Skill type validation: accepts 0-4 range, rejects 1 and 5 (potentially reserved types)\n- Magic Numbers: 0x56 (UI height offset), 0x80 (UI width offset), 0x30 (slot height), 0xd8-0xdc (class range)\n- Note: Function uses 15 compiler-generated SSA temporaries (uVar1-uVar10, iVar2, iVar5-iVar6, bVar2-bVar3) optimized away by compiler - not visible in decompiled view",
