      "comment": "Render skill UI tooltips for 5 horizontal skill slots with mouse-over bounds checking. Iterates through skill tree slots (0-4), fetches unit skills, validates bounds, and calls BuildSkillTooltip if mouse cursor is within bounds and conditions met.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if game state is active (g_dwGameState != 0), exit if inactive\n2. Get game viewport/screen coordinates via FUN_6fb62880()\n3. Initialize UI panel Y-offsets (0x50 pixels each) for 5 horizontal slot groups\n4. Loop through 5 skill slot panels (local_dwSlotIndex 0-4):\n   - For each slot, loop through available skills (iVar3):\n     - Validate skill unit pointer from Ordinal_10966(): check if skill class != 1 (class filter) and != 5\n     - Call Ordinal_10955() to fetch skill parameters (local_dwParam1, local_dwParam2)\n     - Validate slot constraint: (int)local_dwSlotIndex < 4, iVar5 == 0, local_dwParam1 matches unit class byte\n   - Compute bounds check flags via Ordinal_10964() (0x6 means cost, returns iVar6 offset adjustment)\n   - Switch on local_dwSlotIndex (0-4):\n     * Case 0: Check bounds vs local_dwX1/local_dwX1End, build tooltip if within bounds\n     * Case 1: Check bounds vs local_dwX4/local_dwX4End, offset Y by -0x30, build if valid\n     * Case 2: Call FUN_6fb53330() to verify rectangle at (local_dwX3, Y), build if valid\n     * Case 3: Call FUN_6fb53330() to verify rectangle at (local_dwX5, Y), build if valid\n     * Case 4: Call FUN_6fb53330() twice, build tooltip with computed Y offsets\n   - Increment X-offset by 0x30 pixels for next skill icon position\n5. Continue loop until all 5 slots processed\n\nParameters:\n(none - void function)\n\nReturns:\n(void)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If g_dwGameState == 0, function returns immediately (inactive game state)\n- Mouse bounds checks use FUN_6fb8f680() for X, FUN_6fb8f690() for Y coordinates\n- Skill tooltip marker: uses g_InvalidTooltipMarker pointer when bounds invalid, otherwise (iVar6 == 1)\n- Rectangle validation (Case 2-4): FUN_6fb53330() checks if 0x30x0x30 region is drawable\n- Ordinal_10964() returns 6 for certain skill costs, adjusted via (-(uint)(iVar6 != 6) & 0xfffffffd) + 4\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x30 = skill icon size (48 pixels)\n0x50 = initial X-offset for slot group\n0x56 = Y-offset from screen bottom\n0x86 = viewport offset constant\n-0x30 = Y reduction for lower skill slots\n0xd8, 0xec = unit skill class filter offsets\n0xd4 = unit class byte offset for validation\n4 = max valid slot index\n\nRelated Functions:\n- BuildSkillTooltip() - Renders tooltip at specified coordinates with skill data\n- FUN_6fb8f680/FUN_6fb8f690() - Get mouse X/Y coordinates\n- FUN_6fb53330() - Check if drawable rectangle region is valid\n- FUN_6fb62880() - Initialize/fetch game viewport state\n- Ordinal_10320() - Get skill unit from skill tree (D2Common ordinal)\n- Ordinal_10947() - Get next skill in linked list (D2Common ordinal)\n- Ordinal_10955() - Extract skill parameters/cost (D2Common ordinal)\n- Ordinal_10964() - Get skill cost flags/modifier (D2Common ordinal)\n- Ordinal_10966() - Get current player unit pointer (D2Common ordinal)\n- Ordinal_10968() - Modify skill parameter (D2Common ordinal)",
