      "comment": "Process skill UI slots - iterate through 5 skill button slots, validate skills, and build tooltips for valid ones.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if game state is 0 (menu mode)\n2. Get skill list handle from FUN_6fb62880()\n3. Calculate screen position offsets: width - 0x80, height - 0x56\n4. Initialize slot position variables for 4 skill slots + 1 special slot\n5. Loop through skill slots (0-4):\n   a. Get next skill from list (Ordinal_10320)\n   b. Get skill ID (Ordinal_10947) and skill structure pointer (Ordinal_10966)\n   c. Validate: skill not disabled (char at +0x3b == null), not type 1 or 5\n   d. Get resource consumption (Ordinal_10955), validate result and ID range (0xd8-0xdc)\n   e. Determine mouse slot (Ordinal_10964): if result != 6, set iVar6 = 1\n   f. Execute slot-specific action based on dwCurrentSlot (switch 0-4):\n      - Slot 0: Get mouse position, validate against slot bounds (±0x30), build tooltip\n      - Slot 1: Call Ordinal_10968, validate position, build tooltip\n      - Slot 2: Call Ordinal_10968, validate position, build tooltip\n      - Slot 3: Call Ordinal_10968, validate IsPointInRect, build tooltip\n      - Slot 4: Check skill ID (0xd9 or 0xdb), manage state flags, build tooltip or call FUN_6fb53830\n6. Iterate to next skill, increment dwCurrentSlot\n\nParameters:\n(none) - Uses global game state and skill UI configuration globals\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Slot 0 (dw items): Only process if skill type < 6\n- Slots 1-3 (attack skills): Use Ordinal_10968 for mouse detection\n- Slot 4 (special skills): Special handling for skill IDs 0xd9/0xdb with state flags\n- Invalid tooltip marker (g_InvalidTooltipMarker) returned when outside slot bounds\n- Decrements X coordinates by 0x30 pixels after processing each slot\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x80 - Screen width offset adjustment (128 pixels)\n0x56 - Screen height offset adjustment (86 pixels)\n0x30 - Slot size (48 pixels)\n0x3b - Offset of disabled flag in skill structure\n0xd4 - Offset of skill slot index field\n0xec - Offset of skill type field\n0xd8-0xdc - Castable skill ID range\n0xd9, 0xdb - Special skill IDs (quest items)",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_StatList", "PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Path", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "STRUCT_Skill", "STRUCT_Room2", "STRUCT_ItemData", "PARAM_0", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
