      "comment": "Render viewport string based on screen coordinates and mode.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get current viewport screen coordinates via FUN_6fb8f680 (X) and FUN_6fb8f690 (Y)\n2. Check if coordinates exceed bounds: X < nXCoord or X > nXCoord+0x30 or Y < nYCoord-0x30 or Y > nYCoord\n3. If out of bounds, set fIsOutOfBounds = true; else fIsOutOfBounds = (nMode == 1)\n4. Re-fetch current screen coordinates to validate viewport position\n5. If coordinates within valid range (X in [nXCoord, nXCoord+0x30] AND Y in [nYCoord-0x30, nYCoord]):\n   a. Switch on *pCellType (0xd9, 0xda, 0xdb, 0xdc) to determine cell type\n   b. Call Ordinal_10004 to perform viewport operation\n   c. Initialize szUnicodeOutput Unicode buffer (512 wide chars) with constructor\n   d. Call Ordinal_10004 again for viewport state\n   e. Copy and concatenate Unicode strings (multiple strcat operations)\n   f. Initialize aUStack_214 Unicode array (20 wide chars)\n   g. Format dwCellFlags into ANSI buffer using g_szFormatTemplate\n   h. Convert formatted string to Unicode\n   i. Concatenate Unicode strings to output\n   j. Call Ordinal_10129 with offset Y-0x32, fIsOutOfBounds flag, and constant 1\n   k. Resource cleanup after rendering\n\nParameters:\n   pCellType (uint *): Pointer to cell type code (0xd9-0xdc range)\n   nMode (int): Rendering mode flag (checked against 1)\n   dwCellFlags (uint): Cell flags/attributes to format in output string\n   nXCoord (int): Viewport X coordinate boundary\n   nYCoord (int): Viewport Y coordinate boundary\n\nReturns:\n   void (no return value)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n   Out-of-bounds coordinates: fIsOutOfBounds set true, rendering skipped\n   Cell type 0xd9, 0xda, 0xdb, 0xdc: Switch dispatch selects rendering path\n   Multiple ordinal calls: Ensure viewport state consistency\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n   0x30: Viewport boundary expansion (48 pixels)\n   0xd9-0xdc: Cell type discriminators\n   0x100: Unicode buffer element count (512 bytes)\n   0x32: Y coordinate offset to Ordinal_10129\n   0xa: Array size for formatting buffer\n   0x1: Constant parameter to Ordinal_10129",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Path", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "STRUCT_Skill", "PARAM_5", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
