      "instructions": ["0x83A20|PUSH|ESI", "0x83A21|PUSH|EDI", "0x83A22|CALL|0x6fb62880", "0x83A27|PUSH|EAX", "0x83A28|CALL|0x6fb98b6c", "0x83A2D|MOV|ESI, EAX", "0x83A2F|TEST|ESI, ESI", "0x83A31|JNZ|0x6fb53a51", "0x83A33|PUSH|0x405", "0x83A38|PUSH|0x6fbc66b4", "0x83A3D|PUSH|0x6fbb0bec", "0x83A42|CALL|0x6fb99a7a", "0x83A47|ADD|ESP, 0xc", "0x83A4A|PUSH|-0x1", "0x83A4C|CALL|0x6fb9a10f"],
      "comment": "Locate and validate first skill stat with value 0xd9 (217) in skill definition\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get current character/player context via FUN_6fb62880() -> uVar1\n2. Look up skill handle from player context via Ordinal_10320(uVar1) -> iVar2\n3. If skill handle is 0, log error and exit (-1)\n4. Loop through skill definition:\n   a. Get current stat value via Ordinal_10966() -> piVar3 (pointer)\n   b. Get stat count for skill via Ordinal_11011(iVar2) -> iVar4\n   c. If stat count > 0 AND current stat equals 0xd9, found match - exit loop\n   d. Advance to next skill via Ordinal_10947(iVar2) -> iVar2\n   e. If skill handle becomes 0, end of table - return void\n5. Return after finding matching stat or end of table\n\nParameters:\n- None: Uses implicit global character context\n\nReturns:\n- void: No return value; function called from BuildSkillTooltip for skill 0xd9 special case\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Magic number 0xd9 (217): Specific skill type marker in stat definition\n- Called during tooltip generation for special skills (skills 0xd9-0xdc)\n- References global g_szSkillHandleError for error logging\n\nOrdinal References:\n- Ordinal_10320: D2Common.GetSkillHandle - retrieve skill handle from player context\n- Ordinal_10966: D2Common.GetCurrentStatPointer - get pointer to current stat value\n- Ordinal_11011: D2Common.GetStatCount - retrieve count of stats for skill\n- Ordinal_10947: D2Common.GetNextSkillDefinition - advance to next skill\n- Ordinal_10023: Fog.ErrorMsg - log error messages\n- FUN_6fb9a10f: Exit handler with error code -1",
