      "comment": "Validates that a skill property value meets minimum requirements. Iterates through skill properties until finding the magic property (0xdb) with a valid value count.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get initial skill handle via FUN_6fb62880()\n2. Look up skill data record using Ordinal_10320 (D2Common.GetSkillData)\n3. If skill data not found (nSkillId == 0), log error via Ordinal_10023 (Fog.ErrorMsg) and terminate\n4. Loop through skill properties with three compiler-optimized temporaries:\n   a. Call Ordinal_10966 - get pointer to property data (temporary: iVar3/EDI)\n   b. Call Ordinal_11011 - get property value count (temporary: iVar4/EAX)\n   c. If value > 0 AND property dword equals 0xdb, validation passed - exit loop\n   d. Call Ordinal_10947 - advance to next property in iteration (temporary: iVar2/ESI)\n   e. If no more properties (iVar2 == 0), return without validation\n5. Return with valid skill property found\n\nParameters:\n(none - reads from global context via FUN_6fb62880)\n\nReturns:\nvoid (terminates on error via FUN_6fb9a10f with code 0xffffffff, returns normally on success)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Invalid skill data triggers fatal error via Fog.ErrorMsg and FUN_6fb9a10f\n- Property value 0xdb is magic constant for valid skill property marker\n- Loop must find matching property before end of list\n- Three variables are compiler temporaries optimized away: iVar2 (loop iteration), iVar3 (property pointer), iVar4 (value count)\n\nUndocumented Ordinals Referenced:\n- Ordinal_10320 = D2Common.GetSkillData\n- Ordinal_10966 = property data pointer getter\n- Ordinal_11011 = property value counter  \n- Ordinal_10947 = property iterator/next getter",
