      "comment": "Validate skill handle and search for skill with matching data marker.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Retrieve current skill handle via GetSkillHandle() [Ordinal_10320]\n2. Verify handle is valid; if zero, log error and exit (-1)\n3. Enter validation loop: iterate through skill list starting at nSkillHandle\n4. Get pointer to current data via GetCurrentData() [Ordinal_10966]\n5. Query skill count via GetSkillCount() [Ordinal_11011]\n6. Check: count > 0 AND data[0] == 0xDA (skill marker)\n7. If match found: exit loop and return success\n8. If no match: advance to next skill via GetNextSkill() [Ordinal_10947]\n9. If handle becomes null (reached end): return failure\n10. Repeat until skill marker found or list exhausted\n\nParameters:\n(implicit) Requires current UI context with skill data initialized\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Function terminates on success or via FUN_6fb9a10f() on fatal error\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Error case: Invalid initial skill handle triggers FUN_6fb9a10f(-1) which does not return\n- Loop termination: Either finds 0xDA marker in data or exhausts skill list\n- Data pointer dereference: *piVar3 accesses first dword at skill data location\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0xDA - Skill data block marker/identifier\n- 0x439 - Error code (1081 decimal) for handle validation failure\n- 0xFFFFFFFF (-1) - Fatal error code passed to exit handler",
