      "comment": "Validate and return skill template ID for special skill 0xdc property.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Retrieve player/character data context via FUN_6fb62880()\n2. Get skill handle ID via Ordinal_10320(dwPlayerData) - D2Common ordinal\n3. If handle invalid (== 0), log error message via Ordinal_10023 and exit with code -1\n4. Loop through skill properties:\n   a. Retrieve next property pointer via Ordinal_10966() - D2Common ordinal\n   b. Get property value via Ordinal_11011(nSkillHandleId) - D2Common ordinal\n   c. If property value > 0 AND (*ppSkillProperty == 0xdc), break (found match)\n   d. Advance to next handle via Ordinal_10947(nSkillHandleId) - D2Common ordinal\n   e. If no more handles (== 0), return 0 (not found)\n5. Return template ID (found at break point)\n\nOrdinals Used:\n- Ordinal_10320: D2Common.GetSkillHandle\n- Ordinal_10023: D2Common.LogError\n- Ordinal_10966: D2Common.GetPropertyPointer\n- Ordinal_11011: D2Common.GetPropertyValue\n- Ordinal_10947: D2Common.GetNextHandle\n\nParameters:\n- (implicit context, Diablo II calling convention): No explicit parameters\n- Uses global skill state from player context\n\nReturns:\n- uint: Template ID for skill 0xdc property, or 0 if not found/invalid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Handle == 0: Logs \"SkillHandleError\" to file before fatal exit (-1)\n- No matching property (0xdc): Returns 0 (loop completes without match)\n- Property value 0: Skips to next handle (0 < iVar4 condition false)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0xdc (220): Target property value for special skill template\n- 0xffffffff (-1): Fatal exit code for error condition\n- 0x453 (1107): Error line number in source file",
