      "comment": "Processes click input on the skill bar UI area, activating skills when clicked\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get game context and assert it exists\n2. Store current screen Y position\n3. Iterate through skill UI render target array (g_adSkillUIRenderTargets)\n4. For each slot, check if mouse coordinates fall within slot bounds\n5. If within bounds, get skill by ID from player unit\n6. Check if skill has passive state or no remaining charges\n7. If skill unusable, show skill info UI dialog\n8. If skill usable, send skill selection packet (0x3c) to server\n9. Update UI state and initialize targeting system\n10. After loop, check if click was below skill bar with no skill selected\n11. Set callback result fields (+0x18=1, +0x1c=0) and insert cache node\n\nParameters:\n  pEventData (void *) - Pointer to event/callback structure\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Asserts with FogAssert if game context is NULL, then calls ExitApplicationWithCode(-1)\n  - Skills with passive state or no charges open info dialog instead of activating\n  - Click below skill bar area with no skill clicked opens UI\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x3c - Packet ID for skill selection\n  0x30 - Skill slot dimension (48 pixels)\n  0x31 - Screen bottom margin (49 pixels)\n  3 - UI resource ID for skill info panel\n  0x80000000 - High bit flag for skill direction/mode",
