      "instructions": ["0x83D30|PUSH|ESI", "0x83D31|PUSH|EDI", "0x83D32|MOV|EDI, ECX", "0x83D34|CALL|0x6fb62890", "0x83D39|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0x83D3B|JNZ|0x6fb53da1", "0x83D3D|TEST|EDI, EDI", "0x83D3F|SETLE|AL", "0x83D42|DEC|EAX", "0x83D43|AND|EAX, 0x2", "0x83D46|DEC|EAX", "0x83D47|TEST|EDI, EDI", "0x83D49|MOV|ESI, EAX", "0x83D4B|JGE|0x6fb53d51", "0x83D4D|NEG|EDI"],
      "comment": "Navigate skill slot selection by direction (up/down/-1 cycles).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if game state allows interaction (FUN_6fb62890 returns false)\n2. Convert negative slot direction to positive and validate non-zero\n3. Determine movement direction: 1 for up, -1 for down\n4. Search for next available skill slot in circular list (0x0-0xF, wraps)\n5. Skip locked slots (marked -1) and unavailable slots\n6. Execute activation if valid slot found within 16 attempts\n\nParameters:\nnSlotDirection: +1 for next slot, -1 for previous, 0 exits early\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Updates global skill slot and sends activation packet via FUN_6fb54000\n\nNotes:\n- Circular buffer navigation with 16-slot maximum\n- Locked/unavailable slots automatically skipped\n- Multiple conditions checked: slot validity, availability flags\n- Uses optimization where direction encodes wrap behavior",
      "tags": ["PARAM_1"]
