      "comment": "Process skill target validation and effects application\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get current skill node from Ordinal_10966 (D2Common.GetFirstSkill)\n2. Validate skill node with Ordinal_10320 (D2Common.ValidateSkill) - returns iterator or null\n3. If no skill node (null iterator), log error with Ordinal_10023 (D2Common.LogSkillError) and exit with Ordinal_11011 (D2Common.FatalError)\n4. Loop through skill list:\n   a. Get next skill handle with Ordinal_10966 (D2Common.GetFirstSkill)\n   b. Check if skill opcode is in range 0xd8-0xdd (spell types)\n   c. If opcode is 0xd9 or 0xdb (specific spell types), apply effect with FUN_6fb53e30\n   d. Get next skill node with Ordinal_10947 (D2Common.GetNextSkill)\n5. Return when skill iterator exhausted\n\nParameters:\n(none)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - modifies global state through ordinal calls, may terminate process on error\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Error handling: If initial skill node is null, logs error and terminates with status 0xffffffff\n- Spell type filtering: Only processes opcodes 0xd9 and 0xdb out of range 0xd8-0xdd\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0xd8: Lower bound for spell opcode range\n- 0xdd: Upper bound for spell opcode range  \n- 0xd9: Specific spell type requiring effect processing\n- 0xdb: Alternate spell type requiring effect processing\n- 0x526: Error logging line number reference\n- 0xffffffff: Fatal error exit code\n\nOrdinal Comments:\n- Ordinal_10966: D2Common.GetFirstSkill - Get first skill from list\n- Ordinal_10320: D2Common.ValidateSkill - Validate skill iterator\n- Ordinal_10023: D2Common.LogSkillError - Log skill error message\n- Ordinal_11011: D2Common.FatalError - Exit with error code\n- Ordinal_10947: D2Common.GetNextSkill - Iterate to next skill",
