      "comment": "Iterate through skill UI render targets and reset matching icon render targets when threshold met\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize loop through g_adSkillUIRenderTargets array\n2. For each UI target, check if it matches input pTargetId\n3. If match found, iterate through skill icon render targets (g_adSkillIconRenderTargets4) with 4-byte stride\n4. Compare icon target with UI target value\n5. Check if nThreshold parameter is less than 1\n6. If both conditions met, reset three render target arrays (RenderTargets4, RenderTargets3, RenderTargets2) to 0xffffffff\n7. Send packet 0x51 with combined data values (dwData1 incremented by 0x10000 per iteration, 0xffffffff as payload)\n8. Continue icon target loop until dwData1 >= 0x10ffff\n9. Continue UI target loop until array boundary\n\nParameters:\npTargetId (int *) - Pointer to target ID to search for in UI render targets\nnThreshold (int) - Comparison threshold; operation proceeds if nThreshold < 1\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Function has no return value\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0xffff - Initial dwData1 value (packet ID component)\n0x10000 - Increment per iteration in icon target loop\n0x10ffff - Upper bound for dwData1 comparison\n0xffffffff - Reset value for render targets, packet data payload\n0x6fbfcb00 - Base address of g_adSkillUIRenderTargets array\n0x6fbfcd54 - Base address of g_adSkillIconRenderTargets4 array\n0x6fbfc8e0 - Base address of g_adSkillIconRenderTargets3 array\n0x6fbfcdd4 - Base address of g_adSkillIconRenderTargets2 array\n0x6fbfcbf0 - Upper boundary for UI render targets loop\n0x51 - Packet type sent to SendPacketData\n\nStructure Layout (Render Target Arrays):\nOffset | Size | Field Name | Type | Description\n0x0    | 4    | id         | int  | Icon/UI target identifier\n0x4    | 4    | state      | int  | Target state/status\n0x8    | 4    | param      | int  | Additional parameter\n0xC    | 4    | flags      | int  | Control flags",
