      "comment": "Selects a skill slot and sends packet to server with skill and inventory parameters.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate slot index points to active skill (g_adSkillIconRenderTargets4[nSlotIndex] != -1)\n2. Get inventory record from FUN_6fb62880 and validate non-zero\n3. Load skill record ID from g_adSkillIconRenderTargets2[nSlotIndex] via Ordinal_10949\n4. Verify skill state: Ordinal_10957 checks state != -1\n5. Query skill info via Ordinal_10955 with empty params, extract nOutCount into local variable\n6. If nOutCount < 1, return early (skill unavailable)\n7. Set global g_nCurrentSkillSlot to nSlotIndex\n8. Construct packet: opcode 0x3c with skill ID and inventory ID, apply 0x80000000 flag if g_adSkillIconRenderTargets3[nSlotIndex] set\n9. Send packet via SendPacketData\n10. Call Ordinal_10961 or Ordinal_10962 based on flag g_adSkillIconRenderTargets3[nSlotIndex]\n\nParameters:\n- nSlotIndex (int, ECX): Skill slot index (0-based, indexes into 4 global arrays)\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nGlobal Arrays Indexed by nSlotIndex:\n| Offset | Global | Purpose |\n| g_adSkillIconRenderTargets4 | Skill validity flag (-1 = inactive) |\n| g_adSkillIconRenderTargets2 | Skill record ID |\n| g_adSkillIconRenderTargets3 | Activation flag (0x80000000 bit) |\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Skill must be active (not -1) to process\n- nOutCount validation prevents execution of unavailable skills\n- Flag bit 0x80000000 selects between Ordinal_10961 (set) and Ordinal_10962 (clear)",
