      "comment": "Initialize spinner UI element with dimensions, flags, and resource configuration.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Set up exception handling frame with saved exception list\n2. Initialize path buffer for UI menu spinner resource via FUN_6fb9a261\n3. Concatenate path and write file to get initial result code\n4. Store width parameter in object at offset +0x8\n5. Store secondary flags in object at offset +0x3c\n6. Store primary flags in object at offset +0x2c\n7. Store file write result in object at offset +0x50\n8. Initialize 18-element resource array by looping and zeroing each element\n9. Store height parameter in object at offset +0xc\n10. Zero-initialize reserved fields (offsets +0x34, +0x38, +0x30, +0x4c, +0x40)\n11. Call Ordinal_10036 with resource array to query resource provider\n12. Call Ordinal_10038 on result to get resource stat value, store at +0x24\n13. Call Ordinal_10037 on result to get resource size value, store at +0x28\n14. Conditional initialization based on primary flags value:\n    - If flags == 0: Initialize layout variant 1 (width+1, height+1, resource size based coords)\n    - If flags != 0: Initialize layout variant 2 (alternate offset calculations with height)\n15. Restore exception handling frame and return pointer to initialized object\n\nParameters:\npSpinner - Pointer to SpinnerObject instance (SpinnerObject *)\nnWidthParam - Base width dimension (int)\nnHeightParam - Base height dimension (int)\ndwFlags1 - Primary control flags affecting layout selection (dword)\ndwFlags2 - Secondary control flags stored in object (dword)\n\nReturns:\nPointer to initialized SpinnerObject (same as pSpinner parameter on success)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Conditional layout selection based on dwFlags1 zero/nonzero\n- Exception frame required due to C++ exception handling in destructor\n- Resource array size fixed at 18 dwords (72 bytes)",
