      "comment": "Calculate scaled timer duration based on elapsed time intervals.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if timer's state bytes at +0x34 and +0x38 are both zero - return 0 if true\n2. Test flag at +0x20 (active/pending flag)\n3. If pending (flag set): Clear state bytes at +0x34, +0x38 and pending flag at +0x20, return 1\n4. If not pending (flag clear): Call GetTickCount() to get current system time\n5. Check if flag at +0x4c is set: if true, store time at +0x48 and return 1\n6. Calculate elapsed time: dwElapsedTime = dwCurrentTime - value at +0x44\n7. Check if (dwCurrentTime - value at +0x48) < 0x46 (70ms): return 0 if true\n8. Update +0x48 with dwCurrentTime\n9. Scale base value at +0x40 by elapsed time bracket:\n   - If > 0x1000ms: return base * (elapsed >> 0xB)\n   - Else if > 0xBB8ms (3000): return base >> 2\n   - Else if > 0x7D0ms (2000): return base >> 4\n   - Else if > 0x3E8ms (1000): return base >> 5\n10. Return 1 (default)\n\nParameters:\n  nTimer (int) IMPLICIT in ECX - Pointer to timer structure\n\nReturns:\n  dword - Scaled count value (0 for inactive/throttled, 1 for success/pending)\n\nNote: Function uses 1 register-optimized variable (phantom variable uVar1 in EDI)",
