      "comment": "Validate coordinate hit-test against primary and secondary bounds rectangles\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize test flag to 1 at offset 0x30\n2. Extract X coordinate from low word of packed coordinate parameter\n3. Extract Y coordinate from high word of packed coordinate parameter\n4. Test primary bounds region (left=0x10, top=0x14, width=0x28, margin=0x24)\n5. Verify X >= primary.left AND X < primary.left + width\n6. Verify (primary.top - margin) < Y AND Y <= primary.top\n7. If primary bounds pass: store GetTickCount() at 0x44, set flag 0x34=1, invoke callback, return 1\n8. Test secondary bounds region (left=0x18, top=0x1c, width=0x28, margin=0x24)\n9. Verify X >= secondary.left AND X < secondary.left + width\n10. Verify (secondary.top - margin) < Y AND Y < secondary.top\n11. If secondary bounds pass: store GetTickCount() at 0x44, set flag 0x38=1, invoke callback, return 1\n12. Return 0 if no bounds matched\n\nParameters:\npBounds: Opaque structure pointer containing bounds/state data\n  Field Layout (via offset access):\n    0x10: Primary rect left X coordinate (dword)\n    0x14: Primary rect top Y coordinate (dword)\n    0x18: Secondary rect left X coordinate (dword)\n    0x1c: Secondary rect top Y coordinate (dword)\n    0x24: Y-axis margin/offset value (dword)\n    0x28: Rectangle width (shared by both rects, dword)\n    0x30: Test flag (set to 1, undefined4)\n    0x34: Primary hit flag (undefined4)\n    0x38: Secondary hit flag (undefined4)\n    0x3c: Callback function pointer (code *)\n    0x44: Tick count storage (DWORD)\n    0x4c: Callback guard flag (undefined4)\nnCoordinatePacked: 32-bit packed coordinate with X in low word (0-15), Y in high word (16-31)\n\nReturns:\n1: Coordinates matched primary or secondary bounds rectangle\n0: Coordinates outside both bounds rectangles\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Callback is invoked with guard flag (offset 0x4c) set to 1 before call and 0 after\n- Both bounds regions share the same width value at offset 0x28\n- 