      "comment": "C++ destructor for resource wrapper object with SEH protection\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Set up Structured Exception Handling (SEH) frame\n2. Install vtable pointer at offset 0x0 (0x6fba8654)\n3. Initialize SEH state to 0 (construction complete)\n4. Check if resource pointer at offset +0x8 is non-NULL\n5. If resource exists, call virtual function at vtable[0] with parameter 1 (Release/Close)\n6. Update SEH state to 0xFFFFFFFF (destruction phase)\n7. Call base class destructor to finalize vtable (sets vtable to 0x6fba90fc)\n8. Restore previous exception handler and clean up SEH frame\n\nParameters:\n  pThis (ResourceWrapper *) - Pointer to ResourceWrapper instance being destroyed\n  IMPLICIT ECX - Contains pThis pointer per __fastcall convention\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value (destructor)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If resource pointer at offset +0x8 is NULL, skips resource release step\n  - SEH protection ensures exception safety during destruction\n  - Virtual function call uses double indirection: (**(vtable_at_offset_8))(1)\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x6fba8654 - Vtable pointer for this class (destructor vtable)\n  0x6fba90fc - Base class vtable pointer (finalized state)\n  0x6fba4348 - SEH exception handler address\n  0x0 - Initial SEH state (construction complete)\n  0xFFFFFFFF - Final SEH state (destruction in progress)\n  0x1 - Parameter to resource release function (likely release/close operation)\n  0x8 - Offset to managed resource pointer within ResourceWrapper\n\nStructure Layout:\n  Offset | Size | Field Name        | Type    | Description\n  -------|------|-------------------|---------|----------------------------------\n  +0x0   | 4    | vtable            | void *  | Virtual function table pointer\n  +0x4   | 4    | dwUnknown         | uint    | Unknown field\n  +0x8   | 4    | pResource         | void *  | Managed resource pointer (checked for NULL)",
