      "comment": "Initialize text display configuration buffer and read text display mode setting.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Clear 39 dwords (0x27) in text display buffer starting at g_abTextDisplayBuffer\n2. Clear remaining 2 words and 1 byte (total buffer size ~158 bytes)\n3. Call Ordinal_423 (Storm.GetPrivateProfileInt) with Diablo II path, \"Text Display Beta\" key to read configuration\n4. If call succeeds (return != 0), extract dwTextConfig value from output parameter\n5. If call fails, set g_dwTextDisplayMode to 1 (default enabled)\n\nParameters:\n(none)\n\nReturns:\n(void) - Populates g_dwTextDisplayMode global\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Uses REP STOSD/STOSW/STOSB for efficient buffer clearing\n- Magic number 0x27 = 39 dwords = 156 bytes cleared\n- Ordinal_423 = Storm.GetPrivateProfileInt - reads integer setting from registry/Storm configuration\n- Default value 1 indicates text display enabled on read failure\n\nRelated Functions:\n- FUN_6fb5a0b0 - Main initialization routine that calls this function",
