      "comment": "Validates linked list of messages and compacts by clearing head pointer if counts match.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load head node pointer from pMessageListHead[0]\n2. If NULL, skip validation (no messages to process)\n3. Initialize sCountDeleted = 0 to track processed nodes\n4. Iterate through linked list: for each node, validate 6 fields (dwords at +0, +4, +8, +12, +16, +20)\n5. If field non-zero, call Ordinal_10043(0x6ad, 0) to log field validation (Storm.dll assertion)\n6. After all 6 fields checked, call Ordinal_10043(0x6b0, 0) to log node validation\n7. Advance to next node via pMessageListHead->field[+0x22], increment sCountDeleted\n8. Repeat until reached NULL node\n9. Clear head pointer: pMessageListHead[0] = 0\n10. Compare sCountDeleted with expected count in pMessageListHead[1]\n11. If match: clear count field pMessageListHead[1] = 0 and return\n12. If mismatch: log assertion failure and call ExitProcess(0xffffffff)\n\nParameters:\npMessageListHead - Pointer to message list header structure with:\n  [0] = pointer to first message node (or NULL)\n  [1] = expected message count (word)\n  At offset +0x22 in each node: pointer to next message node (or NULL)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value on success; calls ExitProcess on count mismatch\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Null-safe: tolerates NULL head pointer, exits immediately\n- Count validation: fatal error if sCountDeleted != expected count\n- Field validation: calls Ordinal_10043 for each field and node",
