      "instructions": ["0x84A90|SUB|ESP, 0x8", "0x84A93|PUSH|EBX", "0x84A94|PUSH|EBP", "0x84A95|MOV|EBP, ECX", "0x84A97|PUSH|ESI", "0x84A98|MOV|ESI, EDX", "0x84A9A|PUSH|EDI", "0x84A9B|MOV|EBX, dword ptr [EBP + 0x4]", "0x84A9E|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x10], ESI", "0x84AA2|CMP|EBX, 0xa", "0x84AA5|JBE|0x6fb54aac", "0x84AA7|MOV|EBX, 0xa", "0x84AAC|MOV|EDI, dword ptr [EBP]", "0x84AAF|TEST|EBX, EBX", "0x84AB1|JZ|0x6fb54b44"],
      "comment": "Renders items from a linked list within screen bounds, constraining dimensions to max 10 items.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load item count from pListHead[1], cap at 10 items max\n2. Load list head pointer from pListHead[0]\n3. Validate: count > 0, head != NULL, nYOffset >= 0, total height within screen\n4. Call FUN_6fb92980 to setup rendering context with scaled dimensions\n5. Call Ordinal_10127 to begin rendering batch (Storm.dll)\n6. Iterate nIndex from 0 to dwMaxCount:\n   - Break if pNode becomes NULL\n   - Calculate palette index: (nIndex - dwMaxCount + count) * 15 + offset\n   - Call Ordinal_10117 to render item at computed coordinates (Storm.dll)\n   - Advance pNode via pointer at offset +4\n7. Call Ordinal_10127 to end rendering batch\n\nParameters:\n- pListHead (int *): Pointer to structure with [0]=head, [1]=count, [0x10]=width, [0x12]=height\n- nWidgetId (int): Widget/inventory ID passed to rendering functions\n- nYOffset (int): Y-coordinate offset for rendering position\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Items capped at 10 max regardless of list size\n- NULL head pointer bypasses entire rendering\n- Negative Y offset causes early exit\n- Screen height overflow prevents rendering\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x10: Width offset in pListHead structure (ushort)\n- 0x12: Height offset in pListHead structure (ushort, distance from top)\n- 0x4: Next pointer offset in linked list nodes\n- 0xa: Max item count (10)\n- 0xf: Palette stride multiplier (15 bytes per item palette)\n- 0x5: Height padding subtraction\n- 0x12: Base palette offset constant",
