      "comment": "HandleGameStateMessage - Processes game state change messages with throttling.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Skip if message subtype is 0x73 (specific exclusion)\n2. Check if keybinding command 7 matches message - if so, skip (already handled)\n3. Reset frame counter\n4. Throttle: if less than 100ms since last update, cache message and return\n5. Execute ManageGameStateExecution to process state change\n6. On success, cache message with processed flag\n\nParameters:\n  pMessage - Pointer to message structure:\n    +0x08: Message subtype/keycode\n    +0x18: Processed flag (set to 1)\n    +0x1c: Result status (set to 0)\n\nReturns: void\n\nGlobals Used:\n  g_dwFrameCounter - Reset on each call\n  g_dwLastGameStateUpdateTime - Throttle timestamp\n  g_bGameStateProcessing - State flag\n\nCalled from: Message dispatch jump table",
