      "instructions": ["0x85000|PUSH|EBX", "0x85001|PUSH|ESI", "0x85002|PUSH|EDI", "0x85003|MOV|EDI, 0x1", "0x85008|MOV|dword ptr [0x6fbfcfc7], EDI", "0x8500E|CALL|0x6fae52a0", "0x85013|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0x85015|JZ|0x6fb5507c", "0x85017|MOV|EAX, [0x6fbfcf92]", "0x8501C|XOR|EBX, EBX", "0x8501E|CMP|EAX, EBX", "0x85020|JZ|0x6fb5503e", "0x85022|MOV|ECX, dword ptr [0x6fbfcf8a]", "0x85028|MOV|EDX, EDI", "0x8502A|CALL|0x6fb60e10"],
      "comment": "Process and validate game state update, checking resource handles and timing constraints before execution.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Set update flag (DAT_6fbfcfc7 = 1) to indicate processing\n2. Retrieve current validated resource handle via GetValidatedResourceHandle()\n3. If no valid handle exists, proceed to resource initialization check:\n   - Check if DAT_6fbfcfc2 flag is set (indicates resource initialization needed)\n   - If set, attempt to allocate resources: call FUN_6fb60e10 with DAT_6fbfcfc3 param\n   - If allocation fails, return without processing\n   - Verify both resource handles match via second FUN_6fb60e10 call with DAT_6fbfcf8a\n   - If handles don't match, return without processing\n   - Jump to final state update\n4. If valid handle exists:\n   - Check if DAT_6fbfcf92 flag is set (resource validation flag)\n   - If set, compare current handle with stored handle (DAT_6fbfcf8a)\n   - If they match, return early (optimization: skip expensive state update)\n5. Reset DAT_6fbfcf82 = 0 (frame counter or state flag)\n6. Get current tick count via GetTickCount()\n7. Check if time elapsed since last update (GetTickCount() - DAT_6fbfcfb4) is less than 100ms:\n   - If less than 100ms, skip game state execution and jump to state update\n   - If 100ms or more, call ManageGameStateExecution() to process game logic\n8. Check return value from ManageGameStateExecution():\n   - If return is 0 (failure/no-op), return without updating state\n   - Otherwise, proceed to final state update\n9. Final state update:\n   - Set [pGameState + 0x18] = 1 (state flags)\n   - Set [pGameState + 0x1c] = 0 (state counter or status)\n   - Call Ordinal_511(pGameState) for final processing\n   - Clear update flag (DAT_6fbfcfc7 = 0)\n\nParameters:\npGameState (void *) - Pointer to game state structure with fields at offsets 0x18 and 0x1c\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Function returns after state update or early exit conditions\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Returns early if resource handle allocation fails\n- Returns early if resource handles don't match during initialization\n- Returns early if tick count elapsed is less than 100ms (throttling mechanism)\n- Returns early if ManageGameStateExecution() returns 0\n- Ordinal_511 is called with pGameState for final processing (likely D2Common or Game engine function)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x18 - offset in pGameState structure for state flags field\n- 0x1c - offset in pGameState structure for state counter/status field\n- 100 (0x64) - minimum milliseconds required between game state updates (throttle interval)\n- 1, 0 - state flag values written to pGameState offsets\n\nGlobal Dependencies:\nDAT_6fbfcfc7 - update processing flag (set=processing, clear=complete)\nDAT_6fbfcfc2 - resource initialization needed flag\nDAT_6fbfcfc3 - resource initialization parameter\nDAT_6fbfcf8a - stored resource handle for comparison\nDAT_6fbfcf82 - frame counter or state reset flag\nDAT_6fbfcfb4 - timestamp of last game state update (for throttling)\nDAT_6fbfcf92 - resource validation/comparison flag",
