      "comment": "Finalize unit selection state with unit data snapshot.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. If unit pointer is non-null, set finalization flag to 1 (true)\n2. Extract unit data field at offset +8 and store in global snapshot\n3. Return with unit selection marked as finalized\n4. If unit pointer is null, set finalization flag to 0 (false)\n5. Return with unit selection cleared\n\nParameters:\npUnit - Pointer to unit structure being finalized\n        IMPLICIT: Passed in ECX register (__fastcall convention)\n        Structure offsets: +8 = dwUnitData field containing state information\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Updates globals g_bUnitSelectionFinalized and g_dwSelectedUnitData\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Null pointer (zero) clears finalization flag and global data\n- Non-null pointer extracts 32-bit value from offset +8 regardless of unit type\n- Called during unit selection finalization phase by ProcessUnitSelection\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x1 (1 decimal) - Finalization flag SET (true value)\n0x0 (0 decimal) - Finalization flag CLEAR (false/null value)\n0x8 (8 decimal) - Offset within unit structure for data field\n\nGlobal State Modified:\ng_bUnitSelectionFinalized @ 0x6fbfcfc2 - Selection state flag (byte)\ng_dwSelectedUnitData @ 0x6fbfcfc3 - Snapshot of unit data at offset +8 (dword)",
