      "comment": "Place a UI panel on screen with collision detection against reserved areas.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get item handle properties: height, width via Ordinal_10895/10121\n2. Calculate panel dimensions: width = (height+0x14)>>1, height_pixels = height*0xf+6\n3. Calculate initial position from coords: left offset, top offset -0x32\n4. Load reserved area array from globals: DAT_6fbfce30-3c (up to 16 areas)\n5. If area count < 0x10 and count > 0:\n   a. For each reserved area, call IntersectRect to check overlap with panel\n   b. If overlap found: enter collision avoidance loop\n6. Collision avoidance:\n   a. Iterate grid 400x280px with 50px/35px stepping\n   b. For each potential position, check bounds: x >= 0, x+400 <= screen_width, y >= 0, y+280 <= screen_height\n   c. Check intersection with all reserved areas via IntersectRect\n   d. If no collisions found: store position and exit loop\n7. Store final position in next array slot (area_count * 0x10 offset)\n8. Call FUN_6fb55740 to apply panel display\n9. Cleanup: ProcessItemCleanupNotification, Ordinal_10043\n\nParameters:\n  nPanelType (ECX) - Panel/window type identifier\n  dwItemHandle (EDX) - Item handle for property lookup\n  dwFlags (Stack[0x4]) - Flags parameter (used for validation)\n  pCoords (Stack[0x8]) - Pointer to [x, y] coordinate array\n\nReturns:\n  void - Modifies global reserved area array in-place, updates coords array\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If initial height check fails (Ordinal_10895 < DAT_6fbfcf96): clear item flags, return early\n  - Grid collision loop exits if position exhausts width (400px) after testing all heights\n  - Empty area array (count == 0): stores position without collision checking\n  - Max 16 reserved areas supported; addition beyond limit discards excess\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x657 - Ordinal_10042 parameter (allocation size/type)\n  0xb4 - Ordinal_10199 parameter (property offset/size)\n  0x14 - Height padding constant\n  0xf - Height scaling factor\n  0x6 - Height offset constant\n  0x32 - Top offset constant (-50 pixels)\n  0x190 - 400 pixels (grid cell width)\n  0x118 - 280 pixels (grid cell height)\n  0x23 - 35 pixels (vertical step)\n  0x32 - 50 pixels (horizontal step)\n  0x10 - Array stride (16 bytes per reserved area)\n  0xc8 (200 decimal) - Offset in param_1 for clearing flags\n\nReserved Area Array Layout:\n  Offset | Size | Field | Type | Description\n  0x00   | 4    | left  | int  | Left edge of reserved area\n  0x04   | 4    | top   | int  | Top edge of reserved area  \n  0x08   | 4    | right | int  | Right edge of reserved area\n  0x0c   | 4    | bottom| int  | Bottom edge of reserved area",
      "tags": ["MOD_UI", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "STRUCT_ItemData", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData", "STRUCT_StatList", "PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Path", "SRC_text.cpp", "STRUCT_Skill", "PARAM_4", "PROP_LOOPHEAVY"]
