      "instructions": ["0x85740|PUSH|ESI", "0x85741|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0x85743|PUSH|EDI", "0x85744|MOV|EDI, EDX", "0x85746|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [ESI + 0x16]", "0x85749|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0x8574B|JNZ|0x6fb55756", "0x8574D|MOV|dword ptr [ESI + 0x16], 0x1", "0x85754|JMP|0x6fb5575b", "0x85756|CMP|EAX, 0x3", "0x85759|JZ|0x6fb557ac", "0x8575B|CALL|0x6fae4fd0", "0x85760|DEC|EAX", "0x85761|JZ|0x6fb5578c", "0x85763|DEC|EAX"],
      "comment": "Process window panel scrolling with directional boundary validation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize panel scroll state flag (offset 0x16) to 1 if currently zero\n2. Return 1 immediately if panel state equals 3 (panel disabled/blocked)\n3. Query current scroll window mode via GetScrollWindowMode()\n4. Validate horizontal boundary based on scroll mode:\n   - Mode 1 (left panel): Reject if X > (screen_width/2 - 10)\n   - Mode 2 (right panel): Reject if X < (screen_width/2 + 10)\n   - Mode 3 (disabled): Reject immediately\n5. If boundary validation passes, render panel items via RenderLinkedListItems()\n6. Return 1 (success)\n\nParameters:\npPanelData (PanelData *) - Panel structure; offset 0x16 contains state flag\npCoordX (int *) - Coordinate array [0]=X position, [1]=Y position\n\nReturns:\n1 - Boundary check complete; panel rendered or validation rejected\n0 - Not returned (always returns 1)",
      "tags": ["PARAM_2"]
