      "comment": "RenderUnitNameLabel - Renders a floating name label above a unit or missile.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get object pointer from unit structure (field at offset +0x5B)\n2. Return early if object pointer is null\n3. Get unit world coordinates and convert to screen coordinates\n4. Adjust X position based on scroll window mode (left/right panel offsets)\n5. Check if unit is within visible screen bounds\n6. Get unit name string and process UTF-8 text\n7. Validate string ID is in valid range (1-0xFFFF)\n8. Initialize Unicode name buffer with default constructors\n9. Copy name string with length limit (199 chars max)\n10. Place window panel with collision detection for label positioning\n\nParameters:\n  pUnit - Pointer to UnitAny structure to render name for\n\nReturns: void\n\nNotes:\n- Called from ProcessUnitHashTableWithCallback and IterateMissileHashTable\n- Uses PlaceWindowPanelWithCollisionDetection for smart label positioning\n- Screen bounds check includes 100 pixel margin on X axis",
