      "comment": "Process text/UI rendering with timing-based scroll position calculations.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate pScrollState pointer; assert if NULL\n2. Call Ordinal_10127() for pre-render sync\n3. Get current time via timeGetTime()\n4. Initialize scroll timestamps if first call (field 0x1e == 0)\n5. Calculate scroll time deltas and offset accumulation based on frame timing\n6. Update scroll position for current frame (pScrollState[2])\n7. Check display mode and conditionally render UI panels if needed\n8. Process scroll list iteration: loop through linked list, check scroll bounds (0x17800)\n9. Track first visible item and calculate rendering positions\n10. Render visible items with Ordinal_10117/10119/10125 ordinal calls\n11. Call Ordinal_10127() for post-render sync\n12. Calculate final visibility check based on calculated scroll range\n13. Return result: 1 if needs scrollbar, 0 if not needed\n\nParameters:\n  pScrollState (int *) - Pointer to scroll state structure containing:\n    [+0x00] - Head of linked list (first item pointer)\n    [+0x04] - Items per visible area (param_1[1])\n    [+0x08] - Current scroll offset accumulator (param_1[2])\n    [+0x0c] - Scroll multiplier/scale factor (param_1[3])\n    [+0x1a] - Last render time (DWORD)\n    [+0x1e] - Initial timestamp flag (DWORD)\n    [+0x22] - Time divisor for scaling (DWORD)\n    [+0x26] - Accumulated offset (DWORD)\n    [+0x2a] - Frame count (USHORT)\n\nReturns:\n  uint - 1 if scrollbar needed, 0 if content fits\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - NULL pointer parameter triggers assertion and exit\n  - g_dwScreenInitFlag suppresses rendering if set\n  - g_dwRenderStateFlag = 0 resets rendering cache after final frame\n  - Display only happens if g_dwTextDisplayMode or g_dwFrameCounter are non-zero\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x17800 - Scroll boundary threshold (96256 in decimal)\n  0x4800 - Linked list stride/item size (18432 bytes)\n  0x400 - Sub-pixel scaling offset (1024)\n  0x70 - Screen row baseline offset\n  0x5e - Maximum visible row offset\n  0x12 - Maximum row height cap (18)\n  0x1c000 - Final scroll range limit (114688)\n  0x0a - Bit shift for position scaling (>> 10)",
      "tags": ["MOD_UI", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "STRUCT_ItemData", "PARAM_1", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData", "STRUCT_MonsterData", "PROP_LARGE", "SRC_text.cpp", "STRUCT_Skill", "STRUCT_Other", "PROP_LOOPHEAVY"]
