      "instructions": ["0x86400|SUB|ESP, 0x10", "0x86403|PUSH|EDI", "0x86404|XOR|EDI, EDI", "0x86406|CMP|word ptr [0x6fbfcf76], DI", "0x8640D|JZ|0x6fb565a8", "0x86413|PUSH|EBX", "0x86414|PUSH|EBP", "0x86415|PUSH|ESI", "0x86416|MOV|ECX, 0xd", "0x8641B|CALL|0x6fb99a02", "0x86420|MOV|ESI, dword ptr [0x6fbfcf72]", "0x86426|MOV|ECX, 0x6", "0x8642B|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x1c], EAX", "0x8642F|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x10], ESI", "0x86433|MOV|EBP, 0xf"],
      "comment": "Render active slots and clean up expired ones from the slot list\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if slot list is empty (g_nSlotCount2 == 0), exit if so\n2. Call Ordinal_10127() to initialize drawing (D2Common.EndDrawing or FlushDrawBuffer)\n3. Determine opacity level (0x0f or 0x64) based on FUN_6fb5d340() checks for states 6 and 0x11\n4. Iterate through linked list of slots:\n   - For each slot, iterate 6 slot items (stride 0x19 bytes)\n   - If slot item active (*piVar6 != 0): get Unicode strlen, call Ordinal_10123 for color, render with FUN_6fb92980, apply effects with Ordinal_10117\n   - Move to next slot via offset 0x22 (next pointer)\n5. Get current tick count via GetTickCount()\n6. Iterate slots again for expiration check:\n   - If slot lifetime (offset 0x1e) exceeded current tick, mark for removal\n   - Decrement g_nSlotCount2, unlink from list, clear slot data with Ordinal_10043(0x6ad), finalize with Ordinal_10043(0x6b0)\n   - Update previous pointer to skip removed node\n7. Call Ordinal_10127() to finalize drawing\n\nParameters: none (__stdcall)\n\nReturns: void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If g_nSlotCount2 == 0, entire function skipped (early exit)\n- Opacity changes based on game state (15 vs 100)\n- Slot removal is in-place linked list deletion\n- Slot contains 6 items at fixed offsets (stride 0x19)\n- Each item at offset 0x1a contains packed data for rendering\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x0f: Low opacity level (15)\n- 0x64: High opacity level (100)\n- 0x19: Item stride in slot (25 bytes)\n- 0x96: Maximum scan offset for items (150 bytes = 6 items)\n- 0x22: Next slot pointer offset\n- 0x1a: Item data offset within slot\n- 0x1e: Slot lifetime/expiration offset\n- 0x6ad: Ordinal_10043 parameter for item clear\n- 0x6b0: Ordinal_10043 parameter for finalization\n\nStructure Layout (Slot Node):\nOffset | Size | Field Name | Type | Description\n0x00   | 4    | Reserved   | uint | (Unknown, may contain item data)\n0x04   | 4    | Reserved   | uint | (Unknown)\n0x08   | 4    | Reserved   | uint | (Unknown)\n0x0c   | 4    | Reserved   | uint | (Unknown)\n0x10   | 4    | Reserved   | uint | (Unknown)\n0x14   | 4    | Reserved   | uint | (Unknown)\n0x1a   | 4    | ItemData   | uint | Packed item/effect data\n0x1e   | 4    | Expiration | uint | Tick count when slot expires\n0x22   | 4    | NextNode   | Slot* | Pointer to next slot in list\n\nRelated Functions:\n- RenderGameFrame: Calls this function each frame\n- FUN_6fb5d340: Determines game state for opacity\n- FUN_6fb92980: Renders slot with text/color\n- Ordinal_10123 (D2Common): Get color code\n- Ordinal_10127 (D2Common): Draw synchronization\n- Ordinal_10117 (D2Common): Apply visual effects\n- Ordinal_10043 (D2Common): Skill data lookup/cleanup",
