      "comment": "Initialize a slot data structure from source data. Allocates memory, copies slot metadata (count and flags), and links the slot into a linked list.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate 0x26 bytes for new slot structure via Ordinal_10042(0x9ca, 0)\n2. Clear 9 dwords + 1 word in allocated buffer\n3. Loop through source slots by count at [pSlotSource + 0x18], copying strings via strcpy\n4. Copy slot metadata: count (offset 0x18) and flags (offset 0x1a)\n5. If g_wSlotDataCount > 0x1f AND g_slotDataStructure != NULL, traverse list via offset 0x22 pointers to find tail\n6. For last node found: iterate 6 times calling Ordinal_10043(0x6ad) for non-zero entries, then Ordinal_10043(0x6b0)\n7. Unlink old tail by clearing previous node's offset 0x22 pointer\n8. Decrement g_wSlotDataCount\n9. Link new slot at offset 0x22 to current g_slotDataStructure\n10. Increment g_wSlotDataCount and update g_slotDataStructure to new slot\n\nParameters:\npSlotSource (int *): Source slot structure pointer with metadata at +0x18 (ushort count) and +0x1a (uint flags)\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Slot counter g_wSlotDataCount capped at 0x20 (32 slots max)\n- Unaffected registers unaff_ESI and unaff_EDI used for string operations\n- Linked list maintained via pointers at offset 0x22\n- Uses two undocumented Ordinals: Ordinal_10042 (memory allocation), Ordinal_10043 (output/logging)",
      "tags": ["MOD_UI", "STRUCT_Inventory", "SRC_text.cpp", "PARAM_1", "PROP_LOOPHEAVY", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
