      "api_calls": ["SetActiveFont", "FogMemAlloc", "MeasureTextWidthWithEscapes", "FogMemAlloc", "FogAssert", "ReleasePoolAllocation", "ReleasePoolAllocation", "SetActiveFont"],
      "instructions": ["0x86920|SUB|ESP, 0x410", "0x86926|PUSH|EBX", "0x86927|PUSH|EBP", "0x86928|MOV|EBP, ECX", "0x8692A|PUSH|ESI", "0x8692B|PUSH|EDI", "0x8692C|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x18], EDX", "0x86930|MOV|ECX, 0xd", "0x86935|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x10], EBP", "0x86939|CALL|0x6fb99a02", "0x8693E|MOV|EDX, 0x6fbc78a8", "0x86943|MOV|ECX, 0x26", "0x86948|PUSH|0x0", "0x8694A|PUSH|0xd56", "0x8694F|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x24], EAX"],
      "comment": "Process text wrapping for slot display with line breaking and memory allocation\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize temporary slot structure (36 bytes) via Ordinal_10042(0xd56, 0)\n2. Clear structure fields (9 DWORDs + WORD)\n3. Set timeout to current time + 10000ms\n4. Measure text length via Unicode::strlen\n5. Main loop: calculate line width, find break point, wrap text\n6. While measuring text width > (screen width - 0x46):\n   - Decrement position, re-measure until fits\n7. If line content found and width > 0:\n   - Search backwards for valid line break via Unicode::isLineBreak\n   - Continue searching if break invalid\n8. If no break or > 5 lines:\n   - Add slot to list, call InitializeSlotData\n   - If 2+ slots, remove first (FIFO), call Ordinal_10043 cleanup\n   - Check FUN_6fb5d340(0x18) result\n   - If true and callback exists, invoke callback for all slots\n9. Otherwise allocate line buffer, copy text, increment line counter\n10. Continue until all text processed\n\nParameters:\npTextData (int *) - Pointer to Unicode text data (base address for UTF-16 text)\ndwColor (uint) - Color value masked to 0xFF for display\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Modifies global slot list\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Function loops infinitely processing text until completion\n- Line count capped at 6 (removal of oldest slot when exceeded)\n- Callback invoked only if FUN_6fb5d340 returns non-zero\n- Screen width constraint: (g_dwScreenWidth - 0x46) pixels\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0xd56 (3414) - Slot structure allocation size\n0xd80 (3456) - Line buffer allocation size\n0x1e (30) - Offset to timeout field\n0x22 (34) - Offset to next pointer in linked list\n0x1a (26) - Offset to color field\n0x18 - Threshold for special processing\n10000 - Timeout milliseconds\n0x46 (70) - Screen width margin\n0x6 - Maximum line count before removal\n0x6ad, 0x6b0 - Cleanup ordinal parameters\n\nGlobal Data Used:\ng_dwScreenWidth - Screen width in pixels\ng_pSlotList2Head - Head of slot linked list\ng_nSlotCount2 - Current slot count\ng_slotDataStructure - Slot data array\ng_pCallbackFunction - Callback function pointer",
