      "instructions": ["0x86C00|SUB|ESP, 0x20", "0x86C03|MOV|EAX, [0x6fbae0e4]", "0x86C08|PUSH|EBX", "0x86C09|MOV|EBX, EDX", "0x86C0B|ADD|EAX, 0xfffffebb", "0x86C10|CDQ|", "0x86C11|PUSH|EBP", "0x86C12|PUSH|ESI", "0x86C13|SUB|EAX, EDX", "0x86C15|PUSH|EDI", "0x86C16|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0x86C18|XOR|EDI, EDI", "0x86C1A|SAR|EAX, 0x1", "0x86C1C|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x10], EBX", "0x86C20|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x14], ESI"],
      "comment": "Initialize game state after loading configuration and game data.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate screen layout dimensions: item list buffer offset based on screen width\n2. Initialize game state flags to zero (cleanups, packets, item queues)\n3. Initialize targeting system for unit selection\n4. If resource handle exists: unload previous resources via FUN_6fb8d0c0, clear with FUN_6fb8d670\n5. If pGameData is NULL: clear all active item queues, reset item queue flags\n6. Else if validation required: check resource handle validity, reinitialize game arrays if changed\n7. Set validation flag and store new resource handle from pGameData[2]\n8. Calculate viewport bounds: local view rect based on screen dimensions\n9. Configure display data (width 0x145, height 0x70) via CopyConfigurationData()\n10. Clear unit selection state via ClearUnitSelectionState()\n11. If no item list exists:\n    a. Initialize texture system: allocate new GUI window structure (0x2c bytes)\n    b. Set window dimensions: width 0x145 px, height 0x70 px\n    c. Create text rendering object via FUN_6fb56f10()\n    d. Initialize slot list by scanning all items, calculate max text width\n    e. Set final window dimensions based on content\n12. Load game mode-specific data via FUN_6fb7dfd0(nConfigMode)\n13. If load succeeded: initialize game renderer and message processing\n14. Set game initialization flag, update game state\n\nParameters:\npGameData (int *): Pointer to game configuration structure, or NULL to reset; contains resource at offset +2\nnConfigMode (short): Game mode/difficulty configuration flags\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x145 - Window width in pixels (325 decimal)\n0x70 - Window height in pixels (112 decimal)\n0xc - Initial viewport Y offset (12 decimal)\n0xb6 - Viewport height calculation offset (182 decimal)\n0x35 - Screen border offset (53 decimal)\n0x14 - Text row height padding (20 decimal)\n0xf - Character width multiplier (15 decimal)\n0x30 - Message type: RESET_ITEM_QUEUE\n0x609, 0x60a - Item queue message types (1545, 1546)\n0x688 - Clear item queue message type (1672)\n0x657 - Create GUI window message (1623)\n0x2c - Window structure size (44 decimal)\n0x26 - Offset to item list end marker\n\nRelated Functions:\n- FUN_6fb7dfd0() - Load game resources for mode\n- FUN_6fb56f10() - Create text rendering object\n- CopyConfigurationData() - Apply display configuration\n- ClearUnitSelectionState() - Reset unit selection\n- InitializeGameUnitArrays() - Reset unit data\n- FUN_6fb8d0c0() - Unload resource handle\n- FUN_6fb8d210() - Initialize game renderer",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_MonsterData", "PROP_LARGE", "MOD_UI", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PARAM_2", "SRC_text.cpp", "STRUCT_Skill", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
