      "comment": "Parse Unicode-encoded string data into a linked list of line buffers.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize output list (pHead=NULL, pCurrent=NULL)\n2. Loop until wZero terminator (0x0000) encountered:\n   a. Allocate buffer via Ordinal_10042(0x5b2, 0) - allocate 0x5b2 bytes\n   b. Read ushorts until newline (0x000A) or 100 elements collected\n   c. If first iteration: validate input for non-ASCII (wChar > 0x7F), convert via toUtf\n   d. Query window size via Ordinal_10121() - check if line length exceeds 0x133\n   e. Allocate final buffer via Ordinal_10042(0x5e5, 0) - allocate 0x5e5 bytes\n   f. Copy decoded line into buffer via strcpy\n   g. Link buffer into list (pCurrent->next = new buffer)\n   h. Increment line counter\n3. Return pHead (first buffer in list)\n\nParameters:\npwLine (ushort *) - IMPLICIT in ECX - Pointer to Unicode string data (ushort array)\npdwLineCount (dword *) - IMPLICIT in EDX - Pointer to line counter (incremented per line parsed)\npwResult (ushort *) - Stack param - Result buffer for output status codes\n\nReturns:\ndword * - Pointer to head of parsed line buffer list (NULL if input is empty)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Empty input (wZero at start) returns NULL immediately\n- ASCII-only input processed via toUtf conversion\n- Non-ASCII content (wChar > 0x7F) sets pwResult=8, uses wprintfA error\n- Lines exceeding 100 elements truncated\n- Line length validation: fatal if exceeds 0x133 (307 chars)\n- Unaffected registers: ESI (pwLine ptr), EDI (result buffer)",
      "tags": ["PROP_LARGE", "MOD_UI", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "SRC_text.cpp", "PARAM_3", "PROP_LOOPHEAVY", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
