      "comment": "Initialize game state and configure UI viewport based on difficulty and expansion mode settings.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if expansion mode (bExpanded): set viewport Y offset from g_dwUIYOffset and X from g_dwUIXOffset, else use defaults (Y=0xc, X=centered on screen width)\n2. Set g_dwScreenInitFlag based on expansion flag\n3. Call InitializeTargetingSystem() to initialize targeting subsystem\n4. If g_pResourceHandle exists, call FUN_6fb8d0c0 to cleanup old resource, call FUN_6fb8d670 with resource handle and flags, clear handle\n5. Set viewport Y base and clamp to screen height - 0x35 limit\n6. Calculate viewport X bounds: base-10 for left edge, base+0x14f for right edge\n7. Call CopyConfigurationData with viewport offset address to read UI configuration\n8. Call ClearUnitSelectionState() to reset active selection\n9. Store nDifficulty in g_wConfigData global\n10. If g_pFirstItemList is NULL (first initialization only):\n    a. Set g_bGameReadyFlag = 0\n    b. Call Ordinal_10127 (D2Common.AllocMemory) for pool initialization\n    c. Call Ordinal_10004 (D2Common.GetMemoryPoolHandle) to get item data pool handle\n    d. Call Ordinal_10042(0x657, 0) to allocate config structure (1623 bytes)\n    e. Call Ordinal_10127 (D2Common.AllocMemory) again for pool\n    f. Call ParseUnicodeStringLine to parse item data and configure structure\n    g. Set structure fields: offset 0=parsed pointer, 0x4=0x145, 0x12=0x70, 0x1a-0x26=0, 0x2a=0\n    h. Call Ordinal_10127 for final pool allocation\n    i. Loop through item list via offset 4 pointer chain, find max Ordinal_10121 value\n    j. Set structure offset 0x4 to max+0x14, offset 0x12 to (width*0xf)+6\n    k. Set g_pFirstItemList to config structure pointer\n    l. If NULL (allocation failed), call Ordinal_10023 with error message and FUN_6fb9a10f to exit\n    m. Call Ordinal_10127 for pool allocation\n    n. Clear structure offset 0x16\n    o. Set g_bGameInitRequired=1, g_dwFrameCounter=1\n    p. If g_dwGameInitState==0: set to 1, get GetTickCount, call Ordinal_10027, ProcessMessageEntryArray with 7 messages\n    q. Call FUN_6fb7dfd0(nDifficulty) to get rendering resource\n    r. If resource valid: call FUN_6fb62880 for mode, call FUN_6fb8d210 to configure with cleanup flag\n11. Check if nDifficulty matches special values (0x7f, 0x4e22, 0x4ec9, 0x4ea3, 0x18c) and bEnableUI!=0: set g_bPacketPending=1\n\nParameters:\n- nDifficulty (short, CX): Difficulty level/game state ID, controls rendering resource and packet flag\n- bExpanded (int, EDX): Expansion mode flag (1=use expanded UI offsets, 0=use default centered offsets)\n- bEnableUI (int, stack): Enable UI packets flag (1=allow packet pending for special difficulties)\n\nReturns:\n- void: No return value, configures global state variables for game initialization\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- First initialization: Only executes item list setup if g_pFirstItemList==NULL\n- Config allocation failure: Ordinal_10023 called with error paths leading to FUN_6fb9a10f termination\n- Special difficulty values trigger packet pending when bEnableUI flag set\n- Multiple Ordinal_10127 calls manage memory pool state before critical operations\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x105: Max Y viewport before offset adjustment\n- 0xc: Default Y offset (12 pixels) for non-expanded mode\n- 0x145: Default viewport width (325 pixels)\n- 0x70: Item list height (112 pixels)\n- 0xb6: Viewport height offset (182 pixels)\n- 0x35: Screen height reduction (53 pixels)\n- 0x14f: Right edge offset (335 pixels)\n- 0x657: Config structure allocation size (1623 bytes)\n- 0xf: Item height multiplier factor\n- 6: Item list padding pixels\n- 0x14: Width padding (20 pixels)\n- 7: Default message queue count\n- 0x100c: Error code for config init failure\n- 0x7f, 0x4e22, 0x4ec9, 0x4ea3, 0x18c: Special difficulty/game state magic values",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_MonsterData", "PROP_LARGE", "MOD_UI", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "SRC_text.cpp", "PARAM_3", "STRUCT_Skill", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
