      "instructions": ["0x87E40|SUB|ESP, 0x14", "0x87E43|PUSH|ESI", "0x87E44|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0x87E46|PUSH|EDI", "0x87E47|MOV|AL, byte ptr [ESI + 0x1]", "0x87E4A|CMP|AL, 0x1", "0x87E4C|JNZ|0x6fb57ef2", "0x87E52|MOV|ECX, dword ptr [ESI + 0x2]", "0x87E55|MOV|EDX, 0x1", "0x87E5A|CALL|0x6fb60e10", "0x87E5F|MOV|EDI, EAX", "0x87E61|TEST|EDI, EDI", "0x87E63|JZ|0x6fb57ebb", "0x87E65|CMP|byte ptr [ESI + 0x6], 0x1", "0x87E69|JNZ|0x6fb57ebb"],
      "comment": "Processes game event messages for automap, game state, and UI updates. Supports three message types: automap operations (0x01), game state initialization (0x02), and cleanup.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load message type byte from offset +1, branch on value\n2. Type 0x01 (Automap):\n   a. Fetch unit node for resource ID (offset +2) via FUN_6fb60e10\n   b. Validate: unit exists AND offset+6==0x01 AND offset+8==0x03\n   c. If valid and unit.stat[0x32] exists: release stat via Ordinal_10893, update from config\n   d. If not valid: cleanup old automap, create new via Ordinal_10901, init via Ordinal_10910/10911\n3. Type 0x02 (Game State):\n   a. Fetch unit for resource ID\n   b. Check offset +8: if != 0x03, partial init path; if == 0x03, full init path\n   c. Partial (offset+8 != 0x03): set config flags via g_wGameConfigFlags, call InitializeGameState\n   d. Full (offset+8 == 0x03): \n      - Cleanup existing item queue (Ordinal_10043 for UI 0x609, 0x60a, 0x688)\n      - Allocate new item container (Ordinal_10042 for 0x657 resource)\n      - Initialize validation flag, calculate queue timeout from string length\n      - Setup scroll positions based on item dimensions\n4. Other types: cleanup automap via Ordinal_10902\n\nParameters:\nnEventMsg (IMPLICIT ECX, int) - Pointer to event message structure:\n  +0: [1 byte] Type indicator (0x01/0x02/other)\n  +2: [4 bytes] Resource ID (uint)\n  +6: [1 byte] Config flag\n  +8: [1 byte] State indicator (0x03=full init)\n  +10: [2 bytes] Game/Session ID (word)\nunaff_EDI (preserved EDI, char*) - String data pointer for timeout calculation\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- State byte 0x03 enables full initialization path with queue setup\n- Queue timeout multiplier: (strlen(unaff_EDI) + 0x19) * 200ms\n- Scroll calculation: Y = 100 - (item_height >> 2), X = 320 - (item_width >> 1)\n- Config flags stored in g_wGameConfigFlags (0x6fbfcfbc)\n- Automap handle in g_pAutomapHandle (0x6fbfcfe0)\n- Item queue pointer in g_pSecondItemList (0x6fbfcfd8)\n\nOrdinal Mappings (from KNOWN_ORDINALS.md):\n- Ordinal_10042: GetItemData - Allocate item container resource\n- Ordinal_10043: GetSkillData - Destroy/remove UI elements by ID\n- Ordinal_10199: Ordinal_10199 - Get item capacity/data\n- Ordinal_10892: Ordinal_10892 - Get localized config string\n- Ordinal_10893: Ordinal_10893 - Release resource/stat\n- Ordinal_10004: Ordinal_10004 - System initialization\n- Ordinal_10127: Ordinal_10127 - End drawing/flush\n- Ordinal_10901: Ordinal_10901 - Create automap\n- Ordinal_10902: Ordinal_10902 - Release automap\n- Ordinal_10910: Ordinal_10910 - Initialize automap config\n- Ordinal_10911: Ordinal_10911 - Finalize automap\n\nMessage Structure Layout:\nOffset | Size | Field | Type | Description\n0      | 1    | bType | byte | Message type (0x01=Automap, 0x02=State, other=Cleanup)\n1      | 1    | bPad  | byte | Padding/alignment\n2      | 4    | dwId  | uint | Resource ID for unit/item lookup\n6      | 1    | bCfg  | byte | Configuration flag (0x01 for automap)\n7      | 1    | bPad2 | byte | Padding\n8      | 1    | bSt   | byte | State (0x03=full init path)\n9      | 1    | bPad3 | byte | Padding\n10     | 2    | wGid  | word | Game/Session ID for initialization\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x01, 0x02, 0x03 - Type/state discriminators\n0xc8 - Unit stat offset (0x32 * 4 = 0xc8)\n0x609, 0x60a, 0x688 - UI element resource IDs\n0x657 - Item container resource ID\n0xb4 - Item capacity value\n0x16 - Queue validation flag offset\n0x12 - Queue item height offset\n0x10 - Queue item width offset\n0x64 - Scroll Y base value (100)\n0x140 - Scroll X base value (320)\n0x19 - Timeout constant multiplier\n0x200 - Scroll calculation multiplier\n0x100, 0x2 - Right shift amounts for scroll calc\n\nNote: Function contains compiler-optimized SSA intermediate values (piVar1, pvVar2) that appear in decompiled code but are optimized away by compiler. Local buffer abConfigBuffer[20] used for localization data.",
