      "comment": "Calculate ItemQueue container display dimensions based on linked list nodes.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Initialize maximum value tracker to 0 and clear container dimension fields\n  2. Load list head pointer from pContainer->pListHead\n  3. Load width multiplier from pContainer->wWidthMultiplier\n  4. For each node in linked list, call Ordinal_10121 to retrieve node dimension\n  5. Track maximum dimension value across all nodes\n  6. After iteration completes (empty list), calculate total height: max_value + 0x14\n  7. Calculate total width: (width_multiplier * 0xf) + 0x6\n  8. Store calculated height at pContainer->wCalculatedHeight\n  9. Store calculated width at pContainer->wCalculatedWidth\n\nParameters:\n  IMPLICIT ECX: pContainer (ItemQueueContainer*) - Item queue container with linked list head, dimensions, and multipliers\n\nReturns:\n  void - Updates container structure fields wCalculatedHeight and wCalculatedWidth in-place\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Empty list (pListHead == NULL): Height = 0x14, Width calculated from width_multiplier only\n  - Width multiplier field at offset +0x4: Proportionally affects total width calculation\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x14 - Height padding constant added to maximum node dimension\n  0xf - Width scaling factor applied to width_multiplier\n  0x6 - Base width offset added after scaling\n  0x4 - Next node pointer offset within each node structure\n\nStructure Layout (ItemQueueContainer):\n  Offset | Size | Field Name         | Type    | Description\n  0x0    | 4    | pListHead          | void*   | Pointer to first node in linked list\n  0x4    | 4    | dwItemCount        | uint    | Reserved/unused in this function\n  0x8    | 4    | dwReserved1        | uint    | Cleared by initialization\n  0xc    | 2    | wWidthMultiplier   | ushort  | Proportional width factor (multiply by 0xf)\n  0xe    | 2    | wHeightMultiplier  | ushort  | Reserved for future use\n  0x10   | 2    | wCalculatedHeight  | ushort  | Output: calculated total height\n  0x12   | 2    | wCalculatedWidth   | ushort  | Output: calculated total width",
