      "comment": "Iterate through linked list structure and process/clear nodes.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get linked list head pointer from unit handle (Ordinal_10897)\n2. If head pointer valid:\n   a. Load first node value from head pointer\n   b. While node value != 0:\n      - Load next node pointer from current node + 4 offset\n      - Clear flag 0x609 on node\n      - Clear flag 0x60a on node\n      - Move to next node\n   c. Clear flag 0x688 on head pointer\n   d. Finalize/cleanup unit with Ordinal_10898\n3. Cleanup/delete linked list with Ordinal_10893\n\nParameters:\nhUnit (uint, IMPLICIT ECX) - Unit/handle identifying the linked list structure\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value, function performs side effects on D2 unit data\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If head pointer is NULL (0x0), skips list iteration and goes directly to final cleanup\n- Linked list is terminated when node value equals 0x0\n- Linked list node format: [node_value | next_node_ptr @ +4]\n- Flag clearing indicates state transitions or resource cleanup\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x609 - Flag to clear during iteration (node-level)\n0x60a - Flag to clear during iteration (node-level)\n0x688 - Flag to clear after iteration completion (list-level)\n0x4 - Offset to next pointer field in linked list node",
