      "comment": "Process incoming network message with multi-purpose command handler supporting 7 command types.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Parse message type field (byte at +1): 0x01=SlotOp, 0x02=SlotCreate, 0x04=SlotExit, 0x05=SlotUpdate, 0x06=SlotSave, 0x07=SlotList\n2. Validate player ID (param at +4) via ValidateAndRemovePlayerById - return if invalid\n3. Initialize Unicode string buffer (0x100 elements) at [ESP+0x58]\n4. Check message command type (byte at +2) - dispatch to appropriate handler:\n   - Type 6/7/12/9: MultiByteToWideChar decode, validate ASCII range (<0x80), concatenate into slot\n   - Type 5 or else: win2Unicode decode\n5. Check message subcommand (byte at +1):\n   - 0x04: Minimal processing, direct return\n   - 0x06: SetupWideCharData -> Ordinal_10004 -> sprintf format -> CreateSlotObject type 2\n   - 0x02: ValidateNameLength(1-16) -> StringOps -> CreateSlotObject type 2\n   - 0x01: CallNameValidation -> SlotCreate with variable type\n   - 0x05: SlotUpdate -> Ordinal_10004 -> AppendName -> CreateSlotObject with custom type\n   - 0x07: TextSearch -> StorePlayerNameToBuffer\n6. CreateSlotObject with (buffer, type) via (EDX=type byte, ECX=buffer address)\n\nParameters:\nnMessageData (int, ECX): Pointer to message structure containing:\n  +1: Command type (0x01-0x07)\n  +2: Message class/command type (6,7,12,9 for encoding)\n  +3: Subtype or flags\n  +4: Player ID (validated before processing)\n  +8: Numeric type/slot ID parameter\n  +10: Additional name/text parameter (16 bytes max)\n  +26 (0x1a): Main text/name payload (256 bytes max)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Always returns (never fails, error cases logged via Ordinal_10029)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Command type 0x02: Validates name length 1-16, errors on >0x131 (305 bytes text)\n- Command type 0x01: Validates against player ID at +3, skips if +3 is 0x00\n- Ordinal_10007() used to get locale encoding info\n- Multiple Unicode buffer allocations (256/612 elements) for intermediate conversions\n- Error strings logged with source file/line numbers (0x12a1, 0x124b, 0x1278)",
