      "comment": "Game shutdown cleanup - processes resource cleanup and message queue flush.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call CopyConfigurationData to sync/copy current config state\n2. Iterate through g_pFirstItemList linked list nodes, clearing entries with Ordinal_10043\n3. Clear node pointers with Ordinal_10043(0x688, 0)\n4. Set g_pFirstItemList to NULL\n5. Check if g_pResourceHandle exists, call FUN_6fb8d0c0 to validate, then cleanup with FUN_6fb8d670(handle, 0, 0, 4)\n6. Set g_pResourceHandle to NULL\n7. Clear g_dwCleanupFlag to 0\n8. If g_dwGameInitState == 1: set to 0, call Ordinal_10027 (get HWND), process 7 messages from g_aMessageQueue\n9. If g_bPacketPending != 0: send packet 0x31 with data 0xffffffff and config word, clear flag\n10. Clear g_dwFrameCounter to 0\n11. If g_pAutomapHandle exists: call Ordinal_10902 to cleanup, set to NULL\n\nParameters:\n(none)\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Linked list iteration relies on node->next at offset +4 being valid\n- Cleanup proceeds even if some global state pointers are NULL (checked with CMP)\n- Message processing count hardcoded to 7\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x609, 0x60a: Ordinal_10043 subtypes for item list cleanup\n- 0x688: Ordinal_10043 subtype for final cleanup\n- 0x4: FUN_6fb8d670 parameter indicating resource cleanup type\n- 0x31: Packet type for pending data\n- 0xffffffff: Packet parameter (0xffffffff = all bits set)\n- 7: Message count for ProcessMessageArray",
