      "comment": "Dispatch game state handler based on current game state type field\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if g_pGameState pointer is non-null; exit if null\n2. Load dwStateType from offset +0x80 in game state structure\n3. Branch on state type constant:\n   - 0x20736b62 ('sk '): Call ProcessGameStateByType with mode 0\n   - 0x20646b62 ('dk '): Check g_dwExpansionMode flag; if zero call handler with mode 1, else call alternate handler\n   - 0x20317274 ('1rt'): Call alternate handler\n4. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\n(none - __stdcall)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - no return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- g_pGameState must be initialized before call; null pointer protection prevents crashes\n- Three distinct state type constants represent different game mode states\n- Expansion mode flag (g_dwExpansionMode) affects behavior for 'dk ' state type only\n- Magic numbers are little-endian ASCII: 0x20736b62='sk ', 0x20646b62='dk ', 0x20317274='1rt'\n\nRelated Functions:\n- FUN_6fb58b70: Handles 'sk ' and 'dk ' state transitions (parameter 0 or 1)\n- FUN_6fb589e0: Handles 'dk ' expansion and '1rt' state processing",
