      "comment": "Render game state validation UI and display panels.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if game validation system is active via FUN_6fb62880()\n2. Initialize property data arrays (2x 18 integers)\n3. Render base UI menu screen via RenderUIMenuScreen()\n4. Validate and write error log files:\n   - If g_dwValidationError1 == 0: Build path, call FUN_6fb9a261, write file via ConcatenatePathAndWriteFile\n   - If g_dwValidationError2 == 0: Repeat same process\n5. If nState != 0:\n   - Call Ordinal_10127() to begin rendering\n   - Store first error code in property array[1]\n   - Update animation tick counter (g_dwLastGameTick, g_dwValidationTickCount):\n     * If g_dwLastGameTick == 0: Initialize with GetTickCount()\n     * Else: Increment g_dwValidationTickCount if (GetTickCount() - g_dwLastGameTick) >= 0x32ms\n   - Loop through 8 UI panels (array from g_awPanelActiveFlags to g_pdwStatePointers):\n     * Calculate animation frame based on tick delta (0x0-0x4)\n     * If panel index < 6:\n       - Validate panel index (abort if >= 5)\n       - Calculate screen offset (index * 8) from panel coordinate tables\n       - Render property panel via Ordinal_10072 (x,y from g_adwUIScreenX/Y + offsets)\n       - Render secondary panel via Ordinal_10072 (x,y from g_adwUIPanel3X/Y)\n   - Call Ordinal_10127() to end rendering\n\nParameters:\nnState (ECX): Game state flag - non-zero enables rendering pass\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Panel index >= 5 causes fatal error via FUN_6fb9a10f(0xffffffff) with message\n- Animation frame limited to 0x4 (5 levels)\n- Magic number 0x32ms = 50ms animation tick interval\n- UI coordinate offsets: g_dwUIXOffset, g_dwUIYOffset applied to screen positions\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x12 (18): Array size for property data\n0x40 (64): Buffer size for path string\n0x32 (50): Millisecond interval for animation frame increment\n0xa6f (2735): Resource ID for animation effect\n0x5/0x4: Panel index validation limit\n0x6 (6): Maximum panels (0-5)\n0x6fbc7024: End address of panel array (validates loop bounds)",
