      "comment": "Initialize game state and targeting system with expansion mode detection.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Store provided game state pointer in global variable g_pGameState\n2. Call FUN_6fb5d370(0x10, 2, 0) to initialize underlying system components\n3. Call InitializeTargetingSystem() to set up targeting subsystem\n4. Load magic signature from game state at offset 0x80 and compare to 0x20646b62\n5. If expansion signature matches (expansion detected):\n   - Set g_dwExpansionMode flag to 1 (expansion enabled)\n   - Extract packet payload from pPacketData[8] and log via LogFiveBytePacket(0x3e)\n   - Clear global flag g_dwExpansionModeFlag to 0\n   - Return\n6. If signature does not match (standard mode):\n   - Set g_dwExpansionMode flag to 0 (expansion disabled)\n   - Set global flag g_dwExpansionModeFlag to 1\n   - Return\n\nParameters:\n- pPacketData (PacketData*): Incoming packet buffer with command payload at byte offset +8\n- pGameState (GameState*): Game state structure containing expansion mode signature at offset 0x80\n\nReturns:\n- void (updates global state variables)",
