      "comment": "Initializes character information dialog with viewport and dialog lines\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if g_dwDialogState is NULL (dialog not yet created)\n2. If already initialized, exit (early return)\n3. Set up SEH exception handler frame\n4. Call InitializeDialogStructure with dimensions (5 lines, 30 fields, screen width-20, screen height-130)\n5. Set first dialog field value to 1\n6. Call Ordinal_10004 (D2Client dialog event initializer) to initialize event system\n7. Add first dialog line with Y=0x15, index=4, value=1, line=0\n8. Call Ordinal_10004 again for second initialization\n9. Add second dialog line with Y=screen_height-0xa5, fixed at address 0x6fb59190\n10. Allocate memory block (12 bytes, aligned, -1 flags) using Ordinal_401 (Storm.dll/Allocate)\n11. If allocation fails, set g_pCallbackFunction to NULL and return\n12. If allocation succeeds, call InitializeViewportObject with dimensions (width-20, height-200)\n13. Append viewport to dialog linked list via AppendLinkedListNode\n14. Iterate through g_slotDataStructure linked list\n15. For each slot, call viewport render callback [EAX+0x30] with 10 parameters from slot data\n16. Set dialog line index to -1 via SetDialogLineIndex\n17. Restore exception handler and return\n\nParameters:\n(void)\n\nReturns:\n(void)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If g_dwDialogState is already set, function returns immediately without re-initializing\n- If Ordinal_401 memory allocation fails, viewport is not added to dialog\n- Slot structure uses 0x22 byte offset for next pointer in linked list traversal\n- Dialog viewport callback invoked with parameters from slot fields at fixed offsets\n\nVariable Mapping (SSA temporaries in decompiled code):\n- pMemory: Allocated viewport memory pointer from Ordinal_401\n- dwStatus: Status/error code tracking\n- pExceptionHandler: SEH exception handler frame pointer\n- nLineIndex, dwFieldIndex, nYCoord, dwXCoord, dwYCoord: Loop/calculation temporaries\n- pbDialogLabel, pdwSlotData: Structure field access intermediates",
