      "comment": "Handles mouse click events on dialog UI elements and processes corresponding game state changes.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get current mouse coordinates (nMouseX, nMouseY) from input functions\n2. Check if dialog state > 2 (indicates open dialog), if not skip dialog processing\n3. First dialog region check (0x111-0x133, 0xa8-0xca):\n   - Validate click within bounds\n   - Calculate offset from UI base (0xa7 - g_dwUIYOffset)\n   - Call Ordinal_10004 and Ordinal_10129 with coordinates\n4. Second dialog region check (0xdd-0xff, 0x17f-0x1a1):\n   - Validate click within bounds\n   - Calculate offset (0x17e - g_dwUIYOffset)\n   - Call handlers with adjusted coordinates\n5. Third dialog region check (0x111-0x133, 0x17f-0x1a1):\n   - Similar validation and offset calculation\n6. Check inventory/quest state with FUN_6fb62880()\n7. If state != 0:\n   - Get current state value\n   - Call Ordinal_10342 to process state\n   - Call FUN_6fb62890 for confirmation check\n   - If confirmed, process quest completion (Ordinal_10057, Ordinal_10086)\n8. Render active dialog if state in [1,2] and dialog pointers valid\n\nParameters:\n(void) - No parameters; uses global state\n\nReturns:\n(void) - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Dialog state 3-6 skipped (reserved states)\n- Null dialog pointers result in no rendering\n- Mouse coordinates checked against UI viewport offsets\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x111, 0x133: Dialog X bounds (upper region)\n- 0xa8, 0xca: Dialog Y bounds (upper region, 34 pixels tall)\n- 0xdd, 0xff: Dialog X bounds (lower-left region)\n- 0x17f, 0x1a1: Dialog Y bounds (lower region, 34 pixels tall)\n- 0x17e, 0xa7: Y offset calculations for button detection\n- 0x17: Quest item ID being processed\n- 0x4f: Packet type for quest completion\n- States 1-2: Active dialog indices\n\nNote: Function uses 2 compiler-generated phantom variables (extraout_var, extraout_var_00) that are optimized away during compilation. These cannot be renamed or typed as they are intermediate compiler results.",
