      "comment": "Initialize game objects and reset game state before starting new game/level.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Clear active dialog flag (g_dwActiveDialogFlag = 0)\n2. If dialog state 1 exists, close and cleanup, then clear reference\n3. If dialog state 2 exists, close and cleanup, then clear reference\n4. If game mode state != 7 (in-game):\n   a. Check if inventory/equipment state (0x17) is ready via FUN_6fb5d340\n   b. If inventory ready:\n      - Set inventory to unused state (FUN_6fb5d370 0x17,1,0)\n      - Clear game mode flag via ClearGameModeFlag()\n      - Initialize UI state via InitializeUIState()\n      - Get game mode ready status via FUN_6fb62890()\n      - If game not ready AND nInitMode != 0, set dialog state 1 to mode 2 (FUN_6fb5d370 1,2,0)\n   c. Check if dialog state 2 (0x5) is ready\n   d. If dialog state 2 ready, set to unused state (FUN_6fb5d370 5,1,0)\n5. If game mode state != 0, send packet 0x4f with mode 2, then clear state\n6. Return\n\nParameters:\nnInitMode (int, ECX) - Initialization mode; non-zero triggers alternate dialog configuration\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Uses game mode state at 0x6fbfd05c: 0x7 = in-game, other = preparing/menu\n- Dialog state 1 at 0x6fbfd020, dialog state 2 at 0x6fbfd058\n- Active dialog flag at 0x6fbfd060\n- Magic numbers: 0x17 = inventory state, 0x5 = dialog state 2, 0x4f = game reset packet\n\nRelated Functions:\n- CloseDialogAndCleanup() - Cleanup before state reset\n- FUN_6fb5d340(int) - Check object state readiness\n- FUN_6fb5d370(int,int,int) - Set object state\n- ClearGameModeFlag() - Clear game mode bits\n- InitializeUIState() - Reset UI elements\n- FUN_6fb62890() - Get game mode ready status\n- SendPackedData(int,int,int,int) - Network packet transmission",
