      "comment": "Validates whether game mode state allows active gameplay.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load current game mode state from g_dwGameModeState global variable\n2. Test if state value equals 0x1 (Playing mode) - jump to return true if match\n3. Test if state value equals 0x2 (Paused mode) - jump to return true if match\n4. If neither condition met, clear EAX and return false (0x0)\n5. If either condition met, set EAX to 0x1 and return true\n\nParameters:\n(none) - Function uses global game mode state via g_dwGameModeState\n\nReturns:\n0x1 - Game is in playable state (state value is 1 or 2)\n0x0 - Game is not in playable state (state value is any other value)\n\nSpecial Cases:\nMagic number 0x1: Game state representing active playing/gameplay mode\nMagic number 0x2: Game state representing paused mode (gameplay suspended but game active)\nGame logic requires active gameplay only when in these two specific states",
      "tags": ["PARAM_0", "PROP_LEAF", "PROP_SMALL"]
