      "api_calls": ["FogAssert", "ValidateStringId", "ValidateStringId", "QueueLogMessage", "INVENTORY_GetOwner", "ValidateStringId", "ValidateStringId", "ValidateStringId", "QueueLogMessage", "QueueLogMessage", "...+2 more"],
      "instructions": ["0x89700|PUSH|ESI", "0x89701|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0x89703|XOR|EAX, EAX", "0x89705|MOV|AL, byte ptr [ESI + 0x1]", "0x89708|CMP|EAX, 0x25", "0x8970B|JA|0x6fb59c17", "0x89711|XOR|ECX, ECX", "0x89713|MOV|CL, byte ptr [EAX + 0x6fb59c68]", "0x89719|JMP|dword ptr [ECX*0x4 + 0x6fb59c1c]", "0x89720|POP|ESI", "0x89721|JMP|0x6fb19e40", "0x89726|POP|ESI", "0x89727|JMP|0x6fb19490", "0x8972C|POP|ESI", "0x8972D|JMP|0x6fb195d0"],
      "comment": "Process remote player ready/not-ready state notifications in multiplayer game session.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract message subtype from param_1 byte offset 1\n2. Switch on subtype value to handle different notification types:\n   - Type 0x00: Remote player ready - Initialize dialog if not exists (0x6fb59d70), set game mode state to 1\n   - Type 0x01: Remote player in selection phase - Check dialog/query states, create selection dialog (0x6fb59d10), wait for player input\n   - Type 0x02: Cleanup - Reset UI and game objects\n   - Type 0x05: Remote player ready with character - Validate readiness, update UI panel state 1\n   - Type 0x06: Remote player not ready - Reset game mode to 3, close dialogs\n   - Type 0x09/0x0A/0x0C/0x0D: Game state transitions - Initialize objects/modes, reset character storage\n   - Type 0x0E/0x0F: Game mode flags - Set/clear game mode flag\n   - Type 0x10-0x25: Initialization routines - Call corresponding Init functions\n\n3. Validate game mode state (g_dwGameModeState) - prevent duplicate processing\n4. Handle timeout via g_dwGameReadyTimeout: get tick count, set 7-second timeout\n5. Send ACK packet via SendPackedData() for confirmation\n\nParameters:\nnMessageType (int): Message buffer address; byte at +1 contains subtype 0x00-0x25\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Updates global game state, creates/closes dialogs, sends network ACKs\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Type 0x01 phase with existing dialogs results in early SendPackedData ACK (0x4F,2)\n- g_pDialogState1/g_pDialogState2 checked for NULL before creation\n- Subtype extracted via *(undefined1 *)(param_1 + 1) - unsafe cast, assumes param_1 valid\n- FUN_6fb5d340/FUN_6fb5d370 detect key presses (0x17 = Enter/Confirm, 0x05 = Escape)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x00-0x25 = Message subtypes\n0x4F = ACK packet type\n0x140 = Dialog width pixels\n100 = Dialog height pixels\n0x17 = Keyboard code for Confirm key\n0x05 = Keyboard code for Cancel key\n0xf = Number of dialog options/lines\n0xffffffff = Invalid/reset value for dialog index\n0x1a7, 0x1de, etc = Error line numbers in source file",
      "tags": ["PROP_LARGE", "UI_DIALOG", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PROP_NOCALLER", "UI_TRADE", "PARAM_1", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData", "SRC_trade.cpp"]
    },
