      "comment": "Sends a game state update packet to the server indicating game mode state 7.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Set global game mode state variable to 0x7\n2. Extract high word (0x10 bits right) from g_dwUnknownFlag2 as first data value\n3. Extract low word from g_dwUnknownFlag2 as second data value\n4. Call SendPackedData with operation code 0x4F, parameter count 4, and two flag values\n5. Reset global last state change timestamp to 0xFFFFFFFF (marker value)\n6. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\n(none) - Function takes no parameters; operates on global state variables\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Function always succeeds; updates global state and sends packet\n\nSpecial Cases:\nThe operation code 0x4F and parameter value 4 are fixed constants specific to game state\ntransitions. The flag splitting extracts both high and low words from a single 32-bit value,\nsuggesting the packet encodes a two-word flag structure.\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x7 - Game mode state identifier (mode 7 is game active/in-game state)\n0x4F - Packet operation code for game state update\n0x4 - Parameter count (2 words of flag data)\n0x10 - Bit shift for word extraction (16-bit word boundary)\n0xFFFFFFFF - Timestamp marker value (indicates last update time reset)\n\nRelated Functions:\n- SendPackedData() - Sends packed data structure to server\n- TransitionGameState() - Higher-level game state transition handler",
