      "comment": "Convert a wide-character string to uppercase using a lookup table.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate input pointer is not NULL\n2. Get string length via strlen() - exit if empty or NULL\n3. Initialize loop counter with string length, position to first character\n4. Loop through each character:\n   a. Load 16-bit wide character from current position\n   b. Check if character code < 0x100 (ASCII range)\n   c. If yes, use lookup table _toUpperTable_exref to convert to uppercase\n   d. Store converted character back at current position\n   e. Advance pointer by 2 bytes (ushort size)\n   f. Decrement character count, repeat until zero\n5. Return void\n\nParameters:\n  ushort *pwszString - Pointer to wide-character string to convert (null-terminated array of ushort)\n\nReturns:\n  void - Modifies string in-place\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - NULL pointer input: function returns immediately without processing\n  - Empty string: returns immediately after strlen() returns 0\n  - Characters >= 0x100: not processed (remain unchanged)\n  - Only ASCII characters (0x00-0xFF) use lookup table conversion\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x100 - Threshold for using lookup table (256 decimal)\n  0x6fba5c44 - Address of strlen function pointer\n  0x6fba5c5c - Address of _toUpperTable_exref conversion table\n  2 - Byte size of ushort character (wide-character increment)\n\nRelated Functions:\n- RenderPlayerSkillDamageOverlay() - Caller that prepares string",
