      "comment": "Formats display string with localization support by converting and concatenating Unicode strings.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if input string pointer is NULL - if so, return immediately\n2. Initialize large Unicode buffer (1022 wchars) by zeroing all values in loop (0xff iterations)\n3. Initialize small Unicode buffer (8 wchars) for temp operations\n4. Call Ordinal_10004 (Fog.dll ordinal - string locale/encoding initialization)\n5. Copy source Unicode string to destination with Unicode::strcpy\n6. Build localization format string using wsprintfA with param_2 as format argument\n7. Convert ANSI format string to Unicode using Unicode::win2Unicode function\n8. Concatenate formatted string to destination buffer (3x Unicode::strcat calls for Unicode strings)\n9. Return original string pointer in EAX\n\nParameters:\n- pStringBuffer (ECX): short * - Pointer to Unicode string buffer\n- dwOrdinalId (EDX): uint - Ordinal ID for localization configuration (Fog.dll ordinal parameter)\n\nReturns:\n- short * - Same pointer as pStringBuffer input (unchanged)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- NULL input strings cause immediate return at offset 0x6fb5a3b1\n- Stack buffer of 0x410 bytes (1042 wchars) allocated for string operations\n- Implicit FPU register used for temporary string data\n- Phantom variables: szSourceData (unaff_ESI), szDestBuffer (unaff_EDI) - optimized away by compiler\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0xff (255) - loop counter for buffer initialization (REP STOSD)\n- 0x1ff (511) - loop counter for Unicode buffer constructor calls\n- 0x3 - loop count for temp buffer element initialization\n- 0x410 - total stack allocation in bytes\n- 0x20 - offset to initial counter storage [ESP + 0x20]\n- 0x22 - offset to main string buffer [ESP + 0x22]\n- 0x2 - parameter to win2Unicode (conversion mode)\n\nOrdinal Mapping:\n- Ordinal_10004 (Fog.dll) - String locale and encoding initialization before string operations\n\nStructure Layout:\nStack frame during execution:\n| Offset | Size | Field