      "comment": "Replace all occurrences of a pattern in a unicode string.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate source string length is under 500 unicode characters (0x1F4)\n2. If length validation fails, call Ordinal_10023 assertion handler with error code 0x379 (889 decimal - length check violation)\n3. Call Ordinal_10004 to retrieve pattern length in unicode characters (multiply by 2 for bytes)\n4. Call Ordinal_10023 (strstr variant) to search for pattern occurrence in target string\n5. While pattern found and not at end of string (word after match != 0):\n   a. Calculate substring length after pattern: (result_len + pattern_len * 0x7FFFFFFF) \n   b. Call FUN_6fb9af70 (memmove) to copy remaining string backward by pattern_length + 2 bytes\n   c. Call Ordinal_10023 again to search for next pattern occurrence\n6. Return input flags parameter\n\nParameters:\ndwFlags (dword) - Bit flags controlling operation, returned unchanged\nIMPLICIT: ESI = szSource (unicode string source pointer)\nIMPLICIT: EDI = szTarget (unicode string target pointer) \nIMPLICIT: EBX = szPattern (unicode pattern to find)\n\nReturns:\nReturns input dwFlags parameter\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Uses unaffected registers ESI, EDI, EBX for implicit string pointers (__fastcall convention)\n- String length validation at 500 unicode characters (0x1F4 bytes for null-terminated)\n- Checks word boundary after match to determine if at string end\n- Multiple ordinal calls to Unicode string operations (lengths 10004, search 10023)\n- Error code 0x379 (889) indicates assertion failure for string length validation",
