      "comment": "Initializes viewport coordinate configuration for game unit rendering.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Clear the viewport config flag word (set to 0)\n2. Validate unit ID parameter (if nUnitId != 0):\n   a. Call strcpy to copy unit data (unaff_ESI, unaff_retaddr params)\n   b. Store Y coordinate to g_nViewportY global (nYCoord)\n   c. Store Z depth to g_nViewportZ global (nPlayerId)\n   d. Store X coordinate to g_nViewportX global (nXCoord)\n3. Return void\n\nParameters:\n- nUnitId (ECX): Unit entity identifier for validation\n- nXCoord (EDX): Viewport X coordinate to store\n- nYCoord (Stack+4): Viewport Y coordinate to store  \n- nPlayerId (Stack+8): Viewport Z depth/player ID to store\n\nReturns:\nNone (void function)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If nUnitId is 0, skip coordinate initialization (early exit)\n- Uses __fastcall convention with implicit register parameters\n- Config flag is always cleared regardless of unit validity\n\nRelated Functions:\n- FUN_6fb5ba40 (caller) - Main game loop viewport update\n- FUN_6fb5b9b0 (consumer) - Reads stored viewport globals",
