      "comment": "Initialize scrollable game window with resource allocation and event setup.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if scroll window mode is already 3; if so, return failure\n2. Initialize game state with provided game mode parameter\n3. Return failure if game state initialization fails\n4. Clear g_wScrollOffset global variable to zero\n5. Attempt to retrieve resource pointer from first function\n6. If first function returns NULL, attempt alternate function\n7. Return failure if both functions return NULL\n8. Populate g_wScrollOffset buffer (256 bytes) with data from final function using scroll type\n9. Return success (1)\n\nParameters:\n- nGameMode (int): Game mode identifier; passed to game state initialization\n- nScrollType (short): Scroll event type/index; used as parameter to final function\n\nReturns:\n- 0: Initialization failed (scroll mode already active, state init failed, or resource allocation failed)\n- 1: Initialization successful; window ready for use\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If scroll window mode is 3, function returns immediately without state changes\n- Both resource functions must succeed; if either returns NULL before having a value, initialization fails\n- g_wScrollOffset buffer (256 bytes at 0x6fbfd354) reset on each initialization",
