      "comment": "Calculate entity resistance value for spell/attack effects.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate entity pointer is not NULL\n2. Check entity type field [+0x0] equals 1 (required type)\n3. Call FUN_6fb63680 for entity validation; return 0 if validation fails\n4. Search linked list at [entity+0x8] for packed resistance value\n5. If found: calculate nResistanceValue = (foundValue << 7) / 100\n6. If not found: get base resistance via Ordinal_10564, get skill bonus via Ordinal_10519(param, 6)\n   Then calculate: nResistanceValue = (skillBonus << 7) / baseResistance\n7. Clamp result: minimum 2, maximum 0x80 (128 decimal)\n8. Return final resistance value [0x2..0x80]\n\nParameters:\n  pEntity - Pointer to entity structure; must be non-NULL with type field = 1\n\nReturns:\n  0 - Entity NULL or validation failed\n  0x80 (128) - Base resistance lookup failed\n  [0x2..0x80] - Final clamped resistance value\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x1 - Entity type identifier\n  0x8 - Entity resistance data offset\n  0x80 (128) - Maximum resistance cap\n  0x2 - Minimum resistance value\n  0x7 - Left shift for fixed-point calculation\n  0x51eb851f - Reciprocal constant for fast division (magic number for /100)\n  0x5 - SAR shift for magic division result\n  0x1f - Right shift for rounding (signed)\n  0x6 - Skill parameter for Ordinal_10519 call\n\nRelated Functions:\n- FUN_6fb63680 - Entity validation\n- SearchLinkedListForPackedValue - Packed value lookup\n- Ordinal_10564 - Get base resistance (D2Common function)\n- Ordinal_10519 - Get skill level value (D2Common function)",
