      "instructions": ["0x8AB00|SUB|ESP, 0x8a4", "0x8AB06|PUSH|EBX", "0x8AB07|PUSH|EBP", "0x8AB08|PUSH|ESI", "0x8AB09|PUSH|EDI", "0x8AB0A|MOV|EBP, ECX", "0x8AB0C|CALL|0x6fae4fd0", "0x8AB11|CMP|EAX, 0x3", "0x8AB14|JZ|0x6fb5b5d2", "0x8AB1A|XOR|ESI, ESI", "0x8AB1C|CMP|EBP, ESI", "0x8AB1E|JZ|0x6fb5b5d2", "0x8AB24|CMP|dword ptr [EBP], 0x5", "0x8AB28|JNZ|0x6fb5ab3f", "0x8AB2A|CALL|0x6fb62880"],
      "comment": "Render detailed unit information panel with attributes, stats, and item details\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check viewport scroll mode - abort if mode is 3 (disabled)\n2. Validate pUnit parameter is non-NULL\n3. If unit type is 5, verify unit stat value <= 100, abort if exceeded\n4. Initialize coordinate offsets: get viewport X/Y or calculate from unit position\n5. Switch on unit type (param_1[0]):\n   - Type 0: Initialize gold/resource display, render at Y-offset\n   - Type 1: Character detailed view - check class (0x1a1/0x1a2), render attributes/skills\n   - Type 2: Item/inventory display - check item flags, render attributes\n   - Type 4: Check pending request flag, recursively render if set\n   - Type 5: Skill description - render skill name and description\n6. All paths: Initialize game state, check item list availability, render UI panel\n\nParameters:\npUnit (UnitAny *) - Unit entity to display (player, monster, item, or object)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value, updates global UI state\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Type 0: Gold/resource display, fixed Y-offset (-0x48)\n- Type 1: Complex conditional for character/player class rendering (0x1a1/0x1a2)\n- Type 2: Item rendering with multiple flags (0x80=disabled, 0x40=special)\n- Unaffected registers: ESI, EDI used for Unicode string operations (extraout vars)\n- Magic constants: 0x80=unicode array size, 0x1a1/0x1a2=class IDs, 0x275c/0x275d=mode flags\n\nGlobal References:\n- g_dwScreenWidth: Viewport width for coordinate calculations\n- g_dwServerPort: Server connection check (!=0,!=1 = connected)\n- g_wStringSourceIndex, g_wScrollOffset, g_dwInvalidState: State flags\n- g_nXCoordOffset, g_nYCoordOffset: Rendering offsets (set once per viewport update)\n- g_szAttributeFormat, g_szStatusFormat: String format templates",
      "tags": ["PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Path", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "STRUCT_ItemData", "PARAM_1", "PROP_LOOPHEAVY", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
