      "comment": "Processes a unicode string table entry and updates global state flags.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize two Unicode string buffers (0x100 size each) with default constructors (Ordinal_10004)\n2. Iterate through a global string table starting at 0x6fba9a04\n3. For each table entry, call Ordinal_10519(nTableIndex, entry_id) to lookup string value\n4. If result > 99: append strings conditionally based on _Source state, call Ordinal_10004\n5. Continue until pointer reaches table end (0x6fba9a28)\n6. Check stack condition (0x200): if true, clear g_wStringProcessState and return\n7. Otherwise, copy source string and set g_dwStringProcessMode to 4\n\nParameters:\n- nTableIndex (IMPLICIT in ECX): Index to process in string lookup table (0-based)\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Magic value 99: comparison threshold for ordinal result\n- Magic value 0x100: Unicode buffer size (256 wide chars, 512 bytes)\n- Magic value 0x200: stack check sentinel value\n- Global flag 4: completion status code\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n- 0x100: Unicode buffer element count (256 wide characters)\n- 0x204: Total stack allocation (0x100 elements * 2 bytes + 4 bytes extra)\n- 99 (0x63): Threshold for conditional string concatenation\n- 0x6fba9a04: String table base address\n- 0x6fba9a28: String table end (42 bytes total, ~7 entries at 6 bytes each)\n- 4: Process mode completion flag value\n- 0x200: Stack base offset for string data\n\nOrdinals:\n- Ordinal_10004: D2Common resource allocation/initialization function\n- Ordinal_10519: D2Common string table lookup function (takes index and entry ID)",
