      "comment": "Format player display text with PvP status for UI.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Retrieve player target data pointer from info\n2. Check if type field (param_1[3]) equals 0x11 (NPC/Monster):\n   a. Zero output display value\n   b. Allocate and init 256-char Unicode buffer\n   c. Convert player name (ASCII) to Unicode using win2Unicode\n   d. Retrieve language enum via Ordinal_10007\n   e. Retrieve text resource pointer via Ordinal_10004\n   f. Call Personalize with text resource and language enum\n   g. Mark output flag as enabled (1)\n   h. Return\n3. For normal player entities:\n   a. Get player node padding value by player ID (param_1[2])\n   b. Calculate display value: (padding << 7) / 100\n   c. Initialize PvP flag to disabled (0)\n   d. Get active player instance pointer via FUN_6fb62880\n   e. Check if this player can interact with target via CanPlayersInteractPvP\n   f. If allowed, set PvP flag to enabled (1)\n   g. Convert player name to Unicode\n   h. Return with calculated values\n\nParameters:\npnPlayerInfo: Player info pointer (array index 0=type, 1=subtype, 2=player_id, 3=unit_class)\npdwDisplayValue: Output display value (skill damage or calculated padding)\npbIsPvPEnabled: Output PvP interaction flag (0=disabled, 1=enabled)\nwszDisplayText: Output Unicode text buffer (256 chars, 512 bytes)\ndwLanguageId: Language enum for text personalization\n\nReturns:\nvoid; Modifies output parameters with calculated display value, PvP flag, formatted text\n\nSpecial Cases:\nType 0x11 uses personalized text from resource table instead of normal player calculation",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PARAM_5", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
