      "comment": "Initialize/validate viewport window configuration and clear config buffer.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get input string length (Unicode::strlen)\n2. If string is non-empty:\n   a. Ordinal_10121 - Prepare viewport setup\n   b. Ordinal_10125 - Get viewport Y offset value\n   c. Calculate ideal Y position: max(Ordinal_10125+7, ViewportY+2)\n   d. Clamp Y coordinate: min(calculated_Y, ScreenHeight-0x1f)\n   e. Ordinal_10117 - Apply viewport Y bounds with params (y-2, 0, 1)\n   f. Clear 40 (0x28) dwords starting at g_wViewportConfigFlag\n3. Return (void)\n\nParameters:\n(Implicit) - Uses global viewport state variables:\n- g_nViewportY: Current viewport Y coordinate\n- g_dwScreenHeight: Screen height in pixels\n\nReturns:\n(void) - Modifies global viewport config and clears config buffer\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If input string is empty/NULL, entire initialization is skipped\n- Screen height magic number 0x1f (31 pixels) reserved for UI elements\n- Loop clears exactly 0x28 (40) dwords = 160 bytes total\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x28: Config buffer size in dwords (40 dwords = 160 bytes)\n- 0x1f: Screen height offset/reserved UI height\n- 0x7: Viewport Y offset adjustment\n- 0x2: Viewport Y coordinate adjustment for rendering\n\nOrdinal References:\n- Ordinal_10121: Prepare viewport configuration\n- Ordinal_10125: Get/calculate viewport Y offset\n- Ordinal_10117: Apply viewport Y bounds and settings",
