      "instructions": ["0x8BA40|SUB|ESP, 0x13c", "0x8BA46|MOV|EAX, [0x6fbfd7a4]", "0x8BA4B|PUSH|EBP", "0x8BA4C|XOR|EBP, EBP", "0x8BA4E|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0xc], ECX", "0x8BA52|CMP|EAX, EBP", "0x8BA54|JNZ|0x6fb5c1a6", "0x8BA5A|CALL|0x6fb9921a", "0x8BA5F|CMP|EAX, 0x2", "0x8BA62|JNZ|0x6fb5ba7a", "0x8BA64|MOV|dword ptr [0x6fbfd7fc], 0x50", "0x8BA6E|MOV|dword ptr [0x6fbfd800], 0xffffffc4", "0x8BA78|JMP|0x6fb5ba86", "0x8BA7A|MOV|dword ptr [0x6fbfd7fc], EBP", "0x8BA80|MOV|dword ptr [0x6fbfd800], EBP"],
      "comment": "Process game state, render UI frames, handle viewport rendering, and coordinate update\n \nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if rendering disabled flag set (DAT_6fbfd7a4) - if yes, return early\n2. Determine game resolution mode via Ordinal_10005() (SD=2 or non-SD)\n3. Set UI coordinate offsets: SD mode (+0x50,-0x3c) vs normal (0,0)\n4. Initialize UI state with Ordinal_10129(0,0,0)\n5. Check viewport data validity and render setup:\n   - If DAT_6fbfd780 set, call RenderPanelUI()\n   - If DAT_6fbfd788 set, call RenderAutomap()\n6. Validate selected unit and display unit information\n7. If viewport enabled (DAT_6fbfd7e8) and scroll mode != 3:\n   a. Find valid slot via linked list search (type==1)\n   b. Get unit ID and coordinate data\n   c. Handle two rendering modes:\n      - Isometric: Use GetRelativeViewportX/Y to calculate offsets\n      - 2D mode: Call Ordinal_10327/10330 for coordinates, apply viewport pan\n   d. Initialize game state and viewport rendering coordinates\n8. Render conditional UI panels based on state flags:\n   - Skill slots, automap, shop inventory, recipes, dialogs, quest UI, etc.\n9. Handle game state transitions:\n   - If state changed (Ordinal_10057), reinitialize palette\n   - Countdown fade animation for state transitions (DAT_6fbfd83c)\n10. Load and render new act transition strings if needed\n11. Update all active UI elements with UpdateGameUIRenderFrame()\n12. Render main game frame with updated coordinates\n13. Handle viewport updates if pending requests exist\n14. Final: return\n \nParameters: (none)\n \nReturns: void\n \nSpecial Cases:\n- Early return if rendering disabled (DAT_6fbfd7a4 != 0)\n- Mode detection distinguishes SD vs widescreen (Ordinal_10005() == 2)\n- Viewport invalid if slot not found or data verification fails\n- Act string copy uses manual memcpy for expansion acts >= 0x6d\n- State transition countdown: 0 to 0x78 (120 frames)\n- Fade animation timing: (0 if state changed) or (0x78 minus countdown)\n \nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x50/-0x3c = SD mode X,Y offsets\n- 0x6d = Expansion act threshold\n- 0x48 = Viewport Y adjustment constant\n- 0x27 = String coordinate offset\n- 0x78 = State transition fade countdown max (120 frames)\n- 0x88 = Fade fade time computation constant\n- 0x10 = Viewport Y extra offset\n- 3, 1, 2 = Scroll mode constants (2D/isometric/disabled)\n \nStructure Layout:\nOffset | Size | Field Name | Type | Description\n-----  | ---- | ---------- | ---- | -----------\nN/A    | N/A  | Viewport stack buffers (256 chars path, 32 wchars act string, 12 char printf buffer)\n \nNote: Function uses 4 stack-allocated temporaries optimized away. Large coordination complex game rendering loop.",
      "tags": ["PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Path", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PARAM_0", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
