      "comment": "Render game over screen display including death message and video playback.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get current game state pointer via FUN_6fb62880\n2. If null, return early (invalid game state)\n3. Validate game state via FUN_6fb63680\n4. If validation fails, set g_dwGameOverDisplayInitialized=0 and return\n5. Calculate Y position: (screen height / 2) - 0x5e\n6. Initialize memory buffer via Ordinal_10006\n7. Build \"YouDiedHardcore\" UI file path via FUN_6fb9a261\n8. Write file via ConcatenatePathAndWriteFile\n9. Display sprite at Y via Ordinal_10134\n10. Set g_dwGameOverDisplayInitialized=1\n11. Report any validation errors via ReportValidationError\n12. Calculate second Y position: (screen height / 2) - 0x2e\n13. Build \"YouDiedInst\" UI file path\n14. Write second file and display at second Y\n15. Initialize 256-element Unicode string buffer with loop\n16. Check IsVideoFlag4Set for video mode\n17. If video disabled: get stat 0xaf via Ordinal_10519, convert via Ordinal_10004, sprintf to buffer\n18. If video enabled: strcpy from alternate source strings\n19. Call Ordinal_10127 to flush rendering buffer\n20. Call Ordinal_10121 to display sprite frame\n21. Call Ordinal_10117 to finalize sprite display\n22. Check if video playback enabled via GetVideoFrameCount\n23. If frames > 0, check video flag again\n24. If video disabled, render final video with message via Ordinal_10127, Ordinal_10004, Ordinal_10121\n\nParameters:\nNone (void)\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Ordinal_10006: Initialize memory region\n- Ordinal_10519: Query game stat by ID (0xaf)\n- Ordinal_10004: Convert value to Unicode string\n- Ordinal_10127: Flush rendering buffer\n- Ordinal_10121: Display sprite/frame data\n- Ordinal_10134: Render UI sprite element\n- Ordinal_10117: Finalize sprite display\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x5e (94): First Y offset in pixels\n- 0x2e (46): Second Y offset in pixels\n- 0x30 (48): Third Y offset in pixels\n- 0xaf (175): Game stat ID for video data\n- 0x100 (256): Unicode buffer size in elements\n- 0x13e6, 0x13e7, 0x13e8: Internal message string IDs",
