      "comment": "Dispatch UI event to appropriate handler based on event code via message processing\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Switch on nEventCode (0x0-0x25 map to different UI event types)\n2. For each case, retrieve window handle from Ordinal_10027 (GetHWND equivalent)\n3. Set nMessageCount for the specific event type (varies 1-9 messages)\n4. Call ProcessMessageEntryArray or ProcessMessageArray with event-specific message table\n5. Execute optional setup functions before message processing (e.g., InitializeUIState for case 1)\n6. Handle special logic: case 0x5 checks DAT_6fbfd784 flag before processing; case 0xb validates remote session support\n\nParameters:\n- nEventCode (ECX, dword): Event code identifying which UI event to dispatch (0x0-0x25)\n\nReturns:\n- void: Function completes event dispatch\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Case 0x5: Only processes messages if DAT_6fbfd784 != 0; calls NoOperation() after\n- Case 0xb: Validates remote session support/readiness; skips remaining logic if validation fails\n- Cases with initialization: 0x1, 0x5, 0x17, 0x19, 0x1a, 0x1b, 0x1c, 0x1d, 0x1e, 0x1f call setup functions\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x0-0x25: Event code range (38 distinct event types)\n- Message counts vary: 1-9 messages per event type\n- Ordinal_10027: Returns window handle for message processing\n\nRelated Functions:\n- ProcessMessageEntryArray() - Processes message table with count\n- ProcessMessageArray() - Alternative message processing\n- Ordinal_10027() - Retrieves window handle (Storm.dll function)\n- InitializeUIState, InitializeImeForLanguage, SetPanelMessageStateBySessionMode, etc. - Event setup functions",
