      "comment": "Update key binding indices for player movement and action commands.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. For each command slot (param_1[N]): retrieve stored slot index\n2. If slot index != -1:\n   a. Check if key binding active for command (0x16/0x26/0x29/0x2c) and mode (0=down, 1=up)\n   b. If active, lookup key code (ushort) for that command\n   c. If key code valid (!=0xffff, <0xE0), write to structure at [param_1[8] + offset + index*0xC + 4]\n   d. If invalid or not active, write default key code (0xC0/0x1B/0x4E/0x57)\n3. Special handling: For command 0x2C slot, first check Ordinal_10227() returns non-zero\n4. Final check: If Ordinal_10227() nonzero and param_1[7] valid, call FUN_6fb5ccf0\n\nParameters:\n  pKeyIndices (int * __fastcall, ECX): Array of key binding slot indices\n    - [0]: Command 0x26 down key slot\n    - [1]: Command 0x16 down key slot  \n    - [2]: Command 0x26 up key slot\n    - [3]: Command 0x16 up key slot\n    - [4]: Command 0x29 down key slot\n    - [5]: Command 0x29 up key slot\n    - [6]: Command 0x2C down key slot (conditional on Ordinal_10227)\n    - [7]: Command 0x2C up key slot (conditional on Ordinal_10227)\n    - [8]: Pointer to key binding data array\n\nReturns:\n  None (void)\n\nNote: Function contains 7 phantom/compiler-optimized variables (extraout_var) that cannot be resolved to meaningful types. These are intermediate values consumed by CONCAT31 operations.\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0xC0: Default down key for command 0x16 (Left)\n  0x1B: Default down key for command 0x26 (Right)\n  0x4E: Default down key for command 0x29 (Down)\n  0x57: Default down key for command 0x2C (Special)\n  0xFFFF: Invalid key code marker\n  0xE0: Maximum valid key code threshold\n  0x0C: Structure element stride (12 bytes per slot)",
