      "comment": "Assigns a key binding to a command slot with fallback to default key code.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate slot index is not -1 (invalid/uninitialized)\n2. Check if key binding is active for the command via IsKeyBindingActive()\n3. If active, look up key code via LookupKeyBindingByCommandId()\n4. If key code found (not 0xffff) AND less than 0xe0 (valid range), use it\n5. Otherwise fall back to dwDefaultKey parameter\n6. Write final key code (masked to 16-bit) into binding config structure array\n\nParameters:\n  nSlotIndex: Slot index in binding configuration array (-1 = uninitialized, skip)\n  nCommandId: Command ID to bind (e.g., 0x16 for move, 0x26 for turn, 0x29 for melee)\n  nParameter: Additional command parameter or modifier\n  pnConfigArray: Pointer to binding configuration structure (accessed via [pnConfigArray + 0x20])\n  dwDefaultKey: Default key code to use if binding not found (e.g., 0xc0, 0x1b, 0x4e)\n\nReturns:\n  Key code written to binding array entry (uint, masked to 16-bit)\n  Returns implicitly void, but updates pnConfigArray structure in-place\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  If nSlotIndex == -1: Function returns immediately without modifying structure (slot uninitialized)\n  Key code 0xffff indicates binding not found (unbound command)\n  Key codes >= 0xe0 are out of valid range (keyboard scan codes are 0x00-0xdf)\n  Note: Function contains compiler-generated phantom variables (extraout_var, uVar1) from CONCAT31 decompiler artifact\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x20: Offset into pnConfigArray to access binding table base pointer\n  0xc: Stride/size of each binding entry (12 bytes per slot)\n  0x4: Offset within binding entry to store key code\n  0xe0: Upper bound for valid keyboard scan codes\n  0xffff: Sentinel value indicating unbound/not-found binding",
