      "comment": "Dispatcher for game state events (38 states: 0x00-0x25).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Compare nGameStateCode with 0x25 (max state code)\n2. If out of range, return immediately\n3. Index into jump table at 0x6fb5d2a0 using state code\n4. For each state, load message array address from global data\n5. Query game window via Ordinal_10027 (GetGameWindow)\n6. Dispatch message entries via ProcessMessageArray/ProcessMessageEntryArray\n7. Execute state-specific handlers (validation, initialization, reset functions)\n8. Check g_fEnableTimeoutUpdate flag; if set, update g_dwTimeoutValue = GetTickCount() + 100\n9. Return from handler or fall through to common timeout update\n\nParameters:\nnGameStateCode (dword) - Game state identifier (0x00-0x25), passed in ECX (fastcall)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value; side effects via message dispatch and global state updates\n\nSpecial Cases:\nState 0x05 checks 9 state flags (0x78c-0x7dc) must all be zero before proceeding\nState 0x12 is no-op transition (empty case)\nStates 0x01, 0x02, 0x0F, 0x14, 0x16, 0x25 fall through to timeout update\nMultiple states share timeout update pattern: GetTickCount() + 100ms\n\nNote: Function uses 7 stack-allocated temporaries optimized away by compiler (uVar5, pHVar4, iVar2, DVar3, bVar1, extraout_var, extraout_var_00)",
