      "comment": "Process UI state changes and handle element visibility/activation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate input parameters: nUIId (0-0x25), nUIState (0-2)\n2. Check if game is running via Ordinal_10227 (D2Common.ValidateLevelStructureMatch) and GetGlobalSystemState()\n3. Verify UI element state table is initialized (g_dwNumUIElements == 0x26)\n4. If nUIState == 0 or (nUIState == 2 and element inactive):\n   a. Handle special cases: nUIId 5 (inventory), 9 (minimap)\n   b. Check dialog init count and timeout via GetDialogInitCount/GetTickCount\n   c. For minimap: validate resource availability, update game state flags\n   d. Process active UI elements via state table (g_ppUIStateTable)\n   e. For each active element, dispatch state changes (recursive calls)\n5. Update element active/inactive state based on nUIState parameter\n6. Dispatch UI event handler if state changed to active\n7. Update scroll window mode based on element type and state flags:\n   - Mode 0: Left panel, Mode 1: Right panel, Mode 2: Minimap, Mode 3: Expanded\n8. Return success (1) or failure (0)\n\nParameters:\nIMPLICIT (ECX): nUIId - UI element type (0x0-0x25) such as inventory, minimap, quest log\nIMPLICIT (EDX): nUIState - new state: 0=activate, 1=deactivate, 2=toggle\nStack[0x4]: nScrollParam - scroll window position parameter (used for viewport positioning)\n\nReturns:\n1 on success with state change applied\n0 on failure or special case (not running, timeouts, validation failed)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- nUIId 0x23-0x25 (special UI): returns 0 if game not running\n- nUIId 5 (inventory): blocked if dialog count > 0 and cache flag set\n- nUIId 9 (minimap): resets video flags and game state on activation\n- State table validation: aborts if g_dwNumUIElements != 0x26\n- Recursive call for case 1: recursively processes dependent UI elements\n- Ordinal_10023 (D2Common.UpdatePositionWithBounds): assertion function for debug validation\n- Ordinal_10227 (D2Common.ValidateLevelStructureMatch): checks if game session is active\n- Ordinal_10029 (D2Common.AddOrRemoveTimedSkillEffect_Wrapper): used for resource validation\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x25 - Maximum UI element ID\n0x26 - Expected element count in state table\n0x23, 0x24, 0x25 - Special UI element IDs that short-circuit on inactive game\n0x11 - Resource availability flag check",
