      "comment": "Iterate through all UI resource states and trigger state change events for active UI elements.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize result flag (fStateChanged) to 0 (no state changed)\n2. Initialize UI ID counter (nUIId) to 0\n3. Loop through all 0x26 (38) UI resource IDs:\n   a. Check if UI resource buffer indicates state is active (== 1)\n   b. Check if UI state flag is set OR (param_1 is non-zero AND nUIId == 0x0A)\n   c. If condition met, call ProcessUIStateChange(nUIId, 1, dwUIId) to process state change\n   d. Set result flag to 1 (state changed)\n   e. If nUIId is 0x19 or 0x01, call InitializeGameUIState() to reinitialize UI\n   f. Increment nUIId and continue loop\n4. Return result flag (0 = no states changed, 1 = at least one state changed)\n\nParameters:\n- fForceProcess: bool - If true, force processing for UI element at index 0x0A\n- dwUIId: dword - UI state identifier to propagate to ProcessUIStateChange\n\nReturns:\n- dword: 1 if any UI state was changed, 0 if no states were processed\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- UI IDs 0x19 (25) and 0x01 (1) trigger full game UI state reinitialization\n- Force flag allows bypassing normal state checks for specific UI element\n- Multiple UI states can be processed in single invocation (return value only indicates if ANY changed)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x26 (38): Total count of UI resource states to iterate\n- 0x19 (25): UI ID triggering full reinitialization\n- 0x01 (1): Secondary UI ID also triggering reinitialization\n- 0x0A (10): Special UI element index for forced processing",
      "tags": ["PARAM_2"]
    },
