      "comment": "Updates the global timeout value by adding 100ms to current tick count if timeout updates are enabled.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load g_fEnableTimeoutUpdate flag\n2. If flag is non-zero (updates enabled):\n   a. Call GetTickCount() to get current system tick count in milliseconds\n   b. Add 100 to the tick count (100ms timeout offset)\n   c. Store result in g_dwTimeoutValue global\n3. Return\n\nParameters:\nNone - operates on global state (g_fEnableTimeoutUpdate, g_dwTimeoutValue)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - no return value, updates g_dwTimeoutValue as side effect\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If g_fEnableTimeoutUpdate is 0 (false), function does nothing\n- Timeout value is set to current time + 100ms for upcoming expiration check\n- GetTickCount() returns milliseconds since system boot, resets every ~49 days",
