      "comment": "Send mouse move message to window\nConstructs a 32-bit mouse coordinate from two 16-bit values and posts WM_MOUSEMOVE to the target window.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get Y coordinate from FUN_6fb8f690() result, mask to 16 bits, shift left by 16\n2. Get X coordinate from FUN_6fb8f680() result, mask to 16 bits\n3. Combine into single 32-bit LPARAM (Y in high word, X in low word)\n4. Push combined coordinate, message ID (0x200 = WM_MOUSEMOVE), wParam (0)\n5. Get window handle from Ordinal_10027 (GetActiveWindow or similar)\n6. Call SendMessageA with constructed parameters\n\nParameters: (none)\nReturns: void\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0xffff: 16-bit mask for coordinate extraction\n- 0x10: Left shift amount to place Y coordinate in high word\n- 0x200: WM_MOUSEMOVE Windows message identifier",
