      "comment": "Initialize game state with full validation of UI, skills, and data arrays.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Clear character select UI frames and prepare for initialization\n2. Execute placeholder operation (NoOperation)\n3. Clear any existing slot error state\n4. Validate all skill slots and report errors if found\n5. Initialize game data arrays with default values\n6. Initialize primary game state (called twice to ensure stable state)\n7. Validate slot lists and reset validation counters\n8. Reset palette rendering state for display refresh\n9. Check global error flag (g_dwGameStateError) set by prior validation steps\n10. If validation error occurred, report it and clear the flag\n11. Save user preference for \"always run\" setting\n12. Call FUN_6fb8f0c0(0) to finalize initialization\n13. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\n(none) - Uses global state (g_dwGameStateError)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Does not return error codes; errors logged via ReportValidationError\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- g_dwGameStateError may be set by ValidateAllSkillSlots or other validation functions\n- InitializeGameState is called twice to ensure consistent initialization\n- All validation steps execute regardless of prior errors; errors accumulated in g_dwGameStateError",
