      "comment": "Retrieve difficulty level or return magic string index based on game mode.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call Ordinal_10631(nMode) to get difficulty/mode info\n2. If result is 0, call Ordinal_10004() to get default difficulty/mode\n3. If nMode == 8:\n   - Call Ordinal_10002(0, 1) with parameters\n   - If result is non-zero (bResult), return Ordinal_10004() result\n   - Otherwise fall through to return Ordinal_10004() result\n4. Otherwise, add 0x212 (530 decimal) to result and return\n\nParameters:\n  nMode (int) - Game mode or difficulty identifier; value 8 has special handling\n\nReturns:\n  int - Difficulty level or magic string index constant (0x13b7, 0x13b8, or 0x150d + 0x212)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  Mode 8 triggers additional validation via Ordinal_10002\n  Constant 0x212 (530) added when nMode != 8\n  All paths return via Ordinal_10004() or offset from it\n  Ordinal_10631 appears to query main difficulty/mode state\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x8 - Special game mode requiring additional validation\n  0x212 - String index offset (530 decimal), likely UI/menu string table index\n  0x13b7, 0x13b8, 0x150d - String table indices for different result paths",
