      "comment": "Process UI dialog state transitions and cleanup panel callbacks\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check g_dwUIInventoryRow5 flag; if set, notify panel 1 via SetPanelMessageStateBySessionMode(1,1) and clear flag\n2. If g_dwUIInventoryRow2 is non-null, call virtual function at offset 0x2c and store result in g_dwUIDialogReturnValue\n3. If g_dwUIInventoryRow0 is set, call CloseDialogAndCleanup() and clear flag\n4. For each dialog callback (g_dwUIInventoryRow1 through Row4):\n   - If pointer is non-null, call function at [*pointer] with argument 1\n   - Clear the pointer to NULL\n5. Load g_dwUIDialogState value and dispatch via switch table (0-7 indexed)\n6. Based on state:\n   - State 0: Call ClearUnknownStateFlag()\n   - State 1-4,6-7: Call CheckAndNormalizeObjectType()\n   - State 5: Call NoOperation() then CheckAndNormalizeObjectType()\n   - Default (>7): Log error via Ordinal_10029 and return\n\nParameters:\n(none)\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Dialog callbacks expect single parameter (0x1) pushed as argument\n- State machine is 0-indexed with bounds checking (JA to default case)\n- Virtual function dispatch at offset 0x2c assumes vtable at [g_dwUIInventoryRow2]\n- Multiple NULL checks prevent invalid function calls\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x2c - Virtual function table offset for dialog state provider function\n0x1 - Standard parameter value for dialog cleanup callbacks\n0x1639 - Line number in error logging (file: D2Cli source)\n0x6fbc9aec - String constant \"not_implemented_dummy_%s_%d\"\n0x6fbc9974 - String constant \"C:\\\\Projects\\\\Diablo2\\\\Source\\\\D2Cli\"",
