      "api_calls": ["INVENTORY_GetOwner", "GetTotalStatValue", "GetTotalStatValue", "GetTotalStatValue", "GetTotalStatValue", "GetTotalStatValue", "GetTotalStatValue", "GetTotalStatValue", "GetTotalStatValue", "GetGuildFlags", "...+13 more"],
      "instructions": ["0x8DC50|PUSH|-0x1", "0x8DC52|PUSH|0x6fba45b8", "0x8DC57|MOV|EAX, FS:[0x0]", "0x8DC5D|PUSH|EAX", "0x8DC5E|MOV|dword ptr FS:[0x0], ESP", "0x8DC65|SUB|ESP, 0x208", "0x8DC6B|PUSH|EBX", "0x8DC6C|PUSH|EBP", "0x8DC6D|PUSH|ESI", "0x8DC6E|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0x8DC70|PUSH|EDI", "0x8DC71|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x10], ESI", "0x8DC75|CALL|0x6fb62880", "0x8DC7A|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0x8DC7C|JZ|0x6fb5e0fd"],
      "comment": "Initialize game state panel (inventory/skills/character) with type-specific display controls.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate current game state exists via FUN_6fb62880() check\n2. Verify panel not already initialized via g_dwUIInventoryRow0 check\n3. Set SetPanelMessageStateBySessionMode if needed\n4. Calculate width based on panel type: 0x0e (14) or 0x0f (15) pixels\n5. For type 0x5, sum two dimensions (0x0f + 0x0e)\n6. For type 0x7, retrieve container size via Ordinal_11177, clamp to display width\n7. Create main dialog (0xd7x0x8c) via InitializeGameStateDialog\n8. Create Unicode buffer (256 element array)\n9. Format title string for type 0x5, otherwise copy from template\n10. Iterate through linked list (Ordinal_10199 loop)\n11. Add dialog lines via AddDialogLine\n12. Create spinner control at (0xdf, 0xdb)\n13. Create slider control for scrolling\n14. Create two icon display controls\n15. Return on type 0x2 after sending packet\n16. For types 3/6/7, set slider to calculated width\n\nParameters:\nnPanelType (int): Panel type (0-7)\n  0x0 = Inventory main\n  0x1 = Inventory tab\n  0x2 = Inventory transient (sends packet, no slider)\n  0x3 = Skill display\n  0x4 = Character sheet\n  0x5 = Combined inventory (two dimensions)\n  0x6 = Equipment\n  0x7 = Container\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Creates global UI elements\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Type 0x2 returns early after sending game state packet\n- Type 0x5 requires dimension sum instead of single value\n- Type 0x7 clamps container size to display bounds\n- All panel types require FUN_6fb62880() validation first\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x0e (14) - Width for standard panels\n0x0f (15) - Width for equipment/combined panels\n0xd7/0x8c - Dialog dimensions (215 x 140)\n0xdf/0xdb - Spinner Y/X position\n0x102/0xe4 - Slider dimensions\n0xfa/0x11f - Icon display dimensions\n0x163/0x11f - Second icon dimensions\n0x100 - Unicode buffer element count (256 elements)\n0x80 - Clearance loop count (128 dwords)\n0xc8 (200) - Linked list iteration start (Ordinal_10199)\n0x6fb5e140/0x6fb5e150/0x6fb5e250/0x6fb5e330 - Control config addresses\nOrdinal_10519 - Get panel width\nOrdinal_10262 - Check panel state\nOrdinal_11177 - Get container size (64-bit)\nOrdinal_10439 - Get display width\nOrdinal_10004 - Format string\nOrdinal_10199 - Iterate linked list\nOrdinal_10127 - Clear cache\nOrdinal_10043 - Manage state\nOrdinal_401 - Allocate memory\nOrdinal_10262 - D2Common ordinal for state check",
      "tags": ["PROP_LARGE", "MOD_UI", "STRUCT_Inventory", "STRUCT_Skill", "SRC_ui.cpp", "STRUCT_ItemData", "PARAM_1", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
