      "comment": "Dispatches dialog message processing based on game state condition and message state ID.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if nStateId is 0 (default message processing path)\n2. Load global state condition flag (g_fStateCondition)\n3. If state condition is active (non-zero):\n   - Set message count to 5\n   - Retrieve window handle via Ordinal_10027 (Fog.dll ordinal - window management)\n   - Dispatch to ProcessMessageArray (HWND-based processing) if nStateId == 0\n   - Dispatch to ProcessMessageEntryArray (entry-based processing) if nStateId != 0\n4. Return\n\nParameters:\nnStateId (int, in ECX) - Message processing mode identifier (0 = HWND-based, non-zero = entry-based)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Function only processes messages if g_fStateCondition is non-zero\n- Both paths use identical message count value (5)\n- Both paths reference same message array (g_pMessageArrayState5State10)\n- Ordinal_10027 is called twice (once per path) to retrieve window handle\n\nRelated Functions:\n- ProcessMessageArray() - HWND-based message dispatcher\n- ProcessMessageEntryArray() - Entry-based message dispatcher\n- Ordinal_10027 - Window handle retrieval (Fog.dll)",
