      "comment": "Initializes and displays the loading screen UI with progress bar during game startup or area transitions.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if game is already initialized (Ordinal_10026)\n2. If not initialized, call stop/cleanup (Ordinal_10058)\n3. Get current server port to determine target game type\n4. Call main initialization (Ordinal_10044)\n5. If first initialization, load palette files and display image\n6. Set up progress bar rendering with dimensions calculated from screen center\n7. Process port-specific initialization (ports 6, 7, 8, 9 require color palette setup)\n8. Render progress bar with current progress value\n9. Initialize targeting system and clear any previous targeting state\n10. Increment progress counter if fInitialize flag is set\n\nParameters:\nfInitialize - bool flag; if true, increments progress counter (caller signals frame update)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - no return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- First initialization: Loads palette files (loading.pal and loading_pal.pl2) and main screen image\n- Palette setup: Only executed for ports 6, 7, 8, 9\n- Error handling: Fatal error if palette file loading fails (calls Ordinal_10023 with line 6442)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x60: Color palette dark value (Ordinal_10034)\n- 0xff: Color palette bright value (Ordinal_10034)\n- 0x82, 0x80: Screen X offset from center (progress bar positioning)\n- 0x9e, 0xa0, 0xb2, 0xb0: Screen Y offset from center (progress bar positioning)\n- 0x10: Progress bar height in pixels\n- 0x192a: Line number in source (6442 decimal) for error reporting\n- 0x6fbfd82c, 0x6fbfd80c, 0x6fbfda0c: Global progress state tracking\n- 0x6fbfd068, 0x6fbe9274: Progress bar visibility flag\n\nNote: Function uses 3 stack-allocated temporary buffers (dwDisplayFlags, abPalette1, abPalette2, szLoadScreenPath) optimized away in decompilation. Assembly shows: local_104[260] at [EBP-0x104], local_208[260] at [EBP-0x208], local_30c[260] at [EBP-0x30c], local_354[4] at [EBP-0x354].",
