      "instructions": ["0x8E930|CALL|dword ptr [0x6fba6098]", "0x8E936|MOV|EDX, dword ptr [0x6fbfda14]", "0x8E93C|MOV|ECX, EAX", "0x8E93E|SUB|ECX, EDX", "0x8E940|CMP|ECX, 0x32", "0x8E943|JBE|0x6fb5e950", "0x8E945|MOV|[0x6fbfda14], EAX", "0x8E94A|MOV|EAX, 0x1", "0x8E94F|RET|", "0x8E950|XOR|EAX, EAX", "0x8E952|RET|"],
      "comment": "Checks if 50 milliseconds have elapsed since the last timeout check.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Retrieve current tick count via GetTickCount()\n2. Calculate elapsed time as (current_tick - g_dwLastTimeoutCheck)\n3. If elapsed time >= 0x32 (50ms):\n   - Update g_dwLastTimeoutCheck to current tick count\n   - Return 1 (true - timeout elapsed)\n4. Otherwise return 0 (false - timeout not yet elapsed)\n\nParameters:\n(none)\n\nReturns:\n1 (true) - 50ms or more have elapsed since last check\n0 (false) - Less than 50ms have elapsed\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Initial call when g_dwLastTimeoutCheck is 0 will likely return 1\n- Used for frame-rate throttling in rendering loops\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x32 = 50 decimal (millisecond threshold)\n\nRelated Functions:\n- RenderPanelUI() - Calls this function for render throttling\n- GetTickCount() - System API for millisecond timestamp",
      "tags": ["PARAM_0", "PROP_SMALL"]
