      "instructions": ["0x8EA60|PUSH|0xd", "0x8EA62|CALL|0x6fb9922c", "0x8EA67|MOV|ECX, EAX", "0x8EA69|MOV|EDX, 0x6fba95b8", "0x8EA6E|CALL|0x6fad25b0", "0x8EA73|CALL|0x6fadaa70", "0x8EA78|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0x8EA7A|JNZ|0x6fb5ea85", "0x8EA7C|CALL|0x6fadaa30", "0x8EA81|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0x8EA83|JZ|0x6fb5ea98", "0x8EA85|PUSH|0x1", "0x8EA87|CALL|0x6fb9922c", "0x8EA8C|MOV|ECX, EAX", "0x8EA8E|MOV|EDX, 0x6fba9658"],
      "comment": "Process remote session message state by dispatching appropriate message array state handlers.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Set dwMessageCount to 0x0D (13 message types for normal state)\n2. Call Ordinal_10027 to get storage/session index\n3. Dispatch message array entries to g_pMessageArrayState11 with the index and message count\n4. Check IsRemoteSessionSupported() for capability flag\n5. Check IsRemoteSessionHandlingReady() for initialization state\n6. If both checks fail (neither supported nor ready), return early\n7. If either supported or ready: Set dwMessageCount to 0x01 (alternate state)\n8. Call Ordinal_10027 again to get updated storage index\n9. Dispatch message array entries to g_pMessageArrayState11Alt with alternate state\n10. Return\n\nParameters:\n(none)\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Early return when remote session not supported AND not ready\n- Two distinct message array sets based on remote session capability state\n- Ordinal_10027 called twice - once for each message state dispatch\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x0D (13) - Standard message entry count for normal state\n0x01 (1) - Alternate message entry count for remote session state",
      "tags": ["PARAM_0"]
    },
