      "comment": "Process game data state transitions between initialized (mode 1) and active (mode 2) states.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if game data path is initialized (g_dwGameDataMode != 0). If not, skip to cleanup.\n2. Reset game data mode flag to 0\n3. Retrieve current game data pointer via FUN_6fb62880()\n4. If pointer valid (non-zero), extract data at offset 0x84 and call Ordinal_10262 (D2Common.GetUnitStat)\n5. Transition from initialized (mode 1) to active (mode 2):\n   - Set mode flag to 2\n   - Call FUN_6fb8f0c0(0) to prepare state\n   - If data pointer non-zero: save buffer pointer at offset 0x8, call FUN_6fb6bc10 to process\n   - Call FUN_6fb8d210 with offsets (0.0, 0.0, 0) to initialize view\n6. Transition from active (mode 2) to initialized (mode 1):\n   - Set mode flag to 1\n   - Clear buffer pointer to 0\n   - If data pointer non-zero: call FUN_6fb8f0c0 with pointer to cleanup state\n   - Call FUN_6fb8d210 with offset (1) to reset view\n7. Process message queue: call Ordinal_10027 (D2Common.RandSeed) to get window, process 8 messages\n8. If dialog open (g_hDialogHandle != 0): close dialog, reset flag\n9. Update UI state: call ProcessUIStateChange(0xe, 1, 0) for mode 0xe\n10. Copy configuration data\n11. Cleanup: report and clear any pending data path errors from g_dwDataPathHandle1 and g_dwDataPathHandle2\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Modes 1 and 2 are exclusive states: mode 1 (initialized) transitions to mode 2 (active) and vice versa\n- Data pointer validity checked before state-specific operations\n- Ordinal calls: Ordinal_10262 = D2Common.GetUnitStat, Ordinal_10027 = D2Common.RandSeed\n- Message count hardcoded to 8 (0x8)\n- UI state identifier 0xe used for state update notification\n- Note: Function uses SSA-optimized variables (iVar1, fVar2, fVar3, iVar4) that may not be fully renameable due to compiler optimization\n\nRelated Functions:\n- FUN_6fb62880() - Retrieve current game data pointer\n- FUN_6fb6bc10() - Process game data structure\n- FUN_6fb8f0c0() - State transition preparation/cleanup\n- FUN_6fb8d210() - Update viewport coordinates\n- ProcessMessageArray() - Handle queued messages\n- ProcessUIStateChange() - Update UI state\n- CloseDialogAndCleanup() - Close active dialog\n- ReportValidationError() - Report and clear error handles",
