      "comment": "Process game message queue and handle game state transitions.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if game state is 3 (GAME_STATE_QUIT) and return early\n2. If game state is 2 (GAME_STATE_IN_GAME), retrieve game data pointer via FUN_6fb62880\n3. Get message data from offset 0x84 via Ordinal_10262, pass to FUN_6fb8f0c0\n4. Call FUN_6fb8d210 to set initial view parameters (state=1, offsets=0.0, 0.0)\n5. Check DAT_6fbfda18 flag:\n   - If 0: prepare message data (CompressPackedData with mode=2, param2=0)\n   - If non-zero: call ProcessGameStateTransition\n6. Reset game state to 0\n7. Retrieve game data again and extract message data at offset 0x84\n8. Handle state machine:\n   - If state==1: transition to state 2, call FUN_6fb8f0c0, extract data at offset 0x8, call FUN_6fb6bc10\n   - If state==2: transition to state 1, clear data buffer, set nState=1\n9. Call FUN_6fb8d210 with calculated state and float parameters\n10. Retrieve window handle via Ordinal_10027 (8 messages)\n11. Process message array via ProcessMessageArray\n12. Check dialog cleanup flag (DAT_6fbfda2c), if set call CloseDialogAndCleanup and clear flag\n13. Call ProcessUIStateChange(0xe, 1, 0)\n14. Call CopyConfigurationData with NULL pointer\n15. Return\n\nParameters:\n(none - void function, uses global state variables)\n\nReturns:\n(void)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Game state 3 causes early return, skipping all processing\n- Float parameters flXOffset and flYOffset initialized to 0.0 and passed to view management\n- State machine uses game state value to control transitions between states 1 and 2\n- Message window handle retrieved via Ordinal_10027 (Storm DLL function)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x3 - GAME_STATE_QUIT exit code\n0x2 - GAME_STATE_IN_GAME\n0x1 - GAME_STATE_MENU\n0x84 - Message data offset in game object structure\n0x8 - Message data field offset, also number of message queue entries\n0x44 - Message compression parameter\n0xe - UI state identifier for ProcessUIStateChange",
