      "comment": "Process input interaction on unit and manage game state transitions during viewport interaction.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize unit's action ID to 1 and clear action pointer\n2. Call Ordinal_511 to trigger initial state notification\n3. Extract unit ID components: wUnitId (low 16 bits) and wUnitType (high 16 bits)\n4. Check g_dwGameDataMode != 2: If true, call HandleInteractionClick() and exit via ProcessStructureClickEvent\n5. If g_dwGameDataMode == 2: Call ProcessStructureClickEvent, return if non-zero, continue if zero\n6. Call CheckPointInUIViewport() to verify unit is within viewport bounds, exit if false\n7. Return early if g_dwGameDataMode == 3 (special state)\n8. If g_dwGameDataMode == 2: Retrieve current entity, extract offset 0x84, call Ordinal_10262, pass to FUN_6fb8f0c0\n9. Call FUN_6fb8d210(1, 0, 0.0, 0.0, 0) to notify state change\n10. Check g_dwUIViewportMode: If 0, call CompressPackedData(0x44, ...); if non-zero, call ProcessGameStateTransition()\n11. Reset g_dwGameDataMode to 0\n12. Retrieve entity again and get offset 0x84 value via Ordinal_10262\n13. State machine transition:\n    - If g_dwGameDataMode == 1: Set to 2, call FUN_6fb8f0c0(0), set buffer, call FUN_6fb6bc10\n    - Else if g_dwGameDataMode == 2: Set to 1, clear buffer, optionally call FUN_6fb8f0c0\n14. Call FUN_6fb8d210 with state parameters\n15. Retrieve window via Ordinal_10027, call ProcessMessageArray with 8 messages\n16. If g_hDialogHandle non-zero: Call CloseDialogAndCleanup, clear handle\n17. Call ProcessUIStateChange(0xE, 1, 0) to update UI\n18. Call CopyConfigurationData(nullptr) to sync config\n19. Return\n\nParameters:\n  pUnit: Pointer to UnitAny - unit entity being interacted with\n\nReturns:\n  void - Function modifies global game state and UI\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - g_dwGameDataMode values: 1=Init, 2=Normal, 3=Special (returns early)\n  - g_dwUIViewportMode=0 compresses data, non-zero triggers game state transition\n  - Dialog handle cleanup occurs if set from previous UI interaction\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x18: UnitAny.dwActId offset\n  0x1C: UnitAny.pAct offset\n  0xC: UnitAny.dwUnitId offset\n  0x10: Shift amount for unit type extraction\n  0x84: Entity data offset for state value\n  0x44: CompressPackedData code parameter\n  0x8: Message array count\n  0xE: UI state code for viewport interaction\n  0x1: Flag value for initial action ID\n  0x2, 0x3: g_dwGameDataMode state constants\n  \nRelated Functions:\n- HandleInteractionClick() - Validates click within game bounds\n- ProcessStructureClickEvent() - Routes structure-specific input\n- CheckPointInUIViewport() - Viewport boundary validation\n- Ordinal_511() - Initial state notification\n- Ordinal_10262() - Entity state extraction\n- Ordinal_10027() - Window handle retrieval\n- FUN_6fb8d210() - State change notification with parameters\n- FUN_6fb8f0c0() - Entity display update\n- ProcessGameStateTransition() - Complex game state change\n- CompressPackedData() - Data compression for transmission\n- ProcessMessageArray() - Message queue processing\n- CloseDialogAndCleanup() - Dialog cleanup\n- ProcessUIStateChange() - UI state manager update\n- CopyConfigurationData() - Config synchronization",
