      "instructions": ["0x8EF60|SUB|ESP, 0x8", "0x8EF63|PUSH|EBX", "0x8EF64|PUSH|ESI", "0x8EF65|MOV|ESI, EDX", "0x8EF67|PUSH|EDI", "0x8EF68|MOV|EDX, dword ptr [0x6fbc9bf8]", "0x8EF6E|XOR|EBX, EBX", "0x8EF70|XOR|EAX, EAX", "0x8EF72|XOR|EDI, EDI", "0x8EF74|CMP|EDX, EBX", "0x8EF76|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x10], ESI", "0x8EF7A|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0xc], ECX", "0x8EF7E|JLE|0x6fb5f1eb", "0x8EF84|LEA|ECX, [EDI + EDI*0x4]", "0x8EF87|SHL|ECX, 0x3"],
      "comment": "Handles mouse clicks on structure/building objects in the game world.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Iterate through all active structures in the global structure array\n2. For each structure, check if the click coordinates fall within its bounding box\n3. If coordinates match a structure:\n   a. Call FUN_6fb8d210 with parameter 1 (initial setup)\n   b. If this is the first structure (index 0):\n      - Check if game data mode is 2 (world state)\n      - Call FUN_6fb8d210 with parameter 2 (secondary setup)\n      - Initialize new dialog with dimensions 0x96 x 0x82\n      - Set dialog field value to 0\n      - Call Ordinal_10004 (D2Common ordinal - initialization function)\n      - Add dialog line with resource ID 0xd19\n      - Set game data mode to 3 (dialog active)\n      - If g_dwGameDataFlag is 0: compress packed data with mode 0x44\n      - Otherwise: send game status update\n   c. If not first structure and game data mode is not 3:\n      - If mode is 2: retrieve ordinal function result (Ordinal_10262)\n      - Call FUN_6fb8f0c0 with retrieved value\n      - Call FUN_6fb8d210 with parameter 1\n      - If g_dwGameDataFlag is 0: compress packed data with mode 0x44 and flag 2\n      - Otherwise: call ProcessGameStateTransition\n      - Set game data mode to 0\n      - Handle mode transition logic for modes 1 and 2\n      - Clear message array (8 entries) using Ordinal_10027\n      - Close dialog if handle is valid\n      - Call ProcessUIStateChange(0xe, 1, 0)\n      - Call CopyConfigurationData with NULL\n      - Set return value to 1 (click handled)\n4. After checking all structures, clear the structure array (set bytes to 0)\n5. Return 1 if click was handled, 0 otherwise\n\nParameters:\n  nX (int) - X coordinate of mouse click in game world coordinates\n  nY (int) - Y coordinate of mouse click in game world coordinates\n\nReturns:\n  1 if click was handled (structure clicked), 0 if no structure at coordinates\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - g_dwGameDataFlag determines whether to compress data or send update\n  - Magic number 0x44 is used as compress mode indicator\n  - Magic number 0xd19 appears to be a dialog resource ID\n  - Structure iteration uses 0x28 byte stride (structure record size)\n  - Each structure has X/Y bounds at offsets: min_x at [+0xbba], max_x at [+0xbbe], min_y at [+0xbc2], max_y at [+0xbc6]\n  - Note: Function uses 2 stack-allocated temporaries optimized away by compiler (local_4, local_8)\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x96 (150) - Dialog width in pixels\n  0x82 (130) - Dialog height in pixels\n  0x28 (40) - Structure record size in bytes\n  0xd19 (3353) - Dialog resource/string ID\n  0x44 (68) - Data compression mode flag\n  0x0f (15) - Dialog line parameter (purpose unknown)\n  0xe (14) - UI state change code\n  0x3 (3) - Game data mode: dialog active\n  0x2 (2) - Game data mode: world state\n  0x1 (1) - Game data mode: menu state\n  0x0 (0) - Game data mode: no state\n\nOrdinals Used:\n  Ordinal_10004 - Initialization/validation function (D2Common)\n  Ordinal_10262 - Retrieves value from game state structure (D2Common)\n  Ordinal_10027 - Gets window/context handle for message processing (D2Common)\n\nStructure Layout:\n  Offset | Size | Field Name | Type | Description\n  0x00   | 1    | bActive    | byte | Structure active flag (0 = inactive)\n  0xbba  | 4    | nMinX      | int  | Minimum X coordinate of structure\n  0xbbe  | 4    | nMaxX      | int  | Maximum X coordinate of structure\n  0xbc2  | 4    | nMinY      | int  | Minimum Y coordinate of structure\n  0xbc6  | 4    | nMaxY      | int  | Maximum Y coordinate of structure",
      "tags": ["PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PARAM_2"]
    },
