      "api_calls": ["InsertCacheNodeWithCookie", "INVENTORY_GetOwner", "GetItemStatsTableOffset", "IsItemSellable", "CanItemBePersonalized", "ItemCanHaveQuantity"],
      "instructions": ["0x8F290|PUSH|EBX", "0x8F291|PUSH|EBP", "0x8F292|PUSH|ESI", "0x8F293|MOV|ESI, dword ptr [ESP + 0x10]", "0x8F297|PUSH|EDI", "0x8F298|XOR|EBX, EBX", "0x8F29A|MOV|EBP, dword ptr [ESI + 0xc]", "0x8F29D|MOV|BX, word ptr [ESI + 0xc]", "0x8F2A1|PUSH|ESI", "0x8F2A2|MOV|dword ptr [ESI + 0x18], 0x1", "0x8F2A9|SHR|EBP, 0x10", "0x8F2AC|MOV|dword ptr [ESI + 0x1c], 0x0", "0x8F2B3|CALL|0x6fb99c36", "0x8F2B8|MOV|EDI, dword ptr [0x6fba6098]", "0x8F2BE|CALL|EDI"],
      "comment": "UI Viewport Mode Toggle Handler - Manages switching between viewport display modes with coordinate validation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract viewport dimensions: wMouseX = X-axis, dwMouseY = Y-axis from input structure\n2. Initialize viewport flags (field offset +0x18 = 1, +0x1c = 0)\n3. Call Ordinal_511 for viewport state initialization\n4. Get elapsed time since last toggle via GetTickCount()\n5. If elapsed < 400ms, debounce and return (prevent rapid toggling)\n6. Check game mode: if mode 1 (active), call ValidateMouseCoordinatesAndHandleInput; if mode 2 (inactive), call CheckPointInUIViewport\n7. If mode check returned non-zero, exit (coordinate out of bounds)\n8. Call FUN_6fb5f210 with viewport dimensions for preliminary processing\n9. Get current object pointer via FUN_6fb62880()\n10. Extract object stat via Ordinal_10262 at offset +0x84\n11. Extract item data via Ordinal_10600 at offset +0x4\n12. Check g_dwUIViewportMode flag for decision branching\n13. If mode flag = 1: validate state via Ordinal_10830/10831/10832, compare game state (0x9a/0x1ff/0x200)\n14. If mode flag = 0: check item signature at offset +0x80 for 'hst ' (0x20747368)\n15. If conditions match: validate bounding box (0x7b < X < 0xd4, 0x6a < Y < 0xdc)\n16. If game mode = 1: switch to mode 2, initialize viewport, get level data via FUN_6fb6bc10, call FUN_6fb8d210(mode2_setup)\n17. If game mode = 2: switch to mode 1, reset viewport, call FUN_6fb8d210(mode1_setup)\n18. If conditions fail: call FUN_6fb8d210(error_state=3)\n\nParameters:\n  pViewportData (dword *) - Pointer to viewport structure containing X/Y coordinates and flags\n\nReturns:\n  void - No direct return value; updates global UI state and calls display functions\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Debounce protection: 400ms minimum between toggles\n  - Coordinate range checks prevent invalid mode switches\n  - Three distinct game modes (0=inactive, 1=active, 2=display)\n  - Mode flag acts as state lock for invalid mode combinations\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x9a / 0x1ff / 0x200 - Game state constants for world/menu/inventory modes\n  0x7b / 0xd3 - Min/max X coordinates (123-211 pixels)\n  0x6a / 0xdc - Min/max Y coordinates (106-220 pixels)\n  0x190 - 400ms debounce interval in milliseconds\n  0x20747368 - 'hst ' signature for item validation\n  0x1 / 0x2 - Game mode constants (1=active viewport, 2=inactive viewport)\n  0x80 / 0x84 / 0x4 - Structure field offsets for item data access",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Inventory", "PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_1", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
    },
