      "comment": "Handle game state transitions between different modes (initialization, active gameplay, shutdown)\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check game mode flag: if 0 (uninitialized), log error and exit\n2. If game is running (FUN_6fb62890), proceed to state machine transition\n3. State machine transitions:\n   - Mode 1 (ACTIVE): Transition to 2 (GAME_LOADED). Load game buffer, call initialization\n   - Mode 2 (GAME_LOADED): Transition to 1 (ACTIVE). Unload game buffer\n4. After transition, notify UI system with ProcessUIStateChange (0xe = game state notification)\n5. Process message queue with 8 pending messages\n6. Close dialog if open and update configuration\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\nNone (void)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If game mode is 0 on entry, logs critical error with source file location\n- If game buffer cannot be loaded, returns early without state change\n- No return value, but modifies global game state (g_dwGameDataMode, g_pGameDataBuffer)",
      "tags": ["PROP_LARGE", "MOD_UI", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "STRUCT_ItemData", "PARAM_0", "PROP_LOOPHEAVY", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData", "SRC_useitem.cpp"]
