      "api_calls": ["SetActiveFont", "GfxInterfaceCall84", "GfxInterfaceCall84", "ValidateStringId", "SumCharacterValues", "GetCurrentFontProperty", "GetCurrentFontProperty", "RenderUnicodeTextWithLineHeight", "ValidateStringId", "WrapUnicodeText", "...+5 more"],
      "instructions": ["0x8F7C0|SUB|ESP, 0x58", "0x8F7C3|MOV|ECX, 0x1", "0x8F7C8|CALL|0x6fb99a02", "0x8F7CD|MOV|EDX, dword ptr [0x6fbfda18]", "0x8F7D3|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0xc], EAX", "0x8F7D7|CMP|EDX, 0x1", "0x8F7DA|JZ|0x6fb5f7e4", "0x8F7DC|TEST|EDX, EDX", "0x8F7DE|JNZ|0x6fb5fa52", "0x8F7E4|PUSH|EBX", "0x8F7E5|PUSH|ESI", "0x8F7E6|PUSH|EDI", "0x8F7E7|MOV|ECX, 0x12", "0x8F7EC|XOR|EAX, EAX", "0x8F7EE|LEA|EDI, [ESP + 0x1c]"],
      "comment": "Render viewport UI elements and structure slots based on game state.\n\nNote: Function uses 4 stack-allocated temporaries optimized away by compiler (uVar1, iVar2, piVar3, local_EDI_123).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call Ordinal_10127() to initialize rendering state\n2. If UIViewportMode is 0 or 1, proceed with structure rendering:\n   a. Initialize 18-element viewport buffer (anViewportData[18]) with zeros\n   b. Set buffer[1] to current data path handle (depends on mode)\n   c. Call Ordinal_10072() to configure viewport (0x69 width, 0x10e height, -1 color, flags=5)\n   d. Initialize button panel and store return in buffer[1]\n   e. Loop through structure count: Load structure definitions from g_pStructureData\n   f. For each structure, calculate dimensions based on name length, call Ordinal_10072()\n3. Get viewport position (nX, nY) via FUN_6fb8f680, FUN_6fb8f690\n4. If position within bounds (nX < 0x140, nY < screen_height - 0x30):\n   a. Loop through structure list (g_pStructureData array)\n   b. Check if mouse position (nX, nY) within structure bounds\n   c. If structure type == 0xfb1 and game state is valid (not 0x1ff, not 0x200):\n      - Load structure properties and calculate dimensions\n      - Call FUN_6fb92980() to render structure with offset positioning\n      - Call Ordinal_10117() to position element on screen\n5. If UIViewportMode == 1: Iterate linked list of items via Ordinal_10199, call Ordinal_10121/10117/10043 for rendering\n6. Call RenderDialogElements() if global dialog handle exists\n7. Call Ordinal_10127() to finalize rendering\n\nParameters:\n  None\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  Game state values 0x1ff and 0x200 skip structure rendering\n  Structure type 0xfb1 indicates selectable viewport slot\n  \nMagic Numbers:\n  0x69 - Viewport width constant\n  0x10e - Viewport height constant  \n  0x140 - Max X coordinate boundary (320 pixels)\n  0x30 - Screen height offset (48 pixels)\n  0xfb1 - Structure type identifier for selectable slots\n  0x1ff, 0x200 - Invalid game state values\n  0x26, 0x2a, 0xa, 0xc - Position adjustment constants\n  0x14 - Item list stride (20 bytes per item)\n  0x28 - Structure data element stride (40 bytes)\n  0x2c1, 0x2c2 - Configuration ordinal IDs\n  0x1e - Initial Y position for linked list rendering\n  300 - Ordinal_10199 search parameter",
      "tags": ["MOD_UI", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "STRUCT_ItemData", "PARAM_0", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData", "SRC_useitem.cpp", "STRUCT_MonsterData", "PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Path", "STRUCT_Skill", "PROP_LOOPHEAVY"]
