      "instructions": ["0x8FA70|PUSH|EBX", "0x8FA71|PUSH|ESI", "0x8FA72|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0x8FA74|XOR|EAX, EAX", "0x8FA76|MOV|AL, byte ptr [ESI + 0x5]", "0x8FA79|CMP|EAX, 0x7", "0x8FA7C|JA|0x6fb5fd46", "0x8FA82|JMP|dword ptr [EAX*0x4 + 0x6fb5fd64]", "0x8FA89|MOV|dword ptr [0x6fbfda18], 0x0", "0x8FA93|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [ESI + 0x1]", "0x8FA96|MOV|[0x6fbfda24], EAX", "0x8FA9B|CALL|0x6fb5fd90", "0x8FAA0|POP|ESI", "0x8FAA1|POP|EBX", "0x8FAA2|RET|"],
      "comment": "Processes game state command messages from the message queue, managing data mode transitions and viewport updates.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract command code from byte at offset +5 of message structure\n2. Dispatch based on command code (0-7) using jump table at 0x6fb5fd64\n3. Code 0: Clear message prepare flag and initialize game data path; call FUN_6fb5fd90 for initialization\n4. Code 1,5,6,7: Handle state transitions - toggle between modes 1 and 2, manage data buffer lifecycle\n5. Code 4: Set mode to 2 and close dialog if window handle is non-zero\n6. Default (8+): Log critical error with code location and invoke non-returning exit handler\n7. For transition codes: call FUN_6fb62880 to retrieve data item, extract handle from offset +0x84\n8. Set mode flag (0x1 or 0x2) at global g_dwGameDataMode address 0x6fbfda1c\n9. Initialize viewport coordinates (flOffsetX=0.0, flOffsetY=0.0, nFlags=0)\n10. Call FUN_6fb8d210 to update viewport with initialized parameters\n11. Call Ordinal_10027 to get main window handle\n12. Process message array (size 8) using ProcessMessageArray\n13. Close dialog if g_hDialogHandle is non-zero by calling CloseDialogAndCleanup\n14. Call ProcessUIStateChange(0xE, 1, 0) to update UI element state\n15. Call CopyConfigurationData(NULL) to write current configuration\n16. Return\n\nParameters:\n  pGameStateMsg (GameStateMessage*) - Pointer to game state message structure with fields:\n    +0x01: DWORD dwGameDataPath - Game data storage path or buffer reference\n    +0x05: BYTE byCommandCode - Message command code (0=init, 1=toggle, 4=mode2, 5-7=transition)\n    +0x06: CHAR cModeIndicator - Null for mode 3, non-null for mode 5\n    +0x84: Nested structure handle - Data item state reference\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value; side effects include modifying game mode state, updating viewport, and processing messages\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Default case with invalid command invokes critical error logging and non-returning exit (0xFFFFFFFF)\n  - Null dialog handle prevents closure attempt\n  - Zero data item handle skips viewport update\n  - Magic number 0x8 represents fixed message array size\n  - Magic number 0x84 offset contains data item state reference",
      "tags": ["PROP_LARGE", "MOD_UI", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PARAM_1", "SRC_useitem.cpp"]
