      "comment": "Orchestrates game initialization and state transitions, managing mode switches and configuration.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Clear UI message queue (ProcessUIStatesByResourceBuffer)\n2. Set game data mode to 1 (active initialization)\n3. Cache current tick count (_g_dwGameDataPath4)\n4. Initialize message queue with 8 entries from Ordinal_10027 window\n5. Initialize game mode (InitializeGameMode)\n6. Trigger UI state change event (0xe = game init event)\n7. If event returns non-zero:\n   a. Initialize targeting system\n   b. Create 16-byte local config buffer with values:\n      - [0..3]: 0x6b (107 decimal, unit type flag)\n      - [4..7]: 0x5b (91 decimal, skill type flag)\n      - [8..11]: 0xde (222 decimal, item flag)\n      - [12..15]: 0x116 (278 decimal, config version)\n   c. Copy config buffer to global config (CopyConfigurationData)\n   d. Return early\n8. If message prepare flag clear:\n   a. Get game data structure via FUN_6fb62880\n   b. Compress packed data block 0x44 with specified buffer\n9. Else: Process game state transition (ProcessGameStateTransition)\n10. Reset game data mode to 0\n11. Get game data structure again via FUN_6fb62880\n12. Retrieve ordinal data from offset 0x84 via Ordinal_10262\n13. Check game data mode for state machine transitions:\n    - Mode 1->2: Set new game data buffer, reset offsets, call FUN_6fb6bc10\n    - Mode 2->1: Clear game data buffer, toggle mode back\n14. Call FUN_6fb8d210 with offsets and mode flag\n15. Finalize: Process remaining messages, close dialog if open\n16. Trigger final UI state change (0xe = 1 to finalize)\n\nParameters:\n(void) - No parameters\n\nReturns:\n(void) - Returns void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Early return if UI state change (0xe) succeeds\n- Magic number 0x44 appears to be a packed data block identifier\n- Config values (0x6b, 0x5b, 0xde, 0x116) are hardcoded initialization constants\n- Game data mode uses values 0, 1, 2 for state machine transitions\n- Dialog handle cleanup ensures no dangling window references\n- Message queue size fixed at 8 entries\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x6b - 107 decimal, Unit type classification constant\n0x5b - 91 decimal, Skill type classification constant\n0xde - 222 decimal, Item type classification constant\n0x116 - 278 decimal, Configuration version identifier\n0xe - 14 decimal, Game initialization UI event identifier\n0x44 - 68 decimal, Packed data block identifier\n0x84 - Offset into game data structure for ordinal data\n0x8 - Message queue size constant",
