      "comment": "Process UI initialization and cleanup dialog resources.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if UI not initialized (g_bUIInitialized == 0x00)\n2. If not initialized, call FUN_6fb62880() to get initialization result\n3. If result nonzero, call FUN_6fb62880() again to get resource handle\n4. Pass handle to Ordinal_10342() (D2Common.GetUnitStat - validate resource) for validation\n5. If validation passes, send packet 0x49 with g_dwUIPacketCode via SendPacketData()\n6. Set g_bUIInitialized = 0x01\n7. Check if g_pDialogBox is non-zero\n8. If true, call Ordinal_11149(0, g_pDialogBox) to close dialog window\n9. Clear g_pDialogBox = 0\n10. Check and report 3 validation errors: g_pValidationError2, g_pValidationError1, g_pValidationError3\n11. Report each error via ReportValidationError() and clear the error flag\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If UI already initialized (g_bUIInitialized != 0), skips initialization and goes to cleanup\n- Initialization may fail at two points: FUN_6fb62880() return or Ordinal_10342() return\n- Three separate validation error queues checked and cleared sequentially\n- Dialog cleanup happens regardless of initialization success state",
