      "comment": "Initialize UI system and send initial UI packet to game server\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if UI is already initialized (g_bUIInitialized flag)\n2. If not initialized, call FUN_6fb62880() to perform initial setup\n3. Validate setup success by checking returned value against zero\n4. If setup succeeded, call FUN_6fb62880() again to obtain packet handle\n5. Pass packet handle to Ordinal_10342 (D2Common.GetUnitStat) for processing\n6. Check if ordinal call succeeded\n7. If successful, send UI packet with code 0x49 and stored UI packet code\n8. Mark UI as initialized by setting g_bUIInitialized to 0x01\n9. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\nvoid (no return value, sets global state on success)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If UI already initialized, function returns immediately without processing\n- If initial setup call fails (returns 0), function returns without sending packet\n- If ordinal call fails (returns 0), function returns without marking UI initialized\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x49 - UI packet type code (packet opcode for UI initialization)\n0x01 - Boolean true value for UI initialized flag\n0x00 - Boolean false value for initialization state check\n\nNote: Function uses 2 stack-allocated temporaries optimized away by compiler (uVar1, iVar2).\n\nRelated Globals:\ng_bUIInitialized - UI initialization state flag (byte at 0x6fbfda61)\ng_dwUIPacketCode - UI packet code to send (dword at 0x6fbfda59)",
