      "instructions": ["0x906C0|PUSH|ESI", "0x906C1|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0x906C3|PUSH|0x1", "0x906C5|XOR|EDX, EDX", "0x906C7|MOV|ECX, 0x14", "0x906CC|CALL|0x6fb5d370", "0x906D1|CMP|EAX, 0x1", "0x906D4|JNZ|0x6fb60738", "0x906D6|CALL|0x6fadb810", "0x906DB|CALL|0x6fb62880", "0x906E0|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0x906E2|JZ|0x6fb60708", "0x906E4|PUSH|EAX", "0x906E5|CALL|0x6fb98164", "0x906EA|TEST|EAX, EAX"],
      "comment": "Initialize UI viewport dialog and targeting system with packet data\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call ProcessUIStateChange(0x14, 0, 1) to request UI state change\n2. If state change successful (result == 1):\n   a. Initialize targeting system via InitializeTargetingSystem()\n   b. Obtain resource object from FUN_6fb62880()\n   c. Chain validation: apply Ordinal_10342, then Ordinal_10057 to object\n   d. If any validation returns NULL, set resource flag to 0\n   e. Otherwise extract resource flag byte via Ordinal_10001 conversion\n   f. Call FUN_6fb60740 with resource flag (0 or extracted byte)\n   g. Update UI state via FUN_6fb60860()\n   h. Store packet data fields: UI packet code from offset +1, dialog pointer from global\n   i. Pass packet data offset +5 to dialog initialization (Ordinal_11150)\n   j. Clear UI initialization flag (g_bUIInitialized = 0)\n   k. Final UI state update via FUN_6fb60860()\n\nParameters:\npPacketData (ECX, IMPLICIT) - Pointer to UI packet data structure with fields at offsets +1 and +5\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Updates global UI state and initializes dialog system\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If ProcessUIStateChange returns non-1, function returns early without initialization\n- If any object validation step fails (NULL result), resource flag defaults to 0\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x14 - State change request code (20 decimal)\n0x1 - Success flag value for ProcessUIStateChange\n0xff - Byte mask for resource flag conversion (isolates lower 8 bits)\n\nRelated Ordinals:\nOrdinal_10342 - D2Common ordinal function for object processing\nOrdinal_10057 - D2Common ordinal function for object processing\nOrdinal_10001 - D2Common ordinal function extracting resource flag\nOrdinal_11150 - D2Common ordinal function for dialog initialization",
