      "api_calls": ["IsNpcTradeFlagSet", "IsNpcTradeFlagSet", "IsNpcTradeFlagSet", "IsNpcTradeFlagSet", "IsNpcTradeFlagSet", "IsNpcTradeFlagSet", "IsNpcTradeFlagSet", "IsNpcTradeFlagSet", "IsNpcTradeFlagSet"],
      "instructions": ["0x90740|MOV|EAX, [0x6fbc9d08]", "0x90745|PUSH|ESI", "0x90746|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0x90748|CMP|ESI, EAX", "0x9074A|JL|0x6fb6074e", "0x9074C|XOR|ESI, ESI", "0x9074E|LEA|EAX, [ESI + -0x1]", "0x90751|CMP|EAX, 0x3", "0x90754|JA|0x6fb60844", "0x9075A|JMP|dword ptr [EAX*0x4 + 0x6fb6084c]", "0x90761|PUSH|0x0", "0x90763|PUSH|0xf", "0x90765|CALL|0x6fb2a190", "0x9076A|PUSH|EAX", "0x9076B|CALL|0x6fb988a8"],
      "comment": "Validates player skill slots and updates active slot index.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Clamp nSlotIndex to valid range [0, DAT_6fbc9d08-1]\n2. Use switch statement to cascade validate slots starting from nSlotIndex\n3. For each slot index: call GetSlotDataBase() to get base data, then Ordinal_11107() to validate skill exists\n4. If validation fails (returns 0), decrement to previous valid slot or reset to 0\n5. Call Ordinal_11107() with slot index and offset parameters to check slot availability\n6. Write final validated slot index to DAT_6fbfda62 (player active slot global)\n7. Return void\n\nParameters:\nnSlotIndex (dword) - Requested player skill slot (0-based). Will be clamped and validated.\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Result written to global DAT_6fbfda62\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If nSlotIndex >= DAT_6fbc9d08, clamped to 0\n- If all slots fail validation, slot index set to 0\n- Cascades validation: tries slot 4 then 3, 2, 1, 0 in sequence\n- Magic constants: 0xf=15 (slot offset), 0x7=7 (slot offset), 0x17=23 (slot offset), 0x1c=28 (slot offset)\n\nRelated Functions:\n- InitializeUIViewportDialog() - Calls this function to setup viewport\n- GetSlotDataBase() - Retrieves skill slot base data pointer\n- Ordinal_11107() - Validates skill slot availability (likely D2Common.GetUnitStat)",
