      "instructions": ["0x90860|SUB|ESP, 0x8", "0x90863|PUSH|EBP", "0x90864|PUSH|ESI", "0x90865|XOR|ESI, ESI", "0x90867|MOV|dword ptr [0x6fbfda66], ESI", "0x9086D|MOV|dword ptr [0x6fbfda6a], ESI", "0x90873|CALL|0x6fb62880", "0x90878|PUSH|EAX", "0x90879|CALL|0x6fb98164", "0x9087E|PUSH|EAX", "0x9087F|CALL|0x6fb98140", "0x90884|MOV|EBP, EAX", "0x90886|MOV|EAX, 0x6fbfda76", "0x9088B|MOV|dword ptr [EAX + -0x4], ESI", "0x9088E|MOV|byte ptr [EAX], 0x0"],
      "comment": "Initialize viewport dialogs for UI rendering\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Clear viewport data structures (DAT_6fbfda66, DAT_6fbfda6a)\n2. Get active game viewport via FUN_6fb62880()\n3. Get current unit (Ordinal_10342) and unit stat count (Ordinal_10057)\n4. Zero-initialize dialog data array (0x5-element stride array at 0x6fbfda76)\n5. Validate viewport index (must be less than 5)\n6. Mark viewport as initialized in slot table at 0x6fbc9cd0\n7. Iterate through unit count range, populate min/max dialog indices via Ordinal_11152\n8. Scan dialog range, query dialog properties via Ordinal_11146 and Ordinal_11153\n9. Build filtered dialog list (exclude viewport unit ID from active dialogs)\n10. Increment counters for valid dialogs (DAT_6fbfda66, DAT_6fbfda6a)\n\nParameters:\n(none)\n\nReturns:\n(void) - Modifies global dialog state at 0x6fbfda6a-0x6fbfda76\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Viewport index 5+ causes early return without initialization\n- Dialog entry -1 in table means uninitialized slot\n- Matching viewport unit ID vs query result skips dialog marking",
