      "api_count": 4,
      "api_calls": ["UNITS_GetRoom", "InsertCacheNodeWithCookie", "InsertCacheNodeWithCookie", "InsertCacheNodeWithCookie"],
      "instructions": ["0x909E0|PUSH|EBX", "0x909E1|PUSH|EBP", "0x909E2|PUSH|ESI", "0x909E3|MOV|ESI, dword ptr [ESP + 0x10]", "0x909E7|PUSH|EDI", "0x909E8|XOR|EBP, EBP", "0x909EA|MOV|EDI, dword ptr [ESI + 0xc]", "0x909ED|MOV|BP, word ptr [ESI + 0xc]", "0x909F1|SHR|EDI, 0x10", "0x909F4|CALL|0x6fb38390", "0x909F9|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0x909FB|JNZ|0x6fb60bb2", "0x90A01|CMP|EBP, dword ptr [0x6fbae0e4]", "0x90A07|JG|0x6fb60ba1", "0x90A0D|MOV|EAX, [0x6fbae0e8]"],
      "comment": "Processes mouse click events for UI inventory slots and handles slot selection/activation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract mouse X/Y coordinates from nMouseCoordinates (lower 16 bits = X, upper 16 bits = Y)\n2. If click is within UI slot region, return (handled by IsPointInUISlotRegion)\n3. If click within screen bounds and below top menu (Y < screen_height - 0x31):\n   a. Adjust X/Y to UI coordinate space using g_dwUIXOffset/g_dwUIYOffset\n   b. If g_bUISlotDragging is false and g_nUISelectedSlot != -1:\n      - Iterate through slot array to find matching coordinates\n      - Each slot has bounds [X-0x118 to X], [Y to Y+0x1e], and active status flag\n      - On match: Set state to deselecting (0x18=1, 0x1c=0), send packet 0x49, reset globals\n   c. Else if g_bUISlotDragging is true and coordinates in drop zone (0x110-0x135 X, 0x182-0x1a5 Y):\n      - Call ProcessUIStateChange, check g_bUIInitialized\n      - Call FUN_6fb62880 twice to get unit ID\n      - Call Ordinal_10342 to perform drop action\n      - Send packet 0x49 if successful\n4. Reset drag state: g_bUISlotDragging=0, g_nUISelectedSlot=-1\n5. Restore mouse state: 0x18=1, 0x1c=0, call Ordinal_511\n\nParameters:\nnMouseCoordinates (int) - Packed mouse coordinates: bits [31:16]=Y, bits [15:0]=X\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Updates global UI state and sends network packets as side effects\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If click outside screen bounds, only resets drag state without processing slots\n- Coordinate validation prevents negative indexes into slot array\n- Drop zone coordinates (0x110-0x135, 0x182-0x1a5) are hardcoded screen positions\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x0c - Offset to mouse coordinates in nMouseCoordinates structure\n0x10 - Bits to right-shift for Y coordinate extraction\n0x118 - Slot width (280 pixels)\n0x1e - Slot height (30 pixels)\n0x31 - UI menu height (49 pixels)\n0x110 - Drop zone left boundary (272 pixels)\n0x135 - Drop zone right boundary (309 pixels)\n0x182 - Drop zone top boundary (386 pixels)\n0x1a5 - Drop zone bottom boundary (421 pixels)\n0x49 - Packet type for slot action\n0x14 - State change type parameter\n0x8b7 - Magic animation/state ID",
