      "comment": "HandleUISlotClickMessage - Processes mouse click events on UI slot regions.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract click coordinates from message (+0x0C: X in low word, Y in high word)\n2. Early exit if click is in active UI slot region\n3. If click is right of center or below threshold:\n   - Initialize UI if needed (send packet 0x49)\n   - Process UI state change (0x14, 1, 1)\n4. Determine which skill slot was clicked based on coordinates:\n   - Expansion mode: 4 slots with different X thresholds (0x40, 0x80, 0xC0, 0x100)\n   - Classic mode: 4 slots with different X thresholds (0x50, 0xA0, 0xEF)\n5. If slot changed, reinitialize game object properties\n6. Validate player skill slots and initialize viewport dialogs\n7. Check for waygate selection in slot bounds table\n8. Cache message with processed flag\n\nParameters:\n  pMessage - Pointer to click message structure:\n    +0x0C: Packed coordinates (low word = X, high word = Y)\n    +0x18: Processed flag\n    +0x1C: Result status\n\nReturns: void\n\nGlobals Modified:\n  g_nPlayerSlotIndex - Current selected skill slot\n  g_nUISelectedWaygate - Selected waygate index (-1 if none)\n  g_bUISlotDragging - Dragging state flag\n  g_bUIInitialized - UI initialization flag",
      "tags": ["PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_1", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
    },
