      "instructions": ["0x90E10|PUSH|EBX", "0x90E11|PUSH|ESI", "0x90E12|PUSH|EDI", "0x90E13|MOV|EDI, EDX", "0x90E15|MOV|EBX, ECX", "0x90E17|MOV|EAX, EBX", "0x90E19|MOV|ECX, EDI", "0x90E1B|AND|EAX, 0x7f", "0x90E1E|SHL|ECX, 0x7", "0x90E21|ADD|EAX, ECX", "0x90E23|MOV|ESI, dword ptr [EAX*0x4 + 0x6fbfdaa0]", "0x90E2A|TEST|ESI, ESI", "0x90E2C|JZ|0x6fb60e58", "0x90E2E|CMP|dword ptr [ESI + 0x8], EBX", "0x90E31|JNZ|0x6fb60e4e"],
      "comment": "Find and return a unit node from the hash table by unit ID and slot type.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate hash table entry: index = (nUnitId & 0x7f) + nSlotType * 0x80 in g_ppUnitHashTable\n2. Get first node in chain at calculated index\n3. If node is NULL, return NULL (not found)\n4. Check if node.field[2] == nUnitId (ID field at offset 8 bytes)\n5. If ID matches and node.field[0] == nSlotType, return node (found match)\n6. If ID matches but slot differs, trigger assertion error - inconsistent state\n7. If node.field[0] != nSlotType after assertion, crash with abort code\n8. Move to next node in chain: pnCurEntry = pnCurEntry[0x42] (next pointer at offset 0x108)\n9. Repeat from step 3 until found or NULL\n\nParameters:\n- nUnitId (dword): Unit/entity identifier to search for, hashed using low 7 bits (0x7f)\n- nSlotType (int): Slot type or category index, used for secondary hash calculation\n\nReturns:\n- int *: Pointer to found unit node if match found, NULL (0x0) if not found\n- No match with valid state raises assertion error and crashes\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If unit ID found but slot type mismatch detected, assertion error indicates memory corruption\n- Function never returns after assertion failure - calls FUN_6fb9a10f(0xffffffff) to abort\n- Hash table uses 128-slot primary index (0x80 * slot count) with linear probe chains\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n- 0x7f: Hash mask for primary index (128 slots, items 0-127)\n- 0x80: Secondary hash multiplier (128 units per slot type)\n- 0x42: Offset 0x108 (bytes) to next pointer in chain (66*4 or equivalent)\n- 0x57: Error code 87 passed to assertion handler",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Unit", "SRC_CUnit.cpp", "PARAM_2", "MOD_UNIT"]
    },
