      "comment": "Search linked list table for node matching ID and index criteria\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate entry point in global link list table using dwRecordId masked to 0x7f and nTableIndex as offsets\n2. Traverse linked list starting from calculated entry: do-while loop\n3. Check if current node exists (non-NULL pointer)\n4. If exists, compare node.field[2] with dwRecordId\n5. If match found, compare node.field[0] with nTableIndex\n6. If both match, return pointer to node (success case)\n7. If nTableIndex mismatch after field[2] match, call Ordinal_10029 (D2Common.AssertLog), then validate with another check\n8. If still mismatched, call Ordinal_10023 (D2Common.AssertFail) with error code 0x57 (87 decimal), then FUN_6fb9a10f(-1) to halt\n9. If field[2] doesn't match dwRecordId, move to next node via node.field[0x42] (linked list chain)\n10. Repeat traversal until NULL node found (no match) or validation passes\n\nParameters:\n  dwRecordId (uint) - Record identifier to match against node.field[2], lower 7 bits used as table index component\n  nTableIndex (int) - Table index for offset calculation and comparison with node.field[0]\n\nReturns:\n  int * - Pointer to matching node structure if found; NULL if traversal completes without match\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Table hash function uses dwRecordId & 0x7f combined with nTableIndex shifted left 7 (nTableIndex * 128)\n  - Nodes linked via field[0x42] (offset 0x108 in 4-byte units) for collision chain handling\n  - Validation failure (mismatch after field[2] match) is fatal - calls FUN_6fb9a10f(-1)\n  - Returns NULL if any node pointer is NULL (end of chain)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x7f - Mask for dwRecordId lower 7 bits (128 buckets)\n  0x80 - Table stride for nTableIndex (SHL by 7 = * 128)\n  0x42 - Offset field for next node pointer (0x42 * 4 = 0x108 bytes)\n  0x108 - Actual byte offset to next node in chain\n  0x57 - Error code 87 (validation failure indicator)\n\nOrdinal References:\n  Ordinal_10029 - D2Common.AssertLog: Debug assertion logging on validation warning\n  Ordinal_10023 - D2Common.AssertFail: Fatal assertion handler for critical failures",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Unit", "SRC_CUnit.cpp", "PARAM_2", "MOD_UNIT"]
