      "instructions": ["0x90EF0|PUSH|EBX", "0x90EF1|PUSH|ESI", "0x90EF2|TEST|ECX, ECX", "0x90EF4|PUSH|EDI", "0x90EF5|JNZ|0x6fb60f15", "0x90EF7|PUSH|0x80", "0x90EFC|PUSH|0x6fbc9edc", "0x90F01|PUSH|0x6fbc9f40", "0x90F06|CALL|0x6fb99a7a", "0x90F0B|ADD|ESP, 0xc", "0x90F0E|PUSH|-0x1", "0x90F10|CALL|0x6fb9a10f", "0x90F15|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [ECX + 0xec]", "0x90F1B|TEST|AH, 0x4", "0x90F1E|JZ|0x6fb60f72"],
      "comment": "Searches hash table for unit matching ID and type, returning pointer or NULL.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate pUnit not NULL; exit with error if NULL\n2. Check if unit has type tracking flag (0x400 at offset 0xec)\n3. If flag not set, return NULL (unit not tracked)\n4. Read nUnitType from offset 0xb8\n5. Read dwUnitId from offset 0xbc\n6. If nUnitType == 3 (type 3 special case):\n   - Use g_ppUnitTypeHashTable indexed by (dwUnitId & 0x7f) as entry point\n   - Walk linked list via offset 0x108 (pUnitNode->next)\n   - Compare field at offset 0x8 (pUnitNode->dwId) against dwUnitId\n   - If match and type matches, return pUnitNode\n   - If match but type mismatch, call Ordinal_10029 (update), verify type changed, return on success or error exit\n7. Else nUnitType != 3:\n   - Use g_ppUnitHashTable indexed by (dwUnitId & 0x7f) + nUnitType*0x80 as entry point\n   - Walk linked list via offset 0x108 (pUnitNode->next)\n   - Compare field at offset 0x8 against dwUnitId\n   - If match and type equals nUnitType, return pUnitNode\n   - If match but type mismatch, call Ordinal_10029 (update), verify type changed\n   - If list exhausted, return NULL\n8. On type mismatch error (type still wrong after update), exit with error via Ordinal_10023\n\nParameters:\n- pUnit (int * IMPLICIT ECX): pointer to unit structure with ID/type at offsets 0xbc/0xb8\n- (implicit) g_ppUnitTypeHashTable: pointer to type-3 hash table (128 slots)\n- (implicit) g_ppUnitHashTable: pointer to type-specific hash tables (128*n slots)\n\nReturns:\n- pUnitNode (int *): pointer to matching unit in hash table, NULL if not found\n- Never returns if unit NULL or type verification fails (calls non-returning Ordinal_10023)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Type 3 has dedicated hash table (g_ppUnitTypeHashTable), type-specific have combined table\n- Hash index computed as: (dwUnitId & 0x7f) + nUnitType*0x80 for non-type-3\n- Both hash tables searched as linked lists, allowing multiple units at same hash slot\n- Field at offset 0x108 is next pointer in linked list (offset 0x42 DWORDS = 0x108 bytes)\n- Field at offset 0x8 is ID field for comparison (dwId)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x400: Flag mask at offset 0xec indicating unit is tracked in hash tables\n- 0xec: Offset to flags field in unit structure\n- 0xb8: Offset to unit type (nUnitType) in unit structure\n- 0xbc: Offset to unit ID (dwUnitId) in unit structure\n- 0x8: Offset to ID field in unit node for comparison\n- 0x108: Offset to next pointer in linked list (0x42 * 4 bytes)\n- 0x7f: Bitmask for hash slot selection (0-127)\n- 0x80: Stride for type-specific hash table rows (128 slots per type)\n- 0x3: Unit type constant for special case handling",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Unit", "SRC_CUnit.cpp", "MOD_UNIT", "PARAM_1", "PROP_LOOPHEAVY"]
