      "instructions": ["0x90FF0|PUSH|EBX", "0x90FF1|PUSH|ESI", "0x90FF2|MOV|ESI, EDX", "0x90FF4|PUSH|EDI", "0x90FF5|MOV|EDI, ECX", "0x90FF7|SHL|ESI, 0x9", "0x90FFA|AND|EDI, 0x7f", "0x90FFD|ADD|ESI, 0x6fbfdaa0", "0x91003|XOR|EBX, EBX", "0x91005|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [ESI + EDI*0x4]", "0x91008|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0x9100A|JZ|0x6fb61054", "0x9100C|CMP|dword ptr [EAX + 0x8], ECX", "0x9100F|JNZ|0x6fb61015", "0x91011|CMP|dword ptr [EAX], EDX"],
      "comment": "Remove unit from hash table and cleanup resources.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate hash bucket index: (nUnitType * 128) + (nUnitId & 0x7F)\n2. Load bucket head pointer from g_ppUnitHashTable[bucket]\n3. If bucket empty, return (unit not found)\n4. Traverse collision chain: pUnitNode->dwNextUnit (offset 0x108)\n5. For each node, check if pUnitNode->dwUnitId == nUnitId AND pUnitNode->nUnitType == nUnitType\n6. If not found after traversal, return (unit not in table)\n7. If found and pUnitNode is bucket head (pUnitPrev == NULL), update bucket pointer to pUnitNode->dwNextUnit\n8. If found and pUnitNode is in chain (pUnitPrev != NULL), link pUnitPrev->dwNextUnit to pUnitNode->dwNextUnit\n9. Call cleanup callback FUN_6fb62360(pUnitNode)\n\nParameters:\nnUnitId - Unit identifier (0-127 hash, full ID stored in unit)\nnUnitType - Unit type/class index (0-127, multiplied by 128 for bucket offset)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Always succeeds silently (no return value for not-found case)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Empty bucket: returns immediately\n- Unit not in chain: returns silently after chain exhausted\n- Bucket head removal: must update g_ppUnitHashTable directly\n- Chain node removal: must preserve link chain via dwNextUnit field\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x7F - Hash mask (unit ID modulo 128)\n0x80 - Hash table stride (128 buckets per type)\n0x108 - Offset 266 bytes - Next unit pointer in linked list collision chain\n0x8 - Offset 8 bytes - Unit ID field in UnitAny structure\n\nStructure Layout (UnitAny):\nOffset | Size | Field Name | Type | Description\n0x0    | 4    | nUnitType  | int  | Unit type identifier\n0x8    | 4    | dwUnitId   | dword| Unit unique ID\n0x108  | 4    | pNextUnit  | void*| Pointer to next unit in hash chain",
      "tags": ["PARAM_2"]
