      "instructions": ["0x91060|PUSH|EBX", "0x91061|PUSH|ESI", "0x91062|MOV|ESI, EDX", "0x91064|PUSH|EDI", "0x91065|MOV|EDI, ECX", "0x91067|SHL|ESI, 0x9", "0x9106A|AND|EDI, 0x7f", "0x9106D|ADD|ESI, 0x6fbfe6a0", "0x91073|XOR|EBX, EBX", "0x91075|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [ESI + EDI*0x4]", "0x91078|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0x9107A|JZ|0x6fb610c4", "0x9107C|CMP|dword ptr [EAX + 0x8], ECX", "0x9107F|JNZ|0x6fb61085", "0x91081|CMP|dword ptr [EAX], EDX"],
      "comment": "Find and remove a node from a hash-table linked list by matching both table index and list offset.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate hash bucket position: (nListOffset << 9) + (nTableIndex & 0x7f)\n2. Retrieve head node from g_ppLinkListTable hash table\n3. If bucket empty, return\n4. Iterate through linked list at offset 0x108 per node\n5. Compare each node's [offset 0x8] against nTableIndex and [offset 0x0] against nListOffset\n6. When match found:\n   a. If head node matched (ppPreviousNode is NULL), update g_ppLinkListTable bucket\n   b. Otherwise, link ppPreviousNode->0x108 to ppNode->0x108 to remove node\n7. Call FUN_6fb62360 (deallocation/cleanup) on matched node\n8. Return\n\nParameters:\nnTableIndex (ECX, dword) - Table index for node comparison, masked to 0x7f for bucket calculation\nnListOffset (EDX, dword) - List offset (bucket multiplier) for node comparison and hash calculation\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value; side effect is node removal and deallocation\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Empty bucket returns immediately without processing\n- Missing node (mismatch throughout list) returns after traversal\n- Head node removal requires hash table update\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x80 - Bucket count multiplier (nListOffset << 9 = nListOffset * 0x80)\n0x7f - Mask for nTableIndex in hash calculation (128 buckets per offset)\n0x8 - Offset of comparison field 1 (nTableIndex)\n0x108 - Offset of linked list next pointer (0x42 in uint* arrays = 0x108 in bytes)\n0x0 - Offset of comparison field 2 (nListOffset)",
      "tags": ["PARAM_2"]
    },
