      "instructions": ["0x910D0|SUB|ESP, 0x200", "0x910D6|PUSH|EBX", "0x910D7|PUSH|EBP", "0x910D8|MOV|EBP, dword ptr [0x6fbff2a0]", "0x910DE|PUSH|ESI", "0x910DF|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0x910E1|XOR|EBX, EBX", "0x910E3|PUSH|EDI", "0x910E4|MOV|EDI, EDX", "0x910E6|TEST|ESI, ESI", "0x910E8|JNZ|0x6fb610fb", "0x910EA|TEST|EDI, EDI", "0x910EC|JNZ|0x6fb610fb", "0x910EE|XOR|EAX, EAX", "0x910F0|POP|EDI"],
      "comment": "Find room for unit at specified coordinates.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Return early if both X and Y are zero (no-op case)\n2. If game context exists, retrieve unit stat via Ordinal_10342\n3. Check room availability via Ordinal_10042 with unit stat and coordinates\n4. Return early if room found\n5. Query render context handle from global\n6. Attempt room search via Ordinal_10041 with render context and coordinates\n7. If room not found, format error message and log failure\n8. Call Ordinal_578 to format error string with message template\n9. Call Ordinal_10025 to log error with source file/line\n10. Call Ordinal_10023 to log function name and location\n11. Terminate with fatal error code -1\n\nParameters:\nnX (int) - Target X coordinate for room search\nnY (int) - Target Y coordinate for room search\n\nReturns:\n0 if room found successfully\nNon-zero error code if room search failed\n-1 if fatal initialization error\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Both parameters zero returns immediately without allocation checks\n- Missing game context skips unit stat retrieval\n- Room not found triggers assert with error logging",
