      "instructions": ["0x91180|SUB|ESP, 0x10", "0x91183|MOV|EAX, [0x6fbff2a0]", "0x91188|PUSH|EBX", "0x91189|PUSH|EBP", "0x9118A|PUSH|ESI", "0x9118B|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0x9118D|PUSH|EDI", "0x9118E|CMP|ESI, EAX", "0x91190|MOV|EBP, EDX", "0x91192|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x14], EAX", "0x91196|JNZ|0x6fb6119d", "0x91198|CALL|0x6fae5550", "0x9119D|MOV|EDX, dword ptr [ESP + 0x24]", "0x911A1|MOV|ECX, EBP", "0x911A3|CALL|0x6fb610d0"],
      "comment": "Process unit warp request to destination coordinates with validation and state handling.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if unit pointer is valid (non-zero at offset 0xe); abort if invalid\n2. Validate destination coordinates using FUN_6fb610d0; abort if invalid coordinates for non-zero destination\n3. Check unit movement restriction flag (0x10000 at offset 0xe8); exit early if restricted\n4. Validate unit type/subtype compatibility (type at offset 0, subtype at offset 0xc) against allowed transitions\n5. If unit is currently selected (same as g_pGameContext):\n   - Get unit stat using Ordinal_10342\n   - Get unit target room using Ordinal_10323\n   - Get room level using Ordinal_10963; check if level is 0x36 or 0x113\n   - If check fails and nUnknownFlag is set and unit type is not 0, abort with assertion\n   - Set timeout to 500ms if conditions met\n6. For valid destination room (iVar5 != 0):\n   - Update unit path using Ordinal_10093 with old/new room comparison\n   - Get room type using Ordinal_10057 then Ordinal_10634\n   - Set room type state using Ordinal_10008\n   - If source room exists (iVar6), compare room subtypes; if different, call Ordinal_10177 and Ordinal_10097\n7. Call Ordinal_10229 to validate/prepare warp; if fails:\n   - Copy destination coords to stack (nWarpX, nWarpY)\n   - Get unit direction using Ordinal_10336\n   - Call Ordinal_10134 with magic constant 0x1c09 and flag 1\n   - Call Ordinal_10231 to execute warp; abort if fails\n8. Call SetAutomapUpdateThrottle to reduce update frequency\n9. If unit is selected, call InitializeNetworkSettings with nUnknownFlag\n10. For player units (type 0) with valid stat:\n   - If subtype is 1 or 5, call FUN_6fb801c0 to apply visual effect\n\nParameters:\npUnit (UnitAny *) - Unit to warp (checked at offset 0xe for validity)\nnDestX (int) - Destination X coordinate\nnDestY (int) - Destination Y coordinate  \nnUnknownFlag (int) - State/animation flag controlling timeout and visual effects\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Modifies unit position and state; calls abort (Ordinal_10023) if invalid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Unit must have valid stat data (offset 0xe) or function aborts\n- Destination coordinates validated via FUN_6fb610d0\n- Movement restrictions checked via 0x10000 flag\n- Selected unit requires specific level checks (0x36, 0x113 allowed)\n- Player units (type 0) subtype 1 or 5 trigger visual effect after warp\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x10000 - Movement restriction flag in unit.flags at offset 0xe8\n0x1c09 - Unknown warp operation code passed to Ordinal_10134\n0x36, 0x113 - Valid level types for selected unit warp\nOffset 0 - Unit type (0=player, 1=monster)\nOffset 0xc - Unit subtype/class\nOffset 0xe - Unit stat validity flag\nOffset 0xe8 - Unit flags (contains 0x10000 restriction bit)",
      "tags": ["UNIT_PLAYER", "PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Act", "SRC_CUnit.cpp", "STRUCT_Inventory", "MOD_UNIT", "STRUCT_Skill", "PARAM_4", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
