      "comment": "Allocate and initialize a new unit structure.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate 280 bytes (0x46 dwords) from Storm.dll memory pool (Ordinal_10042 = Storm.dll memory allocation)\n2. Initialize all 280 bytes to zero using REP STOSD in loop (0x46 iterations)\n3. Call ProcessUnitInitialization (FUN_6fb61440) with allocated unit pointer and 6 parameters\n4. Return void (unit initialization handled by callee)\n\nParameters:\ndwUnitType (ECX) - Unit type identifier (player=0, monster=1, object=2, missile=3, etc.)\ndwUnitClass (EDX) - Unit class (determines behavior and properties)\nnTownLevel (Stack) - Town/Act level for initialization context\ndwRoomX (Stack) - Initial room X coordinate\ndwRoomY (Stack) - Initial room Y coordinate\nnUnitMode (Stack) - Unit mode/action state\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Allocated unit pointer stored in allocated memory, returned by ProcessUnitInitialization\n\nSpecial Cases:\nMemory allocation failure not checked - caller should validate non-null return from ProcessUnitInitialization\nBlock allocation of 280 bytes assumes Storm.dll memory manager availability\nAll allocated dwords zeroed before initialization to ensure clean state\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x46 = 70 decimal = number of dwords in unit structure (280 bytes total)\n0x207 = 519 decimal = memory allocation size parameter to Storm.dll",
