      "comment": "Initializes a unit with base properties, position, and type-specific initialization.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call GetGlobalSystemState to determine game state\n2. Modify unit state flags: if state==0 clear 0x2000000 else set 0x2000000\n3. Set unit base properties: X (param_2), Y (param_3), Type (param_6)\n4. Initialize unit room index (param_4) and radius (param_5) to zero\n5. If nRoomNum!=0 and dwRadius!=0: FindRoomForUnit, query room properties\n6. Get renderer context from global g_hRenderContext\n7. Call Ordinal_10912 (GlobalSystemNotify) for initialization hooks\n8. If dwType==4: call Ordinal_10687 (PrepareDynamicLight) and Ordinal_10692 (AddDynamicLight)\n9. If room found: get ticks via Ordinal_10917, notify via Ordinal_10913\n10. Switch on dwType (0=Player, 1=Monster, 2=Object, 3=NPC, 4=Special, 5=Elite):\n    - Case 0: Call FUN_6fb7fb00 for player init\n    - Case 1: Call Ordinal_10023 (AssertDebug) and FUN_6fb9a10f (Fatal)\n    - Case 2: Ordinal_10460, FUN_6fb7e210 object init\n    - Case 3: Ordinal_10460, FUN_6fb6e730 NPC init\n    - Case 4: Ordinal_10460, FUN_6fb64720 special init\n    - Case 5: Ordinal_10460, set flags 0x22, Ordinal_10350/10351/10384 elite init\n11. Call FUN_6fb85510 (post-initialization cleanup)\n12. If dwType==0 or 1: Ordinal_10376 (NotifyUnitCreation)\n13. Get next unit via FUN_6fb61610\n14. If next unit found and dwType==2: FUN_6fb7e460 (additional processing)\n\nParameters:\npUnit - pointer to unit structure\ndwX - X coordinate value\ndwY - Y coordinate value\nnRoomNum - room number or 0 for no room\ndwRadius - radius/size value or 0\ndwType - unit type (0=Player, 1=Monster, 2=Object, 3=NPC, 4=Special, 5=Elite)\nnParam7 - type-specific parameter for dwType\ndwParam8 - type-specific parameter for dwType\n\nReturns:\nPointer to next unit in linked list, or NULL if end of list\n\nStructure offsets used:\n[0] = dwType\n[1] = dwY\n[2] = dwX\n[4] = dwRadius (cleared)\n[6] = g_hRenderContext reference\n[0xd] = tick count value\n[0x14] = room property byte (set from room query)\n[0x18] = renderer context reference\n[0x34] = timing/clock value\n[0x3a] = unit state flags (modified)\n[0x3b] = unit flags with 0x2000000 bit\n[0x3e] = cleared to zero\n[0xec] = state flags with 0x22 set for case 5\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x2000000 - State flag bit for game state indication\n0xfdffffff - Mask to clear 0x2000000 (AND with this clears the bit)\n0x22 - Elite unit state flags\n0x1db - Assert line number\n0x4 - Special unit type requiring renderer setup\n0x5 - Elite unit type (highest type)",
