      "comment": "Remove unit from hash table structure and deallocate unit memory\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call FUN_6fb61770 to check if unit has pending references - return early if true\n2. Extract unit type (dword 0) and unit id (dword 8) from unit structure\n3. Hash unit into appropriate hash table: g_ppUnitHashTable or g_ppLinkListTable based on flags\n4. Compute hash index: (unitId & 0x7F) + unitType * 0x80\n5. Search hash chain at computed index for matching unit (same type and id)\n6. Validate hash node type matches unit type - abort on mismatch (asserts)\n7. If found node equals input unit, assert fatal error (unit in wrong table)\n8. If unit has 0x200000 flag set: search g_ppLinkListTable, else search g_ppUnitHashTable\n9. Traverse chain, saving previous node pointer for unlink operation\n10. If found in either table: unlink from chain and deallocate via FUN_6fb62360\n11. Call FUN_6fb61770 again to recheck references - return if any remain\n12. Call FUN_6fb62360(pUnit) to deallocate the input unit\n13. Return NULL on success (unit removed and freed)\n\nParameters:\nparam_1 (pUnit): Pointer to unit structure to remove - contains type at offset 0, id at offset 8, flags at offset 0x3a\n\nReturns:\npUnit if unit has pending references or validation error, NULL if successfully removed and freed\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Unit marked as reference (0x200000 flag) uses different hash table\n- Hash collision handling via linked list traversal at same index\n- Double-check validation: unit type/id must match in all lookups\n- Fatal assertion if unit found in two tables or in wrong table\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x7F: Hash index mask for lower 7 bits of unit id (128-entry hash per type)\n0x80: Hash table stride (unit types * 0x80 = offset for unit type)\n0x200000: Flag indicating unit in reference list vs main hash table\n0x42: Offset to next pointer in hash chain (chain links at +0x42)\n0x3a: Offset to unit flags (contains 0x200000 flag)",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Unit", "SRC_CUnit.cpp", "MOD_UNIT", "PARAM_1", "PROP_LOOPHEAVY"]
