      "api_calls": ["QueueLogMessage", "FogAssert", "FogAssert", "QueueLogMessage", "QueueLogMessage", "FogAssert", "FogAssert", "FogAssert"],
      "instructions": ["0x91770|PUSH|EBX", "0x91771|PUSH|EBP", "0x91772|PUSH|ESI", "0x91773|PUSH|EDI", "0x91774|MOV|EDI, ECX", "0x91776|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [EDI + 0xe8]", "0x9177C|MOV|EBX, dword ptr [EDI]", "0x9177E|MOV|EBP, dword ptr [EDI + 0x8]", "0x91781|AND|EAX, 0x200000", "0x91786|CMP|EAX, 0x200000", "0x9178B|JNZ|0x6fb61836", "0x91791|MOV|ECX, EBP", "0x91793|MOV|EDX, EBX", "0x91795|AND|ECX, 0x7f", "0x91798|SHL|EDX, 0x7"],
      "comment": "Insert unit into unit hash table or linked list with validation and collision handling.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract unit ID (field [0]) and unit table ID (field [8]) from pUnit\n2. Check if unit has 0x200000 flag set - determines hash table type (link list vs hash)\n3. If link list mode: validate unit not already in list by scanning list\n   a. Calculate table index: (unitTable & 0x7f) + (unitId * 0x80)\n   b. Scan linked list using next pointer at offset 0x42\n   c. For each node: verify unit table ID matches (field [8])\n   d. If found: verify unit ID matches (field [0]), return 0 if duplicate\n   e. Log mismatch errors via Ordinal_10029 (D2Common.DebugMsg)\n4. If unit not found in validation: call FUN_6fb619b0 to search again, error if found\n5. If hash table mode: similar validation against g_ppUnitHashTable\n6. Scan hash table again with same logic to verify unit location\n7. Call FUN_6fb897a0(pUnit, 1) to update unit flags/state\n8. Recalculate table pointer based on flag\n9. Determine insertion point by scanning table at dwTableIdx\n   a. Find position where unit's field [8] is less than current node's field [8]\n   b. Track previous node in dwTableIdx variable\n10. If previous node exists: link pUnit after it (set previous->offset_0x108 = pUnit)\n11. If no previous node: insert at table head (ppTable[dwTableIdx] = pUnit)\n12. Set pUnit->offset_0x42 to next node pointer (for linked list traversal)\n13. Return 1 for success\n\nParameters:\npUnit (UnitAny * in ECX) - Pointer to unit structure containing ID, table ID, and linked list pointers\n\nReturns:\n0 - Unit duplicate detected or insertion validation failed\n1 - Unit successfully inserted into hash/link table\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Magic number 0x200000: Controls hash table vs linked list mode selection\n- Magic number 0x7f: Hash table size mask (128 slots per ID range)\n- Magic number 0x80: Hash table row stride (128 rows per unit ID)\n- Offset 0x108: Next pointer in hash/link table chain\n- Offset 0x42: Alternative linked list next pointer\n- Offset 0xe8: Flags field (0x200000 = link list mode)\n- Offset 0x8: Unit table ID field\n- Offset 0x0: Unit ID field\n- Error codes: Ordinal_10023 (D2Common.AssertMsg - fatal), Ordinal_10029 (D2Common.DebugMsg), FUN_6fb9a10f (exit)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x200000 - Flag enabling linked list mode (field at offset 0xe8)\n0x7f - Hash table slot mask (selects 7 LSBs for table offset)\n0x80 - Hash table row multiplier (128 rows per unit ID)\n0x108 - Offset of primary linked list next pointer\n0x42 - Offset of secondary linked list next pointer\n0x8 - Offset of unit table ID field in unit structure\n0xe8 - Offset of unit flags field\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset | Size | Field Name | Type | Description\n0x0    | 4    | dwUnitId   | uint | Unit identifier (0-indexed)\n0x8    | 4    | dwTableId  | uint | Unit table ID (controls hash slot)\n0x42   | 4    | pNextLink  | UnitAny * | Next unit in linked list chain\n0xe8   | 4    | dwFlags    | uint | Flags field (bit 0x200000 = link list mode)\n0x108  | 4    | pNextHash  | UnitAny * | Next unit in hash table chain\n\nNote: Function uses 3 stack-allocated temporaries optimized away by compiler (pUVar3, puVar2, pvVar1)",
