      "instructions": ["0x919B0|PUSH|EBX", "0x919B1|PUSH|ESI", "0x919B2|MOV|ESI, dword ptr [ECX + EDX*0x4]", "0x919B5|PUSH|EDI", "0x919B6|TEST|ESI, ESI", "0x919B8|JZ|0x6fb619ec", "0x919BA|MOV|EDI, dword ptr [ESP + 0x14]", "0x919BE|MOV|EBX, dword ptr [ESP + 0x10]", "0x919C2|CMP|dword ptr [ESI + 0x8], EBX", "0x919C5|JNZ|0x6fb619e2", "0x919C7|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [ESI]", "0x919C9|CMP|EAX, EDI", "0x919CB|JZ|0x6fb61a0f", "0x919CD|PUSH|EDI", "0x919CE|PUSH|EAX"],
      "comment": "Find unit in linked list by type id and unit id.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load unit list head from array indexed by dwTypeIndex at pTypeList base (offset: pTypeList[dwTypeIndex])\n2. Loop through linked list of units (offset 0x108 = next pointer):\n   a. If pUnit is NULL, return NULL (list end reached)\n   b. Load unit type from pUnit[2] (offset 0x8), compare with dwTypeId\n   c. If types match: load unit id from pUnit[0], compare with dwUnitId\n   d. If unit id matches, return pUnit (found)\n   e. If unit id mismatch: call Ordinal_10029 for validation, recheck pUnit[0]\n   f. If still mismatched after validation, log error with Ordinal_10023 and abort\n   g. Move to next unit: pUnit = pUnit[0x108], repeat\n3. If type doesn't match (pUnit[2] != dwTypeId), skip to next unit without id check\n\nParameters:\npTypeList (UnitAny *) - Base pointer of unit type list array\ndwTypeIndex (uint) - Array index to load unit head: pTypeList[dwTypeIndex]\ndwTypeId (uint) - Unit type identifier to match (field offset 0x8)\ndwUnitId (uint) - Unit identifier to match (field offset 0x0)\n\nReturns:\nUnitAny * - Pointer to unit matching both dwTypeId and dwUnitId, or NULL if not found or error\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If unit found but Ordinal_10029 validation fails, Ordinal_10023 logs error and function aborts\n- Offset 0x8 contains type field, offset 0x0 contains unit id field\n- Offset 0x108 is linked list next pointer (constant for all units in list)\n- Calling function guarantees valid pTypeList base and dwTypeIndex range\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset | Size | Field Name | Type     | Description\n0x00   | 4    | dwUnitId   | uint     | Unit identifier (primary key)\n0x04   | 4    | field_4    | uint     | Unknown field\n0x08   | 4    | dwTypeId   | uint     | Unit type identifier\n0x108  | 4    | pNext      | UnitAny* | Pointer to next unit in linked list\n\nRelated Functions:\n- Ordinal_10029 (D2Common) - Validates unit type with assertion logic\n- Ordinal_10023 - Logs assertion failure with file/line info\n- FUN_6fb9a10f - Abort handler (called on validation failure)",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Unit", "STRUCT_Act", "SRC_CUnit.cpp", "STRUCT_Inventory", "MOD_UNIT", "PARAM_4", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "RET_STRUCT_PTR", "STRUCT_Control", "RET_Unit"]
