      "comment": "Allocates memory, initializes a unit structure, and performs type-specific setup.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate 0x212 (530) bytes via Ordinal_10042 (D2Common.MemAlloc)\n2. Clear allocated memory by writing 0x46 (70) dwords using REP STOSD\n3. Call InitializeUnit with allocated block and parameters\n4. If InitializeUnit succeeds (non-NULL), call Ordinal_10422 (D2Common.SetUnitState) with param_5\n5. Return initialized unit pointer\n\nParameters:\nparam_1 (dwType, ECX) - Unit type: 0=Player, 1=Monster, 2=Object, 3=Missile, 4=Object, 5=Special\nparam_2 (dwX, EDX) - X coordinate for unit placement\nparam_3 (nRoomNum, Stack) - Room number (0 for no room)\nparam_4 (dwRadius, Stack) - Radius/size parameter (0 for default)\nparam_5 (dwParam8, Stack) - Type-specific parameter 8 (passed to Ordinal_10422)\n\nReturns:\nPointer to initialized unit structure, or NULL if InitializeUnit fails\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset | Size | Field Name     | Type   | Description\n0x0    | 4    | dwType         | uint   | Unit type enumeration\n0x4    | 4    | dwX            | uint   | X coordinate\n0x8    | 4    | dwY            | uint   | Y coordinate\n0x1EC  | 4    | dwFlags        | uint   | State flags\n0x280  | varies | Additional   | varies | Type-specific data\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x212 - Memory allocation size in bytes (530 bytes)\n0x46 - Number of dwords to clear (70 dwords = 280 bytes)\n\nRelated Functions:\n- InitializeUnit() - Base unit initialization with properties\n- Ordinal_10042 (D2Common.MemAlloc) - Memory allocation\n- Ordinal_10422 (D2Common.SetUnitState) - Post-init type-specific setup",
