      "instructions": ["0x91A80|PUSH|EBX", "0x91A81|PUSH|EBP", "0x91A82|PUSH|ESI", "0x91A83|PUSH|EDI", "0x91A84|MOV|EBX, EDX", "0x91A86|MOV|EBP, ECX", "0x91A88|PUSH|0x0", "0x91A8A|PUSH|0x220", "0x91A8F|MOV|EDX, 0x6fbc9edc", "0x91A94|MOV|ECX, 0x118", "0x91A99|CALL|0x6fb99a98", "0x91A9E|MOV|ESI, EAX", "0x91AA0|MOV|ECX, 0x46", "0x91AA5|MOV|EDX, dword ptr [ESP + 0x1c]", "0x91AA9|XOR|EAX, EAX"],
      "comment": "Allocates memory and initializes a game unit structure with specified properties.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate 0x220 bytes (544 bytes) for unit structure via Ordinal_10042\n2. Zero-initialize entire allocated memory block (0x46 * 4 = 278 dwords)\n3. Call InitializeUnit with allocated memory and all parameters to populate unit fields\n4. If initialization succeeds (returns non-null):\n   a. Write visibility mode byte to unit field at offset 0x70 + 0x4\n   b. Call Ordinal_10393 to apply additional initialization\n   c. If Ordinal_10393 returns non-zero, call FUN_6fb7edd0 for post-processing\n5. Return initialized unit pointer or NULL if initialization failed\n\nParameters:\n  dwUnitType (ECX, uint) - Unit type identifier (class, monster type, etc.)\n  dwUnitSubType (EDX, uint) - Unit subtype specifier\n  nUnitX (Stack+4, int) - X coordinate for unit placement\n  dwInventorySlots (Stack+8, uint) - Number of inventory slots to allocate\n  dwStatCount (Stack+C, uint) - Number of unit stats to track\n  nClassType (Stack+10, int) - Character/unit class identifier\n  dwSpecialFlags (Stack+14, uint) - Special flags for unit behavior/attributes\n  byVisibilityMode (Stack+18, byte) - Visibility mode (HIDDEN, VISIBLE, etc.)\n\nReturns:\n  uint * - Pointer to initialized unit structure (544 bytes), NULL if initialization failed\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If InitializeUnit fails, returns NULL without further processing\n  - Visibility mode is only applied if InitializeUnit succeeds\n  - Post-processing (FUN_6fb7edd0) only runs if Ordinal_10393 returns non-zero\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x220 - Unit structure size (544 bytes)\n  0x46 - Number of dwords to zero-initialize (278 dwords = 1112 bytes, covers structure)\n  0x70 - Base offset in unit structure for visibility field\n  0x4 - Offset within visibility block to write mode byte\n\nRelated Functions:\n  - InitializeUnit() - Populates unit structure fields and AI data\n  - Ordinal_10042() - Memory allocator (Storm.dll)",
