      "comment": "Initialize a game unit/actor with properties and spawn it into the game world.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Search for existing unit by ID in hash table (g_pUnitHashTable)\n   - If found and not claimed (eType != 1), error\n   - If already exists and eType == 1, claim and return\n2. Allocate new SearchableListNode structure (size 0x28f = 655 bytes)\n3. Initialize all 70 fields to 0 (STOSD.REP)\n4. Set initialization flags: if nInitFlags != 0, set unit flag 0x600000\n5. Copy unit properties from pUnit: ID, class, X/Y position\n6. Find spawn room coordinates via FindRoomForUnit()\n7. Set animation frame for class (via FUN_6fb795f0 + FUN_6fb796c0)\n8. Copy initial attribute values (param_4 = wAttributeType) if provided\n9. Copy initial skill data (9 bytes from pbAttributeData) if provided\n10. Copy equipment/item data (16 bytes from pbInitialData) if provided\n11. Place unit in world (FUN_6fb798a0)\n12. Process unit-type-specific initialization (switch on unit eType):\n    - 0xf2, 0x14d: Call FUN_6fb931f0 with animation parameters\n    - 0x154, 0x155, 0x156: Call FUN_6fb97b10 with directional offsets\n    - 0x157, 0x15f-0x161: Call FUN_6fb97b10 with movement values\n    - 0x196: Initialize movement/animation (FUN_6fb979a0, FUN_6fb97b10, FUN_6fb97b40, FUN_6fb97be0, FUN_6fb98000)\n    - 0x1a1, 0x1a2, 0x21f: Call FUN_6fb931f0 with animation parameters\n    - 0x209: Call InitializeGameFeatureWithVersionCheck\n13. Calculate animation frame count via Ordinal_10592\n14. Set unit visual parameters via GetVideoFrameCount (returns 0/1/2 for animation modes)\n15. Register unit with hash table\n16. Remove unit from old room (if applicable) and update room data\n17. Return pointer to initialized SearchableListNode\n\nParameters:\n  pUnit (ECX) - dword*: Pointer to unit template with ID, class, position, properties\n  pbInitialData (EDX) - byte*: Pointer to initial skill/equipment data (9 bytes)\n  pbAttributeData - byte*: Pointer to attribute data (16 bytes)\n  wAttributeType - ushort: Attribute type/class identifier\n  nInitFlags - int: Initialization flags (0x600000 if non-zero)\n\nReturns:\n  eax (dword*): Pointer to initialized SearchableListNode if successful, or NULL on error\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If unit already exists in hash table and eType == 1, function short-circuits and returns immediately\n  - Type-specific initialization depends on unit eType value (6 major type switches)\n  - Local stack temporaries (local_20 to local_30) are optimized away during compilation\n  - XMM register spills possible for struct initialization (STOSD.REP operation)\n\nNote: Function uses 5 stack-allocated temporaries optimized away.",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "MOD_UNIT", "STRUCT_Room2", "STRUCT_Room1", "STRUCT_ItemData", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData", "STRUCT_Unit", "STRUCT_StatList", "PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Path", "SRC_CUnit.cpp", "STRUCT_Skill", "PARAM_5", "PROP_LOOPHEAVY"]
