      "comment": "Allocate and initialize a game unit object with given parameters.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Increment global unit counter g_dwUnitCounter, wrapping from 0xffffffff to 0\n2. Check if dwParamMode equals 1 (stack initialization mode)\n3a. If mode is 1: Initialize local buffer adwUnitData with zeros, set mode flag to 1\n3b. Call FUN_6fb61b00 with stack buffer data and return\n4a. If mode is not 1: Call Ordinal_10042(0x331, 0) to allocate 0x118 bytes for unit\n4b. Zero-initialize all dwords in allocated structure  \n5. Set unit flag field [offset 0x3a] with OR operation: flag |= 0x600000\n6. Call InitializeUnit with allocated unit and all parameters to complete setup\n7. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\n- dwUnitType (ECX): Unit type identifier passed to InitializeUnit\n- nParam2 (EDX): Secondary parameter passed to InitializeUnit\n- dwParam3 (stack): Configuration parameter passed to InitializeUnit  \n- dwParamMode (stack): Mode selector (1=stack init, other=allocate+init)\n- nParam5 (stack): Fifth parameter passed to InitializeUnit\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Function returns no value, side effect is initialized unit\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Stack mode (dwParamMode==1) uses local buffer instead of allocation\n- Unit counter wraps at 0xffffffff, not sign-extended\n- 0x600000 flags applied only to allocated units, not stack mode",
