      "comment": "Validates and applies unit stat modifications on state transition.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Verify unit flag == 0x1 - Unit must be active\n2. Verify bNewState != bOldState - State must actually change\n3. Call Ordinal_10342 (GetUnitStat) to retrieve current stat value\n4. If stat valid (non-zero):\n   a. If bOldState == 0x0: Call Ordinal_10100 (RemoveStat) - Remove stat\n   b. Else if bNewState == 0x0: Call Ordinal_10101 (ResetStat) - Reset stat\n5. Call Ordinal_10214 (CommitStateChange) to finalize modification\n6. Return void\n\nParameters:\n- pUnit: int * (IMPLICIT ECX) - Pointer to unit structure\n- bNewState: byte (IMPLICIT DL) - New state byte value\n- bOldState: byte (Stack[0x4]) - Previous state byte value\n\nReturns:\n- void (no return value, state applied via ordinal functions)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Early exit if unit flag != 0x1\n- Early exit if bNewState == bOldState (no change needed)\n- Early exit if Ordinal_10342 returns zero (no stat found)\n- Ordinal_10100 and Ordinal_10101 only called if stat exists\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x1: Unit active flag value\n- 0x0: Null state indicator",
      "tags": ["PARAM_3"]
