      "instructions": ["0x92300|SUB|ESP, 0x20", "0x92303|PUSH|ESI", "0x92304|PUSH|EDI", "0x92305|MOV|EDI, ECX", "0x92307|PUSH|EDI", "0x92308|CALL|0x6fb98c7a", "0x9230D|MOV|ESI, EAX", "0x9230F|TEST|ESI, ESI", "0x92311|JZ|0x6fb6234b", "0x92313|TEST|byte ptr [ESI + 0x14], 0x1", "0x92317|JZ|0x6fb62344", "0x92319|LEA|EAX, [ESP + 0x8]", "0x9231D|PUSH|EAX", "0x9231E|PUSH|EDI", "0x9231F|CALL|0x6fb9812e"],
      "comment": "Allocate and initialize copies of units from a template list\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call Ordinal_10055(dwUnitType) to get first template unit in linked list\n2. Loop through linked list (iterating via puVar1[7] offset to next node)\n3. For each template with flag bit 0x1 set at offset +0x14:\n   a. Call Ordinal_10034(dwUnitType, &nOffsetX) to get position offset\n   b. Load template coordinates: x=puVar1[3], y=puVar1[4]\n   c. Add offsets: finalX = x + nOffsetX, finalY = y + nOffsetY\n   d. Call AllocateAndInitializeUnit(puVar1[1], finalX, finalY, *puVar1, puVar1[2])\n4. Continue to next template via puVar1[7] until NULL\n\nParameters:\ndwUnitType (IMPLICIT ECX) - Game unit type identifier for template lookup\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Units allocated as side effect\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Only processes templates with flag 0x1 set (initialization flag)\n- Coordinates stored on stack at ESP+8 (nOffsetX) and ESP+12 (nOffsetY)\n- Uses fastcall: dwUnitType passed in ECX register\n- nOffsetY calculated from nOffsetX via stack frame (derived value)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x1 - Flag bit indicating unit should be allocated/initialized\n0x4 - Offset multiplier for structure field access (dword field spacing)\n0x7 - Linked list node pointer offset (next node at +0x1c = [7]*4)",
