      "comment": "Cleans up all units in both hash and link-list tables by iterating through all game groups and slots\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Loop through each game group (from g_nUnitTableStartIndex to 0x6fba9ad8)\n2. For each group, iterate through all 0x80 (128) unit hash table slots\n3. For each non-empty slot, walk the unit chain and cleanup each unit via CleanupGameContextAndResources\n4. Advance to next slot in unit chain via unit[0x42] (next pointer)\n5. Repeat steps 1-4 for link-list table (0x6fbfe6a0)\n\nParameters: none\n\nReturns: void\n\nVariables:\n- pUnitNext (pdVar1): Pointer to next unit in chain, loaded from pUnitCurrent[0x42]\n- pUnitCurrent (pdVar2): Current unit being processed from hash/link-list table\n- Note: SSA temporaries (piVar3, iVar4) optimized away in decompiler but visible in assembly\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x80 (128): Number of hash table slots per group\n- 0x7: Left shift to compute group offset (128 = 2^7)\n- 0x42 (66): Offset to next pointer in unit structure\n- 0x108 (264): Offset to next pointer alternate (used in loop)\n- 0x6fbfdaa0: Base address of unit hash table\n- 0x6fbfe6a0: Base address of link-list table\n- 0x6fba9ac0: Start index for table iteration\n- 0x6fba9ad8: End boundary for table iteration\n\nRelated Functions:\n- CleanupGameContextAndResources() - Cleans individual unit resources",
