      "comment": "Deactivates all units across all hash tables and clears linked unit references.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Iterate player, unit type, item, monster, ghost, unit, and missile hash tables\n2. For each unit in table, extract next node pointer (offset 0x108), unit type (offset 0x8), unit ID (offset 0x0)\n3. Call FUN_6fb85e00 to deactivate the unit\n4. For unit type, item, and monster tables only: lookup linked unit via FindLinkListNodeByIdAndIndex\n5. If linked unit found (non-null), check state field (offset 0x0): 1=call FUN_6fb782f0, 2=call FUN_6fb7f9b0\n6. After all iterations, call FUN_6fb627f0 on ghost and item tables with step 0x6fb62820\n7. Call FUN_6fb627f0 on ghost, item, and unit type tables with step 0x6fb62830\n8. If server mode (g_dwServerPort != 0), call FUN_6fb627f0 on unit type and unit tables with step 0x6fb64150\n\nParameters:\n(none)\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Units contain linked list pointers at offset 0x108 for traversal\n- State-dependent cleanup: state 1 uses FUN_6fb782f0, state 2 uses FUN_6fb7f9b0\n- Server mode flag g_dwServerPort determines if additional cleanup passes required\n- Hash tables are pointer arrays with fixed bounds\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x108 - Next node pointer offset (dword offset 0x42)\n0x8 - Unit type ID field offset\n0x0 - Unit ID field offset and state field offset",
