      "comment": "Iterate through hash table buckets and invoke callback for each linked list node.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize bucket count to 128 (0x80) to iterate all buckets\n2. Load first node pointer from current bucket array entry\n3. Walk linked list by following offset 0x108 (next pointer)\n4. Invoke callback for each non-NULL node\n5. Move to next bucket array entry and repeat until all 128 buckets processed\n\nParameters:\n  ppBucketArray - Pointer to array of bucket heads (each entry is pointer to first node)\n  pfnCallback - Function pointer invoked for each node in all 128 buckets\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value, operates for side effects\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Empty buckets (NULL head) skip inner loop and continue to next bucket\n  - 128 is hardcoded bucket count - matches hashtable size constraint\n  - Callback invocation at EDX register - assumes __fastcall or register parameter passing",
