      "comment": "Validate that a unit pointer is valid and trigger fatal error if null.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. TEST ECX (pUnit parameter) for zero/NULL\n2. If pUnit is NULL (param_1 == 0):\n   - Call Ordinal_10023 with error context (file path, line 0x503)\n   - Call FUN_6fb9a10f(-1) to trigger fatal shutdown\n3. If pUnit is valid:\n   - Load field at offset 0x64 (100 bytes)\n   - JMP to FUN_6fb935f0 for further processing (tail call optimization)\n\nParameters:\nIMPLICIT pUnit (ECX register): Pointer to unit data structure being validated\ndwUnknown (EDX register): Additional parameter passed to FUN_6fb935f0\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Function does not return normally (exits via Ordinal_10023 or fatal error)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If pUnit is NULL, execution terminates (Ordinal_10023 does not return)\n- Field at pUnit+0x64 is loaded as dword and used by FUN_6fb935f0\n- Called by ProcessPlayerSkillCooldowns and ProcessPvPPlayerInteractions\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x64: Offset 100 bytes - Field access within unit structure\n0x503: Line number passed to Ordinal_10023 error handler\n0xFFFFFFFF: Magic value (-1) for fatal shutdown",
