      "comment": "Validate pointer parameter and retrieve field value from offset 0x64\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if input pointer is NULL (param_1 == 0)\n2. If NULL, trigger assertion failure via Ordinal_10023 (assertion handler)\n3. If NULL, abort execution via FUN_6fb9a10f(0xFFFFFFFF) - never returns\n4. If valid, dereference pointer and read 4-byte value at offset +0x64\n5. Tail call to FUN_6fb93620 with the retrieved field value\n\nParameters:\nparam_1 - Pointer to data structure (ECX register implicit parameter, __fastcall)\n          Must not be NULL (validated via assertion)\n\nReturns:\nint - Field value from [param_1 + 0x64] (passed to FUN_6fb93620 as tail call)\n      Never returns on NULL input (assertion failure termination)\n\nSpecial Cases:\nNULL pointer input triggers assertion failure with context\nFunction uses __fastcall convention (parameter in ECX register)\nTail call optimization: jump to FUN_6fb93620 preserves stack\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x64 (100) - Field offset in data structure\n0xFFFFFFFF (-1) - Failure code for abort routine\nNULL - Invalid pointer sentinel value for assertion",
