      "comment": "Validates unit pointer and processes transform data field.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Test if pUnit is NULL (ECX register == 0)\n2. If NULL: Call Ordinal_10023 with assertion details (file, line, message)\n3. After assertion call, invoke FUN_6fb9a10f with error code -1 (terminator)\n4. If valid: Load field at offset 0x64 from unit structure\n5. Pass loaded field value to FUN_6fb93680 for transform processing\n\nParameters:\npUnit (UnitAny *) - IMPLICIT: Passed in ECX register (__fastcall convention)\n  Unit structure pointer, NULL check enforced before field access\n  Assertion terminates execution if NULL\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value, either processes transform or triggers assertion+termination\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- NULL pointer triggers assertion error path with program termination\n- Ordinal_10023 appears to be assertion handler from Fog.dll/Storm.dll\n- Uses __fastcall calling convention: parameter in ECX, callee cleanup\n- Offset 0x64 (100 decimal) accesses specific unit structure field\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x51e - Assertion line number (1310 decimal)\n0x64 - Offset 100 bytes, unit field offset for field access\n0xffffffff - Error code -1 passed to FUN_6fb9a10f terminator",
      "tags": ["SRC_CUnit.cpp", "MOD_UNIT", "PARAM_1", "PROP_SMALL"]
