      "instructions": ["0x92980|SUB|ESP, 0x8", "0x92983|PUSH|EBX", "0x92984|PUSH|ESI", "0x92985|PUSH|EDI", "0x92986|MOV|EDI, ECX", "0x92988|MOV|EBX, EDX", "0x9298A|CMP|dword ptr [EDI], 0x5", "0x9298D|JZ|0x6fb629ad", "0x9298F|PUSH|0x52b", "0x92994|PUSH|0x6fbc9edc", "0x92999|PUSH|0x6fbca074", "0x9299E|CALL|0x6fb99a7a", "0x929A3|ADD|ESP, 0xc", "0x929A6|PUSH|-0x1", "0x929A8|CALL|0x6fb9a10f"],
      "comment": "Validates unit type and checks if coordinates fall within unit bounding box.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Assert unit type is UNIT_PLAYER (value 5) - fatal if not\n2. Get unit stat value via Ordinal_10342 (GetUnitMode)\n3. Get unit render mode via Ordinal_10028 (GetUnitRenderMode)\n4. If render mode exists:\n   - Get viewport offset X via Ordinal_10326\n   - Get viewport offset Y via Ordinal_10329\n   - Normalize offsets via Ordinal_10111\n   - Calculate box bounds: left = [iVar2+4] + nOffsetX, top = [iVar2+8] + nOffsetY\n   - Test all four edges: X>=left, Y>=top, X<=[iVar2+C]+left, Y<=[iVar2+10]+top\n5. Return 1 if all tests pass, 0 otherwise\n\nParameters:\n  pUnit (UnitAny *) - Unit structure pointer, must have type field = 5\n  nX (int) - X coordinate to validate against bounds\n  nY (int) - Y coordinate to validate against bounds\n\nReturns:\n  1 - Coordinates within unit bounding box\n  0 - Unit lacks render mode or coordinates outside bounds",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Unit", "SRC_CUnit.cpp", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PARAM_3", "MOD_UNIT", "STRUCT_Control", "UNIT_ROOMTILE"]
