      "comment": "Validates resource flags by checking type and permission bit.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get current validated resource handle\n2. If handle valid AND resource type equals 2:\n   a. Get data at [handle + 4] offset\n   b. Call Ordinal_10626 to process data\n   c. Check if flag 0x80 at offset 0x177 is SET\n   d. Return false if flag is set (validation fails)\n3. Get another validated resource handle\n4. Return true if handle matches input parameter, false otherwise\n\nParameters:\npnResourceHandle - Resource handle pointer to validate\n\nReturns:\ntrue (1) - Resource validated and flags check passed\nfalse (0) - Resource type not 2 OR flag 0x80 set OR handles don't match\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Returns false immediately if initial resource handle null or type != 2\n- Flag 0x80 set indicates restricted/disabled resource state",
