      "instructions": ["0x92B10|SUB|ESP, 0x44", "0x92B13|PUSH|EBX", "0x92B14|PUSH|EBP", "0x92B15|PUSH|ESI", "0x92B16|PUSH|EDI", "0x92B17|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x10], EDX", "0x92B1B|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0x92B1D|CALL|0x6fb8f680", "0x92B22|MOV|EDI, EAX", "0x92B24|CALL|0x6fae4fd0", "0x92B29|DEC|EAX", "0x92B2A|JZ|0x6fb62b58", "0x92B2C|DEC|EAX", "0x92B2D|JZ|0x6fb62b3e", "0x92B2F|DEC|EAX"],
      "comment": "Validates if a click at screen coordinates is valid for the given unit.\nChecks scroll window mode, unit flags, equipment validity, and collision bounds.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get scroll window mode (1=left panel, 2=right panel, 3=full screen)\n2. Validate click X coordinate within allowed screen region\n3. Load unit from param_1, check if unit has 0x200000 flag set (invalid click area)\n4. Call validation functions: FUN_6fb63e80, FUN_6fb64010, FUN_6fb640a0\n5. If unit type == 1: Check against equipment equipment table (DAT_6fbc9ec0 items), call callback\n6. Check unit byte[0x3a] & 0x2 flag (primary validation)\n7. Check unit byte[0x3b] & 0x80 flag (essential validation)\n8. If nFlags == 0, return 1 (early success)\n9. Copy unit state: dwUnitState, nObjectBase, nUnitType via Ordinal_11013\n10. Switch on nUnitType: 0=ground, 1=monster, 2=object, 4=waypoint, 5=player\n11. For type 1 (monster): Get stats, check bounds with PtInRect, call collision function\n12. For type 2 (object): Get object data, validate visibility, check bounds\n13. For other types: Call GetScrollWindowMode, iterate collision frames 0-15\n14. Return 1 if valid, 0 if invalid\n\nParameters:\n  param_1 (int *): Pointer to unit structure [ECX]\n  param_2 (int): Click screen X coordinate [EDX]\n  param_3 (int): Click screen Y coordinate [Stack+0x4]\n  param_4 (int): Flags - 0 means early return with 1 [Stack+0x8]\n\nReturns:\n  1 if click is valid for the unit, 0 if invalid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Type 1 (monster) uses PtInRect for collision detection\n  - Type 2 (object) validates opacity and click bounds\n  - Type 4 (waypoint) returns 0 if dialog 0xd exists\n  - Type 5 (player) delegates to IsCoordinatesWithinUnitBounds()\n  - Early returns when unit is NULL (assertion crash)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x200000 - Unit flag indicating invalid click area\n  0x02 - Unit status flag (primary validation)\n  0x80 - Unit essential flag (must be set)\n  0x10000 - Unit equipment flag\n  0x0c - Equipment type waypoint marker\n  DAT_6fbc9ec0 - Equipment count for type 1 units\n  0x346, 0x34c, 0x348 - Monster stat offsets (display info)\n  0x14a, 0x1ad - Object visibility flags\n  0x1b0-0x1bc - Object bounds (left, top, right, bottom offsets)\n  0x1dd - Monster palette index for transparency check\n  0x171 - Object palette type\n  0xf - Maximum collision frame count",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "MOD_UNIT", "STRUCT_Room2", "STRUCT_ItemData", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData", "STRUCT_Unit", "STRUCT_StatList", "PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Path", "SRC_CUnit.cpp", "STRUCT_ObjectData", "STRUCT_Skill", "PARAM_4", "STRUCT_Other", "PROP_LOOPHEAVY"]
