      "api_calls": ["UNITS_GetUnitDirection", "LoadOrRetrieveCelFrameData", "FogAssert", "GetCelFileInfoHeight", "GetUnitLevel", "GetCelFileTableIndex", "GetDWordFromPointerField", "GetUnitX", "GetCelModeValue"],
      "instructions": ["0x930D0|SUB|ESP, 0x4c", "0x930D3|PUSH|EBX", "0x930D4|PUSH|ESI", "0x930D5|MOV|ESI, dword ptr [ESP + 0x58]", "0x930D9|PUSH|EDI", "0x930DA|MOV|EBX, ECX", "0x930DC|MOV|EDX, ESI", "0x930DE|CALL|0x6fb95ca0", "0x930E3|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0x930E5|JZ|0x6fb63248", "0x930EB|MOV|ECX, 0x12", "0x930F0|XOR|EAX, EAX", "0x930F2|LEA|EDI, [ESP + 0x10]", "0x930F6|PUSH|-0x1", "0x930F8|STOSD.REP|ES:EDI"],
      "comment": "Calculate display bounds for an animated cell context in screen coordinates.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate cell animation frame exists via FUN_6fb95ca0\n2. Initialize local_48 array (cell context buffer) to zero\n3. Retrieve animation data for cell via FUN_6fb968e0 with cell X coordinate and animation frame\n4. Retrieve cell animation frame reference via Ordinal_10055\n5. Validate cell frame pointer is non-null\n6. Verify cell width (local_34) does not exceed requested X coordinate, else error halt\n7. Calculate left bound: Ordinal_10039(frame) - 0xc + Ordinal_10333(this)\n8. Calculate right bound: Ordinal_10037(frame) + 0x18 + left_bound\n9. Calculate top bound: Ordinal_10334(this) + 0xc + Ordinal_10040(frame)\n10. Calculate bottom bound: top_bound - Ordinal_10038(frame) - 0x18\n11. Adjust horizontal bounds if width < 0x20 pixels (center the content)\n12. Adjust vertical bounds if height < 0x20 pixels (center the content)\n13. Add viewport offsets: FUN_6fb97a30 (X offset), FUN_6fb97a50/FUN_6fb97a70 (Y offsets)\n14. Return success (1) if all validations pass, failure (0) otherwise\n\nParameters:\n  pThis: Pointer to object containing cell animation context (IMPLICIT in ECX)\n  nAnimFrame: Animation frame index to look up\n  dwCellX: Cell X coordinate for validation and animation lookup\n  pBounds: Output pointer to bounds array [left, top, right, bottom]\n\nReturns:\n  1 if bounds successfully calculated and validated\n  0 if animation frame invalid, cell context lookup fails, or coordinate validation fails\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If cell width exceeds dwCellX, function halts with error call to FUN_6fb9a10f\n  - Minimum bound dimensions enforced to 0x20 pixels (32 pixels) with centering adjustment\n  - Viewport offsets applied uniformly to both axes for final screen coordinates",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Act", "SRC_CUnit.cpp", "STRUCT_Inventory", "MOD_UNIT", "STRUCT_Skill", "PARAM_5", "STRUCT_Room2", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
