      "instructions": ["0x93260|PUSH|EBX", "0x93261|MOV|EBX, dword ptr [ESP + 0x8]", "0x93265|PUSH|EBP", "0x93266|PUSH|ESI", "0x93267|PUSH|EDI", "0x93268|MOV|EDI, EDX", "0x9326A|MOV|EBP, ECX", "0x9326C|MOV|EAX, EDI", "0x9326E|MOV|ECX, EBX", "0x93270|SHL|EAX, 0x7", "0x93273|AND|ECX, 0x7f", "0x93276|ADD|EAX, ECX", "0x93278|MOV|ESI, dword ptr [EAX*0x4 + 0x6fbfdaa0]", "0x9327F|TEST|ESI, ESI", "0x93281|JZ|0x6fb632ad"],
      "comment": "Search unit hash table for unit matching ID and type, validate consistency, invoke callback.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Compute hash bucket from unit type and ID: bucket = ((dwUnitId << 7) | (nUnitType & 0x7f))\n2. Load hash chain head from g_ppUnitHashTable[bucket]\n3. Loop through linked list (chain via offset 0x108):\n   a. Check if unit ID [offset 0x8] matches dwUnitId\n   b. If match found, verify unit type [offset 0x0]:\n      - If matches nUnitType, jump to callback (success path)\n      - If mismatch, log validation error via Ordinal_10029, call abort via FUN_6fb9a10f\n   c. Load next unit pointer from [offset 0x108]\n4. If no match found in chain, set pCurrentUnit = NULL\n5. Invoke callback Ordinal_10344(dwCallbackParam, pCurrentUnit)\n\nParameters:\n- dwCallbackParam: Context parameter passed to callback handler (Ordinal_10344)\n- nUnitType: Unit type to match (0=player, 1=monster, etc) [EBP]\n- dwUnitId: Unit ID to search for [EDX]\n\nReturns:\n- void; callback receives unit pointer or NULL\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Type mismatch during iteration triggers assertion and terminates process\n- Empty hash chain results in NULL callback\n- Hash table uses 128 buckets per type (0x80 entries)",
