      "comment": "Validate unit pointer and process associated global data\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call FUN_6fb85820 to prepare unit state\n2. Check if unit field at offset 0x38 is NULL; if so, error log with halt via Ordinal_10023 and FUN_6fb9a10f(-1)\n3. Get valid unit handle via Ordinal_10180(unit[0x38])\n4. If valid handle exists and differs from input unit pointer:\n   a. Fetch unit field from offset 0x38 again\n   b. If NULL, error log with halt (same as step 2)\n   c. Retrieve unit data via Ordinal_10329 and Ordinal_10326\n   d. Process unit via Ordinal_10216 with size and type data and dwParam2\n5. Return void\n\nParameters:\n- pUnitAny (dword): Pointer to unit structure (passed in ECX)\n- dwParam2 (dword): Processing parameter (passed in EDX)\n\nReturns:\n- void (halts via FUN_6fb9a10f on validation failure)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Function contains fatal assertion checks; NULL unit field causes unrecoverable exit\n- Ordinal calls are Storm.dll and D2Common functions for unit validation",
