      "comment": "Initialize game resource validation and setup.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load game context pointer from global g_pGameContext (in ESI)\n2. Extract resource ID from param_1[0x38] (in EDI)\n3. Validate resource ID is non-zero; if null, call error handler (Ordinal_10023 with path strings) and exit\n4. Increment reference count on resource via Ordinal_10348(param_1, 1)\n5. Query game context data via Ordinal_10329(g_pGameContext) -> returns dwContextValue\n6. Query game context state via Ordinal_10326(g_pGameContext) -> returns dwGameContext\n7. Process resource with collected context: Ordinal_10216(nResourceId, dwGameContext, dwContextValue, 0)\n8. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\ndwResourceHandle (dword): Handle or pointer to resource structure; offset +0x38 contains resource ID for validation\n\nReturns:\nvoid; exits fatally if resource validation fails, otherwise succeeds silently\n\nSpecial Cases:\nIf resource ID at [dwResourceHandle + 0x38] is zero, function calls Ordinal_10023 error handler with file path and line 0x783, then terminates with FUN_6fb9a10f(-1). This is non-recoverable.\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x38: Offset within dwResourceHandle structure to resource ID field\n0x783: Line number constant passed to error handler (decimal 1923)\n1: Reference count increment for Ordinal_10348\n0: Zero parameter passed to Ordinal_10216\n\nNote: Function uses SSA temporaries optimized away (uVar1 visible only in disassembly).\n\nRelated Functions:\n- InitializeGameLoad() - Caller that triggers resource initialization\n- FUN_6fb9a10f() - Fatal exit handler\n- Ordinal_10348(pResource, nRefInc) - Increment resource reference count\n- Ordinal_10329(pGameContext) - Query context value\n- Ordinal_10326(pGameContext) - Query context state\n- Ordinal_10216(dwResourceId, dwState, dwValue, dwFlags) - Process resource initialization",
