      "instructions": ["0x93410|PUSH|ESI", "0x93411|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0x93413|PUSH|EDI", "0x93414|MOV|EDI, EDX", "0x93416|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [ESI + 0x84]", "0x9341C|PUSH|EAX", "0x9341D|CALL|0x6fb987c4", "0x93422|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0x93424|JNZ|0x6fb634ab", "0x9342A|CMP|dword ptr [ESI], 0x0", "0x9342D|JNZ|0x6fb634ab", "0x9342F|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [ESI + 0xc]", "0x93432|CMP|EAX, 0x13", "0x93435|JA|0x6fb6346f", "0x93437|XOR|ECX, ECX"],
      "comment": "Validates unit/item property compatibility by type classification.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call Ordinal_10262 on pUnitData[0x21] - if non-zero result, return 0 (validation passed/skip)\n2. Check if *pUnitData (type field) is 0 - if so, return 0 (validation passed/skip)\n3. Switch on pUnitData[3] (unit type code):\n   - Type codes 0,4,7,8,9,10,11,12,17,19: Pass through with return 0\n   - Type 13: Accept only if pUnitData[1] == 3, else return 1 (failure)\n   - Type 14: Accept only if pUnitData[1] == 6, else return 1 (failure)\n   - Type 15-16: Accept only if pUnitData[1] in (4,5,6), else return 1 (failure)\n   - Type 18: Special validation with nItemCode parameter:\n     - Call Ordinal_10963(nItemCode) to get item type\n     - For types 0x29 or 0xe6: Check if (pUnitData[0x11] & 0xffffff00) - 0xa00 >= 0\n     - For type 0x10a: Check if (pUnitData[0x11] & 0xffffff00) - 0xd00 >= 0\n     - If overflow flag != sign, return 1 (failure)\n     - Otherwise continue\n   - All other types: return 1 (failure)\n4. Return 0 (pass)\n\nParameters:\npUnitData (int *) - Pointer to unit structure, accessed at offsets:\n  [0] = type/classification field\n  [1] = subtype/classification field\n  [3] = unit type code\n  [0x11] = resource/capability field (checked against 0xa00 or 0xd00 thresholds)\n  [0x21] = flag field passed to Ordinal_10262\nnItemCode (int) - Item code passed to Ordinal_10963 for type classification\n\nReturns:\n0 - Validation passed/allowed\n1 - Validation failed/not allowed\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Returns 0 early if pUnitData[0x21] validation ordinal returns non-zero\n- Returns 0 early if pUnitData[0] type field is 0\n- Type 18 has conditional validation based on item type codes (0x29, 0xe6, 0x10a)\n- Uses flag/sign bit comparison (SBORROW4) for threshold validation on type 18\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x29 - Item type code constant\n0xe6 - Item type code constant  \n0x10a - Item type code constant\n0xa00 - Resource threshold for types 0x29/0xe6\n0xd00 - Resource threshold for type 0x10a\n0xffffff00 - Mask to extract upper 24 bits from pUnitData[0x11]",
      "tags": ["PARAM_2", "STRUCT_ItemData", "PROP_LOOPHEAVY"]
    },
