      "comment": "Iterate and cleanup all missiles and items when render context changes.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call Ordinal_10933(g_hRenderContext) to get current render tick value\n2. If same as g_dwLastRenderTick, skip processing (optimization)\n3. Update g_dwLastRenderTick to current tick\n4. Iterate through all entries in g_ppMissileHashTable (0x6fbfdea0 to 0x6fbfe0a0):\n   a. For each linked list, traverse using pNextNode = pCurrentNode[0x42]\n   b. Assert that pCurrentNode[0] == 2 (expected object type), call Ordinal_10023 if fails\n   c. Call FUN_6fb7e010(pCurrentNode, 0) to cleanup missile\n5. Iterate through all entries in g_ppItemHashTable (0x6fbfeaa0 to 0x6fbfeca0):\n   a. For each linked list, traverse using pNextNode = pCurrentNode[0x42]\n   b. Assert that pCurrentNode[0] == 2 (expected object type), call Ordinal_10023 if fails\n   c. Call FUN_6fb7e010(pCurrentNode, 0) to cleanup item\n\nParameters: (none)\n\nReturns: void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Hash table bounds: 0x6fbfdea0-0x6fbfe0a0 (missiles), 0x6fbfeaa0-0x6fbfeca0 (items)\n- Offset 0x42 (66 decimal) used as next pointer in linked list\n- Offset 0x0 checked for type field == 2\n- Error line 0x80b: assertion for missile type, line 0x815: assertion for item type\n- Calls Ordinal_10023 with error context before FUN_6fb9a10f(-1) abort\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x42 (66): Offset of next pointer in linked list node\n- 0x108 (264): Offset value for next node calculation in assembly\n- 0x80b (2059): Error code line for missile assertion\n- 0x815 (2069): Error code line for item assertion\n- 0x2: Expected object type for both missiles and items\n\nOrdinals:\n- Ordinal_10933: GetRenderTick - retrieves current render context tick\n- Ordinal_10023: AssertionFailed - assertion failure handler",
