      "comment": "Set entity finalization flag on entity data structure.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load flag value at entity offset 0xe8 (entity dword array index 0x3a)\n2. Set flag bit 0x10000 using logical OR operation\n3. Write updated flag value back to offset 0xe8\n4. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\npEntityData - Pointer to entity data structure (passed in ECX register via __fastcall)\nIMPLICIT: ECX contains pEntityData pointer\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value, modifies entity structure in place\n\nSpecial Cases:\nFlag offset 0xe8 applies to all entity types (monsters, players, objects)\nFlag bit 0x10000 marks entity as requiring finalization processing\nFlag operation is atomic (read-modify-write without interlocking)\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0xe8 - Byte offset to entity flags field in entity structure (uint dword at offset 0x3a in uint array)\n0x10000 - Flag bit value (65536 decimal) indicating entity finalization state\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset  Size  Field Name      Type   Description\n------  ----  ----------      ----   -----------\n0xe8    4     EntityFlags     uint   Entity state flags (bit 0x10000 = finalization required)",
