      "comment": "Validate unit state configuration against type restrictions.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if flag 0x10000 (UNIT_SKIP_VALIDATION) is set in pUnit[0x3a]\n2. If flag set, skip all validation and return success (1)\n3. If flag not set, load unit type from pUnit[0] and subtype from pUnit[3]\n4. For type 0: accept subtypes 0x00 or 0x11, reject others\n5. For type 1: accept subtypes 0x0c or 0x00, reject others\n6. For any other type: reject (return 0)\n7. Return 1 (success) if type/subtype combination valid, 0 (failure) if invalid\n\nParameters:\npUnit - Pointer to unit/entity structure containing type configuration\n        [0x00] = unit type (0=Player, 1=Monster, ...)\n        [0x03] = unit subtype/class\n        [0x3a] = unit flags (offset 0xe8 in assembly) including validation flag\n\nReturns:\n1 - Unit type state is valid or validation skipped\n0 - Unit type/subtype combination is not allowed\n\nSpecial Cases:\nType 0 with subtype 0x11 (special player variant) allowed\nType 1 with subtype 0x0c (specific monster class) allowed\nEmpty subtypes (0x00) valid for types 0 and 1",
