      "comment": "Validates if a unit matches a specified state condition.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load unit state value from pUnit[3] (offset 0xc)\n2. Switch on unit type from pUnit[0] (offset 0x0):\n   - Type 0: Return true if state == 0x11\n   - Type 1: Call Ordinal_10582(pUnit[1]) to get unit data, check byte at +0x343 is null and state == 0xc\n   - Type 2: Call Ordinal_10626(pUnit[1]) to get unit data, check flags at +0x1c7: bit 1 (0x2) set, or bit 0 (0x1) set AND state == 0x2\n   - Type 3: Check if flag 0x10000 set at pUnit[0x3a]\n   - Type 4: Return true if state == 0x3\n3. Return false if no conditions matched\n\nParameters:\npUnit (undefined4 *): Pointer to unit structure containing type, sub-id, and state fields. Fields accessed:\n  [0] = unit type (0-4)\n  [1] = unit sub-id/reference\n  [3] = unit state value (compared against 0x11, 0xc, 0x2, 0x3)\n  [0x3a] = unit flags (tested for 0x10000)\n\nReturns:\ntrue: Unit matches the validation condition for its type\nfalse: Unit does not match validation condition\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Ordinal_10582 and Ordinal_10626 return pointers to external unit data structures\n- All returned checks are independent per type; no cross-type conditions\n- Type values > 4 default to false return",
