      "comment": "Retrieves mercenary unit position coordinates from animation state.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate unit state and animation ID using FUN_6fb85820\n2. Check unit animation ID at offset 0x38 is not NULL\n3. If NULL animation ID, call Ordinal_10023 (assertion function) with error details\n4. Also call FUN_6fb9a10f with exit code 0xffffffff for fatal exit\n5. Retrieve animation ID from unit offset 0x38\n6. Call Ordinal_10180 with animation ID to get mercenary position pointer\n7. Return position array pointer containing x,y coordinates\n\nParameters:\npUnit (UnitAny *): Pointer to unit structure containing animation state at offset 0x38\n\nReturns:\ndword *: Pointer to position coordinate array [x, y, ...]\n         Non-NULL success (assertion prevents NULL return on failure)\n         \nRelated Functions:\n- Ordinal_10023: Assertion/error reporting function\n- Ordinal_10180: D2Common.GetMercenaryPosition or similar animation coordinate retrieval\n- FUN_6fb85820: Pre-validation checks\n- FUN_6fb9a10f: Fatal process exit\n         \nSpecial Cases:\nNULL animation ID triggers assertion and immediate process exit (line 2241)\nFunction assumes UnitAny structure has valid animation ID field at offset 0x38\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x38 (56): Animation ID field offset within UnitAny\n0x8c1 (2241): Source code line number for assertion\n0xffffffff: Exit code passed to FUN_6fb9a10f",
