      "instructions": ["0x937C0|PUSH|EDI", "0x937C1|MOV|EDI, ECX", "0x937C3|TEST|EDI, EDI", "0x937C5|JNZ|0x6fb637e5", "0x937C7|PUSH|0x8dc", "0x937CC|PUSH|0x6fbc9edc", "0x937D1|PUSH|0x6fbca114", "0x937D6|CALL|0x6fb99a7a", "0x937DB|ADD|ESP, 0xc", "0x937DE|PUSH|-0x1", "0x937E0|CALL|0x6fb9a10f", "0x937E5|PUSH|EBX", "0x937E6|PUSH|ESI", "0x937E7|MOV|EBX, 0x6fbfdaa0", "0x937EC|MOV|ECX, dword ptr [EBX]"],
      "comment": "Iterate all units in hash table and invoke callback for each unit\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate callback function pointer is not NULL\n2. If NULL, log critical error (missing unit function handler) and terminate\n3. If valid, initialize hash bucket pointer to start of g_ppUnitHashTable array\n4. For each hash bucket in table (from 0x6fbfdaa0 to 0x6fbfdca0):\n   a. Load unit pointer from current bucket\n   b. While unit pointer is valid (not 0):\n      i. Invoke callback function (IMPLICIT in ECX - pfnCallback)\n      ii. Load next unit from current unit + 0x108 (next pointer in linked list)\n   c. Move to next hash bucket pointer\n5. Return after all buckets processed\n\nParameters:\n- pfnCallback (IMPLICIT ECX): Function pointer to invoke for each unit, no parameters\n\nReturns:\n- void (no return value)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- NULL callback triggers assertion error with code 0x8dc\n- Hash bucket range spans exactly 256 buckets (0x6fbfdaa0 to 0x6fbfdca0)\n- Unit linked list traversal uses offset 0x108 as next pointer",
      "tags": ["SRC_CUnit.cpp", "MOD_UNIT", "PARAM_1"]
