      "comment": "Iterate through all missiles in the missile hash table and invoke a callback function for each missile in each bucket chain.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate callback function pointer (param_1 in ECX) is non-NULL\n2. If NULL, call Ordinal_10023 (Storm.dll assertion handler) with error info (D2Client.cpp:0x8f2)\n3. If invalid, call FUN_6fb9a10f(-0x1) to terminate with error code\n4. Initialize EBX to start of g_ppMissileHashTable array at address 0x6fbfdea0\n5. For each of 256 hash buckets in table (increment by 4 bytes per bucket):\n   a. Load first missile pointer from bucket [EBX]\n   b. Inner loop: for each missile in the chain:\n      - Load next_missile pointer at offset +0x108 from current missile\n      - Call pfnCallback with current missile as implicit ECX parameter\n      - Advance to next missile in chain\n      - Repeat until next_missile is NULL\n   c. Increment bucket pointer by 4 to move to next bucket\n6. Continue until all 256 buckets processed (bucket_ptr >= 0x6fbfe0a0)\n7. Pop saved registers and return\n\nParameters:\n  pfnCallback (dword) - Function pointer passed in ECX register; called once per missile\n    Format: void callback(void) - receives missile via implicit ECX register (__fastcall)\n\nReturns:\n  void - Returns normally if callback is valid; does not return if callback is NULL (assertion failure)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  NULL callback triggers assertion failure via Ordinal_10023 - function never returns\n  Empty buckets (NULL first missile) skip to next bucket immediately\n  Missile chains vary in length; offset 0x108 is missile.next_missile pointer\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x108 - Offset of next_missile field within missile structure (4-byte boundaries)\n  0x6fbfdea0 - Base address of g_ppMissileHashTable array (first bucket)\n  0x6fbfe0a0 - End address limit for array iteration (256 buckets * 4 bytes per pointer)\n  0x8f2 - Line number in D2Client.cpp where assertion occurs (2290 decimal)\n  -0x1 (0xFFFFFFFF) - Error code passed to FUN_6fb9a10f exception handler\n\nCalls:\n  Ordinal_10023() - Storm.dll assertion handler; never returns if called (abort)\n  FUN_6fb9a10f() - Exception/termination handler for error code\n\nRelated Functions:\n- RenderGameFrame() - Calls this with rendering callback\n- Missile processing callbacks from RenderGameFrame",
      "tags": ["SRC_CUnit.cpp", "MOD_UNIT", "PARAM_1"]
