      "instructions": ["0x938B0|SUB|ESP, 0x8", "0x938B3|PUSH|EBX", "0x938B4|PUSH|EBP", "0x938B5|PUSH|ESI", "0x938B6|PUSH|EDI", "0x938B7|MOV|EDI, ECX", "0x938B9|TEST|EDI, EDI", "0x938BB|JNZ|0x6fb638db", "0x938BD|PUSH|0x918", "0x938C2|PUSH|0x6fbc9edc", "0x938C7|PUSH|0x6fbc9f40", "0x938CC|CALL|0x6fb99a7a", "0x938D1|ADD|ESP, 0xc", "0x938D4|PUSH|-0x1", "0x938D6|CALL|0x6fb9a10f"],
      "comment": "Get unit stat field offset based on unit type and status.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate input unit pointer is not null; assert on failure\n2. Switch on unit type field (uint at offset 0):\n   - Type 1: Get unit handler offset, check string length; return stat offset + 0x3C\n   - Type 2: Fall through to type 4 check\n   - Type 4: Get unit skill offset; return offset + 0xE8\n   - Type 5: Continue to main logic\n3. If unit has equipment ([ptr + 0x70][0x1c8] != 0x00) AND unit subtype == 2:\n   a. Get unit via Ordinal_10342 (D2Common.GetUnit)\n   b. Iterate linked list at [result + 0x2C] looking for item type 5\n   c. If found, check item ID at [item + 0x4]\n   d. If not in search results, collect search results via Ordinal_10035\n   e. Iterate collected results searching for type 5 item\n   f. Call Ordinal_10058 to process result, return offset + 0x262\n4. Check unit memory flag ([ptr + 0x70][0x14a] != 0x00):\n   - If set: Call Ordinal_10393, if success return Ordinal_10004 result\n   - Otherwise check flags ([ptr + 0x70][0x181] != 0x00 AND [ptr + 0x70 + 0x4] & 0x80)\n   - If both set, return Ordinal_10004 result; else return offset + 0x40\n5. Default: Check unit subtype (uint at offset 0xC)\n   - Type 5 or 4: Return Ordinal_10004 result  \n   - Type 0: Return Ordinal_10004 result\n   - Type 6: Return Ordinal_10004 result\n   - Other: Return Ordinal_10004 result\n\nParameters:\npUnit (uint *): Pointer to unit structure; implicit in ECX per __fastcall\n  - [pUnit + 0]: Unit type (1, 2, 4, 5)\n  - [pUnit + 0x4]: Unit ID\n  - [pUnit + 0xC]: Unit subtype\n  - [pUnit + 0x70]: Pointer to unit info structure\n\nReturns:\nint: Offset value to apply to unit pointer for stat access\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- NULL unit pointer triggers assertion failure\n- Unicode string length checked via function pointer at 0x6fba5c44\n- Link list traversal assumes [item + 0x10C] points to next item\n- Search results may be empty (count = 0)",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Unit", "PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Act", "SRC_CUnit.cpp", "STRUCT_Inventory", "MOD_UNIT", "PARAM_1", "PROP_LOOPHEAVY", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control"]
