      "comment": "Decrement a resource reference counter and notify system of decrement\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if pData is NULL (ECX == 0)\n   - If NULL, call Ordinal_10023 with assertion file/line (ptUnit, project path, line 0x98e)\n   - Call FUN_6fb9a10f(-1) to terminate error path\n2. Load counter value from offset 0x68 in pData structure\n3. Check if counter is already zero\n   - If zero, return 0 (counter already exhausted, no notification)\n4. Decrement counter by 1 and store back to offset 0x68\n5. Call Ordinal_10487 with pData and flag 0x8f (status update notification)\n6. Convert result to boolean: return 1 if result == 0, else 0\n\nParameters:\npData (void *) - Pointer to resource structure; counter stored at offset 0x68\n\nReturns:\nuint - 1 if Ordinal_10487 returned 0 (success), 0 if Ordinal_10487 non-zero or counter already zero\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- NULL pointer triggers assertion handler with error context\n- Counter bottomed at zero (early return prevents underflow)\n- Return value inverted: Ordinal_10487 == 0 produces true (1)\n- Magic number 0x8f: Flag passed to Ordinal_10487 (unknown semantics)",
