      "comment": "Enumerate and remove items from a unit's inventory with optional child unit preservation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate pUnit parameter - abort if NULL (assertion)\n2. Read unit's item list head from offset 0x84 (param_1[0x21])\n3. Return if no items (nItemListHead == 0)\n4. Iterate through item list:\n   a. Get next item via Ordinal_10304\n   b. Get item hash value via Ordinal_10306, mask to 0x7f\n   c. Lookup hash table bucket in g_ppGhostHashTable[hash]\n   d. If item not found in bucket, traverse chain via offset 0x108\n   e. Validate item type (ITEMTYPE_ITEM = 4), abort on mismatch\n5. Check nPreserveMode flag:\n   - If nPreserveMode == 0: Skip to direct removal (LAB_6fb63ce3)\n   - If nPreserveMode != 0: Search all units for items referencing target\n6. Item ownership check (if nPreserveMode != 0):\n   a. Iterate unit hash tables (2 tables, 0x80 buckets each = 256 units)\n   b. For each unit: enumerate items via Ordinal_10277/Ordinal_10304\n   c. Get item data via Ordinal_10305\n   d. If item matches pTargetItem: mark fItemFound=true, break search\n7. Conditional processing:\n   - If fItemFound==true: Skip FUN_6fb646b0, remove item directly\n   - If fItemFound==false: Call FUN_6fb646b0 (apply transformation type 3 check)\n8. Final removal:\n   a. Call Ordinal_10243 to remove item from list\n   b. Get item type and hash from pTargetItem\n   c. Locate item in hash table chain\n   d. Remove from chain: update previous->next or bucket head\n   e. Call CleanupGameContextAndResources to free memory\n9. Loop back to step 4 until all items processed\n\nParameters:\npUnit: int * - pointer to unit structure containing item list\n  IMPLICIT ECX (fastcall) - unit handle to process\nnPreserveMode: int - flags determining item handling strategy\n  IMPLICIT EDX (fastcall)\n  Value 0: Remove without preservation checks\n  Non-zero: Scan child units before removal\n\nReturns:\nvoid - modifies unit item lists, calls cleanup on removed items\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- NULL pUnit triggers assertion and abort via FUN_6fb9a10f(-1)\n- Missing item list or item count mismatch triggers assertions\n- Item type validation ensures only ITEMTYPE_ITEM (4) processed\n- Hash table lookup offset 0x108 used for chain traversal\n- Hash collision handling via linked list chain traversal\n- Memory cleanup via CleanupGameContextAndResources for each removed item\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x21 - unit offset to item list head (4 bytes)\n0x84 - alternate offset notation same as 0x21*4\n0x7f - hash bucket mask (128 buckets per table)\n0x42 - hash chain next pointer offset (0x108 >> 2)\n0x108 - hash chain next pointer offset (binary: 0x42 dword offset)\n0x80 - hash buckets per table (256 units total)\n0x4 - ITEMTYPE_ITEM constant (validation check)\n0x3 - item transformation type trigger (calls FUN_6fb646b0)\n0x02 - D2 calling convention indicator\nOrdinal offsets reference D2Common.dll exports:\n  10277 - GetItemListStart\n  10304 - GetNextItem\n  10306 - GetItemHashValue\n  10305 - GetItemData\n  10243 - RemoveItem\n  10307 - GetItemType\n  10023 - Error/Assert function\n  10029 - Mismatch assertion\n  10305, 10306, 10307 - Item data accessors\n\nRelated Functions:\n- FUN_6fb646b0: Applies item transformation (called if type==3)\n- CleanupGameContextAndResources: Memory cleanup callback\n- Ordinal_10277/10304/10305/10306/10307: D2Common item accessors\n- FUN_6fb9a10f: Fatal assertion abort handler",
