      "comment": "Compares two units by their attributes, types, and relationships to determine compatibility.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Obtain unit stat from pUnit1 using Ordinal_10342 (D2Common.GetUnitStat)\n2. Check if stat is valid using Ordinal_10082 (D2Common.IsUnitStatValid)\n3. If stat invalid, return 0 (not compatible)\n4. If unit1 type=0 AND unit2 type=0, validate special conditions:\n   - If unit2 has flag 0x10000 OR type field [unit2+0xc]=0 OR type=0x11, check player permission\n   - If CheckPlayerPermission returns 0, return 0\n5. If unit1 type=0 AND unit2 type=1, search unit2 index in linked list and validate using FUN_6fb64010\n6. If above conditions met, return 0; otherwise return 1 (compatible)\n7. If stat valid, normalize types by searching linked list:\n   - If unit1 type=1, replace with SearchLinkedListByKey result, set unit1 type=0\n   - If unit2 type=1, replace with SearchLinkedListByKey result, set unit2 type=0\n8. If normalized types/indices match, return 0 (same unit)\n9. If both types=0, check permission and compare using FUN_6fb823e0 (distance/attribute check)\n10. If unit2 type=1, call Ordinal_10669 and Ordinal_10670 for additional validation\n11. Final comparison using Ordinal_10563, return 1 if equal, 0 if different\n\nParameters:\npUnit1 - Pointer to first unit data structure\npUnit2 - Pointer to second unit data structure\n\nReturns:\n1 - Units are compatible/matching\n0 - Units are incompatible/not matching\n\nSpecial Cases:\nMagic 0x10000: Unit attribute flag (checked at offset 0xe8)\nMagic 0x11: Special unit type value\nMagic -0x1 (0xFFFFFFFF): Invalid list search result",
