      "comment": "Validate whether a player slot meets active quest criteria.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Verify both slot index and player node pointers are non-null\n2. Check if slot[0] is 0 OR player[0] is 1 (quest state conditions)\n3. If true, iterate through two slot references (Ordinal_10321 and Ordinal_10322)\n4. For each slot reference that exists:\n   - Get unit descriptor via Ordinal_10963\n   - Retrieve detailed unit data via Ordinal_10594\n   - Check if byte at offset +0x84 is non-zero (quest flags)\n   - Set fSlotValid=true if any slot has flags set\n5. If fSlotValid is true OR second slot check passes, continue validation\n6. Call SearchLinkedListByKey with player[2] to find matching quest entry\n7. Return true if search result equals slot[2] (quest IDs match)\n\nParameters:\npSlotIndex (int *) - Pointer to slot data structure [0]=quest state\npPlayerNode (int *) - Pointer to player node [0]=player state flag, [2]=quest ID\n\nReturns:\ntrue - Slot is active and quest IDs match player quest record\nfalse - Invalid pointers, failed conditions, or quest mismatch\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Quest validation requires BOTH first condition (state checks) AND second condition (ID match)\n- Offset 0x84 contains quest flags; non-zero indicates active quest status\n- SearchLinkedListByKey failure (returns 0) results in false return\n- Note: Function uses 1 register-based temporary (local_EAX_103) optimized away in decompilation",
