      "comment": "Validates if a unit has availability for skill execution based on target area and player state\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate inputs: both pUnitAny and pSkillData must be non-NULL\n2. Check pSkillData[0] state: must be 0 (idle) or 1 (specific mode)\n3. Get unit skill state via Ordinal_10321(pUnitAny)\n4. If state valid, retrieve unit skill info via Ordinal_10963()\n5. Get status data via Ordinal_10594() and check offset 0x85 for required area flag\n6. Repeat steps 3-5 for secondary unit skill via Ordinal_10322()\n7. Validate at least one required area is present\n8. If pSkillData[0] == 1, search player list via SearchLinkedListByKey(pSkillData[2])\n9. Return 0xFFFFFFFF if player not found\n10. Verify both units target same area via CheckPlayersHaveSameTargetArea()\n11. Return true if area matches, false otherwise\n\nParameters:\npUnitAny (int *): Pointer to primary UnitAny structure - skill source unit\npSkillData (int *): Pointer to skill request data - [0]=mode, [2]=player search key\n\nReturns:\ntrue (1): Units have skill availability and target same area\nfalse (0): Validation failed (NULL inputs, invalid state, mismatched areas, player not found)\n\nSpecial Cases:\nMagic numbers: 0x85 is skill availability flag offset within unit status data",
