      "comment": "Apply light RGB color to unit, extracting color components from attribute.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Fetch light structure pointer from unit at offset 0x88\n2. If light exists, query unit attribute 0x5a via Ordinal_10520\n3. If attribute valid (non-zero), extract RGB components:\n   - Red: bits 16-23 (dwRgbColor >> 0x10)\n   - Green: bits 8-15 (dwRgbColor >> 0x08)\n   - Blue: bits 0-7 (dwRgbColor & 0xFF)\n   - Apply custom color via SetLightRgbColor\n4. If attribute invalid or light not found, apply default white (0xFF, 0xFF, 0xFF)\n\nParameters:\n- pUnit (UnitAny *): IMPLICIT in ECX, unit object containing light pointer\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Light pointer may be NULL: uses default white (0xFF, 0xFF, 0xFF)\n- Attribute value 0: treated as invalid, uses white color\n\nRelated Functions:\n- SetLightRgbColor: Applies RGB triplet to light object\n- Ordinal_10520: Retrieves unit attribute value (0x5a = light color)",
