      "comment": "Update light source radius based on unit properties and light intensity\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load light pointer from unit at offset 0x22\n2. If no light exists, return early\n3. If unit[0] == 0, set radius to 0x0d (default 13), skip intensity check\n4. Otherwise retrieve unit data type via Ordinal_10582 with unit[1]\n5. Get light intensity value via Ordinal_11051 with unit pointer\n6. Extract intensity byte (intensity & 0xff) as working radius value\n7. Load intensity threshold from unit data + 0x2b2\n8. Compare computed intensity against threshold\n9. If intensity < threshold, use threshold value as radius\n10. Load base light radius via Ordinal_10520 with unit pointer and property 0x59\n11. Final radius = base radius + computed intensity\n12. Apply final radius to light via SetLightRadius\n\nParameters:\npUnit (int *): Unit structure pointer, contains:\n  - Offset 0x00: Flag determining intensity vs default path\n  - Offset 0x04: Unit type/data selector\n  - Offset 0x22: Pointer to LightStruct\n\nReturns:\nvoid - modifies light radius as side effect\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Null light pointer (unit[0x22]): Returns without modification\n- Unit flag zero (unit[0] == 0): Uses fixed radius 0x0d, ignores intensity\n- Intensity < threshold: Uses threshold from unit data instead\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x22 - Light structure pointer offset in unit\n0x00 - Flag field determining calculation path\n0x04 - Unit type/data selector offset\n0x0d - Default light radius (decimal 13)\n0xff - Byte mask for intensity extraction\n0x2b2 - Intensity threshold offset in unit data\n0x59 - Property ID for base light radius\n\nNote: Function uses 2 stack-allocated temporaries optimized away in decompilation (iVar1, uVar2)",
