      "comment": "Iterate through handler table and invoke callbacks with optional parameter processing.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if g_dwHandlerCount <= 0; if so, return immediately\n2. Initialize handler index to 0 and get base pointer from g_ppHandlerTable\n3. For each handler in range [0, g_dwHandlerCount):\n   a. If nfProcessParams == 0: Get unit stat via Ordinal_10481, then fetch handler parameter via Ordinal_10466\n   b. Else: Fetch handler parameter directly via Ordinal_10520\n   c. If result is non-zero AND function pointer is valid:\n      - If nfProcessParams != 0: Iterate through g_pHandlerParams array and adjust each parameter via Ordinal_10466/Ordinal_10464\n      - Invoke handler function pointer with ECX=nUnitId\n   d. Advance to next handler (ppHandlerFunc += 3, nHandlerIdx++)\n\nParameters:\n  nUnitId (fastcall ECX): Unit ID to process (passed to Ordinal_10481, Ordinal_10466)\n  nFlags: Mode flag - if 0, fetch via stat lookup; else direct parameter fetch\n  nfProcessParams: If non-zero, process parameter adjustments before handler invocation\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If nFlags == 0 and Ordinal_10481 fails, logs error via Ordinal_10023 and terminates via FUN_6fb9a10f(0xffffffff)\n  - Handler function invoked via indirect call: ECX=nUnitId (implicit __thiscall style)\n  - Ordinal_10464 negates adjusted values (-iVar2) before applying\n  - Note: Function uses 1 stack-allocated temporary (local_EBX_130) optimized away by compiler\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x1000 - Buffer/stat request size for Ordinal_10481\n  0xeb - Error line number for logging\n  3 - Stride in handler table and parameter array (pointer arithmetic)\n  -1 (0xffffffff) - Termination code for error path\n\nOrdinal References:\n  Ordinal_10481 - D2Common.GetUnitStat - Query unit stat value\n  Ordinal_10466 - D2Common.GetStatValue - Get stat value from unit  \n  Ordinal_10520 - D2Common.GetItemStat - Fetch item/handler parameter\n  Ordinal_10464 - D2Common.SetStatValue - Apply st