      "instructions": ["0x94720|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [ESP + 0xc]", "0x94724|PUSH|EBX", "0x94725|PUSH|EBP", "0x94726|PUSH|ESI", "0x94727|PUSH|EDI", "0x94728|CMP|EAX, 0x7", "0x9472B|MOV|EDI, EDX", "0x9472D|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0x9472F|JL|0x6fb6474f", "0x94731|PUSH|0x465", "0x94736|PUSH|0x6fbca31c", "0x9473B|PUSH|0x6fbca350", "0x94740|CALL|0x6fb99a7a", "0x94745|ADD|ESP, 0xc", "0x94748|PUSH|-0x1"],
      "comment": "Transition unit item between equipment modes.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate mode parameter (0-6); fail if >= 7 with assertion at 0x465\n2. Store requested mode in unit->pItemMode[3]\n3. Call Ordinal_10390 to perform base mode recalculation\n4. Execute mode-specific state changes via switch(pItemMode[3]):\n   - Mode 3: Equip armor; set flags 0x3a |= 0x02 (equipped)\n   - Mode 4: Create spell dialog; fall-through to default clear\n   - Modes 0,1,2,6: Clear equipped flag 0x3a &= 0xfffffffd\n   - Mode 5: Process special mode transition; fetch item stat scaling; apply visual effects via FUN_6fb8d210\n5. Set mode-invariant flag bits (0x3a = (0x3a & 0xfffffff3) | 0x20)\n6. If bUpdateDisplay: refresh display, check cursor state, populate item data if cursor empty\n\nParameters:\n- pUnit: UnitAny pointer to item/unit record to modify\n- dwTargetSlot: Equipment slot index parameter\n- dwItemIndex: Item index within inventory\n- dwItemUniqueId: Item unique identifier\n- nNewMode: Target equipment mode 0-6 (ITEM_NONE=0, EQUIPPED=3, etc)\n- bUpdateDisplay: Update UI/display state if non-zero\n\nReturns: void; modifies unit state in-place; traps to FUN_6fb9a10f(-1) on invalid mode\n\nSpecial Cases: Mode 3 sets 0x02 flag (equipped); all modes clear 0x02 except Mode 3; Mode 5 requires item data lookup via pItemMode[1]; display update uses asynchronous Ordinal calls",
