      "instructions": ["0x94970|PUSH|ESI", "0x94971|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0x94973|TEST|ESI, ESI", "0x94975|JNZ|0x6fb64995", "0x94977|PUSH|0x4b9", "0x9497C|PUSH|0x6fbca31c", "0x94981|PUSH|0x6fbc9f40", "0x94986|CALL|0x6fb99a7a", "0x9498B|ADD|ESP, 0xc", "0x9498E|PUSH|-0x1", "0x94990|CALL|0x6fb9a10f", "0x94995|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [ESI + 0xc]", "0x94998|CMP|EAX, 0x6", "0x9499B|JA|0x6fb64a08", "0x9499D|JMP|dword ptr [EAX*0x4 + 0x6fb64a28]"],
      "comment": "Updates unit mode state and flags based on unit type.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if unit pointer is NULL, abort with error (calls Ordinal_10023 with error line 0x4b9) if so\n2. Load unit mode field at offset +0xc (param_1[3])\n3. Switch on mode value:\n   - Cases 0,1,2,4,6: Clear flag bit 0x02 at offset +0xe8 ([0x3a])\n   - Case 3: Set flag bit 0x02 at offset +0xe8, call FUN_6fb8f790 with offset 0x46, return if result != 0\n   - Case 5: Call Ordinal_10378(pUnit) to check state, if non-zero set mode to 3, else call Ordinal_10374 and return\n   - Default: Abort with error (calls Ordinal_10023 with error line 0x4d3)\n4. Call FUN_6fb931f0 with pUnit and parameters (0x46, 6, 8, 0, 0, 8, 0)\n\nParameters:\npUnit: Pointer to unit structure (32-bit pointer, passed in ECX)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Returns to caller on all paths except error cases (which abort)\n\nSpecial Cases:\nNULL unit pointer triggers abort with Ordinal_10023 error (line 0x4b9)\nInvalid mode (>6) triggers abort with Ordinal_10023 error (line 0x4d3)\nOrdinals documented: 10023 (Storm.dll logging), 10378 (D2Common.dll state check), 10374 (D2Common.dll mode update)\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x46 - Offset/parameter passed to Ordinal_10378 and FUN_6fb8f790\n0x3a/0xe8 - Offset in unit structure for mode flags (field stored as [0x3a] in decompiled, [0xe8] in assembly)\n0x02 - Bit flag for mode state (OR/AND with 0xfd for clear, 0x02 for set)\n0x4b9 - Error line number for NULL pointer check\n0x4d3 - Error line number for invalid mode",
