      "comment": "Set unit flag state based on command type.\nModifies the flags field (offset 0xe8) of a unit structure conditionally.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if nCommand equals 2\n2. If command equals 2:\n   a. Call D2Common ordinal function with pUnit and dwFlags\n   b. Load flags field from pUnit at offset 0xe8\n   c. Check if nEnable is non-zero\n   d. If enabled: Set bit 0x02 (OR with 0x02)\n   e. If disabled: Clear bit 0x02 (AND with 0xFD)\n   f. Write modified flags back to pUnit+0xe8\n3. If command is not 2: Return without modification\n\nParameters:\n- nCommand (int): Command type; only 2 triggers flag modification\n- pUnit (UnitAny *): Pointer to unit structure containing flags at offset 0xe8\n- nEnable (int): Enable flag; non-zero sets 0x02, zero clears it\n- dwFlags (dword): Additional flags passed to D2Common ordinal\n\nReturns:\n- void: Modifies pUnit structure in place\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Only modifies structure when nCommand == 2\n- Bit 0x02 indicates some state property of the unit",
