      "comment": "Initialize item unit with properties from item data structure.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate and initialize new unit with base item info (type, position, quality)\n2. If allocation fails, fallback to getting unit from item data at param_6\n3. If both fail, log error and terminate with FUN_6fb9a10f\n4. If allocation succeeds, apply core properties:\n   - Set item power/rarity from offset +5 and +0x25\n   - Copy item flags (0x1000, 0x100, 0x4000, 0x20000) from item data offset +0x21\n   - Check flag 0x10 for special initialization path\n5. For items with flag 0x10 set: allocate properties and apply skill data\n6. Handle item class-specific properties (class 7 for weapons, class 4 for equipment)\n7. Calculate and apply AC/damage modifiers based on quality\n8. Set visual properties (name, color, level) and call finalization\n\nParameters:\ndwItemType (ECX) - Item type enumeration (weapon, armor, scroll, potion, etc.)\ndwX (EDX) - X coordinate (16-bit, masked to 0xffff)\ndwY (Stack+4) - Y coordinate (16-bit, masked to 0xffff)\ndwZ (Stack+8) - Z coordinate (16-bit, masked to 0xffff)\nnQuality (Stack+12) - Item quality level (0=normal, 1-6=enhanced)\npItemData (Stack+16) - Pointer to item definition structure with flags/stats\nnLogPacket (Stack+20) - Flag to log packet info for network sync (0=no log, 1=log)\n\nReturns:\nNon-NULL pointer to initialized unit structure on success\nNULL if allocation fails and fallback unit not available\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Class 7 items allocate special property structures\n- Weapons with skill 0x2d apply AC/damage modifiers via offset +0x60\n- Armor items validate AC value and apply min/max constraints\n- Flag 0x1000000 triggers special property copying\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset | Size | Field Name | Type | Description\n+0x1000 | flag | SOCKETED | - | Item has sockets\n+0x20000 | flag | QUALITY | - | Item has quality bonus\n+0x10 | flag | SPECIAL | - | Requires special initialization\n+0x21 | dword | FLAGS | - | Item property flags\n+0x25 | dword | POWER | - | Item power/rarity level",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "SRC_Item.cpp", "MOD_UNIT", "STRUCT_ItemData", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData", "STRUCT_MonsterData", "PARAM_7", "PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Skill", "STRUCT_Other", "NET_SCMD"]
