      "api_calls": ["SetItemDataValue", "ITEMS_SetAutoMagicId", "SetItemDataField0x28", "SetValidatedStructureField", "ITEMS_GetItemCode", "FogAssert", "ITEMS_GetQualityLevel", "FindQualityRatioEntry", "FogAssert", "GetItemDataFromSlot", "...+54 more"],
      "instructions": ["0x95090|SUB|ESP, 0x8", "0x95093|PUSH|EBX", "0x95094|PUSH|EBP", "0x95095|PUSH|ESI", "0x95096|PUSH|EDI", "0x95097|MOV|EBP, EDX", "0x95099|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0x9509B|XOR|EDI, EDI", "0x9509D|PUSH|EDI", "0x9509E|PUSH|-0x1", "0x950A0|PUSH|ESI", "0x950A1|CALL|0x6fb98dd6", "0x950A6|PUSH|EDI", "0x950A7|PUSH|-0x1", "0x950A9|PUSH|ESI"],
      "comment": "Processes item display properties based on item type and unit context, initializing viewport coordinates and calculating value/damage/defense ranges.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize display mode indexes (loop 3x) with Ordinal_10700/10702\n2. Call Ordinal_10704/10706 for display finalization\n3. Retrieve display mode count via Ordinal_10695; assert non-zero (fatal error on failure)\n4. Retrieve current frame count via GetVideoFrameCount\n5. Query display data array via Ordinal_10623, store pointer\n6. Assert display data exists (fatal error on failure)\n7. For each enabled display mode in DAT_6fbca2d4 array:\n   - Switch on mode value (2-7) to determine base stat offsets\n   - Read item value from pItem[0x1b] (ushort)\n   - Calculate display value by dividing item value by appropriate stat divisor\n   - Subtract divisor result from base stat to get final range\n   - Ensure minimum value of 1\n   - Validate calculation succeeded (call Ordinal_10691 for cleanup on failure)\n8. Retrieve final item type via Ordinal_10695\n9. Query item header data via Ordinal_10707; return if zero\n10. Switch on item type (1-7):\n    - Type 1: Call Ordinal_10874 (armor setup)\n    - Type 2: Call Ordinal_10751 to get class, handle class 0x28 with Ordinal_10733; check for special modes\n    - Type 3: Call Ordinal_10733 with 0xffffffff, apply Ordinal_10873\n    - Type 4: Query Ordinal_10714/10716, setup Ordinal_10865 calls for display modes\n    - Type 5: Call Ordinal_10733 with 0xffffffff, call Ordinal_10870\n    - Type 6: Call Ordinal_10704/10706, apply Ordinal_10868\n    - Type 7: Call Ordinal_10733 twice, retrieve class via Ordinal_10732, validate non-zero class\n    - Default: Fatal error\n11. Check if item has special state (Ordinal_10875 non-zero):\n    - Verify availability flags via Ordinal_10731 (0x2d or 0x32)\n    - Check Ordinal_10811 result and item type > 1\n    - Call cleanup routines if all checks pass\n    - Handle item types 1-3 with FUN_6fb65530 if applicable\n12. Return success\n\nParameters:\n  pUnit - Pointer to unit structure (ECX register IMPLICIT)\n  pItem - Pointer to item structure (EDX register IMPLICIT)\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Fatal errors trigger Ordinal_10023 (error logging) then FUN_6fb9a10f(0xffffffff) for exit\n  - Display mode iteration assumes DAT_6fbca2ec > 0; skipped if false\n  - Division operations use signed division (CDQ/IDIV); results checked via Ordinal_10918\n  - Type 2 item has conditional logic for class value 0x28 vs 0xd vs 0x12 vs 0x16\n  - Stack temporaries optimized away: see get_function_variables output\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x04 - Display offset for item value field\n  0x1b - Offset into pItem for value ushort (item value)\n  0x19 - Offset into pItem for secondary value ushort (item class)\n  0x2ad - Error code: ITEMSDataGetModType_hItem\n  0x275 - Error code: ptRatio calculation failure\n  0x1fe - Error code: Ordinal_10701/10699 failure\n  0x210 - Error code: Ordinal_10608 failure (server descriptor)\n  0x2e0 - Error code: Default switch case\n  0x400000 - Display flag bitmask for Ordinal_10707\n  0x1b0 - Display flag offset constant\n  0x2d - Ordinal_10731 parameter (flag type)\n  0x32 - Ordinal_10731 parameter (flag type)\n  0x28 - Class comparison value\n  0xd - Class comparison value\n  0x12 - Class comparison value\n  0x16 - Class comparison value",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "SRC_Item.cpp", "MOD_UNIT", "STRUCT_ItemData", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData", "STRUCT_MonsterData", "PROP_LARGE", "PARAM_2", "STRUCT_Skill", "STRUCT_Other", "PROP_LOOPHEAVY"]
