      "comment": "Process item affixes (prefixes/suffixes) based on item code and current random state.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if item code is prefix-eligible (Ordinal_10714)\n   - If yes: try to assign 4 prefix groups (Ordinal_10865), exit on error\n   - If no: proceed to suffix/socket check\n2. Check if item code supports sockets (Ordinal_10716)\n   - If yes: assign socket (Ordinal_10700) with current result\n   - If no: check if random state allows suffix (Ordinal_10918)\n3. If random state = 0: try to assign 4 prefix groups (Ordinal_10865)\n   - On failure: try 3 prefix groups (Ordinal_10865 with last param=0), exit on error\n4. If random state != 0: try 3 prefix groups (Ordinal_10865 with last param=0)\n   - On success: jump to apply socket processing\n   - On failure: try 4 prefix groups (Ordinal_10865 with last param=1), exit on error\n5. Apply socket processing (Ordinal_10702) with result code and flags\n\nParameters:\n  nItemCode (uint, IMPLICIT ECX) - Item code to process affixes for\n\nReturns:\n  void - Exits via FUN_6fb9a10f(-1) on error conditions\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Error exit at offset 0x21b with nPrefix error string\n  - Error exit at offset 0x229 with nSuffix error string\n  - Error exit at offset 0x220 with nSuffix error string\n  - Error exit at offset 0x232 with nPrefix error string\n  - Random state check determines prefix/suffix branch (0=prefix first, non-zero=suffix first)\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x21b (539 decimal) - Line number for prefix assignment error\n  0x220 (544 decimal) - Line number for suffix assignment error (socket branch)\n  0x229 (553 decimal) - Line number for suffix assignment error (main branch)\n  0x232 (562 decimal) - Line number for prefix assignment error (random path)\n  0xffffffff (-1) - Fatal error exit code passed to FUN_6fb9a10f\n  \nStructure Layout:\n  Accessed indirectly via item code through ordinal calls. No local structures defined.",
