      "api_calls": ["ParseItemDataFromBuffer", "FogAssert", "GetStatListByKey", "SetUnitStateFlag", "RemoveStatListFromUnit", "FreeStatListChain", "CalculateUnitAnimationFrameCount", "GetItemDataFlags", "SetUnitAnimationMode", "GetItemStatsTableOffset"],
      "instructions": ["0x956B0|SUB|ESP, 0x18", "0x956B3|LEA|EAX, [ESP]", "0x956B7|PUSH|ESI", "0x956B8|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0x956BA|XOR|ECX, ECX", "0x956BC|PUSH|EDI", "0x956BD|MOV|CL, byte ptr [ESI + 0x2]", "0x956C0|PUSH|EAX", "0x956C1|SUB|ECX, 0x8", "0x956C4|PUSH|0x0", "0x956C6|LEA|EDX, [ESI + 0x8]", "0x956C9|PUSH|ECX", "0x956CA|PUSH|EDX", "0x956CB|CALL|0x6fb98ddc", "0x956D0|LEA|EDX, [ESP + 0x8]"],
      "comment": "Initialize item variation properties and apply damage scaling for unique/set items.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load base item properties from item code (Ordinal_10883 = GetItemData)\n2. Call FUN_6fb657c0 to retrieve/validate item coordinates (wX, wY, wZ from stack)\n3. If coordinate validation fails (returns 0):\n   - Log error message \"hItem\" at offset 0x504 via Ordinal_10023\n   - Terminate function immediately via FUN_6fb9a10f(-1)\n4. Retrieve item variation property at offset 0x36:\n   - Ordinal_10480 = Get item property\n5. If variation exists (nVariation != 0):\n   - Ordinal_10486: Clear variation at offset 0x36\n   - Ordinal_10474: Set item with variation value\n   - Ordinal_10485: Free/release variation object\n   - Ordinal_10376: Process item updates\n6. Check item type field at offset 0xc for value 0x3 (unique/set item):\n7. If type == 0x3:\n   - Ordinal_10707: Process type-3 item with flags 0x2000, message 0x508\n   - If processing succeeds:\n     - Ordinal_10348: Set item rarity/property (value 5)\n     - Ordinal_10600: Get stat table entry from item data at offset 0x4\n     - If stat entry valid:\n       - Load scale factor from g_pflItemScaleTable [stat_type * 8]\n       - Load damage from g_pdwItemDamageTable [stat_type * 8]\n       - Apply damage modifier 0xd8 via FUN_6fb8d210\n       - Apply scale factor via second FUN_6fb8d210 call\n       - Apply offset 0xb4 via FUN_6fb8d640\n\nParameters:\nnItemCode (ECX/int): Item code index identifying item type\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Modifies item structure in-place, applies damage/scale properties\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Coordinate validation failure: Function terminates with error code 0xffffffff\n- Non-type-3 items: Skip damage scaling initialization\n- Type-3 processing failure: Skip stat table processing\n- Invalid stat table entry: No damage/scale applied\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x2 - Item type byte offset for property retrieval\n0x8 - Subtraction from property for validation\n0x36 - Item variation property offset\n0xc - Item type classification offset\n0x3 - Type identifier for unique/set items (triggers scaling)\n0x2000 - Processing flags for type-3 items\n0x508 - Error/message code for type-3 processing\n0x28 - Stat type index within item stat structure\n0xd8 - Initial damage modification constant\n0xb4 - Final damage/offset constant\n0x4 - Item stat pointer offset within item structure\n0x5 - Rarity property value (set via Ordinal_10348)",
