      "comment": "Allocate and setup unit with item data. Resolves item attributes if needed.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract item data size from nItemType+2 offset (stored in EBP)\n2. If paItemData is NULL, resolve item data using nItemType base address and Ordinal_10883\n3. Call AllocateAndInitializeUnit with resolved item data and indices\n4. Apply item modifications via Ordinal_10882 to set item-specific data\n5. Check for special item properties via Ordinal_10754\n6. If special properties exist, call Ordinal_10708 to apply flags\n7. If nLogErrors flag set, call Ordinal_10707 to log event, then LogFiveBytePacket if error\n\nParameters:\nnItemType - Item type definition base address (contains size at +2, data ptr at +8)\npaItemData - Pointer to resolved item data array (or NULL to resolve internally)\nnItemVariation - Item variation/style identifier (16-bit masked from param_3)\nnItemIndex - Item slot/inventory index (16-bit masked from param_4)\nnLogErrors - Flag indicating whether to log errors (non-zero = log)\n\nReturns:\nPointer to newly allocated and configured unit structure (returned in EBX), or NULL on failure\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If paItemData is NULL, function resolves from nItemType+8 offset\n- Local array [ESP+0x10] used as temporary item data storage (6 dwords)\n- Item modifications only applied if item has property flags\n- Errors logged only if nLogErrors is non-zero\n- Note: Function uses 2 stack-allocated temporaries optimized away",
