      "comment": "Creates a unit with item data and configures skills based on unit type.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call Ordinal_10883 to process unit type and item parameters\n2. Get game context pointer (contains unit management data)\n3. Check if unit type is 0x04 (player unit)\n4. Find existing unit in hash table by ID from unit record\n5. If unit exists, trigger error log and exit (-1)\n6. Allocate and setup new unit with item data\n7. If allocation fails, trigger error log and exit (-1)\n8. Add unit to game context\n9. Get updated unit index after addition\n10. Configure skill data for newly created unit\n11. Check if unit has special skill attribute (0x36)\n12. If skill exists, clear attribute and apply skill transformations\n\nParameters:\npUnitRecord (int): Pointer to unit creation record containing:\n  - Offset +0x2: Unit type byte (0x04 = player unit)\n  - Offset +0x4: Unit ID for hash table lookup\n  - Offset +0x8: Item data pointer\n\nReturns:\nvoid: Function does not return on allocation failure (calls FUN_6fb9a10f exit)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If unit already exists in hash table, logs error at address 0x6fbca4e8\n- If unit allocation fails, logs error at address 0x6fbb3ee8\n- Calls must succeed or process terminates via FUN_6fb9a10f(-1)\n\nStructure Layout:\n| Offset | Size | Field Name | Type | Description |\n|--------|------|-----------|------|-------------|\n| +0x0 | 4 | dwUnknown | uint | Reserved/padding |\n| +0x2 | 1 | byUnitType | byte | Unit type (0x04=player) |\n| +0x3 | 1 | byReserved | byte | Reserved padding |\n| +0x4 | 4 | dwUnitId | uint | Unit identifier for lookups |\n| +0x8 | 4 | pItemData | void* | Item data pointer |",
