      "comment": "Create and initialize an item in the player's inventory.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract item metadata from pItemData structure (location byte at +2, database reference at +4, item descriptor at +8)\n2. Initialize item buffer with Ordinal_10883 (preprocessing step)\n3. Retrieve current game context via GetGameContext()\n4. Look up item unit in hash table using database reference\n5. If unit exists: remove old selection, unequip current item if necessary, delete from hash table\n6. Allocate new unit via AllocateAndSetupUnitWithItemData with item variation and index\n7. If allocation fails: log fatal error and terminate\n8. Check for equipped item (stat 0x36); if present, deequip old item\n9. Calculate target inventory slot via FindRoomForUnit\n10. Apply item mode (SetItemMode) and update visual state\n\nParameters:\npItemData (fastcall ECX): Pointer to item data structure\n  Offset +2: Item level/difficulty byte\n  Offset +4: Database item ID (dword)\n  Offset +8: Item descriptor bytes\n\nReturns:\nPointer to allocated unit/item (void*), or NULL on allocation failure\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Null unit lookup triggers direct allocation path\n- Equipped item (0x36) requires deequipment before repositioning\n- Item mode 5 with slot 0 indicates inventory placement\n- Function aborts (calls FUN_6fb9a10f(-1)) on allocation failure\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x02: Item level offset in structure\n0x04: Database ID offset in structure\n0x08: Item descriptor offset in structure\n0x84: Current unit offset in game context\n0x36: Equipped item stat ID\n0x20: Item mode value for inventory placement\n-1: Fatal error code to abort execution\n\nNote: Function uses 3 SSA temporaries (pdVar2, pdVar1, iVar3) optimized away by compiler",
