      "comment": "Places an item on the ground for a unit and initializes its properties.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate item structure is non-NULL\n2. Look up unit in hash table at offset +0xB\n3. Check unit's stored items (offset +0xC equals 1 for ground placement)\n4. Find target unit from item's offset +0x2F with unit type at +0x2D\n5. Validate target unit exists and unit ID is zero\n6. Retrieve item stat value from offset +0x84\n7. Initialize item properties and set item mode\n8. Apply transformations and validate item placement\n9. Create inventory record at provided coordinates\n10. Initialize item properties with stat buffers\n11. Check for special properties (offset 0x36) and apply if needed\n\nParameters:\npItem (int): Pointer to item structure containing placement data\n  - +0xB: Unit hash table reference\n  - +0x2D: Target unit type\n  - +0x2F: Target unit ID\n  - +0x84: Item stat value\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Asserts if item pointer is NULL\n- Asserts if target unit lookup fails\n- Asserts if item mode is not 1 (ground placement)\n- Asserts if target unit already has items\n- Validates item can be placed via Ordinal_10707 check\n\nRelated Functions:\n- FindUnitInHashTable() - Locate unit by ID\n- InitializeItemProperties() - Initialize item stats\n- RemoveUnitFromHashTable() - Clean up references",
