      "comment": "Iterates through unit item list and processes item properties based on type and flags.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if unit has items (unit->item_count at offset 0x84)\n2. If *unit == 0, fetch item handlers for types 1 and 3\n3. First iteration: Process items, check type (1 or 3) and flags\n4. If type==3 and flag bit 0x80 set OR type==1 and flag bit 0x01 set with param_1:\n   a. Fail if nFlags==0 (assertion)\n   b. Call Ordinal_10258 if *unit==0\n   c. Call Ordinal_10707 to check flag status (0x100, 0x171)\n   d. If result==0, call Ordinal_10524 (set item flag)\n   e. Call ProcessHandlerTable with nFlags\n   f. Call Ordinal_10954 to set flag bit 0x01\n5. Second iteration: Process items with same conditions\n6. Process item removal and handler cleanup\n7. If nDoUpdate, call Ordinal_10514 (update unit)\n8. If *unit==0 and handlers were fetched, restore handlers\n\nParameters:\npUnit (int *) - Pointer to unit structure, checked at offset [0] and accessed at [0x84]\nnDoUpdate (int) - Flag: if non-zero, triggers Ordinal_10514 update call\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Function returns nothing\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Assertion at 0x422 if nFlags==0 during type 1/3 processing\n- Assertion at 0x434 if item pointer is NULL\n- Handler restoration only occurs if *unit==0 initially\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x84 - Offset to item count in unit structure\n0x21 - Offset to unknown field in unit structure\n0x100, 0x171 - Flags for Ordinal_10707 call\n0x36 - Item flag being checked/modified\n0x01 - Flag bit mask for type 1 items\n0x80 - Flag bit mask for type 3 items\n0x422, 0x434 - Assertion codes",
      "tags": ["PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PARAM_2", "SRC_Item.cpp", "MOD_UNIT", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
