      "api_count": 27,
      "api_calls": ["IsItemNormalQuality", "FogAssert", "GetItemStatsTableOffset", "FogAssert", "GetGemItemModifierRecord", "FogAssert", "ITEMS_GetItemLevel", "ApplyItemModifications", "ValidateItemTypeFlags", "FogAssert", "...+17 more"],
      "instructions": ["0x961D0|PUSH|EBX", "0x961D1|PUSH|ESI", "0x961D2|PUSH|EDI", "0x961D3|MOV|EDI, EDX", "0x961D5|TEST|EDI, EDI", "0x961D7|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0x961D9|JZ|0x6fb66423", "0x961DF|PUSH|ESI", "0x961E0|CALL|0x6fb983e0", "0x961E5|CMP|EAX, 0x14", "0x961E8|JNZ|0x6fb66282", "0x961EE|CMP|dword ptr [EDI], 0x4", "0x961F1|JZ|0x6fb66211", "0x961F3|PUSH|0x101", "0x961F8|PUSH|0x6fbca31c"],
      "comment": "Apply unit item effects and trigger effect handlers based on item type and ownership.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate item parameter is not null; return if null\n2. Determine if unit is item type (0x14):\n   a. If item type: validate item parent is UNIT_ITEM (type 0x4), validate item stats pointer [ESI+0x4], validate gem mods pointer [itemStats+0x7c]\n   b. Call ApplyItemEffects(2, NULL, pUnit, pGemMods, itemFlags, 0)\n3. If not item type:\n   a. Check if unit has property 0x4a (enchantment slot): if none, call RemoveUnitItemEffect(pItem, pUnit, 0); otherwise continue\n   b. For enchanted item: validate item parent, stats, gem mods; call ApplyItemEffects(5, pItem, pUnit, pGemMods, itemFlags, 0)\n   c. Call SetUnitItemEffect(pItem, pUnit, 0)\n4. Check if unit has property 0x4000 (effect applied flag); return if set\n5. Process effect ownership and applicability:\n   a. If item has no owner (*pItem[0] == 0): get owner from pItem[0x21], validate ownership compatibility\n   b. Otherwise: use force apply flag (nForceApply)\n6. Check property 0x100 (another effect flag); return early if set and nForceApply is 0\n7. Call SetItemOwnerEffect(pItem, pUnit, dwEffectState) with computed effect state\n8. Iterate through g_dwHandlerCount handlers: for each matching handler, call handler function with appropriate unit/item\n\nParameters:\n- pUnit (ECX, int *): Unit pointer (player/monster/item); nullptr if effect applies to item only\n- pItem (EDX, int *): Item structure pointer; validation required\n- dwEffectMode (unused, dword): Intended for effect mode but not used in current implementation\n- nForceApply (stack, int): Force effect application (0=normal checks, nonzero=skip 0x100 check)\n\nReturns:\n- void; effects applied as side effect via ordinal calls\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If pItem is null, function returns immediately without processing\n- Item type (0x14) has different effect chain than enchanted items\n- Phantom handlers with null function pointer are skipped\n- Property 0x4000 indicates item effects already applied; returns early\n- Force apply flag allows bypassing property 0x100 checks\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x14: Unit type constant for UNIT_ITEM (identifies item entities)\n- 0x4: UNIT_ITEM parent type validation constant\n- 0x4a: Property index for item enchantment slots\n- 0x7c: Offset to gem modifications pointer within item stats\n- 0x4000: Property flag indicating item effects already applied\n- 0x100: Property flag for effect state; blocks reapplication when set\n- 0x2d: Property for unit possession/ownership check\n- 0x138, 0x144, 0x11c: Property validation codes for assertions",
      "tags": ["PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Inventory", "SRC_Item.cpp", "MOD_UNIT", "PARAM_4", "UNIT_ITEM", "STRUCT_Other", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
