      "instructions": ["0x967E0|PUSH|EBX", "0x967E1|PUSH|EBP", "0x967E2|PUSH|ESI", "0x967E3|MOV|ESI, dword ptr [ESP + 0x18]", "0x967E7|AND|ECX, 0xffff", "0x967ED|PUSH|EDI", "0x967EE|PUSH|ECX", "0x967EF|MOV|EDI, EDX", "0x967F1|PUSH|ESI", "0x967F2|CALL|0x6fb98e2a", "0x967F7|AND|EDI, 0xffff", "0x967FD|PUSH|EDI", "0x967FE|PUSH|ESI", "0x967FF|CALL|0x6fb98e24", "0x96804|MOV|EBP, dword ptr [ESP + 0x18]"],
      "comment": "Validates inventory insertion position and updates game state if item added to player's current inventory.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate inventory object exists (offset 0x84 of pInventory pointer)\n2. Call ordinal functions to set X/Y coordinates\n3. Check item can be placed at grid position via Ordinal_10242\n4. If valid placement, calculate item stats (damage table, stat indexes, game state)\n5. Call Ordinal_10249 to insert item into inventory grid\n6. If insertion successful and current player context:\n   a. If grid position == 0x01: Update damage stats for item at slot\n   b. If grid position == 0x03: Apply equipment effects (helmet/shield check via 0x80 offset, spawn appropriate game mode state)\n7. Return with no errors\n\nParameters:\nwXCoord (ushort) - Grid X coordinate (0x0000-0xFFFF range, masked with 0xFFFF)\nwYCoord (ushort) - Grid Y coordinate (0x0000-0xFFFF range, masked with 0xFFFF)\nbGridPosition (byte) - Item grid position type: 0x01=equipment, 0x03=quest items\npInventory (int *) - Pointer to inventory structure (offset 0x84 contains inventory object)\npUnit (int *) - Pointer to unit/item structure with stat offsets\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Updates inventory state in-place, does not return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\nMagic constant 0x60c - Assert on missing inventory object\nMagic constant 0x108f - Assert on missing item stats\nDamage table lookup at (pUnit + 4) with stat index from offset 0x28\nGame mode check compares 0x80 offset: 0x20747368 (hst ) or 0x20326671 (fq2) for quest triggers",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Inventory", "SRC_Item.cpp", "MOD_UNIT", "STRUCT_Skill", "PARAM_5", "STRUCT_Other", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
