      "instructions": ["0x96960|SUB|ESP, 0x1c", "0x96963|LEA|EAX, [ESP + 0x4]", "0x96967|PUSH|EBX", "0x96968|PUSH|ESI", "0x96969|PUSH|EDI", "0x9696A|MOV|EDI, ECX", "0x9696C|XOR|ECX, ECX", "0x9696E|PUSH|EAX", "0x9696F|MOV|CL, byte ptr [EDI + 0x2]", "0x96972|PUSH|0x0", "0x96974|SUB|ECX, 0x8", "0x96977|LEA|EDX, [EDI + 0x8]", "0x9697A|PUSH|ECX", "0x9697B|PUSH|EDX", "0x9697C|CALL|0x6fb98ddc"],
      "comment": "Process item insertion into player inventory, allocating new unit or reusing existing slot\nValidates item placement location, applies item properties, updates game state\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract item attributes from source data (position byte, stats buffer)\n2. Locate existing unit in hash table via item ID\n3. If unit exists and slot available (iVar1 == 0): apply item to slot\n4. Else if unit exists but no slot: remove old unit, allocate new unit with fresh state\n5. Check inventory index (local_8): if 0xFF, log error and terminate\n6. Insert item into player inventory at calculated position\n7. Apply item effects via ProcessUnitItemEffect\n8. Update unit stat 0x36 (item flag), cascading effect chain\n9. Validate game state consistency\n\nParameters:\npSourceItemData (ECX): pointer to item source structure containing:\n  +0x02: byte - item position offset\n  +0x04: dword - item ID for hash lookup\n  +0x08: byte[N] - item stats buffer\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Triggers game shutdown (Ordinal_10023) on critical validation failures\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Allocation failure: logs error at line 0x682, calls FUN_6fb9a10f(-1) to exit\n- Invalid inventory page 0xFF: logs error at line 0x690, returns\n- Null unit pointer check: logs error at line 0x1540, calls FUN_6fb9a10f(-1) to exit\n- Stat cascade chain: Ordinal_10480 returns non-zero when stat 0x36 requires propagation\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x02, 0x04, 0x08 - item data offsets\n0x36 - item stat index triggering cascade chain\n0xff - invalid inventory page marker\n0x682, 0x690, 0x1540 - error line numbers from source file",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "SRC_Item.cpp", "MOD_UNIT", "PARAM_1", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
