      "api_calls": ["FogAssert", "QueueLogMessage", "FogAssert", "RemoveItemFromInventory", "GetItemStatsTableOffset", "QueueLogMessage", "FogAssert", "GetItemQualityLevel", "GetInventoryPageFromUnit", "InitializeMapTileArray", "...+18 more"],
      "instructions": ["0x96B00|SUB|ESP, 0x8", "0x96B03|PUSH|EBX", "0x96B04|PUSH|EBP", "0x96B05|PUSH|ESI", "0x96B06|PUSH|EDI", "0x96B07|MOV|EDI, ECX", "0x96B09|TEST|EDI, EDI", "0x96B0B|JNZ|0x6fb66b2b", "0x96B0D|PUSH|0x6ab", "0x96B12|PUSH|0x6fbca31c", "0x96B17|PUSH|0x6fbb6df8", "0x96B1C|CALL|0x6fb99a7a", "0x96B21|ADD|ESP, 0xc", "0x96B24|PUSH|-0x1", "0x96B26|CALL|0x6fb9a10f"],
      "comment": "Remove item from inventory grid and update unit/player state\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate input item node (abort if NULL)\n2. Find source unit by ID and class type\n3. Find destination grid item\n4. If destination not found, check player mode and error return\n5. If destination found:\n   a. Validate source unit inventory exists\n   b. Check item at grid location matches destination\n   c. Get color property from item\n   d. Get game state\n   e. Call SetItemProperty with color/game state/mode flag\n   f. Update UI state\n   g. Execute item/unit transform handlers (0x36 item bit test)\n   h. If transform handlers found, execute them and update UI\n   i. Handle destination mode (0x20 or 0x01 bit):\n      - Mode 0x20: Remove from hash table, delete/drop item\n      - Mode 0x01: Create new item with grid properties, set visual mode\n   j. Update grid item visual state (0xFF marker)\n   k. Update hash tables and unit flags\n   l. Update network state if unit is player\n6. If destination found but unit not player, error return\n7. If destination not found and player mode, ignore\n\nParameters:\nnItemNode (ECX) - Item node offset containing:\n  +0x03 - Mode flags (0x01=player, 0x02=cursor)\n  +0x0B - Grid item handle\n  +0x0F - Grid Y position (word)\n  +0x11 - Grid X position (word)\n  +0x13 - Grid Y position (word, duplicate)\n  +0x2D - Unit class type (byte)\n  +0x2E - Item color/quality (byte)\n  +0x2F - Unit ID (dword)\n  +0x21 - Inventory handle (dword)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Updates unit/player state in-place, may call exit handlers\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- NULL input node triggers immediate error\n- Missing inventory handle triggers error\n- Grid item mismatch is fatal error\n- Player deletion triggers view update via FUN_6fb8d210\n- Cursor deletion triggers view update via FUN_6fb8f0c0",
      "tags": ["PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "SRC_Item.cpp", "MOD_UNIT", "PARAM_1", "STRUCT_Other", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
