      "comment": "Remove item from player inventory and handle state updates.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize item removal tracking from input parameters\n2. Find unit by inventory handle and find owner unit\n3. Validate owner exists; exit if not\n4. Get unit inventory handle and validate non-null\n5. Find item in inventory by handle\n6. If item not found: log error and exit\n7. If item mismatch: log fatal error and exit\n8. Extract item state and call Ordinal_10409 for state updates\n9. Call Ordinal_10250 to track removal\n10. Process removal via Ordinal_10840, Ordinal_10707\n11. Update unit state via Ordinal_10524, Ordinal_10514, ProcessHandlerTable\n12. Check item mode via Ordinal_10754 flags\n13. If 0x20 mode: RemoveUnitFromHashTable, reconstruct via FUN_6fb670d0\n14. Otherwise: SetItemMode, finalize via Ordinal_10261/10262\n15. Update viewport via FUN_6fb8f0c0\n16. Check/remove duplicate items via Ordinal_10480\n17. Validate network context if needed\n\nParameters:\n  pItemData (int *) - Item data with offsets: 0x2=mode, 0x4=owner, 0x8=subtype, 0x9=inventory, 0xd=flags\n\nReturns:\n  void - Completes or calls fatal error handler\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  Owner unit validation, null inventory check, mode 0x02 early return, item reconstruction on 0x20 flag",
