      "instructions": ["0x970D0|SUB|ESP, 0x18", "0x970D3|XOR|EAX, EAX", "0x970D5|PUSH|EBX", "0x970D6|PUSH|EBP", "0x970D7|PUSH|ESI", "0x970D8|PUSH|EDI", "0x970D9|MOV|EDI, ECX", "0x970DB|MOV|ESI, EDX", "0x970DD|MOV|AL, byte ptr [EDI + 0x2]", "0x970E0|MOV|EBP, EAX", "0x970E2|SUB|EBP, 0xd", "0x970E5|TEST|ESI, ESI", "0x970E7|JNZ|0x6fb670fd", "0x970E9|LEA|ECX, [ESP + 0x10]", "0x970ED|PUSH|ECX"],
      "comment": "Create a new inventory item unit within an inventory array\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract stat field type from parent unit (byte at offset 0x2, subtract 0xd)\n2. If inventory array pointer is NULL, call Ordinal_10883 to populate default inventory from parent unit\n3. Allocate and initialize new unit with specified item type and quality using AllocateAndInitializeUnit\n4. Copy stat field to new unit via Ordinal_10882 (type 0x57 stat copy)\n5. Query stat field value at index 3 with Ordinal_10754 to check for item sockets\n6. If stat field exists (non-zero return):\n   - Set stat type 2 via Ordinal_10708 to enable stat tracking\n   - If nQuantity parameter is non-zero, attempt to set stat 0x10 (quantity) via Ordinal_10707 with value 0x3ee\n   - If stat assignment fails, log sync packet (command 0x37) with parent unit ID via LogFiveBytePacket\n7. Return newly created unit pointer\n\nParameters:\n- nUnit (int): Parent unit containing stat field at offset 0xd and unit ID at offset 0x4\n- pInventoryArray (void *): Inventory data array pointer with 6 slots, indexed by item properties; if NULL generates default from parent\n- dwItemType (uint): Item type field (16-bit), masked with 0xffff before use\n- dwItemQuality (uint): Item quality field (16-bit), masked with 0xffff before use\n- nQuantity (int): Quantity to assign to item; if 0, skips quantity stat assignment step\n\nReturns:\n- void * pointer to newly allocated and initialized unit on success\n- Stat assignment may fail without affecting unit creation or return value\n- Log packet sent to server when quantity stat fails to set (indicates sync issue)",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Inventory", "SRC_Item.cpp", "MOD_UNIT", "STRUCT_Skill", "PARAM_5", "STRUCT_ItemData", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
