      "comment": "Processes unit items found via node data lookup and update flags\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Unpack unit pointer and type byte from pNodeData structure\n2. Call FindUnitInHashTable with unpacked type and pointer values\n3. If unit found (non-NULL), call ProcessUnitItemProperties with unit and nDoUpdate flag\n4. Return void (caller responsible for handling return values)\n\nParameters:\npNodeData (int *) - IMPLICIT ECX: Pointer to node data structure containing:\n  - Offset +1: BYTE - Item type identifier (passed as uint to hash table lookup)\n  - Offset +3: DWORD - Unit pointer value to lookup in hash table\nnDoUpdate (int) - IMPLICIT EDX: Flag indicating whether to update unit properties (0=no update, non-zero=update)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value, side effects via ProcessUnitItemProperties\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Function returns immediately if FindUnitInHashTable returns NULL\n- Uses __fastcall convention: pNodeData in ECX, nDoUpdate in EDX, callee cleanup (pop ESI before ret)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x1 - Byte offset in pNodeData for item type\n0x3 - Dword offset in pNodeData for unit pointer\n\nRelated Functions:\n- FindUnitInHashTable(0x..., byte) - Retrieves unit from hash table\n- ProcessUnitItemProperties(int*, int) - Processes unit item list and flags",
