      "comment": "Process a unit entry from hash table with optional secondary operation\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract unit reference from entry struct at offset +3 (DWORD)\n2. Extract primary index from entry struct at offset +1 (BYTE)\n3. Call FindUnitInHashTable to locate unit by reference and index\n4. If unit found (non-null result), extract secondary parameter from entry struct at offset +2 (BYTE)\n5. Call FUN_6fb671e0 with found unit pointer in ECX and secondary parameter in EDX\n6. Return via RET instruction\n\nParameters:\npEntry (ECX register): Void pointer to entry structure - contains unit reference, indices, and parameters\n  - Offset +0: Unknown field (not accessed in this function)\n  - Offset +1: BYTE - Primary index for hash table lookup\n  - Offset +2: BYTE - Secondary parameter passed to FUN_6fb671e0\n  - Offset +3: DWORD - Unit reference identifier used for hash lookup\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No explicit return value\n\nStructure Layout (Entry):\nOffset | Size | Field Name | Type | Description\n0x00   | 1    | (unused)   | byte | Unknown field\n0x01   | 1    | byIndex    | byte | Primary lookup index for hash table\n0x02   | 1    | byParam    | byte | Secondary parameter for operation\n0x03   | 4    | dwUnitRef  | dword| Unit reference identifier\n\nNotes:\nCalling convention: __fastcall - pEntry passed in ECX register\nStructure type unknown - define appropriately when discovered\nNo error handling - if unit not found, function silently returns\n\nRelated Functions:\n- FindUnitInHashTable() - Locates unit by reference and index in hash table\n- FUN_6fb671e0() - Performs operation on found unit with secondary parameter",
