      "instructions": ["0x971E0|SUB|ESP, 0x68", "0x971E3|PUSH|EBX", "0x971E4|PUSH|ESI", "0x971E5|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0x971E7|XOR|EBX, EBX", "0x971E9|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x20], EDX", "0x971ED|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x34], EBX", "0x971F1|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [ESI]", "0x971F3|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x10], EBX", "0x971F7|CMP|EAX, EBX", "0x971F9|JNZ|0x6fb678a1", "0x971FF|CALL|0x6fb62880", "0x97204|CMP|ESI, EAX", "0x97206|JNZ|0x6fb678a1", "0x9720C|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [ESI + 0x84]"],
      "comment": "Processes item effects for a game object, handling item placement, state updates, and effect application.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Verify unit is valid by checking against game context\n2. Retrieve unit state from offset 0x84, exit if zero\n3. Query equipped item slot counts (6, 8, 10) and store initial values\n4. Check for primary and secondary items (Ordinal_10321, Ordinal_10322):\n   - Retrieve IDs via Ordinal_10957, save state with Ordinal_10963\n   - Compare with current selection (Ordinal_10323) and set slot marker\n5. Initialize 11-element item flag array (local_2c)\n6. First loop: Process ground items in unit (Ordinal_10257) for 11 iterations:\n   - Check flags 0x100/0x7ff (Ordinal_10707) and 0x4000/0x801\n   - If both clear, mark flag array, set 0x4000 flag (Ordinal_10708)\n   - Get item color (Ordinal_10442), remove from inventory (Ordinal_10290)\n   - If item class==1: Clear flag (0x100/0x171), calculate position\n   - Call ProcessUnitItemEffect if required, process handler table\n7. Secondary loop: Iterate ground items for item placement until no changes:\n   - Check flags 0x100/0x818 and 0x4000/0x81a\n   - Call Ordinal_10756 to validate placement\n   - If Ordinal_10783 returns 0, apply item effect\n   - Else find alternative slot via Ordinal_10731 and retry\n8. Process special items (class==5):\n   - Check flags 0x100/0x849 and 0x4000/0x84a\n   - Call Ordinal_10871 if flags clear\n9. Process container items using Ordinal_10277 for linked list traversal:\n   - Validate class!=4, check flags 0x100/0x85b\n   - Apply placement logic similar to loop 2\n   - Handle 0x4000/0x86d flag cases\n10. Update slot counts to minimum of (current, Ordinal_10564/565/566)\n11. Restore primary/secondary items using Ordinal_10961/962\n12. If any items were changed, call cleanup functions\n\nParameters:\npUnit (ECX): UnitAny pointer - target unit object to process\ndwMonsterId (EDX): dword - monster/unit ID for effect context\n\nReturns: void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Function exits early if unit is null or game context check fails\n- Item class 1 triggers position update and handler table processing\n- Characters 0x0B and 0x0C (item effect immunity flags) skip processing\n- Container items (class==5) handled separately from regular items\n- Slot count minimums prevent inventory overflow\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x84 - Unit state offset\n0x100, 0x7ff - Ground item flag set (bits 8-10)\n0x4000 - Item active state flag\n0x801, 0x81a, 0x84a - Specific item state flags\n0x100/0x171 - Item processing flag\n0x0B, 0x0C - Item effect immunity character codes\n0xB (11) - Maximum item slots in array",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "SRC_Item.cpp", "MOD_UNIT", "STRUCT_Room2", "STRUCT_ItemData", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData", "STRUCT_StatList", "PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Path", "PARAM_2", "STRUCT_Skill", "PROP_LOOPHEAVY"]
