      "api_calls": ["FogAssert", "UNITS_MaskFlags", "FogAssert", "SetItemDataValue", "ITEMS_SetItemControl", "FogAssert", "AddItemToInventory", "QueueLogMessage", "QueueLogMessage", "GetArrayElementPtr", "...+15 more"],
      "instructions": ["0x978C0|SUB|ESP, 0xc", "0x978C3|PUSH|EBX", "0x978C4|PUSH|EBP", "0x978C5|PUSH|ESI", "0x978C6|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0x978C8|TEST|ESI, ESI", "0x978CA|PUSH|EDI", "0x978CB|JNZ|0x6fb678eb", "0x978CD|PUSH|0x90c", "0x978D2|PUSH|0x6fbca31c", "0x978D7|PUSH|0x6fbb6df8", "0x978DC|CALL|0x6fb99a7a", "0x978E1|ADD|ESP, 0xc", "0x978E4|PUSH|-0x1", "0x978E6|CALL|0x6fb9a10f"],
      "comment": "Processes item placement in player or NPC inventory with validation and equipment effect handling.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate input item pointer (pItem != NULL), abort if invalid (line 0x90c)\n2. Get current game state context and retrieve unit owner and item target data\n3. Find item in inventory hash table (dwUnitType @ offset 0xb)\n4. If item not found, initialize item properties and add to inventory\n5. If item exists, check item modification flag (offset 0x21) with Ordinal_10754\n6. If not modified, set item mode (type @ offset 0x2d, byte @ offset 0x2e)\n7. If modified, remove existing item and reinitialize properties\n8. Apply item mode byte (offset 0x2) to inventory system via Ordinal_10690\n9. Retrieve inventory collection pointer from unit->pPath (offset 0x2d)\n10. Determine inventory slot mode (0x03=normal, 0x04=special, 0x05=alt) based on cInventoryType\n11. Validate item can fit via Ordinal_10242, abort if inventory full (line 0x92a)\n12. Insert item into inventory structure via Ordinal_10253\n13. Validate insertion success, abort on error\n14. Update unit state and recalculate stats via FUN_6fb950d0, FUN_6fb92a60\n15. For player/NPC units (dwUnitType 0-1), apply item equipment effects\n16. If owner == current player, record inventory slot mode to g_wInventorySlotMode\n17. Apply item spell effects via Ordinal_10261/10262\n18. Process unit item effects and update game viewport state\n\nParameters:\npItem (UnitAny *) - Item to place in inventory, passed in ECX (__fastcall)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Item placed in inventory or assertion failure if validation fails\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If pItem is NULL, aborts with assertion (line 0x90c)\n- If inventory full or insertion fails, aborts with assertion\n- Magic numbers: 0x90c/0x918/0x92a/0x955 are assertion line numbers\n- Inventory types: 0x04=equipment slot, 0x05=alternate slot\n- Unit types: 0-1=player/NPC, others trigger assertion (line 0x955)\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset | Size | Field Name         | Type     | Description\n0x1    | 1    | byClass           | byte     | Unit class affecting capabilities\n0x2    | 1    | cInventoryType    | char     | Inventory slot type (0x04/0x05)\n0x3    | 1    | byUnknown         | byte     | Unknown flag\n0xb    | 4    | dwItemTargetId    | uint     | Target unit ID for item\n0xf    | 2    | wInventoryMode    | ushort   | Current inventory mode\n0x21   | 4    | dwModificationFlag| uint     | Item modification indicator\n0x2d   | 1    | byItemType        | byte     | Item type identifier\n0x2e   | 1    | byItemQuality     | byte     | Item quality/rarity\n0x2f   | 4    | dwOwnerUnitId     | uint     | Owner unit ID",
      "tags": ["PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Inventory", "SRC_Item.cpp", "MOD_UNIT", "PARAM_1", "STRUCT_Other", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
