      "instructions": ["0x97BC0|SUB|ESP, 0x24", "0x97BC3|PUSH|EBX", "0x97BC4|PUSH|EBP", "0x97BC5|PUSH|ESI", "0x97BC6|PUSH|EDI", "0x97BC7|MOV|EDI, ECX", "0x97BC9|LEA|EAX, [ESP + 0x1c]", "0x97BCD|XOR|ECX, ECX", "0x97BCF|PUSH|EAX", "0x97BD0|MOV|CL, byte ptr [EDI + 0x2]", "0x97BD3|PUSH|0x0", "0x97BD5|SUB|ECX, 0xd", "0x97BD8|LEA|EDX, [EDI + 0xd]", "0x97BDB|PUSH|ECX", "0x97BDC|PUSH|EDX"],
      "comment": "Insert an item into a unit's inventory with validation and effect processing.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract item parameters (offset, class, mode) from input record via Ordinal_10883\n2. Get game context unit (current player) and locate owner/target units by ID\n3. Create new inventory item or verify existing item compatibility with Ordinal_10754\n4. Validate item path exists (pPath at [pUnit+0x84]) and add to inventory via Ordinal_10242\n5. Process item effects on inserting unit and owner via Ordinal_10253\n6. Handle special cases: slot-specific assignments for druid/necro (modes 4-5)\n7. Trigger mouse move update and finish inventory operations\n\nParameters:\npItemData: Pointer to item insertion data record (ECX) with fields at offsets:\n  +0x02: item class/type\n  +0x03: class-specific mode (0-1 = normal, 4-5 = druid/necro slots)\n  +0x04: inventory unit ID\n  +0x08: item location type\n  +0x09: owner unit ID\n  +0x0D: item base offset in structure\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Displays error messages on validation failure via Ordinal_10023\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Line 0x6fb67c0d: Skip item creation if unit already exists (reuse path)\n- Line 0x6fb67d18: Force removal of conflicting item if present\n- Line 0x6fb67d78: Only process item effects if offset < 0x0B\n- Line 0x6fb67de9: Special slot assignment for druid/necro unit types\n- Mode 0x0B (druid) maps to g_wItemSlotOther\n- Mode 0x0C (necro) maps to g_wItemSlotDruid\n\nNote: Function uses 6 SSA temporaries optimized away by compiler (pUVar5, uVar3-4, uVar7, iVar6, bVar1, pvVar2)",
      "tags": ["PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PROP_NOCALLER", "SRC_Item.cpp", "MOD_UNIT", "STRUCT_Skill", "STRUCT_ItemData", "PARAM_1", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
