      "comment": "Removes an item from a unit's inventory and handles cascading updates.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate input nItemData pointer (non-null, accessible)\n2. Get game context and locate target unit by ID at offset +0x2f\n3. Retrieve unit's item container/path at unit+0x84\n4. Find item node in container using operation code at nItemData+0x2\n5. Validate item node found, assert on failure\n6. Check if item at correct container location\n7. Call Ordinal_10871 to mark item for removal\n8. Update unit state if player or monster unit\n9. Handle destination inventory item creation/reuse\n10. Insert item into destination inventory, update effects\n11. Cleanup source item, update game state\n\nParameters:\nnItemData (int) - Pointer to item operation structure with unit ID (+0x2f), operation mode code (+0x2), item index (+0x2d), item properties offset\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Updates game state in place; terminates with fatal error on validation failure\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Forces item removal from source before reinsertion (prevents duplicates)\n- Updates player UI when player unit affected\n- Recreates destination inventory item if missing\n- Handles both player and monster unit types",
