      "api_calls": ["FogAssert", "FogAssert", "FogAssert", "GetArrayElementPtr", "UpdateInventoryAfterItemRemoval", "GetInventoryLocationValue", "RemoveItemFromInventory", "FogAssert", "FogAssert", "ClearInventoryLocationSlot", "...+20 more"],
      "instructions": ["0x98820|SUB|ESP, 0x8", "0x98823|PUSH|EBX", "0x98824|PUSH|EBP", "0x98825|PUSH|ESI", "0x98826|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0x98828|TEST|ESI, ESI", "0x9882A|PUSH|EDI", "0x9882B|JNZ|0x6fb6884b", "0x9882D|PUSH|0xaa4", "0x98832|PUSH|0x6fbca31c", "0x98837|PUSH|0x6fbb6df8", "0x9883C|CALL|0x6fb99a7a", "0x98841|ADD|ESP, 0xc", "0x98844|PUSH|-0x1", "0x98846|CALL|0x6fb9a10f"],
      "comment": "Processes an inventory item transaction (equipping, unequipping, adding to inventory)\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate command structure pointer (pCmd != NULL)\n2. Get current game player unit via GetGameContext()\n3. Extract unit from hash table using ID/type from pCmd[0x2f] and pCmd[0x2d]\n4. Validate unit found and type is empty (dwUnitType == 0)\n5. Get inventory container from unit[2].pPath\n6. Validate inventory exists (not NULL)\n7. Find/create item slot using Ordinal_10257(inventory, pCmd[2])\n8. Return if no item found (slot empty)\n9. Update item via Ordinal_10290, Ordinal_10255\n10. Get removal handle via Ordinal_10243, validate it matches item\n11. Remove item from old location via Ordinal_10254\n12. Call Ordinal_10871 to attach item to unit\n13. If unit is valid (not NULL):\n    a. Process item effects via Ordinal_10707, Ordinal_10524, etc.\n    b. ProcessGameObjectItemEffects and ProcessUnitItemProperties\n14. If unit is current player:\n    a. Sync network state via HandleNetworkValidationAndServerConnection\n    b. Set action state flags (g_wPlayerActionStateHorse or g_wPlayerActionStateMetalOrb to 0)\n    c. Check for skill restrictions via Ordinal_10754(pCmd[0x21])\n    d. Process item properties or create new item via InitializeItemProperties\n    e. Update item effects and modes\n15. Otherwise validate unit found in hash table matches retrieved unit\n\nNote: Function uses 2 stack-allocated temporaries optimized away in decompilation (piVar1, iVar2 exist only in assembly).\n\nParameters:\n- pCmd (int *, IMPLICIT in ECX): Command structure containing:\n  - [0x1]: byte - item slot/property type\n  - [0x2]: byte - inventory type (0x04 = horse, 0x05 = metal orb)\n  - [0x2d]: byte - unit type\n  - [0x2e]: byte - color/mode value\n  - [0x2f]: dword - unit ID\n  - [0xb]: dword - container unit ID\n  - [0x21]: dword - skill/property ID\n\nReturns:\n- void (no return value)\n- Returns early if: item not found, item check fails, skill restrictions prevent action\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If pCmd is NULL, calls Ordinal_10023 with error string and calls FUN_6fb9a10f(-1) to terminate\n- If unit type is non-zero, unit not in inventory, or item validation fails: same error handling\n- Handles both player character and summon unit types\n- Action state flags differ: 0x04 (horse), 0x05 (metal orb)",
      "tags": ["UNIT_PLAYER", "PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "STRUCT_Item", "SRC_Item.cpp", "MOD_UNIT", "PARAM_1", "STRUCT_Other", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
