      "comment": "Adds an item to player inventory and updates associated game state.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Retrieve item handle parameters and validate inventory path exists\n2. Find inventory node for item in hash table by handle\n3. Get next available inventory slot\n4. Update player unit with inventory reference\n5. Apply item mode and property updates to player\n6. If item is for player's current equipment:\n   - Clear item slot global variables based on slot type (0x04=other, 0x05=druid)\n   - Check item flag 0x20 (equipped) - if set, apply item to player equipment\n   - Otherwise create new unit in inventory and link item to it\n   - Update network state and UI\n   - Process item visual effects and equipment requirements\n7. Otherwise update remote player inventory and remove item from source\n\nParameters:\n- nItemHandle (IMPLICIT ECX): Item handle value containing:\n  - [nItemHandle + 0xD]: Item data offset\n  - [nItemHandle + 0x8]: Unit index\n  - [nItemHandle + 0x9]: Unit type (inventory reference)\n  - [nItemHandle + 0x4]: Source container handle\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset | Size | Field Name | Type | Description\n-------|------|------------|------|-------------\n+0x0   | 4    | dwUnitType | dword| Unit type identifier\n+0x84  | 4    | pPath      | ptr  | Inventory path/node\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x04 - Slot type: other inventory\n0x05 - Slot type: druid-specific inventory\n0x20 - Item flag: equipped/active state\n0x36 - Item property identifier\n0x100 - Item effect validation range\n0x171 - Item effect range check value\n0x0FF - Slot index mask (8-bit unsigned)\n0xAFF - Error code for missing inventory\n0xB0A - Error code for missing item node\n0xB0B - Error code for item mismatch\n0xB24 - Error code for inventory unit creation\n0xB37 - Error code for inventory verification\n0x35A - Error code for slot item null pointer\n\nRelated Functions:\n- GetGameContext() - Returns current player context\n- FindUnitInHashTable() - Searches unit by handle\n- ProcessUnitItemProperties() - Updates item attributes on unit\n- CreateUnitInInventory() - Creates new inventory container unit\n- InitializeGameUIState() - Refreshes UI display\n- ProcessGameObjectItemEffects() - Applies visual/effect state",
      "tags": ["PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "STRUCT_Item", "PROP_NOCALLER", "SRC_Item.cpp", "MOD_UNIT", "STRUCT_Skill", "PARAM_1", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
