      "instructions": ["0x98EB0|PUSH|ECX", "0x98EB1|PUSH|EBX", "0x98EB2|PUSH|EBP", "0x98EB3|PUSH|ESI", "0x98EB4|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0x98EB6|TEST|ESI, ESI", "0x98EB8|PUSH|EDI", "0x98EB9|JNZ|0x6fb68ed9", "0x98EBB|PUSH|0xc1e", "0x98EC0|PUSH|0x6fbca31c", "0x98EC5|PUSH|0x6fbb6df8", "0x98ECA|CALL|0x6fb99a7a", "0x98ECF|ADD|ESP, 0xc", "0x98ED2|PUSH|-0x1", "0x98ED4|CALL|0x6fb9a10f"],
      "comment": "Process equipping an item for a player unit.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate pointer is not NULL (exit with assertion if invalid)\n2. Check item command flag 0x40 (quest item requirement)\n3. If flag set, find owner unit in hash table, validate unit type is player (0)\n4. If flag not set, check for flag 0x80 and return early if set\n5. Find item unit in hash table with unit type 4 (item)\n6. Check command flag 0x01 (add to inventory mode)\n7. If flag not set: set item mode, assign item to unit with ordinal call\n8. If flag set: remove existing item from hash table, initialize new item with proper ilvl\n9. Verify both item and inventory exist\n10. Determine inventory slot: 3 for normal items, 4 for quest items (0x0B or 0x0C)\n11. Add item to inventory at calculated slot\n12. Check for conflicts, force remove conflicting items if needed\n13. Insert item into inventory list\n14. Update player properties, refresh item effects, process equipped bonuses\n15. For body/finger slots: update mouse, send input events to other units\n\nParameters:\npItemCmd - pointer to item command structure containing:\n  +0x02: byte - inventory slot or body location (0x04=body, 0x05=finger)\n  +0x03: byte - source inventory mode\n  +0x0B: dword - item unit ID\n  +0x0F: word - item level/quality\n  +0x21: dword - flags (0x01=add mode, 0x40=quest, 0x80=cancel)\n  +0x2D: byte - owner unit type\n  +0x2E: byte - drop location\n  +0x2F: dword - owner unit ID\n\nReturns:\nvoid (exits with assertion on error conditions)",
      "tags": ["UNIT_PLAYER", "PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Inventory", "STRUCT_Item", "SRC_Item.cpp", "MOD_UNIT", "PARAM_1", "STRUCT_Other", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
