      "api_calls": ["FogAssert", "FogAssert", "FogAssert", "GetArrayElementPtr", "UpdateInventoryAfterItemRemoval", "GetInventoryLocationValue", "RemoveItemFromInventory", "FogAssert", "FogAssert", "UpdateUnitSetItemBonuses", "...+19 more"],
      "instructions": ["0x99140|SUB|ESP, 0x8", "0x99143|PUSH|EBX", "0x99144|PUSH|EBP", "0x99145|PUSH|ESI", "0x99146|PUSH|EDI", "0x99147|MOV|EDI, ECX", "0x99149|TEST|EDI, EDI", "0x9914B|JNZ|0x6fb6916b", "0x9914D|PUSH|0xbbc", "0x99152|PUSH|0x6fbca31c", "0x99157|PUSH|0x6fbb6df8", "0x9915C|CALL|0x6fb99a7a", "0x99161|ADD|ESP, 0xc", "0x99164|PUSH|-0x1", "0x99166|CALL|0x6fb9a10f"],
      "comment": "Add an item to a unit's inventory with full validation and UI updates.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate pItemData is not NULL, return -1 if invalid\n2. FindUnitInHashTable(unit_id, unit_type) - Locate unit in database\n3. Validate unit exists and is a player character\n4. Get unit's inventory handle from unit[0x21]\n5. Validate inventory is initialized\n6. Ordinal_10257(inventory, slot) - Allocate/locate item in inventory\n7. Ordinal_10290(inventory, item) - Clear item from old location\n8. FUN_6fb950d0(unit) - Call update handler on unit\n9. FUN_6fb937c0(unit, slot) - Call skill cleanup with item offset\n10. Ordinal_10255(unit, inv, &item, slot) - Update item location\n11. Ordinal_10243(inv, item) - Get item reference\n12. Ordinal_10871(unit, item, 1) - Set item container binding\n13. Ordinal_10707(item, 0x100, 0x171, label) - Check armor class\n14. Ordinal_10524(unit, item) - Add item stats if armor valid\n15. Ordinal_10514(unit) - Update unit menus\n16. ProcessHandlerTable(unit, item, 0) - Process handlers\n17. Ordinal_10954(unit, item, 1) - Update visual effects\n18. Ordinal_10254(inv, slot) - Cleanup references\n19. Ordinal_10754(quest_flag, 1) - Check quest item flag\n20. If not quest: SetItemMode(item, 0, 0, 0, quality, 0) - Set appearance\n21. Ordinal_10720(item, mode) - Apply item visual mode\n22. If quest: RemoveUnitFromHashTable(item_id, 4) - Remove from old location\n23. GetGameContext() - Get current context\n24. If player unit: InitializeItemProperties(...) - Reinit item\n25. Ordinal_10690(item, 0) - Init item appearance\n26. Ordinal_10261(inv, item) - Update inventory display\n27. Ordinal_10262(inv) - Get inventory state\n28. FUN_6fb8f0c0(state) - Update UI\n29. Ordinal_10480(item, 0x36) - Check equipped state\n30. If equipped: Ordinal_10486(item, 0x36, 0) - Apply visual\n31. Ordinal_10474(item, state) - Apply skill mods\n32. Ordinal_10485(state) - Update progression\n33. Ordinal_10376(item) - Finalize equipment\n\nParameters:\n  pItemData (uint *) - Item data structure with offsets:\n    +0x01: Slot (byte)\n    +0x02: Location (byte)\n    +0x03: Mode (byte)\n    +0x0b: Item ID (dword)\n    +0x0f: Type (ushort)\n    +0x2d: Unit type (byte)\n    +0x2e: Quality (byte)\n    +0x2f: Unit ID (dword)\n    +0x21: Quest flag (dword)\n\nReturns:\n  void - Calls FUN_6fb9a10f(-1) on failure\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - NULL pItemData, missing inventory, non-player units trigger exit\n  - Item reference mismatch triggers exit\n  - Quest items handled with full reinitialization\n  - Player context affects UI update behavior\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x21 - Inventory handle field\n  0x2d - Unit type field\n  0x2f - Unit ID field\n  0x100 - Armor class constant\n  0x171 - Max item value constant\n  0x36 - Equipped state flag\n  0xbc1 - Assertion line for inventory\n  0xbc9 - Assertion line for item mismatch",
      "tags": ["UNIT_PLAYER", "PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "STRUCT_Item", "SRC_Item.cpp", "MOD_UNIT", "PARAM_1", "STRUCT_Other", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
