      "comment": "Add item to unit's inventory with validation and UI updates.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Resolve unit reference from param_1 offset 0x9 (type/class) and offset 0x8 (ID)\n2. Validate unit ID is not zero (type must be UNIT_PLAYER)\n3. Get inventory ID from unit at offset 0x84 (unit[0x21])\n4. Retrieve/allocate item slot using Ordinal_10257 with inventory ID and equipment slot\n5. Call FUN_6fb950d0 to process unit inventory state\n6. Call Ordinal_10290 for inventory synchronization\n7. Process unit with FUN_6fb937c0 using param_1[0x3] value\n8. Call Ordinal_10255 for item storage update\n9. Retrieve stored item via Ordinal_10243, validate not null and equals item\n10. Check if unit still valid (pointer not null)\n11. If unit initialized, validate ownership and process handlers\n12. Determine item type from param_2[0xc] using Ordinal_10754\n13. If type matches (iVar4 == 0): set item properties with SetItemMode, update weight via Ordinal_10720\n14. If type differs: remove unit from hash table, create new unit inventory entry\n15. Compare current unit with game context\n16. If game unit: initialize UI, set item flags via Ordinal_10690/10261/10262, process sprite data\n17. If item has properties (Ordinal_10480 >= 0x36): apply property handlers 10486/10474/10485/10376\n\nParameters:\npUnit (uint *): Pointer to unit structure (ECX in __fastcall), accessed at offsets 0x3, 0x4, 0x8, 0x9, 0x84\npParam (uint *): Pointer to item/parameter structure (EDX), accessed at offsets 0x8, 0x10, 0x11, 0xc\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Function validates and aborts on errors (assertion style). Calls FUN_6fb9a10f(0xffffffff) on validation failure.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Multiple assertion-style error checks with Ordinal_10023() and FUN_6fb9a10f() calls\n- Handles both new unit creation and existing unit item updates\n- Contains game context check (GetGameContext) for conditional UI state updates\n- Uses assembly-only temporaries for inventory/item tracking\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x3, 0x4, 0x8, 0x9, 0x84 - Unit structure field offsets\n0x8, 0x10, 0x11, 0xc - Parameter structure field offsets\n0x36 - Property item type indicator\n0x100, 0x171 - Validation parameters\n0xbee, 0xbf0, 0xbf8, 0xbf9, 0x35a, 0xc07, 0x1540 - Debug line numbers",
