      "comment": "Apply inventory item to a unit, handling equipping, property processing, and special item effects.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Create buffer for item data (local_18) via Ordinal_10883\n2. Retrieve player unit by ID from param_1, validate dwUnitType == 0 (UNIT_PLAYER)\n3. Get inventory path from unit[2].pPath, validate not NULL\n4. Test item flags via Ordinal_10754(local_c, 1), must succeed\n5. Update unit body state via FUN_6fb950d0\n6. Find mercenary unit (ID at param_1+4), apply item if found via FUN_6fb69b30\n7. Get linked inventory item via Ordinal_10257(pInventory, dwItemType & 0xFF), apply if found\n8. Create new unit in inventory slot via CreateUnitInInventory\n9. Set item slot ID via Ordinal_10690(pNewUnit, dwItemType)\n10. Determine slot type (3 or 4 based on dwItemType 0x0B or 0x0C)\n11. Add to inventory via Ordinal_10242, must succeed\n12. Apply item properties via Ordinal_10253(pInventory, pNewUnit, dwItemType & 0xFF)\n13. Special handling for types 0x04/0x05: Apply effects, update g_wItemSlotDruid/g_wItemSlotOther via Ordinal_10823\n14. Standard handling: Just apply properties\n15. Send mouse move event via SendMouseMoveMessage\n16. Update stats via Ordinal_10480(pNewUnit, 0x36), apply deltas if non-zero via Ordinals 10486/10474/10485/10376\n\nParameters:\n- nSlotIndex (ECX, int): Inventory slot index parameter\n\nReturns:\n- void: Returns silently on success or aborts with FUN_6fb9a10f on validation failure\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Magic number 0x0d: offset within param_1 for item creation\n- Magic number 0x36: stat code for equipment changes\n- Item types 0x04 (Druid) and 0x05 (Other) trigger special stat tracking via globals\n- Multiple validation points abort entire operation on failure\n- dwItemType byte value (masked with 0xFF) determines item slot/type",
