      "comment": "Detach item from unit and update all system tables.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract unit state pointer from param_1[0x21]\n2. Get item type byte via Ordinal_10689(pItem)\n3. If type is 0x04 or 0x05 (equipment slots):\n   a. Call Ordinal_10290 to remove from main list\n   b. Get equipment status via Ordinal_10442\n   c. Call FUN_6fb937c0 to update unit\n   d. Call Ordinal_10255 to finalize removal\n4. Get item flags via Ordinal_10243\n5. Validate: flags != null, flags == pItem (must match)\n6. If type 0x04/0x05 and unit valid:\n   a. If unit[0] == 0: call Ordinal_10258 cleanup\n   b. Call Ordinal_10707(flags, 0x100, 0x171) validation\n   c. If validation returns 0: call Ordinal_10524 dealloc\n   d. Call Ordinal_10514 finalization\n   e. Call ProcessHandlerTable update\n   f. Call Ordinal_10954 flag update\n7. Call Ordinal_10254(state, type) finalization\n8. Call RemoveUnitFromHashTable(pItem[2], pItem[0]) hash cleanup\n\nParameters:\n- pUnit (ECX): Pointer to unit structure, must be valid for type 0x04/0x05\n- pItem (EDX): Pointer to item structure\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If pItem flags null or don't match pItem: fatal error (calls FUN_6fb9a10f with -1)\n- Type 0x04/0x05 performs equipment-specific removal steps\n- Other types skip equipment removal logic\n- Unit null check: skips equipment processing if unit invalid",
