      "instructions": ["0x99C60|PUSH|ESI", "0x99C61|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0x99C63|TEST|ESI, ESI", "0x99C65|PUSH|EDI", "0x99C66|JNZ|0x6fb69c86", "0x99C68|PUSH|0xcbb", "0x99C6D|PUSH|0x6fbca31c", "0x99C72|PUSH|0x6fbb6df8", "0x99C77|CALL|0x6fb99a7a", "0x99C7C|ADD|ESP, 0xc", "0x99C7F|PUSH|-0x1", "0x99C81|CALL|0x6fb9a10f", "0x99C86|MOV|ECX, dword ptr [ESI + 0xb]", "0x99C89|MOV|EDX, 0x4", "0x99C8E|CALL|0x6fb60e10"],
      "comment": "Process item equip: validates item and applies stat modifications\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate item pointer (nItemData) not null, exit with error 0xcbb if null\n2. Lookup source unit in hash table using unit ID field at nItemData+0xb, type 4\n3. Validate source unit found, exit with error 0xcbe if not found\n4. Set item stat 0x46 with value from nItemData+0x15 using Ordinal_10517\n5. Lookup target unit in hash table using ID at nItemData+0x2f with type from nItemData+0x2d\n6. Validate target unit found, exit with error 0xcc3 if not found\n7. Get unit chain pointer from target unit at offset 0x84\n8. Check if unit slot type 8 exists using Ordinal_10754 on nItemData+0x21\n9. If slot empty (Ordinal_10754 returns 0): clear stat, get next unit, initialize slot\n10. Get next unit in chain via Ordinal_10262\n11. If chain exists: check for property 0x36 using Ordinal_10480\n12. If property exists: unset 0x36, apply new property, activate, and refresh unit state\n\nParameters:\nnItemData (int): Item equip data structure containing unit IDs, stat values, and slot type\n  at offsets: 0xb=source unit ID, 0x15=stat value, 0x2f=target unit ID, 0x2d=unit type,\n  0x21=slot/unit value, 0x84=unit chain offset\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Normal completion or abort via FUN_6fb9a10f on validation failure (non-returning)\n\nSpecial Cases:\nSlot initialization branch only executes when Ordinal_10754 returns 0 (empty slot)\nProperty update chain only processes if next unit and property 0x36 both exist",
