      "instructions": ["0x99E40|SUB|ESP, 0x54", "0x99E43|PUSH|EBX", "0x99E44|PUSH|EBP", "0x99E45|MOV|EBP, ECX", "0x99E47|PUSH|ESI", "0x99E48|TEST|EBP, EBP", "0x99E4A|PUSH|EDI", "0x99E4B|JNZ|0x6fb69e6b", "0x99E4D|PUSH|0xcfa", "0x99E52|PUSH|0x6fbca31c", "0x99E57|PUSH|0x6fbb6df8", "0x99E5C|CALL|0x6fb99a7a", "0x99E61|ADD|ESP, 0xc", "0x99E64|PUSH|-0x1", "0x99E66|CALL|0x6fb9a10f"],
      "comment": "Process an inventory page operation for a player unit.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate input page data pointer (crash if NULL)\n2. Check if page index is valid (0x03 byte not 0xFF)\n3. Initialize game state and retrieve player inventory unit\n4. Copy 46 bytes of page data to stack buffer\n5. Retrieve inventory grid from player unit [+0x84]\n6. If player page char is '9' (delete mode):\n   a. Validate target unit exists\n   b. Check inventory dialog is open\n   c. Call Ordinal_10243 to find/remove item in grid\n   d. If successful, get item page with Ordinal_10719\n   e. Query system state and validate page bounds with Ordinal_10409\n   f. Remove unit from hash table and clear UI selection\n   g. Return\n7. Else insert/replace mode:\n   a. If no target unit, create new item via InitializeItemProperties\n   b. Else retrieve item page with Ordinal_10244 and check replacement conditions\n   c. Call InitializeItemProperties if replacement required\n   d. Validate page index matches\n8. Set item display mode with Ordinal_10720\n9. Call Ordinal_10247 to validate item placement\n10. If valid, insert item via ProcessPlayerItemInsertion\n11. Load item rarity via InitializeItemRarityMode\n12. Set item property via Ordinal_10480 (0x36)\n13. If set, cascade update with Ordinal_10486, Ordinal_10474, Ordinal_10485\n\nParameters:\npPageData - Pointer to 46-byte page structure containing:\n  +0x00 Item ID (dword)\n  +0x04 Item flags/type (dword)\n  +0x0B Target unit ID (dword)\n  +0x0F Item subtype (ushort)\n  +0x11 X position (ushort)\n  +0x13 Y position (ushort)\n  +0x21 Inventory mode flag (dword)\n  Page char [0] = '9' for delete, else insert/replace mode\n  Page index [3] = inventory page index (0-7, 0xFF=error)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Function performs operations in-place, no return value.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Null pointer input crashes with Ordinal_10023 error\n- Invalid page index (0xFF) logs error and returns\n- Missing inventory grid skips operation\n- Dialog not open when deleting logs warning but continues\n- Page index mismatch during replacement logs error\n- Item placement validation failure returns without update\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x3 - Offset of page index byte in page data\n0x21 - Offset of inventory grid/mode flag in page structure\n0x84 - Offset of inventory grid handle in unit structure\n0xb - Number of dwords to copy in memory copy loop\n0x36 - Item property code for Ordinal_10480\n0x0B, 0x0F, 0x11, 0x13 - Offsets of coordinates and IDs in page data",
      "tags": ["PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "SRC_Item.cpp", "MOD_UNIT", "PARAM_1", "STRUCT_Other", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
