      "api_calls": ["ParseItemDataFromBuffer", "QueueLogMessage", "QueueLogMessage", "QueueLogMessage", "RemoveItemFromInventory", "QueueLogMessage", "GetItemQualityLevel", "QueueLogMessage", "GetInventoryPageFromUnit", "InitializeMapTileArray", "...+16 more"],
      "instructions": ["0x9A1C0|SUB|ESP, 0x28", "0x9A1C3|LEA|EAX, [ESP + 0x10]", "0x9A1C7|PUSH|EBX", "0x9A1C8|PUSH|EBP", "0x9A1C9|PUSH|ESI", "0x9A1CA|PUSH|EDI", "0x9A1CB|MOV|EDI, ECX", "0x9A1CD|PUSH|EAX", "0x9A1CE|XOR|ECX, ECX", "0x9A1D0|PUSH|0x0", "0x9A1D2|MOV|CL, byte ptr [EDI + 0x2]", "0x9A1D5|LEA|EDX, [EDI + 0x8]", "0x9A1D8|SUB|ECX, 0x8", "0x9A1DB|PUSH|ECX", "0x9A1DC|PUSH|EDX"],
      "comment": "Process item addition/removal in inventory. Validates page slots, allocates or reuses inventory space, handles item placement with collision detection and UI updates.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract page number from item handle and validate page bounds\n2. Get player inventory unit (type 1) from hash table\n3. Get target item page reference from inventory\n4. Branch on operation type (delete vs add/modify):\n   - DELETE (param_1[1] == 0x0C): Validate inventory dialog open, call page removal, cleanup UI selection\n   - ADD/MODIFY: Allocate new item unit or reuse existing, validate page conflict, setup item data\n5. Call Ordinal_10247 to place item in inventory grid (returns placement slot/result)\n6. If placement succeeds: call ProcessPlayerItemInsertion for stat updates, initialize item rarity mode\n7. Update item owner/parent references and finalize with graphic mode updates\n\nParameters:\nIMPLICIT ECX: nItemHandle - Item unit ID to process\nReturns:\nvoid - Modifies inventory state and item placement via ordinal calls\nSpecial Cases:\n- Page conflicts detected by comparing expected page (local_8) vs actual page from item\n- Null inventory or missing player inventory returns early\n- Dialog must be open for delete operations\n- Item allocation failure triggers error log",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "SRC_Item.cpp", "MOD_UNIT", "STRUCT_ItemData", "PARAM_1", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData", "STRUCT_StatList", "STRUCT_MonsterData", "PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Path", "STRUCT_Skill"]
