      "comment": "Process inventory item operation for target unit, validating handler chain and updating UI state.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate input unit pointer (null check with error exit 0xee3)\n2. Locate primary item handler via hash table lookup (param_1 + 0xb offset, handler ID 4)\n3. Check handler chain status (offset +0xc): if 0 branch to processing, if 4 branch to alt handler\n4. Retrieve secondary item from hash table using param_1+0x2f and inventory count at param_1+0x2d\n5. Get inventory handle reference from primary item (offset +0x84)\n6. Query handler item properties via Ordinal_10243, validate result != 0 and == current handler\n7. Retrieve game system state context via GetGlobalSystemState()\n8. Apply system state to item via Ordinal_10409, propagate to UI via Ordinal_10250\n9. Initialize UI state and retrieve handler flags via Ordinal_10840\n10. If handler flags set and item valid: update item type via Ordinal_10258, check dialog status\n11. If dialog check via Ordinal_10707 succeeds (==0), update item stack via Ordinal_10524\n12. Post-process via Ordinal_10514 and ProcessHandlerTable, apply visual updates\n13. Query operation completion flag (param_1 + 0x21 offset): if set, alternate path (RemoveUnitFromHashTable + InitializeItemProperties)\n14. Finalize item references and check property validity\n15. Query item modification state (Ordinal_10480 0x36), if set apply cleanup sequence\n\nParameters:\npUnit (UnitAny * in ECX) - Target unit for inventory operation, accessed as: param_1+0xb (handler ID), param_1+0x2d (inventory count), param_1+0x2e (unknown param), param_1+0x2f (secondary item ref), param_1+0x11/0x13 (coordinates)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Always returns normally after processing or alternate path. Failure conditions result in fatal exit via Ordinal_10023 (error logging) and FUN_6fb9a10f(-1) termination.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Null unit input triggers immediate fatal error (0xee3) via Ordinal_10023\n- Missing primary handler causes fatal exit (0xe93)\n- Invalid handler chain causes fatal exit (0xe95)\n- Handler mismatch triggers fatal exit (0xe96)\n- Missing inventory handle causes fatal exit (0xea5)\n- Missing item reference triggers fatal exit (0x1540)\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x0b - Handler ID offset in unit structure\n0x2d - Inventory count offset \n0x2e - Operation parameter offset\n0x2f - Secondary item reference offset\n0x11, 0x13 - Coordinate offsets\n0x21 - Operation completion flag offset\n0x3c - Buffer offset [0xc access = +0x3c]\n0x84 - Inventory handle offset\n0x100, 0x171 - Dialog status check constants\n0x36 - Item modification state flag\n0xee3, 0xe93, 0xe95, 0xe96, 0xea5, 0x1540 - Error line numbers\n\nRelated Functions:\n- FindUnitInHashTable() - Locate handler/item by ID and type\n- Ordinal_10243() - Query handler item properties\n- Ordinal_10409() - Apply system state to item\n- Ordinal_10840() - Retrieve handler state flags\n- ProcessHandlerTable() - Process state machine table\n- InitializeItemProperties() - Create new item with properties\n- RemoveUnitFromHashTable() - Remove unit from lookup table",
