      "comment": "Performs item inventory lookup and classification during item drops/pickups.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize item classification temporary (dwTempVar) from input handle\n2. Lookup unit handle in hash table by item ID\n3. Validate unit exists, exit with error 0xefa if not found\n4. Check unit item type: if type != 0, dispatch special handler (0x4) or return early\n5. Get game context, validate game context exists\n6. Lookup unit again by item ID to get item pointer\n7. Query item visual class code from Ordinal_10719\n8. Get inventory handle from game context at offset 0x84\n9. Test item can be equipped: call Ordinal_10840 with unit + game context\n10. If item equipment check passes: remove client inventory tracking, add item to visual, refresh handlers\n11. Lookup item in inventory container via Ordinal_10243\n12. Validate found item matches expected unit pointer, exit with error 0xec7 if mismatch\n13. Get current system state, apply game world filter to item via Ordinal_10409\n14. Update item classification via Ordinal_10250\n15. Initialize game UI state\n16. Attempt inventory update with Ordinal_10754\n17. If update succeeds: set item mode/flags, update visual representation\n18. If update fails: remove old unit from hash, allocate new item unit\n19. Finalize: update inventory, refresh views\n\nParameters:\n nItemHandle (int, __fastcall ECX): Game item handle to process\n\nReturns:\n void (no return value, function exits via RET or error returns)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n - Unit hash lookup failure exits with error code 0xefa\n - Game context missing exits with error code 0xeb9\n - Inventory handle missing exits with error code 0xebe\n - Item-container mismatch exits with error code 0xec7\n - Item allocation failure exits with error code 0xed1\n - Function uses 1 stack-allocated temporary optimized away (local_1c)",
