      "comment": "Places an item into the player's inventory after validating game state and item data.\nNOTE: Function uses 8 SSA temporaries optimized away by compiler (bVar1, iVar2, iVar3, uVar4, uVar5, uVar6, uVar7, uVar8).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get game context (player/inventory state container)\n2. Validate game context exists (fatal error if null)\n3. Find unit in hash table using item ID from unit data\n4. Check item pick-up eligibility via Ordinal_10754\n5. If item is not eligible for pickup (return value != 0):\n   - Remove old unit from hash table\n   - Allocate and setup new unit with item data\n   - Validate allocation succeeded\n6. Otherwise (item eligible for pickup):\n   - Get unit from game context inventory\n   - Validate inventory exists\n   - Setup item in existing unit using SetItemMode\n   - Set item properties using Ordinal_10720\n7. Set unit flags via Ordinal_10328 (ushort from pItemData[1])\n8. Set unit property via Ordinal_10331 (word from pItemData offset+6)\n9. Add unit to inventory hash table via Ordinal_10242\n10. If add failed: log error and return early\n11. Get unit page index via Ordinal_10719\n12. Validate page index != 0xFF (invalid page)\n13. Get global system state and calculate screen position via Ordinal_10409\n14. Get unit properties via Ordinal_10329, Ordinal_10326\n15. Position item on screen via Ordinal_10249 (returns success/failure)\n16. If position failed: fatal error\n17. Apply item effects via ProcessUnitItemEffect if applicable\n18. Send mouse move message to update UI\n19. Check for item socket count via Ordinal_10480\n20. If sockets available: update socket flags via Ordinal_10486, apply socket effects, recalculate display\n\nParameters:\ndwUnitId (uint) - IMPLICIT ECX: Unit identifier to find in hash table\npItemData (uint *) - IMPLICIT EDX: Pointer to item data array with layout:\n  [0] - Game context pointer (verified)\n  [1] - Unit flags (word)\n  [2] - Item equip slot (byte)\n  [3] - Item mode/eligibility flags (tested for pickup)\n  [4] - Item page or reserved value (validated != 0xFF)\n  [6] - Unit property word\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value (always succeeds or asserts)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Line 0xE58: Fatal error if game context invalid\n- Line 0x35A: Fatal error if unit not found when pickup eligible\n- Line 0xE60: Fatal error if unit allocation failed\n- Line 0xE68: Fatal error if inventory context invalid\n- Line 0xFF validation: Returns early with error log if page == 0xFF\n- Line 0xE7A: Fatal error if screen positioning failed\n- Ordinal_10480/0x36 socket check: Performs additional socket processing if count > 0\n\nRelated Functions:\n- GetGameContext() - Retrieves game state container\n- FindUnitInHashTable() - Locates item unit by ID\n- RemoveUnitFromHashTable() - Removes old item unit\n- AllocateAndSetupUnitWithItemData() - Creates new item unit\n- SetItemMode() - Initializes item in inventory slot\n- ProcessUnitItemEffect() - Applies item bonuses to player\n- SendMouseMoveMessage() - Updates UI display",
