      "instructions": ["0x9B070|SUB|ESP, 0x1c", "0x9B073|LEA|EAX, [ESP + 0x4]", "0x9B077|PUSH|EBX", "0x9B078|PUSH|ESI", "0x9B079|PUSH|EDI", "0x9B07A|MOV|EDI, ECX", "0x9B07C|XOR|ECX, ECX", "0x9B07E|PUSH|EAX", "0x9B07F|MOV|CL, byte ptr [EDI + 0x2]", "0x9B082|PUSH|0x0", "0x9B084|SUB|ECX, 0x8", "0x9B087|LEA|EDX, [EDI + 0x8]", "0x9B08A|PUSH|ECX", "0x9B08B|PUSH|EDX", "0x9B08C|CALL|0x6fb98ddc"],
      "comment": "Equips an item on a unit in the inventory system.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract item data from packed parameters (quality, flags, attributes)\n2. Call Ordinal_10883 (item creation) to populate item structure\n3. Get game context inventory object via GetGameContext\n4. Search inventory hash table for unit by ID via FindUnitInHashTable\n5. If unit exists, set item mode via SetItemMode and call item equip ordinals\n6. If unit doesn't exist, allocate new unit via AllocateAndSetupUnitWithItemData\n7. Apply item attributes via Ordinal_10328, Ordinal_10331 (mode, type, subtype)\n8. Check if item should be added to inventory via Ordinal_10242\n9. If has inventory, add item via Ordinal_10266 and update via Ordinal_10261/10262\n10. Apply item effects via ProcessUnitItemEffect\n11. Check for 0x400 flag via Ordinal_10708 and apply special property\n12. Refresh inventory display via FUN_6fb8f0c0 and update game state via SetGameStateByteFlag\n\nParameters:\n  nItemData (int, IMPLICIT in ECX) - Packed item data structure pointer containing encoded item properties\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value, function performs side effects only\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Fatal error if inventory object is null (line 0xf58)\n  - Fatal error if game context is null (line 0xf48)\n  - Fatal error if unit is null after operations (line 0x1540)\n  - Flag 0x400 triggers special property application\n  - Item quality encoded in byte at offset +2 of nItemData\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x8 - Offset adjustment for quality extraction\n  0x4 - Unit hash table type selector\n  0x2 - Inventory slot type identifier\n  0x36 - Item property query code\n  0x400 - Special property flag mask\n  0xf48, 0xf58, 0x1540 - Debug assertion line numbers\n\nStructure Layout:\n  nItemData structure (offsets relative to ECX):\n  Offset | Size | Field Name | Type | Description\n  +0x0   | 4    | id         | uint | Unit/item ID reference\n  +0x2   | 1    | quality    | byte | Item quality level (adjusted -8)\n  +0x4   | 4    | unitId     | uint | Associated unit ID\n  +0x8   | n/a  | data       | var  | Variable item data array\n\nRelated Functions:\n- FindUnitInHashTable() - Search unit by ID\n- AllocateAndSetupUnitWithItemData() - Create new unit\n- SetItemMode() - Apply item mode\n- ProcessUnitItemEffect() - Apply effects\n- GetGameContext() - Get inventory manager\n- SetGameStateByteFlag() - Update game state",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "SRC_Item.cpp", "MOD_UNIT", "PARAM_1", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
