      "comment": "Process equipping an item from the belt inventory slot\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate input command ptCmd is not null\n2. Find source unit ID from ptCmd->dwUnitId (index ptCmd->bUnitType)\n3. Find equipment destination unit from ptCmd->dwEquipUnitId (type 4=item)\n4. Get game context pointer for validation\n5. Verify source unit is valid game context (inventory unit)\n6. Verify inventory slot (ptCmd->nInventorySlot) is valid\n7. Verify target item exists and ownership is correct\n8. Remove item from belt, update inventory flags\n9. If item mode transfer succeeds:\n   - Assign equipment slot from source unit inventory\n   - Remove old equipment if exists\n   - Set new item properties (mode, color)\n   - Update unit stats\n   - If equipment had special bonuses, apply to target unit\n10. Else equipment mode is blocked, remove from belt\n\nParameters:\nptCmd (int *) - Command structure containing:\n  Offset 0xB: Destination unit ID (dword)\n  Offset 0x2D: Source unit type (byte)\n  Offset 0x2E: Unknown flag (byte)\n  Offset 0x2F: Source unit ID (dword)\n  Offset 0x11: Belt slot index (word)\n  Offset 0x21: Inventory index (dword)\n  Offset 0x3: Item color byte (byte)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - modifies game state directly",
