      "comment": "Place item in player inventory slot, updating game state and item properties.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract item mode and calculate layout offset from item record header\n2. Get game context (player unit) and validate it exists\n3. Look up source item unit by ID in hash table\n4. Get player inventory object from game context\n5. Check if item already exists in inventory using ownership lookup\n6. If item found in inventory: validate it's the correct item, clear flags\n7. Update inventory state and run item validation handlers\n8. Get item mode data and check if item can be placed\n9. If placement allowed: update item properties (mode, equip status, quantity)\n10. If placement blocked: remove item from hash table, cancel operation\n\nParameters:\nnItemRecordPtr (int): Pointer to item record structure containing item ID at +0x4, mode at +0x2\n\nReturns:\nvoid (no return value)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Item not found: triggers error message with debug context\n- Inventory uninitialized: triggers error message and process termination\n- Item ownership conflict: triggers error when different item exists in slot\n- Placement blocked: item removed from ownership tracking\n- Note: Function contains 19 ordinal calls to D2Common/D2Game APIs for inventory management\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x2: Byte offset to item mode in record\n0x4: Byte offset to item unit ID in record  \n0x8: Item mode extraction offset\n0x84: Offset to inventory object in game context\n0x21: Offset to inventory unit ID in game context (dword index)\n0x100, 0x171: Item property validation range\n0x36: Equipment slot type identifier\n0x20: Item placement conflict flag threshold\n0xff, 0xffff: Bit masking for flag/mode extraction",
