      "comment": "Process game item action - handles item placement, removal, and effect application.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate nItemAction pointer (NULL check, returns error if invalid)\n2. Find source item unit via hash table lookup at offset +0xB\n3. Validate source unit found in hash table\n4. Check source unit type field at offset +0x3:\n   - If type 2: Jump to inventory processing (remove item path)\n   - If type 4: Handle ground item (place in inventory path)\n   - Other: Return without processing\n5. For type 4 (ground item): Call PlaceUnitItemAtSlot to move item\n6. Get inventory slot handle at offset 0x21 from unit structure\n7. Apply item attribute bonuses via Ordinal_10328, Ordinal_10331\n8. Validate item compatibility with Ordinal_10840\n9. Apply ProcessUnitItemEffect if compatible\n10. Check room in inventory with Ordinal_10707\n11. For type 2 (inventory): Validate item can be removed\n12. Apply all item removal effects: Ordinal_10524, ProcessHandlerTable\n13. Update display: SendMouseMoveMessage, Ordinal_10720\n14. Refresh unit state: Ordinal_10480, Ordinal_10486, Ordinal_10474, Ordinal_10485\n15. Update visuals: Ordinal_10376\n16. Return to caller with no explicit return value\n\nParameters:\nnItemAction (int): Pointer to action structure containing item operation parameters:\n  +0x3: Item location/mode field (byte)\n  +0xB: Source unit type ID for lookup (dword)\n  +0x2D: Item type index (byte)\n  +0x2E: Destination inventory slot (byte)\n  +0x2F: Destination unit ID (dword)\n  +0x11: Target slot X coordinate (word)\n  +0x13: Target slot Y coordinate (word)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - function modifies game state directly, no return value. Calls FUN_6fb9a10f(0xffffffff) on error conditions to trigger game shutdown.\n\nSpecial Cases:\nNULL pointer: Immediate error, logs via Ordinal_10023\nInvalid unit type: Assertion failure through error logging\nMissing inventory slot: Returns error condition code 0xffffffff\n\nNote: Function contains 3 assembly-optimized temporaries not visible in decompiled view:\n- dwExtraParam (undefined4, extraout_ECX register): Carries extra parameter from Ordinal calls\n- byItemLoc (undefined1): Item location field extracted from param at +0x3\n- dwStatValue (undefined4, uVar7): Stat value result from Ordinal_10326",
