      "comment": "Process item action descriptor for player slot management\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract item color from descriptor (at offset +2, minus 8)\n2. Determine action type from unit type field (offset +3): 0x02=remove, 0x04=place\n3. If REMOVE (type 0x02):\n   - Get game context, verify not null\n   - Find unit by descriptor handle (offset +4)\n   - Validate inventory exists (context[0x21])\n   - Find item in inventory using FindUnitInHashTable\n   - Validate removal returns unit (not other item)\n   - Call Ordinal_10840 to unequip item from unit\n   - If unequip succeeds, check handler flag\n   - If handler flag cleared, call Ordinal_10258 to cleanup\n   - Validate item position in range [0x100, 0x171]\n   - If position invalid, move item via Ordinal_10524\n   - Update handlers via ProcessHandlerTable\n   - Call Ordinal_10954 to finalize removal\n   - Update item state via Ordinal_10267, SetItemMode, Ordinal_10720\n   - Call Ordinal_10261 to commit inventory change\n   - Call Ordinal_10262 for post-processing\n4. If PLACE (type 0x04):\n   - Get game context, verify not null\n   - Find unit by descriptor handle\n   - Call PlaceUnitItemAtSlot to place item at slot\n   - Get inventory from context[0x21]\n   - Call Ordinal_10328 to get item X coordinate\n   - Call Ordinal_10331 to get item Y coordinate\n   - Check item effectiveness via Ordinal_10731 (param 0x0d)\n   - If effective, apply effect via ProcessUnitItemEffect\n   - Validate item can occupy slot via Ordinal_10242 (slot type 0x02)\n   - If can occupy, get item value via Ordinal_10326\n   - Insert item in inventory via Ordinal_10266\n   - Send mouse move notification\n   - Update visual state via FUN_6fb6e0c0\n\nParameters:\n- nItemActionDescriptor (ECX): Handle containing unit ID (offset +4), unit type (offset +3), item color (offset +2)\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Game context NULL check at two points (lines 0x1005, 0x1049)\n- Unit lookup validation for both remove and place paths\n- Inventory NULL check (context[0x21])\n- Item position validation range 0x100-0x171",
      "tags": ["PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Inventory", "SRC_Item.cpp", "MOD_UNIT", "PARAM_1", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
    },
