      "instructions": ["0x9BC10|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [ECX + 0x4]", "0x9BC13|PUSH|EAX", "0x9BC14|CALL|0x6fb98824", "0x9BC19|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0x9BC1B|JNZ|0x6fb6bc3b", "0x9BC1D|PUSH|0x108f", "0x9BC22|PUSH|0x6fbca31c", "0x9BC27|PUSH|0x6fbb3bfc", "0x9BC2C|CALL|0x6fb99a7a", "0x9BC31|ADD|ESP, 0xc", "0x9BC34|PUSH|-0x1", "0x9BC36|CALL|0x6fb9a10f", "0x9BC3B|MOV|AL, byte ptr [EAX + 0x28]", "0x9BC3E|XOR|CX, CX", "0x9BC41|MOV|CL, AL"],
      "comment": "Retrieves item damage value from lookup table indexed by item damage stat.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract item stat pointer from pItemData at offset +4 via Ordinal_10600\n2. Validate pointer is non-NULL; if NULL, log error and terminate with FUN_6fb9a10f(-1)\n3. Load damage stat index from itemStatPtr at offset +0x28 (byte)\n4. Check if index < g_wMaxItemDamageStatIndex\n5. If valid, calculate table offset as index * 8 and fetch dword from g_pdwItemDamageTable\n6. Otherwise return 0\n\nParameters:\n  pItemData (dword) - Item data structure pointer, accessed in ECX (fastcall)\n\nReturns:\n  dword - Item damage table entry value, or 0 if stat index out of bounds\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - NULL itemStatPtr terminates process (non-returning call to FUN_6fb9a10f)\n  - Index >= g_wMaxItemDamageStatIndex returns 0\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x4 - Offset of item stat pointer within item data\n  0x28 - Offset of damage stat index within item stats\n  0x8 - Table stride (8 bytes per entry)\n  0x108f - Error code/line number for logging",
