      "instructions": ["0x9BC60|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [ECX + 0x4]", "0x9BC63|PUSH|EAX", "0x9BC64|CALL|0x6fb98824", "0x9BC69|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0x9BC6B|JNZ|0x6fb6bc8b", "0x9BC6D|PUSH|0x109d", "0x9BC72|PUSH|0x6fbca31c", "0x9BC77|PUSH|0x6fbb3bfc", "0x9BC7C|CALL|0x6fb99a7a", "0x9BC81|ADD|ESP, 0xc", "0x9BC84|PUSH|-0x1", "0x9BC86|CALL|0x6fb9a10f", "0x9BC8B|MOV|AL, byte ptr [EAX + 0x28]", "0x9BC8E|XOR|CX, CX", "0x9BC91|MOV|CL, AL"],
      "comment": "Retrieves the damage value for an item stat, validating the stat index against max bounds.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load item stat data pointer from pItemStat + 0x4 via Ordinal_10600\n2. If stat data null, log error via Ordinal_10023 and terminate (non-returning)\n3. Load stat index from pItemData[0x28] (single byte)\n4. Compare stat index against g_wMaxItemDamageStatIndex boundary\n5. If index >= max, return 0 (out of bounds)\n6. Look up damage value from g_pdwItemDamageTable[index * 8] (dword-aligned)\n7. If damage value == 0xed, return special case 0xee\n8. If damage value != 0xf0, return damage; if 0xf0 return 0\n\nParameters:\npItemStat (void *): Pointer to item structure, contains stat data pointer at offset +4\n\nReturns:\nuint: Damage value (0xee for special 0xed case, 0 for bounds/0xf0, or actual damage)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Stat index at offset 0x28 within stat data\n- Magic value 0xed returns 0xee (substitution)\n- Magic value 0xf0 returns 0 (zero out)\n- Out of bounds returns 0\n\nNote: Function calls two unknown ordinals (Ordinal_10600, Ordinal_10023)\n",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Inventory", "SRC_Item.cpp", "MOD_UNIT", "PARAM_1", "STRUCT_Other"]
