      "instructions": ["0x9BCE0|PUSH|ESI", "0x9BCE1|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0x9BCE3|PUSH|EDI", "0x9BCE4|MOV|EDX, 0x4", "0x9BCE9|MOV|ECX, dword ptr [ESI + 0x1]", "0x9BCEC|CALL|0x6fb60e10", "0x9BCF1|MOV|EDI, EAX", "0x9BCF3|TEST|EDI, EDI", "0x9BCF5|JZ|0x6fb6bd6d", "0x9BCF7|MOV|AL, byte ptr [ESI + 0x6]", "0x9BCFA|CMP|AL, 0xcc", "0x9BCFC|JC|0x6fb6bd40", "0x9BCFE|CMP|AL, 0xd5", "0x9BD00|JA|0x6fb6bd40", "0x9BD02|PUSH|0x40"],
      "comment": "Process item interaction effects on a game unit by applying item stats and effects\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract unit ID from pEventData[1] and lookup in unit hash table\n2. Return if unit not found in hash table\n3. Extract item code from pEventData[6] to determine item type\n4. If item code outside armor/weapon range (0xcc-0xd5):\n   - Check pEventData[5] flag, if 1: call Ordinal_10517 (ApplyItemMods) to apply modifications\n   - Call GetGameContext to fetch game state pointer\n   - Call ProcessGameObjectItemEffects to apply effects to unit\n5. If item code within armor/weapon range (0xcc-0xd5):\n   - Call Ordinal_10483 (GetItemStats) with 0x40 flag to fetch armor/weapon stats\n   - If stats found: call Ordinal_10465 (SetItemProperty) to apply stats to item\n   - Validate game context and check unit property at offset 0xc equals 1\n   - If valid: call Ordinal_10954 (FinalizeItemInteraction) to complete item application\n6. Return from function\n\nParameters:\npEventData (int *): Pointer to event data structure with item interaction info\n  Field at offset 1: Unit ID (dword) - passed to FindUnitInHashTable\n  Field at offset 5: Flag byte (0x01 enables stat modification for non-weapons)\n  Field at offset 6: Item code byte (determines item type/rarity code)\n  Field at offset 7: Item quality modifier (dword)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Function returns no value; modifies unit state in-place via ordinal calls\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Non-existent unit ID results in early return without processing\n- Item codes outside 0xcc-0xd5 range use alternative processing path via Ordinal_10517\n- Unit property check at offset 0xc required before finalization call\n\nOrdinal References:\n- Ordinal_10483: GetItemStats from D2Common.dll\n- Ordinal_10465: SetItemProperty from D2Common.dll  \n- Ordinal_10517: ApplyItemMods from D2Common.dll\n- Ordinal_10954: FinalizeItemInteraction from D2Common.dll\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0xcc - Lower bound for armor/weapon item codes (204 decimal)\n0xd5 - Upper bound for armor/weapon item codes (213 decimal)\n0x40 - Stat flags passed to Ordinal_10483 armor/weapon stat lookup\n0x01 - Magic value indicating unit property is initialized/set",
      "tags": ["PARAM_1"]
    },
