      "comment": "Validate unit exists in game hash table before applying stat updates.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Search game hash table for unit matching ID at param_1[+1] using hash key 0x04\n2. If unit not found (EAX == NULL):\n   a. Call Ordinal_10023(szHItemStringLabel, szSourcePathLabel, 0x11a4) - Log error\n   b. Call FUN_6fb9a10f(0xFFFFFFFF) - Fatal exit with error code\n   c. Never returns to caller\n3. If unit found (EAX != NULL), continue to stat update\n4. Invoke Ordinal_10708(pFoundUnit, dwStatValue1, dwStatValue2) - Apply stats to unit\n5. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\npUnitStats - Pointer to structure containing:\n  [+1] dwUnitId - Unit ID for hash table lookup\n  [+5] dwStatValue1 - First stat value\n  [+9] dwStatValue2 - Second stat value\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value, terminates if unit not found\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Fatal error if unit not in hash table (logs error then terminates with 0xFFFFFFFF)\n- No recovery mechanism for missing units - function either completes stat update or terminates\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x04 - Hash table search parameter (lookup type/flags)\n0x11a4 - Source line number for error context (4260 decimal)\n0xFFFFFFFF - Fatal error code (-1 or all bits set)\n\nOrdinal Functions:\nOrdinal_10023 - Error logging function (takes source file/line information)\nOrdinal_10708 - Unit stat update function (applies values to unit attributes)",
