      "comment": "Processes an inventory item within a unit, managing item placement, socketing, and inventory updates.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Retrieve unit from hash table using dwItemParam's unit ID (offset 0x2f) and class byte (offset 0x2d) - FindUnitInHashTable\n2. Return fatal error if unit not found - Ordinal_10023 assertion\n3. Get global game system state - GetGlobalSystemState\n4. Retrieve current item properties and path context via Ordinal_10409, Ordinal_10257\n5. Validate item existence in current path via Ordinal_10243\n6. Clear previous item states via Ordinal_10871, Ordinal_10258\n7. Check item validity and handle socket chain via Ordinal_10707, Ordinal_10480, Ordinal_10486, Ordinal_10474, Ordinal_10485, Ordinal_10376\n8. If target unit is player: Initialize item properties via InitializeItemProperties, insert via Ordinal_10720, Ordinal_10249, Ordinal_10242\n9. If non-player: Skip grid validation, process via Ordinal_10524\n10. Complete item registration via Ordinal_10954, Ordinal_10514, ProcessHandlerTable\n11. For player units: Validate placement, update UI state via InitializeGameUIState, Ordinal_10262, FUN_6fb8f0c0, ProcessGameObjectItemEffects\n\nParameters:\ndwItemRequestParam (uint, __fastcall ECX) - Packed structure pointer containing unit ID, class, inventory info\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No explicit return. Fatal errors cause process termination via FUN_6fb9a10f(-1)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Player unit: Full UI refresh via InitializeGameUIState, class slot clearing (0x04/0x05)\n- Socket item (0x36 stat): Handled via ordinal chain, transferred to new item\n- Missing item or validation failure: Fatal assertion via Ordinal_10023",
