      "api_calls": ["ParseItemDataFromBuffer", "FogAssert", "GetInventoryPageFromUnit", "FogAssert", "GetArrayElementPtr", "FogAssert", "UpdateInventoryAfterItemRemoval", "GetInventoryLocationValue", "RemoveItemFromInventory", "FogAssert", "...+29 more"],
      "instructions": ["0x9C2A0|SUB|ESP, 0x24", "0x9C2A3|PUSH|EBX", "0x9C2A4|PUSH|ESI", "0x9C2A5|PUSH|EDI", "0x9C2A6|MOV|EDI, ECX", "0x9C2A8|XOR|ECX, ECX", "0x9C2AA|LEA|EAX, [ESP + 0x18]", "0x9C2AE|MOV|CL, byte ptr [EDI + 0x2]", "0x9C2B1|PUSH|EAX", "0x9C2B2|SUB|ECX, 0xd", "0x9C2B5|PUSH|0x0", "0x9C2B7|LEA|EDX, [EDI + 0xd]", "0x9C2BA|PUSH|ECX", "0x9C2BB|PUSH|EDX", "0x9C2BC|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x20], EDI"],
      "comment": "Equips an item from inventory into a unit's equipment slots or handles item insertion logic.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract source item data from parameter: parse item reference flags (byte at +0x2, +0x3, +0x8, +0x9)\n2. Locate unit in hash table using item reference IDs\n3. Validate unit exists and has valid inventory path pointer\n4. Get current game system state via Ordinal_10409\n5. Retrieve item from inventory at slot index (dwSlotIndex & 0xff)\n6. Validate item pointer exists and matches expected reference\n7. Check unit type: if type==0, remove item from old location\n8. Process item effects: validate property table (0x100-0x171), handle special property (0x36)\n9. If property 0x36 exists: remove property, process associated logic, cleanup\n10. Attempt to reinsert item: call Ordinal_10754 to check reinsertion status\n11. If reinsertion succeeds: setup item mode, move to new slot\n12. If reinsertion fails: remove old unit ref, create new item copy if unit is game context\n13. Final validation: if unit is game context unit, insert item into grid, update UI state\n14. Process item effects and validate final item pointer\n15. Return success/failure based on insertion completion\n\nParameters:\n- nItemRef (IMPLICIT ECX): Item reference handle encoding source location and flags\n  Encodes: source slot, target slot, unit byte, unit ID in parameter bytes\n\nReturns:\n- void; modifies unit inventory, creates/moves items, updates UI state\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Unit not found: abort with error 0x11f9\n- Inventory path null: abort with error 0x11fe\n- Item not in slot: abort with error 0x1200\n- Property 0x36 requires cleanup logic\n- Game context check: applies slot reset (0x04, 0x05)\n\nNote: Function uses 1 stack-allocated temporary (local_18[4]) optimized away during compilation.",
      "tags": ["PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "STRUCT_Item", "PROP_NOCALLER", "SRC_Item.cpp", "MOD_UNIT", "STRUCT_Skill", "PARAM_1", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
