      "comment": "Processes item insertion into player inventory and applies item effects.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract item descriptor from parameter reference (bytes 0xd-0x10)\n2. Locate source item in item hash table (offset 0x9, type from offset 0x8)\n3. If source item not found, return immediately\n4. Search for target inventory unit (type 4) in unit hash table (offset 0x4)\n5. If target unit not found, create new inventory unit with CreateUnitInInventory\n6. If target unit exists, apply item mode with current equipment settings\n7. Set item mode flags on target unit\n8. Verify source item has valid inventory container (pItem[0x21])\n9. Attempt to place item in inventory container with Ordinal_10242\n10. If placement succeeds, validate item state with Ordinal_10754\n11. Verify game context exists and has active inventory controller\n12. Initialize inventory controller if needed\n13. Apply item effects to target unit with ProcessUnitItemEffect\n14. Apply equipment bonuses with Ordinal_10525\n15. Locate skill reference for inventory item type (stat 0x36)\n16. If skill reference found, remove old skill, update skill data, and refresh unit state\n\nParameters:\nnItemParamRef: int - Reference to item parameter structure with fields:\n  [0x2]: Item class/type identifier (byte)\n  [0x4]: Target unit type identifier (dword)\n  [0x8]: Source item type (byte)\n  [0x9]: Source item hash reference (dword)\n  [0xd]: Item descriptor base offset (int)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value; function applies item effects directly to game state\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If source item not found, function returns without processing\n- If inventory container invalid, triggers assertion error\n- If target unit is NULL, triggers assertion error\n- Function terminates with FUN_6fb9a10f on fatal errors\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x84: Offset to inventory controller in game context\n0x36: Skill type identifier for equipped inventory items\n0x12ca: Error code for invalid inventory container\n0x