      "comment": "Adds an item to the player's inventory and updates game state.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get game context (player unit) via GetGameContext()\n2. Find source unit in hash table using param_1 offsets (GUID at +0x2f, type at +0x2d)\n3. Validate item path (pUnit[2].pPath) - return error 0x1301 if NULL\n4. If adding to player inventory (source == player):\n   a. Find grid unit (container) at param_1+0xb, type 4\n   b. Call Ordinal_10243 to locate item in container (return error if not found)\n   c. Verify item location matches grid position (error 0x1308 if mismatch)\n   d. Get system state flag via GetGlobalSystemState()\n   e. Call Ordinal_10409 to compute grid mode\n   f. Call Ordinal_10250 to place item at grid position (param_1+0x11, +0x13)\n   g. Initialize UI state and send mouse move message\n5. Call Ordinal_10754 with mode flag (param_1+0x21) to check mode\n6. If mode == 0 (normal placement):\n   a. If grid unit not found, create new item via InitializeItemProperties\n   b. Otherwise set item mode via SetItemMode and grid layout via Ordinal_10720\n7. If mode != 0 (swap/replace):\n   a. Remove old grid unit from hash table\n   b. Create new item via InitializeItemProperties (replaces old)\n8. Set item quantity via Ordinal_10690 (param_1+0x2)\n9. Determine storage mode (3=normal, 4=belt) based on byte at param_1+0x2 (0x0b or 0x0c)\n10. Insert item into container via Ordinal_10242 - return error if fails\n11. Check for existing item at position via Ordinal_10257\n    a. If exists, remove via Ordinal_10254 and log warning\n12. Insert item record via Ordinal_10253 - return error if insert fails\n13. Update player state via FUN_6fb950d0()\n14. Notify container via Ordinal_10289()\n15. Update player stats via FUN_6fb936b0()\n16. Apply item effects via ProcessUnitItemEffect()\n17. Update unit item properties via ProcessUnitItemProperties()\n18. Update game object item effects via ProcessGameObjectItemEffects()\n19. Check for item uniqueness (Ordinal_10480, stat 0x36):\n    a. If unique property set, remove it via Ordinal_10486\n    b. Refresh unique state via Ordinal_10474 and Ordinal_10485\n    c. Update item visuals via Ordinal_10376\n\nParameters:\n  nOpDataOffset (IMPLICIT ECX) - Pointer to packed operation structure containing:\n    +0x2 - byte: Container type/mode (0x0b=belt, 0x0c=belt, else=normal)\n    +0x3 - byte: Item quantity\n    +0xb - dword: Target grid unit ID (container/slot)\n    +0x2d - byte: Source unit type\n    +0x2e - byte: Quality/rarity level\n    +0x2f - dword: Source unit GUID\n    +0x11 - word: Grid X coordinate\n    +0x13 - word: Grid Y coordinate\n    +0x21 - dword: Operation mode (0=place, non-0=replace)\n\nReturns:\n  void - Updates inventory state, logs errors for:\n    0x1301: Item path NULL (source inventory corrupted)\n    0x1305: Grid container not found\n    0x1307: Item not in container\n    0x1308: Item location mismatch\n    0x1313/0x1316: Item creation failed\n  All error paths call FUN_6fb9a10f(0xffffffff) to terminate operation\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Swapped items: Ordinal_10254 called if item already exists at position\n  - Belt vs inventory: Storage mode determined by checking source type byte\n  - Unique items: Stat 0x36 indicates uniqueness property requiring state update\n  - Stack temporaries optimized away: SSA variables in decompiler are temporaries",
