      "comment": "Add an item to unit inventory and apply its effects\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate item data structure and inventory path from unit\n2. If item is for player unit, find grid item in inventory\n3. Grid item placement: remove if exists, add if empty; reuse existing slot if grid full\n4. Create unit item in inventory with [EBP+0x8] flags and buffer\n5. Query item class (0x0B=staff, 0x0C=scroll) to determine grid size (3 or 4)\n6. Insert item into inventory grid; abort if placement fails\n7. Update item stats and grid layout\n8. Process unit and inventory effects for all items\n9. Check for quest drop flags (0x36); if set, clear flag and insert item\n\nParameters:\nnItemData (int, ECX): Item definition pointer with fields:\n  [+0x4] = inventory grid index (IMPLICIT in ECX base)\n  [+0x8] = unit type byte  \n  [+0x9] = unit mode dword\n  [+0xD] = item parameter offset\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Updates inventory system, exits via FUN_6fb9a10f on error\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Player unit: verifies grid item in inventory (0x4 type)\n- Non-player: direct inventory operations\n- Staff/scroll items: use grid size 4 instead of 3\n- Failed placement: logs error, does not insert\n- Quest items: clears drop flag after insertion\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0xD = item data offset for first parameter\n0x36 = quest item drop flag for item search\n0x0B = staff item class value\n0x0C = scroll item class value\n0x04 = grid item type constant\n0xFFFF = position mask for grid calculations",
