      "api_calls": ["FogAssert", "FogAssert", "RemoveItemFromInventory", "FogAssert", "CanItemBeEquipped", "GetFirstActiveInventoryItemId", "GetItemDataFlags", "ClearDyeStatFlags", "RecalculateInventoryStats", "ProcessUnitSkillEvents", "...+67 more"],
      "instructions": ["0x9D0D0|SUB|ESP, 0xc", "0x9D0D3|PUSH|EBX", "0x9D0D4|PUSH|EBP", "0x9D0D5|PUSH|ESI", "0x9D0D6|PUSH|EDI", "0x9D0D7|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0x9D0D9|CALL|0x6fb62880", "0x9D0DE|MOV|ECX, dword ptr [ESI + 0x2f]", "0x9D0E1|XOR|EDX, EDX", "0x9D0E3|MOV|DL, byte ptr [ESI + 0x2d]", "0x9D0E6|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x18], EAX", "0x9D0EA|CALL|0x6fb60e10", "0x9D0EF|MOV|EDI, EAX", "0x9D0F1|MOV|EBX, dword ptr [EDI + 0x84]", "0x9D0F7|TEST|EBX, EBX"],
      "comment": "Processes item inventory actions (move, drop, equip).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Retrieve command structure (ptCmd) containing action mode (0x00=drop, 0x01=move, 0x02=belt, 0x04=drop) and inventory coordinates\n2. Get player's item inventory from game context via FindUnitInHashTable\n3. Validate item exists in inventory (ItemHandle must be non-zero)\n4. Route to appropriate handler based on action mode:\n   - Mode 0x00 (drop): Remove from inventory, call handlers, remove from hash table\n   - Mode 0x01 (move): Move item between inventory slots/panels\n   - Mode 0x02 (belt): Move item to belt (if player matches current unit)\n   - Mode 0x04 (drop/cursor): Process item drop from cursor\n5. For each action: Call ProcessUnitItemEffect() to apply item effects, update UI state flags\n6. Return pointer to created/modified item or NULL on failure\n\nParameters:\nptCmd (void *) - Command structure pointer containing:\n  +0x01 (byte) - Inventory type/slot (action-specific)\n  +0x02 (byte) - Secondary slot selector\n  +0x03 (byte) - Tertiary parameter (-1 invalid)\n  +0x0B (dword) - Player unit handle\n  +0x11 (word) - X coordinate\n  +0x13 (word) - Y coordinate\n  +0x2D (byte) - Inventory page\n  +0x2E (byte) - Action mode (0x00/0x01/0x02/0x04)\n  +0x2F (dword) - Item handle in source inventory\n\nReturns:\nPointer to item structure (int *) - Modified/created item in inventory\nNULL (0x0) - On failure (invalid item, operation failed, assertion triggered)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Validates item exists before processing (uVar11 must be non-zero)\n- Rejects if item already occupied in inventory (*pItem != 0)\n- Asserts character mode byte is valid (terminates on invalid)\n- Handles multiple inventory panels with different size constraints\n- Updates global item slot variables (_g_wItemSlotOther, _g_wItemSlotDruid) when in player context\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x00 - Mode: Drop from inventory / Standard move\n0x01 - Mode: Move between inventory panels\n0x02 - Mode: Belt inventory operation\n0x04 - Mode: Drop from cursor\n0x21 - Offset in item structure for inventory handle\n0x2D - Offset in ptCmd for inventory page/type\n0x2E - Offset in ptCmd for action mode\n0x2F - Offset in ptCmd for item handle\n0x0B - Offset in ptCmd for player handle\n0x100, 0x171 - Validation flags (Ordinal_10707)\n0x36 - Item property flag to check (Ordinal_10480)\n\nRelated Functions:\n- InitializeItemProperties() - Creates new item with properties\n- FindUnitInHashTable() - Retrieves unit from hash table\n- ProcessPlayerItemInsertion() - Inserts item into player inventory\n- ProcessUnitItemEffect() - Applies item effect after move\n- ProcessUnitItemProperties() - Updates item display properties",
      "tags": ["PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "SRC_Item.cpp", "MOD_UNIT", "PARAM_1", "STRUCT_Other", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "NET_SCMD", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
