      "comment": "Process inventory item transfer/movement between inventory slots (grid/body/belt).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract item descriptor fields (type, source index, attributes)\n2. Find source unit in hash table by item descriptor ID\n3. Validate unit has inventory (pPath != NULL)\n4. Handle three transfer modes based on bOperationMode:\n   MODE 0x00 (Grid Transfer): Move item from grid to cursor\n     - Find target inventory slot\n     - Verify slot ownership (must be grid item or cursor)\n     - Remove item from source, create new item in inventory\n     - Update UI state, handler table, effects\n   MODE 0x01 (Body Equipment): Move item to character body slot\n     - Get target body location from descriptor\n     - Create new item, update character model\n     - Set body properties, update equipped state\n     - Clear previous slot state (class-specific handling)\n   MODE 0x02/0x04 (Belt/Hand): Move to belt or hand slot\n     - Get target belt/hand index from descriptor\n     - Create new item with proper slot binding\n     - Update game state flags, effects\n5. Final cleanup: Trigger item property callbacks (0x36 flag)\n6. Return created item unit or NULL on failure\n\nParameters:\nnItemDescriptor (ECX): Encoded item transfer descriptor\n  Offset +0: Source unit ID\n  Offset +2: Source item type\n  Offset +3: Target body slot (equipment transfers)\n  Offset +4: Target inventory slot ID\n  Offset +8: Source slot type\n  Offset +9: Source unit type\n  Offset +13: Item data buffer pointer\n\nReturns:\nint *: Pointer to newly created item unit on success, NULL on failure\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x00 = MODE_GRID_TRANSFER\n0x01 = MODE_BODY_EQUIPMENT\n0x02 = MODE_BELT_ITEM\n0x04 = MODE_HAND_ITEM\n0xff = INVALID_PAGE_FLAG (error in slot allocation)\n0x100 = SLOT_VALIDATION_FLAG\n0x171 = SLOT_ERROR_CODE\n0x46 = ITEM_PROPERTY_FLAG\n0x36 = TRIGGER_CALLBACK_FLAG\n0x400 = EQUIPMENT_ACTIVE_FLAG\n\nRelated Functions:\n- CreateUnitInInventory() - Allocates new item unit\n- FindUnitInHashTable() - Locates source/target units\n- ProcessUnitItemEffect() - Applies item magic effects\n- ProcessPlayerItemInsertion() - Updates player inventory state\n- ProcessGameObjectItemEffects() - Updates area effects",
      "tags": ["PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PROP_NOCALLER", "SRC_Item.cpp", "MOD_UNIT", "STRUCT_Skill", "STRUCT_ItemData", "PARAM_1", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
