      "instructions": ["0x9E0C0|PUSH|ESI", "0x9E0C1|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0x9E0C3|TEST|ESI, ESI", "0x9E0C5|PUSH|EDI", "0x9E0C6|JNZ|0x6fb6e0e6", "0x9E0C8|PUSH|0x1540", "0x9E0CD|PUSH|0x6fbca31c", "0x9E0D2|PUSH|0x6fbb3ee8", "0x9E0D7|CALL|0x6fb99a7a", "0x9E0DC|ADD|ESP, 0xc", "0x9E0DF|PUSH|-0x1", "0x9E0E1|CALL|0x6fb9a10f", "0x9E0E6|PUSH|0x36", "0x9E0E8|PUSH|ESI", "0x9E0E9|CALL|0x6fb986a4"],
      "comment": "Remove item from unit inventory slot.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate slot ID is non-zero (return if zero)\n2. If validation fails, log error and exit with code -1\n3. Get item pointer for slot 0x36 using Ordinal_10480\n4. If item exists:\n   - Clear slot 0x36 to null using Ordinal_10486\n   - Detach item from unit using Ordinal_10474\n   - Free item resources using Ordinal_10485\n   - Update unit appearance/state using Ordinal_10376\n\nParameters:\n- nSlotId (int, register ECX): Inventory slot ID to process\n\nReturns:\n- void (no return value)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Slot ID 0x36 is the target slot (0x36 = 54 decimal, likely EQUIPMENT_SLOT)\n- Function exits immediately on zero slot ID with error logging\n- Non-zero items trigger full item removal sequence\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x36 (54): Equipment slot identifier\n- 0x1540: Error string resource size for logging\n- -0x1: Fatal error exit code",
      "tags": ["SRC_Item.cpp", "MOD_UNIT", "PARAM_1"]
