      "comment": "Initialize or reuse resource handle with callback registration.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Query existing resource handle via Ordinal_10480 with magic 0x36\n2. If handle exists (non-zero): Set init flag and return\n3. If handle not found (zero):\n   a. Create new resource via Ordinal_10470 (args: 0, 2, 0x19, *param_1, param_1[2])\n   b. Mark as initialized via Ordinal_10478(resource, 0x36)\n   c. Register ResourceCallbackThunk callback via Ordinal_10477\n   d. Link resource to parent via Ordinal_10475(param_1, resource)\n4. Return void\n\nParameters:\n- pResourceParams (dword *): Pointer to 3-element array\n  - [0]: Parent resource ID\n  - [2]: Additional resource parameter\n\nReturns:\nNone (void)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Magic value 0x36 indicates resource initialization flag\n- Ordinal values 10470, 10475, 10477, 10478, 10480 are Storm.dll resource management functions\n- ResourceCallbackThunk (0x6fb6e170) is registered as event handler\n\nRelated Functions:\n- ValidateResourceState() - Called before this function\n- HandleResourceEvent() - May invoke registered callback\n- ProcessResourceCleanup() - Called on resource disposal",
