      "comment": "Initialize item properties for a unit and register it in item list.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate input unit pointer is not null, exit with error 0x159b if null\n2. Find unit in hash table using unit ID from offset 0x2f and class from offset 0x2d\n3. Validate found unit reference, exit with error 0x159e if not found\n4. Remove old item from hash table at offset 0xb with reference count 4\n5. Initialize new item properties with unit's item ID (offset 0xb) and item flags (offset 0xf)\n6. Validate new item initialization succeeded, exit with error 0x15a1 if failed\n7. Apply item display flags (constant 0x46) via Ordinal_10517\n8. Retrieve unit's base unit reference from offset 0x84 of found unit\n9. Register new item in unit's item list via Ordinal_10261\n10. Complete item registration via Ordinal_10262\n11. Forward processing result to FUN_6fb8f0c0 for finalization\n\nParameters:\n  pUnit (UnitAny*): Pointer to unit structure containing item ID and class information\n\nReturns:\n  void (tail-called to FUN_6fb8f0c0)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  Null unit pointer: Ordinal_10023 logs error at line 0x159b, exits via FUN_6fb9a10f\n  Unit not found: Ordinal_10023 logs error at line 0x159e, exits via FUN_6fb9a10f\n  Item init failed: Ordinal_10023 logs error at line 0x15a1, exits via FUN_6fb9a10f\n\nNote: Function uses 2 stack-allocated temporaries optimized away by compiler",
