      "instructions": ["0x9E4D0|SUB|ESP, 0x8", "0x9E4D3|PUSH|EBX", "0x9E4D4|PUSH|EBP", "0x9E4D5|PUSH|ESI", "0x9E4D6|PUSH|EDI", "0x9E4D7|MOV|EDI, ECX", "0x9E4D9|TEST|EDI, EDI", "0x9E4DB|JZ|0x6fb6e608", "0x9E4E1|MOV|ESI, dword ptr [EDI + 0x84]", "0x9E4E7|TEST|ESI, ESI", "0x9E4E9|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x10], ESI", "0x9E4ED|JZ|0x6fb6e608", "0x9E4F3|PUSH|ESI", "0x9E4F4|CALL|0x6fb98896", "0x9E4F9|MOV|EBP, EAX"],
      "comment": "Processes and removes inventory items from a unit matching specific criteria.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if unit pointer is valid and has inventory items\n2. Get inventory item list handle from unit offset 0x84\n3. Iterate through inventory items using next-item navigation\n4. For each item, retrieve item color and item type attributes\n5. Validate item type is supported (type 1 or 3), fail if type 0\n6. If item type is 3 or (type 1 AND passes validation check via Ordinal_10840):\n   a. Process unit cleanup via FUN_6fb950d0\n   b. Remove item from inventory (Ordinal_10290)\n   c. Verify removal count matches expected item count (Ordinal_10243)\n   d. If item type 3, get item ID and apply it (Ordinal_10260, Ordinal_10254)\n   e. Mark item for processing (Ordinal_10871)\n   f. If unit inventory emptied, clear related data (Ordinal_10258)\n   g. Check for resource constraints (Ordinal_10707 with params 0x100, 0x171)\n   h. If resource check failed, process special handling (Ordinal_10524)\n   i. Notify system of item removal (Ordinal_10514)\n   j. Update handler tables for item (ProcessHandlerTable)\n   k. Update unit item properties (Ordinal_10954, ProcessUnitItemProperties)\n7. Continue iteration to next inventory item\n8. Clean up inventory list after iteration (Ordinal_10300)\n\nParameters:\npUnit (uint *) - Pointer to unit structure; expects inventory handle at offset 0x84\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value; performs in-place modifications to unit inventory\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Item type must be 1 or 3; type 0 triggers assertion failure via Ordinal_10023\n- Removal validation failures trigger assertion failures\n- Empty inventory after removal triggers different handling path\n- Resource constraint failures (type 3) skip certain processing steps",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "SRC_Item.cpp", "MOD_UNIT", "PARAM_1", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
    },
