      "instructions": ["0x9E670|XOR|AX, AX", "0x9E673|MOV|AL, CL", "0x9E675|CMP|AX, word ptr [0x6fbca2b0]", "0x9E67C|JNC|0x6fb6e68c", "0x9E67E|AND|ECX, 0xff", "0x9E684|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [ECX*0x8 + 0x6fbca158]", "0x9E68B|RET|", "0x9E68C|XOR|EAX, EAX", "0x9E68E|RET|"],
      "comment": "Retrieve damage value for specified item damage stat index\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Clear EAX register and load byDamageIndex into AL\n2. Compare index against g_wMaxItemDamageStatIndex limit\n3. If index >= limit, jump to return 0\n4. If index < limit, extend index to 32-bit ECX\n5. Access g_pdwItemDamageTable[index*8] for dword lookup\n6. Return damage value in EAX, or 0 if out of bounds\n\nParameters:\nbyte byDamageIndex - Item damage stat index value (0-based)\n\nReturns:\ndword - Damage value from table entry, or 0 if index exceeds max\n\nSpecial Cases:\nOut of bounds index safely returns 0\nMagic number 0x8 scales index for dword offset calculation",
