      "instructions": ["0x9E730|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [ESP + 0xc]", "0x9E734|PUSH|EBX", "0x9E735|PUSH|ESI", "0x9E736|PUSH|EDI", "0x9E737|MOV|EBX, EDX", "0x9E739|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0x9E73B|PUSH|EAX", "0x9E73C|CALL|0x6fb9836e", "0x9E741|MOV|EDI, EAX", "0x9E743|TEST|EDI, EDI", "0x9E745|JNZ|0x6fb6e762", "0x9E747|PUSH|0x78", "0x9E749|PUSH|0x6fbcdd80", "0x9E74E|PUSH|0x6fbb1418", "0x9E753|CALL|0x6fb99a7a"],
      "comment": "Initialize unit resources and attributes for a unit based on difficulty class and apply state flags.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate difficulty/class via Ordinal_10589(nDestY) - returns pResData or 0\n2. If validation fails, log error and terminate with code -1\n3. Initialize unit state via Ordinal_11115(pUnit)\n4. Retrieve class index from [pResData + 0x63] and apply via Ordinal_10348\n5. Position unit on map via Ordinal_10152(0, nX, nY, nDestX, pUnit, 1)\n6. Load attribute pointer from [pUnit + 0x38]\n7. Check equipped flag at [pResData + 0x64]: 0x00 means not equipped, non-zero means equipped\n8. Call Ordinal_10182 to set attribute value (0 if not equipped, 0x40 if equipped)\n9. Get attribute index from [pResData + 0x63] and lookup in g_pdwAttributeValues table\n10. Apply attribute via Ordinal_10184\n11. Check feature flag at [pResData + 0x69]: if set enable (OR 0x04), if clear disable (AND 0xfb)\n12. Apply final state mask: set bits while clearing specific flags\n\nParameters:\n  pUnit (ECX): Pointer to unit structure to initialize\n  nX (EDX): Starting X coordinate on game map\n  nY (Stack[0x4]): Starting Y coordinate on game map\n  nDestX (Stack[0x8]): Destination X coordinate for pathfinding\n  nDestY (Stack[0xc]): Encoded difficulty and class index passed to Ordinal_10589\n\nReturns:\n  void - Modifies pUnit structure in-place with initialized resources and attributes\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  Magic values: 0x40 (equipped), 0x04 (feature bit), 0xfb (mask), 0xf5 (mask), 0x20 (state)",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "MOD_UNIT", "SRC_Missile.cpp", "PARAM_5", "STRUCT_Other", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
