      "api_count": 5,
      "api_calls": ["GetMissileTemplateRecord", "GetRandomBoundedValue", "GetRandomBoundedValue", "UNITS_GetRoom", "FindRegionByCoordinates"],
      "instructions": ["0x9E820|SUB|ESP, 0x64", "0x9E823|PUSH|EBX", "0x9E824|PUSH|EBP", "0x9E825|PUSH|ESI", "0x9E826|MOV|ESI, dword ptr [ESP + 0x7c]", "0x9E82A|PUSH|EDI", "0x9E82B|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x14], EDX", "0x9E82F|MOV|EBX, ECX", "0x9E831|PUSH|ESI", "0x9E832|CALL|0x6fb9836e", "0x9E837|MOV|EDX, EBX", "0x9E839|MOV|EBP, dword ptr [ESP + 0x7c]", "0x9E83D|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x80], EAX", "0x9E844|MOV|EAX, EBP", "0x9E846|IMUL|EAX, EBP"],
      "comment": "Process all walkable tiles within a circular distance from a center point.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get unit flags from item code parameter using Ordinal_10589\n2. Check if unit pointer is already resolved (values 0 and 1 are reserved), otherwise call GetUnitFromHashTable\n3. Initialize local processing array (22 dwords) to zeros\n4. Set default flags (0x201) and item code in processing structures\n5. Calculate squared radius (nRadius * nRadius) for efficient distance check\n6. For each Y coordinate from -nRadius to +nRadius:\n   - For each X coordinate from -nRadius to +nRadius:\n     - Check if (X^2 + Y^2) <= (nRadius^2) - point is within circular distance\n     - If nRandom parameter is set, call RandSeed to validate random number\n     - Calculate absolute tile coordinates: nLocalX = nDistX + nBaseX, nLocalY = nDistY + nBaseY\n     - Check if unit has active state flag (test at [nFlagsOffset + 0x5c])\n     - If flag set, seed random number generator\n     - Get item data using GetItemData ordinal\n     - Call Ordinal_10042 with item code and coordinates to process tile\n     - If return value non-zero, call FUN_6fb77720 with processing array\n\nParameters:\npUnit (int *) - Unit pointer or reserved value (0=NULL, 1=player)\nnBaseX (int) - Center X tile coordinate\nnBaseY (int) - Center Y tile coordinate\nnRadius (int) - Search radius in tiles (both positive and negative checked)\ndwFlags (dword) - Unit flags/item code for state lookup\nnRandom (int) - Random seed parameter (0=skip random, non-zero=validate)\n\nReturns: void - Processing happens through callback function FUN_6fb77720\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Radius values can be negative; function uses absolute value for distance calculation\n- Processing continues even if some tiles fail validation\n- Random seed call is conditional on nRandom parameter value\n- Active flag check at [nFlagsOffset + 0x5c] determines random seeding behavior\n- Ordinal_10589 resolves item code to flags offset\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x16 - Array size in dwords (22 dwords = 88 bytes for local processing structure)\n0x201 - Default processing flags value\n0x5c - Offset within item code structure to active flag check\n0x64 - Total stack frame size (100 bytes local storage)\n\nRelated Functions:\n- GetUnitFromHashTable - Resolve unit pointers to processing units\n- Ordinal_10589 - Get flags offset from item code\n- Ordinal_10918 - RandSeed for random number generation\n- Ordinal_10342 - GetUnitStat for unit state queries\n- Ordinal_10042 - Get item data structure\n- FUN_6fb77720 - Process tiles matching criteria",
      "tags": ["PARAM_6", "STRUCT_MonsterData", "STRUCT_Path", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Room2", "STRUCT_Room1", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
    },
