      "comment": "Update the visual display position of a game unit based on game state.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call Ordinal_11125 (GetUnitState) - get initial unit classification\n2. Check if returned value < 6 (valid unit range)\n3. If invalid, check special case using bitwise AND 0x80000001 for even/odd conditions\n4. If value is not 0/1, exit without updating display position\n5. Load display configuration from unit[0xe] (offset 0x38)\n6. Call Ordinal_11141 to get X dimension\n7. Call Ordinal_11143 to get Y dimension\n8. Calculate center and half-offset: nCenterY = (X-Y)/2, nCenterX = (X+Y)/2\n9. Call Ordinal_10329 to get Y base, add nCenterX for final Y coordinate\n10. Call Ordinal_10326 to get X base, add nCenterY for final X coordinate  \n11. Call Ordinal_10170 to update viewport coordinate\n12. Call Ordinal_10142 to set unit state/appearance with flag 0\n13. Call Ordinal_11140 with nCenterY parameter\n14. Call Ordinal_11142 with nCenterX parameter\n15. Call FUN_6fb771e0 to finalize unit display update\n\nParameters:\npUnit: uint* - Pointer to unit data structure (passed in ECX via __fastcall)\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Units with classification >= 6 are skipped (inactive/invalid)\n- Even/odd classification check via bitwise manipulation of flag bit 0x80000001\n- Coordinate calculations use signed division with arithmetic shift for center positioning\n- Note: Function uses 9 SSA temporaries (dwFlags, nOffsetX/Y, nCenterX/Y + register spillovers) optimized away in decompilation view",
