      "comment": "Iterate over rectangular area, finding and processing units for spell/ability effects.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize tile data structure and flags with radius parameter\n2. Get unit type info and area Y-offset for the given unit type\n3. Square the radius for distance calculations\n4. Clear local work buffer (22 dwords), set flag 0x8000 if special flags provided\n5. Get unit from hash table for the given unit ID\n6. Start nested loop: outer loop iterates Y from -radius to +radius\n7. Inner loop iterates X from -radius to +radius\n8. For each cell: check if distance squared (X*X + Y*Y) <= radius squared\n9. If in range: iterate through units at that tile position\n10. For each unit found: check if it's valid (not already processed)\n11. If valid: determine item class based on random seed (0=0x45, 1=0x68, 2=0x69)\n12. Store coordinates and class in local buffer\n13. Call FUN_6fb77720 to apply effect if special processing needed\n14. Continue until all cells in radius processed\n\nParameters:\nnUnitType (ECX): Unit type ID to search for\nnRadius (EDX): Radius of effect area\nnSpecialFlags (stack param): Additional processing flags (bit 0x8000 set if non-zero)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Function modifies global state through ordinal calls\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If nRadius is 0, inner loop condition fails and no cells processed\n- Special seed value (0-2) maps to item classes (0x45, 0x68, 0x69)\n- Phantom optimization: Function uses 16 stack-allocated temporaries optimized away in assembly\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x8000: Special processing flag bit\n- 0x2c: Unit structure field offset\n- 0x45, 0x68, 0x69: Item class codes\n- 0x4: Mana drain value check\n- Distance check: X*X + Y*Y <= radius*radius (circular area)",
