      "comment": "Checks if a unit is within viewport bounds and toggles render visibility.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if unit is active/allocated using Ordinal_10378\n2. If active, set finalization flag via SetEntityFinalizationFlag\n3. Clear previous hover/selection state via Ordinal_10146 on unit field offset 0x38\n4. Get unit's X coordinate via Ordinal_10333\n5. Validate X coordinate within viewport: viewport_x <= unitX <= viewport_x + viewport_height\n6. If X valid, get unit's Y coordinate via Ordinal_10334\n7. Validate Y coordinate within viewport with 0x40 buffer: viewport_y <= unitY <= viewport_y + viewport_height + 0x40\n8. If both X and Y valid, set visibility flag 0x80 via Ordinal_11123\n9. Call FUN_6fb771e0 for render setup\n10. If out of bounds, call FUN_6fb773b0 to hide/remove unit with parameters (NULL, 0)\n\nParameters:\n  pUnit (dword *): Pointer to unit structure being visibility-tested\n  IMPLICIT ECX: First parameter (Diablo II __fastcall convention)\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Out-of-bounds units are handled via FUN_6fb773b0 (likely despawn/hide)\n  - Viewport height has 0x40 (64-pixel) buffer on Y axis for partial rendering\n  - Finalization flag set regardless of visibility (cleanup path)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x0e: Offset into unit structure for state field\n  0x38: Offset into unit structure for hover/selection state\n  0x80: Visibility flag set via Ordinal_11123\n  0x40: Y-axis viewport buffer (64 pixels)",
      "tags": ["PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_1"]
    },
