      "comment": "UpdateUnitProjectileOnPathMismatch - Updates projectile state when unit path coordinates mismatch.\n\nThis function checks if the unit's path has a coordinate mismatch flag set,\nand if so, initializes and allocates a new projectile with updated range data.\nAlways processes unit stats afterward.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get path coordinate mismatch flag from unit's pPath (offset 0x38)\n2. If mismatch detected:\n   - Initialize 0x16 DWORDs of message buffer to zero\n   - Set message type to 0x200d (projectile update)\n   - Set message subtype to 0x27 (39)\n   - Get unit references from hash table\n   - Call D2Common ordinals for coordinates\n   - Calculate effective range = missileRange * 2 - 2\n   - Initialize and allocate projectile\n3. Always call ProcessUnitStats on the unit\n\nParameters:\n  pUnit - Pointer to UnitAny structure being processed\n\nReturns: void",
