      "comment": "Initializes player skills by setting up skill table entries and random seed timer.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load skill table entry from pData[0x38] into dwSkillProcessed\n2. Generate random seed value via Ordinal_10918 (RandSeed)\n3. Call FUN_6fb97b10 to initialize skill with adjusted seed (seed - 8)\n4. Load skill unit reference from pUnit[0x38] into dwSkillIdentifier\n5. Process skill data via Ordinal_10158 (skill data processor)\n6. Initialize skill via Ordinal_10161_SkillInit with processed data\n7. Reset skill state via Ordinal_10203 with processed data\n8. Check byte flag at [dwSkillProcessed + 0x58]\n9. If flag set (non-zero): Call RandSeed again, shift left 8 bits, store at pUnit[0x50]\n10. If flag clear (zero): Store 0 at pUnit[0x50]\n\nParameters:\n- pUnit (void*) - Unit data structure pointer with fields:\n  - [0x04] - Item/skill identifier\n  - [0x38] - Skill unit reference\n  - [0x50] - Timer value storage\n- pData (void*) - Data structure with field:\n  - [0x38] - Skill table entry\n\nReturns:\n- void (all results stored in unit structure at offset 0x50)\n\nStructure Offsets:\npUnit layout:\n  Offset | Size | Purpose | Type\n  0x04   | 4    | ID ref  | uint\n  0x38   | 4    | Skill   | uint\n  0x50   | 4    | Timer   | uint\n\npData layout:\n  Offset | Size | Purpose | Type\n  0x38   | 4    | Entry   | uint\n\nRelated Functions:\n- Ordinal_10918 - RandSeed: Generate random number\n- Ordinal_10589 - GetItemData: Retrieve item/skill data\n- Ordinal_10158 - Process skill data\n- Ordinal_10161 - SkillInit: Initialize skill\n- Ordinal_10203 - Reset skill state\n- FUN_6fb97b10 - Initialization routine",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Inventory", "PARAM_2", "PROP_NOCALLER", "STRUCT_UnitAny"]
