      "comment": "InitializeMissileRandomBehavior - Sets up missile targeting and spawns randomized child projectiles.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Gets target unit from missile's hash table reference\n2. Retrieves current target Y coordinate and field 24 value\n3. If target exists, decrements target counter and sets new target\n4. If field 24 is zero, creates child projectile with random parameters:\n   - Random count (1-6), random X offset (-20 to +20), random Y offset (-20 to +20)\n   - Ensures at least one non-zero offset by forcing X if both are zero\n5. Assigns random target index (0-4) to new projectile\n6. Updates missile target unit ID and processes unit stats\n\nParameters:\n  pSourceMissile - The missile unit to initialize random behavior for\n\nReturns: void",
