      "comment": "Initializes a random state array for seed operations.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Create 22-element state array, zero-initialize all elements using REP STOSD (0x16 = 22 dwords)\n2. Set state[0] = 2 (type flag), state[1] = dwParam1, state[2] = dwParam2\n3. Set state offset 0x34 = 1 (flag), offset 0x48 = dwParam3\n4. Get first random seed: nSeed1 = 0x14 - RandSeed() via Ordinal_10918\n5. Get second random seed: nSeed2 = 0x14 - RandSeed() via Ordinal_10918\n6. If both seeds are zero, get third: nSeed1 = RandSeed() + 1 via Ordinal_10918\n7. Allocate result structure via FUN_6fb77720(state array pointer)\n8. If allocated (result != NULL), apply seeds: Ordinal_11140(pResult, nSeed1), Ordinal_11142(pResult, nSeed2)\n9. Return result pointer\n\nParameters:\ndwParam1 (uint) - First seed parameter, stored in state[1]\ndwParam2 (uint) - Second seed parameter, stored in state[2]\ndwParam3 (uint) - Third parameter, stored in state array offset 0x48\n\nReturns:\nint * - Pointer to allocated and initialized result structure, or NULL if allocation fails\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x16 = 22 (array element count for STOSD.REP initialization loop)\n0x14 = 20 (seed offset calculation value for seed bounds)\n0x2 = Type/version flag stored in state[0]\n0x1 = Flag value stored in state offset 0x34\n\nRelated Functions:\n- FUN_6fb77720 - Allocates and configures result structure from state array\n- Ordinal_10918 (RandSeed) - Generates random seed values from internal state\n- Ordinal_11140 - Sets property 1 on result using first seed value\n- Ordinal_11142 - Sets property 2 on result using second seed value\n\nNote: Function uses stack-allocated temporaries optimized away by compiler in final register allocation.",
