      "comment": "Process and initialize a timed spell/effect duration with random seed calculation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get current random seed via Ordinal_10918 (D2Common.RandSeed)\n2. Add 0x9f offset to seed for variance\n3. Fetch base delay value (0x3b) via Ordinal_10992 (D2Common.GetUnitStat)\n4. Fetch modified delay value (0x3b) via Ordinal_10990 (D2Common.GetUnitStat)\n5. Call FUN_6fb72560 with effect pointer, both delay values, and calculated seed\n6. If effect instance created successfully (non-NULL return):\n   - Initialize effect data via FUN_6fb97b10 with 0x78 size parameter\n   - Set effect attributes via FUN_6fb97b40 with magic value -0x5 and flag 1\n   - Apply effect flag 0x18 via Ordinal_11121 (D2Common.ApplyEffectFlag)\n   - Apply effect flag 0x18 via Ordinal_11123 (D2Common.ApplyEffectFlag)\n7. Cleanup via FUN_6fb771e0 with original effect pointer (tail call)\n\nParameters:\npEffectData (uint *): Pointer to effect data structure to process (passed in ECX register via __fastcall)\n\nReturns:\nvoid: No return value; modifies effect data in-place\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If FUN_6fb72560 returns NULL (piVar4), effect initialization block is skipped\n- Magic number 0x9f applied to seed for entropy variation\n- Magic number 0x78 (120 bytes) represents effect data structure size\n- Magic number -0x5 (0xFFFFFFFB) used as effect attribute initialization value\n- Flag 0x18 applied twice via different ordinals (possibly state mode flags)\n- Function uses __fastcall: parameter in ECX, no stack parameters\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x9f: Seed offset variance constant\n0x3b: Stat/delay parameter identifier\n0x78: Effect structure size in bytes (120)\n0x18: Effect state flag or mode constant\n0x0: NULL pointer check value\n-0x5: Signed attribute value (0xFFFFFFFB unsigned)\n0x1: Boolean flag for FUN_6fb97b40\n\nStructure Layout (effect data):\n[Inferred from offset 0x2c access in LEA instruction]\nOffset | Size | Field Name | Type | Description\n0x00   | 4    | dwTyp