      "comment": "Process and apply timed spell statistics to a unit with frequency-based calculations.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate that nFrequencyDivisor is non-zero, exit with error if zero\n2. Get current unit value (Ordinal_11124: GetUnitStat) and check divisibility by nFrequencyDivisor\n3. If not evenly divisible (modulo != 0), skip processing and return NULL\n4. Retrieve unit structure from hash table via GetUnitFromHashTable\n5. If unit not found (NULL), return NULL\n6. Get unit's base property (Ordinal_10326: GetPropertyX) and random seed value\n7. Initialize 22-element stack buffer (88 bytes) with zeros, set element[0] = 0x2003\n8. Store retrieved unit pointer and config param in buffer\n9. Calculate random offsets: if (nFrequency-1)*2 != 0, call RandSeed (Ordinal_10918), else use 0\n10. Calculate adjusted X = GetPropertyX + (nFrequency-1-randomOffset1)\n11. Calculate adjusted Y = GetPropertyY + (nFrequency-1-randomOffset2)\n12. Get unit Y coordinate via Ordinal_10342 (GetUnitYCoord)\n13. If unit has Y coordinate, call Ordinal_10118 (CheckBlockedTile) with adjusted coords and param 4\n14. If CheckBlockedTile returns 0 (success), call FUN_6fb77720 with buffer and return result\n15. If any check fails, return NULL (error path at 0x6fb7267b)\n\nParameters:\n- nUnitId (int, ECX): Unit ID to process\n- nFrequency (int, EDX): Frequency multiplier for calculations\n- nFrequencyDivisor (int, [ESP+0x68]): Divisor for frequency check (must be non-zero)\n- pConfig (void*, implicit): Configuration/context pointer passed to downstream functions\n\nReturns:\n- int*: Pointer to initialized unit buffer (88 bytes) on success, NULL on validation failure or tile blocked condition\n- Success: Buffer contains unit data with 0x2003 flag set\n- Failure: NULL when modulo check fails, unit not found, or tile blocked\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If nFrequencyDivisor is 0, function immediately exits with error code -1\n- Frequency-based modulo check prevents execution on certain iteration counts\n- Random offsets provide variance in coordinate calculations (RandSeed may return 0)\n- Blocked tile check prevents placement on invalid positions\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x16 (22): Number of elements in stack buffer array\n- 0x2003: Flag value set at buffer offset 0 (likely unit type/state indicator)\n- 0x4: Fourth parameter to CheckBlockedTile (movement/validity flag)\n- 0x133: Error code for invalid divisor (passed to assertion)\n- 0xffffffff (-1): Termination code on fatal error\n\nStructure Layout: Stack buffer contains UnitAny structure\n| Offset | Size | Field Name | Type | Description |\n|--------|------|-----------|------|-------------|\n| 0x00 | 4 | dwUnitFlags | uint | Unit state flags (0x2003 initialized) |\n| 0x04 | 4 | pUnit | int* | Pointer to unit structure |\n| 0x08 | 4 | pConfig | void* | Configuration context |\n| 0x0C-0x58 | 76 | abyReserved | byte[19] | Reserved/temporary space |\n\nRelated Functions:\n- ProcessTimedSpellEffect() - Caller, manages spell timer loop\n- GetUnitFromHashTable() - Retrieve unit structure from hash\n- CheckBlockedTile() - Validate target tile accessibility\n- FUN_6fb77720() - Final unit buffer processor",
