      "instructions": ["0xA2990|PUSH|EBX", "0xA2991|PUSH|EBP", "0xA2992|PUSH|ESI", "0xA2993|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0xA2995|PUSH|ESI", "0xA2996|CALL|0x6fb98ee4", "0xA299B|MOV|EBX, EAX", "0xA299D|PUSH|ESI", "0xA299E|CALL|0x6fb98ede", "0xA29A3|MOV|EBP, EAX", "0xA29A5|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [ESI + 0x4]", "0xA29A8|CMP|EAX, 0x240", "0xA29AD|JNZ|0x6fb729b4", "0xA29AF|MOV|EBX, 0x227", "0xA29B4|PUSH|ESI"],
      "comment": "Processes unit render distance and calculates animation parameters based on proximity.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Retrieve unit flags from Ordinal_11132\n2. Retrieve unit radius from Ordinal_11134\n3. Check if unit type is 0x240; if so, override flags to 0x227\n4. Retrieve slot index from Ordinal_11125\n5. If slot index < 10, proceed with distance calculation:\n   - Get X coordinate via Ordinal_10326\n   - Get Y coordinate via Ordinal_10329\n   - Call ProcessCircleWithinDistance with coordinates, index, radius, flags, and radius threshold 0x14\n6. Call FUN_6fb771e0 for post-processing\n\nParameters:\n- pUnit (uint*): Pointer to unit structure containing flags, type, coordinates, and radius\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Type 0x240 forces flags to 0x227 for special render handling\n- Slot index >= 10 skips distance calculation entirely",
      "tags": ["PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_1"]
    },
