      "comment": "Check value and conditionally process data.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call Ordinal_11124(pData) to retrieve nValue from data pointer\n2. Compare nValue against threshold 100 (0x64)\n3. If nValue < 100, call Ordinal_11123(pData, 500) to execute conditional processing\n4. Call FUN_6fb771e0(pData) for data finalization regardless of threshold\n5. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\npData (void *): Generic data pointer passed to all ordinal function calls\n\nReturns:\nvoid: Function does not return meaningful value; all work performed via side effects\n\nSpecial Cases:\nMagic number 0x64 (100) is used as conditional threshold\nMagic number 500 (0x1f4) passed as second parameter to Ordinal_11123\nOrdinal_11124 and Ordinal_11123 from unknown DLL (not in KNOWN_ORDINALS.md)",
