      "comment": "Process rendering state update based on data type check. Applies conditional rendering configuration and finalizes display state.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Query data state from pData using Ordinal_11124 (returns state code in EAX)\n2. If state == 0x96: Set rendering mode 0x19 with timeout 4000ms via SetRenderingState\n3. If state == 0x32: Apply special effect type 0x121e with float coords (0.0, 0.0)\n4. Finalize rendering by calling FUN_6fb771e0 with pData (executed after all state handling)\n\nParameters:\npData (IMPLICIT ECX): void * - Polymorphic data object with state property queried by Ordinal_11124\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value, state changes applied as side effects\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- States 0x96 and 0x32 are mutually exclusive (conditional branches don't overlap)\n- FUN_6fb771e0 called unconditionally AFTER state handling for final rendering\n- Parameter pData should be replaced with specific structure type when identified\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x96 - Primary state code (triggers SetRenderingState path)\n0x32 - Secondary state code (triggers special effect path)\n0x19 - SetRenderingState mode parameter\n0xfa0 - 4000 in decimal, timeout value for SetRenderingState\n0x121e - Special effect identifier code",
