      "comment": "Process unit class-specific effects based on unit type.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get unit class type from unit pointer using Ordinal_11125\n2. If class type is 0x08 (Barbarian):\n   - Clear unit soul (param_1[1]) via Ordinal_10589\n   - Initialize unit graphics/animation state via FUN_6fb97b90 with size=0x100\n   - Apply class-specific stat shift (>>1, divide by 2) via Ordinal_10377\n3. Else if class type is 0x23 (Druid):\n   - Clear unit soul (param_1[1]) via Ordinal_10589\n   - Apply class-specific stat shift (<<1, multiply by 2) via Ordinal_10377\n   - Process druid form finalization via FUN_6fb771e0\n   - Return (skip default processing)\n4. For all other types:\n   - Process default unit finalization via FUN_6fb771e0\n\nParameters:\n- pUnit (uint *): Pointer to UnitAny structure containing class type at offset 0x0 and slot state at 0x4\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Only classes 0x08 and 0x23 receive stat shift effects; other classes use default processing only\n- Stat shift is arithmetic right-shift for Barbarian (signed division by 2), left-shift for Druid (multiplication by 2)\n- FUN_6fb771e0 is called for all paths (always cleans up/finalizes unit state)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x08: Barbarian class type identifier\n- 0x23: Druid class type identifier  \n- 0x4: Unit soul/tracking handle field offset\n- 0x58: Unit stat value field offset (param_1[0x16] = param_1 + 0x58)\n- 0x100: Graphics/animation state size in FUN_6fb97b90\n- >>1 and <<1: Arithmetic shift operations on stat values",
      "tags": ["PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_1"]
    },
