      "comment": "Validates unit attribute configuration and conditionally triggers area-based unit processing.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Return 0 if dwFlags is non-zero (flags indicate skip condition)\n2. Initialize dwParam=1 and dwAnimationType=3\n3. Retrieve unit X coordinate via Ordinal_10329 (D2Common.GetUnitX)\n4. Retrieve unit Y coordinate via Ordinal_10326 (D2Common.GetUnitY)\n5. Retrieve unit stat value via Ordinal_10342 (D2Common.GetUnitStat)\n6. Call Ordinal_10119 (D2Common validation function) with coordinates and stat\n7. If validation fails (nResult==0), allocate 0x150 bytes via Ordinal_10589 (Fog.MemAlloc)\n8. Load pointer from offset 0x78 in allocated block\n9. Call ProcessAreaUnitsAndEffects with effect parameter 0x19\n10. Return 1 on success\n\nParameters:\ndwUnit (ECX): Pointer to unit structure to validate\ndwFlags (EDX): Control flags; non-zero causes immediate early return\n\nReturns:\n1 - validation complete or effects successfully processed\n0 - early exit due to dwFlags being non-zero\n\nSpecial Cases:\nFunction uses 1 stack-allocated temporary optimized away by compiler.\nValidation step (Ordinal_10119) determines if area effects are triggered.\nNote: iVar1 is phantom variable (optimized away) and cannot be renamed.",
