      "comment": "Validate unit state and dispatch processing to ordinal handlers.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Retrieve unit from hash table using unit ID (pUnitId)\n2. If unit lookup failed (NULL), call error handler and return\n3. Check if unit's type field [0] is within valid range [0, 2)\n4. If type in range, validate unit state via ValidateUnitTypeState\n5. If validation fails (non-zero result), call error handler and return\n6. If validation succeeds, dispatch to Ordinal_10235 for processing\n7. Call Ordinal_10374 for post-processing\n8. Return\n\nParameters:\n  pUnitId (uint *) - Unit identifier/reference pointer\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - NULL unit pointer triggers immediate error handler call\n  - Unit type outside [0, 2) range skips validation and goes to ordinal path\n  - ValidateUnitTypeState failure (non-zero) prevents ordinal dispatch",
