      "comment": "Validate unit stat cache and update display.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Retrieve current unit stats value via Ordinal_11141 (returns nCurrentStats or 0)\n2. Get stored/cached stats value from unit via FUN_6fb97c60 (accesses offset 0x40)\n3. If both stats values exist and differ (cache mismatch), trigger stats recalculation:\n   - Call FUN_6fb8d210 with mode 0x970 to force state update/recalculation\n4. Pass stored stats to Ordinal_11140 for synchronization/display update\n5. Call PrepareUnitStatsDisplay() to refresh UI display\n\nParameters:\npUnit (dword *) - Pointer to unit structure (passed in ECX per __fastcall)\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If nCurrentStats is 0 (no current stats), skips recalculation\n- If nStoredStats is 0 (no cached stats), skips recalculation\n- If values match, skips FUN_6fb8d210 call (cache is valid)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x970 - Mode parameter for FUN_6fb8d210 state update operation\n\nOrdinal References:\nOrdinal_11141 - Retrieve current unit stats from game state (unknown - appears to fetch active stat value)\nOrdinal_11140 - Synchronize/display unit stats in UI (unknown - appears to update display with new stats)\n\nRelated Functions:\n- Ordinal_11141 - Retrieve current unit stats (unknown ordinal)\n- FUN_6fb97c60 - Get stored stats from unit structure\n- FUN_6fb8d210 - Force unit state recalculation/update\n- Ordinal_11140 - Synchronize/update unit stats display (unknown ordinal)\n- PrepareUnitStatsDisplay - Refresh stats UI panel",
