      "comment": "Generate randomized movement offsets for a unit and process possible movement paths.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Retrieve unit pointer from hash table using nUnitId\n2. Initialize movement data array (37 elements) with zero values, set element 0x24 to 0x524\n3. Get unit X and Y coordinates using Ordinal_10326 and Ordinal_10329\n4. For each iteration (0 to nIterations-1):\n   - Calculate random offset X = Ordinal_10918() - 2*nIterations + nX\n   - Calculate random offset Y = Ordinal_10918() - 2*nIterations + nY\n   - Call Ordinal_10398 to calculate distance with (nUnitId, offsetX, offsetY)\n   - If distance > 3: store in nX2/nY2 and call FUN_6fb77720 to process\n5. Get unit mode using Ordinal_11120, store in nMode\n6. Initialize movement data table with hardcoded coordinate deltas\n7. For each movement variant (0x00..0x48 in steps of 4):\n   - If pUnit valid: clear temp structure, calculate adjusted coordinates, call FUN_6fb77720\n\nParameters:\n  nUnitId (fastcall ECX): Unit identifier for hash table lookup\n  nIterations (fastcall EDX): Number of random offset iterations (iteration count)\n  nDeltaX (stack): Delta X offset value\n  nDeltaY (stack): Delta Y offset value\n\nReturns:\n  void (no return value)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If distance <= 3: movement offset rejected, no processing\n  - If pUnit is NULL: iteration skipped\n  - Hardcoded movement offsets in pMovementData suggest diagonal and cardinal directions\n  - Note: Function uses compiler-generated stack temporaries (uStack_*) that are optimized away\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x524 - Movement data table size or state marker\n  0x1c8 - Mode-related constant\n  0x16 - Clear loop count (22 elements)\n  0x48 - Final iteration boundary (18 variants * 4 bytes)\n  3 - Distance threshold for movement validity",
