      "api_count": 10,
      "api_calls": ["GetMonsterDirectionTable", "FogAssert", "GetRandomBoundedValue", "UNITS_GetOwnerGuid", "GetRandomBoundedValue", "UNITS_GetUnitY", "GetMissileTemplateRecord", "FogAssert", "ApplyScalars", "ApplyScalars"],
      "instructions": ["0xA52F0|SUB|ESP, 0x70", "0xA52F3|PUSH|EBX", "0xA52F4|MOV|EBX, ECX", "0xA52F6|PUSH|ESI", "0xA52F7|LEA|EAX, [ESP + 0xc]", "0xA52FB|PUSH|EDI", "0xA52FC|LEA|ECX, [ESP + 0xc]", "0xA5300|PUSH|EAX", "0xA5301|XOR|EDI, EDI", "0xA5303|PUSH|ECX", "0xA5304|MOV|ESI, EDX", "0xA5306|PUSH|EBX", "0xA5307|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x18], EDI", "0xA530B|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x1c], EDI", "0xA530F|CALL|0x6fb9862c"],
      "comment": "Initializes projectile data structure and calculates animation frame offsets.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize local offset variables (nOffsetX, nOffsetY) to 0\n2. Call Ordinal_11066 to extract offset values from pProjectile into nOffsetX and nOffsetY\n3. Validate that offsets are non-zero; if both are 0, log error 0x134a and abort\n4. Initialize 5-dword array (aProjectileData) to zeros using REP STOSD\n5. Set aProjectileData[1] = 1, aProjectileData[2] = pProjectile, dwFrameNum = param_3\n6. Call Ordinal_10918 (get random seed) twice to obtain random base values\n7. Call Ordinal_10326 on pMonster to get value, subtract 0x0A, add random base\n8. Call Ordinal_10329 on pMonster to get value, subtract 0x0A, add second random base\n9. Store adjusted values in nPixelsX, nPixelsY\n10. Call FUN_6fb77720 to create/initialize projectile structure with aProjectileData\n11. If structure creation succeeds, validate frame count == 0x19 (25 frames)\n12. If frame count invalid, log error 0x135a and abort\n13. Calculate scaled offsets: nAdjustX = nOffsetX * -0x19, nAdjustY = nOffsetY * -0x19\n14. Call Ordinal_10111 twice to apply coordinate transforms\n15. Call FUN_6fb97b10 with projectile and scaled offsets (0x190 = 400 pixels)\n16. Call FUN_6fb97b40 with projectile and frame info (nPixelsX, nPixelsY, -0x10)\n17. Call FUN_6fb97c90 to finalize projectile\n\nParameters:\n- param_1: Projectile data pointer\n- param_2: Monster pointer providing animation state\n- param_3: Monster animation frame number\n\nReturns:\n- void; modifies projectile structure in-place\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If offset extraction fails (both offsets = 0), function aborts with error\n- If projectile structure creation fails, function returns without modification\n- If frame count != 25, function aborts with error\n- Uses magic values: 0x0A (10-pixel offset), 0x19 (25 frames), 0x190 (400 pixels), -0x10 (-16 for sprite offset)",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_StatList", "STRUCT_MonsterData", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PARAM_3", "MOD_UNIT", "SRC_Missile.cpp", "STRUCT_Other", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
    },
