      "comment": "Initializes drawable display object with mode and dimensional parameters for rendering.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Query RNG state and display mode (Ordinal_10918)\n2. Retrieve width/height from resource (Ordinal_10326, Ordinal_10329)\n3. Initialize mode lookup table (8 entries): mode 0→0x260, 1→0x261, 2→0x262, 3→0x263, default→0x25f\n4. Clear display buffer (22 dwords at [ESP+0x40])\n5. Set mode ID and base coordinates (Offset, DimensionX, DimensionY)\n6. Call display object constructor (FUN_6fb77720)\n7. If object created: apply mode (Ordinal_11140), apply dimensions (Ordinal_11142)\n\nParameters:\nnObjectId (ECX): Resource/object identifier for display target\nnResourceType (EDX): Display resource type (0-3 for mode selection)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Creates display object with applied parameters\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Unknown mode (>3): Uses default mode 0x25f\n- NULL object creation: No property application occurs\n- Stack temporaries optimized away: 11 phantom variables\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x260-0x263: Display mode identifiers (mode values 0-3)\n0x25f: Default/fallback display mode\n0x88: Stack frame size\n0x16: Display buffer clear count (22 dwords × 4 bytes)\n0x1e, 0x4, 0x7d: Calculation multipliers for coordinate transformation",
