      "comment": "Initialize monster unit drop effect with properties.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate unit type using Ordinal_10342 (D2Common.GetUnitStat)\n2. Check validation result via Ordinal_10119 (D2Common.UnitHasSkill)\n3. If validation passes (result == 0):\n   a. Initialize 0x58-byte stack buffer (set to 0)\n   b. Set buffer header to 0x2001 (effect type indicator)\n   c. Retrieve unit from hash table via GetUnitFromHashTable\n   d. Get base time offset via Ordinal_10918 (D2Common.RandSeed), add 0x27b\n   e. Setup configuration in stack locals\n   f. Call FUN_6fb77720 to create effect object with config\n   g. If object created (non-null pointer):\n      - Call FUN_6fb97b10 to set property 0xfa (250)\n      - Call FUN_6fb97b40 to set property -10 (property ID)\n      - Ordinal_11121: Set unit state 0x19\n      - Ordinal_11123: Set unit state 0x19\n      - Ordinal_11139: Set unit state 0x80\n\nParameters:\n- dwUnitId (ECX) - Unit identifier to process\n- dwMonsterType (EDX) - Monster classification code\n- dwFlags (Stack +0x4) - Configuration flags\n\nReturns:\n- void (no return value)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x2001: Effect object type identifier\n- 0x27b: Time offset constant (635 decimal)\n- 0xfa: Property value (250 decimal)\n- 0x19: Unit state value (25 decimal)\n- 0x80: Final property value (128 decimal)\n- 0x16: Loop count (22 decimal) for buffer initialization",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_StatList", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PARAM_3", "STRUCT_Skill", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
