      "instructions": ["0xA5E00|PUSH|EBX", "0xA5E01|PUSH|ESI", "0xA5E02|PUSH|EDI", "0xA5E03|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0xA5E05|CALL|0x6fb60ef0", "0xA5E0A|MOV|EDI, EAX", "0xA5E0C|XOR|EBX, EBX", "0xA5E0E|TEST|EDI, EDI", "0xA5E10|JZ|0x6fb75edc", "0xA5E16|PUSH|EDI", "0xA5E17|CALL|0x6fb98164", "0xA5E1C|PUSH|EAX", "0xA5E1D|CALL|0x6fb98140", "0xA5E22|CMP|EAX, 0x83", "0xA5E27|JL|0x6fb75e35"],
      "comment": "Validates and renders a unit if its class matches specific types (Amazon/Sorceress/Necromancer).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Look up unit pointer from unit ID using GetUnitFromHashTable\n2. If unit not found, call ProcessAndRenderSpecificClassUnit with NULL and exit\n3. Retrieve unit's class bits using GetUnitStat (with implicit register params)\n4. Extract class value using GetUnitMode - check if class is 0x83 or 0x84 (Amazon/Sorceress)\n5. If class invalid, exit without rendering\n6. Call setup/preparation functions: Ordinal_10235, Ordinal_10374\n7. Call Ordinal_11141 - check if returns 0 or RandSeed returns 0\n8. If check passes, call SetRenderingState with params (6, 2000, 3000, 2000) and mark unit with flag\n9. Loop through coordinate retrieval: RandSeed calls (3x) for randomization\n10. Get screen coordinates using Ordinal_10326 and Ordinal_10329\n11. Subtract 0x1e from each coordinate (position offset)\n12. Call FUN_6fb75bc0 with adjusted coordinates for rendering\n13. Exit normally (return without processing invalid units)\n14. Invalid unit/class path: call FUN_6fb773b0 with NULL and 0\n\nParameters:\nIMPLICIT ECX - pUnitId: uint* - pointer to unit ID being processed\n\nReturns:\nvoid - no return value (rendering is done as side effect)\n\nSpecial Cases:\nMagic number 0x83/0x84: Amazon (0x83) and Sorceress (0x84) class codes - may be 0x82/0x85 boundary check instead\nMagic number 0x1e (30): Position offset subtracted from screen coordinates\nMagic number 0x40: Buffer size for internal operation (Ordinal_10326 call)\nMagic number 0x3c (60): Another position parameter passed to coordinate functions\nMagic number 0xa (10): Secondary offset parameter\nRandSeed (Ordinal_10918): Called 3 times for coordinate randomization\nSetRenderingState values: 6=render mode, 2000/3000/2000=timing parameters\nUnit state check: Ordinal_11141 gates entire rendering operation\n\nStructure Layout:\nUnit structure accessed via pUnit pointer:\nOffset | Size | Field      | Type     | Description\n0x00   | 4    | dwUnitId   | uint     | Unit identifier\n0x2c   | 4    | dwCoordPtr | pointer  | Coordinate/rendering data pointer\n?      | ?    | pData      | void*    | Unit class and stat data",
