      "comment": "Validates if a value falls within an acceptable range bounds.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Query minimum bound from Ordinal_11141 - Custom ordinal, purpose unknown\n2. Query maximum bound from Ordinal_11143 - Custom ordinal, purpose unknown\n3. Retrieve value to validate via FUN_6fb97ad0\n4. Check if value is within range: -nMinBound <= nValue <= nMaxBound\n5. If in range, call FUN_6fb771e0 (success handler)\n6. If out of range, call FUN_6fb773b0 with NULL and 0 (failure handler)\n\nParameters:\npData (uint *) - Pointer to data structure containing validation context\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Calls appropriate handler function based on validation result\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Range check is inverted for lower bound (negative of minimum ordinal)\n- NULL and 0 passed to failure handler for cleanup\n- Ordinal_11141 and Ordinal_11143 are custom ordinals not found in docs/KNOWN_ORDINALS.md\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x0 - NULL pointer passed to failure handler",
      "tags": ["PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_1"]
