      "instructions": ["0xA6F30|PUSH|ESI", "0xA6F31|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0xA6F33|TEST|EDX, EDX", "0xA6F35|JNZ|0x6fb76f61", "0xA6F37|PUSH|EDI", "0xA6F38|PUSH|ESI", "0xA6F39|CALL|0x6fb98122", "0xA6F3E|MOV|EDI, EAX", "0xA6F40|PUSH|ESI", "0xA6F41|CALL|0x6fb9811c", "0xA6F46|MOV|EDX, EDI", "0xA6F48|MOV|ECX, ESI", "0xA6F4A|PUSH|0x14", "0xA6F4C|PUSH|0x24f", "0xA6F51|PUSH|0xa"],
      "comment": "Get unit's base coordinates and process nearby entities within a circular region\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if dwMode equals 0 to determine processing mode\n2. If dwMode is 0:\n   a. Call Ordinal_10326 with pUnit to get base X coordinate\n   b. Call Ordinal_10329 with pUnit to get base Y coordinate\n   c. Call ProcessCircleWithinDistance with retrieved coordinates\n   d. Set radius parameter to 10 (0xa)\n   e. Set range parameter to 0x24F (591 units)\n   f. Set max distance parameter to 0x14 (20 units)\n   g. Return 1 (success)\n3. If dwMode is non-zero:\n   a. Return 0 immediately (failure/skip)\n\nParameters:\n  pUnit: Pointer to unit entity structure (likely UnitAny)\n  dwMode: Mode flag; 0 enables circle processing, non-zero returns immediately\n\nReturns:\n  uint: 1 if processing executed (dwMode == 0), 0 if skipped (dwMode != 0)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Radius of 10 units is hardcoded constant\n  - Range 0x24F (591) and distance 0x14 (20) are hardcoded parameters\n  - Function returns 0 without processing if dwMode is non-zero, used as conditional gate",
      "tags": ["PARAM_2", "PROP_NOCALLER"]
