      "comment": "Process unit's time-based effects and stat updates.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate unit table exists via Ordinal_10589 (D2Common.GetUnitLevel), abort if missing\n2. Get unit sequence counter via Ordinal_11125 (D2Common.GetUnitSequenceCounter)\n3. Clear active flag (0xFBFFFFFF) if counter exceeds unit level limit\n4. Check if unit is valid/active via FUN_6fb97fd0, return if invalid\n5. Determine effect source: empty mode (flag 0x17) or armed equipment (flag 0x60)\n6. If armed: verify equipment level via Ordinal_11124 (D2Common.GetUnitManaPool), apply via Ordinal_10375 if within bounds\n7. Otherwise apply standard effect via Ordinal_10374 (D2Common.ApplyStandardEffect)\n8. Get unit class ID via param_1[0xe]\n9. Check class has modifiers via Ordinal_10147 (D2Common.ClassHasModifiers), if yes update via Ordinal_10226\n10. Get effect timer via Ordinal_11124, decrement via Ordinal_11123 (D2Common.SetUnitManaPool)\n11. If timer > 0: verify unit has class (param_1[3]), scan modifier table via Ordinal_10198 (D2Common.GetUnitModifierTable)\n12. For each modifier: lookup unit in stat table via Ordinal_10407 (D2Common.LookupUnitInTable) using Ordinal_10342/10336\n13. Validate unit type via ValidateUnitTypeState, update visual state via FUN_6fb773b0 on match\n14. If no match or timer exhausted: set default state via FUN_6fb773b0\n\nParameters:\npResultUnit (ECX, uint *) - Pointer to unit structure for effect processing\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Updates unit state and visual representation internally\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Returns early if unit table lookup fails\n- Returns early if unit invalid (FUN_6fb97fd0 returns 0)\n- Equipment level validation uses unsigned byte subtraction with bounds checking\n- Table lookup indexed by param_1[3] using g_pUnitStatTableArray base offsets\n- Note: Function uses 10 SSA temporaries (iVar*, uVar*, dVar*, bVar*) optimized away by compiler\n\nNote: Ordinals documented in code comments - see individual calls for D2Common mappings",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "MOD_UNIT", "SRC_Missile.cpp", "PARAM_1", "STRUCT_Other", "PROP_LOOPHEAVY", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
