      "comment": "Initialize unit equipment slots and apply armor/item effects based on unit class.\nValidates equipment compatibility, processes light effects, and updates unit state.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate unit class offset: (dwUnitType * 0x14)\n2. Load unit class index from g_aClassLightIndices[offset]\n3. Retrieve unit from hash table using pUnit->unitId\n4. Validate unit exists, class valid (0-0x283), unit state (0-1)\n5. Check equipment equipment compatibility via Ordinal_10487/10520\n6. If equipment provided: validate equipment flags (0x04 set), compare units\n7. Process equipment effects: check armor requirement (flag 0x6b), apply effects\n8. Execute class validation callback (g_pfnClassValidationCallback[offset])\n9. Initialize light struct for unit (if light support enabled)\n10. Update unit state flags and hash table membership\n11. Return created unit or NULL on validation failure\n\nParameters:\npUnit (UnitAny *): Target unit for equipment initialization (IMPLICIT ECX)\npEquipment (UnitAny *): Equipment/armor to apply (IMPLICIT EDX)\nnMode (int): Mode flag controlling initialization behavior (STACK)\n\nReturns:\nint * - Pointer to created/modified unit structure on success, NULL on failure\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Invalid unit ID returns NULL\n- Class out of range returns NULL\n- Equipment validation failure returns NULL\n- Unit class callback determines success/failure\n- Light struct initialization conditioned on class support\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x14 - Unit class record size (20 bytes)\n0x284 - Maximum valid class index (652)\n0x6b - Equipment requirement check offset\n0x56 - Equipment stat requirement flag\n0x45 - Character level stat flag\n0x9c - Experience requirement stat flag\n0x77 - Class data flag offset\n0x3a - Unit state flags offset (byte 58)\n0x04 - Equipment validation flag mask\n0x67 - Unit comparison validation flag offset\n0x6f - Unit placement constraint flag offset\n0x66 - Equipment/armor equip flag offset\n0x200000 - Special unit movement mode flag\n0x1 - Remove from linked list marker\n0x2 - Remove from hash table marker",
