      "comment": "Initializes and allocates a projectile unit with specified properties, damage, and callbacks.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate projectile base unit index (param_1[1]) - return NULL if invalid\n2. Load projectile stats data from game database via Ordinal_10589\n3. Resolve base coordinates: check flag bit 0 for preset coords or fetch from placement area ID\n4. Validate placement area (param_1[2]) exists when base coord mode is 0\n5. Calculate damage scaling: apply unit class modifier (stat 0x57) then weapon damage 75% factor\n6. If target unit exists: validate X/Y distances are under 100 pixels, else skip target\n7. Allocate projectile unit via AllocateAndInitializeUnit at base position (dwBaseY, dwStartX)\n8. Initialize projectile properties: path, animation, rotation, collision, light effects\n9. Apply damage and velocity scaling based on flags 0x400, 0x2000, 0x800, 0x200\n10. Apply special handling: skill initialization, audio/light context creation, post-spawn callback\n11. For non-NPC parents: apply skill sound/light effects and animation modifiers\n12. Load light/audio context and execute optional callback from param_1[0x14]\n13. Apply visual effect handler and return allocated unit or NULL on failure\n\nParameters:\npProjectileData - Projectile configuration array indexed by projectile type\n  [0] = Control flags (0x001=preset coords, 0x002=adjust target, 0x004=custom dmg, 0x008=scale dmg, 0x010=dmg<<8, 0x020=adjust preset, 0x100=skill init, 0x200=subtract dmg, 0x400=velocity scale, 0x800=custom duration, 0x2000=skill seed, 0x4000=light FX, 0x8000=alt damage source)\n  [1] = Source unit pointer (parent/caster)\n  [2] = Spawn area ID or placement location\n  [3] = Target unit pointer or NULL for no target\n  [4] = Projectile base unit type index\n  [5] = Preset X or coordinate multiplier\n  [6] = Preset Y or coordinate multiplier\n  [7] = Adjustment X offset\n  [8] = Adjustment Y offset\n  [9] = Audio/light effect primary ID\n  [10] = Damage scale numerator or base damage override\n  [11] = Animation speed/duration override\n  [12] = Rotation or direction bias\n  [13] = Reserved/effect parameter\n  [14] = Callback function pointer or NULL\n  [15] = Callback context parameter\n\nReturns:\nPointer to newly allocated UnitAny projectile unit on success. Returns NULL if: base unit invalid, stats unavailable, allocation fails, distance validation fails, or coordinate resolution fails.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- NPC source (type 0 or 1): skip skill sound/light effects\n- Flag 0x8000 set: use param_1[0x12] as base damage instead of calculated\n- Flag 0x200 set: subtract param_1[0xf] from final calculated damage\n- Flag 0x400 set: scale velocity as (distance >> 4) with special handling\n- Distance > 100 pixels: return NULL (projectile placement out of range)\n- Null target with relative coords: auto-calculate direction offsets\n- Same area target: auto-calculate direction via CalculateDirectionalOffsets\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x64 (100) = Maximum X/Y delta threshold in pixels\n  0x4b (75) = Weapon damage percentage multiplier (75%)\n  0x71 = Stats offset for projectile property check\n  0x57 = Stat ID for unit class modifier lookup\n  0x45, 0xa6 = Stat IDs for damage bonuses\n  0x9c = Stat ID for skill level bonus\n  0xa1 = Property ID for damage reduction multiplier\n  0x21 = Light effect property ID\n  0x77 = Animation flag byte offset\n  0xd9 = Rotation offset in stats\n  0x58 = Animation frame offset\n  0x16, 0x10 = Animation duration offsets\n  0x60, 0x61, 0x62 = Damage scaling control bytes",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "MOD_UNIT", "SRC_Missile.cpp", "STRUCT_Room2", "STRUCT_ItemData", "PARAM_1", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData", "STRUCT_StatList", "STRUCT_MonsterData", "PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Path", "STRUCT_Skill", "STRUCT_Other"]
