      "comment": "Initialize 22-element structure buffer and dispatch to handler function with parameters.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate entity/handle parameter (nEntityId) - return NULL if zero\n2. Allocate 22 dword buffer on stack (88 bytes total)\n3. Initialize entire buffer to zero using REP STOSD\n4. Set first element of buffer to 0x1 (structure flag/marker)\n5. Copy all 5 parameters into buffer at specific offsets:\n   - Buffer[0] = 0x1 (marker)\n   - Buffer[1] = nEntityId (parameter 1)\n   - Buffer[2] = dwTypeId (parameter 2) \n   - Buffer[3] = nXCoord (parameter 3)\n   - Buffer[4] = nYCoord (parameter 4)\n   - Buffer[7] = dwFlags (parameter 5)\n6. Call FUN_6fb77720 with initialized buffer as argument\n7. Return result from FUN_6fb77720\n\nParameters:\nnEntityId (dword) - Entity or handle identifier, checked for NULL\ndwTypeId (dword) - Type/class identifier for structure\nnXCoord (int) - X coordinate value\nnYCoord (int) - Y coordinate value  \ndwFlags (dword) - Configuration flags or options\n\nReturns:\nvoid * - Pointer returned by FUN_6fb77720 (typically newly allocated structure or NULL on failure)\n\nSpecial Cases:\nNULL input validation prevents processing of invalid handles\nBuffer initialized with magic number 0x1 at offset 0\nParameter layout suggests 22-dword structure has defined field schema\nFunction acts as wrapper/dispatcher for FUN_6fb77720\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x1 - Structure initialization marker at buffer[0]\n0x16 (22) - Total number of dwords in buffer (88 bytes)\nStack offsets calculated by __fastcall calling convention (ECX=param1, EDX=param2)",
