      "comment": "Create projectile from source unit with target coordinates and attack type.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate pUnit parameter (non-NULL)\n2. Check if pUnit is valid entity (value 0 or 1 = direct pointer, otherwise resolve from hash table)\n3. Return NULL if unit resolution fails\n4. Initialize local buffer (22 dwords, 0x58 bytes)\n5. Clear buffer by writing 22 dwords of 0x00\n6. Set buffer[0] = 0x20 (projectile buffer size marker)\n7. Populate buffer with parameters:\n   - buffer[4] = pResolvedUnit (resolved unit pointer)\n   - buffer[5] = pSourceUnit (original unit pointer)\n   - buffer[7] = dwTargetX\n   - buffer[10] = dwTargetY\n   - buffer[14] = dwAttackType\n8. Call InitializeAndAllocateProjectile with buffer pointer\n9. Return projectile pointer or NULL on failure\n\nParameters:\n  int *pUnit (ECX) - Pointer to unit data or hash table key\n  dword dwUnknown1 (EDX) - Attack subtype/parameter\n  dword dwTargetX (Stack[0x4]) - Target X coordinate\n  dword dwTargetY (Stack[0x8]) - Target Y coordinate\n  dword dwAttackType (Stack[0xc]) - Attack type (projectile class)\n\nReturns:\n  int * - Pointer to allocated projectile structure on success\n  NULL (0x0) - If unit validation/resolution fails\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If pUnit == 0, returns NULL immediately\n  - If pUnit values 0 or 1, uses pUnit directly; otherwise resolves via hash table\n  - Hash table resolution failure returns NULL (cascades to caller)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x16 - Number of dwords to clear (22 * 4 = 0x58 bytes total buffer)\n  0x20 - Projectile buffer size marker at offset 0\n  0x58 - Total stack buffer size (88 bytes)",
