      "comment": "Creates and initializes a projectile object from source unit and target parameters, resolving unit pointers and applying default target type if needed.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate pUnit pointer - return NULL if NULL\n2. Load unit value from [pUnit], test if 0 or 1 (valid IDs)\n3. If value is neither 0 nor 1, call GetUnitFromHashTable(pUnit) for unit resolution\n4. Validate resolved unit - return NULL if resolution fails\n5. Check nTargetType parameter - if 0, apply default 0x1e\n6. Initialize 88-byte structure on stack with STOSD zero-fill loop (22 dwords)\n7. Populate structure:\n   Offset 0x00 = 0x520 (structure size marker)\n   Offset 0x04 = pUnit (original unit input)\n   Offset 0x14 = pResolvedUnit (resolved unit pointer)\n   Offset 0x18 = pResolvedUnit (redundant copy for data layout)\n   Offset 0x20 = dwX (source x from EDX)\n   Offset 0x2c = dwXTarget (projectile target x)\n   Offset 0x30 = dwY (source y)\n   Offset 0x34 = nTargetType (with default 0x1e applied)\n   Offset 0x3c = dwYTarget (projectile target y)\n8. Call InitializeAndAllocateProjectile(&structure) for allocation\n9. Return allocated projectile pointer or NULL\n\nParameters:\npUnit - Unit pointer or ID (0/1 valid), IMPLICIT ECX fastcall register\ndwX - Source x coordinate, IMPLICIT EDX fastcall register\ndwY - Source y coordinate from stack\ndwXTarget - Projectile target x coordinate\ndwYTarget - Projectile target y coordinate\nnTargetType - Target type (0 replaced with default 0x1e)\n\nReturns:\nAllocated projectile pointer on success\nNULL on unit validation/resolution failure",
