      "comment": "Initialize and allocate projectile for a unit with specified missile type and ID.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate input: Check if pOwner pointer is non-NULL\n2. Determine unit reference: If pOwner value is 0 or 1, retrieve actual unit from hash table\n3. Validate retrieved unit: Return NULL if unit not found\n4. Get position data: Query mercenary position status from unit's mercenary component\n5. Retrieve coordinates: Get X/Y from Ordinal_10175/10176 (unit memory) or Ordinal_10326/10329 (mercenary)\n6. Clear stack buffer: Zero 22 dwords of projectile initialization structure\n7. Set missile constant: Store 0x420 (magic missile marker) at buffer start\n8. Store parameters: Copy unit pointer, missile type/ID into buffer offsets\n9. Allocate projectile: Call InitializeAndAllocateProjectile with populated buffer\n10. Return: New projectile pointer or NULL on failure\n\nParameters:\n- pOwner (UnitAny *): Unit pointer, may be hash table reference or direct pointer\n- dwMissileType (uint): Missile type identifier (IMPLICIT EDX register)\n- dwMissileId (uint): Missile ID (IMPLICIT stack param at offset +4)\n\nReturns:\n- int *: Pointer to newly allocated projectile unit, or NULL if initialization fails\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If pOwner is NULL, returns NULL immediately without processing\n- If pOwner dereference is 0 or 1, performs unit hash table lookup for actual unit reference\n- If mercenary position query fails, falls through to use unit memory coordinates\n- Stack buffer cleared ensures all fields initialized before projectile creation\n\nNote: Function uses 1 stack-allocated temporary optimized away by compiler (local_5c phantom variable).",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Path", "PARAM_3", "STRUCT_Room2", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
