      "instructions": ["0xA7FA0|SUB|ESP, 0x14", "0xA7FA3|PUSH|EBX", "0xA7FA4|PUSH|EBP", "0xA7FA5|PUSH|ESI", "0xA7FA6|PUSH|EDI", "0xA7FA7|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0xA7FA9|MOV|EDI, EDX", "0xA7FAB|PUSH|ESI", "0xA7FAC|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x1c], EDI", "0xA7FB0|CALL|0x6fb98164", "0xA7FB5|MOV|EBX, EAX", "0xA7FB7|PUSH|EDI", "0xA7FB8|CALL|0x6fb98206", "0xA7FBD|LEA|EBP, [ESI + 0x2c]", "0xA7FC0|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x14], EAX"],
      "comment": "Allocates and initializes random units within bounds\nSpawns nUnitCount units at random map coordinates with validation\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get unit stat data from dwUnitCode (Ordinal_10342 = D2Common.GetUnitStat)\n2. Get player data from dwPlayerIndex (Ordinal_10582 = Get player/entity data)\n3. Get base coordinates from unit (Ordinal_10332 = Initialize base coordinates, stored in nBaseX/nBaseY)\n4. Loop up to 10 times while nUnitCount > 0:\n   a. Generate random X coordinate via Ordinal_10918 (D2Common.RandSeed) - 2 + nBaseX\n   b. Generate random Y coordinate via Ordinal_10918 (D2Common.RandSeed) - 2 + nBaseY\n   c. Get item placement data at coordinates via Ordinal_10042 (D2Common.GetItemData)\n   d. Validate location is passable via Ordinal_10119 (Check passability, result == 0 means walkable)\n   e. If walkable, allocate unit at that position via AllocateAndInitializeUnit()\n   f. Decrement nUnitCount counter\n   g. Increment loop counter, exit if counter >= 10\n\nParameters:\n  dwUnitCode (dword) - Unit type code to spawn\n  dwPlayerIndex (dword) - Player index for ownership\n  nUnitCount (int) - Number of units to allocate\n\nReturns:\n  void - Function modifies global state by allocating units\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Loop exits if nUnitCount reaches 0 (all units allocated)\n  - Loop exits after 10 iterations maximum (prevents infinite loop)\n  - Validates each spawn location; skips invalid tiles\n  - Uses ordinal Ordinal_10119 to check passability with flags 0x3f11\n  - Note: Function uses 1 stack-allocated temporary optimized away (local_EAX_24)",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Inventory", "PARAM_3", "STRUCT_Skill", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
