      "api_count": 2,
      "api_calls": ["UNITS_GetRoom", "ExtractRoomTileList"],
      "instructions": ["0xA8210|SUB|ESP, 0xc", "0xA8213|PUSH|EBX", "0xA8214|PUSH|EBP", "0xA8215|PUSH|ESI", "0xA8216|PUSH|EDI", "0xA8217|MOV|EDI, ECX", "0xA8219|MOV|EBX, EDX", "0xA821B|PUSH|EDI", "0xA821C|CALL|0x6fb98164", "0xA8221|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0xA8223|JZ|0x6fb78280", "0xA8225|LEA|ECX, [ESP + 0x14]", "0xA8229|LEA|EDX, [ESP + 0x18]", "0xA822D|PUSH|ECX", "0xA822E|PUSH|EDX"],
      "comment": "Iterates through a list of items, invoking a callback on each element\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Retrieve list handle from dwListId using Ordinal_10342 (D2Common.GetUnit equivalent)\n2. If handle is NULL, return 0\n3. Retrieve list pointer and count using Ordinal_10035 (GetList/GetListInfo equivalent)\n4. Initialize loop counter dwIndex to 0\n5. If dwItemCount is 0, skip to return 0\n6. For each item at offset dwItemCount:\n   a. Load item pointer from [ppListItems + dwIndex * 4]\n   b. Navigate chain at offset 0x2c until NULL\n   c. Call pfnCallback(dwParam1, dwParam2) for each item in chain\n   d. If callback returns non-zero, return that value immediately (early exit)\n   e. Move to next item in chain at offset 0x10c\n7. Increment dwIndex, continue until dwIndex >= dwItemCount\n8. Return 0 (success - all callbacks returned 0)\n\nParameters:\ndwListId (uint, ECX) - List identifier or handle ID passed to GetUnit\ndwParam1 (uint, EDX) - First parameter to pass to callback function\ndwParam2 (uint, [ESP+0x20]) - Second parameter to pass to callback function\npfnCallback (void *, [ESP+0x24]) - Generic callback function pointer, invoked as callback(dwParam1, dwParam2)\n\nReturns:\nNon-zero value returned by callback if any callback returns non-zero (early exit)\n0 if all callbacks succeed or list is empty\n\nSpecial Cases:\nList iteration uses two-level structure: outer array indexed by dwIndex, inner linked chain at offset 0x2c\nCallback short-circuits iteration on first non-zero return value\nEmpty list (dwItemCount == 0) safely skips iteration loop entirely\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x2c - Offset in list element to start of linked chain head\n0x10c - Offset to next element in linked chain",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PARAM_4", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
