      "comment": "Process directional spell cast by calculating target coordinates based on direction and step count.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract unit coordinates from pUnit via Ordinal_10326/10329 (dwUnitX, dwUnitY)\n2. Extract target coordinates from pTargetUnit via Ordinal_10326/10329 (dwTargetX, dwTargetY)\n3. Calculate direction deltas: iXDelta = (dwTargetX < dwUnitX) ? -1 : (dwTargetX > dwUnitX) ? 1 : 0; iYDelta similar for Y\n4. Get unit type via Ordinal_10181(pUnit[0xE])\n5. Calculate new position: iNewX = iXDelta + dwUnitX; iNewY = iYDelta + dwUnitY\n6. Validate new position with Ordinal_10119(unit_stat, iNewX, iNewY, 1, unit_type)\n7. If validation fails (result != 0), return 0\n8. Calculate final coordinates: dwCalcX = ((nSteps & 0xFF) * iXDelta) + dwUnitX; dwCalcY similar\n9. Get unit collision type via Ordinal_10187(pUnit[0xE])\n10. Get movement speed mask via Ordinal_10189(pUnit[0xE]), mask with 0xFF\n11. Call FUN_6fb7b140 with calculated coordinates to apply movement\n12. Return 1 on success\n\nParameters:\npUnit - Pointer to source unit structure\npTargetUnit - Pointer to target unit structure\nnSteps - Movement step count (byte value, masked with 0xFF)\nnSkillLevel - Skill level modifier (0x0C common value)\ndwSkillId - Skill identifier (0x78 = teleport, 0x1E = other)\n\nReturns:\n1 on successful spell cast execution\n0 if position validation fails\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Returns 0 if position validation by Ordinal_10119 fails (blocked path/invalid coordinates)\n- Handles 8-direction movement (N, NE, E, SE, S, SW, W, NW) based on target coordinates\n- Masks step count to byte range (& 0xFF) before calculation\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0xFF - Byte mask for step count extraction\n0xE - Offset to unit type/collision data in unit structure\n1 - Unit range check constant (third param to validation)\n0x0C, 0x78, 0x1E - Skill-specific identifiers/levels\n\nRelated Functions:\n- Ordinal_10326/10329: Get unit X/Y coordinates from unit structure\n- Ordinal_10181: Get uni