      "comment": "Process spell target coordinates and apply effects based on spell state.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract spell mode from pSpellData[3]\n2. Query spell state via Ordinal_11064(pSpellData)\n3. If spell is not in state 0:\n   - Return without processing\n4. Otherwise, retrieve target coordinates:\n   - Get nTargetX via Ordinal_10326(pSpellData)\n   - Get nTargetY via Ordinal_10329(pSpellData)\n   - Get nSourceXCoord via Ordinal_10326(nSourceX)\n   - Get nSourceYCoord via Ordinal_10329(nSourceX)\n5. If target coordinates match source coordinates:\n   - Initialize 7-element coordinate buffer with zeros\n   - Set buffer[0] = nTargetX, buffer[1] = nTargetY\n   - Call FUN_6fb7b140(8, pSpellData, anCoordBuffer) for main effect\n   - Return\n6. If spell mode == 1:\n   - Get random seed via Ordinal_10918()\n   - If seed value (upper 32 bits) < 0x28:\n     * Get spell target data from pSpellData[0x1c]\n     * Retrieve target via FUN_6fb796c0()\n     * Verify pointer with PassthroughPointerIdentity()\n     * Set spell flags field to 0x14\n     * Initialize coordinate buffer with zeros\n     * Set buffer[0] = nTargetX, buffer[1] = nTargetY\n     * Call FUN_6fb7b140(7, pSpellData, anCoordBuffer) for alternate effect\n     * Return\n   - Otherwise: Apply coordinate offset via ApplyCoordinateOffset()\n\nParameters:\npSpellData (uint *) - Pointer to spell data structure; indexed fields at offsets 0x1c, [3]\nnSourceX (dword) - Source spell coordinates; used as parameter to coordinate query ordinals\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value; applies spell effects in place\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Spell state checking determines processing path\n- Random seed check (< 0x28) gates secondary effect\n- Coordinate buffer reused across both branches (main vs alternate effect)",
