      "instructions": ["0xA8D20|SUB|ESP, 0x2c", "0xA8D23|PUSH|EBX", "0xA8D24|PUSH|EBP", "0xA8D25|PUSH|ESI", "0xA8D26|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0xA8D28|PUSH|EDI", "0xA8D29|MOV|EDI, EDX", "0xA8D2B|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [ESI + 0xc]", "0xA8D2E|CMP|EAX, 0xc", "0xA8D31|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x18], EAX", "0xA8D35|JZ|0x6fb78f9e", "0xA8D3B|XOR|EBP, EBP", "0xA8D3D|CMP|EAX, EBP", "0xA8D3F|JZ|0x6fb78f9e", "0xA8D45|MOV|ECX, dword ptr [ESP + 0x40]"],
      "comment": "Process spell casting actions for a unit, handling directional casts and targeted spells.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if unit type (param_1[3]) is valid (not 0 or 0xc), return early if invalid\n2. If slot index < 2 (basic spells): Compare unit and target location coordinates via Ordinal_10326/10329, return if match\n3. If unit type == 1 (special spell mode):\n   a. If slot index < 4: Call ProcessDirectionalSpellCast(param_1, param_2, 6, 1, 0) and return\n   b. If slot index >= 7: Retrieve unit stat via Ordinal_10342, call Ordinal_10035 to get location data\n   c. Iterate through target list at offset 0x2c per location, call FUN_6fb78fb0 for each target\n   d. Check spell cast state via FUN_6fb7c7e0, if no valid target found or state not set:\n      - Get unit stat via Ordinal_10342 and field at offset 0xe\n      - Set spell cooldown via local_1c array with Ordinal_10187/10189\n      - Call FUN_6fb7b140 with mode 0 to initialize spell state\n      - Set state flag to 1\n   e. If state is set, check random value vs 0x14 via Ordinal_10918; if below, clear state\n   f. If no slot available, check random vs 0x4b; if below, set state flag 0x1e\n   g. Otherwise call ApplyCoordinateOffset with delay value from random\n\nParameters:\n  pUnit (dword *) - Pointer to unit structure, contains type at offset 0xc, stat at 0xe, location at 0x70\n  pTargetLoc (dword *) - Target location coordinates passed to comparisons\n  dwSlotIndex (dword) - Spell slot index (0-7+), determines spell type and behavior\n\nReturns:\n  void - Updates unit spell state indirectly via ordinal calls\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Returns early if unit type is 0 or 0xc (invalid unit states)\n  - Slot index 0-1: Location-based comparison, returns immediately if match\n  - Slot index 1-3: Calls ProcessDirectionalSpellCast then returns\n  - Slot index >= 7: Full target iteration and state management\n  - Random seed value affects cooldown reset threshold (0x14) and fallback logic (0x4b)\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0xc - Invalid unit type constant (used in comparisons, likely UNIT_NONE or UNIT_INVALID)\n  0x2 - Threshold for location comparison spell slots\n  0x4 - Threshold for directional spell casting\n  0x7 - Threshold for full targeting iteration (minimum slot for complex spell logic)\n  0x14 (20) - Random value threshold for cooldown reset (Ordinal_10918 result)\n  0x4b (75) - Random value threshold for spell fallback delay\n  0x5 - Hardcoded delay parameter in ApplyCoordinateOffset\n  0x20 (32) - Spell state flag value (0x20)\n  0x1e (30) - Alternative spell state flag value (0x1e)\n  0x6 - Spell mode for ProcessDirectionalSpellCast\n  0x8 - Spell initialization mode (FUN_6fb7b140)\n  0x1c - Offset in unit structure for spell-related data (param_1[0x1c])\n  0x2c - Offset in location structure for target list head\n  0x38 - Offset in unit structure for spell stat/flag data (param_1[0x38])\n  0x43 - Offset stride in linked list for target iteration (puVar7 = puVar7[0x43])\n  0x70 - Offset in unit structure for location/coordinate data (param_1[0x70])\n  0x10c - Offset in target node for next pointer (piVar4[0x10c])\n\nRelated Functions:\n- ProcessDirectionalSpellCast() - Casts directional spells, called for slot index 1\n- FUN_6fb78fb0() - Target validation filter, checks if target is valid for casting\n- FUN_6fb796c0() - Retrieves spell state container from unit\n- FUN_6fb7c7e0() - Gets spell cast flag status\n- FUN_6fb7b140() - Initializes/manages spell state array\n- Ordinal_10918() - D2Common.RandSeed - Returns random seed value for cooldown logic\n- Ordinal_10326() - D2Common.GetUnitX - Gets unit X coordinate\n- Ordinal_10329() - D2Common.GetUnitY - Gets unit Y coordinate\n- Ordinal_10342() - D2Common.GetUnitStat - Gets unit stat value by index\n- Ordinal_10187() - Spell cooldown calculation function\n- Ordinal_10189() - Spell effect/flag retrieval function\n- Ordinal_10035() - D2Common.GetAreaData - Gets location data table\n- ApplyCoordinateOffset() - Updates unit position with delay offset",
