      "comment": "Process spell effect timing and coordinate validation for directional unit spell casting.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if unit is marked active via Ordinal_11064—if true, return early to prevent reprocessing\n2. Get unit spell coordinate: X1 = Ordinal_10326(pUnit), Y1 = Ordinal_10329(pUnit)\n3. Get target spell coordinate: X2 = Ordinal_10326(pTarget), Y2 = Ordinal_10329(pTarget)\n4. If coordinates match (X1==X2 && Y1==Y2): Initialize spell coordinate array, apply spell with slot 8, return\n5. Check unit spell state flag at pUnit[3]:\n   - If flag != 1: Return (no spell state)\n   - If dwDistance < 2: Call ProcessDirectionalSpellCast with slot 4, flags 1, duration 0\n6. Get random seed (Ordinal_10918) for spell timing variation:\n   - If seed < 0x4b (75): Get spell counter buffer, write 0x20, apply spell with slot 7, return\n   - If seed >= 0x4b: Apply coordinate offset with seed high-word and duration 0\n\nParameters:\npUnit (uint *) - Unit structure pointer; offset [3]=spell state flag, [0x1c]=spell counter ID\npTarget (uint *) - Target structure or coordinates pointer; coordinates via Ordinal_10326/Ordinal_10329\ndwDistance (uint) - Horizontal/calculated distance from unit to target (affects spell timing path)\n\nReturns:\nvoid (no explicit return value; side effects: spell effects applied via FUN_6fb7b140 or ProcessDirectionalSpellCast)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Early return when Ordinal_11064 indicates unit already has active spell effect\n- Coordinates extracted via ordinals must match exactly for synchronized spell timing\n- Random seed threshold 0x4b determines timing path (< 0x4b: slot 7 effect, >= 0x4b: offset effect)\n- Distance check < 2 bypasses seed-based timing, applies immediate directional cast\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x4b (75) - Random seed threshold distinguishing spell timing paths\n0x20 (32) - Spell counter buffer value for seed < 0x4b path\n0x1c - Unit structure offset for spell counter buffer ID\n0x3 - Unit structure offset for spell state flags (0=inactive, 1=active)\n0x28 - Right shift for extracting high 32-bits of 64-bit seed value",
