      "instructions": ["0xA9160|SUB|ESP, 0x28", "0xA9163|PUSH|EBX", "0xA9164|MOV|EBX, ECX", "0xA9166|PUSH|EBP", "0xA9167|PUSH|ESI", "0xA9168|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [EBX + 0xc]", "0xA916B|PUSH|EDI", "0xA916C|CMP|EAX, 0x1", "0xA916F|JNZ|0x6fb792fd", "0xA9175|PUSH|0x1c0", "0xA917A|PUSH|EBX", "0xA917B|CALL|0x6fb9811c", "0xA9180|PUSH|EAX", "0xA9181|PUSH|EBX", "0xA9182|CALL|0x6fb98122"],
      "comment": "Auto-target spell slot for unit's current class spell abilities.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if unit class is druid (dwUnitId == 1)\n2. Query class spell skill IDs: ability ID (uVar4), category (uVar5), spell ID (uVar6)\n3. Verify skill in unit's skill array with Ordinal_10118 (nCheckResult)\n4. If skill not active, initialize local_1c array with skill IDs and set ability state via FUN_6fb7b140\n5. If skill active, search unit list for valid targets:\n   - Iterate through all monsters (UnitType 0) or summoned minions (UnitType 1, except class IDs 0x95, 0x22c)\n   - Validate unit state with ValidateUnitTypeState\n   - Calculate distance with Ordinal_10397, track minimum distance target\n6. If valid target found (pTargetUnit):\n   - Load unit stats pointer from EBX[0x38]\n   - Set stat 0x3c01 with Ordinal_10182 (mana consumption)\n   - If target within 6 range: Set stat 0xc01, cast spell with ProcessDirectionalSpellCast\n   - Else if random value < 30: Apply coordinate offset to current position (no spell cast)\n   - Else: Set spell cooldown state value to 5 via FUN_6fb796c0 and PassthroughPointerIdentity\n\nParameters:\npUnit (UnitAny *) - Current unit processing auto-target spell, __fastcall in ECX\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No explicit return value, modifies unit state and target selection via Ordinal calls\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Druid units only (dwUnitId == 1), other classes return immediately\n- Skill must be active in unit's skill array to search for targets\n- Target distance 0x7fffffff used as infinity for minimum distance comparison\n- CONCAT31 and extraout_EDX indicate output parameter from ProcessDirectionalSpellCast\n- Magic number 0x1e (30) is random threshold for spell range determination\n- Array local_1c[7] is stack-allocated temp array passed to ability state function\n\nRelated Functions:\n- ProcessUnitSpellInput - Caller that triggers auto-spell processing\n- ValidateUnitTypeState - Validates target unit state requirements\n- ProcessDirectionalSpellCast - Executes spell cast with directional adjustment\n- ApplyCoordinateOffset - Applies coordinate movement without spell casting",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "STRUCT_Skill", "STRUCT_ItemData", "PARAM_1", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
