      "instructions": ["0xA9310|PUSH|ECX", "0xA9311|PUSH|EBX", "0xA9312|MOV|EBX, ECX", "0xA9314|PUSH|ESI", "0xA9315|PUSH|EDI", "0xA9316|LEA|EDI, [EBX + 0x2c]", "0xA9319|CALL|0x6fb62880", "0xA931E|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0xA9320|JNZ|0x6fb7933e", "0xA9322|MOV|ECX, dword ptr [EBX + 0x70]", "0xA9325|CALL|0x6fb796c0", "0xA932A|MOV|ECX, EAX", "0xA932C|CALL|0x6fb5a350", "0xA9331|MOV|dword ptr [EAX], 0x5", "0xA9337|POP|EDI"],
      "comment": "Apply spell effect to unit based on game context state.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if game context is initialized via GetGameContext()\n2. If context NULL: Retrieve context from unit's offset 0x70, set status to 0x5\n3. Generate random offset values (nRand1-3) and calculate position adjustments (X/Y)\n4. Create structure with InitializeStructureAndCallHandler using computed offsets\n5. Branch on nRand3 value: if 0, apply cold effect; else apply fire effect\n6. Apply three effects to structure: temperature adjustment, damage modifier, duration bonus\n7. Configure display properties via Ordinal calls (11121, 11123, 11140, 11142)\n\nParameters:\npUnit (void *) - Unit pointer containing spell data at offset 0x70\n\nReturns:\n(void) - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If context initialization fails, sets status to 0x5 and returns early\n- If structure creation fails, entire effect application is skipped\n- Temperature effects are inverted based on random state\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x70 - Offset to spell context pointer in unit structure\n0x2c - Offset to yadda field (used in offset calculation)\n0x23a (570) - Base value added to random offset\n-0x1e (-30) - Adjustment factor for position calculation\n0x3c (60) - Duration parameter for display configuration\n100, 300 - Effect power constants",
      "tags": ["PARAM_1", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
