      "instructions": ["0xA9480|SUB|ESP, 0x8", "0xA9483|PUSH|ESI", "0xA9484|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0xA9486|LEA|ECX, [ESP + 0x4]", "0xA948A|CALL|0x6fb9834a", "0xA948F|MOV|EDX, ESI", "0xA9491|LEA|ECX, [ESP + 0x4]", "0xA9495|CALL|0x6fb9820c", "0xA949A|MOV|EAX, [0x6fbff4e4]", "0xA949F|MOV|dword ptr [0x6fbff4e0], ESI", "0xA94A5|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0xA94A7|JZ|0x6fb794b5", "0xA94A9|MOV|EDX, 0x6fbff2cc", "0xA94AE|XOR|ECX, ECX", "0xA94B0|CALL|0x6fb981be"],
      "comment": "Initialize the active controlled unit for the game engine.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Lock rendering system (Ordinal_10912) and rendering data (Ordinal_10913)\n2. Store unit ID to global g_pActiveUnit\n3. If unit was previously initialized (g_bActiveUnitInitialized != 0), unlock previous rendering state (Ordinal_11073)\n4. Get current video frame count and initialize unit rendering data (Ordinal_11072) with unit ID and frame count\n5. Obtain game context from GetGameContext()\n6. If game context is NULL, log error to \"hCtrlUnit\" at line 0x2a and terminate with exit code -1\n7. Get room index from game context (Ordinal_10342)\n8. If room index is 0, log error to \"hRoom\" at line 0x2c and terminate with exit code -1\n9. Get room data from room index (Ordinal_10057)\n10. Get slot count from room data (Ordinal_10001)\n11. Update active unit controller data (FUN_6fb940b0) with slot count\n12. Mark unit as initialized (g_bActiveUnitInitialized = 1)\n\nParameters:\n  dwUnitId (uint, ECX) - Unit ID to initialize as active controlled unit\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Terminates with -1 if game context is invalid\n  - Terminates with -1 if room index is invalid (0)\n  - Initializes rendering frame tracking to current video frame\n  - Note: Function uses 1 stack-allocated temporary (abSlotState) optimized away by compiler\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x2a (42) - Line number for hCtrlUnit error log\n  0x2c (44) - Line number for hRoom error log\n  0xffffffff (-1) - Termination exit code",
      "tags": ["SRC_MonRegion.cpp", "PARAM_1"]
