      "comment": "Return pointer to active unit initialization flags array and set caller's flag value.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load current active unit initialized state from g_bActiveUnitInitialized (dword at 0x6fbff4e4)\n2. Store state value to caller's output parameter via pointer in ECX\n3. Load address of global active unit data array into EAX (0x6fbff2cc = g_aActiveUnitData)\n4. Return with array pointer in EAX\n\nParameters:\npInitFlags (dword *) - Pointer to output variable for active unit initialization state\n  - Passed in ECX register (IMPLICIT __fastcall convention)\n  - Will be filled with current g_bActiveUnitInitialized value\n\nReturns:\ndword * - Constant pointer to global active unit data array\n  - Points to g_aActiveUnitData at 0x6fbff2cc\n  - Array size: 0x85 elements (133 dwords = 532 bytes / 0x214 bytes)\n  - Returned in EAX register\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Function uses __fastcall calling convention with first parameter in ECX\n- Return value is always the same static address (0x6fbff2cc)\n- Side effect: function modifies caller's output parameter\n- Called from: InitializeRenderingAndGameState, InitializeActiveUnit, InitializeDataBuffer",
