      "comment": "Validates unit state and conditionally processes or returns state-dependent result.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call Ordinal_11056(pUnit) to retrieve unit state value\n2. Check if state equals 0x10b AND nStateType equals 0xa7:\n   - If true, call FUN_6fb931f0(pUnit, 0x55, 2, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0) to process unit\n   - Return 0x54 (success indicator)\n3. Check if nStateType equals 0xb7:\n   - Compare nCheckValue against 0xaa\n   - If equal, set result to 0x22\n   - If not equal, set result to nDefaultReturn\n4. Return computed result (0x22 or nDefaultReturn)\n\nParameters:\n  pUnit: Pointer to UnitAny structure to validate\n  nStateType: State type code for conditional logic (0xa7 or 0xb7 trigger special paths)\n  nDefaultReturn: Default return value when conditions not met\n  nCheckValue: Value to compare against when nStateType is 0xb7\n\nReturns:\n  0x54: When state is 0x10b and nStateType is 0xa7 (processed successfully)\n  0x22: When nStateType is 0xb7 and nCheckValue matches 0xaa\n  nDefaultReturn: All other conditions (fallback return value)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  Function requires specific state 0x10b only when nStateType is 0xa7\n  The 0xaa constant is a special flag/mode indicator for 0xb7 path\n  Magic number constants control branching behavior throughout",
