      "comment": "Initializes audio playback context for a unit.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Fetch unit's audio config from game state (Ordinal_10582)\n2. Query audio priority level for unit (Ordinal_11051)\n3. Enforce minimum priority from game settings (offset +0x2b2)\n4. Get current audio volume/quality state (Ordinal_10342)\n5. Check audio effect type (Ordinal_10057)\n6. If type is 8 (specific audio category) AND audio enabled (Ordinal_10002):\n   a. Verify unit not flagged with 0x200000 (audio suppression flag)\n   b. Verify game audio not in restricted state (offset +0x2a5 != 0x01/0x02)\n   c. Override priority to 3 (high priority audio)\n7. If priority is 0, exit early (no audio playback)\n8. Create audio context with parameters from game state (offsets +0x2d6/0x2d7/0x2d8)\n9. If unit has existing audio context, clear it first (ClearAudioContextReference)\n10. Assign new audio context to unit (offset +0x88)\n11. Update unit stat with new audio priority (SetUnitStatValue)\n\nParameters:\npUnit: UnitAny * - Pointer to unit entity with audio configuration fields\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Audio context created and assigned to unit\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x2b2 - Audio priority field in game state\n0x2a5 - Audio restriction mode flag (1=silent, 2=limited)\n0x2d6/0x2d7/0x2d8 - Audio quality/volume configuration bytes\n0x200000 - Unit flag for audio suppression\n0xe8 - Unit flags field (for 0x200000 test)\n0x88 - Unit audio context pointer field\n0x8 - Audio effect type code\n0xff - Audio priority mask\n\nRelated Functions:\n- SetUnitStatValue() - Updates unit statistics\n- CreateAudioContext() - Allocates audio context\n- ClearAudioContextReference() - Cleanup existing audio",
