      "comment": "Extract unit state flag bit from buffer pointer at offset 0x70.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load byte pointer from offset 0x70 in unit parameter (ECX + 0x70)\n2. Test if pointer is NULL for early exit\n3. If NULL, return NULL pointer without dereferencing\n4. Load byte value from dereferenced pointer [EAX]\n5. Right shift byte right by 2 bits (SHR EAX, 0x2)\n6. Mask with 0x01 to isolate bit 2 only\n7. Cast result to byte pointer and return\n\nParameters:\nnUnit (int in ECX) - Unit structure pointer passed as 32-bit integer\n\nReturns:\nbyte * - NULL if state buffer pointer at offset 0x70 is NULL; otherwise returns bit 2 value (0 or 1) cast as byte pointer\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- NULL pointer at offset 0x70 terminates early without dereferencing\n- Bit extraction isolates only bit 2 from the state byte\n- Return value cast to byte pointer despite containing boolean result",
