      "comment": "Extract and test bit flag from unit data structure.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load pointer from unit at offset 0x70\n2. Test if pointer is NULL\n3. If NULL, return NULL (false)\n4. Load first byte from pointed-to data\n5. Extract bit 4 (shift right 4, AND 0x1)\n6. Return bit value as byte (0 or 1)\n\nParameters:\n- pUnit (uint *): Unit structure containing flag data pointer at offset 0x70\n\nReturns:\n- Non-zero (1): Bit 4 is set\n- Zero (0): Bit 4 is clear\n- NULL: Field pointer was NULL\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- NULL pointer field: early return avoids dereference\n- Return type byte allows boolean interpretation",
