      "comment": "Initialize unit statistics, resistances, and skills based on difficulty and unit type.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate difficulty level (must be < 3)\n2. Get difficulty table offset using unit type as index\n3. Reset unit class (0x0c) and base resistances (0x44, 0x43, 0x45) to defaults\n4. Initialize elemental resistances from difficulty tables (offsets 0x2d9-0x2e8)\n5. Set skill point pools to 0x6400 (fields 0x6, 0x7)\n6. Assign unit class/skill tree via Ordinal_10152\n7. Set spell aura if unit class supports active skills\n8. Initialize class-specific abilities (Ordinal_10223, Ordinal_10211, Ordinal_10182)\n9. Setup random seed if unit has summoned minions\n10. Configure behavior flags based on difficulty (freeze immunity, physical immunity, magic immunity)\n11. Initialize dynamic skill slots (0x70) with allocated buffers if not set\n12. Initialize unit audio context\n13. Configure skill bindings for unit class (5 skill slots)\n14. Set experience table pointer\n15. Configure initial skill states via Ordinal_10161_SkillInit based on unit type\n\nParameters:\n- pUnit (UnitAny *): Unit structure to initialize\n- dwTownLevel (uint): Difficulty level (0-2: Normal, Nightmare, Hell)\n- dwSeed (uint): Random seed for unit initialization\n- pDifficultyData (int *): Difficulty-specific unit configuration table\n- nUnitType (int): Unit classification (0x123=missile, 0x165=summon, 0x1a1-0x1a2=special)\n- dwUnitSubtype (uint): Unit subtype for skill initialization\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Modifies unit structure in place\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Difficulty validation: Crashes if level >= 3 (FUN_6fb9a10f)\n- Skill initialization: Only executed if param_1[0x21] == 0 (prevents double initialization)\n- Class-specific behavior: Ordinal_10655 provides class-dependent table\n- Summoned minions: Ordinal_10918() sets random seed counter\n",
      "tags": ["PARAM_6", "PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "MOD_UNIT", "STRUCT_Skill", "SRC_Monster.cpp", "STRUCT_ItemData", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
