      "comment": "Process unit statistics based on stat mode. Initializes stat calculations, applies mode-specific processing.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate input: Exit with -1 if pUnit is NULL\n2. Get unit class (0x116 check) via Ordinal_11056 (D2Common.GetUnitClass)\n3. If unit class is 0x116 and pUnit[3]==0 and Ordinal_10378 returns nonzero:\n   a. Initialize 7-element stat buffer (adStatValues) to zeros\n   b. Call ProcessStatMode9 (FUN_6fb7b140) with buffer\n4. Initialize nResult to 0\n5. Switch on nStatMode extracted from parameter (param_2 + 4):\n   - Case 0: No action\n   - Case 1: Call Ordinal_10378 (GetUnitStat), return value if nonzero\n   - Case 2: Call Ordinal_10378; if nonzero: clear pUnit[0x16], set pUnit[0x14]=pUnit[0x15]-0x100, set flag 0x20 if pUnit[3]==0\n   - Case 3: Set pUnit[0x14]=0x100, clear pUnit[0x16]\n   - Default: No action\n6. Call Ordinal_10373 (D2Common.SetUnitStat or finalization)\n7. Return nResult\n\nParameters:\n- pUnit (ECX): Pointer to unit structure\n- nStatMode (EDX): Pointer to mode struct; mode value at offset +4\n\nReturns:\n- 0 on success (modes 0,3) or if processing complete (mode 2)\n- Stat value from Ordinal_10378 (mode 1 or 2 if nonzero)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- NULL input triggers assertion and fatal exit\n- Mode dependent stat processing with field adjustments\n- SSA temporaries optimize register usage",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Inventory", "PARAM_2", "MOD_UNIT", "SRC_Monster.cpp"]
