      "instructions": ["0xAA5F0|SUB|ESP, 0x64", "0xAA5F3|PUSH|EBX", "0xAA5F4|PUSH|EBP", "0xAA5F5|PUSH|ESI", "0xAA5F6|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0xAA5F8|TEST|ESI, ESI", "0xAA5FA|PUSH|EDI", "0xAA5FB|JZ|0x6fb7abbf", "0xAA601|CMP|dword ptr [ESI], 0x1", "0xAA604|JNZ|0x6fb7abbf", "0xAA60A|PUSH|0x1", "0xAA60C|PUSH|ESI", "0xAA60D|CALL|0x6fb98404", "0xAA612|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0xAA614|JZ|0x6fb7a625"],
      "comment": "Process unit skill effect activation and execution for Diablo II units.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate unit pointer and unit state (must be type 1)\n2. Validate skill equipment slots (0-15 range)\n3. Select data table based on unit type and equipment slot combination:\n   - Certain unit/slot pairs map to fixed skill tables (e.g., 0xf3 slot 11 -> DAT_6fbcdfa0)\n   - Other combinations check skill preset at offset 0x228, 0x250, 0x278, 0x2a0, 0x2a1, 0x2a2, 0x2a4\n   - If skill not set (null), use default table based on equipment slot\n4. Execute skill effect processing based on equip slot type\n5. Handle special case: mercenary - determine position (mercenary or unit position)\n6. Based on projectile type, initialize projectile or handle special skills (0x196, 0xee, 0xef)\n7. Execute unit-level skill effect processing\n8. Update ammunition/resource counts for mercenary skills\n9. Check game state and trigger skill callbacks if needed\n\nParameters:\n  pUnit (UnitAny *) - Unit entity to process skill effect for (in ECX)\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Validates unit type != 3 for missile units to prevent invalid state\n  - Magic number 0xc1 skill has dynamic projectile range calculation\n  - Skills 0xb2 and 0x11a have capped movement values (0x600, 0x800 respectively)\n  - Handles 3 types of projectile creation: normal, missile unit, and preset tables",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "MOD_UNIT", "SRC_Monster.cpp", "STRUCT_ItemData", "PARAM_1", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData", "STRUCT_MonsterData", "PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Path", "UNIT_MISSILE"]
