      "comment": "Initialize a game unit with type-specific properties and register event handlers.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get random seed counter (Ordinal_10918)\n2. Validate seed value <= 4; if greater, abort with error 0x19d via FUN_6fb9a10f(-1)\n3. Look up unit type ID from g_adwUnitTypeTable[seed]\n4. Get unit Y coordinate via Ordinal_10329(nUnitIndex)\n5. Get unit X coordinate via Ordinal_10326(nUnitIndex)\n6. Initialize unit structure via InitializeStructureAndCallHandler(nUnitIndex, dwUnitTypeId, nXCoord, nYCoord, 0x1)\n7. If initialization successful (result != NULL):\n   a. Register bidirectional event handlers via Ordinal_10415 (link unit both directions)\n   b. Apply post-init processing via FUN_6fb979a0\n   c. Set flags via FUN_6fb97f70 with parameter 1\n   d. Set flag 0x40000 at offset 0xec (state flag indicating initialization complete)\n\nParameters:\n  nUnitIndex (ECX): Index of game unit to initialize\n\nReturns:\n  void - Side effects on global unit structures\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If seed value > 4, function terminates via FUN_6fb9a10f(-1) error handler\n  - If InitializeStructureAndCallHandler returns NULL, handler registration is skipped\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x04 - Maximum valid seed index\n  0x01 - Initial flags value for handler registration\n  0xec - Offset of unit status flags within unit structure\n  0x40000 - Status flag value indicating initialized state (0x40000 = bit 18 set)\n  0x19d - Error code for invalid seed value (413 decimal)",
