      "comment": "Create projectiles in a spiral pattern for a skill effect.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Verify unit class ID is 0x3f (Unique Monster/Boss)\n2. Get unit's special attribute from param_1[1]\n3. Return early if attribute is null\n4. Initialize offset deltas to +5 x, +5 y\n5. Call Ordinal_10912 and Ordinal_10913 (skill initialization)\n6. Load projectile count from unit attribute[0x1e6]\n7. For each projectile in count:\n   a. Call Ordinal_10917 for x randomization: if result & 1, negate nDeltaX\n   b. Call Ordinal_10917 for y randomization: if result & 1, negate nDeltaY\n   c. Create projectile with adjusted offsets: x=nDeltaX+nDeltaY, y=nDeltaY+nDeltaY\n   d. Return value is always 1 (success)\n\nParameters:\n- pUnit (int *): Pointer to unit instance, requires class ID 0x3f validation\n- dwSkillEffect (dword): Skill/ability index (stored in caller's stack)\n- nDeltaX (int): Base x-axis offset applied to each projectile (+/-5)\n- nDeltaY (int): Base y-axis offset applied to each projectile (+/-5)\n\nReturns:\n- void: No return value, operates via side effects (projectile creation)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Only processes if unit class is 0x3f (specific unit type check)\n- Requires valid unit attribute pointer (param_1[1]) or returns silently\n- Projectiles created with randomized direction based on Ordinal_10917 results\n- Direction negation toggled on each random call (alternating x/y randomization)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x3f: Unit class ID for processing (identifies specific unit type)\n- 0x1e6 (486 decimal): Offset in unit attribute struct for projectile count\n- 0x5: Initial x/y offset magnitude before randomization\n- 0x1: Projectile creation success flag\n\nFunction Calls:\n- Ordinal_11056(pUnit): Get unit class ID\n- Ordinal_10582(pUnit[1]): Get unit attribute pointer\n- Ordinal_10912(): Skill/ability initialization (purpose unknown, side effects)\n- Ordinal_10913(): Skill/ability initialization (purpose unknown, side effects)\n- Ordinal_10917(): Random bit generator for direction selection\n- CreateProjectileFromUnit(): Create single projectile with computed offsets\n\nRelated Functions:\n- ProcessUnitSkillEffect(): Caller function that invokes skill projectile creation\n- CreateProjectileFromUnit(): Creates individual projectiles in spiral pattern",
