      "instructions": ["0xAAD20|PUSH|ESI", "0xAAD21|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0xAAD23|TEST|ESI, ESI", "0xAAD25|PUSH|EDI", "0xAAD26|JZ|0x6fb7af7b", "0xAAD2C|CMP|dword ptr [ESI], 0x1", "0xAAD2F|JNZ|0x6fb7af7b", "0xAAD35|CMP|dword ptr [ESI + 0xc], 0x10", "0xAAD39|JNC|0x6fb7af7b", "0xAAD3F|PUSH|ESI", "0xAAD40|CALL|0x6fb985e4", "0xAAD45|MOV|EDI, EAX", "0xAAD47|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [ESI + 0xc]", "0xAAD4A|CMP|EAX, 0xd", "0xAAD4D|JNZ|0x6fb7ad82"],
      "comment": "Validate unit state and execute unit-specific action handlers based on type/class.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate pnUnitData is non-null (NULL check return)\n2. Check unit marker *pnUnitData == 1 (invalid unit return)\n3. Check unit type pnUnitData[3] < 0x10 (out-of-range return)\n4. Get unit class ID using Ordinal_11056(pnUnitData)\n5. Special merc handling: if type 0xd and class != 0x4e\n   - Get resource from pnUnitData[0xe] (merc weapon ID)\n   - Ordinal_10233: lookup weapon resource\n   - Ordinal_10208: clear weapon assignment\n   - Ordinal_10186: cleanup weapon properties\n   - Call FUN_6fb86790(pnUnitData, 0x3) and return\n6. Get mercenary position GetMercenaryPosition(pnUnitData)\n7. If valid merc, call ValidateUnitAndProcessGlobalData()\n8. Ordinal_10582(class) returns inventory/unit data block\n9. If inventory NULL, return\n10. Check inventory[0x341] != 0 (if zero, goto finalization)\n11. Switch on unit type with class-specific logic:\n    - Type 2: reject classes 0xe7, 0x76\n    - Type 4: special missile handling (0x1f1)\n      - GetUnitFromHashTable resolve reference\n      - Validate unit.dwUnitType == 3\n      - InitializeUnitEquipmentSlots reset equipment\n      - Ordinal_10918 get random seed\n      - Load g_adwUnitTypeTable[seed] type ID\n      - Ordinal_10329, Ordinal_10326 get position\n      - InitializeStructureAndCallHandler create unit\n      - Ordinal_10415 link units bidirectional\n      - FUN_6fb979a0 initialize properties\n      - FUN_6fb97f70 set active flag\n      - Set flag 0x40000 (initialized)\n    - Types 5,8,9: special logic for classes 0x193, 0x194\n    - Type 8: reject class 0x6e\n    - Type 10: handle class 0x88 with state 0xb\n    - Types 0xb,0xc,0xe: specific class filters\n12. If inventory empty (inventory[0x341]==0), skip to finalization\n13. Final validation: pnUnitData[8]==0, *pnUnitData==1, type 0-0xf, type!=0 and !=0xc\n14. If all valid: ValidateUnitAndProcessGlobalData(), FUN_6fb858b0(), FUN_6fb86790(state 1)\n\nParameters:\n  pnUnitData: Pointer to unit structure (__fastcall ECX register)\n    [0]: Unit valid marker (1=valid)\n    [3]: Unit type/class ID\n    [8]: Unit state/activity flags\n    [0xc]: Unit type classification\n    [0x20]: Unit state flags\n    [0x38]: Resource/weapon ID\n    Other: Unit property fields\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  Mercenary units (type 0xd) - weapon reset path, early return\n  Missile types (0x1f1) - full unit creation and linking\n  Empty inventory - skips main processing, goes to finalization\n  State flags set - skips finalization entirely\n  Multiple early returns for invalid configurations\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x1: Unit valid marker value\n  0xf: Max unit type (exclusive upper bound)\n  0xd: Mercenary unit type code\n  0x4e: Mercenary class filter threshold\n  0xe7, 0x76, 0x6e, 0x88, 0x193, 0x194, 0x1f1: Type-specific class codes\n  0x11c, 0xf7: Additional class filters\n  0x341: Inventory empty check offset\n  0x20: Unit state flags offset\n  0x3c: Animation state parameter (merc)\n  0x8, 0xb: Animation state codes\n  0x1: Standard animation state\n  0x40000: Unit initialized/active property flag",
