      "comment": "Create projectiles in all 8 directions from a unit based on skill level and directional offsets.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Return early if nSkillLevel is 0 or if unit type is 1 with field[0xc] == 3 and validation fails\n   (Check: Ordinal_10918 = D2Common.GetTickCount)\n2. Query unit slot count at offset 0x8c using Ordinal_10520 (D2Common.GetUnitData), default to 1\n3. Loop through each slot (nLoopIndex) from 0 to nMaxSlots-1\n4. For each slot, get associated unit using Ordinal_10582 (D2Common.GetUnitByIndex) and check if byte at offset 0x2b0 is non-zero\n5. If non-zero, determine direction index:\n   - Check directional capability with Ordinal_10147 (D2Common.HasDirection)\n   - If no direction: get default via Ordinal_10917 (D2Common.GetDefaultDirection)\n   - If has direction: get skill direction via Ordinal_10457 (D2Common.GetSkillDirection)\n   - Extract bit [2:5] using Ordinal_10918 (D2Common.GetTickCount), shift right 3, combine with dwDirection\n6. Calculate end direction as dwDirection - 1 (3-bit mask)\n7. Get projectile ID via Ordinal_10342 (D2Common.GetProjectileEntity)\n8. Iterate directions using Ordinal_10326 (D2Common.GetUnitX) and Ordinal_10329 (D2Common.GetUnitY)\n9. For each direction, load X/Y offsets from g_adDirectionOffsetsX/Y arrays\n10. Test collision at (X + offset, Y + offset) using Ordinal_10118 (D2Common.TestCollision)\n11. If collision detected, break; otherwise create projectile via CreateProjectileFromUnit\n12. Continue to next slot\n\nParameters:\nIMPLICIT ECX: pUnit - Unit structure pointer\nIMPLICIT EDX: nSkillLevel - Skill level (0 triggers early exit)\n\nReturns:\nvoid (no return value)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Early exit for skill level 0 or specific unit types\n- Direction calculation depends on directional capability\n- Collision detection on all 8 directions before creation\n- Empty collision set skips projectile creation\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x8c - Unit slot count offset\n0x2b0 - Active status byte offset\n0x38 - Direction/state field offset\n0x100 - Direction validation bit mask\n0x12 - Projectile creation offset adjustment",
