      "api_calls": ["UNITS_GetUnitY", "UNITS_GetOwnerGuid", "UNITS_GetRoom", "ClearMapCellFlagWrapper", "UNITS_GetUnitY", "UNITS_GetOwnerGuid", "UNITS_GetRoom", "ClearMapCellFlagWrapper", "SetNestedField48", "ITEMS_SetItemDataField50", "...+10 more"],
      "instructions": ["0xAC3B0|PUSH|ESI", "0xAC3B1|CMP|ECX, 0xc", "0xAC3B4|MOV|ESI, EDX", "0xAC3B6|JNZ|0x6fb7c465", "0xAC3BC|MOV|ECX, dword ptr [ESI + 0xe8]", "0xAC3C2|PUSH|0x1000", "0xAC3C7|AND|ECX, 0xfffffff1", "0xAC3CA|PUSH|ESI", "0xAC3CB|MOV|dword ptr [ESI + 0xe8], ECX", "0xAC3D1|CALL|0x6fb9811c", "0xAC3D6|PUSH|EAX", "0xAC3D7|PUSH|ESI", "0xAC3D8|CALL|0x6fb98122", "0xAC3DD|PUSH|EAX", "0xAC3DE|PUSH|ESI"],
      "comment": "Process animation frame states for skill execution (animation types 0x0C, 0x0A, 0x0E).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. If nAnimationType == 0x0C:\n   a. Load unit flags at offset 0xE8, clear bits [3:0] (AND 0xFFFFFFF1)\n   b. Store cleared flags back at offset 0xE8\n   c. Call Ordinal_10329 (GetUnitX) to get unit X coordinate\n   d. Call Ordinal_10326 (GetUnitY) to get unit Y coordinate  \n   e. Call Ordinal_10342 (GetUnitStat) to get unit handle/stat\n   f. Call Ordinal_10123 with range 0x1000 (clear animation frame, large range)\n   g. Repeat steps c-f for range 0x100 (clear animation frame, small range)\n   h. Call Ordinal_10211 with mode 5 (set animation frame mode)\n   i. Call Ordinal_10184 with offset 0x38 and value 0x00 (clear frame speed)\n   j. Call FUN_6fb97a70 to check frame index state\n   k. If result == 0, initialize animation: call FUN_6fb979a0, FUN_6fb97fb0, FUN_6fb98000(1), FUN_6fb97b40(2,1), FUN_6fb97be0(0xa0,0)\n2. Else if nAnimationType == 0x0E or 0x0A:\n   a. Load unit flags, set bits [3:1] (OR 0x0E)\n   b. Store modified flags back\n   c. Get X, Y, handle via same ordinals as step 1c-e\n   d. Call Ordinal_10127 with range 0x1000 (set animation frame)\n   e. Repeat for range 0x100\n   f. Call Ordinal_10211 with mode 1 (set animation frame mode)\n   g. Call Ordinal_10184 with offset 0x38 and value 0x3C01 (set frame speed)\n   h. Call FUN_6fb97a70 to check frame index\n   i. If result != 0, finalize: call FUN_6fb97fb0, FUN_6fb98000(0), FUN_6fb97b40(-8,1), FUN_6fb97be0(0,0)\n3. Return\n\nParameters:\n  nAnimationType (ECX, dword): Animation control code\n    0x0C = Reset/clear animation frames\n    0x0A = Set animation frames (alternate)\n    0x0E = Set animation frames (primary)\n  pUnit (EDX, int*): Pointer to UnitAny structure\n    Offset 0xE8 = Animation control flags (bits [3:1], [3:0])\n    Offset 0x38 = Frame speed/duration field\n\nReturns:\n  void (no return value, function always returns via RET 0x4)\n\nStructure Layout (UnitAny offsets used):\n  Offset | Size | Field Name | Type | Description\n  0x38   | 4    | dwSpeed    | dword| Frame speed/duration (set to 0x00 or 0x3C01)\n  0xE8   | 4    | dwFlags    | dword| Animation control flags\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x1000 = Large frame range for animation processing\n  0x100  = Small frame range for animation processing\n  0x0E   = Animation flag mask (bits [3:1])\n  0xFFFFFFF1 = Clear bits [3:0] mask\n  0x3C01 = High speed frame duration constant\n  0x00   = Zero speed (pause animation)\n  Mode 5 = Reset animation frame mode\n  Mode 1 = Set animation frame mode\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Type 0x0C uses Ordinal_10123 (clear animation)\n  - Type 0x0E/0x0A use Ordinal_10127 (set animation)\n  - FUN_6fb97a70 returns 0 for reset case, non-zero for set case (opposite logic)",
      "tags": ["PARAM_2"]
    },
