      "instructions": ["0xAC510|SUB|ESP, 0x4c", "0xAC513|PUSH|EBX", "0xAC514|PUSH|EBP", "0xAC515|MOV|EBP, ECX", "0xAC517|MOV|EBX, EDX", "0xAC519|PUSH|ESI", "0xAC51A|PUSH|EDI", "0xAC51B|TEST|EBP, EBP", "0xAC51D|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x18], EBX", "0xAC521|JZ|0x6fb7c6ea", "0xAC527|TEST|EBX, EBX", "0xAC529|JZ|0x6fb7c6ea", "0xAC52F|MOV|EDX, dword ptr [EBP + 0xe8]", "0xAC535|XOR|ECX, ECX", "0xAC537|OR|EDX, 0x202"],
      "comment": "Initialize skill levels for hireling unit based on game time.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate unit and skill array pointers non-null\n2. Set unit state flag (0xe8) with 0x202 bit\n3. Call game initialization (Ordinal_11086)\n4. Get current video frame count via GetVideoFrameCount\n5. Retrieve skill table entry for frame (Ordinal_11082)\n6. Resolve to skill definition record (Ordinal_10583)\n7. Calculate elapsed time: base - current\n8. Loop 6 skill slots: load ID, validate, calculate level\n9. Retrieve unit name pointer from offset 0x70\n10. Copy name to buffer with Unicode functions\n\nParameters:\nnUnit (implicit ECX, int) - Unit structure pointer to update\npSkillArray (implicit EDX, short *) - Skill value array\nIMPLICIT AL - Frame count from GetVideoFrameCount\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Modifies unit structure and applies visual effects",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PARAM_2", "UI_SKILLS", "MOD_UNIT", "SRC_Monster.cpp", "STRUCT_Room1", "STRUCT_Other", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
