      "instructions": ["0xAC700|PUSH|ESI", "0xAC701|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0xAC703|TEST|ESI, ESI", "0xAC705|JNZ|0x6fb7c70b", "0xAC707|XOR|EAX, EAX", "0xAC709|POP|ESI", "0xAC70A|RET|", "0xAC70B|CMP|dword ptr [ESI], 0x1", "0xAC70E|JZ|0x6fb7c714", "0xAC710|XOR|EAX, EAX", "0xAC712|POP|ESI", "0xAC713|RET|", "0xAC714|MOV|ECX, dword ptr [ESI + 0x4]", "0xAC717|CALL|0x6fb98fda", "0xAC71C|TEST|EAX, EAX"],
      "comment": "Validates unit state conditions before allowing action execution\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if pUnit pointer is valid (non-null)\n2. Verify unit type field (first DWORD) equals 1\n3. Call Ordinal_10317() to check random seed state (returns 0 if not ready)\n4. Load unit state pointer from offset +0x1c\n5. If state pointer exists:\n   a. Check bit 0 is clear (state flag 0x01 must not be set)\n   b. If state flag clear, validate nested state at offset +0xcc\n   c. Call FUN_6fb7c7e0() on nested state pointer\n6. Validate result from FUN_6fb7c7e0():\n   a. Check return is non-null\n   b. Verify first word (offset +0) is less than 0xffbd (0xffbc < result)\n7. Return 0 (fail) on any validation failure, 1 (success) if all pass\n\nParameters:\n  pUnit (IMPLICIT ECX): int * - Pointer to unit structure to validate\n\nReturns:\n  EAX: 0 if validation fails, 1 if all conditions pass\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - NULL unit pointer returns 0\n  - Unit type != 1 returns 0\n  - Ordinal_10317() returning 0 (random seed not ready) returns 0\n  - Nested state flag validation is skipped if state pointer is NULL\n  - Magic number 0xffbd (65469 in decimal) used as upper bound check",
      "tags": ["PARAM_1"]
    },
