      "comment": "Allocates and initializes a resource pool structure (0x27 bytes)\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call Ordinal_10042(0x27, 0) to allocate 0x27 bytes via Storm memory allocator\n2. Initialize pTemp pointer to point to allocated memory\n3. Loop 0xb (11) times: zero-fill each 4-byte dword via REP STOSD instruction\n4. Return pointer to zero-initialized resource pool structure\n\nParameters:\n  None\n\nReturns:\n  uint * - Pointer to allocated and zero-initialized resource pool (0x27 bytes = 39 decimal)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  Allocation size: 0x27 bytes (39 decimal bytes, 11 dwords)\n  Zero-fill: REP STOSD instruction clears all allocated memory\n  Magic constant: 0x27 = resource pool structure size\n  \nMagic Numbers:\n  0x27 - Resource pool allocation size (39 decimal bytes)\n  0xb - Loop count for zero-fill (11 dword iterations = 44 bytes cleared)\n  0x2c - Size passed to allocator in ECX (total copy size)\n  \nOrdinals Used:\n  Ordinal_10042 - Storm.dll memory allocator (malloc-like function)\n  \nRelated Functions:\n  - Ordinal_10042() - Storm memory allocator\n  - AllocateGameObjectMemory() - Primary caller, stores result at unit offset 0x33\n  - InitializeUnitOnCreation() - Caller, allocates resource pool for equipment slots\n  - InitializeUnitStats() - Caller, initializes unit statistics with allocated resource pool",
