      "comment": "Set or clear the skill activation flag (bit 1 at offset +6) in a skill structure.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Test if nActivate parameter is non-zero\n2. If nActivate != 0: Set bit 1 (0x02) at offset +6 using bitwise OR\n3. If nActivate == 0: Clear bit 1 (0x02) at offset +6 using bitwise AND with 0xFFFD\n\nParameters:\n  pSkillNode (int) - Pointer to skill structure base address\n  nActivate (int) - Non-zero to activate, zero to deactivate\n\nReturns:\n  void - Modifies skill structure in-place\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  The flag is stored at offset +6 as a word (2 bytes) in the skill structure.\n  Bit 0x02 indicates whether the skill is currently active/enabled.\n\nRelated Functions:\n  ProcessSkillActionByType() - Calls this function to update skill state",
