      "instructions": ["0xAC820|SUB|ESP, 0x268", "0xAC826|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [ESP + 0x26c]", "0xAC82D|PUSH|EBX", "0xAC82E|PUSH|EBP", "0xAC82F|PUSH|ESI", "0xAC830|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0xAC832|PUSH|EDI", "0xAC833|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x14], EDX", "0xAC837|MOV|EBX, ECX", "0xAC839|JZ|0x6fb7ca83", "0xAC83F|LEA|ESI, [ESP + 0x20]", "0xAC843|MOV|EDI, 0x12c", "0xAC848|MOV|ECX, ESI", "0xAC84A|CALL|dword ptr [0x6fba5c30]", "0xAC850|ADD|ESI, 0x2"],
      "comment": "Builds a Unicode string representation of game unit state for display.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize 600-element Unicode buffer on stack\n2. If param_3 (flags) is zero, return immediately\n3. Copy format string from g_szBattleNetFormat (%s\\UI\\AutoMap\\MaxiMap_addr)\n4. Convert format string to Unicode, store in local Unicode array\n5. Get unit data pointer from param_1 + 0x70 offset\n6. Retrieve unit state field via GetUnitFieldAt0xCC\n7. Check if state field at offset 0x4 exceeds 0xffbc:\n   - If yes: map state ID via Ordinal_10668, retrieve string from DAT at ID+0x3c\n   - If no: get unit state flag via GetUnitStateFlag, search state table g_adwStateIndexTable\n8. Retrieve corresponding string from ordinal function (Ordinal_10004)\n9. Process string for bracketed content via ProcessBracketedStringData\n10. Check param_2 special cases (0xc, 0xf3, 0x9c, 0xd3, 0xf2, 0x100, 0x220)\n11. For unmatched cases, chain Ordinal_10653->Ordinal_10652 for secondary data\n12. Check random seed (Ordinal_10918) and conditionally append tertiary data if < 0x32\n13. Copy final Unicode string to unit structure via CopyUnicodeStringWithValidation\n\nParameters:\nnUnitPtr (ECX): Pointer to unit structure with state info at +0x70\nnStateId (EDX): State identifier to process\nnFormatFlags (stack +0x4): Control flags; 0 = no processing\n\nReturns:\nNone (modifies unit structure in place)\n\nSpecial Cases:\nMagic 0xffbc: State field threshold value\nMagic 0xffbd: Offset adjustment when state exceeds threshold\nStates 0x9c, 0xd3, 0xf2: Special unit states requiring alternate text\nStates 0xf3, 0x100, 0x220: Specific handling paths with ordinal mappings\nRandom threshold 0x32: Controls whether tertiary text is appended (50 in decimal)",
      "tags": ["PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Path", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "SRC_MonUnique.cpp", "PARAM_3", "MOD_UNIT", "STRUCT_ItemData", "STRUCT_Other", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
