      "instructions": ["0xACB90|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [ESP + 0x4]", "0xACB94|PUSH|EBX", "0xACB95|PUSH|ESI", "0xACB96|MOV|EBX, EDX", "0xACB98|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0xACB9A|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0xACB9C|JZ|0x6fb7cd1c", "0xACBA2|PUSH|EDI", "0xACBA3|PUSH|0x27", "0xACBA5|PUSH|ESI", "0xACBA6|XOR|EDI, EDI", "0xACBA8|CALL|0x6fb9826c", "0xACBAD|CMP|EAX, 0x4b", "0xACBB0|JLE|0x6fb7cbb7", "0xACBB2|MOV|EDI, 0x1"],
      "comment": "ApplyShrineStatBonus - Applies stat bonuses to a unit based on shrine type.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. If bApply is 0, do nothing\n2. Count how many resistances are already maxed (>75)\n3. If 2+ resistances are maxed, skip applying bonus\n4. Switch on shrine type to apply appropriate stat bonus:\n   - Type 8: Fire+Cold resist +75\n   - Type 9: Fire resist +75\n   - Type 17: Cold resist +75\n   - Type 18: Lightning resist +75 (with fire+cold from case 8)\n   - Type 23: Poison resist +75\n   - Type 25: Poison resist +20 (reads stamina recovery)\n   - Type 27: All resists +20\n   - Type 28: Mana recovery +50\n\nParameters:\n  pUnit - Pointer to the unit receiving the shrine bonus\n  nShrineType - Shrine type ID determining which stat bonus to apply\n  bApply - Boolean flag; if 0, no bonus is applied\n\nReturns: void",
      "tags": ["PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_3"]
    },
