      "instructions": ["0xAD2F0|SUB|ESP, 0x8", "0xAD2F3|PUSH|ESI", "0xAD2F4|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0xAD2F6|PUSH|EDI", "0xAD2F7|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [ESI + 0xc]", "0xAD2FA|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0xAD2FC|JNZ|0x6fb7d35c", "0xAD2FE|LEA|EAX, [ESP + 0xc]", "0xAD302|LEA|ECX, [ESP + 0x8]", "0xAD306|PUSH|EAX", "0xAD307|PUSH|ECX", "0xAD308|PUSH|ESI", "0xAD309|CALL|0x6fb98656", "0xAD30E|CMP|dword ptr [ESP + 0x8], 0xd", "0xAD313|JNZ|0x6fb7d39e"],
      "comment": "Processes unit state transitions and executes state-specific handlers.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load unit state type from pUnit[3]\n2. If state is 0:\n   a. Call Ordinal_10379 to get state information (fills nStateType, abStateData)\n   b. If nStateType equals 0xd (13):\n      - Call FUN_6fb935a0 to initialize unit\n      - Call FUN_6fb931f0 twice with offsets 0x34 and 0x9c, parameter 5\n      - Clear byte at pUnit[0x5c]\n   c. Return on state mismatch\n3. If state is 0xc (12):\n   a. Get unit stat pointer from pUnit[0x1c]\n   b. Get random seed value via Ordinal_10918\n   c. Check if random value is 0 AND stat value < 100:\n      - Call Ordinal_10326 for state handler\n      - Call Ordinal_10329 for state handler\n      - Allocate random units with type 0xe3, count 4\n      - Increment stat pointer by 4\n4. Return\n\nParameters:\npUnit (int *) - IMPLICIT in ECX: Pointer to unit structure; field [3] contains state type (0, 0xc, etc.)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Function returns at two points: after state 0 handling (via RET 0x4 at 0x6fb7d359) or final return (RET 0x4 at 0x6fb7d3a3)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- State 0x0 handler clears byte at offset 0x5c\n- State 0xc has random seed condition check\n- All random allocation checks for stat < 100 before proceeding\n- Magic values 0x34, 0x9c, 0xe3, 100 used in state transitions",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Inventory", "PROP_NOCALLER", "STRUCT_ItemData", "PARAM_1", "STRUCT_UnitAny"]
    },
