      "instructions": ["0xAD510|SUB|ESP, 0x7c", "0xAD513|PUSH|EBX", "0xAD514|PUSH|EBP", "0xAD515|PUSH|ESI", "0xAD516|MOV|ESI, dword ptr [ESP + 0x8c]", "0xAD51D|MOV|EBX, ECX", "0xAD51F|MOV|EBP, EDX", "0xAD521|TEST|ESI, ESI", "0xAD523|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0xc], EBX", "0xAD527|JNZ|0x6fb7d52e", "0xAD529|MOV|ESI, 0x1", "0xAD52E|CMP|EBP, 0xc3", "0xAD534|JNZ|0x6fb7d548", "0xAD536|MOV|ECX, dword ptr [EBX + 0x70]", "0xAD539|CALL|0x6fb796b0"],
      "comment": "Initialize and allocate projectiles in a 2x4 grid pattern based on unit position and type.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Normalize count: if count is 0, set to 1\n2. Check termination condition: skip if projectile type is 0xC3 AND unit field has flag 0x02\n3. Initialize grid array (adGridData): Clear last 22 elements, set magic value 0x21 at offset 8\n4. Populate grid control block: Set indices 0-7 with default values (offsets, limits, counts)\n5. Retrieve unit position: Call Ordinal_10326(unit) for X-base, Ordinal_10329(unit) for Y-base\n6. Loop grid rows (0, 4, 8, 12): For each row, calculate cell positions and allocate projectile\n7. For each cell (2 columns per row): Add row offset to X-base, add row offset to Y-base\n8. Call InitializeAndAllocateProjectile with grid control block and calculated position\n\nParameters:\n- dwUnitBaseAddr (IMPLICIT ECX): Base address of unit structure\n- nProjectileType (IMPLICIT EDX): Projectile type code (0xC3 is terminator)\n- nCount (Stack +4): Number of projectile groups to create (default 1 if 0)\n\nReturns: void (modifies projectile state in-place)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Type 0xC3 with flag 0x02: Function returns immediately without allocating\n- Count parameter normalized to minimum 1\n- Grid contains 4 rows of 3 elements each (12 elements total)\n- Note: Function uses 1 stack-allocated temporary optimized away by compiler\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x21: Grid structure magic/control value at offset 8\n- 0xC3: Special terminator projectile type\n- 0x141: Type used for callback selection\n- 0x02: Flag mask for unit field byte at offset 6\n- 0xFFFFFFFF: Default limit values in grid\n\nStructure Layout:\n| Offset | Size | Field Name | Type | Description |\n| 0 | 4 | flags | uint | Initialization flags |\n| 4 | 4 | count | uint | Projectile count |\n| 8 | 4 | magic | uint | Magic value 0x21 |\n| 12 | 4 | unitPtr | uint | Pointer to unit structure |\n| 16-44 | 7*4 | reserved | uint[7] | Reserved/limit values |\n\nRelated Functions:\n- GetUnitFieldAt0xCC() - Retrieves unit position field\n- Ordinal_10326() - Get unit X coordinate (D2Common ordinal)\n- Ordinal_10329() - Get unit Y coordinate (D2Common ordinal)\n- InitializeAndAllocateProjectile() - Allocate single projectile instance",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "STRUCT_Room2", "STRUCT_Room1", "STRUCT_ItemData", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData", "STRUCT_StatList", "STRUCT_MonsterData", "STRUCT_Path", "PARAM_3", "STRUCT_Skill"]
