      "comment": "Apply skill modifiers with level 2 enhancement to a unit.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Push modifier level constant (0x2) onto stack\n2. Clear EDX register (zero parameter)\n3. Call ApplySkillModifiers with unit pointer and level parameter\n4. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\npUnit (void*) - Pointer to unit entity to modify with skill level 2\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value, modifiers applied in-place to unit\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Level parameter hard-coded to 0x2 (level 2 modification)\n- Function serves as convenient wrapper for common skill modifier level\n- EDX cleared before call (padding parameter)\n- Note: Function uses 1 stack-allocated temporary (unaff_retaddr) optimized away by compiler\n\nRelated Functions:\n- ApplySkillModifiers - Core skill modifier application with configurable level\n- ProcessUnitSkillEffect - Caller that triggers skill effect processing",
