      "comment": "Validate skill parameters and apply skill modifiers if conditions met\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Verify skill ID pointer is not NULL (param in ECX)\n2. Verify skill level is non-zero (param in EDX)\n3. Check if skill level value equals 1 (dereference pointer check)\n4. If all conditions pass, call ApplySkillModifiers with skill data and hard-coded type 0x4\n5. Return void\n\nParameters:\npSkillId (dword *) - Pointer to skill ID value, must not be NULL\nnSkillLevel (dword) - Skill level number, must be non-zero\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value, function performs side effects through ApplySkillModifiers\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If any precondition fails (NULL pointer, zero level, or dereferenced value != 1), function returns immediately without calling ApplySkillModifiers\n- Hard-coded constant 0x4 is passed as third parameter to ApplySkillModifiers (likely modifier type or flag)\n- Note: unaff_retaddr is compiler-optimized return address variable, cannot be renamed",
