      "comment": "Build unit action string for skill display\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize output buffer to zero\n2. Retrieve unit pointer from nUnit base + 0x70 offset\n3. Check if unit has bit flags set via GetBitFlag()\n4. If flags exist (pbBits != NULL):\n   - If wFlags != 0, concatenate skill prefix twice (0xc95, 0xf9b)\n   - If wFlags == 0, concatenate skill prefix once (0xc95)\n   - Return early\n5. If no flags (pbBits == NULL):\n   - Call GetUnitFieldAt0xCC(pUnit) twice to get field value\n   - Call Ordinal_10127() - appears to be state management\n   - For wFlags != 0: add initial prefix string, get initial width via Ordinal_10121()\n   - Loop 9 times through slot index array [dVar2+8]:\n     a. Check if slot is active via g_aSlotActive lookup\n     b. If active and width fits: concatenate separator and string, accumulate width\n     c. If accumulated width exceeds 0x1e0 (480 pixels), exit loop\n   - Call Ordinal_10127() - state cleanup before return\n\nParameters:\n  nUnit (int, ECX) - Unit index/ID to process\n  pnResult (ushort *, EDX) - Pointer to output unicode string buffer\n  nMaxLen (int, Stack[0x4]) - Maximum buffer length including null terminator\n  wFlags (ushort, Stack[0x8]) - Flag bits: 0x0000=standard, 0x0001=add prefix\n\nReturns:\n  void - Result string written to pnResult buffer with null terminator\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - pbBits NULL path: processes 9 possible skill slots with width limit\n  - pbBits non-NULL path: early return with simplified prefix string\n  - Width calculation: 0x1e0 (480) pixel limit prevents buffer overrun\n  - Empty slot check: g_aSlotActive array indicates active slots (word indexed)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x70 - Offset in unit structure to unit pointer field\n  0xCC - Field offset accessed via GetUnitFieldAt0xCC\n  0xf9b - Skill prefix string identifier (param to Ordinal_10004)\n  0xc95 - Skill separator string identifier (param to Ordinal_10004)\n  0x1e0 - Accumulated width threshold (480 pixels)\n  0x6fbce504 - Global array g_aSlotActive (word array, active slot flags)",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Inventory", "STRUCT_Skill", "PARAM_4", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
    },
