      "comment": "Retrieves and updates unit animation state from type-specific handler tables\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate: Return 0 if pUnit is NULL\n2. Read unit type ID from pUnit+0x04, map to handler table using switch\n3. Handler table format: [baseFrame, altFrame, rendererFrame, cachedState, frameCounter, timestampCounter]\n4. Mode check: If nMode==2, return cached baseFrame at index 0 only\n5. Animation update loop (max 20 iterations): Load baseFrame from table[0]\n6. Check mode conditions: If mode 0/1 match, select alt/renderer frames accordingly\n7. Call FUN_6fb8cc90 to process animation state\n8. Break if result matches previous cached value; otherwise update cache and timestamp\n9. Return final animation state\n\nParameters:\npUnit (UnitAny *): Unit structure pointer; contains unit type ID at offset +4\nnMode (int): Mode flag; 2=cached state only, 0/1=update with respective logic paths\n\nReturns:\nint: Current animation state value, or 0 if unit invalid or type not mapped",
