      "api_count": 4,
      "api_calls": ["GetActRoomXPos", "InitializeUnitAnimation", "LogPoolWarning", "InitializeUnitAnimation"],
      "instructions": ["0xAE010|PUSH|EBX", "0xAE011|PUSH|ESI", "0xAE012|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0xAE014|PUSH|EDI", "0xAE015|MOV|EBX, EDX", "0xAE017|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [ESI + 0x70]", "0xAE01A|MOV|EDI, dword ptr [EAX]", "0xAE01C|MOV|AL, byte ptr [EDI + 0x149]", "0xAE022|TEST|AL, AL", "0xAE024|JNZ|0x6fb7e02c", "0xAE026|POP|EDI", "0xAE027|POP|ESI", "0xAE028|XOR|EAX, EAX", "0xAE02A|POP|EBX", "0xAE02B|RET|"],
      "comment": "Validate item/missile state transitions and update internal flags.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Retrieve state node from pItemNode[0x1c]\n2. Check if state enabled at offset 0x149 in state node; return 0 if disabled\n3. Get current render state via Ordinal_10933 (render context check)\n4. Branch on render state value (0, 1-3, or other):\n   a) If state = 1-3: Check pItemNode[3] slot value\n      - If slot = 0: Set slot to 1, optionally call ProcessSlotDetail if nSkipDetail=0\n      - Call Ordinal_10349 to update visual representation\n      - Load slot value again, check animation flag at [nStateNode + 0xc4 + slot]\n      - Update dwFlags (pItemNode[0x3a]): OR 0x02 if enabled, AND 0xfffffffd if disabled\n   b) If state = 0: Check if pItemNode[3] = 1 or 2 (active slot states)\n      - If not active, return 0\n      - If active: Set slot to 0, optionally call ProcessSlotDetail if nSkipDetail=0\n      - Call Ordinal_10349 to update visual\n      - Load animation flag at [nStateNode + 0xc4 + slot]; update dwFlags accordingly\n5. Call FUN_6fb7e160 to render animation with parameters from state node (offsets 0x120, 0x174-0x176)\n6. Return 1 on successful state transition\n\nParameters:\npItemNode (int *): Pointer to item/unit structure; field offsets: 0x1c=state pointer, 0xc=slot index, 0x3a=flag register\nnSkipDetail (int): 0=process visual detail via ProcessSlotDetail, non-zero=skip detail processing\nIMPLICIT EBX: Register preserved across calls\nIMPLICIT ESI: Register preserved across calls  \nIMPLICIT EDI: Register preserved across calls\n\nReturns:\n1: State transition successful\n0: No state transition (disabled, invalid state, or early exit)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- State node must be non-NULL and properly initialized (checked via byte at +0x149)\n- Slot value ranges 0-2; invalid slots trigger early exit\n- Flag register field 0x3a uses bit 1 (0x02) for animation enabled/disabled state\n- Animation parameters fetched from state node: offset 0x120 = animation index, 0x174-0x176 = frame/timing values\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x1c: Offset to state node pointer in item structure\n0x149: Byte offset in state node for enabled flag check\n0xc: Offset to slot index in item structure\n0x3a: Offset to flag register in item structure\n0xc4: Base offset for animation flag lookup table\n0x120: Base offset for animation index lookup table\n0x174, 0x175, 0x176: Offsets for animation frame/timing parameters\n0x02: Flag bit for animation enabled state (OR to enable, AND 0xfffffffd to disable)",
      "tags": ["PARAM_2", "MOD_UNIT", "SRC_Object.cpp"]
    },
