      "comment": "Creates, updates, or removes light source for a unit (brazier/tiki torch).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract light data pointer from unit at offset 0x88 (0x22 * 4)\n2. If wLightRadius == 0 (disable light):\n   - If light exists, check unit type and log message (0x1d=brazier, 0x25=tiki torch)\n   - Clear audio context reference and return\n3. If wLightRadius > 0 (enable/update light):\n   - If no light exists, create audio context with type 0x2 (light), scaled radius (wLightRadius >> 1), alpha 0xff, RGB color bytes\n   - Store returned light pointer back to unit[0x88]\n   - Return if creation failed\n4. Update existing light radius by calling SetLightRadius with scaled radius (wLightRadius >> 1)\n\nParameters:\npUnit (void *): Unit structure pointer; offset 0x4=unit type, 0x88=light data, 0x120+iType=light radius\nwLightRadius (ushort): Light radius in source units; divided by 2 for SetLightRadius call\nbyColorR (byte): Red component (0-255) for light color\nbyColorG (byte): Green component (0-255) for light color  \nbyColorB (byte): Blue component (0-255) for light color\n\nReturns:\nvoid: No return value; modifies unit light source in place. Sets unit[0x88] to NULL or light pointer, or updates existing light radius.\n\nSpecial Cases:\nUnit type 0x1d (brazier) and 0x25 (tiki torch) trigger logging via Ordinal_10029\nRadius right-shift by 1 converts internal units to display units\nAlpha channel always 0xff (fully opaque)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x88: Offset to light data pointer in unit (0x22 * 4)\n0x4: Offset to unit type field\n0x1d: Brazier unit type ID\n0x25: Tiki torch unit type ID\n0x2: Audio context type ID for light source\n0xff: Full alpha opacity value (255)\n0x1: Radius scale shift amount",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Act", "PARAM_5", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control"]
