      "comment": "Process object subtype and trigger appropriate initialization handlers.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if object has active AI (offset 0x1c5 in room data)\n2. Load object subtype from pUnit[1]\n3. Validate subtype against known ranges:\n   - If 0x95 or 0x98: Require param[3]==1 (specific flag), call FUN_6fb931f0(0xb6,...)\n   - If 0x18d: Fall through to param[3] check\n   - If 0x162, 0x163, 0x164: Valid range, fall through\n   - If 0x195-0x197 or 0x1c7: Valid range, fall through\n   - All others: Return without processing\n4. If object index (pUnit[3]) is 0, call FUN_6fb931f0(0x47,...) with 3 push params\n5. Return\n\nParameters:\npUnit - Pointer to UnitAny structure for object type (dwType==2)\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Subtypes 0x95/0x98 require pUnit[3]==1 to proceed\n- Subtypes outside 0x95-0x98, 0x18d, 0x162-0x164, 0x195-0x197, 0x1c7 are rejected\n- Called only for object types (dwType==2) during InitializeUnit\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x1c5 - Offset to AI active flag in room data\n0xb6 - Handler ID for type A objects (subtypes 0x95/0x98)\n0x47 - Handler ID for type B objects (remaining valid subtypes)\n0x95, 0x98, 0x18d, 0x162-0x164, 0x195-0x197, 0x1c7 - Valid object subtype ranges",
