      "comment": "Cleanup all resources and context for a game unit\n \nAlgorithm:\n1. Clear internal unit state via FUN_6fb90bc0(pUnit)\n2. If render context is initialized (g_hRenderContext != 0):\n   a. Release rendering resources for unit (Ordinal_10352 - Release unit rendering)\n   b. Release graphics context for unit (Ordinal_10386 - Release unit graphics)\n   c. Clear audio references (ClearAudioContextReference)\n3. Query skill data table entry for skill 0xFA (Ordinal_10043 - GetSkillData, magic skill ID 250)\n4. Return void\n\nParameters:\npUnit (void *) - Pointer to game unit structure, contains rendering/audio/graphics context\n  (Note: void* used; specific structure type (UnitAny) not available in this binary)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Skips rendering/graphics cleanup if g_hRenderContext is NULL (0)\n- Unconditionally calls Ordinal_10043 with magic number 0xFA (250 decimal) - purpose unclear\n- Function uses global state g_hRenderContext to check context validity\n- Called from CleanupGameContextAndResources during shutdown sequence\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0xFA (250 decimal): Skill ID passed to Ordinal_10043/GetSkillData, purpose unknown\n- 0x70: Byte offset into unit structure at final call\n\nRelated Functions:\n- FUN_6fb90bc0() - Clear internal unit state\n- ClearAudioContextReference() - Cleanup audio subsystem\n- CleanupGameContextAndResources() - Caller, main cleanup orchestrator",
