      "instructions": ["0xAE610|PUSH|EBX", "0xAE611|PUSH|EBP", "0xAE612|PUSH|ESI", "0xAE613|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0xAE615|PUSH|EDI", "0xAE616|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [ESI + 0x70]", "0xAE619|MOV|EDI, dword ptr [EAX]", "0xAE61B|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [ESI + 0xc]", "0xAE61E|MOV|ECX, dword ptr [EDI + EAX*0x4 + 0xd8]", "0xAE625|CMP|ECX, 0x100", "0xAE62B|JZ|0x6fb7e834", "0xAE631|XOR|EBX, EBX", "0xAE633|MOV|BL, byte ptr [EAX + EDI*0x1 + 0x118]", "0xAE63A|TEST|EBX, EBX", "0xAE63C|JNZ|0x6fb7e7aa"],
      "comment": "Process unit animation slot state transitions and frame advancement.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load unit state base from pUnit->offset_0x1c\n2. Load slot animation length from state[offset_0xd8 + slot_index*4]\n3. If animation length == 0x100, exit (animation complete)\n4. Load animation state byte from state[offset_0x118 + slot_index]\n5. If animation state == 0 (initial):\n   a. Check forced state flag at state[offset_0x14a]\n   b. If forced, call ProcessUnitAnimationState and exit\n   c. Validate pUnit->offset_0x50 >= animation_length - 0x100\n   d. If pUnit->offset_0x4 == 0xbd and slot in {2,3}: increment slot\n   e. If slot == 1: allocate units, set frame from state[0x13b], apply class flags\n   f. Set light parameters from state[0x122, 0x174-0x176]\n   g. Check special animation conditionals at state[0x130-0x131]\n6. Else (animation already started):\n   a. Handle class type 0xc: decrement frame counter\n   b. Handle class type 0xbd with slot 3: similar decrement\n   c. Other types: advance frame with modulo wrapping\n7. Call animation callback from g_ppAnimationCallbacks[state[0x1c4]]\n8. Validate callback index <= 0x12, else assertion error\n\nParameters:\npUnit: Unit animation control structure pointer (dword array)\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Animation length 0x100 indicates end state, skips processing\n- Callback dispatch via function pointer table indexed by class type byte\n- Slot 1 triggers unit allocation and special class setup\n- Frame calculation handles wrapping for cyclic animations\n- Callback index >0x12 causes fatal assertion",
