      "comment": "Activates a shrine effect on the given unit by executing two associated actions.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load shrine index from byte pointer parameter\n2. Validate shrine index against shrine count limit (0x6fbd042c)\n3. If index >= limit, trigger fatal error (Ordinal_10023) with shrine code location and line 0x35c\n4. Calculate offset into shrine effect tables using formula: (index * 0x14)\n5. Check first effect table (g_pShrineEffectTable1 + offset) for valid entry (-1 = empty)\n6. If valid, apply first effect via FUN_6fb93500, then conditionally execute FUN_6fb931f0 if param_1[3] == 0\n7. Check second effect table (g_pShrineEffectTable2 + offset) for valid entry (-1 = empty)\n8. If valid, apply second effect via FUN_6fb93500, then conditionally execute FUN_6fb931f0 if param_1[3] == 0\n9. Return void\n\nParameters:\npUnitAny (int *) - Pointer to target unit structure with field at offset 3 (condition flag)\npbShrineIndex (byte *) - Pointer to byte containing shrine index (0-based)\n\nReturns:\nvoid (no return value, may trigger fatal error via Ordinal_10023 if index out of bounds)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Invalid shrine index (>= shrine count) causes fatal error\n- Effects are skipped if corresponding table entry is -1\n- Both effects require pUnitAny[3] == 0 to execute secondary handler (FUN_6fb931f0)\n- Magic number 0x14 is fixed offset stride (20 bytes per shrine effect entry)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x14 - Shrine effect entry stride (20 bytes)\n0x35c - Line number in shrine source code (858 decimal)\n-0x1 - Empty shrine effect table entry marker\n0xc - Offset of condition flag field in unit structure (param_1[3] = param_1 + 0xc)",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Inventory", "PARAM_2", "PROP_NOCALLER", "MOD_UNIT", "SRC_Object.cpp", "STRUCT_Other"]
