      "instructions": ["0xAEDD0|PUSH|ESI", "0xAEDD1|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0xAEDD3|XOR|ECX, ECX", "0xAEDD5|PUSH|EDI", "0xAEDD6|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [ESI + 0x70]", "0xAEDD9|MOV|CL, byte ptr [EAX + 0x4]", "0xAEDDC|PUSH|ECX", "0xAEDDD|CALL|0x6fb9901c", "0xAEDE2|PUSH|EAX", "0xAEDE3|PUSH|ESI", "0xAEDE4|CALL|0x6fb99016", "0xAEDE9|PUSH|ESI", "0xAEDEA|CALL|0x6fb99010", "0xAEDEF|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0xAEDF1|JNZ|0x6fb7ee11"],
      "comment": "Executes the shrine ability handler associated with a shrine code.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract shrine code from unit at offset 0x70 + 4\n2. Call Ordinal_10624 to normalize/retrieve shrine code value\n3. Call Ordinal_10396 to trigger shrine effect processing\n4. Retrieve pointer to shrine code via Ordinal_10395\n5. Validate shrine code is not NULL (must be non-zero)\n6. Validate shrine code is less than g_dwMaxShrineCode (bounds check)\n7. Index into g_aaShrineHandlers function pointer table using shrine code\n8. If handler exists, invoke it via function pointer\n\nParameters:\nnPUnit (int) - Unit entity containing shrine data at offset 0x70\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value. Function will abort via FUN_6fb9a10f(-1) on error.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- NULL code pointer triggers abort with error line 0x39a\n- Code >= g_dwMaxShrineCode triggers abort with error line 0x39b\n- Missing function pointer is silently ignored (NULL check before call)",
