      "api_calls": ["LogPoolWarning", "IsMonsterFlagBit0Set", "OBJECTS_GetDataField08", "GetObjectDataEntryOffset", "OBJECTS_GetDataField08", "FogAssert", "FogAssert", "SetUnitAnimationMode", "ClearUnitMapCellFlags", "InitializeUnitAnimation", "...+4 more"],
      "instructions": ["0xAEE60|PUSH|EBX", "0xAEE61|PUSH|EBP", "0xAEE62|PUSH|ESI", "0xAEE63|CMP|ECX, 0x3", "0xAEE66|PUSH|EDI", "0xAEE67|MOV|ESI, EDX", "0xAEE69|JZ|0x6fb7ef74", "0xAEE6F|CMP|ECX, 0x15", "0xAEE72|JZ|0x6fb7ee92", "0xAEE74|PUSH|0x3bc", "0xAEE79|PUSH|0x6fbd047c", "0xAEE7E|PUSH|0x6fbae7f4", "0xAEE83|CALL|0x6fb99af8", "0xAEE88|ADD|ESP, 0xc", "0xAEE8B|POP|EDI"],
      "comment": "Process shrine/skill activation effect for unit based on action type.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check nShrineAction = 3 (Place Item)\n   a. Load unit data pointer from pUnit->unitData (offset 0x70)\n   b. Check if unit has been processed (unitData[0x14a] == 0)\n   c. If unprocessed:\n      - Set shrine slot with pGameData[1]\n      - Update unit's animation/state\n      - Validate class-specific shrine compatibility (classes 0x162, 0x163, 0x18d, 0x195, 0x197, 0x196, 0x164)\n      - Initialize enchantment if applicable\n      - Update buff flags (0x2, 0x100000)\n      - Update light source\n   d. If processed: call FUN_6fb7f130 to handle alternate path\n2. Check nShrineAction = 0x15 (Receive/Deactivate)\n   a. Get current shrine code from Ordinal_10393/Ordinal_10395\n   b. Find unit in game hash table by ID\n   c. Look up shrine deactivation handler in g_ppShrineCodeTableReceive\n   d. Execute handler if exists\n   e. Get new shrine code\n   f. Validate code range against g_dwShrineMaxType\n   g. Look up action handler in g_ppShrineCodeTableAction\n   h. Execute action handler if exists (for complex shrine types)\n3. Other nShrineAction: Assert failure with debug output\n\nParameters:\n- nShrineAction: int in ECX - 3 (Place) or 0x15 (Receive), others fail\n- pUnit: UnitAny * in EDX - Unit receiving shrine effect\n- pGameData: uint * on stack - [0] = game context, [1] = shrine parameters\n\nReturns:\n- byte *: Shrine data pointer or NULL on failure/assertion\n- Implicit: Assert on unrecognized nShrineAction\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Shrine must be valid code (0 <= code < g_dwShrineMaxType)\n- Class compatibility validation (0x162-0x197 range)\n- Enchantment initialization conditional on flag at unitData[0x1c5]\n- Buff flag manipulation: 0x2 (set/clear based on state), 0x100000 (set conditionally)\n- Light source update uses color values from unitData offsets 0x174-0x176\n- Error paths call assertion function FUN_6fb9a10f with 0xffffffff\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n- 0x3: Place/Apply action type\n- 0x15: Receive/Deactivate action type\n- 0x70: Offset to pUnitData in UnitAny structure\n- 0x14a: Unit processed flag offset in unitData\n- 0x1c5: Enchantment valid flag offset\n- 0x162-0x197: Valid class IDs for shrine compatibility check\n- 0xc4, 0x130, 0x141, 0x128: Feature flag offsets in unitData\n- 0x174-0x176: RGB color value offsets for light source\n- 0x120: Intensity/brightness parameter offset\n- 0x39a, 0x39b: Assertion line numbers in source\n- 0x372, 0x373: Assertion line numbers for receive path\n- 0x3bc: Assertion line number for invalid action\n- 0x2: Buff flag (0x2 = enabled state)\n- 0x100000: Special effect flag\n- 0xfffffffd: Mask to clear 0x2 flag\n- 0xffffffdf: Mask to clear 0x20 flag\n- 0x14: Array element size in function pointer tables",
      "tags": ["PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PARAM_3", "MOD_UNIT", "SRC_Object.cpp", "STRUCT_Other", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control"]
