      "comment": "Process unit animation state machine with timing and slot management.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get unit animation state index from pUnitAny->state field (offset 0x1c4)\n2. Validate state index is not greater than 0x12 (assertion check)\n3. Test state value for validity (JZ if zero, default return case)\n4. Setup ECX register and mask state value for switch table dispatch\n5. Dispatch to state handler via jump table (0x6fbd0430 base address)\n6. For each state 2-0x12: execute specific animation/timing logic\n7. State cases handle: idle animation, spell effects, cooldown phases\n8. Use GetTickCount() for time-based state transitions\n9. Call ordinal functions for slot data and state modifications\n10. Return combined result with low byte status and alignment masking\n\nParameters:\npUnitAny - Pointer to unit structure, contains animation state at offset 0x1c4\n\nReturns:\nuint - State machine result (CONCAT31 format with low byte status)\n\nSpecial Cases:\nState > 0x12 triggers assertion failure and program termination via FUN_6fb9a10f",
      "tags": ["MOD_UNIT", "SRC_Object.cpp", "PARAM_1", "STRUCT_Other"]
