      "comment": "Transfer unit class attributes from source handle to target unit.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate input: If nUnitClassHandle is NULL, log error and exit process\n2. Extract unit ID from input handle [offset +0x3] and lookup unit in global hash table\n3. Validate unit class: Ensure found unit has class 0x3b or 0x3c; if not, log error and exit\n4. Copy class attribute: Transfer byte from handle [+0x2] to unit field [pUnit[28]+0x4]\n5. Build flags: Call Ordinal_10427 to get current flags, OR with bits from handle [+0x1]\n   - If bit 0x02 set in handle, OR result with 0x02\n   - If bit 0x01 set in handle, OR result with 0x01\n6. Set modified flags: Call Ordinal_10428(pUnit, bFlags) to apply flags\n\nParameters:\nnUnitClassHandle (int): Handle/pointer to class attribute structure containing:\n  [+0x1]: Flag field (bits 0x01, 0x02 for flag transfer)\n  [+0x2]: Class attribute byte to transfer\n  [+0x3]: Unit ID to lookup in hash table\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- NULL input handle triggers fatal error (exit process)\n- Invalid unit class (not 0x3b/0x3c) triggers fatal error\n- No return path on error conditions (calls FUN_6fb9a10f exit)\n- Function uses 1 stack-allocated temporary optimized away (local_4)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x03: Offset in handle to unit ID\n0x02: Offset in handle to attribute byte / flag bit 0x02\n0x01: Offset in handle to flag field / flag bit 0x01\n0x3b: Valid unit class ID 1 (priest)\n0x3c: Valid unit class ID 2 (sorceress)\n0x1c: Array index in unit structure (offset 0x70 for flags pointer)\n0x04: Offset within flags structure to set attribute\n0x576, 0x579, 0x57c, 0x57e: Error line numbers for assertions\n\nStructure Layout:\nInput Handle Structure:\nOffset | Size | Field       | Type  | Description\n0x00   | 1    | [reserved]  | byte  | unused\n0x01   | 1    | bFlagField  | byte  | contains bits 0x01 and 0x02 for flag transfer\n0x02   | 1    | bAttribute  | byte  | class attribute to transfer\n0x03   | 1    | nUnitId     | dword | unit ID to lookup in hash table",
      "tags": ["MOD_UNIT", "SRC_Object.cpp", "PARAM_1", "STRUCT_Other", "NET_SCMD"]
