      "comment": "Apply data payload to a game object's fields based on structure offset.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load pointer from unit field at offset +0x70\n2. Add offset 0x28 to the loaded pointer (calculated field offset)\n3. Push parameter 0x10 onto stack (data size/type parameter)\n4. Call Ordinal_501 (likely D2Common.SetUnitFields) with calculated address\n5. Return from function\n\nParameters:\npUnit (int *) - IMPLICIT in ECX, pointer to game unit structure\npbDataPayload (byte *) - IMPLICIT in EDX, pointer to data payload buffer containing values to apply\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value, modifies unit structure in-place\n\nSpecial Cases:\nMagic value 0x70 offset appears to be a table/object reference pointer\nMagic value 0x28 offset into pointed structure indicates field block location\nMagic value 0x10 suggests 16-byte data block being applied\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x70 (112) - Offset to object reference table/pointer within unit structure\n0x28 (40) - Offset within referenced object to target field block\n0x10 (16) - Size parameter for data operation",
