      "instructions": ["0xAFCE0|SUB|ESP, 0x8", "0xAFCE3|PUSH|ESI", "0xAFCE4|PUSH|EDI", "0xAFCE5|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0xAFCE7|CALL|0x6fb782b0", "0xAFCEC|MOV|ECX, ESI", "0xAFCEE|CALL|0x6fb90bc0", "0xAFCF3|MOV|EAX, [0x6fbe9284]", "0xAFCF8|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0xAFCFA|JZ|0x6fb7fd08", "0xAFCFC|PUSH|ESI", "0xAFCFD|CALL|0x6fb98e90", "0xAFD02|PUSH|ESI", "0xAFD03|CALL|0x6fb98c86", "0xAFD08|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [ESI + 0x38]"],
      "comment": "Clear unit data and inventory, with special handling for active game context.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Clear the active/current slot reference\n2. Clear unit-specific rendering resources\n3. If render context exists (g_hRenderContext != 0):\n   a. Call Ordinal_10228(pUnit) - Clear render surface textures\n   b. Call Ordinal_10386(pUnit) - Clear render viewport data\n4. Release unit event listener - Ordinal_10156(0, pUnit[0xe])\n5. Remove all items from unit inventory - EnumerateAndRemoveItemsFromUnit\n6. Get unit skill/ability pointer at offset 0x84\n7. Call Ordinal_10241(pUnit[0x84]) - Clear ability pointer\n8. Set pUnit[0x84] to 0 to clear reference\n9. Call Ordinal_10527(pUnit) - Clear skill effects\n10. Call Ordinal_10960(pUnit) - Clear cooldowns/buffs\n11. Clear unit audio context reference\n12. Get game context via GetGameContext()\n13. If unit is current game context unit (pUnit == GetGameContext()):\n    a. Call InitializeGameContextAndState(NULL) to reset game context\n14. Call Ordinal_10421(0, pUnit) - Release unit-specific game context associations\n15. If valid game context exists and has active units:\n    a. Call Ordinal_10035(dwSlotCount, &pdwSlotArray, &dwSlotArrayCount) to get unit slots\n    b. Initialize loop counter dwSlotIndex = 0\n    c. Iterate for each slot (dwSlotIndex < dwSlotArrayCount):\n       i. Load unit from slot: *(pdwSlotArray[dwSlotIndex] + 0x2c)\n       ii. Walk unit linked list via offset 0x10c (next pointer):\n           - For each unit pCurrentUnit in list:\n             * Check unit type (offset 0) == 1\n             * Call Ordinal_10487(pCurrentUnit, 0x3f) to check special flag\n             * If flag set (result != 0):\n               - Call FUN_6fb936b0(pCurrentUnit) for special unit cleanup\n             * Advance to next unit via pCurrentUnit[0x10c]\n\nParameters:\n  UnitAny * pUnit - pointer to unit structure to clear\n\nReturns:\n  void - no return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If pUnit is the current game context unit, context is reset to NULL\n  - Processes only type 1 units with flag 0x3f set in inventory walk\n  - Empty inventory is valid condition (dwSlotArrayCount == 0, skips walk)\n  - Null render context skips rendering cleanup (g_hRenderContext check)\n  - Null game context skips inventory cleanup (pvVar2 != NULL check)\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x0e - unit event index offset in UnitAny\n  0x21 - unit skill/ability pointer offset in UnitAny (historical reference point)\n  0x38 - alternate unit event index offset used in assembly\n  0x84 - unit skill cooldown/ability data offset\n  0x2c - first item in unit inventory/slot linked list offset\n  0x3f - special flag value checked for each unit (type 1 only)\n  0x43 - next unit pointer in linked list offset (used in inner loop)\n  0x10c - unit chain next pointer offset",
