      "comment": "Processes state changes and skill effects for a game unit entity.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize return status to 0 and cache unit's animation state\n2. If unit class type (index 3) is 1 (Player):\n   a. Call GetPlayerState to determine if unit state changed\n   b. If state changed, retrieve skill IDs from ordinal functions\n   c. If unit is current player, call ProcessSkillEffect for animation update\n   d. Call ProcessPlayerUpdate for housekeeping\n3. If unit class type is 2 (Monster):\n   a. Retrieve monster state from ordinal\n   b. If monster state is valid:\n      i. Get monster flags using Ordinal_10985\n      ii. Check if \"attack enabled\" flag (bit 0) is set\n      iii. If flag clear, set \"skip attack\" flag (bit 1) and process skill effect\n      iv. If state valid and current player, update skill from ordinal calls\n   c. Check character state (byte at offset 0x5c): if 1/2/3 and not \"frozen\" flag (0x40), process skill effect\n4. Execute switch statement on unit class type (offset 0xc * 0xc + table 0x6fbd0664):\n   a. Case 0 or type 2 with invalid state: Call ResetAnimation\n   b. Case 1 with valid state or type 2 with valid state: Set animation frame = 0x100\n   c. Case 2 with valid state: Set animation frame = animation_max - 0x100\n   d. Case 3: Set animation frame = 0x100, clear animation subsection\n5. If unit class type is 0x12 with \"special_ability\" flag (0x4000):\n   a. Call SpecialAbilityProcessor for custom processing\n6. Check unit class action state (offset 0xc * 0xc + table 0x6fbd0668):\n   a. If state == 1 or (state >= 2 and state <= 3):\n      i. Retrieve animation state and set nReturnStatus = animation_state\n7. If nReturnStatus != 0:\n   a. If unit type is 0x13 (Pet):\n      i. Clear 7-uint coordinate array\n      ii. Retrieve and cache pet attachment coordinates\n      iii. Call GetPetAnimationId and GetPetSoundId\n      iv. Call PlayPetAnimation with animation parameters\n   b. Else if unit has \"no_animate\" flag (offset 0x20):\n      i. Call PlayAnimation with type 7 (default animation)\n   c. Else: Set \"pending_animation\" flag at offset 0x1c\n8. Check unit rotation/orientation (Ordinal_10355 result):\n   a. If non-zero, clear rotation lock with Ordinal_10356\n   b. If unit is current player and rotation valid:\n      i. Get rotation controller state from Ordinal_10057\n      ii. Combine with GetPlayerAnimState using OR operation\n      iii. Get current player ID and call UpdateAnimationState\n      iv. Check if rotation controller is \"moving\" using Ordinal_10082\n      v. Update g_hRenderContext based on controller state\n      vi. Call SetCurrentUnitId with controller owner\n      vii. Call InitializeUnitSpecialFeature for controller setup\n9. Synchronize unit animation state using Ordinal_10193 (animation sync function)\n10. If unit type is 3 (Mercenary) and unit is current player:\n    a. Call CheckMercenaryAbility with parameter 0x0a\n    b. If ability check fails (returns 0):\n       i. Clear 7-uint coordinate array\n       ii. Retrieve mercenary position from FUN_6fb63760\n       iii. Retrieve position source (base position vs. skill position)\n       iv. Set coordinate array based on source check\n       v. Call PlayMercenaryAnimation with appropriate coordinates\n11. Check for state chart callbacks using Ordinal_10502:\n    a. If callbacks registered, execute ProcessStateChartCallbacks\n12. If unit type is 1 (Player) or 5 (Hired):\n    a. Retrieve player ID from Ordinal_10326\n    b. Retrieve player skill from Ordinal_10329\n    c. If player has valid skill (Ordinal_10342):\n       i. Call GetPlayerLevel to retrieve player level\n       ii. Call CheckSkillCast with magic parameter 0xc01\n       iii. If skill cast check succeeds (returns non-zero):\n           - Call GetPlayerTarget for current target\n           - Call ApplySkillEffect with target and magic parameter\n           - Call UpdatePlayerAnimation with current coordinates\n\nParameters:\npUnit: UnitAny * - Pointer to unit entity structure; contains all unit attributes including class type, state, animation data, and skill information\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value; function modifies unit state in-place\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0xc: Offset of unit class type (used with table lookups)\n0xc * 0xc: Scaling factor for class type lookup in global tables\n0x6fbd0660: Base address of unit state table (states 1-2 for player/monster)\n0x6fbd0664: Base address of unit animation type table (cases 0-3)\n0x6fbd0668: Base address of unit action state table\n0x6fbd0660 + offset: Lookup format [class_id] = state_value\n0x38: Offset of unit animation ID field\n0x14: Offset of animation frame offset field (L)\n0x15: Offset of maximum animation frame field\n0x16: Offset of animation subsection field\n0x5c: Offset of character state field (1=walk, 2=neutral, 3=attack)\n0xe8: Offset of flags field (0x40=frozen, 0x4000=special_ability)\n0x20: Offset of \"no_animate\" flag\n0x1c: Offset of \"pending_animation\" flag\n0x100: Animation frame offset constant\n0x0a: Mercenary ability ID constant\n0xc01: Magic skill parameter constant\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- SSA temporaries (bVar3, cVar1, sVar4, uVar6, uVar7, uVar8, uVar9, uVar11, uVar12, iVar10, iVar13, extraout_var, extraout_var_00, pVar2, puVar5, pUVar14) are compiler-generated SSA form variables that represent intermediate calculation results optimized by the decompiler. These cannot be renamed as they exist only in the decompiled representation, not in the actual code. In assembly, their values reside in registers (EAX, EBX, EDI, EBP, EDX, ESI, etc.) and are reused across different logical operations. To understand their purpose, examine the decompiled code context where they appear.\n- Stack array at [ESP+0x20] used for coordinate storage during animation setup\n- Multiple conditional branches create complex state machine; refer to decompiled code for exact conditions\n- Unit type 0x12 requires special ability processing\n- Unit