      "comment": "PlayStatusSound - Play a sound effect based on unit status\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Assert unit pointer (param_1) is non-NULL - otherwise log assertion and exit\n2. Assert sound ID output pointer (param_2) is non-NULL - otherwise log assertion and exit\n3. Get the current game context via GetGameContext()\n4. Check if param_1 matches the active game context\n5. If context matches:\n   - Get status code via Ordinal_10964(param_1, *param_2)\n   - Get context data via Ordinal_10966()\n   - Check if status in valid range (0 < status <= 2 or status == 4) AND context->offset_0x94 != 0\n   - If condition met: get alternative sound via Ordinal_10949(-1), update *param_2, re-fetch status\n   - Check final status: if not in {5, 0} proceed to sound play\n   - Verify status doesn't exceed g_dwMaxSoundStatus threshold\n   - Lookup sound ID in g_aSndsoundIdByStatus[status]\n   - If sound ID non-zero, play via FUN_6fb88d60(param_1, sound_data)\n   - Return 0 on success\n6. Return 1 if context mismatch or status excluded\n\nParameters:\n  param_1 (int/void*) - Unit pointer to play sound for\n  param_2 (undefined4*) - Pointer to sound ID value\n\nReturns:\n  0 if sound was played\n  1 if sound was skipped (context mismatch or status excluded)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Function uses 3 XMM-spilled stack temporaries optimized away in decompilation\n  - NULL param_1 triggers assertion and exit\n  - NULL param_2 triggers assertion and exit\n  - Status code validated against array bounds before access\n  - Generic void* parameter type used; actual structure type unknown",
