      "comment": "Validates skill handle and target unit handle, computing skill level difference.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get game context via GetGameContext; assert not NULL\n2. Assert dwTargetUnitId is non-zero (target unit must exist)\n3. Assert dwSkillId is non-zero (skill must be valid)\n4. Initialize pnSkillLevelDiff to 0\n5. Get skill's file handle via GetFileHandle(pGameContext, dwSkillId, 1)\n6. Get skill type/class code via GetSkillData(dwSkillId)\n7. Get skill level from intersection via GetNextInventoryItem(dwSkillType, dwSkillFileHandle)\n8. Compute level difference: ((nLevel + (nLevel >> 0x1f & 3)) >> 2) - 2\n9. Store result in *pnSkillLevelDiff\n10. Get target unit's level via GetMonsterData(pGameContext, dwTargetUnitId)\n11. Store target level in *pnTargetLevel\n12. Return whether nTargetLevel <= *pnSkillLevelDiff (skill level sufficient for target)\n\nParameters:\ndwSkillId (uint): Skill handle/ID to validate\ndwTargetUnitId (uint): Target unit handle to check against\npnSkillLevelDiff (uint *): Output - computed skill level difference from target\npnTargetLevel (uint *): Output - target unit's level\n\nReturns:\nbool: true if skill level difference is <= target level (condition: SETLE), false otherwise\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Assertion failures (NULL game context, zero handles) call FUN_6fb9a10f(-1) which terminates\n- Magic constant 2 subtracted from computed difference (skill level adjustment)\n- Division by 4 with sign extension (CDQ + AND for proper arithmetic shift on negative values)",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Inventory", "UI_SKILLS", "MOD_UNIT", "PARAM_4", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData", "SRC_Player.cpp"]
