      "instructions": ["0xB0950|SUB|ESP, 0x28", "0xB0953|PUSH|EBX", "0xB0954|PUSH|ESI", "0xB0955|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0xB0957|PUSH|EDI", "0xB0958|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0xc], EDX", "0xB095C|MOV|ECX, 0x9", "0xB0961|CALL|0x6fb5d340", "0xB0966|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0xB0968|JZ|0x6fb80975", "0xB096A|POP|EDI", "0xB096B|POP|ESI", "0xB096C|XOR|EAX, EAX", "0xB096E|POP|EBX", "0xB096F|ADD|ESP, 0x28"],
      "comment": "Process UI interaction command for game unit/resource selection.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate game state: Check if UI resource context is active (dwUIFlags checks)\n2. Prevent recursive calls: Return if DAT_6fbff60c is already set\n3. Transform screen coordinates: Convert dwActionType, nScreenX, nScreenY via TransformScreenCoordinates\n4. Initialize UI state array: Zero-fill dwUIFlags region (8 dwords)\n5. Retrieve context: Get pGameContext and pdwResourceHandle pointers\n6. Adjust coordinates: If resource type is 2 or 4, recalculate nOffsetX/nOffsetY via ordinals\n7. Set conditional flags: If dwFlags & 0x08 and Ordinal_10519 returns non-zero, set dwUIFlags |= 0x40\n8. Set flag bits: If dwFlags & 0x04, set dwUIFlags |= 0x20\n9. Process action by type (dwActionType):\n   - 0: Unit selection - validate, set dwUIFlags |= 0x05, call FUN_6fb81e90, validate properties\n   - 1: Property check - validate, set dwUIFlags |= 0x09, call FUN_6fb81e90, check mercenary position\n   - 2: Resource search - set dwUIFlags |= 0x11, search units, update linked list\n   - 3: Data fetch type 1 - set dwUIFlags |= 0x06, fetch via ordinals, load from offset 0x90\n   - 4: Data fetch type 2 - set dwUIFlags |= 0x0A, fetch via ordinals, load from offset 0x90\n   - 5: Clear selection - set dwUIFlags |= 0x12, call FUN_6fb81f00\n   - default: Continue to final handler\n10. If data is type 1 and flag 0x40 not set, set dwUIFlags |= 0x80\n11. Call final UI handler FUN_6fb80e00 with dwUIFlags\n\nParameters:\n- dwActionType (IMPLICIT ECX): Action command (0-5 switch cases, 6+ default)\n- nScreenX (IMPLICIT EDX): Base X coordinate for interaction\n- nScreenY (Stack +0x4): Base Y coordinate for interaction\n- dwFlags (Stack +0x8): Modifier flags (0x04=Property, 0x08=Context check, 0x80=???, etc)\n\nReturns:\n- 0: Action failed or early exit (bad resource, UI busy, property invalid)\n- 1: Action processed successfully or default case reached\n- Other: Return value from FUN_6fb81f00 (action type 5 only)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x04: dwFlags property modifier bit\n- 0x08: dwFlags context check bit\n- 0x0A: dwUIFlags for action type 4 (0x02 | 0x08)\n- 0x05: dwUIFlags for action type 0 (0x01 | 0x04)\n- 0x09: dwUIFlags for action type 1 (0x01 | 0x08)\n- 0x06: dwUIFlags for action type 3 (0x02 | 0x04)\n- 0x11: dwUIFlags for action type 2 (0x01 | 0x10)\n- 0x12: dwUIFlags for action type 5 (0x02 | 0x10)\n- 0x20: dwUIFlags property flag (from dwFlags & 0x04)\n- 0x40: dwUIFlags context flag (set if Ordinal_10519 succeeds)\n- 0x80: dwUIFlags data type 1 marker\n- 0x43: Stat ID for mercenary check\n- 100: Divisor for stat calculation\n- 0x90: Offset in fetched structure for data extraction",
