      "comment": "Update AI positioning data for mercenary slots in the game world.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract UnitAny pointer from mercenary slot structure (offset +4)\n2. Check if unit type is not 0 (PLAYER) - exit if not player type\n3. Call GetMercenaryPosition to validate position is NULL (no existing position)\n4. Extract unit ID from UnitAny (offset +0xc) to determine mercenary class\n5. Map unit ID to slot type: ID 2→slot 1, ID 3→slot 3, ID 6→slot 1\n6. Extract memory pool pointer from UnitAny (offset +0x38)\n7. Call Ordinal_10170 (Storm.dll) to initialize positioning context\n8. Call Ordinal_10142 (D2Common) to prepare AI slot, check return code\n9. If initialization successful, retrieve coordinates:\n   - Call Ordinal_10177 to get Y coordinate\n   - Call Ordinal_10178 to get X coordinate\n10. Call FUN_6fb86120 to apply slot type, unit pointer, and coordinates to AI state\n\nParameters:\npMercSlot (UnitAny *): Pointer to mercenary slot/player unit structure containing unit data at +4, position check at +0xc (unit ID), memory pool at +0x38\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Updates AI positioning system as side effect; validation failures cause early return\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x4: Offset to unit pointer in slot structure\n0xc: Offset to unit ID field (determines mercenary class)\n0x10, 0x14: Coordinate offsets (X, Y) passed to positioning functions\n0x38: Offset to memory pool pointer in UnitAny\n0x2, 0x3, 0x6: Unit ID constants (mercenary unit type identifiers)\n1, 3: Slot type constants for positioning\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Non-player units (dwUnitType != 0) cause immediate return\n- Missing mercenary position (NULL return) causes immediate return\n- Unknown unit IDs (not 2, 3, 6) cause immediate return\n- Failed AI initialization (Ordinal_10142 returns 0) skips coordinate application",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Inventory", "PARAM_1", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control"]
    },
