      "api_calls": ["CheckMissileEntityState", "SKILLS_GetSkillId", "UNITS_GetRoom", "ValidateEntityDrlgSubType", "CheckMissileEntityState", "SKILLS_GetSkillId", "FogAssert", "UNITS_GetOwnerGuid", "UNITS_GetUnitY", "SetPositionCoords", "...+29 more"],
      "instructions": ["0xB0E00|SUB|ESP, 0x28", "0xB0E03|PUSH|EBX", "0xB0E04|PUSH|EBP", "0xB0E05|PUSH|ESI", "0xB0E06|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0xB0E08|PUSH|EDI", "0xB0E09|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [ESI + 0x1c]", "0xB0E0C|MOV|ECX, dword ptr [ESI + 0x4]", "0xB0E0F|PUSH|EAX", "0xB0E10|PUSH|ECX", "0xB0E11|CALL|0x6fb9908e", "0xB0E16|MOV|ECX, dword ptr [ESI + 0x1c]", "0xB0E19|TEST|ECX, ECX", "0xB0E1B|JZ|0x6fb80e6e", "0xB0E1D|TEST|byte ptr [ESI], 0x2"],
      "comment": "Process mouse/game interaction command on target unit or interactive object.\nCalled from: ProcessUIInteractionCommand.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate source unit skill state (Ordinal_11016: GetSkillState)\n2. If target exists, check player stat via Ordinal_10082 (IsDataCompressed)\n3. If stat blocked, return early (invalid skill state)\n4. Set action mode flags: params[5-6] = (1,2) if flag 0x40 clear, else (3,4)\n5. Process unit state transitions (handle resurrect if unit[0x20]==0x13)\n6. Exit if no target action (params[7]==0)\n7. Compute targeting mode: bit 5 of params[0]; override if 0x2 & params[0] && params[2]==0\n8. Call FindTargetUnit with computed mode, store result in params[2]\n9. Send frame-based updates: if game_frame_counter==6, call SendResourceUpdate\n10. Distance check: clamp delta_x, delta_y to 0x100 each\n11. For interactive objects (unit[0x3a] & 0x4): validate range via object[0x17e]\n12. Update interaction frame counter (g_dwLastInteractionFrame)\n13. Apply movement adjustments via coordinate conversion (FUN_6fb816d0)\n14. Send unit action packet and play audio\n15. Return based on validation\n\nParameters:\n  pCommand (dword*) - Command state array\n    [0] = flag bits (0x2=skill, 0x4=physical, 0x8=move, 0x10=spell, 0x20=melee, 0x40=defensive)\n    [1] = source unit pointer (player/npc)\n    [2] = target unit pointer (may be 0)\n    [3] = target X coordinate\n    [4] = target Y coordinate\n    [5-6] = action IDs (set by algorithm step 4)\n    [7] = action type/classification\n    [24-28] = temporary coordinate storage\n\nReturns:\n  void - Modifies pCommand in place, updates coordinates and action state\n  Early returns on: invalid skill, no target, distance limit, animation override\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Unit type 0: Player - requires valid stat check\n  - Unit type 1: Superunique/Boss - limited action validation\n  - Unit type 2-5: Monster/NPC/Summon - type-specific handlers\n  - Type 0x13: Resurrect action - triggers unit state change\n  - Flag 0x40: Defensive mode reverses action priorities\n  - Flag 0x20: Melee range - skips distance validation\n  - Object interactions: validate class via object[0x17e] range field\n  - Phantom variables: lVar12 (longlong from __ftol conversion)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x0e9 - UI state byte offset (skill ready flag)\n  0x0ec - UI validation offset\n  0x20 - Unit type change flag (resurrection context)\n  0x24 - Unit ID field offset\n  0x28 - Unit class field offset\n  0x3a - Unit flags word (bit 4=interactive object)\n  0x100 - Pixel distance limit\n  0x17e - Object class/max-range field\n  0x804 - Skill validation constant\n  0x1f - Unit state validation offset\n  0x38 - Unit metadata offset\n  0x2b, 0x5a - Special spell action codes\n  0x3b - Object type classification threshold\n  0x66 - Game context resource ID\n  0x276, 0x3f9, 0x3fb - Assertion line numbers\n  0x6fbff608 - Global last interaction frame cache (update throttle)",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "MOD_UNIT", "STRUCT_Room2", "STRUCT_Room1", "STRUCT_ItemData", "PARAM_1", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData", "SRC_Player.cpp", "PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Path", "UI_SKILLS", "STRUCT_ObjectData", "STRUCT_Skill", "STRUCT_Other"]
