      "comment": "Draw unit status frame with appropriate visual elements based on unit flags and frame type.\n\nNote: Function uses 4 stack-allocated temporaries optimized away (visible only as register reuse in assembly).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get maximum viewport Y and current viewport scroll offset\n2. Validate viewport state - return if viewport exceeds maximum Y\n3. Check frame type parameter:\n   - If nFrameType == 1: Use status frame mode (flags 0x01, 0x02 check different offsets in pUnit[2])\n   - If nFrameType == 0: Use alternative mode (flags use pUnit[3], pUnit[4] offsets)\n4. Extract unit flags from pUnit[0] for visual rendering decisions\n5. Based on flag combinations, determine which frame index (0x05-0x11) to render:\n   - Flag 0x01 set: Render life/status frame (index 5-10 based on flag 0x08, 0x20)\n   - Flag 0x02 set: Render secondary status frame (index 0x0c-0x11 based on flag 0x08, 0x20)\n6. Call FUN_6fb86120 with determined frame index and coordinate data\n7. Return after processing all applicable flags\n\nParameters:\npUnit (ECX): Pointer to unit structure containing flags and frame offsets\n- pUnit[0]: Unit flags (0x01=render_life, 0x02=render_status, 0x08=alt_mode, 0x20=special_mode)\n- pUnit[1]: Pointer to frame data structure\n- pUnit[2]: Frame coordinate/offset Y value (when nFrameType==1)\n- pUnit[3]: Frame coordinate/offset X value\n- pUnit[4]: Frame coordinate/offset X value (when nFrameType==0)\nnFrameType (EDX): Frame rendering mode (0=alternate, 1=status)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If viewport scroll exceeds maximum Y, function returns immediately without rendering\n- Different flag combinations yield different frame indices even for same flag\n- Both flag 0x01 and 0x02 may trigger, resulting in multiple FUN_6fb86120 calls\n- Frame index values: 0x05=alt_life_primary, 0x06=status_life_0x20clear_0x08clear, 0x07=status_life_0x20set_0x08clear, 0x08=alt_life_0x08set, 0x09=status_life_0x20clear_0x08set, 0x0a=status_life_0x20set_0x08set, 0x0c-0x11=secondary_status_variants",
