      "instructions": ["0xB16D0|SUB|ESP, 0x8", "0xB16D3|LEA|EAX, [ESP]", "0xB16D7|PUSH|ESI", "0xB16D8|PUSH|EDI", "0xB16D9|MOV|ESI, EDX", "0xB16DB|MOV|EDI, ECX", "0xB16DD|PUSH|EAX", "0xB16DE|CALL|0x6fb62880", "0xB16E3|PUSH|EAX", "0xB16E4|CALL|0x6fb982ea", "0xB16E9|PUSH|ESI", "0xB16EA|PUSH|EDI", "0xB16EB|CALL|0x6fb982ea", "0xB16F0|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [ESI]", "0xB16F2|MOV|ECX, dword ptr [ESP + 0x8]"],
      "comment": "Clamp two coordinate values to their respective maximum bounds.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get game context and retrieve maximum X bound (local_8)\n2. Get current game state and retrieve maximum Y bound (local_4)\n3. Clamp first coordinate (param_2[0]): if less than max_x, increment; else if greater, decrement\n4. Clamp second coordinate (param_2[1]): if less than max_y, increment; else if greater, decrement\n5. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\nIMPLICIT ECX (dwMinValue): Reference value used by Ordinal_10332\nIMPLICIT EDX (pCoordinates): Pointer to coordinate pair [x, y] to be clamped\n\nReturns:\nvoid - coordinates updated in place via pCoordinates pointer\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x6fb62880 - GetGameContext() function address\n0x6fb982ea - Ordinal_10332 (unknown - appears to extract bounds from context/state)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Uses __fastcall convention with ECX/EDX for parameters\n- Coordinates are treated as signed comparisons (JBE checks)\n- Equal values result in no clamping",
