      "comment": "Processes mouse actions on status frame (skill casting, targeting).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate input parameter pStatusFrame is not NULL\n2. Get sound status via PlayStatusSound for pStatusFrame[1]\n3. If sound status is valid:\n   a. Play sound effect via Ordinal_11016\n   b. Find target unit in hash table by dwUnitIndex\n   c. Validate targeting via Ordinal_10361\n   d. If valid, draw status frame and return\n4. Check sound type for skill casting trigger (0x29 or 0xe6):\n   a. Validate skill handle and target unit handle via ValidateSkillAndTargetHandles\n   b. If valid, calculate interpolated movement:\n      i. Get unit coordinates via Ordinal_10326/10329\n      ii. Interpolate position based on distance ratio\n      iii. Update unit position via Ordinal_10170\n      iv. Render unit via Ordinal_10142\n      v. Apply skill animation via FUN_6fb86120\n   c. If validation fails, draw frame with error flag\n5. If sound type not skill-related, check sound status (1 or 4):\n   a. If pStatusFrame[0] has 0x20 flag set, draw frame with show-all flag\n   b. Otherwise, for specific target types, perform special handling\n   c. Apply movement and animations as needed\n\nParameters:\n  pStatusFrame (uint *): Pointer to status frame structure containing unit references, animation state, and control flags\n  dwUnitIndex (uint): Index of target unit in entity hash table\n  dwDistance (uint): Distance parameter for movement interpolation calculations\n\nReturns:\n  void (function handles rendering internally)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - NULL pStatusFrame triggers assertion failure\n  - Zero sound status skips entire frame processing\n  - Invalid skill/target handles trigger defensive error assertions\n  - Flag 0x20 (bit 5) of pStatusFrame[0] controls targeted vs area-of-effect behavior\n  \nNote: Function uses 12 SSA temporaries optimized away by compiler (local_EAX_53, local_EAX_574, local_EAX_582, piVar1, iVar2-4, iVar6, uVar5-6, dwSkillId, extraout_var)",
