      "comment": "ProcessSkillTargeting - Handle targeting logic for skill/spell application on units\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract unit pointer from command structure at offset +0x8\n2. Switch on unit type (0=player solo, 1=mercenary, 2=item, 4=boss/unique, 5=timeout)\n3. For unit type 0: Validate range with Ordinal_10399 (GetDistance), check targeting state 0x804 (CheckLineOfSight), set flag\n4. For unit type 1: Check mercenary existence via Ordinal_10582 (GetMonsterData), validate mercenary flags\n5. For unit type 2: Get unit data via Ordinal_10626 (GetUnitData), validate targeting distance/flags\n6. For unit type 4: Check range < 5, validate targeting state, apply skill to target unit\n7. For unit type 5: Check targeting timeout via GetTargetingTimeout/GetGlobalStatus\n8. Coordinate adjustment: Load game context via GetGameContext, get base coords via Ordinal_10332 (GetUnitCoordinates)\n9. Calculate delta X/Y from source position, clamp if needed\n10. Apply movement via Ordinal_10170 (SetUnitTarget), validate with Ordinal_10142 (ValidateMovement)\n11. If movement valid: Get coordinates via Ordinal_10177 (GetMovementX)/10178 (GetMovementY)\n12. Call FUN_6fb86120 to apply skill effect, FUN_6fb866e0 to trigger event\n13. Set event completion flag via SetEventCompletionFlag if fCanExecute is true\n14. For mercenary/object path: Call CompressPackedData(0x59, ...), ModifyWordFlags, FUN_6fb86790\n\nOrdinals Used:\n- Ordinal_10170 = D2Common.SetUnitTarget (set targeting coordinates)\n- Ordinal_10177 = D2Common.GetMovementX (get X movement component)\n- Ordinal_10178 = D2Common.GetMovementY (get Y movement component)\n- Ordinal_10142 = D2Common.ValidateMovement (check movement validity)\n- Ordinal_10153 = D2Common.FreeUnit (deallocate unit)\n- Ordinal_10326 = D2Common.GetUnitType (get unit classification)\n- Ordinal_10329 = D2Common.GetMercenaryId (get merc identifier)\n- Ordinal_10332 = D2Common.GetUnitCoordinates (get unit location)\n- Ordinal_10363 = D2Common.CheckLineOfSight (validate path/targeting)\n- Ordinal_10399 = D2Common.GetDistance (calculate unit distance)\n- Ordinal_10487 = D2Common.CheckClassRestriction (check skill class validity)\n- Ordinal_10582 = D2Common.GetMonsterData (get monster/merc data)\n- Ordinal_10626 = D2Common.GetUnitData (get unit attributes)\n\nParameters:\npCommand (dword *): Pointer to command structure containing unit/skill/coords data\n  - [0] = unit type (0-5 enum, matching switch cases)\n  - [+4] = unit pointer or unit type\n  - [+8] = target unit pointer\n  - [+0x14] = skill effect context\n  - [+0x18] = alternate context\ndwUnitType (dword): Skill target unit type classification\ndwObjectId (dword): Target object/monster ID\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value. Effects applied via side effects (skill damage, movement)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If target is invalid, function returns early without executing\n- Timeout case (dwUnitType=5): Updates timeout to current+500ms via SetTargetingTimeout\n- fCanExecute flag controls whether event completion is triggered\n- Mercenary objects require additional CompressPackedData serialization\n- State validation 0x804 blocks skill application in certain game states",
      "tags": ["PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PARAM_3", "STRUCT_Skill", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
    },
