      "comment": "Validate UI interaction flags for contextual menu operations.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load flags from input parameter (pFlags[0])\n2. Check 0x10 (disabled) flag - if set, clear state and return 0\n3. Check 0x4 (selection) flag:\n   - If clear, check 0x8 (context menu) flag\n   - If 0x8 set, validate state is non-zero; check pFlags[2] pointer validity\n   - If pFlags[2] non-null, read value; reject if negative, value in (1,5) range, or offset +0xC matches 2 or 3\n   - If 0x4 set, compute state as 1+(pFlags[2]!=0) and update global\n4. Return 1 on success, 0 on validation failure\n\nParameters:\npFlags (uint *) - Pointer to 3-element flags array [flags, object_ptr, subdata_ptr]\n\nReturns:\n1 - Interaction allowed\n0 - Interaction rejected\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- 0x10 flag forces immediate reject and state clear\n- State validation depends on 0x8 flag being set\n- Rejects negative or out-of-range values in subdata\n- Magic offsets +0x8, +0xC match structure field access patterns",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Inventory", "PARAM_1", "PROP_LOOPHEAVY", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "PROP_LEAF", "STRUCT_Control"]
