      "comment": "TransferCorpseItemsToPlayer - Transfers items from a corpse back to the player.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate unit type byte is non-zero from packet\n2. Find unit in hash table using GUID from packet offset +2\n3. Validate unit state, clear and process transition if invalid\n4. If unit is current player context:\n   a. Find dead body unit from packet offset +6\n   b. Assert dead body exists (crash if not)\n   c. Get corpse coordinates via Ordinal_10329/10326 (GetUnitY/X)\n   d. Warp items to player location using SetPathTargetPosition\n5. Iterate inventory items in location 3 (corpse inventory)\n6. For each item: remove from inventory, clear slots, update graphics\n7. Remove item from hash table after processing\n\nParameters:\n  pCorpsePacket - Pointer to corpse transfer packet:\n                  +1: Unit type (byte, must be non-zero)\n                  +2: Unit GUID (dword)\n                  +6: Dead body GUID (dword)\n\nReturns: void\n\nOrdinal Calls:\n  Ordinal_10329 (D2COMMON.DLL) - GetUnitY - returns Y coordinate\n  Ordinal_10326 (D2COMMON.DLL) - GetUnitX - returns X coordinate\n\nCalled By: ProcessCorpseMessage (network packet handler)",
