      "comment": "Add a related player ID to the linked list for a given player.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Retrieve player node by nPlayerId via GetPlayerDataById\n2. Return if player not found OR if nPlayerId equals nRelatedPlayerId (self-reference)\n3. Retrieve player data structure (first field points to linked list head)\n4. Traverse linked list via offset +0x8 (next pointer)\n5. If nRelatedPlayerId found in list, return early (already linked)\n6. Allocate new 12-byte node via Ordinal_10042(0x73, 0) - D2Common pool allocator\n7. Initialize new node: [+0x0]=nRelatedPlayerId, [+0x4]=0, [+0x8]=current_head\n8. Update head pointer to new node\n\nParameters:\n  nPlayerId (int in ECX): Player ID to find in database\n  nRelatedPlayerId (int in EDX): Player ID to add to the list\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nStructure Layout (12-byte linked list node):\n  Offset | Size | Field      | Type | Description\n  0x0    | 4    | id         | int  | Related player ID\n  0x4    | 4    | unused     | int  | Padding/reserved field\n  0x8    | 4    | next       | ptr  | Pointer to next node in list\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x73: Allocation size/type identifier (12 bytes)\n  0x0: NULL pointer constant\n  0x8: Linked list next pointer offset\n\nNote: Function uses compiler-optimized intermediate temporaries that cannot be renamed in decompilation view.",
