      "comment": "Search unit linked list and modify node flags - SET or CLEAR operation\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call GetPlayerDataById(nStartUnitId) to retrieve starting player data node\n2. Verify player node exists and nStartUnitId differs from nTargetUnitId (exit if same)\n3. Dereference player node to get first element in linked list at offset 0x0\n4. Loop: Compare ID at offset +0x0 of current node against nTargetUnitId\n5. If match found: Proceed to step 6; Otherwise advance to next node at offset +0x8 and loop\n6. Test nSetFlags: If non-zero, set flags via OR; If zero, clear via AND with inverted mask\n7. If nSetFlags != 0: dwTempFlags = node[1] | dwFlagMask; store to node[1]\n8. If nSetFlags == 0: dwTempFlags = node[1] & ~dwFlagMask; store to node[1]\n9. Return (success or node not found both return without error)\n\nParameters:\nnStartUnitId (int) - Starting unit ID to look up in player data table\nnTargetUnitId (int) - Target unit ID to search for within linked list\ndwFlagMask (uint) - Bitmask indicating which flags to modify\nnSetFlags (int) - Non-zero=set flags, zero=clear flags\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Modifies node in-place; silent if target not found\n\nSpecial Cases:\nExits if nStartUnitId==nTargetUnitId; traverses via +0x8 (next); accesses flags at +0x4",
