      "comment": "Searches a linked list for a specific node ID and returns masked field value.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call GetPlayerDataById(dwPlayerId) to fetch player/unit base data pointer\n2. Validate pointer is non-null and dwPlayerId != dwSearchId\n3. Load first linked list node from base data + offset 0x0\n4. Loop through linked list:\n   - Check if node ID at offset 0x0 matches dwSearchId\n   - If match found: load value at offset 0x4, AND with dwMask, return result\n   - If no match: advance to next node at offset 0x8, continue loop\n5. Return 0x0 if search ID not found or initial checks fail\n\nParameters:\n- dwPlayerId (implicit ECX): unit/player ID to fetch data from\n- dwSearchId (implicit EDX): node ID value to search for in linked list\n- dwMask (stack): bitmask to apply to returned field value\n\nReturns:\n- Masked field value (EAX) if node found: (node[0x4] & dwMask)\n- 0x0 if node not found or validation fails\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If dwPlayerId == dwSearchId, returns 0x0 without list traversal\n- If player data pointer is null, returns 0x0\n- Early return avoids false positive when piVar1 becomes null during loop\n- Note: Loop iteration variable (pNode) exists only in assembly form\n\nStructure Layout (Linked List Node):\nOffset | Size | Field Name | Type | Description\n  0x00 |  0x4 | dwNodeId   | dword| Node identifier for matching\n  0x04 |  0x4 | dwValue    | dword| Value field (masked before return)\n  0x08 |  0x4 | pNextNode  | uint*| Pointer to next list node",
