      "comment": "Updates a flag field in a linked-list node within a player's data structure.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Retrieve player data using nPlayerId via GetPlayerDataById\n2. Return early if player data is null or nPlayerId equals nTargetNodeId\n3. Load first node from player data pointer (dereference: [pPlayer])\n4. Return if first node is null\n5. Iterate through linked list: while current node ID != nTargetNodeId\n6. Load next pointer from offset +0x8: pNodeCurrent = [pNodeCurrent + 0x8]\n7. Return if next pointer becomes null (node not found)\n8. When match found (node ID == nTargetNodeId at offset +0x0):\n   - Load flag field from offset +0x4\n   - Clear lower 16 bits: flags = flags & 0xFFFF0000\n   - Merge new flags: flags = flags | wNewFlags\n   - Store updated flags: [pNodeCurrent + 0x4] = flags\n\nParameters:\n- nPlayerId (ECX): Player/unit ID to lookup\n- nTargetNodeId (EDX): Target node ID to find in linked list\n- wNewFlags (ESP+0xC): New lower 16-bit flag value to set\n\nReturns: void (no return value)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Returns silently if player not found\n- Returns silently if nPlayerId equals nTargetNodeId (no self-reference)\n- Returns silently if linked list is empty\n- Returns silently if target node not found\n- Preserves upper 16 bits of existing flags (0xFFFF0000 mask)\n\nStructure Layout (Linked List Node):\nOffset | Size | Field Name | Type | Description\n0x0    | 4    | nNodeId    | int  | Node identifier\n0x4    | 4    | dwFlags    | uint | Flag field (upper 16-bits preserved, lower 16-bits updated)\n0x8    | 4    | pNext      | int* | Pointer to next node in list",
