      "comment": "Render visual effects for skill usage based on unit type and skill ID.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get unit type/class via Ordinal_10323 - returns 0 if unit not valid\n2. Check unit base type field (offset 0): 0=normal unit, 1=special unit\n3. Retrieve unit subtype field (offset 0xC):\n   - If base type 0: expect value 0x12\n   - If base type 1: expect value 0x0E\n4. If subtype matches, get skill code via Ordinal_10963\n5. Compare skill code: 0x6B (spell) vs 0x97 (charge effect)\n6. For spell (0x6B): check bit 0 of Ordinal_10985 result\n   - If set: render charged spell effect with RenderChargeSkillEffect\n7. For charge (0x97): render control transparency effect and return\n\nParameters:\n- pUnit (ECX): Pointer to unit data structure\n- nSkillId (EDX): Skill/effect ID to render (unused in logic, passed to renderers)\n\nReturns:\n- void (no return value)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Returns early if Ordinal_10323 returns 0 (invalid unit)\n- Returns early if base type not 0 or 1\n- Returns early if subtype doesn't match expected value\n- Only two skill codes (0x6B, 0x97) trigger rendering\n- Charge effect (0x97) has dedicated rendering path\n- Function uses 2 optimizer-phantom variables (bVar2, uVar1) not visible in decompilation\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x0C: Offset in unit structure for subtype field\n- 0x12: Expected subtype for base type 0\n- 0x0E: Expected subtype for base type 1\n- 0x6B: Spell skill code (101 decimal)\n- 0x97: Charge effect code (151 decimal)\n\nOrdinals Referenced:\n- Ordinal_10323: Get unit type/mode\n- Ordinal_10963: Get skill/effect ID\n- Ordinal_10985: Get skill state flags",
