      "comment": "Render skill effect overlay on player or unit based on skill definition.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Retrieve skill ID from definition pointer (Ordinal_10323)\n2. If skill ID is 0, check if pSkillDef[3] equals 0x12 (class-specific skill type)\n3. If skill ID is 1, check if pSkillDef[3] equals 0x0e (alternate skill type)\n4. If skill ID is other value, exit (only types 0,1 supported)\n5. If skill type validation passed, retrieve skill base class (Ordinal_10963)\n6. If class is 0x6b (charge-based skill), get skill flags (Ordinal_10985)\n7. If flag 0x01 bit set, render charge effect via RenderChargeSkillEffect\n8. If class is 0x97 (control-based skill), render with transparency and exit\n\nParameters:\n  pSkillDef (uint *): Pointer to skill definition structure (offsets: [0]=ID, [3]=type)\n  dwSkillLevel (uint): Skill level parameter passed to rendering functions\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Only skill classes 0x6b and 0x97 trigger visual rendering\n  - Charge skill requires flag 0x01 set to render\n  - Function returns early if skill ID not 0 or 1\n  - No rendering occurs if type mismatch (0x12 for ID=0, 0x0e for ID=1)",
