      "comment": "Process unit data cleanup operations\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call FUN_6fb825c0 to initialize unit processing context with nUnit and 0\n2. Call Ordinal_10480(nUnit, 0x18) to retrieve data handle from unit at offset 0x18\n3. Store retrieved data handle in nData\n4. Test nData for validity (if nData == 0, skip cleanup and proceed to step 5)\n5. If nData is valid:\n   a. Call Ordinal_10474(nUnit, nData) to process data cleanup\n   b. Call Ordinal_10485(nData) to finalize data structures\n6. Call Ordinal_10376(nUnit) to execute final unit cleanup\n7. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\n- nUnit (int, IMPLICIT in ECX): Unit identifier for processing\n\nReturns:\n- void: No return value, all processing done via side effects\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Data handle may be null, triggering conditional cleanup skip\n- All ordinal calls target external DLL functions",
