      "comment": "Apply color to unit's light based on unit state and type.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Retrieve light pointer from unit at offset 0x88\n2. Check if unit is currently being viewed (Ordinal_10536 = D2Common.IsUnitOnScreen)\n3. If not visible on screen:\n   a. Check unit type via Ordinal_10487(unit, 2) = D2Common.GetUnitStat for specific type flag\n   b. If type match:\n      - Check if player is the active context (GetGameContext)\n      - If player unit: set white light (0xff, 0xff, 0xff)\n      - If not player: check for additional type (Ordinal_10006 = D2Common.CheckUnitExtraType)\n      - If additional type match: set light to green (0x80, 0xff, 0x80)\n      - Otherwise: set light flag 0x68 and return\n   c. If type mismatch:\n      - Check unit type via Ordinal_10487(unit, 0x60) for alternate type flag\n      - Set default color value from parameter or 0x49 flag\n      - If player unit: set light to cyan (0x96, 0xd7, 0xff)\n4. If unit is currently visible (Ordinal_10536 succeeds):\n   - Set light flag 0x6c\n   - If player unit: set light to light blue (0x96, 0xd7, 0xff)\n\nParameters:\npUnit - Pointer to game unit/entity (UnitAny structure)\ndwDefaultColor - Default color value (0xBBGGRR format, applies when unit status 0x60)\n\nReturns:\nVoid - Modifies unit light in place\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Function only applies light color if unit matches player context (GetGameContext)\n- Multiple conditional paths skip color update for non-player units\n- Color assignments use 0xBBGGRR format: 0xff=255 (full intensity per channel)\n- Magic constants: 0x88=light offset, 0x90=light color flag offset, 0x68/0x6c/0x49=light state flags\n- Note: Function uses 2 stack-allocated temporaries (iVar2, pUVar1) optimized away by compiler\n\nRelated Functions:\n- Ordinal_10536 (D2Common.IsUnitOnScreen) - Check if unit is visible on screen\n- Ordinal_10487 (D2Common.GetUnitStat) - Check unit type/state flags\n- Ordinal_10006 (D2Common.CheckUnitExtraType) - Additional unit type/state check\n- GetGameContext - Retrieve active player unit\n- SetLightRgbColor - Apply RGB color to light structure",
