      "comment": "Initialize a unit/entity structure with default values and internal state\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Save ESI register for temporary storage\n2. Move unit pointer from ECX (fastcall) to ESI\n3. Call FUN_6fb929b0 to initialize base unit state and structures\n4. Call FUN_6fb86790(pUnit, 1) to enable/activate the unit\n5. Call FUN_6fb936b0(pUnit) to process unit-specific initialization\n6. Call Ordinal_10349(pUnit) - invoke external Storm/D2Common setup operation\n7. Clear field at offset 0x50 (unit flag/counter field) to 0\n8. Call Ordinal_10324(pUnit, 0) - finalize unit initialization with reset flag\n9. Restore ESI and return\n\nParameters:\npUnit (uint *) - Pointer to unit/entity structure; IMPLICIT in ECX register via __fastcall convention\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No value returned; modifies unit structure in-place\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Uses __fastcall convention: first parameter passed in ECX, callee responsible for cleanup\n- Field at offset 0x50 is explicitly zeroed (likely represents unit action count or state flag)\n- Initialization sequence involves multiple external ordinal calls to Storm/D2Common DLLs",
