      "comment": "ApplyWerewolfTransformation - Applies Druid werewolf/werebear transformation skills.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract packed parameters:\n   - nWolfLevel (param_2 & 0xFFFF), nWolfBonus (param_2 >> 16)\n   - nLycLevel (param_3 & 0xFFFF), nLycBonus (param_3 >> 16)\n2. Validate bounds: Wolf 0-20, Lyc 0-20, bonuses 0-12\n3. Set Werewolf skill (0xDF) level and passive bonus\n4. If Lycanthropy level > 0, set Werebear skill (0xE0) level and passive\n5. Allocate stat list for transformation buffs\n6. Calculate and apply vine beast stats based on skill level\n7. Clear component graphics and reset unit state\n8. Reinitialize unit graphics and animation\n9. If unit mode is 10 (transformation), dispatch state action 0x19\n\nParameters:\n  pUnit - Pointer to UnitAny being transformed\n  dwWolfParams - Packed: low word = wolf level, high word = wolf bonus\n  dwLycParams - Packed: low word = lyc level, high word = lyc bonus\n\nReturns: void\n\nSkills:\n  0xDF = Werewolf\n  0xE0 = Werebear\n\nOrdinal Calls:\n  Ordinal_10324, Ordinal_10326, Ordinal_10329 (D2COMMON.DLL) - Unit state management",
