      "comment": "Initialize structure/entity state through sequential setup operations.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call Ordinal_11229 with pData - Unknown initialization ordinal\n2. Call FUN_6fb929b0 with pData as int (pre-processing)\n3. Call FUN_6fb86790 with pData and flag 1\n4. Call FUN_6fb936b0 with pData cast to int pointer\n5. Call Ordinal_10349 with pData - Unknown post-setup ordinal\n6. Set pData[0x14] = 0 (clear offset 0x50 in structure)\n7. Call Ordinal_10324 with pData and 0 - Unknown finalization ordinal\n\nParameters:\n  pData (dword *) - Pointer to structure to initialize\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  The function performs sequential initialization steps on a structure pointed to by pData. Three external ordinal calls and internal helper functions handle initialization phases.\n\nOrdinal Calls:\n  - Ordinal_11229 - Pre-initialization ordinal (purpose unknown)\n  - Ordinal_10349 - Post-setup ordinal (purpose unknown)\n  - Ordinal_10324 - Finalization ordinal (purpose unknown)\n\nStructure Layout (Referenced):\n  Offset | Size | Field Name | Type | Description\n  0x14   | 4    | field_0x50 | dword| Cleared to 0 during initialization\n\nRelated Functions:\n  - FUN_6fb929b0() - Pre-processing step\n  - FUN_6fb86790() - Intermediate initialization \n  - FUN_6fb936b0() - Post-processing step",
