      "comment": "Initializes a unit (monster or player) based on its type ID.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate that unit type is 1 (alive unit), assert if not\n2. Get unit's current type ID via Ordinal_11056 (GetUnitType)\n3. If type ID is 0x1c5 (monster):\n   a. Retrieve current type again\n   b. Calculate offset: (unit[1] - type) + 0x1cd\n   c. Call InitializeUnitOnCreation with offset\n   d. Set multiplier: 1 normally, 8 if unit[3] == 8\n   e. Call FUN_6fb86790 to apply multiplier\n4. Else if type ID is 0x21f (player):\n   a. Call InitializeUnitOnCreation with offset 0x22f\n   b. Get unit[0xe] skill count\n   c. Get skill offset via Ordinal_10329 (GetUnitSkillOffset) + 10\n   d. Get skill type via Ordinal_10326 (GetUnitSkillType)\n   e. Call Ordinal_10216 (SetUnitSkill) with count, type, offset\n\nParameters:\npUnit (UnitAny *) - IMPLICIT ECX - Pointer to unit structure to initialize\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Unit initialized in place\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Non-alive units (type != 1) trigger assertion\n- Unknown unit type IDs skip processing entirely\n- Type 0x1c5: Monster setup with optional 8x multiplier\n- Type 0x21f: Player setup with skill initialization",
      "tags": ["SRC_PlrSkills.cpp", "PROP_NOCALLER", "UI_SKILLS", "MOD_UNIT", "UNIT_MONSTER", "PARAM_1"]
