      "comment": "Apply effect to unit by type with initialization and effect parameters.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate offset multiplier: nOffsetCalc = nUnitType * 32 (0x20)\n2. Load three effect-related data offsets from global tables (DAT_6fba9f80, DAT_6fba9f78, DAT_6fba9f7c)\n3. For each loaded offset: check if offset != -1, then add random value if RandSeed returns non-zero\n4. If nHasInitialValue != 0: call Ordinal_10486 twice (indices 0 and 1) for setup, check Ordinal_10503 for validation\n5. Determine which effect paths to apply based on nPrimaryItem validity and nHasInitialValue flags\n6. Call FUN_6fb931f0 to apply effect configuration with computed parameters (nMode 3/4/8/9 based on flag state)\n7. Check DAT_6fba9f84[offset] for -1: if true, return early (no further processing needed)\n8. Determine effect mask (0x00, 0x10, or 0x20) based on Ordinal_10497, Ordinal_10500 checks\n9. Create effect handle via Ordinal_10480 or Ordinal_10481, then create visual via Ordinal_10470\n10. Apply huge switch statement (150+ cases) with type-specific effect configurations\n11. For each case, call appropriate Ordinal functions to set specific effect stat values (0x27, 0x2b, 0x29, etc.)\n12. Validate result: call ValidateUnitTypeState, if true and Ordinal_10557 returns valid, set unit flags (0xe8 |= 0x20, 0xec |= 0x40000)\n\nParameters:\npUnit (int *) - pointer to unit/player structure, used for effect configuration\ndwEffectParam1 (dword) - primary effect parameter, passed to effect ordinal functions\ndwEffectParam2 (dword) - secondary effect parameter, effects interpretation depends on unit type\nnUnitType (int) - unit/skill type code (0-0x9f range), determines effect behavior path via switch\n\nReturns:\nvoid - no explicit return value, modifies pUnit structure in-place\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If nPrimaryItem == -1: skips to nStorageIdx path; if nStorageIdx also -1, returns early\n- Case 0x0b/0x2c/0x8d: call Ordinal_10376 for additional effect confirmation\n- Case 0x1d: requires nEffectVal validation; performs scaled percentage calculations\n- Case 0x2f: special handling for game context comparison and SetUnitState-type effects\n- Default case: applies single stat modification via Ordinal_10463/Ordinal_10465\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x20 (32) - offset multiplier for type-indexed global tables\n0x28/0x2a/0x2c - effect stat IDs for percentage-based damage calculations\n0x27/0x2b/0x29/0x2d - primary effect stat IDs (various resistances/attributes)\n0x43/0x44/0x45 - effect stat IDs for multi-stat effects\n0x10 - effect mask bit for 16-bit effect variant\n0x20 - effect mask bit for 32-bit effect variant\n0x7b (123 decimal) - penalty base value\n-1 - invalid/disabled effect marker\n0x40000 - state flag indicating effect active (bit 18)\n0xfd/0x20 - flag manipulation masks for unit state byte",
      "tags": ["PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "STRUCT_Skill", "PARAM_4", "STRUCT_Room2", "STRUCT_ItemData", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
