      "instructions": ["0xB3E70|PUSH|EBX", "0xB3E71|PUSH|ESI", "0xB3E72|PUSH|EDI", "0xB3E73|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0xB3E75|PUSH|0xe", "0xB3E77|PUSH|ESI", "0xB3E78|CALL|0x6fb986a4", "0xB3E7D|MOV|EDI, EAX", "0xB3E7F|TEST|EDI, EDI", "0xB3E81|JZ|0x6fb83e90", "0xB3E83|PUSH|EDI", "0xB3E84|PUSH|ESI", "0xB3E85|CALL|0x6fb989b6", "0xB3E8A|PUSH|EDI", "0xB3E8B|CALL|0x6fb989da"],
      "comment": "Process unit stat arrays for enumeration and initialization\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call Ordinal_10480(pUnit, 0x0e) to fetch display data\n2. If display data != 0: assign via Ordinal_10474, then cleanup with Ordinal_10485\n3. First stat pass: iterate types 0x8c, 0x8d, 0x8e, 0x8f:\n   - Ordinal_10680(type) returns array element count\n   - Loop: FUN_6fb93500(pUnit, type + index) for each element\n4. Second pass: iterate types 0x8c, 0x8d, 0x8e\n5. Third pass: iterate type 0x90 only\n6. Final pass: iterate types 0x8c, 0x8d, 0x8e\n7. Return\n\nParameters:\npUnit - Unit structure pointer (fastcall ECX convention)\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x0e - Display data offset type\n0x8c - Stat array type 1 \n0x8d - Stat array type 2\n0x8e - Stat array type 3\n0x8f - Stat array type 4\n0x90 - Stat array type 5\n\nNote: Function uses 2 register temporaries optimized away",
      "tags": ["PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_1", "PROP_LOOPHEAVY"]
    },
