      "instructions": ["0xB4050|PUSH|EBX", "0xB4051|PUSH|ESI", "0xB4052|PUSH|EDI", "0xB4053|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0xB4055|PUSH|0x97", "0xB405A|PUSH|ESI", "0xB405B|CALL|0x6fb986a4", "0xB4060|MOV|EDI, EAX", "0xB4062|TEST|EDI, EDI", "0xB4064|JZ|0x6fb84073", "0xB4066|PUSH|EDI", "0xB4067|PUSH|ESI", "0xB4068|CALL|0x6fb989b6", "0xB406D|PUSH|EDI", "0xB406E|CALL|0x6fb989da"],
      "comment": "Process render layer data for a unit across 6 render modes.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Query equipment/attachment state stat (0x97) from unit\n2. If stat returns valid non-zero value: set on unit then release resources\n3. For each render mode ID in sequence (0xCF, 0xD1, 0xD3, 0xD0, 0xD2, 0xD4):\n   a. Query count of items in render mode via Ordinal_10680\n   b. If count > 0: iterate each item index from 0 to count-1\n   c. For each index, call FUN_6fb93500(pUnit, mode_id + index)\n4. Return void\n\nParameters:\npUnit (ECX) - Pointer to UnitAny structure being rendered\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Equipment stat (0x97) may be 0 (no equipment) - conditional processing skipped\n- Render mode counts may be 0 - iteration loops skipped\n- Multiple render modes processed sequentially\n- Uses __fastcall convention: pUnit passed in ECX register",
      "tags": ["PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_1", "PROP_LOOPHEAVY"]
