      "instructions": ["0xB43B0|PUSH|EBX", "0xB43B1|PUSH|ESI", "0xB43B2|PUSH|EDI", "0xB43B3|MOV|EDI, ECX", "0xB43B5|MOV|EBX, EDX", "0xB43B7|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [EDI + 0x8]", "0xB43BA|MOV|ECX, dword ptr [EDI]", "0xB43BC|PUSH|EAX", "0xB43BD|PUSH|ECX", "0xB43BE|PUSH|0x0", "0xB43C0|PUSH|0x8", "0xB43C2|PUSH|0x0", "0xB43C4|CALL|0x6fb98494", "0xB43C9|MOV|ESI, EAX", "0xB43CB|TEST|ESI, ESI"],
      "comment": "Apply animation frames to a game unit based on position calculations.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Create/allocate unit using Ordinal_10470 with initial parameters from pUnitData\n2. Validate unit creation - if failed, log error and terminate process (0xffffffff)\n3. Set unit property 0x0E using Ordinal_10478\n4. Set unit properties 0x84 (X-position) and 0x85 (Y-position) using Ordinal_10465\n5. Register unit with Ordinal_10475\n6. Calculate animation frame count: nAnimationFrame = nYPosition / 3\n7. Determine animation tier based on X-position:\n   - If nXPosition >= (nYPosition / 3): nAnimationFrame = 2\n   - If nXPosition >= (nYPosition / 3) * 2: nAnimationFrame = 2 (no change)\n   - Decrement nAnimationFrame if additional borrow condition detected\n8. Switch on animation frame (1, 2, or 3):\n   - Frame 3: Call FUN_6fb931f0 with property 0x8F and 7 parameters\n   - Frame 2: Call FUN_6fb931f0 with property 0x90 and 7 parameters\n   - Frame 1 or default: Call FUN_6fb931f0 with property 0x8C, 4 parameters, 0x8D and 0x8E\n\nParameters:\nIMPLICIT pUnitData (ECX) - int *: Pointer to unit data structure (contains initial unit properties at offsets 0x0 and 0x8)\nIMPLICIT nXPosition (EDX) - int: X-coordinate position for animation tier calculation\nnYPosition (Stack) - int: Y-coordinate position used for animation frame count calculation (divided by 3)\n\nReturns:\nvoid: No return value, animates unit in-place. Side effect: May call FUN_6fb9a10f(0xFFFFFFFF) for error termination.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Unit creation failure: Calls Ordinal_10023 with error string pointer, then terminates with FUN_6fb9a10f\n- Magic constants: 0x8C, 0x8D, 0x8E, 0x8F, 0x90 are animation property codes; 0x84, 0x85 are position property codes\n- SBORROW4 operation: Detects signed borrow for secondary tier calculation",
      "tags": ["SRC_PlrSkills.cpp", "STRUCT_Inventory", "UI_SKILLS", "PARAM_3", "MOD_UNIT", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control"]
    },
