      "comment": "Initialize skill tree interface with difficulty-based level display configuration.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Create skill tree display list with dimensions (width, height)\n2. If list creation fails, log error and terminate process\n3. Set list properties: border style (0x97), width (0x84), height (0x85)\n4. Calculate difficulty level: nDifficulty = (height / 3) based on width comparison\n5. Branch on nDifficulty value:\n   - nDifficulty=3: Set skill icons 0xCF, 0xD0, 0xD1, 0xD2\n   - nDifficulty=2: Set skill icons 0xD1, 0xD2\n   - nDifficulty=1: Set skill icons 0xD3, 0xD4\n6. Call FUN_6fb931f0 for each selected skill icon with value 0x3\n\nParameters:\n- pSkillTree (IMPLICIT ECX): pointer to skill tree structure instance\n- dwWidth (IMPLICIT EDX): display window width in pixels\n- dwHeight (Stack[0x4]): display window height in pixels\n\nReturns:\n- void (no return value)\n- Modifies skill tree display list on success\n- Terminates process (calls FUN_6fb9a10f) on list creation failure\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- List creation failure triggers immediate termination with FUN_6fb9a10f(0xffffffff)\n- Width must be checked relative to (height/3)*2 to determine difficulty\n- All skill icon setup calls pass 0x3 as the last parameter\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x97: Skill tree list border style constant\n- 0x84: List property ID for width\n- 0x85: List property ID for height\n- 0xCF, 0xD0: High difficulty skill icons\n- 0xD1, 0xD2: Medium difficulty skill icons\n- 0xD3, 0xD4: Low difficulty skill icons\n- 0x3: Skill level setting parameter\n\nOrdinals Referenced:\n- Ordinal_10470: Create display list with dimensions\n- Ordinal_10478: Set list border/frame property\n- Ordinal_10465: Set list dimension properties\n- Ordinal_10475: Associate data with list\n- Ordinal_10023: Log error messages\n- FUN_6fb931f0: Configure skill icon display\n- FUN_6fb9a10f: Terminate process with exit code",
      "tags": ["SRC_PlrSkills.cpp", "STRUCT_Inventory", "UI_SKILLS", "PARAM_3", "MOD_UNIT", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control"]
    },
