      "instructions": ["0xB4A80|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [ESP + 0x4]", "0xB4A84|PUSH|EBX", "0xB4A85|PUSH|EBP", "0xB4A86|PUSH|ESI", "0xB4A87|PUSH|EDI", "0xB4A88|MOV|EDI, EDX", "0xB4A8A|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0xB4A8C|PUSH|EAX", "0xB4A8D|CALL|0x6fb98b42", "0xB4A92|MOV|EBX, EAX", "0xB4A94|PUSH|0xe9", "0xB4A99|CALL|0x6fb98524", "0xB4A9E|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0xB4AA0|JNZ|0x6fb84ac0", "0xB4AA2|PUSH|0x6f8"],
      "comment": "Apply skill overlay effects to character based on skill type and level.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate overlay ID by querying Ordinal_11048(dwSkillId) for charges per level\n2. Validate skill level does not exceed charges per level using Ordinal_10990(0xe9) check\n3. Calculate overlay index: (nSkillLevel * 5 - 5) / nSkillChargesPerLevel, must be 0-4\n4. Apply base overlay: Loop through 5 base overlays, skip matching index\n   - If nOverlayId == 0xe8, use g_dwMaulOverlayTable/g_dwMaulChargeTable\n   - If nOverlayId == 0xe9, use g_dwWereformOverlayTable/g_dwWereformChargeTable\n   - Call FUN_6fb93500(pCharInfo, overlay) for each\n5. Apply skill-specific overlay: Loop through 2 skill overlays at calculated index+nSkillChargesPerLevel\n   - Check FUN_6fb8f790(pCharInfo, overlay) returns 0\n   - If valid, call FUN_6fb931f0(pCharInfo, overlay, 3, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0)\n6. Return void\n\nParameters:\npCharInfo (int *): IMPLICIT in ECX - pointer to character data structure\nnSkillLevel (int): IMPLICIT in EDX - skill level (0+)\ndwSkillId (int): IMPLICIT in Stack[0x4] - skill ID code to determine table\nnOverlayId (int): IMPLICIT in Stack[0x8] - overlay type ID (0xe8=Maul, 0xe9=Wereform)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - function applies overlays and returns without value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Invalid nSkillLevel > nSkillChargesPerLevel triggers Ordinal_10023 assertion (s_nCharges_<__nMaxCharges_)\n- Invalid overlay index outside [0,4] triggers Ordinal_10023 assertion (s_nOverlay_>__0____nOverlay_<__4_)\n- Invalid dwSkillId (Ordinal_11048 fails) triggers Ordinal_10023 assertion (s_SkillGetSkillParam1__SKILL_MAUL_)\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0xe8 = Maul skill ID\n0xe9 = Wereform skill ID\n0x5 = Multiplier for skill level to overlay index calculation\n0x4 = Maximum overlay index (0-4 valid range)\n0x2 = Number of skill-specific overlays processed\n0x3 = Overlay level parameter to FUN_6fb931f0\n\nStructure Layout:\nNot applicable - uses external global data tables indexed by skill type and level.",
      "tags": ["SRC_PlrSkills.cpp", "UI_SKILLS", "MOD_UNIT", "PARAM_4"]
    },
