      "comment": "Validates unit state and applies combat effects with error handling.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if unit state matches expected values (type=1, subtype=0x1a8)\n2. If state invalid, attempt to acquire unit reference (Ordinal_10480 with 0x95 flag)\n3. If reference successful, apply effects chain:\n   - Apply skill effect (Ordinal_10474)\n   - Release resource (Ordinal_10485)\n4. Attempt to create/allocate new unit instance (Ordinal_10470)\n5. If allocation fails, log error message to debug file and terminate with code 0xffffffff\n6. If allocation succeeds, apply unit state flags (Ordinal_11240) and effect multipliers (ApplyUnitEffectByType)\n7. Function returns after effect application (no explicit return value)\n\nParameters:\n- pUnitData (int *): Pointer to unit state array [0]=type, [1]=subtype, [2]=flags\n- dwStateFlag (dword): Effect flags bitmask (e.g., 0x95 for combat state)\n\nReturns:\n- void (no return value); effects applied in-place to unit data\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If unit allocation fails at step 4, function calls exit handler with -1 code (does not return)\n- Allocation failure is fatal to caller - error message logged with filename and line 0x780\n- Function only executes if EITHER type field is not 1 OR subtype field is not 0x1a8\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x1a8: Expected unit subtype value (424 decimal)\n- 0x95: Combat effect flag constant\n- 0x780: Source line number in error log (1920 decimal)\n- 0xffffffff: Fatal exit code (-1)",
      "tags": ["SRC_PlrSkills.cpp", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PARAM_2", "PROP_NOCALLER", "UI_SKILLS", "MOD_UNIT"]
