      "instructions": ["0xB4FD0|SUB|ESP, 0x8", "0xB4FD3|PUSH|EBX", "0xB4FD4|PUSH|EBP", "0xB4FD5|PUSH|ESI", "0xB4FD6|PUSH|EDI", "0xB4FD7|MOV|EDI, EDX", "0xB4FD9|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0xB4FDB|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x10], EDI", "0xB4FDF|CALL|0x6fb929b0", "0xB4FE4|MOV|EDX, 0x1", "0xB4FE9|MOV|ECX, ESI", "0xB4FEB|CALL|0x6fb86790", "0xB4FF0|MOV|EDX, 0x1", "0xB4FF5|MOV|ECX, ESI", "0xB4FF7|CALL|0x6fb936b0"],
      "comment": "Initialize a unit (player, NPC, minion) with its base assets, equipment, and skill configurations based on class.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Reset unit state (calls FUN_6fb929b0, FUN_6fb86790, FUN_6fb936b0)\n2. Initialize unit tracking structures (Ordinal_10349)\n3. Clear unit stat cache at offset +0x50\n4. Initialize quest progression (Ordinal_10324)\n5. Load base assets for class: iterate through class asset table from g_pInitialAssets\n   - Get asset table index from g_pInitialAssets[nUnitClassId * 0x20]\n   - Enumerate all assets in table using Ordinal_10680 (get count)\n   - Add each asset to unit using FUN_6fb93500\n6. Load equipment assets: repeat for g_pEquipmentAssets table\n7. Determine starting skill based on class:\n   - If Ordinal_10497(nUnitClassId) != 0: allocate skill size 0x20\n   - Else if Ordinal_10500(nUnitClassId) != 0: allocate skill size 0x10\n   - Else: use Ordinal_10480 to get default skill\n8. Validate allocated skill:\n   - If skill allocated and Ordinal_10479(skill) == nUnitClassId: activate skill\n   - Otherwise: skip activation\n\nParameters:\n  pUnit (dword *): Pointer to unit structure to initialize (ECX register - __fastcall)\n  nUnitClassId (int): Unit class identifier (EDX register - __fastcall)\n\nReturns:\n  void: No return value; modifies unit structure in-place\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If g_pInitialAssets[nUnitClassId * 0x20] is -1, skip asset loading\n  - If Ordinal_10680 returns 0 or negative count, skip asset enumeration\n  - Skill allocation may fail (Ordinal_10479 != nUnitClassId); if so, skip activation\n  - Skill size determined by class: 0x20 for certain classes, 0x10 for others\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x50: Offset in unit structure for stat cache\n  0x20: Equipment skill slot size (32 bytes)\n  0x10: Basic skill slot size (16 bytes)\n  0x20: Asset table stride (class descriptor size)\n  -1: Sentinel value indicating no assets/skills available",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Inventory", "PARAM_2", "PROP_NOCALLER", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
    },
