      "comment": "Apply light color and visual effects to a unit based on type classification.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate unit type is UNIT_MON (1), abort if incorrect with error call\n2. Initialize unit state via FUN_6fb86790 call\n3. Check if light color index == 2 AND unit type == 1 AND dwClassId in range [0x1a6..0x1a8]\n4. If condition fails: apply generic effects via ApplyUnitEffectByType, set light color from table\n5. Query aura/visual effect ID via Ordinal_10470 (D2Common - creates visual aura effect)\n6. If aura exists: get light flags via Ordinal_10994, apply properties via Ordinal_10465, attach to unit via Ordinal_10475\n\nParameters:\npUnit (UnitAny *) - Unit object to apply effects to, must be monster type (dwUnitType==1)\ndwEffectId (uint) - Effect identifier passed to ApplyUnitEffectByType\ndwUnknown (uint) - Effect parameter passed to ApplyUnitEffectByType\nnLightColorIndex (int) - Index into g_aLightColorTable array for light color selection (0-based)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No explicit return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Magic value 0x1a6: Lower bound for dwClassId range check (unit class/subtype validation)\n- Magic value 0x1a8: Upper bound for dwClassId range check (inclusive check: classid <= 0x1a8)\n- Magic value 0x5f: Light intensity/color modifier passed to Ordinal_10994\n- Magic value 0x43: Aura effect opcode passed to Ordinal_10465 (likely AURA_APPLY or equivalent)\n- Magic value 0x20: Light color table entry stride (4 bytes per entry, 8 entries per index: index * 32 bytes)\n- Function does not return normally if unit type validation fails (calls Ordinal_10023 error handler)\n\nOrdinal Functions (D2Common.dll):\n- Ordinal_10470(dw1, dw2, dw3, dwUnitType, pMemPool): Create/query aura effect, returns aura handle (0 if none)\n- Ordinal_10994(dwIntensity): Get light rendering properties/flags for intensity value\n- Ordinal_10465(nAuraId, dwOpcode, dwFlags): Apply rendering properties to aura (opcode 0x43 = apply)\n- Ordinal_10475(pUnit, nAuraId): Attach aura visual effect to unit for rendering\n- Ordinal_10023(lpszMsg, lpszFile, dwLine): Error reporting function (noreturn)\n\nRelated Functions:\n- ApplyUnitEffectByType(pUnit, dwEffectId, dwUnknown, nLightIndex) - Generic effect application\n- SetUnitLightColor(pUnit, dwColor) - Set unit light color from color value\n- FUN_6fb86790(pUnit, dwValue) - Initialize unit state/animation state",
      "tags": ["SRC_PlrSkills.cpp", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PROP_NOCALLER", "UI_SKILLS", "MOD_UNIT", "PARAM_4", "UNIT_MONSTER", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
