      "instructions": ["0xB51E0|PUSH|ECX", "0xB51E1|PUSH|EBX", "0xB51E2|PUSH|EBP", "0xB51E3|PUSH|ESI", "0xB51E4|PUSH|EDI", "0xB51E5|MOV|EDI, ECX", "0xB51E7|MOV|EBP, EDX", "0xB51E9|PUSH|EDI", "0xB51EA|CALL|0x6fb99106", "0xB51EF|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0xB51F1|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x10], EAX", "0xB51F5|JNZ|0x6fb85215", "0xB51F7|PUSH|0x82e", "0xB51FC|PUSH|0x6fbd09ac", "0xB5201|PUSH|0x6fbd0ae0"],
      "comment": "Process state changes for a game unit and invoke appropriate handler callbacks.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate unit pointer via Ordinal_10494; assert if NULL\n2. Initialize state block iterator: nStateIndex=0, pHandlerArray=g_pStateChangeHandlers\n3. Loop through all unit state blocks (32 blocks max):\n   - Calculate block index: nBlockIndex = (nStateIndex + sign_extension) >> 5\n   - Validate block index; assert if >= 4\n   - Extract current state flags: dwStateValue = pStateBlocks[nBlockIndex]\n   - Calculate bit position within block: dwBitMask = 1 << (nStateIndex & 0x1F)\n   - Check OLD state (param_2 flags) vs NEW state (dwResult flags):\n     a) If NOT SET->SET transition: invoke state_on callback, call SetUnitLight\n     b) If SET->NOT SET transition: invoke state_off callback\n   - Advance handler array pointer by 0x20 bytes (8 handlers per block)\n   - Advance nStateIndex\n4. Call Ordinal_10491 to finalize state changes\n5. Return\n\nParameters:\n- pUnit (ECX): Pointer to UnitAny structure being updated\n- pdwStateBlocks (EDX): Pointer to array of 4 DWORD state block values (128 state flags total)\n\nReturns:\n- void; state change handlers invoked as side effects\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Assertions triggered on NULL pUnit or nBlockIndex >= 4 (defensive checks)\n- Ordinal_10491 finalizes changes; does not return on error\n- Handler pointers can be NULL; test before calling\n- State callback signature: void (uint nState, int nIndex) or void (void)\n- Note: Function uses 1 stack-allocated temporary optimized away\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x1F: Bit position mask (state flags are 32-bit blocks)\n- 0x20: Handler array stride (8 function pointers × 4 bytes each)\n- 4: Maximum state block count\n- 0x6fba9f88: g_pStateChangeHandlers table base\n- 0x6fbab388: g_pStateChangeHandlers end boundary",
      "tags": ["SRC_PlrSkills.cpp", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PARAM_2", "UI_SKILLS", "MOD_UNIT", "PROP_LOOPHEAVY", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control"]
