      "instructions": ["0xB52D0|PUSH|ESI", "0xB52D1|PUSH|EDI", "0xB52D2|MOV|ESI, EDX", "0xB52D4|MOV|EDI, ECX", "0xB52D6|PUSH|ESI", "0xB52D7|PUSH|EDI", "0xB52D8|CALL|0x6fb98404", "0xB52DD|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0xB52DF|JNZ|0x6fb852f6", "0xB52E1|PUSH|EAX", "0xB52E2|PUSH|EAX", "0xB52E3|PUSH|EAX", "0xB52E4|MOV|EAX, ESI", "0xB52E6|SHL|EAX, 0x5", "0xB52E9|MOV|EDX, EDI"],
      "comment": "Process unit state change: check if state is already set, call cleanup handler, mark state changed, invoke callback\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call Ordinal_10487(nUnitId, dwStateType) to check if state transition is valid\n2. If check returns 0 (state can be changed):\n   a. Load handler pointer from g_pStateChangeTable[dwStateType]\n   b. Call FUN_6fb8d210 with handler, nUnitId, and coordinates (0.0, 0.0, 0)\n3. Call Ordinal_10486(nUnitId, dwStateType, 1) to mark state as changed\n4. Load callback from g_pStateChangeHandlers[dwStateType * 0x20]\n5. If callback is not NULL, invoke it with parameters (0, dwStateType)\n6. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\n  nUnitId (ECX, uint): Unit identifier for state change\n  dwStateType (EDX, uint): State type index (0-7, 32-byte stride)\n\nReturns:\n  void - no return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - g_pStateChangeTable is indexed by dwStateType * 0x20 (32-byte entries)\n  - Ordinal_10487 may fail for certain unit/state combinations\n  - Callback at g_pStateChangeHandlers may be NULL (null check present)\n\nRelated Globals:\n  - g_pStateChangeTable @ 0x6fba9f94 - state handler array\n  - g_pStateChangeHandlers @ 0x6fba9f88 - callback handler array",
