      "instructions": ["0xB5320|PUSH|ESI", "0xB5321|PUSH|EDI", "0xB5322|MOV|ESI, EDX", "0xB5324|MOV|EDI, ECX", "0xB5326|PUSH|ESI", "0xB5327|PUSH|EDI", "0xB5328|CALL|0x6fb98404", "0xB532D|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0xB532F|JNZ|0x6fb85346", "0xB5331|PUSH|EAX", "0xB5332|PUSH|EAX", "0xB5333|PUSH|EAX", "0xB5334|MOV|EAX, ESI", "0xB5336|SHL|EAX, 0x5", "0xB5339|MOV|EDX, EDI"],
      "comment": "Apply state change to entity and invoke registered handler\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if state nStateIndex is already applied to unit nUnitId via Ordinal_10487\n2. If not applied (return 0), initialize state by calling FUN_6fb8d210 with init handler from g_apStateInitHandlers array\n3. Mark state as applied via Ordinal_10486(nUnitId, nStateIndex, 1)\n4. If state change handler registered in g_pStateChangeHandlers[nStateIndex], invoke it with (dwStateData, nStateIndex)\n\nParameters:\n- nUnitId (int, ECX): Entity/unit identifier\n- nStateIndex (int, EDX): State index (0-based), scaled by 32 (0x20) for array access\n- dwFlags (uint, stack): Reserved/unused flags parameter\n- dwStateData (uint, stack): Data passed to state change handler callback\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If state already applied, initialization handler skipped\n- Handler invocation conditional on g_pStateChangeHandlers[nStateIndex] != NULL\n- Uses Diablo II calling convention with implicit EBX register parameter",
