      "instructions": ["0xB5380|PUSH|EBX", "0xB5381|PUSH|EBP", "0xB5382|PUSH|ESI", "0xB5383|PUSH|EDI", "0xB5384|MOV|EDI, ECX", "0xB5386|PUSH|0x69", "0xB5388|MOV|EBP, EDX", "0xB538A|PUSH|EDI", "0xB538B|MOV|EBX, 0x4", "0xB5390|CALL|0x6fb986a4", "0xB5395|MOV|ESI, EAX", "0xB5397|TEST|ESI, ESI", "0xB5399|JNZ|0x6fb853e4", "0xB539B|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [EDI + 0x8]", "0xB539E|MOV|ECX, dword ptr [EDI]"],
      "comment": "Initialize or allocate state for a unit, then validate state change\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Query current unit state 0x69 using Ordinal_10480 (pUnitState parameter)\n2. If unit state doesn't exist:\n   a. Allocate new state with Ordinal_10470 (five zero parameters + unit fields)\n   b. If allocation fails, log error with Ordinal_10025 and return\n   c. If allocation succeeds:\n      - Assign state handle to new allocation with Ordinal_10478\n      - Set unit association with Ordinal_10475\n      - Apply state 0x69 to unit with Ordinal_10486\n3. If unit state exists (non-zero from step 1):\n   - Read state 0xac value with Ordinal_10466 into byFinalState\n4. Apply dwNewState to state 0xac with Ordinal_10465\n5. Call ValidateUnitStateChange to confirm state transition with byFinalState and dwNewState\n\nParameters:\n- pUnitState: Pointer to unit state array or linked unit data (IMPLICIT ECX)\n- dwNewState: New state value to apply to state 0xac (IMPLICIT EDX)\n\nReturns:\n- void (result validation via side effects in ValidateUnitStateChange)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- State allocation failure: logs to hList with error code 0x87a\n- State 0x69 vs 0xac: dual-state system (initialization vs active state)",
