      "api_calls": ["GetUnitStateFlag", "GetUnitStateFlag", "GetUnitStateFlag", "GetExpansionModeIfInitialized", "UNITS_GetUnitX", "STATLIST_GetUnitOwnerType", "ValidateCoordinateRange", "UNITS_GetRoom", "GetEntityField", "GetGameConfigValue80", "...+7 more"],
      "instructions": ["0xB5590|SUB|ESP, 0x14", "0xB5593|PUSH|EBX", "0xB5594|PUSH|EBP", "0xB5595|PUSH|ESI", "0xB5596|PUSH|EDI", "0xB5597|MOV|EDI, dword ptr [ESP + 0x28]", "0xB559B|MOV|EBX, EDX", "0xB559D|TEST|EDI, EDI", "0xB559F|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x14], EBX", "0xB55A3|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0xB55A5|JNZ|0x6fb855b7", "0xB55A7|TEST|dword ptr [ESI + 0xec], 0x40000", "0xB55B1|JNZ|0x6fb8580a", "0xB55B7|CMP|dword ptr [ESI], 0x0", "0xB55BA|JNZ|0x6fb855d2"],
      "comment": "Render skill effects and visual appearance for a unit. Handles viewport offset calculations, overlay rendering for different unit types, and sets visibility flags.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Early exit if unit has 0x40000 flag set and display mode is 0\n2. Validate unit is not a summoned minion with state 0x11 (NPCs)\n3. Check unit type range [0,2) if display mode is 0 and verify states 0x8f, 0x92 are clear\n4. Call Ordinal_10010 to get rendering context availability\n5. Fetch unit animation (Ordinal_10327) and frame (Ordinal_10330)\n6. Validate animation frame exists (Ordinal_10065)\n7. Determine context unit based on unit type (0=PC, 1=Monster, 4=Object)\n8. If context unit valid, check owner (Ordinal_10342) and equipment (Ordinal_10057/10002)\n9. Call Ordinal_10362 to update unit flags - if successful, clear 0x80 flag and return\n10. Set 0x80 flag on unit[0x3b]\n11. If rendering context unavailable, get Y offset from Ordinal_10333, display mode from Ordinal_10334\n12. If rendering context available, check unit type 2 for special flag (Ordinal_10626/10369 check 0x141+offset==0x02)\n13. Call Ordinal_10067 to transform coordinates with 0x60 param, adjust by viewport offsets\n14. For unit type 0: render skill VFX, call FUN_6fb91fe0 with flag 0, render overlay\n15. For unit type 1: check flag via CheckBitFlag, render skill VFX, call FUN_6fb91fe0 with flag result, render overlay\n16. For other types: call FUN_6fb91fe0 directly\n17. If rendering context was available, call Ordinal_10068 to cleanup\n\nParameters:\npUnit (dword *) - Unit being rendered, IMPLICIT ECX; indexed at offsets 0x3a, 0x3b, [0], [1], [3]\ndwSkillId (dword) - Skill ID passed to rendering functions, IMPLICIT EDX\nnDisplayMode (int) - Display/visibility mode flag, controls early validation and coordinate calculation\n\nReturns:\nvoid (no explicit return, modifies unit flags 0x3a bit 28 and 0x3b bits 0-7)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n0x40000 flag on unit[0x3b] skips all rendering (summoned status check)\nUnit type 0x11 in unit[3] indicates NPC/summoned minion (skipped)\nState bits 0x8f, 0x92 must be clear for PC units in range [0,2)\nContext unit validation depends on unit type and unit[3] field values\nDisplay mode 0 triggers different coordinate fetch (no viewport adjustment)\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x40000 - Summoned/invisible unit flag (unit[0x3b] bit 18)\n0x80 - Rendering active flag (unit[0x3b] bit 7)\n0x10000000 - Shield/buff indicator flag (unit[0x3a] bit 28)\n0x3a, 0x3b - Unit status flag offsets (indices 58, 59)\n0x3f, 0x140, 0x141 - Animation data offsets in context unit\n[0], [1], [3] - Unit type, owner, class fields\n0x11, 0x0c - Type codes for NPC, specific monster class\n0x8f, 0x92 - State bit indices for PC validation\n0x60 - Coordinate transformation parameter for Ordinal_10067\n0x02 - Special flag check value for unit type 2\n\nStructure Layout:\nNone (unit structure accessed via array offsets only)",
      "tags": ["PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PARAM_3", "STRUCT_Skill", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
