      "comment": "Validates unit data consistency and field references.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate param_1 is non-NULL; if NULL, call Ordinal_10023 (assertion) and FUN_6fb9a10f exit\n2. Load field at param_1[0x38]; store as iVar1\n3. If iVar1 is NULL (not equal 0), skip validation; else call Ordinal_10023 and exit\n4. Call Ordinal_10180 with iVar1 to get valid unit handle reference\n5. If return value iVar2 is 0, return early; skip remaining checks\n6. Call Ordinal_10171 with iVar1, passing addresses of local_8 and local_4 (output parameters)\n7. Call FindUnitInHashTable with local_4, local_8 to get unit pointer; store as piVar3\n8. Call Ordinal_10180 again with iVar1 to get comparison reference; store as piVar4\n9. If piVar3 != piVar4, call Ordinal_10179 with iVar1 and 0 to reset unit state\n10. Return void\n\nParameters:\nparam_1 (int): Pointer to unit data structure (must be non-NULL); passed via ECX (__fastcall)\n\nReturns:\nvoid (function terminates early via FUN_6fb9a10f if validations fail)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- NULL parameter validation causes fatal exit with assertion error\n- NULL field at offset 0x38 also causes fatal exit\n- If unit handle lookup returns 0, validation is skipped\n- Unit pointer mismatch triggers state reset via Ordinal_10179\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x38 (56): Offset of critical unit reference field within structure\n0xffffffff (-1): Exit code passed to FUN_6fb9a10f for fatal termination\n\nRelated Functions:\n- Ordinal_10023 (D2Common assertion/error logging)\n- Ordinal_10180 (D2Common unit handle lookup/validation)\n- Ordinal_10171 (D2Common field extraction)\n- FindUnitInHashTable (Hash table lookup for unit records)\n- Ordinal_10179 (D2Common unit state reset)",
