      "instructions": ["0xB58C0|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [ESP + 0x4]", "0xB58C4|PUSH|ESI", "0xB58C5|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0xB58C7|PUSH|EDI", "0xB58C8|PUSH|EAX", "0xB58C9|PUSH|EDX", "0xB58CA|MOV|EDI, dword ptr [ESI + 0x38]", "0xB58CD|PUSH|EDI", "0xB58CE|CALL|0x6fb98386", "0xB58D3|MOV|ECX, dword ptr [ESI + 0xe8]", "0xB58D9|SHR|ECX, 0x15", "0xB58DC|AND|ECX, 0x1", "0xB58DF|PUSH|ECX", "0xB58E0|PUSH|ESI", "0xB58E1|PUSH|EDI"],
      "comment": "Apply state modifiers to unit by invoking D2Common ordinal functions.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load state value from unit structure offset +0x38\n2. Call Ordinal_10170(dwStateValue, dwModifier1, dwModifier2) to apply effect\n3. Read flag value from unit offset +0xe8, shift right 0x15 bits, mask 0x01\n4. Call Ordinal_10142(dwStateValue, nUnit, flag) to apply state with flag\n5. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\nnUnit (int): Unit structure pointer (contains state at offset +0x38, flags at +0xe8)\ndwModifier1 (dword): First modifier value passed to Ordinal_10170\ndwModifier2 (dword): Second modifier value passed to Ordinal_10170\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Flag bit 21 (0x200000) controls conditional modifier application\n- Both ordinal calls use identical state value from offset +0x38\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x38: Unit state value offset\n0xe8: Unit flags offset\n0x15: Shift amount for flag extraction (bit 21)\n0x01: Mask to isolate single bit flag\n\nRelated Functions:\n- ProcessSkillActionByType: Caller that manages skill-related state changes\n- ProcessUnitStateOperation: Caller that applies general unit state operations\n- Ordinal_10170: Apply modifier effect (D2Common)\n- Ordinal_10142: Apply state with flag (D2Common)",
