      "instructions": ["0xB58F0|SUB|ESP, 0xc", "0xB58F3|PUSH|EBX", "0xB58F4|PUSH|EBP", "0xB58F5|PUSH|ESI", "0xB58F6|PUSH|EDI", "0xB58F7|MOV|EBX, EDX", "0xB58F9|XOR|EDI, EDI", "0xB58FB|CMP|EBX, EDI", "0xB58FD|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0xB58FF|JZ|0x6fb85b42", "0xB5905|MOV|EBP, dword ptr [ESP + 0x20]", "0xB5909|CMP|EBP, EDI", "0xB590B|JZ|0x6fb85b42", "0xB5911|CALL|0x6fb63680", "0xB5916|TEST|EAX, EAX"],
      "comment": "Validate unit type state, check movement range limits, and broadcast unit position to other clients.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate input coordinates (nXCoord, nYCoord) are non-zero; return if invalid\n2. Call ValidateUnitTypeState to check unit is active; return on error\n3. Store new coordinates at pUnit[0x2c] (nXCoord) and pUnit[0x2d] (nYCoord)\n4. Retrieve unit stat values: dwStatValue (stat 0), nCurrentX (stat 1), nCurrentY (stat 2)\n5. Calculate movement distance limit (nDistance) based on nMovementType:\n   - Type 1: distance = 10\n   - Type 2: distance = 0 (no movement allowed)\n   - Other: distance based on GetMovementRange() and unit class\n6. Check if new position exceeds distance limit from current position using absolute difference\n7. If out of range OR nMovementType==0 AND nTargetX<1 AND distance validation fails, proceed to LAB_6fb85acd\n8. Get unit viewport coordinates, call path validation (Ordinal_10111) if needed\n9. Call FUN_6fb95ad0 twice to validate movement paths; return on failure\n10. Call Ordinal_10042 and Ordinal_10041 to render position; if success, broadcast or update viewport\n11. If pUnit == game context unit, send 0x5f protocol message with new coordinates\n12. If pUnit[0] == 0 (player), call ProcessUnitViewportWithMercenary to update viewport\n13. Otherwise call Ordinal_10230 to update unit viewport data\n\nParameters:\npUnit (IMPLICIT ECX): Pointer to unit structure; offset 0x2c=nXCoord, 0x2d=nYCoord, [3]=class\nnXCoord (IMPLICIT EDX): New X coordinate\nnYCoord (Stack+0x4): New Y coordinate\nnMovementType (Stack+0x8): Movement type (0=normal, 1=fixed dist 10, 2=no movement)\nnTargetX (Stack+0xc): Target X for path validation\nnTargetY (Stack+0x10): Target Y for path validation\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If nXCoord or nYCoord is 0, function returns immediately\n- Unit class affects distance calculation (Barbarian=3 steps, Druid=7 steps, etc.)\n- Game unit (player) has different range validation than hired units\n- Movement validation includes path collision check via Ordinal_10220",
