      "instructions": ["0xB5CF0|PUSH|EBX", "0xB5CF1|PUSH|ESI", "0xB5CF2|PUSH|EDI", "0xB5CF3|MOV|EDI, ECX", "0xB5CF5|MOV|ECX, dword ptr [ESP + 0x10]", "0xB5CF9|MOV|EBX, dword ptr [EDI + 0x38]", "0xB5CFC|CALL|0x6fb60e10", "0xB5D01|MOV|ESI, EAX", "0xB5D03|PUSH|ESI", "0xB5D04|PUSH|EBX", "0xB5D05|CALL|0x6fb985cc", "0xB5D0A|TEST|ESI, ESI", "0xB5D0C|JNZ|0x6fb85d16", "0xB5D0E|POP|EDI", "0xB5D0F|POP|ESI"],
      "comment": "Processes a unit action by validating unit existence and executing ordinal callbacks.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load control object handle from pObject->0x38\n2. Find unit in hash table using nUnitId and nSlotType\n3. Invoke Ordinal_10179 with handle and unit pointer (setup)\n4. Check if unit pointer is NULL - return 0 if unit not found\n5. Invoke Ordinal_10142 with handle, pObject, and flag 0 (process action)\n6. Return result from Ordinal_10142\n\nParameters:\n- pObject (void *): Base object/controller structure containing handle at offset 0x38\n- nSlotType (int): Unit slot type for hash table lookup\n- nUnitId (dword): Unit identifier to locate in hash table\n\nReturns:\n- dword: Success result from Ordinal_10142, or 0 if unit not found in hash table\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Returns 0 and exits without calling Ordinal_10142 if unit lookup fails\n- Always invokes Ordinal_10179 (setup) before checking unit validity\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x38: Offset within pObject structure for control handle storage\n- 0x0: Flag passed to Ordinal_10142 (zero parameter)",
      "tags": ["PARAM_3"]
    },
