      "instructions": ["0xB63A0|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [EDX]", "0xB63A2|CMP|EAX, 0x4", "0xB63A5|JA|0x6fb863ca", "0xB63A7|JMP|dword ptr [EAX*0x4 + 0x6fb86400]", "0xB63AE|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [ESP + 0x8]", "0xB63B2|PUSH|EAX", "0xB63B3|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [ESP + 0x8]", "0xB63B7|PUSH|EAX", "0xB63B8|CALL|0x6fb801c0", "0xB63BD|RET|0x8", "0xB63C0|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [ESP + 0x4]", "0xB63C4|PUSH|EAX", "0xB63C5|CALL|0x6fb7b140", "0xB63CA|MOV|EAX, 0x1", "0xB63CF|RET|0x8"],
      "comment": "Dispatch unit action based on operation type from unit state.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load operation type from pUnit->dwStateOp (first dword)\n2. Compare operation ID against boundary value 0x4\n3. If operation > 0x4, operation is invalid; return 1\n4. Otherwise, load case handler from jump table at 0x6fb86400\n5. Case 0: Execute ProcessUnitStateOperation(nUnitType, pUnit, pParams, nFlags), return result\n6. Case 1: Execute ProcessSkillActionByType(nUnitType, pUnit, pParams), return 1\n7. Case 2: Execute ProcessShrineEffect(nUnitType, pUnit, pParams), return 1\n8. Case 4: Execute SetUnitFlagState(nUnitType, pUnit, pParams[0], pParams[1]), return 1\n9. Case 3: No handler (invalid), fallthrough to return 1\n\nParameters:\n- nUnitType (int, ECX): Unit type identifier or class\n- pUnit (UnitAny*): Pointer to unit data structure\n- pParams (dword*): Pointer to parameter array [size 2 for flags and state]\n- nFlags (dword): Operation flags\n\nReturns:\n- dword: Operation result (usually 1 for success, operation-specific otherwise)",
