      "comment": "Process player skill/item targeting action from action queue.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if action context valid (param 7 non-zero), return if empty\n2. Extract action type (param 8), unit ID (param 10), target type (param 9) from context\n3. Find target unit in hash table by ID and type\n4. Clear all action parameters (params 7-10 set to zero)\n5. Handle targeting delay: if action=0x13 and target=5, set 500ms timeout\n6. Validate unit pointer - return if not found\n7. Return early if action type is zero\n8. Route by target type:\n   - Type 0 (player): Validate player state, check permissions, execute skill\n   - Type 1 (friendly): Similar path with state validation for allies\n   - Type 2+: Direct skill execution\n9. Special handling for actions 5-7 (item use), 0xC-0xF (melee), 0x13 (ranged)\n10. Validate skill data matches expected spell IDs (0x29, 0xE6, 0x10A)\n11. Execute skill with system state flags (bit 0x8 determines difficulty context)\n\nParameters:\npActionContext (dword *) - Action queue entry containing target unit ID, action type, target type, timeout state\n  [pActionContext + 0x1C] = enabled flag (must be non-zero to process)\n  [pActionContext + 0x20] = action type (0=walk, 1-0x1A = skill/item, 0x13=ranged attack)\n  [pActionContext + 0x24] = target type (0=self/player, 1=friendly unit)\n  [pActionContext + 0x28] = target unit ID\n  [pActionContext + 0x2] = player unit pointer (in ECX via __fastcall)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Side effects: clears action context, executes skill via ProcessSkillActionExecution, may update UI selection\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Empty action queue returns immediately without processing\n- Invalid unit pointer bypasses skill execution\n- Action type 0 treated as cancel, clears queue\n- Spell IDs validated: 0x29 (fireball), 0xE6 (teleport), 0x10A (static field)\n- System state flag 0x8 indicates nightmare/hell difficulty level\n- Note: Function uses 6 stack-allocated temporaries optimized away by __fastcall convention (extraout_var_00, extraout_var, iVar3, uVar2, dVar1, dwSpellType)\n\nRelated Functions:\n- FindUnitInHashTable() - Locates unit by ID in hash database\n- ValidateUnitTypeState() - Validates unit state compatibility\n- ProcessSkillActionExecution() - Executes the skill on target\n- GetSystemStateFlags() - Retrieves current difficulty/game state\n- Ordinal_10361 - Unknown: Validates skill action context\n- Ordinal_10594 - Unknown: Retrieves extended skill data\n- Ordinal_10321 - Unknown: Gets left-hand skill from action queue\n- Ordinal_10322 - Unknown: Gets right-hand skill from action queue\n- Ordinal_10963 - Unknown: Extracts spell/item ID from skill handle\n- Ordinal_10319 - Unknown: Gets skill properties/flags from unit",
