      "comment": "Validate unit state transition and execute state action if valid\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load unit base state from pUnit[0]\n2. Branch on base state value (0 or 1)\n3. If state=0: Accept transitions to 0x00, 0x04, 0x13\n4. If state=1: Accept transitions to 0x00, 0x03, 0x0d\n5. Early return if state not in valid set\n6. Load state field from pUnit[0x35] (offset 0xd4)\n7. Extract high nibble with mask 0xf0\n8. Check both high nibble (0xf0) and low nibble (0x0f) are set\n9. Search global state transition table (g_pStateTransitionTable)\n10. Loop through table with 8-byte stride comparing entries\n11. Match dwStateMask value against previous table entry\n12. On match, load action value and call FUN_6fb931f0(pUnit, nAction, 2, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0)\n13. Return void\n\nParameters:\npUnit (int *) - Unit structure pointer, passed in ECX register\nnState (int) - Requested state value, passed in EDX register\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value, performs state transition as side effect\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Early return if unit base state invalid (not 0 or 1)\n- Early return if nState not in valid transitions for base state\n- Early return if state field nibbles don't satisfy mask check\n- Early return if state not found in transition table\n- Table bounds check: loop until address 0x6fbab414",
