      "comment": "Clear unit state flag and process state transition.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Save ESI and EDI registers for local variable storage\n2. Load unit state flags from offset 0xe8\n3. Mask out bit 0x40 to clear the target flag\n4. Store updated state back at offset 0xe8\n5. Call Ordinal_10348 to validate unit state transition\n6. If validation succeeds (return non-zero):\n   a. Invoke FUN_6fb936b0 for unit cleanup/finalization\n   b. Invoke ValidateUnitStateTransition to record state change\n   c. Invoke FUN_6fb881f0 with transition type for post-state processing\n7. Restore ESI and EDI registers\n8. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\npUnit (uint *, IMPLICIT ECX): Pointer to unit structure with state flags at offset 0xe8\ndwTransitionType (uint, IMPLICIT EDX): State transition type code passed to validation and finalization handlers\n\nReturns:\nvoid (no return value): Function modifies unit state in-place via callee functions\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If Ordinal_10348 returns 0 (validation failed): state machine transition is skipped\n- Flag at offset 0xe8 bit 0x40 is always cleared regardless of validation outcome\n- Uses __fastcall convention with parameters in ECX and EDX registers",
