      "comment": "Clear pending action flag from skill action state.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call NoOperation() for synchronization\n2. Load skill action state field at offset 0xe8 [pSkillAction + 0x3a]\n3. Clear bit 0x40 from state using AND 0xffffffbf mask\n4. Store modified state back to field\n5. Call Ordinal_10348 with skill action pointer and flags parameter\n6. If Ordinal_10348 returns nonzero, call FUN_6fb936b0 to handle state change\n7. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\npSkillAction (int *): Pointer to skill action/unit data structure\ndwFlags (uint): IMPLICIT parameter in EDX, flags controlling behavior\n\nReturns:\nvoid (no explicit return value)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Bit 0x40 is unconditionally cleared regardless of dwFlags\n- Ordinal_10348 call determines whether FUN_6fb936b0 cleanup is needed\n- Magic number 0x3a is field offset scaled for array indexing\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0xe8 - Field offset (offset in structure)\n0x3a - Array index into pSkillAction (equivalent to pSkillAction[0x3a])\n0x40 - Bit mask for pending action flag\n0xffffffbf - Inverted mask (AND) for clearing bit 0x40",
