      "comment": "Initialize game data memory structures with zeros and default values.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Clear memory block starting at 0x6fbff614 (132 dwords = 528 bytes) with zeros\n2. Set global data at 0x6fbff828 to 0\n3. Set global data at 0x6fbff82c to 0\n4. Set global data at 0x6fbff830 to 0x5a (90 decimal)\n5. Set global data at 0x6fbff834 to 0\n6. Set global data at 0x6fbff838 to 0\n7. Return with void\n\nParameters:\n(none)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Always succeeds\n\nSpecial Cases:\nMagic number 0x85 (133 decimal) = dword count for bulk memory clear\nMagic number 0x5a = default initialization value (possibly array count or state flag)\n\nMemory Layout:\n0x6fbff614 - Game state array (528 bytes zeroed)\n0x6fbff828 - Game mode flag\n0x6fbff82c - Game state counter\n0x6fbff830 - Configuration value (initialized to 0x5a)\n0x6fbff834 - Game status flag\n0x6fbff838 - Game subsystem state",
