      "instructions": ["0xB6850|TEST|ECX, ECX", "0xB6852|JNZ|0x6fb86872", "0xB6854|PUSH|0x13ad", "0xB6859|PUSH|0x6fbd7a78", "0xB685E|PUSH|0x6fbc9f40", "0xB6863|CALL|0x6fb99a7a", "0xB6868|ADD|ESP, 0xc", "0xB686B|PUSH|-0x1", "0xB686D|CALL|0x6fb9a10f", "0xB6872|AND|EDX, 0xf", "0xB6875|JL|0x6fb86884", "0xB6877|CMP|EDX, 0xe", "0xB687A|JGE|0x6fb86884", "0xB687C|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [EDX*0x8 + 0x6fbd0ba0]", "0xB6883|RET|"],
      "comment": "Retrieve hit class base damage value from lookup table.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate nUnitPtr is non-zero (assert if null)\n2. Validate dwHitClass masked to 0xF is within valid range [0..13]\n3. If invalid, raise assertion error (Ordinal_10023) with line 0x13b1\n4. Index into g_aHitClassBaseTable array using (dwHitClass & 0xF) * 8 byte stride\n5. Return dword value from indexed array element\n\nParameters:\n  nUnitPtr (int): IMPLICIT ECX - Unit pointer for validation (must be non-zero)\n  dwHitClass (dword): IMPLICIT EDX - Hit class type (0-13 valid range after masking 0xF)\n\nReturns:\n  dword - Base damage value for the specified hit class from table\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If nUnitPtr is 0: triggers assertion at line 0x13ad\n  - If (dwHitClass & 0xF) > 13: triggers assertion at line 0x13b1\n  - Valid range: 0-13 (14 hit class types)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0xF - Hit class mask (extracts low 4 bits)\n  0xD (13) - Maximum valid hit class index\n  8 - Array stride in bytes (dword per entry)\n  0x6fbd0ba0 - g_aHitClassBaseTable array base\n  0x13ad, 0x13b1 - Assertion line numbers\n\nRelated Functions:\n  - Ordinal_10023 - D2Common assertion handler\n  - FUN_6fb9a10f - Fatal exit function",
