      "api_calls": ["FogAssert", "FogAssert"],
      "instructions": ["0xB68B0|TEST|ECX, ECX", "0xB68B2|JNZ|0x6fb868d2", "0xB68B4|PUSH|0x13bc", "0xB68B9|PUSH|0x6fbd7a78", "0xB68BE|PUSH|0x6fbc9f40", "0xB68C3|CALL|0x6fb99a7a", "0xB68C8|ADD|ESP, 0xc", "0xB68CB|PUSH|-0x1", "0xB68CD|CALL|0x6fb9a10f", "0xB68D2|AND|EDX, 0xf", "0xB68D5|JL|0x6fb868fc", "0xB68D7|CMP|EDX, 0xe", "0xB68DA|JGE|0x6fb868fc", "0xB68DC|MOV|ECX, dword ptr [ECX + 0x58]", "0xB68DF|TEST|ECX, ECX"],
      "comment": "Get hit class base value for unit with validation and calculation\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate unit pointer is not null (ECX != 0), call Ordinal_10023 (D2Common.LogError) if invalid\n2. Extract hit class id from EDX, AND with 0xf to get 4-bit index (0-15)\n3. Validate hit class id is within valid range (0-13, 0 < id <= 13), halt if out of range\n4. Read unit stat value from unit + 0x58 (likely unit level or base damage multiplier)\n5. If unit stat value is zero, use default value of 1\n6. Index g_adwHitClassBaseValues table with hit class id * 8 to fetch base value for hit class\n7. Shift base value left by 8 bits (multiply by 256)\n8. Add 0x80 (128) rounding constant\n9. Divide result by unit stat value to get final scaled hit class base value\n10. Return result in EAX\n\nParameters:\n  nUnitPtr (ECX) - Pointer to UnitAny struct, must be non-null\n  dwHitClass (EDX) - Hit class identifier, must be 0-13 (4-bit value after AND 0xf)\n\nReturns:\n  uint (EAX) - Calculated hit class base value = (table[id] * 256 + 128) / unit_stat\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Null unit pointer triggers assertion halt (calls Ordinal_10023 then FUN_6fb9a10f)\n  - Invalid hit class id (>13) triggers assertion halt\n  - Zero unit stat value replaced with 1 to prevent division by zero\n  - Rounding via adding 0x80 before division\n  - Note: Function uses register temporaries optimized away in decompilation\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x58 - Offset into unit structure for stat multiplier\n  0xf - Hit class id mask (keeps 4-bit value)\n  0xd (13) - Maximum valid hit class id\n  0x8 - Stride in table (8 bytes per entry, dword indexed)\n  0x100 (256) - Shift multiplier\n  0x80 (128) - Rounding constant for integer division\n  g_adwHitClassBaseValues - Hit class base value lookup table (dword[27] at 0x6fbd0ba4)\n\nStructure Layout (unit at offset 0x58 from param):\n  Offset | Size | Field Name         | Type  | Description\n  0x58   | 4    | dwStatMultiplier   | uint  | Unit level or base damage modifier\n\nRelated Functions:\n  - Ordinal_10023 - D2Common.LogError (assertion/error reporting)\n  - FUN_6fb9a10f - Fatal halt handler\n  - PlayHitSound, ProcessGameInterfaceDifficulty, ApplySkillStatModifier - Callers that use calculated values",
