      "api_count": 6,
      "api_calls": ["FogAssert", "UNITS_GetDirection", "UpdateAnimationModeFromStates", "UNITS_GetDirection", "UpdateAnimationModeFromStates", "GetMonsterInitStatsPtr"],
      "instructions": ["0xB6920|SUB|ESP, 0xc", "0xB6923|PUSH|EBX", "0xB6924|PUSH|EBP", "0xB6925|PUSH|ESI", "0xB6926|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0xB6928|TEST|ESI, ESI", "0xB692A|PUSH|EDI", "0xB692B|MOV|EBX, EDX", "0xB692D|JNZ|0x6fb8694d", "0xB692F|PUSH|0x13d3", "0xB6934|PUSH|0x6fbd7a78", "0xB6939|PUSH|0x6fbc9f40", "0xB693E|CALL|0x6fb99a7a", "0xB6943|ADD|ESP, 0xc", "0xB6946|PUSH|-0x1"],
      "comment": "Retrieves animation indices for a given skill level and mode.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate input pSkillData pointer (fail if NULL)\n2. Load current skill level from *pSkillData, *pSkillData[4], fetch skill layout via Ordinal_10369\n3. If skill level is 0, invoke Ordinal_11013 to initialize skill structure (updates level/secondary/animation)\n4. If skill level is 1, dereference pSkillData[0] as skill pointer and validate with Ordinal_10369\n5. Fetch skill metadata via Ordinal_10582 using the resolved level\n6. Check metadata byte at offset 0x2ae (animation flag) - return early if set\n7. Process lower nibble (dwSkillId & 0x0F) via switch table, mapping skill ranges to base animation indices:\n   - 1 → 0x141, 2-5 → 0x155, 6-7 → 0x14F, 8-9 → 0x149, 10-11 → 0x15B, 12 → 0x145\n8. Process upper nibble (dwSkillId & 0xF0) via secondary switch table (offset by -0x10):\n   - 0x10 (16): Return 0x17B if base animation set\n   - 0x20 (32): Return 0x161 + (0 or 3 based on base animation)\n   - 0x30 (48): Validate skill level matches mode (0→must be 0, 1→must match mode or 1)\n   - 0x40 (64): Return 0x170 + (0 or 4 based on base animation)\n   - 0x50 (80): Similar validation as 0x30, return 0x178\n   - 0x60 (96): Return 0x17E\n   - 0x70 (112): Return 0x18B\n   - 0x80 (128): Return 0x956\n   - 0xB0 (176): Return 0x187\n\nParameters:\n  pSkillData (dword *) - Pointer to skill data structure [ECX]\n  dwSkillId (dword) - Skill identifier with level (lower nibble) and mode (upper nibble) [EDX]\n  nMode (int) - Operation mode for validation [Stack+4]\n  pnAnimIndex (dword *) - Output pointer for primary animation index [Stack+8]\n  pdwAnimRate (dword *) - Output pointer for animation rate/secondary index [Stack+C]\n\nReturns:\n  Void. Sets *pnAnimIndex to base animation index (0x141-0x15B or 0x145) or 0 if mode 0x30/0x50 fails.\n  Sets *pdwAnimRate to animation rate/secondary index based on mode, or 0x956/0x187 for high modes.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If pSkillData is NULL, calls Ordinal_10023 (assertion/error) and Ordinal_10582 (exit with -1)\n  - Skill level 0: Auto-initializes via Ordinal_11013\n  - Mode 0x30/0x50: Returns error 0x16A if nMode != skill level\n  - Animation flag check (offset 0x2ae in metadata) causes early return without output\n  - Magic numbers: 0x0F (nibble mask), 0xF0 (upper nibble), 0x2AE (animation flag offset), various animation codes (0x141-0x956)\n\nRelated Functions:\n  - Ordinal_10023 - Error/assertion handler\n  - Ordinal_10369 - Fetch skill layout\n  - Ordinal_11013 - Initialize skill structure\n  - Ordinal_10582 - Get skill metadata\n  - FUN_6fb9a10f - Process error exit",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Unit", "PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "MOD_UNIT", "STRUCT_Skill", "PARAM_5", "SRC_UnitSnd.cpp", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
