      "comment": "Validates unit pointer and initializes unit-related resources.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if nUnitPtr (in ECX) is zero\n2. If zero, log error via Ordinal_10023 with error code 0x147b\n3. Call FUN_6fb9a10f(-1) to terminate initialization (no return)\n4. If nUnitPtr non-zero, call Ordinal_10058 to proceed with unit initialization\n5. Return from function\n\nParameters:\n- nUnitPtr (int, in ECX): Unit pointer value; zero indicates initialization error\n\nReturns:\n- void: Function terminates via FUN_6fb9a10f if nUnitPtr is zero; otherwise returns normally after unit initialization\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Error condition (nUnitPtr == 0): Logs error 0x147b and terminates execution\n- Magic Numbers: 0x147b = error code for invalid unit pointer\n\nRelated Functions:\n- FUN_6fb8d210(): Caller that provides unit pointer\n- Ordinal_10023(): Error logging function\n- FUN_6fb9a10f(): Termination handler\n- Ordinal_10058(): Unit initialization routine",
