      "comment": "Validate unit type and initialize related components\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Test if nUnitType is zero (null/invalid check)\n2. If nUnitType == 0:\n   a. Call Ordinal_10023 with unit pointer, source file path, and line number 0x147b\n   b. Call FUN_6fb9a10f with error code 0xffffffff to trigger error handler\n   c. Function does not return from error path\n3. If nUnitType != 0:\n   a. Call Ordinal_10059 to perform initialization\n4. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\n  int nUnitType - IMPLICIT in ECX register via __fastcall; validation flag or unit type identifier\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value. On error (nUnitType == 0), calls non-returning error handler.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  Error path: When nUnitType == 0, calls FUN_6fb9a10f(0xffffffff) which triggers fatal error handling\n  Magic Numbers: 0x147b (line number), 0xffffffff (error code indicator)\n\nRelated Functions:\n  - FUN_6fb9a10f - Error handler (non-returning)\n  - Ordinal_10023 - Validation/logging function\n  - Ordinal_10059 - Initialization function",
