      "comment": "Notify all event handlers in a context's handler linked list about a resource event.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Verify context pointer is valid (pContext != NULL):\n   - If NULL, call Ordinal_10023 with error code 0x147b (fatal error), then exit via FUN_6fb9a10f\n   - This fails if context allocation has failed\n2. Load handler linked list from context+0x9c (first handler node)\n3. For each handler in list:\n   a. Load handler data from current node [handler+0] (handler function/ID)\n   b. Load next node pointer from current node [handler+4] (linked list traversal)\n   c. Call FUN_6fb8cf80(nHandlerData, pContext, nEventMode) to invoke handler\n4. Repeat step 3 until handler list exhausted (pEventHandler == NULL)\n5. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\npContext (ECX:int) - Pointer to game context/unit structure containing handler list at offset 0x9c\nnEventMode (EDX:int) - Event notification mode/phase:\n                      0 = Resource cleanup initiated\n                      1 = Resource cleanup completed\n                      Other values = Additional context-specific modes\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Always returns successfully if context is valid. Never fails after validation.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- NULL context: Fatal error path (calls Ordinal_10023 with code 0x147b, never returns)\n- Empty handler list: Returns immediately without error\n- Handler execution: Each handler invoked even if prior handlers terminate\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x9c - Offset in context structure to handler linked list head pointer\n0x4 - Size of linked list node (pair of 32-bit pointers: [data, next])\n\nRelated Functions:\n- CleanupGameContextAndResources() - Calls this to notify handlers during cleanup with nEventMode=0,1\n- FUN_6fb8cf80() - Invoked handler with data from list node\n- Ordinal_10023() - Fatal error handler (does not return)",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Unit", "PARAM_2", "MOD_UNIT", "SRC_UnitSnd.cpp"]
    },
