      "comment": "Retrieves unit state status code based on on-screen position and flag flags.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get current game type via FUN_6fb8b5c0 and FUN_6fb8b600\n2. Determine default status (1-6) from game type; range [1,6]\n3. Query unit position (nXPos, nYPos) and tile properties via Ordinal_10326/10329\n4. Get tile data via Ordinal_10342 (dwSlotData)\n5. Search primary slot data (Ordinal_10030/10034):\n   - Calculate grid coordinates: nDeltaX = nXPos-slot_x, nDeltaY = nYPos-slot_y\n   - Iterate through slots; on match check flags at +0x18 offset\n   - Extract ushort flags at offset +6\n6. Check flag bits in sequence:\n   - 0x20 set → return 1 (FLAG_BLOCKED)\n   - 0x08 set → return 2 (FLAG_HIDDEN)\n   - 0x10 set → return 3 (FLAG_FROZEN)\n   - 0x40 set → return 4 (FLAG_SPECIAL)\n   - 0x80 clear & 0x400 clear → return default (nDefaultState)\n   - 0x80 set → return 6 (FLAG_UNWALKABLE)\n   - 0x400 set → return 5 (FLAG_SLOWING)\n7. If primary search fails, query secondary slots (Ordinal_10035)\n8. Repeat slot search against secondary slot array\n9. Return nDefaultState if no match found\n\nParameters:\ndwUnitId (uint): Unit identifier (ECX register, __fastcall)\n\nReturns:\nint: Status code 1-6 based on tile/unit flags\n1 = FLAG_BLOCKED\n2 = FLAG_HIDDEN  \n3 = FLAG_FROZEN\n4 = FLAG_SPECIAL\n5 = FLAG_SLOWING\n6 = FLAG_UNWALKABLE\nor nDefaultState (usually 1) if no flags match\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Game type determines default status (1-6); clamped to valid range\n- No slot found: returns nDefaultState\n- Slot found but pointer NULL: returns nDefaultState\n- Searches both primary and secondary tile slots\n- Flag checking order critical (0x20 checked before 0x400)",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_StatList", "PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Path", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "STRUCT_Skill", "STRUCT_ItemData", "PARAM_1", "PROP_LOOPHEAVY", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
