      "instructions": ["0xB7090|SUB|ESP, 0xc", "0xB7093|PUSH|EBX", "0xB7094|PUSH|ESI", "0xB7095|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0xB7097|PUSH|EDI", "0xB7098|MOV|EBX, EDX", "0xB709A|PUSH|ESI", "0xB709B|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [ESI]", "0xB709D|MOV|ECX, dword ptr [ESI + 0x4]", "0xB70A0|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x10], EAX", "0xB70A4|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x18], ECX", "0xB70A8|CALL|0x6fb98c9e", "0xB70AD|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x10], EAX", "0xB70B1|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [ESP + 0xc]", "0xB70B5|TEST|EAX, EAX"],
      "comment": "Get unit skill effect offset based on class and type.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load unit class (0=player, 1=monster, 2=object) from unit structure\n2. If class is 0 (player): retrieve player class index and validate < 7\n3. Else if class is 1 (monster): retrieve monster ID and validate <= 0x23e\n4. Retrieve effect table from appropriate global: player or monster tables\n5. Check effect table type and apply special handling for poison/curse effects\n6. Verify table is non-NULL; return 0 if NULL\n7. Get base effect offset from table field (offset 0x50 in monster, 0x28 in player)\n8. Return 0 if base offset is NULL\n9. Get skill type (2-6) via FUN_6fb86df0\n10. Apply skill type bonus: base + ((type-2) * 0x4)\n11. If bApplyBonus flag set, add 0x18 to result\n12. Return final offset value\n\nParameters:\n  pUnit (UnitAny *) - Unit structure; effect offset calculated for this unit\n  nApplyBonus (int) - Non-zero to apply additional 0x18 bonus to result\n\nReturns:\n  int - Byte offset to effect value; returns 0 if invalid or no effects\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Returns 0 if effect table pointer is NULL\n  - Returns 0 if base effect offset is NULL\n  - Fatal error if player class >= 7 or monster ID >= 0x23f\n  - Note: Function uses 8 stack-allocated temporaries optimized away\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x7 - NUM_PLAYERCLASS limit\n  0x23e - NUM_MONSTERCLASS limit (0x23f with boundary)\n  0x28 - Player effect offset field in table\n  0x50 - Monster effect offset field in table\n  0x4 - Per-level skill type bonus\n  0x18 - Apply bonus offset\n\nRelated Ordinals:\n  Ordinal_10369 - Initialize/validate unit attributes\n  Ordinal_11013 - Reload unit data if uninitialized\n  Ordinal_10023 - Fog.LogMessage for error reporting\n  Ordinal_10342 - D2Common.GetUnitStat get stat values\n  Ordinal_10001 - GetUnitRoom / validate value\n  Ordinal_10057 - D2Common process stat/value",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PARAM_2", "MOD_UNIT", "SRC_UnitSnd.cpp", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
