      "api_count": 12,
      "api_calls": ["UNITS_GetDirection", "UpdateAnimationModeFromStates", "UNITS_GetDirection", "UpdateAnimationModeFromStates", "GetMonsterArmorType", "UNITS_GetDirection", "UpdateAnimationModeFromStates", "FogAssert", "UNITS_GetRoom", "GetEntityField", "...+2 more"],
      "instructions": ["0xB7280|SUB|ESP, 0x2c", "0xB7283|PUSH|EBX", "0xB7284|PUSH|EBP", "0xB7285|PUSH|ESI", "0xB7286|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0xB7288|PUSH|EDI", "0xB7289|PUSH|ESI", "0xB728A|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [ESI]", "0xB728C|MOV|ECX, dword ptr [ESI + 0x4]", "0xB728F|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x14], EAX", "0xB7293|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x30], ECX", "0xB7297|CALL|0x6fb98c9e", "0xB729C|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x30], EAX", "0xB72A0|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [ESP + 0x10]", "0xB72A4|TEST|EAX, EAX"],
      "comment": "Apply skill/spell effects and modifiers to unit based on skill class and level.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Read unit skill class (offset 0x10), skill level (offset 0x4), and special flags from unit\n2. If skill class = 1: Check skill type (0x0f, 0x6e) and apply class-specific validations\n3. If skill type = 0x0f and class = 1: Skip effect application (special case)\n4. If skill type = 0x6e: Effect only applies if skill class = 8, else exit with current value\n5. Read skill effect table pointer from g_ppSkillEffectArray indexed by skill level\n6. Check for curse restrictions: if immunity flag set OR curse count exceeded, use g_pCurseSpellEffect\n7. Otherwise use selected skill effect pointer from effect table\n8. Extract effect properties: duration, min value, max skill level, offset multiplier (<<8)\n9. Calculate base duration divisor: duration / (effective_value * multiplier)\n10. Get frame counter elapsed since last update: current - unit.last_update_frame\n11. If effective_value > 1 and elapsed < (2/3 * duration): return early with scaled value\n12. Calculate three damage samples: base_offset, base_offset+multiplier, base_offset-multiplier\n13. Select max damage sample among the three\n14. Determine skill amplification flag based on skill class/type combinations\n15. Get skill effect modifiers via GetUnitSkillEffectOffset()\n16. Compute final effect value via FUN_6fb8d210()\n17. If result non-zero: apply damage scaling via FUN_6fb8d640() based on unit context\n18. If local modifier value set: check secondary effect with FUN_6fb8ebc0()\n19. Update unit.last_update_frame to current frame counter\n20. Return computed effect value or modifier value\n\nParameters:\n  pUnit (UnitAny*) - Unit to apply skill effect to; must not be NULL\n\nReturns:\n  uint - Computed skill effect value or modifier value; 0 if effect not applicable\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Skill class 1 (spell-specific): Additional type validation required\n  - Skill type 0x0f: Only applies if skill class = 1\n  - Skill type 0x6e: Only applies if skill class = 8\n  - Curse damage capped by max curse count check\n  - Unit context matters: player unit uses 0xff damage cap, other units use 0xc8\n  - Frame rate adaptive: returns scaled value if insufficient time elapsed\n  - NULL unit assertion will terminate program at line 0x1536\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x0f - Special skill type marker (immunity checks)\n  0x6e - Curse-type skill identifier\n  0x8 - Skill class for curse effects\n  0x1 - Player unit class marker\n  0x3, 0xf - Special skill class combinations requiring amplification\n  0x23f - Maximum skill level threshold\n  0x58, 0x50, 0x54 - Unit structure offsets (effect pointers)\n  0x5c, 0x58, 0x54, 0x60 - Effect structure offsets (values)\n  0x64 - Base effect duration constant (100 frames)\n  0xa8 - Unit last_update_frame offset\n  0xa0/0xff - Damage scaling multiplier ratio\n  0x55555556 - Magic constant for (x*2/3) calculation\n\nStructure Layout:\n  Offset | Size | Field Name           | Type        | Description\n  0x00   | 4    | unit_id              | uint        | Unique unit identifier\n  0x04   | 4    | skill_level          | uint        | Current skill points/level\n  0x10   | 4    | skill_class          | uint        | Skill classification (0=spell, 1=phys)\n  0x50   | 4    | effect_min_damage    | uint        | Minimum skill effect value\n  0x54   | 4    | effect_max_damage    | uint        | Maximum skill effect value\n  0x58   | 4    | effect_duration      | uint        | Duration of effect in frames\n  0xa8   | 4    | last_update_frame    | uint        | Last frame counter update",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "MOD_UNIT", "STRUCT_Room2", "STRUCT_ItemData", "PARAM_1", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData", "STRUCT_Unit", "PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Path", "STRUCT_Skill", "SRC_UnitSnd.cpp"]
