      "comment": "Retrieve and conditionally initialize unit animation state values.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load state value from unit pointer [pnState + 0x00]\n2. Load mode value from unit pointer [pnState + 0x04]\n3. Call Ordinal_10369 (D2Common - Retrieve unit animation result) to get current state\n4. Test if state value is zero (uninitialized)\n5. If state is non-zero, return immediately with existing state value\n6. If state is zero, call Ordinal_11013 (D2Common - Initialize animation state) with retrieved values\n7. Return initialized state value in EAX\n\nParameters:\n  pnState (int *) - Pointer to state data structure containing animation state and mode fields\n  IMPLICIT ECX - Function parameter passed in ECX register (__fastcall convention)\n\nReturns:\n  int - State value: non-zero if already initialized, updated/initialized value if zero\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Ordinal_10369: Unknown D2Common ordinal - appears to query unit animation state\n  - Ordinal_11013: Unknown D2Common ordinal - appears to initialize animation state conditionally\n  - Early return when state != 0 avoids reinitialization\n  - Local nResult stores Ordinal_10369 output before state check",
