      "comment": "Returns the appropriate aura effect table for a unit based on its aura properties.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract aura class and index from unit structure (first two DWORDs)\n2. Initialize aura effect table ID via Ordinal_10369 (D2Common.GetUnitAuraState)\n3. If aura class is zero, initialize defaults via Ordinal_11013 (D2Common.InitializeAuraClass)\n4. Bounds check: ensure aura index does not exceed 0x23E (574 maximum auras)\n5. Look up aura table pointer in g_pAuraTableArray at [index]\n6. Special case: if aura is poison effect (matches g_pPoisonEffectMarker):\n   - Check alternate attack flag via GetStructureFieldBit()\n   - If flag set, return alternate attack aura table (g_pAltAttackAuraTable)\n   - Check additional bit flag via GetBitFlag()\n   - If set, return alternate attack aura table\n7. Special case: if aura is curse effect (matches g_pCurseEffectTable):\n   - Check if unit exceeds max curse count via CheckUnitExceedMaxCurseCount()\n   - If yes, retrieve aura state via Ordinal_10342 (D2Common.GetAuraState)\n   - Convert to class via Ordinal_10057 (D2Common.ConvertAuraStateToClass)\n   - Convert to character via Ordinal_10001 (D2Common.CharacterFromClass)\n   - If result is null, return null aura table (g_pNullAuraTable)\n8. Return the aura effect table pointer\n\nParameters:\n- pUnit (UnitAny *): Unit structure containing aura class at offset 0 and aura index at offset 4\n\nReturns:\n- undefined4 * pointer to aura effect table (g_pAltAttackAuraTable, g_pCurseEffectTable, g_pNullAuraTable, or indexed aura table)\n- NULL/empty table for invalid or blocked aura conditions\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Poison effect units with alternate attack flag get alternate attack aura table instead of poison table\n- Curse effect units exceeding max curse count return null aura table\n- Invalid aura index (>= 0x23F) triggers assertion failure and program termination\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x23E: Maximum valid aura index (574)\n- 0x1398: Source code line number for assertion\n\nRelated Functions:\n- Ordinal_10369: Retrieves aura effect table ID from unit\n- Ordinal_11013: Initializes aura class defaults\n- Ordinal_10342: Gets aura state from unit\n- Ordinal_10057: Converts aura state to class ID\n- Ordinal_10001: Converts class ID to character representation\n- GetStructureFieldBit: Checks alternate attack flag in unit structure\n- GetBitFlag: Checks additional bit flag\n- CheckUnitExceedMaxCurseCount: Validates curse count limits",
