      "instructions": ["0xB7E60|SUB|ESP, 0x10", "0xB7E63|PUSH|EBX", "0xB7E64|PUSH|EBP", "0xB7E65|PUSH|ESI", "0xB7E66|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0xB7E68|PUSH|EDI", "0xB7E69|MOV|EBP, EDX", "0xB7E6B|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [ESI]", "0xB7E6D|MOV|ECX, dword ptr [ESI + 0x4]", "0xB7E70|PUSH|ESI", "0xB7E71|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x20], EBP", "0xB7E75|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x14], EAX", "0xB7E79|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x18], ECX", "0xB7E7D|CALL|0x6fb98c9e", "0xB7E82|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x18], EAX"],
      "comment": "Apply an aura effect to a unit with optional damage cost.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load aura info from unit pointer: get table index, damage value, skill level\n2. If aura not initialized, initialize it from global aura table (Ordinal_11013: InitializeAuraData)\n3. Validate aura table index is valid (less than 14 for hit class)\n4. If invalid, assert and exit with error code -1\n5. Calculate base damage from hit class table, scaling by 0x100 precision\n6. Apply divisor from unit's resistances (offset 0x16), default to 1\n7. If cost not applied (nApplyCost == 0), set damage to 0.0\n8. Call FUN_6fb8d210 to apply damage effect to unit\n9. Update unit's last aura apply timestamp (offset 0x28)\n10. Return early if aura initialization not needed\n11. Load aura type and damage from selected aura table\n12. Check curse count if aura is curse type, use null table if exceeded\n13. Validate aura table exists, return if null\n14. Select aura table offset based on nAuraType (4 vs other)\n15. If aura has active status and acceptable apply frequency:\n16.    - Iterate through existing aura effects on unit (from offset 0x27 linked list)\n17.    - Compare each aura's type against current effect's type\n18.    - If same type, call appropriate cleanup (FUN_6fb8d670) or update (FUN_6fb8cf80)\n19.    - Update game state counter timestamp\n20. Apply final damage to unit with FUN_6fb8d210\n21. Apply secondary effect (skill ID from aura table) with FUN_6fb8d640\n\nParameters:\npUnit (ECX): Pointer to unit structure - unit receiving aura effect\nnAuraType (EDX): Aura type identifier - determines damage lookup offset (4=skill attack, other=normal attack)\nnApplyCost (Stack[0x4]): Cost application flag - if 0, damage zeroed; if 1, normal damage applied\n\nReturns:\nvoid - modifies unit state in place, updates timestamps and active aura list\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Hit class > 13 triggers assertion and program termination\n- Unit class > 0x23e triggers assertion and program termination\n- Curse aura exceeding max count uses null table instead of normal curse effects\n- Poison and poison attacks may redirect to alternate attack aura table (Ordinal_10342, Ordinal_10057, Ordinal_10001)\n- Apply frequency throttling: only applies if frame counter >= 14 since last apply\n- Divide-by-zero protection: unit resistance (offset 0x16) defaults to 1 if 0\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x100: Fixed-point damage scaling factor (24.8 format)\n0x80: Rounding constant for division (128)\n0xf: Bitmask for hit class validation\n0xe: Hit class upper bound\n0x23e: Unit class upper bound (574)\n0x16: Unit offset - resistance divisor\n0x28: Unit offset - last aura apply timestamp\n0x27: Unit offset - head of aura effect linked list\n0x19: Aura table field - aura type value\n0x4: Aura type identifier for skill attacks\n\nNote: Function uses SSA temporaries (iVar*, DVar*, bVar* variables) optimized away at assembly level. These are compiler-generated intermediate calculations not directly renameable in decompiled view.",
