      "comment": "Apply aura state transition effects to a unit based on aura type and state\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract aura class (nAuraClass) from unit's aura array index\n2. Normalize aura state: if state is 0, initialize by calling Ordinal_11013\n3. Branch based on unit aura state (0 or 1):\n   CASE 0 - Unit has no aura:\n     a. Extract action code from unit aura state\n     b. Switch on action codes: 0,4,13=RemoveEffect; 7,8=ToggleAnimation; 9=PlayAnimation; C=DamageEffect; F,10=ConditionalEffect\n     c. Call appropriate effect handler (FUN_6fb88890, FUN_6fb87e60, etc)\n   CASE 1 - Unit has active aura:\n     a. Get aura table pointer from g_pAuraTableArray[nAuraClass]\n     b. Validate nAuraClass <= 0x23e, else crash with assertion\n     c. Check special aura conditions: poison/curse tables with field bits/curse count limits\n     d. Extract skill ID (iVar7) from unit's skill system, default 0x13f if not found\n     e. If action=0xE (unknown action), remap to specific action based on aura table identity\n     f. If action=7, apply alternate remapping for select aura tables\n     g. If action < 0xE, dispatch to effect handler via jump table at &DAT_6fb886c4\n4. Return after effect handling\n\nParameters:\n  pUnit (ECX) - UnitAny pointer, unit receiving aura effect\n  nAuraState (EDX) - uint, aura effect action code (0-16 range)\n  nInitialAuraClass (Stack[4]) - uint, initial aura class, if 0 then extracted from unit\n\nReturns:\n  void, effects applied in-place\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If pUnit is NULL on action 9, triggers assertion with crash via FUN_6fb9a10f\n  - If nAuraClass > 0x23e, triggers assertion with crash\n  - Poison/curse table checks use GetStructureFieldBit and GetBitFlag to detect conflicting auras\n  - Curse count validation rejects curse if unit exceeds max curse limit\n  - Unknown action 0xE has complex remapping logic to alternate action based on aura table source\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x35 - offset in UnitAny for aura state field\n  0x28 - offset in UnitAny to store frame counter on animation start\n  0x23e - max valid aura class index (DOM_SKILL_CLASS_COUNT)\n  0x18e,0x191 - skill animation IDs for action 9\n  0x13f - default skill ID if not found in unit",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Unit", "PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PARAM_3", "MOD_UNIT", "SRC_UnitSnd.cpp", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
