      "instructions": ["0xB8890|SUB|ESP, 0x18", "0xB8893|PUSH|EBX", "0xB8894|PUSH|EBP", "0xB8895|PUSH|ESI", "0xB8896|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0xB8898|PUSH|EDI", "0xB8899|MOV|EDI, EDX", "0xB889B|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [ESI]", "0xB889D|MOV|ECX, dword ptr [ESI + 0x4]", "0xB88A0|PUSH|ESI", "0xB88A1|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x18], EDI", "0xB88A5|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x14], EAX", "0xB88A9|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x20], ECX", "0xB88AD|CALL|0x6fb98c9e", "0xB88B2|MOV|EBX, dword ptr [ESP + 0x10]"],
      "comment": "Apply aura state animation effects for monster units with skill animations\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load unit type, class ID, and calculate aura index from unit pointer\n2. Validate unit type; reinitialize if needed (type == 0)\n3. Retrieve skill animation index via GetSkillAnimationIndex()\n4. Check if unit in animation state (type==1) with blocking skill (0x92) -> return if blocked\n5. Apply skill animations to unit using FUN_6fb8d210()\n6. If unit == current game context player, apply visual effect with FUN_6fb8d640(0xff)\n7. For type==1 && param2==0: invoke skill end/transition handlers (FUN_6fb886f0, FUN_6fb897a0)\n8. Check aura class byte flags (& 0xf0); if == 0xa0 -> return (locked state)\n9. For type==1 (monster):\n   - Reload unit class data, validate aura index < 0x23f\n   - Select aura table based on conditions: poison override, curse limits, or default\n   - If table valid, select animation frames based on param2 (skill level):\n     - param2==3||13: Check FUN_6fb8e720() gate; use offsets 0x30/0x38\n     - else: use offsets 0x34/0x3c\n   - Compare selected frame 0x2e9; if match, apply secondary frame 0x2ea/0x2eb\n   - Apply animation with FUN_6fb8d210()\n10. For type==0 (player):\n   - Reload unit data, validate player class < 7\n   - Select class animation table from g_ppPlayerClassTable[]\n   - Similar frame selection as monster path (offsets 0x00/0x04 vs 0x04/0x04)\n   - Apply animation frame\n11. Final: Store global frame counter in unit[0x28]; update _g_dwGameStateCounter\n\nParameters:\n  pUnit (UnitAny *) - Unit entity pointer; ECX register implicit\n  nAuraState (int) - Aura state code (0,3,4,13 for skills, etc.)\n\nReturns: void; side effects: unit animation state updated, global state modified\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - NULL unit assertion at final check (line 0x6fb88b7c)\n  - Type==1, aura index >= 0x23f: fatal assertion\n  - Type==0, player class >= 7: fatal assertion\n  - Poison/curse table selection requires helper function checks\n  - Blocking skill state (0x92) prevents animation application\n  - NOTE: Function uses 18 SSA compiler temporaries optimized away in decompilation\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x92 = blocking skill check ID\n  0xf0, 0xa0 = aura state byte flags\n  0x23f = max monster aura class index\n  0x2e9, 0x2ea, 0x2eb = special animation frame IDs\n  0x28 = unit frame counter offset in unit structure\n  0xa0 = 256-byte offset for frame counter field\n\nOrdinal Functions:\n  Ordinal_10369 - Get unit aura class index\n  Ordinal_11013 - Reinitialize unit type/class data\n  Ordinal_10487 - Check unit skill/ability state\n  Ordinal_10342 - Get unit skill ID\n  Ordinal_10057 - Query skill properties\n  Ordinal_10001 - Get skill animation frame\n",
