      "comment": "Process and validate level game state initialization\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get game context from GetGameContext() ordinal call\n2. Retrieve current player unit from game context via D2Common.GetUnitStat (Ordinal_10342)\n3. Check if player unit exists; return if null\n4. Get unit's current level via D2Common.GetUnitStat (Ordinal_10057)\n5. Validate level ID does not exceed 0x84 (132 levels); assert and exit if invalid\n6. Check if level already initialized in g_nCurrentLevelId global; return if same\n7. Check game state array at [levelId] offset; if set, update g_nCurrentLevelId and return\n8. Search g_ppLevelSlotArrays list for matching level entry (array of up to 10 entries)\n9. If found, mark level as initialized in g_abGameStateData array\n10. Validate slot array structure at offset 0x28; if invalid or not initialized, return\n11. If slot initialized, check if frame counter exceeded 0x3e (62 frames) since last update\n12. If frame count threshold exceeded and FUN_6fb8da90 returns success, trigger skill equipment processing\n\nParameters:\nReturns: none\nNote: Function uses 9 stack-allocated temporaries optimized away\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x84 - Maximum level ID upper bound validation threshold\n0x3e - Frame counter threshold for skill equipment update check\n0x28 - Offset to slot validation flag within slot structure\n0x0a0 - Offset to last update frame counter within player structure\n0x2c - Offset to equipment slot ID within slot data",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Unit", "MOD_UNIT", "PARAM_0", "SRC_UnitSnd.cpp", "PROP_LOOPHEAVY"]
