      "comment": "Initialize and apply aura effects to a unit. Determines aura table, checks constraints, and applies active auras.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load aura type (param_1[0x0]), aura index (param_1[0x4]), and aura state (via Ordinal_10369)\n2. If aura type is 0x00, call Ordinal_11013 to refresh unit aura data\n3. Verify aura type == 0x01 (active aura flag); return if not set\n4. Capture current frame counter for timestamp tracking\n5. Reload and re-validate aura type, index, state\n6. Boundary check: aura index must be < 0x23f (575 max); assert and fail if exceeded\n7. Retrieve aura table from g_pAuraTableArray[aura_index]\n8. Poison Aura Path: If poison aura AND (structure field set OR bit flag set), use g_pAltAttackAuraTable\n9. Curse Path: If curse aura AND unit curse count exceeded, convert via Ordinal_10342/10057/10001; if result is null char, use g_pNullAuraTable\n10. Default Path: Use retrieved aura table\n11. If aura table is valid (not null): \n    - Load function pointer from aura table offset 0x6c\n    - If function pointer exists AND ValidateUnitTypeState succeeds (return 0):\n      - Verify unit pointer is not null\n      - Check if unit's aura activation flag (offset 0xa4) is clear\n      - If clear: Call aura application function via offset 0x6c with parameters\n      - Store frame counter in g_dwGameModeFlag and unit offset 0xa4\n      - Load and store configuration value (0x1e, 0x5a) in g_dwGameConfigValue\n      - Return early\n    - Reload aura type, index, state with validation\n    - If aura state == 0x08 (AURA_STATE_IMMUNIZE), call ProcessUnitAuraApplication\n\nParameters:\npUnit (UnitAny *) - Unit to apply auras to; checked for null; used to access aura flags and state\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Function always returns normally (no error codes); side effects on global state and unit data\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Assertion failures (aura_index >= 0x23f or null unit pointer) trigger FUN_6fb9a10f(-0x1) fatal error\n- Poison auras with special flags redirect to alternate attack aura table\n- Curse auras over limit redirect to null aura table (suppresses effect)\n- Units with active aura inhibit flag skip application step\n- Aura state 0x08 triggers secondary processing via ProcessUnitAuraApplication\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x23f (575) - Maximum valid aura index boundary check\n0xa4 - Unit struct offset for aura activation/inhibit flag\n0x6c - Aura table offset for application function pointer\n0x1e, 0x5a - Configuration parameters for game config lookup\n0x08 - Special aura state value triggering ProcessUnitAuraApplication\n\nRelated Functions:\n- ValidateUnitTypeState() - Validates unit state eligibility\n- GetGlobalFrameCounter() - Timestamp for aura application tracking\n- ProcessUnitAuraApplication() - Secondary aura processing for state 0x08\n- InitializeGameUnit() - Caller; initializes unit after creation",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Unit", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "MOD_UNIT", "PARAM_1", "SRC_UnitSnd.cpp", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
