      "comment": "Validates that sound data structure has proper initialization state and contains valid WAVE audio format.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Verify pSoundData->eDataState (offset 0x86) equals 2 (ESOUNDDATA_NOTPROCESSED)\n2. If state mismatch, trigger assertion failure with source location\n3. Extract dwDataState from pSoundData->dwNewBuffer (offset 0x70)\n4. Call Ordinal_10056 (likely Storm.dll wave format reader) to parse format from local stack buffer\n5. Validate returned wFormatTag (offset +0x16 from call output) equals 0x10 (PCM)\n6. Validate dwSampleRate (offset +0x0c from call output) equals 0x5622 Hz\n7. Check wBitsPerSample (offset +0xa from call output) equals 0x2 (16-bit)\n8. If all validations pass, store nWaveResult and dwDataState in pSoundData, set flag at offset 0x50\n9. Return 1 on success, 0 on validation failure\n\nParameters:\npSoundData (int *): Pointer to sound data structure, must have eDataState==2 at offset 0x86\n\nReturns:\n1 if all WAVE format validations passed\n0 if format validation fails or state assertion triggered\n\nSpecial Cases:\nReturns 0 on any format mismatch (not PCM, wrong sample rate, wrong bit depth)\nSets byte at offset 0x81 to 1 on any failure (error flag)",
