      "instructions": ["0xB9D60|MOV|EAX, [0x6fbd7b5c]", "0xB9D65|SUB|ESP, 0x34", "0xB9D68|PUSH|EDI", "0xB9D69|MOV|EDI, ECX", "0xB9D6B|CMP|EDI, EAX", "0xB9D6D|JZ|0x6fb89e35", "0xB9D73|PUSH|ESI", "0xB9D74|CALL|0x6fb8b600", "0xB9D79|MOV|ESI, EAX", "0xB9D7B|CALL|0x6fb998ee", "0xB9D80|CMP|EAX, 0x2", "0xB9D83|JZ|0x6fb89d8d", "0xB9D85|TEST|EDI, EDI", "0xB9D87|JNZ|0x6fb89e2e", "0xB9D8D|CALL|0x6fb998e8"],
      "comment": "Update the global current game ID state and initialize game resources if the ID changes.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load global game ID (g_nCurrentGameId) into EAX\n2. Compare with input nGameId parameter (in ECX)\n3. If IDs match, skip resource initialization and exit\n4. If different:\n   a. Call FUN_6fb8b600(nGameId) to perform game ID conversion\n   b. Call Ordinal_10044 - Get game state for validation\n   c. Check if state == 2 or if input nGameId is 0\n   d. If condition true:\n      - Call Ordinal_10004 - Get current difficulty level\n      - If difficulty != 0, call Ordinal_10006 - Initialize unit Y coordinate\n      - Load multiple dword values from offset 0x24-0x54 of structure\n      - Perform floating-point conversion of each value (FILD * FMUL)\n      - Store results to stack locations\n      - Call Ordinal_10044 - Apply converted coordinate values\n5. Store final nGameId value back to g_nCurrentGameId\n\nParameters:\nIMPLICIT ECX: nGameId - int, game ID to set as current\n               0 = initialize/reset, >0 = specific game\n\nReturns:\nNone (void)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If input nGameId equals current g_nCurrentGameId, function returns immediately without processing\n- Conversion only occurs if difficulty is valid (!= 0)\n- Magic number 0x6fbab414 is floating-point scale factor for coordinate conversion\n- Ordinal_10044: Get game state / Apply state changes (called twice)\n- Ordinal_10004: Retrieve difficulty level for validation\n- Ordinal_10006: Fetch unit Y coordinate for initialization\n\nNote: 13 stack-allocated floating-point temporaries optimized away by compiler",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_StatList", "STRUCT_Path", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "STRUCT_Room2", "STRUCT_ItemData", "PARAM_1", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
