      "comment": "Apply mouse coordinates to game state if conditions met\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. If state[0] (root) is non-NULL:\n     - If state[2] (target structure pointer) is non-NULL:\n       - Call Ordinal_10018 to get mouse X coordinate\n       - Store result at offset +0x41 in target structure\n     - Call Ordinal_10012 (likely mouse-related operation on root)\n  2. If state[2] (target structure pointer) is non-NULL:\n     - Set offset +0x30 to value 0x2 (flag or counter)\n     - Set offset +0x2c to value 0x0 (zero field)\n     - Clear state[2] (nullify target structure pointer)\n\nParameters:\n  IMPLICIT ECX - pState (int *): Pointer to state array [3 elements minimum]\n                 [0] = root/context pointer\n                 [1] = unknown/unused\n                 [2] = target structure pointer\n\nReturns:\n  void - modifies state array in-place\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Both NULL checks prevent operations: if state[0] or state[2] are NULL, operations skip\n  - State cleanup always occurs if state[2] exists (unconditional second block)\n  - Offset +0x41, +0x30, +0x2c suggest struct members in target structure\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x41 (65) - field offset for mouse X storage in target structure\n  0x30 (48) - field offset for status/flag (value set to 0x2)\n  0x2c (44) - field offset for counter/state (zeroed)\n  0x2 (2) - status flag value (meaning unclear without structure definition)",
