      "comment": "Calculate and apply dynamic color rendering with difficulty/expansion modifiers.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate unit channel type (param_1[2]) is valid, assert if null\n2. Classify unit from channel data (param_1[4]), get stat bonus and base quality\n3. Apply difficulty modifier if unit has special property (0x53 flag)\n4. Apply overall difficulty scaling (DAT_6fbd8090 global)\n5. Check unit ID against hardcoded ranges (0x1230-0x1259, 0x34-0x47, 0x1-0xf)\n6. Apply special expansion modifier for valid ranges (DAT_6fbd8094)\n7. Check expansion mode flag (DAT_6fbffa44) for further adjustments\n8. If expansion: calculate delta modifier (2*Ordinal_10050() - 100) / 3\n9. Apply delta modifiers based on color alpha flags (param_1[0] and param_1[1] & 2)\n10. Check if values unchanged: compare nColorValue with param_1[6] and float at param_1[7]\n11. If unchanged, verify 3 sequential comparison dwords match - if all match, return early (no update needed)\n12. Calculate rendering distance from position data\n13. Verify distance within render range (float distance vs fVar11)\n14. Apply coordinate scaling with global factor (DAT_6fbab418)\n15. Call rendering ordinals based on parameter flags\n16. Update all color data fields and return\n\nParameters:\npColorData (int*): Color data structure pointer (32 bytes)\n  [0] = Alpha channel flag (bool)\n  [1] = Option flags (0x2 = special effect)\n  [2] = Unit channel type (must be non-zero)\n  [3-5] = Previous color RGB values\n  [6] = Cached color value\n  [7] = Cached float value\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Updates color data in place\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Null unit channel triggers assertion and immediate exit\n- Early return if all color values match previous state\n- Expansion mode has complex modifier calculations based on difficulty\n- Magic number 0x51eb851f is signed division constant\n- Flag patterns: 0x2 in param_1[1] indicates special effect mode",
