      "comment": "Iterates game object slots and processes unit state transitions.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize pointer to game structure array (0x6fbff848)\n2. Loop through array (stride 0x20 bytes per entry)\n3. For each slot pointer (valid non-zero):\n   a. Get unit from offset +0x4\n   b. Lookup unit state via FUN_6fb8b480\n   c. Check if unit state byte at +0x3e is null (inactive)\n   d. If inactive: verify room transition (Ordinal_10013 - Unknown)\n   e. If room ready (Ordinal_10023 - Unknown), get room data (Ordinal_10018 - Unknown)\n   f. Store value at [*piVar3 + 0x41]\n   g. Execute transition (Ordinal_10012 - Unknown)\n4. Clear slot state: [*piVar3 + 0x30] = 2, [*piVar3 + 0x2c] = 0, *piVar3 = 0\n5. Continue until 0x6fbffa48 boundary reached\n\nParameters: None (uses global game state)\n\nReturns: void (modifies game structures in-place)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Early exits if slot pointer is null\n- Skips if unit state is active (non-null byte at +0x3e)\n- Handles missing room transition (Ordinal_10013 = 0)\n- Duplicate cleanup occurs when room ready fails\n\nOrdinal Mappings (Unknown - requires D2 DLL analysis):\n- Ordinal_10012: Room transition executor\n- Ordinal_10013: Room transition verifier\n- Ordinal_10018: Room data retriever (returns 32-bit value)\n- Ordinal_10023: Room readiness check",
