      "comment": "Initialize game state and manage expansion mode game structures.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get current game mode (Ordinal_10044 = D2Common.GetGameMode)\n2. Check mode-specific initialization status:\n   - If mode == 1: Call Ordinal_10003 (D2Common.IsMode1Active)\n   - If mode == 2: Call Ordinal_10004 (D2Common.IsMode2Active)\n3. If expansion mode active (g_dwExpansionModeActive != 0), iterate through slot structures:\n   a. Lock structures with Ordinal_10027 (D2Common.LockGameStructures)\n   b. For each slot structure at g_dwSlotSearchBase + offset (0x20 stride):\n      - Check if slot enabled via reserved1 pointer\n      - If enabled and pNode valid, get unit stat (Ordinal_10018 = D2Common.GetUnitStat) and store at offset 0x41\n      - Initialize slot structure fields (InitializeStructureFields)\n      - Unlock with Ordinal_10012 (D2Common.UnlockStructure)\n   c. Clear all slot data pointers in g_dwSlotSearchBase array via Ordinal_10008 (D2Common.ClearSlotData)\n4. Call InitializeGameSlots(nGameMode) to validate mode settings\n5. If initialization failed, check if mode changed (Ordinal_10044), call Ordinal_10045 (D2Common.ReleaseGameMode) and return\n6. If expansion mode still active, iterate through game structure array (g_ppGameStructureArray):\n   a. Lock structures with Ordinal_10027\n   b. For each structure slot (0x20 stride):\n      - Check occupied via pointer at [-2] offset\n      - If occupied and pointer valid, get unit stat (Ordinal_10018) and store at offset 0x41\n      - If pointer valid, set offset 0x30 to 2, offset 0x2c to 0, then clear pointer\n      - Unlock with Ordinal_10012\n   c. Clear all pointers in g_dwSlotSearchBase array\n7. Get game context (Ordinal_10002 = D2Common.GetGameContext) for data initialization\n8. If context valid, initialize game data array (g_pdwGameDataArray with 0x20 stride):\n   a. For each element, get initial value (Ordinal_10007 = D2Common.InitializeGameData)\n   b. Store value at offset -0x4 from current position\n   c. If value is 0, abort with ResetExpansionGameStructures() call and return\n   d. Loop until reaching 0x6fbffa44\n9. Set game state to 0 via SetCurrentGameState()\n10. Set expansion mode active flag to 1\n11. Get mode again (Ordinal_10044), if non-zero call Ordinal_10045 (D2Common.ReleaseGameMode)\n\nParameters:\n  void: No parameters, function modifies global game state\n\nReturns:\n  void: No return value, function modifies global game state variables\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If InitializeGameSlots returns non-zero: mode change triggers early exit\n  - If expansion mode not cleared properly: assertion failure via D2Common_AssertionOrdinal\n  - If game data initialization returns 0: immediate abort with ResetExpansionGameStructures\n  \nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x20 (32): Array element stride for slot structures and data arrays\n  0x41 (65): Offset in structure for unit stat value\n  0x2c (44): Offset for clearing structure field (state reset)\n  0x30 (48): Offset for status flag (set to 2 for inactive state)\n  0x6fbff848/0x6fbff840/0x6fbff844: Base addresses of managed data arrays\n  0x6fbffa40/0x6fbffa44/0x6fbffa48: Upper bounds for array iteration\n  \nNote: Function uses assembly-only temporaries for array boundary checks optimized away",
