      "comment": "Reset and clear game structure data when disabling expansion mode.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if expansion mode is active (g_dwExpansionModeActive != 0), return if inactive\n2. Push ESI for preservation (callee-saved register)\n3. Call Ordinal_10002 (Fog.dll MemRealloc - memory/state validation)\n4. Call Ordinal_10027 (unknown ordinal - phase 1 preparation)\n5. Iterate structure array (0x6fbff848, stride 0x20, limit 0x6fbffa48):\n   - Check structure flag at offset -2\n   - If structure pointer exists (*piVar2 != 0):\n     * Call Ordinal_10018 (D2Win.dll - unknown context, likely value extraction)\n     * Store result at structure offset +0x41\n     * Call Ordinal_10012 (unknown ordinal - process structure)\n   - Reset structure fields: offset 0x30=2, offset 0x2c=0, null pointer\n6. Call Ordinal_10027 (unknown ordinal - finalize cleanup)\n7. Iterate slot array (0x6fbff840, stride 0x20, limit 0x6fbffa40):\n   - Call Ordinal_10008 with uVar1 parameter\n   - Zero each slot entry\n8. Clear expansion mode flag (g_dwExpansionModeActive = 0)\n9. Restore ESI, return\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Function is guard-checked for expansion mode before execution\n- Two independent cleanup loops: structures and slots\n- Ordinal calls: Ordinal_10002, Ordinal_10027 (×2), Ordinal_10018, Ordinal_10012, Ordinal_10008\n- Note: Function uses stack-allocated temporaries optimized away by compiler\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x6fbffa44: Global expansion mode flag address\n- 0x6fbffa48: Structure array upper bound\n- 0x6fbffa40: Slot array upper bound\n- 0x6fbff848: Structure array start address\n- 0x6fbff840: Slot array start address\n- 0x20: Array element stride (32 bytes per entry)\n- 0x41: Structure field offset for Ordinal_10018 result\n- 0x30: State field offset (set to 2 during reset)\n- 0x2c: Configuration field offset (cleared to 0)\n\nOrdinal Mappings:\n- Ordinal_10002 = Fog.dll MemRealloc (validate/prepare memory state)\n- Ordinal_10027 = Unk