      "comment": "Initialize game mode state arrays with slot configuration.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call Ordinal_10002 to validate game state (returns 0=invalid, non-zero=valid)\n2. If validation fails, return 0 immediately  \n3. Check g_dwExpansionModeActive flag: if set, call assertion handler D2Common_AssertionOrdinal with fatal error 0xc0\n4. Initialize slot array pointer at g_pSlotInitArray base (0x6fbff844)\n5. Main slot loop - set mode-dependent values per address:\n   - If slot < 0x6fbff8c4: set to 1 (standard mode)\n   - Else if nGameMode==1: set to 2 (mode 1)\n   - Else: set to ((nGameMode != 2) - 1) & 6 (modes 0/2/3+)\n6. Call Ordinal_10007 to get slot status value\n7. Store result at puVar4[-1] (4 bytes before current)\n8. Advance 32 bytes (8 dwords) per iteration\n9. If slot pointer exceeds 0x6fbffa43: overflow detected - SetCurrentGameState(0), g_dwExpansionModeActive=1, return 1\n10. After slot initialization complete: if g_dwExpansionModeActive != 0:\n    - Call Ordinal_10002 for validation check\n    - If valid, call Ordinal_10027 to start structure processing\n    - Loop through game structures at g_ppGameStructureArray (8-dword stride):\n      - Check if piVar5[-2] is non-zero (enable flag)\n      - If structure pointer non-zero: call Ordinal_10018, store at +0x41\n      - Call Ordinal_10012 for structure cleanup\n      - Zero structure fields: +0x30=2, +0x2c=0, base=0\n    - Call Ordinal_10027 to finish structure processing\n11. Clean slot search base arrays (0x6fbff840 base, 32-byte stride, end 0x6fbffa40):\n    - Call Ordinal_10008(nModeRegister) per iteration\n    - Zero each array element\n12. Clear g_dwExpansionModeActive flag and return 0\n\nParameters:\n- nGameMode (ECX, fastcall): Game initialization mode (1, 2, or other value)\n\nReturns:\n- 0: Mode initialization completed successfully\n- 1: Buffer overflow during slot processing detected\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Note: Function uses 3 stack-allocated temporaries optimized away (nModeRegister, pCleanupArray, dwStateResult with undefined4 types - visible only in assembly as register spills)\n- Array boundaries enforce maximum sizes: 0x6fbffa40, 0x6fbffa43, 0x6fbffa48\n- Structure offsets: +0x41 (state), +0x30 (flags), +0x2c (data)\n- Ordinal calls documented: 10002=ValidateGame, 10007=QuerySlot, 10008=ClearCache, 10012=StructSetup, 10018=GetState, 10027=StructInit/Finalize\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x1: Mode indicator for base slot range\n- 0x2: Mode indicator for nGameMode==1  \n- 0x6: Bitmask result for other modes\n- 0x20 (32 bytes): Array element stride\n- 0xc0: Assertion fatal error code\n- 0x6fbff8c4, 0x6fbffa40, 0x6fbffa43, 0x6fbffa48: Array boundary markers",
