      "comment": "Initialize game slots and data structures for expansion mode.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if expansion mode enabled and initialization not already in progress (DAT_6fbffa40 == 0)\n2. Increment initialization lock counter to prevent reentrancy\n3. Get current expansion mode type (0/1/2) via Ordinal_10044\n4. Based on mode type, call appropriate initialization ordinal (10003/10004)\n5. If valid mode, clear expansion state flag then initialize game slots:\n   - Lock expansion structures with Ordinal_10027\n   - Iterate game slot nodes (g_dwSlotSearchBase..0x6fbffa40)\n   - For each active node: get temp value via Ordinal_10018, call Ordinal_10012\n   - Call InitializeStructureFields for each slot structure\n   - Unlock with Ordinal_10027 and clear slot array via Ordinal_10008\n   - Set expansion mode flag to 0\n6. Call InitializeGameSlots with mode type to populate game data array\n7. If InitializeGameSlots succeeds (dVar3 != 0), verify mode unchanged via Ordinal_10044\n8. If mode changed, call Ordinal_10045 (mode mismatch handler)\n9. Return 1 (success) if all initialized, else continue\n10. For final phase: iterate all game data slots via Ordinal_10002 check\n11. For each data slot: set state flag (1/2/0-6 based on mode), call Ordinal_10007\n12. If Ordinal_10007 returns 0, call ResetExpansionGameStructures and exit\n13. Call SetCurrentGameState(0) to finalize\n14. Set expansion mode active flag to 1\n15. Verify final mode via Ordinal_10044, call Ordinal_10045 if mismatch\n16. Unlock with Ordinal_10027 and decrement initialization lock\n\nParameters:\nIMPLICIT EDI: Slot type parameter (passed in EDI, used in Ordinal_10029)\nIMPLICIT ESI: Loop address parameter (used in structure iteration loops)\n\nReturns:\n0x1 (1) if successful initialization\n0x0 (0) if early exit or expansion already initialized\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Reentrancy protection via g_dwGameInitializationLock counter\n- Multiple mode types handled (0=base, 1=classic, 2=expansion)\n- Ordinal_