      "comment": "Initialize game environment with specified mode (single/multiplayer/expansion)\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check expansion mode flag (g_dwExpansionModeActive) and initialization lock (g_dwGameInitializationLock)\n2. Return 0 if mode not active or already initializing (lock exists)\n3. Increment initialization lock to prevent concurrent initialization\n4. Query current game mode using Ordinal_10044() (D2Common.GetGameMode)\n5. Determine target mode: if mode=2 then target=1, else target=2\n6. Initialize game slots for target mode via InitializeGameSlots()\n7. If multiplayer or expansion mode, perform additional initialization:\n   - Initialize structure fields for each game slot (InitializeStructureFields)\n   - Reset quest records and character states (Ordinal_10012, Ordinal_10027)\n   - Set expansion flags on structure fields\n8. Loop through game data array and initialize each data slot:\n   - Set data state based on current mode (0, 1, or 2)\n   - Call Ordinal_10007() (D2Common.CreateGameData) for each slot\n   - Return 0 if any slot fails to initialize\n9. Call SetCurrentGameState(0) to finalize\n10. Set g_dwExpansionModeActive = 1 and check mode consistency\n11. Decrement initialization lock to allow next initialization\n\nParameters:\n  None\n\nReturns:\n  dword - 1 if successfully initialized, 0 on failure or if already initializing\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Returns 0 immediately if expansion mode not active\n  - Returns 0 if another initialization is in progress (lock > 0)\n  - Validates mode consistency after initialization\n  - Clears expansion structures if initialization fails midway\n  - Assertion failure if mode inconsistency detected during slot initialization",
