      "comment": "Updates render viewport settings based on game state and camera scaling.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate slot table activity status; return if inactive\n2. Verify active slot existence; return if none\n3. Query render context mode via Ordinal_10930 (Storm.dll function)\n4. Determine viewport coordinates from structure at iVar5 (adjusted by mode)\n5. Calculate API camera scaling capability flags (0x40 = scaling enabled)\n6. If scaling enabled, compare current scale vs default at _DAT_6fbab420\n7. If scaled, multiply by scale factor at _DAT_6fbab41c and convert to integer\n8. Compare viewport mode against global tracking variable\n9. If changed: invalidate previous mode, apply new mode structure setup\n10. If no scaling enabled: clear g_pCameraZoomObject, reset zoom level\n11. If scaling enabled: create/update zoom object with calculated level (±6 range)\n12. Process camera height updates if applicable (compute scaled height, track time)\n13. Update slot tracking globals for next frame\n\nParameters:\nuint dwTimeElapsed (ECX) - Elapsed time in milliseconds for frame timing\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Updates global viewport state variables\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x04 - Render context offset in structure\n0x08 - Base viewport coordinate offset\n0x0c - Alternative coordinate offset for mode 0\n0x10 - Alternate coordinate offset for mode 1\n0x14 - Camera height field offset\n0x1c/0x20 - Slot index fields for processing\n0x40 - Scaling capability flag (API mask)\n0xff - Full opacity value for viewport mode\n0xfa - Default opacity threshold\n0xaa0-0xb3d - Configuration block range\n0x2ee/0x1c2 - Camera angle constants\n1.0 (default camera scale at _DAT_6fbab420)\n\nRelated Functions:\n- GetSlotTableActiveStatus() - Checks slot table activation\n- FUN_6fb8b5a0() - Retrieves slot count\n- Ordinal_10930(g_hRenderContext) - Gets render context mode (Storm.dll)\n- ValidateApiCapability() - Checks graphics API features\n- GetDefaultCameraScale() - Returns default camera scale value\n- FUN_6fb8d210() - Creates viewport object\n- FUN_6fb8d640() - Sets object property\n- FUN_6fb8d670() - Applies effect/color to viewport\n- FUN_6fb8d060() - Destroys viewport object\n- FUN_6fb8ec10()/FUN_6fb8ebc0()/FUN_6fb8ebe0() - Camera calculations\n- SetCurrentGameState() - Updates game state after render setup",
