      "comment": "Retrieve unit data structure by unit index\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if unit array base (g_pUnitArrayBase) is initialized (non-NULL)\n2. If NULL, return 0 (no units available)\n3. Validate unit index is in valid range [0, 0x125a) where 0x125a = 4698 max units\n4. If invalid, call assertion handler with error details\n5. Calculate unit structure offset: index * 0x8e (142 bytes per unit)\n6. Return pointer to unit data: base + calculated offset\n\nParameters:\ndwUnitIndex (uint): Index of unit to retrieve, range [0, 0x125a)\n\nReturns:\nvoid*: Pointer to unit data structure if valid, 0 if base uninitialized\nCalls assertion handler if index out of range\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Returns 0 (NULL) when g_pUnitArrayBase is not initialized\n- Asserts with line 0x5c if index >= 0x125a or index < 0\n- Unit structure size is 0x8e (142) bytes\n- Maximum valid unit index is 0x1259 (4697)",
