      "comment": "Retrieve a dword stat value from a unit by its index in the unit array.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load unit array base pointer from global g_pUnitArrayBase\n2. If pointer is NULL, return 0 (unit array not initialized)\n3. Validate unit index nUnitIndex is in valid range [0, 0x125a)\n4. If index < 0 or >= 0x125a: invoke assertion failure and terminate with error code 0xFFFFFFFF\n5. Calculate memory offset: (nUnitIndex * 0x8e) + 0x60, where 0x8e is the unit record size\n6. Load and return dword value from [g_pUnitArrayBase + offset]\n\nParameters:\n- nUnitIndex (int): Index into unit array, must be in range [0, 0x125a) or assertion fails\n  IMPLICIT ECX: Contains nUnitIndex (fastcall calling convention)\n\nReturns:\n- dword: Stat value at offset 0x60 within unit record if valid index, otherwise 0 if array not initialized\n- On invalid index: does NOT return, terminates via D2Common_AssertionOrdinal and FUN_6fb9a10f\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If g_pUnitArrayBase is NULL/zero, returns 0 immediately without checking index validity\n- Invalid indices trigger assertion and process termination (0xFFFFFFFF error code)\n- Magic offset 0x60 appears to reference a specific unit stat field (possibly mana, life, or other resource)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x8e (142 decimal): Size of each unit record in the global array\n- 0x125a (4698 decimal): Maximum valid unit index (exclusive upper bound)\n- 0x60 (96 decimal): Byte offset within unit record where stat value is stored",
