      "instructions": ["0xBB500|MOV|EAX, [0x6fbffa68]", "0xBB505|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0xBB507|JNZ|0x6fb8b50c", "0xBB509|XOR|AL, AL", "0xBB50B|RET|", "0xBB50C|TEST|ECX, ECX", "0xBB50E|JL|0x6fb8b527", "0xBB510|CMP|ECX, 0x125a", "0xBB516|JGE|0x6fb8b527", "0xBB518|LEA|EDX, [ECX + ECX*0x8]", "0xBB51B|SHL|EDX, 0x3", "0xBB51E|SUB|EDX, ECX", "0xBB520|LEA|EAX, [EAX + EDX*0x2]", "0xBB523|MOV|AL, byte ptr [EAX + 0x3d]", "0xBB526|RET|"],
      "comment": "Retrieves a unit pointer from the global unit array by index with validation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if global unit array base is initialized (g_pUnitArrayBase == 0)\n2. Validate unit index is within valid range (0 to 0x125a - 1)\n3. Calculate unit offset: g_pUnitArrayBase + (nUnitIndex * 0x8e)\n4. Extract unit pointer from array at calculated offset\n5. Return unit pointer as 32-bit value\n\nParameters:\nnUnitIndex (ECX, int) - Unit index to look up (0-4697)\n\nReturns:\nuint - Unit pointer from array, or 0 if array not initialized or index out of bounds\nAssertion failure if index invalid (calls FUN_6fb9a10f with 0xffffffff)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Returns 0 if g_pUnitArrayBase is NULL\n- Index must be in range [0, 0x125a), 0x125a = 4698 units max\n- Invalid index triggers assertion failure, does not return\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x8e - Unit structure size in bytes (142 bytes per unit)\n0x125a - Maximum valid unit index (4698 units)",
