      "comment": "Retrieves sound effect index byte from unit array by unit index with bounds validation\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if unit array base pointer (g_pUnitArrayBase) is initialized; return 0 if NULL\n2. Validate unit index within range: 0 <= nUnitIndex < 0x125a (4698 units max)\n3. If out of range, trigger assertion failure via D2Common_AssertionOrdinal (non-returning)\n4. Calculate byte offset: (nUnitIndex * 0x8e) where 0x8e (142) is unit struct size\n5. Read and return single byte at offset: g_pUnitArrayBase + 0x3e + calculated_offset\n6. Offset 0x3e (62 decimal) is sound effect index field within unit structure\n\nParameters:\nnUnitIndex (int) - Unit array index (0-based), must be < 0x125a; -1 triggers assertion\n\nReturns:\nByte value (0x00-0xFF) representing unit sound effect index/state on valid index\n0 if unit array not initialized\nNon-returning: FUN_6fb9a10f(0xffffffff) called on invalid index (assertion failure)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Negative indices trigger bounds check failure and assertion\n- Indices >= 0x125a trigger bounds check failure and assertion\n- NULL g_pUnitArrayBase returns 0 early (graceful null check)\n- Assertion path is non-returning (crashes/exits on out of bounds)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x125a (4698 decimal) - Maximum unit count in game array\n0x8e (142 decimal) - Size of unit structure in bytes\n0x3e (62 decimal) - Byte offset of sound effect index field within unit struct\n0xffffffff (-1) - Error parameter to FUN_6fb9a10f indicating assertion failure",
