      "comment": "Returns pointer to array element by index with bounds validation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate index range: 0 <= nIndex < 0x32 (50 elements)\n2. Check if global array pointer g_pElementArray is non-null\n3. If null, return 0 (NULL pointer)\n4. Calculate element offset: nIndex * 0x58 (88 bytes per element)\n5. Return base pointer + calculated offset\n6. If index out of range, trigger assertion failure\n\nParameters:\nnIndex (int, ECX): Zero-based array index [0..49]\n\nReturns:\nPointer to structure element if index valid and array initialized\nNULL (0) if array pointer is null\nAssertion failure if index out of bounds\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Returns NULL when g_pElementArray is null\n- Out-of-bounds access triggers fatal assertion\n- Element size is 0x58 (88) bytes\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x32 (50) - Maximum valid index (array element count)\n0x58 (88) - Size of each element in bytes",
