      "instructions": ["0xBB690|SUB|ESP, 0x5bc", "0xBB696|MOV|EAX, 0x3", "0xBB69B|PUSH|EBX", "0xBB69C|PUSH|EBP", "0xBB69D|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x284], EAX", "0xBB6A4|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x298], EAX", "0xBB6AB|XOR|EBX, EBX", "0xBB6AD|MOV|ECX, 0x4", "0xBB6B2|MOV|EAX, 0x2", "0xBB6B7|MOV|EBP, 0x4c", "0xBB6BC|PUSH|ESI", "0xBB6BD|PUSH|EDI", "0xBB6BE|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x1e8], 0x6fbd7f80", "0xBB6C9|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x1ec], 0x1", "0xBB6D4|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x1f0], 0x3b"],
      "comment": "InitializeSoundSystem - Initialize D2 sound system with unit and environment data\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Assert that global sound arrays (g_pUnitArrayBase, g_pElementArray) are NULL\n2. Format path to sounds.txt, load Excel table (Ordinal_10038 opens file, FUN_6fb994dc parses)\n3. Validate sounds.txt size is 0x125a rows using Ordinal_10210 \n4. On mismatch, print error with actual vs expected row count\n5. Allocate g_pUnitArrayBase for 0x125a sound units (each 0x8e bytes), clear to zero\n6. Populate sound units from Excel using Ordinal_10207 (field mapping), Ordinal_10209 closes file\n7. Format path to soundenviron.txt, load Excel table (repeat steps 2-3)\n8. Validate soundenviron.txt size is 0x32 rows, fail if mismatch with assertion\n9. Allocate g_pElementArray for 0x32 sound environments (each 0x58 bytes), clear to zero\n10. Populate sound environments from Excel using same pattern\n11. Post-process sound units: for each unit, calculate priority relationships\n    - Check if unit's Fade In flag (offset +0x3d) is set\n    - If not set, mark as set and record previous unit index\n    - Count non-empty fadeout references (offset +0x54, up to 3 per unit)\n    - Store count at offset +0x80\n12. Loop continues until processed all 0x125a units (offset advances by 0x8e per iteration)\n\nParameters:\n(void) - No parameters\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Initializes globals g_pUnitArrayBase and g_pElementArray on success; asserts and terminates on validation failure\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If g_pUnitArrayBase already allocated, assertion failure with \"sgptSoundHeaderTable____NULL\" terminates function\n- If g_pElementArray already allocated, assertion failure with \"sgptSoundEnvironTable____NULL\" terminates function\n- If sounds.txt row count != 0x125a, prints mismatch error but continues (non-fatal)\n- If soundenviron.txt row count != 0x32, assertion failure terminates function\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x125a (4698) - Expected number of sound units in sounds.txt\n0x32 (50) - Expected number of sound environments in soundenviron.txt\n0x8e (142) - Size of each sound unit structure in bytes\n0x58 (88) - Size of each sound environment structure in bytes\n0x3d (61) - Offset of Fade In flag within sound unit\n0x54 (84) - Offset of fadeout reference array within sound unit\n0x80 (128) - Offset to store fadeout reference count within sound unit\n0x60 (96) - Offset of priority field within sound unit\n0xec (236) - Line number in C source for sounds.txt assertion\n0xfd (253) - Line number in C source for soundenviron.txt assertion\n\nNote: Function contains extensive hardcoded field descriptor tables (140+ entries) for Excel column mapping, each with: name pointer, field width, offset, and column ID.",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "SND_SYSTEM", "STRUCT_Room2", "TBL_sounds", "STRUCT_Room1", "STRUCT_ItemData", "PARAM_0", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData", "STRUCT_StatList", "SRC_SoundHdr.cpp", "PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Path", "MOD_SOUND", "STRUCT_Level", "STRUCT_Skill", "TBL_soundenviron"]
