      "comment": "Initialize and cleanup game units with sound processing.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if game is running via Ordinal_10002 (D2.IsGameRunning)\n2. If not running, return immediately\n3. Process element array cleanup via ProcessGameStructureArray()\n4. Call FUN_6fb8da40 and FUN_6fb8e570 for additional setup\n5. Call DeactivateExpansionMode to disable expansion content\n6. If element array (g_pElementArray) is allocated:\n   - Call Ordinal_10043(0x13d, 0) to stop element sounds\n   - Set g_pElementArray to NULL\n7. If unit array (g_pUnitArrayBase) is allocated:\n   - Loop through all unit records (stride 0x8e, limit 0xa2dec)\n   - For each active unit (offset 0x86 != 0):\n     * Verify unit doesn't exist via FindGameStructureByIdentifier\n     * Decrement g_dwSoundChannelCount by unit's channel count (offset 0x70)\n     * Call Ordinal_10059 to stop unit sounds\n     * Clear sound frame counter (offset 0x7c = 0)\n     * If sound state (offset 0x82) is 0: call Ordinal_10043(0x225, 0) to stop sounds\n     * Else: call Ordinal_10097 to play cleanup sound, clear state\n     * Clear sound animation (offset 0x6c = 0)\n     * Clear active flag (offset 0x86 = 0)\n   - Call Ordinal_10043(0x148, 0) for final sound cleanup\n   - Set g_pUnitArrayBase to NULL\n\nParameters:\n  (none) - Operates on global state: g_pElementArray, g_pUnitArrayBase, g_dwSoundChannelCount\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value\n\nNote: Function uses 2 stack-allocated temporaries (iVar2, ppiVar1) optimized away by compiler.",
