      "instructions": ["0xBC200|PUSH|EBX", "0xBC201|PUSH|EBP", "0xBC202|PUSH|ESI", "0xBC203|PUSH|EDI", "0xBC204|TEST|ECX, ECX", "0xBC206|MOV|EBP, EDX", "0xBC208|JZ|0x6fb8c2aa", "0xBC20E|MOV|EAX, [0x6fbffa68]", "0xBC213|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0xBC215|JZ|0x6fb8c2aa", "0xBC21B|TEST|ECX, ECX", "0xBC21D|JL|0x6fb8c2e8", "0xBC223|CMP|ECX, 0x125a", "0xBC229|JGE|0x6fb8c2e8", "0xBC22F|LEA|EDX, [ECX + ECX*0x8]"],
      "comment": "Adjust reference count for all items owned by a unit.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate unit index (0x0-0x1259) and unit array base pointer\n2. Calculate unit pointer: g_pUnitArrayBase + (nUnitIdx * 0x8e)\n3. Retrieve item count from unit.nItems [+0x3d] and first item from unit.nFirstItem [+0x60]\n4. If unit has items and (item reference data exists at [+0x8a] OR nAdjustment != -1):\n   a. Loop through all items: for each item starting at nFirstItem\n   b. Calculate item pointer: g_pUnitArrayBase + (nItemIdx * 0x8e)\n   c. Validate item index (0x0-0xa2dec)\n   d. If item exists and (no item header data at [+0x8a] AND nAdjustment == -1): assertion failure\n   e. Adjust item reference count: item[0x8a] += nAdjustment\n   f. Increment nItemIdx, continue to next item until nItemIdx >= nFirstItem + nItems\n\nParameters:\nnUnitIdx (ECX:4 int) - Unit array index to process (0-0x1259)\nnAdjustment (EDX:4 int) - Reference count adjustment value (typically +1 or -1)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value; asserts on invalid indices or missing item data\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- nAdjustment = -1: Requires valid item header data at offset 0x8a\n- nAdjustment != -1: Can proceed even if item header missing\n- Assertion failure on index out of bounds or missing required item data",
