      "instructions": ["0xBC3D0|PUSH|ECX", "0xBC3D1|MOV|EAX, [0x6fbffa68]", "0xBC3D6|PUSH|EBX", "0xBC3D7|PUSH|EBP", "0xBC3D8|PUSH|ESI", "0xBC3D9|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0xBC3DB|PUSH|EDI", "0xBC3DC|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x10], ECX", "0xBC3E0|JZ|0x6fb8c4d1", "0xBC3E6|XOR|EAX, EAX", "0xBC3E8|TEST|ECX, ECX", "0xBC3EA|SETZ|AL", "0xBC3ED|TEST|ECX, ECX", "0xBC3EF|MOV|EBP, EAX", "0xBC3F1|JZ|0x6fb8c406"],
      "comment": "Iterate sound data table and process audio entries based on game state changes.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if unit array base is initialized and state time is valid (0 or > 0x18 from current state)\n2. Initialize loop: nEntryIndex = 1, nTableOffset = 0x8e (entry stride)\n3. For each sound entry in table (while nTableOffset < 0x65ae7):\n   a. Calculate sound entry pointer from base + offset\n   b. Check if state flag at offset 0x86 is 0 (not loaded) AND has sound reference (offset 0x8a != 0 OR byte at 0x13 != 0)\n   c. If so: check if caller triggered update (param_1 == 0) or time delta > 0xf9 from session counter\n   d. If condition met: call ProcessSoundDataEntries to trigger sound initialization\n   e. If state at 0x86 == 1 (ready): call ordinal to get sound playback info, store volume values at offsets 0x1b, 0x1c, set state to 2 (active), validate state, decrement game mode counter\n4. Advance to next entry (offset += 0x8e) and repeat\n5. Update global game state time to passed parameter value\n\nParameters:\ndwGameStateTime - Current game state time (0 = force immediate processing, else time delta check)\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If g_pUnitArrayBase == NULL, entire operation skipped (early exit at 6fb8c4d1)\n- If dwGameStateTime != 0 AND delta from state <= 0x18, early exit without processing\n- Assertion error if sound entry state check fails (state must remain == 1 after initial check)\n- Game mode counter decremented on each active sound entry processed\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x8e - Sound entry size/stride in table\n0x65ae7 - Total bytes in sound data table (0x65ae7 / 0x8e = 0x8007 entries approx)\n0x86 - Offset to entry state flag (0=unload, 1=ready, 2=active)\n0x8a - Offset to sound reference pointer\n0x13 - Offset to sound data identifier byte\n0x1b, 0x1c - Offsets for volume/playback parameters\n0xf9 - Time delta threshold for processing (249 ticks)\n0xf - Game mode value threshold check\n0x18 - Minimum state time delta to trigger processing",
      "tags": ["SRC_SoundHdr.cpp", "MOD_SOUND", "SND_SYSTEM", "PARAM_1", "STRUCT_Other"]
