      "comment": "Wrapper function that plays a video and reconfigures graphics settings.\n\nClassification: Thunk/Wrapper - calls PlayVideoById then tail-jumps to ReadResolutionAndConfigureGraphics.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract video ID from pbVideoInfo[1] (offset +1 in structure)\n2. Call PlayVideoById with the extracted video ID byte\n3. Tail-jump to ReadResolutionAndConfigureGraphics to reload display settings\n\nParameters:\n- pbVideoInfo (ECX, byte *): Pointer to video info structure where:\n  - Offset +0: Unknown (not used by this function)\n  - Offset +1: Video ID byte passed to PlayVideoById\n\nReturns: void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- This is a thin wrapper combining video playback with graphics reconfiguration\n- Typical use case: after video cutscene, reload resolution/graphics settings",
