      "api_calls": ["FogAssert", "RemoveListNode", "FreeAsyncData", "ReleasePoolAllocation", "FogAssert"],
      "instructions": ["0xBC570|MOV|EAX, [0x6fbffa68]", "0xBC575|PUSH|EBX", "0xBC576|XOR|EBX, EBX", "0xBC578|PUSH|ESI", "0xBC579|PUSH|EDI", "0xBC57A|CMP|EAX, EBX", "0xBC57C|MOV|EDI, ECX", "0xBC57E|JNZ|0x6fb8c584", "0xBC580|XOR|ESI, ESI", "0xBC582|JMP|0x6fb8c5a3", "0xBC584|CMP|EDI, EBX", "0xBC586|JL|0x6fb8c63c", "0xBC58C|CMP|EDI, 0x125a", "0xBC592|JGE|0x6fb8c63c", "0xBC598|LEA|ECX, [EDI + EDI*0x8]"],
      "comment": "Release and cleanup sound channel resources for a given channel ID\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate channel ID is within valid range (0x0-0x1259)\n2. If g_pUnitArrayBase is null, set channel pointer to 0 and return\n3. Calculate channel data structure address: g_pUnitArrayBase + (dwChannelId * 0x8e)\n4. Check if sound channel is active via offset 0x86 (channel state)\n5. If channel is inactive (state == 0), return immediately\n6. If channel is active:\n   a. Verify no existing game structure reference (offset 0x82)\n   b. Subtract channel sample count from g_dwSoundChannelCount (offset 0x70)\n   c. Call Ordinal_10059 to cleanup audio subsystem\n   d. Clear channel data pointer (offset 0x7c)\n   e. If channel has auxiliary data (offset 0x82):\n      - Call Ordinal_10097 to release auxiliary resources\n      - Clear all channel-related fields (0x82, 0x6c, 0x86)\n   f. Otherwise call Ordinal_10043 with skill data flag (0x225, 0)\n7. Clear all channel fields regardless of branch taken\n\nParameters:\ndwChannelId - Channel identifier (0x0-0x1259), passed in ECX register per __fastcall\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- When g_pUnitArrayBase is null, function safely returns with zero pointer\n- Channel is only cleaned up if state field (offset 0x86) is non-zero\n- Range validation includes assertion that aborts on invalid ID\n- Auxiliary data path requires additional cleanup vs. standard skill data path\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x8e - Size of individual channel structure in unit array\n0x1259 - Maximum valid channel ID (4697 decimal)\n0x86 - Offset to channel state/status field\n0x70 - Offset to sample count within channel structure\n0x7c - Offset to channel data pointer\n0x82 - Offset to auxiliary data/resource handle\n0x6c - Offset to channel-specific resource reference\n0x225 - Skill data flag passed to Ordinal_10043\n\nRelated Functions:\n- ValidateSoundDataState() - Validate sound structure integrity after cleanup\n- FindGameStructureByIdentifier() - Lookup associated game structure\n- Ordinal_10059() - Audio subsystem cleanup notification\n- Ordinal_10097() - Release auxiliary/extended resource data\n- Ordinal_10043() - Skill data table cleanup",
      "tags": ["SRC_SoundHdr.cpp", "MOD_SOUND", "SND_SYSTEM", "PARAM_1"]
    },
