      "comment": "Return color value (float10) for a unit based on its type classification.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load global unit array base address from g_pUnitArrayBase\n2. If unit array not initialized, return default color (DAT_6fbab42c)\n3. Validate unit index nUnitIndex within range [0, 0x1259]\n   - If out of range, trigger assertion and exit\n4. Calculate unit record address: base + nUnitIndex * 0x8E bytes\n5. Load unit type field from offset 0x47 (32-bit value)\n6. Perform indexed jump on type value (0-4):\n   - Type 2: return g_flUnitType2Color\n   - Type 3: return g_flUnitType3Color\n   - Type 4: return g_flUnitType4Color\n   - Default: return g_flDefaultUnitColor\n\nParameters:\nECX nUnitIndex: Unit index in global unit array (0 to 0x1259)\n\nReturns:\nfloat10: Color value loaded from global color array based on unit type\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Uninitialized unit array returns default color (g_flDefaultUnitColor)\n- Invalid unit indices trigger assertion\n- Unit type field at offset 0x47 acts as index into color lookup",
