      "comment": "Retrieve the display color value for a unit based on its type.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load the global unit array base pointer\n2. If base pointer is null, return default color (0x44BBBB80)\n3. Validate unit index is in range [0, 0x1259]\n4. Calculate unit structure offset: index * 0x8e bytes\n5. Load unit type field at offset 0x47 (dword)\n6. Switch on unit type:\n   - Type 0 (Monster): return g_flUnitColorMonster (0x43C80000)\n   - Type 2 (Player): return g_flUnitColorPlayer (0x442F0000)\n   - Type 3 (NPC): return g_flUnitColorNPC (0x44BBBB00)\n   - Type 4 (Object): return g_flUnitColorObject (0xC4FA0000)\n   - Default: return g_flUnitColorDefault (0x42700000)\n\nParameters:\n  IMPLICIT ECX - nUnitIndex: Unit index to look up (range 0-0x1259)\n\nReturns:\n  EAX (FLD result): float10 color value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If unit array base is null, returns default color without validation\n  - Invalid indices trigger assertion and call to FUN_6fb9a10f(-1)\n  - All return values loaded via FLD instruction (x87 FPU)",
