      "comment": "Finds the unit slot index corresponding to a given unit class index.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate unit class index is in range [0x0, 0x1259]\n2. Calculate unit record pointer: base + (index * 0x8e)\n3. Read class value from unit record offset 0x3d\n4. If class <= 1, return original index\n5. Initialize search depth: class - 1, capped at 2\n6. If class < 4, call FUN_6fb8ebc0(class+1) to adjust depth; if returns 0, decrement depth\n7. Loop: Get current slot class via FUN_6fb8ebc0, add index offset\n8. Search array at offset +0x64: scan up to depth entries\n9. On match, return computed slot index; else continue\n10. If depth exhausted, return slot index\n\nParameters:\ndwUnitClassIndex: Unit class index (0x0-0x1259), passed in ECX per __fastcall\n\nReturns:\nMatching unit slot index\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Class <= 1: Returns original index unchanged\n- Invalid index (<0 or >0x1259): Triggers assertion, calls abort\n- Search depth limited to max 2 entries\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x8e: Unit record size in bytes\n0x3d: Offset to class field within unit record\n0x64: Offset to slot search array (100 bytes from record start)\n0x125a: Maximum valid unit class index + 1\n0x2: Maximum search depth\n\nStructure Layout:\n| Offset | Size | Field Name | Type | Description |\n| 0x00   | 8    | (unit data) | unknown | Unit record header |\n| 0x3d   | 1    | byUnitClass | byte | Class identifier |\n| 0x64   | 8    | dw_SlotArray | uint[2] | Search slot table |",
