      "comment": "Construct audio file path for unit by concatenating LOCAL/GLOBAL strings with unit data.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate dwUnitIndex (0x0-0x1259), retrieve unit base structure from g_pUnitArrayBase\n2. Select data path: LOCAL (0x0-0xb75) or GLOBAL (>= 0xb76)\n3. Calculate string length of selected data path using SCASB\n4. Copy path data to output buffer\n5. Select suffix path: \\MUSIC\\ (0x1230-0x1259) or _SFX_ suffix (others)\n6. Calculate suffix length\n7. Calculate destination buffer end position\n8. Copy suffix to end of path\n9. Retrieve unit structure data string and calculate its length\n10. Ensure final path length <= 0x4f bytes (80 char limit)\n11. Append unit data string to path\n12. (Implicit: buffer overflow check and unit indexing)\n\nParameters:\n  IMPLICIT dwUnitIndex (ECX, uint): Unit index (0x0-0x1259), maps to UnitAny array offset\n  IMPLICIT szDestPath (EDX, char*): Output buffer for file path (must be >= 80 bytes)\n\nReturns:\n  void (modifies szDestPath in-place)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - dwUnitIndex >= 0x1259: Triggers assertion failure via FUN_6fb9a10f\n  - dwUnitIndex >= 0xb76: Uses GLOBAL data path instead of LOCAL\n  - Final path length > 0x4f: Triggers assertion failure (buffer too small)\n  - NULL g_pUnitArrayBase: Results in NULL unit data (fallback handled)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x1259 (4697): Maximum valid unit index\n  0xb76 (2934): Threshold for LOCAL vs GLOBAL path selection\n  0x1230 (4656): Threshold for MUSIC vs SFX suffix selection\n  0x8e (142): Unit structure size (sizeof UnitAny)\n  0x4f (79): Maximum path length (80 char buffer limit)\n  0xffffffff (-1): Sentinel for string length calculations",
