      "comment": "Sets the game session flags for a unit in the global unit array.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load g_pUnitArrayBase pointer\n2. If base pointer is NULL, skip offset calculation\n3. If nUnitIndex is negative or >= 0x125A (4698), trigger assertion and exit\n4. Calculate unit offset: nUnitIndex * 0x8E (142 bytes per unit)\n5. Add offset to g_pUnitArrayBase to get unit record pointer\n6. Store g_dwGameSessionFlags value at offset 0x7C within unit record\n7. Call Ordinal_10059 (Storm.DLL ordinal - likely initialization)\n8. Call Ordinal_10063 (Storm.DLL ordinal - likely completion/sync)\n\nParameters:\nnUnitIndex (dword) - Index into unit array, range [0x00, 0x1259]; triggers assertion if out of bounds\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value; function assertion terminates on invalid index\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If g_pUnitArrayBase is NULL, writes to NULL+offset instead of returning\n- Unit record size is 0x8E bytes; field at +0x7C is flags field (4 bytes)\n- Maximum valid index is 0x1258 (not 0x1259, upper bound exclusive)\n- Max units in array: 4698",
