      "comment": "Search linked list for matching entry and check flag field\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. If nTarget is zero, return false (early exit)\n2. Load global list head pointer g_pListHead\n3. If list head is NULL, return false (empty list)\n4. Loop through linked list:\n   a. Load current node value (dword at offset 0x0)\n   b. Compare field at offset 0x8 with nTarget\n   c. If match found, proceed to step 5\n   d. Otherwise load next pointer (dword at offset 0x4)\n   e. If next pointer is NULL, return false (not found)\n   f. Continue loop\n5. If current node is non-NULL:\n   a. Check flag at offset 0x30 equals 1\n   b. Return true if flag == 1, false otherwise\n6. Return false if list empty or no match found\n\nParameters:\n  nTarget (int) - Target value to search for in linked list node field at offset 0x8\n\nReturns:\n  byte - true (non-zero) if entry found with flag field at offset 0x30 == 1; false (0) otherwise; false if nTarget is zero or list empty\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  NULL input (nTarget == 0) returns false\n  Empty list (g_pListHead == NULL) returns false\n  Match found but current node NULL returns false\n  Flag field != 1 returns false\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x8 - Comparison field offset in list node structure\n  0x4 - Next pointer offset in list node structure\n  0x30 - Flag field offset in list node structure\n  0x1 - Magic flag value (1 = enabled/success state)",
