      "comment": "Locate first valid inventory slot for player and validate contents.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate nPlayerId is non-zero, exit with NULL if invalid\n2. Load inventory list head pointer (g_pInventoryListHead), exit if NULL\n3. Walk inventory list comparing each node's player ID (offset +0x08) to nPlayerId\n4. On match, verify node is not NULL and inventory slot pointer (offset +0x2c) is not NULL\n5. Walk list again finding matching player to perform state validation\n6. Verify node's state flag at offset +0x30 equals 1\n7. Call IsInventoryPointerValid to validate inventory pointer contents\n8. Return g_InvalidTooltipMarker address on success; return NULL on any failure\n\nParameters:\nnPlayerId (int, ECX register): Player unique identifier to locate in inventory list\n\nReturns:\nint*: Address of g_InvalidTooltipMarker if valid inventory found, NULL on failure\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Player ID 0 is invalid, returns NULL\n- Empty inventory list returns NULL\n- Player not in list returns NULL\n- Inventory pointer NULL at offset +0x2c returns NULL\n- State flag at offset +0x30 must equal 1, else returns NULL\n- IsInventoryPointerValid returning 0 returns NULL\n\nNote: Function contains 2 SSA temporaries optimized away by compiler.\n\nRelated Functions:\n- IsInventoryPointerValid(): Validates inventory data integrity\n- RenderGameFrame(): Caller; uses result for tooltip display",
