      "instructions": ["0xBCF80|PUSH|EBP", "0xBCF81|PUSH|ESI", "0xBCF82|PUSH|EDI", "0xBCF83|MOV|EDI, ECX", "0xBCF85|TEST|EDI, EDI", "0xBCF87|MOV|EBP, EDX", "0xBCF89|JZ|0x6fb8d03a", "0xBCF8F|TEST|EBP, EBP", "0xBCF91|JZ|0x6fb8d03a", "0xBCF97|MOV|EDX, EDI", "0xBCF99|MOV|ECX, EBP", "0xBCF9B|CALL|0x6fb86cb0", "0xBCFA0|MOV|EAX, [0x6fc04018]", "0xBCFA5|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0xBCFA7|JZ|0x6fb8cfb7"],
      "comment": "Process unit inventory-related effects or animations based on slot and effect type.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate parameters: Check if nUnitIndex and nSlotIndex are non-zero; if either zero, assert with error code 0xce and exit\n2. Initialize unit: Call ValidateAndInitializeUnit with nSlotIndex parameter\n3. Search inventory list: Iterate through g_pInventoryListHead linked list to find node matching nUnitIndex at offset +0x8\n4. If inventory node not found or is NULL, return early\n5. Get unit data: Retrieve unit structure pointer via GetUnitDataByIndex using value at offset +0x4 of inventory node\n6. Call Ordinal_10059 (unknown D2Common function)\n7. Determine effect eligibility: Set fHasEffect=true if (unit_data[0x3e]==0) OR (inventory[0x45]!=0 AND inventory[0x4d]==0), else false\n8. Check inventory blocked: If inventory[0x28]!=0, return early (slot already processing)\n9. Validate effect type: If nEffectType==0 AND fHasEffect==true, return early (invalid combination)\n10. Retrieve updated unit data: Call GetUnitDataByIndex again\n11. Mark slot as processing: Set inventory[0x3d]=1\n12. Check unit enabled: If unit_data[0x40]==0, return early (unit not enabled)\n13. Validate slot type: If inventory[0x30]!=1, return early (incorrect slot type)\n14. Apply effect: Call FUN_6fb8d670 with parameters (inventory[0x8], 0, 0, unit_data[0x40] & 0xff)\n\nParameters:\nnUnitIndex (int, in ECX): Unit index for validation; zero triggers assertion\nnSlotIndex (int, in EDX): Slot index parameter passed to ValidateAndInitializeUnit\nnEffectType (int, Stack[0x4]): Effect type flag; determines early exit condition when combined with fHasEffect\n\nReturns:\nvoid: Function returns after completing effect processing or early exit conditions. Asserts and terminates if parameters invalid.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Assertion failure: nUnitIndex==0 or nSlotIndex==0 triggers assert(error=0xce) + FUN_6fb9a10f(-1) termination\n- Inventory node not found: Returns early without processing\n- Effect eligibility depends on two separate conditions OR'd together: (unit_data[0x3e]==0) indicates effect eligible; (inventory[0x45]!=0 AND inventory[0x4d]==0) indicates alternate eligibility\n- Multiple early returns prevent redundant processing when conditions not met\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0xce = Assertion error code for invalid unit/slot parameters\n0x8 = Offset to unit index field in inventory node\n0x4 = Offset to unit index field in inventory node structure\n0x28 = Offset to blocked/processing flag in inventory node\n0x45, 0x4d = Offsets to condition flags in inventory node (effect eligibility checks)\n0x3d = Offset to processing marker flag (set to 1 when processing)\n0x3e = Offset in unit data structure for effect state check\n0x40 = Offset in unit data for enabled flag and effect parameter (masked to 0xff)\n0x30 = Offset to slot type field in inventory node",
      "tags": ["MOD_SOUND", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PARAM_3", "STRUCT_Skill", "SND_SYSTEM", "SRC_SoundInst.cpp", "PROP_LOOPHEAVY", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control"]
