      "comment": "Initializes inventory item state by finding it in the inventory list and setting initialization flags.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate nItemId is non-zero\n2. Acquire head pointer of global inventory list (g_pInventoryListHead)\n3. Walk linked list comparing item ID at offset +8 until match found\n4. If no match found (end of list), return early\n5. If match found, retrieve item data via GetUnitDataByIndex() using value at offset +4\n6. Set initialization flag at offset +0x3d to 1\n7. Check if item has special property (byte at data offset +0x40 non-zero)\n8. If property exists AND state field at offset +0x30 equals 1, call FUN_6fb8d670 with item ID, flags, and property value\n\nParameters:\n- nItemId (ECX): Item identifier to locate in inventory list\n\nReturns:\nNone (void function)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If nItemId is 0, function returns immediately\n- If inventory list head is NULL, function returns immediately\n- If item not found in list, function returns early without error\n- Item property check requires both conditions: non-zero property byte AND state == 1\n\nNote: Function uses 2 SSA-generated temporaries (pvVar2, puVar1) optimized away by compiler. These variables represent transient linked list pointers and item data addresses, generated during list traversal and data lookups.",
