      "comment": "Updates inventory item position and clamps values to valid range.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate item ID and inventory list exists, return if not\n2. Search inventory linked list for matching item ID\n3. When found, verify item pointer is not null\n4. Convert integer position Y to float\n5. Add offset constant (g_flMinimumBounds) to param Y for adjusted position\n6. Validate stack offset check\n7. Store converted X, Y, and adjusted Y in inventory item structure\n8. Clamp X value: use minimum if below g_flMinValue, use 2000.0 if above _g_flUnitType4Color\n9. Clamp Y value: use minimum if below g_flMinValue, use 2000.0 if above _g_flUnitType4Color\n10. Call FUN_6fb8ec60 with clamped values to calculate bounds\n11. Store result in inventory item bounds field\n\nParameters:\nnItemId (int, ECX) - Item ID to locate in inventory list\nnPositionY (int, EDX) - Y position offset as integer\nflX (float, Stack[0x4]) - X coordinate\nflY (float, Stack[0x8]) - Y coordinate offset\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Modifies inventory item fields in-place\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Returns early if nItemId is 0\n- Returns early if inventory list is empty\n- Returns early if item not found in inventory list\n- Assertion triggered if stack offset validation fails (at 0x1a6)",
