      "instructions": ["0xBD210|SUB|ESP, 0x18", "0xBD213|MOV|EAX, [0x6fc0401c]", "0xBD218|PUSH|EBX", "0xBD219|PUSH|EBP", "0xBD21A|PUSH|ESI", "0xBD21B|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0xBD21D|PUSH|EDI", "0xBD21E|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x10], EDX", "0xBD222|MOV|EBP, ECX", "0xBD224|JNZ|0x6fb8d232", "0xBD226|POP|EDI", "0xBD227|POP|ESI", "0xBD228|POP|EBP", "0xBD229|XOR|EAX, EAX", "0xBD22B|POP|EBX"],
      "comment": "Initializes game object properties and allocates object instance slot.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if game state enabled (g_dwGameObjectStateFlag != 0), return 0 if disabled\n2. Validate nObjectId parameter (non-zero), return 0 if invalid\n3. Retrieve unit data via GetUnitDataByIndex(nObjectId)\n4. Get current game session flags/ticks via GetGameSessionFlags()\n5. Check unit state byte at offset 0x3c (must be non-zero), return 0 if uninitialized\n6. If unit has property list (short at offset 0x45 != 0):\n   - Iterate linked list at g_pGameObjectListHead to find compatible item\n   - Check if item quantity matches unit property (offset 0x60)\n   - Verify item valid (offset 0x3d == 0) and duration satisfied\n   - If conditions met, jump to finalization (LAB_6fb8d519)\n7. Find first available object slot in g_pGameObjectListHead (stride 0x59 bytes)\n8. Clear 22 dwords at slot + 1 null byte (initialization to zero)\n9. Set slot[0] = 1 (active marker)\n10. Call Ordinal_10058() - enable sound context\n11. Increment g_dwObjectInstanceCounter, store in slot[2]\n12. Return if slot allocation failed (slot == NULL)\n13. Populate object properties:\n    - slot[14] = flY (Y coordinate)\n    - slot[1] = nObjectId\n    - slot[13] = dwGameFlags + flX (computed value)\n    - slot[9] = dwFlags\n    - slot[7] = 0xFF (opacity)\n    - slot[15] = unit property byte from offset 0x4e\n14. If nMode == 0 (default mode):\n    - Initialize local X/Y to 0.0, base distance to 0x43a00000 (1024.0)\n    - Call FUN_6fb8ec60(0.0, 0.0) for default distance calculation\n    - Store result in slot[6]\n15. Else (nMode > 0):\n    - Call FUN_6fb8d550(nMode, nObjectId, &flLocalX) to get positioned coordinates\n    - Load threshold from g_flMinimumFloatThreshold\n    - Clamp flLocalX/flLocalY to [threshold, 2000.0] range\n    - Call FUN_6fb8ec60(clampedX, clampedY) for distance\n    - Store in slot[6]\n    - Retrieve unit data again\n16. Determine property index:\n    - If unit data NULL, get from GetGameContext() + Ordinal_10362(game, nMode)\n    - Else if unit type != 4, check unit property (0xCA), retrieve stat index\n    - Store in slot[8] with fallback to g_flDefaultCameraScale\n17. If nMode == game context, add 'P' flag to slot[15]\n18. If nMode non-zero, call Ordinal_10058() again and ValidateAndInitializeUnit(nMode)\n19. Return slot[2] (object instance ID)\n\nParameters:\n  nObjectId (__fastcall ECX): Unit/entity ID to initialize\n  nMode (__fastcall EDX): Mode 0-3, 0=default 1-3=positioned modes\n  flX (stack): X coordinate displacement or iteration parameter\n  flY (stack): Y coordinate displacement or iteration parameter\n  dwFlags (stack): Object flags/state bits\n\nReturns:\n  dword: Object instance ID (slot[2]) on success, 0 on validation failure\n  \nSpecial Cases:\n  - Returns 0 if game state disabled (g_dwGameObjectStateFlag == 0)\n  - Returns 0 if nObjectId invalid or unit data check fails\n  - Returns 0 if no available object slot in g_pGameObjectListHead\n  - Ordinal_10362 maps game mode to internal property index\n  - Assertion failures trigger FUN_6fb9a10f(-1) termination\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x3c: Unit state flag offset (0=uninitialized, non-0=active)\n  0x45: Unit property list duration offset (short)\n  0x60: Unit property ID offset (dword)\n  0x3d: Item validity flag offset (0=valid, non-0=consumed)\n  0x4e: Unit type/class offset (byte)\n  0x59: Object slot stride in g_pGameObjectListHead (89 bytes)\n  0xCA: Special unit mode indicator\n  0x18: Mode-specific flag offset\n  0xFF: Default opacity value\n  0x43a00000: 1024.0 in float format\n  0x44FA0000: 2000.0 in float format",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "SND_SYSTEM", "SRC_SoundInst.cpp", "STRUCT_ItemData", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData", "STRUCT_StatList", "STRUCT_MonsterData", "PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Path", "MOD_SOUND", "STRUCT_Skill", "PARAM_5", "STRUCT_Other"]
