      "comment": "Calculate viewport coordinates for game rendering.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Retrieve game context using GetGameContext()\n2. Get offset coordinates for game context (Ordinal_10335)\n3. Get offset coordinates for target game state (Ordinal_10335)\n4. If offset type is 0xa27 (special viewport mode):\n   - Convert floating-point Y coordinate to integer (lVar2)\n   - Convert floating-point X coordinate to integer (lVar3)\n   - Store converted Y in nAdjustedX (note: assembly layout)\n   - Store converted X in nAdjustedY\n5. Set output array[2] to constant 640.0 (viewport width)\n6. Calculate and write X differential to output[0]\n7. Calculate and write Y differential (doubled) to output[1]\n8. Return\n\nParameters:\nnGameState (undefined4) - Game state/entity identifier\nnOffsetType (int) - Offset type; 0xa27 triggers coordinate conversion\npOutCoords (float *) - Output array: [0]=X diff, [1]=Y diff (doubled), [2]=640.0\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Results written to pOutCoords array\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- When nOffsetType != 0xa27, uses stack-based fallback coordinate calculation\n- Y coordinate is doubled before output (param_3[1] = 2 * (nAdjustedY - nOffsetX))\n- Magic constant 0x44200000 (640.0 in IEEE float) represents viewport width\n\nStructure Layout:\nOutput array (pOutCoords):\nOffset | Size | Field Name | Meaning\n0      | 4    | [0]        | X coordinate difference (float)\n4      | 4    | [1]        | Y coordinate difference * 2 (float)\n8      | 4    | [2]        | Viewport width constant 640.0",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PARAM_3", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
