      "instructions": ["0xBD640|PUSH|ESI", "0xBD641|TEST|ECX, ECX", "0xBD643|JZ|0x6fb8d665", "0xBD645|MOV|EAX, [0x6fc04018]", "0xBD64A|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0xBD64C|JZ|0x6fb8d665", "0xBD64E|MOV|ESI, dword ptr [EAX]", "0xBD650|CMP|dword ptr [ESI + 0x8], ECX", "0xBD653|JZ|0x6fb8d65e", "0xBD655|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [EAX + 0x4]", "0xBD658|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0xBD65A|JNZ|0x6fb8d64e", "0xBD65C|POP|ESI", "0xBD65D|RET|", "0xBD65E|TEST|ESI, ESI"],
      "comment": "Search for inventory item by ID and set a value field.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate input: if nItemId is 0, return\n2. Get global inventory list head (g_pInventoryListHead)\n3. Validate list exists, if NULL return\n4. Loop through linked list:\n   a. Load current node pointer from list\n   b. Check if node's ID field (offset +0x8) matches nItemId\n   c. If match found, break loop\n   d. Advance to next node (offset +0x4)\n   e. If next node is NULL, return\n5. If valid node found (ESI != 0), write dwValue to offset +0x1c\n6. Return\n\nParameters:\n- nItemId (ECX/dword): Inventory item ID to search for\n- dwValue (EDX/dword): Value to assign to the matched item's field at offset 0x1c\n\nReturns:\n- void: Function modifies item in-place if found\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If nItemId is 0, function returns immediately without searching\n- If inventory list is empty/null, function returns\n- If item ID not found in list, function returns without modifying anything\n- Function silently fails (no error return) if item not found\n\nNotes:\n- Uses __fastcall convention: parameters in ECX (nItemId), EDX (dwValue)\n- Linked list structure: [node_ptr][next_ptr][...][id_field@offset_8][...][target_field@offset_1c]\n- Called by item/skill/aura modification routines",
      "tags": ["PARAM_2", "PROP_LEAF", "PROP_SMALL"]
    },
