      "instructions": ["0xBD670|SUB|ESP, 0x8", "0xBD673|PUSH|EBX", "0xBD674|PUSH|ESI", "0xBD675|PUSH|EDI", "0xBD676|MOV|EDI, EDX", "0xBD678|MOV|EDX, ECX", "0xBD67A|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0xc], EDI", "0xBD67E|TEST|EDX, EDX", "0xBD680|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x10], EDX", "0xBD684|JZ|0x6fb8d7e4", "0xBD68A|MOV|ECX, dword ptr [0x6fc04018]", "0xBD690|TEST|ECX, ECX", "0xBD692|MOV|EAX, ECX", "0xBD694|JZ|0x6fb8d7e4", "0xBD69A|MOV|ESI, dword ptr [EAX]"],
      "comment": "Applies a fade effect timer to an inventory item in the game world.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate unit ID parameter is non-zero\n2. Search inventory list for unit entry matching nUnitId\n3. Return early if unit not found or list is empty\n4. Verify unit doesn't have active fade (check field at offset 0x28)\n5. Get unit stat data via GetUnitDataByIndex()\n6. Adjust dwDuration based on nFadeType: 0xff uses max_physical_resist (offset 0x3f), 0x00 uses max_cold_resist (offset 0x40)\n7. Check if fade already active (field 0x45):\n   - If active: verify same fade type and remaining time won't exceed bound, then return\n   - If inactive: check previous fade type, set flag at 0x3d if conditions met\n8. If dwDuration == 0: if nDelay > 0, trigger assertion failure; else find unit and set fade_type_stored (0x1c)\n9. If dwDuration > 0: retrieve current game ticks, store previous state, set all fade parameters (0x49, 0x51, 0x4d, 0x55), mark fade active (0x45 = 1)\n\nParameters:\nnUnitId (ECX) - Unit identifier to apply fade to; must be non-zero\nnFadeType (EDX) - Fade type: 0x00 (cold), 0xff (physical), or other values\nnDelay (Stack[0x4]) - Delay in game ticks before fade starts\ndwDuration (Stack[0x8]) - Duration of fade effect in game ticks; 0 = no fade\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value; modifies inventory state and fade parameters\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Returns early if nUnitId is 0 or inventory list is empty\n- Returns if unit already has fade effect (may exceed time bounds)\n- Asserts and exits if dwDuration is 0 AND nDelay > 0 (invalid state)\n- Sets field 0x3d flag based on fade type transition rules\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x08 - Offset to unit ID field in inventory node\n0x1c - Offset to stored fade type field\n0x28 - Offset to parent reference field (indicates active fade)\n0x3d - Offset to conditional flag (set during fade setup)\n0x3f - Offset to maximum physical resistance value\n0x40 - Offset to maximum cold resistance value\n0x45 - Offset to fade active flag\n0x49 - Offset to previous state backup\n0x4d - Offset to fade type field\n0x51 - Offset to fade start tick field\n0x55 - Offset to fade end tick field\n0xff - Special fade type value (physical)\n\nNote: Function uses 2 stack-allocated temporaries optimized away (local_4, local_8).",
      "tags": ["MOD_SOUND", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PARAM_4", "SND_SYSTEM", "SRC_SoundInst.cpp", "PROP_LOOPHEAVY", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
