      "comment": "Iterate inventory list and mark matching unit slot as active, triggering fade effect if conditions met.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get global inventory list head pointer\n2. Return if list is empty (NULL)\n3. Loop through linked list nodes:\n   a. Load unit ID from offset +0x4 of node data\n   b. If matches dwUnitId parameter:\n      - Fetch unit data via GetUnitDataByIndex()\n      - Set offset +0x3d in node to 1 (mark as active/visible)\n      - Check if byte at unit data offset +0x40 is nonzero\n      - Check if offset +0x30 in node equals 1\n      - If both true, call ProcessInventoryFadeEffect with unit fade value\n   c. Advance to next node via offset +0x4 pointer\n4. Exit when node pointer NULL\n\nParameters:\ndwUnitId (ECX): Unit ID to match against inventory list entries\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- No-op if inventory list is empty\n- Fade effect only triggered if both unit has nonzero fade value AND node flag at +0x30 is 1\n- List traversal via offset +0x4 pointer chain (doubly-linked or pointer table)",
