      "comment": "Iterate through inventory linked list and apply fade effects to qualifying items.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load head of inventory linked list from g_pInventoryListHead\n2. If list is empty (NULL), return immediately\n3. Loop through each inventory node:\n   a. Extract unit value from node offset +0x0\n   b. Extract unit index from node offset +0x4\n   c. Check if index is in player inventory range (0x1230-0x124a)\n   d. If outside range, skip to next node\n   e. Call GetUnitDataByIndex to retrieve unit structure\n   f. Mark fade effect processed at node offset +0x3d\n   g. Check if unit has fade effect value (byte at unit offset +0x40)\n   h. Check if node state flag at offset +0x30 equals 1\n   i. If both conditions true, call ProcessInventoryFadeEffect with fade value\n   j. Move to next node via offset +0x4 (linked list pointer)\n4. Continue loop until next node pointer is NULL\n\nParameters:\nNone (accesses global inventory list)\n\nReturns:\nvoid (no return value)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Empty inventory list: function returns immediately without processing\n- Out-of-range unit indices: skipped automatically\n- Missing fade effect: item processed but no effect applied\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x1230 (4656): Minimum player inventory slot index\n- 0x124a (4682): Maximum player inventory slot index\n- 0x04: Offset to unit index within inventory node\n- 0x08: Offset to first process parameter in inventory node\n- 0x30: Offset to state flag within inventory node\n- 0x3d: Offset to fade effect marker within inventory node\n- 0x40: Offset to fade effect value within unit structure\n- 0xff: Mask to extract fade effect byte",
