      "comment": "Iterate through inventory list and apply fade effects to units matching stat type criteria.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get pointer to inventory list head (g_pInventoryListHead)\n2. If list is empty, return immediately\n3. For each inventory node in the linked list:\n   - Extract unit ID from node offset +4\n   - Get unit stat using GetUnitStatByIndex() and compare against nStatType1\n   - If not matching nStatType1, get stat again and compare against nStatType2\n   - Extract unit index from offset +4, verify range [0x33..0x48)\n   - Get unit data via GetUnitDataByIndex()\n   - Mark inventory node at offset +0x3d as active (set to 1)\n   - If unit has transparency flag (byte at pUnitData+0x40) AND inventory fade state equals 1:\n     * Call ProcessInventoryFadeEffect() with inventory ID, parameters 0, transparency byte\n   - Move to next node via offset +4\n4. Repeat until next node pointer is NULL\n\nParameters:\nnStatType1 (int) - First unit stat type to match (ECX)\nnStatType2 (int) - Second unit stat type to match (EDX)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Empty inventory list handled via initial NULL check\n- Unit index boundary check ensures valid stat lookup [0x33..0x48)\n- Transparency flag at unit+0x40 must be non-zero to trigger fade effect\n- Inventory state at offset +0x30 must equal 1 for fade processing\n- Note: Function uses 1 stack-allocated temporary optimized away (dwTemp at ESP-0x4 phantom)",
