      "comment": "Iterates through inventory items and applies visibility flags to units matching specified stat IDs.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load head pointer of inventory linked list (g_pInventoryListHead)\n2. If list is empty, exit function\n3. For each inventory item in linked list:\n   a. Load unit index from item offset 0x4\n   b. Call GetUnitStatByIndex to retrieve unit stat value\n   c. If unit stat does NOT match nStatId1 AND does NOT match nStatId2:\n      - Verify unit index is in valid range (0x47 < index < 0xCA)\n      - Call GetUnitDataByIndex to get unit data structure\n      - Set visibility flag at item offset 0x3D to 1\n      - If unit has property at offset 0x40 != 0 AND item flag at offset 0x30 == 1:\n        * Call ProcessInventoryFadeEffect with unit property value\n   d. Advance to next inventory item in linked list\n4. Exit when list terminator (NULL pointer) reached\n\nParameters:\nnStatId1 (ECX) - int: First unit stat ID to exclude from visibility updates\nnStatId2 (EDX) - int: Second unit stat ID to exclude from visibility updates\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Empty inventory list: Function returns immediately without processing\n- Unit index out of valid range (< 0x48 or >= 0xCA): Item skipped\n- Unit property at offset 0x40 is zero: Fade effect not applied even if visibility flag is set\n- Item flag at offset 0x30 != 1: Fade effect not applied\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x47 - Lower bound check for unit index (72 decimal)\n0xCA - Upper bound check for unit index (202 decimal)\n0x3D - Offset of visibility flag in inventory item structure\n0x30 - Offset of flag field in inventory item structure\n0x40 - Offset of property field in unit data structure\n0x8 - Offset of unit ID/reference in inventory item structure\n0x4 - Offset of unit index in inventory item structure",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Inventory", "PARAM_2", "STRUCT_Skill"]
