      "comment": "Process inventory item visibility and apply fade effects to valid items\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize pInventoryCurr from global inventory list head g_pInventoryListHead\n2. Loop through linked list of inventory items\n3. For each item, extract base structure pointer (nItemStructBase) from list node\n4. Read unit ID (dwUnitId) from structure offset +4\n5. Validate unit ID in range [0xb76, 0x122f] (valid unit index bounds)\n6. If valid: call GetUnitDataByIndex(dwUnitId) to fetch unit data structure\n7. Set visibility flag (offset +0x3d) to 1\n8. Check unit visibility byte at pUnitData offset +0x40\n9. If visible AND item field at +0x30 equals 1: call ProcessInventoryFadeEffect\n10. Move to next list node via pInventoryNext (offset +4 from current)\n11. Continue until pInventoryNext is NULL\n\nParameters:\n(none - accesses global g_pInventoryListHead)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - modifies inventory item visibility and fade state in place\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If g_pInventoryListHead is NULL, function exits immediately\n- Unit IDs outside range [0xb76, 0x122f] are skipped\n- Fade effect only applied if visibility byte is non-zero AND item field +0x30 is 1\n- Magic constants: 0xb75/0xb76 (lower unit index bound), 0x122f/0x1230 (upper unit index bound)\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0xb76 - Lower bound for valid unit index (first inventory item ID)\n0x122f - Upper bound for valid unit index (last inventory item ID)  \n0x3d - Offset in item structure for visibility flag\n0x40 - Offset in unit data for visibility byte\n0x30 - Offset in item structure for enabled flag\n0x8 - Offset in item structure for some parameter passed to fade effect\n0x4 - Offset in linked list node for next pointer\n\nRelated Functions:\n- GetUnitDataByIndex() - Fetch unit data by ID\n- ProcessInventoryFadeEffect() - Apply fade animation to item",
