      "comment": "Process inventory list fade effects for all inventory items.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load head pointer from global inventory list (g_pInventoryListHead)\n2. If list is empty, return immediately\n3. For each node in the linked list:\n   a. Load unit index from offset [node + 0x4]\n   b. Call GetUnitDataByIndex to retrieve unit data pointer\n   c. Set fade effect flag at [node + 0x3d] = 1\n   d. Check if unit data valid and unit state flag set (0x40):\n      - If both conditions true, call ProcessInventoryFadeEffect\n      - Pass unit slot from [node + 0x8], fade level from unit data offset 0x40\n   e. Advance to next node via pointer at [node + 0x4]\n4. Continue until NULL pointer encountered\n\nParameters:\n  None\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Empty list: function exits without processing\n  - Invalid unit data: ProcessInventoryFadeEffect is not called\n  - Unit state flag (0x40): Controls whether fade effect is processed\n\nNote: Function uses SSA-optimized temporaries (pvVar2, iVar1) that cannot be individually renamed - these are synthetic compiler-generated values during decompilation.",
