      "comment": "Search inventory list for item with ID in specific range\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load global inventory list head pointer from g_pInventoryListHead\n2. If list is empty (NULL), jump to return 0\n3. Loop through linked list:\n   a. Read type field at [node+0x30]\n   b. If type equals 2, skip to next node\n   c. Read item ID field at [node+0x4]\n   d. Check if ID > 0x122f (4655 decimal)\n   e. Check if ID < 0x125a (4698 decimal)\n   f. If both conditions true, return 1 (found)\n   g. Move to next node at [node+0x4]\n4. If loop completes without match, return 0 (not found)\nParameters:\n(none)\nReturns:\n1 if inventory item with ID in range [0x1230, 0x1259] found (type != 2)\n0 if no matching item found or list empty\nSpecial Cases:\nItem type field at offset 0x30 must not equal 2 to qualify as match\nOnly items with ID in range 0x1230-0x1259 are searched\nNote: Compiler optimizations create SSA temporaries (iVar1, iVar2) for compound expression: (iVar2 = *(int *)(*piVar3 + 4), 0x122f < iVar2). Only pInventoryNode variable is directly renameable by standard tools.\nStructure Layout:\nOffset | Size | Field Name | Type | Description\n0x0    | 4    | next       | ptr  | Pointer to next inventory node\n0x4    | 4    | itemId     | uint | Item identifier\n0x30   | 4    | itemType   | uint | Item type (0=normal, 2=skip)\nRelated Functions:\n- FUN_6fb8e830 - Calls this function to validate inventory state",
