      "comment": "Render game viewport with inventory/unit sorting and dynamic positioning\nAlgorithm:\n1. If game object state flag clear, exit immediately\n2. If object render flag set and game session flags divisible by 3, create initial object\n3. Bubble sort inventory list by depth (Z-order), position (Y), then pixel x-coordinate\n4. For each inventory item: validate state, apply mouse input, update animation state\n5. For selected units with post-game render flag: calculate viewport position, update smoothing\n6. Manage unit slot animation states and transitions (start/stop animations based on time)\n7. Render unit display slot if distance threshold met\n8. Update animation state tracking and game session flags based on difficulty\n9. Update color modifier values (expansion) based on rendering state\n\nParameters:\nnGameTick (uint) - Current game session tick counter, used for animation timing\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Phantom variables at stack offsets -0x1c, -0x20, -0x24, -0x28, -0x2c, -0x3c, -0x48, -0x4c are optimized away\n- Multiple nested loops with float comparisons for smooth coordinate transitions\n- Complex conditional logic for unit slot activation and rendering visibility\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x3c - Unit depth/priority field offset\n0x18 - Unit position Y field offset\n0x34 - Unit position X field offset\n0x1230-0x124b - Special unit ID range check\n0xb75, 0x122f - Inventory unit ID boundaries\n0x45, 0x4d, 0x55, 0x51 - Animation state/timing field offsets",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "SND_SYSTEM", "STRUCT_Room2", "SRC_SoundInst.cpp", "STRUCT_ItemData", "PARAM_1", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData", "STRUCT_StatList", "PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Path", "MOD_SOUND", "STRUCT_Skill", "STRUCT_Other", "PROP_LOOPHEAVY"]
