      "api_calls": ["RemoveListNode", "RemoveLinkedListNodes", "FogAssert"],
      "instructions": ["0xBE570|PUSH|EBX", "0xBE571|PUSH|ESI", "0xBE572|PUSH|EDI", "0xBE573|CALL|0x6fb8b080", "0xBE578|MOV|EAX, [0x6fc04018]", "0xBE57D|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0xBE57F|JZ|0x6fb8e5d9", "0xBE581|MOV|EDI, dword ptr [EAX]", "0xBE583|TEST|EDI, EDI", "0xBE585|JZ|0x6fb8e5d5", "0xBE587|MOV|EDX, EDI", "0xBE589|MOV|ECX, 0x6fc04018", "0xBE58E|CALL|0x6fb998d6", "0xBE593|MOV|ESI, dword ptr [EDI + 0x28]", "0xBE596|LEA|EBX, [EDI + 0x28]"],
      "comment": "Validate and initialize all units in the inventory list, processing item stacks and applying UI updates.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Clear game state before processing\n2. Get inventory list head from global pointer\n3. Loop through inventory node chain:\n   a. Check if current node is null - if so, mark game object state flag and return\n   b. Dereference node pointer to get inventory object\n   c. If inventory object null, continue to next iteration\n   d. Call Ordinal_10059 (game loop tick/frame advance)\n   e. Iterate through items in inventory at offset 0x28 (linked list of unit IDs)\n   f. For each item, call ValidateAndInitializeUnit with unit ID\n   g. Call Ordinal_10062 (game loop cleanup/finalize)\n   h. Check if inventory object at offset 0x30 equals 1 (active/visible flag)\n   i. If true, call ApplyMouseCoordinates with inventory object at offset 0x2c (cursor position)\n   j. Check if inventory object at offset 0x2c (cursor position data) is non-zero\n   k. If cursor position data exists, break loop (cursor is valid)\n   l. Otherwise, zero out inventory object pointer and reload list head\n4. If no valid cursor position data, trigger assertion with D2Common_AssertionOrdinal\n5. Call FUN_6fb9a10f with error code 0xffffffff (non-returning cleanup)\n\nParameters:\nNone (uses global inventory list pointer)\n\nReturns:\nvoid (non-returning on assertion failure)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Assertion failure path is non-returning (FUN_6fb9a10f does not return)\n- Handles null inventory nodes gracefully\n- Cursor position data (offset 0x2c) must be valid for loop to complete\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x28: Offset to item/unit linked list head in inventory object\n- 0x2c: Offset to cursor position data in inventory object\n- 0x30: Offset to active/visible flag in inventory object\n- 0x04: Offset to next item in linked list chain\n- 0x8: Offset within unit structure for some field access\n- 0x93: Assertion error code line number\n\nRelated Functions:\n- ClearGameState: Initializes game rendering state\n- ValidateAndInitializeUnit: Validates and sets up individual unit data\n- ApplyMouseCoordinates: Updates viewport based on cursor position\n- Ordinal_10059: D2Client frame/loop tick function\n- Ordinal_10062: D2Client frame/loop finalize function",
      "tags": ["MOD_SOUND", "STRUCT_Inventory", "STRUCT_Skill", "SND_SYSTEM", "SRC_SoundInst.cpp", "STRUCT_ItemData", "PARAM_0", "STRUCT_Other", "STRUCT_UnitAny"]
