      "instructions": ["0xBE610|TEST|ECX, ECX", "0xBE612|JZ|0x6fb8e630", "0xBE614|MOV|EAX, [0x6fc04018]", "0xBE619|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0xBE61B|JZ|0x6fb8e630", "0xBE61D|MOV|EDX, dword ptr [EAX]", "0xBE61F|CMP|dword ptr [EDX + 0x8], ECX", "0xBE622|JZ|0x6fb8e62c", "0xBE624|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [EAX + 0x4]", "0xBE627|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0xBE629|JNZ|0x6fb8e61d", "0xBE62B|RET|", "0xBE62C|TEST|EDX, EDX", "0xBE62E|JNZ|0x6fb8e633", "0xBE630|XOR|EAX, EAX"],
      "comment": "Search inventory list for item by ID with channel validation\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate nItemId parameter is non-zero\n2. Get global g_pInventoryListHead, validate not NULL\n3. Iterate through linked list via next pointers at offset +4\n4. Compare each item's ID field (offset +8) against nItemId\n5. When match found, validate item has channel (offset +0x2c != 0)\n6. If channel is NULL, trigger assertion and terminate\n7. Return pointer to inventory item\n8. Return NULL if list is NULL, nItemId is zero, or no match found\n\nParameters:\n- nItemId (ECX:4): Item ID to search for, must be non-zero\n\nReturns:\n- EAX: Pointer to inventory item (void*) if found with valid channel\n- NULL: If nItemId is zero, list is NULL, or no matching item\n- Termination: If item found but channel is NULL (assertion failure)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Channel NULL triggers D2Common_AssertionOrdinal assertion failure\n- GetMouseXPosition called on success (purpose unclear - may be side effect)\n- Function uses register-based SSA temporaries (piVar2, iVar1) optimized for fast register access\n\nStructure Layout (Inventory Item):\nOffset | Size | Field Name | Type | Description\n0      | 4    | next       | ptr  | Pointer to next item in linked list\n4      | 4    | prev       | ptr  | Pointer to previous item\n8      | 4    | itemId     | uint | Item identifier\n...    | ...  | ...        | ...  | ...\n0x2c   | 4    | channel    | ptr  | Pointer to channel (must be non-NULL)\n\nRelated Functions:\n- g_pInventoryListHead - Global head of inventory list\n- D2Common_AssertionOrdinal - Failure handler for assertion\n- GetMouseXPosition - Called on successful match (purpose unclear)",
      "tags": ["MOD_SOUND", "SND_SYSTEM", "SRC_SoundInst.cpp", "PARAM_1", "STRUCT_Other"]
