      "instructions": ["0xBE660|PUSH|ESI", "0xBE661|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0xBE663|MOV|CL, byte ptr [EDX + 0x3c]", "0xBE666|MOV|AL, byte ptr [ESI + 0x3c]", "0xBE669|CMP|AL, CL", "0xBE66B|JBE|0x6fb8e676", "0xBE66D|MOV|EAX, 0x1", "0xBE672|POP|ESI", "0xBE673|RET|0x8", "0xBE676|JNC|0x6fb8e67e", "0xBE678|XOR|EAX, EAX", "0xBE67A|POP|ESI", "0xBE67B|RET|0x8", "0xBE67E|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [ESP + 0x8]", "0xBE682|TEST|EAX, EAX"],
      "comment": "Compares two units for sorting/ordering based on type and optional criteria.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Compare unit type (offset 0x3c byte) - sort by type ascending\n2. If types match and nCompareY enabled, compare Y coordinate (offset 0x18 float)\n3. If Y values match and nCompareCount enabled, compare unit count (offset 0x34 uint)\n4. Final tiebreaker: compare unit addresses directly (lower address wins)\n\nParameters:\n  dwUnitA (uint) - First unit address to compare\n  dwUnitB (uint) - Second unit address to compare\n  nCompareY (int) - Enable Y coordinate comparison if non-zero\n  nCompareCount (int) - Enable unit count comparison if non-zero\n\nReturns:\n  true if dwUnitA should sort before dwUnitB\n  false if dwUnitB should sort before or equals dwUnitA\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  If both units have same type, Y coordinate, and count, sorts by address.\n  Comparisons use unsigned comparison for counts, signed for coordinates.",
      "tags": ["PARAM_4", "PROP_LEAF", "STRUCT_Control"]
