      "comment": "Determines if a visual effect should be rendered based on viewport distance.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate viewport coordinates for the entity using dwEntityId\n2. Retrieve effect distance value from viewport calculation and stack storage\n3. Compare effect distance against maximum allowed distance threshold (g_flMaxEffectDistance)\n4. Return 1 if effect distance is within viewport, 0 if outside viewport\n\nParameters:\ndwEntityId (dword) - Entity identifier in ECX register, used to calculate viewport coordinates\n\nReturns:\n1 (TRUE) - Effect is within maximum viewport distance\n0 (FALSE) - Effect exceeds maximum viewport distance or invalid entity\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Magic value 490000 is the maximum effect distance threshold stored at g_flMaxEffectDistance\n- Floating point comparison uses FCOMP instruction for precise distance evaluation\n- Called during animation effect processing for visual optimization\n\nStructure Layout:\nN/A - No structure parameters\n\nRelated Functions:\n- CalculateViewportCoordinates() - Calculates effect distance from viewport\n- FUN_6fb8ec60() - Additional distance calculations\n- ProcessUnitAnimationEffect() - Caller that determines if effect should render",
