      "instructions": ["0xBE720|PUSH|EBX", "0xBE721|PUSH|ESI", "0xBE722|PUSH|EDI", "0xBE723|MOV|EDI, dword ptr [0x6fc04018]", "0xBE729|TEST|EDI, EDI", "0xBE72B|MOV|EBX, ECX", "0xBE72D|JZ|0x6fb8e765", "0xBE72F|MOV|ESI, dword ptr [EDI]", "0xBE731|TEST|ESI, ESI", "0xBE733|JZ|0x6fb8e75e", "0xBE735|CMP|dword ptr [ESI + 0x30], 0x1", "0xBE739|JNZ|0x6fb8e75e", "0xBE73B|TEST|EBX, EBX", "0xBE73D|JZ|0x6fb8e74d", "0xBE73F|MOV|ECX, dword ptr [ESI + 0x28]"],
      "comment": "Validates inventory item in weapon/armor slot range with optional callback validation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if global inventory list (g_pInventoryListHead) is empty; return false if null\n2. Iterate through linked list of inventory nodes (ppInventoryNode->next at offset 0x4)\n3. For each node, verify field at offset 0x30 equals 1 (state check)\n4. If nValidateWithCallback is set, call Ordinal_10060 for additional validation; skip item if callback returns 0\n5. Check item field at offset 0x4 is within valid range: 0xb76 &lt; value &lt; 0x1230\n6. Return true if any item passes all validations, false if no items found or validation fails\n\nParameters:\nnValidateWithCallback: ECX register - non-zero triggers callback validation via Ordinal_10060\n\nReturns:\nAL: true (1) if valid item found in range, false (0) otherwise\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Empty inventory list returns false immediately\n- If callback flag set, item skipped if Ordinal_10060 returns 0 (validation failed)\n- Range bounds: 0xb76 (weapon/armor range lower) to 0x1230 (upper bound exclusive)\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x30: Offset to item state field (must equal 1 for valid items)\n0x4: Offset to item type/ID field (range validation)\n0xb76: Lower bound of valid item range (2934 decimal)\n0x1230: Upper bound of valid item range (4656 decimal)",
