      "instructions": ["0xBE780|MOV|EDX, dword ptr [0x6fc04028]", "0xBE786|XOR|EAX, EAX", "0xBE788|TEST|EDX, EDX", "0xBE78A|SETZ|AL", "0xBE78D|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0xBE78F|PUSH|EDI", "0xBE790|MOV|[0x6fc04028], EAX", "0xBE795|JNZ|0x6fb8e7ec", "0xBE797|MOV|EDI, dword ptr [0x6fc04018]", "0xBE79D|TEST|EDI, EDI", "0xBE79F|JZ|0x6fb8e7ec", "0xBE7A1|PUSH|EBX", "0xBE7A2|PUSH|ESI", "0xBE7A3|MOV|EBX, 0x1", "0xBE7A8|MOV|ESI, dword ptr [EDI]"],
      "comment": "Process inventory fade effects for valid units.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Toggle g_dwObjectRenderFlag: set to 1 if currently 0, else skip processing\n2. If flag now 0 (was already set), return early\n3. If g_pInventoryListHead is NULL, return early\n4. Iterate through inventory linked list starting at g_pInventoryListHead:\n   a. Load inventory node at current position\n   b. Extract unit index from node+4\n   c. Validate unit index range: 0xb76 <= index <= 0x122f (2934-4655 in decimal)\n   d. If index out of range, skip to next node\n   e. Call GetUnitDataByIndex to get unit data\n   f. Set inventory node+0x3d to 1 (mark processed)\n   g. Check unit validity: byte at (pUnitData + 0x40) must be non-zero\n   h. Check node state: dword at (node + 0x30) must equal 1\n   i. If both conditions true, call ProcessInventoryFadeEffect with parameters:\n      - ECX = node+8 (first parameter)\n      - EDX = 0 (second parameter)\n      - [ESP+4] = 0 (third parameter)\n      - [ESP] = unit_flag & 0xFF (fourth parameter from unit byte)\n   j. Advance to next node: pCurrentNode = pCurrentNode[1]\n5. Continue until pCurrentNode[1] is NULL (end of list)\n6. Return\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Uses global toggle flag to prevent multiple processing passes\n- Only processes units with valid IDs in range (Diablo II inventory constraint)\n- Node state check (value 1 at +0x30) gates fade effect processing\n- Retrieves dynamically allocated unit data via GetUnitDataByIndex",
      "tags": ["PROP_NOCALLER", "STRUCT_Skill", "PARAM_0"]
