      "instructions": ["0xBE7F0|PUSH|EDI", "0xBE7F1|XOR|EAX, EAX", "0xBE7F3|MOV|ECX, 0x1c", "0xBE7F8|MOV|EDI, 0x6fc0402c", "0xBE7FD|STOSD.REP|ES:EDI", "0xBE7FF|MOV|[0x6fc0409c], EAX", "0xBE804|MOV|[0x6fc040a0], EAX", "0xBE809|MOV|[0x6fc040a4], EAX", "0xBE80E|MOV|[0x6fc040a8], EAX", "0xBE813|MOV|[0x6fc040ac], EAX", "0xBE818|MOV|[0x6fc040b0], EAX", "0xBE81D|MOV|[0x6fc040d0], EAX", "0xBE822|POP|EDI", "0xBE823|RET|"],
      "comment": "Initialize game memory block and global state variables to zero.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Set EDI to address of memory buffer at 0x6fc0402c\n2. Clear EAX to 0x00000000\n3. Set ECX to 0x1c (28 dwords = 112 bytes)\n4. Execute REP STOSD to fill buffer with zeros (28 iterations)\n5. Zero all 7 game state global variables (flags, session ID, game state, mode, loaded flags, config, checksum)\n6. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\n(none)\n\nReturns:\n(void) - Function returns void after initialization completes\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Function does not validate target addresses; assumes memory is allocated and writable\n- Uses register EAX for zero value; caller must not depend on EAX containing values\n- EDI is restored via POP after REP STOSD execution\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x1c = 28 decimal (number of dwords to zero in buffer, 112 bytes total)\n0x6fc0402c = Base address of game state buffer\n0x6fc0409c = Address of g_dwGameFlags global\n0x6fc040a0 = Address of g_dwGameSessionId global\n0x6fc040a4 = Address of g_dwCurrentGameState global\n0x6fc040a8 = Address of g_dwGameMode global\n0x6fc040ac = Address of g_dwLoadedGameFlags global\n0x6fc040b0 = Address of g_dwGameConfigFlags global\n0x6fc040d0 = Address of g_dwGameStateChecksum global\n\nRelated Functions:\n- InitializeGameSession() - Calls this function as part of game session setup\n- PlayVideoById() - Calls this function before video playback",
