      "instructions": ["0xBE830|PUSH|EBP", "0xBE831|PUSH|ESI", "0xBE832|PUSH|EDI", "0xBE833|MOV|EBP, ECX", "0xBE835|CALL|0x6fb8b5a0", "0xBE83A|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0xBE83C|JZ|0x6fb8eaa6", "0xBE842|CMP|EAX, dword ptr [0x6fc040a8]", "0xBE848|JZ|0x6fb8e855", "0xBE84A|MOV|[0x6fc040a8], EAX", "0xBE84F|MOV|dword ptr [0x6fc0409c], EBP", "0xBE855|XOR|ESI, ESI", "0xBE857|CALL|0x6fb8b5c0", "0xBE85C|MOV|ECX, EAX", "0xBE85E|CALL|0x6fb8b600"],
      "comment": "Process inventory slot updates and fading effects for player items.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call ProcessUnitStatData() to update unit state\n2. Get current item slot index from array element pointer\n3. Validate slot index in valid range (0x1230-0x124b)\n4. Check Ordinal_10046 (animation system check) - returns nonzero if available\n5. If Ordinal_10046 returns 0, check Ordinal_10048 (secondary state) - if both 0, animation unavailable\n6. Set fHasValidInventory = (both ordinals returned nonzero)\n7. If slot changed and frame delta > 0x4a OR animation unavailable OR no slot selected:\n   - Update current item ID to new slot value\n   - Store frame counter at update time\n8. If animation unavailable, trigger ProcessInventoryListFadeEffects()\n9. If no item selected, trigger ProcessInventoryListFadeEffects()\n10. If fade system active:\n    - Check highlight state 1 expiry and reinitialize if needed\n    - Check highlight state 2 expiry and validate unit, reinitialize if valid\n    - Check global frame counter vs expiry time, exit if not ready\n    - Clear fade flag\n    - If animation available, ProcessInventorySlot()\n11. If current item found but no inventory entry exists:\n    - Search inventory for item and get slot type\n    - Set fade alpha (2.8026e-45 if not found, 0.0 otherwise)\n    - Initialize object properties with fade effect\n    - Store frame counter\n12. If unit index changed and frame delta > 0x3d:\n    - ProcessLevelGameState()\n    - Update last processed unit index\n13. If current item exists and frame delta > 0x7d:\n    - Get unit data and find inventory item\n    - Check search flag\n    - Validate inventory slot boundaries\n    - Determine correct slot list (weapon/armor/belt)\n    - Store result in global slot data array\n\nParameters:\ndwFrameCounter (dword, ECX) - Current game frame counter, used to detect timing intervals\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Ordinal_10046: Animation/effect system availability check (unknown ordinal - see comment at 0x6fb8e87f)\n- Ordinal_10048: Secondary animation state check (unknown ordinal - see comment at 0x6fb8e888)\n- Frame deltas: 0x4a (74 frames), 0x3d (61 frames), 0x7d (125 frames) - update frequency thresholds\n- Slot validation range: 0x1230-0x124b\n- Float constant 2.8026e-45 used as fade alpha marker\n- Note: Function uses SSA-form temporaries (extraout_var, extraout_var_00) from function returns - these are compiler optimizations\n\nGlobal Variables Used:\n- g_dwCurrentUnitIndex: Currently processed unit ID\n- g_dwCurrentItemId: Currently selected item slot\n- g_dwLastProcessedUnit: Track unit changes\n- g_fItemFadeActive: Fade effect state flag\n- g_adItemSlotData: Item slot inventory slot mapping array (indexed by item ID)\n- g_dwInventoryFrameBase: Frame counter at last update\n- g_dwSlotCheckFrame: Frame counter for slot validation\n- g_dwInventoryUpdateTime: Time of inventory update\n- g_fHighlightState1: Highlight 1 fade state\n- g_fHighlightState2: Highlight 2 fade state\n- g_dwHighlightFrame1: Highlight 1 expiry frame\n- g_dwHighlightFrame2: Highlight 2 expiry frame",
      "tags": ["PROP_LARGE", "PARAM_1"]
