      "instructions": ["0xBEAB0|PUSH|EBX", "0xBEAB1|MOV|EBX, ECX", "0xBEAB3|MOV|ECX, dword ptr [0x6fc040a4]", "0xBEAB9|PUSH|ESI", "0xBEABA|PUSH|EDI", "0xBEABB|MOV|EDI, EDX", "0xBEABD|TEST|ECX, ECX", "0xBEABF|JZ|0x6fb8eb09", "0xBEAC1|CALL|0x6fb8b480", "0xBEAC6|MOV|ECX, dword ptr [0x6fc040a4]", "0xBEACC|MOV|ESI, EAX", "0xBEACE|CALL|0x6fb8d0c0", "0xBEAD3|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0xBEAD5|JZ|0x6fb8eb09", "0xBEAD7|MOV|ECX, EAX"],
      "comment": "Configures fade effect parameters for inventory item display transitions.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if current game state exists (g_dwCurrentGameState != 0)\n2. Retrieve unit data for current game state via GetUnitDataByIndex\n3. Find inventory item by ID via FindInventoryItemById\n4. If item found, check flag status with SearchListAndCheckFlag\n5. If flag check succeeds and nInventorySlot != 0, retrieve property value from unit data at offset 0x50 + (nInventorySlot * 4)\n6. Store property value in g_aCurrentInventoryItem array\n7. Retrieve and store current game session flags via GetGameSessionFlags\n8. Process inventory list fade effects via ProcessInventoryListFadeEffects\n9. Initialize first fade effect: set active flag, duration, and frame-based start time (frame_counter + nSecondEffectDuration)\n10. Initialize second fade effect: set active flag, parameter, and frame-based start time (frame_counter + nSecondEffectDelay)\n11. Initialize third fade effect: set parameter and frame-based start time (frame_counter + nThirdEffectDuration)\n\nParameters:\n- dwFadeDuration: Duration in frames for initial fade effect display\n- nSecondEffectDuration: Duration in frames for second effect delay\n- nThirdEffectDuration: Duration in frames for third effect timing\n- nInventorySlot: Inventory slot index to retrieve property value from (0 = skip retrieval)\n- dwSecondEffect: Parameter value for second fade effect\n- nSecondEffectDelay: Frame delay before second effect triggers\n- dwThirdEffect: Parameter value for third fade effect\n\nReturns:\n- void (always succeeds if game state exists)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If nInventorySlot == 0, property value retrieval is skipped\n- If item not found or flag check fails, only global fade effect globals are initialized\n- Game state existence is prerequisite for item lookup and property retrieval",
      "tags": ["PARAM_7", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
    },
