      "comment": "Calculate the squared Euclidean distance between two points on a 2D plane.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Convert flDeltaX to float10 extended precision\n2. Multiply flDeltaX by itself (flDeltaX²)\n3. Convert flDeltaY to float10 extended precision\n4. Multiply flDeltaY by itself (flDeltaY²)\n5. Add the two squared values (flDeltaX² + flDeltaY²)\n6. Return the sum as float10\n\nParameters:\n- flDeltaX: X-axis delta distance (float)\n- flDeltaY: Y-axis delta distance (float)\n\nReturns:\n- float10: Sum of squares (flDeltaX² + flDeltaY²), representing squared distance\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Zero inputs: Returns 0.0\n- Negative inputs: Squared values always positive\n- Used for range/viewport checks where exact distance not needed\n\nRelated Functions:\n- RenderGameViewport() - Uses distance for viewport clipping checks\n- IsEffectInViewport() - Validates effect visibility based on squared distance\n- InitializeGameObjectProperties() - Sets object position/collision calculations\n- UpdateInventoryItemPosition() - Calculates item offset distances",
