      "comment": "Calculate minimum cyclic distance between two values in modular arithmetic space.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if nModulus is power of 2 via (nModulus & (nModulus - 1)) == 0\n2. If power of 2: calculate remainders using bitwise AND (nModulus - 1) & nValue\n3. If not power of 2: calculate remainders using modulo division (nValue % nModulus)\n4. Compute delta distance: nRemainder2 - nRemainder1\n5. Calculate absolute delta: abs(nDeltaDistance)\n6. Calculate distance +modulus: abs(nDeltaDistance - nModulus)\n7. Calculate distance -modulus: abs(nRemainder1 - nRemainder2 - nModulus)\n8. Find minimum of three distances and return as result\n\nParameters:\n  nValue1 (uint): First value in modular space [0, nModulus)\n  nValue2 (uint): Second value in modular space [0, nModulus)\n  nModulus (uint): Modulus for cyclic distance (may be power of 2 for optimization)\n\nReturns:\n  int: Minimum cyclic distance between nValue1 and nValue2",
