      "comment": "Conditionally dispatch game state callbacks through legacy engine interface.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate input parameters: check if wParamA and wParamB are non-zero\n2. If either parameter is zero, return failure (0)\n3. On first call: initialize g_pLegacyEngine by calling Ordinal_11155(0) to obtain engine interface pointer\n4. Dispatch callback to Ordinal_11158 with all 5 parameters: engine pointer and 4 data parameters\n5. Return success (1)\n\nParameters:\n  pGameState (void*) - Engine interface pointer passed to callback dispatcher (ECX, implicit __fastcall)\n  wParamA (ushort) - First validation parameter, checked for non-zero (EDX, implicit __fastcall, 16-bit)\n  wParamB (ushort) - Second validation parameter, checked for non-zero (stack param +0x10, 16-bit)\n  dwParamC (dword) - First data parameter passed to Ordinal_11158 (stack param +0x14)\n  dwParamD (dword) - Second data parameter passed to Ordinal_11158 (stack param +0x18)\n\nReturns:\n  1 - Callback dispatched successfully (both parameters valid, dispatch completed)\n  0 - Parameters invalid (wParamA or wParamB was zero, no callback dispatched)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Lazy initialization: g_pLegacyEngine initialized only on first call via Ordinal_11155\n  - If g_pLegacyEngine already initialized, Ordinal_11155 is not called\n  - Early return on parameter validation failure saves initialization overhead\n\nOrdinal References:\n  Ordinal_11155 - Engine initialization function (returns engine interface pointer, called once)\n  Ordinal_11158 - Legacy engine callback dispatcher (processes game state updates with engine context)",
      "tags": ["PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_5", "STRUCT_Control"]
    },
