      "comment": "HandleMouseMoveMessage - Processes mouse movement messages and updates cursor position.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract X coordinate from low word at pMessage+0xC, Y from high word\n2. Call Ordinal_10047 to check input state, verify no exception active\n3. Clamp cursor X/Y to screen bounds (0 to width-1, 0 to height-1)\n4. If out of bounds, call SetCursorPos to reposition cursor\n5. Show cursor and update frame timestamp\n6. If screen state is 4 or 2, transition to state 3 with screen=2\n7. Validate cursor table size (must be 7) or assert and exit\n8. Clear return values at pMessage+0x18 and pMessage+0x1C\n\nParameters:\n  pMessage - Pointer to message structure containing cursor coordinates at offset 0xC\n\nReturns: void (modifies globals and message structure)",
