      "instructions": ["0xBEF90|PUSH|ESI", "0xBEF91|MOV|ESI, dword ptr [ESP + 0x8]", "0xBEF95|XOR|EAX, EAX", "0xBEF97|MOV|AX, word ptr [ESI + 0xc]", "0xBEF9B|MOV|[0x6fc04118], EAX", "0xBEFA0|MOV|ECX, dword ptr [ESI + 0xc]", "0xBEFA3|SHR|ECX, 0x10", "0xBEFA6|MOV|dword ptr [0x6fc0411c], ECX", "0xBEFAC|CALL|dword ptr [0x6fba6098]", "0xBEFB2|MOV|[0x6fc04104], EAX", "0xBEFB7|MOV|EAX, [0x6fc04108]", "0xBEFBC|MOV|ECX, 0x5", "0xBEFC1|CMP|EAX, ECX", "0xBEFC3|JZ|0x6fb8effe", "0xBEFC5|MOV|EAX, [0x6fc040f8]"],
      "comment": "Validates screen state transition and handles state machine logic for UI rendering\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract resource ID (low 16 bits) from handle offset 0x0c → g_wResourceID\n2. Extract resource flags (high 16 bits) from handle offset 0x0c → g_wResourceFlags\n3. Store current tick count as frame timestamp → g_dwLastFrameTimestamp via GetTickCount()\n4. Check if current screen state != 5 (SCREEN_GAME_MODE):\n   a. Load screen data table entry: g_aScreenDataTable[g_nSelectedScreen * 7]\n   b. If entry is non-zero, set g_dwScreenState = 5 and g_nSelectedScreen = 4\n   c. Clear g_nScreenParam\n5. Clear resource handle field at offset 0x18 (always set to 0)\n6. If state == 5 (SCREEN_GAME_MODE), skip to final cleanup\n7. Return with stack frame cleanup\n\nParameters:\nnResourceHandle: int - Handle/pointer to resource structure (offset 0x0c contains composite ID/flags value, offset 0x18 for state field)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value; modifies global screen state variables g_dwScreenState, g_nSelectedScreen, g_nScreenParam",
