      "comment": "Initialize game screen state variables.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Clear g_dwInitializationFlag to 0\n2. Set g_nSelectedScreen to 6 (target screen identifier)\n3. Store dwScreenParam in g_nScreenParam for later use\n4. Calculate g_dwScreenState based on nInitFlag: (nInitFlag != 0) evaluates to 1 if true, 0 if false\n5. Add 7 to boolean result, yielding 7 for uninitialized (false) or 8 for initialized (true)\n\nParameters:\ndwScreenParam (dword) - Screen identifier passed via ECX register (__fastcall)\nnInitFlag (int) - Initialization flag passed via EDX register; 0 = not initialized, non-zero = initialized\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Updates four global state variables (g_dwInitializationFlag, g_nSelectedScreen, g_nScreenParam, g_dwScreenState)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Screen state is calculated as boolean + 7 offset to generate distinct state codes (7 or 8)\n- Initialization flag is unconditionally cleared to prevent re-initialization",
