      "comment": "Set game screen state based on unit parameter.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Store unit ID in global g_pCurrentUnit (ECX register value)\n2. If unit ID is 0:\n   - Set g_dwScreenState = 1 (player state)\n   - Set g_nSelectedScreen = 5 (inventory screen)\n   - Set g_nScreenParam = 0 (no parameter)\n   - Return\n3. If unit ID is non-zero:\n   - Set g_nSelectedScreen = 5 (inventory screen)\n   - Set g_nScreenParam = 0 (no parameter)\n   - Set g_dwScreenState = 4 (alternate game state)\n   - Return\n\nParameters:\nnUnitId - Unit identifier (via ECX register, __fastcall)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Updates global game state variables\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Unit ID 0 triggers player state (g_dwScreenState = 1)\n- Non-zero unit ID triggers alternate state (g_dwScreenState = 4)\n- Both paths set inventory screen (5) and zero parameter",
