      "instructions": ["0xBF110|SUB|ESP, 0x50", "0xBF113|MOV|dword ptr [0x6fc04114], ECX", "0xBF119|PUSH|EBX", "0xBF11A|PUSH|ESI", "0xBF11B|PUSH|EDI", "0xBF11C|PUSH|0x3", "0xBF11E|CALL|0x6fb9922c", "0xBF123|MOV|ECX, EAX", "0xBF125|MOV|EDX, 0x6fbd8138", "0xBF12A|CALL|0x6fad25b0", "0xBF12F|MOV|EBX, dword ptr [0x6fba6210]", "0xBF135|MOV|EDI, 0x6fc040dc", "0xBF13A|MOV|ESI, 0x6fbd8178", "0xBF13F|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [ESI]", "0xBF141|LEA|ECX, [ESP + 0xc]"],
      "comment": "Initialize UI cursor resources and screen state for game window.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Retrieve current window handle via Ordinal_10027\n2. Process 3 message entries to register cursor resources  \n3. Iterate through 7 cursor definition pointers (Gaunt, etc.)\n4. For each cursor: format resource path using wsprintfA with UI_CURSOR template\n5. Concatenate path and load resource file via ConcatenatePathAndWriteFile, store result\n6. Initialize screen state globals: screen mode, selected screen (5), resource IDs\n7. Capture current tick count for frame timing\n8. Calculate screen center coordinates (width/2, height/2)\n9. Return success code (1)\n\nParameters:\nnMode - uint (__fastcall ECX): Window mode/state identifier passed to resource loader\n\nReturns:\nuint - Success code (1 = success)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Iterates exactly 7 cursor pointer entries (stride 0x1c bytes)\n- Hardcoded screen ID 5 (main game screen)\n- Screen width/height calculated at runtime via globals\n- Null check on ConcatenatePathAndWriteFile results stored directly (no error handling)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x3 - Message entry count (3 entries)\n0x1c - Cursor pointer stride (28 bytes = 7 dwords)\n5 - Screen ID constant\n0x6fbd823c - Loop terminator address (points past last cursor pointer)",
      "tags": ["PARAM_1"]
