      "comment": "Process and report all validation errors collected during game initialization.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Push ESI register (callee-saved)\n2. Get application window handle via Ordinal_10027 (Storm.GetWindowHandle)\n3. Process 3 message entries via ProcessMessageArray (display UI messages)\n4. Clear validation state flag (g_dwValidationState = 0)\n5. Initialize pointer to start of error array (g_pValidationErrors)\n6. Loop while pointer < end of error array (0x6fc040f8):\n   a. Load error code from current array position\n   b. Test if non-zero (error present)\n   c. If zero, skip to next (JZ)\n   d. If non-zero, call ReportValidationError(errorCode)\n   e. Clear error entry (set to 0)\n   f. Advance pointer by 4 bytes\n7. Pop ESI and return\n\nParameters:\nNone. Uses global error array g_pValidationErrors.\n\nReturns:\nvoid. Clears all validation errors and reports them to the application window.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Error array is fixed size (48 bytes, 12 entries at 4 bytes each)\n- Function runs during initialization path only\n- Loop is guaranteed to process all 12 error slots even if some are zero",
