      "comment": "Retrieves a cursor record by index with bounds validation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Assert cursor table size equals NUM_CURSORS (7)\n2. Assert cursor index parameter is less than 7\n3. Calculate record offset: (index * 7 - index * 8) * 4 + base\n4. Load cursor record from g_aCursorRecords table\n5. Shift record address left by 8 bits (multiply by 256)\n6. Return shifted cursor record address\n\nParameters:\nnCursorIndex (int) - Cursor index, must be 0-6 for valid cursor IDs\n\nReturns:\nint - Shifted cursor record address (record_address << 8). Asserts on invalid index.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Asserts terminate execution if table size != NUM_CURSORS\n- Asserts terminate execution if index >= NUM_CURSORS (7)\n- Uses lea/sub to compute (index*7 - index*8) = -index offset pattern",
