      "comment": "Process the current screen's resource drawing operation.\nInitializes a CEL context buffer, loads the appropriate resource data,\nand delegates rendering to screen-specific handlers based on current state.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if UI is initialized (g_bUIInitialized != 0)\n2. If screen state is out of range or initialization flag is not set:\n   - Call screen-specific handler from g_apfnScreenHandlers table\n3. Otherwise:\n   - Zero-initialize a local 18-dword CEL buffer (72 bytes)\n   - Call FUN_6fb968e0 to load CEL context data from initialization flag\n   - If load successful, call Ordinal_10055 (D2Common.GetCelCount) with buffer\n   - Assert buffer[0] is non-zero (CEL context must be valid)\n   - Get CEL width via Ordinal_10038 (D2Common.GetCelWidth)\n   - Get CEL height via Ordinal_10037 (D2Common.GetCelHeight)\n   - Call FUN_6fb91bf0 to render with calculated position and dimensions\n\nParameters:\nNone - Uses global variables:\n  g_bUIInitialized - UI ready flag\n  g_dwInitializationFlag - Resource initialization state\n  g_dwScreenState - Current screen mode (0-7 valid)\n  g_nSelectedScreen - Active screen index\n  g_wResourceID - Resource identifier\n  g_wResourceFlags - Resource flags\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Delegates to screen-specific handlers or renders directly\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If CEL context buffer is invalid (buffer[0] == 0), triggers assertion failure\n- Screen state values 5-7 and 8+ are out of range and skip rendering\n- CEL width/height are right-shifted by 1 bit in calculations",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Inventory", "PARAM_0", "SRC_Cursor.cpp"]
