      "api_calls": ["FogAssert", "FogAssert", "GfxIsVideoDisabled", "GetInitFlag"],
      "instructions": ["0xBF6A0|SUB|ESP, 0x10", "0xBF6A3|PUSH|EBX", "0xBF6A4|MOV|EBX, ECX", "0xBF6A6|PUSH|EDI", "0xBF6A7|MOV|EDI, EDX", "0xBF6A9|TEST|EBX, EBX", "0xBF6AB|JGE|0x6fb8f6cb", "0xBF6AD|PUSH|0x306", "0xBF6B2|PUSH|0x6fbd8388", "0xBF6B7|PUSH|0x6fbd83ec", "0xBF6BC|CALL|0x6fb99a7a", "0xBF6C1|ADD|ESP, 0xc", "0xBF6C4|PUSH|-0x1", "0xBF6C6|CALL|0x6fb9a10f", "0xBF6CB|TEST|EDI, EDI"],
      "comment": "Sets the cursor position within a window's client area with validation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate nX >= 0 (assertion if negative, exits with code -1)\n2. Validate nY >= 0 (assertion if negative, exits with code -1)\n3. Query window mode state via Ordinal_10028 (Storm.dll, likely IsWindowMode)\n4. If in window mode (result == 0):\n   a. Obtain active window handle via Ordinal_10027 (Storm.dll, likely GetActiveWindow)\n   b. Retrieve window rectangle using GetWindowRect\n   c. Get screen metrics: metric 4 = screen height, metric 7 = screen width\n   d. Calculate adjusted cursor position: (screen_width + window.left + nX, screen_height + window.top + nY)\n   e. Call SetCursorPos with calculated absolute coordinates\n5. If in fullscreen mode (result != 0):\n   a. Call SetCursorPos with coordinates as-is\n6. Store nY in g_wResourceFlags and nX in g_wResourceID (UI state tracking)\n\nParameters:\n  nX: int - X coordinate (cursor column) - must be non-negative (0x306 assertion)\n  nY: int - Y coordinate (cursor row) - must be non-negative (0x307 assertion)\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Assertions fail with FUN_6fb9a10f(0xffffffff) if coordinates negative\n  - Window mode detected by Ordinal_10028() == 0\n  - Fullscreen mode bypasses window rectangle adjustments\n  - Global state updated: g_wResourceID and g_wResourceFlags store params for UI tracking\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  - 0x306: Line number for nX validation assertion error\n  - 0x307: Line number for nY validation assertion error\n  - 0xffffffff: Exit code (-1) on assertion failure\n  - Metric 4: Screen height (GetSystemMetrics parameter)\n  - Metric 7: Screen width (GetSystemMetrics parameter)",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Act", "PARAM_2", "SRC_Cursor.cpp", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control"]
    },
