      "comment": "Process timed spell effect - manages lifecycle and node ordering of active timed spell effects\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load spell time duration from spell data at offset +0x38\n2. Check if spell timer is active (Ordinal_10487) - returns nonzero if active\n3. If active, disable spell state (Ordinal_10486 with param 0)\n4. Check if spell duration has expired (Ordinal_10503) - returns 0 if expired\n5. If expired (iVar5==0), clear spell data field at +0x08 and reset active flag\n6. First loop: scan container nodes starting at pContainer[0x2c]\n   - Find nodes matching spell time with type==8 (timed effect)\n   - Reset field[0xf]=0 and field[2]=-1\n7. Second loop: find min/max timed effect times among active nodes\n   - Track minimum time in iVar4 and maximum time in iVar5\n8. Third loop: mark target node with field[0xf]=1, field[2]=0\n   - Uses iVar5 if varied, else defaults to iVar4\n\nParameters:\n- dwUnitId (ECX): Unit identifier, 32-bit value\n- pContainer (EDX): Pointer to container with node list at offset +0x2c\n- pSpellData (Stack[0x4]): Pointer to spell data, duration at offset +0x38\n\nReturns:\n- void (no return value)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x38: Spell duration offset in spell data structure\n- 0x2c: Container node list head offset\n- 0x08: Spell data clear field offset\n- 0xf: Timed effect flag field offset\n- 0x2: Type field offset (value 8 = timed effect)\n- 0xa4: Next node pointer offset (linked list)\n- 0x29: Next node pointer offset (iteration)",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Inventory", "PARAM_3", "PROP_LOOPHEAVY", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
