      "instructions": ["0xBFB90|PUSH|ECX", "0xBFB91|PUSH|EBX", "0xBFB92|PUSH|EBP", "0xBFB93|PUSH|ESI", "0xBFB94|PUSH|EDI", "0xBFB95|MOV|EBP, EDX", "0xBFB97|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x10], ECX", "0xBFB9B|CALL|0x6fb628b0", "0xBFBA0|MOV|EBX, EAX", "0xBFBA2|TEST|EBX, EBX", "0xBFBA4|JNZ|0x6fb8fbc4", "0xBFBA6|PUSH|0x1b0", "0xBFBAB|PUSH|0x6fbd84f4", "0xBFBB0|PUSH|0x6fbd84e8", "0xBFBB5|CALL|0x6fb99a7a"],
      "comment": "Removes an audio context node from the linked list in GFX info structure\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get GFX info pointer for the specified index; assert if null\n2. Initialize current pointer to head of linked list (offset 0x2c), previous to null\n3. Traverse list comparing each node until matching target context\n4. When found, unlink: if first in list, update head; else update previous node's next\n5. If node has audio context (offset 0x40), remove it from audio list first\n6. If node type is 8, call cleanup handler\n7. Signal resource change via Ordinal_10043 (Storm.dll resource cache invalidation)\n\nParameters:\nnGfxIndex - Graphics engine index for GFX info structure\npContextToRemove - Target audio context node to unlink from list\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Always succeeds (asserts if GFX info invalid)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Assertion failure if GFX info pointer is NULL (line 0x1b0)\n- Early exit if list empty or target not found\n- Automatic audio context cleanup before unlinking\n\nOrdinal Calls:\nOrdinal_10043(0x1d2, 0) - Storm.dll: Resource cache invalidation notification\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x2c - Offset of linked list head in GFX info structure\n0xa4 - Offset of next pointer in linked list node\n0x40 - Offset of audio context pointer in node\n0x10 - Offset of audio context field (check in field access)\n0x8 - Node type indicator for cleanup operation\n0x1d2 - Ordinal parameter (resource invalidation code)",
