      "instructions": ["0xBFCB0|PUSH|EBX", "0xBFCB1|PUSH|ESI", "0xBFCB2|PUSH|EDI", "0xBFCB3|MOV|EBX, EDX", "0xBFCB5|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0xBFCB7|CALL|0x6fb628b0", "0xBFCBC|MOV|EDI, EAX", "0xBFCBE|TEST|EDI, EDI", "0xBFCC0|JNZ|0x6fb8fce0", "0xBFCC2|PUSH|0x33f", "0xBFCC7|PUSH|0x6fbd84f4", "0xBFCCC|PUSH|0x6fbd84e8", "0xBFCD1|CALL|0x6fb99a7a", "0xBFCD6|ADD|ESP, 0xc", "0xBFCD9|PUSH|-0x1"],
      "comment": "Searches inventory item list for entry matching stat and level values.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get graphics info pointer from pGfxInfo parameter via GetGfxInfoPointer\n2. Validate pointer not NULL, assert and terminate on failure with error code\n3. Check if nStat equals -1 (auto-detect mode)\n4. If nStat == -1, retrieve default stat from item using FUN_6fb95870(pGfxInfo)\n5. Load head of inventory item list from GfxCell structure offset 0x28\n6. Loop through linked list of items:\n   a. Check if current node is NULL (end of list), return NULL if so\n   b. Check if node[0] (item level) matches nStat parameter\n   c. Check if node[1] (item stat) matches nLevel parameter\n   d. Both conditions satisfied, return pointer to matching item node\n   e. Otherwise advance to next node via offset [node+0x10]\n7. Return NULL if no matching item found in list\n\nParameters:\npGfxInfo (GfxCell*) - Graphics info structure containing inventory list\nnLevel (int, EDX) - Item level to match\nnStat (int, stack) - Item stat to match; -1 triggers auto-detection\n\nReturns:\nint* - Pointer to matching inventory item node structure, NULL if not found\n\nSpecial Cases:\nnStat parameter equals -1 for default stat auto-detection\nNULL graphics pointer triggers assertion and process termination\nEmpty inventory list or no matching items returns NULL",
      "tags": ["SRC_Gfx.cpp", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PARAM_3", "STRUCT_Other"]
