      "comment": "Retrieves a graphics unit record from the GFX data structure matching item ID and slot.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get unit type from param_1 (0=normal, 1=quest, 2=unique)\n2. Resolve nGfxSlot to actual graphics index if -1 (use unit's current index)\n3. Branch on unit type:\n   - Type 1 (quest): Call FUN_6fb90660 setup, iterate pGfxInfo[10] list for record matching nGfxIndex and nItemId\n   - Type 0 (normal): Verify not already quest, call FUN_6fb8fef0 for COF data, call FUN_6fb96ec0 setup, iterate pGfxInfo[10] for match\n   - Type 2 (unique): Call FUN_6fb90890 setup, iterate pGfxInfo[10] for match\n4. Return matching record pointer or NULL if not found\n\nParameters:\n  pUnitAny (int *) - pointer to unit object\n  nItemId (int) - item ID to match (slot index in quest/unique lists)\n  nGfxSlot (int) - graphics slot index (-1 to use unit's current slot)\n\nReturns:\n  int * - pointer to graphics unit record containing item ID and slot info, or NULL if not found\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If nGfxSlot is -1, fetched from unit's current graphics index via FUN_6fb95870\n  - Quest units (type=1) directly search graphics records\n  - Normal units (type=0) require COF (CODE OF FRAME) data initialization before search\n  - Unique units (type=2) follow same search pattern as quest units\n  - Function asserts on missing gfx info structure (should never happen)",
