      "comment": "Insert a graphics unit record into the gfx info structure for a specific unit and slot.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize a 64-byte zero buffer (local_103) for data storage\n2. Call FUN_6fb96e10 to validate pUnit - assert if null/invalid\n3. Call FUN_6fb958f0 to initialize unit graphics properties\n4. Call Ordinal_10885 (Fog.dll graphics init)\n5. Get graphics info pointer from unit with GetGfxInfoPointer - assert if null\n6. Determine target record ID: use nSlotIndex if != -1, else call FUN_6fb95870 to get slot ID\n7. Search gfx table linked list starting at [gfxInfo + 0x28]:\n   - If matching record ID found with valid data (piVar5[1] != 0), process existing\n   - Otherwise continue search or initialize new record\n8. Call Ordinal_10042 to allocate new record structure\n9. Determine color table source: call FUN_6fb95830 - if true use g_ppColorTableSpecial, else g_ppColorTableStandard\n10. Clear secondary buffer area\n11. Extract file extension from szFilenameExt (find last '.' then backtrack to last '\\')\n12. Copy extension substring to abExtensionBuffer with _strncpy\n13. Call FUN_6fb9b2e0 to process/uppercase extension string\n14. Calculate hash from extension using Ordinal_502 with custom hash algorithm\n15. Use hash to index into color table and lookup matching record\n16. If found, check field comparison at offset 0xc/0x10 for match\n17. If not found, call FUN_6fb90310 to create new record from color table\n18. Initialize record structure with nSlotIndex, pointer, and link into gfx list\n19. Verify insertion: search list for matching record ID and return graphics pointer\n\nParameters:\n  pUnit (ECX) - Pointer to unit being processed\n  pdwRecordId (EDX) - Pointer to output record ID\n  nSlotIndex (Stack) - Target slot index (-1 to auto-determine)\n\nReturns:\n  EAX - Graphics record pointer (at offset 0x14 in linked structure), 0 if search fails after insertion\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Slot index -1: auto-determine current slot with FUN_6fb95870\n  - New record allocation via Ordinal_10042\n  - Color table selection based on FUN_6fb95830 (two distinct tables)\n  - Filename extension parsing for color lookup\n  - Multiple assertion points for null pointer validation\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x28 - Gfx info table start offset (linked list head)\n  0x10 - Gfx record next pointer offset\n  0x14 - Graphics pointer field offset in record\n  0x8 - Secondary pointer offset in record\n  0x1ff0000, 0x1ff00, 0x1ff - Hash algorithm bit masks\n  0x40 - Zero buffer size (64 bytes)\n  7 - Minimum extension string length validation\n\nStructure Layout (Gfx Record):\n  Offset | Size | Field Name | Type | Description\n  0x0    | 4    | dwSlotId   | uint | Record ID/slot index\n  0x4    | 4    | dwFlags    | uint | Record state flags\n  0x8    | 4    | pGraphics  | void*| Graphics structure pointer\n  0xc    | 4    | dwColorId1 | uint | Color table entry hash\n  0x10   | 4    | dwColorId2 | uint | Secondary color identifier\n  0x14   | 4    | pNextRec   | void*| Next record in linked list\n\nNote: Function uses 4 phantom stack-allocated temporaries optimized away in decompilation.",
      "tags": ["SRC_Gfx.cpp", "PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PARAM_3", "STRUCT_Skill", "STRUCT_Other", "PROP_LOOPHEAVY", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
