      "comment": "Allocates and initializes a COF (Component Object File) data unit for a D2 graphics animation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract file extension from input filename using string search\n2. Validate filename length < MAX_COFDATA_FILENAME (0x50 bytes)\n3. Convert extension string to hash code via hash function (Ordinal_502 = D2Common_GetFileHash)\n4. Check if unit already exists in hash table by comparing extension hash + extension code\n5. If duplicate found, return NULL\n6. If new unit: allocate 0x1c bytes, zero-fill, set flags\n7. Copy filename extension to allocated structure\n8. Read COF file header data via Ordinal_10038 (D2Common_GetFileHandle) and validate direction count <= 0x40\n9. Insert new node into hash table at computed position\n10. Update global node counter with allocation size\n11. Return new allocated node pointer\n\nParameters:\nnHashTableIndex - [ECX] Hash table base offset from param_1 + 0xc\npszFilename - [EDX] Pointer to filename string (includes path and extension)\nIMPLICIT: bExtBuffer - 0x200 byte filename extension buffer\nIMPLICIT: dwExtensionCode - 0x100 byte secondary processing buffer\n\nReturns:\nEAX = pointer to allocated COF data unit (dword[8]) on success\nEAX = NULL if unit already exists or allocation fails\n\nSpecial Cases:\nOrdinal_10042 = D2Common allocator - allocation size 0xde used for COF unit allocation\nMagic constant 0x1c = allocation header size (added to node counter)\nHash computation uses triple XOR folding: (val & 0x1ff0000 ^ val >> 8) >> 8 ^ val & 0x1ff00 >> 8 ^ val & 0x1ff\nDirection count validation checks byte at offset +0x2 <= 0x40\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x50 (80) - Maximum COF filename length limit\n0x40 (64) - Maximum direction count in COF header\n0xde (222) - COF data unit allocation size (Ordinal_10042 parameter)\n0x1c (28) - COF header size added to node counter\n0x1ff0000, 0x1ff00, 0x1ff - Hash computation mask constants\n0xc, 0x10 - Field offsets in allocated structure\n\nStructure Layout (COF Data Unit):\nOffset | Size | Field Name | Type | Description\n0      | 4    | pNext      | dword* | Next node in hash chain\n4      | 4    | dwFlags    | dword  | Flags (bit 0 = initialized)\n8      | 4    | piFileData | int*   | File handle or memory pointer\n12     | 4    | dwExtHash  | dword  | Extension hash code\n16     | 4    | dwExtCode  | dword  | Extension code from hash\n20     | 4    | pFileHdr   | dword* | COF file header pointer\n24     | 4    | reserved   | dword  | Reserved/padding\n\nNote: Function uses 2 stack-allocated temporaries (bTerminator, abPathBuffer) optimized away in decompilation but present in assembly.\n\nRelated Functions:\n- Ordinal_502 - D2Common_GetFileHash (Storm ordinal 502)\n- Ordinal_10042 - D2Common allocator (Storm ordinal 10042)\n- Ordinal_10038 - D2Common_GetFileHandle (Storm ordinal 10038)\n- FUN_6fb994dc - COF file reader (validates header structure)\n- FUN_6fb9b2e0 - String processor/converter (case normalization)\n- InsertGfxUnitRecord - Caller that uses returned unit\n",
