      "comment": "Remove graphics list node by search value.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get graphics info pointer from graphics ID (nGfxId in ECX)\n2. Assert pointer is not NULL; terminate if NULL\n3. Load list head pointer from gfx info + 0x28 (offset to linked list head)\n4. Loop through linked list comparing node[8] with search value (nSearchValue in EDX)\n5. When match found, unlink node from list:\n   - If previous node exists (dwPrevNode != 0): update previous[0x10] = current[0x10]\n   - If head node (dwPrevNode == 0): update gfxInfo[0x28] = current[0x10]\n6. Call Ordinal_10043(0x363, 0) for notification/logging\n7. Return 1 on success (node removed), 0 if not found\n\nParameters:\nnGfxId (ECX): Graphics info ID, passed to GetGfxInfoPointer\nnSearchValue (EDX): Value to match at offset +0x08 in list nodes\n\nReturns:\n0x00000001 (1): Node found and removed from linked list\n0x00000000 (0): Node not found in linked list (list traversal completed without match)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Assertion failure: Triggers if graphics info pointer is NULL (never returns)\n- Empty list: Returns 0 immediately (dVar1 == 0 at offset 0x28)\n- Head node removal: Updates gfxInfo[0x28] directly instead of prev pointer\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x28: Offset of linked list head pointer in graphics info structure\n0x08: Offset of search key field within each list node\n0x10: Offset of next pointer within each list node (links to next node)\n0x363: Ordinal_10043 notification code\n0xFFFFFFFF: Error value passed to FUN_6fb9a10f on assertion failure\n\nRelated Functions:\n- GetGfxInfoPointer() - Retrieves graphics info structure by ID\n- D2Common_AssertionOrdinal() - Assertion handler\n- Ordinal_10043() - Notification/logging function",
