      "comment": "Validate and clean up graphics data structures for a unit stat record.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Retrieve unit stat pointer from unit record using FUN_6fb958b0\n2. Validate stat pointer is non-null using Ordinal_10582; assert on failure\n3. If nStatIndex is 0xe (14 - animation stat), convert to effective stat index via FUN_6fb95870\n4. Check if stat at [nResult + 0x1e9 + nStatIndex] equals 0x01 (enabled)\n5. If stat 0x0c (graphics), perform special cleanup:\n   a. Retrieve graphics info pointer via GetGfxInfoPointer\n   b. Iterate through linked list at [pdwGfxInfo + 0x28] (offset 0x10 increment)\n   c. Free each node via Ordinal_10043(0x765, 0)\n   d. Clear graphics list head to NULL\n   e. Clear all graphics info buffer bytes (20 entries of 2 bytes each)\n   f. Notify graphics cache of cleanup via FUN_6fb90780\n6. If stat not 0x0c but enabled, call FUN_6fb90780 with converted index\n7. Return with no value\n\nParameters:\npUnit - Unit record pointer (passed in ECX via __fastcall)\nnStatIndex - Stat array index (passed in EDX via __fastcall)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Stat 0xe (animation) is converted to its effective index before processing\n- Graphics cleanup (stat 0x0c) requires traversal and freeing of linked list\n- Failed assertions immediately terminate via FUN_6fb9a10f(0xffffffff)\n- Magic numbers: 0x1e9 (stat enabled flags offset), 0x0c (graphics stat), 0x0e (animation stat), 0x28 (graphics list head), 0x10 (node next pointer offset), 0x765 (Ordinal_10043 param)",
