      "comment": "Validate and insert a unit graphics record into the GFX tracking table.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate unit type using FUN_6fb95830 - must return 1 (Ordinal_10582 = D2Common.GetUnitStat)\n2. Get unit stats pointer using FUN_6fb958b0\n3. Validate stats pointer is non-NULL using Ordinal_10582\n4. Check that GFX mode is enabled (byte at [stats + 0x1E9 + dwMode] must be 0x01)\n5. Check if mode already applied using FUN_6fb96e90, return 0 if true\n6. Initialize record buffer to 0x00\n7. Insert GFX record using InsertGfxUnitRecord, must succeed\n8. Commit mode changes using FUN_6fb96ec0 with mode flag 0x01\n9. Return success (0x01)\n\nParameters:\npUnit (UnitAny *) - Pointer to unit entity\ndwMode (dword) - GFX mode index to insert\n\nReturns:\nint - 0x01 on success, calls FUN_6fb9a10f(0xFFFFFFFF) on error (no return)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Assertion failures trigger abort via FUN_6fb9a10f(0xFFFFFFFF)\n- Invalid unit type or missing stats both trigger assertions at line 0x3E9/0x3EE\n- Disabled mode (stats[0x1E9 + dwMode] != 0x01) triggers format assertion (Ordinal_10018 = D2Common.AssertLog)\n- Already-applied mode returns early with 0x00 (no assertion)\n- InsertGfxUnitRecord failure triggers assertion at line 0x400\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x1E9 - Offset within stats structure to GFX mode flags array\n0x01 - GFX mode enabled/active flag value\n0x3E9, 0x3EE, 0x400, 0x408 - Assertion line numbers in source code\n\nNote: Function uses 2 stack-allocated temporaries optimized away (phantom variables in decompiler)",
