      "comment": "Initialize graphics unit record for rendering with mode-specific statistics\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Verify unit is valid type (must be type 2)\n2. Get unit stats pointer via GetUnitStats (Ordinal_10626)\n3. Lookup stat count for unit\n4. Check if requested mode stat is marked as initialized (0x01)\n5. Validate mode setup with CheckModeSetup - if invalid, format error message and abort\n6. Insert unit into graphics record table with slot ID\n7. Update graphics unit mode state (Ordinal_10024)\n\nParameters:\npUnit - Pointer to unit structure to initialize\nnMode - Mode index (0-based, used to index stat array at offset 0x14f)\n\nReturns:\n1 = Success, graphics unit record initialized\n0 = Failure, mode validation failed\n\nSpecial Cases:\nReturns immediately if CheckModeSetup fails (mode not ready)\nMultiple error assertion checks trigger abort with -1 parameter\nStack buffer abMsgBuffer[256] used for sprintf error formatting\nNote: Function uses SSA temporaries optimized by compiler",
