      "comment": "Initialize game memory arrays and random seed for new game instance.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Store game instance ID in g_dwCurrentGameId\n2. Clear inventory array (0x203 dwords)\n3. Clear equipment array (0x203 dwords)\n4. Clear skill array (0x118 dwords)\n5. Clear monster array (0x59d8 dwords / 23000 elements)\n6. Call Ordinal_10185 to seed Storm.dll random number generator\n7. Store RNG seed result in g_dwRandomSeed\n8. Chain to InitializeGameObjectData via JMP\n\nParameters:\n- dwGameInstanceId (ECX): Game instance/session identifier\n\nReturns:\n- void (continues to InitializeGameObjectData)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x203 (515 dwords = 2060 bytes): Inventory pool size\n- 0x118 (280 dwords = 1120 bytes): Skill pool size\n- 0x59d8 (23000 dwords = 92000 bytes): Monster pool size\n\nNote: Decompiler shows SSA temporaries (puVar2, iVar1) which are register reuse artifacts from compiler optimization. Actual code uses EDI/ECX for array iteration.",
