      "comment": "Finalize and clear COF (Compound Object Format) component data structures.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Iterate through COF component 1 table (g_pCofComponent1TableStart to g_pCofComponent1TableEnd)\n   - For each node with active flag (byte[1] & 0x01), subtract size from g_dwCofDataNodeCount\n   - Call Ordinal_10043(0xd07, 0) and Ordinal_10043(0xd08, 0) to finalize node\n2. Subtract g_dwCofDataNodeCount by component 1 count (g_dwCofComponent1DataSize)\n3. If g_dwCofComponent1Flag is set, call Ordinal_10043(0xd1b, 0) and clear flag\n4. Clear component 1 buffer with 0x203 DWORDs (515 * 4 = 2060 bytes)\n5. Iterate through COF component 2 table (g_pCofComponent2TableStart to g_pCofComponent2TableEnd)\n   - For each node with active flag, subtract size from g_dwCofDataNodeCount, finalize\n6. Subtract g_dwCofDataNodeCount by component 2 count (g_dwCofComponent2DataSize)\n7. If g_dwCofComponent2Flag is set, call Ordinal_10043(0xd2c, 0) and clear flag\n8. Clear component 2 buffer with 0x203 DWORDs\n9. Return\n\nParameters:\n(none)\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Each node has 1-byte flags at offset +0x04 (active = 0x01 bit set)\n- Node size stored at offset +0x08 (4-byte value, multiplied by -0x1c before subtraction)\n- Component tables are fixed size with boundary pointers\n- Both components use identical iteration pattern with different magic constants (0xd07/0xd08 vs others)\n- Note: Local variables use generic names (puVar1, iVar2, puVar3, puVar4) due to compiler optimizations\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0xd07, 0xd08: Ordinal constants for component 1 node finalization\n- 0xd1b: Ordinal constant for component 1 cleanup\n- 0xd2c: Ordinal constant for component 2 cleanup\n- 0x203: Buffer clear count (515 DWORDs)\n- 0xffffffe4: Multiplication constant (-28 in signed)",
