      "comment": "Remove entries from a graphics effect linked list that don't match valid state values (0x00 and 0x11).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call GetGfxInfoPointer(dwGfxType) to retrieve graphics info structure pointer\n2. If pointer is NULL, log assertion error and terminate with FUN_6fb9a10f(-1)\n3. Access linked list head at gfxInfo[0x28] (offset 40 bytes)\n4. Initialize pnPrevNode=NULL and iterate through list nodes\n5. For each node: read value at [node+0x00]\n6. If value != 0x00 AND value != 0x11 (invalid state):\n   a. Call Ordinal_10043(0x77c, 0) to trigger state invalidation handler\n   b. Remove node from list by updating next pointers:\n      - If pnPrevNode==NULL: update gfxInfo[0x28] = pnNextNode (unlink head)\n      - Else: update pnPrevNode[0x10] = pnNextNode (unlink middle node)\n   c. Stay at pnPrevNode for next iteration\n7. Else: advance pnPrevNode=pnCurrentNode to next node\n8. Read next pointer from pnCurrentNode[0x10] and continue iteration\n9. When pnCurrentNode==NULL, exit loop\n\nParameters:\ndwGfxType (ECX, uint): Graphics effect type ID passed to GetGfxInfoPointer\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Returns to caller after list cleanup complete\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If gfxInfo pointer is NULL, terminates with assertion (non-returning call)\n- Multiple invalid entries processed in single pass\n- List integrity maintained by unlinking removed nodes\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x28 - Offset to linked list head pointer within graphics info structure\n0x10 - Offset to next pointer field within linked list node\n0x00 - Valid state value (no removal)\n0x11 - Valid state value (no removal)\n0x77c - Ordinal_10043 event code for state invalidation\n0x772 - Assertion line number for NULL gfxInfo check",
      "tags": ["SRC_Gfx.cpp", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PARAM_1", "STRUCT_Other", "STRUCT_Control"]
