      "comment": "Render items within viewport bounds, applying position offsets and scroll adjustments.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if item has 0x20 flag set - return 0 if true (hidden/disabled)\n2. Validate item with Ordinal_10487 (D2Common.IsValidEntity) - return 0 if invalid\n3. Get scroll mode via Ordinal_10010 (D2Common.GetGameState)\n4. Retrieve item frame/class offset via FUN_6fb95870\n5. Get item class type via FUN_6fb95830 - if type==2 (special class):\n   - Retrieve stats table via FUN_6fb958b0\n   - Load from stats via Ordinal_10626\n   - Validate table entries at offsets 0x160, 0x128+offset - return 0 if null\n   - Extract base position: nOffsetX=[0x158], nOffsetY=[0x15c]\n6. Calculate base screen coordinates:\n   - nScreenX = nOffsetX - viewport_x + item_x + Ordinal_10333\n   - nScreenY = nOffsetY - viewport_y + item_y + Ordinal_10334\n7. Apply scroll mode adjustment (Ordinal_10010 return):\n   - Mode 1: Subtract quarter screen width\n   - Mode 2: Add quarter screen width\n   - Otherwise: Add 0x10 to Y offset\n8. Test rendering at adjusted coordinates via FUN_6fb93e10\n9. If rendering succeeds:\n   - Get transparency via Ordinal_10457 (D2Common.GetItemRarity)\n   - Initialize item data cache (18 dwords)\n   - Call FUN_6fb968e0 to populate cache\n   - If population succeeds: render via Ordinal_10075 (D2Common.DrawItem), return 1\n10. Return 0 (failed/clipped)\n\nParameters:\n  pItemStats (uint *) - Pointer to item structure containing flags, class, coordinates\n\nReturns:\n  1 if item rendered successfully, 0 if clipped/invalid/failed\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Null check after Ordinal_10626 triggers assertion + crash if failed\n  - Viewport offset adjustments vary by scroll mode (quarter-width offsets)\n  - Item class type==2 uses different stat table (special rendering)\n  - Cache initialization uses REP STOSD (18 dwords = 0x48 bytes)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x20 - Item visibility flag (0x20=hidden)\n  0x3a - Flag field offset in item structure\n  0x92 - Entity validation code for Ordinal_10487\n  0x160 - Stats table name field offset\n  0x128 - Class offset table base in stats\n  0x158 - Position X field in stats table\n  0x15c - Position Y field in stats table\n  0x10 - Default Y coordinate adjustment\n  0x12 - Cache element count (18 = 0x48 / 4 bytes per element)\n  2 - Item class type discriminant (special class requiring stats lookup)",
      "tags": ["SRC_Gfx.cpp", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PARAM_1", "STRUCT_Other", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
