      "comment": "Render a single game unit within the viewport display area.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check unit disabled flag (param_1[0x3a] & 0x20) - if set, return 0\n2. Get unit visual type via Ordinal_10487, return 0 if unavailable\n3. Get unit viewport state via FUN_6fb96e10\n4. If viewport state unavailable, render viewport items and return 1\n5. Initialize viewport offset state: check if active viewport via Ordinal_10007, Ordinal_10010\n6. Calculate base viewport coordinates from Ordinal_10333/10334 or Ordinal_10327/10330\n7. Adjust coordinates based on viewport scroll mode (Ordinal_10327, Ordinal_10330, Ordinal_10065, Ordinal_10066)\n8. Apply relative viewport offsets via GetRelativeViewportX/GetViewportYOffsetAdjusted\n9. Apply unit position offsets via FUN_6fb97a30, FUN_6fb97a50\n10. Calculate screen position offsets for unit special case (player unit) via FUN_6fb958b0\n11. Check for texture/graphics data via FUN_6fb93e10 - if unavailable, return 0\n12. Get graphics unit record via FUN_6fb95870\n13. Get graphics unit type/variant via Ordinal_10888\n14. Search graphics info list (GetGfxInfoPointer) for matching graphics unit record\n15. If not found, process unit graphics cleanup/initialization via FUN_6fb95830, ProcessUnitGfxCleanup, InsertGfxUnitRecord, InitializeGfxUnitRecord\n16. Get COF data pointer and component data via FUN_6fb96be0\n17. Get component orientation via Ordinal_10457\n18. Calculate component frame indices via FUN_6fb96f00, FUN_6fb96d10, FUN_6fb97260\n19. For each component layer, generate graphics layer data via FUN_6fb968e0\n20. If component graphics valid, render graphics layer via Ordinal_10075\n21. If viewport state was activated, restore original state via Ordinal_10008\n22. Return 1 if successful, 0 otherwise\n\nParameters:\n- pUnit (in ECX, pointer): UnitAny structure containing unit entity data (type flags at offset 0x3a, viewport state at offset 0x0)\n\nReturns:\n- EAX: 1 if unit rendered successfully, 0 if skipped/unavailable\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Player units (*pUnit == 2) receive special coordinate offset handling via FUN_6fb958b0\n- Units with disabled flag (0x20) are skipped immediately\n- Viewport scroll mode affects X-coordinate calculation by screen width / 4\n- Multiple graphics cleanup/initialization paths based on unit graphics state",
      "tags": ["SRC_Gfx.cpp", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "STRUCT_Room2", "STRUCT_ItemData", "PARAM_1", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData", "UNIT_PLAYER", "PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Path", "STRUCT_Skill", "STRUCT_Other", "PROP_LOOPHEAVY"]
