      "instructions": ["0xC14C0|SUB|ESP, 0x5c", "0xC14C3|PUSH|EBX", "0xC14C4|PUSH|EBP", "0xC14C5|PUSH|ESI", "0xC14C6|PUSH|EDI", "0xC14C7|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0xC14C9|XOR|EDI, EDI", "0xC14CB|XOR|EBX, EBX", "0xC14CD|CALL|0x6fb95870", "0xC14D2|MOV|EBP, EAX", "0xC14D4|CALL|0x6fb99256", "0xC14D9|MOV|ECX, ESI", "0xC14DB|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x10], EAX", "0xC14DF|CALL|0x6fb95830", "0xC14E4|CMP|EAX, 0x2"],
      "comment": "Renders inventory items in viewport with viewport offset adjustment.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Retrieve current stat pointer (param via ECX)\n2. Get current stat index from GetRelativeViewportX/GetViewportYOffsetAdjusted\n3. If viewport mode == 2, load base item coordinates from internal cache\n4. Calculate adjusted draw coordinates by subtracting relative viewport offsets\n5. Apply scroll window mode adjustment: Mode 1 = negative offset, Mode 2 = positive offset\n6. Call viewport validation to ensure coordinates within bounds\n7. If validation passes, retrieve item color and decoration from stat table\n8. Build 18-element integer array of item rendering parameters\n9. Call rendering backend with coordinates, color, decoration flags\n10. Return success (1) if rendered, failure (0) if validation/render failed\n\nParameters:\npStatIndices (uint *) - Pointer to stat index array (ECX register)\n\nReturns:\nbool - 1 (TRUE) if items rendered successfully, 0 (FALSE) if validation failed or viewport inactive\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Returns early if viewport mode != 2 (inactive viewport)\n- Returns 0 if stat table byte at offset 0x160 is null terminator\n- Returns 0 if stat decoration at offset 0x128 + index is null terminator\n- Scroll window adjustment: applies only if GetScrollWindowMode returns 1 or 2\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x160 - Offset in stat structure for viewport active flag\n0x128 - Offset in stat structure for stat decoration array base\n0x158 - Offset in stat structure for base X coordinate\n0x15c - Offset in stat structure for base Y coordinate\n0x3 - Mask for signed division rounding\n0x12 (18) - Size of item rendering parameter array in dwords\n0x8d5 - Assertion failure error code (line number reference)\n0xffffffff (-1) - Scroll window mode indicator\n0x1 - Success return code\n\nOrdinal References:\nOrdinal_10010 - GetWindowManagerState\nOrdinal_10076 - DrawItemInViewport\nOrdinal_10333 - GetItemViewportOffsetX\nOrdinal_10334 - GetItemViewportOffsetY\nOrdinal_10379 - GetStatDecorationInfo\nOrdinal_10457 - GetItemDecorationFlags\nOrdinal_10626 - ResolveStatHandle\n\nRelated Functions:\nGetRelativeViewportX() - Provides X viewport base offset\nGetViewportYOffsetAdjusted() - Provides Y viewport base offset\nGetScrollWindowMode() - Returns current scroll mode (0=none, 1=left, 2=right)\nFUN_6fb93e10() - Validates render coordinates within viewport bounds\nFUN_6fb91640() - Retrieves item color from stat\nFUN_6fb968e0() - Renders item array to viewport",
      "tags": ["SRC_Gfx.cpp", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PARAM_1", "STRUCT_Other", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
