      "comment": "Returns unit status indicator color based on health percentage threshold.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize global color palette on first call with Ordinal_10034 (CreateColor)\n2. Check if unit is valid via FUN_6fb95830 (unit validation)\n3. If invalid, return default green color (full health)\n4. Get unit health percentage via FUN_6fb958b0 and check stat offset 0x2fb\n5. Calculate health percentage: (resourceCount * 100) / maxResources\n6. Return color based on threshold: blue if <33%, yellow if 33-66%, green if 66-100%\n\nParameters:\npUnit (IMPLICIT ECX): undefined4 * - Pointer to unit structure\n\nReturns:\nbyte - Color palette index (blue/yellow/green per health threshold)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x0c0 - Color parameter for CreateColor (green high intensity)\n0x0e0 - Color parameter for CreateColor (yellow)\n0x2fb - Offset to unit stat check field\n0x21 (33 decimal) - Lower health threshold\n0x42 (66 decimal) - Upper health threshold\n6 - Resource stat ID for health",
      "tags": ["PARAM_1"]
