      "comment": "Render a graphics unit on the viewport with animation and level-specific graphics.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get current screen state (game/menu mode)\n2. Retrieve unit type and validate (0, 1, or 2 are valid)\n3. Calculate viewport position: origin + relative offset + unit-specific offset\n4. Adjust Y coordinate if scrolling horizontally (add 0x10 for mode 1/2)\n5. Perform visibility check via FUN_6fb93e10()\n6. If visible:\n   a) Get unit's graphic info (gfx ID, color index)\n   b) Lookup COF data in graphics table by gfx ID and item level\n   c) If not found and unit type is PLAYER (1):\n      - Cleanup old gfx via ProcessUnitGfxCleanup()\n      - Re-insert gfx via InsertGfxUnitRecord()\n      - Lookup again\n   d) If not found and unit type is MONSTER (0):\n      - Initialize empty gfx via InitializeGfxUnitRecord()\n      - Insert gfx record\n      - Lookup again\n   e) If not found and unit type is OBJECT (2):\n      - Search inventory for matching stat/level\n   f) For each composite frame (loop until frame count exhausted):\n      - Get component byte for frame\n      - Initialize 18-dword temp array for each frame\n      - Render frame via FUN_6fb968e0()\n      - If render succeeds, draw to screen via Ordinal_10076()\n   g) Return 1 (success)\n7. Return 0 (not visible or error)\n\nParameters:\n  pUnit (UnitAny *) - Unit entity to render (ECX register, fastcall)\n\nReturns:\n  dword - 1 if rendered successfully, 0 if not visible or error\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Player units (type 1) trigger cleanup/reinsertion if gfx missing\n  - Monster units (type 0) auto-initialize empty gfx\n  - Object units (type 2) search inventory for matching definitions\n  - Assertion errors terminate on invalid graphics pointers\n  - Phantom variables: 1 (local_60 optimized away)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x10 - Y adjustment for horizontal scroll modes\n  0xff - Color index bitmask (low byte only)\n  18 - Dword array size for frame rendering\n  0xffffffff - Default inventory index (all items)\n\nStructure Layout:\n  Offset | Size | Field Name | Type | Description\n  0x00   | 4    | adGfxFrames | dword[18] | Temp rendering frames\n  -0x4c  | 4    | dwGfxOption | dword | Temp COF option flags\n  -0x50  | 4    | dwInventoryType | dword | Item type from inventory\n  -0x54  | 4    | abFrameIndices | byte[4] | Component frame selector\n  -0x58  | 4    | abComponentIndices | byte[4] | Composite component index\n  -0x5c  | 4    | dwGfxComponent | dword | Current gfx component ID\n  -0x64  | 8    | anGfxOffsets | dword[2] | X/Y viewport offsets\n  -0x68  | 4    | pbGfxData | byte * | COF data pointer\n  -0x6c  | 4    | pGfxNode | uint * | Graphics table node pointer\n  -0x70  | 4    | dwColorIndex | dword | Unit color index (0x00-0xff)\n  -0x74  | 4    | nAnimationMode | dword | COF animation sequence\n  -0x78  | 4    | nViewportX | dword | Calculated X coordinate\n  -0x7c  | 4    | nViewportY | dword | Calculated Y coordinate",
      "tags": ["SRC_Gfx.cpp", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "STRUCT_Room2", "STRUCT_Room1", "STRUCT_ItemData", "PARAM_1", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData", "UNIT_PLAYER", "STRUCT_StatList", "PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Path", "STRUCT_Skill", "STRUCT_Other", "PROP_LOOPHEAVY"]
