      "api_calls": ["FogAssert", "IsItemNormalQuality", "GetTotalStatValue", "LoadOrRetrieveCelFrameData", "GetCelModeValue", "GetItemTransformPaletteShift", "GetItemDataFlags", "GetCelModeValue", "GfxInterfaceCall84", "GetCelModeValue", "...+1 more"],
      "instructions": ["0xC1BF0|SUB|ESP, 0x54", "0xC1BF3|PUSH|EBX", "0xC1BF4|PUSH|EBP", "0xC1BF5|PUSH|ESI", "0xC1BF6|MOV|EBP, EDX", "0xC1BF8|PUSH|EDI", "0xC1BF9|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0xC1BFB|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x14], EBP", "0xC1BFF|CALL|0x6fb95830", "0xC1C04|CMP|EAX, 0x4", "0xC1C07|JZ|0x6fb91c27", "0xC1C09|PUSH|0x988", "0xC1C0E|PUSH|0x6fbd84f4", "0xC1C13|PUSH|0x6fbd8718", "0xC1C18|CALL|0x6fb99a7a"],
      "comment": "Render a unit's sprite graphics with positional offset\nApplies sprite animation, orientation, and position transformations for unit rendering\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate unit is not type 4 (assert failure if invalid)\n2. Determine sprite tier level (0-3) based on unit experience points:\n   - 0-99: tier 0 (unskilled)\n   - 100-499: tier 1 (experienced)\n   - 500-4999: tier 2 (veteran)\n   - 5000+: tier 3 (elite)\n3. Initialize local 288-byte sprite buffer [18 dwords] with zeros via REP STOSD\n4. Call RenderSpriteSequence to populate sprite data, returns 0 on failure (early exit)\n5. Verify sprite sequence initialized (Ordinal_10055), return 0 on failure\n6. Retrieve base sprite frame index via Ordinal_10038\n7. Call RenderUnitSpriteFrame to validate sprite frame rendering with offset\n8. Fetch draw priority (uVar6) and sprite tag from Ordinal_10829\n9. Check configuration flag (0x400000, 0x9c2) via Ordinal_10707, set priority to 1 if set\n10. Call Ordinal_10072 to apply sprite positioning with offsets and priority\n11. Retrieve sprite dimensions via Ordinal_10037 (right coordinate >> 1) and Ordinal_10038 (height >> 1)\n12. Call RenderUnitGraphicsLayer to finalize rendering with computed dimensions\n\nParameters:\n  pUnit (ECX) - Pointer to unit data structure\n  nOffsetX (EDX) - Horizontal position offset\n  nOffsetY (Stack[4]) - Vertical position offset\n\nReturns:\n  0x1 - Rendering successful\n  0x0 - Early exit on sprite sequence failure\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Units with experience >= 100 get scaled sprite tiers\n  - Configuration flag 0x400000 forces priority mode 1 (high priority rendering)\n  - Sprite dimensions are right-shifted by 1 before use (divide by 2)\n  - Multiple early returns on sprite sequence validation failures",
      "tags": ["SRC_Gfx.cpp", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PARAM_3", "STRUCT_Skill", "UNIT_ITEM", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
    },
