      "api_calls": ["FogAssert", "GetExpansionModeIfInitialized", "STATLIST_GetUnitOwnerType", "UNITS_GetUnitX", "GfxIsDisplayTypeAccelerated", "GetUnitLevel", "GetUnitX", "GetOverlayStatEntry", "UNITS_GetUnitDirection", "GfxInterfaceCall84", "...+1 more"],
      "instructions": ["0xC1D70|SUB|ESP, 0x58", "0xC1D73|PUSH|EBX", "0xC1D74|PUSH|EBP", "0xC1D75|PUSH|ESI", "0xC1D76|PUSH|EDI", "0xC1D77|MOV|EDI, ECX", "0xC1D79|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x1c], EDX", "0xC1D7D|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x18], EDI", "0xC1D81|CALL|0x6fb628b0", "0xC1D86|MOV|ESI, EAX", "0xC1D88|TEST|ESI, ESI", "0xC1D8A|JNZ|0x6fb91daa", "0xC1D8C|PUSH|0x209", "0xC1D91|PUSH|0x6fbd84f4", "0xC1D96|PUSH|0x6fbd84e8"],
      "comment": "Render unit sprite graphics within adjusted viewport coordinates with animation frames.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get graphics info pointer from unit; assert if invalid\n2. Get root graphics node from info block; return if none exists\n3. Determine coordinate mode (normal or transformed):\n   - If mode 0 or (mode 4 with animation state 3): calculate base viewport offsets\n   - Else: apply coordinate transformation using Ordinal_10330/10327, adjust for scroll mode\n4. Adjust Y coordinate by image offsets (FUN_6fb97a30, FUN_6fb97a50, FUN_6fb97a70)\n5. If param_6 != 0, subtract 8 from Y coordinate\n6. Iterate through graphics node chain (offset 0x29 to next):\n   - Check visibility: skip if node type 6/8 with empty data or node has zero color\n   - Skip if param_3 == 0 and node color index is zero\n   - If visible: retrieve image subtype (piVar10[6]>>8), load stats with Ordinal_10591\n   - Clear 44-byte stat buffer (local_48)\n   - Call FUN_6fb968e0 to get render parameters with IMPLICIT piVar16=-1, piVar14=&param_4\n   - If render result != 0:\n     * Check image height against max height\n     * If color mode enabled and stat color flag 0x7d set: get green blood palette\n     * Call Ordinal_10072 to render image at (X+local_54+iVar2, Y+local_58)\n\nParameters:\n- pUnit (ECX): Pointer to unit data structure containing graphics pointer\n- dwPaletteMode (EDX): Palette/lighting mode applied during rendering\n- nBaseX (Stack[0x4]): Base X coordinate for viewport\n- nBaseY (Stack[0x8]): Base Y coordinate for viewport  \n- nOffsetX (Stack[0xc]): X offset within viewport\n- nOffsetY (Stack[0x10]): Y offset within viewport\n\nReturns:\n- void: Function renders directly via Ordinal_10072 calls\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Assertion failure: Graphics info pointer null or stats lookup fails\n- Early return: No graphics nodes exist for unit\n- Coordinate adjustment: Screen width >> 2 with sign extension for scroll modes 1/2\n- Animation: param_5 == -1 uses base Y; param_4 == -1 uses base X\n- Stat buffer: 44 bytes (11 dwords) allocated on stack for animation state\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x2c: Graphics info offset from unit pointer\n- 0x29: Next graphics node offset\n- 0x0b: Graphics node chain root offset in info\n- 0x34, 0x3c: Node visibility color indices\n- 0x7d: Sprite color mode flag offset in stats\n- 0x78: Sprite palette index offset in stats\n- 0x4, 0x8, 0x18, 0x1c, 0x20, 0x24: Node field offsets for dimensions/colors\n- 0x12: Loop count for buffer clearing (18 = 44/2.4, effectively clears 44 bytes)\n- 0xff: Color mask for palette lookup\n- 0x8: Y offset adjustment when param_6 != 0\n- 0x10: Default Y offset when param_5 == -1\n\nRelated Functions:\n- GetGfxInfoPointer() - Retrieve graphics info from unit (called first)\n- FUN_6fb95830() - Query unit animation state\n- FUN_6fb95870() - Get animation sub-state\n- Ordinal_10333/10334 - Get unit sprite X/Y coordinates\n- GetRelativeViewportX/Y() - Get viewport base offsets\n- FUN_6fb97a30/50/70 - Get image dimension offsets\n- FUN_6fb968e0 - Resolve animation frame parameters\n- Ordinal_10591 - Load sprite statistics/properties\n- Ordinal_10072 - Draw sprite image at coordinates\n",
      "tags": ["SRC_Gfx.cpp", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "STRUCT_Room2", "STRUCT_Room1", "STRUCT_ItemData", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData", "PARAM_6", "PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Path", "STRUCT_Skill", "STRUCT_Other"]
