      "api_calls": ["GetExpansionModeIfInitialized", "GetObjectDataEntryOffset", "FogAssert", "GetExpansionModeIfInitialized", "GetColorDepth", "SetColorDepth", "SetColorDepth", "GetUnitTargetXY", "GetDataTableEntry", "ProcessUnitWithWeaponAnimToken", "...+28 more"],
      "instructions": ["0xC1FE0|SUB|ESP, 0x100", "0xC1FE6|PUSH|EBX", "0xC1FE7|PUSH|EBP", "0xC1FE8|PUSH|ESI", "0xC1FE9|PUSH|EDI", "0xC1FEA|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x10], EDX", "0xC1FEE|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0xC1FF0|CALL|0x6fb99256", "0xC1FF5|MOV|ECX, ESI", "0xC1FF7|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x4c], EAX", "0xC1FFB|CALL|0x6fb95830", "0xC2000|CMP|EAX, 0x5", "0xC2003|JNZ|0x6fb92014", "0xC2005|POP|EDI", "0xC2006|POP|ESI"],
      "comment": "Render graphics components for a game unit (player, monster, object, etc)\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get unit type via FUN_6fb95830() and early exit if dead (type==5)\n2. Decrement and check resource handle validity via DecrementResourceCount()\n3. Calculate screen coordinates: apply viewport offsets (GetRelativeViewportX/Y), unit offset parameters, base position adjustments\n4. For player type (type==2): add equipment-based position offsets from stats at offset 0x158/0x15c\n5. If unit has graphics (FUN_6fb96e10 non-zero):\n   a. Calculate relative screen position\n   b. Adjust for scroll window mode (mode 1: subtract quarter-width, mode 2: add quarter-width)\n   c. Validate screen bounds via FUN_6fb93e10()\n   d. If validation fails, return 0\n   e. Call FUN_6fb91d70() if bDrawOutline=1\n   f. Iterate through component bytes (composition count from pbCofBytes[0]):\n      - For each component (byte value):\n        - If component=0xf: special effect rendering\n          - If unit type==1 and special flag set and color mode enabled: use green blood\n          - Call FUN_6fb968e0() to build component graphics\n          - Call FUN_6fb97350() to process component\n          - Apply FUN_6fb97600() for transformation if visible\n          - Render via Ordinal_10072() with calculated alpha\n        - Else component=0xe: render attached unit skill via RenderUnitSkill()\n        - Other components: standard rendering\n6. For non-graphics units:\n   a. Build graphics data via FUN_6fb968e0() with type-specific parameters\n   b. Validate via Ordinal_10055()\n   c. Calculate adjusted screen position with scroll offset\n   d. Render via Ordinal_10072() with type-specific alpha (3/4/5/7)\n   e. Apply color mode for special effects\n\nParameters:\npUnit - Pointer to UnitAny structure (unit to render)\ndwGfxFrame - Graphics frame number/index for animation\nnOffsetX - Additional X coordinate offset (from caller)\nnOffsetY - Additional Y coordinate offset (from caller)\nnFlags - Control flags (bit 0: special processing)\nbDrawOutline - If 1, draw selection outline around unit\n\nReturns:\n1 - Rendering succeeded and unit displayed\n0 - Unit not renderable (invalid, dead, off-screen, or resource unavailable)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Dead units (type==5) return immediately without rendering\n- Units without graphics delegate to simplified rendering path\n- Player type adds equipment offsets for proper visual appearance\n- Component 0xf triggers special effect rendering (blood type varies by color mode)\n- Green blood used when color mode enabled and unit is corpse with special flag\n- Alpha blending varies: standard (5), special effects (3/4/7), corpse-specific (varies)",
      "tags": ["SRC_Gfx.cpp", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "STRUCT_Room2", "STRUCT_Room1", "STRUCT_ItemData", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData", "STRUCT_StatList", "PARAM_6", "PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Path", "STRUCT_Skill", "STRUCT_Other", "PROP_LOOPHEAVY"]
