      "instructions": ["0xC2A60|PUSH|EBX", "0xC2A61|MOV|BL, DL", "0xC2A63|CALL|0x6fb628b0", "0xC2A68|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0xC2A6A|JNZ|0x6fb92a8a", "0xC2A6C|PUSH|0xab4", "0xC2A71|PUSH|0x6fbd84f4", "0xC2A76|PUSH|0x6fbd84e8", "0xC2A7B|CALL|0x6fb99a7a", "0xC2A80|ADD|ESP, 0xc", "0xC2A83|PUSH|-0x1", "0xC2A85|CALL|0x6fb9a10f", "0xC2A8A|MOV|ECX, 0x14", "0xC2A8F|MOV|byte ptr [EAX], BL", "0xC2A91|ADD|EAX, 0x2"],
      "comment": "Fill graphics info structure with repeated byte pattern\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Retrieve graphics info pointer for unit ID (ECX) via GetGfxInfoPointer\n2. Validate pointer is non-NULL; assert if NULL\n3. Initialize loop counter to 0x14 (20 iterations)\n4. Write fill byte (BL/param_2) to current offset, increment pointer by 2\n5. Decrement counter and repeat until zero\n6. Return\n\nThis writes 20 bytes at 2-byte strides (40 bytes total span) to initialize graphics metadata.\n\nParameters:\n- nUnitId (ECX): Unit/item ID to look up graphics info for\n- byFillValue (DL): Byte value to write repeatedly (0x00 for clear/reset)\n\nReturns:\n- void (no return value)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Assert failure if GetGfxInfoPointer returns NULL (invalid unit ID)\n- Assertion triggers abnormal termination via FUN_6fb9a10f(-1)",
