      "instructions": ["0xC2AA0|MOV|EAX, [0x6fc1bd34]", "0xC2AA5|SUB|ESP, 0x20", "0xC2AA8|PUSH|EBX", "0xC2AA9|PUSH|EBP", "0xC2AAA|XOR|EBP, EBP", "0xC2AAC|PUSH|ESI", "0xC2AAD|CMP|EAX, EBP", "0xC2AAF|PUSH|EDI", "0xC2AB0|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0xC2AB2|JNZ|0x6fb92ace", "0xC2AB4|CALL|dword ptr [0x6fba6098]", "0xC2ABA|MOV|ECX, dword ptr [0x6fc1bd24]", "0xC2AC0|ADD|ECX, 0x258", "0xC2AC6|CMP|EAX, ECX", "0xC2AC8|JC|0x6fb92d8b"],
      "comment": "Initialize monster and skill entity slots for game units.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if initialization forced or timing constraint met (> 600ms elapsed)\n2. Get game context and validate entity data structure exists (Ordinal_10342)\n3. Call Ordinal_10035 to retrieve unit class list and count\n4. Loop through each unit class:\n   a. Check player input requirement or seed validation\n   b. Get entity list head pointer from unit class at offset 0x2c\n   c. Traverse linked list of entities (pointer at offset 0x10c)\n   d. For each entity, determine unit class (0 = Skill, 1 = Monster)\n   e. If unit class is Monster (1):\n      - Get monster type, unit index, skill index\n      - Validate monster type not 0xc or corresponding flag not set\n      - Retrieve monster stat structure via Ordinal_10582\n      - Iterate through all monster definition array entries\n      - Check if entity-definition slot is initialized\n      - If not, call InitializeMonsterSlot; if success set slot=1, else clear\n      - If initialized, update monster state via Ordinal_10058\n   f. If unit class is Skill (0):\n      - Clear loading mode flag if random seed active\n      - Iterate through all skill definition array entries\n      - Check if entity-definition slot is initialized\n      - If not, call InitializeMonsterSlot; if success set slot=1, else clear\n      - If initialized, update skill state via Ordinal_10058\n5. Check frame rate cap (Ordinal_10057 < 0x1d) before processing next unit\n6. Update g_dwInitFlags with current tick count\n\nParameters:\nnMode (ECX): int - Loading screen mode flag (0=normal, 1=show loading screen)\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Function requires valid entity data structure; assertion on null\n- Frame rate capped at 30 FPS (0x1e = 30)\n- Timing delay of 600ms (0x258) between full initializations\n- Skill/monster init disabled during normal play if random seed set\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x2c - Entity list head offset in unit class structure\n0x43 - Entity next pointer offset in linked list\n0x1e9 - Monster availability byte offset in stat structure\n0x10c - Entity next pointer offset for linked list traversal\n0x1d - Frame rate cap (30 FPS)\n0x258 - 600ms timing delay between initializations\n0x1f - Bit mask for status flag validation\n0xa0 - Unit class data structure size\n\nOrdinal Mappings:\nOrdinal_10342 - D2Common.GetUnitStat - Get active unit pointer\nOrdinal_10035 - D2Common.GetQuestRecord - Get unit class list and count\nOrdinal_10057 - D2Game.CheckFrameRate - Frame rate check\nOrdinal_10582 - D2Common.GetPlayerStats - Get stat structure\nOrdinal_10058 - D2Common.UpdateEntityState - Update entity state\n\nRelated Functions:\n- InitializeLoadingScreenUI(bool) - Show loading animation\n- GetTickCount() - Retrieve system tick count\n- FUN_6fb95870(pEntity) - Get entity type\n- FUN_6fb95830(pEntity) - Get unit class\n- FUN_6fb958b0(pEntity) - Get unit index\n- FUN_6fb92dc0(pEntity, pDef, nMode) - Initialize entity slot\n- GetGameContext() - Get current game context",
      "tags": ["SRC_Gfx.cpp", "PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PARAM_1", "STRUCT_Other", "PROP_LOOPHEAVY", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
