      "comment": "Initializes overlay data structure with effect parameters and properties.\n\nOrdinals Used:\n  Ordinal_10227 - Check class-specific overlay restrictions\n  Ordinal_10591 - Retrieve overlay stat entry by type index\n  Ordinal_10582 - Query related stat structure for mode validation\n  Ordinal_10042 - Allocate overlay structure memory (0xA8 bytes)\n  Ordinal_10430 - Get unit light mode for intensity adjustment\n  Ordinal_10918 - Generate random color seed for effect variation\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate overlay type (param_2) is within valid range (0x0-0x124)\n2. If type >= 0xBE, check class restriction via Ordinal_10227 - abort if restricted\n3. Retrieve stat entry via Ordinal_10591 based on overlay type\n4. Abort if stat entry is NULL or invalid\n5. Call GetGameContext to obtain current game state reference\n6. Check unit forbidden flag (0x40000) in param_1[0x3B] - early return if set\n7. Validate special case conditions:\n   - If mode in {3,4,8} AND unit type==1 AND Ordinal_10582 returns valid entry AND entry[0x199] != 0x00 return\n8. If overlay type < 0x8C or (0x8C < type < 0x8E excluding 0x9E), call FUN_6fb93500\n9. Allocate overlay structure (0xA8 bytes = 42 dwords) via Ordinal_10042(0xB36)\n10. Zero-initialize all 42 fields of overlay structure\n11. Set overlay type (field[0]) and class (field[1]) from parameters\n12. Call FUN_6fb97910 to calculate initial duration, store in field[7]\n13. Initialize overlay mode (field[2]):\n    - If mode==2 set field[2]=1\n    - If mode==6: field[6] = (duration > 0) ? Ordinal_10918() : 0\n    - Else: field[2]=param_5, field[3]=param_6, field[4]=param_7\n14. Copy stat properties into overlay: field[8-10] from stat offsets 0x50, 0x54, 0x74\n15. Query unit light mode via Ordinal_10430, apply conditional adjustment to field[9]:\n    - Mode 0: add stat[0x58]\n    - Mode 1: add stat[0x5C]\n    - Mode 2: add stat[0x60]\n    - Mode 3: add stat[0x64]\n    - Mode -1: add 0x4B\n16. Create light effect if stat[0x70] != 0 via CreateAudioContext, store in field[0x10]\n17. If light has separate radius, apply SetLightRadius(light, stat[0x70])\n18. Query graphics context via GetGfxInfoPointer\n19. Store stat[0x44] in field[0xD] (color/appearance data)\n20. Link overlay into graphics chain via field[0x29]\n21. For mode==8 overlays (special case):\n    - Set field[0xE]=param_5\n    - Scan existing mode 8 overlays in chain for matching param_5\n    - If found with field[0xF]==0: copy both field[0xF] and field[2]\n    - If found with field[0xF]!=0: set field[0xF]=0\n    - If no match found: set field[0xF]=1, field[2]=0\n22. Apply color parameters (param_4, param_8) with Ordinal_10918 for random colors\n    - If param_4 != 0 and (param_4 & 0xFFFFFF) != 0: field[6] = random color\n    - If param_8 != 0 and (param_8 & 0xFFFFFFF) != 0: field[5] += random color\n23. Store final duration multiplier from stat[0x68] << 4 into field[5]\n24. Copy param_8 duration modifier to field[0xA] via stat[0x74]\n\nParameters:\n  pUnit (IMPLICIT ECX): int* - pointer to unit structure being affected\n  nOverlayType (IMPLICIT EDX): int - overlay type index into stat tables (0x0-0x124)\n  nMode (Stack[0x4]): int - overlay operational mode (2=default, 6=light, 8=special, etc)\n  dwColorParam (Stack[0x8]): dword - color parameter with random seed (RGB component)\n  nParam5 (Stack[0xC]): int - mode-specific parameter 5 (time value, mode-2 default)\n  nParam6 (Stack[0x10]): int - mode-specific parameter 6 (time value)\n  nParam7 (Stack[0x14]): int - mode-specific parameter 7 (time value)\n  dwColorParam2 (Stack[0x18]): dword - secondary color parameter with random component\n\nReturns:\n  void - always returns successfully after initialization; failures abort via FUN_6fb9a10f\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Overlay type validation: must be 0-0x124 (290 valid types)\n  - Class restriction: types >= 0xBE may be restricted based on game class\n  - Unit forbidden flag: 0x40000 in unit[0x3B] blocks all overlay creation\n  - Mode 8 special handling: scans existing mode-8 overlays for duplicate param_5 state management\n  - Light mode -1: uses fallback value 0x4B for light intensity adjustment\n  - Color randomization: requires non-zero RGB component to apply Ordinal_10918 seed\n  - Phantom Variables: Function uses compiler-optimized register temporaries not visible in decompilation\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x124 (292) - maximum valid overlay type index\n  0x125 - overlay type validation limit (0x124 < check)\n  0xBE (190) - class restriction threshold\n  0xA8 (168) - overlay structure size in bytes (42 dwords)\n  0xB36 (2870) - memory allocation ID for overlay structures\n  0x40000 - unit forbidden flag mask for overlay creation\n  0x199 - stat entry restriction check offset\n  0x50,0x54 - stat base property offsets (RGB color components)\n  0x58,0x5C,0x60,0x64 - stat light mode adjustment offsets\n  0x68 - stat duration multiplier offset (value << 4)\n  0x70 - stat light effect existence check offset\n  0x6C - stat light intensity base offset\n  0x79,0x7A,0x7B - stat color component offsets (RGB bytes)\n  0x4B (75) - light mode -1 fallback intensity value\n\nRelated Functions:\n  - FUN_6fb93500: Apply overlay mode-specific initialization\n  - FUN_6fb97910: Calculate overlay duration based on unit stats\n  - Ordinal_10227: Check class-specific overlay restrictions\n  - Ordinal_10591: Look up overlay stat entry by type index\n  - Ordinal_10582: Retrieve related stat structure for mode validation\n  - Ordinal_10042: Allocate overlay structure memory\n  - Ordinal_10430: Query unit light mode for intensity adjustment\n  - Ordinal_10918: Generate random color seed for effect variation\n  - CreateAudioContext: Create light effect with color properties\n  - SetLightRadius: Override default light effect radius\n  - GetGfxInfoPointer: Retrieve graphics rendering chain",
