      "comment": "Remove audio context from graphics list by context state.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Retrieve gfx info pointer from this object via GetGfxInfoPointer()\n2. Assert gfx info pointer is valid, panic if null\n3. Validate context state via Ordinal_10591() lookup\n4. Assert state lookup succeeds, panic if 0\n5. Walk context linked list from gfx_info[0xb] (list head)\n6. For each context node:\n   - Check if node[1] == param_1: context state matches, remove it\n   - Check if node[0] type == 0x4 or 0x9:\n     - If type match: check node[8] == param_1 or node[12] == param_1\n   - If no match: continue to next node via node[0xa4]\n7. Call RemoveAudioContextFromGfxList() to unlink matching context\n8. Return on end of list or successful removal\n\nParameters:\nthis (void*): GfxInfo object containing audio context list\nnContextState (int): Context state ID to search and remove\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0xb: Offset in gfxInfo to audio context list head pointer\n0x4, 0x9: Context type flags indicating audio context types\n0x8, 0xc: Field offsets within context node for state IDs\n0xa4: Offset in context node to next node pointer\n0x2c: Offset to linked list head in decompiled view",
