      "comment": "Remove all audio contexts associated with a unit from the graphics system.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call GetGfxInfoPointer to retrieve graphics info structure for unit\n2. Assert if graphics info is null, then terminate with error code -1\n3. Access audio context list at offset 0xB from graphics info\n4. While audio context list is not empty:\n   - Store next context pointer from current context at offset 0x29\n   - Call RemoveAudioContextFromGfxList to remove current context\n   - Move to next context in chain\n5. Return after all contexts processed\n\nParameters:\n  param_1 (int): Unit ID - identifies which unit's audio contexts to remove\n\nReturns:\n  void - Function returns after all audio contexts have been removed or error exit\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If graphics info pointer is null, assertion failure triggers with code 0xBB6 (3000 decimal)\n  - Function does not return on assertion failure; error handler exits process\n  \nMagic Numbers:\n  0xBB6: Assertion error code (line 3000 in source)\n  0xB: Offset of audio context list within graphics info structure\n  0x29: Offset of next context pointer within audio context node\n  0xA4: Offset of next linked context within audio context structure (assembly offset EDX+0xA4)\n  0x2C: Offset within graphics info to audio context chain base (assembly offset EAX+0x2C)",
