      "comment": "Handles unit graphics initialization based on unit state mode. Note: Function uses SSA temporary (iVar1) optimized away by decompiler.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Query unit initialization state via FUN_6fb95830 (returns mode: 0=new, 1=existing, 2=reinit)\n2. Query unit animation state via FUN_6fb958b0 (returns animation flags)\n3. Query unit graphic slot index via FUN_6fb95870 (returns gfx slot)\n4. Call Ordinal_11013 (Unknown - updates state references, possibly Ordinal_11013 = D2Client.GetUnitGfxMode or similar)\n5. Switch on dwInitMode:\n   - Mode 0 (New unit): Insert gfx unit record, validate no existing gfx state, initialize graphics asset\n   - Mode 1 (Existing unit): Clean up existing graphics before reinit\n   - Mode 2 (Reinit): Reinitialize graphics record for same unit\n   - Invalid: Assert and terminate with 0xffffffff error code\n\nParameters:\npUnit - Pointer to UnitAny structure for unit being initialized\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value, asserts on invalid state\n\nSpecial Cases:\nMode 0 validates dwInitMode is 0 after Ordinal call (else assertion at 0x465)\nInsertGfxUnitRecord must succeed (else assertion at 0x469)\nInvalid mode triggers assertion at 0xc0d and fatal error\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x465 - Assertion line number for dwInitMode validity check\n0x469 - Assertion line number for InsertGfxUnitRecord success\n0xc0d - Assertion line number for invalid dwInitMode (2850 decimal)\n0xffffffff - Fatal error code parameter to FUN_6fb9a10f",
