      "comment": "Clear inventory slots for a unit based on its type.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if nUnitType >= 0x10, if so return early (no action needed)\n2. Call FUN_6fb95830 to get unit type and store in nSlotIndex\n3. If nSlotIndex == 0: process 0x14 (20) slots via ClearInventorySlot loop\n4. If nSlotIndex == 1: verify second call returns 1, then clear 0x10 (16) slots via ClearInventorySlot loop\n5. If nSlotIndex == 2: verify second call returns 2, then clear 0x8 (8) slots via ClearInventorySlot loop\n6. For any other value: trigger assertion failure with FUN_6fb9a10f\n\nParameters:\npUnitData (uint *) - Pointer to unit structure data, passed in ECX\nnUnitType (int) - Unit type value for conditional checks, passed in EDX\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If nUnitType >= 0x10: early return, function is a no-op\n- Assertion failures call FUN_6fb9a10f(0xffffffff) which terminates execution\n- Type validation ensures unit structure matches expected inventory slot count\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x10 (16) - Threshold for early return, inventory type boundary, slot count for type 1\n0x14 (20) - Total slots for type 0\n0x8 (8) - Slot count for type 2\n0xc25, 0x5de, 0x5b4, 0x5a4 - Assertion file/line references for debug info",
