      "comment": "Initialize unit graphics rendering data for display and animation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Retrieve current unit properties (level, type from param_1)\n2. Check for existing graphics record in GfxInfo list\n3. If exists: use current mode; if missing: process unit state\n4. Unit state 0: Insert new graphics record and initialize\n5. Unit state 1: Clear old graphics, search mode adjusted if 0xFFFFFFFF\n6. Unit state 2: Initialize graphics record directly\n7. For valid graphics record: load cel context from COF data\n8. Extract graphics width/height from cel context via Ordinal calls\n9. Write output dimensions to pnGfxWidth and pnGfxHeight\n\nParameters:\npUnitAny: Pointer to unit structure (contains level, type, graphics state at offset 0x38)\nnMode: Graphics/animation mode identifier (0xFFFFFFFF indicates refresh)\npnGfxWidth: Output pointer for graphics width (set from cel context)\npnGfxHeight: Output pointer for graphics height (set from cel context)\n\nReturns:\nVoid; output parameters pnGfxWidth and pnGfxHeight filled with dimensions on success. Asserts on missing GfxInfo or invalid records.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- nMode=0xFFFFFFFF triggers mode refresh from current unit\n- Missing GfxInfo pointer asserts (program termination)\n- Missing graphics record after loading asserts (program termination)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x0E: Offset in unit structure for level field\n0x38: Offset in unit structure for graphics state\n0x50: Offset in unit structure for sprite palette offset\n0x14: Graphics record offset for COF data flag check\n0xFF: Mask for animation frame extraction\n0x08: Shift for palette index extraction",
      "tags": ["SRC_Gfx.cpp", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "STRUCT_Room1", "STRUCT_ItemData", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData", "UNIT_PLAYER", "PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Skill", "PARAM_4", "STRUCT_Other", "PROP_LOOPHEAVY"]
