      "instructions": ["0xC3BA0|SUB|ESP, 0xc", "0xC3BA3|PUSH|EBX", "0xC3BA4|PUSH|EBP", "0xC3BA5|PUSH|ESI", "0xC3BA6|PUSH|EDI", "0xC3BA7|PUSH|0x1", "0xC3BA9|LEA|EAX, [ESP + 0x1c]", "0xC3BAD|PUSH|-0x1", "0xC3BAF|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x1c], EDX", "0xC3BB3|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0xC3BB5|PUSH|EAX", "0xC3BB6|CALL|0x6fb958f0", "0xC3BBB|PUSH|EAX", "0xC3BBC|PUSH|ESI", "0xC3BBD|CALL|0x6fb98482"],
      "comment": "Initialize or update unit graphics state and validate position bounds.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Setup temporary structures: abLevelBuf[4], dwOne=1, dwUnitLevel=0xFFFFFFFF\n2. Call FUN_6fb958f0 to get initial graphics mode type\n3. Call Ordinal_10888(GetUnitStat) to retrieve unit stat value, stored in dwUnitLevel\n4. Get gfx info pointer via GetGfxInfoPointer, assert if NULL\n5. Search linked list at [pGfxInfo+0x28] for matching dwMode/dwLevel pair\n6. If found: validate and branch to final bounds check (LAB_6fb93d20)\n7. If mode==1: call ProcessUnitGfxCleanup, then rescan list with new position\n8. If mode==0: validate unit not in gfx, insert new record, call InitializeGfxUnitRecord\n9. If mode==2: call InitializeGfxUnitRecord to reinitialize\n10. Call SearchInventoryItemByStatAndLevel to update equipped items\n11. Final validation: retrieve matching gfx node from updated list\n12. Call FUN_6fb96be0 to get COF (costume/frame) bounds\n13. Validate X bounds: (cof[8] - 0x10 + dwXCoordOffset <= nX2 < cof[12] + 0x10 + dwXCoordOffset)\n14. Validate Y bounds: (cof[16] - 0x10 + nY <= nY2 < cof[20] + 0x10 + nY)\n15. Return 1 if bounds valid, 0 otherwise\n\nParameters:\npUnit (IMPLICIT ECX, UnitAny *) - Unit to process for graphics initialization\nnX (IMPLICIT EDX, int) - X viewport coordinate base offset\nnY (int) - Y viewport coordinate base offset\nnX2 (int) - X position coordinate to validate against COF bounds\nnY2 (int) - Y position coordinate to validate against COF bounds\n\nReturns:\n1 (EAX=0x1) - Position valid within COF bounds, unit gfx initialized\n0 (EAX=0x0) - Position outside COF bounds or gfx initialization failed\n\nSpecial Cases:\nMagic number 0xFFFFFFFF indicates initial unset level value\nMagic number 0x10 collision padding added/subtracted from COF bounds\nMagic number 0x28 offset to gfx list head in GfxInfo struct\nMagic number 0x14 offset increment for linked list traversal\nAssertion D2Common_AssertionOrdinal called at 0x33f, 0x328, 0xc73, 0x465, 0x469, 0x32e on gfx resource failures\nFunction calls ProcessUnitGfxCleanup, InitializeGfxUnitRecord, InsertGfxUnitRecord to modify unit state\n\nStructure Layout (GfxInfo):\nOffset | Size | Field Name      | Type | Description\n0x28   | 4    | pGfxListHead    | int* | Linked list of active gfx units [10]\n0x8-14 | 4    | CofBoundsTable  | int* | COF bounds for X/Y dimensions (indexed by ID)\n\nOrdinal Calls:\nOrdinal_10888 = D2Common.GetUnitStat(pUnit, nMode, pbBuffer, dwMaxVal, dwDefaultVal) - Retrieves unit stat values\n\nRelated Functions:\n- FUN_6fb958f0() - Get initial unit gfx mode\n- FUN_6fb95870() - Get unit frame/animation ID\n- FUN_6fb95830() - Check/validate unit gfx mode type\n- ProcessUnitGfxCleanup() - Clear existing gfx state for unit\n- GetGfxInfoPointer() - Retrieve global gfx database\n- InitializeGfxUnitRecord() - Create or reinitialize gfx record\n- InsertGfxUnitRecord() - Add unit record to gfx list\n- FUN_6fb96be0() - Retrieve COF header/bounds by ID\n- FUN_6fb96ec0() - Assign skills/position to gfx record\n- SearchInventoryItemByStatAndLevel() - Update equipped items for gfx\n- FUN_6fb9a10f() - Assert failure handler",
      "tags": ["UNIT_PLAYER", "SRC_Gfx.cpp", "PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "STRUCT_Skill", "PARAM_5", "STRUCT_Other", "PROP_LOOPHEAVY", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
