      "api_count": 8,
      "api_calls": ["ProcessUnitWithWeaponAnimToken", "FogAssert", "FogAssert", "FogAssert", "FogAssert", "FogAssert", "FogAssert", "FogAssert"],
      "instructions": ["0xC3E10|SUB|ESP, 0xc", "0xC3E13|PUSH|EBX", "0xC3E14|PUSH|EBP", "0xC3E15|PUSH|ESI", "0xC3E16|PUSH|EDI", "0xC3E17|PUSH|0x1", "0xC3E19|LEA|EAX, [ESP + 0x1c]", "0xC3E1D|PUSH|-0x1", "0xC3E1F|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x1c], EDX", "0xC3E23|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0xC3E25|PUSH|EAX", "0xC3E26|CALL|0x6fb958f0", "0xC3E2B|PUSH|EAX", "0xC3E2C|PUSH|ESI", "0xC3E2D|CALL|0x6fb98482"],
      "comment": "Renders graphics components for a game unit at specified viewport position\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize search parameters: level byte buffer (0xffffffff, 0x1), offset storage\n2. Get unit level via Ordinal_10888 (D2Common.GetUnitStat - STAT_LEVEL)\n3. Fetch GfxInfo pointer, assert non-NULL\n4. Get unit graphics type via FUN_6fb95870, search GfxInfo linked list for matching (type, level)\n5. If found, render existing graphics node and exit\n6. Get unit type state (0=new, 1=cleanup needed, 2=reinit)\n7. If type==1: cleanup old graphics via ProcessUnitGfxCleanup, then search linked list for mode match\n8. If type==0: allocate new GfxUnit via InsertGfxUnitRecord, initialize graphics via FUN_6fb96ec0\n9. If type==2: reinitialize via InitializeGfxUnitRecord\n10. Search inventory items via SearchInventoryItemByStatAndLevel with level=-1\n11. Reacquire current unit mode, fetch GfxInfo, search linked list for node with matching (type, level)\n12. Get COF (Composition Object Format) header via FUN_6fb96be0\n13. Calculate adjusted screen position: x=currX + cofOffset.x - (centered ? (width_diff/2) : 0), y=currY + cofOffset.y\n14. Validate position within bounds: check x vs (screenWidth-1), y vs (screenHeight-1)\n15. If position valid, check layout validity then return true; otherwise return false\n\nParameters:\npUnit (__fastcall ECX) - Unit to render graphics for\nnCurrX (__fastcall EDX) - Current viewport X coordinate\nnCurrY (stack+0x4) - Current viewport Y coordinate\ndwMode (stack+0x8) - Graphics mode/state identifier\nfCenterAdjust (stack+0xc) - Non-zero to center graphics, subtract half-width from position\n\nReturns:\ntrue - Graphics bounds check passed, position is valid within viewport\nfalse - Position exceeds viewport boundaries or layout invalid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Handles unit type transitions: new (0), cleanup (1), reinitialization (2)\n- Validates GfxInfo pointer multiple times to catch NULL dereference bugs\n- Manages linked list of graphics nodes by (type, level) pairing\n- Centers large sprites by subtracting (width_diff/2) from X coordinate\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0xffffffff - Search ID for full range lookup\n0x1 - Index ID constant\n0x328, 0x33f, 0x465, 0x469, 0xc9e, 0x32e - Assertion line numbers in original source\n\nRelated Functions:\n- ProcessUnitGfxCleanup() - Removes old graphics before type transitions\n- SearchInventoryItemByStatAndLevel() - Inventory search with level/stat filtering\n- InsertGfxUnitRecord() - Allocates new graphics node to linked list\n- InitializeGfxUnitRecord() - Resets existing graphics node state\n- GetGfxInfoPointer() - Retrieves global graphics info table",
      "tags": ["UNIT_PLAYER", "SRC_Gfx.cpp", "PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "STRUCT_Skill", "PARAM_5", "STRUCT_Other", "PROP_LOOPHEAVY", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
