      "comment": "Initialize COF (Component Object Format) component data for equipment rendering.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate component data not already initialized (g_aEquipmentArray)\n2. Format component path: sprintf with base path + component name from lookup table\n3. Load component file via Ordinal_10038() and FUN_6fb994dc()\n4. Parse component data: iterate through COF components, validate direction count\n5. Build hash table: compute hash from component filename, chain component nodes\n6. Update global counters: increment total COF data node count\n\nParameters:\n  dwComponentType (ECX): IMPLICIT - equipment component type (0-255, masked)\n\nReturns:\n  void - initializes global g_aEquipmentArray flag when complete\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Assertion if component file fails to load (ptHash->lpbFileData missing)\n  - Assertion if direction count > 0x40 (invalid COF header)\n  - Assertion if filename length >= 255 bytes (buffer overflow check)\n  - No return on failed assertions - calls FUN_6fb9a10f(0xffffffff) for termination\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x104: buffer size for formatted filename\n  0xff: component type mask (param_1 & 0xff)\n  0x18: COF structure field offset stride\n  0x1a: offset to direction count byte in COF header\n  0x40: maximum direction count (assertion limit)\n  0x1ff0000/0xff00/0x1ff: hash computation bit masks\n  0xffffffff: initial string length counter, error flag for FUN_6fb9a10f\n\nStructure Layout:\n  Offset | Size | Field Name | Type | Description\n  0x0    | 4    | pNextNode  | uint*| Hash table chain link\n  0x4    | 4    | dwUnused   | uint | Unused/alignment field\n  0x8    | 4    | dwStrLen   | int  | Filename string length counter\n  0xc    | 4    | pStrStart  | uint*| Pointer to string data start\n  0x10   | 4    | pReserved  | uint*| Reserved/alignment field\n  0x14   | 4    | dwFileSize | int  | Loaded file size from FUN_6fb994dc\n  0x18   | varies | szFilename| char[]| Null-terminated component filename\n\nRelated Functions:\n- Ordinal_10038: Load file resource (likely D2Common.OpenFile)\n- Ordinal_502: Compute hash of string (likely D2Common.GetHashCode)\n- FUN_6fb994dc: Load component data from file\n- FUN_6fb9a10f: Assertion failure handler (terminates execution)",
