      "comment": "Reset COF (Character Object Format) component data and clear equipment array\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize loop counter for COF component table traversal (pdwTablePtr = &g_pCofComponent2TableStart)\n2. Outer loop: Iterate through COF component table from start to end address\n3. Inner loop: Walk linked list of COF nodes starting at current table entry\n4. Check node flag: If byte[node+1] & 0x01 is set, decrement g_dwCofDataNodeCount\n5. On flagged node: Call Ordinal_10043(0xd07, 0) to notify subsystem (GetSkillData ordinal)\n6. On flagged node: Call Ordinal_10043(0xd08, 0) to notify subsystem (GetSkillData ordinal)\n7. Move to next node in linked list via *node pointer (pdwNodePtr = *pdwCofComponent)\n8. After all linked lists processed: Subtract g_dwCofComponent2DataSize from g_dwCofDataNodeCount\n9. Check flag: If g_dwCofComponent2Flag != 0, call Ordinal_10043(0xd2c, 0) (GetSkillData ordinal)\n10. Clear equipment flag: Set g_dwCofComponent2Flag = 0\n11. Initialize equipment array: Zero out 0x203 (515) dwords starting at g_aEquipmentArray via REP STOSD\n12. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\n(implicit) g_pCofComponent2TableStart: Pointer to start of COF component table\n(implicit) g_pCofComponent2TableEnd: Pointer to end of COF component table\n(implicit) g_dwCofDataNodeCount: Global count of active COF data nodes\n(implicit) g_aEquipmentArray: Global equipment array at 0x6fc04db0\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Equipment array initialized to zero, COF components disabled\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Linked list traversal continues until null pointer encountered\n- Only decrements counter for flagged nodes (byte offset +1 with bit 0x01 set)\n- Equipment array size is fixed at 0x203 (515) dwords\n- SSA temporaries (iVar1, puVar2, pdwTablePtr, nLoopCount) optimized away\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x01: Flag bit mask for COF node status check\n0x1c: Byte offset constant used in calculation (-0x1c - puVar2[2])\n0xd07: Ordinal_10043 parameter for subsystem notification (disabled node type 1)\n0xd08: Ordinal_10043 parameter for subsystem notification (disabled node type 2)\n0xd2c: Ordinal_10043 parameter for subsystem notification (clear flag operation)\n0x203: Equipment array element count (515 dwords)\n0x4: Byte offset increment within COF component table entries",
