      "comment": "Initialize monster region statistics and data structures\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get active unit data pointer for current region\n2. Validate unit data is initialized (dwUnitDataFlags != 0)\n3. Call Ordinal_10582(dwMonsterType) to get monster class/type index\n4. Iterate through all monster definitions (g_dwMonsterDefCount)\n5. For each definition, check if class matches at offset 0x1e9 (byte == 0x01)\n6. If matched, initialize monster data: clear all 5 uint parameters (dw1-dw4, dwType)\n7. Call FUN_6fb943e0 with monster class, definition ptr, and parameters\n8. Return after successful initialization\n\nParameters:\n  dwMonsterType (ECX) - Monster type/class identifier\n  nRegionId (EDX) - Region or level identifier\n\nReturns:\n  void - Modifies internal monster data structures\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Asserts if unit data pointer is null\n  - Asserts if monster class lookup fails (Ordinal_10582 returns 0)\n  - Asserts if unit not initialized (dwUnitDataFlags == 0)\n  - All failures call FUN_6fb9a10f(0xFFFFFFFF) which terminates\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x1e9 - Byte offset in monster definition for class match check\n  0xFFFFFFFF - Fatal error code passed to termination function\n\nRelated Functions:\n  GetActiveUnitDataPointer() - Retrieves unit data for region\n  Ordinal_10582() - Maps monster type to class index\n  FUN_6fb943e0() - Initializes individual monster statistics",
