      "comment": "Initialize monster definition unit graphics and slot status.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get monster index from unit via FUN_6fb958b0\n2. Get monster type ID via FUN_6fb95830\n3. Calculate slot pointer address as (index * 10 * 8) bytes offset from pMonsterDef\n4. Check if monster array entry is uninitialized (== 0)\n5. If array empty, check slot status field at [0x6fc05610 + index*4]\n6. If slot status is 0 (not in use):\n   - Call ProcessUnitGraphicsAppearance to initialize graphics and particle effects\n   - If graphics init fails (return != 1), clear slot status and array entry, return\n   - If graphics init succeeds (return == 1), set slot status to 1, return\n7. If slot status != 0 (in use):\n   - Call Ordinal_10058 (Storm/Fog - unknown initialization function) with type, def, index\n   - If Ordinal_10058 returns 0 success, set array entry at [0x6fc055c0 + index*4] to 1\n\nParameters:\npUnit (UnitAny *) - The monster unit to initialize, passed in ECX (__fastcall reg)\npMonsterDef (dword *) - Monster definition array base pointer, passed in EDX (__fastcall reg)\ndwParam3 (dword) - Auxiliary parameter, stacked after return address (Stack[0x4])\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value, modifies global state in g_aMonsterArray and g_aMonsterSlotStatus\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Monster array stored at [0x6fc055c0 + slotIndex*4] tracks allocated/initialized monsters\n- Slot status at [0x6fc05610 + slotIndex*4] indicates initialization state (0=free, 1=allocated)\n- Slot index calculated as (unitIndex * 10 * 8) / 4 where unitIndex from FUN_6fb958b0\n- Ordinal_10058 purpose unknown - likely performs Storm.dll initialization or resource loading",
