      "comment": "Process skill slots for a unit with optional graphics update\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get unit skill slot index via FUN_6fb958b0(pUnit)\n2. Get unit skill ID via FUN_6fb95830(pUnit)\n3. Calculate slot array offset: pSlotArray + (nSlotIndex * 10)\n4. Check if skill slot array entry is empty [offset]\n5. If empty, check skill slot status [offset+20]:\n   - If uninitialized (==0):\n     a. Call ProcessUnitGraphicsAppearance to setup graphics\n     b. If successful (==1), set status to 1 and return\n     c. If fails, zero both status and array entry, return\n6. If status already initialized (!0), call Ordinal_10058(dwSkillId, pSlotArray, nSlotIndex)\n   - If result==0, set array entry to 1\n7. Return (implicit void)\n\nParameters:\n- pUnit: UnitAny pointer to unit entity\n- pSlotArray: dword pointer to skill slot array base (indexed by slot)\n- dwFlags: dword flags controlling graphics update behavior\n\nReturns:\n- void (modifies unit skill state in-place)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Array indexing: slot offset calculated as (nSlotIndex * 10)\n- Two persistent arrays accessed: g_aSkillArray (skill storage) and g_aSkillSlotStatus (init flag)\n- Magic offset 0x6fc04950 and 0x6fc049a0 reference global skill state arrays\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x6fc04950: g_aSkillArray base address (skill slot values)\n- 0x6fc049a0: g_aSkillSlotStatus base address (0=uninitialized, 1=ready)\n- 0x10: multiplier for slot array index (10 slots per unit)\n- 0x4: word size multiplier for offset calculation\n- 0x1: success return value from ProcessUnitGraphicsAppearance, ready flag value\n- 0x0: failure/uninitialized state",
