      "api_count": 8,
      "api_calls": ["UNITS_GetRoom", "ExtractRoomTileList", "CountPendingAsyncOperations", "GetMonsterInitStatsPtr", "FindAsyncDataNode", "FindAsyncDataNode", "CountPendingAsyncOperations", "FogAssert"],
      "instructions": ["0xC4DE0|SUB|ESP, 0x20", "0xC4DE3|PUSH|EBX", "0xC4DE4|PUSH|EBP", "0xC4DE5|PUSH|ESI", "0xC4DE6|PUSH|EDI", "0xC4DE7|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x10], ECX", "0xC4DEB|CALL|0x6fb62880", "0xC4DF0|PUSH|EAX", "0xC4DF1|CALL|0x6fb98164", "0xC4DF6|XOR|EBP, EBP", "0xC4DF8|CMP|EAX, EBP", "0xC4DFA|JZ|0x6fb9509b", "0xC4E00|LEA|ECX, [ESP + 0x24]", "0xC4E04|LEA|EDX, [ESP + 0x28]", "0xC4E08|PUSH|ECX"],
      "comment": "Initialize graphics appearance for all monsters and skills in the game.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call GetGameContext to retrieve the current game state pointer\n2. Call GetActiveUnits(GameContext) to get the unit system reference\n3. If unit system exists, call GetSlotArrays(UnitSystem, &dwSlotArray, &dwSlotCount) to retrieve slot data\n4. Initialize dwLoopCounter to 0 and dwSlotIndex to 0\n5. For each slot (dwSlotIndex < dwSlotCount):\n   a. Check g_bInitForced flag - if 0 (not forced), check elapsed time via Ordinal_10057\n   b. If time > 0x1d (29 units), abort and return\n   c. If forced initialization and nInitType=0 or random seed mode enabled, increment loading counter\n   d. For each unit in slot's unit list:\n      - Get unit type, class, and index via FUN_6fb95870, FUN_6fb95830, FUN_6fb958b0\n      - If class == 1 (monster):\n        * If type != 0x0c OR monster flag not set:\n          - Get monster definition via Ordinal_10582(nMonsterIndex)\n          - For each monster definition (dwDefIndex < g_dwMonsterDefCount):\n            * Check if definition is active (byte at offset 0x1e9 == 0x01)\n            * If monster slot empty:\n              - Process graphics via ProcessUnitGraphicsAppearance(pUnit, pMonsterDef, nInitType)\n              - Set g_aMonsterSlotStatus and g_aMonsterArray based on result\n            * Else slot occupied:\n              - Check monster update via Ordinal_10058(nMonsterIndex, pMonsterDef, nType)\n              - Update g_aMonsterArray accordingly\n      - If class == 0 (skill):\n        * If random seed mode, disable initialization flag (nInitType=0)\n        * For each skill definition (dwDefIndex < g_dwSkillDefCount):\n          - Similar processing as monster branch using g_aSkillArray/g_aSkillSlotStatus\n      - Check timeout after each unit via Ordinal_10057\n6. Next slot via dwSlotIndex increment\n7. Return (void)\n\nParameters:\nnInitType (ECX): int - Initialization type flag (0=disabled, 1=enabled, affects random mode behavior)\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If g_bInitForced=0, processing checks elapsed time every iteration via Ordinal_10057\n- Timeout at 0x1d (29) causes immediate return\n- Random seed mode forces nInitType to 0 for skill processing\n- Assertion failure if Ordinal_10582 returns NULL (invalid monster definition lookup)\n- Note: Function uses multiple SSA temporaries (iVar4, iVar6, iVar7, uVar5, uVar8, dVar9) optimized by compiler and unaffected registers passed implicitly (EBP, ESI, EDI)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x1d (29): Timeout threshold for processing duration\n- 0x1f (31): Bitmask for loading counter animation frame (dwLoopCounter & 0x1f)\n- 0x1e9: Offset of active flag in monster definition structure\n- 0x0c: Specific monster type value for special handling\n- 0xa0 (160): Size/stride of monster class flag array element\n- 10: Stride multiplier in monster definition array access\n- 0x2c: Offset to unit linked list pointer in slot structure\n- 0x10c: Offset to next unit pointer in unit structure\n\nRelated Functions:\n- ProcessUnitGraphicsAppearance: Applies graphics/animation properties to units\n- InitializeLoadingScreenUI: Updates loading screen display during initialization\n- GetGameContext: Returns game state pointer\n- FUN_6fb95870: Extract unit type field\n- FUN_6fb95830: Extract unit class field\n- FUN_6fb958b0: Extract unit index field",
      "tags": ["SRC_Gfx.cpp", "PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PARAM_1", "STRUCT_Other", "PROP_LOOPHEAVY", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
