      "comment": "Initialize monster palette data for specified difficulty level\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Clean monster data systems\n2. Get active unit data pointer\n3. Iterate difficulty-based monster classes, load palette shifts\n4. For each monster item, get palette class ID\n5. Calculate class difference and load appropriate palettes\n6. Load secondary class palettes if present\n7. Process unique monsters by difficulty and load palettes\n\nParameters:\ndwDifficulty (uint) - Game difficulty level (indexed into palette tables)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Initializes global palette structures\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0xFF - Difficulty mask for indexing\n0x23E - Max valid monster class ID\n0x44-0x48 - First palette shift range\n0x12A-0x12F - Second palette shift range\n0x1C5-0x1D1 - Third palette shift range\n0x10 - Character count field offset\n0x1C - Class indices field offset",
