      "comment": "Return pointer to monster slot in global array by index.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Receive monster index in ECX (__fastcall)\n2. Multiply index by 0x28 (40 bytes per monster slot)\n3. Add base address of g_aMonsterArray (0x6fc055c0)\n4. Return pointer in EAX\n\nParameters:\nnMonsterIndex (ECX) - Index into monster array, 0-based\n\nReturns:\nEAX - Pointer to UnitAny structure at calculated offset, NULL if invalid index\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Minimal bounds checking; caller must validate index range\n- Magic number 0x28 represents UnitAny structure size (40 bytes)\n- Uses optimized LEA+SHL for index calculation (equivalent to multiply by 0x28)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x28 - 40 decimal, size of UnitAny structure (one monster slot)\n0x6fc055c0 - Base address of g_aMonsterArray global array",
