      "instructions": ["0xC5530|SUB|ESP, 0x10", "0xC5533|PUSH|EBX", "0xC5534|PUSH|ESI", "0xC5535|PUSH|EDI", "0xC5536|MOV|EBX, ECX", "0xC5538|CALL|0x6fb958b0", "0xC553D|MOV|ECX, EBX", "0xC553F|MOV|ESI, EAX", "0xC5541|CALL|0x6fb95870", "0xC5546|MOV|ECX, EBX", "0xC5548|MOV|EDI, EAX", "0xC554A|CALL|0x6fb95830", "0xC554F|DEC|EAX", "0xC5550|JNZ|0x6fb9568f", "0xC5556|LEA|EAX, [ESI + ESI*0x4]"],
      "comment": "Update monster rendering graphics based on slot status and appearance attributes.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get unit inventory slot, type, and validity via GetInventorySlot, GetUnitType, IsUnitValid\n2. If unit is valid (type == 1):\n   a. Initialize graphic validity flag = 1\n   b. Clear slot array entry and slot status array  \n   c. Check unit stat record (Ordinal_10342 = D2Common.GetUnitStat); assert if missing\n   d. Check graphics display via loading screen flag\n3. Validate monster definition exists (Ordinal_10582 = D2Common.GetMonsterData); abort if missing\n4. Loop g_dwMonsterDefCount entries in g_pMonsterDefArray:\n   a. Load definition pointer\n   b. Check graphics available (definition[0x1e9] == 0x01)\n   c. If slot array empty AND slot status empty:\n      - Call ProcessUnitGraphicsAppearance: if success, set status=1; else clear both\n   d. Else if slot status filled:\n      - Call Ordinal_10058 = D2Common render/validate\n      - If returns 0, set array=1\n   e. Increment\n5. Return\n\nParameters:\npUnit (UnitAny *): Unit entity pointer; passed in ECX register (__fastcall convention)\n\nReturns:\nvoid (no return value)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Assertion failure if monster definition not found\n- Graphics validity flag reset if stat record missing or loading screen active\n- Monster definitions may not support graphics (field 0x1e9 != 0x01)\n- Compiler-optimized: 5 register-reused SSA temporaries that cannot be renamed (register assignments)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x28: Inventory slot stride (bytes per slot entry)\n0x1e9: Monster definition graphics availability flag offset\n0x01: Graphics enabled value\n0x04: Array stride multiplier\n0x10: Return stack frame size\n\nRelated Functions:\n- GetLoadingScreenDisplayFlag() - Loading screen state check\n- ProcessUnitGraphicsAppearance(pUnit, pDef, nValid) - Render to graphics slot\n- Ordinal_10342(pUnit) = GetUnitStat - Unit stat record access\n- Ordinal_10582(nType) = GetMonsterData - Monster definition loader\n- Ordinal_10058(nType, pDef, nSlot) = Unit render operation\n- Ordinal_10026(nType, pDef) = Related unit state verification\n- FUN_6fb95830() - Get unit type\n- FUN_6fb958b0() - Get inventory slot\n- FUN_6fb95870() - Check unit valid",
      "tags": ["SRC_Gfx.cpp", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PARAM_1", "STRUCT_Other", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
    },
