      "instructions": ["0xC56A0|PUSH|ESI", "0xC56A1|PUSH|EDI", "0xC56A2|MOV|ECX, 0x10", "0xC56A7|XOR|EAX, EAX", "0xC56A9|MOV|EDI, 0x6fc1bd84", "0xC56AE|MOV|ESI, 0x6fc1bd84", "0xC56B3|STOSD.REP|ES:EDI", "0xC56B5|XOR|EDI, EDI", "0xC56B7|PUSH|EDI", "0xC56B8|CALL|0x6fb99196", "0xC56BD|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0xC56BF|JZ|0x6fb95706", "0xC56C1|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [EAX + 0x20]", "0xC56C4|INC|EDI", "0xC56C5|MOV|dword ptr [ESI], EAX"],
      "comment": "Initialize five game data type arrays by querying ordinals and copying ptr fields.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Clear TownUnits array (16 DWORDs) and populate with ordinal 10649 items (0x20 offset)\n2. Clear MonsterTypes array (20 DWORDs) and populate with ordinal 10646 items (0x20 offset)\n3. Clear ObjectData array (16 DWORDs) and populate with ordinal 10647 items (0x20 offset)\n4. Clear UniqueActors array (8 DWORDs) and populate with ordinal 10648 items (0x20 offset)\n5. Clear MissileData array and populate with ordinal 10650 items (0x20 offset)\n6. On ordinal failure, trigger assertion at file/line and call abort (-1)\n\nParameters: (none)\n\nReturns: void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Each ordinal query must return non-NULL pointer to data structure\n- If any ordinal returns NULL, assertion error with hardcoded line numbers\n- Arrays are bounded by fixed endpoints: 0x6fc1bdc4, 0x6fc1be40, 0x6fc1bd84, 0x6fc1bde4, 0x6fc1bdf0\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x20: Offset within queried structures containing pointer values\n- 0x10, 0x14, 0x8: Array sizes (in DWORDs)\n- 0x3d, 0x46, 0x4f, 0x58, 0x61: Error line numbers from source\n\nNote: Uses D2Common ordinals (Ordinal_10646-10650) for dynamic item enumeration.",
