      "comment": "Retrieves graphics state value for a unit, returning default offset if state validation fails.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call Ordinal_10487(nUnitId, 0x3f) - Unknown ordinal validating unit graphics state with flag 0x3f\n2. If state validation returns non-zero (valid), retrieve unit data from hash table\n3. If unit data found, return graphics value from offset +0x21 in unit structure\n4. Otherwise return default graphics value from unit parameter at offset +0x84\n\nParameters:\nnUnitId (int): IMPLICIT ECX - Unit identifier or unit data pointer\n\nReturns:\nint - Graphics state value; 0x21 offset from unit data if state valid, else offset 0x84 value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Ordinal_10487: Unknown function - validates graphics state; appears to be D2Common ordinal\n- State validation flag 0x3f: Bitmask for graphics state validation\n- Hash table lookup may fail if unit ID invalid\n- Fallback offset 0x84 always accessible from parameter directly",
