      "comment": "Validate token type and retrieve associated data structure pointer\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load token type identifiers from pnTokenInfo (fields at +0 and +4)\n2. Call Ordinal_10369 to get initial type classification\n3. Call Ordinal_11013 to update and validate token fields  \n4. Retrieve updated type from pnTokenInfo[0] into dwTokenType\n5. Switch on dwTokenType value (0, 1, or 2):\n   - Case 0: Call Ordinal_10646 with dwTokenId1 to get data structure\n   - Case 1: Call Ordinal_10647 with dwTokenId1 to get data structure\n   - Case 2: Call Ordinal_10648 with dwTokenId1 to get data structure\n6. Validate result is non-zero; if zero, assert and terminate\n7. Return value at result + 0x20 offset\n\nParameters:\n  pnTokenInfo: Pointer to token info structure with type and identifier fields\n  IMPLICIT ECX: Contains pnTokenInfo on entry (__fastcall)\n\nReturns:\n  dword: Value from offset 0x20 of the data structure\n  0: If token validation fails (assertion triggers termination)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Unknown token type (not 0, 1, or 2) returns 0\n  - Failed validation calls FUN_6fb9a10f(-1) which doesn't return\n\nOrdinal Calls (Not in KNOWN_ORDINALS.md):\n  Ordinal_10369: Unknown - appears to classify token type\n  Ordinal_10646: Unknown - retrieves type 0 token data\n  Ordinal_10647: Unknown - retrieves type 1 token data\n  Ordinal_10648: Unknown - retrieves type 2 token data\n  Ordinal_11013: Unknown - validates and updates token structure",
