      "instructions": ["0xC5A30|SUB|ESP, 0x48", "0xC5A33|PUSH|ESI", "0xC5A34|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0xC5A36|PUSH|EDI", "0xC5A37|MOV|ECX, 0x12", "0xC5A3C|XOR|EAX, EAX", "0xC5A3E|LEA|EDI, [ESP + 0x8]", "0xC5A42|STOSD.REP|ES:EDI", "0xC5A44|LEA|ECX, [ESP + 0x54]", "0xC5A48|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0xc], EAX", "0xC5A4C|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [ESP + 0x54]", "0xC5A50|PUSH|-0x1", "0xC5A52|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x18], EDX", "0xC5A56|PUSH|ECX", "0xC5A57|LEA|EDX, [ESP + 0x10]"],
      "comment": "Retrieves CEL context information (graphic coordinates) from a game unit.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize 7-element local buffer (28 bytes) with zeros via REP STOSD loop\n2. Set buffer[1]=0, buffer[2]=dwMode, buffer[3]=dwType\n3. Mark buffer[0x2b]=1 (context initialization flag)\n4. Call FUN_6fb95e60 with unit ptr, buffer, mode, -1 sentinel, EDI register (IMPLICIT param)\n5. If FUN_6fb95e60 returns 0: exit (unit not found or invalid)\n6. Call Ordinal_10055 (GetCelContextUnitInfo) with buffer, 0, 1\n7. If Ordinal_10055 returns 0: exit (no CEL context available)\n8. Assert buffer[0] != 0 (context must be initialized); call D2Common_AssertionOrdinal and abort if fails\n9. Call Ordinal_10037 (GetCelContextXCoordinate) on buffer[0], store result in *pdwX\n10. Call Ordinal_10038 (GetCelContextYCoordinate) on buffer[0], store result in *pdwY\n11. Return void\n\nParameters:\n- pdwUnit: Pointer to unit/entity data (typically UnitAny structure pointer)\n- dwType: Unit type identifier (0=player, 1=NPC, 2=object, etc.)\n- dwMode: Mode/state flag for context lookup\n- pdwX: Output pointer to receive X coordinate\n- pdwY: Output pointer to receive Y coordinate\n- IMPLICIT: nImplicitParam (EDI register input parameter)\n\nReturns:\n- void (results via output pointers pdwX, pdwY)\n- Side effects: Populates pdwX and pdwY with CEL context coordinates if successful\n- Failure: Both pdwX and pdwY unchanged if unit invalid or CEL context unavailable\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Assertion failure if CEL context buffer[0] is zero after Ordinal_10055 succeeds (indicates initialization bug)\n- Silent failure if FUN_6fb95e60 returns 0 (unit not found in context tables)\n- Silent failure if Ordinal_10055 returns 0 (CEL not available for unit)\n\nOrdinal Calls:\n- Ordinal_10055 = GetCelContextUnitInfo - Query CEL context unit info from buffer\n- Ordinal_10037 = GetCelContextXCoordinate - Get CEL context X coordinate  \n- Ordinal_10038 = GetCelContextYCoordinate - Get CEL context Y coordinate\n\nNote: Function uses 2 stack-allocated temporaries (uStack_44, puVar1) optimized away in decompilation.",
