      "comment": "Render unit graphics with boundary validation against screen dimensions.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get viewport X offset and adjust screen X coordinate\n2. Get viewport Y offset and adjust screen Y coordinate\n3. Call RenderUnitComponentGraphics to render unit components at adjusted coordinates\n4. If render succeeded, extract unit component data via Ordinal_10379\n5. Initialize local component buffer by zeroing 18 integers\n6. Get unit flags via Ordinal_10457 and mask to byte\n7. Set component data flag and call FUN_6fb95e60 to process component data\n8. If processing succeeded, call Ordinal_10055 to get component bounds\n9. If bounds found and component index valid:\n   - Get component width via Ordinal_10038\n   - Get component height via Ordinal_10040, add screen Y offset\n   - Get component X offset via Ordinal_10039, add adjusted X\n   - Get component X extent via Ordinal_10037\n10. Validate bounds: check component fits within screen width\n11. Validate bounds: check component doesn't exceed left edge\n12. Validate bounds: check component height fits within screen height\n13. Return success if bottom edge doesn't exceed screen (EBX + EAX >= 0)\n\nParameters:\npUnit (UnitAny *) - Unit instance to render\nnScreenX (int) - Screen X coordinate (before adjustment)\nnScreenY (int) - Screen Y coordinate (before adjustment)\n\nReturns:\ntrue if unit rendered successfully and all boundary checks pass\nfalse if render failed, bounds invalid, or unit index invalid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Returns false if RenderUnitComponentGraphics fails\n- Returns false if component data processing fails\n- Returns false if no valid components found\n- Returns false if any boundary check fails\n- Validates against global screen dimensions g_dwScreenWidth and g_dwScreenHeight\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x12 (18) - Component buffer size in integers\n0xff - Unit flag mask to extract byte component\n-0x1 (0xFFFFFFFF) - Sentinel for component processing\n0x1 - Component data presence flag\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset | Size | Field | Type | Description\n0x0    | 4    | [0]   | int  | Component X position\n0x4    | 4    | [1]   | int  | Component Y position\n0x8    | 4    | [2]   | uint | Flags/type from Ordinal_10457\n0xC+   | 24   | [3-6] | int  | Reserved component data\n\nNote: Function uses stack-allocated temporaries optimized away: local_50 (byte[4]), piVar6, extraout_var",
