      "comment": "Validates graphics output bounds against screen dimensions with optional border adjustment.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Query handle top bound via Ordinal_10038\n  2. Query handle left bound via Ordinal_10040\n  3. Query handle height dimension via Ordinal_10039, add nOffsetX to result\n  4. Query handle bottom bound via Ordinal_10037\n  5. If nAdjustForBorder != 0: subtract top bound from height, add top bound to bottom bound\n  6. Check if height > g_dwScreenWidth (return false if exceeded)\n  7. Check if bottom bound + height < 0 (return false if negative)\n  8. Check if (left bound + nOffsetY - top bound) > g_dwScreenHeight (return false if exceeded)\n  9. Check if (left bound + nOffsetY + top bound) >= -1 (return this result)\n\nParameters:\n  dwHandle (dword) - Graphics handle for dimension queries\n  nOffsetX (int) - Horizontal offset to add to height\n  nOffsetY (int) - Vertical offset to add to left bound\n  nAdjustForBorder (int) - Non-zero enables border adjustment (subtract/add top bound)\n\nReturns:\n  true - All boundary validations passed\n  false - Any dimension exceeds screen limits or results in invalid negative bounds",
      "tags": ["PARAM_4", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
