      "comment": "Validate component statistics data and return success/failure status.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check component index parameter is within valid range (0-15)\n2. Call Ordinal_10369 twice to extract component coordinate data into locals\n3. Call Ordinal_11013 twice to normalize component data\n4. Switch on component type (local_c value):\n   - Case 0: Linear search g_adComponentList for matching component index, return 1 if found, 0 if not\n   - Case 1: Call Ordinal_10582 to get stats pointer, add 0x1cd offset, check byte at result == 0x01\n   - Case 2: Call Ordinal_10626 to get stats pointer, add 0x161 offset, check byte at result == 0x01\n   - Case 4: Check if nComponentIndex == 1\n   - Default: Fatal assertion failure\n5. Return 1 if validation succeeds, 0 if fails\n\nParameters:\npComponentData (int *): Pointer to component structure with coordinate data at [0] and [1]\nnComponentIndex (int): Component index to validate (0-15, must be < g_dwComponentCount for type 0)\n\nReturns:\n1 - Validation passed (component stats are valid/active)\n0 - Validation failed (component not found, stats invalid, or index out of range)\n\nSpecial Cases:\nComponent type 0 uses linear search through g_adComponentList\nTypes 1 and 2 require valid pointer returns from ordinal calls\nType 4 only validates if nComponentIndex == 1\nIndex must be &lt;= 15 (0xf) or assertion is triggered",
