      "instructions": ["0xC5E60|SUB|ESP, 0x20", "0xC5E63|MOV|EAX, 0x6", "0xC5E68|PUSH|EBX", "0xC5E69|PUSH|EBP", "0xC5E6A|PUSH|ESI", "0xC5E6B|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0xC5E6D|PUSH|EDI", "0xC5E6E|MOV|EDI, EDX", "0xC5E70|TEST|ESI, ESI", "0xC5E72|JZ|0x6fb95f67", "0xC5E78|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [ESI]", "0xC5E7A|MOV|ECX, dword ptr [ESI + 0x4]", "0xC5E7D|PUSH|ESI", "0xC5E7E|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x1c], EAX", "0xC5E82|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x14], ECX"],
      "comment": "Resolves celcontext graphics data for rendering a unit's visual representation\nBased on unit type, component, and game state, retrieves the appropriate CelFile\ndata, weapon class, monster type data, and missile/skill animation information.\nValidates all pointers and data structures with assertions.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. NULL unit check: If pUnit is NULL, set default error code 0x6 and process game state\n2. For game state processing (piVar5=0x3, 0x4, 0x6): Extract unit stats and CelFile pointers\n3. If nComponentIndex >= 0 (player inventory): Resolve inventory item graphics data\n   - Retrieve inventory item by stat and level\n   - Get graphics node by component ID\n   - Validate graphics and token data pointers\n   - Extract weapon class and skill animation IDs\n4. If nComponentIndex == -1 or special markers: Handle corpse/monster rendering\n   - Resolve monster type array index based on game context\n   - Check for special cases: corpse (player/NPC), equip item (marker 1), object (marker 2)\n   - Retrieve appropriate stat table for missile data or corpse class\n5. Animation resolution based on component type and unit stats\n   - For components 5-6: Use skill stat table (nStatValue)\n   - For component 5 with alternate weapon: Look up skill animation data\n   - For other components: Retrieve missile animation data by component-stat pair\n6. Validate final celcontext pointers: Must not be NULL or 0x20787878 (invalid marker)\n7. Extract 4-byte animation ID from stat table[0x1e:0x22], replacing 0x00 with 0x20 spacing\n\nParameters:\npUnit (ECX) - Pointer to unit structure containing unit ID, class, and stats\nnComponentIndex (EDX) - Component/equipment index (0-15=equipment, 0xFFFFFFFF=monster, 0x1/0x2=special)\npOutCelContext (stack) - Output: pointer to 4-byte animation ID (wClass format)\npGfxType (stack) - Output: graphics type (0x0/0x1=missile, 0x2=corpse, 0x3=special), or -1 if not resolved\nnUnknown (stack) - Unused parameter\n\nReturns:\n1 - Success: all required pointers resolved and output populated\n0 - Failure: could not resolve required graphics data (NULL returns at inventory resolution points)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Player corpse: Check if unit == GameContext player\n- NPC corpse: Component 5 with class offset +0x2b4 marking\n- Corpse class variations: Uses stat table offsets (+0x168 for type 3, +0x1a8 for type 5)\n- Invalid component range: Triggers assertion error\n- Missing stat tables: Assertions prevent invalid data propagation\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x6 - Default error code for NULL unit\n0x3f - Unit stat index for animation (Ordinal_10487 parameter)\n0x1e - Stat offset for animation ID (6-byte animation data)\n0x2074696c - Default animation (tili - tile indicator)\n0x20776278 - Special animation selector for weapon/skill lookup\n0x20776f62 - Alternate weapon class indicator\n0x20687368 - Special shield animation marker\n0x20787878 - Invalid/placeholder marker (replaces in assertions)\n0xFFFFFFFF - Sentinel value for game state transition\n0x1 - Equip item marker\n0x2 - Object marker\n0x0-0x6 - Component types (0-6 valid, 0xF+ invalid)",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "STRUCT_Room1", "STRUCT_ItemData", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData", "STRUCT_StatList", "PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Path", "UNIT_MISSILE", "STRUCT_Skill", "PARAM_5", "STRUCT_Other", "PROP_LOOPHEAVY", "SRC_GfxUtil.cpp"]
