      "comment": "Initializes unit display context with position and mode.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Set unit X coordinate to parameter dwX at offset +0x4\n2. Set unit Z coordinate to parameter dwZ at offset +0xc  \n3. Set unit Y coordinate to parameter dwY at offset +0x8\n4. Set unit display mode flag to parameter byMode at offset +0x1d\n5. Call GetCelContextFromUnit to populate CEL rendering context\n6. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\nnUnit (int) - Unit structure base address to initialize\npSrcUnitData (uint *) - Source unit attribute array\ndwX (uint) - X coordinate for display\ndwY (uint) - Y coordinate for display\ndwZ (uint) - Z coordinate for display\npCelContext (uint *) - CEL context array output\nbyMode (byte) - Display render mode flag\npResultData (int *) - Result data buffer output\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Modifies unit structure in place\n\nSpecial Cases:\nFunction assumes nUnit points to valid allocated unit structure\nCoordinate storage starts at offset 0x4 for X coordinate",
