      "comment": "Validates that COF data pointer is not NULL, triggers assertion failure if invalid.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Test if pCofData == NULL\n2. If not NULL, exit function immediately (valid pointer)\n3. If NULL, push assertion parameters (line 0x430, source file path, COF data buffer address)\n4. Call assertion ordinal function (D2Common_AssertionOrdinal)\n5. Push 0xFFFFFFFF (-1) as abort code\n6. Call aborting function (FUN_6fb9a10f) - never returns\n\nParameters:\npCofData (void *) - Pointer to COF (Component Object File) data structure, must not be NULL\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Function returns normally if pCofData is valid, never returns if NULL (assertion abort)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- NULL pointer triggers fatal assertion with debug info (source file, line number)\n- Return is unreachable if assertion fires (marked with WARNING in decompiler)",
