      "comment": "Searches a component buffer array for a specific component ID and returns associated data.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate pbBuffer pointer is not NULL (assertion failure)\n2. Validate nComponentId is less than 16 (component limit)\n3. Initialize search: bResult = 0, pbSearchPtr = pbBuffer + 0x1c (first entry), dwSearchIndex = 0\n4. If buffer contains components (*pbBuffer != 0), enter search loop\n5. Loop: Compare current component ID (*pbSearchPtr) with nComponentId target\n6. If match found: Extract value from pbSearchPtr[1] and return\n7. If no match: Advance pbSearchPtr by 9 bytes (entry size), increment dwSearchIndex\n8. If dwSearchIndex exceeds component count (*pbBuffer), return 0 (not found)\n9. If no components, return 0 (default)\n\nParameters:\npbBuffer (byte*): Pointer to component buffer containing count at offset 0, entries at offset 0x1c\nnComponentId (dword): Component ID to search for (0-15 range)\n\nReturns:\nbyte: Component data value if found, 0 if not found or invalid input\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- NULL buffer triggers assertion at line 0x453\n- Component ID >= 16 triggers assertion at line 0x454\n- Empty buffer (count=0) returns 0\n- Overflow protection: stops if search count exceeds buffer capacity\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x1c: Offset to first component entry in buffer (28 bytes header)\n0x9: Size of each component entry (9 bytes per entry)\n0x10: Maximum component ID value (16 components max)",
