      "comment": "Validates COF data buffer pointers for component offset calculations\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if pbCofBytes is NULL - if so, assert and abort\n2. Calculate target address: pbCofBytes + ((pbCofBytes[1] * dwStrideSize + 9 + dwComponentIdx) * pbCofBytes[0] + pbCofBytes[1] + 0x1c)\n3. Check if calculated address is NULL - if so, assert and abort\n4. Return normally if both validations pass\n\nParameters:\npbCofBytes - Pointer to COF data buffer (composition byte array)\ndwStrideSize - Stride/row size for component indexing calculation\ndwComponentIdx - Component index offset to validate access for\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Function returns only if validation succeeds; asserts and aborts on NULL pointers\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- NULL input buffer triggers assertion at line 0x484\n- NULL calculated offset triggers assertion at line 0x48c\n- Both assertions call FUN_6fb9a10f(0xffffffff) which never returns\n- Used by RenderUnitComponentGraphics to validate COF structure before graphics rendering\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x484 (1156) - First assertion line number\n- 0x48c (1164) - Second assertion line number\n- 0x1c (28) - Offset adjustment for buffer boundary calculation\n- 0x9 (9) - Fixed offset in stride calculation",
