      "comment": "Searches component data table for matching component index and returns associated value.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate pbComponentData pointer is not null, else assert\n2. Validate dwComponentId is less than 0x10 (NUM_COMPONENTS limit), else assert\n3. Initialize pbCurComponent = pbComponentData + 0x1c (offset to first component record)\n4. Initialize dwComponentIndex = 0\n5. Check if component count at [pbComponentData] is non-zero\n6. Loop through component records (stride 9 bytes):\n   - Compare current component type at [pbCurComponent] with dwComponentId\n   - If match found, return value at offset 4 in component record ([pbCurComponent + 4])\n   - Increment dwComponentIndex, advance pbCurComponent by 9 bytes\n   - Continue while dwComponentIndex < component count\n7. If no match found, assert failure with \"0\" string\n8. Call FUN_6fb9a10f(0xffffffff) for assertion failures (terminates)\n\nParameters:\npbComponentData (byte *): Pointer to component data structure containing count and component records\ndwComponentId (uint): Component index to search for (0-15)\n\nReturns:\nbyte: Value at offset 4 in matching component record (component data)\nNever returns normally - function uses assertions for all error paths\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- pbComponentData == NULL triggers assertion at line 0x496\n- dwComponentId >= 0x10 triggers assertion at line 0x497\n- Component count == 0 or no match found triggers assertion at line 0x4a3\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset | Size | Field Name | Type | Description\n0x00   | 1    | bComponentCount | byte | Number of active components\n0x1c   | var  | aComponents | array | Array of component records (stride 9 bytes)",
      "tags": ["PARAM_2", "SRC_GfxUtil.cpp"]
