      "comment": "Search unit data in global table by comparing against table entries.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if global table count > 0, exit early if empty\n2. Initialize table pointer to start of g_pUnitDataTable\n3. Loop through each table entry until count exhausted:\n   a. Load first value from pUnitData (offset +0)\n   b. Load second value from pUnitData (offset +4)\n   c. Call Ordinal_10369 (D2Common.GetUnitStat) on pUnitData\n   d. Call Ordinal_11013 (unknown transform) with all three values\n   e. Compare first loaded value against current table entry [0]\n   f. Return 1 (TRUE) if match found\n   g. Increment table index and advance table pointer by 4 bytes\n4. Return 0 (FALSE) if no match found after exhausting table\n\nParameters:\n  pUnitData (int *) - pointer to unit data structure with at least 8 bytes [+0] and [+4]\n\nReturns:\n  1 (TRUE) - if matching entry found in table\n  0 (FALSE) - if no matches or table empty\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Empty table (g_dwUnitDataTableCount = 0) returns 0\n  - Early exit on first match prevents checking remaining entries",
