      "comment": "Retrieve byte value from graphics unit info record at specified offset\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Request graphics info structure pointer for unit type (nUnitType)\n2. Validate pointer is not NULL; if NULL, trigger assertion and terminate\n3. Calculate byte offset as (nOffset * 2) within the structure\n4. Return byte at computed memory location\n\nParameters:\nnUnitType - Unit type identifier for graphics info lookup\nnOffset - Offset index within structure (multiplied by 2 for byte address)\n\nReturns:\nByte value at [pGfxInfo + (nOffset * 2)]\n\nSpecial Cases:\nNULL graphics info pointer triggers assertion failure and abnormal termination (FUN_6fb9a10f)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x4bf - Line number in source file for assertion\n0x2 - Byte stride multiplier (nOffset * 2)\n\nRelated Functions:\nGetGfxInfoPointer() - Returns graphics structure pointer\nInitializeGfxUnitRecord() - Primary caller\nInsertGfxUnitValidate() - Secondary caller",
