      "comment": "Gets the base graphics direction for a game unit based on its type and player/monster index.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate pDirCount < 0x40 (64 directions max)\n2. Get game context via GetGameContext()\n3. Initialize local_14/local_20/local_18 with unit direction data (Ordinal_11013)\n4. Determine dwBaseDir (default 6) based on unit type:\n   - Type 0: Check if player unit vs g_bRandomSeedMode (0x10 or 0x08)\n   - Type 1: Load stat value via Ordinal_10647, check if monster type 8\n   - Type 2,4: Return 0x01\n   - Type 3: Load stat via Ordinal_10589, extract byte at offset 0xd8\n   - Type 5: Assert failure (RoomTile not supported)\n   - Default: Call FUN_6fb97230()\n5. Store dwBaseDir in pOutValue\n6. If bApplyTransform:\n   - Validate nDirMode (0x08 or 0x10)\n   - Call Ordinal_10019() to transform direction based on param_2\n   - Update pDirCount with transformed direction\n7. Load unit direction again, check param_2 state\n8. If param_2 NULL/INVALID: Get GFX frame, call Ordinal_10161_SkillInit() if frame matches\n9. If param_2 INVALID_MARKER: Increment g_pMonsterTypesArrayEnd\n10. Call Ordinal_10022() with final direction/mode, store in pOutDirection\n11. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\npUnit (ECX) - Pointer to UnitAny struct (unit being queried)\npParam2 (EDX) - Parameter affecting direction calculation\npDirCount (Stack+0x4) - Pointer to direction count (0-0x40)\npOutDirection (Stack+0x8) - Output: base direction from Ordinal_10022\npOutValue (Stack+0xc) - Output: base direction (0x01, 0x04, 0x08, 0x10, etc.)\nnDirMode (Stack+0x10) - Direction mode (0x08 or 0x10)\nbApplyTransform (Stack+0x14) - If nonzero, apply direction transform\n\nReturns:\nVoid (results via pOutValue, pOutDirection pointers)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Type 0 unit: Returns 0x10 if player AND g_bRandomSeedMode==0, else 0x08\n- Type 1 monster: Returns 0x04 if stat check fails or special flag\n- Type 5 (RoomTile): Always asserts/crashes\n- Invalid pDirCount: Asserts and terminates\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x40 - Maximum direction count\n0x24 - Stat offset in monster struct (Ordinal_10647 result)\n0xd8 - Stat offset in another type (Ordinal_10589 result)\n0x10, 0x08, 0x04, 0x01 - Direction values",
