      "comment": "Render CEL component composite layers for a unit with palette tinting and lighting effects.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate component index within NUM_COMPONENTS range (0x0-0xF)\n2. Loop for each CEL component layer in the unit\n3. Allocate and clear 0x48-byte buffer for CEL context structure (0x12 dwords)\n4. Call GetCelContextFromUnit to retrieve layer graphics context and output dimensions\n5. If context valid, get CEL data block size via Ordinal_10055\n6. Calculate adjusted Y position: Y_adjusted = layer_Y - viewport_Y + unit_base_Y\n7. Update *pnMaxHeight if calculated position exceeds current maximum\n8. Increment rendered layer counter on successful rendering\n9. Continue looping through all layers until complete or validation error\n10. Return count of successfully rendered CEL component layers\n\nParameters:\npUnit (uint*) - IMPLICIT ECX: Pointer to UnitAny game object containing CEL component data\npbNumLayers (byte*) - IMPLICIT EDX: Pointer to count of CEL component layers in unit\nnLayerDataSize (int) - Stack offset 0x4: Size in bytes of each component's CEL data block\npnMaxHeight (int*) - Stack offset 0x8: Pointer to maximum Y coordinate value (updated if exceeded)\ndwGammaTint (uint) - Stack offset 0xC: Gamma and tint palette value for CEL rendering\ndwLightColor (uint) - Stack offset 0x10: Light color palette applied to CEL rendering\n\nReturns:\nEAX = Number of successfully rendered CEL component layers (0-N)\n      Returns 0 if *pbNumLayers is empty or CEL context retrieval fails\n      Assertion failure (never returns) if component index exceeds 0x0F\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Component indices 0x0-0xF are valid; 0x10+ trigger assertion failure via D2Common_AssertionOrdinal\n- Empty layer list (*pbNumLayers == 0) returns 0 immediately without processing\n- Failed GetCelContextFromUnit returns 0 for that layer, continues processing next\n- *pnMaxHeight only updated if new Y position exceeds existing value\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x10 (16) - NUM_COMPONENTS constant, maximum valid component index + 1\n0x12 (18) - CEL context buffer size in dwords (0x48 bytes)\n0xFFFFFFFF (-1) - Null parameter sentinel for GetCelContextFromUnit call\n0x548 - Assertion error code for component index validation failure",
