      "instructions": ["0xC7350|SUB|ESP, 0xc", "0xC7353|PUSH|EBX", "0xC7354|PUSH|ESI", "0xC7355|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0xC7357|PUSH|EDI", "0xC7358|MOV|EBX, EDX", "0xC735A|PUSH|ESI", "0xC735B|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [ESI]", "0xC735D|MOV|ECX, dword ptr [ESI + 0x4]", "0xC7360|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x10], EAX", "0xC7364|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x18], ECX", "0xC7368|CALL|0x6fb98c9e", "0xC736D|LEA|EDX, [ESP + 0x10]", "0xC7371|LEA|ECX, [ESP + 0xc]", "0xC7375|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x10], EAX"],
      "comment": "Validates unit component flags and returns output status\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load unit coordinates and mode from param_1\n2. Call Ordinal_10369 (GetUnitMode) to resolve mode value\n3. Call Ordinal_11013 (TransformUnitCoords) with local copies\n4. Check if nCompType equals 0x123:\n   - If yes: iterate components at [param_1 + 0x84] via Ordinal_10277 (GetFirstComponent)\n   - For each component: get component ID via Ordinal_10305, verify via Ordinal_10707\n   - Return 1 if valid component found\n5. Else if nCompType equals 0x127: return 1 immediately\n6. Else: check nParam4 via Ordinal_10600 (GetComponentData)\n   - If component at offset 0x2b is non-null, copy byte at 0x2c to pdwOutFlags\n7. If nParam4 == -1 or component lookup fails:\n   - Determine owner unit via Ordinal_10487 or GetUnitFromHashTable\n   - Load component list from owner's [0x84]\n   - Check param_2 against 5, 6, 7:\n     - param_2==5: Ordinal_10259 index 5, validate with Ordinal_10707 at 0x5ad\n     - param_2==6: Ordinal_10259 index 6, validate with Ordinal_10707 at 0x5b7\n     - param_2==7: Ordinal_10259 index 7, validate with Ordinal_10707 at 0x5c1, set pdwOutFlags=2\n8. Return 1 on success, 0 on failure\n\nParameters:\n  pUnit (int *): Unit pointer passed in ECX, accessed via offsets for mode/coordinates\n  nComponentType (int): Component type ID passed in EDX, compared against 0x123, 0x127\n  pdwOutFlags (dword *): Output parameter on stack [ESP+0x1c], receives flag value (1 or 2)\n  nParam4 (int): Component lookup parameter on stack [ESP+0x20], -1 for default behavior\n\nReturns:\n  1: Component validated successfully, pdwOutFlags set with result code\n  0: No valid component found or validation failed\n  pdwOutFlags receives: 1 for normal component, 2 for special component type\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Component type 0x123: Iterates components from list at pUnit[0x21]\n  - Component type 0x127: Fast path, returns 1 immediately\n  - Type mismatch (not 0x123/0x127): Falls through to param4 checking\n  - nParam4==-1: Uses owner unit's component list instead of direct lookup\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x123: Special component type marker (iterate list)\n  0x127: Special component type marker (fast validation)\n  0x400000: Flag value for component validation\n  0x84: Offset to component list in unit structure\n  0x21: Offset to owner/parent unit reference\n  0x3f: Component type filter parameter\n  0x2b, 0x2c: Offsets in component data structure\n  0x586, 0x5ad, 0x5b7, 0x5c1: Source line numbers for error reporting\n\nRelated Functions:\n  - Ordinal_10369: GetUnitMode - Extract unit animation mode\n  - Ordinal_11013: TransformUnitCoords - Transform coordinates to new space\n  - Ordinal_10277: GetFirstComponent - Get first component from list\n  - Ordinal_10304: GetNextComponent - Iterate to next component\n  - Ordinal_10305: GetComponentId - Extract component ID\n  - Ordinal_10707: ValidateComponentProperty - Validate component against criteria\n  - Ordinal_10600: GetComponentData - Get component data table entry\n  - Ordinal_10487: FindComponentOwner - Locate owner unit with 0x3f filter\n  - Ordinal_10259: GetComponentByIndex - Get component by index (5, 6, 7)\n  - GetUnitFromHashTable: Retrieve unit from hash lookup",
