      "comment": "Retrieve unit component data or stat value with fallback logic.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate component type <= 0xf (max 15 components)\n2. If unit pointer provided (non-null):\n   a. Load unit base component info and secondary values\n   b. Query component rendering properties via Ordinal_10369 (GetComponentInfo)\n   c. Call Ordinal_11013 (Component initialization) to update state\n   d. If component marked inactive (zero state):\n      - Check for alternate unit via Ordinal_10487 (IsLowResolution?) with 0x3f mask\n      - If found, use alternate unit via GetUnitFromHashTable; else use base unit\n      - Retrieve stat ID at offset 0x21 via Ordinal_10259 (GetStat?)\n      - If stat returns 0: check if component type 1 (return nDefault immediately)\n      - Otherwise query Ordinal_10889 (???) to validate component\n      - If validation fails, return nDefault\n      - Re-fetch stat ID from alternate/base unit for component type 1\n      - If component type 1 stat is 0, return nDefault\n   e. If component still invalid: call Ordinal_10747 (GetComponentType?) and check magic 'lit ' (0x2074696c)\n   f. If magic matches 'lit ' variant, return 0 (component lit/active)\n   g. Otherwise call Ordinal_10829 (SetComponentBuffer?) with component and &byComponentValid\n   h. If error returned, return error code\n3. Return nDefault\n\nParameters:\n  pUnitData: Unit structure containing component data\n  nComponentType: Component index (0-15, range validated)\n  nDefault: Fallback return value if component inactive/unavailable\n\nReturns:\n  nResult: Component stat value, 0 (lit component), nDefault (fallback), or error code\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Component type 1 has fast-path early return of nDefault\n  - Magic number 0x2074696c ('lit ' in little-endian) indicates lit/active component\n  - Alternate unit lookup via hash table handles complex unit references\n  - byComponentValid is single-byte buffer passed to Ordinal_10829 for state\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0xf: Maximum component type index\n  0x3f: Bitmask for alternate unit lookup\n  0x21: Offset to stat ID field in unit structure\n  1: Component type 1 (special validation)\n  0x2074696c: 'lit ' magic number indicating lit component\n  0x84: Offset to color/component field in unit data\n\nInline Comments: See decompiler comments for validation logic, magic number checks, and ordinal purposes.",
