      "comment": "Render unit graphics with component graphics overlay and viewport transformation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if in perspective mode (Ordinal_10010 == 0)\n   a. If perspective: Calculate relative viewport X using GetRelativeViewportX\n   b. Calculate unit screen X position (Ordinal_10333 - offset)\n   c. Calculate relative viewport Y using GetViewportYOffsetAdjusted\n   d. Calculate unit screen Y position (Ordinal_10334 - offset)\n2. If not perspective: Use quadrant transformation (Ordinal_10066) with scroll window mode\n   a. Get viewport coordinates via Ordinal_10330, Ordinal_10327\n   b. Apply screen width adjustment based on scroll mode: 1=subtract, 2=add\n3. Render unit component graphics at calculated viewport coordinates\n4. If rendering succeeded (CONCAT31 != 0), proceed to item lookup\n5. Check if unit has active stat 0x3f using Ordinal_10487\n   a. If stat active: Get unit node from hash table, extract unit record at offset 0x84\n   b. Otherwise: Use param_1[0x84] directly\n6. Get unit outfit/appearance data using Ordinal_10888\n7. Search for inventory item matching outfit appearance level in item database\n   a. Try SearchInventoryItemByStatAndLevel first\n   b. Fall back to GetGfxUnitRecord if not found\n   c. Assertion failure (0x626) if both fail\n8. Initialize component search: Extract unit base coordinates from param_1[0], param_1[4]\n9. Call Ordinal_11013 to transform coordinates\n10. Get graphics node by component ID using GetGfxNodeByID\n    a. Assertion failure (0x628) if not found\n11. Validate component index < 0x10\n    a. Assertion failure (0x46c) if invalid\n12. Search component array at [graphics_node + 0x1c] for matching component ID\n    a. Each component entry is 9 bytes\n    b. Count is at offset 0 of graphics node\n    c. Return success byte at offset 2 of matching entry\n    d. Return 0 if count exhausted\n\nParameters:\n  UnitAny * pUnit - IMPLICIT in ECX, unit record to render with graphics component\n  dword nComponent - IMPLICIT in EDX, component graphics index (0x0-0xf)\n\nReturns:\n  byte - Component found flag: non-zero if component ID matched, 0 if not found\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Assertion failures call FUN_6fb9a10f(-1) which terminates\n  - Component index must be < 0x10 or assertion fails\n  - Component array count of 0 returns 0\n  - If CONCAT31(extraout_var, render_result) == 0, returns render_result without item lookup\n  - Hash table lookup uses Ordinal_10487 stat check for unit appearance\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x3f - Unit appearance/stat flag for outfit determination\n  0x84 - Offset into UnitAny structure for unit record reference\n  0x1c - Offset into graphics node for component array start\n  0x9 - Size of each component entry (9 bytes)\n  0xf, 0x10 - Component count limit/validation constant\n  0x626, 0x628, 0x46c - Assertion error codes\n\nRelated Functions:\n  - RenderUnitComponentGraphics - Renders base unit graphics\n  - SearchInventoryItemByStatAndLevel - Finds inventory items by stats\n  - GetGfxUnitRecord - Retrieves graphics unit record\n  - GetGfxNodeByID - Retrieves graphics node structure\n  - GetScrollWindowMode - Returns scroll panel state (0=normal, 1=left, 2=right)\n  - Ordinal_10330, Ordinal_10327 - Get unit viewport coordinates\n  - Ordinal_10066 - Quadrant coordinate transformation\n  - Ordinal_10333, Ordinal_10334 - Get unit screen position\n  - Ordinal_10487 - Get unit stat value\n  - Ordinal_10888 - Get outfit appearance/gfx data\n  - Ordinal_11013 - Transform coordinate pair\n  - Ordinal_10010 - Get perspective mode flag",
