      "comment": "Allocate and initialize a graphics info field buffer\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Retrieve existing graphics info field for unit via GetGfxInfoField()\n2. If not allocated (NULL returned):\n   a. Allocate 0x47 bytes (71 bytes) via Ordinal_10042 (Fog.MemAlloc)\n   b. If allocation fails, trigger assertion error and exit with code -1\n3. Clear allocated buffer by writing 19 DWORDs (0x13 = 19) of zeros\n4. Store allocated graphics info buffer via SetGfxInfoField()\n\nParameters:\nnUnitIndex (int): Unit index to allocate graphics info for\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Function allocates memory and updates internal field\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Memory allocation failure triggers D2Common assertion (terminates program)\n- Clears exactly 19 DWORDs (76 bytes) if allocation occurs\n- Existing allocated buffers are reused (no double allocation)\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x47 (71 decimal) - Size of graphics info buffer to allocate\n0x13 (19 decimal) - Number of DWORDs to clear (19 * 4 = 76 bytes)",
