      "comment": "Sets X, Y, Z coordinates for a drawable object with fixed-point scaling.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Retrieve graphics info structure via GetGfxInfoField(nDrawableIndex)\n2. If structure exists (non-NULL pointer):\n   - Write nX << 0xB to offset +0x4 (X coordinate, 11-bit left shift = /2048 fixed-point)\n   - Write nY << 0xB to offset +0x8 (Y coordinate, 11-bit left shift = /2048 fixed-point)\n   - Write nZ << 0xB to offset +0xC (Z coordinate, 11-bit left shift = /2048 fixed-point)\n3. Return (stack cleanup of 4 parameters)\n\nParameters:\n  int nDrawableIndex - Index/ID of drawable object in graphics system\n  int nX - X coordinate to set (scaled by left shift 11)\n  int nY - Y coordinate to set (scaled by left shift 11)\n  int nZ - Z coordinate to set (scaled by left shift 11)\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If GetGfxInfoField returns NULL, function returns without modification\n  - Coordinates are scaled via 11-bit left shift (equivalent to *2048 in fixed-point)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0xB = 11 (bit shift count for fixed-point coordinate scaling)\n  0x4, 0x8, 0xC = Offsets in graphics info structure (+4, +8, +12 bytes)\n\nStructure Layout:\n  GfxInfo structure (inferred):\n  Offset | Size | Field Name     | Type   | Description\n  0x0    | 4    | (unknown)      | uint   | Header/unknown\n  0x4    | 4    | dwXCoord       | uint   | X coordinate (scaled)\n  0x8    | 4    | dwYCoord       | uint   | Y coordinate (scaled)\n  0xC    | 4    | dwZCoord       | uint   | Z coordinate (scaled)",
