      "comment": "Set GFX property values (position/offset) for a game object.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call GetGfxInfoField(nGfxId) to retrieve GFX info structure pointer\n2. If structure pointer is NULL, return immediately (no structure)\n3. If fScaleValues flag is set:\n   - Scale param_2 left 11 bits (multiply by 2048), store at offset +0x10\n   - Scale param_3 left 11 bits, store at offset +0x14\n   - Scale param_4 left 11 bits, store at offset +0x18\n4. If fScaleValues flag is clear:\n   - Store param_2 directly at offset +0x10\n   - Store param_3 directly at offset +0x14\n   - Store param_4 directly at offset +0x18\n\nParameters:\n- nGfxId (int): Graphics object ID to query\n- nValue1 (int): X position or offset value\n- nValue2 (int): Y position or offset value\n- nValue3 (int): Z position or offset value\n- fScaleValues (int): Flag - non-zero to scale values by 2048, zero for raw values\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If GetGfxInfoField returns NULL, all three offset fields remain unchanged\n- Bit shift left 11 (0xb) equivalent to multiplying by 2048\n- Used for both scaled fixed-point and raw integer coordinate storage",
