      "comment": "Sets graphics information structure coordinate fields with optional fixed-point scaling.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Retrieve graphics info structure via GetGfxInfoField(nGfxType)\n2. If structure pointer is null, exit\n3. If nShiftFlag is set, left-shift coordinates by 0xB (11 bits) for fixed-point format\n4. Write shifted/unshifted X coordinate to offset 0x1C\n5. Write shifted/unshifted Y coordinate to offset 0x20\n6. Write shifted/unshifted Z coordinate to offset 0x24\n\nParameters:\n- nGfxType (int): Graphics type identifier for structure lookup\n- nXCoord (int): X coordinate value (raw or fixed-point)\n- nYCoord (int): Y coordinate value (raw or fixed-point)\n- nZCoord (int): Z coordinate value (raw or fixed-point)\n- nShiftFlag (int): If nonzero, apply 11-bit left shift for fixed-point conversion\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- NULL structure pointer (GetGfxInfoField returns 0): Early exit, no fields modified\n- Zero nShiftFlag: Direct assignment without shifting\n- Nonzero nShiftFlag: Applies 0x800 multiplier (1 << 11) to each coordinate\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0xB (11): Bit shift count for fixed-point scaling (2048x multiplier)\n- 0x1C: Offset of X field in graphics structure\n- 0x20: Offset of Y field in graphics structure\n- 0x24: Offset of Z field in graphics structure\n\nGraphics Info Structure Layout:\n| Offset | Size | Field Name | Type | Description |\n| 0x1C   | 4    | nX         | int  | X coordinate (raw or fixed-point) |\n| 0x20   | 4    | nY         | int  | Y coordinate (raw or fixed-point) |\n| 0x24   | 4    | nZ         | int  | Z coordinate (raw or fixed-point) |",
