      "comment": "Apply RGB color effect values to graphics info structure (shift bits if flag set)\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call GetGfxInfoField(nGfxId) to retrieve graphics info pointer\n2. Return if pGfxInfo is NULL (gfx ID invalid)\n3. If fShiftBits != 0, shift R/G/B values left by 11 bits (multiply by 2048)\n4. Write shifted/unshifted R value to pGfxInfo+0x28\n5. Write shifted/unshifted G value to pGfxInfo+0x2c\n6. Write shifted/unshifted B value to pGfxInfo+0x30\n\nParameters:\n- nGfxId: Graphics ID (passed to GetGfxInfoField)\n- nRedValue: Red component value (0-255 typical)\n- nGreenValue: Green component value (0-255 typical)\n- nBlueValue: Blue component value (0-255 typical)\n- fShiftBits: Flag controlling bit shift (0=direct, non-zero=shift left 11)\n\nReturns:\n- void (always succeeds, silently returns if gfx ID invalid)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Invalid gfx ID: GetGfxInfoField returns NULL, all writes skipped\n- Bit shift (<<11): Scales RGB values for internal fixed-point representation\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x28: Offset to red value in graphics info structure\n- 0x2c: Offset to green value in graphics info structure\n- 0x30: Offset to blue value in graphics info structure\n- 0xb (11): Left shift amount for value scaling",
