      "instructions": ["0xC7C90|MOV|ECX, dword ptr [ESP + 0x4]", "0xC7C94|SUB|ESP, 0x8", "0xC7C97|PUSH|EBX", "0xC7C98|PUSH|EBP", "0xC7C99|PUSH|ESI", "0xC7C9A|PUSH|EDI", "0xC7C9B|CALL|0x6fb931c0", "0xC7CA0|MOV|ESI, EAX", "0xC7CA2|TEST|ESI, ESI", "0xC7CA4|JZ|0x6fb97ef6", "0xC7CAA|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [ESI]", "0xC7CAC|TEST|AL, 0x1", "0xC7CAE|JNZ|0x6fb97ef6", "0xC7CB4|MOV|ECX, dword ptr [ESI + 0x10]", "0xC7CB7|MOV|EDX, dword ptr [ESI + 0x1c]"],
      "comment": "Updates graphics rendering info offsets for viewport transformation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Fetch graphics info block for unit via GetGfxInfoField()\n2. Return if pointer invalid or rendering disabled (flag 0x01)\n3. Apply velocity deltas to position offsets (x, y, z components)\n4. Update animation frame counter, decrement if flag 0x02 set\n5. If rotated (flag 0x04): Update rotation angle via lookup table\n6. If has unit reference (flag 0x10): Fetch unit, extract graphic frame/type\n7. Call ProcessUnitGfxInitialization to calculate actual frame/type offsets\n8. Apply unit-specific graphics adjustments (e.g., +10 for monster type 3)\n9. Update viewport position arrays via Ordinal_10108\n10. For non-rotated modes: Check viewport boundaries, update position if outside\n11. Set rendering active flag (0x01) at end\n\nParameters:\npUnitId (int *) - pointer to unit id (1=player, 3=monster, etc)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - updates graphics structure in-place\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Unit type 1 uses frame offset 8, type 3 uses frame offset 14 (0xe)\n- Monster type 3 with ID 0 or 0xc skips processing (early return)\n- Flag 0x20 disables boundary checking\n- Rotation angle uses fixed-point magic number 0xae147ae1 for conversion\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x01 - Graphics rendering active flag\n0x02 - Animation frame countdown active flag\n0x04 - Rotated graphics mode flag\n0x10 - Has unit reference flag\n0x20 - Skip boundary check flag\n0x800 - Fixed-point scaling divisor (11-bit shift)\n0x0b - Right shift count for fixed-point conversion\n0xae147ae1 - Magic multiplier for rotation angle conversion\n0x48/0x40/0x44/0x30 - Field offsets in graphics structure",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "STRUCT_ItemData", "UNIT_MONSTER", "PARAM_1", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData", "STRUCT_StatList", "PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Path", "STRUCT_Skill", "SRC_Particle.cpp"]
