      "comment": "Set or clear graphics info flag 0x10 for a graphics object.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call GetGfxInfoField(dwGfxInfoId) to retrieve graphics flags pointer\n2. If pointer is NULL, return early (no graphics info)\n3. If fEnable is TRUE, set flag bit 0x10 via OR operation\n4. If fEnable is FALSE, clear flag bit 0x10 via AND with 0xFFFFFFEF\n5. Store modified flags back to graphics info structure\n\nParameters:\ndwGfxInfoId (uint) - Graphics object identifier passed to GetGfxInfoField\nfEnable (bool) - TRUE to set flag 0x10, FALSE to clear it\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value, modifies graphics info flags in-place\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If graphics object not found (NULL pointer returned), operation silently returns\n- Flag 0x10 meaning: graphics rendering or display-related flag state\n\nRelated Functions:\n- GetGfxInfoField() - Retrieves graphics info structure pointer",
