      "comment": "Set animation flag in graphics frame data.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Retrieve graphics frame information pointer by calling GetGfxInfoField(nGfxInfoId)\n2. If pointer is valid (non-NULL):\n   a. Load current flags value from pointer (dereference)\n   b. Clear bit 0 using AND with 0xFFFFFFFE (bit 0 = 0)\n   c. Set bit 3 using OR with 0x8 (bit 3 = 1)\n   d. Store modified flags back to memory\n3. Return (void function)\n\nParameters:\nnGfxInfoId (int): Graphics information record identifier\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If GetGfxInfoField returns NULL, function does nothing (early exit via NULL check)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0xFFFFFFFE - Bit mask to clear bit 0 (frame active indicator)\n0x8 - Bit value 3 set (animation enabled flag)\n\nRelated Functions:\n- GetGfxInfoField() - Retrieves pointer to graphics frame data\n- SetDrawableObjectCoordinates() - Called before this to set base animation parameters\n- FUN_6fb97f90() - Called before this to apply initial animation effects",
