      "comment": "Reads and processes file data with system validation and error handling.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call Ordinal_10102 (Storm.IsInitialized) to check if system initialized\n2. If not initialized, log error via Ordinal_10026 and abort with FUN_6fb9a10f(-1)\n3. Call ValidateAndHandleState to validate handle state\n4. Call Ordinal_10042 with dwMode to read/process data and return byte count\n5. If bytes read = 0, return immediately (no data)\n6. Call FUN_6fb99435 to process read data\n7. Check validity of nStatus result - if zero, assertion error\n8. Call Ordinal_10103 to finalize operation\n9. Store result nStatus in pDataOut pointer if provided\n10. Return nResult (bytes processed) to caller\n\nParameters:\n  nHandle: File handle or context ID (int) - IMPLICIT ECX register\n  dwFlags: Operation flags/configuration (DWORD) - IMPLICIT EDX register\n  pDataOut: Optional output pointer for processed result (int*) - may be NULL\n  dwSize: Size of data region to process (DWORD)\n  dwMode: Processing mode/operation type (DWORD)\n\nReturns:\n  int - Number of bytes processed, 0 if operation failed or no data\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If system not initialized, terminates immediately via assertion\n  - If result data is invalid, terminates with D2Common assertion\n  - NULL pDataOut pointer is handled gracefully (data discarded)\n  - Magic number 0x320 is offset in structure for data region\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x320: Offset within structure to data processing region\n  0x3b: Error line number (from source file reference)\n  0x49: Assertion line number (from source file reference)\n  -1: Termination code passed to FUN_6fb9a10f\n\nNote: Function uses 3 stack-allocated temporaries optimized away.",
