      "comment": "Iterate through linked list of automated messages and free each entry with SMemFree.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load pointer from [pListBase + 8] - beginning of linked list\n2. Validate pointer is >= 1 (non-zero, non-negative)\n3. Loop while pointer not NULL:\n   a. Call cleanup function thunk_FUN_6fb997be(pCurItem) - destructor\n   b. Call Ordinal_403 (SMemFree) to deallocate pCurItem with RTTI class \".?AUTMESSAGESOURCE@@\"\n   c. Load next item from [pCurItem + 8]\n4. Exit loop when pointer becomes NULL\n\nParameters:\npListBase - Base address of list header; offset +8 contains first list entry pointer\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Function returns to caller after all items freed\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Handles invalid pointers: if loaded pointer < 1, treats as NULL\n- Offset 0x8 is consistent linked-list pointer field location\n- RTTI string \".?AUTMESSAGESOURCE@@\" indicates C++ automated message class\n- Ordinal_403 is Storm.dll SMemFree function\n\nRelated Functions:\n- thunk_FUN_6fb997be - Calls destructor on individual list item",
