      "comment": "Allocate and initialize a language entry in items array.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate offset by adding 0x0c to nDataOffset parameter\n2. Call Ordinal_401 (SMemAlloc) to allocate memory with flags (dwFlags | 0x08)\n3. Check allocation result for NULL pointer\n4. If allocation failed, return NULL\n5. If successful, zero-initialize first two dwords of allocated block\n6. If nEntryIndex is non-zero, call FUN_6fb99728 to configure entry\n7. Return allocated entry pointer\n\nParameters:\npItemsArray (LanguageItemsArray *) - IMPLICIT ECX: Array container for language items\nnEntryIndex (int) - Index/identifier for entry (0 skips configuration)\nnDataOffset (int) - Base offset into data structure (0x0c added before allocation)\ndwFlags (uint) - Memory allocation flags (0x08 bit set for this allocation)\n\nReturns:\nAllocated entry pointer (uint *) on success, NULL (0x0) on allocation failure\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Magic constant 0xfffffffe (-2) passed as allocation flag to SMemAlloc\n- If nEntryIndex == 0, returns zero-initialized block without calling FUN_6fb99728\n- Return type is uint* allowing array-style access: pEntry[0], pEntry[1], etc.\n- Calling code accesses returned pointer as array (e.g., pEntry[2] for index storage)",
