      "comment": "Process buffered data through I/O handlers with buffer management and error handling\n\nNote: Function uses 5 SSA/compiler temporaries (piVar1, pcVar1-4, iVar2-3, uVar3) that are optimized away in decompilation and cannot be renamed. See Algorithm for logical variable mappings.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. szTotalSize = dwElementSize * dwElementCount; initialize to output buffer size\n2. If szTotalSize is zero, set dwElementCount = 0 and return\n3. szDestPtr = szData; szRemainingSize = szTotalSize\n4. Get buffer limit: (pIOState[6] != 0) ? pIOState[6] : 0x1000\n5. Loop until szRemainingSize == 0:\n   a. Check if I/O state closed: (pIOState[3] & 0x10c) == 0 OR pIOState[1] == NULL\n   b. If closed/empty state:\n      - If szRemainingSize < buffer limit: single-char read via GetCharFromHandler\n      - Check for error return 0xffffffff; if error: set pIOState[3] |= 0x10, return\n      - Store byte to *szDestPtr, update pIOState[6] (context), szDestPtr++, szRemainingSize--\n      - Else: bulk copy via CopyDataToBuffer with size = szRemainingSize % buffer_limit\n      - Check return: 0=complete (set 0x10), -1=error (set 0x20), else=bytes_written\n   c. Else if open state with data:\n      - szCopySize = min(szRemainingSize, pIOState[1])\n      - Copy via MemcpyDataBlock(pIOState[4], szDestPtr, szCopySize)\n      - Update: szRemainingSize -= szCopySize; pIOState[1] -= szCopySize\n      - pIOState[0] += szCopySize; szDestPtr += szCopySize\n6. Return (szTotalSize - szRemainingSize) / dwElementSize\n\nParameters:\nszData (char *) - Pointer to destination buffer for processed data\ndwElementSize (uint) - Size of each element in bytes\ndwElementCount (uint) - Number of elements to write\npIOState (int *) - Pointer to I/O state structure with fields:\n  [0] Current input position (offset within buffered data)\n  [1] Available input data size (bytes remaining in buffer)\n  [3] State flags: 0x10=EOF/complete, 0x20=critical error, 0x100/0x10c=closed state mask\n  [4] Buffer