      "comment": "Convert string to lowercase or apply locale-based character mapping. Handles both uninitialized and initialized locale mapping states with thread synchronization.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize output buffer to NULL\n2. If locale mapping not initialized, perform simple ASCII uppercase-to-lowercase conversion (A-Z to a-z)\n3. Otherwise:\n   a. Increment critical section lock counter atomically\n   b. Check if initialization queue is empty (fQueueEmpty = g_dwInitializationQueueDepth == 0)\n   c. If queue not empty, decrement counter and signal waiting thread with error 0x13\n   d. If locale mapping still uninitialized after check:\n      - Decrement counter if queue was empty, otherwise signal completion with FUN_6fb9b6fd(0x13)\n      - Perform ASCII lowercase conversion\n   e. Otherwise (locale mapping initialized):\n      - Call FUN_6fb9f4c1 to get required buffer size with parameters (0x100, input string, -1, NULL)\n      - If size > 0, allocate buffer with malloc\n      - If buffer allocated, call FUN_6fb9f4c1 again with allocated buffer to perform locale-based conversion\n      - If conversion successful (return != 0), call FUN_6fb9f840 to apply conversion to input buffer\n      - Decrement counter or signal completion\n      - Call FUN_6fb9b712 to free temporary buffer\n\nParameters:\n  pszInput (char *) - IMPLICIT: Pointer to null-terminated input string to convert, modified in-place\n\nReturns:\n  char * - Pointer to the input string (pszInput) after conversion\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If locale mapping uninitialized, function performs simple ASCII case conversion (0x41-0x5A converted by adding 0x20)\n  - Thread synchronization uses InterlockedIncrement/InterlockedDecrement for g_dwCriticalSectionLockedCount\n  - Magic number 0x13 used as error/completion code for queue signal handlers\n  - Buffer size 0x100 (256) used as fixed size limit for locale mapping operations\n  - Conversion value 0x20 (space character in ASCII) used as offset for uppercase-to-lowercase conversion",
