      "comment": "Validate stream property ID and set result in TLS context.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get TLS context buffer pointer (offset +3)\n2. Store input property ID in TLS buffer\n3. Search property lookup table (g_dwStreamPropertyTable) with stride 8 bytes:\n   - Iterate through table entries until match or table end\n   - If match: retrieve corresponding value (at matched_index * 8 + 0x6fbd9504)\n4. If not found in table, check range constraints:\n   - If 0x12 < dwPropertyId < 0x25: set result to 0xD\n   - If 0xBB < dwPropertyId < 0xCA: set result to 0x8\n   - Otherwise: set result to 0x16\n5. Store result in TLS context buffer (offset +2)\n\nParameters:\ndwPropertyId (uint): Stream property identifier to validate\n\nReturns:\n(void) Result value stored in TLS context offset +2:\n- Lookup table value if match found\n- 0xD for range 0x13-0x24\n- 0x8 for range 0xBC-0xCA\n- 0x16 for all other values\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- TLS context must be initialized before call\n- Lookup table has paired 8-byte elements (ID, value pairs)\n- Range checks are exclusive of boundaries (< not <=)\n- Function contains SSA temporaries optimized away (puVar1, pdVar2)\n\nRelated Functions:\n- GetOrCreateTlsContext() - Provides TLS storage\n- FUN_6fb9eaf1() - Retrieves TLS context\n- FUN_6fb9eae8() - Gets offset +2 in TLS context",
