      "comment": "Writes formatted error message from table to stdout or displays error dialog.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Search g_ppErrorMessages array for matching error code (8-byte strides)\n2. If found and g_nErrorHandlingEnabled=1, write message to StdErr via WriteFile\n3. If error handling disabled or g_nStdErrorFlagSet=1, build dialog text:\n   - Retrieve module path via GetModuleFileNameA (max 0x104=260 bytes)\n   - Build header: \"Runtime Error!\n\nProgram: <path>\n\n<message>\"\n   - If path+header > 0x3C chars (60), truncate with \"...\"\n4. Display MessageBox via FUN_6fba30f0 with \"Microsoft Visual C++ Runtime Library\" caption\n5. Error code 1 or special flag triggers alternate handler with _abort_termination\n\nParameters:\nnErrorCode - Error code to locate in g_ppErrorMessages\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return; function terminates via dialog/abort\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x104 (260) - MAX_PATH buffer size for module filename\n0x3C (60) - Maximum path length before truncation in dialog\n0xFC (252) - Special error code bypassing dialog (invalid/unrecognized)\n0xFFFFFFFF4 - Standard error device handle (GetStdHandle)\n0x12010 - MessageBox flags for error display\n\nSpecial Cases:\nEmpty module path falls back to \"<program name unknown>\"\nPath exceeding 60 chars auto-truncates with \"...\" suffix\nError code 0xFC skips standard error handling\nError code 1 or g_nErrorHandlingEnabled=0 uses alternate path",
