      "comment": "Validates buffer expansion and updates size metadata.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load current size from first byte of pbBuffer\n2. Calculate metadata pointer offset: nAllocContext + ((pbBuffer offset >> 12) * 8) + 0x18\n3. If dwNewSize < byCurrentSize: Update size, adjust delta, set flag 0xf1, return 1\n4. If dwNewSize == byCurrentSize: Return 1 (no change)\n5. If dwNewSize > byCurrentSize: Scan from current to new size\n6. Verify all bytes in expansion region are 0x00\n7. Update size field\n8. If metadata pointer within expansion range: Count trailing zeros\n9. Update metadata pointer and padding count\n10. Adjust metadata delta and return 1\n11. Return 0 on any validation failure\n\nParameters:\nnAllocContext (int) - Base of allocation context structure\npbBuffer (byte *) - Buffer pointer for offset calculation\nbyCurrentSize (byte) - Current size of buffer in bytes\ndwNewSize (uint) - New size to validate and apply\n\nReturns:\n1 - Success, size and metadata updated\n0 - Failure: bounds exceeded, non-zero bytes detected, or invalid range\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Maximum buffer size 0xf8 bytes\n- Expansion region must contain only 0x00 bytes\n- Metadata updates depend on pointer position relative to expansion",
