      "comment": "Performs right bit shift operation on 128-bit integer stored as 4-element uint32 array.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate word shifts (dwShiftCount / 0x20) and bit shifts (dwShiftCount % 0x20)\n2. Initialize carry accumulator (param_2 = 0) and bit shift amount (byBitShifts)\n3. For each of 4 array elements (index 0-3):\n   a. Load current element value (dwCurrentElement)\n   b. Shift element right by bit amount, OR with previous carry\n   c. Calculate new carry from bits being shifted out\n   d. Store shifted result back to array element\n   e. Advance to next element pointer\n4. Handle additional word-level shifts for elements 2 down to 0:\n   a. If source index < word shifts: clear destination element (set to 0)\n   b. Otherwise: copy element from shifted source position\n   c. Decrement both source index and destination offset by 4 bytes\n\nParameters:\n  pBigInteger: Pointer to 4-element uint32 array representing 128-bit integer\n  dwShiftCount: Number of bits to shift right (0-127 valid range)\n\nReturns:\n  void - Operation modifies array in-place\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Shift count 0: No operation performed, array unchanged\n  - Shift count >= 32: Combines bit shifts with word-level element movement\n  - Shift count >= 128: All elements become 0 (complete right shift out)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x20 (32): Bits per 32-bit word, used for word/bit shift separation\n  0x1f (31): Bit mask for shift amount (ensures valid 0-31 bit shifts)\n  0x3: Initial element counter (processes 4 elements: indices 0,1,2,3)\n  0x8 (8): Starting byte offset for element 2 (8 = 2 * sizeof(uint32))\n  0x2: Starting element index for reverse copy (element 2)\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset | Size | Field       | Type | Description\n-------|------|-------------|------|----------------------------------\n0x00   | 4    | element[0]  | uint | Least significant 32 bits\n0x04   | 4    | element[1]  | uint | Second 32-bit word  \n0x08   | 4    | element[2]  | uint | Third 32-bit word\n0