      "comment": "Convert locale-mapped byte character to wide character using code page translation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate input: wszDest may be NULL, pbSrc and dwCchMax must be non-zero\n2. Load first byte from pbSrc into byChar\n3. If byChar is null (0x00):\n   - If wszDest provided, write wide null terminator (0x0000)\n   - Return 0 (no conversion)\n4. If locale map NOT initialized (g_fLocaleMapInitialized == 0):\n   - If wszDest provided, write byChar as wide character (sign-extended)\n   - Return 1 (1 character output)\n5. Check binding state flag for byChar in g_pBindingStates array (offset = byChar*2+1):\n   - If 0x80 bit CLEAR: Single-byte conversion\n     - Call MultiByteToWideChar(g_dwDefaultCodePage, 9, pbSrc, 1, wszDest, boolDest)\n     - Return 1 if success, else fall through to error\n   - If 0x80 bit SET: Multi-byte conversion\n     - If g_dwBindingMode > 1 and dwCchMax < g_dwBindingMode: fail\n     - Call MultiByteToWideChar(g_dwDefaultCodePage, 9, pbSrc, g_dwBindingMode, wszDest, boolDest)\n     - Return g_dwBindingMode if success\n     - If dwCchMax >= g_dwBindingMode AND pbSrc[1] != 0: return g_dwBindingMode\n6. On error: Set TLS context slot to 0x2a (error code), return 0xFFFFFFFF\n\nParameters:\n- wszDest (wchar_t*): Destination buffer for wide character (may be NULL for size query)\n- pbSrc (byte*): Source buffer with at least 1 byte (may contain multi-byte sequence)\n- dwCchMax (dword): Maximum characters available in wszDest (0 if NULL)\n\nReturns:\n- 1: Single-byte character converted\n- g_dwBindingMode (usually 1-2): Multi-byte character converted\n- 0: Null character encountered or uninitialized state\n- 0xFFFFFFFF: Error (TLS slot set to 0x2a error code)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Multi-byte sequences: Check g_dwBindingMode for sequence length\n- Code page 9 (CP_OEMCP): OEM code page conversion\n- Locale initialization: Early return with single-byte output if map not ready\n- NULL destination: boolDest parameter prevents actual writing\n-