      "comment": "Performs a left shift by 1 bit on a 96-bit value represented as three 32-bit integers.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Cache the original low and mid 32-bit values for carry propagation\n2. Shift low 32-bit word left by 1 (multiply by 2)\n3. Shift mid 32-bit word left by 1 and add carry from low word (bit 31 → bit 0)\n4. Shift high 32-bit word left by 1 and add carry from mid word (bit 31 → bit 0)\n5. Store all three shifted values back to the bitfield structure\n\nParameters:\n- pBitfield96: Pointer to 96-bit value stored as array of 3 uint values\n  [0] = low 32 bits, [1] = mid 32 bits, [2] = high 32 bits\n\nReturns:\n- void (modifies input bitfield in-place)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Carry propagation: 0x1f extracts bit 31 (MSB) for carry to next higher word\n- Overflow: High bit (bit 95) is lost if set before the shift operation\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n- 0x1f: Shift count to extract bit 31 (MSB) as carry bit\n- * 2: Left shift by 1 bit (equivalent to << 1)\n- << 1: Direct left shift by 1 bit for high word\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset | Size | Field Name | Type | Description\n-------|------|------------|------|-------------\n0x00   | 4    | dwLowBits  | uint | Low 32 bits (bits 0-31)\n0x04   | 4    | dwMidBits  | uint | Mid 32 bits (bits 32-63)\n0x08   | 4    | dwHighBits | uint | High 32 bits (bits 64-95)",
