      "comment": "Parses a string representation of a floating-point number into extended float components.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Skip leading whitespace characters (space, tab, newline, carriage return)\n2. Initialize state machine with 12 parsing states (0-11) for different number parts\n3. Parse optional sign character (+ or -), storing sign bit in wSignBits (0x8000 for negative)\n4. State 0: Initial state - handle sign, leading zero, or first digit\n5. State 1: After leading zero - check for decimal point or exponent notation\n6. State 2: After sign - require digit or decimal point\n7. State 3: Integer part parsing - collect digits into abDigitBuffer, track dwDigitCount\n8. State 4: Fractional part parsing - collect digits after decimal point\n9. State 5: After decimal point - require at least one digit\n10. State 6: Exponent character found (E/e) - prepare for exponent parsing\n11. State 7: Exponent sign parsing - handle +/- after exponent character\n12. State 8: Leading zeros in exponent - skip and track position\n13. State 9: Exponent value parsing - accumulate nExponentValue (max 5200)\n14. State 10-11: Error recovery and cleanup states\n15. Convert collected digits to binary using FUN_10021ec1 (digit to binary conversion)\n16. Calculate final exponent: nExponentValue + nExponentAdjust + nDecimalScale + nExponentOffset\n17. Apply precision scaling using FUN_1002290c if exponent in valid range (-5200 to +5200)\n18. Handle overflow (nReturnCode=2) and underflow (nReturnCode=1) conditions\n19. Store result components: wMantissaLow, wExponentField, dwMantissaHigh, wSignBits\n20. Return parsing status code indicating success or error type\n\nParameters:\nthis - Method object pointer (thiscall convention)\npExtFloat - Output buffer for parsed extended float components (mantissa and exponent fields)\nppszEndPosition - Receives pointer to first character after parsed number in input string\npszInputString - Input string containing number representation to parse\nnPrecision - Decimal precision control parameter for rounding and accuracy\nnDecimalScale - Scale factor applied to decimal point position during parsing\nnExponentOffset - Bias value added to final exponent calculation\nbEnableExponent - Boolean flag enabling/disabling scientific notation parsing (E/e)\n\nReturns:\n0 - Parse error or invalid input format detected\n1 - Underflow condition (number too small to represent)\n2 - Overflow condition (number too large to represent)  \n3 - Reserved status code\n4 - Success with valid number parsed and stored\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Leading whitespace automatically skipped before parsing begins\n- Multiple consecutive zeros treated as single zero value\n- Decimal point without digits triggers error return\n- Exponent values exceeding ±5200 clamped to prevent integer overflow\n- Empty or null input strings return error status immediately\n- Mixed case exponent notation (E/e) supported when bEnableExponent enabled\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x20 (32) - ASCII space character for whitespace detection\n0x09 (9) - ASCII tab character for whitespace detection  \n0x0A (10) - ASCII newline character for whitespace detection\n0x0D (13) - ASCII carriage return for whitespace detection\n0x30 (48) - ASCII '0' character for digit conversion base\n0x8000 (32768) - Sign bit mask for negative number indication\n0x19 (25) - Maximum digits storable in abDigitBuffer before overflow\n0x1450 (5200) - Maximum/minimum exponent value to prevent overflow\n0x7FFF (32767) - Maximum positive exponent field value\n0x80000000 - Infinity representation for overflow conditions\n\nError Handling:\n- Invalid characters trigger immediate parsing termination\n- Exponent overflow/underflow handled gracefully with saturation\n- Buffer overflow protection prevents stack corruption from excessive digits\n- State machine prevents infinite loops through explicit state transitions\n- Parse position tracking enables caller error recovery and continuation\n\nState Machine:\nState 0: Initial - Whitespace/Sign/Zero/Digit detection\nState 1: Post-Zero - Decimal/Exponent/Continuation decision  \nState 2: Post-Sign - Require valid number start\nState 3: Integer-Part - Accumulate whole number digits\nState 4: Fraction-Part - Accumulate decimal digits with scaling\nState 5: Post-Decimal - Validate fractional part presence\nState 6: Exponent-Start - Validate exponent notation format\nState 7: Exponent-Sign - Process exponent sign character\nState 8: Exponent-Leading - Handle leading zeros in exponent\nState 9: Exponent-Digits - Accumulate exponent magnitude\nState 10: Error-State - Cleanup and error indication\nState 11: Conditional-Exponent - Branch based on bEnableExponent flag",
